   )]\n            #[action(namespace = $namespace)]\n            $(#[$attr])*\n            pub struct $name;\n        )*\n    };\n    ([ $( $(#[$attr:meta])* $name:ident),* $(,)? ]) => {\n        $(\n            #[derive(\n                ::std::clone::Clone,\n                ::std::cmp::PartialEq,\n                ::std::default::Default,\n                ::std::fmt::Debug,\n                $crate::Action\n            )]\n            $(#[$attr])*\n            pub struct $name;\n        )*\n    };\n}\n\n// Public facade decision — 2026-09-08:\n// GPUI Kit is the application-facing entry point. Users should depend on and\n// import gpui-kit without needing to know which GPUI crates implement it.\n// Keep GPUI APIs available through the Kit root and preserve the published\n// #[gpui_kit::test] macro. Do not replace it with Rust's built-in #[test].\n// A future switch to official GPUI crates is an internal dependency migration,\n// not a reason to steer Kit users toward gpui:: paths or require import changes.\n// Keep the existing gpui namespace re-export hidden for source compatibility;\n// it is not the recommended application API.\n//\n// With test-support, the glob below includes GPUI's test macro. Test modules\n// should import their Kit types explicitly to avoid shadowing Rust's #[test].\npub use ::gpui::*;\n\n#[doc(hidden)]\npub use ::gpui;\n\n/// UI integration testing: render real components in headless windows, dispatch\n/// pointer and keyboard events, and assert state, focus, layout and callbacks.\n/// Run tests with `#[gpui_kit::test]`; use this module to interact with their UI.\n#[cfg(feature = \"test-support\")]\npub mod test;\n\npub use ::gpui_base as base;\n#[cfg(not(any(target_os = \"ios\", target_os = \"android\")))]\npub use ::gpui_platform as platform;\n#[cfg(target_family = \"wasm\")]\npub use ::gpui_web as web;\npub use gpui_base::is_mobile;\n\n/// The styled component library.\n///\n/// ```no_run\n/// use gpui_kit::component::button::*;\n/// use gpui_kit::*;\n///\n/// struct Hello;\n///\n/// impl Render for Hello {\n///     fn render(&mut self, _: &mut Window, _: &mut Context<Self>) -> impl IntoElement {\n///         div().child(Button::new(\"ok\").primary().label(\"Let's Go!\"))\n///     }\n/// }\n///\n/// fn main() {\n///     gpui_kit::application().run(|cx| {\n///         gpui_kit::init(cx);\n///         gpui_kit::open_window(WindowOptions::default(), cx, |_, cx| cx.new(|_| Hello))\n///             .expect(\"failed to open window\");\n///     });\n/// }\n/// ```\n#[cfg(feature = \"component\")]\npub use ::gpui_component as component;\n\n#[cfg(feature = \"assets\")]\npub use ::gpui_kit_assets as assets;\n\n/// Open a window with a Base Root and return the window and application content.\n/// Applications own quit/close actions and confirmation flows.\n/// Call [`init`] before opening application windows.\n/// The builder returns application content, not another Root.\n///\n/// In an async context, call this inside `cx.update`.\npub fn open_window<V: Render>(\n    options: WindowOptions,\n    cx: &mut App,\n    build: impl FnOnce(&mut Window, &mut App) -> Entity<V>,\n) -> Result<(AnyWindowHandle, Entity<V>)> {\n    let mut built = None;\n    let window = cx.open_window(options, |window, cx| {\n        let view = build(window, cx);\n        built = Some(view.clone());\n        cx.new(|cx| base::Root::new(view, window, cx))\n    })?;\n    Ok((\n        window.into(),\n        built.expect(\"open_window ran its build closure\"),\n    ))\n}\n\n// Mobile applications provide their platform with `Application::with_platform`.\n#[cfg(not(any(target_os = \"ios\", target_os = \"android\")))]\npub use ::gpui_platform::application;\n\n/// Initializes every enabled layer. Call it once, before using anything else.\n///\n/// With the `component` feature (on by default) this is\n/// `gpui_component::init`, which also initializes `gpui-base`; otherwise it\n/// is `gpui_base::init`.\npub fn init(cx: &mut App) {\n    #[cfg(feature = \"component\")]\n    gpui_component::init(cx);\n    #[cfg(not(feature = \"component\"))]\n    gpui_base::init(cx);\n}\n\n/// Fluent UI test observation, inert unless `test-support` is enabled.\npub use gpui_base::TestSupportExt;\n"},"started_at_ms":1791203089347,"completed_at_ms":1791203089347}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-05T12:24:49.368Z","ordinal":40286,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a10537-909f-77a3-96d8-dd07161f91ae","turn_id":"01a10c03-2660-75c2-b09f-9987333f7d6c","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-6e6e238e-766d-4446-a8d6-ea2c390a56ee","process_id":"41429","command":["/bin/bash","-lc","rtk proxy sed -n '1,200p' desktop/gpui/fixtures/gen-ui/README.md"],"cwd":"file:///home/diogenes/Projects/twyne","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"rtk proxy sed -n '1,200p' desktop/gpui/fixtures/gen-ui/README.md"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"# In-flow writing tools\n\nThe full hosted Twyne desktop remains the reference. This wave covers four\nnative tool bodies and their spec, stream and deterministic seed contracts.\n\n`src/gen_ui/view.rs` implements Sentence Lab, Rhythm Strip, Claim Check and\nReader Questions with the existing original fonts, palette and Source spacing.\nRetained inputs survive streamed props. Rhythm bars emit hover, focus and\nselection requests. Jot and research require qualified host acknowledgments;\na retired tool ignores late results.\n\nThe view is exported but **not mounted in WritingRoom**. The margin rail,\npopover/card positioning, saved-tool shelf and naming/footer, editor commands,\nstruggle tracking, provider requests and actual Apparatus/notebook callbacks\nremain to be integrated. Source/native render and interaction comparisons have\nnot been performed. Checkbox appearance, inline hint layout, stepper geometry,\ntooltips and hover/focus paint still require that work.\n\nSource opens deterministic writer material without applying model-output\nlength limits. `ToolSnapshot::seeded` and `fill_offline` preserve that behavior;\n`ToolSnapshot::new` validates externally supplied specs. Every streamed\ncandidate is validated, retaining its preceding snapshot on failure. A model\ncannot rewrite the writer's sentence or earlier attempts.\n\nThe oracles execute unchanged Source TypeScript with `@json-render/core` 0.21.0\nand Zod 4.4.3. They retain 45 validation results, 32 snapshots from 18 cumulative\nstream cases, 59 deterministic seeds and offline fill results, and 11\nsentence/word cases. The focused native tests also cover retained edits, local\nsupport choices, exact live acknowledgments, retired requests and long writer\nmaterial. Receipts and full logs live under `target/verification`; the current\npointers start with `genui-`. Failed earlier receipts are retained.\n\nRun the Root-owned checks sequentially:\n\n```sh\nrtk proxy python3 desktop/gpui/fixtures/gen-ui/check.py core\nrtk proxy python3 desktop/gpui/fixtures/gen-ui/check.py desktop\n```\n\nThese checks do not launch or replace the user's preview. No Source web/Convex\nfile, provider registration or account data is changed by this wave.\n\nThe `*-proposal` directories preserve actual Sakana fugu-max outputs and inputs.\nParent review corrected Rust syntax/types, stream tests, JS whitespace,\nwrapper normalization, Source safe integers, sentence regex and JSON\nconstruction. The action review remains advisory; check its statements against\nSource when mounting the editor.\n\nRust/serde_json cannot represent JavaScript lone UTF-16 surrogates. That is an\nopen parity gap for escaped model strings, changed cumulative offsets inside a\npair, and support labels sliced through a pair at 60 units. Unsupported label\nedits currently preserve the writer's input.\n\nThe next integration must translate Source `textContent`/`posAtOffset` through\nthe native rich document model, preserve marks and undo, and qualify callbacks\nby folio, visit and tool identity. ProseMirror offsets cannot be copied into\nnative scalar coordinates. Connected account, knowledge-base and AI transport\nwork remains part of the full port objective.\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"# In-flow writing tools\n\nThe full hosted Twyne desktop remains the reference. This wave covers four\nnative tool bodies and their spec, stream and deterministic seed contracts.\n\n`src/gen_ui/view.rs` implements Sentence Lab, Rhythm Strip, Claim Check and\nReader Questions with the existing original fonts, palette and Source spacing.\nRetained inputs survive streamed props. Rhythm bars emit hover, focus and\nselection requests. Jot and research require qualified host acknowledgments;\na retired tool ignores late results.\n\nThe view is exported but **not mounted in WritingRoom**. The margin rail,\npopover/card positioning, saved-tool shelf and naming/footer, editor commands,\nstruggle tracking, provider requests and actual Apparatus/notebook callbacks\nremain to be integrated. Source/native render and interaction comparisons have\nnot been performed. Checkbox appearance, inline hint layout, stepper geometry,\ntooltips and hover/focus paint still require that work.\n\nSource opens deterministic writer material without applying model-output\nlength limits. `ToolSnapshot::seeded` and `fill_offline` preserve that behavior;\n`ToolSnapshot::new` validates externally supplied specs. Every streamed\ncandidate is validated, retaining its preceding snapshot on failure. A model\ncannot rewrite the writer's sentence or earlier attempts.\n\nThe oracles execute unchanged Source TypeScript with `@json-render/core` 0.21.0\nand Zod 4.4.3. They retain 45 validation results, 32 snapshots from 18 cumulative\nstream cases, 59 deterministic seeds and offline fill results, and 11\nsentence/word cases. The focused native tests also cover retained edits, local\nsupport choices, exact live acknowledgments, retired requests and long writer\nmaterial. Receipts and full logs live under `target/verification`; the current\npointers start with `genui-`. Failed earlier receipts are retained.\n\nRun the Root-owned checks sequentially:\n\n```sh\nrtk proxy python3 desktop/gpui/fixtures/gen-ui/check.py core\nrtk proxy python3 desktop/gpui/fixtures/gen-ui/check.py desktop\n```\n\nThese checks do not launch or replace the user's preview. No Source web/Convex\nfile, provider registration or account data is changed by this wave.\n\nThe `*-proposal` directories preserve actual Sakana fugu-max outputs and inputs.\nParent review corrected Rust syntax/types, stream tests, JS whitespace,\nwrapper normalization, Source safe integers, sentence regex and JSON\nconstruction. The action review remains advisory; check its statements against\nSource when mounting the editor.\n\nRust/serde_json cannot represent JavaScript lone UTF-16 surrogates. That is an\nopen parity gap for escaped model strings, changed cumulative offsets inside a\npair, and support labels sliced through a pair at 60 units. Unsupported label\nedits currently preserve the writer's input.\n\nThe next integration must translate Source `textContent`/`posAtOffset` through\nthe native rich document model, preserve marks and undo, and qualify callbacks\nby folio, visit and tool identity. ProseMirror offsets cannot be copied into\nnative scalar coordinates. Connected account, knowledge-base and AI transport\nwork remains part of the full port objective.\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":17765},"formatted_output":"# In-flow writing tools\n\nThe full hosted Twyne desktop remains the reference. This wave covers four\nnative tool bodies and their spec, stream and deterministic seed contracts.\n\n`src/gen_ui/view.rs` implements Sentence Lab, Rhythm Strip, Claim Check and\nReader Questions with the existing original fonts, palette and Source spacing.\nRetained inputs survive streamed props. Rhythm bars emit hover, focus and\nselection requests. Jot and research require qualified host acknowledgments;\na retired tool ignores late results.\n\nThe view is exported but **not mounted in WritingRoom**. The margin rail,\npopover/card positioning, saved-tool shelf and naming/footer, editor commands,\nstruggle tracking, provider requests and actual Apparatus/notebook callbacks\nremain to be integrated. Source/native render and interaction comparisons have\nnot been performed. Checkbox appearance, inline hint layout, stepper geometry,\ntooltips and hover/focus paint still require that work.\n\nSource opens deterministic writer material without applying model-output\nlength limits. `ToolSnapshot::seeded` and `fill_offline` preserve that behavior;\n`ToolSnapshot::new` validates externally supplied specs. Every streamed\ncandidate is validated, retaining its preceding snapshot on failure. A model\ncannot rewrite the writer's sentence or earlier attempts.\n\nThe oracles execute unchanged Source TypeScript with `@json-render/core` 0.21.0\nand Zod 4.4.3. They retain 45 validation results, 32 snapshots from 18 cumulative\nstream cases, 59 deterministic seeds and offline fill results, and 11\nsentence/word cases. The focused native tests also cover retained edits, local\nsupport choices, exact live acknowledgments, retired requests and long writer\nmaterial. Receipts and full logs live under `target/verification`; the current\npointers start with `genui-`. Failed earlier receipts are retained.\n\nRun the Root-owned checks sequentially:\n\n```sh\nrtk proxy python3 desktop/gpui/fixtures/gen-ui/check.py core\nrtk proxy python3 desktop/gpui/fixtures/gen-ui/check.py desktop\n```\n\nThese checks do not launch or replace the user's preview. No Source web/Convex\nfile, provider registration or account data is changed by this wave.\n\nThe `*-proposal` directories preserve actual Sakana fugu-max outputs and inputs.\nParent review corrected Rust syntax/types, stream tests, JS whitespace,\nwrapper normalization, Source safe integers, sentence regex and JSON\nconstruction. The action review remains advisory; check its statements against\nSource when mounting the editor.\n\nRust/serde_json cannot represent JavaScript lone UTF-16 surrogates. That is an\nopen parity gap for escaped model strings, changed cumulative offsets inside a\npair, and support labels sliced through a pair at 60 units. Unsupported label\nedits currently preserve the writer's input.\n\nThe next integration must translate Source `textContent`/`posAtOffset` through\nthe native rich document model, preserve marks and undo, and qualify callbacks\nby folio, visit and tool identity. ProseMirror offsets cannot be copied into\nnative scalar coordinates. Connected account, knowledge-base and AI transport\nwork remains part of the full port objective.\n"},"started_at_ms":1791203089368,"completed_at_ms":1791203089368}}
