n, serde, regex already available. Reuse super::seed::{ToolKind,split_sentences}. Implement public ClassifyInput with passage:String, versions:Vec<String>, hints:Vec<ClassificationHint> (kind:String,strength:f64,reason:String), goal:String,audience:String. ClassificationHint serializable so can later construct from native struggle output. Define serde-serializable Classification with kind:Option<String>, tentative:bool, optional claimIndex:Option<usize> and filled:Option<BTreeMap<String,bool>>, omit absent optional fields. Public make_request(input:&ClassifyInput,slots:&[String])->Result<Value,ClassificationError>, read_response(input:&ClassifyInput,response:&Value,slots:&[String])->Result<Classification,ClassificationError>, fallback_classification(hints:&[ClassificationHint])->Classification. Preserve EXACT original classify(input,ask,slots) as given: question instructions/options verbatim, first12 sentences indexed1, UTF16slices160/3000/1500/500, last3versions, signals reason strings, first5slots/slot.toLowerCase, sends claim questions only when hints include claim-check and at least1sentence. Response Source tool choice only exact matching OPTION_FOR recognized, all otherstrings returnkindnull, confidence/probabilities thresholds strict below0.5/0.6. Source choice answers only discriminated by type property; valid protocol payloads required numeric confidence/probability object. Do not add range/normalization rules that reject valid Source protocol values. Claim Number.parseInt decimal prefix ignores trailing words, +/- andleading JS whitespace; include index only0<=index<first12sentencecount. Slot outputs include onlytype=noul, boolean true iff noul>=0.6; repeated slot names lastvalid wins. Alwaysprocessclaim/slotanswers regardless chosenkind or wantsClaim when actuallysupplied. ErrorResponsefalse orwrongtooltype matches unavailable. Support absence answers. If JS UTF16slice would create an unpaired surrogate, return explicit UnpairedUtf16 error and note open parity limit, never silentlytruncate another unit. Use ECMAScript whitespace for parseInt trim. ValidUnicode toLowerCase should matchJS contextual lowercasing; if Rust differs explain innotes. Include several meaningful protocol tests. No provider calls, API keys, GPUI, Cargo edits or automatic tracker integration. Parent independently executes unchanged Source classify with a fakeAsk to verify exact request and outcome.\\n\\nFrozen input bundle follows:\\n'''+json.dumps(bundle,ensure_ascii=False)\\nprompt_path=base/'sakana-classification-prompt.txt';prompt_path.write_text(prompt)\\ngraph_path=base/'genui-integration-graph.json';graph=json.loads(graph_path.read_text());graph['nodes'].append({'id':'classification','role':'sakana-fugu-max','owns':['proposal only: src/gen_ui/classification.rs'],'output':'Original Jev classification request and response semantics','depends':[],'gate':'Parent review and unchanged Source fakeAsk oracle; does not prove live TypeSafe/provider transport'})\\ngraph_path.write_text(json.dumps(graph,indent=2)+'\\\\n')\\nprint(json.dumps({'bundle':str(bundle_path),'prompt':str(prompt_path),'inputs':list(bundle)}))\\nPY\",\"max_output_tokens\":900}));\ntext(await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"rtk proxy python3 desktop/gpui/target/verification/run-sakana-advisory.py sakana-genui-classification desktop/gpui/target/verification/sakana-classification-input.json desktop/gpui/target/verification/sakana-classification-prompt.txt\",\"yield_time_ms\":1000,\"max_output_tokens\":550}));\ntext(await tools.write_stdin({session_id:66844,chars:\"\",\"yield_time_ms\":1000,\"max_output_tokens\":4400}));\ntext(await tools.write_stdin({session_id:7301,chars:\"\",\"yield_time_ms\":1000,\"max_output_tokens\":800}));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a10c03-2660-75c2-b09f-9987333f7d6c","create_time":1791203465.577102}}}
