{"timestamp":"2026-10-05T13:20:11.588Z","ordinal":40788,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a10537-909f-77a3-96d8-dd07161f91ae","turn_id":"01a10c03-2660-75c2-b09f-9987333f7d6c","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-0846191d-0d33-46e5-81c4-b61c7f3d4aac","process_id":"87930","command":["/bin/bash","-lc","rtk proxy rg -n -C 2 'GPUI|gpui-kit|GPUI Kit' /home/diogenes/.codex/memories/MEMORY.md"],"cwd":"file:///home/diogenes/Projects/twyne","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"rtk proxy rg -n -C 2 'GPUI|gpui-kit|GPUI Kit' /home/diogenes/.codex/memories/MEMORY.md"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"1:# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/baste Makepad versus GPUI studio-framework selection\n2-scope: Choose a Rust GUI foundation for Baste’s native studio based on whether productivity workflows or expressive cross-platform graphics are primary.\n3:applies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/baste; reuse_rule=confirm the current GPUI/GPUI Kit release and target platforms before implementation because GPUI is pre-1.0.\n4-\n5:## Task 1: Compare Makepad and GPUI for a Baste studio\n6-\n7-### rollout_summary_files\n--\n11-### keywords\n12-\n13:- Makepad, GPUI, GPUI Kit, Rust GUI, Zed, Studio, WASM, native desktop, candidate grids, inspectors, generation queues\n14-\n15-## User preferences\n--\n19-## Reusable knowledge\n20-\n21:- GPUI is the Baste default for a dense native productivity studio: entities/shared state, declarative views, imperative custom elements, keyboard actions, async services, and testing support fit projects, candidate grids, inspectors, and generation queues. [Task 1]\n22-- Prefer Makepad when animated visual design, custom GPU graphics, or one UI shared across native/web/mobile is central; it is Rust-first with a live-editable/scriptable UI DSL, Studio workflow, GPU 2D/3D rendering, and broad targets. [Task 1]\n23:- GPUI Kit is separate from core GPUI; verify its exact matching version and accessibility/component capabilities instead of attributing them to GPUI itself. [Task 1]\n24-\n25-## Failures and how to do differently\n26-\n27:- GPUI is pre-1.0 with frequent breaking changes -> inspect the exact release/fork and Zed source before committing Baste architecture to an API or platform assumption. [Task 1]\n28-\n29-# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/notorganic-provider shared account knowledge connections for Keating and Twyne\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"1:# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/baste Makepad versus GPUI studio-framework selection\n2-scope: Choose a Rust GUI foundation for Baste’s native studio based on whether productivity workflows or expressive cross-platform graphics are primary.\n3:applies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/baste; reuse_rule=confirm the current GPUI/GPUI Kit release and target platforms before implementation because GPUI is pre-1.0.\n4-\n5:## Task 1: Compare Makepad and GPUI for a Baste studio\n6-\n7-### rollout_summary_files\n--\n11-### keywords\n12-\n13:- Makepad, GPUI, GPUI Kit, Rust GUI, Zed, Studio, WASM, native desktop, candidate grids, inspectors, generation queues\n14-\n15-## User preferences\n--\n19-## Reusable knowledge\n20-\n21:- GPUI is the Baste default for a dense native productivity studio: entities/shared state, declarative views, imperative custom elements, keyboard actions, async services, and testing support fit projects, candidate grids, inspectors, and generation queues. [Task 1]\n22-- Prefer Makepad when animated visual design, custom GPU graphics, or one UI shared across native/web/mobile is central; it is Rust-first with a live-editable/scriptable UI DSL, Studio workflow, GPU 2D/3D rendering, and broad targets. [Task 1]\n23:- GPUI Kit is separate from core GPUI; verify its exact matching version and accessibility/component capabilities instead of attributing them to GPUI itself. [Task 1]\n24-\n25-## Failures and how to do differently\n26-\n27:- GPUI is pre-1.0 with frequent breaking c