ls/house-sync.test.ts\\n?? src/utils/house-sync.ts\\n?? src/utils/illuminated-initials.ts\\n?? src/utils/margin-surface.test.ts\\n?? src/utils/margin-surface.ts\\n?? src/utils/model-context.ts\\n?? src/utils/page-ornaments.ts\\n?? src/utils/print-ornaments.ts\\n?? src/utils/typst/assets.ts\\n?? src/utils/typst/client.ts\\n?? src/utils/typst/decorative-assets.ts\\n?? src/utils/typst/document.test.ts\\n?? src/utils/typst/document.ts\\n?? src/utils/typst/render-assets.test.ts\\n?? src/utils/typst/render-assets.ts\\n?? src/utils/typst/session.test.ts\\n?? src/utils/typst/session.ts\\n?? src/utils/typst/source-drafts.ts\\n?? src/utils/typst/string.ts\\n?? src/utils/typst/syntax.ts\\n?? src/utils/typst/theme.ts\\n?? tests/playwright-config.test.ts\\n\"}}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"i\":1,\"status\":\"fulfilled\",\"value\":{\"chunk_id\":\"1b1655\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000013998,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":1360,\"output\":\"---\\nname: plan-execution-graph\\ndescription: \\\"Convert an approved implementation plan or substantial coding request into a dependency-aware build execution graph for subagents and the coordinator. Use when executing multi-file or cross-subsystem plans, when the user asks for a build graph, dependency graph, subagent plan, parallel implementation, or coordinated worker execution, and before spawning workers for work that benefits from parallelism.\\\"\\n---\\n\\n# Plan Execution Graph\\n\\nTurn a decision-complete plan into an executable directed acyclic graph (DAG), then coordinate bounded subagents without duplicated work or file conflicts.\\n\\n## Workflow\\n\\n### 1. Ground the graph\\n\\nBefore delegating:\\n\\n- Read repository instructions and relevant skills.\\n- Inspect `git status` and treat pre-existing edits as protected.\\n- Identify required generated files, migrations, quality gates, and runtime verification.\\n- Separate discoverable repository facts from user decisions fixed by the plan.\\n- Do not delegate the immediate blocking step when the coordinator can execute it faster locally.\\n\\n### 2. Decompose by deliverable\\n\\nCreate nodes that produce concrete artifacts, not vague research activity. Prefer:\\n\\n- A short preflight or audit node.\\n- Foundation nodes for shared types, contracts, schemas, or primitives.\\n- Parallel implementation nodes with disjoint write sets.\\n- A coordinator-only integration node for protected or highly coupled files.\\n- Test and runtime-verification nodes after integration.\\n\\nEach node must specify:\\n\\n- Stable ID and concise name.\\n- Agent role: explorer, worker, verifier, or coordinator.\\n- Exact responsibility and output.\\n- Owned files or subsystem.\\n- Dependencies.\\n- Acceptance gate.\\n- Explicit exclusions when nearby work belongs to another node.\\n\\n### 3. Build dependency edges\\n\\nAdd an edge only when a downstream task consumes an upstream artifact or decision.\\n\\nUse these dependency rules:\\n\\n- Shared contracts precede all consumers.\\n- Backend and client adapters precede feature integration when their interfaces change.\\n- UI primitives precede surfaces that render them.\\n- Generated API or codegen follows source changes but precedes typecheck.\\n- Tests depend on the interfaces or behavior they validate.\\n- Integration precedes broad verification.\\n- Runtime verification follows a successful production build.\\n\\nAvoid false serialization. Independent file sets should run in the same wave.\\n\\n### 4. Assign safe ownership\\n\\nFor every coding worker:\\n\\n- Give an exclusive, disjoint write set.\\n- State that the worker is not alone in the codebase.\\n- Instruct it not to revert others' edits.\\n- Route dirty, protected, generated, or tightly coupled files to the coordinator unless a worker has explicit sole ownership.\\n- Keep shared barrel files and central configuration coordinator-owned when parallel edits would conflict.\\n\\nIf two tasks need the same file, either merge them into one node or make the later task depend on the earlier one. Never let workers race on the same file.\\n\\n### 5. Plan execution waves\\n\\nGroup ready nodes into waves based on dependencies and concurrency limits.\\n\\nDefault shape:\\n\\n1. Preflight and audit.\\n2. Shared foundations in parallel.\\n3. Feature slices in parallel.\\n4. Coordinator integration and codegen.\\n5. Tests and static checks.\\n6. Production build and real runtime verification.\\n\\nLimit concurrent workers to available agent capacity. Reserve one slot for urgent exploration or verification when useful.\\n\\n### 6. Execute the DAG\\n\\nWhen the user requested implementation, do not stop at the graph:\\n\\n- Start all ready, non-blocking sidecar nodes.\\n- Continue local critical-path work while workers run.\\n- Wait only when the next step truly depends on a worker result.\\n- Review each returned patch against its ownership and acceptance gate.\\n- Close finished agents promptly.\\n- Update the graph when a discovered dependency changes the critical path.\\n- Run repository-required checks after each logical integration unit.\\n\\n### 7. Verify completion\\n\\nThe final gate must include:\\n\\n- No ownership violations or lost pre-existing edits.\\n- Focused tests for each feature slice.\\n- Typecheck, lint, and production build as applicable.\\n- Generated artifacts refreshed when required.\\n- Real rendered or runtime validation for UI, auth, provider, deployment, or integration behavior.\\n- A search for incomplete migrations, stale call sites, raw errors, TODOs, or silent fallbacks relevant to the plan.\\n\\n## Output Format\\n\\nWhen presenting the graph, include:\\n\\n1. A Mermaid DAG.\\n2. A waves table with concurrency and gates.\\n3. Agent contracts with ownership, dependencies, and acceptance criteria.\\n4. Coordinator integration responsibilities.\\n5. Ordered verification commands and runtime scenarios.\\n\\nUse the compact template in [references/template.md](references/template.md). Omit sections that add no implementation value.\\n\\n## Delegation Rules\\n\\n- Delegate bounded sidecar work that can proceed without blocking the coordinator's next action.\\n- Keep urgent, tightly coupled, or immediate blockers local.\\n- Prefer workers that make concrete patches over explorers that only restate the codebase.\\n- Use explorers for independent codebase questions whose answers materially affect decomposition.\\n- Never duplicate a delegated task locally.\\n- If a worker flails, stop it and reassign a narrower task or complete it locally.\\n- Do not claim execution is complete until integration and verification nodes pass.\\n\"}}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"i\":2,\"status\":\"fulfilled\",\"value\":{\"chunk_id\":\"c73d84\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.00002504,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":2695,\"output\":\"//! The four original tool bodies. The host owns passage geometry, document\\n//! commands, provider requests, and the surrounding rail/popover/card shell.\\nuse super::model::{ToolModel, ToolSnapshot, rhythm_summary};\\nuse crate::{\\n    chrome,\\n    theme::{self, Palette, SERIF_FONT, TYPEWRITER_FONT},\\n};\\nuse gpui_kit::base::{\\n    Button,\\n    input::{InputBase, InputEvent, InputState, Textarea, TextareaState},\\n};\\nuse gpui_kit::component::{Disableable, checkbox::Checkbox, input::Input};\\nuse gpui_kit::prelude::*;\\nuse gpui_kit::{\\n    AnyElement, Context, Entity, EventEmitter, FocusHandle, IntoElement, Render, Role,\\n    SharedString, Subscription, TestSupportExt, Window, div, px, relative, rgb,\\n};\\nuse serde_json::Value;\\nuse std::{collections::BTreeMap, sync::Arc};\\nuse uuid::Uuid;\\n\\n#[derive(Clone, PartialEq, Eq)]\\npub struct ToolScope {\\n    pub folio: Arc<str>,\\n    pub visit: Uuid,\\n}\\n#[derive(Clone)]\\npub enum ToolAction {\\n    ApplyVariant(String),\\n    HighlightSentence(Option<usize>),\\n    SelectSentence(usize),\\n    SetRhythmBand { min: f64, max: f64 },\\n    Reask(String),\\n    Research { request: Uuid, claim: String },\\n    Jot { request: Uuid, question: String },\\n}\\n#[derive(Clone)]\\npub struct ToolEvent {\\n    pub scope: ToolScope,\\n    pub tool: Uuid,\\n    pub action: ToolAction,\\n}\\n\\npub struct ToolView {\\n    scope: ToolScope,\\n    model: ToolModel,\\n    working: Entity<TextareaState>,\\n    adding: Entity<InputState>,\\n    angle: Entity<InputState>,\\n    minimum: Entity<InputState>,\\n    maximum: Entity<InputState>,\\n    subscriptions: Vec<Subscription>,\\n    bars: BTreeMap<String, BarFocus>,\\n}\\nstruct BarFocus {\\n    handle: FocusHandle,\\n    _subscriptions: [Subscription; 2],\\n}\\nimpl EventEmitter<ToolEvent> for ToolView {}\\n\\nimpl ToolView {\\n    pub fn new(\\n        scope: ToolScope,\\n        snapshot: ToolSnapshot,\\n        window: &mut Window,\\n        cx: &mut Context<Self>,\\n    ) -> Self {\\n        let model = ToolModel::new(snapshot);\\n        let working = cx.new(|cx| {\\n            TextareaState::new(window, cx)\\n                .rows(3)\\n                .submit_on_enter(false)\\n                .default_value(model.working.clone())\\n        });\\n        let adding =\\n            cx.new(|cx| InputState::new(window, cx).placeholder(\\\"Another kind of support…\\\"));\\n        let angle = cx.new(|cx| {\\n            InputState::new(window, cx)\\n                .placeholder(\\\"the piece's intended reader\\\")\\n                .default_value(model.angle.clone())\\n        });\\n        let minimum = cx.new(|cx| {\\n            InputState::new(window, cx)\\n                .default_value(number_text(&model.snapshot.props()[\\\"targetMin\\\"]))\\n        });\\n        let maximum = cx.new(|cx| {\\n            InputState::new(window, cx)\\n                .default_value(number_text(&model.snapshot.props()[\\\"targetMax\\\"]))\\n        });\\n        let mut view = Self {\\n            scope,\\n            model,\\n            working,\\n            adding,\\n            angle,\\n            minimum,\\n            maximum,\\n            subscriptions: Vec::new(),\\n            bars: BTreeMap::new(),\\n        };\\n        view.subscriptions.push(cx.subscribe(\\n            &view.working,\\n            |view, input, event: &InputEvent, cx| {\\n                if matches!(event, InputEvent::Change) && view.model.writable() {\\n                    view.model.working = input.read(cx).value().to_string();\\n                    cx.notify();\\n                }\\n            },\\n        ));\\n        view.subscriptions.push(cx.subscribe_in(\\n            &view.adding,\\n            window,\\n            |view, input, event: &InputEvent, window, cx| {\\n                if matches!(event, InputEvent::PressEnter { .. })\\n                    && view.model.add_support(input.read(cx).value().as_ref())\\n                {\\n                    input.update(cx, |input, cx| input.set_value(\\\"\\\", window, cx));\\n                    cx.notify();\\n                }\\n            },\\n        ));\\n        view.subscriptions.push(cx.subscribe(\\n            &view.angle,\\n            |view, input, event: &InputEvent, cx| {\\n                if !view.model.writable() {\\n                    return;\\n                }\\n                if matches!(event, InputEvent::Change) {\\n                    view.model.angle = input.read(cx).value().to_string();\\n                    cx.notify();\\n                }\\n                if matches!(event, InputEvent::PressEnter { .. }) {\\n                    view.emit(ToolAction::Reask(input.read(cx).value().to_string()), cx);\\n                }\\n            },\\n        ));\\n        for (input, is_min) in [(view.minimum.clone(), true), (view.maximum.clone(), false)] {\\n            view.subscriptions.push(cx.subscribe(\\n                &input,\\n                move |view, input, event: &InputEvent, cx| {\\n                    if !matches!(event, InputEvent::Change | InputEvent::Blur)\\n                        || view.model.snapshot.component() != \\\"RhythmStrip\\\"\\n                    {\\n                        return;\\n                    }\\n                    let Ok(mut value) = input.read(cx).value().parse::<f64>() else {\\n                        return;\\n                    };\\n                    if !value.is_finite() {\\n                        return;\\n                    }\\n                    let props = view.model.snapshot.props();\\n                    let min = props[\\\"targetMin\\\"].as_f64().unwrap();\\n                    let max = props[\\\"targetMax\\\"].as_f64().unwrap();\\n                    if matches!(event, InputEvent::Blur) {\\n                        value = if is_min {\\n                            value.max(1.0).min(max - 1.0).round()\\n                        } else {\\n                            value.max(min + 1.0).min(120.0).round()\\n                        };\\n                    }\\n                    if value != if is_min { min } else { max } {\\n                        view.emit(\\n                            ToolAction::SetRhythmBand {\\n                                min: if is_min { value } else { min },\\n                                max: if is_min { max } else { value },\\n                            },\\n                            cx,\\n                        );\\n                    }\\n                },\\n            ));\\n        }\\n        view.sync_bar_focus(window, cx);\\n        view\\n    }\\n    pub fn scope(&self) -> &ToolScope {\\n        &self.scope\\n    }\\n    pub fn snapshot(&self) -> &ToolSnapshot {\\n        &self.model.snapshot\\n    }\\n    pub fn update(\\n        &mut self,\\n        snapshot: ToolSnapshot,\\n        window: &mut Window,\\n        cx: &mut Context<Self>,\\n    ) -> bool {\\n        if !self.model.update(snapshot) {\\n            return false;\\n        }\\n        if self.model.snapshot.component() == \\\"RhythmStrip\\\" {\\n            for (input, key) in [(&self.minimum, \\\"targetMin\\\"), (&self.maximum, \\\"targetMax\\\")] {\\n                let value = number_text(&self.model.snapshot.props()[key]);\\n                if input.read(cx).value().as_ref() != value {\\n                    input.update(cx, |input, cx| input.set_value(value, window, cx));\\n                }\\n            }\\n        }\\n        self.sync_bar_focus(window, cx);\\n        cx.notify();\\n        true\\n    }\\n    fn sync_bar_focus(&mut self, window: &mut Window, cx: &mut Context<Self>) {\\n        if self.model.snapshot.component() != \\\"RhythmStrip\\\" {\\n            self.bars.clear();\\n            return;\\n        }\\n        let keys: Vec<String> = self.model.snapshot.props()[\\\"sentences\\\"]\\n            .as_array()\\n            .unwrap()\\n            .iter()\\n            .enumerate()\\n            .map(|(i, s)| format!(\\\"{i}-{}\\\", number_text(&s[\\\"words\\\"])))\\n            .collect();\\n        self.bars.retain(|key, _| keys.contains(key));\\n        for (index, key) in keys.into_iter().enumerate() {\\n            if self.bars.contains_key(&key) {\\n                continue;\\n            }\\n            let handle = cx.focus_handle();\\n            let focus = cx.on_focus_in(&handle, window, move |view, _, cx| {\\n                view.emit(ToolAction::HighlightSentence(Some(index)), cx)\\n            });\\n            let blur = cx.on_focus_out(&handle, window, |view, _, _, cx| {\\n                view.emit(ToolAction::HighlightSentence(None), cx)\\n            });\\n            self.bars.insert(\\n                key,\\n                BarFocus {\\n                    handle,\\n                    _subscriptions: [focus, blur],\\n                },\\n            );\\n        }\\n    }\\n    pub fn retire(&mut self, cx: &mut Context<Self>) {\\n        self.emit(ToolAction::HighlightSentence(None), cx);\\n        self.model.retire();\\n        self.bars.clear();\\n        cx.notify();\\n    }\\n    pub fn finish_research(\\n        &mut self,\\n        request: Uuid,\\n        result: Result<(), String>,\\n        cx: &mut Context<Self>,\\n    ) -> bool {\\n        let accepted = self.model.finish_research(request, result);\\n        if accepted {\\n            cx.notify();\\n        }\\n        accepted\\n    }\\n    pub fn finish_jot(&mut self, request: Uuid, saved: bool, cx: &mut Context<Self>) -> bool {\\n        let accepted = self.model.finish_jot(request, saved);\\n        if accepted {\\n            cx.notify();\\n        }\\n        accepted\\n    }\\n    fn emit(&self, action: ToolAction, cx: &mut Context<Self>) {\\n        if self.model.writable() {\\n            cx.emit(ToolEvent {\\n                scope: self.scope.clone(),\\n                tool: self.model.snapshot.id,\\n                action,\\n            });\\n        }\\n    }\\n    fn sentence_lab(&self, colors: Palette, cx: &mut Context<Self>) -> AnyElement {\\n        self.working.update(cx, |state, cx| {\\n            state.set_editor_paddings(gpui_kit::Edges::default());\\n            state.set_readonly(!self.model.writable(), cx);\\n        });\\n        let props = self.model.snapshot.props();\\n        let mut body = body();\\n        for (field, label) in [\\n            (\\\"attempts\\\", \\\"Your earlier tries\\\"),\\n            (\\\"variants\\\", \\\"Other ways\\\"),\\n        ] {\\n            let choices = props[field].as_array().unwrap();\\n            if field == \\\"attempts\\\" && choices.is_empty() {\\n                continue;\\n            }\\n            let mut section = div()\\n                .flex()\\n                .flex_col()\\n                .gap(px(4.8))\\n                .child(label_element(label, colors));\\n            let mut rows = div().flex().flex_col().gap(px(4.8));\\n            for (index, choice) in choices.iter().enumerate() {\\n                let text = choice.as_str().unwrap().to_owned();\\n                let selected = self.model.working == text;\\n                let label = text.clone();\\n                rows = rows.child(\\n                    Button::new(SharedString::from(format!(\\\"in-flow-{field}-{index}\\\")))\\n                        .accessibility_label(SharedString::from(format!(\\n                            \\\"Load this {} into the working copy\\\",\\n                            if field == \\\"attempts\\\" {\\n\"}}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"i\":3,\"status\":\"fulfilled\",\"value\":{\"chunk_id\":\"758c2a\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000015494,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":651,\"output\":\"desktop/gpui/src/app/gen_ui_coordinator.rs:2://! Provider generation and automatic struggle classification remain separate\\ndesktop/gpui/src/app/gen_ui_coordinator.rs:31:    saved_generation: u64,\\ndesktop/gpui/src/app/gen_ui_coordinator.rs:286:        let (store, saved, generation) = match ToolStore::open(library.root()).and_then(|store| {\\ndesktop/gpui/src/app/gen_ui_coordinator.rs:290:            Ok((store, loaded)) => (Some(store), loaded.saved_tools, loaded.generation),\\ndesktop/gpui/src/app/gen_ui_coordinator.rs:309:                saved_generation: generation,\\ndesktop/gpui/src/app/gen_ui_coordinator.rs:747:        if ack.generation >= self.gen_ui.saved_generation {\\ndesktop/gpui/src/app/gen_ui_coordinator.rs:749:            self.gen_ui.saved_generation = ack.generation;\\ndesktop/gpui/target/verification/genui-integration-graph.json:60:      \\\"id\\\": \\\"struggle\\\",\\ndesktop/gpui/target/verification/genui-integration-graph.json:63:        \\\"proposal only: src/gen_ui/struggle.rs\\\"\\ndesktop/gpui/target/verification/genui-integration-graph.json:65:      \\\"output\\\": \\\"Exact Source pure paragraph struggle detector\\\",\\ndesktop/gpui/target/verification/genui-integration-graph.json:67:      \\\"gate\\\": \\\"Parent code review and original Source execution oracle; not automatic classification proof\\\"\\ndesktop/gpui/target/verification/genui-integration-graph.json:70:      \\\"id\\\": \\\"classification\\\",\\ndesktop/gpui/target/verification/genui-integration-graph.json:73:        \\\"proposal only: src/gen_ui/classification.rs\\\"\\ndesktop/gpui/target/verification/genui-integration-graph.json:75:      \\\"output\\\": \\\"Original Jev classification request and response semantics\\\",\\ndesktop/gpui/fixtures/gen-ui/README.md:14:struggle tracking, provider requests and actual Apparatus/notebook callbacks\\ndesktop/gpui/src/gen_ui/struggle.rs:194:    text.trim_end_matches(|character| matches!(character, '.' | '!' | '?' | '…'))\\ndesktop/gpui/src/gen_ui/struggle.rs:254:pub fn read_struggle(activity: &BlockActivity, now: f64, context: ReadContext) -> StruggleReading {\\ndesktop/gpui/src/gen_ui/struggle.rs:377:        let reading = read_struggle(&activity, 4.0, ReadContext::default());\\ndesktop/gpui/src/gen_ui/struggle.rs:396:            read_struggle(&activity, 4.0, ReadContext::default())\\ndesktop/gpui/src/gen_ui/struggle.rs:420:            read_struggle(&activity, 4.0, ReadContext::default())\\ndesktop/gpui/src/gen_ui/struggle.rs:443:            read_struggle(&activity, 1_004.0, ReadContext::default()).score,\\ndesktop/gpui/src/gen_ui/struggle.rs:446:        assert!(read_struggle(&activity, 1_005.0, ReadContext::default()).score > 0.0);\\n\"}}"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a10c3a-4441-7890-a25b-a9acd621d3aa","create_time":1791206534.2179768}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
