{"timestamp":"2026-10-05T14:28:51.105Z","ordinal":41541,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a10537-909f-77a3-96d8-dd07161f91ae","turn_id":"01a10c6f-d724-7b02-bb99-7845fa255153","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-1e2450b7-aa2b-486b-9194-93927123ceb2","process_id":"90769","command":["/bin/bash","-lc","rtk proxy python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport json\np=Path('desktop/gpui/target/verification/sakana-genui-step-map-review-c1ae5769a73e')\nr=json.loads((p/'response.txt').read_text())\nprint(json.dumps({k:v for k,v in r.items() if k!='code'},indent=2))\nprint(r['code'])\nPY"],"cwd":"file:///home/diogenes/Projects/twyne","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"rtk proxy python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport json\np=Path('desktop/gpui/target/verification/sakana-genui-step-map-review-c1ae5769a73e')\nr=json.loads((p/'response.txt').read_text())\nprint(json.dumps({k:v for k,v in r.items() if k!='code'},indent=2))\nprint(r['code'])\nPY"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"{\n  \"corrections\": [\n    \"map_result: replaced the flat-array stride (i += 3 with bound i < ranges.len(), which visited only every third range and stopped early) with a per-range ordinal r that increments by 1 up to ranges.len(); range access now uses ranges[r][old_index] and ranges[r][new_index] instead of ranges[i + old_index]/ranges[i + new_index].\",\n    \"map_result recovery index: make_recover(i / 3, pos - start) corrected to make_recover(r, pos - start); the range ordinal is the loop index itself, not i/3.\",\n    \"touches: same stride fix (r += 1, bound r < ranges.len()); the membership test i == index * 3 corrected to r == index.\",\n    \"changed_ranges: loop stride i += 3 corrected to r += 1, and the output capacity Vec::with_capacity(len / 3) corrected to Vec::with_capacity(len) because len is already the number of ranges, not the flat element count.\",\n    \"recover: verified already correct under triples (ranges[j][2] - ranges[j][1] and ranges[index][0]); no stride/index change needed there, only confirmation.\",\n    \"Added StepMap::offset(i64) to restore source API parity; negative n maps to [0, -n, 0], positive n to [0, 0, n], and n == 0 yields empty.\",\n    \"StepMap::new now returns empty() when handed no ranges, mirroring the source constructor's `!ranges.length` shortcut.\",\n    \"Retained u64 recovery tokens rather than switching to f64; make_recover/recover_index/recover_offset reproduce JS bit-for-bit on the exact domain, and a debug_assert documents the 16-bit index bound.\",\n    \"Preserved all Source boundary/assoc/deletion semantics: side selection order, recover = None at the assoc boundary, the DEL_AFTER/DEL_BEFORE/DEL_ACROSS/DEL_SIDE flags, Arc-shared invert, and the inverted old_index/new_index swaps.\"\n  ],\n  \"limitations\": [\n    \"u64 recovery tokens are exact only where JS makeRecover is exact: index in [0, 2^16) and index + offset*65536 <= 2^53 - 1 (JS safe-integer limit). This caps a map at 65535 ranges; beyond that the token domain is undefined and JS itself loses precision/collides.\",\n    \"recover() and touches() read ranges[index] / compare r == index; a token whose lower-16-bit index is >= ranges.len() will panic, whereas JS would return NaN/undefined. Tokens must originate from map_result.\",\n    \"map_result and changed_ranges cast i64 intermediates to usize and assume valid inputs keep results nonnegative; malformed ranges could wrap (i64 only guards inverted-start underflow before the break).\",\n    \"f64 tokens were rejected: they differ from u64 only for tokens >= 2^53, exactly where JS rounds, so f64 would reproduce JS precision loss instead of adding value and would complicate Eq/Ord token comparison. Chosen contract: u64 with an explicit documented exact domain that covers all realistic document lengths (offset <= document length, far below 2^37).\",\n    \"toString/JSON serialization not ported to avoid a dependency; StepMap derives Debug instead.\",\n    \"map/map_result take an explicit assoc (no default of 1) and only the sign of assoc is significant, matching JS usage with -1/1; callers must pass 1 for default behavior.\",\n    \"No Mapping pipeline included (out of scope), so multi-step pipeline recovery accumulation and map_through are not provided.\",\n    \"Ranges are stored as Arc<[[usize; 3]]> for cheap structural sharing on invert; the source's flat number[] layout is intentionally not reproduced.\"\n  ]\n}\nuse std::sync::Arc;\n\nconst LOWER16: u64 = 0xffff;\nconst FACTOR16: u64 = 1 << 16;\n\nconst DEL_BEFORE: u32 = 1;\nconst DEL_AFTER: u32 = 2;\nconst DEL_ACROSS: u32 = 4;\nconst DEL_SIDE: u32 = 8;\n\n/// Encode a range ordinal (lower 16 bits) plus an offset into one token.\n/// Exact only when `index < 2^16` and `index + offset * 65536 <= 2^53 - 1`\n/// (the JavaScript safe-integer limit where `makeRecover` is itself exact).\n#[inline]\nfn make_recover(index: usize, offset: usize) -> u64 {\n    debug_assert!((index as u64) < FACTOR16);\n    index as u64 + offset as u64 * FACTOR16\n}\n\n#[inline]\nfn recover_index(value: u64) -> usize {\n    (value & LOWER16) as usize\n}\n\n#[inline]\nfn recover_offset(value: u64) -> u64 {\n    (value - (value & LOWER16)) / FACTOR16\n}\n\n#[derive(Debug, Clone, PartialEq, Eq)]\npub struct MapResult {\n    pub pos: usize,\n    pub del_info: u32,\n    pub recover: Option<u64>,\n}\n\nimpl MapResult {\n    pub fn new(pos: usize, del_info: u32, recover: Option<u64>) -> Self {\n        MapResult { pos, del_info, recover }\n    }\n\n    pub fn deleted(&self) -> bool {\n        (self.del_info & DEL_SIDE) > 0\n    }\n\n    pub fn deleted_before(&self) -> bool {\n        (self.del_info & (DEL_BEFORE | DEL_ACROSS)) > 0\n    }\n\n    pub fn deleted_after(&self) -> bool {\n        (self.del_info & (DEL_AFTER | DEL_ACROSS)) > 0\n    }\n\n    pub fn deleted_across(&self) -> bool {\n        (self.del_info & DEL_ACROSS) > 0\n    }\n}\n\n#[derive(Debug, Clone)]\npub struct StepMap {\n    pub ranges: Arc<[[usize; 3]]>,\n    pub inverted: bool,\n}\n\nimpl StepMap {\n    pub fn new(ranges: Vec<[usize; 3]>) -> Self {\n        if ranges.is_empty() {\n            return StepMap::empty();\n        }\n        StepMap { ranges: Arc::from(ranges), inverted: false }\n    }\n\n    pub fn empty() -> Self {\n        StepMap { ranges: Arc::from(Vec::new()), inverted: false }\n    }\n\n    pub fn is_empty(&self) -> bool {\n        self.ranges.is_empty()\n    }\n\n    pub fn invert(&self) -> StepMap {\n        StepMap { ranges: Arc::clone(&self.ranges), inverted: !self.inverted }\n    }\n\n    pub fn offset(n: i64) -> StepMap {\n        if n == 0 {\n            StepMap::empty()\n        } else if n < 0 {\n            StepMap::new(vec![[0, (-n) as usize, 0]])\n        } else {\n            StepMap::new(vec![[0, 0, n as usize]])\n        }\n    }\n\n    pub fn recover(&self, token: u64) -> usize {\n        let index = recover_index(token);\n        let mut diff: i64 = 0;\n        if !self.inverted {\n            let mut j = 0;\n            while j < index {\n                diff += self.ranges[j][2] as i64 - self.ranges[j][1] as i64;\n                j += 1;\n            }\n        }\n        (self.ranges[index][0] as i64 + diff + recover_offset(token) as i64) as usize\n    }\n\n    pub fn map(&self, pos: usize, assoc: i32) -> usize {\n        self.map_result(pos, assoc).pos\n    }\n\n    pub fn map_result(&self, pos: usize, assoc: i32) -> MapResult {\n        let pos_i = pos as i64;\n        let assoc_i = assoc as i64;\n        let assoc_neg = assoc < 0;\n        let old_index: usize = if self.inverted { 2 } else { 1 };\n        let new_index: usize = if self.inverted { 1 } else { 2 };\n        let mut diff: i64 = 0;\n        let len = self.ranges.len();\n        let mut r: usize = 0;\n        while r < len {\n            let range = &self.ranges[r];\n            let start = range[0] as i64 - (if self.inverted { diff } else { 0 });\n            if start > pos_i {\n                break;\n            }\n            let old_size = range[old_index] as i64;\n            let new_size = range[new_index] as i64;\n            let end = start + old_size;\n            if pos_i <= end {\n                let side = if old_size == 0 {\n                    assoc_i\n                } else if pos_i == start {\n                    -1\n                } else if pos_i == end {\n                    1\n                } else {\n                    assoc_i\n                };\n                let result = start + diff + (if side < 0 { 0 } else { new_size });\n                let boundary = if assoc_neg { start } else { end };\n                let recover = if pos_i == boundary {\n                    None\n                } else {\n                    Some(make_recover(r, (pos_i - start) as usize))\n                };\n                let mut del = if pos_i == start {\n                    DEL_AFTER\n                } else if pos_i == end {\n                    DEL_BEFORE\n                } else {\n                    DEL_ACROSS\n                };\n                let off_side = if assoc_neg { pos_i != start } else { pos_i != end };\n                if off_side {\n                    del |= DEL_SIDE;\n                }\n                return MapResult { pos: result as usize, del_info: del, recover };\n            }\n            diff += new_size - old_size;\n            r += 1;\n        }\n        MapResult { pos: (pos_i + diff) as usize, del_info: 0, recover: None }\n    }\n\n    pub fn touches(&self, pos: usize, token: u64) -> bool {\n        let pos_i = pos as i64;\n        let index = recover_index(token);\n        let old_index: usize = if self.inverted { 2 } else { 1 };\n        let new_index: usize = if self.inverted { 1 } else { 2 };\n        let mut diff: i64 = 0;\n        let len = self.ranges.len();\n        let mut r: usize = 0;\n        while r < len {\n            let range = &self.ranges[r];\n            let start = range[0] as i64 - (if self.inverted { diff } else { 0 });\n            if start > pos_i {\n                break;\n            }\n            let old_size = range[old_index] as i64;\n            let end = start + old_size;\n            if pos_i <= end && r == index {\n                return true;\n            }\n            diff += range[new_index] as i64 - old_size;\n            r += 1;\n        }\n        false\n    }\n\n    pub fn changed_ranges(&self) -> Vec<[usize; 4]> {\n        let old_index: usize = if self.inverted { 2 } else { 1 };\n        let new_index: usize = if self.inverted { 1 } else { 2 };\n        let len = self.ranges.len();\n        let mut out: Vec<[usize; 4]> = Vec::with_capacity(len);\n        let mut diff: i64 = 0;\n        let mut r: usize = 0;\n        while r < len {\n            let range = &self.ranges[r];\n            let start = range[0] as i64;\n            let old_start = start - (if self.inverted { diff } else { 0 });\n            let new_start = start + (if self.inverted { 0 } else { diff });\n            let old_size = range[old_index] as i64;\n            let new_size = range[new_index] as i64;\n            out.push([\n                old_start as usize,\n                (old_start + old_size) as usize,\n                new_start as usize,\n                (new_start + new_size) as usize,\n            ]);\n            diff += new_size - old_size;\n            r += 1;\n        }\n        out\n    }\n}\n\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"{\n  \"corrections\": [\n    \"map_result: replaced the flat-array stride (i += 3 with bound i < ranges.len(), which visited only every third range and stopped early) with a per-range ordinal r that increments by 1 up to ranges.len(); range access now uses ranges[r][old_index] and ranges[r][new_index] instead of ranges[i + old_index]/ranges[i + new_index].\",\n    \"map_result recovery index: make_recover(i / 3, pos - start) corrected to make_recover(r, pos - start); the range ordinal is the loop index itself, not i/3.\",\n    \"touches: same stride fix (r += 1, bound r < ranges.len()); the membership test i == index * 3 corrected to r == index.\",\n    \"changed_ranges: loop stride i += 3 corrected to r += 1, and the output capacity Vec::with_capacity(len / 3) corrected to Vec::with_capacity(len) because len is already the number of ranges, not the flat element count.\",\n    \"recover: verified already correct under triples (ranges[j][2] - ranges[j][1] and ranges[index][0]); no stride/index change needed there, only confirmation.\",\n    \"Added StepMap::offset(i64) to restore source API parity; negative n maps to [0, -n, 0], positive n to [0, 0, n], and n == 0 yields empty.\",\n    \"StepMap::new now returns empty() when handed no ranges, mirroring the source constructor's `!ranges.length` shortcut.\",\n    \"Retained u64 recovery tokens rather than switching to f64; make_recover/recover_index/recover_offset reproduce JS bit-for-bit on the exact domain, and a debug_assert documents the 16-bit index bound.\",\n    \"Preserved all Source boundary/assoc/deletion semantics: side selection order, recover = None at the assoc boundary, the DEL_AFTER/DEL_BEFORE/DEL_ACROSS/DEL_SIDE flags, Arc-shared invert, and the inverted old_index/new_index swaps.\"\n  ],\n  \"limitations\": [\n    \"u64 recovery tokens are exact only where JS makeRecover is exact: index in [0, 2^16) and index + offset*65536 <= 2^53 - 1 (JS safe-integer limit). This caps a map at 65535 ranges; beyond that the token domain is undefined and JS itself loses precision/collides.\",\n    \"recover() and touches() read ranges[index] / compare r == index; a token whose lower-16-bit index is >= ranges.len() will panic, whereas JS would return NaN/undefined. Tokens must originate from map_result.\",\n    \"map_result and changed_ranges cast i64 intermediates to usize and assume valid inputs keep results nonnegative; malformed ranges could wrap (i64 only guards inverted-start underflow before the break).\",\n    \"f64 tokens were rejected: they differ from u64 only for tokens >= 2^53, exactly where JS rounds, so f64 would reproduce JS precision loss instead of adding value and would complicate Eq/Ord token comparison. Chosen contract: u64 with an explicit documented exact domain that covers all realistic document lengths (offset <= document length, far below 2^37).\",\n    \"toString/JSON serialization not ported to avoid a dependency; StepMap derives Debug instead.\",\n    \"map/map_result take an explicit assoc (no default of 1) and only the sign of assoc is significant, matching JS usage with -1/1; callers must pass 1 for default behavior.\",\n    \"No Mapping pipeline included (out of scope), so multi-step pipeline recovery accumulation and map_through are not provided.\",\n    \"Ranges are stored as Arc<[[usize; 3]]> for cheap structural sharing on invert; the source's flat number[] layout is intentionally not reproduced.\"\n  ]\n}\nuse std::sync::Arc;\n\nconst LOWER16: u64 = 0xffff;\nconst FACTOR16: u64 = 1 << 16;\n\nconst DEL_BEFORE: u32 = 1;\nconst DEL_AFTER: u32 = 2;\nconst DEL_ACROSS: u32 = 4;\nconst DEL_SIDE: u32 = 8;\n\n/// Encode a range ordinal (lower 16 bits) plus an offset into one token.\n/// Exact only when `index < 2^16` and `index + offset * 65536 <= 2^53 - 1`\n/// (the JavaScript safe-integer limit where `makeRecover` is itself exact).\n#[inline]\nfn make_recover(index: usize, offset: usize) -> u64 {\n    debug_assert!((index as u64) < FACTOR16);\n    index as u64 + offset as u64 * FACTOR16\n}\n\n#[inline]\nfn recover_index(value: u64) -> usize {\n    (value & LOWER16) as usize\n}\n\n#[inline]\nfn recover_offset(value: u64) -> u64 {\n    (value - (value & LOWER16)) / FACTOR16\n}\n\n#[derive(Debug, Clone, PartialEq, Eq)]\npub struct MapResult {\n    pub pos: usize,\n    pub del_info: u32,\n    pub recover: Option<u64>,\n}\n\nimpl MapResult {\n    pub fn new(pos: usize, del_info: u32, recover: Option<u64>) -> Self {\n        MapResult { pos, del_info, recover }\n    }\n\n    pub fn deleted(&self) -> bool {\n        (self.del_info & DEL_SIDE) > 0\n    }\n\n    pub fn deleted_before(&self) -> bool {\n        (self.del_info & (DEL_BEFORE | DEL_ACROSS)) > 0\n    }\n\n    pub fn deleted_after(&self) -> bool {\n        (self.del_info & (DEL_AFTER | DEL_ACROSS)) > 0\n    }\n\n    pub fn deleted_across(&self) -> bool {\n        (self.del_info & DEL_ACROSS) > 0\n    }\n}\n\n#[derive(Debug, Clone)]\npub struct StepMap {\n    pub ranges: Arc<[[usize; 3]]>,\n    pub inverted: bool,\n}\n\nimpl StepMap {\n    pub fn new(ranges: Vec<[usize; 3]>) -> Self {\n        if ranges.is_empty() {\n            return StepMap::empty();\n        }\n        StepMap { ranges: Arc::from(ranges), inverted: false }\n    }\n\n    pub fn empty() -> Self {\n        StepMap { ranges: Arc::from(Vec::new()), inverted: false }\n    }\n\n    pub fn is_empty(&self) -> bool {\n        self.ranges.is_empty()\n    }\n\n    pub fn invert(&self) -> StepMap {\n        StepMap { ranges: Arc::clone(&self.ranges), inverted: !self.inverted }\n    }\n\n    pub fn offset(n: i64) -> StepMap {\n        if n == 0 {\n            StepMap::empty()\n        } else if n < 0 {\n            StepMap::new(vec![[0, (-n) as usize, 0]])\n        } else {\n            StepMap::new(vec![[0, 0, n as usize]])\n        }\n    }\n\n    pub fn recover(&self, token: u64) -> usize {\n        let index = recover_index(token);\n        let mut diff: i64 = 0;\n        if !self.inverted {\n            let mut j = 0;\n            while j < index {\n                diff += self.ranges[j][2] as i64 - self.ranges[j][1] as i64;\n                j += 1;\n            }\n        }\n        (self.ranges[index][0] as i64 + diff + recover_offset(token) as i64) as usize\n    }\n\n    pub fn map(&self, pos: usize, assoc: i32) -> usize {\n        self.map_result(pos, assoc).pos\n    }\n\n    pub fn map_result(&self, pos: usize, assoc: i32) -> MapResult {\n        let pos_i = pos as i64;\n        let assoc_i = assoc as i64;\n        let assoc_neg = assoc < 0;\n        let old_index: usize = if self.inverted { 2 } else { 1 };\n        let new_index: usize = if self.inverted { 1 } else { 2 };\n        let mut diff: i64 = 0;\n        let len = self.ranges.len();\n        let mut r: usize = 0;\n        while r < len {\n            let range = &self.ranges[r];\n            let start = range[0] as i64 - (if self.inverted { diff } else { 0 });\n            if start > pos_i {\n                break;\n            }\n            let old_size = range[old_index] as i64;\n            let new_size = range[new_index] as i64;\n            let end = start + old_size;\n            if pos_i <= end {\n                let side = if old_size == 0 {\n                    assoc_i\n                } else if pos_i == start {\n                    -1\n                } else if pos_i == end {\n                    1\n                } else {\n                    assoc_i\n                };\n                let result = start + diff + (if side < 0 { 0 } else { new_size });\n                let boundary = if assoc_neg { start } else { end };\n                let recover = if pos_i == boundary {\n                    None\n                } else {\n                    Some(make_recover(r, (pos_i - start) as usize))\n                };\n                let mut del = if pos_i == start {\n                    DEL_AFTER\n                } else if pos_i == end {\n                    DEL_BEFORE\n                } else {\n                    DEL_ACROSS\n                };\n                let off_side = if assoc_neg { pos_i != start } else { pos_i != end };\n                if off_side {\n                    del |= DEL_SIDE;\n                }\n                return MapResult { pos: result as usize, del_info: del, recover };\n            }\n            diff += new_size - old_size;\n            r += 1;\n        }\n        MapResult { pos: (pos_i + diff) as usize, del_info: 0, recover: None }\n    }\n\n    pub fn touches(&self, pos: usize, token: u64) -> bool {\n        let pos_i = pos as i64;\n        let index = recover_index(token);\n        let old_index: usize = if self.inverted { 2 } else { 1 };\n        let new_index: usize = if self.inverted { 1 } else { 2 };\n        let mut diff: i64 = 0;\n        let len = self.ranges.len();\n        let mut r: usize = 0;\n        while r < len {\n            let range = &self.ranges[r];\n            let start = range[0] as i64 - (if self.inverted { diff } else { 0 });\n            if start > pos_i {\n                break;\n            }\n            let old_size = range[old_index] as i64;\n            let end = start + old_size;\n            if pos_i <= end && r == index {\n                return true;\n            }\n            diff += range[new_index] as i64 - old_size;\n            r += 1;\n        }\n        false\n    }\n\n    pub fn changed_ranges(&self) -> Vec<[usize; 4]> {\n        let old_index: usize = if self.inverted { 2 } else { 1 };\n        let new_index: usize = if self.inverted { 1 } else { 2 };\n        let len = self.ranges.len();\n        let mut out: Vec<[usize; 4]> = Vec::with_capacity(len);\n        let mut diff: i64 = 0;\n        let mut r: usize = 0;\n        while r < len {\n            let range = &self.ranges[r];\n            let start = range[0] as i64;\n            let old_start = start - (if self.inverted { diff } else { 0 });\n            let new_start = start + (if self.inverted { 0 } else { diff });\n            let old_size = range[old_index] as i64;\n            let new_size = range[new_index] as i64;\n            out.push([\n                old_start as usize,\n                (old_start + old_size) as usize,\n                new_start as usize,\n                (new_start + new_size) as usize,\n            ]);\n            diff += new_size - old_size;\n            r += 1;\n        }\n        out\n    }\n}\n\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":15961},"formatted_output":"{\n  \"corrections\": [\n    \"map_result: replaced the flat-array stride (i += 3 with bound i < ranges.len(), which visited only every third range and stopped early) with a per-range ordinal r that increments by 1 up to ranges.len(); range access now uses ranges[r][old_index] and ranges[r][new_index] instead of ranges[i + old_index]/ranges[i + new_index].\",\n    \"map_result recovery index: make_recover(i / 3, pos - start) corrected to make_recover(r, pos - start); the range ordinal is the loop index itself, not i/3.\",\n    \"touches: same stride fix (r += 1, bound r < ranges.len()); the membership test i == index * 3 corrected to r == index.\",\n    \"changed_ranges: loop stride i += 3 corrected to r += 1, and the output capacity Vec::with_capacity(len / 3) corrected to Vec::with_capacity(len) because len is already the number of ranges, not the flat element count.\",\n    \"recover: verified already correct under triples (ranges[j][2] - ranges[j][1] and ranges[index][0]); no stride/index change needed there, only confirmation.\",\n    \"Added StepMap::offset(i64) to restore source API parity; negative n maps to [0, -n, 0], positive n to [0, 0, n], and n == 0 yields empty.\",\n    \"StepMap::new now returns empty() when handed no ranges, mirroring the source constructor's `!ranges.length` shortcut.\",\n    \"Retained u64 recovery tokens rather than switching to f64; make_recover/recover_index/recover_offset reproduce JS bit-for-bit on the exact domain, and a debug_assert documents the 16-bit index bound.\",\n    \"Preserved all Source boundary/assoc/deletion semantics: side selection order, recover = None at the assoc boundary, the DEL_AFTER/DEL_BEFORE/DEL_ACROSS/DEL_SIDE flags, Arc-shared invert, and the inverted old_index/new_index swaps.\"\n  ],\n  \"limitations\": [\n    \"u64 recovery tokens are exact only where JS makeRecover is exact: index in [0, 2^16) and index + offset*65536 <= 2^53 - 1 (JS safe-integer limit). This caps a map at 65535 ranges; beyond that the token domain is undefined and JS itself loses precision/collides.\",\n    \"recover() and touches() read ranges[index] / compare r == index; a token whose lower-16-bit index is >= ranges.len() will panic, whereas JS would return NaN/undefined. Tokens must originate from map_result.\",\n    \"map_result and changed_ranges cast i64 intermediates to usize and assume valid inputs keep results nonnegative; malformed ranges could wrap (i64 only guards inverted-start underflow before the break).\",\n    \"f64 tokens were rejected: they differ from u64 only for tokens >= 2^53, exactly where JS rounds, so f64 would reproduce JS precision loss instead of adding value and would complicate Eq/Ord token comparison. Chosen contract: u64 with an explicit documented exact domain that covers all realistic document lengths (offset <= document length, far below 2^37).\",\n    \"toString/JSON serialization not ported to avoid a dependency; StepMap derives Debug instead.\",\n    \"map/map_result take an explicit assoc (no default of 1) and only the sign of assoc is significant, matching JS usage with -1/1; callers must pass 1 for default behavior.\",\n    \"No Mapping pipeline included (out of scope), so multi-step pipeline recovery accumulation and map_through are not provided.\",\n    \"Ranges are stored as Arc<[[usize; 3]]> for cheap structural sharing on invert; the source's flat number[] layout is intentionally not reproduced.\"\n  ]\n}\nuse std::sync::Arc;\n\nconst LOWER16: u64 = 0xffff;\nconst FACTOR16: u64 = 1 << 16;\n\nconst DEL_BEFORE: u32 = 1;\nconst DEL_AFTER: u32 = 2;\nconst DEL_ACROSS: u32 = 4;\nconst DEL_SIDE: u32 = 8;\n\n/// Encode a range ordinal (lower 16 bits) plus an offset into one token.\n/// Exact only when `index < 2^16` and `index + offset * 65536 <= 2^53 - 1`\n/// (the JavaScript safe-integer limit where `makeRecover` is itself exact).\n#[inline]\nfn make_recover(index: usize, offset: usize) -> u64 {\n    debug_assert!((index as u64) < FACTOR16);\n    index as u64 + offset as u64 * FACTOR16\n}\n\n#[inline]\nfn recover_index(value: u64) -> usize {\n    (value & LOWER16) as usize\n}\n\n#[inline]\nfn recover_offset(value: u64) -> u64 {\n    (value - (value & LOWER16)) / FACTOR16\n}\n\n#[derive(Debug, Clone, PartialEq, Eq)]\npub struct MapResult {\n    pub pos: usize,\n    pub del_info: u32,\n    pub recover: Option<u64>,\n}\n\nimpl MapResult {\n    pub fn new(pos: usize, del_info: u32, recover: Option<u64>) -> Self {\n        MapResult { pos, del_info, recover }\n    }\n\n    pub fn deleted(&self) -> bool {\n        (self.del_info & DEL_SIDE) > 0\n    }\n\n    pub fn deleted_before(&self) -> bool {\n        (self.del_info & (DEL_BEFORE | DEL_ACROSS)) > 0\n    }\n\n    pub fn deleted_after(&self) -> bool {\n        (self.del_info & (DEL_AFTER | DEL_ACROSS)) > 0\n    }\n\n    pub fn deleted_across(&self) -> bool {\n        (self.del_info & DEL_ACROSS) > 0\n    }\n}\n\n#[derive(Debug, Clone)]\npub struct StepMap {\n    pub ranges: Arc<[[usize; 3]]>,\n    pub inverted: bool,\n}\n\nimpl StepMap {\n    pub fn new(ranges: Vec<[usize; 3]>) -> Self {\n        if ranges.is_empty() {\n            return StepMap::empty();\n        }\n        StepMap { ranges: Arc::from(ranges), inverted: false }\n    }\n\n    pub fn empty() -> Self {\n        StepMap { ranges: Arc::from(Vec::new()), inverted: false }\n    }\n\n    pub fn is_empty(&self) -> bool {\n        self.ranges.is_empty()\n    }\n\n    pub fn invert(&self) -> StepMap {\n        StepMap { ranges: Arc::clone(&self.ranges), inverted: !self.inverted }\n    }\n\n    pub fn offset(n: i64) -> StepMap {\n        if n == 0 {\n            StepMap::empty()\n        } else if n < 0 {\n            StepMap::new(vec![[0, (-n) as usize, 0]])\n        } else {\n            StepMap::new(vec![[0, 0, n as usize]])\n        }\n    }\n\n    pub fn recover(&self, token: u64) -> usize {\n        let index = recover_index(token);\n        let mut diff: i64 = 0;\n        if !self.inverted {\n            let mut j = 0;\n            while j < index {\n                diff += self.ranges[j][2] as i64 - self.ranges[j][1] as i64;\n                j += 1;\n            }\n        }\n        (self.ranges[index][0] as i64 + diff + recover_offset(token) as i64) as usize\n    }\n\n    pub fn map(&self, pos: usize, assoc: i32) -> usize {\n        self.map_result(pos, assoc).pos\n    }\n\n    pub fn map_result(&self, pos: usize, assoc: i32) -> MapResult {\n        let pos_i = pos as i64;\n        let assoc_i = assoc as i64;\n        let assoc_neg = assoc < 0;\n        let old_index: usize = if self.inverted { 2 } else { 1 };\n        let new_index: usize = if self.inverted { 1 } else { 2 };\n        let mut diff: i64 = 0;\n        let len = self.ranges.len();\n        let mut r: usize = 0;\n        while r < len {\n            let range = &self.ranges[r];\n            let start = range[0] as i64 - (if self.inverted { diff } else { 0 });\n            if start > pos_i {\n                break;\n            }\n            let old_size = range[old_index] as i64;\n            let new_size = range[new_index] as i64;\n            let end = start + old_size;\n            if pos_i <= end {\n                let side = if old_size == 0 {\n                    assoc_i\n                } else if pos_i == start {\n                    -1\n                } else if pos_i == end {\n                    1\n                } else {\n                    assoc_i\n                };\n                let result = start + diff + (if side < 0 { 0 } else { new_size });\n                let boundary = if assoc_neg { start } else { end };\n                let recover = if pos_i == boundary {\n                    None\n                } else {\n                    Some(make_recover(r, (pos_i - start) as usize))\n                };\n                let mut del = if pos_i == start {\n                    DEL_AFTER\n                } else if pos_i == end {\n                    DEL_BEFORE\n                } else {\n                    DEL_ACROSS\n                };\n                let off_side = if assoc_neg { pos_i != start } else { pos_i != end };\n                if off_side {\n                    del |= DEL_SIDE;\n                }\n                return MapResult { pos: result as usize, del_info: del, recover };\n            }\n            diff += new_size - old_size;\n            r += 1;\n        }\n        MapResult { pos: (pos_i + diff) as usize, del_info: 0, recover: None }\n    }\n\n    pub fn touches(&self, pos: usize, token: u64) -> bool {\n        let pos_i = pos as i64;\n        let index = recover_index(token);\n        let old_index: usize = if self.inverted { 2 } else { 1 };\n        let new_index: usize = if self.inverted { 1 } else { 2 };\n        let mut diff: i64 = 0;\n        let len = self.ranges.len();\n        let mut r: usize = 0;\n        while r < len {\n            let range = &self.ranges[r];\n            let start = range[0] as i64 - (if self.inverted { diff } else { 0 });\n            if start > pos_i {\n                break;\n            }\n            let old_size = range[old_index] as i64;\n            let end = start + old_size;\n            if pos_i <= end && r == index {\n                return true;\n            }\n            diff += range[new_index] as i64 - old_size;\n            r += 1;\n        }\n        false\n    }\n\n    pub fn changed_ranges(&self) -> Vec<[usize; 4]> {\n        let old_index: usize = if self.inverted { 2 } else { 1 };\n        let new_index: usize = if self.inverted { 1 } else { 2 };\n        let len = self.ranges.len();\n        let mut out: Vec<[usize; 4]> = Vec::with_capacity(len);\n        let mut diff: i64 = 0;\n        let mut r: usize = 0;\n        while r < len {\n            let range = &self.ranges[r];\n            let start = range[0] as i64;\n            let old_start = start - (if self.inverted { diff } else { 0 });\n            let new_start = start + (if self.inverted { 0 } else { diff });\n            let old_size = range[old_index] as i64;\n            let new_size = range[new_index] as i64;\n            out.push([\n                old_start as usize,\n                (old_start + old_size) as usize,\n                new_start as usize,\n                (new_start + new_size) as usize,\n            ]);\n            diff += new_size - old_size;\n            r += 1;\n        }\n        out\n    }\n}\n\n"},"started_at_ms":1791210531105,"completed_at_ms":1791210531105}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-05T14:28:51.194Z","ordinal":41542,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a10c77-a97a-7901-b675-b0f0ffaef07b","call_id":"call_YoviYITj4CHLemgjJyBPtLDN","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.2 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"task\":0,\"status\":\"fulfilled\",\"value\":{\"chunk_id\":\"9c9f69\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000012846,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":2290,\"output\":\"//! The inline strong label and smaller hint from Source Claim Check.\\n//! Each face is shaped at its actual size; soft wraps share one baseline.\\nuse crate::theme::{Palette, SERIF_FONT};\\nuse gpui_kit::prelude::*;\\nuse gpui_kit::{\\n    AnyElement, App, AvailableSpace, Bounds, Element, ElementId, Font, FontWeight, GlobalElementId,\\n    InspectorElementId, IntoElement, LayoutId, Pixels, Point, ShapedLine, SharedString, Size,\\n    StrikethroughStyle, Style, TextAlign, TextRun, Window, div, font, point, px, rgb, size,\\n};\\nuse std::{cell::RefCell, ops::Range, rc::Rc};\\n\\nconst LINE_HEIGHT: f32 = 14. * 1.55;\\n\\npub fn support_text(label: &str, hint: Option<&str>, filled: bool, colors: Palette) -> AnyElement {\\n    let mut whitespace = false;\\n    let label = collapse_spaces(label, &mut whitespace);\\n    let hint = if filled {\\n        String::new()\\n    } else {\\n        hint.map(|hint| collapse_spaces(&format!(\\\" — {hint}\\\"), &mut whitespace))\\n            .unwrap_or_default()\\n    };\\n    div()\\n        .flex_1()\\n        .min_w_0()\\n        .child(SupportText {\\n            label,\\n            hint,\\n            filled,\\n            colors,\\n        })\\n        .into_any_element()\\n}\\n\\n// CSS normal whitespace collapses segment breaks, tabs and ASCII spaces.\\n// NBSP, narrow NBSP and other Unicode content keep their own break semantics.\\nfn collapsible(character: char) -> bool {\\n    matches!(character, ' ' | '\\\\t' | '\\\\n' | '\\\\r' | '\\\\u{000c}')\\n}\\n\\nfn collapse_spaces(text: &str, previous_space: &mut bool) -> String {\\n    let mut out = String::new();\\n    for character in text.chars() {\\n        if collapsible(character) {\\n            if !*previous_space {\\n                out.push(' ');\\n            }\\n            *previous_space = true;\\n        } else {\\n            out.push(character);\\n            *previous_space = false;\\n        }\\n    }\\n    out\\n}\\n\\nstruct SupportText {\\n    label: String,\\n    hint: String,\\n    filled: bool,\\n    colors: Palette,\\n}\\n\\nstruct FaceRun {\\n    from: usize,\\n    shape: ShapedLine,\\n}\\n\\nstruct InlineLayout {\\n    text: String,\\n    runs: Vec<FaceRun>,\\n    breaks: Vec<usize>,\\n    baseline: Pixels,\\n    placements: Vec<(ShapedLine, Point<Pixels>)>,\\n}\\n\\nimpl InlineLayout {\\n    fn trimmed_range(&self, range: Range<usize>) -> Range<usize> {\\n        let text = &self.text[range.clone()];\\n        let start = range.start + text.len() - text.trim_start_matches(' ').len();\\n        let end = start + self.text[start..range.end].trim_end_matches(' ').len();\\n        start..end\\n    }\\n\\n    fn width(&self, range: Range<usize>) -> Pixels {\\n        let range = self.trimmed_range(range);\\n        self.runs\\n            .iter()\\n            .map(|run| {\\n                let start = range.start.max(run.from);\\n                let end = range.end.min(run.from + run.shape.len());\\n                if end > start {\\n                    run.shape.x_for_index(end - run.from) - run.shape.x_for_index(start - run.from)\\n                } else {\\n                    px(0.)\\n                }\\n            })\\n            .sum()\\n    }\\n\\n    fn measure(&mut self, wrap_width: Option<Pixels>) -> Size<Pixels> {\\n        self.placements.clear();\\n        let mut start = 0;\\n        let mut row = 0;\\n        let mut widest = px(0.);\\n        while start < self.text.len() {\\n            start += self.text[start..].len() - self.text[start..].trim_start_matches(' ').len();\\n            if start == self.text.len() {\\n                break;\\n            }\\n            let mut chosen = None;\\n            for end in self.breaks.iter().copied().filter(|end| *end > start) {\\n                if wrap_width.is_some_and(|width| self.width(start..end) > width) {\\n                    chosen = chosen.or(Some(end));\\n                    break;\\n                }\\n                chosen = Some(end);\\n            }\\n            let end = chosen.unwrap_or(self.text.len());\\n            let range = self.trimmed_range(start..end);\\n            let mut x = px(0.);\\n            for run in &self.runs {\\n                let from = range.start.max(run.from);\\n                let to = range.end.min(run.from + run.shape.len());\\n                if to <= from {\\n                    continue;\\n                }\\n                let (_, remainder) = run.shape.split_at(from - run.from);\\n                let (fragment, _) = remainder.split_at(to - from);\\n                let own_baseline =\\n                    (px(LINE_HEIGHT) - fragment.ascent - fragment.descent) / 2. + fragment.ascent;\\n                let width = fragment.width();\\n                self.placements.push((\\n                    fragment,\\n                    point(\\n                        x,\\n                        px(row as f32 * LINE_HEIGHT) + self.baseline - own_baseline,\\n                    ),\\n                ));\\n                x += width;\\n            }\\n            widest = widest.max(x);\\n            row += 1;\\n            start = end;\\n        }\\n        let intrinsic = self.width(0..self.text.len());\\n        let width = wrap_width.map_or(intrinsic, |width| intrinsic.min(width).max(widest));\\n        size(width, px(row.max(1) as f32 * LINE_HEIGHT))\\n    }\\n}\\n\\nimpl IntoElement for SupportText {\\n    type Element = Self;\\n    fn into_element(self) -> Self {\\n        self\\n    }\\n}\\n\\nimpl Element for SupportText {\\n    type RequestLayoutState = Rc<RefCell<InlineLayout>>;\\n    type PrepaintState = ();\\n    fn id(&self) -> Option<ElementId> {\\n        None\\n    }\\n    fn source_location(&self) -> Option<&'static core::panic::Location<'static>> {\\n        None\\n    }\\n    fn request_layout(\\n        &mut self,\\n        _: Option<&GlobalElementId>,\\n        _: Option<&InspectorElementId>,\\n        window: &mut Window,\\n        _: &mut App,\\n    ) -> (LayoutId, Self::RequestLayoutState) {\\n        let color = if self.filled {\\n            self.colors.ink_muted\\n        } else {\\n            self.colors.ink\\n        };\\n        let strong = window.text_system().shape_line(\\n            SharedString::from(self.label.clone()),\\n            px(14.),\\n            &[TextRun {\\n                len: self.label.len(),\\n                font: Font {\\n                    weight: FontWeight::BOLD,\\n                    ..font(SERIF_FONT)\\n                },\\n                color: rgb(color).into(),\\n                strikethrough: self.filled.then_some(StrikethroughStyle {\\n                    thickness: px(1.),\\n                    color: Some(rgb(color).into()),\\n                }),\\n                ..Default::default()\\n            }],\\n            None,\\n        );\\n        let strut = window.text_system().shape_line(\\n            \\\"Mg\\\".into(),\\n            px(14.),\\n            &[TextRun {\\n                len: 2,\\n                font: font(SERIF_FONT),\\n                ..Default::default()\\n            }],\\n            None,\\n        );\\n        let baseline = (px(LINE_HEIGHT) - strut.ascent - strut.descent) / 2. + strut.ascent;\\n        let mut runs = vec![FaceRun {\\n            from: 0,\\n            shape: strong,\\n        }];\\n        if !self.hint.is_empty() {\\n            runs.push(FaceRun {\\n                from: self.label.len(),\\n                shape: window.text_system().shape_line(\\n                    SharedString::from(self.hint.clone()),\\n                    px(12.),\\n                    &[TextRun {\\n                        len: self.hint.len(),\\n                        font: font(SERIF_FONT),\\n                        color: rgb(self.colors.ink_muted).into(),\\n                        ..Default::default()\\n                    }],\\n                    None,\\n                ),\\n            });\\n        }\\n        let text = format!(\\\"{}{}\\\", self.label, self.hint);\\n        let breaks = unicode_linebreak::linebreaks(&text)\\n            .map(|(end, _)| end)\\n            .collect();\\n        let state = Rc::new(RefCell::new(InlineLayout {\\n            text,\\n            runs,\\n            breaks,\\n            baseline,\\n            placements: Vec::new(),\\n        }));\\n        let measure_state = state.clone();\\n        let id = window.request_measured_layout(Style::default(), move |known, available, _, _| {\\n            let width = known.width.or(match available.width {\\n                AvailableSpace::Definite(width) => Some(width),\\n                AvailableSpace::MinContent => Some(px(0.)),\\n                AvailableSpace::MaxContent => None,\\n            });\\n            measure_state.borrow_mut().measure(width)\\n        });\\n        (id, state)\\n    }\\n    fn prepaint(\\n        &mut self,\\n        _: Option<&GlobalElementId>,\\n        _: Option<&InspectorElementId>,\\n        bounds: Bounds<Pixels>,\\n        state: &mut Self::RequestLayoutState,\\n        _: &mut Window,\\n        _: &mut App,\\n    ) {\\n        state.borrow_mut().measure(Some(bounds.size.width));\\n    }\\n    fn paint(\\n        &mut self,\\n        _: Option<&GlobalElementId>,\\n        _: Option<&InspectorElementId>,\\n        bounds: Bounds<Pixels>,\\n        state: &mut Self::RequestLayoutState,\\n        _: &mut (),\\n        window: &mut Window,\\n        cx: &mut App,\\n    ) {\\n        for (shape, position) in &state.borrow().placements {\\n            let _ = shape.paint(\\n                bounds.origin + *position,\\n                px(LINE_HEIGHT),\\n                TextAlign::Left,\\n                None,\\n                window,\\n\"}}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"task\":1,\"status\":\"fulfilled\",\"value\":{\"chunk_id\":\"ddaef4\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000015879,\"exit_code\":2,\"original_token_count\":2920,\"output\":\"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 2920)\\nTotal output lines: 100\\n\\nrg: desktop/gpui/vendor/gpui-pre/src/layout.rs: No such file or directory (os error 2)\\ndesktop/gpui/vendor/gpui-pre/src/taffy.rs:5:        ceil_to_device_pixel, round_half_toward_zero, round_stroke_to_device_pixel,\\ndesktop/gpui/vendor/gpui-pre/src/taffy.rs:6:        round_to_device_pixel,\\ndesktop/gpui/vendor/gpui-pre/src/taffy.rs:34:    /// Unrounded absolute border-box top-left per-node coordinate in device pixels.\\ndesktop/gpui/vendor/gpui-pre/src/taffy.rs:45:        taffy.disable_rounding();\\ndesktop/gpui/vendor/gpui-pre/src/taffy.rs:130:                taffy::style::Dimension::length(round_to_device_pixel(size.width.0, scale_factor));\\ndesktop/gpui/vendor/gpui-pre/src/taffy.rs:134:                taffy::style::Dimension::length(round_to_device_pixel(size.height.0, scale_factor));\\ndesktop/gpui/vendor/gpui-pre/src/taffy.rs:283:    // We pixel-snap by rounding in device-pixel space, after multiplying\\ndesktop/gpui/vendor/gpui-pre/src/taffy.rs:287:    // Midpoints are rounded toward zero. This is a stylistic choice: a\\ndesktop/gpui/vendor/gpui-pre/src/taffy.rs:294:    //     authored absolute lengths are rounded in `to_taffy`. This\\ndesktop/gpui/vendor/gpui-pre/src/taffy.rs:296:    //     Custom-measured leaf nodes have their measured sizes rounded up\\ndesktop/gpui/vendor/gpui-pre/src/taffy.rs:312:    // These goals are in tension because rounding is not associative.\\ndesktop/gpui/vendor/gpui-pre/src/taffy.rs:315:    //  - Absolute edge rounding gives each window coordinate one answer,\\ndesktop/gpui/vendor/gpui-pre/src/taffy.rs:317:    //    length is `round(far) - round(near)`, which may change by 1 dp\\ndesktop/gpui/vendor/gpui-pre/src/taffy.rs:320:    //  - Parent-relative edge rounding rounds each child inside its\\ndesktop/gpui/vendor/gpui-pre/src/taffy.rs:323:    //    accumulate different rounding, causing non-closure between\\ndesktop/gpui/vendor/gpui-pre/src/taffy.rs:326:    //  - Length rounding rounds each width, height, and thickness\\ndesktop/gpui/vendor/gpui-pre/src/taffy.rs:327:    //    independently and then places boxes from those rounded lengths.\\ndesktop/gpui/vendor/gpui-pre/src/taffy.rs:332:    // We apply absolute edge rounding for each element's outer box in\\ndesktop/gpui/vendor/gpui-pre/src/taffy.rs:333:    // post-layout rounding to preserve closure. Border and padding widths\\ndesktop/gpui/vendor/gpui-pre/src/taffy.rs:334:    // are not touched by post-layout rounding; they keep their pre-layout\\ndesktop/gpui/vendor/gpui-pre/src/taffy.rs:335:    // rounded value so that they remain stable under translation.\\ndesktop/gpui/vendor/gpui-pre/src/taffy.rs:339:    // rounding covers that in most cases. The exception is metrics\\ndesktop/gpui/vendor/gpui-pre/src/taffy.rs:372:            absolute_outer_origin.map(round_half_toward_zero),\\ndesktop/gpui/vendor/gpui-pre/src/taffy.rs:373:            absolute_far.map(round_half_toward_zero),\\ndesktop/gpui/vendor/gpui-pre/src/taffy.rs:422:        taffy::style::LengthPercentage::length(round_stroke_to_device_pixel(\\ndesktop/gpui/vendor/gpui-pre/src/taffy.rs:525:        round_to_device_pixel(self.to_pixels(rem_size).0, scale_factor)\\ndesktop/gpui/vendor/gpui-pre/src/window.rs:9:    AsyncWindowContext, AtlasTile, AvailableSpace, Background, BorderStyle, Bounds, BoxShadow,\\ndesktop/gpui/vendor/gpui-pre/src/window.rs:23:    TransformationMatrix, Underline, UnderlineStyle, WindowAppearance, WindowBackgroundAppearance,\\ndesktop/gpui/vendor/gpui-pre/src/window.rs:75:    atomic_incr_if_not_zero, ceil_to_device_pixel, floor_to_device_pixel, round_half_toward_zero,\\ndesktop/gpui/vendor/gpui-pre/src/window.rs:76:    round_half_toward_zero_f64, round_stroke_to_device_pixel, round_to_device_pixel,\\ndesktop/gpui/vendor/gpui-pre/src/window.rs:1347:                    .saturating_sub(cx.background_executor().now() - started_at)\\ndesktop/gpui/vendor/gpui-pre/src/window.rs:1531:            window_background,\\ndesktop/gpui/vendor/gpui-pre/src/window.rs:1598:        platform_window.set_background_appearance(window_backgr…920 tokens truncated…s:4512:            background: quad.background.opacity(opacity),\\ndesktop/gpui/vendor/gpui-pre/src/window.rs:4519:        if !quad.background.is_transparent() {\\ndesktop/gpui/vendor/gpui-pre/src/window.rs:4524:        // Splitting a border-only quad around its empty interior avoids shading\\ndesktop/gpui/vendor/gpui-pre/src/window.rs:4573:    pub fn paint_path(&mut self, mut path: Path<Pixels>, color: impl Into<Background>) {\\ndesktop/gpui/vendor/gpui-pre/src/window.rs:4580:        let color: Background = color.into();\\ndesktop/gpui/vendor/gpui-pre/src/window.rs:4615:            origin: origin.map(|c| ScaledPixels(round_to_device_pixel(c.0, scale_factor))),\\ndesktop/gpui/vendor/gpui-pre/src/window.rs:4654:            round_half_toward_zero(glyph_origin.x.0 * SUBPIXEL_VARIANTS_X as f32)\\ndesktop/gpui/vendor/gpui-pre/src/window.rs:4656:            round_half_toward_zero(glyph_origin.y.0 * SUBPIXEL_VARIANTS_Y as f32)\\ndesktop/gpui/vendor/gpui-pre/src/window.rs:4718:        if self.platform_window.background_appearance() != WindowBackgroundAppearance::Opaque {\\ndesktop/gpui/vendor/gpui-pre/src/window.rs:4755:        let integer_origin = glyph_origin.map(|c| ScaledPixels(round_half_toward_zero(c.0)));\\ndesktop/gpui/vendor/gpui-pre/src/window.rs:4847:            .map_origin(|value| ScaledPixels(round_half_toward_zero(value.0)))\\ndesktop/gpui/vendor/gpui-pre/src/window.rs:4925:            let sub_origin_x = tile_origin_x + (x_offset_ratio * tile_width as f32).round() as i32;\\ndesktop/gpui/vendor/gpui-pre/src/window.rs:4926:            let sub_origin_y = tile_origin_y + (y_offset_ratio * tile_height as f32).round() as i32;\\ndesktop/gpui/vendor/gpui-pre/src/window.rs:4927:            let sub_width = (width_ratio * tile_width as f32).round() as i32;\\ndesktop/gpui/vendor/gpui-pre/src/window.rs:4928:            let sub_height = (height_ratio * tile_height as f32).round() as i32;\\ndesktop/gpui/vendor/gpui-pre/src/window.rs:5005:            self.platform_window.background_appearance() == WindowBackgroundAppearance::Opaque,\\ndesktop/gpui/vendor/gpui-pre/src/window.rs:5829:            cx.background_executor.timer(duration).await;\\ndesktop/gpui/vendor/gpui-pre/src/window.rs:6086:        let started_at = cx.background_executor().now();\\ndesktop/gpui/vendor/gpui-pre/src/window.rs:6088:            cx.background_executor.timer(remaining).await;\\ndesktop/gpui/vendor/gpui-pre/src/window.rs:6268:        let now = cx.background_executor().now();\\ndesktop/gpui/vendor/gpui-pre/src/window.rs:6519:    /// Focus the current window and bring it to the foreground at the platform level.\\ndesktop/gpui/vendor/gpui-pre/src/window.rs:6540:    /// screen including the menu bar and, on notched displays, the area around the\\ndesktop/gpui/vendor/gpui-pre/src/window.rs:7663:    /// The background color of the quad.\\ndesktop/gpui/vendor/gpui-pre/src/window.rs:7664:    pub background: Background,\\ndesktop/gpui/vendor/gpui-pre/src/window.rs:7698:    /// Sets the background color of the quad.\\ndesktop/gpui/vendor/gpui-pre/src/window.rs:7699:    pub fn background(self, background: impl Into<Background>) -> Self {\\ndesktop/gpui/vendor/gpui-pre/src/window.rs:7701:            background: background.into(),\\ndesktop/gpui/vendor/gpui-pre/src/window.rs:7711:    background: impl Into<Background>,\\ndesktop/gpui/vendor/gpui-pre/src/window.rs:7719:        background: background.into(),\\ndesktop/gpui/vendor/gpui-pre/src/window.rs:7726:/// Creates a filled quad with the given bounds and background color.\\ndesktop/gpui/vendor/gpui-pre/src/window.rs:7727:pub fn fill(bounds: impl Into<Bounds<Pixels>>, background: impl Into<Background>) -> PaintQuad {\\ndesktop/gpui/vendor/gpui-pre/src/window.rs:7731:        background: background.into(),\\ndesktop/gpui/vendor/gpui-pre/src/window.rs:7747:        background: transparent_black().into(),\\ndesktop/gpui/vendor/gpui-pre/src/window.rs:8884:                let rounded =\\ndesktop/gpui/vendor/gpui-pre/src/window.rs:8886:                ScaledPixels((scaled.signum() * rounded) as f32)\\n\"}}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"task\":2,\"status\":\"fulfilled\",\"value\":{\"chunk_id\":\"f0d182\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000015961,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":2537,\"output\":\"{\\n  \\\"corrections\\\": [\\n    \\\"map_result: replaced the flat-array stride (i += 3 with bound i < ranges.len(), which visited only every third range and stopped early) with a per-range ordinal r that increments by 1 up to ranges.len(); range access now uses ranges[r][old_index] and ranges[r][new_index] instead of ranges[i + old_index]/ranges[i + new_index].\\\",\\n    \\\"map_result recovery index: make_recover(i / 3, pos - start) corrected to make_recover(r, pos - start); the range ordinal is the loop index itself, not i/3.\\\",\\n    \\\"touches: same stride fix (r += 1, bound r < ranges.len()); the membership test i == index * 3 corrected to r == index.\\\",\\n    \\\"changed_ranges: loop stride i += 3 corrected to r += 1, and the output capacity Vec::with_capacity(len / 3) corrected to Vec::with_capacity(len) because len is already the number of ranges, not the flat element count.\\\",\\n    \\\"recover: verified already correct under triples (ranges[j][2] - ranges[j][1] and ranges[index][0]); no stride/index change needed there, only confirmation.\\\",\\n    \\\"Added StepMap::offset(i64) to restore source API parity; negative n maps to [0, -n, 0], positive n to [0, 0, n], and n == 0 yields empty.\\\",\\n    \\\"StepMap::new now returns empty() when handed no ranges, mirroring the source constructor's `!ranges.length` shortcut.\\\",\\n    \\\"Retained u64 recovery tokens rather than switching to f64; make_recover/recover_index/recover_offset reproduce JS bit-for-bit on the exact domain, and a debug_assert documents the 16-bit index bound.\\\",\\n    \\\"Preserved all Source boundary/assoc/deletion semantics: side selection order, recover = None at the assoc boundary, the DEL_AFTER/DEL_BEFORE/DEL_ACROSS/DEL_SIDE flags, Arc-shared invert, and the inverted old_index/new_index swaps.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"limitations\\\": [\\n    \\\"u64 recovery tokens are exact only where JS makeRecover is exact: index in [0, 2^16) and index + offset*65536 <= 2^53 - 1 (JS safe-integer limit). This caps a map at 65535 ranges; beyond that the token domain is undefined and JS itself loses precision/collides.\\\",\\n    \\\"recover() and touches() read ranges[index] / compare r == index; a token whose lower-16-bit index is >= ranges.len() will panic, whereas JS would return NaN/undefined. Tokens must originate from map_result.\\\",\\n    \\\"map_result and changed_ranges cast i64 intermediates to usize and assume valid inputs keep results nonnegative; malformed ranges could wrap (i64 only guards inverted-start underflow before the break).\\\",\\n    \\\"f64 tokens were rejected: they differ from u64 only for tokens >= 2^53, exactly where JS rounds, so f64 would reproduce JS precision loss instead of adding value and would complicate Eq/Ord token comparison. Chosen contract: u64 with an explicit documented exact domain that covers all realistic document lengths (offset <= document length, far below 2^37).\\\",\\n    \\\"toString/JSON serialization not ported to avoid a dependency; StepMap derives Debug instead.\\\",\\n    \\\"map/map_result take an explicit assoc (no default of 1) and only the sign of assoc is significant, matching JS usage with -1/1; callers must pass 1 for default behavior.\\\",\\n    \\\"No Mapping pipeline included (out of scope), so multi-step pipeline recovery accumulation and map_through are not provided.\\\",\\n    \\\"Ranges are stored as Arc<[[usize; 3]]> for cheap structural sharing on invert; the source's flat number[] layout is intentionally not reproduced.\\\"\\n  ]\\n}\\nuse std::sync::Arc;\\n\\nconst LOWER16: u64 = 0xffff;\\nconst FACTOR16: u64 = 1 << 16;\\n\\nconst DEL_BEFORE: u32 = 1;\\nconst DEL_AFTER: u32 = 2;\\nconst DEL_ACROSS: u32 = 4;\\nconst DEL_SIDE: u32 = 8;\\n\\n/// Encode a range ordinal (lower 16 bits) plus an offset into one token.\\n/// Exact only when `index < 2^16` and `index + offset * 65536 <= 2^53 - 1`\\n/// (the JavaScript safe-integer limit where `makeRecover` is itself exact).\\n#[inline]\\nfn make_recover(index: usize, offset: usize) -> u64 {\\n    debug_assert!((index as u64) < FACTOR16);\\n    index as u64 + offset as u64 * FACTOR16\\n}\\n\\n#[inline]\\nfn recover_index(value: u64) -> usize {\\n    (value & LOWER16) as usize\\n}\\n\\n#[inline]\\nfn recover_offset(value: u64) -> u64 {\\n    (value - (value & LOWER16)) / FACTOR16\\n}\\n\\n#[derive(Debug, Clone, PartialEq, Eq)]\\npub struct MapResult {\\n    pub pos: usize,\\n    pub del_info: u32,\\n    pub recover: Option<u64>,\\n}\\n\\nimpl MapResult {\\n    pub fn new(pos: usize, del_info: u32, recover: Option<u64>) -> Self {\\n        MapResult { pos, del_info, recover }\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn deleted(&self) -> bool {\\n        (self.del_info & DEL_SIDE) > 0\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn deleted_before(&self) -> bool {\\n        (self.del_info & (DEL_BEFORE | DEL_ACROSS)) > 0\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn deleted_after(&self) -> bool {\\n        (self.del_info & (DEL_AFTER | DEL_ACROSS)) > 0\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn deleted_across(&self) -> bool {\\n        (self.del_info & DEL_ACROSS) > 0\\n    }\\n}\\n\\n#[derive(Debug, Clone)]\\npub struct StepMap {\\n    pub ranges: Arc<[[usize; 3]]>,\\n    pub inverted: bool,\\n}\\n\\nimpl StepMap {\\n    pub fn new(ranges: Vec<[usize; 3]>) -> Self {\\n        if ranges.is_empty() {\\n            return StepMap::empty();\\n        }\\n        StepMap { ranges: Arc::from(ranges), inverted: false }\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn empty() -> Self {\\n        StepMap { ranges: Arc::from(Vec::new()), inverted: false }\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn is_empty(&self) -> bool {\\n        self.ranges.is_empty()\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn invert(&self) -> StepMap {\\n        StepMap { ranges: Arc::clone(&self.ranges), inverted: !self.inverted }\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn offset(n: i64) -> StepMap {\\n        if n == 0 {\\n            StepMap::empty()\\n        } else if n < 0 {\\n            StepMap::new(vec![[0, (-n) as usize, 0]])\\n        } else {\\n            StepMap::new(vec![[0, 0, n as usize]])\\n        }\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn recover(&self, token: u64) -> usize {\\n        let index = recover_index(token);\\n        let mut diff: i64 = 0;\\n        if !self.inverted {\\n            let mut j = 0;\\n            while j < index {\\n                diff += self.ranges[j][2] as i64 - self.ranges[j][1] as i64;\\n                j += 1;\\n            }\\n        }\\n        (self.ranges[index][0] as i64 + diff + recover_offset(token) as i64) as usize\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn map(&self, pos: usize, assoc: i32) -> usize {\\n        self.map_result(pos, assoc).pos\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn map_result(&self, pos: usize, assoc: i32) -> MapResult {\\n        let pos_i = pos as i64;\\n        let assoc_i = assoc as i64;\\n        let assoc_neg = assoc < 0;\\n        let old_index: usize = if self.inverted { 2 } else { 1 };\\n        let new_index: usize = if self.inverted { 1 } else { 2 };\\n        let mut diff: i64 = 0;\\n        let len = self.ranges.len();\\n        let mut r: usize = 0;\\n        while r < len {\\n            let range = &self.ranges[r];\\n            let start = range[0] as i64 - (if self.inverted { diff } else { 0 });\\n            if start > pos_i {\\n                break;\\n            }\\n            let old_size = range[old_index] as i64;\\n            let new_size = range[new_index] as i64;\\n            let end = start + old_size;\\n            if pos_i <= end {\\n                let side = if old_size == 0 {\\n                    assoc_i\\n                } else if pos_i == start {\\n                    -1\\n                } else if pos_i == end {\\n                    1\\n                } else {\\n                    assoc_i\\n                };\\n                let result = start + diff + (if side < 0 { 0 } else { new_size });\\n                let boundary = if assoc_neg { start } else { end };\\n                let recover = if pos_i == boundary {\\n                    None\\n                } else {\\n                    Some(make_recover(r, (pos_i - start) as usize))\\n                };\\n                let mut del = if pos_i == start {\\n                    DEL_AFTER\\n                } else if pos_i == end {\\n                    DEL_BEFORE\\n                } else {\\n                    DEL_ACROSS\\n                };\\n                let off_side = if assoc_neg { pos_i != start } else { pos_i != end };\\n                if off_side {\\n                    del |= DEL_SIDE;\\n                }\\n                return MapResult { pos: result as usize, del_info: del, recover };\\n            }\\n            diff += new_size - old_size;\\n            r += 1;\\n        }\\n        MapResult { pos: (pos_i + diff) as usize, del_info: 0, recover: None }\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn touches(&self, pos: usize, token: u64) -> bool {\\n        let pos_i = pos as i64;\\n        let index = recover_index(token);\\n        let old_index: usize = if self.inverted { 2 } else { 1 };\\n        let new_index: usize = if self.inverted { 1 } else { 2 };\\n        let mut diff: i64 = 0;\\n        let len = self.ranges.len();\\n        let mut r: usize = 0;\\n        while r < len {\\n            let range = &self.ranges[r];\\n            let start = range[0] as i64 - (if self.inverted { diff } else { 0 });\\n            if start > pos_i {\\n                break;\\n            }\\n            let old_size = range[old_index] as i64;\\n            let end = start + old_size;\\n            if pos_i <= end && r == index {\\n                return true;\\n            }\\n            diff += range[new_index] as i64 - old_size;\\n            r += 1;\\n        }\\n        false\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn changed_ranges(&self) -> Vec<[usize; 4]> {\\n        let old_index: usize = if self.inverted { 2 } else { 1 };\\n        let new_index: usize = if self.inverted { 1 } else { 2 };\\n        let len = self.ranges.len();\\n        let mut out: Vec<[usize; 4]> = Vec::with_capacity(len);\\n        let mut diff: i64 = 0;\\n        let mut r: usize = 0;\\n        while r < len {\\n            let range = &self.ranges[r];\\n            let start = range[0] as i64;\\n            let old_start = start - (if self.inverted { diff } else { 0 });\\n            let new_start = start + (if self.inverted { 0 } else { diff });\\n            let old_size = range[old_index] as i64;\\n            let new_size = range[new_index] as i64;\\n            out.push([\\n                old_start as usize,\\n                (old_start + old_size) as usize,\\n                new_start as usize,\\n                (new_start + new_size) as usize,\\n            ]);\\n            diff += new_size - old_size;\\n            r += 1;\\n        }\\n        out\\n    }\\n}\\n\\n\"}}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"task\":3,\"status\":\"fulfilled\",\"value\":{\"chunk_id\":\"155226\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000019633,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":31,\"output\":\"{\\\"output\\\":\\\"desktop/gpui/target/verification/genui-source-cards-20261005-e\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"captured\\\",\\\"cases\\\":4,\\\"pageErrors\\\":0}\\n\"}}"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a10c6f-d724-7b02-bb99-7845fa255153","create_time":1791210531.1944394}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
