{"timestamp":"2026-10-05T14:51:11.429Z","ordinal":41755,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_0acb6e766bb0227d016ac3b9371e7087d19816ca92c9519329","status":"completed","call_id":"call_uRPtzCsI4AFS2j8O1GTQ7mbf","name":"exec","input":"text(await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"rtk proxy python3 - <<'PY'\\nfrom pathlib import Path\\nPath('desktop/gpui/fixtures/gen-ui/README.md').write_text('''# In-flow writing tools\\n\\nThe full hosted Twyne desktop is the reference. Native Sentence Lab, Rhythm\\nStrip, Claim Check and Reader Questions are mounted in `WritingRoom`, with the\\noriginal fonts, palette, labels, card, rail/popover positioning and saved-tool\\nshelf. This is progress toward the complete desktop port, not full-app parity.\\n\\nThe host translates paragraph text and UTF-16 sentence offsets into the native\\nrich document's scalar coordinates. Applying a working copy preserves the\\nother sentences, marks outside its replacement, and the original Undo caret.\\nChanges to the anchored sentence retain the proposal and show Source's notice.\\nFolio, editor visit, tool identity and request identity guard late callbacks.\\nSaved tools and successful Jots are written locally and read back before their\\nacknowledgments. Real mounted button tests verify persistence after reopen.\\n\\nInputs use GPUI Kit's base editing engine with Twyne's own field presentation,\\nfocus bindings and accessibility actions. The compact Rhythm controls include\\nthe original widths, internal suffix and number font. A replay of seven real\\nSource browser interactions verifies arrow keys, bounds, typed values, clearing\\nand subsequent stepping in the mounted native editor. The checkbox and mixed\\nsize Claim labels use Source's dimensions and shared inline baseline.\\n\\nSource/browser and actual native GPU captures have been made for all four\\ndefault cards at 1280 x 860, scale 1. They establish those states only. The\\nSource captures run the real editor in isolated browser storage; they do not\\nestablish Electrobun-host equivalence. Fractional spacing, emoji/font raster,\\nfocus rings, tooltips, narrow layouts, night mode and further states still need\\ncomparison. Current runtime and capture receipts are under `target/verification`.\\nExisting failed receipts remain available there.\\n\\nThe executed Source oracles cover:\\n\\n- Catalog validation, cumulative append-only streams, deterministic writer\\n  seeds and offline fill. Writer-owned sentences and attempts remain uncapped;\\n  model candidates retain Source's caps and validation behavior.\\n- Kept-tool and notebook normalization, native paragraph/atom offsets and\\n  rail/popover geometry.\\n- 63 paragraph signal cases with 791 frames and six hedge strings.\\n- 15 shared System One budget timelines with 852 frames.\\n- 150 exact classification request/response cases and four fallback cases,\\n  including JavaScript coercions, UTF-16 clips and malformed answers.\\n- 112 forward/inverse ProseMirror StepMap cases with 9,476 frames, including\\n  deletion boundaries, multiple ranges and IEEE-754 recovery rounding.\\n\\nStepMap accepts valid nonnegative native coordinates within JavaScript's safe\\ninteger domain. It refuses invalid native maps and uses opaque floating-point\\nrecovery tokens to preserve the original Number arithmetic. Source NaN\\nrecovery is represented as failure. The host still uses a single projection\\nreplacement between snapshots; ordered transaction maps, rebase mirrors and\\ncomplex moves remain unfinished. The adapted algorithm's MIT notice is in\\n`prosemirror-transform-LICENSE.txt`.\\n\\nThe detector, classification and budget modules have Source-backed pure\\ncontracts. Automatic struggle tracking and shared live transport are not\\nconnected. Classification's exact JSON can contain an escaped lone UTF-16\\nsurrogate; parsing that request through `serde_json::Value` would change or\\nreject it. Other Rust strings still cannot represent JavaScript lone\\nsurrogates in generated specs or writer labels sliced through a pair.\\n\\nResearch currently opens the native Apparatus and reports its unavailable\\nadapter. Jot storage is integrated; the writing-tools notebook surface still\\nneeds its bridge. Live Jev/System One, writer model generation, account-owned\\nknowledge, connected authentication and online sync remain part of the full\\nport objective and are not proved by these tests or captures.\\n\\nRun Root-owned Cargo checks sequentially:\\n\\n```sh\\nrtk proxy python3 desktop/gpui/fixtures/gen-ui/check.py ui\\nrtk proxy python3 desktop/gpui/fixtures/gen-ui/check.py lint\\n```\\n\\nFreeze and capture a checked build using an explicit document-helper origin:\\n\\n```sh\\nrtk proxy python3 desktop/gpui/fixtures/gen-ui/build.py --helper /absolute/path/to/twyne-document\\nrtk proxy python3 desktop/gpui/fixtures/gen-ui/capture-native.py /absolute/path/to/frozen/build\\n```\\n\\nThese use isolated capture libraries and displays. They leave the user's\\nrunning preview and existing writing untouched. Source web/Convex files,\\nprovider registrations and account data are preserved.\\n\\nThe `*-proposal` folders retain actual isolated Sakana fugu-max inputs and\\noutputs. Review receipts distinguish adopted code, coordinator corrections,\\ntimeouts and remaining proof boundaries. The coordinator executes the original\\nimplementation for comparison rather than treating an advisory response as\\nverification.\\n''')\\nprint('Updated mounted-tool evidence and remaining full-port work')\\nPY\",\"max_output_tokens\":400}));\ntext(await tools.write_stdin({session_id:40485,chars:\"\",yield_time_ms:1000,max_output_tokens:2600}));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a10c6f-d724-7b02-bb99-7845fa255153","create_time":1791211818.62711}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-05T14:51:11.537Z","ordinal":41756,"type":"token_usage_record","payload":{"thread_id":"01a10537-909f-77a3-96d8-dd07161f91ae","turn_id":"01a10c6f-d724-7b02-bb99-7845fa255153","session_id":"01a10537-909f-77a3-96d8-dd07161f91ae","root_turn_id":"01a10c6f-d724-7b02-bb99-7845fa255153","response_id":"resp_0acb6e766bb0227d016ac3b92a7bd887d18ef4ad8aee78d95d","usage":{"input_tokens":174636,"cached_input_tokens":172800,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":1416,"reasoning_output_tokens":288,"total_tokens":176052},"turn_token_usage":{"input_tokens":4097864,"cached_input_tokens":3954560,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":46439,"reasoning_output_tokens":24353,"total_tokens":4144303},"thread_token_usage":{"input_tokens":528686905,"cached_input_tokens":508116096,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":3372203,"reasoning_output_tokens":1484451,"total_tokens":532059108}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-05T14:51:11.561Z","ordinal":41757,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a10537-909f-77a3-96d8-dd07161f91ae","turn_id":"01a10c6f-d724-7b02-bb99-7845fa255153","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-962990bd-6c77-4eba-91d0-2414575a26ad","process_id":"28571","command":["/bin/bash","-lc","rtk proxy python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nPath('desktop/gpui/fixtures/gen-ui/README.md').write_text('''# In-flow writing tools\n\nThe full hosted Twyne desktop is the reference. Native Sentence Lab, Rhythm\nStrip, Claim Check and Reader Questions are mounted in `WritingRoom`, with the\noriginal fonts, palette, labels, card, rail/popover positioning and saved-tool\nshelf. This is progress toward the complete desktop port, not full-app parity.\n\nThe host translates paragraph text and UTF-16 sentence offsets into the native\nrich document's scalar coordinates. Applying a working copy preserves the\nother sentences, marks outside its replacement, and the original Undo caret.\nChanges to the anchored sentence retain the proposal and show Source's notice.\nFolio, editor visit, tool identity and request identity guard late callbacks.\nSaved tools and successful Jots are written locally and read back before their\nacknowledgments. Real mounted button tests verify persistence after reopen.\n\nInputs use GPUI Kit's base editing engine with Twyne's own field presentation,\nfocus bindings and accessibility actions. The compact Rhythm controls include\nthe original widths, internal suffix and number font. A replay of seven real\nSource browser interactions verifies arrow keys, bounds, typed values, clearing\nand subsequent stepping in the mounted native editor. The checkbox and mixed\nsize Claim labels use Source's dimensions and shared inline baseline.\n\nSource/browser and actual native GPU captures have been made for all four\ndefault cards at 1280 x 860, scale 1. They establish those states only. The\nSource captures run the real editor in isolated browser storage; they do not\nestablish Electrobun-host equivalence. Fractional spacing, emoji/font raster,\nfocus rings, tooltips, narrow layouts, night mode and further states still need\ncomparison. Current runtime and capture receipts are under `target/verification`.\nExisting failed receipts remain available there.\n\nThe executed Source oracles cover:\n\n- Catalog validation, cumulative append-only streams, deterministic writer\n  seeds and offline fill. Writer-owned sentences and attempts remain uncapped;\n  model candidates retain Source's caps and validation behavior.\n- Kept-tool and notebook normalization, native paragraph/atom offsets and\n  rail/popover geometry.\n- 63 paragraph signal cases with 791 frames and six hedge strings.\n- 15 shared System One budget timelines with 852 frames.\n- 150 exact classification request/response cases and four fallback cases,\n  including JavaScript coercions, UTF-16 clips and malformed answers.\n- 112 forward/inverse ProseMirror StepMap cases with 9,476 frames, including\n  deletion boundaries, multiple ranges and IEEE-754 recovery rounding.\n\nStepMap accepts valid nonnegative native coordinates within JavaScript's safe\ninteger domain. It refuses invalid native maps and uses opaque floating-point\nrecovery tokens to preserve the original Number arithmetic. Source NaN\nrecovery is represented as failure. The host still uses a single projection\nreplacement between snapshots; ordered transaction maps, rebase mirrors and\ncomplex moves remain unfinished. The adapted algorithm's MIT notice is in\n`prosemirror-transform-LICENSE.txt`.\n\nThe detector, classification and budget modules have Source-backed pure\ncontracts. Automatic struggle tracking and shared live transport are not\nconnected. Classification's exact JSON can contain an escaped lone UTF-16\nsurrogate; parsing that request through `serde_json::Value` would change or\nreject it. Other Rust strings still cannot represent JavaScript lone\nsurrogates in generated specs or writer labels sliced through a pair.\n\nResearch currently opens the native Apparatus and reports its unavailable\nadapter. Jot storage is integrated; the writing-tools notebook surface still\nneeds its bridge. Live Jev/System One, writer model generation, account-owned\nknowledge, connected authentication and online sync remain part of the full\nport objective and are not proved by these tests or captures.\n\nRun Root-owned Cargo checks sequentially:\n\n```sh\nrtk proxy python3 desktop/gpui/fixtures/gen-ui/check.py ui\nrtk proxy python3 desktop/gpui/fixtures/gen-ui/check.py lint\n```\n\nFreeze and capture a checked build using an explicit document-helper origin:\n\n```sh\nrtk proxy python3 desktop/gpui/fixtures/gen-ui/build.py --helper /absolute/path/to/twyne-document\nrtk proxy python3 desktop/gpui/fixtures/gen-ui/capture-native.py /absolute/path/to/frozen/build\n```\n\nThese use isolated capture libraries and displays. They leave the user's\nrunning preview and existing writing untouched. Source web/Convex files,\nprovider registrations and account data are preserved.\n\nThe `*-proposal` folders retain actual isolated Sakana fugu-max inputs and\noutputs. Review receipts distinguish adopted code, coordinator corrections,\ntimeouts and remaining proof boundaries. The coordinator executes the original\nimplementation for comparison rather than treating an advisory response as\nverification.\n''')\nprint('Updated mounted-tool evidence and remaining full-port work')\nPY"],"cwd":"file:///home/diogenes/Projects/twyne","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"rtk proxy python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nPath('desktop/gpui/fixtures/gen-ui/README.md').write_text('''# In-flow writing tools\n\nThe full hosted Twyne desktop is the reference. Native Sentence Lab, Rhythm\nStrip, Claim Check and Reader Questions are mounted in `WritingRoom`, with the\noriginal fonts, palette, labels, card, rail/popover positioning and saved-tool\nshelf