:applies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne; reuse_rule=reuse existing Twyne UI primitives and live-review ownership; do not represent this rollout as browser visually verified.\n1385:scope: Audit an interrupted agent video run against actual artifacts, then complete and verify all renderable Twyne launch films on this Linux workstation.\n1429:- Twyne’s visual language is aged cream paper, near-black brown ink, vermilion, literary serif display type, DM Sans UI, and Special Elite/typewriter labels—avoid generic AI-chat/SaaS treatment. `_gen` scripts/manifests stage imagery, music, TTS, alignment, captions, fonts, SFX, and brand SVGs; word timing is bundled inline as `assets/js/words.js` to avoid render-time fetches. [Task 3]\n1436:# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/twyne Jev editor live-review, Not Organic linking, and v0.20.2 release\n1437:scope: Integrate typed Jev review into the real saved-draft editor loop, securely provision the Not Organic boundary, and verify clean CI/release evidence.\n1450:## Task 2: Provision Not Organic and publish reproducible v0.20.2\n1458:- judgement:evaluate, DPoP, PKCE, NOTORGANIC_AUDIENCE, invalid_product_assertion, hushed-aardvark-411, jsdom@26.1.0, Undici, .dagger/src/index.ts, twyne-tools, v0.20.2, 402 insufficient_funds\n1464:- when styling should be “consistent with our other styles” -> reuse Twyne tokens, shared controls, typography, and Editorial Board vocabulary rather than a local styling system [Task 1]\n1471:- Not Organic production uses `https://api.notorganic.info`, capability `judgement:evaluate`, and DPoP-bound tokens. Link with PKCE one-time state and server-side token/account verification; do not trust a browser-supplied DID, expose gateway credentials, or send upstream error bodies to browsers. [Task 2]\n1477:- `401 invalid_product_assertion` -> keep `NOTORGANIC_AUDIENCE` separate from `NOTORGANIC_ISSUER` and set the production audience to `notorganic`; direct `/v1/judgement` requests correctly fail without the signed assertion-to-DPoP path. A `402 insufficient_funds` probe proves the funded review itself was not verified. [Task 2]\n1481:scope: Reuse the Not Organic judgement transport and conservative semantic decisions across Weave/Woven/Worn without replacing deterministic or safety-critical logic.\n1492:- POST /v1/judgement, judgement:evaluate, notOrganicClient.ts, product assertion, DPoP, typed wire codec, calibrationSha256, abstention, confect/host/judgments, Woven, Worn\n1507:- for deep integration across “weave, woven and worn,” start with cross-repository archaeology of Keating/Twyne/TypeSafe/Not Organic rather than editing one call site [Task 1]\n1512:- Reuse `confect/handlers/lib/notOrganicClient.ts`: it signs a short-lived Ed25519 product assertion, exchanges a DPoP token, caches it, signs each request, and adds product/idempotency/cost headers. Route to `POST /v1/judgement` with `judgement:evaluate`; gateway keeps the TypeSafe key. Locally validate, return failures rather than throw, retry only retryable statuses, do not echo upstream bodies, and abstain/fallback when unavailable. [Task 1][Task 2]\n1618:scope: Operate Twyne's shared remote-BYOK transport and harden Convex, Not Organic, and ATProto browser-session recovery without overstating signed-in account proof.\n1631:## Task 2: Refresh Convex tokens and reconnect existing Not Organic links\n1639:- createConvexTokenFetcher, forceRefreshToken, hasAuthenticatedConvexIdentity, convexAuthenticated, Reconnect Not Organic, Check again, providerIdentity.ts\n1666:- Do not claim the account-specific Not Organic callback/link flow or the user's exact Bluesky 400 recovery is fixed until a signed-in browser verifies it. [Task 2][Task 3]\n1820:## Task 1: Investigate Needle and publish Twyne 0.21.0\n1843:- for Twyne, use Keating’s approach: deconstruct persona/system behavior into typed inspectable Jev rules that control generation, rather than only locating or rewriting prompt prose. [Task 2]\n1853:- Static tests (1549 pass/39 skip) did not prove an actual Jev/provider/Not Organic run. Do not expose rejected candidate text or hidden reasoning in repair prompts/status UI. [Task 2]\n1856:scope: Keep legal/mail/payment launch gates explicit, expose replaceable code-execution through Not Organic, and release the provider only through its verified private Radicle boundary.\n1887:- Execution remains behind Not Organic’s provider-neutral `SandboxGateway`: account authorization, spend limits, idempotency, cancellation, durable records, filesystem/workspace, bounded networking, secrets mediation, artifact export, resource limits, and provenance remain outside Cloudflare. Cloudflare, microVM, self-hosted runner, or future provider are adapters. [Task 1] [ad-hoc note]\n1912:- for “system one judge integration,” classification/actions/notifications, Not Organic, sandbox, and Trigger.dev-like durability -> use typed reusable judgments, code-owned actions, and approval gates, not opaque generative automation. “Leave it unfunded for now” means automatic judgments stay off. [Task 1]\n1917:- TypeSafe worker asks seven per-message typed questions and batches at most eight. It stores no mail bodies/credentials in its atomic journal; it validates account/owner/signature/capability/DPoP/freshness/replay and does not authorize sending/deleting/paying/link following/executing email code. [Task 1]\n2100:scope: Implement and extend account/product-scoped, developer-reviewed Jev rulesets through the metered Not Organic judgement boundary; keep Phase 1 limits explicit.\n2116:- when the user clarified “jev refers to typesafe's model” and approved reading the ledger before planning -> keep TypeSafe behind Not Organic’s authenticated, metered provider boundary rather than exposing direct credentials. [Task 1]\n2122:- Evaluation loads the exact immutable revision, filters dotted `state_binding` paths such as `metadata.source`, canonicalizes state, computes `state_digest`, and invokes `JudgementGateway.evaluate` with deterministic inner idempotency/request hashes. The gateway retains DPoP/authentication, wallet reservation, dispatch, usage settlement, and conservative reconciliation; TypeSafe credentials remain server-held. [Task 1]\n2299:scope: Route typed Jev judgements through Not Organic, maintain Jev-first rubric and optional writing lenses, and distinguish local implementation from verified provider production.\n2300:applies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne plus /home/diogenes/Projects/notorganic-provider; reuse_rule=reinspect both dirty worktrees and deploy state; direct TypeSafe use is local-only when Not Organic is enabled.\n2302:## Task 1: Stage then complete the Not Organic Jev provider boundary, partial\n2311:- Jev, TypeSafe, Not Organic, POST /v1/judgement, judgement:evaluate, DPoP, GatewayConfig.typesafe, TYPESAFE_API_KEY, ProviderStore, reserve dispatch accept settle\n2336:- when hosted TypeSafe/Jev integration was discussed, the user said it \"should work through notorganic in actuality rather than tied through this deployment directly\" and wanted an API \"that just works with jev\" -> place provider credentials, authorization, customer inspection, and ledger accounting behind Not Organic. [Task 1]\n2342:- Production Twyne calls Not Organic using DPoP and `judgement:evaluate` at `POST /v1/judgement`; direct `TYPESAFE_API_KEY` is only loopback/local fallback. The provider owns the key, typed state/questions transport, model alias resolution, and per-account reserve -> dispatch -> accept -> settle/reconcile accounting. [Task 1]\n2343:- Jev question types are `noul`, `choice`, and `score`; normalize Twyne arrays into TypeSafe Choice maps, retain Score ordered arrays, bound requests, avoid upstream response bodies that may echo documents, and surface uncertain/missing usage rather than silently billing zero. The observed rate was `0.042` microUSD per input token. [Task 1]\n2387:- `DEFAULT_LAYOUT.marginBottom: 1` overrides the normal 4rem fallback, and nested scrollers lack `scrollMargin`/`scrollThreshold`. Twyne's IndexedDB/service-worker shell is genuinely local-first, but sync, AI, auth, collaboration, and publishing remain remote; browser local models likely use Transformers.js/WebGPU/cached ONNX and desktop has a LiteRT seam. [Task 2]\n2513:- voxq, PRODUCT_IDS, FIRST_PARTY_PRODUCTS, ProductTheme, VOXQ_ASSERTION_PUBLIC_JWK, DPoP, micro-USD, --approve-for-me, --sandbox, adaptive-interviews, SSE\n2632:# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/keating chat sign-in continuation and Not Organic inference failure handling\n2633:scope: Keep learner chat immediate through account authorization and diagnose the actual Keating-to-Not Organic inference path without treating health checks as end-to-end proof.\n2634:applies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating and /home/diogenes/Projects/notorganic-provider; reuse_rule=recheck dirty worktrees, installed desktop version, fresh token/DPoP flow, Portkey configuration, and Convex behavior.\n2636:## Task 1: Preserve a pending chat send across Not Organic sign-in and push focused changes\n2654:- optimistic UI, retry, DPoP, Portkey, pc-keatin-bb473e, product: keating, INSUFFICIENT_FUNDS, HTTP 402, Passthrough target requires a provider\n2670:- Health/Railway success/direct Portkey stream do not prove desktop chat. Verify fresh public token exchange, DPoP request, exact stream, reservation, and rendered UI. Retryable failures get fresh DPoP proofs; insufficient credits do not retry. [Task 2]\n2767:scope: Run and verify the local survey studio, keep its Rust/Bun boundary safe, and expose a Not Organic model alias without falsely advertising an unwired upstream.\n2809:- Not Organic aliases are capability tiers (`infer:<alias>`), not upstream IDs. Add `persona` to contracts and the exhaustive admin-cap map, but omit it from Railway `ENABLED_MODEL_ALIASES` and gateway `/v1/models` fallbacks until configuration is real. Local deterministic fixtures do not prove human-like realism. [Task 2]\n2811:- The appeal may connect voxq's simulated-respondent benchmarking to Keating's authored-learner limitation and Persimmon TutorMoments, but must not claim a human interview or live Persimmon flow. Run repository `detect-changes` before later commits because unrelated Not Organic changes exist. [Task 3]\n2874:## Task 1: Immediate learner-message visibility and Not Organic account sign-in, partial\n2882:- AssistantChatPanel, FlueConversation, sendPrepared, optimistic-message, flue-immediate-send.test.ts, NotOrganic, PKCE, DPoP, publicClientConfig, VITE_NOTORGANIC_ENABLED, keating.help, spawnSync bun EPERM\n2914:- Not Organic browser auth uses PKCE plus a device-bound DPoP key, pending state in browser storage, exact issuer/client/redirect matching, and callback receipt/code-hash guards. `VITE_NOTORGANIC_ENABLED` should gate hosted inference, not account sign-in; authorization instead requires explicit issuer and authorization URL configuration. The inspected Railway production value was `VITE_NOTORGANIC_ENABLED=false`; focused Not Organic suites reported 25 passing tests, authorization redirected, token preflight returned 204 for `https://keating.help`, and the OpenAI device route returned 200. [Task 1]\n2982:scope: Repair and prove the Not Organic OAuth/authorization path across Keating client, portal styling, and the public gateway; distinguish client or container health from a working public token exchange.\n2993:- OAuth, PKCE, public-client.ts, sessionStorage, NotOrganicCallback, globalThis.fetch.bind(globalThis), Firefox, receipt, exchange map, CORS\n3165:applies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating; reuse_rule=report files and packaging workflow are reusable after rechecking current benchmark inputs and Railway state; Tinker/Not Organic integration remains an unverified feasibility direction until an authorized account, spend cap, and end-to-end run exist.\n3210:- Keating has canonical/provenance-rich training exports and an Unsloth LoRA SFT starter, but no integrated Tinker trainer, SDPO loop, or per-user adapter-serving path. Not Organic supplies account-scoped evolution metadata, authorization, artifact/result attestation, and atomic active revisions, not a verified authorized-Tinker-checkpoint connection. Tinker's continual-learning recipe is SDFT, not SDPO; it distinguishes sampler checkpoints from resumable training state. [Task 3]\n3220:scope: Operate Not Organic's own ATProto PDS signup path, retain the current did:plc decision, and provision Resend DNS without overstating live account/email readiness.\n3223:## Task 1: Direct Not Organic PDS account signup and deployment\n3265:- when discussing identity/signup, the user said Not Organic “should have its own pds” and people “should be able to create an account that way without going through bsky” -> implement and verify first-party PDS signup rather than redirecting account creation through Bluesky. [Task 1]\n3283:- Browser `fetch` overwrites `Sec-Fetch-Mode` as `cors`; use raw Node HTTP to reproduce navigation Fetch Metadata headers. Health/header/invalid-case checks and fresh signup authorization-page load prove the narrow same-site fix, not consent, email verification, cookies, callback/PKCE, token exchange, or an authenticated app session. [Task 4]\n3629:scope: Not Organic public/company surfaces, branded portal and email package, Railway landing snapshots, and release/Radicle constraints.\n3660:- Interleave, Twyne, Keating, product-icons, interleave-mark.png, twyne-mark.png, 268e9bd, git push rad main, rad auth, dirty-worktree, prek\n3677:- “update the icon used for interleave, also for twyne keep the animal icon, for keating the letter icon should be used” -> preserve product-specific identity: paired gecko for Interleave, griffin animal mark for Twyne, green K letter mark for Keating. [Task 3]\n3739:scope: Review, version, tag, publish, and verify the Twyne Qwik/Devenv release path.\n3866:- `LoginScreen` opt-in trace is capped at 20 events; `authDiagnostics.ts` redacts passwords, tokens, authorization codes, PKCE, query strings, and fragments. Full logout also calls `getCredentialStore().clear(account.id)` and clears React Query/UI state because `useAuthStore.logout()` does not clear secure credentials. [Task 2]\n4001:# Task Group: cross-repository native Devenv git hooks for Keating, Not Organic, and Twyne\n4023:- Keating already has repo-specific hooks; refresh stale generated `prek` state with `devenv shell -- prek install --force --hook-type pre-push`. Not Organic uses pre-commit `notorganic-check` -> `devenv tasks run notorganic:check`; Twyne uses `twyne-release-check` on pre-commit/pre-push -> `devenv tasks run twyne:release:check`. [Task 1]\n4028:- Do not use Twyne `twyne:check` as a hook while its baseline has 165 unrelated Prettier failures. Preserve dirty changes; `devenv info` may print secrets, so never use/store its full output. Vet `unknown error` is unverified. [Task 1]\n4108:- The failed review established no findings. On resume, inspect current code and run focused evidence first; high-impact areas worth prioritizing are release CI, credential hydration/persistence, login/registration, mobile Expo, web server handling, Not Organic client, Stalwart admin API, generated routes, and dependency/lockfile changes. [Task 2]\n4192:applies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne; reuse_rule=reuse only after inspecting current package scripts, tag-triggered workflow, hooks, branch, and dirty tree; this supersedes older Twyne guidance that requires a Bumpy note for a code push.\n4194:## Task 1: Migrate Twyne from Bumpy to Bun-native versioning\n4211:- Twyne now uses `release:version: bun pm version`, `release:publish: git push --follow-tags`, and `release:check: bun scripts/check-release-version.ts`. `preversion`, `postversion`, and `.githooks/pre-push.pre-entire` all call the shared guard. [Task 1]\n4212:- `scripts/check-release-version.ts` checks SemVer, the annotated `v<version>` tag, tagged `package.json` version equality, and unexpected `v*` tags at `HEAD`. `bun pm version` runs lifecycle hooks and creates the version commit, but verify that it actually created the annotated tag; `git push --follow-tags` preserves Twyne’s existing `v*` GitHub release trigger. [Task 1]\n4221:scope: Plan early validation for Twyne/Keating, review secure public-client payments, and turn hiring critiques into concise questions.\n4242:- NotOrganic Provider, public-client OAuth, PKCE, DPoP, POST /v1/public/token, self-hosting, atomic code redemption, Creem, checkout, webhooks, entitlements\n4266:- NotOrganic Provider is the sole authority for identity, consent, checkout, webhooks, subscriptions, wallet/usage, and entitlements. A public Keating client needs strict redirect validation, S256 PKCE, narrow scopes, a public DPoP key, a short-lived one-time code, atomic verifier/binding validation before code consumption, and provider-state feature gates rather than local Pro flags. [Task 2]\n4272:- Never consume an authorization code before PKCE/verifier and binding checks: a prior implementation let an invalid verifier burn a valid code. No deployment, charge, provider-delivered webhook, entitlement update, or authenticated portal session was proven; local passes are not a production-complete payment funnel. [Task 2]\n4314:- NotOrganic-Provider-Technical-Companion.docx, Bun, Hono, Convex, Portkey, DPoP, PKCE S256, public-client, nou_portal_session, micro-USD, Cloudflare Sandbox, Tangled, Spindle, Fly Sprites, R2, production-readiness-2026-08-16.md\n4323:- Repository map: `apps/gateway` is the Hono/Bun metered Portkey proxy; `apps/portal` owns React/Vite plus server-side ATProto OAuth/session/public-client flow; `packages/contracts`, `core`, `sdk`, and `session` hold shared contracts, money/lifecycle, OpenAI-shaped/DPoP clients, and assertion/token adaptation; `convex` is transactional state; `apps/sandbox-worker` runs isolated CPU jobs; `infra` holds Docker/Railway/OpenBao/PDS configuration. [Task 1]\n4324:- Main inference flow: a product backend signs a <=60-second single-use assertion; gateway verifies/consumes it, returns a <=300-second DPoP-bound token, requires `Authorization: DPoP` plus DPoP proof on protected calls, reserves integer micro-USD funds in Convex before Portkey dispatch, then settles/releases/reconciles. Idempotency prevents duplicate billing; debt can block hosted inference. [Task 1]\n4325:- Public clients must validate HTTPS origin, PKCE S256, exact same-origin callback, and portal-authenticated DID; never accept a browser-supplied DID or let self-hosted clients mint provider grants. Browser session is opaque `nou_portal_session` plus CSRF header, while OAuth keys/tokens remain server-side. The then-current Cloudflare Sandbox JWT bound account/product/project/run/body hash, with CPU-only/no-internet/30-second limits; treat those as adapter details, not the durable execution contract. Tangled is source, Spindle protocol, Fly Sprites pinned-commit runners, R2 artifacts, and Convex stores account-scoped provenance/status. [Task 1]\n4327:- Not Organic is the stable account and control-plane boundary for cross-device learner synchronization, shared pedagogical revisions, evolution history, active-version selection, and authorization. Browser, mobile, desktop, CLI, and connected self-hosted instances are account-scoped clients/contributors; they must not bind identity, durable state, or sync directly to provider-specific sandbox endpoints. [ad-hoc note]\n4488:## Task 2: File dossiers, fix reviewer findings, and publish Twyne 0.17.0\n4537:- VITE_NOTORGANIC_ENABLED, public-client.ts, NotOrganicCallback, keating_pack_10, DPoP, wallet, hosted inference, check-env-docs.ts, signed webhook\n4547:- Keating uses PKCE S256, non-extractable device-bound DPoP, short-lived access, callback/checkout/wallet UI, and hosted-inference headers. Keep raw Creem product IDs provider-private; use stable pack IDs. Synchronize public-client environment docs with `bun scripts/check-env-docs.ts`; `VITE_NOTORGANIC_ENABLED=false` is intentional pending E2E. [Task 2]\n4835:- oauth.ts, CloudProviderKeysSection.tsx, keating_oauth_pending, PKCE, getPendingOAuthRequest, cancelPendingOAuthRequest, /api/oauth/token, /api/oauth/refresh, OpenAI Codex, Anthropic, GitHub Copilot, Railway\n4845:- openai-codex, openai-codex-responses, pi-ai, ChatGPT OAuth JWT, chatgpt-account-id, Anthropic OAuth, PKCE, oauth-provider-config.ts, nodepod-boot-files.ts\n4855:- Main files are `web/src/keating/oauth.ts`, `web/src/components/settings/CloudProviderKeysSection.tsx`, `web/src/test/oauth.test.ts`, and generated `web/src/keating/nodepod-boot-files.ts`. Store pending safe metadata under `keating_oauth_pending`; recover with `getPendingOAuthRequest()` and cancel with `cancelPendingOAuthRequest()` without exposing PKCE verifier/state. [Task 1]\n4856:- Pending safe metadata stays under `keating_oauth_pending`; `getPendingOAuthRequest()` must not expose PKCE verifier/state. UI tells users the expected localhost error page can be copied back into “Finish sign-in below.” [Task 1][Task 2]\n4941:scope: Twyne application-error contract, notices, offline UX, sanitized diagnostics, and interview recovery.\n5035:scope: Diagnose browser auth/sync evidence, avoid ATProto scope and DPoP bootstrap failures, guard Convex mutations by real identity, and present normalized recoverable errors.\n5036:applies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne; reuse_rule=reuse these local contracts for Twyne auth/error work; recheck OAuth grants, live Convex deployment/logs, and dirty worktree before a deployment claim.\n5046:- ATProto, Bluesky, ScopeMissingError, app.bsky.actor.getProfile, PUBLIC_BSKY_APPVIEW, DPoP, use_dpop_nonce, initSessionPromise, resolveAtprotoProfile\n5074:- Hydrate public ATProto profiles through `PUBLIC_BSKY_APPVIEW = \"https://public.api.bsky.app\"` while preserving the OAuth session DID; existing `atproto blob:image/* include:site.standard.authFull` does not grant arbitrary audience-bound RPC scope. Use module-level `initSessionPromise` to prevent rotating DPoP nonce races; the library already captures/retries `DPoP-Nonce`. [Task 1]\n5085:scope: Maintain consumer-facing Not Organic account/identity UX separately from technical integration docs, including static docs-service build and Railway wiring.\n5096:- identity-shell, identity-creek-bg.webp, Continue with your handle, Your account wherever your ideas go, docs.notorganic.info, Caddyfile, Dockerfile.docs, docs.railpack.json, check-railpack.ts, PKCE S256, DPoP, WebP\n5098:## Task 2: Create and browser-verify Not Organic social preview cards\n5110:- signed-out identity UX uses “Your Not Organic account” and “Continue with your handle” rather than operator language -> write plain, user-facing account copy [Task 1]\n5111:- consumer pages should answer what Not Organic is, connected products, what stays with the person, and where it is managed; keep developer navigation visible but secondary and send implementation detail to dedicated docs [Task 1]\n5199:# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/stich commercial pricing, Not Organic boundaries, and voice direction\n5203:## Task 1: Implement and deploy fail-closed pricing with Creem and Not Organic\n5211:- pricing.tsx, Creem, Not Organic, stable pack_id, /v1/billing/checkout, idempotency-key, PKCE S256, DPoP, OpenBao, Checkout unavailable, wallet, signed webhook\n5231:- Not Organic owns identity, checkout, signed webhooks, wallet, usage, entitlements, and provider secrets; Stich consumes wallet state through stable server-resolved pack/plan IDs. `POST /v1/billing/checkout` needs HTTPS `return_url` and `idempotency-key`. Browser auth is PKCE S256 plus a device-bound DPoP key; never put Creem, OpenBao, or model-provider credentials in Stich client code. [Task 1]\n5232:- Deployed pricing tiers were Free, Personal `$10/month`, Household `$25/month`, and Studio `$50/month`, with hosted intelligence credits and one-cycle roll