{"timestamp":"2026-10-05T15:06:59.791Z","ordinal":41904,"type":"token_usage_record","payload":{"thread_id":"01a10537-909f-77a3-96d8-dd07161f91ae","turn_id":"01a10c99-5363-7262-baff-cdf89af89903","session_id":"01a10537-909f-77a3-96d8-dd07161f91ae","root_turn_id":"01a10c99-5363-7262-baff-cdf89af89903","response_id":"resp_0acb6e766bb0227d016ac3bcf440a087d1beb82fd3d23a84a9","usage":{"input_tokens":230461,"cached_input_tokens":220800,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":765,"reasoning_output_tokens":516,"total_tokens":231226},"turn_token_usage":{"input_tokens":867109,"cached_input_tokens":836992,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":1882,"reasoning_output_tokens":1032,"total_tokens":868991},"thread_token_usage":{"input_tokens":531060474,"cached_input_tokens":510306048,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":3393162,"reasoning_output_tokens":1500489,"total_tokens":534453636}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-05T15:06:59.803Z","ordinal":41905,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a10537-909f-77a3-96d8-dd07161f91ae","turn_id":"01a10c99-5363-7262-baff-cdf89af89903","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-5fd76a4d-c4b4-48ef-96cd-9b3c0e9c3d44","process_id":"62387","command":["/bin/bash","-lc","rtk proxy sed -n '1,158p' convex/auth.ts"],"cwd":"file:///home/diogenes/Projects/twyne","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"rtk proxy sed -n '1,158p' convex/auth.ts"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"import { createClient, type GenericCtx } from \"@convex-dev/better-auth\";\nimport { convex, crossDomain } from \"@convex-dev/better-auth/plugins\";\nimport { components } from \"./_generated/api\";\nimport { betterAuth, type BetterAuthOptions } from \"better-auth/minimal\";\nimport { DataModel } from \"./_generated/dataModel\";\nimport authConfig from \"./auth.config.js\";\nimport { makeFunctionReference } from \"convex/server\";\nimport { notOrganicIssuer } from \"./lib/notorganic\";\nimport {\n  notOrganicSignIn,\n  redeemNotOrganicSignIn,\n} from \"./lib/notorganicSignIn\";\n\nconst siteUrl = normalizeOrigin(\n  process.env.SITE_URL ??\n    process.env.BETTER_AUTH_URL ??\n    \"http://localhost:5173\",\n);\nconst TWYNE_PRODUCTION_ORIGINS = [\n  \"https://twyne.love\",\n  \"https://www.twyne.love\",\n] as const;\nconst saveVerifiedLink = makeFunctionReference<\n  \"mutation\",\n  { did: string; subject: string; sessionVersion: number }\n>(\"providerIdentity:saveVerifiedLink\");\n\nconst authComponents = components as any;\n\nexport const authComponent = createClient<DataModel>(\n  authComponents.betterAuth,\n  {\n    verbose: false,\n  },\n);\n\nexport const createAuthOptions = (ctx: GenericCtx<DataModel>) =>\n  ({\n    baseURL: process.env.CONVEX_SITE_URL,\n    secret: process.env.BETTER_AUTH_SECRET,\n    trustedOrigins: trustedOrigins(siteUrl),\n    database: authComponent.adapter(ctx),\n    emailAndPassword: {\n      enabled: false,\n    },\n    session: {\n      cookieCache: {\n        enabled: true,\n        maxAge: 5 * 60,\n      },\n    },\n    plugins: [\n      notOrganicSignIn({\n        // The browser's origin is the PKCE client_id; it must be one Twyne\n        // trusts (twyne.love and www.twyne.love are separate client ids).\n        redeem: ({ code, verifier, origin }) => {\n          if (!trustedOrigins(siteUrl).includes(origin)) {\n            throw new Error(\"This sign-in came from an untrusted origin.\");\n          }\n          return redeemNotOrganicSignIn(\n            { code, verifier },\n            origin,\n            notOrganicIssuer(),\n          );\n        },\n        onSignedIn: async ({ did, userId, sessionVersion }) => {\n          if (!(\"runMutation\" in ctx)) {\n            throw new Error(\"Not Organic sign-in needs a mutation context.\");\n          }\n          await ctx.runMutation(saveVerifiedLink, {\n            did,\n            subject: userId,\n            sessionVersion,\n          });\n        },\n      }),\n      crossDomain({ siteUrl }),\n      convex({ authConfig }),\n    ],\n  }) satisfies BetterAuthOptions;\n\nexport const createAuth = (ctx: GenericCtx<DataModel>) =>\n  betterAuth(createAuthOptions(ctx));\n\nfunction normalizeOrigin(value: string): string {\n  const url = new URL(value);\n  if (\n    ![\"http:\", \"https:\"].includes(url.protocol) ||\n    url.username ||\n    url.password ||\n    url.hostname.includes(\"*\")\n  ) {\n    throw new Error(\"Twyne auth needs an exact HTTP(S) origin.\");\n  }\n  return url.origin;\n}\n\nfunction isLoopbackOrigin(value: string): boolean {\n  const host = new URL(value).hostname;\n  return (\n    host === \"localhost\" ||\n    host === \"127.0.0.1\" ||\n    host === \"::1\" ||\n    host === \"[::1]\"\n  );\n}\n\nexport function trustedOrigins(\n  origin: string,\n  configuredOrigins = process.env.TRUSTED_ORIGINS ?? \"\",\n): string[] {\n  const origins = new Set<string>([origin]);\n  const addAliases = (value: string) => {\n    if (isLoopbackOrigin(value)) {\n      const url = new URL(value);\n      const port = url.port ? `:${url.port}` : \"\";\n      for (const host of [\"localhost\", \"127.0.0.1\", \"[::1]\"]) {\n        origins.add(`${url.protocol}//${host}${port}`);\n      }\n    }\n    if (isTwyneProductionOrigin(value)) {\n      for (const prodOrigin of TWYNE_PRODUCTION_ORIGINS)\n        origins.add(prodOrigin);\n    }\n  };\n  addAliases(origin);\n  for (const raw of configuredOrigins.split(\",\")) {\n    const trimmed = raw.trim();\n    if (!trimmed) continue;\n    const normalized = normalizeOrigin(trimmed);\n    origins.add(normalized);\n    addAliases(normalized);\n  }\n  return [...origins];\n}\n\nfunction isTwyneProductionOrigin(value: string): boolean {\n  try {\n    return TWYNE_PRODUCTION_ORIGINS.includes(\n      new URL(value).origin as (typeof TWYNE_PRODUCTION_ORIGINS)[number],\n    );\n  } catch {\n    return false;\n  }\n}\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"import { createClient, type GenericCtx } from \"@convex-dev/better-auth\";\nimport { convex, crossDomain } from \"@convex-dev/better-auth/plugins\";\nimport { components } from \"./_generated/api\";\nimport { betterAuth, type BetterAuthOptions } from \"better-auth/minimal\";\nimport { DataModel } from \"./_generated/dataModel\";\nimport authConfig from \"./auth.config.js\";\nimport { makeFunctionReference } from \"convex/server\";\nimport { notOrganicIssuer } from \"./lib/notorganic\";\nimport {\n  notOrganicSignIn,\n  redeemNotOrganicSignIn,\n} from \"./lib/notorganicSignIn\";\n\nconst siteUrl = normalizeOrigin(\n  process.env.SITE_URL ??\n    process.env.BETTER_AUTH_URL ??\n    \"http://localhost:5173\",\n);\nconst TWYNE_PRODUCTION_ORIGINS = [\n  \"https://twyne.love\",\n  \"https://www.twyne.love\",\n] as const;\nconst saveVerifiedLink = makeFunctionReference<\n  \"mutation\",\n  { did: string; subject: string; sessionVersion: number }\n>(\"providerIdentity:saveVerifiedLink\");\n\nconst authComponents = components as any;\n\nexport const authComponent = createClient<DataModel>(\n  authComponents.betterAuth,\n  {\n    verbose: false,\n  },\n);\n\nexport const createAuthOptions = (ctx: GenericCtx<DataModel>) =>\n  ({\n    baseURL: process.env.CONVEX_SITE_URL,\n    secret: process.env.BETTER_AUTH_SECRET,\n    trustedOrigins: trustedOrigins(siteUrl),\n    database: authComponent.adapter(ctx),\n    emailAndPassword: {\n      enabled: false,\n    },\n    session: {\n      cookieCache: {\n        enabled: true,\n        maxAge: 5 * 60,\n      },\n    },\n    plugins: [\n      notOrganicSignIn({\n        // The browser's origin is the PKCE client_id; it must be one Twyne\n        // trusts (twyne.love and www.twyne.love are separate client ids).\n        redeem: ({ code, verifier, origin }) => {\n          if (!trustedOrigins(siteUrl).includes(origin)) {\n            throw new Error(\"This sign-in came from an untrusted origin.\");\n          }\n          return redeemNotOrganicSignIn(\n            { code, verifier },\n            origin,\n            notOrganicIssuer(),\n          );\n        },\n        onSignedIn: async ({ did, userId, sessionVersion }) => {\n          if (!(\"runMutation\" in ctx)) {\n            throw new Error(\"Not Organic sign-in needs a mutation context.\");\n          }\n          await ctx.runMutation(saveVerifiedLink, {\n            did,\n            subject: userId,\n            sessionVersion,\n          });\n        },\n      }),\n      crossDomain({ siteUrl }),\n      convex({ authConfig }),\n    ],\n  }) satisfies BetterAuthOptions;\n\nexport const createAuth = (ctx: GenericCtx<DataModel>) =>\n  betterAuth(createAuthOptions(ctx));\n\nfunction normalizeOrigin(value: string): string {\n  const url = new URL(value);\n  if (\n    ![\"http:\", \"https:\"].includes(url.protocol) ||\n    url.username ||\n    url.password ||\n    url.hostname.includes(\"*\")\n  ) {\n    throw new Error(\"Twyne auth needs an exact HTTP(S) origin.\");\n  }\n  return url.origin;\n}\n\nfunction isLoopbackOrigin(value: string): boolean {\n  const host = new URL(value).hostname;\n  return (\n    host === \"localhost\" ||\n    host === \"127.0.0.1\" ||\n    host === \"::1\" ||\n    host === \"[::1]\"\n  );\n}\n\nexport function trustedOrigins(\n  origin: string,\n  configuredOrigins = process.env.TRUSTED_ORIGINS ?? \"\",\n): string[] {\n  const origins = new Set<string>([origin]);\n  const addAliases = (value: string) => {\n    if (isLoopbackOrigin(value)) {\n      const url = new URL(value);\n      const port = url.port ? `:${url.port}` : \"\";\n      for (const host of [\"localhost\", \"127.0.0.1\", \"[::1]\"]) {\n        origins.add(`${url.protocol}//${host}${port}`);\n      }\n    }\n    if (isTwyneProductionOrigin(value)) {\n      for (const prodOrigin of TWYNE_PRODUCTION_ORIGINS)\n        origins.add(prodOrigin);\n    }\n  };\n  addAliases(origin);\n  for (const raw of configuredOrigins.split(\",\")) {\n    const trimmed = raw.trim();\n    if (!trimmed) continue;\n    const normalized = normalizeOrigin(trimmed);\n    origins.add(normalized);\n    addAliases(normalized);\n  }\n  return [...origins];\n}\n\nfunction isTwyneProductionOrigin(value: string): boolean {\n  try {\n    return TWYNE_PRODUCTION_ORIGINS.includes(\n      new URL(value).origin as (typeof TWYNE_PRODUCTION_ORIGINS)[number],\n    );\n  } catch {\n    return false;\n  }\n}\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":11590},"formatted_output":"import { createClient, type GenericCtx } from \"@convex-dev/better-auth\";\nimport { convex, crossDomain } from \"@convex-dev/better-auth/plugins\";\nimport { components } from \"./_generated/api\";\nimport { betterAuth, type BetterAuthOptions } from \"better-auth/minimal\";\nimport { DataModel } from \"./_generated/dataModel\";\nimport authConfig from \"./auth.config.js\";\nimport { makeFunctionReference } from \"convex/server\";\nimport { notOrganicIssuer } from \"./lib/notorganic\";\nimport {\n  notOrganicSignIn,\n  redeemNotOrganicSignIn,\n} from \"./lib/notorganicSignIn\";\n\nconst siteUrl = normalizeOrigin(\n  process.env.SITE_URL ??\n    process.env.BETTER_AUTH_URL ??\n    \"http://localhost:5173\",\n);\nconst TWYNE_PRODUCTION_ORIGINS = [\n  \"https://twyne.love\",\n  \"https://www.twyne.love\",\n] as const;\nconst saveVerifiedLink = makeFunctionReference<\n  \"mutation\",\n  { did: string; subject: string; sessionVersion: number }\n>(\"providerIdentity:saveVerifiedLink\");\n\nconst authComponents = components as any;\n\nexport const authComponent = createClient<DataModel>(\n  authComponents.betterAuth,\n  {\n    verbose: false,\n  },\n);\n\nexport const createAuthOptions = (ctx: GenericCtx<DataModel>) =>\n  ({\n    baseURL: process.env.CONVEX_SITE_URL,\n    secret: process.env.BETTER_AUTH_SECRET,\n    trustedOrigins: trustedOrigins(siteUrl),\n    database: authComponent.adapter(ctx),\n    emailAndPassword: {\n      enabled: false,\n    },\n    session: {\n      cookieCache: {\n        enabled: true,\n        maxAge: 5 * 60,\n      },\n    },\n    plugins: [\n      notOrganicSignIn({\n        // The browser's origin is the PKCE client_id; it must be one Twyne\n        // trusts (twyne.love and www.twyne.love are separate client ids).\n        redeem: ({ code, verifier, origin }) => {\n          if (!trustedOrigins(siteUrl).includes(origin)) {\n            throw new Error(\"This sign-in came from an untrusted origin.\");\n          }\n          return redeemNotOrganicSignIn(\n            { code, verifier },\n            origin,\n            notOrganicIssuer(),\n          );\n        },\n        onSignedIn: async ({ did, userId, sessionVersion }) => {\n          if (!(\"runMutation\" in ctx)) {\n            throw new Error(\"Not Organic sign-in needs a mutation context.\");\n          }\n          await ctx.runMutation(saveVerifiedLink, {\n            did,\n            subject: userId,\n            sessionVersion,\n          });\n        },\n      }),\n      crossDomain({ siteUrl }),\n      convex({ authConfig }),\n    ],\n  }) satisfies BetterAuthOptions;\n\nexport const createAuth = (ctx: GenericCtx<DataModel>) =>\n  betterAuth(createAuthOptions(ctx));\n\nfunction normalizeOrigin(value: string): string {\n  const url = new URL(value);\n  if (\n    ![\"http:\", \"https:\"].includes(url.protocol) ||\n    url.username ||\n    url.password ||\n    url.hostname.includes(\"*\")\n  ) {\n    throw new Error(\"Twyne auth needs an exact HTTP(S) origin.\");\n  }\n  return url.origin;\n}\n\nfunction isLoopbackOrigin(value: string): boolean {\n  const host = new URL(value).hostname;\n  return (\n    host === \"localhost\" ||\n    host === \"127.0.0.1\" ||\n    host === \"::1\" ||\n    host === \"[::1]\"\n  );\n}\n\nexport function trustedOrigins(\n  origin: string,\n  configuredOrigins = process.env.TRUSTED_ORIGINS ?? \"\",\n): string[] {\n  const origins = new Set<string>([origin]);\n  const addAliases = (value: string) => {\n    if (isLoopbackOrigin(value)) {\n      const url = new URL(value);\n      const port = url.port ? `:${url.port}` : \"\";\n      for (const host of [\"localhost\", \"127.0.0.1\", \"[::1]\"]) {\n        origins.add(`${url.protocol}//${host}${port}`);\n      }\n    }\n    if (isTwyneProductionOrigin(value)) {\n      for (const prodOrigin of TWYNE_PRODUCTION_ORIGINS)\n        origins.add(prodOrigin);\n    }\n  };\n  addAliases(origin);\n  for (const raw of configuredOrigins.split(\",\")) {\n    const trimmed = raw.trim();\n    if (!trimmed) continue;\n    const normalized = normalizeOrigin(trimmed);\n    origins.add(normalized);\n    addAliases(normalized);\n  }\n  return [...origins];\n}\n\nfunction isTwyneProductionOrigin(value: string): boolean {\n  try {\n    return TWYNE_PRODUCTION_ORIGINS.includes(\n      new URL(value).origin as (typeof TWYNE_PRODUCTION_ORIGINS)[number],\n    );\n  } catch {\n    return false;\n  }\n}\n"},"started_at_ms":1791212819803,"completed_at_ms":1791212819803}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-05T15:06:59.837Z","ordinal":41906,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a10537-909f-77a3-96d8-dd07161f91ae","turn_id":"01a10c99-5363-7262-baff-cdf89af89903","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-ac610eb3-b231-4881-994d-3f6f781bcc8c","process_id":"18414","command":["/bin/bash","-lc","rtk proxy sed -n '1,165p' src/utils/auth-client.ts"],"cwd":"file:///home/diogenes/Projects/twyne","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"rtk proxy sed -n '1,165p' src/utils/auth-client.ts"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"import { createAuthClient } from \"better-auth/client\";\nimport {\n  convexClient,\n  crossDomainClient,\n} from \"@convex-dev/better-auth/client/plugins\";\nimport { isDev } from \"@qwik.dev/core/build\";\n\nconst convexSiteUrl = import.meta.env.VITE_CONVEX_SITE_URL as\n  | string\n  | undefined;\n\n/* ── Dev-mode passthrough ──\n * In local dev the Convex backend isn't wired up. Return a no-op client so\n * auth never blocks any UI or throws network errors. */\nconst mockClient = {\n  useSession: {\n    get: () => ({ data: null, isPending: false }),\n    subscribe: () => () => {},\n  },\n  signOut: async () => {},\n} as any;\n\nexport const authClient =\n  isDev && !convexSiteUrl\n    ? mockClient\n    : createAuthClient({\n        baseURL: convexSiteUrl,\n        plugins: [\n          // `crossDomainClient()` ships a `getActions` signature that\n          // drifts from the `BetterAuthClientPlugin` constraint in this\n          // better-auth version. The runtime contract is fine; suppress\n          // the structural-typing noise.\n          crossDomainClient() as any,\n          convexClient(),\n        ],\n      });\n\nexport const { signOut, useSession } = authClient;\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"import { createAuthClient } from \"better-auth/client\";\nimport {\n  convexClient,\n  crossDomainClient,\n} from \"@convex-dev/better-auth/client/plugins\";\nimport { isDev } from \"@qwik.dev/core/build\";\n\nconst convexSiteUrl = import.meta.env.VITE_CONVEX_SITE_URL as\n  | string\n  | undefined;\n\n/* ── Dev-mode passthrough ──\n * In local dev the Convex backend isn't wired up. Return a no-op client so\n * auth never blocks any UI or throws network errors. */\nconst mockClient = {\n  useSession: {\n    get: () => ({ data: null, isPending: false }),\n    subscribe: () => () => {},\n  },\n  signOut: async () => {},\n} as any;\n\nexport const authClient =\n  isDev && !convexSiteUrl\n    ? mockClient\n    : createAuthClient({\n        baseURL: convexSiteUrl,\n        plugins: [\n          // `crossDomainClient()` ships a `getActions` signature that\n          // drifts from the `BetterAuthClientPlugin` constraint in this\n          // better-auth version. The runtime contract is fine; suppress\n          // the structural-typing noise.\n          crossDomainClient() as any,\n          convexClient(),\n        ],\n      });\n\nexport const { signOut, useSession } = authClient;\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":14241},"formatted_output":"import { createAuthClient } from \"better-auth/client\";\nimport {\n  convexClient,\n  crossDomainClient,\n} from \"@convex-dev/better-auth/client/plugins\";\nimport { isDev } from \"@qwik.dev/core/build\";\n\nconst convexSiteUrl = import.meta.env.VITE_CONVEX_SITE_URL as\n  | string\n  | undefined;\n\n/* ── Dev-mode passthrough ──\n * In local dev the Convex backend isn't wired up. Return a no-op client so\n * auth never blocks any UI or throws network errors. */\nconst mockClient = {\n  useSession: {\n    get: () => ({ data: null, isPending: false }),\n    subscribe: () => () => {},\n  },\n  signOut: async () => {},\n} as any;\n\nexport const authClient =\n  isDev && !convexSiteUrl\n    ? mockClient\n    : createAuthClient({\n        baseURL: convexSiteUrl,\n        plugins: [\n          // `crossDomainClient()` ships a `getActions` signature that\n          // drifts from the `BetterAuthClientPlugin` constraint in this\n          // better-auth version. The runtime contract is fine; suppress\n          // the structural-typing noise.\n          crossDomainClient() as any,\n          convexClient(),\n        ],\n      });\n\nexport const { signOut, useSession } = authClient;\n"},"started_at_ms":1791212819837,"completed_at_ms":1791212819837}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-05T15:06:59.921Z","ordinal":41907,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a10c9a-95d1-7c50-a67b-73403a64fb01","call_id":"call_63m7FkCz6NxLoE6yGUE6xKJl","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.3 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"task\":0,\"status\":\"fulfilled\",\"value\":{\"chunk_id\":\"3f837b\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000014938,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":742,\"output\":\"[package]\\nname = \\\"twyne-desktop\\\"\\nversion = \\\"0.1.0\\\"\\nedition = \\\"2024\\\"\\nrust-version = \\\"1.92\\\"\\ndescription = \\\"Twyne's native, offline writing room, built with GPUI\\\"\\npublish = false\\n\\n[features]\\ndefault = [\\\"desktop\\\"]\\ndesktop = [\\\"dep:gpui-kit\\\", \\\"dep:image\\\", \\\"dep:roxmltree\\\", \\\"dep:base64\\\", \\\"dep:hypher\\\", \\\"dep:unicode-linebreak\\\", \\\"dep:x11rb\\\", \\\"dep:gpui-linux\\\", \\\"native-typst\\\"]\\nnative-typst = [\\\"dep:typst\\\", \\\"dep:typst-pdf\\\", \\\"dep:typst-svg\\\", \\\"dep:sha2\\\", \\\"dep:image\\\"]\\nnative-audio = [\\\"dep:sha2\\\"]\\nui-tests = [\\\"desktop\\\", \\\"gpui-kit/test-support\\\", \\\"gpui-linux?/test-support\\\"]\\n\\n[dependencies]\\nanyhow = \\\"1.0\\\"\\ndirectories = \\\"6.0\\\"\\nfs2 = \\\"0.4\\\"\\ngpui-kit = { version = \\\"=0.7.0\\\", optional = true }\\nchrono = \\\"=0.4.45\\\"\\nhtml5ever = \\\"=0.27.0\\\"\\nunicode-segmentation = \\\"=1.13.3\\\"\\nmarkup5ever_rcdom = \\\"=0.3.0\\\"\\nimage = { version = \\\"=0.25.10\\\", default-features = false, features = [\\\"png\\\", \\\"webp\\\", \\\"jpeg\\\", \\\"gif\\\"], optional = true }\\nroxmltree = { version = \\\"=0.20.0\\\", optional = true }\\nbase64 = { version = \\\"=0.22.1\\\", optional = true }\\nhypher = { version = \\\"=0.1.8\\\", default-features = false, features = [\\\"alloc\\\", \\\"english\\\"], optional = true }\\nunicode-linebreak = { version = \\\"=0.1.5\\\", optional = true }\\nserde = { version = \\\"1.0\\\", features = [\\\"derive\\\", \\\"rc\\\"] }\\nserde_json = \\\"1.0\\\"\\nregex = \\\"=1.13.1\\\"\\nunicode-normalization = \\\"=0.1.25\\\"\\nurl = \\\"=2.5.8\\\"\\ntempfile = \\\"3.23\\\"\\nuuid = { version = \\\"1.18\\\", features = [\\\"v4\\\", \\\"serde\\\"] }\\nsha2 = { version = \\\"=0.10.9\\\", optional = true }\\ntypst = { git = \\\"https://github.com/Myriad-Dreamin/typst.git\\\", rev = \\\"951788cc614cd805d5d786e17bbf93796df73d10\\\", optional = true }\\ntypst-pdf = { git = \\\"https://github.com/Myriad-Dreamin/typst.git\\\", rev = \\\"951788cc614cd805d5d786e17bbf93796df73d10\\\", optional = true }\\ntypst-svg = { git = \\\"https://github.com/Myriad-Dreamin/typst.git\\\", rev = \\\"951788cc614cd805d5d786e17bbf93796df73d10\\\", optional = true }\\n\\n[target.'cfg(target_os = \\\"linux\\\")'.dependencies]\\nx11rb = { version = \\\"=0.13.2\\\", optional = true }\\ngpui-linux = { package = \\\"gpui-pre-linux\\\", version = \\\"=0.3.7\\\", default-features = false, features = [\\\"wayland\\\"], optional = true }\\n\\n[[bin]]\\nname = \\\"twyne-desktop\\\"\\npath = \\\"src/main.rs\\\"\\nrequired-features = [\\\"desktop\\\"]\\n\\n[[example]]\\nname = \\\"twyne-clipboard-probe\\\"\\npath = \\\"fixtures/editor/clipboard-probe.rs\\\"\\nrequired-features = [\\\"desktop\\\"]\\n\\n[[example]]\\nname = \\\"twyne-wayland-clipboard-probe\\\"\\npath = \\\"fixtures/wayland-clipboard/native-probe.rs\\\"\\nrequired-features = [\\\"desktop\\\"]\\n\\n[[example]]\\nname = \\\"twyne-dossier-multiply-probe\\\"\\npath = \\\"fixtures/dossier-multiply/native-probe/main.rs\\\"\\nrequired-features = [\\\"ui-tests\\\"]\\n\\n[[test]]\\nname = \\\"native-audio-contract\\\"\\npath = \\\"fixtures/native-audio/synthetic_loopback.rs\\\"\\nrequired-features = [\\\"native-audio\\\"]\\n\\n[profile.dev]\\ndebug = 0\\n\\n[patch.crates-io]\\ngpui-base = { path = \\\"vendor/gpui-base\\\" }\\ngpui-pre = { path = \\\"vendor/gpui-pre\\\" }\\ngpui-pre-wgpu = { path = \\\"vendor/gpui-pre-wgpu\\\" }\\ngpui-pre-linux = { path = \\\"vendor/gpui-pre-linux\\\" }\\n\\n[profile.release]\\nlto = \\\"thin\\\"\\ncodegen-units = 1\\nstrip = true\\n\"}}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"task\":1,\"status\":\"fulfilled\",\"value\":{\"chunk_id\":\"509580\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000029117,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":1876,\"output\":\"//! Unconnected coordinator with bounded, generation-qualified request tickets.\\n//! Host result adoption still requires its own current entity/scope/revision CAS.\\nuse super::{\\n    litert_lifecycle::{LiteRtConfig, LiteRtError, LiteRtProcessManager, LiteRtState},\\n    loopback_transport::{AiError, CompletionResult, LoopbackClient, validate_request},\\n    provider_types::{\\n        AiFeature, AiProviderType, AiSettingsRecord, ResolvedFeatureConfig, resolve_feature_config,\\n        resolve_feature_config_for_persona,\\n    },\\n    request::{AiRequestId, CancellationToken, CompletionRequest, RevisionIdentity},\\n    stream_accumulator::GenerationStreamSnapshot,\\n};\\nuse std::{\\n    collections::{HashMap, VecDeque},\\n    sync::Mutex,\\n};\\nuse uuid::Uuid;\\n\\npub const MAX_IN_FLIGHT: usize = 4;\\npub const MAX_TERMINAL_TICKETS: usize = 64;\\n\\n#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Eq)]\\npub struct RequestTicket {\\n    pub request_id: AiRequestId,\\n    nonce: Uuid,\\n    epoch: Uuid,\\n    revision: Option<RevisionIdentity>,\\n}\\n#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, PartialEq, Eq)]\\npub enum RequestTerminal {\\n    SucceededSynthetic,\\n    Failed,\\n    Cancelled,\\n    Stale,\\n}\\nstruct InFlightEntry {\\n    ticket: RequestTicket,\\n    cancel: CancellationToken,\\n}\\nstruct Registry {\\n    epoch: Uuid,\\n    active: Option<RevisionIdentity>,\\n    in_flight: HashMap<AiRequestId, InFlightEntry>,\\n    terminal: VecDeque<(RequestTicket, RequestTerminal)>,\\n}\\nimpl Registry {\\n    fn current(&self, ticket: &RequestTicket) -> bool {\\n        self.epoch == ticket.epoch && self.active == ticket.revision\\n    }\\n    fn invalidate(&mut self) {\\n        self.epoch = Uuid::new_v4();\\n        let entries = self\\n            .in_flight\\n            .drain()\\n            .map(|(_, entry)| entry)\\n            .collect::<Vec<_>>();\\n        for entry in entries {\\n            entry.cancel.cancel();\\n            self.remember(entry.ticket, RequestTerminal::Stale);\\n        }\\n    }\\n    fn remember(&mut self, ticket: RequestTicket, state: RequestTerminal) {\\n        self.terminal.push_back((ticket, state));\\n        while self.terminal.len() > MAX_TERMINAL_TICKETS {\\n            self.terminal.pop_front();\\n        }\\n    }\\n}\\n\\npub struct NativeAiCoordinator {\\n    litert_manager: LiteRtProcessManager,\\n    settings: AiSettingsRecord,\\n    registry: Mutex<Registry>,\\n}\\n/// A synthetic result carrying the exact ticket needed for a later adoption guard.\\n#[derive(Clone, Debug)]\\npub struct GuardedCompletion {\\n    pub ticket: RequestTicket,\\n    pub result: CompletionResult,\\n}\\n\\nimpl NativeAiCoordinator {\\n    pub fn new(config: LiteRtConfig, settings: AiSettingsRecord) -> Self {\\n        Self {\\n            litert_manager: LiteRtProcessManager::new(config),\\n            settings,\\n            registry: Mutex::new(Registry {\\n                epoch: Uuid::new_v4(),\\n                active: None,\\n                in_flight: HashMap::new(),\\n                terminal: VecDeque::new(),\\n            }),\\n        }\\n    }\\n    pub fn litert_manager(&self) -> &LiteRtProcessManager {\\n        &self.litert_manager\\n    }\\n    pub fn litert_manager_mut(&mut self) -> &mut LiteRtProcessManager {\\n        &mut self.litert_manager\\n    }\\n    pub fn litert_state(&self) -> &LiteRtState {\\n        self.litert_manager.state()\\n    }\\n    pub fn is_local_ai_ready(&self) -> bool {\\n        self.litert_manager.is_ready()\\n    }\\n    pub fn start_local_ai(&mut self) -> Result<Option<String>, LiteRtError> {\\n        self.litert_manager.start()\\n    }\\n    pub fn stop_local_ai(&mut self) {\\n        if let Ok(mut registry) = self.registry.lock() {\\n            registry.invalidate();\\n        }\\n        self.litert_manager.stop();\\n    }\\n    pub fn update_settings(&mut self, settings: AiSettingsRecord) {\\n        if self.settings != settings {\\n            if let Ok(mut registry) = self.registry.lock() {\\n                registry.invalidate();\\n            }\\n            self.settings = settings;\\n        }\\n    }\\n    pub fn settings(&self) -> &AiSettingsRecord {\\n        &self.settings\\n    }\\n    pub fn resolve_feature(&self, feature: &AiFeature) -> Option<ResolvedFeatureConfig> {\\n        resolve_feature_config(&self.settings, feature)\\n    }\\n    pub fn resolve_feature_for_persona(\\n        &self,\\n        feature: &AiFeature,\\n        id: Option<&str>,\\n        model: Option<&str>,\\n        temperature: Option<f64>,\\n    ) -> Option<ResolvedFeatureConfig> {\\n        resolve_feature_config_for_persona(&self.settings, feature, id, model, temperature)\\n    }\\n    /// Constant-size host context boundary, never manuscript serialization.\\n    /// Revisit/settings changes invalidate old tickets even if the folio/gen returns.\\n    pub fn set_active_revision(&self, revision: Option<RevisionIdentity>) -> Result<(), AiError> {\\n        let mut registry = self.registry.lock().map_err(|_| AiError::StaleRequest)?;\\n        if registry.active != revision {\\n            registry.invalidate();\\n            registry.active = revision;\\n        }\\n        Ok(())\\n    }\\n    pub fn begin_request(&self, req: &CompletionRequest) -> Result<RequestTicket, AiError> {\\n        validate_request(req)?;\\n        let mut registry = self.registry.lock().map_err(|_| AiError::StaleRequest)?;\\n        if req.revision.is_none() || registry.active != req.revision {\\n            return Err(AiError::StaleRequest);\\n        }\\n        if registry.in_flight.contains_key(&req.request_id)\\n            || registry\\n                .terminal\\n                .iter()\\n                .any(|(t, _)| t.request_id == req.request_id)\\n        {\\n            return Err(AiError::DuplicateRequest);\\n        }\\n        if registry.in_flight.len() >= MAX_IN_FLIGHT {\\n            return Err(AiError::QueueFull);\\n        }\\n        let ticket = RequestTicket {\\n            request_id: req.request_id.clone(),\\n            nonce: Uuid::new_v4(),\\n            epoch: registry.epoch,\\n            revision: req.revision.clone(),\\n        };\\n        registry.in_flight.insert(\\n            req.request_id.clone(),\\n            InFlightEntry {\\n                ticket: ticket.clone(),\\n                cancel: req.cancel_token.clone(),\\n            },\\n        );\\n        Ok(ticket)\\n    }\\n    pub fn accepts_snapshot(&self, ticket: &RequestTicket) -> bool {\\n        self.registry.lock().ok().is_some_and(|registry| {\\n            registry.current(ticket)\\n                && registry\\n                    .in_flight\\n                    .get(&ticket.request_id)\\n                    .is_some_and(|entry| entry.ticket == *ticket && !entry.cancel.is_cancelled())\\n        })\\n    }\\n    /// Exact ticket match prevents an old completion/unwind from unregistering\\n    /// a replacement request. Terminal transition is accepted once only.\\n    pub fn finish_request(\\n        &self,\\n        ticket: &RequestTicket,\\n        outcome: RequestTerminal,\\n    ) -> Result<(), AiError> {\\n        let mut registry = self.registry.lock().map_err(|_| AiError::StaleRequest)?;\\n        let entry = registry\\n            .in_flight\\n            .get(&ticket.request_id)\\n            .ok_or(AiError::StaleRequest)?;\\n        if entry.ticket != *ticket {\\n            return Err(AiError::StaleRequest);\\n        }\\n        let state = if !registry.current(ticket) {\\n            RequestTerminal::Stale\\n        } else if entry.cancel.is_cancelled() {\\n            RequestTerminal::Cancelled\\n        } else {\\n            outcome\\n        };\\n        registry.in_flight.remove(&ticket.request_id);\\n        registry.remember(ticket.clone(), state);\\n        match state {\\n            RequestTerminal::Stale => Err(AiError::StaleRequest),\\n\"}}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"task\":2,\"status\":\"fulfilled\",\"value\":{\"chunk_id\":\"e285e2\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000014241,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":290,\"output\":\"import { createAuthClient } from \\\"better-auth/client\\\";\\nimport {\\n  convexClient,\\n  crossDomainClient,\\n} from \\\"@convex-dev/better-auth/client/plugins\\\";\\nimport { isDev } from \\\"@qwik.dev/core/build\\\";\\n\\nconst convexSiteUrl = import.meta.env.VITE_CONVEX_SITE_URL as\\n  | string\\n  | undefined;\\n\\n/* ── Dev-mode passthrough ──\\n * In local dev the Convex backend isn't wired up. Return a no-op client so\\n * auth never blocks any UI or throws network errors. */\\nconst mockClient = {\\n  useSession: {\\n    get: () => ({ data: null, isPending: false }),\\n    subscribe: () => () => {},\\n  },\\n  signOut: async () => {},\\n} as any;\\n\\nexport const authClient =\\n  isDev && !convexSiteUrl\\n    ? mockClient\\n    : createAuthClient({\\n        baseURL: convexSiteUrl,\\n        plugins: [\\n          // `crossDomainClient()` ships a `getActions` signature that\\n          // drifts from the `BetterAuthClientPlugin` constraint in this\\n          // better-auth version. The runtime contract is fine; suppress\\n          // the structural-typing noise.\\n          crossDomainClient() as any,\\n          convexClient(),\\n        ],\\n      });\\n\\nexport const { signOut, useSession } = authClient;\\n\"}}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"task\":3,\"status\":\"fulfilled\",\"value\":{\"chunk_id\":\"a39c9a\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.00001159,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":1055,\"output\":\"import { createClient, type GenericCtx } from \\\"@convex-dev/better-auth\\\";\\nimport { convex, crossDomain } from \\\"@convex-dev/better-auth/plugins\\\";\\nimport { components } from \\\"./_generated/api\\\";\\nimport { betterAuth, type BetterAuthOptions } from \\\"better-auth/minimal\\\";\\nimport { DataModel } from \\\"./_generated/dataModel\\\";\\nimport authConfig from \\\"./auth.config.js\\\";\\nimport { makeFunctionReference } from \\\"convex/server\\\";\\nimport { notOrganicIssuer } from \\\"./lib/notorganic\\\";\\nimport {\\n  notOrganicSignIn,\\n  redeemNotOrganicSignIn,\\n} from \\\"./lib/notorganicSignIn\\\";\\n\\nconst siteUrl = normalizeOrigin(\\n  process.env.SITE_URL ??\\n    process.env.BETTER_AUTH_URL ??\\n    \\\"http://localhost:5173\\\",\\n);\\nconst TWYNE_PRODUCTION_ORIGINS = [\\n  \\\"https://twyne.love\\\",\\n  \\\"https://www.twyne.love\\\",\\n] as const;\\nconst saveVerifiedLink = makeFunctionReference<\\n  \\\"mutation\\\",\\n  { did: string; subject: string; sessionVersion: number }\\n>(\\\"providerIdentity:saveVerifiedLink\\\");\\n\\nconst authComponents = components as any;\\n\\nexport const authComponent = createClient<DataModel>(\\n  authComponents.betterAuth,\\n  {\\n    verbose: false,\\n  },\\n);\\n\\nexport const createAuthOptions = (ctx: GenericCtx<DataModel>) =>\\n  ({\\n    baseURL: process.env.CONVEX_SITE_URL,\\n    secret: process.env.BETTER_AUTH_SECRET,\\n    trustedOrigins: trustedOrigins(siteUrl),\\n    database: authComponent.adapter(ctx),\\n    emailAndPassword: {\\n      enabled: false,\\n    },\\n    session: {\\n      cookieCache: {\\n        enabled: true,\\n        maxAge: 5 * 60,\\n      },\\n    },\\n    plugins: [\\n      notOrganicSignIn({\\n        // The browser's origin is the PKCE client_id; it must be one Twyne\\n        // trusts (twyne.love and www.twyne.love are separate client ids).\\n        redeem: ({ code, verifier, origin }) => {\\n          if (!trustedOrigins(siteUrl).includes(origin)) {\\n            throw new Error(\\\"This sign-in came from an untrusted origin.\\\");\\n          }\\n          return redeemNotOrganicSignIn(\\n            { code, verifier },\\n            origin,\\n            notOrganicIssuer(),\\n          );\\n        },\\n        onSignedIn: async ({ did, userId, sessionVersion }) => {\\n          if (!(\\\"runMutation\\\" in ctx)) {\\n            throw new Error(\\\"Not Organic sign-in needs a mutation context.\\\");\\n          }\\n          await ctx.runMutation(saveVerifiedLink, {\\n            did,\\n            subject: userId,\\n            sessionVersion,\\n          });\\n        },\\n      }),\\n      crossDomain({ siteUrl }),\\n      convex({ authConfig }),\\n    ],\\n  }) satisfies BetterAuthOptions;\\n\\nexport const createAuth = (ctx: GenericCtx<DataModel>) =>\\n  betterAuth(createAuthOptions(ctx));\\n\\nfunction normalizeOrigin(value: string): string {\\n  const url = new URL(value);\\n  if (\\n    ![\\\"http:\\\", \\\"https:\\\"].includes(url.protocol) ||\\n    url.username ||\\n    url.password ||\\n    url.hostname.includes(\\\"*\\\")\\n  ) {\\n    throw new Error(\\\"Twyne auth needs an exact HTTP(S) origin.\\\");\\n  }\\n  return url.origin;\\n}\\n\\nfunction isLoopbackOrigin(value: string): boolean {\\n  const host = new URL(value).hostname;\\n  return (\\n    host === \\\"localhost\\\" ||\\n    host === \\\"127.0.0.1\\\" ||\\n    host === \\\"::1\\\" ||\\n    host === \\\"[::1]\\\"\\n  );\\n}\\n\\nexport function trustedOrigins(\\n  origin: string,\\n  configuredOrigins = process.env.TRUSTED_ORIGINS ?? \\\"\\\",\\n): string[] {\\n  const origins = new Set<string>([origin]);\\n  const addAliases = (value: string) => {\\n    if (isLoopbackOrigin(value)) {\\n      const url = new URL(value);\\n      const port = url.port ? `:${url.port}` : \\\"\\\";\\n      for (const host of [\\\"localhost\\\", \\\"127.0.0.1\\\", \\\"[::1]\\\"]) {\\n        origins.add(`${url.protocol}//${host}${port}`);\\n      }\\n    }\\n    if (isTwyneProductionOrigin(value)) {\\n      for (const prodOrigin of TWYNE_PRODUCTION_ORIGINS)\\n        origins.add(prodOrigin);\\n    }\\n  };\\n  addAliases(origin);\\n  for (const raw of configuredOrigins.split(\\\",\\\")) {\\n    const trimmed = raw.trim();\\n    if (!trimmed) continue;\\n    const normalized = normalizeOrigin(trimmed);\\n    origins.add(normalized);\\n    addAliases(normalized);\\n  }\\n  return [...origins];\\n}\\n\\nfunction isTwyneProductionOrigin(value: string): boolean {\\n  try {\\n    return TWYNE_PRODUCTION_ORIGINS.includes(\\n      new URL(value).origin as (typeof TWYNE_PRODUCTION_ORIGINS)[number],\\n    );\\n  } catch {\\n    return false;\\n  }\\n}\\n\"}}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"task\":4,\"status\":\"fulfilled\",\"value\":{\"chunk_id\":\"f375b7\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000022485,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":1086,\"output\":\"- Public client scopes are explicitly allowlisted in `apps/portal/server/public-client.ts`; gateway authorization checks the granted capability before dispatch.\\n- Google Drive research identified `drive.file` plus Google Picker as the narrow initial scope pattern; full Drive access was not implemented.\\n\\nReferences:\\n- Provider cwd: `/home/diogenes/Projects/notorganic-provider`\\n- Main portal files: `apps/portal/server/routes.ts`, `apps/portal/server/store.ts`, `apps/portal/src/api.ts`, `apps/portal/src/App.tsx`, `apps/portal/src/views/Integrations.tsx`\\n- Security files: `apps/portal/server/public-client.ts`, `apps/portal/server/authorization-page.ts`, `apps/gateway/src/auth.ts`, `packages/contracts/src/catalog.ts`, `packages/contracts/src/claims.ts`\\n- Documentation artifact: `docs/knowledge-connections.md`\\n\\n## Task 2: Keating shared knowledge integration\\n\\nOutcome: partial\\n\\nKey steps:\\n- Added account-source selection near the model selector and in Models & Providers settings.\\n- Added resource browsing/reading, explicit separate tool opt-in, exact-argument review before remote calls, and fail-closed behavior for cancellation, account changes, revocation, changed tool definitions, and failed calls.\\n- Added explicit OAuth scope upgrade behavior that preserves existing permissions; DPoP account/selection checks occur immediately before dispatch.\\n- Added Google Drive as “Coming soon,” not as a working connector.\\n- Validation: 53 focused tests and 260 assertions passed; browser QA covered reading, cancellation with zero dispatches, exact approved payload, lost-network uncertain-action behavior, and mobile dialog layout. Keating Android export/typecheck passed, but full web typecheck/build remained blocked by pre-existing assistant-ui/PDF/router incompatibilities.\\n\\nReusable knowledge:\\n- Keating’s implementation files include `web/src/notorganic-provider/knowledge.ts`, `web/src/keating/browser-tools/knowledge.ts`, `web/src/components/settings/KnowledgeSources.tsx`, and `web/src/test/knowledge.test.ts`.\\n- Do not claim Keating web production readiness from the focused checks: the full build remained blocked and no deployment or live-account verification occurred.\\n\\n## Task 3: Twyne shared knowledge integration\\n\\nOutcome: partial\\n\\nKey steps:\\n- Added trusted Convex actions using verified DID/sessionVersion and fresh Twyne DPoP tokens.\\n- Added account source selection, document browsing/reading, sharing handoff, explicit research/editor tool selection, exact reviewed arguments, cancellation, account-change clearing, revocation/schema-change failure handling, and preservation of local MCP integrations.\\n- Integrated the feature into Settings and Apparatus. Twyne research requires selecting the source, enabling research, choosing the search tool, and selecting “Your MCP servers” as the research provider.\\n- Validation: 98 targeted checks passed, including 6 authenticated Convex-action tests, 29 account-knowledge/MCP tests, and 63 adjacent regressions; application/Convex typechecks and client/server production builds passed. Browser QA used synthetic actions and covered browsing, reading, cancellation, approval, sign-out clearing, and mobile layout.\\n- Deployment of new Convex functions and real-account end-to-end gateway verification remained outstanding.\\n\\nFailures and how to do differently:\\n- A later Twyne browser reload hit `ERR_CONNECTION_REFUSED` after the owned preview process had stopped; do not treat that failed reconnect as a product regression.\\n- Twyne’s browser preview also showed expected local CORS failure when calling a deployed Convex endpoint from localhost. Real deployment configuration must be verified separately.\\n\\nReferences:\\n- Twyne implementation files include `convex/knowledge.ts`, `src/utils/account-knowledge.ts`, `src/components/knowledge/account-knowledge.tsx`, and `src/components/knowledge/account-tool-review.tsx`.\\n- Twyne integration points: `src/utils/auth-context.tsx`, `src/routes/settings/index.tsx`, and `src/routes/apparatus/index.tsx`.\\n- Final documentation: `docs/knowledge-connections.md`\\n\\nOverall status: feature implementation and focused validation succeeded across the affected apps, but the rollout is partial because Google Drive remains unimplemented, deployment was not performed, and real-account cross-app verification was not completed.\\n\"}}"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a10c99-5363-7262-baff-cdf89af89903","create_time":1791212819.921244}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
