{"timestamp":"2026-10-05T15:17:45.874Z","ordinal":41991,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a10ca4-7112-7d23-90ad-35a5cb96db78","call_id":"call_KKDCHRdzxm3L09S3TZZGn6rX","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.2 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"check\":0,\"chunk_id\":\"4c08bf\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000015011,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":1201,\"output\":\"# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/notorganic-provider shared account knowledge connections for Keating and Twyne\\nscope: Implement account-owned knowledge sources with app-specific grants, explicit tool consent, and fail-closed revocation across Not Organic, Keating, and Twyne.\\napplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/notorganic-provider with integrations in /home/diogenes/Projects/{keating,twyne}; reuse_rule=retest current provider contracts, dirty diffs, deployment/CORS, and a real account before claiming cross-app readiness.\\n\\n## Task 1: Establish provider-owned shared knowledge and app access\\n\\n### rollout_summary_files\\n\\n- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/notorganic-provider, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/10/03/rollout-2026-10-03T08-22-46-01a101b7-83a5-7863-897a-869bf3d11c1b.jsonl, updated_at=2026-10-03T23:33:08+00:00, thread_id=01a101b7-83a5-7863-897a-869bf3d11c1b, partial; implementation/focused validation passed, deployment and real-account proof open)\\n\\n### keywords\\n\\n- knowledge-bases, account-sources, Google Drive, OAuth, PKCE S256, DPoP, consent, revocation, apps/portal, apps/gateway, Convex, GitNexus\\n\\n## Task 2: Integrate reviewed knowledge tools in Keating\\n\\n### rollout_summary_files\\n\\n- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/notorganic-provider, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/10/03/rollout-2026-10-03T08-22-46-01a101b7-83a5-7863-897a-869bf3d11c1b.jsonl, updated_at=2026-10-03T23:33:08+00:00, thread_id=01a101b7-83a5-7863-897a-869bf3d11c1b, partial; 53 focused tests/260 assertions, full web build blocked)\\n\\n### keywords\\n\\n- web/src/notorganic-provider/knowledge.ts, KnowledgeSources.tsx, browser-tools/knowledge.ts, exact-argument review, Google Drive Coming soon, knowledge.test.ts\\n\\n## Task 3: Integrate account sources and MCP review in Twyne\\n\\n### rollout_summary_files\\n\\n- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/notorganic-provider, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/10/03/rollout-2026-10-03T08-22-46-01a101b7-83a5-7863-897a-869bf3d11c1b.jsonl, updated_at=2026-10-03T23:33:08+00:00, thread_id=01a101b7-83a5-7863-897a-869bf3d11c1b, partial; 98 targeted checks/typechecks/builds passed, live gateway proof open)\\n\\n### keywords\\n\\n- convex/knowledge.ts, account-knowledge.ts, account-tool-review.tsx, Settings, Apparatus, Your MCP servers, sessionVersion, DPoP, CORS\\n\\n## User preferences\\n\\n- when asking for knowledge bases to “carry over” into Keating and Twyne and be “easy to add or revoke an apps access to them” -> default to account-level ownership, per-app grants, explicit revocation, and guided setup [Task 1]\\n- when mentioning Google sign-in and easy connection setup -> include understandable consent/onboarding, not only API plumbing [Task 1]\\n\\n## Reusable knowledge\\n\\n- Not Organic is the control plane: portal sessions and upstream credentials stay server-owned; public clients validate HTTPS origins, same-origin callbacks, PKCE S256, narrow allowlisted scopes, and DPoP-bound tokens; gateway checks capabilities immediately before dispatch. [Task 1]\\n- Google Drive remains unimplemented. The narrow researched direction is Google Picker with `drive.file`, and product UI must label it “Coming soon,” never as an available connector. [Task 1][Task 2]\\n- Keating selects account sources, browses/reads resources, separately opts into tools, and reviews exact arguments; cancellation, account change, revocation, tool-definition change, and failed/lost-network calls fail closed. [Task 2]\\n- Twyne trusted Convex actions bind verified DID/sessionVersion to fresh DPoP tokens. Research requires enabling research, choosing a source search tool, and selecting “Your MCP servers”; sign-out, revocation, and schema changes clear/fail closed. [Task 3]\\n\\n## Failures and how to do differently\\n\\n- GitNexus `ENOENT: .../.gitnexus/registry-lock` -> run `node .gitnexus/run.cjs analyze --index-only`, but treat absent/truncated graph edges as unknown and confirm with `rg`/source. Preserve unrelated dirty provider work; aggregate impact reports are not feature-local evidence. [Task 1]\\n- Focused Keating validation does not prove web production readiness: pre-existing assistant-ui/PDF/router incompatibilities blocked the full web build, and neither deployment nor live-account flow was tested. [Task 2]\\n- `ERR_CONNECTION_REFUSED` after an owned Twyne preview stopped is an environment/process condition, while localhost-to-deployed Convex CORS preflight must be verified separately; neither establishes deployed feature behavior. [Task 3]\\n\\n\"}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"check\":1,\"chunk_id\":\"16e513\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000025061,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":182,\"output\":\"convex/knowledge.test.ts\\nconvex/knowledge.ts\\nconvex/auth.ts\\nconvex/auth.config.ts\\nconvex/lib/authIdentity.test.ts\\nconvex/lib/authIdentity.ts\\nsrc/components/knowledge/account-knowledge.tsx\\nsrc/components/auth/auth-panel.tsx\\nsrc/utils/lix-auth.ts\\nsrc/utils/account-knowledge.test.ts\\nsrc/utils/account-knowledge.ts\\nsrc/utils/auth-context.tsx\\nsrc/utils/auth-context.test.ts\\nsrc/utils/auth-client.ts\\nsrc/utils/auth-analytics.ts\\nsrc/utils/auth-analytics.test.ts\\ndesktop/gpui/src/native_accounts/auth.rs\\ndesktop/gpui/fixtures/math-write/native-source-form/sakana-key-decisions.json\\ndesktop/gpui/fixtures/math-write/native-source-form/sakana-key-review.json\\ndesktop/gpui/fixtures/dossier-layout-correction/authoring-input-history.json\\n\"}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"check\":2,\"chunk_id\":\"183492\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000012982,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":853,\"output\":\"        &self.return_to\\n    }\\n\\n    /// Fixture/router access only; state must remain tied to this attempt.\\n    pub fn state(&self) -> &str {\\n        &self.state\\n    }\\n}\\n\\n#[derive(Clone, Debug, Deserialize, Serialize, PartialEq, Eq)]\\n#[serde(rename_all = \\\"camelCase\\\")]\\npub struct AccountIdentity {\\n    pub issuer: String,\\n    pub subject: String,\\n    pub token_identifier: String,\\n}\\n\\nimpl AccountIdentity {\\n    /// Consistency validation only. Values must originate in a separately\\n    /// authenticated transport/JWT callback, not text fields or decoded claims.\\n    pub fn validate(&self) -> Result<()> {\\n        // Some configured issuers retain a trailing slash. Validate syntax while\\n        // preserving the exact original issuer in the canonical identifier.\\n        validate_origin(self.issuer.strip_suffix('/').unwrap_or(&self.issuer))?;\\n        ensure!(\\n            !self.subject.is_empty()\\n                && self.subject.len() <= 1024\\n                && !self.subject.chars().any(char::is_control),\\n            \\\"Invalid account subject.\\\"\\n        );\\n        ensure!(\\n            self.token_identifier == format!(\\\"{}|{}\\\", self.issuer, self.subject),\\n            \\\"The account identifier does not match its issuer and subject.\\\"\\n        );\\n        Ok(())\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn partition_id(&self) -> Result<String> {\\n        self.validate()?;\\n        Ok(format!(\\n            \\\"{:x}\\\",\\n            Sha256::digest(self.token_identifier.as_bytes())\\n        ))\\n    }\\n}\\n\\n/// This is a parsed consistency receipt, not a verified-authentication type.\\n#[derive(Clone, Debug)]\\npub struct SignInReceipt {\\n    pub issued_user_id: String,\\n    pub refreshed_user_id: String,\\n    pub session_user_id: String,\\n    pub session_id: String,\\n    pub redemption_error: bool,\\n    pub refresh_error: bool,\\n}\\n\\nimpl SignInReceipt {\\n    pub fn consistent_account(&self, trusted_issuer: &str) -> Result<AccountIdentity> {\\n        ensure!(\\n            !self.redemption_error\\n                && !self.refresh_error\\n                && !self.issued_user_id.is_empty()\\n                && !self.session_id.is_empty()\\n                && self.issued_user_id == self.refreshed_user_id\\n                && self.issued_user_id == self.session_user_id,\\n            \\\"Twyne could not confirm your session. Please sign in again.\\\"\\n        );\\n        let identity = AccountIdentity {\\n            issuer: trusted_issuer.to_owned(),\\n            subject: self.issued_user_id.clone(),\\n            token_identifier: format!(\\\"{trusted_issuer}|{}\\\", self.issued_user_id),\\n        };\\n        identity.validate()?;\\n        Ok(identity)\\n    }\\n}\\n\\n/// A unique operation-lifetime guard. Constructing it does not authenticate;\\n/// Root must create it only after its transport reports accepted Convex auth.\\n#[derive(Clone, Debug, Deserialize, Serialize, PartialEq, Eq)]\\n#[serde(rename_all = \\\"camelCase\\\")]\\npub struct SessionLease {\\n    pub account: AccountIdentity,\\n    pub id: Uuid,\\n}\\n\\nimpl SessionLease {\\n    pub fn new(account: AccountIdentity) -> Result<Self> {\\n        account.validate()?;\\n        Ok(Self {\\n            account,\\n            id: Uuid::new_v4(),\\n        })\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn require_current(&self, active: Option<&Self>, account: &AccountIdentity) -> Result<()> {\\n        ensure!(\\n            active == Some(self) && self.account == *account,\\n            \\\"The active account changed before this operation completed.\\\"\\n        );\\n        Ok(())\\n    }\\n}\\n\"}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"check\":3,\"chunk_id\":\"b97784\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000011302,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":1324,\"output\":\"#!/usr/bin/env python3\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"Isolated, advisory-only fugu-max job; never persist or print credentials.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\nimport argparse\\nimport hashlib\\nimport json\\nimport os\\nfrom pathlib import Path\\nimport sqlite3\\nimport subprocess\\nimport time\\nfrom urllib.parse import urlparse\\nimport uuid\\n\\n\\ndef sha(path):\\n    return hashlib.sha256(path.read_bytes()).hexdigest()\\n\\n\\nparser = argparse.ArgumentParser()\\nparser.add_argument(\\\"tag\\\")\\nparser.add_argument(\\\"bundle\\\", type=Path)\\nparser.add_argument(\\\"prompt\\\", type=Path)\\nargs = parser.parse_args()\\nbase = Path(__file__).resolve().parent\\nroot = base.parents[3]\\nassert args.tag.replace(\\\"-\\\", \\\"\\\").isalnum()\\nbundle = json.loads(args.bundle.read_text())\\nfor path, item in bundle.items():\\n    assert sha(root / path) == item[\\\"sha256\\\"], \\\"Delegation input drift: \\\" + path\\njob = base / (args.tag + \\\"-\\\" + uuid.uuid4().hex[:12])\\njob.mkdir(mode=0o700)\\nfor name in [\\\"config\\\", \\\"data\\\", \\\"skills\\\", \\\"workspace\\\"]:\\n    (job / name).mkdir(mode=0o700)\\n(job / \\\"input-bundle.json\\\").write_bytes(args.bundle.read_bytes())\\n(job / \\\"prompt.txt\\\").write_bytes(args.prompt.read_bytes())\\ntemplate = base / \\\"sakana-resize-guard-review-7c6186b386aa/config/crush.json\\\"\\nconfig = json.loads(template.read_text())\\nprovider = config[\\\"providers\\\"][\\\"sakana\\\"]\\nurl = urlparse(provider[\\\"base_url\\\"])\\nassert url.scheme == \\\"https\\\" and not url.username and not url.password and not url.query\\nassert provider[\\\"api_key\\\"] == \\\"${SAKANA_API_KEY}\\\"\\nprovider[\\\"discover_models\\\"] = False\\nfor model in provider[\\\"models\\\"]:\\n    assert model[\\\"id\\\"] == \\\"fugu-max\\\"\\n    model.update(default_max_tokens=20000, default_reasoning_effort=\\\"high\\\")\\nfor model in config[\\\"models\\\"].values():\\n    model.update(max_tokens=20000, reasoning_effort=\\\"high\\\")\\nconfig[\\\"options\\\"].update(disable_metrics=True, auto_lsp=False,\\n    disabled_tools=[\\\"bash\\\", \\\"edit\\\", \\\"multi_edit\\\", \\\"write\\\", \\\"view\\\", \\\"read\\\", \\\"ls\\\", \\\"glob\\\", \\\"grep\\\",\\n                    \\\"fetch\\\", \\\"web_fetch\\\", \\\"web_search\\\", \\\"sourcegraph\\\", \\\"agent\\\", \\\"todo_write\\\"])\\nconfig_path = job / \\\"config/crush.json\\\"\\nconfig_path.write_text(json.dumps(config, indent=2) + \\\"\\\\n\\\")\\nconfig_path.chmod(0o600)\\ncredential = subprocess.run([\\\"rtk\\\", \\\"proxy\\\", \\\"skate\\\", \\\"get\\\", \\\"sakana_api_key@secrets\\\"],\\n                            capture_output=True, timeout=20)\\nsecret = credential.stdout.decode().strip() if credential.returncode == 0 else \\\"\\\"\\nassert secret and len(secret) >= 20, \\\"Credential resolution failed before provider launch\\\"\\nenv = {k: v for k, v in os.environ.items() if k in {\\n    \\\"PATH\\\", \\\"HOME\\\", \\\"LANG\\\", \\\"LC_ALL\\\", \\\"LC_CTYPE\\\", \\\"NIX_SSL_CERT_FILE\\\", \\\"SSL_CERT_FILE\\\", \\\"LD_LIBRARY_PATH\\\", \\\"TERM\\\",\\n}}\\nenv.update(SAKANA_API_KEY=secret, CRUSH_GLOBAL_CONFIG=str(job / \\\"config\\\"),\\n           CRUSH_GLOBAL_DATA=str(job / \\\"data\\\"), CRUSH_SKILLS_DIR=str(job / \\\"skills\\\"))\\nreceipt = {\\n    \\\"status\\\": \\\"running\\\", \\\"provider\\\": \\\"sakana\\\", \\\"model\\\": \\\"fugu-max\\\", \\\"reasoningEffort\\\": \\\"high\\\",\\n    \\\"maxCompletionTokens\\\": 20000, \\\"scope\\\": \\\"advisory-only; no product edits\\\",\\n    \\\"inputSha256\\\": sha(job / \\\"input-bundle.json\\\"), \\\"promptSha256\\\": sha(job / \\\"prompt.txt\\\"),\\n    \\\"launcherSha256\\\": sha(Path(__file__).resolve()), \\\"globalConfigModified\\\": False,\\n    \\\"credential\\\": \\\"privately resolved from Skate; never persisted in config\\\", \\\"startedUnix\\\": time.time(),\\n}\\nreceipt_path = job / \\\"process.json\\\"\\nreceipt_path.write_text(json.dumps(receipt, indent=2) + \\\"\\\\n\\\")\\nprint(json.dumps({\\\"job\\\": str(job), \\\"status\\\": \\\"running\\\", \\\"model\\\": \\\"sakana/fugu-max\\\"}), flush=True)\\nstarted = time.monotonic()\\ntry:\\n    result = subprocess.run([\\n        \\\"rtk\\\", \\\"proxy\\\", \\\"crush\\\", \\\"run\\\", \\\"--quiet\\\", \\\"--cwd\\\", str(job / \\\"workspace\\\"),\\n        \\\"--data-dir\\\", str(job / \\\"data\\\"), \\\"--model\\\", \\\"sakana/fugu-max\\\", \\\"--small-model\\\", \\\"sakana/fugu-max\\\",\\n    ], input=(job / \\\"prompt.txt\\\").read_bytes(), capture_output=True, env=env, timeout=900)\\n    stdout, stderr = result.stdout, result.stderr\\n    receipt.update(status=\\\"completed\\\" if result.returncode == 0 else \\\"failed\\\", exitCode=result.returncode)\\nexcept subprocess.TimeoutExpired as error:\\n    stdout, stderr = error.stdout or b\\\"\\\", error.stderr or b\\\"\\\"\\n    receipt.update(status=\\\"timed_out\\\", exitCode=None)\\nfor name, data in [(\\\"response.txt\\\", stdout), (\\\"stderr.txt\\\", stderr)]:\\n    safe = data.replace(secret.encode(), b\\\"[REDACTED]\\\")\\n    path = job / name\\n    path.write_bytes(safe)\\n    path.chmod(0o600)\\n    receipt[name + \\\"Sha256\\\"] = sha(path)\\ntry:\\n    json.loads((job / \\\"response.txt\\\").read_text())\\n    receipt[\\\"responseJsonValid\\\"] = True\\nexcept (json.JSONDecodeError, UnicodeDecodeError):\\n    receipt[\\\"responseJsonValid\\\"] = False\\ndatabase = job / \\\"data/crush.db\\\"\\nif database.exists():\\n    with sqlite3.connect(\\\"file:\\\" + str(database) + \\\"?mode=ro\\\", uri=True) as db:\\n        finishes = []\\n        for role, parts in db.execute(\\\"SELECT role,parts FROM messages\\\"):\\n            if role == \\\"assistant\\\":\\n                for part in json.loads(parts):\\n                    if part.get(\\\"type\\\") == \\\"finish\\\":\\n                        finishes.append(part[\\\"data\\\"][\\\"reason\\\"])\\n        recei