{"timestamp":"2026-10-05T15:19:23.535Z","ordinal":42019,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a10537-909f-77a3-96d8-dd07161f91ae","turn_id":"01a10ca3-f662-7822-9d58-47f08a989563","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-d5722d77-c2ae-4e16-9ada-9e09a9a3f25c","process_id":"42164","command":["/bin/bash","-lc","rtk proxy rg -n -C 2 'export interface McpToolInfo|type McpToolInfo' src/utils/mcp-client.ts"],"cwd":"file:///home/diogenes/Projects/twyne","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"rtk proxy rg -n -C 2 'export interface McpToolInfo|type McpToolInfo' src/utils/mcp-client.ts"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"29-import type { McpServerConfig } from \"../types\";\n30-\n31:export interface McpToolInfo {\n32-  name: string;\n33-  title?: string;\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"29-import type { McpServerConfig } from \"../types\";\n30-\n31:export interface McpToolInfo {\n32-  name: string;\n33-  title?: string;\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":18532},"formatted_output":"29-import type { McpServerConfig } from \"../types\";\n30-\n31:export interface McpToolInfo {\n32-  name: string;\n33-  title?: string;\n"},"started_at_ms":1791213563535,"completed_at_ms":1791213563535}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-05T15:19:23.552Z","ordinal":42020,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a10537-909f-77a3-96d8-dd07161f91ae","turn_id":"01a10ca3-f662-7822-9d58-47f08a989563","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-bb5469ba-1780-4112-808b-1ed4b7fe5133","process_id":"76254","command":["/bin/bash","-lc","rtk proxy sed -n '1,220p' .agents/skills/convex-expert/SKILL.md"],"cwd":"file:///home/diogenes/Projects/twyne","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"rtk proxy sed -n '1,220p' .agents/skills/convex-expert/SKILL.md"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"---\nname: convex-expert\ndescription: \"Convex backend specialist. Use this agent for any code inside a `convex/` directory — function definitions, schemas, indexes, queries, mutations, actions, HTTP endpoints, cron jobs, file storage, auth wiring, and component installation. Knows the object-form function syntax, validator patterns, resource limits, and component ecosystem that generic Claude routinely gets wrong.\"\n---\n\n<!-- GENERATED from convex-agents content/capabilities/convex-expert.json — do not edit by hand. -->\n\n# Convex backend specialist\n\nAlways-on Convex backend specialist invoked before touching any code inside a convex/ directory. Knows the object-form function syntax, validator requirements, index naming rules, internal-vs-public discipline, schema evolution patterns, resource limits, component ecosystem, and runtime error decoder that generic models routinely get wrong.\n\n## Workflow\n\n1. When about to write or edit any file under convex/: read convex/schema.ts first (and convex/_generated/ai/guidelines.md if present).\n2. Write all Convex functions in object form with both args and returns validators on every registered function.\n3. Use withIndex(...) for every read path — never .filter() for anything that would be a SQL WHERE clause.\n4. Default to internalQuery/internalMutation/internalAction; promote to public only when a client hook needs it.\n5. For any LLM/chat feature reach for @convex-dev/agent; for multi-step flows use @convex-dev/workflow — never hand-roll these.\n6. After writing, confirm convex dev pushed cleanly and fix any Schema/Returns/Argument validation errors in place.\n\n## Rules\n\n- DATA ACCESS + IMPORTS — read before writing any convex/*.ts (front-loaded, not a post-hoc lint):\n- Never an unbounded `.collect()` on a table that can grow — use `.withIndex(...)` and `.paginate(paginationOptsValidator)`/`.take(n)` instead. This is the single most common Convex deploy-blocking and perf defect.\n- Index, don't filter — add `.index(...)` in schema.ts for every read path and query it with `.withIndex(...)`; `.filter()` is a full table scan, never a substitute for a WHERE.\n- The exact import table — get this wrong and the app fails to deploy: `query`/`mutation`/`action`/`internalQuery`/`internalMutation`/`internalAction` come from `\"./_generated/server\"`; `api`/`internal` come from `\"./_generated/api\"`; NEVER `import { query } from \"convex/server\"` or `import { internal } from \"./_generated/server\"` in application code — both are hard deploy failures.\n- `v.literal(\"exact value\")` for a fixed string/enum member (e.g. `v.union(v.literal(\"open\"), v.literal(\"closed\"))`) — not a bare `v.string()` when the set of values is fixed.\n- `\"use node\";` goes only at the top of action-only modules — a file with `\"use node\"` can never also export a `query` or `mutation` (they don't run in the Node runtime); split the file if you need both.\n- Object form only — never the legacy positional query(args, handler) syntax.\n- args and returns validators on every registered function, no exceptions.\n- v.id(tableName) for IDs, never v.string(); undefined is not a Convex value (use null).\n- Never add a required field to a populated table — add v.optional(...) first, backfill, then tighten.\n- Never include _creationTime as a column in a custom index (reserved; causes IndexNameReserved error).\n- Never store storage URLs in tables — store the Id<'_storage'> and call ctx.storage.getUrl(id) on read.\n- Mutations cannot fetch — all external IO goes in actions; persist via ctx.runMutation(internal.x.y).\n- Don't add a parallel database, cache, real-time service, API server, job queue, or object store — Convex is the backend.\n- Convex functions only run from the `convex/` directory — never write schema.ts/queries/mutations/actions at the project root.\n- SELF-VERIFY RULE — before declaring backend work done, verify it compiles and pushes: run `npx tsc --noEmit` and, when a deployment is available (or via a local anonymous one: `CONVEX_AGENT_MODE=anonymous npx convex dev --once`), push it. Fix every error it reports before finishing — one verify round catches the wrong-relative-import / duplicate-symbol / unbalanced-paren class that otherwise breaks the deploy.\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"---\nname: convex-expert\ndescription: \"Convex backend specialist. Use this agent for any code inside a `convex/` directory — function definitions, schemas, indexes, queries, mutations, actions, HTTP endpoints, cron jobs, file storage, auth wiring, and component installation. Knows the object-form function syntax, validator patterns, resource limits, and component ecosystem that generic Claude routinely gets wrong.\"\n---\n\n<!-- GENERATED from convex-agents content/capabilities/convex-expert.json — do not edit by hand. -->\n\n# Convex backend specialist\n\nAlways-on Convex backend specialist invoked before touching any code inside a convex/ directory. Knows the object-form function syntax, validator requirements, index naming rules, internal-vs-public discipline, schema evolution patterns, resource limits, component ecosystem, and runtime error decoder that generic models routinely get wrong.\n\n## Workflow\n\n1. When about to write or edit any file under convex/: read convex/schema.ts first (and convex/_generated/ai/guidelines.md if present).\n2. Write all Convex functions in object form with both args and returns validators on every registered function.\n3. Use withIndex(...) for every read path — never .filter() for anything that would be a SQL WHERE clause.\n4. Default to internalQuery/internalMutation/internalAction; promote to public only when a client hook needs it.\n5. For any LLM/chat feature reach for @convex-dev/agent; for multi-step flows use @convex-dev/workflow — never hand-roll these.\n6. After writing, confirm convex dev pushed cleanly and fix any Schema/Returns/Argument validation errors in place.\n\n## Rules\n\n- DATA ACCESS + IMPORTS — read before writing any convex/*.ts (front-loaded, not a post-hoc lint):\n- Never an unbounded `.collect()` on a table that can grow — use `.withIndex(...)` and `.paginate(paginationOptsValidator)`/`.take(n)` instead. This is the single most common Convex deploy-blocking and perf defect.\n- Index, don't filter — add `.index(...)` in schema.ts for every read path and query it with `.withIndex(...)`; `.filter()` is a full table scan, never a substitute for a WHERE.\n- The exact import table — get this wrong and the app fails to deploy: `query`/`mutation`/`action`/`internalQuery`/`internalMutation`/`internalAction` come from `\"./_generated/server\"`; `api`/`internal` come from `\"./_generated/api\"`; NEVER `import { query } from \"convex/server\"` or `import { internal } from \"./_generated/server\"` in application code — both are hard deploy failures.\n- `v.literal(\"exact value\")` for a fixed string/enum member (e.g. `v.union(v.literal(\"open\"), v.literal(\"closed\"))`) — not a bare `v.string()` when the set of values is fixed.\n- `\"use node\";` goes only at the top of action-only modules — a file with `\"use node\"` can never also export a `query` or `mutation` (they don't run in the Node runtime); split the file if you need both.\n- Object form only — never the legacy positional query(args, handler) syntax.\n- args and returns validators on every registered function, no exceptions.\n- v.id(tableName) for IDs, never v.string(); undefined is not a Convex value (use null).\n- Never add a required field to a populated table — add v.optional(...) first, backfill, then tighten.\n- Never include _creationTime as a column in a custom index (reserved; causes IndexNameReserved error).\n- Never store storage URLs in tables — store the Id<'_storage'> and call ctx.storage.getUrl(id) on read.\n- Mutations cannot fetch — all external IO goes in actions; persist via ctx.runMutation(internal.x.y).\n- Don't add a parallel database, cache, real-time service, API server, job queue, or object store — Convex is the backend.\n- Convex functions only run from the `convex/` directory — never write schema.ts/queries/mutations/actions at the project root.\n- SELF-VERIFY RULE — before declaring backend work done, verify it compiles and pushes: run `npx tsc --noEmit` and, when a deployment is available (or via a local anonymous one: `CONVEX_AGENT_MODE=anonymous npx convex dev --once`), push it. Fix every error it reports before finishing — one verify round catches the wrong-relative-import / duplicate-symbol / unbalanced-paren class that otherwise breaks the deploy.\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":10211024},"formatted_output":"---\nname: convex-expert\ndescription: \"Convex backend specialist. Use this agent for any code inside a `convex/` directory — function definitions, schemas, indexes, queries, mutations, actions, HTTP endpoints, cron jobs, file storage, auth wiring, and component installation. Knows the object-form function syntax, validator patterns, resource limits, and component ecosystem that generic Claude routinely gets wrong.\"\n---\n\n<!-- GENERATED from convex-agents content/capabilities/convex-expert.json — do not edit by hand. -->\n\n# Convex backend specialist\n\nAlways-on Convex backend specialist invoked before touching any code inside a convex/ directory. Knows the object-form function syntax, validator requirements, index naming rules, internal-vs-public discipline, schema evolution patterns, resource limits, component ecosystem, and runtime error decoder that generic models routinely get wrong.\n\n## Workflow\n\n1. When about to write or edit any file under convex/: read convex/schema.ts first (and convex/_generated/ai/guidelines.md if present).\n2. Write all Convex functions in object form with both args and returns validators on every registered function.\n3. Use withIndex(...) for every read path — never .filter() for anything that would be a SQL WHERE clause.\n4. Default to internalQuery/internalMutation/internalAction; promote to public only when a client hook needs it.\n5. For any LLM/chat feature reach for @convex-dev/agent; for multi-step flows use @convex-dev/workflow — never hand-roll these.\n6. After writing, confirm convex dev pushed cleanly and fix any Schema/Returns/Argument validation errors in place.\n\n## Rules\n\n- DATA ACCESS + IMPORTS — read before writing any convex/*.ts (front-loaded, not a post-hoc lint):\n- Never an unbounded `.collect()` on a table that can grow — use `.withIndex(...)` and `.paginate(paginationOptsValidator)`/`.take(n)` instead. This is the single most common Convex deploy-blocking and perf defect.\n- Index, don't filter — add `.index(...)` in schema.ts for every read path and query it with `.withIndex(...)`; `.filter()` is a full table scan, never a substitute for a WHERE.\n- The exact import table — get this wrong and the app fails to deploy: `query`/`mutation`/`action`/`internalQuery`/`internalMutation`/`internalAction` come from `\"./_generated/server\"`; `api`/`internal` come from `\"./_generated/api\"`; NEVER `import { query } from \"convex/server\"` or `import { internal } from \"./_generated/server\"` in application code — both are hard deploy failures.\n- `v.literal(\"exact value\")` for a fixed string/enum member (e.g. `v.union(v.literal(\"open\"), v.literal(\"closed\"))`) — not a bare `v.string()` when the set of values is fixed.\n- `\"use node\";` goes only at the top of action-only modules — a file with `\"use node\"` can never also export a `query` or `mutation` (they don't run in the Node runtime); split the file if you need both.\n- Object form only — never the legacy positional query(args, handler) syntax.\n- args and returns validators on every registered function, no exceptions.\n- v.id(tableName) for IDs, never v.string(); undefined is not a Convex value (use null).\n- Never add a required field to a populated table — add v.optional(...) first, backfill, then tighten.\n- Never include _creationTime as a column in a custom index (reserved; causes IndexNameReserved error).\n- Never store storage URLs in tables — store the Id<'_storage'> and call ctx.storage.getUrl(id) on read.\n- Mutations cannot fetch — all external IO goes in actions; persist via ctx.runMutation(internal.x.y).\n- Don't add a parallel database, cache, real-time service, API server, job queue, or object store — Convex is the backend.\n- Convex functions only run from the `convex/` directory — never write schema.ts/queries/mutations/actions at the project root.\n- SELF-VERIFY RULE — before declaring backend work done, verify it compiles and pushes: run `npx tsc --noEmit` and, when a deployment is available (or via a local anonymous one: `CONVEX_AGENT_MODE=anonymous npx convex dev --once`), push it. Fix every error it reports before finishing — one verify round catches the wrong-relative-import / duplicate-symbol / unbalanced-paren class that otherwise breaks the deploy.\n"},"started_at_ms":1791213563542,"completed_at_ms":1791213563552}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-05T15:19:23.654Z","ordinal":42021,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a10ca5-ef06-77c1-a9b8-950369503ca2","call_id":"call_Pq5aAzs3A0dthRdMyeiDnPLE","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.3 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"check\":0,\"chunk_id\":\"da832e\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000015715,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":1119,\"output\":\"//! Pure checks derived from notorganic-connect.ts, auth.ts, and the current\\n//! Not Organic public-client/product validators. Neither a successful check nor\\n//! a constructed receipt authenticates an account. The parent transport must\\n//! establish TLS/session/JWT authenticity and accepted Convex auth separately.\\n\\nuse anyhow::{Result, bail, ensure};\\nuse base64::{Engine, engine::general_purpose::URL_SAFE_NO_PAD};\\nuse serde::{Deserialize, Serialize};\\nuse sha2::{Digest, Sha256};\\nuse std::fmt;\\nuse uuid::Uuid;\\n\\npub const CALLBACK_PATH: &str = \\\"/auth/notorganic/\\\";\\npub const ATTEMPT_LIFETIME_MS: u64 = 600_000;\\npub const AUTHORIZE_URL: &str = \\\"https://id.notorganic.info/authorize\\\";\\n/// Root must continue capability-gating live account controls. Pure registration\\n/// or receipt consistency checks cannot make this transport available.\\npub const CONNECTED_AUTH_AVAILABLE: bool = false;\\n\\n/// Operator configuration, not an inferred capability from a URL's syntax.\\n#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Eq)]\\npub struct CallbackRegistration {\\n    pub origin: String,\\n    pub twyne_backend_trusted: bool,\\n    /// Must come from the operator-approved gateway catalog, never the cosmetic\\n    /// `product` query parameter. Unconfigured loopback currently maps to Keating.\\n    pub gateway_product: Option<String>,\\n}\\n\\nimpl CallbackRegistration {\\n    pub fn require_supported(&self) -> Result<()> {\\n        validate_origin(&self.origin)?;\\n        ensure!(\\n            self.twyne_backend_trusted && self.gateway_product.as_deref() == Some(\\\"twyne\\\"),\\n            \\\"Native sign-in requires this exact callback origin to be approved by both Twyne and Not Organic.\\\"\\n        );\\n        Ok(())\\n    }\\n}\\n\\n/// Conservatively accepts canonical ASCII origins only. This is not a general\\n/// URL parser; the eventual router must supply separately parsed URL components.\\n/// Rejecting an unsupported representation never broadens backend trust.\\npub fn validate_origin(origin: &str) -> Result<()> {\\n    ensure!(\\n        origin.len() <= 256 && origin.is_ascii(),\\n        \\\"Unsupported callback origin.\\\"\\n    );\\n    let (scheme, authority) = origin\\n        .split_once(\\\"://\\\")\\n        .ok_or_else(|| anyhow::anyhow!(\\\"Unsupported callback origin.\\\"))?;\\n    ensure!(\\n        !authority.is_empty() && !authority.contains(['/', '?', '#', '@', '\\\\\\\\']),\\n        \\\"Unsupported callback origin.\\\"\\n    );\\n    let (host, port) = if let Some(tail) = authority.strip_prefix(\\\"[::1]\\\") {\\n        ensure!(\\n            tail.is_empty() || tail.starts_with(':'),\\n            \\\"Unsupported callback origin.\\\"\\n        );\\n        (\\\"[::1]\\\", tail.strip_prefix(':'))\\n    } else {\\n        let mut parts = authority.split(':');\\n        let host = parts.next().unwrap_or_default();\\n        let port = parts.next();\\n        ensure!(parts.next().is_none(), \\\"Unsupported callback origin.\\\");\\n        ensure!(\\n            host.split('.').all(|label| !label.is_empty()\\n                && !label.starts_with('-')\\n                && !label.ends_with('-')\\n                && label\\n                    .bytes()\\n                    .all(|b| b.is_ascii_lowercase() || b.is_ascii_digit() || b == b'-')),\\n            \\\"Unsupported callback origin.\\\"\\n        );\\n        (host, port)\\n    };\\n    if let Some(port) = port {\\n        let number = port.parse::<u16>().ok().filter(|port| *port > 0);\\n        ensure!(\\n            number.is_some() && !port.starts_with('0') && port.bytes().all(|b| b.is_ascii_digit()),\\n            \\\"Unsupported callback port.\\\"\\n        );\\n        ensure!(\\n            !(scheme == \\\"https\\\" && number == Some(443) || scheme == \\\"http\\\" && number == Some(80)),\\n            \\\"Use the canonical callback origin.\\\"\\n        );\\n    }\\n    ensure!(\\n        scheme == \\\"https\\\"\\n            || scheme == \\\"http\\\" && matches!(host, \\\"localhost\\\" | \\\"127.0.0.1\\\" | \\\"[::1]\\\"),\\n        \\\"Only registered HTTPS or loopback callbacks are supported.\\\"\\n    );\\n    Ok(())\\n}\\n\\npub fn safe_return_to(value: &str) -> String {\\n    if value.starts_with('/')\\n        && !value.starts_with(\\\"//\\\")\\n        && !value.contains('\\\\\\\\')\\n        && !value.chars().any(|c| c < ' ' || c == '\\\\u{7f}')\\n    {\\n        value.to_owned()\\n    } else {\\n        \\\"/\\\".to_owned()\\n    }\\n}\\n\\nfn query_escape(value: &str) -> String {\\n    value.bytes().fold(String::new(), |mut out, byte| {\\n        if byte.is_ascii_alphanumeric() || matches!(byte, b'-' | b'_' | b'.' | b'~') {\\n            out.push(char::from(byte));\\n        } else {\\n            use fmt::Write;\\n            let _ = write!(out, \\\"%{byte:02X}\\\");\\n\"}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"check\":1,\"chunk_id\":\"25ef57\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000019699,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":1170,\"output\":\"12:  resources_allowed: boolean;\\n17:  resources: boolean;\\n20:  toolDefinitions?: Record<string, string>;\\n32:  review?: {\\n46:  resources: makeFunctionReference<\\\"action\\\", { sourceId: string }, unknown>(\\n47:    \\\"knowledge:resources\\\",\\n62:let generation = 0;\\n78:export function accountKnowledgeGeneration() {\\n79:  return generation;\\n81:export function accountKnowledgeSnapshot(): AccountKnowledgeSnapshot {\\n84:export function subscribeAccountKnowledge(listener: () => void) {\\n105:            resources: (value as AccountSourceChoice).resources === true,\\n106:            toolDefinitions:\\n107:              typeof (value as AccountSourceChoice).toolDefinitions ===\\n109:              (value as AccountSourceChoice).toolDefinitions !== null\\n110:                ? (value as AccountSourceChoice).toolDefinitions\\n128:export function setAccountKnowledgeContext(\\n134:  generation++;\\n156:export function chooseAccountSource(\\n158:  mode: \\\"research\\\" | \\\"model\\\" | \\\"resources\\\",\\n162:  if (!source || (mode === \\\"resources\\\" && !source.resources_allowed)) return;\\n167:      resources: false,\\n171:  if (!enabled && snapshot.review?.sourceId === id)\\n176:function toolDefinition(info: McpToolInfo) {\\n184:export function chooseAccountSearchTool(id: string, name: string) {\\n195:      resources: false,\\n198:    toolDefinitions: {\\n199:      ...snapshot.choices[id]?.toolDefinitions,\\n200:      [name]: toolDefinition(\\n207:  if (snapshot.review?.sourceId === id && snapshot.review.tool !== name)\\n212:export function chooseAccountModelTool(\\n226:    resources: false,\\n233:    toolDefinitions: {\\n234:      ...choice.toolDefinitions,\\n235:      [name]: toolDefinition(\\n244:    snapshot.review?.sourceId === id &&\\n245:    snapshot.review.tool === name\\n251:export function cancelAccountResearchReview() {\\n252:  if (snapshot.review?.mode === \\\"research\\\") resolveAccountToolReview(false);\\n254:export function resolveAccountToolReview(allowed: boolean) {\\n257:  snapshot.review = undefined;\\n258:  pending?.resolve(allowed && pending.epoch === generation);\\n261:export function safeKnowledgeError(error: unknown): string {\\n276:export async function refreshAccountKnowledge(): Promise<AccountSource[]> {\\n278:    epoch = generation,\\n286:    if (epoch !== generation || active !== client || request !== catalogRequest)\\n306:        typeof source.resources_allowed !== \\\"boolean\\\"\\n336:            choice.toolDefinitions?.[name] === toolDefinition(tool),\\n349:      snapshot.review &&\\n352:          source.id === snapshot.review?.sourceId &&\\n353:          source.tools.some((tool) => tool.name === snapshot.review?.tool),\\n357:    if (snapshot.review) {\\n358:      const review = snapshot.review,\\n359:        choice = snapshot.choices[review.sourceId];\\n361:        !choice?.[review.mode] ||\\n362:        (review.mode === \\\"model\\\"\\n363:          ? !choice.modelTools?.includes(review.tool)\\n364:          : choice.searchTool !== review.tool)\\n371:    if (epoch === generation && request === catalogRequest) {\\n377:    if (epoch === generation && request === catalogRequest) {\\n383:function selected(id: string, mode: \\\"research\\\" | \\\"model\\\" | \\\"resources\\\") {\\n387:  return { source, active: client, epoch: generation };\\n390:  if (epoch !== generation)\\n415:    choice?.toolDefinitions?.[name] !==\\n416:    toolDefinition(access.source.tools.find((tool) => tool.name === name)!)\\n429:export async function callAccountTool(\\n439:  const review = JSON.stringify(args, null, 2);\\n440:  const reviewedArguments: Record<string, unknown> = JSON.parse(review);\\n441:  if (review.length > 16_000)\\n443:      \\\"These arguments are too large to review. Use a smaller request.\\\",\\n446:    throw new Error(\\\"Finish reviewing the previous external tool call first.\\\");\\n447:  snapshot.review = {\\n451:    argumentsJson: review,\\n475:      arguments: reviewedArguments,\\n486:export async function accountResources(id: string): Promise<AccountResource[]> {\\n487:  const { source, active, epoch } = selected(id, \\\"resources\\\");\\n488:  if (!source.resources_allowed)\\n491:    const result = (await active.action(refs.resources, { sourceId: id })) as {\\n492:      resources?: AccountResource[];\\n495:    selected(id, \\\"resources\\\");\\n496:    if (!Array.isArray(result?.resources) || result.resources.length > 200)\\n498:    return result.resources.filter(\\n511:export async function readAccountResource(\\n515:  const { active, epoch } = selected(id, \\\"resources\\\");\\n519:  selected(id, \\\"resources\\\");\\n525:    selected(id, \\\"resources\\\");\\n534:export function knowledgeSetupUrl(origin: string, returnPath: string) {\\n551:export async function accountKnowledgeTools(): Promise<ToolSet> {\\n554:  const epoch = generation;\\n600:export async function searchAccountKnowledge(input: {\\n607:  const epoch = generation;\\n\"}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"check\":2,\"chunk_id\":\"953571\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000016371,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":1245,\"output\":\"35-  /** True only after a Better Auth token has been installed in Convex. */\\n36-  convexAuthenticated?: boolean;\\n37-  /**\\n38:   * Restored ATProto OAuth session, used only to write records to a PDS.\\n39-   * It is never a Twyne identity; sign-in is Not Organic only.\\n40-   */\\n41-  atproto?: {\\n--\\n44-    displayName?: string;\\n45-    avatar?: string;\\n46-  };\\n47:  /** Set once a Not Organic–backed Better Auth session is present. */\\n48-  provider?: \\\"convex\\\";\\n49-}\\n50-\\n--\\n85-      let unsubscribe: (() => void) | undefined;\\n86-      let unsubscribeProfile: (() => void) | undefined;\\n87-      let profile: AccountProfile | null = null;\\n88:      let sessionUser: AuthUser | null = null;\\n89-      cleanup(() => {\\n90-        disposed = true;\\n91-        authGeneration++;\\n--\\n110-          };\\n111-        }\\n112-      };\\n113:      // A PDS publishing session must not delay the Twyne/Convex session.\\n114-      void import(\\\"./atproto\\\").then(\\n115-        async ({ initSession, ATPROTO_SESSION_CHANGED }) => {\\n116-          if (disposed) return;\\n--\\n131-        },\\n132-      );\\n133-\\n134:      const sessionAtom = authClient.useSession;\\n135:      if (!sessionAtom || typeof sessionAtom !== \\\"object\\\") {\\n136-        betterAuthPending = false;\\n137-        return;\\n138-      }\\n139-\\n140-      function syncFromAtom() {\\n141-        if (disposed) return;\\n142:        const val = sessionAtom.get?.() ?? sessionAtom;\\n143-        betterAuthPending = val?.isPending ?? false;\\n144:        const sessionData = val?.data;\\n145:        if (val?.isPending && !sessionData?.user) return;\\n146:        if (sessionData?.user) {\\n147-          const user: AuthUser = {\\n148:            id: sessionData.user.id,\\n149-            // Not Organic users carry an undeliverable placeholder address.\\n150:            email: sessionData.user.email?.endsWith(\\\"@notorganic.invalid\\\")\\n151-              ? \\\"\\\"\\n152:              : (sessionData.user.email ?? \\\"\\\"),\\n153:            name: sessionData.user.name ?? undefined,\\n154:            image: sessionData.user.image ?? undefined,\\n155-          };\\n156:          if (currentUserId === user.id && sessionUser) {\\n157-            // A refresh can update a name/photo without changing the account.\\n158-            // Keep the token callback's base user current as well as the UI.\\n159:            Object.assign(sessionUser, user);\\n160-            authState.value = {\\n161-              ...authState.value,\\n162:              user: withAccountProfile(sessionUser, profile),\\n163-            };\\n164-            return;\\n165-          }\\n166-          unsubscribeProfile?.();\\n167-          unsubscribeProfile = undefined;\\n168-          profile = null;\\n169:          sessionUser = user;\\n170-          currentUserId = user.id;\\n171-          const generation = ++authGeneration;\\n172:          const isCurrent = () => !disposed && generation === authGeneration;\\n173-          authState.value = {\\n174-            user: withAccountProfile(user, profile),\\n175-            loading: isAtprotoCallback && atprotoPending,\\n--\\n181-          if (!convex) return;\\n182-          const fetchToken = createConvexTokenFetcher(async () => {\\n183-            try {\\n184:              const result = await (authClient as any).convex.token({\\n185-                fetchOptions: { throw: false },\\n186-              });\\n187-              const token = result?.data?.token ?? null;\\n188:              if (isCurrent())\\n189-                user.analyticsId = analyticsIdFromConvexJwt(token);\\n190-              return token;\\n191-            } catch (error) {\\n192:              if (isCurrent())\\n193-                reportApplicationError(\\n194-                  \\\"twyne:auth:install-convex-token\\\",\\n195-                  error,\\n--\\n202-                );\\n203-              return null;\\n204-            }\\n205:          }, isCurrent);\\n206:          convex.setAuth(fetchToken, (authenticated) => {\\n207:            if (!isCurrent()) return;\\n208-            if (!authenticated) {\\n209-              unsubscribeProfile?.();\\n210-              unsubscribeProfile = undefined;\\n--\\n224-                  api.profiles.getMyHandle,\\n225-                  {},\\n226-                  (row) => {\\n227:                    if (!isCurrent() || !authState.value.convexAuthenticated)\\n228-                      return;\\n229-                    profile = row;\\n230-                    authState.value = {\\n--\\n241-          unsubscribeProfile?.();\\n242-          unsubscribeProfile = undefined;\\n243-          profile = null;\\n244:          sessionUser = null;\\n245-          currentUserId = null;\\n246-          authGeneration++;\\n247:          convex?.setAuth(async () => null);\\n248-          clearConvexSyncContext();\\n249-          authState.value = { user: null, loading: val?.isPending ?? false };\\n250-          publishAtproto();\\n251-        }\\n252-      }\\n253-      syncFromAtom();\\n254:      if (typeof sessionAtom.subscribe === \\\"function\\\") {\\n255:        unsubscribe = sessionAtom.subscribe(syncFromAtom);\\n256-      }\\n257-    },\\n258-    { strategy: \\\"document-ready\\\" },\\n\"}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"check\":3,\"chunk_id\":\"463c6f\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000018532,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":33,\"output\":\"29-import type { McpServerConfig } from \\\"../types\\\";\\n30-\\n31:export interface McpToolInfo {\\n32-  name: string;\\n33-  title?: string;\\n\"}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"check\":4,\"chunk_id\":\"e0b959\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000025097,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":742,\"output\":\"[package]\\nname = \\\"twyne-desktop\\\"\\nversion = \\\"0.1.0\\\"\\nedition = \\\"2024\\\"\\nrust-version = \\\"1.92\\\"\\ndescription = \\\"Twyne's native, offline writing room, built with GPUI\\\"\\npublish = false\\n\\n[features]\\ndefault = [\\\"desktop\\\"]\\ndesktop = [\\\"dep:gpui-kit\\\", \\\"dep:image\\\", \\\"dep:roxmltree\\\", \\\"dep:base64\\\", \\\"dep:hypher\\\", \\\"dep:unicode-linebreak\\\", \\\"dep:x11rb\\\", \\\"dep:gpui-linux\\\", \\\"native-typst\\\"]\\nnative-typst = [\\\"dep:typst\\\", \\\"dep:typst-pdf\\\", \\\"dep:typst-svg\\\", \\\"dep:sha2\\\", \\\"dep:image\\\"]\\nnative-audio = [\\\"dep:sha2\\\"]\\nui-tests = [\\\"desktop\\\", \\\"gpui-kit/test-support\\\", \\\"gpui-linux?/test-support\\\"]\\n\\n[dependencies]\\nanyhow = \\\"1.0\\\"\\ndirectories = \\\"6.0\\\"\\nfs2 = \\\"0.4\\\"\\ngpui-kit = { version = \\\"=0.7.0\\\", optional = true }\\nchrono = \\\"=0.4.45\\\"\\nhtml5ever = \\\"=0.27.0\\\"\\nunicode-segmentation = \\\"=1.13.3\\\"\\nmarkup5ever_rcdom = \\\"=0.3.0\\\"\\nimage = { version = \\\"=0.25.10\\\", default-features = false, features = [\\\"png\\\", \\\"webp\\\", \\\"jpeg\\\", \\\"gif\\\"], optional = true }\\nroxmltree = { version = \\\"=0.20.0\\\", optional = true }\\nbase64 = { version = \\\"=0.22.1\\\", optional = true }\\nhypher = { version = \\\"=0.1.8\\\", default-features = false, features = [\\\"alloc\\\", \\\"english\\\"], optional = true }\\nunicode-linebreak = { version = \\\"=0.1.5\\\", optional = true }\\nserde = { version = \\\"1.0\\\", features = [\\\"derive\\\", \\\"rc\\\"] }\\nserde_json = \\\"1.0\\\"\\nregex = \\\"=1.13.1\\\"\\nunicode-normalization = \\\"=0.1.25\\\"\\nurl = \\\"=2.5.8\\\"\\ntempfile = \\\"3.23\\\"\\nuuid = { version = \\\"1.18\\\", features = [\\\"v4\\\", \\\"serde\\\"] }\\nsha2 = { version = \\\"=0.10.9\\\", optional = true }\\ntypst = { git = \\\"https://github.com/Myriad-Dreamin/typst.git\\\", rev = \\\"951788cc614cd805d5d786e17bbf93796df73d10\\\", optional = true }\\ntypst-pdf = { git = \\\"https://github.com/Myriad-Dreamin/typst.git\\\", rev = \\\"951788cc614cd805d5d786e17bbf93796df73d10\\\", optional = true }\\ntypst-svg = { git = \\\"https://github.com/Myriad-Dreamin/typst.git\\\", rev = \\\"951788cc614cd805d5d786e17bbf93796df73d10\\\", optional = true }\\n\\n[target.'cfg(target_os = \\\"linux\\\")'.dependencies]\\nx11rb = { version = \\\"=0.13.2\\\", optional = true }\\ngpui-linux = { package = \\\"gpui-pre-linux\\\", version = \\\"=0.3.7\\\", default-features = false, features = [\\\"wayland\\\"], optional = true }\\n\\n[[bin]]\\nname = \\\"twyne-desktop\\\"\\npath = \\\"src/main.rs\\\"\\nrequired-features = [\\\"desktop\\\"]\\n\\n[[example]]\\nname = \\\"twyne-clipboard-probe\\\"\\npath = \\\"fixtures/editor/clipboard-probe.rs\\\"\\nrequired-features = [\\\"desktop\\\"]\\n\\n[[example]]\\nname = \\\"twyne-wayland-clipboard-probe\\\"\\npath = \\\"fixtures/wayland-clipboard/native-probe.rs\\\"\\nrequired-features = [\\\"desktop\\\"]\\n\\n[[example]]\\nname = \\\"twyne-dossier-multiply-probe\\\"\\npath = \\\"fixtures/dossier-multiply/native-probe/main.rs\\\"\\nrequired-features = [\\\"ui-tests\\\"]\\n\\n[[test]]\\nname = \\\"native-audio-contract\\\"\\npath = \\\"fixtures/native-audio/synthetic_loopback.rs\\\"\\nrequired-features = [\\\"native-audio\\\"]\\n\\n[profile.dev]\\ndebug = 0\\n\\n[patch.crates-io]\\ngpui-base = { path = \\\"vendor/gpui-base\\\" }\\ngpui-pre = { path = \\\"vendor/gpui-pre\\\" }\\ngpui-pre-wgpu = { path = \\\"vendor/gpui-pre-wgpu\\\" }\\ngpui-pre-linux = { path = \\\"vendor/gpui-pre-linux\\\" }\\n\\n[profile.release]\\nlto = \\\"thin\\\"\\ncodegen-units = 1\\nstrip = true\\n\"}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"check\":5,\"chunk_id\":\"412383\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000014874,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":15,\"output\":\"?? desktop/gpui/src/native_accounts/\\n?? desktop/gpui/tools/\\n\"}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"check\":6,\"chunk_id\":\"5d4beb\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.010223109,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":1064,\"output\":\"---\\nname: convex-expert\\ndescription: \\\"Convex backend specialist. Use this agent for any code inside a `convex/` directory — function definitions, schemas, indexes, queries, mutations, actions, HTTP endpoints, cron jobs, file storage, auth wiring, and component installation. Knows the object-form function syntax, validator patterns, resource limits, and component ecosystem that generic Claude routinely gets wrong.\\\"\\n---\\n\\n<!-- GENERATED from convex-agents content/capabilities/convex-expert.json — do not edit by hand. -->\\n\\n# Convex backend specialist\\n\\nAlways-on Convex backend specialist invoked before touching any code inside a convex/ directory. Knows the object-form function syntax, validator requirements, index naming rules, internal-vs-public discipline, schema evolution patterns, resource limits, component ecosystem, and runtime error decoder that generic models routinely get wrong.\\n\\n## Workflow\\n\\n1. When about to write or edit any file under convex/: read convex/schema.ts first (and convex/_generated/ai/guidelines.md if present).\\n2. Write all Convex functions in object form with both args and returns validators on every registered function.\\n3. Use withIndex(...) for every read path — never .filter() for anything that would be a SQL WHERE clause.\\n4. Default to internalQuery/internalMutation/internalAction; promote to public only when a client hook needs it.\\n5. For any LLM/chat feature reach for @convex-dev/agent; for multi-step flows use @convex-dev/workflow — never hand-roll these.\\n6. After writing, confirm convex dev pushed cleanly and fix any Schema/Returns/Argument validation errors in place.\\n\\n## Rules\\n\\n- DATA ACCESS + IMPORTS — read before writing any convex/*.ts (front-loaded, not a post-hoc lint):\\n- Never an unbounded `.collect()` on a table that can grow — use `.withIndex(...)` and `.paginate(paginationOptsValidator)`/`.take(n)` instead. This is the single most common Convex deploy-blocking and perf defect.\\n- Index, don't filter — add `.index(...)` in schema.ts for every read path and query it with `.withIndex(...)`; `.filter()` is a full table scan, never a substitute for a WHERE.\\n- The exact import table — get this wrong and the app fails to deploy: `query`/`mutation`/`action`/`internalQuery`/`internalMutation`/`internalAction` come from `\\\"./_generated/server\\\"`; `api`/`internal` come from `\\\"./_generated/api\\\"`; NEVER `import { query } from \\\"convex/server\\\"` or `import { internal } from \\\"./_generated/server\\\"` in application code — both are hard deploy failures.\\n- `v.literal(\\\"exact value\\\")` for a fixed string/enum member (e.g. `v.union(v.literal(\\\"open\\\"), v.literal(\\\"closed\\\"))`) — not a bare `v.string()` when the set of values is fixed.\\n- `\\\"use node\\\";` goes only at the top of action-only modules — a file with `\\\"use node\\\"` can never also export a `query` or `mutation` (they don't run in the Node runtime); split the file if you need both.\\n- Object form only — never the legacy positional query(args, handler) syntax.\\n- args and returns validators on every registered function, no exceptions.\\n- v.id(tableName) for IDs, never v.string(); undefined is not a Convex value (use null).\\n- Never add a required field to a populated table — add v.optional(...) first, backfill, then tighten.\\n- Never include _creationTime as a column in a custom index (reserved; causes IndexNameReserved error).\\n- Never store storage URLs in tables — store the Id<'_storage'> and call ctx.storage.getUrl(id) on read.\\n- Mutations cannot fetch — all external IO goes in actions; persist via ctx.runMutation(internal.x.y).\\n- Don't add a parallel database, cache, real-time service, API server, job queue, or object store — Convex is the backend.\\n- Convex functions only run from the `convex/` directory — never write schema.ts/queries/mutations/actions at the project root.\\n- SELF-VERIFY RULE — before declaring backend work done, verify it compiles and pushes: run `npx tsc --noEmit` and, when a deployment is available (or via a local anonymous one: `CONVEX_AGENT_MODE=anonymous npx convex dev --once`), push it. Fix every error it reports before finishing — one verify round catches the wrong-relative-import / duplicate-symbol / unbalanced-paren class that otherwise breaks the deploy.\\n\"}"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a10ca3-f662-7822-9d58-47f08a989563","create_time":1791213563.654629}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
