{"timestamp":"2026-10-05T15:19:46.665Z","ordinal":42025,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a10537-909f-77a3-96d8-dd07161f91ae","turn_id":"01a10ca3-f662-7822-9d58-47f08a989563","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_0acb6e766bb0227d016ac3c010831887d1b7bccec1d370f862","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"The desktop has local account state, but no network session yet. I’m reusing Twyne’s existing sign-in and Convex clients for that connection, with isolated Sakana jobs handling the callback parser and knowledge-tool review logic."}],"phase":"commentary"},"started_at_ms":1791213584540,"completed_at_ms":1791213586665}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-05T15:19:46.675Z","ordinal":42026,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"message","id":"msg_0acb6e766bb0227d016ac3c010831887d1b7bccec1d370f862","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"output_text","text":"The desktop has local account state, but no network session yet. I’m reusing Twyne’s existing sign-in and Convex clients for that connection, with isolated Sakana jobs handling the callback parser and knowledge-tool review logic."}],"phase":"commentary","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a10ca3-f662-7822-9d58-47f08a989563","create_time":1791213564.493075,"content_item_kinds":["unknown"]}},"metadata":{"retained_source":{"id":{"message_id":"msg_0acb6e766bb0227d016ac3c010831887d1b7bccec1d370f862","turn_id":"01a10ca3-f662-7822-9d58-47f08a989563","role":"assistant"},"revision":"retained_01a10ca6-48f2-7d93-8ca9-e05bd7ad2e43","complete":true},"client_authored":false,"user_input_order":2347}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-05T15:20:36.305Z","ordinal":42027,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_0acb6e766bb0227d016ac3c012a1dc87d1944d172d3690005a","status":"completed","call_id":"call_pbK51Qziww2pf2tv0SpxF8iO","name":"exec","input":"text(await tools.exec_command({\ncmd:\"rtk proxy python3 - <<'PY'\\nfrom pathlib import Path\\nimport hashlib\\nimport json\\nroot = Path.cwd()\\nbase = root / 'desktop/gpui/target/verification/connected-session-inputs'\\nbase.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\\nshared = '''You are an advisory worker on Twyne's GPUI port. You are not alone in the codebase. Other workers and Root own other modules; do not revert anyone else's edits. You have NO repository-write, shell, network, deployment, credential or user-account authority. All needed source is below. Ownership is ONLY the named proposal module. Root reviews, edits and integrates every result. Use Sakana fugu-max carefully; do not guess APIs or claim runtime proof. Return one valid JSON object with keys files (array of objects {path,content}), checks (array of strings), limitations (array of strings). No markdown fences. Keep the proposal focused and compilable Rust 2024 with existing anyhow, serde/serde_json, url 2.5.8, uuid, std. No new dependencies, no manifest/barrel/host edits. Never log or derive Debug for secrets/callback codes/state.\\\\n'''\\ncallback_spec = '''Propose desktop/gpui/src/native_accounts/callback.rs, a bounded loopback HTTP callback listener usable by Root's worker-thread account actor. Existing native_accounts/auth.rs below is authoritative. API: pub struct CallbackListener; pub fn bind(registration: &CallbackRegistration) -> anyhow::Result<Self>; pub fn origin(&self)->&str; pub fn poll(&self, expected_state:&str)->anyhow::Result<Option<CallbackInput>>. bind calls registration.require_supported(), accepts only canonical HTTP 127.0.0.1, localhost (bind127.0.0.1; noDNS), or [::1] with explicit nonzero fixed approved port; never arbitrary hosts/dynamicport or HTTPS pretending. Nonblocking listener; stream deadline <=250ms total; at most 16KiB request headers, no body, GET only, origin-form target only, HTTP1.0/1.1, exactly one Host identical to registered authority; reject duplicate Host, Transfer-Encoding, body, invalid newline/controlbytes, target fragment, percent/dot-path normalization bypass. Raw pathname must literally CALLBACK_PATH before parsing. URL query duplicates preserved via url::Url; CallbackInput has origin,path,fragment,error_present,codes,states; inspect actual definition. Ignore invalid/unsolicited/mismatched state callbacks (404 generic, return None) WITHOUT consuming Root's legitimate attempt. Valid matching state, including an OAuth error, becomes CallbackInput; Root then performs auth.rs single-use checks. Wrong code duplicates must not be hidden. No state/code reflected in responses/logs; successful listener acknowledgement says only Return to Twyne; sign-in is being completed, not authenticated. Set no-store/referrer-policy no-referrer/nosniff and Connection close; no external assets, redirects or cookies. An expired attempt is Root actor responsibility. Implement parse_request as private testable pure function and focused in-module tests with raw HTTP fixtures (duplicate state/code preserved; Host spoof, absolute target, body, fragments, path normalization, oversize, unsolicited state ignored); a actual local socket test is useful if cannotflake. No writing production or modifying auth.rs. Describe cancellation/lifecycle requirements separately.\\\\n'''\\nknowledge_spec = '''Propose desktop/gpui/src/native_accounts/knowledge.rs: a focused native knowledge-consent state machine and transport DTOs, preserving Source account-knowledge.ts selection/review/account-generation behavior. No GUI/transport/backend changes. DTOs for account sources/tools/resources use exact Source field names, resource wrapper and action arguments from convex/knowledge.ts. Source tool definitions are JSON.stringify({name,description,inputSchema}) with Source defaults; avoid claiming Rust sorted object serialization has the same JavaScript insertion ordering. Define catalog tools with an explicit helper-produced definition fingerprint string and require exact current fingerprint matches before consent is used. Root's authenticated helper will supply it. Account identity via SessionLease is authoritative operation qualifier. Pure engine should let Root install validated bounded catalog, choose research/model/resources and named allowed tools, prepare exactly one pending review with immutable exact arguments and pretty printable JSON <=16000 UTF16 code units, approve/cancel only the exact pending token and current session/catalog/choice; reject revocation/schema changes/account switch/late responses. Tool calls have no automatic retry; unknown outcome must be surfaced separately from unexecuted cancellation. Preserve resources_allowed and selected source/mode guards. Avoid overbuilding persistence or provider credentials; parent holds authenticated transport. Include deterministic in-module tests for account switch, definition change, disabled mode/tool, argument mutation after review, double approval, one pending at time and lost-network outcome. Tool name/source ID bounds<=256; uri<=4096; catalog<=100 sources/tools per source<=128/resources<=200 matching Source where possible. Inspect Source limit checks precisely; if additional native bounds needed document rather than call them Source identical. Own only knowledge.rs proposal. It is a difficult authorization/race task, prioritize invariant correctness and concise code.\\\\n'''\\nfor name, spec, files in [\\n    ('callback', callback_spec, ['desktop/gpui/src/native_accounts/auth.rs','desktop/gpui/Cargo.toml']),\\n    ('knowledge', knowledge_spec, ['src/utils/account-knowledge.ts','src/utils/mcp-client.ts','convex/knowledge.ts','desktop/gpui/src/native_accounts/auth.rs'])\\n]:\\n    folder = base / name\\n    folder.mkdir(exist_ok=True)\\n    bundle = {}\\n    parts = [shared,spec]\\n    for relative in files:\\n        content = (root / relative).read_text()\\n        bundle[relative] = {'sha256':hashlib.sha256(content.encode()).hexdigest()}\\n        if relative == 'src/utils/mcp-client.ts':\\n            content = '\\\\n'.join(content.splitlines()[29:45])\\n        parts.append('\\\\nSOURCE '+relative+'\\\\n'+content+'\\\\nEND SOURCE\\\\n')\\n    (folder/'input-bundle.json').write_text(json.dumps(bundle,indent=2)+'\\\\n')\\n    (folder/'prompt.txt').write_text(''.join(parts))\\n    print(json.dumps({'task':name,'promptBytes':(folder/'prompt.txt').stat().st_size,'inputs':len(bundle),'files':str(folder)}))\\nPY\",\nworkdir:\"/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne\",max_output_tokens:1200}));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a10ca3-f662-7822-9d58-47f08a989563","create_time":1791213564.493075}}}
