ted plan, the user wanted the existing plan continued rather than a fresh redesign -> preserve shared dirty edits and recover task context before proposing replacement work [Task 1]\n   221\t- when asking whether there was `devenv up` and then asking to “get them done” -> prefer native Devenv processes/tasks over ad-hoc workflow commands for Baste [Task 2]\n   222\t- when requesting profile creation, sign-in, models, and payments and authorizing reuse from other projects -> reuse server-side PKCE/DPoP, wallet, model-catalog, and checkout boundaries; never put provider credentials or durable upstream tokens in the browser [Task 2]\n   223\t\n   224\t## Reusable knowledge\n   225\t\n   226\t- For an interrupted `/side` task, inspect fork/parent relationships and local session metadata first. `list_threads` accepts at most 50; the parent Baste thread was `01a0f9d2-5142-74a3-8cfb-0809f2fe0564`, while the unrelated HyperFrames/Claude session was separate. [Task 1]\n   227\t- Saved Projects live in `site/src/components/studio/flows/projects.tsx`, client API `site/src/lib/projects.ts`, server wiring `src/gui/api.ts`, and persistence `src/projects/{commands,store,repair-lock}.ts`. The verified implementation supports account/DID isolation, CSRF-protected writes, receipts, stale-revision rejection, restore, and lock recovery. [Task 1]\n   228\t- A missing import that now exists can be stale Vite SSR state: run `devenv processes restart site`, then inspect rendered HTML for `studio-main` and browser console—not just HTTP 200. The repair command is `node dist/src/projects/repair-lock.js --project <id> [--account <did>] --server-stopped`, only after every writer is stopped. [Task 1]\n   229\t- Intended Baste workflow is `devenv shell`, `devenv tasks run baste:install`, then `devenv up`; API/site are intended at 3456/5173, with `/gui/` and `/docs/`. It was documented but not runtime-verified in the scaffold rollout. [Task 2]\n   230\t- `src/notorganic/server.ts` keeps PKCE/DPoP transport, HttpOnly `baste_session`, CSRF, verified account/models/wallet/checkout calls server-side. Hosted generation/judgement fails closed and does not silently fall back to local BYOK; checkout accepts only provider-advertised IDs and HTTPS return origins. [Task 2]\n   231\t\n   232\t## Failures and how to do differently\n   233\t\n   234\t- A development error page can return HTTP 200 -> inspect `<title>Error</title>`, `Cannot find module`, expected app markers, and console output before treating the preview as healthy. [Task 1]\n   235\t- Do not infer production readiness from Baste build/test success: live signup, callback, funded generation, checkout, webhook, provider registration, and deployment were not verified. In-memory sessions expire after eight hours and need shared storage or affinity for multi-replica production. [Task 2]\n   236\t- `npm outdated` failed with `EAI_AGAIN`; retry with working registry access before calling dependencies current. Inspect Baste and provider `git status`/diff before assuming the long-running provider patch applied; provider typecheck still needed a `baste` first-party product entry. [Task 2]\n   237\t\n   238\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/keating documentation visual audit and Textbook/OpenTUI workshop\n   239\tscope: Keep Keating documentation grounded in current product evidence and use the offline Textbook workshop to exercise production Sacred TUI components alongside Storybook.\n   240\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating; reuse_rule=reinspect current docs/assets, OpenTUI/Textbook version compatibility, fixture coverage, and actual browser evidence before calling captures or interactivity current.\n   241\t\n   242\t## Task 1: Audit current documentation visuals and reorganize guidance\n   243\t\n   244\t### rollout_summary_files\n   245\t\n   246\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/10/01/rollout-2026-10-01T01-