pture.mjs`, `scripts/capture-web-clips.mjs`, and `docs/tui-*.tape`. Key missing states are current classroom/onboarding, provider/offline-download, credit recovery, completed feedback, assignment delivery, populated TUI, and desktop/mobile learner surfaces. [Task 1]\n   270\t- Record capture commit, date, viewport, surface, fixture/live status, and visible state. Existing screenshot validation checks dimensions/captions but not release freshness. [Task 1]\n   271\t- `textbook-sh@0.2.0` needs an `@opentui/core` `0.4.3` root override for Keating. `bun run textbook -- --web --host 127.0.0.1 --port 6007 --cwd textbook --pattern '**/*.stories.ts'` exposes `/healthz` and `/api/stories`; the workshop is offline/fixture-based and never starts Pi, inference, real sessions, credentials, or file mutation. [Task 2]\n   272\t- The 12 `Keating/Transcript` and `Keating/Sidebar` stories exercise production `SacredTranscriptRenderable` and `createSacredSidebar`; `bun run textbook:check` renders every story at 60x20 and 120x36. Sacred tests passed 9/9, and the docs build produced 16 pages and 34 inline screenshots. [Task 2]\n   273\t\n   274\t## Failures and how to do differently\n   275\t\n   276\t- Sandbox local binding initially raised `EPERM`; permitted local binding worked. Browser inspection was unavailable, so do not infer interactive browser validation from health/catalog checks. [Task 2]\n   277\t- `TextBuffer is destroyed` appeared during OpenTUI teardown -> await asynchronous highlighting and treat `console.error` during render/destruction as a failed story check. [Task 2]\n   278\t\n   279\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/keating architecture audit and bounded TabPFN online adaptation\n   280\tscope: Explain Keating’s actual teaching/policy architecture and evolve activity selection through privacy-bounded background TabPFN inference without claiming causal learning, provider retraining, or live integration that was not tested.\n   281\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogene