e and underlying problem, make coherent prototypes autonomously, and return genuinely distinct working alternatives for the user to judge.\n   415\tapplies_to: workflow=user collaboration across projects; reuse_rule=apply when the user supplies intent/context and asks for best judgement or alternatives, but do not substitute agent confidence for user acceptance.\n   416\t\n   417\t## Task 1: Preserve the user’s evolving intent-first design workflow\n   418\t\n   419\t### rollout_summary_files\n   420\t\n   421\t- rollout_summaries/2026-10-02T00-14-41-Rkbe-intent_first_prototyping_prompting_workflow.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/10/01/rollout-2026-10-01T20-14-41-01a0f9f6-93bb-7e81-89ce-93463a016870.jsonl, updated_at=2026-10-02T00:15:59+00:00, thread_id=01a0f9f6-93bb-7e81-89ce-93463a016870, success; workflow preference assessed, not quantitatively measured)\n   422\t\n   423\t### keywords\n   424\t\n   425\t- intent behind the solution, use its best judgement, three separate solutions, prototyping, fluid organization, joyful interaction, fewer intuitive flags, human in the loop\n   426\t\n   427\t## User preferences\n   428\t\n   429\t- when the user describes “the intent behind the solution of the problem instead of describing the fix,” including what they are struggling with -> understand the underlying outcome before selecting implementation details [Task 1]\n   430\t- when the desired experience is fluid organization, joyful interaction, and common workflows with “fewer or intuitive flags” -> use those as acceptance criteria for defaults, wording, feedback, and interaction—not decorative prose [Task 1]\n   431\t- when asked to “use its best judgement” and “come up with three separate solutions” -> proceed when context is sufficient and make alternatives materially different in assumptions or strategy, not cosmetic variants [Task 1]\n   432\t- when the user is “prototyping the whole way through ... less human in the loop” -> build inspectable prototypes autonomously, then reserve their attention for comparison and experiential acceptance [Task 1]\n   433\t\n   434\t## Reusable knowledge\n   435\t\n   436\t- Intent-rich prompts supply a decision framework for coordinated product choices. Preserve recurring principles and rationale; “common CLI workflows should require little flag recall” is more reusable than one flag change. [Task 1]\n   437\t\n   438\t## Failures and how to do differently\n   439\t\n   440\t- This pattern was recognized from prior work, not measured as an increasing behavioral trend. Reduced human involvement does not eliminate evaluation: return for comparison/acceptance because a coherent prototype can still miss the intended experience. [Task 1]\n   441\t\n   442\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/baste Graphite procedural backgrounds, Material room, and Devenv recovery\n   443\tscope: Produce quiet atelier-grade procedural assets, verify the Material room, and diagnose Baste local startup without mistaking orphaned processes for source/configuration defects.\n   444\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/baste; reuse_rule=recheck the installed Graphite engine, current asset inventory, active listeners, and process ancestry before rendering or altering Baste configuration.\n   445\t\n   446\t## Task 1: Connect Graphite and create several Baste background directions\n   447\t\n   448\t### rollout_summary_files\n   449\t\n   450\t- rollout_summaries/2026-10-02T01-22-30-Cnbg-graphite_baste_material_room.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/baste, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/10/01/rollout-2026-10-01T21-22-30-01a0fa34-aa54-7c01-bfed-1339d8537436.jsonl, updated_at=2026-10-02T05:33:30+00:00, thread_id=01a0fa34-aa54-7c01-bfed-1339d8537436, partial; Material room/browser QA passed, Graphite engine-render proof remains incomplete)\n   451\t\n   452\t### keywords\n   453\t\n   454\t- editor.graphite.art, graphite-editor-mcp, graphite-art-mcp, graphite-editor, graphene-cli, CLI_NOT_FOUND, render.mjs, graphite-experiments-20261001, flax linen, cutting room, chalk draft, ink selvedge\n   455\t\n   456\t## Task 2: Build and verify the Baste Material room\n   457\t\n   458\t### rollout_summary_files\n   459\t\n   460\t- rollout_summaries/2026-10-02T01-22-30-Cnbg-graphite_baste_material_room.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/baste, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/10/01/rollout-2026-10-01T21-22-30-01a0fa34-aa54-7c01-bfed-1339d8537436.jsonl, updated_at=2026-10-02T05:33:30+00:00, thread_id=01a0fa34-aa54-7c01-bfed-1339d8537436, success; build, typecheck, lint, recipe, browser, and gallery-download checks passed)\n   461\t\n   462\t### keywords\n   463\t\n   464\t- /materials/, perceptual color blending, hue rotation, pointer bending, tap ripples, PNG export, wardrobe button, flexShrink, 390x844, verification-summary.json\n   465\t\n   466\t## Task 3: Diagnose and recover `devenv up` after an orphaned API process\n   467\t\n   468\t### rollout_summary_files\n   469\t\n   470\t- rollout_summaries/2026-10-02T12-04-09-pIR9-baste_devenv_up_orphan_api_port.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/baste, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/10/02/rollout-2026-10-02T08-04-09-01a0fc80-1c09-7c80-9142-ee3afd2325b7.jsonl, updated_at=2026-10-02T12:09:06+00:00, thread_id=01a0fc80-1c09-7c80-9142-ee3afd2325b7, success; two foreground starts and clean port release verified)\n   471\t\n   472\t### keywords\n   473\t\n   474\t- devenv up, EADDRINUSE, 127.0.0.1:3456, BASTE_API_PORT, scripts/runtime.mjs, devenv processes list, kill -TERM, /api/health, /gui/\n   475\t\n   476\t## User preferences\n   477\t\n   478\t- when visual work is needed, the user said “editor.graphite.art is a great site to use and create beautiful procedural backgrounds and images” -> consider Graphite first for editable/procedural backgrounds, while distinguishing it from the unrelated code-review product [Task 1]\n   479\t- when requesting “a few different background options for baste” -> deliver materially distinct directions, not variations of one optimized result; flax linen, cutting room, chalk draft, and ink selvedge are an established starting vocabulary [Task 1]\n   480\t\n   481\t## Reusable knowledge\n   482\t\n   483\t- Baste’s quiet atelier palette is paper `#F1ECE2`, ink `#1C1B19`, thread `#D2402A`, and chalk `#2F55A4`; backgrounds should retain reading space. The local renderer is `assets/output/graphite-baste-20261001/source/render.mjs` and generated studies/QA live below `assets/output/graphite-experiments-20261001/`. [Task 1]\n   484\t- `graphite-editor-mcp` is for headless deterministic node-graph rendering, node discovery, document validation, and batch variants; `graphite-art-mcp` targets visible editable layers. The configured local server is `graphite-editor`. [Task 1]\n   485\t- `/materials/` has six live procedural backgrounds plus recipe/export interaction. Browser QA at 390x844 found no width overflow; the wardrobe glyph needs `paddingInline: 0` and `flexShrink: 0` to avoid collapsing. [Task 2]\n   486\t- Baste Devenv defines `api` (default 3456) and `site` (5173); `scripts/runtime.mjs api` launches `src/cli.ts gui --port $BASTE_API_PORT`, and site proxies `/api` to it. [Task 3]\n   487\t\n   488\t## Failures and how to do differently\n   489\t\n   490\t- `CLI_NOT_FOUND` or MCP registration does not prove Graphite can render -> first confirm the connector’s `graphene-cli` exists, then obtain a validated render artifact with its hash. Native editor pointer behavior was not tested. [Task 1]\n   491\t- If Playwright `locator('header')` matches two nodes, scope it or use `.first()`; write build QA output to an absolute existing directory. [Task 2]\n   492\t- `listen EADDRINUSE: address already in use 127.0.0.1:3456` is not evidence of a Devenv/source defect -> inspect listener and ancestry. If it is an orphan from this checkout and `devenv processes list` says no manager, terminate only that identified process group, restart, check `/api/health` and `/gui/`, then run `devenv down` to prove release. Restricted sandboxes may require host listener inspection because Nix/netlink access is unavailable. [Task 3]\n   493\t\n   494\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/twyne fluid manuscript editor, House attention policy, and Claude-work continuation\n   495\tscope: Continue and critique Twyne’s in-flow writing surfaces while preserving deliberate side-panel browsing, authorship, scoped validation boundaries, and return-to-writing continuity.\n   496\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne; reuse_rule=reinspect the dirty worktree, running Vite server, current House/flow contracts, and authenticated/model/sync behavior before treating local fixture results as complete product proof.\n   497\t\n   498\t## Task 1: Continue and verify Claude’s unfinished fluid-editor UI\n   499\t\n   500\t### rollout_summary_files\n   501\t\n   502\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/30/rollout-2026-09-30T02-30-15-01a0f101-b3b4-7e41-9e3c-8d3ec580aba0.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-30T08:46:14+00:00, thread_id=01a0f101-b3b4-7e41-9e3c-8d3ec580aba0, partial; scoped E2E/format/diff/TypeScript checks passed, full typecheck remained blocked)\n   503\t\n   504\t### keywords\n   505\t\n   506\t- all in flow, flow-surface.tsx, flow-ribbon.tsx, manuscript-panel.tsx, twyne-editor.tsx, margin-surface.ts, MARGIN_SLOT_EVENT, OPEN_MARGIN_THREAD_EVENT, pneumatic post, galley slip, way in, 5180\n   507\t\n   508\t## Task 2: Assess attention-policy and House-model direction\n   509\t\n   510\t### rollout_summary_files\n   511\t\n   512\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/30/rollout-2026-09-30T02-30-15-01a0f101-b3b4-7e41-9e3c-8d3ec580aba0.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-30T08:46:14+00:00, thread_id=01a0f101-b3b4-7e41-9e3c-8d3ec580aba0, success; source, plan, tests, browser evidence, and gaps compared)\n   513\t\n   514\t### keywords\n   515\t\n   516\t- shared attention policy, flow-conductor.ts, House, Collection, Folio, dossier, amendments, flow-state.ts, flow-profile.ts, flow-connections.ts, TF-IDF, Jev, stuckPauseMs\n   517\t\n   518\t## User preferences\n   519\t\n   520\t- when shaping the manuscript experience, the user wants it “all in flow,” with the side panel retained for deliberate browsing -> prioritize inline margin surfaces, quiet queues, and progressive disclosure over new panel-first workflows [Task 1]\n   521\t- on large Twyne features, the user explicitly prefers UI/design work first and allows backend/plumbing to be delegated to Codex -> preserve that sequencing [Task 1]\n   522\t\n   523\t## Reusable knowledge\n   524\t\n   525\t- The flow surface reserves the margin slot and the editor mounts/tracks its conversation card through `MARGIN_SLOT_EVENT` and `OPEN_MARGIN_THREAD_EVENT`. The visible desk includes held items (pneumatic post), completed-focus galley slips, a `working`/`settling`/`flow`/`stuck` ink ribbon, and a way-in card. The contract is in `docs/flow-and-context.md`. [Task 1]\n   526\t- The strongest direction is one shared attention policy for comments, sources, prior writing, suggestions, and charter items; flow mode suppresses ambient interruptions. House → Collection → Folio → dossier/amendments preserves provenance, while an explicit amendment protects the writer from silent dossier rewrites. [Task 2]\n   527\t- `flow-state.ts` combines cadence, deletion/active ratio, pause duration, and struggle/reaching context; defaults are `stuckPauseMs: 18_000`, `exitPauseMs: 25_000`, `flowMs: 90_000`. `flow-profile.ts` uses Laplace-smoothed engagement, and `flow-connections.ts` only proposes local TF-IDF candidates for Jev semantic confirmation. [Task 2]\n   528\t\n   529\t## Failures and how to do differently\n   530\t\n   531\t- Scoped success is not full-project success: unrelated docs typing issues (`bun:test`/Bun types and `marked`) blocked full TypeScript. Report the focused E2E, formatting, diff check, and temporary scoped TypeScript result precisely. [Task 1]\n   532\t- Seed a folio in IndexedDB via `/house/` before screenshot/browser checks at `/editor/`; do not start another Vite server while the app is already at `http://127.0.0.1:5180`, as shared optimization can break it. Preserve the heavily dirty, behind-main worktree additively. [Task 1]\n   533\t- Do not equate pauses/deletions with being stuck or card opens with benefit. Next work should make interventions complete a small task, improve return-to-writing continuity and explicit editorial relationships, consolidate large coordinators, and prove live model use plus authenticated two-device Convex sync separately from fixtures/mocks. [Task 2]\n   534\t\n   535\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/keating Railway public-endpoint abuse hardening and GunJS boundaries\n   536\tscope: Audit observed Railway exposure separately from static risk, protect public expensive endpoints without degrading ordinary browsing, and keep GunJS within its encrypted small-record sync role.\n   537\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating; reuse_rule=reinspect current deployment/code/configuration and actual Railway metrics before attributing traffic/cost or claiming protections are live.\n   538\t\n   539\t## Task 1: Explain GunJS architecture and activation status\n   540\t\n   541\t### rollout_summary_files\n   542\t\n   543\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/30/rollout-2026-09-30T06-21-33-01a0f1d5-7623-7fc3-832b-d5e571874fcd.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-30T18:40:51+00:00, thread_id=01a0f1d5-7623-7fc3-832b-d5e571874fcd, success; source-backed architecture answer)\n   544\t\n   545\t### keywords\n   546\t\n   547\t- GunJS, browser-sync.ts, gun-transport.ts, sync-coordinator.ts, learner-sync.ts, VITE_KEATING_GUN_PEERS, keating-encrypted-sync-v1, AES-GCM, 32 KiB, 10 MiB\n   548\t\n   549\t## Task 2: Audit and harden Railway public endpoints\n   550\t\n   551\t### rollout_summary_files\n   552\t\n   553\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/30/rollout-2026-09-30T06-21-33-01a0f1d5-7623-7fc3-832b-d5e571874fcd.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-30T18:40:51+00:00, thread_id=01a0f1d5-7623-7fc3-832b-d5e571874fcd, partial; infrastructure is live, application protections await deployment/smoke)\n   554\t\n   555\t### keywords\n   556\t\n   557\t- KEATING_ABUSE_REDIS_URL, public-abuse.ts, bounded-body.ts, chat-proxy-policy.ts, public-oauth-limits.ts, Nitro handlers, Railway CDN, Under Attack Mode, Retry-After, 503, 429\n   558\t\n   559\t## User preferences\n   560\t\n   561\t- when the user asked to “add the cdn caching for this project and also twyne” -> favor invisible server-side limits and CDN controls that preserve ordinary browsing; do not add CAPTCHAs or sign-in friction unless explicitly needed [Task 2]\n   562\t- when the user said “look at my traffic” -> distinguish observed Railway traffic/cost samples from static exposure analysis and state sampling or interval limits plainly [Task 2]\n   563\t\n   564\t## Reusable knowledge\n   565\t\n   566\t- GunJS is prepared encrypted cross-device transport, not the primary database/blob store: graph root is `keating-encrypted-sync-v1/accounts/<namespace>`, using AES-GCM, SHA-256, 32 KiB chunks, a 10 MiB snapshot cap, IndexedDB/Rindexed persistence, and HTTP/WebSocket relays. There were no production UI callers for `createBrowserGunSyncSession`, `pushCurrentLearnerData`, or restore helpers; use content-addressed/resumable transfer for large artifacts. [Task 1]\n   567\t- Public protections use distributed Redis limits, bounded streamed body reads, exact provider host/path allowlisting, deadlines, output caps, and concurrency leases. On Railway, missing Redis must fail protected actions closed with `503`/`Retry-After: 10` while ordinary pages stay available; operator-added chat gateways require exact HTTPS origins in `KEATING_CHAT_PROXY_EXTRA_ORIGINS`. [Task 2]\n   568\t- Relevant limits are documented in `docs/public-endpoint-security.md`; the rollout verified 62 focused tests, 9 Redis cross-client tests, TypeScript, Nitro build, and built-server page/OAuth/oversized-body/missing-Redis behavior. Railway Redis, Keating’s Redis reference, CDN for Keating/Twyne, a $75 workspace alert, and service ceilings were configured. [Task 2]\n   569\t\n   570\t## Failures and how to do differently\n   571\t\n   572\t- Nitro’s explicit `handlers` list bypassed automatic discovery of `server/middleware/public-oauth-limits.ts`; register `{ route: \"/**\", middleware: true, handler: \"server/middleware/public-oauth-limits.ts\" }` and test the generated server, not only unit imports. [Task 2]\n   573\t- Railway HTTP logs/metrics can be sampled or reject requested intervals; a 1,000-request sample and current-period cost cannot establish complete bot-cost attribution. The application hardening code was not deployed in this rollout, so do not call endpoint protection live before deployment and production smoke. [Task 2]\n   574\t\n   575\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/keating Jev production 402 diagnosis and TypeSafe BYOK relay\n   576\tscope: Diagnose hosted judgement failures precisely, expose direct TypeSafe/Jev BYOK without leaking credentials, and verify deployed error-path behavior separately from funded provider use.\n   577\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating with hosted judgement at /home/diogenes/Projects/notorganic-provider; reuse_rule=reinspect live gateway funding/budgets, Nitro route registration, provider API contract, and the dirty-tree/deployment state before claiming end-to-end judgement success.\n   578\t\n   579\t## Task 1: Diagnose production judgement 402 and correct the UI error\n   580\t\n   581\t### rollout_summary_files\n   582\t\n   583\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/30/rollout-2026-09-30T13-58-46-01a0f378-0f99-7f51-a002-7878751ae01e.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-30T18:39:51+00:00, thread_id=01a0f378-0f99-7f51-a002-7878751ae01e, success; 402 diagnosis and focused verification)\n   584\t\n   585\t### keywords\n   586\t\n   587\t- Jev, /v1/judgement, HTTP 402, backend-payment-required, insufficient_quota, budget_exceeded, errorForStatus, DraftReviewStatus, draft-gate.ts\n   588\t\n   589\t## Task 2: Add and deploy direct TypeSafe/Jev API-key judgement\n   590\t\n   591\t### rollout_summary_files\n   592\t\n   593\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/30/rollout-2026-09-30T13-58-46-01a0f378-0f99-7f51-a002-7878751ae01e.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-30T18:39:51+00:00, thread_id=01a0f378-0f99-7f51-a002-7878751ae01e, partial; relay and safe live negative paths verified; funded review not run)\n   594\t\n   595\t### keywords\n   596\t\n   597\t- typesafe-judgement, /api/judgement/typesafe, https://api.typesafe.ai/v1/systemone, jev-latest, JudgementSettings, backend-unauthorized, Nitro handlers, 29d7f132-6090-4c8a-a645-bd3c45473c20\n   598\t\n   599\t## User preferences\n   600\t\n   601\t- when the user reported “jev does not seem like it is working in prod,” clarified “the judge model is not configured,” and browser logs showed `/v1/judgement` HTTP 402 -> distinguish configuration, authorization, funding, and request-budget failures; do not trust a generic UI message [Task 1]\n   602\t- when choosing a custom judgement API, the user selected “Direct TypeSafe/Jev API key” -> retain direct BYOK as a visible independent option, not only the Not Organic account path [Task 2]\n   603\t\n   604\t## Reusable knowledge\n   605\t\n   606\t- `packages/learner-contracts/src/judgement/wire.ts:errorForStatus` is the shared mapper: 402 is `backend-payment-required`, 401/403 unauthorized, 429 rate-limited, and 503/529 overloaded. Hosted browser traffic can bypass Keating server logs and go straight to Not Organic, whose judgement gateway maps 402 to `insufficient_quota` or `budget_exceeded`. [Task 1]\n   607\t- Store the TypeSafe key in the existing device provider credential store under `typesafe-judgement`, never in judgement-model settings. The same-origin `POST /api/judgement/typesafe` relay validates origin, bearer-key shape, body/model, size/rate/concurrency limits; sends to the fixed `/v1/systemone` upstream; returns sanitized stable errors; and requires a concrete returned model identity, one attempt, timeout/cancellation, and no calibration by default. [Task 2]\n   608\t- Nitro uses an explicit handlers configuration here: register `{ route: \"/api/judgement/typesafe\", method: \"POST\", handler: \"server/api/judgement/typesafe.post.ts\" }` and prove the live endpoint. Deployment `29d7f132-6090-4c8a-a645-bd3c45473c20` succeeded; missing key produced 401 and deliberately invalid key produced sanitized `backend-unauthorized`. [Task 2]\n   609\t\n   610\t## Failures and how to do differently\n   611\t\n   612\t- Browser requests to hosted judgement bypassed Keating logs, so initial production-log inspection missed the problem -> inspect browser/network evidence and the Not Organic gateway path. Refresh stale GitNexus before relying on its traces. [Task 1]\n   613\t- A deployed UI bundle can coexist with a 404 relay when an explicit Nitro handler is missing -> register the route and check the live endpoint, not only the build/bundle. A funded TypeSafe review was not executed because no user credential was available; do not upgrade safe negative-path proof to provider success. [Task 2]\n   614\t- The direct production upload came from a dirty snapshot with `promotionEligible:false`; report it as deployed, not clean-release/promotion proof. Broad root tests had unrelated failures, so scope claims to the focused judgement/web suites that passed. [Task 2]\n   615\t\n   616\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/twyne Open Graph editorial preview and Seedance desk-scene video\n   617\tscope: Replace generic Twyne social previews with project-bound editorial assets and produce a real physical-motion desk video only when the requested fal Seedance output is available and validated.\n   618\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne; reuse_rule=reinspect current metadata, generated assets, provider balance, and final video evidence before claiming crawler or Seedance completion.\n   619\t\n   620\t## Task 1: Replace the default Open Graph image and verify local desk preview\n   621\t\n   622\t### rollout_summary_files\n   623\t\n   624\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/29/rollout-2026-09-29T17-06-37-01a0eefd-acc3-7f01-a57d-1f767284796b.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-29T23:43:49+00:00, thread_id=01a0eefd-acc3-7f01-a57d-1f767284796b, partial; metadata and an earlier local HyperFrames MP4 were validated, crawler proof remains open)\n   625\t\n   626\t### keywords\n   627\t\n   628\t- opengraph, og:image, TWYNE_SOCIAL_IMAGE, RouterHead, router-head.tsx, seo.ts, twyne-editorial-v2.jpg, magick, twyne-writers-desk-loop-v1.mp4, ffprobe\n   629\t\n   630\t## Task 2: Replace camera shift with fal Seedance 2.5 physical motion\n   631\t\n   632\t### rollout_summary_files\n   633\t\n   634\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/29/rollout-2026-09-29T17-06-37-01a0eefd-acc3-7f01-a57d-1f767284796b.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-29T23:43:49+00:00, thread_id=01a0eefd-acc3-7f01-a57d-1f767284796b, failed/pending; fal rejected before queueing for exhausted balance)\n   635\t\n   636\t### keywords\n   637\t\n   638\t- bytedance/seedance-2.5/image-to-video, Seedance 2.5, fal, SUBMISSION_REJECTED, exhausted balance, seedance-job-v1.json, generate-social-desk-video.ts, twyne-writers-desk-overlay.svg\n   639\t\n   640\t## User preferences\n   641\t\n   642\t- when the user asked for “a much nicer embed with opengraph. use your images” -> create a polished project-bound social asset and wire it into metadata rather than retaining a generic wordmark card [Task 1]\n   643\t- when the user said “use fal to render a video of the scene instead of shift” and “use the seeddance 2.5 video model” -> use `bytedance/seedance-2.5/image-to-video`, with locked overhead physical scene motion and separate sharp branding; a camera shift is not an acceptable substitute [Task 2]\n   644\t- when the user asked to watch the actual scene locally -> provide direct MP4 and preview URLs, not only a still or prototype [Task 1]\n   645\t\n   646\t## Reusable knowledge\n   647\t\n   648\t- Site defaults come from `src/components/router-head/router-head.tsx`, route declarations override them, and social constants belong in `src/utils/seo.ts` with `TWYNE_SITE_ORIGIN=https://twyne.love`. The new source asset is `public/assets/social/twyne-editorial-v2.jpg`; Prettier and ESLint passed, but final crawler/browser proof was not recorded. [Task 1]\n   649\t- The old `twyne-writers-desk-loop-v1.mp4` is a verified 1200×630, 30 fps, 6-second silent H.264 local artifact. Intel Mesa HyperFrames capture required translating Chrome `--use-angle=gl-egl` to `--use-angle=gl`; it is historical camera-shift output, not a Seedance result. [Task 1]\n   650\t- Seedance preparation is resumable: `scripts/generate-social-desk-video.ts` persists `social-preview-video/seedance-job-v1.json` before submission to avoid duplicate charges. Request 720p, 6 seconds, silent, high-bitrate H.264 with the clean background as start/end; composite `twyne-writers-desk-overlay.svg` in HyperFrames, never in generated footage. [Task 2]\n   651\t\n   652\t## Failures and how to do differently\n   653\t\n   654\t- `sharp` failed from missing `libstdc++.so.6` and Pillow was unavailable; use `/home/diogenes/.nix-profile/bin/magick` for conversion. [Task 1]\n   655\t- fal returned `HTTP 403: User is locked. Reason: Exhausted balance.` before queueing. After credits are restored, run `rtk proxy bun scripts/generate-social-desk-video.ts`, then render/check and visually inspect frames; no raw or final Seedance MP4 currently exists. [Task 2]\n   656\t\n   657\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/keating launch-film composition, landing integration, and Railway playback proof\n   658\tscope: Update Keating's canonical launch film as an audiovisual composition, connect it to the actual landing page, and verify live playback rather than reporting a local render as deployed.\n   659\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating; reuse_rule=reinspect video source/generated output, landing consumer, current Railway deployment, and cache state before a subsequent media release.\n   660\t\n   661\t## Task 1: Edit, deploy, and verify the canonical launch film\n   662\t\n   663\t### rollout_summary_files\n   664\t\n   665\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/29/rollout-2026-09-29T17-16-16-01a0ef06-8438-7c73-bda3-78739f0b13d3.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-30T10:06:14+00:00, thread_id=01a0ef06-8438-7c73-bda3-78739f0b13d3, success; live deployment and browser playback verified)\n   666\t\n   667\t### keywords\n   668\t\n   669\t- video/keating-launch, index.template.html, scripts/build.mjs, wall-x-first, wall-x-second, LandingIntro.tsx, keating-4-launch.mp4, .railwayignore, Playwriter, bf5957f16e1c\n   670\t\n   671\t## User preferences\n   672\t\n   673\t- when the user asked to “add music” and make the wall “look like a response from an llm” with an X -> implement visible audiovisual beats in the composition, not merely narration/copy changes [Task 1]\n   674\t- when the user said “we should be using this in the laning if we aren't already” and then “deploy” -> verify the canonical landing consumer, cache invalidation, remote deployment, public asset, and browser playback [Task 1]\n   675\t\n   676\t## Reusable knowledge\n   677\t\n   678\t- Edit `video/keating-launch/src/index.template.html`; `index.html` is generated by `scripts/build.mjs`. The quiz beat uses an AI prompt card, `AI assistant` label, and `#wall-x-first`/`#wall-x-second` SVG X strokes. The final MP4 was 1920×1080, 30 fps, 69.5 seconds, H.264/AAC, with full decode and sampled frames checked. [Task 1]\n   679\t- `web/src/components/LandingIntro.tsx` consumes `/tapes/keating-4-launch.mp4?v=bf5957f16e1c`; public checksum matched local, and Playwriter confirmed unmuted 69.5-second playback with no media error on `https://keating.help/`. Deployment `e6eb53cb-2d88-4f91-84dd-ba696012198f` succeeded. [Task 1]\n   680\t\n   681\t## Failures and how to do differently\n   682\t\n   683\t- fal/Lyria returned exhausted-balance 403; check balance or reuse suitable local media before retrying. GitNexus `UNKNOWN` callers are not safety proof—confirm generated-video dependencies via direct source search. [Task 1]\n   684\t- Railway failed at 502 then 413 for a 282MB temporary bundle. Excluding `web/artwork/` in `.railwayignore` unblocked deployment. An old service-worker/cache served stale media; use a versioned query parameter and bypass cache temporarily for validation. [Task 1]\n   685\t\n   686\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/twyne illuminated initials, Typst proof, and editorial-native tooling\n   687\tscope: Make Typst authoring/proof and generated initial artwork feel native to Twyne’s paper/ink/vermilion writing desk while preserving editable manuscript text, export fidelity, and explicit publication gates.\n   688\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne; reuse_rule=reinspect current editor/export contracts, actual generated-asset inventory, and landing-image approval before changing styling, claiming asset coverage, or publishing.\n   689\t\n   690\t## Task 1: Redesign native Typst source/proof tooling and proof theme\n   691\t\n   692\t### rollout_summary_files\n   693\t\n   694\t- rollout_summaries/2026-09-29T02-53-14-wfgW-twyne_typst_native_tooling_proof_styling.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/28/rollout-2026-09-28T22-53-14-01a0eb14-a63e-75c1-840d-6c9f28175f26.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-29T03:56:43+00:00, thread_id=01a0eb14-a63e-75c1-840d-6c9f28175f26, partial; final browser/typecheck claim was reported, earlier focused E2E setup failed)\n   695\t\n   696\t### keywords\n   697\t\n   698\t- Twypst, typst-workspace, typst-code-editor, compositor-toolbar, Reicon, CodeMirror, proof, HTML export, paper-ink, Typeset page N, BUN_TMPDIR\n   699\t\n   700\t## Task 2: Add illuminated initials, optimize AVIF assets, and hold publication for landing-image choice\n   701\t\n   702\t### rollout_summary_files\n   703\t\n   704\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/29/rollout-2026-09-29T00-33-25-01a0eb70-5e56-7400-88f6-69c619eb553f.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-29T19:26:16+00:00, thread_id=01a0eb70-5e56-7400-88f6-69c619eb553f, success; editor/export and rendered pages validated, publication awaits user landing-image selection)\n   705\t\n   706\t### keywords\n   707\t\n   708\t- illuminated-initials, drop-cap, imagegen, transparent-assets, AVIF, Typst, browser-print, twyne-release-023, landing-options, manuscript garden\n   709\t\n   710\t## User preferences\n   711\t\n   712\t- when the user said the Typst UI looked “tagged on as an afterthought” and requested “much better tooling that also appears visually native to the rest of the editor” -> reuse Twyne’s established paper/ink/vermilion toolbar language rather than creating a separate Typst visual system [Task 1]\n   713\t- when the user requested “good icons in the tool bar” -> use semantic Reicon-backed controls with accessible names and tooltips [Task 1]\n   714\t- when the user asked for “auto illuminated initials,” “30 of them,” “kind of as svgs,” and “high quality” -> provide a coherent transparent, reduction-safe family, preserve editable text, and explicitly distinguish raster output from true SVG [Task 2]\n   715\t- when a creative landing image still awaits a user choice -> commit verified work if requested but hold publication; do not choose or overwrite the hero autonomously [Task 2]\n   716\t\n   717\t## Reusable knowledge\n   718\t\n   719\t- Preserve Typst E2E accessible names `Write`, `Source`, `Proof`, `Apply source`, `Manuscript workspace`, `Typst source`, and `Typeset page N`. The workspace sources are `src/components/editor/typst-workspace.tsx`, `typst-workspace.css`, and `typst-code-editor.ts`; established toolbar/icon conventions are `compositor-panel.tsx`, `global.css`, `src/components/ui/icon.tsx`, and `src/utils/icon-system.ts`. [Task 1]\n   720\t- Source tools can use CodeMirror commands for undo/redo, find, go-to-line, comment toggling, snippets, wrapping, cursor state, and download; proof uses zoom/status controls. Align proof defaults with `src/utils/exchange.ts`: Lora/Libre Baskerville/DM Sans families, paper-toned surface, ink, vermilion, restrained rules, editorial spacing, locally bundled fonts, and no external font requests. [Task 1]\n   721\t- The current drop cap is CSS-driven at `.twyne-editor .ProseMirror > p:first-of-type::first-letter`; artwork must layer around the editable opening character, not replace manuscript text. Relevant helpers include `src/utils/illuminated-initials.ts`, `print-ornaments.ts`, `page-ornaments.ts`, and `src/utils/typst/decorative-assets.ts`. [Task 2]\n   722\t- For transparent initials, explicitly prohibit parchment, frames, shadows, glow, captions, watermarks, and extra lettering. Normalize generated output before committing; generated workspace assets must not remain only in an image-generation cache. AVIF conversion was reported as 62.49 MB to 12.14 MB. The isolated commit in `/tmp/twyne-release-023` passed the full 1,628-test suite, production build, and `git diff --check`, but was not published. [Task 2]\n   723\t\n   724\t## Failures and how to do differently\n   725\t\n   726\t- A focused Playwright run was blocked first by sandbox frontend startup and then by missing `.ProseMirror` during seed/setup. Treat the later claim of four passing browser checks as reported evidence needing an independent rerun after final changes; four existing lint warnings also remained. `bun add` can need `BUN_TMPDIR=/tmp BUN_INSTALL_CACHE_DIR=/tmp/twyne-bun-cache`. [Task 1]\n   727\t- The project-local Impeccable context path was absent; use `/home/diogenes/.agents/skills/impeccable/scripts/context.mjs`. Enumerate, persist, and inspect every requested initial rather than inferring a family is complete from one master asset. [Task 2]\n   728\t- A successful isolated commit is not publication. The gallery at `public/assets/landing/options-2026-09/index.html` contains five options; option 3 “the manuscript garden” was only an assistant recommendation and publication remains on hold. [Task 2]\n   729\t\n   730\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/twyne landing artwork, avatars, editor actions, and fluid House work\n   731\tscope: Apply Twyne's editorial UI direction across landing imagery, writer identity, compact editor actions, and the in-flow/House experience without overstating incomplete browser or sync proof.\n   732\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne; reuse_rule=reinspect the live worktree, SSR route, current editor/store contracts, and authenticated profile flow before claiming UI or persistence completion.\n   733\t\n   734\t## Task 1: Use the selected landing artwork and provide AVIF profile avatars\n   735\t\n   736\t### rollout_summary_files\n   737\t\n   738\t- rollout_summaries/2026-09-29T16-46-26-rtLH-twyne_landing_artwork_and_profile_avatars.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/29/rollout-2026-09-29T12-46-26-01a0ee0f-7a28-7c02-91fa-0e4cc2271ce9.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-29T19:27:49+00:00, thread_id=01a0ee0f-7a28-7c02-91fa-0e4cc2271ce9, partial; landing composition planned, avatar code/assets added but final browser and checks remain open)\n   739\t\n   740\t### keywords\n   741\t\n   742\t- option-01, option-03, option-05, The editorial table, The manuscript garden, The impression, landing-page.tsx, WorkspaceTour, engraved-2026-09, image/avif, handleDefaultAvatar\n   743\t\n   744\t## Task 2: Standardize Reicon editor actions and flag an unfiled dossier\n   745\t\n   746\t### rollout_summary_files\n   747\t\n   748\t- rollout_summaries/2026-09-29T19-19-02-GE0c-twyne_editor_icon_and_dossier_label_polish.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/29/rollout-2026-09-29T15-19-02-01a0ee9b-2e36-7f43-904b-e4af84b76ebc.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-29T19:23:21+00:00, thread_id=01a0ee9b-2e36-7f43-904b-e4af84b76ebc, partial; icon/state implementation checked, final copy and browser spacing unverified)\n   749\t\n   750\t### keywords\n   751\t\n   752\t- Reicon, icon-system.ts, account-menu.tsx, folio-menu.tsx, Create dossier, Refine dossier, dossier-action-pending, prefers-reduced-motion\n   753\t\n   754\t## Task 3: Build House first and establish one in-flow interaction surface\n   755\t\n   756\t### rollout_summary_files\n   757\t\n   758\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/29/rollout-2026-09-29T21-21-53-01a0efe7-60c8-7c41-aeae-38137ec6cbde.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-29T18:54:27+00:00, thread_id=01a0efe7-60c8-7c41-aeae-38137ec6cbde, partial; route/flow/backend work exists but SSR, browser, codegen, and deployment proof are open)\n   759\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/29/rollout-2026-09-29T21-21-53-01a0efe7-60e5-7fa1-b18e-e9b4851fd5d4.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-30T10:14:40+00:00, thread_id=01a0efe7-60e5-7fa1-b18e-e9b4851fd5d4, partial; UI/architecture exists, but flow/House browser-sync proof remains bounded)\n   760\t\n   761\t### keywords\n   762\t\n   763\t- House, Collection, Folio, Editions, Charter, Amendments, Revisions, flow-conductor.ts, FlowSurface, twyne:zen-mode, house-sync.ts, convex/house.ts, cover lookups\n   764\t\n   765\t## Task 4: Fix immediate-navigation draft loss and publish v0.23.3\n   766\t\n   767\t### rollout_summary_files\n   768\t\n   769\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/29/rollout-2026-09-29T21-21-53-01a0efe7-60e5-7fa1-b18e-e9b4851fd5d4.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-30T10:14:40+00:00, thread_id=01a0efe7-60e5-7fa1-b18e-e9b4851fd5d4, success; release/production navigation replay passed, authenticated flows remain unexercised)\n   770\t\n   771\t### keywords\n   772\t\n   773\t- v0.23.3, draft-navigation.e2e.ts, pagehide, crash-mirror.ts, anti-tabula-rasa.ts, IndexedDB, lifecycle flush, folio-scoped, b9a3579995635d066215291aa70350c3856d87a4\n   774\t\n   775\t## User preferences\n   776\t\n   777\t- when the user said “i really like one three and five, I would like those to be used” and approved the sequence -> use option 3 “The manuscript garden” as hero, option 1 “The editorial table” at the editorial-room introduction, and option 5 “The impression” at the closing invitation; use existing landing surfaces rather than a carousel [Task 1]\n   778\t- when the user followed avatar work with “avif” -> use AVIF assets and correct `image/avif` references when feasible [Task 1]\n   779\t- when the user said File and dossier text was “too similar” and requested a pulse -> use semantically mapped Reicon controls, concise differentiated copy, and subtle reduced-motion-safe missing-state emphasis; the later “the text is a bit redundant” means the final wording remains unresolved [Task 2]\n   780\t- when the user said “the side panel is fine but i want to get everything all in flow” -> prioritize inline/margin surfaces and quiet queues, not panel-first navigation [Task 3]\n   781\t- when the user said “go User interface first here, the backend you can send off to codex” -> prioritize the writer-facing UI and use bounded backend delegation rather than delaying the visible slice [Task 3]\n   782\t- when the user interrupted test work with “just do the house page first” -> complete the visible writer-facing House route before expanding into planned tests [Task 3]\n   783\t\n   784\t## Reusable knowledge\n   785\t\n   786\t- Landing page already has `.landing-hero`, `WorkspaceTour`, preview plates, and `.landing-closing-photo`; integrate chosen imagery there. AVIF avatars are `public/assets/avatars/engraved-2026-09/{owl,fox,hare,raven}.avif`; settings fetches/wraps them through the existing upload path, while `account-menu.tsx` follows `api.profiles.getMyHandle` updates. A claimed Twyne handle is required and this is separate from a Not Organic account profile. [Task 1]\n   787\t- Extend `src/utils/icon-system.ts` and render through `src/components/ui/icon.tsx`, not raw symbols/SVGs. Pending dossier state is `store.hydrated && store.activeFolioId && !store.brief`; `dossier-action-pending` pulses only under `prefers-reduced-motion: no-preference`, otherwise uses a steady vermilion border. [Task 2]\n   788\t- Existing flow primitives are `struggle-tracker.ts`, `struggle-signals.ts`, `margin-rail.tsx`, `background-research.ts`, `user-comments.ts`, and `twyne:zen-mode`. New work is `flow-conductor.ts`, `flow-surface.tsx`, House model/store/sync, and `src/routes/house/index.tsx`; use Twyne palette tokens plus `.dept-label`, `.btn-paper`, `.btn-press`. Cover lookup sends only a Jev-selected title, never draft text. Reconcile legacy comment/persona popovers and anchor widgets with `FlowSurface`: route to the flow card when available and reserve popovers for narrow/docked/offline fallback. [Task 3]\n   789\t- The v0.23.3 draft-loss fix uses explicit departure state, lifecycle flushing, a folio-scoped crash mirror, matching acknowledgements, enqueue-time timestamps, transactional recovery, and remote-restoration/native-Typst protections without per-keystroke synchronous serialization. It passed 3/3 browser regressions, 56 focused tests, 1,751 application tests, and production replay on both domains (4/4 immediate-navigation preserves, 2/2 settled-autosave controls). [Task 4]\n   790\t\n   791\t## Failures and how to do differently\n   792\t\n   793\t- The approved landing sequence was only planned; inspect the current git state and browser before saying it shipped. After the final avatar MIME correction rerun Prettier, ESLint for settings/account menu, and `bunx tsc --noEmit --incremental false`; authenticated upload/account-menu proof was not done. [Task 1]\n   794\t- Browser tooling was unavailable for icon work, so source checks do not establish visual spacing. Do not call the remaining dossier-copy request resolved without a user decision or an inspected surrounding control vocabulary. [Task 2]\n   795\t- `/house/` initially hung under SSR and Chrome integration was unavailable; typecheck/source evidence does not prove the route or flow interactions. Convex codegen failed offline and generated declarations were edited manually: rerun official codegen, targeted route/browser proof, and sync/deployment checks before relying on this feature. Do not show both legacy modal/popover and flow card for one interaction, and do not add deferred flow tests before the House page is visibly complete. [Task 3]\n   796\t- Anonymous UI checks after v0.23.3 do not prove authenticated provider exchange, cloud sync, paid AI, or microphone behavior. [Task 4]\n   797\t\n   798\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/twyne Devenv port separation\n   799\tscope: Prevent `devenv up` from colliding with standalone Twyne Vite and Storybook processes while keeping configuration and proof boundaries explicit.\n   800\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne; reuse_rule=recheck live listeners, `devenv.nix`, package scripts, and the full app path before treating process startup as full application proof.\n   801\t\n   802\t## Task 1: Separate Devenv frontend and Storybook ports\n   803\t\n   804\t### rollout_summary_files\n   805\t\n   806\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/29/rollout-2026-09-29T16-52-56-01a0eef1-251c-7410-a715-47ba2909ea0c.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-29T21:03:08+00:00, thread_id=01a0eef1-251c-7410-a715-47ba2909ea0c, partial; individual processes and task evaluation passed, full `devenv up`/app behavior unverified)\n   807\t\n   808\t### keywords\n   809\t\n   810\t- devenv.nix, package.json, TWYNE_DEV_PORT, TWYNE_STORYBOOK_PORT, 5173, 6006, 5180, 6010, readiness probes, devenv tasks list\n   811\t\n   812\t## User preferences\n   813\t\n   814\t- when the user reported “the application does not work and crashes because it starts on the same port with devenv up” -> reproduce and remove the actual coexistence collision before pursuing unrelated app changes [Task 1]\n   815\t\n   816\t## Reusable knowledge\n   817\t\n   818\t- Standalone `dev.frontend`/Storybook defaults are 5173/6006; `devenv.nix` gives `devenv up` 5180/6010 through `TWYNE_DEV_PORT` and `TWYNE_STORYBOOK_PORT`. Keep readiness probes on those same variables and document both URL pairs. Storybook uses `--host 127.0.0.1`, configured port, and `--ci`. [Task 1]\n   819\t- Overrides can live in `devenv.local.nix` or the two environment variables. Evidence confirmed frontend at 5180, Storybook at 6010 while 6006 remained occupied, `devenv tasks list`, and `git diff --check`. [Task 1]\n   820\t\n   821\t## Failures and how to do differently\n   822\t\n   823\t- `ss -ltnp` may fail with `Cannot open netlink socket: Operation not permitted`; use permitted elevated listener inspection. A read-only Nix fetcher lock initially blocked `devenv tasks list`; retry where cache writes are allowed. Process startup is not full application or complete `devenv up` proof. [Task 1]\n   824\t\n   825\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/twyne v0.22.1 bilingual launch-film release and deployment\n   826\tscope: Release Twyne with one locale-resolved landing/docs film while preserving unrelated work and requiring CI, public assets, deployment, and browser proof before completion.\n   827\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne; reuse_rule=reinspect the dirty tree, native release scripts, current Convex/Railway credentials, remote CI, and live locale behavior before publishing another release.\n   828\t\n   829\t## Task 1: Publish v0.22.1 with one bilingual launch film\n   830\t\n   831\t### rollout_summary_files\n   832\t\n   833\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/28/rollout-2026-09-28T17-54-33-01a0ea03-320c-7363-8153-d4a4fe122ae8.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-29T01:19:04+00:00, thread_id=01a0ea03-320c-7363-8153-d4a4fe122ae8, success; CI, GitHub release/assets, Railway, and live locale smoke passed)\n   834\t\n   835\t### keywords\n   836\t\n   837\t- v0.22.1, v0.22.0, release:version, release:check, release:publish, convex@1.46.0, scripts/railway-build.sh, The Room, the-room-en.mp4, the-room-fr.mp4, Dagger, Prek, Object.defineProperty\n   838\t\n   839\t## User preferences\n   840\t\n   841\t- when the user said “just one video should be added to the landing page” and requested it “in both english and french depending on the language of the speaker” -> integrate one selected film through the existing locale preference/browser resolution; do not expose the full launch-video gallery [Task 1]\n   842\t- when the user asked to add the launch video “to documentation” -> update release notes/manual documentation alongside the landing-page integration [Task 1]\n   843\t- when release work encountered a large dirty tree -> explicitly separate release contents from unrelated Typst/editor changes and raw launch-video projects before committing [Task 1]\n   844\t\n   845\t## Reusable knowledge\n   846\t\n   847\t- Twyne’s release sequence is `bun run release:version`, `bun run release:check`, then `bun run release:publish`; release check requires an annotated matching `v<package.version>` tag. v0.22.1 is `692fe6b6d3c48a2a09299e616a58548e3569b5da` / `v0.22.1`, with source plus Linux/macOS/Windows desktop assets. [Task 1]\n   848\t- The bilingual film uses `public/assets/launch/the-room-en.mp4` and `the-room-fr.mp4` with posters and `.vtt` captions. Live smoke verified English, French, automatic French detection, English fallback, mobile, playback, captions, seeking, byte ranges, and preference persistence; `/assets/launch/the-room-fr.mp4` returned `200` and `video/mp4`. [Task 1]\n   849\t- Railway production used service `twyne`, deployment `e802c911-53ff-4d0b-b500-fb8c9b8e6f0a`, and Convex target `prod:hushed-aardvark-411`. For deploy-only keys, pin `npx --yes convex@1.46.0 deploy --cmd 'bun run build.client && bun run build.server'` in `scripts/railway-build.sh`. [Task 1]\n   850\t- Browser mocks must use configurable/writable `Object.defineProperty` descriptors, snapshot/restore globals, and restore timers. This fixed v0.22.0’s 179 test-order-dependent failures; v0.22.1 reached `1578 pass`, `39 skip`, `0 fail` and Dagger success. Related skill: skills/release-publication-verification/SKILL.md. [Task 1]\n   851\t\n   852\t## Failures and how to do differently\n   853\t\n   854\t- v0.22.0 was published before remote CI and deployment verification: Railway failed because the older Convex CLI requested `deployment:data:view`, while CI failed from leaked read-only browser globals/timers. Treat a release as incomplete until remote checks, public assets, deployment, and live smoke all pass. [Task 1]\n   855\t- A stale Prek/Devenv shim blocked push. Preserve `.git/hooks/pre-push.pre-entire`, repair the generated shim, run `bun run release:check` directly, and never fabricate tags. [Task 1]\n   856\t- A secret-list command exposed credentials in a tool log. Do not repeat or preserve values; rotate exposed credentials outside memory. [Task 1]\n   857\t\n   858\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/keating hosted routing, autonomous learning plans, authentication, and media/docs placement\n   859\tscope: Complete current Keating web/product changes with clear proof boundaries across chat hosting, durable learning state, browser auth, and contextual launch media.\n   860\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating; reuse_rule=reinspect this checkout, dirty-tree scope, live DNS/Railway state, and browser/provider evidence before claiming a release or end-to-end behavior.\n   861\t\n   862\t## Task 1: Implement sticky active work and autonomous plan revisions\n   863\t\n   864\t### rollout_summary_files\n   865\t\n   866\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/28/rollout-2026-09-28T22-53-14-01a0eb14-a6c7-7422-9c4d-663ea1786c5e.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-24T04:01:55+00:00, thread_id=01a0eb14-a6c7-7422-9c4d-663ea1786c5e, partial; focused tests passed, full integration remains unverified)\n   867\t\n   868\t### keywords\n   869\t\n   870\t- projectActiveWork, formatActiveWork, openui-presentations, TeachingPolicyTurn.activeWork, PlanChangeMode, applyPlanRevision, plan_revised, keating:plan-revised, revise_study_plan\n   871\t\n   872\t## Task 2: Repair OAuth restored messages and device-session refresh\n   873\t\n   874\t### rollout_summary_files\n   875\t\n   876\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/28/rollout-2026-09-28T22-53-14-01a0eb14-a6c0-7b10-809f-b67a21eb51d1.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-23T15:46:30+00:00, thread_id=01a0eb14-a6c0-7b10-809f-b67a21eb51d1, success; focused 43 tests/typecheck passed, changes uncommitted)\n   877\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/29/rollout-2026-09-29T22-21-17-01a0f01d-c17a-7f50-8657-7200b63f110f.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-30T03:51:48+00:00, thread_id=01a0f01d-c17a-7f50-8657-7200b63f110f, partial; Keating recovery UI deployed, provider guard/root fix remains undeployed and real callback unverified)\n   878\t\n   879\t### keywords\n   880\t\n   881\t- pending-chat-turn.ts, undelivered, FlueConversation.sendRestored, device_session, DPoP, localStorage, refresh token, public-client.ts, ProviderAuthRecovery, invalid_authorization_code, publicClientAuth.ts, Popmelt\n   882\t\n   883\t## Task 3: Put the single launch film in contextual docs and publish additional formats\n   884\t\n   885\t### rollout_summary_files\n   886\t\n   887\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/28/rollout-2026-09-28T22-53-14-01a0eb14-a64e-7f12-a5a1-0d2995ce9f64.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-26T20:41:45+00:00, thread_id=01a0eb14-a64e-7f12-a5a1-0d2995ce9f64, success)\n   888\t- rollout_summaries/2026-09-29T02-53-14-y2dp-keating_additional_film_formats_and_pipeline.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/28/rollout-2026-09-28T22-53-14-01a0eb14-a77c-73f0-bdfb-ff103f0412a7.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-25T16:01:22+00:00, thread_id=01a0eb14-a77c-73f0-bdfb-ff103f0412a7, success; outputs published, no commit)\n   889\t\n   890\t### keywords\n   891\t\n   892\t- keating-4-launch.mp4, getting-started.json, learning.json, LandingFilms.tsx, video/spotlights, Seedance 2.5, Lyria 3.5, gpt-image-2.5-sunburst, FAL_BUDGET, aspect, ffprobe\n   893\t\n   894\t## User preferences\n   895\t\n   896\t- when the user said “we want a way to accept plans, also i want plan changes to autonomous by default” -> default plan mutations to autonomous while exposing an explicit approval mode; add the lifecycle/browser hook for applied revisions [Task 1]\n   897\t- when the user supplied `POST https://api.notorganic.info/v1/public/token 401 (Unauthorized)` -> trace the actual browser-to-provider token exchange and separate incidental preload/service-worker warnings from the failing authentication path [Task 2]\n   898\t- when the user asked for a natural/context-related placement rather than videos “all at the bottom with a picker,” then said “i think the right place is in docs or in onboarding” -> prefer one contextual docs/onboarding launch film over a landing-page gallery; do not modify onboarding without approval [Task 3]\n   899\t- when the user asked to “make more videos and different ones” -> use clear, large visual storytelling and varied formats, not another near-duplicate feature explainer; Seedance 2.5 and Lyria 3.5 were explicitly approved within the shared budget ledger [Task 3]\n   900\t\n   901\t## Reusable knowledge\n   902\t\n   903\t- `projectActiveWork`/`formatActiveWork` deterministically select focus items, join presentation/attempt evidence, bound outline/interactions, and keep independence unknown. `openui-presentations` (DB v8) persists source linkage `{documentId, revision, nodeId}`; thread `TeachingPolicyTurn.activeWork` through policy, draft gate, evidence, prompts, and receipts. [Task 1]\n   904\t- `PlanChangeMode` is `autonomous | approval`; `applyPlanRevision` supports `complete-item`, `insert-prerequisite`, and `expand-item`, validates the full document and rejects invalid/duplicate/over-limit changes without partial application. `planChanges` defaults to `autonomous`; `PlanRevisionCard`, `revise_study_plan`, `plan_revised`, and `keating:plan-revised` connect UI/tool/lifecycle paths. [Task 1]\n   905\t- For a restored OAuth turn, use `sendRestored()` when the message never reached Flue and reserve `resume()` for a previously delivered message that failed later. Browser device sessions request `device_session: true`, hold refresh credentials in `localStorage`, refresh 15 seconds early with DPoP bound to the refresh token, deduplicate refreshes, revoke at sign-out, and preserve a session on transient network/5xx failures. [Task 2]\n   906\t- Keating sends `device_session: true` from `web/src/notorganic-provider/public-client.ts`; the diagnosed provider failure is `convex/publicClientAuth.ts` allowing device sessions only for `environment === \"mobile\"` while browser codes are `\"browser\"`. Permit browser and mobile while retaining short-lived legacy environment-less codes; this provider change was identified but not made/deployed. Keating's deployed recovery offers fresh Not Organic `Sign in / Sign up`, retains API-key re-entry for other providers, and preserves/retries pending chat correctly. [Task 2]\n   907\t- `getting-started.json` already embeds `keating-4-launch.mp4`; `learning.json` embeds feature spotlights. The launch file is 69.5 seconds by `ffprobe`, so user-facing copy says 70 seconds. Shared films live at `video/spotlights/{id}`; `gen-video.mjs` has aspect/model/cache/ledger controls, and docs now accept `16:9`, `9:16`, and `1:1`. [Task 3]\n   908\t\n   909\t## Failures and how to do differently\n   910\t\n   911\t- Focused green plan-revision tests did not clear the full suite: tests that replace `window`/`EventTarget` made `window.dispatchEvent(new CustomEvent(...))` reject events. Guard non-DOM dispatch or use the active window constructor; keep unrelated dirty-tree/GitNexus and pre-existing type failures separate. [Task 1]\n   912\t- Do not call the auth work committed or full-suite clean: 43 focused tests/typecheck passed, but the full suite’s five failures reproduced with changes stashed and no commit was made. [Task 2]\n   913\t- The deployed recovery does not prove real Bluesky/provider authorization: no real approval/callback occurred. Keep provider-side root cause separate from the unrelated preload warning. Popmelt toolbar proof is independent of optional Codex plugin registration; two full-repo missing-module/fixture errors were pre-existing. [Task 2]\n   914\t- Reject generated clips that shift Keating green to yellow/orange or invent text rather than global hue-correcting; Seedance was more faithful than H3. Do not treat an instrumental Whisper transcript as proof of vocals; warm Vite before screenshot capture, and use an explicit `silent` flag so music-only films are not muted. [Task 3]\n   915\t\n   916\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/dio-machines COSMIC Machines manager and Devenv development workflow\n   917\tscope: Build, launch, and develop the native local/remote Machines utility without losing unsaved configuration drafts or mistaking a headless build for GUI proof.\n   918\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/dio-machines; reuse_rule=reinspect pinned COSMIC dependencies, Devenv process state, current GPU/runtime libraries, and local/remote target requirements before changing or claiming the app workflow.\n   919\t\n   920\t## Task 1: Build native local/remote COSMIC Machines manager\n   921\t\n   922\t### rollout_summary_files\n   923\t\n   924\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/dio-machines, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/27/rollout-2026-09-27T18-51-29-01a0e510-f62a-79d3-91d4-edfad7d98e79.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-28T08:28:37+00:00, thread_id=01a0e510-f62a-79d3-91d4-edfad7d98e79, success; app tests, benchmark, optimized GPU launch, and Devenv checks passed)\n   925\t\n   926\t### keywords\n   927\t\n   928\t- apps/machines, COSMIC, libcosmic, wgpu, Vulkan, Intel(R) Iris(R) Xe Graphics (ADL GT2), runner.rs, manifest.rs, SSH, AppImages, app:test, app:benchmark\n   929\t\n   930\t## Task 2: Make `devenv up` the native COSMIC development workflow\n   931\t\n   932\t### rollout_summary_files\n   933\t\n   934\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/dio-machines, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/27/rollout-2026-09-27T18-51-29-01a0e510-f62a-79d3-91d4-edfad7d98e79.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-28T08:28:37+00:00, thread_id=01a0e510-f62a-79d3-91d4-edfad7d98e79, success; GUI process and opt-in checker verified)\n   935\t\n   936\t### keywords\n   937\t\n   938\t- rtk devenv up, machines, machines-check, processes.machines-check.watch.paths, config.devenv.root, devenv processes list, devenv processes restart machines, cargo check, README.md\n   939\t\n   940\t## User preferences\n   941\t\n   942\t- when choosing the manager scope, the user selected “Include remote computers” and “All three equally” for inspection, editing, and maintenance -> make local and SSH targets plus all three workflows first-class, rather than treating remote administration as an afterthought [Task 1]\n   943\t- when delegating visual direction with “best judgement most helpful” -> default to a calm, practical native utility, not a decorative infrastructure dashboard [Task 1]\n   944\t- when the user asked for “devenv up for doing this sort of stuff and deving on the cosmic app and stuff” -> use documented native Devenv processes/tasks as the canonical workflow; do not auto-restart the GUI on source edits because drafts must survive [Task 2]\n   945\t\n   946\t## Reusable knowledge\n   947\t\n   948\t- `apps/machines/` is a libcosmic application pinned at revision `8768bce2e2a4921ced57d95cff74bc7c92ef08b8` with `wgpu`. `runner.rs` owns local/SSH execution, host validation, atomic saves, external-change detection, and confirmation; SSH uses `BatchMode=yes`, stores no passwords, and root operations require a terminal TTY. [Task 1]\n   949\t- Cache manifest parsing in `apps/machines/src/manifest.rs`: 200 redraws measured about 74.1 ms with repeated parsing versus about 21 µs cached. `devenv tasks run app:test` passed 17 Rust plus 3 Python safety tests; normal optimized launch selected Intel Iris Xe through Vulkan/Mesa 25.1.9. [Task 1]\n   950\t- `devenv.nix` supplies `machines` (optimized GUI) and opt-in `machines-check` (compile checks). The checker watches absolute `${config.devenv.root}/apps/machines/{src,scripts,Cargo.toml,Cargo.lock}` paths and intentionally never restarts the GUI. Use `rtk devenv up`, or `rtk devenv up machines machines-check`; then use `rtk devenv processes restart machines|logs machines|attach`, `rtk devenv down`, and `rtk devenv tasks run app:test`. Root `README.md` and `apps/machines/README.md` are the operational source. [Task 2]\n   951\t\n   952\t## Failures and how to do differently\n   953\t\n   954\t- Plain/offline Cargo builds can inherit the mixed Nix/Guix environment and fail on `libgcc_s.so.1` -> build in the pinned `devenv.nix` app environment. For GPU launches, Fedora Vulkan ICD dependencies can be hidden by Nix `LD_LIBRARY_PATH` -> scope Fedora driver paths to the final GUI process and keep matching Nix glibc first. [Task 1]\n   955\t- Makepad headless rendering had Linux modules gated out -> it is not evidence that the native COSMIC UI started. Verify an optimized real GUI launch and app log instead. [Task 1]\n   956\t- Relative `processes.machines-check.watch.paths` causes `...is not of type absolute path` -> use `${config.devenv.root}/...`. `devenv processes list` fails with no manager -> start `devenv up -d` first. [Task 2]\n   957\t\n   958\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/keating subscription value and offline-edition validation\n   959\tscope: Evaluate a compelling recurring Keating offer and validate a paid offline local-model edition before pricing, training, or hardware-support claims.\n   960\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating; reuse_rule=recheck current plan/catalog economics and current model documentation before changing pricing or publishing hardware requirements.\n   961\t\n   962\t## Task 1: Assess subscription value and $150 offline local-model edition\n   963\t\n   964\t### rollout_summary_files\n   965\t\n   966\t- rollout_summaries/2026-09-27T05-32-32-lTig-keating_subscription_offline_edition_monetization.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/27/rollout-2026-09-27T01-32-32-01a0e159-c770-7e33-8611-d18bf7cc6630.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-27T05:44:20+00:00, thread_id=01a0e159-c770-7e33-8611-d18bf7cc6630, uncertain; strategy analysis, no product/pricing change)\n   967\t\n   968\t### keywords\n   969\t\n   970\t- subscription, Personal, keating_personal_v2, hosted-credit, credit-packs, persistent study management, offline-model, Gemma-4-12B, 32GB unified memory, 16GB VRAM, waitlist, refundable reservation, post-training\n   971\t\n   972\t## User preferences\n   973\t\n   974\t- when the user said the subscription “currently doesn't seem appealing at all” and asked why people would buy it -> find one compelling recurring outcome rather than adding generic extras [Task 1]\n   975\t- when considering a $150 offline edition, the user wanted a waitlist and recognized post-training is expensive -> collect hardware, use case, willingness to pay, and testing commitment before funding training [Task 1]\n   976\t\n   977\t## Reusable knowledge\n   978\t\n   979\t- Current repo terms were Personal at $25/month, $5 monthly hosted credit, and one billing-cycle rollover; $10/$25/$50 top-up packs do not expire. The recurring promise proposed here is persistent study management across devices: materials, plan, next lesson/review, progress, and sufficient hosted use. Storage/workspace alone are weak subscription reasons. [Task 1]\n   980\t- Checkout is entitlement-gated: `subscriptionCheckoutEnabled` requires `VITE_NOTORGANIC_CHECKOUT_ENABLED === \"true\"` and `keating_v2`; `subscriptionAvailable` also needs wallet checkout availability and `keating_personal_v2`. [Task 1]\n   981\t- An offline edition sells installation, hardware detection, tested model configuration, Keating harness/tool behavior, local materials/progress, and a defined update period—not just weights. Candidate Gemma 4 12B tiers (32GB unified memory or 16GB VRAM) are hypotheses because context cache/runtime overhead matter. Measure tool calls, grading, lesson-state adherence, and teaching behavior in Keating before commissioning post-training. [Task 1]\n   982\t\n   983\t## Failures and how to do differently\n   984\t\n   985\t- Free users can buy non-expiring credit and retain the teaching tools, leaving an apparent $20/month without an obvious recurring benefit. Do not assume more credit fixes that; model full-allowance, storage, compute, support, and payment costs before promising $35 credit on a $25 plan. [Task 1]\n   986\t- Do not promise support for every 32GB unified-memory or 16GB-VRAM machine. Establish supported hardware, context limits, and measured speeds; a refundable reservation tied to concrete scope/funding threshold is stronger demand evidence than a free waitlist. [Task 1]\n   987\t\n   988\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/notorganic-provider judgement purpose telemetry\n   989\tscope: Trace and extend auditable Not Organic judgement usage without retaining submitted content by default.\n   990\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/notorganic-provider with investigation initiated from cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating; reuse_rule=reinspect current gateway/schema/portal code and obtain a product/privacy decision before implementing a purpose field.\n   991\t\n   992\t## Task 1: Trace judgement usage and purpose logging\n   993\t\n   994\t### rollout_summary_files\n   995\t\n   996\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/26/rollout-2026-09-26T20-02-33-01a0e02b-ac77-7f83-b60d-875d511511b1.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-27T00:04:06+00:00, thread_id=01a0e02b-ac77-7f83-b60d-875d511511b1, partial; analysis only, no implementation)\n   997\t\n   998\t### keywords\n   999\t\n  1000\t- JudgementGateway, judgement.settled, purpose, apps/gateway/src/judgement.ts, convex/schema.ts, Usage.tsx, feature: \"judgement\", TypeSafe, HMAC-SHA256, draft_review, venue_ranking, quiz_feedback\n  1001\t\n  1002\t## User preferences\n  1003\t\n  1004\t- when the user said Not Organic should “log the use of judgement api and what it was used for” -> expose concrete feature/use-case purpose, not merely generic model, token, and cost metrics [Task 1]\n  1005\t\n  1006\t## Reusable knowledge\n  1007\t\n  1008\t- `JudgementGateway.evaluate` reserves credit with `feature: \"judgement\"`, dispatches TypeSafe, settles actual usage, and emits `judgement.settled`. Current fields are `product`, `alias`, question count, `input_tokens`, `usage_complete`, and `billed_usd`; no purpose field exists in the inspected path. [Task 1]\n  1009\t- `#emitSettled` pseudonymizes `principal.accountId` using HMAC-SHA256 and swallows telemetry errors, so analytics cannot fail a paid/settled request. `convex/schema.ts` persists metered lifecycle/product/feature/model/token/cost data; portal `Usage.tsx` renders the feature but no purpose column. [Task 1]\n  1010\t\n  1011\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  1012\t\n  1013\t- This was not implemented or privacy-approved. First decide whether a caller supplies a bounded purpose (for example `draft_review`) and whether only aggregate usage is retained; do not store full questions/answers by default. Refresh GitNexus before treating its one-commit-stale graph as complete edit guidance. [Task 1]\n  1014\t\n  1015\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/keating GPT Live video corrections\n  1016\tscope: Keep the GPT Live spotlight’s captured product state and SVG budget-meter geometry accurate through deterministic HyperFrames verification.\n  1017\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating; reuse_rule=reinspect actual provider descriptors, capture manifests, browser configuration, and rendered frames for any new video edit.\n  1018\t\n  1019\t## Task 1: Correct the GPT Live picker capture\n  1020\t\n  1021\t### rollout_summary_files\n  1022\t\n  1023\t- rollout_summaries/2026-09-26T20-00-24-7c9T-fix_gpt_live_video_picker_budget_needle.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/26/rollout-2026-09-26T16-00-24-01a0df4d-f93b-75c2-baaa-3eb370d6335d.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-26T20:13:00+00:00, thread_id=01a0df4d-f93b-75c2-baaa-3eb370d6335d, success)\n  1024\t\n  1025\t### keywords\n  1026\t\n  1027\t- GPT Live, gpt-live-1, gptLiveProvider, ModelSelector.stories.tsx, models-modelselector--gpt-live-voice-models, shots.json, picker.png, Storybook\n  1028\t\n  1029\t## Task 2: Fix SVG spending-budget needle placement\n  1030\t\n  1031\t### rollout_summary_files\n  1032\t\n  1033\t- rollout_summaries/2026-09-26T20-00-24-7c9T-fix_gpt_live_video_picker_budget_needle.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/26/rollout-2026-09-26T16-00-24-01a0df4d-f93b-75c2-baaa-3eb370d6335d.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-26T20:13:00+00:00, thread_id=01a0df4d-f93b-75c2-baaa-3eb370d6335d, success; render, snapshots, and contact sheet reviewed)\n  1034\t\n  1035\t### keywords\n  1036\t\n  1037\t- HyperFrames 0.8.78, SVG needle, rotate(112 357 322), svgOrigin, video/spotlights/live/src/index.template.html, KEATING_CHROME_BINARY, check, snapshot, contact-sheet.jpg\n  1038\t\n  1039\t## User preferences\n  1040\t\n  1041\t- when the user pointed out that the picker “shows gpt realtime 2.1 and not gpt live 1” -> verify captured UI uses the exact requested provider/model, not a visually similar fixture [Task 1]\n  1042\t\n  1043\t## Reusable knowledge\n  1044\t\n  1045\t- `gptLiveProvider` in `web/src/keating/speech-providers/gpt-live.ts` supplies `gpt-live-1` / `GPT Live`. The capture manifest is `video/spotlight-live/shots.json`; the dedicated story is `models-modelselector--gpt-live-voice-models`, staged at `video/spotlights/live/assets/shots/picker.png`. [Task 1]\n  1046\t- For a sub-composition SVG dial, animate explicit transforms around its center (`rotate(0 357 322)` → `rotate(112 357 322)` → return) instead of GSAP `rotation` plus `svgOrigin`, which can shift when mounted. The validated render was copied to spotlight, `web/public/tapes`, and docs-site tape paths. [Task 2]\n  1047\t\n  1048\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  1049\t\n  1050\t- `spawnSync ffmpeg EPERM` blocked the first sandbox build; host execution completed it. A generated Chrome wrapper with unset `KEATING_CHROME_BINARY` blocked checks/snapshots; pass an explicit Chrome path. Ensure `history begin` actually succeeds before edits and close it with `history end`. [Task 2]\n  1051\t\n  1052\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/keating Gemini narration, voice casting, and campaign-video publication\n  1053\tscope: Replace narrated campaign-video voices, generate auditionable English and Québec French alternatives, regenerate captions/renders, and locate published versus full-quality deliverables.\n  1054\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating; reuse_rule=reinspect current voice scripts, HyperFrames pins, Chrome/runtime setup, and media outputs before rerendering or claiming audiovisual approval.\n  1055\t\n  1056\t## Task 1: Migrate campaign narration to Gemini 3.8 TTS and publish eight videos\n  1057\t\n  1058\t### rollout_summary_files\n  1059\t\n  1060\t- rollout_summaries/2026-09-26T17-39-31-7qyn-gemini_tts_video_voice_casting_and_regeneration.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/26/rollout-2026-09-26T13-39-31-01a0decc-ff7a-7d43-9968-7b95d1b8a263.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-26T19:54:33+00:00, thread_id=01a0decc-ff7a-7d43-9968-7b95d1b8a263, success; streams/captions/copy equality verified, no per-film audiovisual review)\n  1061\t\n  1062\t### keywords\n  1063\t\n  1064\t- Gemini 3.8 TTS, fal, voice design, Québec French, HyperFrames 0.8.78, voice.mjs, Whisper word timings, web/public/tapes, ffprobe, video/voice-casting\n  1065\t\n  1066\t## User preferences\n  1067\t\n  1068\t- when requesting narration, the user asked to “generate a ton of different voice options with voice design as well” and specifically requested Québec French -> deliver tangible auditionable alternatives instead of silently choosing one voice [Task 1]\n  1069\t- when the user asked “where arer all the videos” -> report exact filesystem locations and distinguish published encodes from source/full-quality renders [Task 1]\n  1070\t\n  1071\t## Reusable knowledge\n  1072\t\n  1073\t- `video/spotlights/shared/scripts/voice.mjs` and `video/keating-launch/scripts/voice.mjs` support Gemini/fal narration with content-hash caching keyed by engine/model/voice/instructions and retain Whisper word timings for captions. Voice galleries are `video/voice-casting/fal/` and `video/voice-casting/cartesia/`, with English and French Canadian/Québécois samples. [Task 1]\n  1074\t- Published deliverables are `web/public/tapes/{keating-4-launch,keating-intro,keating-spotlight-recall,keating-lesson,keating-manifesto,keating-spotlight-live,keating-spotlight-judgements,keating-spotlight-onboarding}.mp4`; docs mirrors are `scripts/docs-site/assets/tapes/`. Full renders are `video/keating-launch/renders/`, `.keating/outputs/video/keating-intro/`, and `video/spotlights/*/renders/`. [Task 1]\n  1075\t- HyperFrames pins were upgraded to 0.8.78. Standard checks passed for launch plus all six narrated spotlights; `ffprobe -v error -show_entries format=duration -show_entries stream=codec_type -of compact <file>` verified video/audio streams (38.4–69.5 seconds), and published web/docs copies matched. [Task 1]\n  1076\t\n  1077\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  1078\t\n  1079\t- Chrome shared-library preflight fails under the Nix loader -> render HyperFrames with `env -u LD_LIBRARY_PATH PATH=/usr/bin:$PATH`. `ffmpeg`/`ffprobe` child processes can return `EPERM` in the restricted sandbox even if output exists -> use the permitted proxy/escalated media command path for validation. [Task 1]\n  1080\t- Stream, duration, caption-count, and copy-equality checks do not establish creative quality -> explicitly listen and visually review every regenerated video before final audiovisual approval. [Task 1]\n  1081\t\n  1082\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/keating launch preview, staging health, and app-only packaging\n  1083\tscope: Diagnose the exact playback/deployment surface, verify staging beyond HTTP 200, and package chat/CLI/TUI independently from landing/docs without overclaiming publication or DNS completion.\n  1084\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating; reuse_rule=recheck browser, Railway, DNS/TLS, worktree, native-install environment, and release state before treating any partial evidence as shipped.\n  1085\t\n  1086\t## Task 1: Diagnose launch-video voiceover silence\n  1087\t\n  1088\t### rollout_summary_files\n  1089\t\n  1090\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/26/rollout-2026-09-26T16-35-25-01a0df6e-0774-78a2-b175-4a0a3a2be832.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-26T23:19:47+00:00, thread_id=01a0df6e-0774-78a2-b175-4a0a3a2be832, partial; browser/audio-output proof unavailable)\n  1091\t\n  1092\t### keywords\n  1093\t\n  1094\t- launch-video, Local video preview, video/keating-launch/index.html, mix.wav, HyperFrames 0.8.78, ffprobe, volumedetect, timeline --json, localhost:3017\n  1095\t\n  1096\t## Task 2: Investigate staging failure and Devenv\n  1097\t\n  1098\t### rollout_summary_files\n  1099\t\n  1100\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/26/rollout-2026-09-26T16-35-25-01a0df6e-0774-78a2-b175-4a0a3a2be832.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-26T23:19:47+00:00, thread_id=01a0df6e-0774-78a2-b175-4a0a3a2be832, partial; stale deployment identified)\n  1101\t\n  1102\t### keywords\n  1103\t\n  1104\t- scripts/staging.ts, devenv up, keating:staging-deploy, keating-staging.up.railway.app, staging-build.json, promotionEligible, Railway, /chat\n  1105\t\n  1106\t## Task 3: Create app-only chat/CLI/TUI package\n  1107\t\n  1108\t### rollout_summary_files\n  1109\t\n  1110\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/26/rollout-2026-09-26T16-35-25-01a0df6e-0774-78a2-b175-4a0a3a2be832.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-26T23:19:47+00:00, thread_id=01a0df6e-0774-78a2-b175-4a0a3a2be832, partial; package validated, unpublished and DNS/TLS unresolved)\n  1111\t\n  1112\t### keywords\n  1113\t\n  1114\t- chat.keating.help, KEATING_WEB_BUILD_TARGET=app, APP_ONLY, web-build-target.ts, nitro.config.ts, verify-package-manifest.mjs --app-only, node-pty, 46.7 MB, 837 files\n  1115\t\n  1116\t## Task 4: Correct chat DNS/TLS and deploy host-aware routing\n  1117\t\n  1118\t### rollout_summary_files\n  1119\t\n  1120\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/27/rollout-2026-09-27T23-25-54-01a0e60c-32ee-7f00-a6c2-e8a4640f63c4.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-28T22:12:46+00:00, thread_id=01a0e60c-32ee-7f00-a6c2-e8a4640f63c4, partial; DNS records and live host routing verified, Railway’s final explicit certificate status was not captured)\n  1121\t\n  1122\t### keywords\n  1123\t\n  1124\t- chat.keating.help, keating.help, Railway, Porkbun, Sesame, _railway-verify.chat, CERTIFICATE_STATUS_TYPE_VALIDATING_OWNERSHIP, hosted-navigation.ts, PWA cache IDs, v4.0.6\n  1125\t\n  1126\t## Task 5: Prepare 4.0.7 installer-size and release fixes\n  1127\t\n  1128\t### rollout_summary_files\n  1129\t\n  1130\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/27/rollout-2026-09-27T23-25-54-01a0e60c-32ee-7f00-a6c2-e8a4640f63c4.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-28T22:12:46+00:00, thread_id=01a0e60c-32ee-7f00-a6c2-e8a4640f63c4, partial; 4.0.7 remained uncommitted/unpublished)\n  1131\t\n  1132\t### keywords\n  1133\t\n  1134\t- 4.0.7, stage-onnx-runtime.mjs, onnx-packaging.test.ts, 2 GiB, full-payload-xz-proof.json, AppImage, promotional tapes, posters, release.yml\n  1135\t\n  1136\t## User preferences\n  1137\t\n  1138\t- when the user clarified “Local video preview” after saying “no sound” -> identify the exact playback surface before diagnosing or concluding [Task 1]\n  1139\t- when the user said “the page fails to load and devenv up doesnt seem to work” -> investigate both deployed-page behavior and the Devenv/service path [Task 2]\n  1140\t- when requesting `chat.keating.help`, the user clarified “the package only includes chat, cli, and tui instead of the landing page and docs” -> treat hostname routing and build/package separation as distinct deliverables; inspect requested Entire/OpenCode history before implementation [Task 3]\n  1141\t- when the user interrupted release work with “we’ll have to get the remain chat dns and tls please first” -> resolve DNS/TLS before commit/publish steps when it is an outstanding dependency [Task 4]\n  1142\t- when the user said “let’s get my changes commited and pushed all changs need to get released” -> after prerequisites are verified, carry the coherent intended worktree through commit, push, tag, and publication instead of stopping at local validation [Task 5]\n  1143\t\n  1144\t## Reusable knowledge\n  1145\t\n  1146\t- HyperFrames uses muted timed visual `<video>` clips and a separate identified audio element. `video/keating-launch/index.html` has `<audio id=\"mix\" ...>`; the MP4 has 69.5-second stereo AAC and the served `mix.wav`/timeline were valid, so the remaining boundary is browser/player mute or host audio output. [Task 1]\n  1147\t- Use `bun scripts/staging.ts deploy|status|snapshot` or `devenv tasks run keating:staging-deploy`. A staging homepage/main JS 200 can still be stale: observed `/tapes/keating-4-launch.mp4` and `/staging-build.json` were 404. Dirty snapshots are `promotionEligible: false`. [Task 2]\n  1148\t- `KEATING_WEB_BUILD_TARGET=app` keeps chat/auth/courses/shares/live/learner activity/review plus CLI/TUI runtime assets. `web/scripts/web-build-target.ts`, `web/nitro.config.ts`, and compile-time `APP_ONLY` remove landing/docs/videos/reports/downloads/source artwork. `scripts/verify-package-manifest.mjs --app-only` rejects excluded paths and archives over 70 MiB. The validated artifact was 46.7 MB/837 files; `/chat` was 200 while excluded video/reports were 404. [Task 3]\n  1149\t- Railway required CNAME `chat` → `j0huj6qp.up.railway.app` and TXT `_railway-verify.chat`; Sesame/Porkbun preserved all 23 existing records. App paths on `keating.help` map to `https://chat.keating.help/`, public paths map back to `https://keating.help`; app builds render chat at `/` while retaining `/chat`, query/course handoffs, and distinct site/app PWA cache IDs. Commit `6514b0fc3ecef30fd0e3f1e6a2b1e57a0069b833`/`v4.0.6` deployed successfully; 2,254 web tests (1 skip) and 936 root tests passed. [Task 4]\n  1150\t- `desktop/scripts/stage-onnx-runtime.mjs` stages only the target platform/architecture ONNX Runtime closure; `desktop/test/onnx-packaging.test.ts` passed 13 tests. Release workflow checks each Linux installer against GitHub’s 2 GiB per-file limit, but full-payload XZ remained over: x64 2,267,136,000 bytes and arm64 2,252,914,688 bytes. [Task 5]\n  1151\t\n  1152\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  1153\t\n  1154\t- Valid audio streams, timeline records, or served assets do not prove audible preview playback; use a real browser/player and inspect mute/volume/output. Railway SUCCESS or homepage 200 does not prove current assets, readiness, sign-in, hosted inference, judgement, DNS/TLS, or browser functionality. [Task 1][Task 2]\n  1155\t- Do not claim npm 4.0.2 publication or deploy app-only output over the shared production service: publication was pending, `node-pty` native install remained Nix-environment-dependent, `chat.keating.help` ownership/certificate validation was incomplete, and replacing the shared service could remove the apex landing. [Task 3]\n  1156\t- CNAME propagation is not sufficient: verify Railway ownership, certificate status, and `curl -I https://chat.keating.help` with certificate validation. `railway domain certificate retry` is unavailable until issuance fails; later HTTPS/browser success is not the same as captured explicit `ISSUED` status. [Task 4]\n  1157\t- SquashFS-only size is insufficient: include AppImage wrapper overhead and measure the actual target installer. Do not report 4.0.7 released until commit SHA, tag, GitHub workflow conclusion, npm version, release assets, and clean worktree are verified. [Task 5]\n  1158\t\n  1159\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/keating approachable Jev judgement-model setup\n  1160\tscope: Make independent judgement configuration discoverable in Providers & Models, recommend Jev, and route unavailable reviews into setup without exposing provider credentials.\n  1161\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating; reuse_rule=recheck desktop/browser capability, Not Organic authorization, and live provider behavior before asserting end-to-end availability.\n  1162\t\n  1163\t## Task 1: Add Jev judgement picker and setup guidance\n  1164\t\n  1165\t### rollout_summary_files\n  1166\t\n  1167\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/26/rollout-2026-09-26T19-06-37-01a0dff8-768f-7371-a6c0-67f2467f7b3b.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-26T23:12:08+00:00, thread_id=01a0dff8-768f-7371-a6c0-67f2467f7b3b, partial; focused tests/typecheck passed, browser/provider unverified)\n  1168\t\n  1169\t### keywords\n  1170\t\n  1171\t- Jev, JudgementSettings, ProvidersModelsTab, settings-section-judgement, backend-unavailable, backend-unauthorized, review-unavailable, docs/judgement-models.md, MiniCPM5, Not Organic, TypeSafe API key\n  1172\t\n  1173\t## User preferences\n  1174\t\n  1175\t- when the user asked for “an easy way to set one up just like other models” with “a picker with the various models and options” -> integrate judgement setup into normal Providers & Models instead of a hidden backend setting [Task 1]\n  1176\t- when requesting docs “linked to jev as well with that as our recommendation” -> visibly recommend Jev and link official documentation while making limits clear [Task 1]\n  1177\t\n  1178\t## Reusable knowledge\n  1179\t\n  1180\t- `web/src/components/settings/JudgementSettings.tsx` owns the picker/setup UI mounted from `ProvidersModelsTab.tsx` under `judgement`. It offers `Jev · Not Organic · Recommended`, desktop MiniCPM5 where supported, browser alternatives marked scoring-unavailable, and `Off · built-in checks only`; unavailable reviews link to `/chat?settings=judgement`. [Task 1]\n  1181\t- Hosted judgement remains separate from tutor model and uses Not Organic. Never ask users to paste a TypeSafe API key into the browser. `docs/judgement-models.md` covers authorization, local setup, browser limitations, token limits, and calibration boundaries. [Task 1]\n  1182\t\n  1183\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  1184\t\n  1185\t- UI-copy tests can false-match explanatory text (for example `judgement access is connected`); assert actual button markup or state-specific output. No browser interaction or live Jev/Not Organic authorization/review ran, and GitNexus was three commits stale, so do not promote this to end-to-end proof. [Task 1]\n  1186\t\n  1187\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/twyne persistence, Not Organic migration, rubric copy, and configurable judgement\n  1188\tscope: Preserve every Twyne writer’s work across guest/auth paths, make normal editing controls reliable, and migrate identity/judgement configuration without overstating live production proof.\n  1189\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne; reuse_rule=reinspect the broad dirty migration, production account scope/origins, PDS scopes, and real provider endpoints before deployment or irreversible account action.\n  1190\t\n  1191\t## Task 1: Repair dossier persistence, folio title carry-over, and editor Ctrl+A\n  1192\t\n  1193\t### rollout_summary_files\n  1194\t\n  1195\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/28/rollout-2026-09-28T22-53-14-01a0eb14-a6ed-79a2-bdfb-508802dcd4c2.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-23T15:23:10+00:00, thread_id=01a0eb14-a6ed-79a2-bdfb-508802dcd4c2, success; targeted browser tests passed)\n  1196\t\n  1197\t### keywords\n  1198\t\n  1199\t- DataCloneError, Qwik useStore, toStorable, IndexedDB, saveProjectBriefForFolio, withFolioTitle, dossier-persistence.e2e.ts, Ctrl+A, Mod-A, twyne-editor.tsx\n  1200\t\n  1201\t## Task 2: Replace legacy Twyne identity/billing with Not Organic-native sign-in\n  1202\t\n  1203\t### rollout_summary_files\n  1204\t\n  1205\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/28/rollout-2026-09-28T22-53-14-01a0eb14-a6ed-79a2-bdfb-508802dcd4c2.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-23T15:23:10+00:00, thread_id=01a0eb14-a6ed-79a2-bdfb-508802dcd4c2, partial; uncommitted migration, production/browser/PDS proof pending)\n  1206\t\n  1207\t### keywords\n  1208\t\n  1209\t- Not Organic, PKCE, providerIdentities, Better Auth, Creem, legacyAccounts.ts, sendDeprecationNotices, retireLegacyAccounts, Standard.site, include:site.standard.authFull\n  1210\t\n  1211\t## Task 3: Make rubric copy writer-readable and route judgement models/BYOK\n  1212\t\n  1213\t### rollout_summary_files\n  1214\t\n  1215\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/28/rollout-2026-09-28T22-53-14-01a0eb14-a65e-7873-ac1f-577a624acee3.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-26T04:27:48+00:00, thread_id=01a0eb14-a65e-7873-ac1f-577a624acee3, partial; UI/build checks passed, benchmark/live endpoint unverified)\n  1216\t\n  1217\t### keywords\n  1218\t\n  1219\t- rubric-copy.ts, SPINE_CRITERIA, rubric-grade.ts, 120-character truncation, JudgementSettings, judgement-client.ts, TypeSafe, POST /v1/systemone, Kev-4B, 127.0.0.1:8009\n  1220\t\n  1221\t## User preferences\n  1222\t\n  1223\t- when the user called dossier loss “critical” across signed-in/out and new-account paths -> fixes must cover guest and authenticated persistence, not just an account-specific path; a new folio title should seed its brief title unless the writer changes it [Task 1]\n  1224\t- when the user requested removal of old subscriptions/accounts and a deprecation email with zero real subscribers -> preserve the direction, but require recipient/count review, backup/export, and explicit confirmation before sending notices or deleting production data [Task 2]\n  1225\t- when the user said rubric copy should be “far more readable” -> use plain writer-facing explanations and actionable next moves, not model/scoring jargon; when asking for “a kev 4b” and other models, support local/private endpoints and benchmark-driven selection [Task 3]\n  1226\t\n  1227\t## Reusable knowledge\n  1228\t\n  1229\t- Qwik `useStore` values can be proxies despite plain TypeScript types; IndexedDB rejects them with `DataCloneError`. Detach values via `toStorable()` at every `.put()` boundary, never swallow write failures, and read after write. The dossier flow and named-folio title carry-over were exercised by two passing Playwright tests. [Task 1]\n  1230\t- A document capture-phase Mod-A handler restores editor selection from toolbar/page margins while preserving native selection in inputs, textareas, selects, dialogs, and editable controls; all 10 select-all scenarios passed. [Task 1]\n  1231\t- The migration removes Creem tables/webhooks/checkout and moves entitlement to the Not Organic wallet; verified DID maps to Better Auth plus `providerIdentities`. Keep ATProto only as a PDS publishing connection. `legacyAccounts.ts` supports dry-run notice/retirement commands; development only had e2e accounts. [Task 2]\n  1232\t- `rubric-copy.ts` centralizes visible score words/verdicts/next moves while frozen wording in `rubric-grade.ts` keeps historical judgement comparable. Keep summaries within the panel’s 120-character limit. `judgement-client.ts` routes Twyne-hosted, one-use TypeSafe BYOK through Convex, or a compatible direct endpoint and validates endpoint/response contracts. [Task 3]\n  1233\t\n  1234\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  1235\t\n  1236\t- Existing formatting E2E timeouts waiting for “Type options” reproduce against HEAD; do not attribute them to Ctrl+A. [Task 1]\n  1237\t- Migration is broad/uncommitted: review the diff, safely inspect production, register intended Not Organic origins, and test real sign-in/PDS publication. Do not send mail/delete accounts until dry-run recipient list, backup, and explicit approval; `include:site.standard.authFull` PDS scope remains unresolved. [Task 2]\n  1238\t- No benchmark, dataset, scores, report, real TypeSafe key flow, or ready Kev server was verified. CPU-only Kev was still starting/downloading; do not retry autonomous-agent spawning after denial—build the benchmark directly in the active session if authorized. [Task 3]\n  1239\t\n  1240\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/twyne persistent intentional grammar choices\n  1241\tscope: Preserve intentional wording as a compact, browser-local exception without silencing unrelated Harper grammar findings.\n  1242\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne; reuse_rule=reuse the precise local dictionary/matching design for Twyne grammar UI; manually exercise persistence and removal whenever a browser is available.\n  1243\t\n  1244\t## Task 1: Add persistent intentional grammar choices\n  1245\t\n  1246\t### rollout_summary_files\n  1247\t\n  1248\t- rollout_summaries/2026-09-26T09-40-38-4ytO-persistent_intentional_grammar_choices.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/26/rollout-2026-09-26T05-40-38-01a0dd16-8f41-7822-80c1-8224fb133b70.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-26T10:01:22+00:00, thread_id=01a0dd16-8f41-7822-80c1-8224fb133b70, success; focused tests passed, browser UI unverified)\n  1249\t\n  1250\t### keywords\n  1251\t\n  1252\t- Harper, grammar-panel, twyne:grammar-dictionary:v1, importWords, exportWords, clearWords, intentional choice, localStorage, ×, aria-label\n  1253\t\n  1254\t## User preferences\n  1255\t\n  1256\t- when the user asked for intentional wording to be remembered and then corrected that “this is intentional is too long just an cancel mark or something” -> use a compact ×/cancel control with tooltip and accessible label, plus a persistent exception rather than merely dismissing the current card [Task 1]\n  1257\t\n  1258\t## Reusable knowledge\n  1259\t\n  1260\t- `src/utils/grammar.ts` persists validated, deduplicated choices under `twyne:grammar-dictionary:v1`; match `problem`, `kind`, and `message` so one accepted wording does not disable an entire Harper rule. Spelling choices synchronize through `exportWords`, `clearWords`, and `importWords`; non-spelling choices filter only exact matches. [Task 1]\n  1261\t- `src/components/editor/grammar-panel.tsx` provides the × action, “Your dictionary” details list, removal/undo actions, and status notices. Focused grammar/runtime tests passed 10/0 and Prettier passed. [Task 1]\n  1262\t\n  1263\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  1264\t\n  1265\t- The visible sentence-length “This is intentional” control was rejected -> retain explanation in `title`/`aria-label`, not the button face. Browser clicking, reload persistence, and removal were not exercised, so do not call UI behavior verified without that pass. [Task 1]\n  1266\t\n  1267\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/twyne grade and workflow stamp effects\n  1268\tscope: Apply the editorial stamp system to grades and Filed/Revised workflow states, with dramatic but accessible tiered effects.\n  1269\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne; reuse_rule=recheck actual generated assets and visual behavior before reuse; the asset-count/model claim in this rollout is not independently established.\n  1270\t\n  1271\t## Task 1: Generate and integrate grade/workflow stamps\n  1272\t\n  1273\t### rollout_summary_files\n  1274\t\n  1275\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/26/rollout-2026-09-26T04-54-37-01a0dcec-6ed9-7913-b710-05f13e701fef.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-26T09:34:57+00:00, thread_id=01a0dcec-6ed9-7913-b710-05f13e701fef, partial; exact model, asset persistence, and claimed checks unverified)\n  1276\t\n  1277\t### keywords\n  1278\t\n  1279\t- GradeStamp, rubricGradeStampAsset, stamp-shader.tsx, WebGL, solar corona, sunburst, Filed, Revised, reduced-motion, context-loss, imagegen\n  1280\t\n  1281\t## User preferences\n  1282\t\n  1283\t- when the user asked for “a stamp with each grade,” “filed” and “revised,” and “really cool shaders” that become “more impressive with the highest” -> retain editorial ink-on-paper stamps while making B/A/A+ visibly escalating and honoring reduced motion [Task 1]\n  1284\t- when the user explicitly requested “gpt image 2.5 sunburst” -> report model-selector limitations rather than claiming exact model usage without tool evidence [Task 1]\n  1285\t\n  1286\t## Reusable knowledge\n  1287\t\n  1288\t- Extend existing `GradeStamp`, exact-grade `rubricGradeStampAsset`, sound profiles, `resultFresh`, and animation hooks instead of building a parallel grade-feedback system. A/B/C/D-F map to `a`/`b`/`c`/`revise`; `src/components/rubric/stamp-shader.tsx` is the WebGL solar-corona surface with reduced-motion/context-loss fallback. [Task 1]\n  1289\t- `src/components/ui/workflow-stamp.tsx` supplies Filed/Revised states; Revised is tied to accepted manuscript edits and dossier flows. Twyne’s expected visual baseline is editorial, ink-on-paper, restrained UI with reduced-motion handling. [Task 1]\n  1290\t\n  1291\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  1292\t\n  1293\t- `MODULE_NOT_FOUND` for a repo-local Impeccable script -> use `/home/diogenes/.agents/skills/impeccable/scripts/context.mjs` when the project path is absent. Only four generated files were visible at a checkpoint while 15 persisted assets were claimed -> enumerate `public/assets/...` and capture actual check output before declaring completion. [Task 1]\n  1294\t\n  1295\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/twyne dossier live title, brief editions, and Storybook\n  1296\tscope: Keep dossier editing visibly live and preserve folio-scoped, browsable saved brief history in established Twyne editorial cards.\n  1297\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne; reuse_rule=reuse the separate brief-edition model for saved replacements, not manuscript revisions or unsaved typing; browser interaction remains a required proof boundary.\n  1298\t\n  1299\t## Task 1: Fix live dossier title and add versioned briefs\n  1300\t\n  1301\t### rollout_summary_files\n  1302\t\n  1303\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/26/rollout-2026-09-26T04-13-58-01a0dcc7-3905-7aa3-9ad8-8db73307470f.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-26T08:55:04+00:00, thread_id=01a0dcc7-3905-7aa3-9ad8-8db73307470f, partial; typecheck passed, browser interaction unavailable)\n  1304\t\n  1305\t### keywords\n  1306\t\n  1307\t- AntiTabulaRasa, DossierPreview, ProjectBriefCard, brief-history.ts, brief-editions:<folioId>, IndexedDB, saveProjectBriefForFolio, onInput$, TS2322, EarlierEditions, Storybook\n  1308\t\n  1309\t## Task 2: Add a version-card Storybook state\n  1310\t\n  1311\t### rollout_summary_files\n  1312\t\n  1313\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/26/rollout-2026-09-26T04-13-58-01a0dcc7-3905-7aa3-9ad8-8db73307470f.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-26T08:55:04+00:00, thread_id=01a0dcc7-3905-7aa3-9ad8-8db73307470f, success; build.types and diff check passed)\n  1314\t\n  1315\t### keywords\n  1316\t\n  1317\t- project-brief-card.stories.tsx, EarlierEditions, BriefEdition, current filed copy, earlier editions\n  1318\t\n  1319\t## User preferences\n  1320\t\n  1321\t- when the user wanted the left-side title to show what was being entered and asked for “versioned briefs that i could look at and see” -> expose live state plus read-only historical saved versions [Task 1]\n  1322\t- when asking how “other posts” look -> reuse `ProjectBriefCard`/filed-dossier styling and vocabulary, not a novel visual pattern; when asking to “add this version card to storybook,” include representative interactive component states [Task 1][Task 2]\n  1323\t\n  1324\t## Reusable knowledge\n  1325\t\n  1326\t- `src/utils/brief-history.ts` keeps at most 20 superseded `ProjectBrief` records under IndexedDB metadata `brief-editions:<folioId>`. `saveProjectBriefForFolio` archives a changed previous brief then verifies the write; selection is wired through preview, card, form, conversational refinement, and editor load, and historical editions are read-only. [Task 1]\n  1327\t- Brief editions are distinct from `src/utils/revision-history.ts`: they are local-device saved replacements, never every unsaved keystroke. Qwik nested fields require explicit `onInput$` mutation of `store.answers[step.field!]`; the attempted `bind:value` path yielded TS2322. `EarlierEditions` provides two dated fixtures for Storybook. [Task 1][Task 2]\n  1328\t\n  1329\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  1330\t\n  1331\t- A first completion claimed the typing bug