ens, newest-write-wins, Run this check\n  1356\t\n  1357\t## Task 3: Make drawer identity and access meaningful\n  1358\t\n  1359\t### rollout_summary_files\n  1360\t\n  1361\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/26/rollout-2026-09-26T03-30-40-01a0dc9f-9346-7ac0-9e6c-d4e92f4211cf.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-26T08:54:19+00:00, thread_id=01a0dc9f-9346-7ac0-9e6c-d4e92f4211cf, success; TypeScript, ESLint, and diff check passed)\n  1362\t\n  1363\t### keywords\n  1364\t\n  1365\t- Drawer No. III, folioNumeral, owner, editor, commenter, Read and comment only, workspace-preview, Reicon\n  1366\t\n  1367\t## User preferences\n  1368\t\n  1369\t- when blue accents and dense explanatory copy were out of place, the user asked to remove redundant/onboarding text -> preserve paper/ink/vermilion styling, keep panels concise, and move limits/explanations to help links or tooltips [Task 1]\n  1370\t- when the user said icons “let people figure out what buttons and information do more easily” -> use accessible Reicon icons with short labels/tooltips; use `SiteSelect`, not native `<select>`, and preserve order: check buttons, selected description, inputs, results [Task 1]\n  1371\t- when material “should just be saved by default” and Jev should use checks automatically, with the tool reserved for explicit control -> autosave editable fields and make the board observe workspace-owned background results; adding passages/sources stays explicit [Task 2]\n  1372\t- when the target was “Drawer No. III / Pieces in Progress” and icons should communicate it quickly -> show dynamic drawer/folio/access context with compact icon-supported labels [Task 3]\n  1373\t\n  1374\t## Reusable knowledge\n  1375\t\n  1376\t- Use `src/components/ui/icon.tsx` and `src/utils/icon-system.ts`; `SiteSelect` is `src/components/ui/site-select.tsx`, and tokens are in `src/global.css`. `src/routes/help/review/index.tsx` holds long-form review explanation. Focused revision tests passed 7/0 and writing/lens tests 19/0. [Task 1]\n  1377\t- `src/utils/live-review.ts` owns background review and emits `twyne:live-review`; `cachedWritingLens` shares cache/in-flight work. Store folio notes as `writing-tools:${folioId}` in `src/utils/writing-tools-storage.ts`; serialized saves guarantee newest-write-wins. Automatic review remains read-only and retains findings, uncertainty, and evidence. [Task 2]\n  1378\t- Roles are `owner`, `editor`, `commenter`; commenters show “Read and comment only.” `folioNumeral()` in `src/utils/editorial-format.ts` provides Roman labels; live editor and landing preview should match. [Task 3]\n  1379\t\n  1380\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  1381\t\n  1382\t- CUA had no browser provider (`listBrowsers()` returned `[]`; `Browser is not available: iab`) -> report visual verification incomplete. The initial project-relative Impeccable context path failed; use `/home/diogenes/.agents/skills/impeccable/scripts/context.mjs`. [Task 1]\n  1383\t\n  1384\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/twyne HyperFrames launch-video audit and production\n  1385\tscope: Audit an interrupted agent video run against actual artifacts, then complete and verify all renderable Twyne launch films on this Linux workstation.\n  1386\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne; reuse_rule=reinspect the project/CLI/browser GPU configuration before rendering; the Intel ANGLE workaround is host-specific.\n  1387\t\n  1388\t## Task 1: Audit prior Entire/Claude launch-video work\n  1389\t\n  1390\t### rollout_summary_files\n  1391\t\n  1392\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/26/rollout-2026-09-26T02-10-19-01a0dc56-01ea-7e51-a7aa-600909e6091b.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-26T06:45:21+00:00, thread_id=01a0dc56-01ea-7e51-a7aa-600909e6091b, success)\n  1393\t\n  1394\t### keywords\n  1395\t\n  1396\t- Entire, Claude Code, be257798-5920-4b1f-a6d7-a542b054a90d, launch-videos, scaffold, MP4, render logs, contrast\n  1397\t\n  1398\t## Task 2: Finish, render, and verify six launch films\n  1399\t\n  1400\t### rollout_summary_files\n  1401\t\n  1402\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/26/rollout-2026-09-26T02-10-19-01a0dc56-01ea-7e51-a7aa-600909e6091b.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-26T06:45:21+00:00, thread_id=01a0dc56-01ea-7e51-a7aa-600909e6091b, success; six exports decoded and sampled)\n  1403\t\n  1404\t### keywords\n  1405\t\n  1406\t- HyperFrames 0.8.78, HYPERFRAMES_BROWSER_PATH, --use-angle=gl-egl, --use-angle=gl, BeginFrame, hardware gpu, render-newsreel.py, Sequential screenshot capture stalled, verification.json, ffprobe\n  1407\t\n  1408\t## Task 3: Generate the initial warm-editorial launch-media suite\n  1409\t\n  1410\t### rollout_summary_files\n  1411\t\n  1412\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/28/rollout-2026-09-28T22-53-14-01a0eb14-a661-78a0-90d3-a5ab174e7cc2.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-26T06:09:49+00:00, thread_id=01a0eb14-a661-78a0-90d3-a5ab174e7cc2, partial; source-media/compositions built, later completion is captured in Task 2)\n  1413\t\n  1414\t### keywords\n  1415\t\n  1416\t- Seedance 2.5, Gemini 3.8 Flash TTS, Lyria 3.5, GPT Image 2.5, launch-videos/_gen, 01-the-room, 02-roll-call, 03-edited, assets/js/words.js, paper-texture.jpg\n  1417\t\n  1418\t## User preferences\n  1419\t\n  1420\t- when the user asked to “check out the last entire session how far was claude from completing the task” -> inspect Entire metadata, transcript, composition source, actual MP4s, logs, and validation artifacts before estimating completion [Task 1]\n  1421\t- when the user said “finish the rest of the clean up” -> continue from saved project state through composition fixes, renders, and verification rather than merely reporting status [Task 2]\n  1422\t- when the user asked to “make a bunch of different commercials and videos” and “be creative” -> make autonomous creative decisions and retain the selected Seedance 2.5/Gemini 3.8 TTS/Lyria 3.5/GPT Image 2.5 toolset unless unavailable [Task 3]\n  1423\t\n  1424\t## Reusable knowledge\n  1425\t\n  1426\t- Session metadata/touched files do not distinguish authored, checked, rendered, and scaffolded output. In the audited run, only `01-the-room`/`02-roll-call` existed as MP4s; `03-edited` had contrast failures and `04-newsreel`/`05-the-strike`/`06-sting` were scaffolds. [Task 1]\n  1427\t- Pin was HyperFrames `0.8.78`. On this workstation, bundled Chrome’s Intel Mesa path worked with `--use-angle=gl`, whereas HyperFrames requested `gl-egl`; `rtk proxy python3 launch-videos/_gen/scripts/render-newsreel.py` translates the flag and sets `HYPERFRAMES_BROWSER_PATH`, enabling hardware BeginFrame rendering. [Task 2]\n  1428\t- Final evidence is `launch-videos/verification.json`: six MP4s at 60/46/46/34/15/6 seconds, expected dimensions, 30fps/audio, clean FFmpeg decode, and sampled frame review; outputs/gallery/readme/checks/posters are under `launch-videos/`. [Task 2]\n  1429\t- Twyne’s visual language is aged cream paper, near-black brown ink, vermilion, literary serif display type, DM Sans UI, and Special Elite/typewriter labels—avoid generic AI-chat/SaaS treatment. `_gen` scripts/manifests stage imagery, music, TTS, alignment, captions, fonts, SFX, and brand SVGs; word timing is bundled inline as `assets/js/words.js` to avoid render-time fetches. [Task 3]\n  1430\t\n  1431\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  1432\t\n  1433\t- Plain `--browser-gpu` fell back to software and stalled with `Sequential screenshot capture stalled: no frame progress for 60000ms (stuck at frame 114/1020)` -> use the saved host wrapper for shader/film compositions, not repeated retries. Fix contrast reported by `hyperframes check` before rendering; `03-edited` required darkening struck text and a vermilion label. [Task 2]\n  1434\t- Empty TTS `speakers: []`/`turns: []` triggers dialogue validation -> pass `speakers: null, turns: null`. A texture prompt needs explicit edge-to-edge/no-desk constraints; use `assets/img/paper-texture.jpg`, not `img/...`. `PATH=/usr/bin:$PATH npx hyperframes render -q delivery ...` works when bundled Chrome misses system libraries. [Task 3]\n  1435\t\n  1436\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/twyne Jev editor live-review, Not Organic linking, and v0.20.2 release\n  1437\tscope: Integrate typed Jev review into the real saved-draft editor loop, securely provision the Not Organic boundary, and verify clean CI/release evidence.\n  1438\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne; reuse_rule=recheck production provider funding, gateway configuration, and current release state; reuse editor wiring and clean-install lessons for this checkout.\n  1439\t\n  1440\t## Task 1: Move typed Jev review into the saved-draft/idle editor loop\n  1441\t\n  1442\t### rollout_summary_files\n  1443\t\n  1444\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/20/rollout-2026-09-20T01-56-11-01a0bd62-eabf-7a61-bb50-27a4047f7c4a.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-20T07:49:22+00:00, thread_id=01a0bd62-eabf-7a61-bb50-27a4047f7c4a, success; funded end-to-end review remains unverified)\n  1445\t\n  1446\t### keywords\n  1447\t\n  1448\t- live-review.ts, LiveReviewStatus, twyne:live-review, twyne:quick-review, twyne:content, twyne:draft-saved, saved-draft, idle delay, pause/resume, TypeSafe, Noul, Choice, Score\n  1449\t\n  1450\t## Task 2: Provision Not Organic and publish reproducible v0.20.2\n  1451\t\n  1452\t### rollout_summary_files\n  1453\t\n  1454\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/20/rollout-2026-09-20T01-56-11-01a0bd62-eabf-7a61-bb50-27a4047f7c4a.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-20T07:49:22+00:00, thread_id=01a0bd62-eabf-7a61-bb50-27a4047f7c4a, success; provider transport/release verified, no funded review probe)\n  1455\t\n  1456\t### keywords\n  1457\t\n  1458\t- judgement:evaluate, DPoP, PKCE, NOTORGANIC_AUDIENCE, invalid_product_assertion, hushed-aardvark-411, jsdom@26.1.0, Undici, .dagger/src/index.ts, twyne-tools, v0.20.2, 402 insufficient_funds\n  1459\t\n  1460\t## User preferences\n  1461\t\n  1462\t- when review should “no longer be on request” and happen “in editor ... as a person is saving” -> default editor AI to quiet saved-draft/idle processing, not isolated manual tools [Task 1]\n  1463\t- when asking whether features are “implemented in editor” -> verify real editor event wiring and visible in-editor output, not only a standalone route or panel [Task 1]\n  1464\t- when styling should be “consistent with our other styles” -> reuse Twyne tokens, shared controls, typography, and Editorial Board vocabulary rather than a local styling system [Task 1]\n  1465\t- when the user authorized “Configure the integration” -> provision and verify the live provider boundary rather than stopping at source code [Task 2]\n  1466\t\n  1467\t## Reusable knowledge\n  1468\t\n  1469\t- `src/utils/live-review.ts` owns saved-draft review, persistence by folio, retry/backoff, and `twyne:live-review` / `twyne:quick-review`; `src/components/writing-tools/live-review-status.tsx` provides status, findings, pause/resume, and unavailable-state routing. Preserve typed findings, uncertainty, evidence passages, and read-only behavior: review must not edit prose automatically. [Task 1]\n  1470\t- Background work needs spend guards: substantive word threshold, idle delay, minimum interval, and per-session cap. TypeSafe calls use typed `state` plus `noul`, `choice`, and `score`; Choice has a criteria map, Score ordered levels, and Noul has no confidence. [Task 1]\n  1471\t- Not Organic production uses `https://api.notorganic.info`, capability `judgement:evaluate`, and DPoP-bound tokens. Link with PKCE one-time state and server-side token/account verification; do not trust a browser-supplied DID, expose gateway credentials, or send upstream error bodies to browsers. [Task 2]\n  1472\t- Production gateway audience is `notorganic`, independent of issuer. The release added declared `jsdom@26.1.0` compatible with the pinned Undici and installs the separate `packages/twyne-tools/bun.lock` in `.dagger/src/index.ts` before CLI checks. Final evidence: 1,474 tests with 39 skips/0 failures, CLI 22 tests, type/build/lint/format/package checks, successful release assets, and Railway `SUCCESS` for `254ad09a8346972910fcab59e62d2b75033578b7`. [Task 2]\n  1473\t\n  1474\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  1475\t\n  1476\t- Isolated `/writing-tools/` and button-triggered rubric paths are not editor integration -> trace `twyne:content`, `twyne:draft-saved`, and folio lifecycle events, then inspect the visible editor state. [Task 1]\n  1477\t- `401 invalid_product_assertion` -> keep `NOTORGANIC_AUDIENCE` separate from `NOTORGANIC_ISSUER` and set the production audience to `notorganic`; direct `/v1/judgement` requests correctly fail without the signed assertion-to-DPoP path. A `402 insufficient_funds` probe proves the funded review itself was not verified. [Task 2]\n  1478\t- Local green tests can hide clean-CI dependency faults -> run an isolated install and the full CI dependency graph. `jsdom@29.1.1` expected an Undici handler absent from this checkout; missing `twyne-tools` install also failed Dagger. Preserve unrelated `devenv.lock` and `skills-lock.json` changes. [Task 2]\n  1479\t\n  1480\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/interleave-app Jev/TypeSafe integration, automatic Weave matching, and venue ranking\n  1481\tscope: Reuse the Not Organic judgement transport and conservative semantic decisions across Weave/Woven/Worn without replacing deterministic or safety-critical logic.\n  1482\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/interleave-app; reuse_rule=inspect the active branch/worktree and rerun Devenv codegen/typecheck/lint/test before claiming integration complete; this evidence has no live gateway/browser/deployment proof.\n  1483\t\n  1484\t## Task 1: Map a Jev foundation across Weave, Woven, and Worn\n  1485\t\n  1486\t### rollout_summary_files\n  1487\t\n  1488\t- rollout_summaries/2026-09-21T05-07-40-GKiq-jev_interleave_integration_investigation.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/interleave-app, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/21/rollout-2026-09-21T01-07-40-01a0c25c-da82-7483-8908-41db1075e4fe.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-20T05:23:06+00:00, thread_id=01a0c25c-da82-7483-8908-41db1075e4fe, partial; archaeology only, no plan/file implementation)\n  1489\t\n  1490\t### keywords\n  1491\t\n  1492\t- POST /v1/judgement, judgement:evaluate, notOrganicClient.ts, product assertion, DPoP, typed wire codec, calibrationSha256, abstention, confect/host/judgments, Woven, Worn\n  1493\t\n  1494\t## Task 2: Implement automatic Weave matchmaking and conservative venue ranking\n  1495\t\n  1496\t### rollout_summary_files\n  1497\t\n  1498\t- rollout_summaries/2026-09-20T05-28-30-RqmQ-jev_interleave_matchmaking_venue_ranking.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/interleave-app, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/20/rollout-2026-09-20T01-28-30-01a0bd49-92b6-7b73-8d4f-101d07ce09c8.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-20T06:38:38+00:00, thread_id=01a0bd49-92b6-7b73-8d4f-101d07ce09c8, partial; scoped tests passed, repository-wide verification incomplete)\n  1499\t\n  1500\t### keywords\n  1501\t\n  1502\t- weaveMatchmakingPolicy.ts, weaveMatchmaking.ts, probability >= 0.98, confidence >= 0.95, margin >= 0.9, uncalibrated judgement provenance, weaveVenueJudgement.ts, nearby order, CONVEX_TMPDIR\n  1503\t\n  1504\t## User preferences\n  1505\t\n  1506\t- when the user said “yeah continue from this session.” -> continue from existing session and Git context rather than restarting discovery or asking for a recap [Task 2]\n  1507\t- for deep integration across “weave, woven and worn,” start with cross-repository archaeology of Keating/Twyne/TypeSafe/Not Organic rather than editing one call site [Task 1]\n  1508\t- “matching won't require administrative review unless the profile spikes Jev's judgement. The bar should be high for getting admin review” -> submitted profiles match automatically; human review is only for unusually strong explicit serious-concern judgements [Task 2]\n  1509\t\n  1510\t## Reusable knowledge\n  1511\t\n  1512\t- Reuse `confect/handlers/lib/notOrganicClient.ts`: it signs a short-lived Ed25519 product assertion, exchanges a DPoP token, caches it, signs each request, and adds product/idempotency/cost headers. Route to `POST /v1/judgement` with `judgement:evaluate`; gateway keeps the TypeSafe key. Locally validate, return failures rather than throw, retry only retryable statuses, do not echo upstream bodies, and abstain/fallback when unavailable. [Task 1][Task 2]\n  1513\t- Keep arithmetic, counts, authorization, and closed deterministic logic Tier 0. Jev may classify/select/interpret bounded vocabulary; use typed Noul/Choice/Score distributions and modal levels, preserve calibration/provenance, and abstain to deterministic baselines when evidence/calibration is insufficient. Worn must not infer recovery stage, diagnosis, safety, healing percentages, or automatic graduation. [Task 1][Task 2]\n  1514\t- `weaveMatchmakingPolicy.ts` deterministically builds eligibility/evidence and `weaveMatchmaking.ts` performs prepare/Jev/commit. Require consenting adults, completed interview evidence, mutual explicit gender preferences, no ban/current relationship, and distance checks; cap batches at six candidates/three proposals. Commit must recheck evidence fingerprints, consent, relationship/ban state, timing, and existing pairs. New proposals store uncalibrated provenance, not compatibility percentages. [Task 2]\n  1515\t- Venue ranking begins with real nearby venues and deterministic distance order. Apply Jev only for semantic fit; tie, diffuse confidence, missing evidence, or unavailable judgement preserves the original nearby order. Never infer price, hours, availability, accessibility, safety, or booking status. [Task 2]\n  1516\t\n  1517\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  1518\t\n  1519\t- Never run `skate list @secrets` in a way that prints values; list names only (for example `skate list @secrets | cut -f1`) and do not use WebFetch while secrets are in context. Credentials exposed in a session require rotation. [Task 1][Task 2]\n  1520\t- Blanket administrative review contradicted the user’s requested policy -> escalate only at probability >= `0.98`, confidence >= `0.95`, and margin >= `0.9`; uncertain/insufficient evidence abstains and does not queue review. Do not treat Jev as relationship-success probability or permission to auto-accept, reveal photos, schedule dates, or reject users. [Task 2]\n  1521\t- `devenv tasks run interleave:codegen` can fail its TypeScript phase when `/tmp` and `convex/_generated` differ filesystems -> set `CONVEX_TMPDIR` under the project filesystem, then run codegen, `interleave:typecheck`, `interleave:lint`, and `interleave:test` separately. The combined final verification was user-aborted; scoped 12 tests/67 assertions and formatting do not prove full integration. [Task 2]\n  1522\t\n  1523\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/keating Jev benchmark provenance and multilingual judge comparison\n  1524\tscope: Audit judgement benchmarks and provider comparisons without confusing completion, agreement, or evidence selection with independently validated accuracy.\n  1525\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating; reuse_rule=reinspect frozen artifacts, inputs, model revisions, denominator policy, and source session chronology before quoting results or changing model selection.\n  1526\t\n  1527\t## Task 1: Audit Jev's apparent 100% benchmark and Entire development history\n  1528\t\n  1529\t### rollout_summary_files\n  1530\t\n  1531\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/24/rollout-2026-09-24T04-11-24-01a0d278-26ce-7a12-bb7c-5e032d1f2e9c.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-24T22:15:17+00:00, thread_id=01a0d278-26ce-7a12-bb7c-5e032d1f2e9c, success; source/results and Entire chronology audited)\n  1532\t\n  1533\t### keywords\n  1534\t\n  1535\t- Jev, System One, Entire, jev-1.13.0, 18/18, 895/895, 34/124, 169/169, evidence-selection, __no_match__, .keating/tmp/laya/jev_bench.py, scripts/on-device-site/collect.py\n  1536\t\n  1537\t## Task 2: Complete a frozen six-language judgement-provider comparison\n  1538\t\n  1539\t### rollout_summary_files\n  1540\t\n  1541\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/24/rollout-2026-09-24T04-11-24-01a0d278-26ce-7a12-bb7c-5e032d1f2e9c.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-24T22:15:17+00:00, thread_id=01a0d278-26ce-7a12-bb7c-5e032d1f2e9c, success; integrity and temporary-GPU cleanup verified)\n  1542\t\n  1543\t### keywords\n  1544\t\n  1545\t- multilingual-v1, Kev, CLM, Laya, Astra, final-integrity-check.json, gpu-cleanup.json, 3600 receipts, 3599 validResponses, Jev Spanish, native-speaker review, sjuxnw207vhqvd\n  1546\t\n  1547\t## User preferences\n  1548\t\n  1549\t- when Jev was “getting a hundred” and “it seems sus,” the user asked to “check with entire to see as well the session and how that developed” -> audit both saved artifacts/current source and the original agent-session chronology before judging credibility. [Task 1]\n  1550\t- for benchmark claims, report what each metric proves and does not prove; distinguish response coverage, agreement, evidence selection, and independently validated accuracy. [Task 1]\n  1551\t- for provider comparisons, preserve failed/aborted work, keep accuracy and abstention separate, and clean up temporary compute instead of obscuring spend/failure boundaries. [Task 2]\n  1552\t\n  1553\t## Reusable knowledge\n  1554\t\n  1555\t- `.keating/tmp/laya/jev_bench.py` defined 18 authored subject-routing cases and 11 categories before calling `jev-1.13.0`; recorded `18/18` shows exact matches on that small explicit-label probe, not general judgement accuracy. `895/895` is answered dispatched requests, `34/124` is KEV agreement with Jev over 11 requests, and `169/169` only means non-`__no_match__` selection; none independently validate correctness/support. [Task 1]\n  1556\t- The audited Entire session `01a0c25c-da83-74d3-9568-05dd6ed00110` showed labels existed before the Jev call and no later mutation made results match. Needle remains reliable for verbatim-span extraction/local retrieval, not semantic routing. [Task 1]\n  1557\t- Frozen artifacts live in `.keating/benchmarks/context-window/multilingual-v1/`; retain original questions, labels, rubrics, Choice IDs, request hashes, provider/native revisions, full-context proof, and invalid/missing responses in `execution/final-integrity-check.json`. [Task 2]\n  1558\t- Twelve retained models produced 3,600 receipts and 3,599 valid responses. Jev led fixed-0.5 authored-label accuracy at roughly 92.6–95.1%; Kev 9B led local models at roughly 81.5–86.4%. These are not production calibration or human-learning evidence; evidence selection is a separate metric. [Task 2]\n  1559\t\n  1560\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  1561\t\n  1562\t- Do not call 18/18 general judgement accuracy, compare models with unequal criteria/input information, or infer calibrated correctness from confidence/abstention without independently labelled data. [Task 1]\n  1563\t- Keep cancelled Astra and the Jev Spanish validation failure in planned denominators; do not silently rerun, replace, or rank partial work. Translation variants share 25 workflow families, and hosted/native latency includes unlike transport/preflight costs. [Task 2]\n  1564\t\n  1565\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/keating Jev cascade investigation and production chat/model-picker fixes\n  1566\tscope: Advance the Jev/model-cascade only from current evidence, then ship narrowly scoped Keating chat/model-picker behavior without overstating visual proof.\n  1567\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating; reuse_rule=reinspect the current cascade plan, imports, shared-picker callers, worktree, and Railway status before extending or claiming deployment success.\n  1568\t\n  1569\t## Task 1: Audit Jev/model-cascade implementation against the full plan\n  1570\t\n  1571\t### rollout_summary_files\n  1572\t\n  1573\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/19/rollout-2026-09-19T16-07-23-01a0bb47-dbc1-7973-907b-80bc6b52bec1.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-20T18:45:21+00:00, thread_id=01a0bb47-dbc1-7973-907b-80bc6b52bec1, partial; focused judgement checks passed, full plan remains open)\n  1574\t\n  1575\t### keywords\n  1576\t\n  1577\t- Jev, TypeSafe, System One, docs/plans/jev-model-cascade.md, Choice, Score, Noul, questionDigest, contracts.ts, router.ts, proxy, observed, calibration, 120 pass\n  1578\t\n  1579\t## Task 2: Hide empty Flue assistant placeholders while preserving saved failures\n  1580\t\n  1581\t### rollout_summary_files\n  1582\t\n  1583\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/19/rollout-2026-09-19T16-07-23-01a0bb47-dbc1-7973-907b-80bc6b52bec1.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-20T18:45:21+00:00, thread_id=01a0bb47-dbc1-7973-907b-80bc6b52bec1, success; focused tests/typecheck, commit, push, and Railway success verified)\n  1584\t\n  1585\t### keywords\n  1586\t\n  1587\t- Flue, empty assistant rows, shouldRenderFlueMessage, AssistantChatPanel.tsx, assistant-chat-messages.ts, flue-message-visibility.test.ts, 29d69253f436524c38f2b91100096871ac9fb62b\n  1588\t\n  1589\t## Task 3: Pin Keating Cloud's provider default in shared model search\n  1590\t\n  1591\t### rollout_summary_files\n  1592\t\n  1593\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/19/rollout-2026-09-19T16-07-23-01a0bb47-dbc1-7973-907b-80bc6b52bec1.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-20T18:45:21+00:00, thread_id=01a0bb47-dbc1-7973-907b-80bc6b52bec1, success; focused tests/typecheck, clean tree, push, and Railway success verified)\n  1594\t\n  1595\t### keywords\n  1596\t\n  1597\t- ModelPicker, ModelSelector, orderedPickerItems, NOTORGANIC_DEFAULT_MODEL, Provider default, Inkling Small, model-picker-pinning.test.tsx, 170652660840096c43829f6205f5fb4c115989ae\n  1598\t\n  1599\t## User preferences\n  1600\t\n  1601\t- when advancing the cascade, the user explicitly asked for “Entire history, TypeSafe/System One, decomposed Jev questions, exhaustive self-judgement, and subagents” -> inspect current state first; use narrow typed questions with abstention and prove every plan requirement from current files/tests/runtime evidence. [Task 1]\n  1602\t- when the user asked to push changes once done -> complete focused checks, commit, push, deployment-status, and clean-tree verification; do not call the UI visually verified without a browser/manual pass. [Task 2][Task 3]\n  1603\t- when the user clarified “it should have provider default and be pinned to the top” -> label the provider default explicitly and keep it first through model switching and search without resurrecting caller-excluded items. [Task 3]\n  1604\t\n  1605\t## Reusable knowledge\n  1606\t\n  1607\t- TypeSafe System One is `POST https://api.typesafe.ai/v1/systemone` with `{state, model, questions}`; batch independent questions over the same narrowly structured state. Use `Noul` for one absolute condition, `Choice` for relative alternatives, explicit abstention, and code-owned arithmetic/counts/dates. `Score` levels are not reliable magnitude interpolation. [Task 1]\n  1608\t- Judgement outputs are `proxy`, never `observed` or promotion eligibility; selected evidence must come from real learner spans. Calibration keys include backend/model/question digest and cannot cross backends. `questionDigest` lives in `packages/learner-contracts/src/judgement/contracts.ts`, not `router.ts`; importing it from `router.ts` caused module-load failures. [Task 1]\n  1609\t- Empty failed Flue attempts are a render-projection issue: `shouldRenderFlueMessage` hides only empty/whitespace assistant placeholders and non-visible diagnostics, while retaining user messages, partial text, reasoning, tools, attachments, settlement notices, lifecycle/error state, and retry controls. [Task 2]\n  1610\t- The shared picker serves chat/live/review/training/speech/image. Use opt-in item metadata: `NOTORGANIC_DEFAULT_MODEL` (`balanced`, `Inkling Small`) is pinned, then the selected non-default model, then ordinary query-filtered items; caller exclusions remain excluded. [Task 3]\n  1611\t\n  1612\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  1613\t\n  1614\t- Focused post-fix judgement validation (`120 pass, 0 fail`) does not establish the full cascade: benchmark agreement, remaining judge-site migrations, end-to-end learner integrations, and calibration/runtime gates remained unverified. Entire semantic search failed on authentication/keyring access; use local `entire session list`/`checkpoint explain` or restore auth. [Task 1]\n  1615\t- Production deployment status proves the scoped code shipped, not browser/manual behavior. The Flue and picker fixes had focused tests/typecheck plus Railway `SUCCESS`, but no browser/manual test. [Task 2][Task 3]\n  1616\t\n  1617\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/twyne production provider relay and auth/session recovery\n  1618\tscope: Operate Twyne's shared remote-BYOK transport and harden Convex, Not Organic, and ATProto browser-session recovery without overstating signed-in account proof.\n  1619\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne; reuse_rule=recheck current provider configuration, Railway proxy headers, OAuth grants, Convex deployment, live account state, and dirty worktree before reuse or production claims.\n  1620\t\n  1621\t## Task 1: Deploy a generalized remote-provider relay\n  1622\t\n  1623\t### rollout_summary_files\n  1624\t\n  1625\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/20/rollout-2026-09-20T13-41-47-01a0bfe8-ea41-7552-a283-0faea9208674.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-20T18:52:35+00:00, thread_id=01a0bfe8-ea41-7552-a283-0faea9208674, success; MiniMax/OpenAI dummy-key transport smoke verified)\n  1626\t\n  1627\t### keywords\n  1628\t\n  1629\t- /api/provider/, provider-fetch.ts, provider-relay.server.ts, SSRF, DNS pinning, X-Forwarded-Proto, PROTOCOL_HEADER, CSRF check failed, MiniMax, OpenAI, Railway d7378eae-ef0c-4369-ad4c-9e4dc0a70b65\n  1630\t\n  1631\t## Task 2: Refresh Convex tokens and reconnect existing Not Organic links\n  1632\t\n  1633\t### rollout_summary_files\n  1634\t\n  1635\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/20/rollout-2026-09-20T13-41-47-01a0bfe8-ea41-7552-a283-0faea9208674.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-20T18:52:35+00:00, thread_id=01a0bfe8-ea41-7552-a283-0faea9208674, partial; unit proof, signed-in account flow open)\n  1636\t\n  1637\t### keywords\n  1638\t\n  1639\t- createConvexTokenFetcher, forceRefreshToken, hasAuthenticatedConvexIdentity, convexAuthenticated, Reconnect Not Organic, Check again, providerIdentity.ts\n  1640\t\n  1641\t## Task 3: Recover ATProto/Bluesky stale sessions without consuming other callbacks\n  1642\t\n  1643\t### rollout_summary_files\n  1644\t\n  1645\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/20/rollout-2026-09-20T13-41-47-01a0bfe8-ea41-7552-a283-0faea9208674.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-20T18:52:35+00:00, thread_id=01a0bfe8-ea41-7552-a283-0faea9208674, partial; exact production 400 not reproduced)\n  1646\t\n  1647\t### keywords\n  1648\t\n  1649\t- atproto.ts, ATPROTO_SESSION_CHANGED, initSessionPromise, stale token set, invalid_grant, use_dpop_nonce, /auth/callback/, PUBLIC_BSKY_APPVIEW\n  1650\t\n  1651\t## User preferences\n  1652\t\n  1653\t- when the user said “make sure that this solution doesn't only work for minimax but is gen purpose” -> fix provider transport as a shared abstraction across configured remote providers, not a reported-provider special case. [Task 1]\n  1654\t- when an already-connected account could not connect in Settings, the user expected existing state to be queried/reactively exposed with a reconnect path rather than an initial-connect-only UI. [Task 2]\n  1655\t\n  1656\t## Reusable knowledge\n  1657\t\n  1658\t- Remote providers use same-origin `/api/provider/` via `src/utils/provider-fetch.ts`; loopback endpoints remain direct. `provider-relay.server.ts` restricts targets to public HTTPS, pins DNS, rejects private/reserved/mapped addresses and redirects, restricts headers/cookies, bounds bodies, and forwards streaming responses without response cookies/CORS headers. [Task 1]\n  1659\t- Railway TLS termination needs `PROTOCOL_HEADER=x-forwarded-proto` in `server.js`; otherwise Qwik inferred `http://twyne.love` and rejected production POSTs with `403 CSRF check failed`. Dummy MiniMax/OpenAI keys returned expected readable 401s, proving transport but not valid-key behavior for all providers. [Task 1]\n  1660\t- `createConvexTokenFetcher` single-flights refreshes and must honor `forceRefreshToken`; `hasAuthenticatedConvexIdentity` still requires a product user, `provider: \"convex\"`, and `convexAuthenticated === true`. Existing link UI supports reactive DID state, reconnect, and check-again. [Task 2]\n  1661\t- Reuse active ATProto session/profile with single-flight initialization; consume OAuth callback parameters only at `/auth/callback/`. Public profile hydration uses `https://public.api.bsky.app`; preserve the DID rather than adding arbitrary audience-bound scope. [Task 3]\n  1662\t\n  1663\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  1664\t\n  1665\t- Configure forwarded-protocol handling before live POST tests. Focused `76 pass`, typecheck/lint/build, diff check, `/settings/` 200, and smoke were verified, but a dirty worktree remained and no Convex production deployment occurred. [Task 1]\n  1666\t- Do not claim the account-specific Not Organic callback/link flow or the user's exact Bluesky 400 recovery is fixed until a signed-in browser verifies it. [Task 2][Task 3]\n  1667\t\n  1668\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/keating MiniCPM5 WebGPU diagnostics and error classification\n  1669\tscope: Diagnose actual browser-model runtime failures and expose bounded, privacy-safe diagnostic evidence without mistaking adapter support for model execution.\n  1670\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating; reuse_rule=reinspect target hardware, browser/runtime versions, model artifact, and deployment state; this verified instrumentation, not a Windows-GPU root-cause fix.\n  1671\t\n  1672\t## Task 1: Diagnose and instrument MiniCPM5 ONNX Runtime WebGPU failures\n  1673\t\n  1674\t### rollout_summary_files\n  1675\t\n  1676\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/20/rollout-2026-09-20T15-12-01-01a0c03b-8622-7e20-95bf-bb748d4fb7fc.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-20T19:41:27+00:00, thread_id=01a0c03b-8622-7e20-95bf-bb748d4fb7fc, partial; diagnostics/build verified, target device not retested)\n  1677\t\n  1678\t### keywords\n  1679\t\n  1680\t- MiniCPM5-2B-ONNX, RASMUS, q4f16, OrtRun, BufferManager::Download, mapAsync, Invalid Buffer, local-model-diagnostics.ts, keating:local-model-debug, shader-f16\n  1681\t\n  1682\t## User preferences\n  1683\t\n  1684\t- when the user supplied hardware and `edge://gpu` evidence, they wanted diagnosis based on the actual adapter/runtime rather than generic compatibility advice; when they asked to “see if we can expose this with some improved errors,” -> add observability before claiming a root-cause fix. [Task 1]\n  1685\t\n  1686\t## Reusable knowledge\n  1687\t\n  1688\t- `web/src/lib/local-model-diagnostics.ts` observes the actual ONNX Runtime device without creating a second adapter/device/model; reports capture model/dtype/phase, runtime versions, token limits, features/limits, adapter info, first device error/loss, capped operation errors, and original runtime error. Enable with `localStorage.setItem(\"keating:local-model-debug\", \"1\")`, reload, copy `[local-model] diagnostics`, then remove the key. [Task 1]\n  1689\t- `classifyLocalModelError` distinguishes device loss, allocation/buffer-limit failures, invalid-buffer readback, missing adapter/`shader-f16`, unsupported quantization, and generic WebGPU execution. Eight focused tests, web typecheck, production build, and `git diff --check` passed. [Task 1]\n  1690\t\n  1691\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  1692\t\n  1693\t- `shader-f16`, a working adapter, and 2 GiB limits do not prove MiniCPM5 can execute. `Invalid Buffer` alone does not prove OOM: capture the first validation/allocation error or device-loss reason. The Intel Iris Xe target root cause remains unverified. [Task 1]\n  1694\t\n  1695\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/keating Jev/Needle routing, teaching-policy benchmark, and draft gate\n  1696\tscope: Use typed Jev decisions and deterministic checks for teaching/OpenUI behavior; restrict Needle to measured extraction/shortlisting rather than semantic authority.\n  1697\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating; reuse_rule=recheck model/provider availability, corpus, benchmark configuration, and dirty-worktree state before activation or claims of learning efficacy.\n  1698\t\n  1699\t## Task 1: Evaluate Needle subject routing and local-model roles\n  1700\t\n  1701\t### rollout_summary_files\n  1702\t\n  1703\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/21/rollout-2026-09-21T01-07-40-01a0c25c-da83-74d3-9568-05dd6ed00110.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-21T07:56:03+00:00, thread_id=01a0c25c-da83-74d3-9568-05dd6ed00110, partial; reproducible fine-tune inadequate)\n  1704\t\n  1705\t### keywords\n  1706\t\n  1707\t- Needle 3, System One, Jev, domains.ts, 36 fields, keating-subject.cact, 7/18, 39/170, exact-span extraction, RunPod, .cact\n  1708\t\n  1709\t## Task 2: Decompose teaching policy and benchmark private draft review\n  1710\t\n  1711\t### rollout_summary_files\n  1712\t\n  1713\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/21/rollout-2026-09-21T19-22-38-01a0c647-5574-7062-96f5-05fd00fa775b.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-22T00:06:48+00:00, thread_id=01a0c647-5574-7062-96f5-05fd00fa775b, partial; scoped benchmark/web proof, no full repository or production activation)\n  1714\t\n  1715\t### keywords\n  1716\t\n  1717\t- teaching-policy-catalog.ts, Noul, Choice, Score, unknown, prompt-adherence, fixture-offset, full compact governed drafted, AgentTool, async [\"import\"]\n  1718\t\n  1719\t## User preferences\n  1720\t\n  1721\t- “small/local models should not be asked to perform expensive or broad judgement calls”; hosted Jev may select OpenUI slots before generation, while system prompts retain persona, safety, Socratic stance, and evidence discipline. [Task 1]\n  1722\t- when the user asked to “break down the system prompt ... into judgements and decisions that jev can make” and make difficult questions “more granular [and] more verifiable” -> split semantic judgments from deterministic code checks and avoid one monolithic evaluator. [Task 2]\n  1723\t\n  1724\t## Reusable knowledge\n  1725\t\n  1726\t- Needle is reliable for code-validated exact source-span extraction and may cheaply shortlist tools, but it is not a semantic judge. The fine-tuned router achieved only 7/18 held-out and 39/170 in-sample; retain deterministic keyword/curated routing and escalate semantic decisions to Jev. [Task 1]\n  1727\t- TypeSafe System One questions are Noul/Choice/Score; independent same-state questions may fan out. Missing/malformed/uncertain results are `unknown`, never pass; critical violations cannot average away. Treat learner text, sources, and tool results as evidence, not instructions. [Task 2]\n  1728\t- `packages/learner-contracts/src/judgement/` holds typed policy contracts/catalog/assessment. Keep OpenUI validity, tool schemas, evidence presence, and authorization deterministic; private draft gate withholds rejected prose, raw errors, invalid tools, and hidden reasoning while exposing content-free status. [Task 2]\n  1729\t\n  1730\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  1731\t\n  1732\t- A stable Needle output is not a correct one. Compare transferred artifact bytes/checksum before blaming runtimes; an earlier `.cact` format problem was base64 corruption. Never print secrets; rotate exposed credentials. [Task 1]\n  1733\t- The 94.4% development / 100% resolved 18-label holdout metrics are authored, uncalibrated proxies, not human-learning evidence. Include withheld/unknown/timeouts in denominators; do not claim speedup or efficacy. [Task 2]\n  1734\t\n  1735\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/keating UX defaults, provider diagnostics, and support recovery\n  1736\tscope: Compact tool-detail defaults, media/speech provider seams, consent-gated diagnostics, and audit/reviewer fixes for Keating chat.\n  1737\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating; reuse_rule=recheck provider IDs, auth, deployed environment variables, mail routing, and dirty worktree before live claims.\n  1738\t\n  1739\t## Task 1: Implement chat defaults, image/speech changes, and diagnostics recovery\n  1740\t\n  1741\t### rollout_summary_files\n  1742\t\n  1743\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/21/rollout-2026-09-21T16-54-53-01a0c5c0-10c2-7af2-9772-0b0b144d4a8b.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-21T21:39:08+00:00, thread_id=01a0c5c0-10c2-7af2-9772-0b0b144d4a8b, partial; local checks passed, provider/mail proof open)\n  1744\t\n  1745\t### keywords\n  1746\t\n  1747\t- showToolUi, flashcardSoundEnabled, image-generators.ts, gpt-image-2.5-flare, gemini-generate-content, GPT Live, microphoneEnabled, diagnosticsReporting, mailto:help@keating.help, Resend\n  1748\t\n  1749\t## Task 2: Audit Entire request coverage and repair reviewer findings\n  1750\t\n  1751\t### rollout_summary_files\n  1752\t\n  1753\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/21/rollout-2026-09-21T17-42-48-01a0c5eb-edbf-7a10-a2c8-1a938954381d.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-21T22:47:13+00:00, thread_id=01a0c5eb-edbf-7a10-a2c8-1a938954381d, success; local audit/focused fixes only)\n  1754\t\n  1755\t### keywords\n  1756\t\n  1757\t- entire checkpoint explain --raw-transcript, ModelPicker, KeatingApiKeyPromptDialog, Retry-After, 429, resolveImageQuality, nodepod-boot-files.ts, railway logs --service keating\n  1758\t\n  1759\t## User preferences\n  1760\t\n  1761\t- the user does not want “tool calling details to be shown in chat by default” and wants flashcard sounds on by default -> use compact transcripts and enabled feedback sounds unless settings explicitly say otherwise. [Task 1]\n  1762\t- for unknown failures, the user wants contextual diagnostics submission, an easy email fallback when declined, and a small consent step -> offer actionable recovery rather than generic error text. [Task 1]\n  1763\t- when auditing prior work, the user asked to check the Entire CLI session and “the things thata i requested” -> extract every substantive request and compare it item by item with implementation, distinguishing local completion, partial work, blocks, and live verification. [Task 2]\n  1764\t\n  1765\t## Reusable knowledge\n  1766\t\n  1767\t- Web settings are `showToolUi: false`, `flashcardSoundEnabled: true`; mobile's `showToolDetails: false` is distinct from interactive-card `showToolUi`. Diagnostics default off, redact/cap client data, use `/api/diagnostics/report`, then send via Resend or log fallback; specialized known errors keep specialized actions. [Task 1]\n  1768\t- GPT Live is gated by `NOTORGANIC_ENABLED`; duplex selection/enabling turns on `microphoneEnabled`, but TTS stays opt-in. `web/src/lib/image-generators.ts` is the catalog; provider model IDs have not had live smoke proof. [Task 1]\n  1769\t- Entire fallback for parser failure is `entire checkpoint explain <id> --raw-transcript`. Close `ModelPicker` before the API-key dialog. A per-process diagnostics limiter returns explicit `Response.json` 429 plus `Retry-After: 900`; regenerate NodePod boot files after source changes. [Task 2]\n  1770\t\n  1771\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  1772\t\n  1773\t- `help@keating.help` is not operational proof: forwarding MX/SPF without DKIM/DMARC, destination inbox, and external send/receive remains insufficient. Diagnostics throttling resets per replica/restart and is not a deployment-wide quota. [Task 1][Task 2]\n  1774\t- Do not treat Entire's index as complete, GitNexus stale/truncated output as conclusive, or local focused tests as browser/live-provider/deployment/email validation. [Task 2]\n  1775\t\n  1776\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/textbook package publication, Radicle, copyable docs, and production routing\n  1777\tscope: Publish Textbook safely, maintain the repo-local/public Radicle workflow, make dynamically rendered docs controls work, and keep production destinations distinct from local defaults.\n  1778\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/textbook; reuse_rule=reinspect package availability, configured Radicle remote/RID, Railway service state, and current URL variables before publishing/deploying.\n  1779\t\n  1780\t## Task 1: Publish textbook-sh and deploy all four product surfaces\n  1781\t\n  1782\t### rollout_summary_files\n  1783\t\n  1784\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/textbook, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/21/rollout-2026-09-21T02-00-34-01a0c28d-4957-75e2-8569-a6e6a687566f.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-21T09:28:16+00:00, thread_id=01a0c28d-4957-75e2-8569-a6e6a687566f, success; package/live surfaces verified)\n  1785\t\n  1786\t### keywords\n  1787\t\n  1788\t- textbook-sh, bunx textbook, delegated click handling, role=status, RAD_HOME, .radicle, railway pre-push, textbook.sh, docs.textbook.sh\n  1789\t\n  1790\t## Task 2: Repair public landing localhost redirects\n  1791\t\n  1792\t### rollout_summary_files\n  1793\t\n  1794\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/textbook, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/21/rollout-2026-09-21T18-11-14-01a0c605-f556-7002-8478-41263fd6c87e.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-21T23:06:56+00:00, thread_id=01a0c605-f556-7002-8478-41263fd6c87e, partial; diagnosis)\n  1795\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/textbook, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/21/rollout-2026-09-21T19-09-00-01a0c63a-d7fd-7161-81ad-7380b176e6e2.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-22T00:53:50+00:00, thread_id=01a0c63a-d7fd-7161-81ad-7380b176e6e2, success; public redirects verified)\n  1796\t\n  1797\t### keywords\n  1798\t\n  1799\t- railway.landing.json, LANDING_URL, DOCS_URL, TERMINAL_URL, CANVAS_URL, localhost:8008, /canvas, a53b9fd4-0bde-429f-a169-4667a13eac30, rad\n  1800\t\n  1801\t## User preferences\n  1802\t\n  1803\t- “if textbook-sh is free as a package name let's take that” -> prefer the simplest available unscoped package; “just push to main without republish right now” -> do not republish as an implied deploy step. [Task 1]\n  1804\t- “search for what is sending you to localhost in prod ... change it to the correct host unless we are launching local,” then “deplpy” -> preserve local defaults but make production navigation environment-driven and deploy the verified correction. [Task 2]\n  1805\t\n  1806\t## Reusable knowledge\n  1807\t\n  1808\t- `textbook-sh@0.2.0` provides `textbook`, `tb`, and `textbook-sh`. Docs injected after load need delegated document-level handling, with accessible copied/failure status. Repo-local Radicle uses `RAD_HOME=/home/diogenes/Projects/textbook/.radicle`; its pre-push hook deploys landing/docs/terminal/canvas independently. [Task 1]\n  1809\t- `src/site.ts` keeps local 8000/8001/8002/8008 defaults; `railway.landing.json` and live service variables must explicitly set all four public hosts. After config deployment, inspect actual Railway service state and live redirect locations. [Task 2]\n  1810\t\n  1811\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  1812\t\n  1813\t- Per-button listeners fail for dynamic docs; test DOM mocks require `addEventListener`/`removeEventListener`. Bare `git push rad main` can fail without repo-local `RAD_HOME`. [Task 1]\n  1814\t- Do not replace every `localhost` occurrence: local documentation may be intentional. Legacy Railway service-level settings can survive a repo-config deployment; verify `/canvas`, `/docs`, and `/terminal` publicly. [Task 2]\n  1815\t\n  1816\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/twyne Needle scope, v0.21.0 release, and adaptive editorial drafting\n  1817\tscope: Keep the Cactus Needle concept separate from an unrelated npm dependency, verify desktop/release boundaries, and apply Keating-style typed private review to editorial generation.\n  1818\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne; reuse_rule=recheck provider/model behavior, credentials, passkey deployment, and worktree state; local/static proof does not establish live judgement behavior.\n  1819\t\n  1820\t## Task 1: Investigate Needle and publish Twyne 0.21.0\n  1821\t\n  1822\t### rollout_summary_files\n  1823\t\n  1824\t- rollout_summaries/2026-09-21T06-48-19-f9lZ-twyne_needle_investigation_and_v0210_release.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/21/rollout-2026-09-21T02-48-19-01a0c2b9-00e5-79a2-be4b-13a578e0598f.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-21T09:41:56+00:00, thread_id=01a0c2b9-00e5-79a2-be4b-13a578e0598f, success; release/Railway/assets verified)\n  1825\t\n  1826\t### keywords\n  1827\t\n  1828\t- Cactus-Compute/needle, passage-triage.ts, nothing advice question evidence cut, MiniCPM5-2B, LFM2.5, --jinja, v0.21.0, passkey-origin.ts, twyne.love\n  1829\t\n  1830\t## Task 2: Implement adaptive editorial drafting with Jev\n  1831\t\n  1832\t### rollout_summary_files\n  1833\t\n  1834\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/21/rollout-2026-09-21T21-52-13-01a0c6d0-476b-7642-8dae-393ed1e4e8ad.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-22T02:34:25+00:00, thread_id=01a0c6d0-476b-7642-8dae-393ed1e4e8ad, success; static/full-suite verification, no live provider run)\n  1835\t\n  1836\t### keywords\n  1837\t\n  1838\t- buildSystemPrompt, editorial-protocol.md, adaptive-editorial-draft.ts, reviewEditorialNote, systemOne.ask, reasoning-effort.ts, unreviewed, withheld\n  1839\t\n  1840\t## User preferences\n  1841\t\n  1842\t- the user prefers a smaller local model over Gemma 4 E4B for packaging/performance, suggesting MiniCPM5-2B or LFM2.5 2B. [Task 1]\n  1843\t- for Twyne, use Keating’s approach: deconstruct persona/system behavior into typed inspectable Jev rules that control generation, rather than only locating or rewriting prompt prose. [Task 2]\n  1844\t\n  1845\t## Reusable knowledge\n  1846\t\n  1847\t- The npm `needle@3.5.0` is an unrelated transitive `less` dependency. Intended Cactus Needle has no loader in this checkout; `passage-triage.ts` describes a closed-label offline adapter while active live triage uses hosted Jev. [Task 1]\n  1848\t- Active prompt builder is `convex/agentPrompts.ts` `buildSystemPrompt()` with `buildUserPrompt()` context assembly. Separate persona identity from `prompts/editorial-protocol.md`; controller retries private candidates using code-owned repair instructions and exposes content-free statuses. Missing Jev output is `unreviewed`, never a synthetic pass; critical vetoes withhold output. [Task 2]\n  1849\t\n  1850\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  1851\t\n  1852\t- A discovered package name is not the product model integration. Passkey production must use RP ID `twyne.love` and allow both apex/www origins; validate the deployed endpoint. [Task 1]\n  1853\t- Static tests (1549 pass/39 skip) did not prove an actual Jev/provider/Not Organic run. Do not expose rejected candidate text or hidden reasoning in repair prompts/status UI. [Task 2]\n  1854\t\n  1855\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/notorganic-provider launch readiness, sandbox neutrality, and private Radicle release\n  1856\tscope: Keep legal/mail/payment launch gates explicit, expose replaceable code-execution through Not Organic, and release the provider only through its verified private Radicle boundary.\n  1857\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/notorganic-provider; reuse_rule=recheck legal review, DNS/mail, Paddle mode, paid-provider status, credentials, and current private RID before external claims/actions.\n  1858\t\n  1859\t## Task 1: Harden legal, Paddle, mail, and hosted-sandbox readiness\n  1860\t\n  1861\t### rollout_summary_files\n  1862\t\n  1863\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/notorganic-provider, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/21/rollout-2026-09-21T04-14-08-01a0c307-9223-7c91-82d5-ed9d8bfb43f9.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-21T09:38:45+00:00, thread_id=01a0c307-9223-7c91-82d5-ed9d8bfb43f9, partial; checks/catalog/worker upload succeeded, launch gates remain)\n  1864\t\n  1865\t### keywords\n  1866\t\n  1867\t- quebec-launch-readiness, build-legal-pdfs.py, notorganic-support-mail-password@secrets, Paddle sandbox, PADDLE_PRICE_CATALOG, Workers Paid, SandboxGateway, E2B, Trigger.dev\n  1868\t\n  1869\t## Task 2: Release v0.1.1 to private Radicle\n  1870\t\n  1871\t### rollout_summary_files\n  1872\t\n  1873\t- rollout_summaries/2026-09-22T01-28-28-0ZAT-notorganic_provider_v011_private_radicle_release.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/notorganic-provider, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/21/rollout-2026-09-21T21-28-28-01a0c6ba-897d-7482-a2b3-f558cfde4ba3.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-28T23:17:11+00:00, thread_id=01a0c6ba-897d-7482-a2b3-f558cfde4ba3, success; private refs/visibility verified)\n  1874\t\n  1875\t### keywords\n  1876\t\n  1877\t- v0.1.1, cbb38d23336fa37416fda29ffed8458bb369d1d2, rad:REDACTED, SKIP=notorganic-railway, rad inspect --refs, .zero/cache, Rad Garden\n  1878\t\n  1879\t## User preferences\n  1880\t\n  1881\t- before payments go live, make policies “production ready” and keep support/privacy credentials saved in the secret manager, never transcripts. [Task 1]\n  1882\t- when the user asked to “create new commit and i want a release and this saved in radicle but a private rad. we should consider rad garden, put that in a note” -> preserve private visibility, do not use public `rad publish`/broad sync, and record Rad Garden as an evaluation rather than an enabled integration. [Task 2]\n  1883\t\n  1884\t## Reusable knowledge\n  1885\t\n  1886\t- Legal PDFs are generated by `scripts/build-legal-pdfs.py`; use `env -u PYTHONHOME -u PYTHONPATH uv run --with beautifulsoup4 --with reportlab python scripts/build-legal-pdfs.py` if system Python is broken. Sandbox checkout stays disabled with empty `PADDLE_PRICE_CATALOG`; transaction/webhook validations must fail closed. [Task 1]\n  1887\t- Execution remains behind Not Organic’s provider-neutral `SandboxGateway`: account authorization, spend limits, idempotency, cancellation, durable records, filesystem/workspace, bounded networking, secrets mediation, artifact export, resource limits, and provenance remain outside Cloudflare. Cloudflare, microVM, self-hosted runner, or future provider are adapters. [Task 1] [ad-hoc note]\n  1888\t- Private release uses `SKIP=notorganic-railway`; explicitly push `refs/tags/v0.1.1` and inspect private refs/visibility. Release commit `cbb38d23336fa37416fda29ffed8458bb369d1d2` and annotated tag `v0.1.1` were verified. Exclude `.zero/cache/`, preserve `.zero/cbb38d23336fa37416fda29ffed8458bb369d1d2` as local output, and keep the Rad Garden note as an evaluation only. GitNexus found 125 files/377 symbols/67 affected flows at critical risk, so disclose its broad auth/billing/gateway/portal/signup impact. [Task 2]\n  1889\t\n  1890\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  1891\t\n  1892\t- Do not call legal/mail/payment launch ready without French review, qualifying operator address/contact/retention controls, DNS+SPF/DKIM/DMARC and external mail proof, Paddle.js/browser payment/webhook/grant proof. Cloudflare containers were blocked by Workers Paid plan `401 Unauthorized`; gateway remains disconnected. [Task 1]\n  1893\t- `--follow-tags` is not enough Radicle advertised-tag proof: explicitly push the tag and verify `rad inspect --refs`. Sandbox `EPERM` for Bun listening/GitNexus, `.git` writes, and SSH-agent access are execution-environment blockers, not code failures; retry narrowly with required access. [Task 2]\n  1894\t\n  1895\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/stich multi-account identity and durable System One inbox agent\n  1896\tscope: Put account switching in the expected profile area and maintain an approval-gated, typed, durable inbox-judgement architecture.\n  1897\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/stich; reuse_rule=recheck mailbox principals, funding, deployment/runtime, secret rotation, and policy state before enabling automatic judgments or notifications.\n  1898\t\n  1899\t## Task 1: Implement profile-area account switching and inbox judgement worker\n  1900\t\n  1901\t### rollout_summary_files\n  1902\t\n  1903\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/stich, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/21/rollout-2026-09-21T04-17-25-01a0c30a-953a-7602-880d-b6adcfa77d71.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-21T09:39:24+00:00, thread_id=01a0c30a-953a-7602-880d-b6adcfa77d71, partial; deployment/manual synthetic evaluation, automation paused)\n  1904\t\n  1905\t### keywords\n  1906\t\n  1907\t- AccountSwitcher, serverOrigin::principal, TypeSafe System One, durable-inbox.ts, atomic disk journal, stich-agent, node:sqlite, Node 22, HTTP 402, policy disabled\n  1908\t\n  1909\t## User preferences\n  1910\t\n  1911\t- account switching should be “in a sensible place like where the profile image is like other email clients” -> put it inside/adjacent to profile identity rather than a separate top strip. [Task 1]\n  1912\t- for “system one judge integration,” classification/actions/notifications, Not Organic, sandbox, and Trigger.dev-like durability -> use typed reusable judgments, code-owned actions, and approval gates, not opaque generative automation. “Leave it unfunded for now” means automatic judgments stay off. [Task 1]\n  1913\t\n  1914\t## Reusable knowledge\n  1915\t\n  1916\t- Auth stores redacted `accounts[]`; account identity is `${serverOrigin}::${principal}`. Switching resets workspace/query/UI state and selected-account logout removes only that account. [Task 1]\n  1917\t- TypeSafe worker asks seven per-message typed questions and batches at most eight. It stores no mail bodies/credentials in its atomic journal; it validates account/owner/signature/capability/DPoP/freshness/replay and does not authorize sending/deleting/paying/link following/executing email code. [Task 1]\n  1918\t\n  1919\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  1920\t\n  1921\t- Initial chooser placement above workspace was rejected. Bun runtime lacks `node:sqlite`; build with Bun but run agent on Node 22. Use Stalwart principal `stich-agent`, not its email address. [Task 1]\n  1922\t- HTTP 402 insufficient funds and user choice keep automatic judgment paused. Synthetic results do not validate production notifications; tune on representative labelled cases and rotate the previously exposed Stalwart credential before reliance. [Task 1]\n  1923\t\n  1924\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/keating auth stop-motion visual direction\n  1925\tscope: Resume visual authentication work by locating the real surface, using existing discrete sprite conventions, and anchoring imagery to the recognized Keatingbot identity.\n  1926\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating; reuse_rule=exploration only; inspect current auth flow and existing assets before implementation, generation, or validation.\n  1927\t\n  1928\t## Task 1: Explore stop-motion sign-in/sign-up beautification\n  1929\t\n  1930\t### rollout_summary_files\n  1931\t\n  1932\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/22/rollout-2026-09-22T00-39-43-01a0c769-9ea5-7880-b04b-bdf660a7b065.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-22T00:53:24+00:00, thread_id=01a0c769-9ea5-7880-b04b-bdf660a7b065, partial; exploration only)\n  1933\t\n  1934\t### keywords\n  1935\t\n  1936\t- OAuthCallback.tsx, oauth.ts, ChatOnboarding, steps(1, end), keating-credit-sprite, keating-bot__sprite, mascot-head-v2.png, Keatingbot, image generation\n  1937\t\n  1938\t## User preferences\n  1939\t\n  1940\t- for auth, the user asked for “images and animations” with “stop motion like we have some of the other stuff” -> match the existing discrete/sprite animation language, not unrelated motion. [Task 1]\n  1941\t- the user corrected the claim that Codex cannot generate images: it can generate and report a temporary output path -> investigate/use the available image-generation workflow and preserve/report the generated asset path. [Task 1]\n  1942\t\n  1943\t## Reusable knowledge\n  1944\t\n  1945\t- Existing stop-motion styles use sprite/background animation and `steps(1, end)` in `keating-credit-recovery.css`, `keating-bot.css`, and `app-status-screen.css`. Keatingbot's canonical reference is `web/public/brand/mascot-head-v2.png`: cream rounded CRT shell, vivid green screen/side pods, black bezel, left antenna, friendly compact retro-futurist proportions; derivative art should stay recognizably Keatingbot. [Task 1] [ad-hoc note]\n  1946\t\n  1947\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  1948\t\n  1949\t- No actual sign-in/sign-up surface was conclusively identified and no edits were validated. Locate it first, then inspect existing stop-motion patterns; do not substitute code-only work after incorrectly declaring image generation unavailable. [Task 1]\n  1950\t\n  1951\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/keating staging chat deployment, dirty snapshots, and promotion worker\n  1952\tscope: Deploy the current Keating worktree (including approved uncommitted and Claude-session work) to a directly testable Railway staging URL, while keeping dirty candidates ineligible for production promotion.\n  1953\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating; reuse_rule=reinspect the current worktree, Railway environments, deployment status, and worker variables; URLs, tokens, and deployment state are time-specific.\n  1954\t\n  1955\t## Task 1: Reconcile current worktree and deploy it to Railway staging\n  1956\t\n  1957\t### rollout_summary_files\n  1958\t\n  1959\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/24/rollout-2026-09-24T02-39-28-01a0d223-fc86-7c00-aabd-3a99e0efca57.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-24T08:09:02+00:00, thread_id=01a0d223-fc86-7c00-aabd-3a99e0efca57, partial overall; staging UI and deterministic checks passed, live provider/login proof remains open)\n  1960\t\n  1961\t### keywords\n  1962\t\n  1963\t- Railway, staging, devenv up, scripts/staging.ts, keating:staging-deploy, Entire, Claude, dirty-worktree, promotionEligible, keating-staging.up.railway.app/chat, RAILWAY_TOKEN, RAILWAY_STAGING_TOKEN\n  1964\t\n  1965\t## User preferences\n  1966\t\n  1967\t- when deploying the current work, the user asked for “the work that is done in the claude session” to be “up in the staging environment for me to try” -> reconcile Entire, Git, Codex sessions, and the worktree together; include intended dirty work in a staging snapshot and provide a directly usable URL, but never promote it as a clean production candidate. [Task 1]\n  1968\t- when the user explicitly asked to “use `sh entire`” -> do not infer missing work from Git or Entire alone; cross-check both with Codex session archives/checkpoints. [Task 1]\n  1969\t\n  1970\t## Reusable knowledge\n  1971\t\n  1972\t- `scripts/staging.ts` snapshots tracked and untracked application files while excluding `.env*`, credentials, generated state, databases, and build output. `devenv up` includes the staging process; use `bun scripts/staging.ts deploy`, `bun scripts/staging.ts status`, or `devenv tasks run keating:staging-deploy`. Dirty snapshots are marked `promotionEligible: false` and deliberately cannot promote. [Task 1]\n  1973\t- Captured staging proof: Railway project `keating` has a `staging` environment; deployment `7fe59e0f-300f-43f5-95a5-56bf04c0302f` reached `SUCCESS`, and `https://keating-staging.up.railway.app/chat` rendered the chat UI. Production branch auto-deploy was disconnected; staging uploads do not use GitHub. [Task 1]\n  1974\t- Promotion service `keating-promotion` uses hourly cron `17 * * * *` and persistent `/data`. A fresh diagnostic container, not sealed-variable metadata, established that `RAILWAY_STAGING_TOKEN` was nonempty and could access staging while `RAILWAY_TOKEN` was present but empty; edit only the production token value, then freshly verify both environment accesses. [Task 1]\n  1975\t- Local judgement direct mode is `KEATING_JUDGEMENT_DEV_DIRECT=1|true` with server-only `TYPESAFE_API_KEY`; browser same-origin is exact `VITE_KEATING_JUDGEMENT_SAME_ORIGIN=true`. Captured checks: root `bun run test` 837 pass/0 fail, web 2,215 pass/1 skipped/0 failures, `git diff --check`, and `bun scripts/check-env-docs.ts` passed. [Task 1]\n  1976\t\n  1977\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  1978\t\n  1979\t- A staging `SUCCESS` and rendered shell do not prove signed-in login, hosted inference, hosted judgement, or `chat.keating.help` DNS/TLS. Keep those as open runtime checks. [Task 1]\n  1980\t- Sealed Railway variable metadata does not prove a usable secret: symptom `RAILWAY_TOKEN present=true nonEmpty=false` -> re-enter only that production value and run a fresh worker/container probe before calling promotion operational. [Task 1]\n  1981\t- `bun test test` selects unrelated mobile/native suites. Use canonical root `bun run test`; report the known wider judgement-runtime local-first versus hosted-first test conflict separately. [Task 1]\n  1982\t\n  1983\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/keating OpenUI component selection and sticky learning state\n  1984\tscope: Trace and improve OpenUI generation/judgement so component use is capability-based, longitudinal, and bounded rather than a narrow question-answer gate.\n  1985\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating; reuse_rule=reinspect the dirty worktree and actual runtime turns; this rollout provides source-backed architecture and partial code evidence, not a verified live root cause or completed redesign.\n  1986\t\n  1987\t## Task 1: Trace OpenUI generation, judgment, budgets, and reasoning ratings\n  1988\t\n  1989\t### rollout_summary_files\n  1990\t\n  1991\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/23/rollout-2026-09-23T17-57-52-01a0d046-715d-7b92-b395-bacd83824b1c.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-24T00:58:17+00:00, thread_id=01a0d046-715d-7b92-b395-bacd83824b1c, partial; trace complete, reasoning-rating change lacks package-green proof)\n  1992\t\n  1993\t### keywords\n  1994\t\n  1995\t- OpenUI, keatingOpenUIPrompt, AssistantChatPanel, withTeachingDraftGate, teaching-drafts.ts, 90 seconds, max_length 1024, openui_valid, TS2345, local fallback, hosted-primary\n  1996\t\n  1997\t## Task 2: Design capability-based component selection and sticky active work\n  1998\t\n  1999\t### rollout_summary_files\n  2000\t\n  2001\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/23/rollout-2026-09-23T17-57-52-01a0d046-715d-7b92-b395-bacd83824b1c.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-24T00:58:17+00:00, thread_id=01a0d046-715d-7b92-b395-bacd83824b1c, uncertain; design direction only)\n  2002\t\n  2003\t### keywords\n  2004\t\n  2005\t- component-selection, interactive-underuse, sticky-context, teachingDraftEvidence, ComingUpReadiness, StudyPlan, ConceptMap, assisted correctness, independent correctness, retention, transfer, nested judgments\n  2006\t\n  2007\t## User preferences\n  2008\t\n  2009\t- when diagnosing absent interfaces, the user asked for “where the budget code is,” “which model is the judge,” and “what happens when creating one” -> explain prompt, private generation, validation, rendering, persistence, and runtime configuration as separate stages. [Task 1]\n  2010\t- “local should be the fallback not the default” -> use hosted-primary/local-fallback as the target direction, while clearly marking that this rollout did not implement it. [Task 1]\n  2011\t- “depend on question would also underuse openui” -> do not gate interaction only on immediate learner answers; assess useful component capabilities across all component families and preserve active lesson-plan/result context beyond the sliding transcript window. [Task 2]\n  2012\t\n  2013\t## Reusable knowledge\n  2014\t\n  2015\t- Tutor output contains fenced OpenUI source: `useKeatingAgent.tsx` appends `keatingOpenUIPrompt`, then `AssistantChatPanel` parses/renders it. `withTeachingDraftGate` privately generates, runs Jev/deterministic review, retries/revises, and releases only approved text. Default budget is 90 seconds (cap 180), normally 3 attempts; local browser generation defaults to `max_length: 1024`. [Task 1]\n  2016\t- OpenUI compilation is inert and bounded: source 131072, 64 statements, collection 512, depth 24. Current checks validate OpenUI when emitted (`openui_valid`, activity/checkpoint constraints), so no OpenUI generally passes and underuse is not detected. [Task 1][Task 2]\n  2017\t- Use deterministic state for presented/submitted/tested/graded/completed facts; use Jev for open-response adequacy, support need, move-on readiness, plan-item detail, and revision. `teachingDraftEvidence()` already exposes learner state/goals/results/gaps/pending submissions; `ComingUpReadiness` binds saved plans to document revisions, prerequisites, and receipts. [Task 2]\n  2018\t- Sticky active-work records should retain component/document/revision, objective or plan-item linkage, presented content, submission, assistance/grading, unresolved work, and next action; send only a bounded outline/current branch/relevant prerequisites/evidence projection to the judge. Keep exposure, completion, assisted correctness, independent correctness, retention, and transfer distinct. [Task 2]\n  2019\t\n  2020\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  2021\t\n  2022\t- Do not claim a runtime root cause without a real observed turn; source review identified plausible suppressors only. GitNexus was stale/incomplete, so pivot to `rg` and direct source reads. [Task 1]\n  2023\t- Source-only TypeScript passed after replacing one broad reasoning Choice with three Score questions, but package typecheck had `TS2345` in `packages/learner-contracts/test/teaching-drafts.test.ts:23,42` and tests were not run. Do not call it green until package checks are repaired/rerun. [Task 1]\n  2024\t- Avoid maximizing interface count or reevaluating a full curriculum every turn. Use benefit/burden, existing active artifacts, and relevant nested state; a binary “interactive needed?” selector suppresses simulations, maps, and plans. [Task 2]\n  2025\t\n  2026\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/keating Needle on-device retrieval audit and measurement plan\n  2027\tscope: Evaluate Needle and phone-suitable retrieval/judgement alternatives with local corpus/device measurements, preserving exact-span extraction while not overstating unmeasured replacements.\n  2028\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating; reuse_rule=recheck pinned runtime, corpus, device profile, artifact licenses, and current benchmark harnesses before choosing or shipping a replacement.\n  2029\t\n  2030\t## Task 1: Audit Needle and identify a measured replacement path\n  2031\t\n  2032\t### rollout_summary_files\n  2033\t\n  2034\t- rollout_summaries/2026-09-22T19-25-32-LkDZ-needle_on_device_alternatives_and_measurement_plan.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/22/rollout-2026-09-22T15-25-32-01a0ca94-9f32-7140-b035-542d903b93b7.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-24T07:23:12+00:00, thread_id=01a0ca94-9f32-7140-b035-542d903b93b7, partial; existing Needle evidence found, alternatives unmeasured)\n  2035\t\n  2036\t### keywords\n  2037\t\n  2038\t- Needle 3.0.1, b274efcb211a9eef48c9a88da4b43bd569696a39, 3072-dimensional, docs/blog/needle-subject-routing.md, Model2Vec, Potion, reranker, LiteRT, ONNX, needle-recall-bench.ts, KEV, mobile\n  2039\t\n  2040\t## User preferences\n  2041\t\n  2042\t- when considering a replacement, the user said it must be “reasonable to package with application and not be absurd to run on phones” -> treat package bytes, RAM, battery/thermal behavior, cancellation, portability, and offline support as first-class acceptance criteria. [Task 1]\n  2043\t- the user asked to “try measuring them” and inspect “entire cli sessions for experiments” -> use reproducible local corpus/device measurements and inspect the actual historical session artifacts before recommendations. [Task 1]\n  2044\t\n  2045\t## Reusable knowledge\n  2046\t\n  2047\t- Needle 3.0.1 is pinned at `b274efcb211a9eef48c9a88da4b43bd569696a39`; weights are 35,335,380 bytes, embeddings are 3,072-dimensional, and execution spans CLI Python subprocess, browser WASM, and native C-ABI mobile bindings. Native mobile execution is process-global without cancellation/unload. [Task 1]\n  2048\t- Existing `docs/blog/needle-subject-routing.md` evidence: subject classification 2/8 with tool calls, 1/8 enum extraction, 0/8 embedding-prototype top-1; paraphrase recall R@1 10%, below lexical baselines. Needle remains reliable for exact quote/span extraction but not semantic routing/classification. [Task 1]\n  2049\t- Candidate architecture remains a proposal: static embeddings for shortlist/ranking, tiny cross-encoder reranking/exact-span/category selection, and existing LiteRT/ONNX or hosted Jev for consequential judgement. Start from `.keating/tmp/needle-recall-bench.ts`, `needle-recall-bench2.ts`, and Laya/Von/GLiNER harnesses. [Task 1]\n  2050\t\n  2051\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  2052\t\n  2053\t- No candidate benchmark, phone profile, license check, or artifact integration was completed. Measure latency, resident memory, artifact size, recall/classification accuracy, cancellation, battery, and thermal impact on Keating corpus/target phone before treating published claims as comparable. [Task 1]\n  2054\t- Historical CLI/KEV search was partial; enumerate `/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions` and inspect relevant rollout/session artifacts directly rather than relying only on repo grep. [Task 1]\n  2055\t\n  2056\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/dio-machines environment configuration and Fugu tool sync\n  2057\tscope: Route machine, service, project, and secret environment variables correctly and mirror the canonical Codex Fugu catalog/default into OpenCode and Crush.\n  2058\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/dio-machines with user config paths under /home/diogenes; reuse_rule=reinspect current Home Manager configuration, live secret-store access, provider availability, and persisted tool state before edits or claims.\n  2059\t\n  2060\t## Task 1: Map environment-variable scope and secret handling\n  2061\t\n  2062\t### rollout_summary_files\n  2063\t\n  2064\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/dio-machines, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/22/rollout-2026-09-22T14-04-16-01a0ca4a-36df-77e2-aedd-cc561a1f7447.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-22T18:06:21+00:00, thread_id=01a0ca4a-36df-77e2-aedd-cc561a1f7447, uncertain; repository map verified, live secret contents unavailable)\n  2065\t\n  2066\t### keywords\n  2067\t\n  2068\t- home.sessionVariables, home.sessionPath, load-secret-env, Skate, @secrets, secrets.env.sops, EnvironmentFile, services/.env, Home Manager, machine:switch\n  2069\t\n  2070\t## Task 2: Mirror Codex Fugu catalog and pin fugu-max/high defaults\n  2071\t\n  2072\t### rollout_summary_files\n  2073\t\n  2074\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/dio-machines, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/22/rollout-2026-09-22T14-57-28-01a0ca7a-eac3-7a41-8e91-6e2fb318a526.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-22T19:34:41+00:00, thread_id=01a0ca7a-eac3-7a41-8e91-6e2fb318a526, success; live defaults and outgoing effort verified)\n  2075\t\n  2076\t### keywords\n  2077\t\n  2078\t- fugu, sakana, fugu-max, fugu-ultra-v2.0, opencode.jsonc, crush.json, reasoningEffort, reasoning_effort, models.large, ProviderModelNotFoundError, recent_models.large\n  2079\t\n  2080\t## User preferences\n  2081\t\n  2082\t- when the user asked to “figure out how i add environment variables to this computer in this repo” -> first map actual scope and secret conventions instead of assuming one env mechanism. [Task 1]\n  2083\t- “just look at the codex profile and copy that to the others”; “adding max and the latest ultra models is important” -> use `/home/diogenes/.codex/sakana-models.json` and `fugu.config.toml` as catalog source of truth, then verify questionable IDs live. [Task 2]\n  2084\t- “set fugu max as the default model for both at high” -> change declarative config and persisted active state, then validate outgoing requests rather than merely listing models. [Task 2]\n  2085\t\n  2086\t## Reusable knowledge\n  2087\t\n  2088\t- Put shared non-secret variables in `home/default.nix` `home.sessionVariables`; narrower non-secrets in host/profile Nix files; PATH additions in `home.sessionPath`; apply Home Manager changes with `devenv tasks run machine:switch`. Project-only variables normally belong in that project’s `devenv.nix`. [Task 1]\n  2089\t- Credentials are outside tracked Nix: `~/bin/load-secret-env` reads Skate `@secrets` and optional `~/.config/mise/secrets.env.sops`; `load-secrets` evaluates its shell-safe exports. Service Compose secrets are git-ignored `services/<name>/.env` copied from `.env.example`; systemd non-secrets can use `Environment`, but file-backed secrets require `EnvironmentFile` because `Environment` lands in the Nix store. [Task 1]\n  2090\t- OpenCode deep-merges `~/.config/opencode/opencode.json` and `opencode.jsonc`; set default `\"model\": \"sakana/fugu-max\"` and its `options.reasoningEffort: \"high\"`. Crush requires both `~/.config/crush/crush.json` and persisted `~/.local/share/crush/crush.json`: `models.large = { model: \"fugu-max\", provider: \"sakana\", reasoning_effort: \"high\" }`, with `fugu-max/sakana` first in `recent_models.large`. [Task 2]\n  2091\t- Captured catalog supported `fugu`, `fugu-ultra`, `fugu-ultra-v2.0`, `fugu-ultra-20260615`, `fugu-ultra-v1.0`, `fugu-ultra-v1.1`, `fugu-max`, `fugu-max-v1.0`, and `fugu-cyber`; `fugu-cyber-v1.0`/`sakana-namazu*` returned 404, while `fugu-cyber` was form-gated 403. [Task 2]\n  2092\t\n  2093\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  2094\t\n  2095\t- Sandbox `skate list -k @secrets` hit a read-only lock-file failure, and the SOPS file was absent. Do not infer current secret contents; re-run on the writable machine and use `~/bin/secrets-edit`, never tracked Nix credentials. [Task 1]\n  2096\t- `sakana/fugu-max/high` is invalid as OpenCode’s global model (`ProviderModelNotFoundError`); keep plain model ID and pin effort in `options`. A JSONC insertion script first failed parsing: test a throwaway copy and run sync twice for idempotency before live writes. [Task 2]\n  2097\t- Updating only Crush config leaves a prior `models.large` active because persisted data overrides it. Crush supports only `low|medium|high`; use OpenCode variants/session overrides for xhigh/max. [Task 2]\n  2098\t\n  2099\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/notorganic-provider Jev semantic-rules API\n  2100\tscope: Implement and extend account/product-scoped, developer-reviewed Jev rulesets through the metered Not Organic judgement boundary; keep Phase 1 limits explicit.\n  2101\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/notorganic-provider; reuse_rule=reinspect the dirty worktree, current rules schema, and gateway deployment; do not infer calibration, spans, training, continuous encoding, or revision-aware serving from Phase 1.\n  2102\t\n  2103\t## Task 1: Implement first-class Jev rules API\n  2104\t\n  2105\t### rollout_summary_files\n  2106\t\n  2107\t- rollout_summaries/2026-09-22T04-39-43-JM9T-implement_jev_rules_api_phase_one.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/notorganic-provider, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/22/rollout-2026-09-22T00-39-43-01a0c769-9eae-7de1-8e79-8e3d4d46462d.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-28T23:24:42+00:00, thread_id=01a0c769-9eae-7de1-8e79-8e3d4d46462d, success; focused tests/typecheck/build passed; full suite had one sandbox socket-permission failure)\n  2108\t\n  2109\t### keywords\n  2110\t\n  2111\t- Jev, TypeSafe, RulesService, JudgementGateway, /v1/rules/decompose, /v1/rulesets, rules:write, rules:read, rules:evaluate, expected_revision, RULESET_STALE_REVISION, state_binding, state_digest, calibration.status\n  2112\t\n  2113\t## User preferences\n  2114\t\n  2115\t- when the user proposed using “another model to deconstruct some things into jev rules” and adding spans/general-purpose rules -> preserve a reviewable draft workflow; do not auto-activate model-generated rules. [Task 1]\n  2116\t- when the user clarified “jev refers to typesafe's model” and approved reading the ledger before planning -> keep TypeSafe behind Not Organic’s authenticated, metered provider boundary rather than exposing direct credentials. [Task 1]\n  2117\t\n  2118\t## Reusable knowledge\n  2119\t\n  2120\t- `RulesService` in `apps/gateway/src/rules.ts` performs decomposition, developer-reviewed publication, immutable revision retrieval, state binding, digest calculation, author/scorer separation, and Jev evaluation. `POST /v1/rules/decompose` uses the metered Portkey `reasoning` model, validates 1–64 unique claims, and leaves output draft-only. [Task 1]\n  2121\t- Accepted claims compile to Jev `choice` questions with `satisfied`, `violated`, `insufficient_context`, and `not_applicable`. Rulesets persist account/product-scoped in `convex/rules.ts`; `expected_revision` is CAS and stale writes map to `409 ruleset_stale_revision`. [Task 1]\n  2122\t- Evaluation loads the exact immutable revision, filters dotted `state_binding` paths such as `metadata.source`, canonicalizes state, computes `state_digest`, and invokes `JudgementGateway.evaluate` with deterministic inner idempotency/request hashes. The gateway retains DPoP/authentication, wallet reservation, dispatch, usage settlement, and conservative reconciliation; TypeSafe credentials remain server-held. [Task 1]\n  2123\t- SDK surface: `client.rules.decompose` and `client.rulesets.create/list/retrieve/evaluate`; capabilities are `rules:write`, `rules:read`, `rules:evaluate`. Responses expose `backend_model`, `questions_digest`, `state_digest`, usage, and `calibration.status = \"advisory\"`; schema-only `rulesetCalibrations` is not fitted calibration. Author/scorer matching is rejected as `rules_author_scorer_conflict`; limits are 64 questions and about 96k state/question characters. Inference endpoints do not yet consume a ruleset or active evolution revision. [Task 1]\n  2124\t\n  2125\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  2126\t\n  2127\t- GitNexus `UNKNOWN`/partial coverage means unresolved, not safe: the index was one commit stale, so refresh it, resolve exact symbols, then confirm callers with text search. Dotted bindings initially behaved as literal keys; use explicit path traversal and nested-binding tests. [Task 1]\n  2128\t- `apps/gateway/src/bun-live.test.ts` failed under sandbox socket permissions with `EPERM` but passed with socket access. Report it as an environment limitation separate from implementation failure. [Task 1]\n  2129\t\n  2130\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/keating Railway static report deployment and naming\n  2131\tscope: Resume, verify, retitle, rebuild, and deploy the `on-device-ledger` static report on Railway with live positive and negative HTTP proof.\n  2132\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating; reuse_rule=recheck current Railway project/service/deployment status and report sources before changing content or claiming live behavior.\n  2133\t\n  2134\t## Task 1: Resume and verify Railway deployment\n  2135\t\n  2136\t### rollout_summary_files\n  2137\t\n  2138\t- rollout_summaries/2026-09-23T12-38-01-qzCo-railway_report_title_redeploy.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/23/rollout-2026-09-23T08-38-01-01a0ce45-e3b1-7e81-9dd6-5d6c57921238.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-23T12:54:14+00:00, thread_id=01a0ce45-e3b1-7e81-9dd6-5d6c57921238, success; live routes, title, health, and 404 verified)\n  2139\t\n  2140\t### keywords\n  2141\t\n  2142\t- Railway, on-device-ledger, on-device-ledger-production.up.railway.app, railway.toml, Dockerfile, /healthz, railway up --service, deployment SUCCESS\n  2143\t\n  2144\t## Task 2: Rename and redeploy report\n  2145\t\n  2146\t### rollout_summary_files\n  2147\t\n  2148\t- rollout_summaries/2026-09-23T12-38-01-qzCo-railway_report_title_redeploy.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/23/rollout-2026-09-23T08-38-01-01a0ce45-e3b1-7e81-9dd6-5d6c57921238.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-23T12:54:14+00:00, thread_id=01a0ce45-e3b1-7e81-9dd6-5d6c57921238, success; final deployment `ed7a8e47-aa26-4c4f-a5f5-f70cffd79d2d`)\n  2149\t\n  2150\t### keywords\n  2151\t\n  2152\t- A Measure of Machine Judgement, scripts/on-device-site/build.py, shell(...), homepage hero, wordmark, Railway logs --deployment, --build\n  2153\t\n  2154\t## User preferences\n  2155\t\n  2156\t- when continuing a deployment, the user said \"hey continue the railway deployment\" and supplied a prior Entire session ID -> inspect the concrete prior session/checkpoint state rather than restarting diagnosis. [Task 1]\n  2157\t- the user rejected \"actually,\" said \"think outside on device,\" and selected \"A Measure of Machine Judgement\" -> prefer concept-led, distinctive report titles over implementation-focused wording. [Task 2]\n  2158\t\n  2159\t## Reusable knowledge\n  2160\t\n  2161\t- Railway project `keating` service `on-device-ledger` is served at `https://on-device-ledger-production.up.railway.app`; source deploy context is `scripts/on-device-site`, with `railway.toml`, Dockerfile, and `/healthz`. Use `railway up --service on-device-ledger --path-as-root scripts/on-device-site --detach`. [Task 1]\n  2162\t- Rebuild titles consistently in `scripts/on-device-site/build.py`: its `shell(...)` title calls plus homepage hero/wordmark. Run `python3 scripts/on-device-site/build.py`, deploy, then check final title/heading, `/healthz` 200, expected site routes, and an unknown route 404. [Task 1][Task 2]\n  2163\t\n  2164\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  2165\t\n  2166\t- Interrupted polling, approval limits, and transient DNS do not prove deploy failure; inspect current Railway status/domain. GitNexus did not index `scripts/on-device-site/build.py`, so direct `rg`/file inspection was the correct pivot. [Task 1][Task 2]\n  2167\t- `railway logs --deployment` and `--build` are mutually exclusive; run them separately. [Task 2]\n  2168\t\n  2169\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/keating structured learner profile and guided onboarding\n  2170\tscope: Maintain optional local learner details, migration-compatible prompt composition, guided web onboarding, and consentful pursuit switching without overstating unfinished UI or end-to-end verification.\n  2171\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating; reuse_rule=reinspect high-impact learner-context callers and generated NodePod artifacts; preserve local-only/privacy boundaries and legacy free-text compatibility.\n  2172\t\n  2173\t## Task 1: Add structured learner profile and local migration, partial\n  2174\t\n  2175\t### rollout_summary_files\n  2176\t\n  2177\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/19/rollout-2026-09-19T18-16-34-01a0bbbe-1e34-7900-abf6-56c41c92e53a.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-19T23:22:34+00:00, thread_id=01a0bbbe-1e34-7900-abf6-56c41c92e53a, partial; targeted checks passed, full end-to-end completion not shown)\n  2178\t\n  2179\t### keywords\n  2180\t\n  2181\t- learner-profile-declared, AGE_BANDS, parseDeclaredProfile, keating:learner-profile:v2, createLocalSetting, loadLearnerContext, GitNexus, learner-context\n  2182\t\n  2183\t## Task 2: Add settings profile UI, guided onboarding, and pursuits, partial\n  2184\t\n  2185\t### rollout_summary_files\n  2186\t\n  2187\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/19/rollout-2026-09-19T18-16-34-01a0bbbe-1e34-7900-abf6-56c41c92e53a.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-19T23:22:34+00:00, thread_id=01a0bbbe-1e34-7900-abf6-56c41c92e53a, partial; coachmarks, locale override, and complete telemetry remain unfinished)\n  2188\t\n  2189\t### keywords\n  2190\t\n  2191\t- ChatOnboarding, ProfileFieldGroups, LearnerProfileTab, Panda CSS, seedCurrentPursuitFromGoal, pursuitCandidatesFromNeedle, applyPursuitSwitchProposal, EPERM, nodepod-boot-files\n  2192\t\n  2193\t## User preferences\n  2194\t\n  2195\t- when requesting learner details, the user said \"personal details about the learner age etc language etc\" and \"think of more things here\" -> offer broad optional fields, never mandatory or overly sensitive intake. [Task 1]\n  2196\t- when the user said \"wait just continue on the plan now\" -> after an approved plan, make reasonable implementation decisions instead of repeatedly reopening clarification. [Task 1]\n  2197\t- the user wanted onboarding to \"guide people using the interface\" -> explain composer, side panel, sessions, and Settings, not merely provider setup. [Task 2]\n  2198\t\n  2199\t## Reusable knowledge\n  2200\t\n  2201\t- Shared dependency-free contract is `packages/learner-contracts/src/learner-profile-declared.ts`. Use age bands (including `prefer-not-to-say`), not date of birth. `parseDeclaredProfile()` never throws; it validates enums, bounds text/lists/durations, and distinguishes unanswered from declined values. Persist v2 at `keating:learner-profile:v2`; migrate legacy `keating:learner-profile` text into `notes` and retain the legacy mirror. [Task 1]\n  2202\t- `loadLearnerContext()` had 99 upstream impacts/CRITICAL GitNexus risk: preserve its signature and add structured context only through optional prompt parameters plus the parallel store. The prompt must not infer ability, intelligence, personality, or learning style from age, language, pronouns, or education stage. Telemetry-safe helpers expose field IDs/counts, not values. [Task 1]\n  2203\t- Use Panda CSS and existing `Select`, `Toggle`, `fieldInput`, and `textarea` recipes. Share `ProfileFieldGroups.tsx` between settings and onboarding. `ChatOnboarding.tsx` has resumable v2 eight-step metadata while recognizing completed v1 records; it stays non-modal so provider/account dialogs do not compete for focus. [Task 2]\n  2204\t- `seedCurrentPursuitFromGoal()` makes a non-empty onboarding goal a current declared pursuit. Prompt it as `Standing pursuit (not assumed for this session)`. Observed pursuits require exact evidence, SHA-256 quote hash, and provenance offsets; only exact `study-context` candidates with valid provenance are accepted, and `applyPursuitSwitchProposal()` requires explicit approval. [Task 2]\n  2205\t\n  2206\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  2207\t\n  2208\t- GitNexus `--target-uid` is invalid; use `-u/--uid`. `UNKNOWN` on new symbols is unresolved: bound callers with direct grep/import searches, never treat it as safe. [Task 1]\n  2209\t- Coachmark tour, getting-started checklist, locale override, complete telemetry, full Storybook/build validation, and final `detect_changes --scope all` were not demonstrated. Do not claim them complete. [Task 2]\n  2210\t- An offline learner-context harness failed `EPERM .../.keating/tmp/.../rpc.sock`; rerun where Unix socket creation is allowed. After source changes regenerate `web/src/keating/nodepod-boot-files.ts` with `bun scripts/generate-nodepod-boot-files.ts` or generated copies become stale. [Task 2]\n  2211\t\n  2212\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/keating Jev/model-cascade shared judgement foundation\n  2213\tscope: Continue the shared cross-surface judgement foundation while completing the still-unreplaced judge sites, telemetry, evolution wiring, and full validation.\n  2214\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating; reuse_rule=reinspect the heavily dirty branch and targeted diffs; treat the shared contracts as partial implementation, not completion of docs/plans/jev-model-cascade.md.\n  2215\t\n  2216\t## Task 1: Add typed Jev/model-cascade contracts and pure decision helpers, partial\n  2217\t\n  2218\t### rollout_summary_files\n  2219\t\n  2220\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/19/rollout-2026-09-19T08-03-45-01a0b98d-1310-7722-85ad-98bdd317bee4.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-19T12:41:05+00:00, thread_id=01a0b98d-1310-7722-85ad-98bdd317bee4, partial; foundation implemented, post-boosting full suite not rerun)\n  2221\t\n  2222\t### keywords\n  2223\t\n  2224\t- Jev, TypeSafe, System One, JudgementCaller, learner-contracts, cascade-router, MiniCPM5, Needle, evidence-by-selection, assessment, retrieval, boosting\n  2225\t\n  2226\t## Task 2: Replace all LLM-as-judge paths and finish cascade phases, partial\n  2227\t\n  2228\t### rollout_summary_files\n  2229\t\n  2230\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/19/rollout-2026-09-19T08-03-45-01a0b98d-1310-7722-85ad-98bdd317bee4.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-19T12:41:05+00:00, thread_id=01a0b98d-1310-7722-85ad-98bdd317bee4, partial; all three delegated workers hit usage limits)\n  2231\t\n  2232\t### keywords\n  2233\t\n  2234\t- benchmark_judge.py, export-judge.ts, trajectory-passes.ts, model-adapters.ts, policy-judgement.ts, mastery.ts, learner-state.ts, runtime_or_model_changed, telemetry, injection tests\n  2235\t\n  2236\t## User preferences\n  2237\t\n  2238\t- when the user required “do it all end to end” and “Full replacement everywhere” -> continue through all planned judge sites; do not present the contract layer as sufficient completion [Task 1][Task 2]\n  2239\t- when the user required a local judgement model “separate model configurable in settings” -> keep tutor-model and judgement-model settings independent [Task 1]\n  2240\t\n  2241\t## Reusable knowledge\n  2242\t\n  2243\t- The shared cross-platform location is `packages/learner-contracts/src/judgement/`: `contracts.ts`, `projections.ts`, `router.ts`, `wire.ts`, `system-one.ts`, `local-backend.ts`, `assessment.ts`, `retrieval.ts`, and `boosting.ts`, exported through the package root. CLI, web, and mobile already consume `@keating/learner-contracts`. [Task 1]\n  2244\t- Cascade routing starts at the cheapest tier, escalates only residue, skips uncalibrated tiers, never falls back from a pinned backend, and returns deterministic baseline plus abstention when exhausted. Thresholds key on backend/model/calibration/question digest. [Task 1]\n  2245\t- Hosted System One is `POST https://api.typesafe.ai/v1/systemone`; Choice is a criteria map, Score an ordered criteria array, and Noul has no confidence. Do not surface upstream bodies; same-origin gateway calls omit credentials. [Task 1]\n  2246\t- `web/src/keating/judgement-model.ts` stores the independent `off|local|hosted` setting, defaults local to `RASMUS/MiniCPM5-2B-ONNX`, and accepts only same-origin gateway paths. Local Needle answers are typed/closed-vocabulary and omit unanswerable questions. [Task 1]\n  2247\t- Assessment helpers keep readiness Nouls one-directional, use per-item performance Nouls, bucket duration/due dates, and mark uncertain open answers `grading: \"pending\"`. Retrieval uses calibrated z-scores, exact learner-message evidence, observed confidence <=0.65, and a 128-fact cap. Start boosting with a depth-limited tree and deterministic held-out rows. [Task 1]\n  2248\t- The remaining plan targets include `scripts/training/benchmark_judge.py`, `web/src/keating/export-judge.ts`, `web/src/keating/trajectory-passes.ts`, `shared/evolution/model-adapters.ts`, `src/core/policy-judgement.ts`, `src/core/mastery.ts`, and `src/core/learner-state.ts`. Preserve server-side-only TypeSafe credentials, `NEEDLE_TELEMETRY=0`, `DO_NOT_TRACK=1`, evidence taxonomy, and no automatic irreversible action from judgement alone. [Task 2]\n  2249\t\n  2250\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  2251\t\n  2252\t- Bun tests can pass while a type-only import is wrong because imports are stripped. After tests, always run `bun run typecheck`; assessment types belong in `contracts.ts`, not `projections.ts`. [Task 1]\n  2253\t- Symptom: `ReferenceError: localStorage is not defined` in web setting tests -> use the existing inline storage/window/custom-event shim pattern in `web/src/test/learner-context.test.ts`. [Task 1]\n  2254\t- The recorded `187 pass / 0 fail` package result and typecheck predate later boosting changes. Rerun the entire package suite before calling it green. For web: `cd web && bun run panda`, `bunx tsc --noEmit`, then `bun test`; also run root/Bun, benchmark, evidence-integrity, cache-key, offline/no-network, and injection checks. [Task 1][Task 2]\n  2255\t- All three workers terminated with usage-limit errors and delivered no implementation result. Continue directly or use smaller bounded tasks; do not assume their files changed. [Task 2]\n  2256\t\n  2257\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/textbook native terminal UI Canvas parity and Jev review\n  2258\tscope: Continue native OpenTUI/Canvas parity and targeted UX refinement with modular TUI seams, verified local behavior, and an honest boundary around the blocked second Jev review.\n  2259\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/textbook; reuse_rule=reuse the module/layout and OpenTUI behavior findings after checking the current TUI API and worktree; do not infer a second external review or new tests from this rollout.\n  2260\t\n  2261\t## Task 1: Implement Canvas parity in the native TUI, partial\n  2262\t\n  2263\t### rollout_summary_files\n  2264\t\n  2265\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/textbook, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/19/rollout-2026-09-19T08-03-45-01a0b98d-1314-74b3-b9ff-f31175a6e455.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-19T05:08:40+00:00, thread_id=01a0b98d-1314-74b3-b9ff-f31175a6e455, partial; implementation and local verification succeeded, new tests intentionally deferred)\n  2266\t\n  2267\t### keywords\n  2268\t\n  2269\t- textbook, native-tui, canvas, OpenTUI, src/tui, src/themes.ts, renderer.keyInput, destroyRecursively, VHS, similarity-ts\n  2270\t\n  2271\t## Task 2: Apply Jev terminal UX review refinements, partial\n  2272\t\n  2273\t### rollout_summary_files\n  2274\t\n  2275\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/textbook, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/19/rollout-2026-09-19T08-03-45-01a0b98d-1314-74b3-b9ff-f31175a6e455.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-19T05:08:40+00:00, thread_id=01a0b98d-1314-74b3-b9ff-f31175a6e455, partial; first external review plus local follow-up, second review blocked)\n  2276\t\n  2277\t### keywords\n  2278\t\n  2279\t- Jev, TypeSafe, systemone, search_typing_safe, borderless inspector, footer scanability, auto-mode classifier, skate typesafe_api_key@secrets\n  2280\t\n  2281\t## User preferences\n  2282\t\n  2283\t- when scoping implementation, the user said \"use your best judgement tbh\" after rejecting repeated questions -> decide a reasonable product scope and proceed rather than asking more product questions. [Task 1]\n  2284\t- when asked for Canvas parity, the user said \"Don't write tests right now, just focus on implementation\" -> do not add new tests until that boundary is re-enabled; retain existing tests as evidence only. [Task 1]\n  2285\t\n  2286\t## Reusable knowledge\n  2287\t\n  2288\t- The native TUI is modular under `src/tui/{index,state,keymap,focus,preview,sidebar,panel}.ts`; `src/app.ts` is a compatibility re-export, and `src/themes.ts` is the shared Canvas/TUI palette and chrome source consumed by `src/web/html.ts`. Generation guards plus `destroyRecursively()` prevent stale asynchronous story renderables and leaks. [Task 1]\n  2289\t- In this OpenTUI version, use `renderer.keyInput.on(\"keypress\", ...)`; `renderer.on(\"keypress\")` is a no-op. `InputRenderableOptions` excludes `height`, so collapse its wrapping `BoxRenderable`; omit `borderColor` entirely when `border: false`, because supplying it forces a border. [Task 1]\n  2290\t- Verified locally: `npx tsc --noEmit` clean, `bun test` 36 pass/0 fail, VHS showed search/navigation/sidebar/inspector/theme/viewport/footer behavior, and `similarity-ts src/tui src/themes.ts` found no duplicate functions or similar types. [Task 1]\n  2291\t- Search-mode safety was checked mechanically by enumerating printable characters through `resolveAction(..., \"search\")`; none are intercepted. Apply the evidence rather than trusting Jev's lower `search_typing_safe` score. [Task 2]\n  2292\t\n  2293\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  2294\t\n  2295\t- VHS reports `Module not found \"dist/index.js\"` from a scratchpad -> put an explicit `cd /home/diogenes/Projects/textbook` inside the tape and use relative output filenames; an apparent `>` artifact can be the VHS shell prompt, not a TUI scrollbar defect. [Task 1]\n  2296\t- The second Jev submission was blocked by the auto-mode classifier -> do not bypass it; retain the first HTTP-200 review and local checks as the available external-review evidence. Never print or persist the Skate-provided TypeSafe credential. [Task 2]\n  2297\t\n  2298\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/twyne Jev provider, rubric, and writing tools\n  2299\tscope: Route typed Jev judgements through Not Organic, maintain Jev-first rubric and optional writing lenses, and distinguish local implementation from verified provider production.\n  2300\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne plus /home/diogenes/Projects/notorganic-provider; reuse_rule=reinspect both dirty worktrees and deploy state; direct TypeSafe use is local-only when Not Organic is enabled.\n  2301\t\n  2302\t## Task 1: Stage then complete the Not Organic Jev provider boundary, partial\n  2303\t\n  2304\t### rollout_summary_files\n  2305\t\n  2306\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/18/rollout-2026-09-18T19-43-22-01a0b6e7-3c95-7543-9f88-4698f314c385.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-18T23:58:45+00:00, thread_id=01a0b6e7-3c95-7543-9f88-4698f314c385, partial; source changes uncommitted and undeployed)\n  2307\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/18/rollout-2026-09-18T19-09-28-01a0b6c8-324a-7d60-a2fa-a16f00cc5a18.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-18T23:37:12+00:00, thread_id=01a0b6c8-324a-7d60-a2fa-a16f00cc5a18, partial; staged gateway work preceded guarded completion)\n  2308\t\n  2309\t### keywords\n  2310\t\n  2311\t- Jev, TypeSafe, Not Organic, POST /v1/judgement, judgement:evaluate, DPoP, GatewayConfig.typesafe, TYPESAFE_API_KEY, ProviderStore, reserve dispatch accept settle\n  2312\t\n  2313\t## Task 2: Use Jev-first rubric scoring with safe fallback, partial\n  2314\t\n  2315\t### rollout_summary_files\n  2316\t\n  2317\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/18/rollout-2026-09-18T19-43-22-01a0b6e7-3c95-7543-9f88-4698f314c385.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-18T23:58:45+00:00, thread_id=01a0b6e7-3c95-7543-9f88-4698f314c385, partial; final checks intentionally omitted)\n  2318\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/18/rollout-2026-09-18T19-09-28-01a0b6c8-324a-7d60-a2fa-a16f00cc5a18.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-18T23:37:12+00:00, thread_id=01a0b6c8-324a-7d60-a2fa-a16f00cc5a18, partial; earlier 1104-test evidence)\n  2319\t\n  2320\t### keywords\n  2321\t\n  2322\t- runRubricPass, judgementRubricResult, rubric-grade, rubric-judgement-result, draftFingerprint, scoringMethod: judgement, Choice map, Score criteria\n  2323\t\n  2324\t## Task 3: Add optional read-only writing lenses, partial\n  2325\t\n  2326\t### rollout_summary_files\n  2327\t\n  2328\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/18/rollout-2026-09-18T19-43-22-01a0b6e7-3c95-7543-9f88-4698f314c385.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-18T23:58:45+00:00, thread_id=01a0b6e7-3c95-7543-9f88-4698f314c385, partial; UI checks deferred to user)\n  2329\t\n  2330\t### keywords\n  2331\t\n  2332\t- writing-lenses, WRITING_LENSES, reader, revision, voice, promises, scraps, room, circling, research, writing-tools-storage, stale-result\n  2333\t\n  2334\t## User preferences\n  2335\t\n  2336\t- when hosted TypeSafe/Jev integration was discussed, the user said it \"should work through notorganic in actuality rather than tied through this deployment directly\" and wanted an API \"that just works with jev\" -> place provider credentials, authorization, customer inspection, and ledger accounting behind Not Organic. [Task 1]\n  2337\t- when dirty provider files were deliberately left alone, the user asked to \"finish the application\" -> complete the requested product side with guarded/narrow patches while preserving unrelated in-flight provider work. [Task 1]\n  2338\t- when implementation was requested, the user said \"don't manual test things here ... don't bother with tests either pure implementation\" -> stop tests and browser/manual UI checks at that explicit boundary and report the resulting verification gap plainly. [Task 2][Task 3]\n  2339\t\n  2340\t## Reusable knowledge\n  2341\t\n  2342\t- Production Twyne calls Not Organic using DPoP and `judgement:evaluate` at `POST /v1/judgement`; direct `TYPESAFE_API_KEY` is only loopback/local fallback. The provider owns the key, typed state/questions transport, model alias resolution, and per-account reserve -> dispatch -> accept -> settle/reconcile accounting. [Task 1]\n  2343\t- Jev question types are `noul`, `choice`, and `score`; normalize Twyne arrays into TypeSafe Choice maps, retain Score ordered arrays, bound requests, avoid upstream response bodies that may echo documents, and surface uncertain/missing usage rather than silently billing zero. The observed rate was `0.042` microUSD per input token. [Task 1]\n  2344\t- `runRubricPass()` batches enabled criteria and degrades safely; `judgementRubricResult()` rejects incomplete criteria and protects saves with folio/brief/criteria/draft fingerprint freshness guards. Confidence is distribution concentration, not truth or permission to act. [Task 2]\n  2345\t- The eight read-only lenses (`reader`, `revision`, `voice`, `promises`, `scraps`, `room`, `circling`, `research`) live in `src/utils/writing-lenses.ts`, with UI/storage at `src/components/writing-tools/writing-tools.tsx` and `src/utils/writing-tools-storage.ts`. Quote supplied passages, bound inputs, expose missing evidence/uncertainty, reject stale results, and never edit prose automatically. [Task 3]\n  2346\t\n  2347\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  2348\t\n  2349\t- Source edits, a configured gateway variable, and a later successful Railway status call are not deployment/live-route/ledger proof. Final state was uncommitted and undeployed, with no final typecheck, tests, browser checks, or live request after the last edits. [Task 1][Task 2][Task 3]\n  2350\t- Broken Python `PYTHONHOME`/`PYTHONPATH` -> use `env -u PYTHONHOME -u PYTHONPATH python3 ...` for required scripts. GitNexus `UNKNOWN` from wrong symbols -> resolve the exact symbol (`createGateway`) before treating impact output as evidence. [Task 1]\n  2351\t\n  2352\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/twyne editor drag/drop and offline interaction plan\n  2353\tscope: Restore native ProseMirror dragging without false file overlays; route remaining editor-UX, offline-banner, and local-model work through verified seams.\n  2354\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne; reuse_rule=retest exact browser/editor behavior before claiming completion; planning notes are not implementation authority.\n  2355\t\n  2356\t## Task 1: Restore native selected-text dragging and file-drop handling, partial\n  2357\t\n  2358\t### rollout_summary_files\n  2359\t\n  2360\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/18/rollout-2026-09-18T19-09-28-01a0b6c8-3247-7842-bca9-9750c78aad2e.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-18T21:18:15+00:00, thread_id=01a0b6c8-3247-7842-bca9-9750c78aad2e, partial; focused tests passed but E2E has two unresolved cases)\n  2361\t\n  2362\t### keywords\n  2363\t\n  2364\t- Qwik, TipTap, ProseMirror, preventdefault:dragover, preventdefault:dragleave, preventdefault:drop, Dropcursor, twyne-dropcursor, file-drag.ts, drag-selection.e2e.ts\n  2365\t\n  2366\t## Task 2: Plan slash menu, viewport, offline toast, and browser/desktop local models, partial\n  2367\t\n  2368\t### rollout_summary_files\n  2369\t\n  2370\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/18/rollout-2026-09-18T19-09-28-01a0b6c8-3247-7842-bca9-9750c78aad2e.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-18T21:18:15+00:00, thread_id=01a0b6c8-3247-7842-bca9-9750c78aad2e, partial; combined plan selected, local-model design incomplete)\n  2371\t\n  2372\t### keywords\n  2373\t\n  2374\t- slash-command-menu, computePopoverGeometry, DEFAULT_LAYOUT.marginBottom, scrollMargin, global-connectivity-banner, sticky top-0 z-50, IndexedDB, service-worker, Transformers.js, WebGPU, LiteRT\n  2375\t\n  2376\t## User preferences\n  2377\t\n  2378\t- for editor dragging, the user expects selected prose to move on drop, show where it will land, and work for paragraphs and larger blocks. [Task 1]\n  2379\t- the user chose \"Everything in one plan,\" including browser and desktop local models, and chose a bottom-left toast-pattern offline notice; markdown shortcuts were \"not a required part of the editor.\" [Task 2]\n  2380\t- uncertain H1 behavior should be reproduced/verified before being treated as a bug. [Task 2]\n  2381\t\n  2382\t## Reusable knowledge\n  2383\t\n  2384\t- Ancestor `preventdefault:dragover`, `preventdefault:dragleave`, and `preventdefault:drop` in `src/components/editor/manuscript-panel.tsx` are handled by Qwik's capture listener before ProseMirror, making events `defaultPrevented` and disabling native text/image drops. Remove them; `SectionReorder` is not the general blocker. Filter the overlay by `event.dataTransfer` so it appears only for file drags. [Task 1]\n  2385\t- Focused evidence: `bun test --conditions=production --preload ./tests/qwik-test-preload.ts src/utils/file-drag.test.ts` passed 6/0 and `bun run build.types` passed. [Task 1]\n  2386\t- Generalize tested `computePopoverGeometry` for slash-menu flip/clamp/height behavior; current `coords.bottom + 6` has no flip, clamp, or scroll/resize refresh. The fixed toast region in `src/global.css` is the right pattern for replacing `global-connectivity-banner.tsx`'s normal-flow `sticky top-0 z-50` banner. [Task 2]\n  2387\t- `DEFAULT_LAYOUT.marginBottom: 1` overrides the normal 4rem fallback, and nested scrollers lack `scrollMargin`/`scrollThreshold`. Twyne's IndexedDB/service-worker shell is genuinely local-first, but sync, AI, auth, collaboration, and publishing remain remote; browser local models likely use Transformers.js/WebGPU/cached ONNX and desktop has a LiteRT seam. [Task 2]\n  2388\t\n  2389\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  2390\t\n  2391\t- After Chromium installation, E2E had 1 pass/2 fail: multi-paragraph move works, but single-paragraph movement and drop-caret visibility fail and `.twyne-dropcursor` was absent. Inspect the exact test plus generated Dropcursor DOM/configuration before claiming drag/drop complete. [Task 1]\n  2392\t- The rollout ended after an interrupted/rejected follow-up tool call; do not continue edits without renewed direction when that interruption is material. A plan-agent timeout left the local-model design incomplete. [Task 1][Task 2]\n  2393\t\n  2394\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/twyne local Codex Fugu/Sakana catalog configuration\n  2395\tscope: Update and strictly validate the user-level Fugu/Sakana Codex profile and catalog.\n  2396\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne with user config at /home/diogenes/.codex; reuse_rule=recheck provider documentation/live model endpoint and installed config before changing aliases, versions, or defaults.\n  2397\t\n  2398\t## Task 1: Expand Fugu/Sakana model IDs, aliases, and default profile\n  2399\t\n  2400\t### rollout_summary_files\n  2401\t\n  2402\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/18/rollout-2026-09-18T18-47-44-01a0b6b4-4bfc-7fe2-8b6a-2c1695320c03.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-18T23:09:36+00:00, thread_id=01a0b6b4-4bfc-7fe2-8b6a-2c1695320c03, success; installed and strict-config validated)\n  2403\t\n  2404\t### keywords\n  2405\t\n  2406\t- fugu, fugu-ultra, fugu-max, fugu-cyber, sakana-namazu, sakana-models.json, fugu.config.toml, model_catalog_json, strict-config, react-grab-mcp\n  2407\t\n  2408\t## User preferences\n  2409\t\n  2410\t- when the user said \"update fugu config to support the new models\" and supplied all IDs -> update the actual user-level catalog/profile, not merely a proposed configuration. [Task 1]\n  2411\t\n  2412\t## Reusable knowledge\n  2413\t\n  2414\t- Installed paths are `/home/diogenes/.codex/sakana-models.json` and `/home/diogenes/.codex/fugu.config.toml`; the profile defaults to `model = \"fugu-ultra\"` and uses `model_catalog_json` for the 11-model catalog. Custom metadata supports `context_window`, `default_reasoning_level`, and `supported_reasoning_levels`. [Task 1]\n  2415\t- Fugu variants are represented at 1,000,000 context tokens; Namazu at 256,000. `fugu-ultra-v1.1` supports `high,xhigh,max`; other Fugu entries support `high,xhigh`; Namazu uses `none` because thinking is provider-specific. [Task 1]\n  2416\t- Validate with `codex -c 'model_catalog_json=\"/home/diogenes/.codex/sakana-models.json\"' debug models` and `codex exec -p fugu --strict-config --ephemeral`; the latter reaching expected `No prompt provided via stdin` proves strict config loaded. The parent `[mcp_servers.react-grab-mcp]` transport with `npx -y @react-grab/mcp --stdio` is required for strict parsing. [Task 1]\n  2417\t\n  2418\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  2419\t\n  2420\t- `ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'encodings'` in the system Python -> generate JSON with Bun/Node. Sandboxed `api.sakana.ai` DNS failed while an escalated read-only call returned HTTP 200; live `/v1/models` validated current Fugu IDs only, so clearly label Namazu/Cyber version entries as documentation-validated. [Task 1]\n  2421\t\n  2422\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/keating training corpus audit and Learning to Teach artifact\n  2423\tscope: Audit training/benchmark evidence into a narrative report, reuse the canonical Learning to Teach theme, and maintain strict measurement/evidence boundaries.\n  2424\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating; reuse_rule=reinspect benchmark inputs, generated outputs, stylesheet authority, artifact publication state, and mobile rendering before revising or quoting counts.\n  2425\t\n  2426\t## Task 1: Audit the entire training/benchmark corpus and publish The Null Ledger\n  2427\t\n  2428\t### rollout_summary_files\n  2429\t\n  2430\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/18/rollout-2026-09-18T19-09-28-01a0b6c8-3246-7761-bb3d-00f3fdfd84bf.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-15T21:04:50+00:00, thread_id=01a0b6c8-3246-7761-bb3d-00f3fdfd84bf, success; artifact republished at same URL)\n  2431\t\n  2432\t### keywords\n  2433\t\n  2434\t- training corpus, benchmark, The Null Ledger, Learning to Teach, teaching-v4, Delivery Contracts Teaching, benchmark gaps, scripts/training/BENCHMARK.md\n  2435\t\n  2436\t## Task 2: Restyle report with the canonical Learning to Teach visual system\n  2437\t\n  2438\t### rollout_summary_files\n  2439\t\n  2440\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/18/rollout-2026-09-18T19-09-28-01a0b6c8-3246-7761-bb3d-00f3fdfd84bf.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-15T21:04:50+00:00, thread_id=01a0b6c8-3246-7761-bb3d-00f3fdfd84bf, success; rendering follow-up still advisable)\n  2441\t\n  2442\t### keywords\n  2443\t\n  2444\t- report.css, research-story.css, paper-ink-phosphor, VT323, Roboto, JetBrains Mono, claude.ai/artifact, null-ledger.html\n  2445\t\n  2446\t## User preferences\n  2447\t\n  2448\t- when auditing, the user asked to \"check entire,\" create \"a page and story,\" and review improvements and gaps -> combine inventory, editorial judgment, narrative chronology, and ranked actionable gaps rather than only listing files. [Task 1]\n  2449\t- when restyling, the user said \"use the theme from learning to teach\" -> use existing canonical tokens and typography instead of a bespoke visual system. [Task 2]\n  2450\t\n  2451\t## Reusable knowledge\n  2452\t\n  2453\t- The audit counted 155 authored benchmark cases across seven suites, 320 pinned multidomain sources, 460 accepted contextual examples, 42 native-learning artifact directories, and roughly 51 GB under `.keating`. Delivery, Contracts, and Teaching are separate result classes; unreviewed Teaching dimensions remain null. [Task 1]\n  2454\t- Preserve material gaps: broken Python 3.12 environment, no full-corpus human teaching ratings, incomplete/void comparison arms, v3 cohort interruption, small v4 paid pilot, 12 drifted frozen contract sources, 38 untested modules, and 139 untracked training files. The strongest found protocol was blinded two-grader review with pre-unblinding adjudication. [Task 1]\n  2455\t- `web/public/reports/learning-to-teach/report.css` is authoritative; `scripts/report-site/research-story.css` is companion-only. Use paper `#f1ece0`, deep paper `#e9e2d2`, card `#f6f2e8`, ink `#1c211b`, green `#14743c`, terminal `#0c1510`, phosphor `#4be388`, VT323/Roboto/JetBrains Mono, and semantic measured/null/void colors. Artifact-hosted fonts need Google Fonts links, not local paths. [Task 2]\n  2456\t- Republish the existing scratchpad path or use its artifact URL to retain the link: `https://claude.ai/artifact/1meBvkGXLs6Mm9aTST5o3P`. [Task 2]\n  2457\t\n  2458\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  2459\t\n  2460\t- Do not confuse `research-story.css` with the canonical stylesheet; verify authority first. A report can be republished successfully without final rendering proof, so inspect mobile bar rows and inverted legend/state-color contrast before the next revision. [Task 2]\n  2461\t\n  2462\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/keating multidomain teaching corpus expansion and queue generation\n  2463\tscope: Maintain the source-grounded 16-domain corpus catalog and safely run/verify small asynchronous generation jobs.\n  2464\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating; reuse_rule=reinspect catalog, licenses, queue status, worker receipts, and validated exports; do not treat live workers or receipts as completed corpus output.\n  2465\t\n  2466\t## Task 1: Expand and validate the 16-domain source catalog\n  2467\t\n  2468\t### rollout_summary_files\n  2469\t\n  2470\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/13/rollout-2026-09-13T05-30-49-01a09a1a-e577-7681-a64c-a576ae11485e.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-15T04:14:07+00:00, thread_id=01a09a1a-e577-7681-a64c-a576ae11485e, partial; catalog verified, generation remains incomplete)\n  2471\t\n  2472\t### keywords\n  2473\t\n  2474\t- multidomain_corpus, agy_multidomain, music, OpenStax, Open-Music-Theory, multidomain_sources.py, ORIGINAL_URLS, families_per_batch, catalog.json\n  2475\t\n  2476\t## Task 2: Relaunch 32,000-contrast generation in small worker jobs, partial\n  2477\t\n  2478\t### rollout_summary_files\n  2479\t\n  2480\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/13/rollout-2026-09-13T05-30-49-01a09a1a-e577-7681-a64c-a576ae11485e.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-15T04:14:07+00:00, thread_id=01a09a1a-e577-7681-a64c-a576ae11485e, partial; workers running with no completed/reviewed batches at final check)\n  2481\t\n  2482\t### keywords\n  2483\t\n  2484\t- MiniMax-M3, DeepSeek, 32768, music-00-f01, music-01-f01, status.json, worker-process.json, completed_batches, validated artifacts\n  2485\t\n  2486\t## User preferences\n  2487\t\n  2488\t- during domain expansion, the user added \"music too\" -> include music as a complete first-class domain with source and task constraints. [Task 1]\n  2489\t\n  2490\t## Reusable knowledge\n  2491\t\n  2492\t- The validated catalog has 320 source groups: 20 each for history, biology, ml, geology, philosophy, chemistry, physics, computer-science, statistics, economics, psychology, literature, writing, civics, environmental-science, and music. `test_multidomain_expansion.py` passed 16 tests; all 320 raw/text hashes and extraction results matched the catalog/config. [Task 1]\n  2493\t- Preserve literal music chord notation such as `<c e g>4` in `multidomain_sources.py`; HTML-style parsing corrupts it. `multidomain_corpus.py` supports `families_per_batch=1|5`, priority scheduling, `batch_order`, pilot/checkpoint metadata; `agy_multidomain.py` holds `run_locked_queue`, validates membership, and checkpoints reviewed exports. [Task 1]\n  2494\t- The durable v2 design is one family/job, two learner profiles, 20 contrasts. Each MiniMax/DeepSeek worker targets 16,000 contrasts (800 families, 1,600 profiles, 160 source groups) and uses worker-local 32,768 output cap; DeepSeek uses low reasoning effort. [Task 2]\n  2495\t\n  2496\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  2497\t\n  2498\t- Source selection overlapped original URLs -> exclude `ORIGINAL_URLS` before asserting disjointness. When a patch's expected text differs, inspect exact anchors with `rg`/`sed`. [Task 1]\n  2499\t- The original 100-contrast jobs timed out/exhausted output and produced no usable final JSON; retain receipts/logs as superseded, not corpus output. At final check v2 had zero completed batches/reviews, so require `status.json`, `worker-process.json`, drafts/reviews, validation, and exported artifacts before claiming quality or completion. [Task 2]\n  2500\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/voxq platform, canonical research exports, and private Radicle workflow\n  2501\tscope: Extend Voxq without overstating unfinished live integrations; maintain canonical exports and native Devenv-managed private Radicle lifecycle.\n  2502\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/voxq and /home/diogenes/Projects/notorganic-provider; reuse_rule=recheck the heavily dirty worktrees, live assertion configuration, and authorized remote-peer state before committing, deploying, or claiming replication.\n  2503\t\n  2504\t## Task 1: Register Voxq and delegate the broader survey platform, partial\n  2505\t\n  2506\t### rollout_summary_files\n  2507\t\n  2508\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/12/rollout-2026-09-12T17-02-31-01a0976d-cff1-7600-a08d-7d054ba9c9ca.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-10T03:09:16+00:00, thread_id=01a0976d-cff1-7600-a08d-7d054ba9c9ca, partial; registration passed, Codex build exit -1)\n  2509\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/12/rollout-2026-09-12T17-02-31-01a0976d-d008-7870-adcf-810fb461d97e.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-10T02:43:32+00:00, thread_id=01a0976d-d008-7870-adcf-810fb461d97e, partial; platform work unverified)\n  2510\t\n  2511\t### keywords\n  2512\t\n  2513\t- voxq, PRODUCT_IDS, FIRST_PARTY_PRODUCTS, ProductTheme, VOXQ_ASSERTION_PUBLIC_JWK, DPoP, micro-USD, --approve-for-me, --sandbox, adaptive-interviews, SSE\n  2514\t\n  2515\t## Task 2: Complete canonical CSV/JSON exports, docs, and marketing site\n  2516\t\n  2517\t### rollout_summary_files\n  2518\t\n  2519\t- rollout_summaries/2026-09-12T21-02-31-bjn0-voxq_site_export_readme_completion.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/voxq, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/12/rollout-2026-09-12T17-02-31-01a0976d-cff6-7bc2-bec8-12607e1b3476.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-13T00:26:03+00:00, thread_id=01a0976d-cff6-7bc2-bec8-12607e1b3476, success)\n  2520\t\n  2521\t### keywords\n  2522\t\n  2523\t- csv and json should be identical, exportRecords, resultsCsv, resultsJson, ExportResults.tsx, Cache-Control: no-store, smoke-exports.ts, landing/server.ts, embed/embed.js, SurveySim\n  2524\t\n  2525\t## Task 3: Add native Devenv Radicle hooks and verify local node/peers, partial\n  2526\t\n  2527\t### rollout_summary_files\n  2528\t\n  2529\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/voxq, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/12/rollout-2026-09-12T20-58-53-01a09846-3743-7a80-ab37-2f04b80438f4.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-13T01:07:50+00:00, thread_id=01a09846-3743-7a80-ab37-2f04b80438f4, partial; local node healthy, remote replication unconfirmed)\n  2530\t\n  2531\t### keywords\n  2532\t\n  2533\t- git-hooks.nix, voxq:radicle:init, voxq:radicle:status, scripts/radicle.sh, rad:z3X34hv7fz8WAgzTHnMmhJ8rvZz87, core.hooksPath=/dev/null, rad://<rid>/<did>, Railway\n  2534\t\n  2535\t## Task 4: Resume triage in a broadly dirty Voxq worktree\n  2536\t\n  2537\t### rollout_summary_files\n  2538\t\n  2539\t- rollout_summaries/2026-09-12T22-15-23-K2z1-voxq_resume_triage.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/voxq, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/12/rollout-2026-09-12T18-15-23-01a097b0-867c-7553-9dd4-06aaf2db6843.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-12T22:15:34+00:00, thread_id=01a097b0-867c-7553-9dd4-06aaf2db6843, uncertain; no follow-up selected)\n  2540\t\n  2541\t### keywords\n  2542\t\n  2543\t- resume, rtk git status --short, landing, site-shared, webapp, embed, voxq-python, Persimmon, Portkey\n  2544\t\n  2545\t## Task 5: Implement Twin-2K-500 ingestion and data-backed personas, partial\n  2546\t\n  2547\t### rollout_summary_files\n  2548\t\n  2549\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/voxq, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/12/rollout-2026-09-12T21-21-51-01a0985b-3e80-7283-8a35-598e36299050.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-13T08:24:17+00:00, thread_id=01a0985b-3e80-7283-8a35-598e36299050, partial; compilation/diff hygiene only)\n  2550\t\n  2551\t### keywords\n  2552\t\n  2553\t- Twin-2K-500, hyparquet, webapp/server/datasets/twin-2k.ts, registry.ts, dataset_evidence, DatasetAudiencePanel, survey-persona-v3-dataset-evidence, VOXQ_DATASET_CACHE, parquet, checksum\n  2554\t\n  2555\t## User preferences\n  2556\t\n  2557\t- when the user said “nah keep the framwork dude” -> preserve mandated devenv/prek and other repository tooling instead of hand-rolled substitutes [Task 1]\n  2558\t- when the user said “have codex do that” -> delegate the bounded large platform build, but keep authored survey subject matter fixed; personalization may reorder/rephrase, not invent it [Task 1]\n  2559\t- when the user said “csv and json should be identical man” -> prepare one complete canonical record snapshot; vary only serialization/spreadsheet escaping [Task 2]\n  2560\t- when the user clarified “Local Radicle node and peers” and requested the “devenv githooks feature ... not .githooks” -> distinguish local connectivity from replication, and use `git-hooks.nix` in `devenv.nix` [Task 3]\n  2561\t- when the user says “implement that next” after agreeing a roadmap item -> proceed with the next concrete implementation slice without reopening scope; report unrun tests/evaluations plainly [Task 5]\n  2562\t\n  2563\t## Reusable knowledge\n  2564\t\n  2565\t- Voxq registration requires `PRODUCT_IDS`, `FIRST_PARTY_PRODUCTS`, and exhaustive email `ProductTheme`; an unset optional `VOXQ_ASSERTION_PUBLIC_JWK` keeps the gateway booting but rejects Voxq assertions. `bun run typecheck` and 231 tests passed. GitNexus `risk: UNKNOWN` is not clearance: search literal arrays and `.includes()` gates. [Task 1]\n  2566\t- `--sandbox` and `--approve-for-me` cannot be combined. The corrected background Codex task exited `-1`; inspect its output/diff rather than treating intended platform files as delivered. [Task 1]\n  2567\t- Export route/UI uses one `exportRecords` list for `resultsCsv` and `resultsJson`; include study, responses, discoveries/comparisons, population, costs, and caveats, but omit credentials, session capabilities, private interview IDs, and raw provider payloads. Browser downloads matched 106 records/22 columns; Rust 43 and web 184 tests passed. [Task 2]\n  2568\t- Private Radicle initialization succeeded as `rad:z3X34hv7fz8WAgzTHnMmhJ8rvZz87`; `rad/main...main` was `0 0`, and the local node was active on `0.0.0.0:8776` with 11 peers. `scripts/radicle.sh` skips direct `rad`/non-main pushes, bypasses internal mirror hooks, and prevents direct Radicle pushes from deploying Railway. [Task 3]\n  2569\t- Resume requests in this checkout are ambiguous: preserve the broad dirty tree and use the recent cwd/task context; ask a concise clarification when several unfinished workstreams remain. Local survey simulation passed previously, but live Persimmon/Portkey remains credential- and route-gated. [Task 4]\n  2570\t- Twin-2K-500 is pinned to release `f883165a3026fde855dfd448e0cd16443ab257b6`, CC BY 4.0, and seven fixed Parquet parts. The adapter uses fixed publisher URLs/SHA-256, 32 MB/120-second bounded downloads, atomic caching under `webapp/.data/datasets/twin-2k-500/<release>` (or `VOXQ_DATASET_CACHE`), and workspace-scoped transactional/idempotent imports. [Task 5]\n  2571\t- Keep projection narrow: selected demographics QID11/QID13/QID14/QID21/QID23/QID24, QID25 personality items, and QID224–QID229 economic preferences. `dataset_evidence` binds provenance/observations to the importing workspace; observations enter prompts as labeled data, with `survey-persona-v3-dataset-evidence`, never as instructions. Do not infer OCEAN scores; explicit researcher-authored Big Five remains separate. [Task 5]\n  2572\t- Dataset UI permits up to 30 selected profiles and response groups; imports/audience creation call no models. Cost uses a documented four-characters-per-token heuristic and remains an estimate, not a spending ceiling. `bun run check`, `bun run build`, `cargo build --quiet`, and `git diff --check` passed; Cargo retained an existing unused-`qid` warning. [Task 5]\n  2573\t\n  2574\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  2575\t\n  2576\t- Do not claim the delegated platform implementation or landing deployment succeeded from a background launch; registration/typecheck proof is narrower. [Task 1]\n  2577\t- Do not serialize CSV and JSON from separate fresh API responses; do not infer competitor details from an empty SPA shell. [Task 2]\n  2578\t- `rad init` needs the signing key in `ssh-agent`/`rad auth` and must bootstrap with `core.hooksPath=/dev/null`; accept bare and DID-qualified Radicle URLs. Connected peers/local refs do not prove remote private-repository replication. [Task 3]\n  2579\t- GitNexus missing edges/zero callers are unknown, not safety proof: supplement with repository text search. Browser tool inventory was empty and no automated tests, model evaluations, or full acceptance checks ran; do not call the dataset UI visually or end-to-end verified. [Task 5]\n  2580\t\n  2581\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects filesystem organization and Markdown catalog maintenance\n  2582\tscope: Classify/move repositories without losing local work, delete only explicitly approved targets, and repair Projects/Programs catalogs.\n  2583\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects and /home/diogenes/Programs; reuse_rule=inspect current origin/author history and filesystem boundaries before moving or deleting; treat catalog paths as checkout-specific.\n  2584\t\n  2585\t## Task 1: Move third-party repositories, remove approved redundant data, and repair catalogs\n  2586\t\n  2587\t### rollout_summary_files\n  2588\t\n  2589\t- rollout_summaries/2026-09-12T21-02-31-9H9T-projects_programs_cleanup_and_catalog_repair.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/12/rollout-2026-09-12T17-02-31-01a0976d-cff4-7022-a2dd-4f8596be7579.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-12T20:37:49+00:00, thread_id=01a0976d-cff4-7022-a2dd-4f8596be7579, success; 22 moves and 239 catalog-link checks passed)\n  2590\t\n  2591\t### keywords\n  2592\t\n  2593\t- Projects, Programs, mv -n, git origin, authorship, SUMMARY.md, INDEX.md, ../../Programs, ../.archive, keating.bc, bad object HEAD\n  2594\t\n  2595\t## User preferences\n  2596\t\n  2597\t- when organizing files, the user said “don’t delete anything” and clarified “for repos that don't have any git repo assume they are me and local to this computer” -> default to non-destructive moves and leave non-git directories in place [Task 1]\n  2598\t- deletion became allowed only after explicit requests to “remove empty dirs” and “remove keating.bc” -> resolve exact targets and preserve data unless deletion is expressly approved [Task 1]\n  2599\t\n  2600\t## Reusable knowledge\n  2601\t\n  2602\t- Projects and Programs share one filesystem, so `mv -n` is an atomic rename that preserves dirty/untracked work; use source/destination existence checks. Inspect both git origin and author history before moving mixed-ownership repositories. The completed move reported `moved:22 failed:0`; `semdiff` stayed by user choice. [Task 1]\n  2603\t- A stray empty `Projects/.git` can cause false repository detection. Before recursive deletion, move the shell cwd out of the target; `keating.bc` had corrupt history (`fatal: bad object HEAD`) but deletion followed explicit approval and active `keating` was checked intact. [Task 1]\n  2604\t- In Projects category `SUMMARY.md`, use `../X` for Projects targets, `../../Programs/X` for moved targets, and `../.archive/X` for archived targets. Keep genuinely absent rows as `_no longer on disk_` when organizing rather than deleting catalog information; 239 catalog links were checked with no catalog failures. [Task 1]\n  2605\t\n  2606\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  2607\t\n  2608\t- Do not classify a directory as a real repository only because a parent/empty `.git` exists; confirm the repository and history first. Do not run `rm -rf` while the shell remains inside the target. [Task 1]\n  2609\t\n  2610\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/autopsy benchmark playground and provider-boundary review\n  2611\tscope: Review runtime correctness beyond passing typecheck/tests; this records findings only, not fixes.\n  2612\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/autopsy; reuse_rule=reinspect the current implementation and add focused regression tests before applying any repair.\n  2613\t\n  2614\t## Task 1: Review benchmark playground and custom-provider changes\n  2615\t\n  2616\t### rollout_summary_files\n  2617\t\n  2618\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/autopsy, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/10/rollout-2026-09-10T05-48-28-01a08ab7-fafb-7db3-8fec-6b0670cc88d7.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-10T09:50:16+00:00, thread_id=01a08ab7-fafb-7db3-8fec-6b0670cc88d7, success; findings only)\n  2619\t\n  2620\t### keywords\n  2621\t\n  2622\t- benchmark/server.ts, JSON.stringify cannot serialize cyclic structures, cycle-free DTO, diagnostic-service.ts, diagnosis cache, Error serialization, minimaxApiKey, MINIMAX_API_KEY\n  2623\t\n  2624\t## Reusable knowledge\n  2625\t\n  2626\t- Keep the intentional circular todo graph internal and return a cycle-free DTO; use a fresh diagnosis cache per benchmark invocation; serialize `Error` name/message/stack explicitly at HTTP boundaries; honor configured `minimaxApiKey` before falling back to `MINIMAX_API_KEY`. [Task 1]\n  2627\t\n  2628\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  2629\t\n  2630\t- Passing typecheck and 75 tests did not exercise these runtime boundaries. No fixes or post-change verification happened; write focused regression coverage before declaring any repair complete. [Task 1]\n  2631\t\n  2632\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/keating chat sign-in continuation and Not Organic inference failure handling\n  2633\tscope: Keep learner chat immediate through account authorization and diagnose the actual Keating-to-Not Organic inference path without treating health checks as end-to-end proof.\n  2634\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating and /home/diogenes/Projects/notorganic-provider; reuse_rule=recheck dirty worktrees, installed desktop version, fresh token/DPoP flow, Portkey configuration, and Convex behavior.\n  2635\t\n  2636\t## Task 1: Preserve a pending chat send across Not Organic sign-in and push focused changes\n  2637\t\n  2638\t### rollout_summary_files\n  2639\t\n  2640\t- rollout_summaries/2026-09-09T09-07-30-nEVR-keating_landing_and_signin_message_continuation_push.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/09/rollout-2026-09-09T05-07-30-01a0856c-1ddf-73c3-a1a7-04c0f52e6c4b.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-09T21:03:57+00:00, thread_id=01a0856c-1ddf-73c3-a1a7-04c0f52e6c4b, success; mocked browser proof only)\n  2641\t\n  2642\t### keywords\n  2643\t\n  2644\t- pending-chat-turn.ts, sessionStorage, stream_not_found, AppStorage, IndexedDB oncomplete, FlueConversation.resume, b45e0d8b, core.hooksPath=/dev/null\n  2645\t\n  2646\t## Task 2: Diagnose immediate-send/retry and production funding failures, partial\n  2647\t\n  2648\t### rollout_summary_files\n  2649\t\n  2650\t- rollout_summaries/2026-09-09T21-09-56-9d3N-keating_notorganic_chat_e2e_inference_retry_partial.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Documents/Codex/2026-09-09/recently-in-keeting-we-worked-on, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/09/rollout-2026-09-09T17-09-56-01a08801-84fe-7a31-be23-ea11379e0ac7.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-10T00:43:27+00:00, thread_id=01a08801-84fe-7a31-be23-ea11379e0ac7, partial)\n  2651\t\n  2652\t### keywords\n  2653\t\n  2654\t- optimistic UI, retry, DPoP, Portkey, pc-keatin-bb473e, product: keating, INSUFFICIENT_FUNDS, HTTP 402, Passthrough target requires a provider\n  2655\t\n  2656\t## User preferences\n  2657\t\n  2658\t- when the user said a send “should immediately see it in the chat” and requested retry -> independently accept optimistic insertion, sending status, failed-turn retention, and retry without manual resend [Task 2]\n  2659\t- when the user said “most computer use, don't do computer use on your own” -> use code/logs/HTTP/tests and leave desktop/browser interaction to the user [Task 2]\n  2660\t- when the user said “you will need to push changes then we shall see” -> push explicitly requested focused work after validation while leaving unrelated dirty work unstaged [Task 1]\n  2661\t\n  2662\t## Reusable knowledge\n  2663\t\n  2664\t- Persist `{sessionId, timestamp, ready}` before sign-in; only mark ready after callback exchange and claim once by exact session/message timestamp. Clear before resume to avoid StrictMode duplicates. New Flue streams legitimately yield 404 `stream_not_found` before their first prompt, and IndexedDB must await transaction `oncomplete`. Focused tests: 35 pass; mocked flow rendered one learner turn/one answer and cleared the marker. [Task 1]\n  2665\t- Portkey `balanced` only worked with metadata `product: \"keating\"`; `fast` returned `Passthrough target requires a provider`. Convex `INSUFFICIENT_FUNDS` was hidden behind a generic 500 because production wraps ordinary errors; propagate a structured code and map it to non-retryable 402. [Task 2]\n  2666\t\n  2667\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  2668\t\n  2669\t- `git -c core.hooksPath=/dev/null push` was an exceptional, separately validated bypass after unrelated failures/locked key/checkpoint rejection, not normal release procedure. Mocked OAuth/provider tests and remote ref proof do not establish real-account or production inference. [Task 1]\n  2670\t- Health/Railway success/direct Portkey stream do not prove desktop chat. Verify fresh public token exchange, DPoP request, exact stream, reservation, and rendered UI. Retryable failures get fresh DPoP proofs; insufficient credits do not retry. [Task 2]\n  2671\t\n  2672\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/keating MiniCPM5 offline tutoring, v3.15.0 release, and publication/privacy boundary\n  2673\tscope: Evaluate MiniCPM5 for browser/native tutoring, retain safe text-only media behavior, and distinguish release artifacts from verified public publication and credential remediation.\n  2674\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating; reuse_rule=recheck model/runtime support, JDK/NDK environment, release assets, GitHub cache state, and secrets rotation before reuse.\n  2675\t\n  2676\t## Task 1: Keep MiniCPM5 out of unsupported browser runtime; add native offline path, partial\n  2677\t\n  2678\t### rollout_summary_files\n  2679\t\n  2680\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/10/rollout-2026-09-10T05-12-38-01a08a97-2eee-70c3-87c4-20f4245238ef.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-10T11:05:38+00:00, thread_id=01a08a97-2eee-70c3-87c4-20f4245238ef, partial)\n  2681\t\n  2682\t### keywords\n  2683\t\n  2684\t- MiniCPM5-2B-LiteRT, .litertlm, BROWSER_MODELS, WeakMap<Blob,string>, recording-transcripts, JDK 21, CPATH, keating-litert, SHA-256\n  2685\t\n  2686\t## Task 2: Publish v3.15.0, remediate public checkpoint credential exposure, and assess Windows/APK assets, partial\n  2687\t\n  2688\t### rollout_summary_files\n  2689\t\n  2690\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/10/rollout-2026-09-10T07-05-46-01a08afe-c05c-7ba3-868b-da12a887728f.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-10T20:56:02+00:00, thread_id=01a08afe-c05c-7ba3-868b-da12a887728f, partial; public cache/rotation unresolved)\n  2691\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/10/rollout-2026-09-10T16-55-01-01a08d1a-3be9-7611-9f53-4aafb458285a.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-10T23:13:11+00:00, thread_id=01a08d1a-3be9-7611-9f53-4aafb458285a, partial; assets absent/Windows check failed)\n  2692\t\n  2693\t### keywords\n  2694\t\n  2695\t- v3.15.0, Entire checkpoints, Paddle, GitHub cached objects, credential rotation, release.yml, desktop-release.yml, Windows .exe, Android .apk\n  2696\t\n  2697\t## User preferences\n  2698\t\n  2699\t- when the user asked for MiniCPM5 as primary browser model plus image/audio errors -> verify model/runtime compatibility before changing defaults and visibly reject unsupported media [Task 1]\n  2700\t- when the user said “new release”/“do that” -> take commit/tag/push/publication through independent proof and distinguish preparation from public release [Task 2]\n  2701\t\n  2702\t## Reusable knowledge\n  2703\t\n  2704\t- MiniCPM5 LiteRT is text-only `.litertlm`; Keating browser loader is Transformers.js ONNX, and LiteRT-LM JS did not support arbitrary bundles. Keep it out of `BROWSER_MODELS`. For recordings, suppress only a successful transcript tied to that exact Blob via `WeakMap<Blob,string>`; focused web tests 16 passed. [Task 1]\n  2705\t- Native Android build requires a full JDK 21 with `javac`; clear `CPATH`, `C_INCLUDE_PATH`, `CPLUS_INCLUDE_PATH`, and `LIBRARY_PATH` before NDK builds. APK compilation/package inclusion and 57 focused tests do not prove device inference/iOS. [Task 1]\n  2706\t- The checkpoint incident requires private copy/removal from public branch plus credential rotation and GitHub cached-object purge; never retain or reproduce the exposed credential. Treat release/tag/workflow claims and Windows/APK publication as separate checks. [Task 2]\n  2707\t\n  2708\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  2709\t\n  2710\t- Do not change high-impact shared `modelInputModalities` for a narrow attachment fix, and do not claim arbitrary LiteRT browser support without actual loading/generation. [Task 1]\n  2711\t- Release assets were absent, Windows verification failed, and Android retry remained in progress. A release workflow trigger or source publication is not proof that `.exe`/`.apk` assets exist and install. [Task 2]\n  2712\t\n  2713\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/textbook web review, OpenTUI branding, docs separation, and deployment\n  2714\tscope: Apply bounded review fixes and product presentation changes while keeping broad implementation claims separate from final verification.\n  2715\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/textbook; reuse_rule=recheck current dirty tree, generated assets, Railway deployment, and browser behavior before claiming completion.\n  2716\t\n  2717\t## Task 1: Address review findings, branding/docs work, and deployment, partial\n  2718\t\n  2719\t### rollout_summary_files\n  2720\t\n  2721\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/textbook, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/11/rollout-2026-09-11T01-13-09-01a08ee2-48f5-7292-876b-cd7fca859165.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-11T06:31:38+00:00, thread_id=01a08ee2-48f5-7292-876b-cd7fca859165, partial; final verification generally skipped)\n  2722\t\n  2723\t### keywords\n  2724\t\n  2725\t- textbook, OpenTUI, review P1 P2, social cards, Railway, hosted-vs-local docs, verification skipped\n  2726\t\n  2727\t## Reusable knowledge\n  2728\t\n  2729\t- This rollout is a routing record for broad review/branding/docs/deployment implementation; open its summary before making completion claims because final verification was generally skipped. [Task 1]\n  2730\t\n  2731\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  2732\t\n  2733\t- Do not convert wide code changes or deployment setup into security/reliability/browser proof without the missing targeted checks. [Task 1]\n  2734\t\n  2735\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/dio.computer research-grounded high-impact design direction and content QA\n  2736\tscope: Explore actual browser-shaped personal-site directions from repository/blog/photo evidence; avoid restrained generic moodboards and preserve source data integrity boundaries.\n  2737\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/dio.computer with Keating indexing context; reuse_rule=recheck Paper quota, source content, photo mapping, and user feedback before making design or source edits.\n  2738\t\n  2739\t## Task 1: Index repos, recover Keating files, and explore a louder dio.computer direction, partial\n  2740\t\n  2741\t### rollout_summary_files\n  2742\t\n  2743\t- rollout_summaries/2026-09-12T21-02-31-lJJC-dio_computer_design_direction_and_multi_repo_indexing.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/12/rollout-2026-09-12T17-02-31-01a0976d-d04b-77f2-91de-e06f4b2bea68.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-09T20:02:02+00:00, thread_id=01a0976d-d04b-77f2-91de-e06f4b2bea68, partial; second UI artifact awaiting feedback)\n  2744\t\n  2745\t### keywords\n  2746\t\n  2747\t- yell HERE I AM, bland and muted, agentFacts.ts, sitePhotos.ts, Paper Desktop, Weekly MCP limit reached, GitNexus, graft build, PYTHONHOME\n  2748\t\n  2749\t## User preferences\n  2750\t\n  2751\t- when the user said “it isn't a celebration of myself and my interests,” “bland and muted,” and “yell HERE I AM” -> favor strong personality, saturation, contrast, density, real interests/photos, humor, and memorable hierarchy [Task 1]\n  2752\t- when the user said eight directions “just feel off” -> change the format/assumption rather than generating more themed poster variants [Task 1]\n  2753\t- when the user said inspect code/blog/site information and “use your best judgement” -> research before asking more design questions [Task 1]\n  2754\t\n  2755\t## Reusable knowledge\n  2756\t\n  2757\t- Start with `src/data/agentFacts.ts`, `src/data/sitePhotos.ts`, `PRODUCT.md`, `soul.md`, and `posts/*.md`. Show actual browser/UI composition, navigation, hierarchy, and interaction rather than illustrative moodboards. [Task 1]\n  2758\t- `graft build` creates ignored cache; `gitnexus analyze <path>` indexes a repo, while `gitnexus status` takes no path. Keating `release.yml` is separate from `devenv.nix`; `OPERATIONS.md` is checked against config by `bun scripts/check-env-docs.ts`. [Task 1]\n  2759\t- A contact sheet found photos 01–11 likely shuffled in `sitePhotos.ts`; Paper usage was corrected but application source remains an open bug pending explicit scope. Use `env -u PYTHONHOME -u PYTHONPATH python3` for poisoned Python env. [Task 1]\n  2760\t\n  2761\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  2762\t\n  2763\t- The initial genre-pastiche poster directions were rejected; desaturation, sparse accents, and hairline borders reinforced the muted result. Paper MCP had a weekly hard limit; do not attempt a workaround without user direction. [Task 1]\n  2764\t- Verify architecture/references before restoring suspected zero-byte files; an auto-mode denial should be handled through a safe alternate command or reported, not bypassed. [Task 1]\n  2765\t\n  2766\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/voxq survey webapp and contract-only Persimmon persona tier\n  2767\tscope: Run and verify the local survey studio, keep its Rust/Bun boundary safe, and expose a Not Organic model alias without falsely advertising an unwired upstream.\n  2768\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/voxq and /home/diogenes/Projects/notorganic-provider; reuse_rule=reuse local webapp and alias-contract guidance after checking both dirty worktrees; Persimmon/Portkey production availability requires fresh credentials and a real route.\n  2769\t\n  2770\t## Task 1: Fix and verify the voxq survey webapp\n  2771\t\n  2772\t### rollout_summary_files\n  2773\t\n  2774\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/voxq, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/12/rollout-2026-09-12T17-02-31-01a0976d-cff7-7932-863d-f23bba79fa99.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-11T07:26:51+00:00, thread_id=01a0976d-cff7-7932-863d-f23bba79fa99, success; local end-to-end simulation verified)\n  2775\t\n  2776\t### keywords\n  2777\t\n  2778\t- voxq, webapp/server.ts, 127.0.0.1:3100, 127.0.0.1:3101, api_version === 2, reqwest, rustls-tls, openssl-sys, embed-config, PIPESTATUS\n  2779\t\n  2780\t## Task 2: Add the `persona` alias contract-only\n  2781\t\n  2782\t### rollout_summary_files\n  2783\t\n  2784\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/voxq, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/12/rollout-2026-09-12T17-02-31-01a0976d-cff7-7932-863d-f23bba79fa99.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-11T07:26:51+00:00, thread_id=01a0976d-cff7-7932-863d-f23bba79fa99, success; live Persimmon/Portkey intentionally gated)\n  2785\t\n  2786\t### keywords\n  2787\t\n  2788\t- persona, infer:persona, catalog.ts, ADMIN_CAPS_MICROUSD, ENABLED_MODEL_ALIASES, /v1/models, Portkey, missing bearer API key, Unsupported model alias\n  2789\t\n  2790\t## Task 3: Produce an honest Persimmon access appeal and walkthrough\n  2791\t\n  2792\t### rollout_summary_files\n  2793\t\n  2794\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/voxq, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/12/rollout-2026-09-12T17-02-31-01a0976d-cff7-7932-863d-f23bba79fa99.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-11T07:26:51+00:00, thread_id=01a0976d-cff7-7932-863d-f23bba79fa99, success)\n  2795\t\n  2796\t### keywords\n  2797\t\n  2798\t- TutorMoments, simulated respondents, authored learner replies, research-access appeal, detect-changes, no commits or deployments\n  2799\t\n  2800\t## User preferences\n  2801\t\n  2802\t- when the user asked to “get the web app working” and requested a walkthrough -> verify the running application end-to-end and distinguish verified behavior from unwired behavior [Task 1]\n  2803\t- when the user selected alias `persona` and said “Contract-only, not enabled” -> define it for local tooling but do not advertise or deploy it until a verified Persimmon key and Portkey route exist [Task 2]\n  2804\t\n  2805\t## Reusable knowledge\n  2806\t\n  2807\t- `webapp/server.ts` starts Rust privately at `127.0.0.1:3101`; the Bun BFF at `127.0.0.1:3100` requires Rust `/healthz` with `api_version === 2`. `reqwest` was the only `openssl-sys` consumer; disabling default features and selecting `rustls-tls` produced a clean build without it. [Task 1]\n  2808\t- Verify create -> estimate -> run -> analysis -> cost -> publish -> embed-config. Demo cost is explicitly zero; unknown provider rates must remain nonzero/unknown. Public embed config must expose only accepting state, name, product, and question count. [Task 1]\n  2809\t- Not Organic aliases are capability tiers (`infer:<alias>`), not upstream IDs. Add `persona` to contracts and the exhaustive admin-cap map, but omit it from Railway `ENABLED_MODEL_ALIASES` and gateway `/v1/models` fallbacks until configuration is real. Local deterministic fixtures do not prove human-like realism. [Task 2]\n  2810\t- The provisional 2,000,000 µUSD cap is a ceiling, not published Persimmon pricing. Current evidence is HTTP 401 `missing bearer API key` and WorkOS-gated docs; no live request or Portkey mapping was verified. [Task 2]\n  2811\t- The appeal may connect voxq's simulated-respondent benchmarking to Keating's authored-learner limitation and Persimmon TutorMoments, but must not claim a human interview or live Persimmon flow. Run repository `detect-changes` before later commits because unrelated Not Organic changes exist. [Task 3]\n  2812\t\n  2813\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  2814\t\n  2815\t- `cargo build 2>&1 | tail` masks Cargo status: inspect `PIPESTATUS[0]` or avoid the pipe. Shell cwd does not persist between background calls, so use absolute paths or explicit `cd`; direct Rust health without its internal bearer token should return 401. [Task 1]\n  2816\t- Treat GitNexus `risk: UNKNOWN` as unresolved and confirm by text search. Do not enable `persona` or invent upstream pricing from the admin ceiling. [Task 2]\n  2817\t\n  2818\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/keating MiniCPM5 browser WebGPU diagnosis and model-loading UX\n  2819\tscope: Diagnose local MiniCPM5 WebGPU execution failures, preserve loading visibility, align ONNX Runtime Web packages, and source-review model generation guidance.\n  2820\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating; reuse_rule=recheck target GPU/browser, npm publication state, model artifacts, and branch before reuse; no target-device MiniCPM5 fix was proven.\n  2821\t\n  2822\t## Task 1: Diagnose MiniCPM5 `Invalid Buffer` during WebGPU execution\n  2823\t\n  2824\t### rollout_summary_files\n  2825\t\n  2826\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/11/rollout-2026-09-11T19-20-26-01a092c5-ba40-79b1-8a49-6c9c2b750e63.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-12T01:41:26+00:00, thread_id=01a092c5-ba40-79b1-8a49-6c9c2b750e63, partial; target-device failure unresolved)\n  2827\t\n  2828\t### keywords\n  2829\t\n  2830\t- MiniCPM5, RASMUS/MiniCPM5-2B-ONNX, WebGPU, shader-f16, OrtRun, mapAsync, Invalid Buffer, q4f16, GPU device-lost, GitNexus\n  2831\t\n  2832\t## Task 2: Keep browser-model download/loading visible across navigation\n  2833\t\n  2834\t### rollout_summary_files\n  2835\t\n  2836\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/11/rollout-2026-09-11T19-20-26-01a092c5-ba40-79b1-8a49-6c9c2b750e63.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-12T01:41:26+00:00, thread_id=01a092c5-ba40-79b1-8a49-6c9c2b750e63, success; page/tab close still cancels)\n  2837\t\n  2838\t### keywords\n  2839\t\n  2840\t- BrowserModelDownloadStatus, ModelDownloadBar.tsx, model-download-progress.ts, describeDownload, Cancel download, GPU preparation, 1 of 2 files\n  2841\t\n  2842\t## Task 3: Pin published ONNX Runtime Web packages and review MiniCPM5 guidance\n  2843\t\n  2844\t### rollout_summary_files\n  2845\t\n  2846\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/11/rollout-2026-09-11T19-20-26-01a092c5-ba40-79b1-8a49-6c9c2b750e63.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-12T01:41:26+00:00, thread_id=01a092c5-ba40-79b1-8a49-6c9c2b750e63, success)\n  2847\t\n  2848\t### keywords\n  2849\t\n  2850\t- onnxruntime-web@1.29.0, onnxruntime-common, onnxruntime-node, Transformers.js, max_new_tokens, top_p=0.95, enable_thinking, XML tool calls\n  2851\t\n  2852\t## User preferences\n  2853\t\n  2854\t- when the user said browser acceleration was enabled and Edge was version 153 -> do not repeat generic compatibility advice; separate adapter preflight from actual runtime/backend errors [Task 1]\n  2855\t- when the user asked to read the Hugging Face README, generation notes, and model report before behavior changes -> source-review model integration guidance first [Task 3]\n  2856\t\n  2857\t## Reusable knowledge\n  2858\t\n  2859\t- `checkWebGpuAvailable()` only proves `navigator.gpu`, adapter, and `shader-f16`; MiniCPM5 is a ~1.83 GB `q4f16` export with a ~535 MB unquantized embedding table, and passing preflight does not prove `OrtRun`. Refresh GitNexus (`analyze`, then `status`) before trusting its call graph. [Task 1]\n  2860\t- `BrowserModelDownloadStatus` in `web/src/components/ModelDownloadBar.tsx`, mounted by `web/src/App.tsx`, keeps store-owned loads visible after picker close/route change; show percentage, bytes, file count, rate, ETA, preparation/GPU loading, and accessible cancellation. 1,713 web tests, production build, and `git diff --check` passed. [Task 2]\n  2861\t- Browser JS packages published at 1.29.0 while native ONNX Runtime was 1.30.0. Pin `onnxruntime-common`, `onnxruntime-node`, and `onnxruntime-web` together at published 1.29.0; do not pin a native-only version. [Task 3]\n  2862\t- MiniCPM5's documented browser path uses `device: 'webgpu'`, `dtype: 'q4f16'`, message arrays, and `max_new_tokens`; OpenBMB guidance is `temperature=1.0, top_p=0.95`. Current browser chat disables thinking and does not convert XML-style tool calls, so treat it as direct-answer chat. [Task 3]\n  2863\t\n  2864\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  2865\t\n  2866\t- `failed to call OrtRun(). ... Invalid Buffer (unlabeled)` remains unresolved model/backend/GPU compatibility or device loss, not evidence that Edge/acceleration is unsupported. Capture device-lost diagnostics, test smaller/q4 models, and compare runtimes on target hardware. [Task 1]\n  2867\t- Raw Hugging Face file URLs were blocked by the web tool; use model-card/README pages or repository tools. [Task 3]\n  2868\t\n  2869\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/keating immediate chat, production account auth, and signed desktop distribution\n  2870\t\n  2871\tscope: Make chat publication immediate, keep account authorization distinct from hosted inference, and package Keating for Windows plus signed Linux/AppImage/DEB/RPM/Flatpak distribution.\n  2872\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating; reuse_rule=recheck the heavily dirty worktree, live Railway configuration, CI/desktop runners, signing/publication state, and real desktop/browser flows; focused/local checks do not prove public release or authenticated production use.\n  2873\t\n  2874\t## Task 1: Immediate learner-message visibility and Not Organic account sign-in, partial\n  2875\t\n  2876\t### rollout_summary_files\n  2877\t\n  2878\t- rollout_summaries/2026-09-09T04-11-52-opTc-keating_auth_chat_windows_flatpak_packaging.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/09/rollout-2026-09-09T00-11-52-01a0845d-7684-7db2-a6bb-71e3adda3052.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-09T08:36:03+00:00, thread_id=01a0845d-7684-7db2-a6bb-71e3adda3052, partial; focused tests and endpoint checks passed, browser callback/inference not proved)\n  2879\t\n  2880\t### keywords\n  2881\t\n  2882\t- AssistantChatPanel, FlueConversation, sendPrepared, optimistic-message, flue-immediate-send.test.ts, NotOrganic, PKCE, DPoP, publicClientConfig, VITE_NOTORGANIC_ENABLED, keating.help, spawnSync bun EPERM\n  2883\t\n  2884\t## Task 2: Windows Electron packaging and native runtime hardening, partial\n  2885\t\n  2886\t### rollout_summary_files\n  2887\t\n  2888\t- rollout_summaries/2026-09-09T04-11-52-opTc-keating_auth_chat_windows_flatpak_packaging.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/09/rollout-2026-09-09T00-11-52-01a0845d-7684-7db2-a6bb-71e3adda3052.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-09T08:36:03+00:00, thread_id=01a0845d-7684-7db2-a6bb-71e3adda3052, partial; local Nitro/Lean tests passed, no Windows runner)\n  2889\t\n  2890\t### keywords\n  2891\t\n  2892\t- dist:windows, NSIS, Electron, windows-latest, native-runtime.ts, nitro-runtime.ts, lean-verifier.ts, verify-windows-runtime.cjs, taskkill, Job Object, .elan/bin/lean.exe\n  2893\t\n  2894\t## Task 3: Signed AppImage/DEB/RPM releases and self-hosted Flatpak, partial\n  2895\t\n  2896\t### rollout_summary_files\n  2897\t\n  2898\t- rollout_summaries/2026-09-09T04-11-52-opTc-keating_auth_chat_windows_flatpak_packaging.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/09/rollout-2026-09-09T00-11-52-01a0845d-7684-7db2-a6bb-71e3adda3052.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-09T08:36:03+00:00, thread_id=01a0845d-7684-7db2-a6bb-71e3adda3052, partial; local signed exports/install passed, public repository/release unproved)\n  2899\t\n  2900\t### keywords\n  2901\t\n  2902\t- AppImage, DEB, RPM, SHA256SUMS, sign-release.mjs, keating-release-key.asc, fingerprint.txt, Flatpak, Electron2.BaseApp//25.08, Zypak, appstreamcli compose, --no-net, OSTree, .flatpakrepo, .flatpakref, GitHub Pages\n  2903\t\n  2904\t## User preferences\n  2905\t\n  2906\t- when the user said a sent message “should appear in chat immediately” and be visible “the moment i press enter” -> publish the learner turn before credentials, workspace preparation, or model admission; reconcile later rather than delaying visible feedback. [Task 1]\n  2907\t- when the user wanted Anthropic token handling “done automatically” -> distinguish provider/browser OAuth limits from desktop-native callbacks, and do not claim automatic web authentication without real provider/browser verification. [Task 1]\n  2908\t- when the user said “we should also get the desktop app working for windows” -> cross-platform delivery includes an installer plus native dependencies, process handling, filesystem/OAuth/credential paths, and GUI/runtime smoke proof, not merely a build target. [Task 2]\n  2909\t- when the user requested DEB/RPM “along with a signed key,” retained AppImage, and chose self-hosted Flatpak -> preserve all three Linux formats, publish an out-of-band public signing key, and use a signed self-hosted Flatpak repository rather than Flathub unless redirected. [Task 3]\n  2910\t\n  2911\t## Reusable knowledge\n  2912\t\n  2913\t- `web/src/keating/flue/conversation.ts` supports synchronous local publication through `sendPrepared`, cancellable preparation, retained failed/repeated submissions, and native acknowledgement reconciliation. `web/src/test/flue-immediate-send.test.ts` covered delayed preparation, repeated failed text, and cancellation; focused immediate-send/chat/audio tests reported 13 passing tests. [Task 1]\n  2914\t- Not Organic browser auth uses PKCE plus a device-bound DPoP key, pending state in browser storage, exact issuer/client/redirect matching, and callback receipt/code-hash guards. `VITE_NOTORGANIC_ENABLED` should gate hosted inference, not account sign-in; authorization instead requires explicit issuer and authorization URL configuration. The inspected Railway production value was `VITE_NOTORGANIC_ENABLED=false`; focused Not Organic suites reported 25 passing tests, authorization redirected, token preflight returned 204 for `https://keating.help`, and the OpenAI device route returned 200. [Task 1]\n  2915\t- Windows packaging adds `dist:windows`/NSIS and a `windows-latest` release job that packages, silently installs, and runs a packaged native-runtime smoke test. Windows runtime needs command quoting, case-insensitive environment overrides, early spawn/exit listeners, hidden background processes, and distinct immutable `resources/nitro` versus mutable user-data paths. Lean verification resolves `~/.elan/bin/lean.exe`, restricts syntax/tactics, bounds execution/output, and audits axioms; focused Nitro/Lean tests reported 16 tests/68 assertions, with Lean 4.30 accepting valid and rejecting invalid examples. [Task 2]\n  2916\t- The dedicated release key's public fingerprint/key live at `desktop/signing/fingerprint.txt` and `desktop/signing/keating-release-key.asc`; private material belongs only in isolated CI secrets/keyrings. `sign-release.mjs` makes deterministic `SHA256SUMS`, detached signatures, public-key export, and optional embedded RPM signatures. [Task 3]\n  2917\t- Flatpak can be self-hosted: retain OSTree objects, refs, summary, signatures, AppStream catalogs, `.flatpakrepo`, `.flatpakref`, and the public key. Build from an already-published architecture-matching AppImage or unpacked Electron app after ELF-architecture validation. Local x86_64/aarch64 signed exports and installation succeeded, and packaged `hyperswarm`/`corestore` loaded in sandbox; Flatpak runtime dependencies are not bundled and may still come from Flathub. [Task 3]\n  2918\t\n  2919\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  2920\t\n  2921\t- Browser automation lacked a connected Playwriter extension, headless navigation timed out, and CUA had no browser. Endpoint/CORS/focused-test evidence is not real callback completion, persistence, refresh, or authenticated model-use proof. Treat local `spawnSync bun EPERM` from the `keating-flue-runtime` Vite plugin as an environment limitation unless CI reproduces it. [Task 1]\n  2922\t- No Windows runner executed. Do not claim installer launch, GUI startup, OAuth return, encrypted credential persistence, native dependency loading, or descendant cleanup; `taskkill` fallback is not a Job Object guarantee, and symlink tests may need junctions or Developer Mode. [Task 2]\n  2923\t- AppStream compose initially failed from a missing compose addon and partial URLs: require host `appstreamcli compose`, run `--no-net`, and fail before export if catalog generation is unavailable. `rpmsign` was initially missing and end-to-end RPM embedded signing remains unproved. Headless Flatpak DBus errors are not desktop-session/OAuth/audio/permissions/storage proof; local exports/GitHub Pages enablement do not prove the repository or release artifacts were committed, pushed, public, or install-tested. [Task 3]\n  2924\t\n  2925\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/keating settings controls, Codex search UX, and Railway production deployment\n  2926\t\n  2927\tscope: Maintain responsive settings/provider controls and deploy the Keating web surface, including native Codex web search and copyable diagnostics, while preserving unrelated dirty work.\n  2928\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating; reuse_rule=recheck the current dependency graph, Railway target, and dirty-tree scope; local tests/typechecks do not establish live search behavior.\n  2929\t\n  2930\t## Task 1: Responsive settings navigation and complete provider visibility controls\n  2931\t\n  2932\t### rollout_summary_files\n  2933\t\n  2934\t- rollout_summaries/2026-09-08T03-25-44-ctrB-keating_settings_cleanup_and_context_report_site.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/07/rollout-2026-09-07T23-25-44-01a07f0c-dd35-75f0-b5c3-9ce89342b033.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-08T05:01:02+00:00, thread_id=01a07f0c-dd35-75f0-b5c3-9ce89342b033, success; web typecheck passed)\n  2935\t\n  2936\t### keywords\n  2937\t\n  2938\t- SettingsDialog, Panda CSS, md breakpoint, aria-label, title, double-box, setProvidersVisibility, hiddenProviders, customProviders, ProviderVisibilitySection\n  2939\t\n  2940\t## Task 2: Codex native web search and copyable diagnostics\n  2941\t\n  2942\t### rollout_summary_files\n  2943\t\n  2944\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/08/rollout-2026-09-08T07-47-21-01a080d8-1ab0-79f0-a1af-6170040588bf.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-08T21:43:08+00:00, thread_id=01a080d8-1ab0-79f0-a1af-6170040588bf, success locally; live behavior unverified)\n  2945\t\n  2946\t### keywords\n  2947\t\n  2948\t- web_search, external_web_access, codex-search-fetch.ts, response.output_item.done, zstd, pdfjs-dist, WebSearchPart, CopyDiagnosticButton, DiagnosticsTab\n  2949\t\n  2950\t## Task 3: Deploy the scoped Keating snapshot to Railway\n  2951\t\n  2952\t### rollout_summary_files\n  2953\t\n  2954\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/08/rollout-2026-09-08T07-47-21-01a080d8-1ab0-79f0-a1af-6170040588bf.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-08T21:43:08+00:00, thread_id=01a080d8-1ab0-79f0-a1af-6170040588bf, success; deployment 2459726e-340e-477b-8b79-db0c5601eea4)\n  2955\t\n  2956\t### keywords\n  2957\t\n  2958\t- Railway, keating.help, --path-as-root, filtered snapshot, Dockerfile.web, railway.toml, pdfjs-dist@5.4.394, Healthcheck succeeded\n  2959\t\n  2960\t## User preferences\n  2961\t\n  2962\t- when mobile tab text was occluded, the user asked for icons only, then clarified “they should expand as the size increses” -> use icon-only controls at narrow widths and reveal labels at a larger breakpoint. [Task 1]\n  2963\t- the user called nested bordered settings elements an anti-pattern -> avoid double-boxed sections; retain one clear boundary around actionable rows. [Task 1]\n  2964\t- when the user requested “toggle all of them at once,” then only desired providers, including custom providers -> provide bulk hide/show plus individual controls over the complete loaded provider set. [Task 1]\n  2965\t- when the user asked for “better search visuals” and “copy diagnostic failures in settings” -> expose scannable sources with progressive disclosure and individual/failures-only copy with a selectable fallback. [Task 2]\n  2966\t- when the user said “push to prod” -> deploy the scoped current changes while preserving unrelated dirty work; do not commit or delete the whole dirty checkout. [Task 3]\n  2967\t\n  2968\t## Reusable knowledge\n  2969\t\n  2970\t- In `SettingsDialog.tsx`, Panda CSS hides tab labels below `md` and shows them at `md`; preserve accessible names with `aria-label` and `title`. Remove a surrounding Storybook border when bordered rows already provide the actionable surface. Run `bun run typecheck` from `web/`, not the repository root. [Task 1]\n  2971\t- `setProvidersVisibility(providers, hidden)` in `web/src/keating/model-prefs.ts` supports bulk persistence while retaining unrelated entries; derive the deduplicated list from built-ins plus asynchronously loaded `customProviders` in `ProvidersModelsTab.tsx`. [Task 1]\n  2972\t- Codex native search sends `{ type: \"web_search\", external_web_access: true }`. Preserve URL citations from `response.output_item.done` in `web/src/keating/search/codex-search-fetch.ts`, because the SDK drops URL annotations; zstd-decompress SDK request bodies before JSON assertions. [Task 2]\n  2973\t- Explicitly declare every imported dependency: the local `node_modules` masked undeclared `pdfjs-dist`, while Railway failed until `pdfjs-dist@5.4.394` was added and locked. The corrected filtered-snapshot deployment reached `SUCCESS` and `/` healthcheck succeeded. [Task 2][Task 3]\n  2974\t\n  2975\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  2976\t\n  2977\t- Root `bun run typecheck` fails because there is no root script; use `/home/diogenes/Projects/keating/web`. Vet was unavailable without Anthropic credentials, so leave it unverified. [Task 1]\n  2978\t- Do not infer a clean production dependency graph from local builds with preexisting modules. Simulate a clean install/build before upload, then poll Railway to terminal `SUCCESS` and inspect healthcheck output. [Task 2][Task 3]\n  2979\t\n  2980\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/notorganic-provider authorization UI and Railway gateway custom-domain routing\n  2981\t\n  2982\tscope: Repair and prove the Not Organic OAuth/authorization path across Keating client, portal styling, and the public gateway; distinguish client or container health from a working public token exchange.\n  2983\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/notorganic-provider and /home/diogenes/Projects/keating; reuse_rule=recheck Railway authentication, domain attachment, DNS/TLS, exact CORS allowlist, and a fresh browser/token exchange before enabling sign-in or billing.\n  2984\t\n  2985\t## Task 1: Make Keating OAuth callback handling idempotent and Firefox-safe\n  2986\t\n  2987\t### rollout_summary_files\n  2988\t\n  2989\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/08/rollout-2026-09-08T01-03-11-01a07f66-1500-77f2-99d3-21882a4658b9.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-08T11:46:55+00:00, thread_id=01a07f66-1500-77f2-99d3-21882a4658b9, partial; client checks passed, live sign-in blocked)\n  2990\t\n  2991\t### keywords\n  2992\t\n  2993\t- OAuth, PKCE, public-client.ts, sessionStorage, NotOrganicCallback, globalThis.fetch.bind(globalThis), Firefox, receipt, exchange map, CORS\n  2994\t\n  2995\t## Task 2: Apply and prove the portal authorization styling\n  2996\t\n  2997\t### rollout_summary_files\n  2998\t\n  2999\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/08/rollout-2026-09-08T07-47-21-01a080d8-1ab0-79f0-a1af-6170040588bf.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-08T21:43:08+00:00, thread_id=01a080d8-1ab0-79f0-a1af-6170040588bf, partial; stylesheet deployed and HTTP-verified)\n  3000\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/08/rollout-2026-09-08T01-03-11-01a07f66-1500-77f2-99d3-21882a4658b9.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-08T11:46:55+00:00, thread_id=01a07f66-1500-77f2-99d3-21882a4658b9, partial; original patch was prepared only)\n  3001\t\n  3002\t### keywords\n  3003\t\n  3004\t- authorization-page.ts, authorization.css, CSP, escaped dynamic values, exact POST transaction, id.notorganic.info, authorizationStyles\n  3005\t\n  3006\t## Task 3: Diagnose the `api.notorganic.info` public-routing failure\n  3007\t\n  3008\t### rollout_summary_files\n  3009\t\n  3010\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/08/rollout-2026-09-08T07-47-21-01a080d8-1ab0-79f0-a1af-6170040588bf.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-08T21:43:08+00:00, thread_id=01a080d8-1ab0-79f0-a1af-6170040588bf, partial; generated hostname healthy, custom domain still 404)\n  3011\t\n  3012\t### keywords\n  3013\t\n  3014\t- api.notorganic.info, gateway-production-8930.up.railway.app, Application not found, /healthz, /v1/public/token, CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGINS, Railway custom domain, gateway service\n  3015\t\n  3016\t## User preferences\n  3017\t\n  3018\t- when the user supplied successive browser errors, they expected the integration to be traced and fixed end-to-end, not merely explained. [Task 1]\n  3019\t- when the authorization page was “once again unstyled” -> deploy and verify the live stylesheet, not just a local patch. [Task 2]\n  3020\t- after a claimed success still produced CORS/404, the user established that signup is working only after a real browser/token exchange succeeds. [Task 3]\n  3021\t\n  3022\t## Reusable knowledge\n  3023\t\n  3024\t- Preserve pending callback state until validation/token exchange succeeds. Validate issuer, client ID, redirect URI, state, verifier, expiry, and cancellation; make exchange idempotent per transaction and share concurrent exchanges. Store a default fetcher as `globalThis.fetch.bind(globalThis)` to avoid Firefox’s `'fetch' called on an object that does not implement interface Window.'` [Task 1]\n  3025\t- Provider consent UI must escape dynamic values, preserve the exact approve/deny POST transaction, use external `/authorization.css` under `style-src 'self'`, and have tests. Public `https://id.notorganic.info/authorization.css` returned 200 and matched local `authorizationStyles`; that proves styling, not signup. [Task 2]\n  3026\t- The gateway itself was healthy internally and through generated Railway hostname `gateway-production-8930.up.railway.app`, but `api.notorganic.info` returned Railway fallback `404 Application not found`; isolate this as custom-domain edge attachment/routing rather than browser CORS or container failure. [Task 3]\n  3027\t\n  3028\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  3029\t\n  3030\t- Passing client tests, local portal checks, internal health, valid DNS/TLS, and stylesheet deployment do not prove public signup. Re-authenticate Railway, inspect gateway custom-domain attachment/service deployment, restore routing, then verify `/healthz`, `/v1/public/token`, and CORS from `https://keating.help` in a fresh browser. [Task 1][Task 2][Task 3]\n  3031\t- A patch in `/tmp` is not an applied provider change; open the provider repository as an authorized workspace, apply it, run its tests/build, deploy, and prove the public asset. [Task 2]\n  3032\t\n  3033\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Documents/Codex/2026-09-07/realtime-voice-chat Keating learner-activity brief and static benchmark clarification\n  3034\t\n  3035\tscope: Route conceptual learner-activity/product discussion separately from implementation and from the static benchmark; use the linked worktree handbook for the actual shared-contract implementation.\n  3036\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Documents/Codex/2026-09-07/realtime-voice-chat; reuse_rule=the preferences/design distinction generalize to Keating, but implementation facts belong to the cited worktree and benchmark files were not inspected here.\n  3037\t\n  3038\t## Task 1: Specify the complete learner-activity set and game-shell boundary\n  3039\t\n  3040\t### rollout_summary_files\n  3041\t\n  3042\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Documents/Codex/2026-09-07/realtime-voice-chat, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/07/rollout-2026-09-07T15-33-18-01a07d5c-56f8-7333-a1bf-8ae4c7d898ff.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-24T07:04:04+00:00, thread_id=01a07d5c-56f8-7333-a1bf-8ae4c7d898ff, partial; implementation was resumed in another worktree)\n  3043\t\n  3044\t### keywords\n  3045\t\n  3046\t- transition learning, Representation Transfer, Spot & Repair, Build Assemble, Predict Next State, game shell, streamed OpenUI payload, learner-contracts, shared-renderer.tsx\n  3047\t\n  3048\t## Task 2: Keep static benchmark integration separate from games and components\n  3049\t\n  3050\t### rollout_summary_files\n  3051\t\n  3052\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Documents/Codex/2026-09-07/realtime-voice-chat, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/07/rollout-2026-09-07T15-33-18-01a07d5c-56f8-7333-a1bf-8ae4c7d898ff.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-24T07:04:04+00:00, thread_id=01a07d5c-56f8-7333-a1bf-8ae4c7d898ff, uncertain; no benchmark files changed)\n  3053\t\n  3054\t### keywords\n  3055\t\n  3056\t- static benchmark, benchmark page, benchmark-real.ts, shared/pedagogy, docs/study.typ, test/traces, final_dataset.json, keating.help\n  3057\t\n  3058\t## User preferences\n  3059\t\n  3060\t- “transition learning” includes equation→code, French→English, and program→mathematics -> treat representation transformation as its own activity family. [Task 1]\n  3061\t- “find the mistake,” “find the difference,” and finding N issues, optionally timed -> support diagnosis, multi-error selection, repair/explanation, and timers that are not speed-only. [Task 1]\n  3062\t- after additional activity ideas, “Let’s make all those” -> implement the complete agreed set rather than only the top few. [Task 1]\n  3063\t- “No, I'm talking about ... the static benchmark” -> acknowledge topic shifts and keep benchmark work distinct from game mechanics/component monitoring. [Task 2]\n  3064\t\n  3065\t## Reusable knowledge\n  3066\t\n  3067\t- Architect reusable game shells for movement, pacing, feedback, and score separately from bounded streamed OpenUI round payloads. The implementation guide is `/home/diogenes/.codex/worktrees/36ab/keating/docs/learner-activities.md`; consult the shared-worktree learner-activities task group for tested contract details. [Task 1]\n  3068\t- The static benchmark is a running view of system evolution/improvement, conceptually distinct from visual game shells; inspect the existing benchmark page and define presentation/integration before altering it. No benchmark-page files were verified in this rollout. [Task 2]\n  3069\t\n  3070\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  3071\t\n  3072\t- Initial delegation stalled without readable coordinator state. The successful fallback was `mcp__codex_app__send_message_to_thread` / `wait_threads` with thread `01a07d66-6098-7180-97a0-f2382279d2da`; dynamic app tools were unavailable. [Task 1]\n  3073\t- Do not claim full implementation verification: focused 318-test/build/typecheck/Storybook evidence was reported, but browser/native interaction remained unverified and broad unrelated failures were reported. [Task 1]\n  3074\t\n  3075\t# Task Group: cross-repository agent-context cleanup audit and private Sites report\n  3076\t\n  3077\tscope: Audit instruction/context cleanup with measured evidence, identify repeatable automation candidates, and publish a verified private visual report.\n  3078\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating with evidence across multiple repositories; reuse_rule=recompute aggregate counts and deployment state for a new audit; reported file-word reduction is not direct token-savings measurement.\n  3079\t\n  3080\t## Task 1: Measure cleanup and publish “Headroom — context cleanup”\n  3081\t\n  3082\t### rollout_summary_files\n  3083\t\n  3084\t- rollout_summaries/2026-09-08T03-25-44-ctrB-keating_settings_cleanup_and_context_report_site.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/07/rollout-2026-09-07T23-25-44-01a07f0c-dd35-75f0-b5c3-9ce89342b033.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-08T05:01:02+00:00, thread_id=01a07f0c-dd35-75f0-b5c3-9ce89342b033, success; private deployment succeeded)\n  3085\t\n  3086\t### keywords\n  3087\t\n  3088\t- Headroom, context cleanup, Graft, GitNexus, analyze --index-only, package-site.sh, context-cleanup-ledger, verify-site.ts, 73,638, 16,053\n  3089\t\n  3090\t## User preferences\n  3091\t\n  3092\t- when the user asked to “create a site visualizing the clean up” -> make the primary report immediately usable and interactive, distinguish verified measurements from possible future savings, and avoid a marketing-landing substitute. [Task 1]\n  3093\t\n  3094\t## Reusable knowledge\n  3095\t\n  3096\t- The applied manifest measured 50 files in 30 repositories, 73,638 words before and 16,053 after (78.2% aggregate file-word reduction). Browser verification/capture was the strongest measured repeat-work candidate: 19 reviewed snippets across 4 sessions/3 repositories, about 19,653 command-input characters. [Task 1]\n  3097\t- Use GitNexus `analyze --index-only` to avoid AGENTS/CLAUDE/skill injection and Graft structural builds without deep summaries for low-risk trials. The existing browser-verification harness is `/home/diogenes/Projects/dio.computer/scripts/verify-site.ts`. [Task 1]\n  3098\t- For Sites: validate local HTTP 200 plus production build/typecheck, initialize site-local Git, package through `package-site.sh`, save a version, deploy privately, and poll until `status: succeeded`. The report deployed to `https://context-cleanup-ledger.diothedebugger.chatgpt.site`. [Task 1]\n  3099\t\n  3100\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  3101\t\n  3102\t- Mixed Guix/Nix compiler/linker/glibc paths caused native Graft/GitNexus parser failures; isolate system compiler/linker paths or use a clean container. [Task 1]\n  3103\t- Do not submit multiple `apply_patch` operations against the same file in one patch; replace content separately, then apply CSS/layout updates. [Task 1]\n  3104\t\n  3105\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/.codex/worktrees/36ab/keating shared OpenUI learner activities\n  3106\t\n  3107\tscope: Implement or audit the canonical 12-kind learner-activity contract across OpenUI source compilation, web, mobile, TUI, durable review evidence, Storybook, and generated NodePod artifacts.\n  3108\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/.codex/worktrees/36ab/keating; reuse_rule=reuse the cross-surface contract and failure shields in another Keating checkout only after reconciling its current branch/worktree and generated files; focused verification does not prove browser, native-device, live-provider, or clean-install behavior.\n  3109\t\n  3110\t## Task 1: Shared activity contracts and OpenUI source mappings\n  3111\t\n  3112\t### rollout_summary_files\n  3113\t\n  3114\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/.codex/worktrees/36ab/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/07/rollout-2026-09-07T15-44-16-01a07d66-6098-7180-97a0-f2382279d2da.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-24T07:04:40+00:00, thread_id=01a07d66-6098-7180-97a0-f2382279d2da, success; 12 canonical activity kinds and fixture pack 6)\n  3115\t\n  3116\t### keywords\n  3117\t\n  3118\t- UiActivityNode, UiActivityResponse, submit-activity, activityResponseIsComplete, formatActivityResponse, learner-contracts, openui-source.ts, compare-defend, fixture pack 6\n  3119\t\n  3120\t## Task 2: Tactile accessible web, mobile, and TUI activity controls\n  3121\t\n  3122\t### rollout_summary_files\n  3123\t\n  3124\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/.codex/worktrees/36ab/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/07/rollout-2026-09-07T15-44-16-01a07d66-6098-7180-97a0-f2382279d2da.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-24T07:04:40+00:00, thread_id=01a07d66-6098-7180-97a0-f2382279d2da, success; focused suites and Storybook passed)\n  3125\t\n  3126\t### keywords\n  3127\t\n  3128\t- ActivityRenderer.tsx, activity.css, ActivityLearner.stories.tsx, mobile/src/components/Activity.tsx, activity-input.ts, 21 activity stories, paused timer, not scored\n  3129\t\n  3130\t## Task 3: Durable ungraded evidence, review presentation, and generated artifacts\n  3131\t\n  3132\t### rollout_summary_files\n  3133\t\n  3134\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/.codex/worktrees/36ab/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/07/rollout-2026-09-07T15-44-16-01a07d66-6098-7180-97a0-f2382279d2da.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-24T07:04:40+00:00, thread_id=01a07d66-6098-7180-97a0-f2382279d2da, success; deterministic NodePod generation and focused checks passed)\n  3135\t\n  3136\t### keywords\n  3137\t\n  3138\t- shared-actions.ts, IndexedDB, learner-response.ts, durable receipts, pending/ungraded, OpenUIPreview, nodepod-boot-files.ts, generate-nodepod-boot-files.ts, learner-activities.md\n  3139\t\n  3140\t## User preferences\n  3141\t\n  3142\t- when implementing learner activities, the brief required “canonical shared OpenUI path and shared learner-contracts, not web-only or legacy rendering” -> extend the shared contract and every consuming surface rather than create parallel UI concepts. [Task 1]\n  3143\t- the brief required timers to be optional and “never speed-only scoring” -> preserve elapsed time as descriptive evidence only; never use it for scoring, deadlines, or auto-submit. [Task 1][Task 2]\n  3144\t- the brief explicitly requested activities to be “tactile and accessible” and sensible Storybook states -> include keyboard/native controls, focus states, readable labels, narrow layouts, submitted/retry states, and inspectable stories rather than static rendering alone. [Task 2]\n  3145\t- preserve pre-existing dirty work; inspect status first and do not revert unrelated changes. Do not commit, tag, release, or deploy when the delegated implementation brief excludes them. [Task 2][Task 3]\n  3146\t- completion is not correctness or mastery -> reviews should say “judgement required,” accept defensible alternatives, and never expose transport JSON as learner-facing prose. [Task 3]\n  3147\t\n  3148\t## Reusable knowledge\n  3149\t\n  3150\t- `packages/learner-contracts/src/activity.ts` defines all 12 canonical kinds, structured responses, labels, positional fields, bounded validation, `activityResponseIsComplete`, and `formatActivityResponse`. `openui-source.ts` registers positional field order `id,title,prompt,context,items,options,targets,issueCount,requireReason,timeLimit,responseLabel`. [Task 1]\n  3151\t- Reject fresh `submit-activity` when its target node already has a response, while separately allowing durable receipt replay. `compare-defend` needs exactly two options, a selected alternative, and a reason; best explanation needs a reason; apply-in-context needs one method plus written application; build/order need a full permutation; classification is many-to-one and matching one-to-one. [Task 1]\n  3152\t- Surface implementation anchors are `web/src/keating/openui/ActivityRenderer.tsx`, `activity.css`, `library.tsx`, `ActivityLearner.stories.tsx`; `mobile/src/components/Activity.tsx`, `activity-state.ts`, `UiDocumentRenderer.tsx`, `ui-action-mutations.ts`; and `src/tui/ui/activity-input.ts`, `host-controller.ts`, `render.ts`, `rpc-action-transport.ts`. Timers can pause or disable, remain usable after expiration, and display elapsed time as not scored. [Task 2]\n  3153\t- Persist readable, ungraded activity evidence atomically in IndexedDB with action receipts through `shared-actions.ts`, `storage.ts`, and `learner-response.ts`; render activity nodes as inert preview chips in comparison/review. Individual activity text is bounded to 16,384 characters, while formatted portable question-check evidence allows `MAX_QUESTION_ANSWER_LENGTH = 524_288`. Regenerate `web/src/keating/nodepod-boot-files.ts` with `bun scripts/generate-nodepod-boot-files.ts`. [Task 3]\n  3154\t- Recorded focused evidence: shared contracts 91 pass, web 127 pass, mobile 47 pass, TUI 53 pass (318 total); Storybook static build, root build/typecheck, mobile/shared typechecks, deterministic NodePod generation, and `git diff --check` passed. [Task 1][Task 2][Task 3]\n  3155\t\n  3156\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  3157\t\n  3158\t- Answered documents initially accepted a second fresh submission -> reject a new submission against an existing response but retain idempotent receipt replay. New components initially missed web parity -> register each in the live web library and update parity fixtures together. [Task 1]\n  3159\t- TUI drafts keyed by document revision orphaned sibling activity drafts after a submission -> key by document ID plus node definition excluding the response. Mobile evidence exceeded the old question-check limit -> bound input fields separately from the persisted formatted-evidence capacity. [Task 2]\n  3160\t- Playwriter was disconnected, so browser click-through and native-device interaction are unverified. Vet was unavailable through DNS/credentials; production web build hit existing Flue `Error: spawnSync bun EPERM`; Devenv could not create `/run/user/1000/devenv-*` on the read-only filesystem. Record these as environment boundaries, not activity regressions, and keep focused results distinct from unrelated broad-suite failures. [Task 2][Task 3]\n  3161\t\n  3162\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/keating Learning to Teach report, benchmark audit, and account-owned continual-learning boundary\n  3163\t\n  3164\tscope: Improve and publish the Learning to Teach report with explainable trajectory evidence, audited public data, and an honest boundary between a proposed account-owned Tinker pilot and executed training/serving.\n  3165\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating; reuse_rule=report files and packaging workflow are reusable after rechecking current benchmark inputs and Railway state; Tinker/Not Organic integration remains an unverified feasibility direction until an authorized account, spend cap, and end-to-end run exist.\n  3166\t\n  3167\t## Task 1: Explain learner profiles and trajectories; produce a substantive report conclusion\n  3168\t\n  3169\t### rollout_summary_files\n  3170\t\n  3171\t- rollout_summaries/2026-09-07T00-00-16-dkxb-keating_learning_to_teach_report_tinker_and_railway_deployme.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/06/rollout-2026-09-06T20-00-16-01a0792a-645e-7ac0-9052-ab9fa401b691.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-07T13:39:27+00:00, thread_id=01a0792a-645e-7ac0-9052-ab9fa401b691, success; user will conduct visual review on Railway)\n  3172\t\n  3173\t### keywords\n  3174\t\n  3175\t- Learning to Teach, learner-memory.json, benchmark-trajectories.js, loadV3Data, memoryFacts, memoryChanges, trajectory walkthrough, conclusion, reduced-motion\n  3176\t\n  3177\t## Task 2: Package audited benchmark data, deploy report to Railway, and verify public assets\n  3178\t\n  3179\t### rollout_summary_files\n  3180\t\n  3181\t- rollout_summaries/2026-09-07T00-00-16-dkxb-keating_learning_to_teach_report_tinker_and_railway_deployme.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/06/rollout-2026-09-06T20-00-16-01a0792a-645e-7ac0-9052-ab9fa401b691.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-07T13:39:27+00:00, thread_id=01a0792a-645e-7ac0-9052-ab9fa401b691, success; deployment b868eb5b-8c40-434a-b7bd-2f583a928eb8)\n  3182\t\n  3183\t### keywords\n  3184\t\n  3185\t- benchmark-v3, package.py, railway-report-v17, snapshot.json, /healthz, deployment-verification.json, 184 attempts, 14 public assets, BUILDING, SUCCESS\n  3186\t\n  3187\t## Task 3: Assess account-owned Tinker continual learning and serving feasibility\n  3188\t\n  3189\t### rollout_summary_files\n  3190\t\n  3191\t- rollout_summaries/2026-09-07T00-00-16-dkxb-keating_learning_to_teach_report_tinker_and_railway_deployme.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/06/rollout-2026-09-06T20-00-16-01a0792a-645e-7ac0-9052-ab9fa401b691.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-07T13:39:27+00:00, thread_id=01a0792a-645e-7ac0-9052-ab9fa401b691, partial; architecture assessed, no end-to-end run)\n  3192\t\n  3193\t### keywords\n  3194\t\n  3195\t- Tinker, SDFT, SDPO, sampler checkpoint, training-state checkpoint, account evolution, active revision, Unsloth LoRA SFT, adapter serving, spend cap\n  3196\t\n  3197\t## User preferences\n  3198\t\n  3199\t- when a report “assumes you know what the learner's profile is,” the user requested “a visual of a long trajectory,” then a “better visual of the json” and “better transitions” -> explain unfamiliar structured data through concrete facts, evidence, source, confidence, provenance, and changes over time, not raw JSON or disconnected charts. [Task 1]\n  3200\t- when the conclusion was too short, the user said “conclusion could be way more detailed disappointed” -> substantial reports need evidence-backed synthesis, limitations, next experiment, and what success means before being called complete. [Task 1]\n  3201\t- when reviewing deployment, the user said “don’t check browser i will just update railway” and “push the latest to railway and i will check that my self” -> do not reopen a browser; leave visual review to the user and verify the deployment technically over HTTP. [Task 1][Task 2]\n  3202\t- for continual learning, the user asked for a Keating-created user and case-study data -> favor a real account-owned pilot over abstract architecture, while explicitly requesting/confirming account identity and spend authority before running it. [Task 3]\n  3203\t\n  3204\t## Reusable knowledge\n  3205\t\n  3206\t- `benchmark-trajectories.js` provides `loadV3Data`, `memoryFacts`, `memoryChanges`, `messageText`, interactive step navigation, profile-memory change labels, full-source disclosures, keyboard navigation, and reduced-motion handling. The v3.2 example separates benchmark starting context from facts learned during the run, preserving evidence, `explicit`/`observed` source, confidence semantics, and provenance. [Task 1]\n  3207\t- The report conclusion should cover training effects, benchmark revisions, harness failures, result limitations, a proposed next experiment, and human learning/retention requirements. [Task 1]\n  3208\t- Final benchmark audit: 184 attempts, 183 completed, 1 call-limit failure, 154 scored, 29 output-limited; all 184 hashes verified and runtime attestations unchanged. The 1,021 receipt-bound native calls have an uncached estimate of `$4.89493897`; unknown cache usage means that view is not an invoice. Do not aggregate semantic scores for output-limited episodes. [Task 2]\n  3209\t- Package only through `uv run --project scripts/training --locked --no-sync python scripts/report-site/package.py --output-dir .keating/outputs/railway-report-v17`; deploy the package with Railway `--path-as-root --no-gitignore --detach --json`. Verify every public asset hash against `snapshot.json`, `/healthz` is `200 ok`, and a missing JSON path returns 404. [Task 2]\n  3210\t- Keating has canonical/provenance-rich training exports and an Unsloth LoRA SFT starter, but no integrated Tinker trainer, SDPO loop, or per-user adapter-serving path. Not Organic supplies account-scoped evolution metadata, authorization, artifact/result attestation, and atomic active revisions, not a verified authorized-Tinker-checkpoint connection. Tinker's continual-learning recipe is SDFT, not SDPO; it distinguishes sampler checkpoints from resumable training state. [Task 3]\n  3211\t\n  3212\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  3213\t\n  3214\t- The initial conclusion was rejected as too brief; expand the synthesis before claiming completion. Once the user says they will inspect Railway, browser inspection is unnecessary and should not be substituted for HTTP/hash deployment verification. [Task 1][Task 2]\n  3215\t- `python -m unittest scripts/report-site/test_export_benchmark_v3.py` failed from the wrong import path. Use `python -m unittest discover -s scripts/report-site -p test_export_benchmark_v3.py`. Wait through Railway `BUILDING`/`DEPLOYING` until `SUCCESS` before reporting deployment complete. [Task 2]\n  3216\t- No end-to-end Tinker run occurred because no account/DID or spend cap was supplied and local Tinker modules were absent. Do not describe SFT/DPO/KTO/GRPO exports as executed training, or checkpoint metadata as serving integration; keep provider credentials and model bytes server-side. [Task 3]\n  3217\t\n  3218\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/notorganic-provider first-party PDS signup, ATProto identity, and Resend DNS\n  3219\t\n  3220\tscope: Operate Not Organic's own ATProto PDS signup path, retain the current did:plc decision, and provision Resend DNS without overstating live account/email readiness.\n  3221\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/notorganic-provider; reuse_rule=recheck Railway domain/TLS, Resend domain verification/SMTP, PDS configuration, and live signup in a fresh browser before calling this production-complete.\n  3222\t\n  3223\t## Task 1: Direct Not Organic PDS account signup and deployment\n  3224\t\n  3225\t### rollout_summary_files\n  3226\t\n  3227\t- rollout_summaries/2026-09-06T20-20-28-hyl9-notorganic_pds_signup_webvh_resend_dns.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/notorganic-provider, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/06/rollout-2026-09-06T16-20-28-01a07861-27f5-7df1-ab23-4e06ec4986df.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-06T22:23:21+00:00, thread_id=01a07861-27f5-7df1-ab23-4e06ec4986df, partial; deployment/internal PDS checks passed, public signup remains unproven)\n  3228\t\n  3229\t### keywords\n  3230\t\n  3231\t- ATProto, PDS, OAuth, prompt=create, /api/auth/signup, pds.notorganic.info, PDS_INVITE_REQUIRED, Railway, Litestream, notorganic-pds, SMTP, TLS\n  3232\t\n  3233\t## Task 2: WebVH architecture assessment, retain did:plc\n  3234\t\n  3235\t### rollout_summary_files\n  3236\t\n  3237\t- rollout_summaries/2026-09-06T20-20-28-hyl9-notorganic_pds_signup_webvh_resend_dns.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/notorganic-provider, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/06/rollout-2026-09-06T16-20-28-01a07861-27f5-7df1-ab23-4e06ec4986df.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-06T22:23:21+00:00, thread_id=01a07861-27f5-7df1-ab23-4e06ec4986df, success; documented assessment, no migration)\n  3238\t\n  3239\t### keywords\n  3240\t\n  3241\t- WebVH, did:plc, PLC directory, docs/webvh-assessment.md, verifiable history, witnesses, portability, ATProto compatibility\n  3242\t\n  3243\t## Task 3: Provision Resend DNS records at Porkbun\n  3244\t\n  3245\t### rollout_summary_files\n  3246\t\n  3247\t- rollout_summaries/2026-09-06T20-20-28-hyl9-notorganic_pds_signup_webvh_resend_dns.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/notorganic-provider, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/06/rollout-2026-09-06T16-20-28-01a07861-27f5-7df1-ab23-4e06ec4986df.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-06T22:23:21+00:00, thread_id=01a07861-27f5-7df1-ab23-4e06ec4986df, success; records re-read and unrelated records preserved)\n  3248\t\n  3249\t### keywords\n  3250\t\n  3251\t- Resend, Porkbun, Sesame, resend._domainkey, rsend.forge.rmta.net, send.forge.rmta.net, _dmarc, smtp.resend.com, port 465\n  3252\t\n  3253\t## Task 4: Patch and deploy same-site PDS OAuth authorization\n  3254\t\n  3255\t### rollout_summary_files\n  3256\t\n  3257\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/notorganic-provider, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/20/rollout-2026-09-20T13-54-17-01a0bff4-5931-7fe2-8285-537770cb3f69.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-20T18:56:35+00:00, thread_id=01a0bff4-5931-7fe2-8285-537770cb3f69, success; exact header regression fixed/deployed, full browser lifecycle open)\n  3258\t\n  3259\t### keywords\n  3260\t\n  3261\t- Sec-Fetch-Site, same-site, atproto-5147, patch-oauth-same-site.mjs, check-oauth-same-site.mjs, Dockerfile.pds, Forbidden sec-fetch-site header, 907d0552-a6df-4043-9df3-4227546431e3\n  3262\t\n  3263\t## User preferences\n  3264\t\n  3265\t- when discussing identity/signup, the user said Not Organic “should have its own pds” and people “should be able to create an account that way without going through bsky” -> implement and verify first-party PDS signup rather than redirecting account creation through Bluesky. [Task 1]\n  3266\t- when WebVH was raised, the user corrected that “removing reliance on plc directory is not a central requirement at all” and asked to “note webvh down sides and advantages somewhere” -> retain `did:plc` unless a concrete need changes; document tradeoffs rather than proposing a migration. [Task 2]\n  3267\t- when the user said “please just add these you have the ability” and specified “resend should be used for smtp” -> with authorization and working integrations, apply the DNS records directly, verify them, and preserve the provider decision. [Task 3]\n  3268\t- after confirming scope, the user said “deploy”; when they later asked whether it was “a mock tested,” -> confirm production scope first and clearly distinguish local/container checks from real production HTTP and unverified browser proof. [Task 4]\n  3269\t\n  3270\t## Reusable knowledge\n  3271\t\n  3272\t- `/api/auth/signup` uses an operator-configured HTTPS PDS origin and `oauth.authorize(pdsUrl.origin, { scope: \"atproto\", prompt: \"create\" })`; do not accept browser-supplied PDS or DID values. Defaults were `PDS_HOSTNAME=pds.notorganic.info`, `PDS_SERVICE_HANDLE_DOMAINS=.pds.notorganic.info`, and `PDS_INVITE_REQUIRED=false`. [Task 1]\n  3273\t- PDS/portal/landing deployments succeeded; internal PDS checks returned health 200, version `0.4.219`, `inviteCodeRequired:false`, hosted handle domain, and OAuth metadata. The private Railway bucket `notorganic-pds` passed empty-object PUT/GET/DELETE `200/200/204`; Litestream uploaded an initial SQLite snapshot. [Task 1]\n  3274\t- `docs/webvh-assessment.md` records verifiable history, key rotation, optional witnesses, portability, hosting model, ATProto incompatibility, DID-string changes on portability, operational overhead, and lack of account/recovery semantics. Current decision: retain `did:plc`; reconsider only for a concrete organizational/service identity need or future ecosystem support. [Task 2]\n  3275\t- For Porkbun via Sesame, list records at exact target names, detect conflicts, apply only intended changes, then re-list and compare while preserving existing IDs. The verified TTL-600 records were TXT `resend._domainkey`, CNAME `rsend` -> `rsend.forge.rmta.net`, CNAME `send` -> `send.forge.rmta.net`, and TXT `_dmarc` -> `v=DMARC1; p=none;`. Resend SMTP is `smtp.resend.com`, port 465 implicit TLS, username `resend`, API key as password, after sending-domain verification. [Task 3]\n  3276\t- Live PDS `0.4.219` rejected `Sec-Fetch-Site: same-site` at `/oauth/authorize`. `infra/pds/patch-oauth-same-site.mjs`, wired by `infra/docker/Dockerfile.pds`, asserts OAuth provider version/source shape and narrowly backports atproto PR #5147. The local original image fails the same-site test; patched container passed nine checks, and Railway deployment retained `/pds` volume. Remove the patch when upgrading to a PDS release containing the upstream fix. [Task 4]\n  3277\t\n  3278\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  3279\t\n  3280\t- Passing focused tests/builds and internal PDS checks do not prove live signup: require public DNS/TLS, Resend domain verification, SMTP delivery, and a fresh-browser registration before declaring account creation complete. Railway certificates were still `ISSUING`/`VALIDATING_OWNERSHIP` and public HTTPS had certificate-name errors during this rollout. [Task 1]\n  3281\t- No Resend key was found in Skate. Do not retrieve or reuse another project's production credential without explicit cross-project authorization. [Task 1]\n  3282\t- DNS record success does not prove Resend domain verification or SMTP delivery. CNAMEs cannot coexist with other records at the same name, so abort on conflicts rather than overwriting them. [Task 3]\n  3283\t- Browser `fetch` overwrites `Sec-Fetch-Mode` as `cors`; use raw Node HTTP to reproduce navigation Fetch Metadata headers. Health/header/invalid-case checks and fresh signup authorization-page load prove the narrow same-site fix, not consent, email verification, cookies, callback/PKCE, token exchange, or an authenticated app session. [Task 4]\n  3284\t\n  3285\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/keating product-promise and educational-efficacy assessment\n  3286\tscope: Conduct candid, outcome-oriented assessment of Keating against its hyperteacher promise without mistaking implementation breadth, dirty work, or deterministic benchmarks for validated learner outcomes.\n  3287\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating; reuse_rule=re-read current PRODUCT.md, SYSTEM.md, study limitations, worktree state, and complete browser/test evidence before issuing any rating; this assessment was not completed.\n  3288\t\n  3289\t## Task 1: Rate Keating against its product promise, incomplete\n  3290\t\n  3291\t### rollout_summary_files\n  3292\t\n  3293\t- rollout_summaries/2026-09-06T10-49-02-OJTS-keating_application_goal_assessment_incomplete.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/06/rollout-2026-09-06T06-49-02-01a07655-ffbe-75a0-80e8-b2f9f2ec7edc.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-07T00:30:16+00:00, thread_id=01a07655-ffbe-75a0-80e8-b2f9f2ec7edc, partial; no final rating or synthesized conclusion)\n  3294\t\n  3295\t### keywords\n  3296\t\n  3297\t- Keating, PRODUCT.md, SYSTEM.md, hyperteacher, cognitive empowerment, educational efficacy, human participants, benchmark, Playwriter, unable to open database file\n  3298\t\n  3299\t## User preferences\n  3300\t\n  3301\t- when asking to “rate how good this current application is at accomplishing its goals and promise,” the user seeks a candid, outcome-oriented assessment rather than a feature inventory or purely aesthetic review. [Task 1]\n  3302\t\n  3303\t## Reusable knowledge\n  3304\t\n  3305\t- `PRODUCT.md` defines Keating’s purpose as a hyperteacher that helps learners configure a model, start useful tutoring, understand changes, and trust local-first privacy and self-improvement boundaries. `SYSTEM.md` requires learner authorship through diagnosis, questioning, reconstruction, retrieval, verification, and learner-created artifacts; AI must not become a surrogate for thought. [Task 1]\n  3306\t- Separate broad implemented capability from educational efficacy. `docs/study/sections/limitations.typ` says no human participants were studied; archived learners are language models in student roles, and deterministic benchmark behavior is not evidence of human mastery, retention, engagement, transfer, or confusion. [Task 1]\n  3307\t- The assessed checkout was heavily dirty with active OpenUI, learner-response, courses, submissions, simulation, and renderer work. Distinguish committed baseline behavior from work in progress. [Task 1]\n  3308\t\n  3309\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  3310\t\n  3311\t- This rollout never reached a final rating, strengths/gaps synthesis, or complete test conclusion. Treat it as incomplete evidence; restart from the stated product criteria and finish the evidence table before giving a score. [Task 1]\n  3312\t- Browser learner-flow evidence was unavailable: Playwriter reported `The Playwriter Chrome extension is not connected` after CLI/temporary-directory failures. Do not imply visual validation. [Task 1]\n  3313\t- `devenv tasks run keating:test keating:test-web` was blocked by `unable to open database file` and Nix daemon `Operation not permitted`; report infrastructure blockage separately from application failure, then rerun with suitable access or narrower direct commands. [Task 1]\n  3314\t\n  3315\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/keating Bun-native v3.11.0 release publication\n  3316\t\n  3317\tscope: Release Keating with Bun-native versioning, preserve a confirmed content boundary, and distinguish publication from registry propagation.\n  3318\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating; reuse_rule=release/registry/provider/browser facts are time-specific; inspect current branch, workflow, tag, and artifacts before action.\n  3319\t\n  3320\t## Task 1: Review, publish, and verify Keating 3.11.0\n  3321\t\n  3322\t### rollout_summary_files\n  3323\t\n  3324\t- rollout_summaries/2026-09-05T09-46-39-tkNY-keating_3_11_0_release_bun_versioning.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/05/rollout-2026-09-05T05-46-39-01a070f6-84ec-78e0-af81-0b5adf3e5652.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-05T10:25:31+00:00, thread_id=01a070f6-84ec-78e0-af81-0b5adf3e5652, partial; GitHub release verified, npm processing)\n  3325\t\n  3326\t### keywords\n  3327\t\n  3328\t- bun pm version, sync-version.ts, v3.11.0, Prek, Entire wrapper, nodepod-boot-files.ts, npm provenance, 33959745612\n  3329\t\n  3330\t## User preferences\n  3331\t\n  3332\t- “yes include the uncommited changes” -> include a complete dirty worktree only after explicit scope confirmation; never silently reduce it to committed content. [Task 1]\n  3333\t- “hey instead of bumpy you should use bun pm version” -> Keating releases use Bun-native versioning, not Bumpy, unless explicitly overridden. [Task 1]\n  3334\t\n  3335\t## Reusable knowledge\n  3336\t\n  3337\t- Use `bun pm version <increment> --no-git-tag-version`, `scripts/sync-version.ts`, changelog edits/checks, explicit annotated tag and push. The Devenv task is `keating:bump-version`; regenerate generated NodePod artifacts after source-integration conflicts instead of hand-merging output. [Task 1]\n  3338\t- v3.11.0 GitHub workflow `33959745612` and four Darwin/Linux assets were verified; its downloaded Linux x64 bundle ran independently and matched published digest. [Task 1]\n  3339\t\n  3340\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  3341\t\n  3342\t- An accepted npm publish is not registry availability: v3.11.0 was still processing and registry metadata remained v3.10.2 at final check. Browser/provider/physical-device/full Vet evidence remained unavailable. [Task 1]\n  3343\t\n  3344\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/keating Flue worktree, NodePod boundary, and platform-aware downloads\n  3345\t\n  3346\tscope: Locate the isolated Flue prototype, state the exact NodePod proof boundary, or update Keating’s downloads showcase and direct release links.\n  3347\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating and sibling /home/diogenes/Projects/keating-flue-runtime; reuse_rule=worktree/branch facts require a live git-worktree check; v3.11.0 artifact availability is time-specific.\n  3348\t\n  3349\t## Task 1: Locate and assess the Flue worktree and real-NodePod proof\n  3350\t\n  3351\t### rollout_summary_files\n  3352\t\n  3353\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/06/rollout-2026-09-06T09-18-04-01a076de-6f27-7e91-994f-59f477efae8a.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-06T13:34:53+00:00, thread_id=01a076de-6f27-7e91-994f-59f477efae8a, partial proof boundary)\n  3354\t\n  3355\t### keywords\n  3356\t\n  3357\t- keating-flue-runtime, spike/flue-runtime, git worktree list, @flue/runtime, NodePod, sandbox-adapter.ts, flue-host, proof.txt\n  3358\t\n  3359\t## Task 2: Redesign Downloads with real app captures and platform-specific artifacts\n  3360\t\n  3361\t### rollout_summary_files\n  3362\t\n  3363\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/06/rollout-2026-09-06T08-03-56-01a0769a-914d-7531-b321-a4f223dd58f3.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-06T12:50:34+00:00, thread_id=01a0769a-914d-7531-b321-a4f223dd58f3, partial; test typing unresolved)\n  3364\t\n  3365\t### keywords\n  3366\t\n  3367\t- Download.tsx, detect-platform.ts, TutorialShot.tsx, react-icons, v3.11.0, darwin-arm64, linux-x64, gh api, Cache miss\n  3368\t\n  3369\t## User preferences\n  3370\t\n  3371\t- when repository evidence conflicted with their expectation, the user said “but there should be a worktree that does can you look in the dir above” -> inspect sibling worktrees/repositories before concluding a feature is absent. [Task 1]\n  3372\t- when discussing product downloads, the user asked for “actual shots of a phone with the app in a spread that makes sense” and that images be replaceable later -> use real product captures in a coherent sequence, isolate screenshot paths, and keep frame sizing stable. [Task 2]\n  3373\t- “detect the platform and give the user the file to download use icons for each platform” -> make the primary CTA platform-aware/direct when an artifact exists, retain all choices, and use real icon-library logos. [Task 2]\n  3374\t\n  3375\t## Reusable knowledge\n  3376\t\n  3377\t- Main Keating v3.11.0 has no `flue`/`@flue/*` dependency; `/home/diogenes/Projects/keating-flue-runtime` is sibling worktree `spike/flue-runtime`, an older-base prototype. `spikes/flue-host` is a real Node Flue host; `spikes/flue-browser` consumes hosted conversations but cannot run `@flue/runtime`; portable `packages/agent-runtime` intentionally does not execute turns. [Task 1]\n  3378\t- NodePod is the sandbox layer, Flue the orchestration layer. The decisive proof starts a real NodePod, runs built host with the production adapter, creates/reads `/workspace/proof.txt`, checks both reply and pod filesystem, then disposes it; add isolation, cancellation, capability, credential, restart, and provider tests. [Task 1]\n  3379\t- `web/src/lib/detect-platform.ts` is SSR-safe, uses `userAgentData` with iPadOS touch-point handling; `TutorialShot.tsx` is the replacement-friendly image-frame pattern. Verify current releases with `gh api` plus direct artifact `HEAD` rather than relying on a cached public release page. [Task 2]\n  3380\t\n  3381\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  3382\t\n  3383\t- Do not claim “Keating runs its Flue agent in NodePod”: existing normal-Node host proof plus adapter contract only support “NodePod-to-Flue adapter and working Flue host spike.” [Task 1]\n  3384\t- v3.11.0 had macOS/Linux archives only; no Windows installer, Android APK, or iOS download was verified. Fix `download-release.test.ts` fixtures (`unknown` before `Navigator`, `DetectedPlatform` expected values) and rerun tests/typecheck before claiming page completion. [Task 2]\n  3385\t\n  3386\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/keating game-like learner activities and shared OpenUI rendering\n  3387\t\n  3388\tscope: Redesign quizzes, flashcards, language/activity rounds, and their shared learner-facing renderer without breaking durable learning behavior.\n  3389\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating; reuse_rule=use for learner-activity UI work; preserve the heavily dirty worktree and separately verify live browser behavior.\n  3390\t\n  3391\t## Task 1: Flashcard and quiz minigame styling with a prominent urgency timer\n  3392\t\n  3393\t### rollout_summary_files\n  3394\t\n  3395\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/06/rollout-2026-09-06T04-37-01-01a075dd-21ab-7b10-a78d-5dfeadb38633.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-06T10:09:03+00:00, thread_id=01a075dd-21ab-7b10-a78d-5dfeadb38633, partial; deterministic/Storybook build evidence only)\n  3396\t\n  3397\t### keywords\n  3398\t\n  3399\t- FlashcardRenderer, QuizRenderer, QuizSessionPanel, FlashcardShaderField, quizTimerState, keating:quiz-shader-preset, quiz-game.test.ts, PandaCSS, reduced-motion\n  3400\t\n  3401\t## Task 2: Shared activity renderer, learner interactions, and simulation evidence boundary\n  3402\t\n  3403\t### rollout_summary_files\n  3404\t\n  3405\t- rollout_summaries/2026-09-06T09-59-01-YxOq-keating_learning_ui_session_library_redesign.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/06/rollout-2026-09-06T05-59-01-01a07628-3290-74d1-947d-9cb9c6253bda.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-06T12:33:56+00:00, thread_id=01a07628-3290-74d1-947d-9cb9c6253bda, partial; full web/root suites pass, production browser incomplete)\n  3406\t\n  3407\t### keywords\n  3408\t\n  3409\t- shared-renderer.tsx, retryableAggregateAttempt, RenderingSmoke, QuestionRenderer, LanguagePractice, ActivityRounds.stories.tsx, rendering-smoke, SimulationRenderer, simulation-chart.test.tsx\n  3410\t\n  3411\t## User preferences\n  3412\t\n  3413\t- when redesigning learner interaction, the user asked for “really good styling,” “a variety of animations,” and “preset shaders that would make it pop and be fun to play” -> use polished state feedback, purposeful motion, and selectable visual atmospheres, not merely functional styling. [Task 1]\n  3414\t- “i think the timer should be more prominent to give a sense of urgency” -> make time a primary instrument: large digits, progress rail, warning/critical states, and accessible status messaging. [Task 1]\n  3415\t- quizzes and flashcards should “feel like games,” with “less overall text,” “jolts movement,” “dynamism,” and excitement -> prefer compact, tactile, action-driven flows over form-heavy layouts. [Task 2]\n  3416\t\n  3417\t## Reusable knowledge\n  3418\t\n  3419\t- `FlashcardRenderer.tsx` already owns SRS review, flip/swipe/keyboard interaction, bookmarks, sounds, completion effects, and persistence; extend it rather than building a parallel reviewer. `useCardGestures.ts` maps left/down/right/up to Again/Hard/Good/Easy. [Task 1]\n  3420\t- `QuizSessionPanel` delegates active behavior to canonical `QuizRenderer`; do not restore separate timing/scoring logic. `quizTimerState` clamps values, warns in the final quarter (maximum 20 seconds), becomes critical at 5 seconds or less, and the shader preference key is `keating:quiz-shader-preset`. [Task 1]\n  3421\t- `web/src/keating/openui/shared-renderer.tsx` is the cross-surface activity path for question, question-group, quiz, deck, simulation, and task nodes; legacy-renderer-only changes do not reach all learner activities. Aggregate host actions should use `retryableAggregateAttempt` so failed delivery retains byte-identical retry intent. [Task 2]\n  3422\t- Open-ended answers remain pending teacher grading and must not enter settled score. `/rendering-smoke` uses isolated local journals, so it is safe for rendering smoke checks without learner-session writes. [Task 2]\n  3423\t- Final recorded deterministic evidence: targeted quiz/flashcard/open-ended tests 35/0 and Storybook build passed in Task 1; later full web suite 1284/0 and root suite 425/0 passed in Task 2. [Task 1][Task 2]\n  3424\t\n  3425\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  3426\t\n  3427\t- Passing typecheck, focused tests, or Storybook build does not establish live visual quality, timer smoothness, mobile layout, or click-through. The rollout was interrupted before final browser inspection; keep that boundary explicit. [Task 1]\n  3428\t- Large replacements can leave duplicate component code/display names; inspect boundaries with `rg` immediately after bulk edits. Use `rg` rather than malformed directory-as-file `grep`. [Task 1]\n  3429\t- Long-running Playwriter/CDP interactions timed out, and Storybook had parse/index errors in existing stories. Treat earlier focused browser checks as scoped; run a clean Storybook index/build and actual production scenario before a broad health claim. Simulation graph completion remains unverified until the delegated patch, chart tests, and rendered scenario are inspected. [Task 2]\n  3430\t\n  3431\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/keating OpenUI task contracts, review presentation, and local-first course submissions\n  3432\t\n  3433\tscope: Extend OpenUI safely across review, quiz recovery, declarative task/simulation contracts, course integration, and offline learner submission delivery.\n  3434\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating; reuse_rule=use for OpenUI/course submission changes; contract changes require cross-surface compilation, and final local-first edits require fresh verification.\n  3435\t\n  3436\t## Task 1: Inert OpenUI previews and partial/recoverable quiz presentation\n  3437\t\n  3438\t### rollout_summary_files\n  3439\t\n  3440\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/06/rollout-2026-09-06T05-41-36-01a07618-40fd-7e92-bdb6-7dfb2dd7a5aa.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-06T10:06:03+00:00, thread_id=01a07618-40fd-7e92-bdb6-7dfb2dd7a5aa, mixed success/partial; final local-first state unverified)\n  3441\t\n  3442\t### keywords\n  3443\t\n  3444\t- OpenUIPreview, parseOpenUIMessageSegments, ResponseComparisonPanel, TrajectoryCanvas, quiz-progress.ts, complete-quiz, shared-renderer.tsx, unsafe, regeneration\n  3445\t\n  3446\t## Task 2: Four task kinds, declarative simulation, and two-way course assignment integration\n  3447\t\n  3448\t### rollout_summary_files\n  3449\t\n  3450\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/06/rollout-2026-09-06T05-41-36-01a07618-40fd-7e92-bdb6-7dfb2dd7a5aa.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-06T10:06:03+00:00, thread_id=01a07618-40fd-7e92-bdb6-7dfb2dd7a5aa, partial)\n  3451\t\n  3452\t### keywords\n  3453\t\n  3454\t- task node, Assignment, Practice, Draft, Fieldwork, complete-task-item, submit-task, learner-contracts, task-assignments.ts, SaveTaskToCourse, src/tui/ui/render.ts\n  3455\t\n  3456\t## Task 3: Local-first attachments and asynchronous course submission delivery\n  3457\t\n  3458\t### rollout_summary_files\n  3459\t\n  3460\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/06/rollout-2026-09-06T05-41-36-01a07618-40fd-7e92-bdb6-7dfb2dd7a5aa.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-06T10:06:03+00:00, thread_id=01a07618-40fd-7e92-bdb6-7dfb2dd7a5aa, uncertain; no final checks)\n  3461\t\n  3462\t### keywords\n  3463\t\n  3464\t- local-store.ts, course-outbox.ts, IndexedDB, SubmissionAttachments, SubmissionDeliveryStatus, Saved on this device, Delivered to course, submission-attachments, immutable revisions\n  3465\t\n  3466\t## User preferences\n  3467\t\n  3468\t- the user selected “Inert preview + chip” -> comparison/review should preserve prose but collapse OpenUI artifacts and never wire interactive state/actions. [Task 1]\n  3469\t- for malformed components, the user wanted “partial results for quizzes and stuff to have a nicer render then just text,” auto-retry up to three attempts, and “Score + status, answers hidden” -> show structured status, cap safe regeneration, and avoid answer-key disclosure. [Task 1]\n  3470\t- the user chose Assignment, Practice set, Draft with revisions, Fieldwork/investigation, and “Both directions” -> task-to-course saving and existing-course-to-task rendering are both required. [Task 2]\n  3471\t- when the server-first design was challenged with “do you know why this can't just be local first?” -> save answer, metadata, and file blobs immediately; show “Saved on this device” separately from “Delivered to course.” [Task 3]\n  3472\t- “just get straight to implemetnation and i will verify don't even write tests for now” and “skip vet” -> for this requested OpenUI implementation mode, do not add tests or run Vet unless asked; hand off concisely and preserve the verification boundary. [Task 1][Task 3]\n  3473\t\n  3474\t## Reusable knowledge\n  3475\t\n  3476\t- Live OpenUI is unsuitable for response comparison: it can mount controls, persist state, or dispatch actions. `preview.ts`/`OpenUIPreview.tsx` parse source/JSON fences in document order; use distinct side scopes and preserve/rebase review offsets. [Task 1]\n  3477\t- `complete-quiz` can be canonical without `params.interaction`; response summaries must branch on action type. Auto-retry malformed/unsupported component failures, but never retry `unsafe` failures. [Task 1]\n  3478\t- OpenUI simulation evaluators must be declarative, bounded, deterministic, and fail closed: no arbitrary JS, calls, property access, or generated HTML execution. [Task 2]\n  3479\t- Contract additions touch learner-contracts UI/source/rendering, parity fixtures, web/mobile/TUI renderers, action mutation/storage, and generated NodePod boot files. Extend existing course authoring/submission/review infrastructure rather than parallel course concepts. [Task 2]\n  3480\t- IndexedDB in `local-store.ts` is immediate submission truth. `course-outbox.ts` queues immutable revisions with predecessor ordering, account checks, attachment upload during sync, retries, and conflict preservation; server attachment storage is sync destination only. Limits are 10 files and 25 MB each. [Task 3]\n  3481\t\n  3482\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  3483\t\n  3484\t- Parser fixtures initially had closing-fence/cursor offset and positional-argument errors: use parser output and exact mapper signatures. Contract expansion broke parity fixtures and TUI exhaustive rendering: update expected node lists and compile every consumer. [Task 1][Task 2]\n  3485\t- Final recovery and local-first changes were not typechecked/tested. Preserve the pre-existing dirty worktree, inspect `git status`, and run focused checks before calling them complete. [Task 1][Task 3]\n  3486\t\n  3487\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/keating mobile session library and session-switch performance\n  3488\t\n  3489\tscope: Design a responsive session browser with hierarchy/filtering and harden session switching without claiming speed gains that were not measured.\n  3490\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating; reuse_rule=use for session-library/mobile selector work; remeasure performance after current changes.\n  3491\t\n  3492\t## Task 1: Rebuild mobile and desktop session library with fork/category navigation\n  3493\t\n  3494\t### rollout_summary_files\n  3495\t\n  3496\t- rollout_summaries/2026-09-06T09-59-01-YxOq-keating_learning_ui_session_library_redesign.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/06/rollout-2026-09-06T05-59-01-01a07628-3290-74d1-947d-9cb9c6253bda.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-06T12:33:56+00:00, thread_id=01a07628-3290-74d1-947d-9cb9c6253bda, partial; web/root suites pass, final build blocked elsewhere)\n  3497\t\n  3498\t### keywords\n  3499\t\n  3500\t- SessionBrowser, SessionBrowserDesktop, SessionBrowserSheet, SESSION_BROWSER_BREAKPOINT, SessionCard, Select.tsx, session-switch.ts, session-library-refresh.ts, 320px, 109.4ms, 147.6ms\n  3501\t\n  3502\t## User preferences\n  3503\t\n  3504\t- the mobile session list needed redesign “from scratch,” elegantly representing sessions, forks, categories, descriptions, and future tag/category navigation -> hierarchy, metadata, filtering, and mobile ergonomics are core requirements. [Task 1]\n  3505\t\n  3506\t## Reusable knowledge\n  3507\t\n  3508\t- `SESSION_BROWSER_BREAKPOINT = 1024`: desktop uses `SessionBrowserDesktop`, mobile uses `SessionBrowserSheet`. Filters live inside the mobile dialog; shared `Select` replaces native selects and needs dialog-safe positioning, keyboard support, long-menu scrolling, and label truncation. [Task 1]\n  3509\t- `session-switch.ts` provides latest-request protection, save-before-commit sequencing, and ordered per-session writes; `session-library-refresh.ts` coalesces storage-notification bursts and only publishes the freshest read. [Task 1]\n  3510\t- Browser checks at 320px found no dropdown overflow, correct category filtering/fork tree, and focus return to trigger on Escape. [Task 1]\n  3511\t\n  3512\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  3513\t\n  3514\t- Do not say switching is faster: baseline median was 109.4ms, first post-change measure was 147.6ms, and no post-memoization comparison was captured. [Task 1]\n  3515\t- Repository-wide build remained blocked by unrelated root TypeScript nullability errors in benchmark-evolution code; distinguish that from the passing web/root test suites. [Task 1]\n  3516\t\n  3517\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/keating landing-page code review and accessibility maintenance\n  3518\t\n  3519\tscope: Diagnose and prioritize Keating landing defects in install copy, hero motion, semantic accessibility, navigation, and orphaned code/styles.\n  3520\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating; reuse_rule=review findings are checkout-specific; inspect current code and perform a browser pass before closing fixes.\n  3521\t\n  3522\t## Task 1: Review landing implementation and reproduce user-facing install failure\n  3523\t\n  3524\t### rollout_summary_files\n  3525\t\n  3526\t- rollout_summaries/2026-09-06T09-41-36-Wvsi-landing_page_code_review_findings.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/06/rollout-2026-09-06T05-41-36-01a07618-40ca-73a1-b131-11cb0c47dd56.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-06T07:51:30+00:00, thread_id=01a07618-40ca-73a1-b131-11cb0c47dd56, success; review only)\n  3527\t\n  3528\t### keywords\n  3529\t\n  3530\t- Landing.tsx, LandingWonder.tsx, TAB_COPY_TEXT, navigator.clipboard, bash: line 1: $: command not found, requestAnimationFrame, resetDepth, CrtPlaythrough, scroll-margin-top, crt-program, Panda CSS\n  3531\t\n  3532\t## Reusable knowledge\n  3533\t\n  3534\t- Landing entry is `web/src/pages/Landing.tsx`; hero interaction is `web/src/components/LandingWonder.tsx`; sticky nav is `src/components/Nav.tsx`; landing CSS is generated from `panda.config.ts`. `bun run typecheck` passed after Panda generation. [Task 1]\n  3535\t- Keep executable clipboard payload separate from formatted terminal display text. Guard missing/rejected `navigator.clipboard` and do not make analytics depend solely on a successful copy. [Task 1]\n  3536\t- `resetDepth` must cancel pending `requestAnimationFrame` before clearing CSS variables. Use a real visually-hidden alternative for hero text, headings for use-card titles, visible/touch pause-status controls for `CrtPlaythrough`, and `scroll-margin-top` for sticky-nav anchors. [Task 1]\n  3537\t- `TerminalDemo`, `TERM_LINES`, `lineSpeed`, `INSTALL_TABS[].isAgent`, and associated terminal styles were unused; `crt-program-*`, `manifesto-grid`, and `manifesto-quote` styles were orphaned. Audit before deleting because missing CRT controls may indicate an incomplete replacement. [Task 1]\n  3538\t\n  3539\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  3540\t\n  3541\t- The reproduced copied display command failed with `bash: line 1: $: command not found`; never copy decorative prompts/comments as executable shell input. [Task 1]\n  3542\t- Static review/typecheck is not interaction proof: test the CRT carousel, sticky anchors, lazy hero, clipboard fallback, and reduced-motion behavior in a browser. [Task 1]\n  3543\t\n  3544\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/interleave-app product surfaces, effects, Storybook, and Railway snapshot deployment\n  3545\t\n  3546\tscope: Marketing/product-spread work, shared UI effects, Storybook routing, and the dedicated Railway web snapshot.\n  3547\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/interleave-app; reuse_rule=inspect the dirty `feat/storybook-coverage` worktree and live Railway/trusted-origin state before reuse.\n  3548\t\n  3549\t## Task 1: Product spreads, generated About asset, and Events runtime restoration\n  3550\t\n  3551\t### rollout_summary_files\n  3552\t\n  3553\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/interleave-app, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/04/rollout-2026-09-04T20-26-19-01a06ef5-8656-7032-8e06-1f6bf398b1cf.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-05T05:07:56+00:00, thread_id=01a06ef5-8656-7032-8e06-1f6bf398b1cf, mixed partial/success)\n  3554\t\n  3555\t### keywords\n  3556\t\n  3557\t- Landing.tsx, landing.stories.tsx, WovenDashboard, storybook:build, loom-photoreal-v2.webp, eventsAtproto.ts, Convex functions ready\n  3558\t\n  3559\t## Task 2: Recover Claude interaction effects and deploy the Railway snapshot\n  3560\t\n  3561\t### rollout_summary_files\n  3562\t\n  3563\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/interleave-app, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/05/rollout-2026-09-05T05-04-26-01a070cf-df3e-7133-924c-837b7a82c9b8.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-05T10:48:04+00:00, thread_id=01a070cf-df3e-7133-924c-837b7a82c9b8, partial; deployment health verified)\n  3564\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/interleave-app, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/06/rollout-2026-09-06T05-41-36-01a07618-40cf-71b0-9419-13ddb45523c1.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-05T08:05:01+00:00, thread_id=01a07618-40cf-71b0-9419-13ddb45523c1, rate-limited)\n  3565\t\n  3566\t### keywords\n  3567\t\n  3568\t- Claude Code, session limit, HTTP 429, surface-shader, Ripple, ChangeFlash, NavIndicator, RAILPACK_START_CMD, healthz, Access-Control-Allow-Origin\n  3569\t\n  3570\t## User preferences\n  3571\t\n  3572\t- for landing work, “take screenshots of various parts of the application” and “create product spreads” -> use authentic application workflows rather than generic marketing cards; “components are in storybook to test as well” means realistic inspectable stories. [Task 1]\n  3573\t- “add texture and juice with generated assets” -> tactile generated material is welcome when product readability survives. [Task 1]\n  3574\t- the user said “check the entire session,” continue “the one done by claude last session,” then “just get straight to it” and “use the claude subagents yourself don't use crush” -> inspect history/worktree once, then implement directly with Claude workers; Codex may generate assets. [Task 2]\n  3575\t\n  3576\t## Reusable knowledge\n  3577\t\n  3578\t- Storybook discovers `apps/web/src/**/*.stories.@(ts|tsx)` through `packages/ui/.storybook/main.ts`; use `bun run storybook`/`storybook:build` or `devenv up web storybook`. New UI components need package export-map entries and `packages/ui/src/index.ts` exports. [Task 1][Task 2]\n  3579\t- Landing implementation/captures are not evidenced, but the About asset is `apps/web/public/brand/about/loom-photoreal-v2.webp`; Events restoration returned `0 groups, 0 events, 7 lexicons`, fixed five `eventsAtproto` queries, and passed 5 tests/22 assertions. [Task 1]\n  3580\t- Deployment `a9f7b958-16af-4a42-aee8-62820c287200` used `bun run prepare:railway`, `RAILPACK_BUILD_CMD=bun run build:railway`, `RAILPACK_START_CMD=bun run start:railway`, and `/healthz`; SSR/assets/routes/locales/mobile checks passed. [Task 2]\n  3581\t\n  3582\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  3583\t\n  3584\t- CDP failures (`Failed to start CDP relay server within 5031ms`, `No connected browsers detected`) mean no visual-QA claim. Agent 429 status is not proof of missing files: inspect the worktree, but do not call exports/stories/repo checks complete. [Task 1][Task 2]\n  3585\t- Railway-hostname authentication remains blocked because `api.interleave.love` omitted `Access-Control-Allow-Origin`; update trusted origins or move canonical domain before claiming sign-in works. Separate pre-existing Storybook/typecheck diagnostics from new effects. [Task 2]\n  3586\t\n  3587\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/interleave-app release/Radicle lifecycle and settings-led Weave memory\n  3588\t\n  3589\tscope: Native Devenv release mirror/hook design and privacy-controlled long-term memory injection.\n  3590\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/interleave-app; reuse_rule=checkout is dirty and release remains unverified; validate generated API and current consent behavior first.\n  3591\t\n  3592\t## Task 1: Native Devenv main-push private Radicle mirror and blocked release\n  3593\t\n  3594\t### rollout_summary_files\n  3595\t\n  3596\t- rollout_summaries/2026-09-05T22-38-05-esl2-interleave_release_native_devenv_radicle_hook.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/interleave-app, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/05/rollout-2026-09-05T18-38-05-01a073b8-c9d7-7782-b923-1ac78450ec78.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-05T23:54:18+00:00, thread_id=01a073b8-c9d7-7782-b923-1ac78450ec78, partial)\n  3597\t\n  3598\t### keywords\n  3599\t\n  3600\t- git-hooks.nix, interleave-private-radicle, mirror-radicle-main.ts, rad inspect --visibility, interleave:check, convex codegen, .githooks\n  3601\t\n  3602\t## Task 2: Settings-led shared Weave memory and saved-reply injection\n  3603\t\n  3604\t### rollout_summary_files\n  3605\t\n  3606\t- rollout_summaries/2026-09-06T00-08-32-j0vp-interleave_settings_led_weave_memory_sharing.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/interleave-app, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/05/rollout-2026-09-05T20-08-32-01a0740b-9853-7f02-b21d-1b6e5cbf5e93.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-06T00:43:42+00:00, thread_id=01a0740b-9853-7f02-b21d-1b6e5cbf5e93, partial; focused checks pass)\n  3607\t\n  3608\t### keywords\n  3609\t\n  3610\t- weave-memory:v1, AppSettings.tsx, memorySystem.ts, conversationReplies.ts, getMemoryContextForConversation, userConsents, 8000 characters\n  3611\t\n  3612\t## User preferences\n  3613\t\n  3614\t- “use the devenv githooks feature pls not .githooks” -> use `git-hooks.nix` declarations in `devenv.nix`, never a tracked custom `.githooks` solution. [Task 1]\n  3615\t- “but that would be in settings rather than up front” -> consent/privacy controls belong in Settings without interrupting shared-chat start; preserve global default, partner overrides, and individual approval model. [Task 2]\n  3616\t\n  3617\t## Reusable knowledge\n  3618\t\n  3619\t- `mirror-radicle-main.ts` skips non-main, requires `rad` remote/private visibility, and performs the internal mirror without recursive hooks. Private Radicle repos must not use `rad publish`; a different repository RID is never reusable. [Task 1]\n  3620\t- Memory refresh runs every six hours, flush every three minutes, and stale reset hourly. `getMemoryContextForConversation` injects bounded reference data, never instructions/verbatim memory; shared context only applies to eligible Weave matches and non-Weave shared chat stays isolated. [Task 2]\n  3621\t\n  3622\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  3623\t\n  3624\t- Release is blocked: use native hook declarations, but do not tag/publish while `interleave:check` has unresolved stale API/type errors. Codegen alone cannot repair UI references to absent namespaces. [Task 1]\n  3625\t- Security/format/lint/diff checks passed, but project `tsc` still had 68 unrelated errors and there was no authenticated live-Weave/browser proof; report that boundary. [Task 2]\n  3626\t\n  3627\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/notorganic-provider public landing, portal/emails, release scope, and private Radicle\n  3628\t\n  3629\tscope: Not Organic public/company surfaces, branded portal and email package, Railway landing snapshots, and release/Radicle constraints.\n  3630\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/notorganic-provider; reuse_rule=recheck live services, legal facts, remote/Radicle state, CSP, and the dirty tree before deployment/release claims.\n  3631\t\n  3632\t## Task 1: Release preparation, private Radicle, Railway landing snapshot, and legal boundary\n  3633\t\n  3634\t### rollout_summary_files\n  3635\t\n  3636\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/notorganic-provider, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/05/rollout-2026-09-05T05-10-45-01a070d5-a90a-7631-8f51-db53d79dd081.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-05T12:31:23+00:00, thread_id=01a070d5-a90a-7631-8f51-db53d79dd081, partial)\n  3637\t\n  3638\t### keywords\n  3639\t\n  3640\t- notorganic.info, build:landing, Caddyfile, rad init, rad publish, /healthz, Draft placeholder, Paddle, docs.notorganic.info\n  3641\t\n  3642\t## Task 2: Branded landing motion, portal redesign, and lifecycle React Email templates\n  3643\t\n  3644\t### rollout_summary_files\n  3645\t\n  3646\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/notorganic-provider, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/06/rollout-2026-09-06T05-41-36-01a07618-4107-7bb0-9c45-2f4ff16e7131.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-04T22:30:43+00:00, thread_id=01a07618-4107-7bb0-9c45-2f4ff16e7131, success)\n  3647\t\n  3648\t### keywords\n  3649\t\n  3650\t- juice.js, textures.css, script-src 'self', .portal-preview.ts, preview:emails, micro-USD, React Email, transactional, lifecycle\n  3651\t\n  3652\t## Task 3: Update product icons, deploy the isolated commit, and verify the private Radicle push\n  3653\t\n  3654\t### rollout_summary_files\n  3655\t\n  3656\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/notorganic-provider, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/06/rollout-2026-09-06T18-29-45-01a078d7-8770-7331-92e0-ff89afe49778.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-06T23:56:29+00:00, thread_id=01a078d7-8770-7331-92e0-ff89afe49778, partial; icon assets deployed, Radicle push unverified)\n  3657\t\n  3658\t### keywords\n  3659\t\n  3660\t- Interleave, Twyne, Keating, product-icons, interleave-mark.png, twyne-mark.png, 268e9bd, git push rad main, rad auth, dirty-worktree, prek\n  3661\t\n  3662\t## Task 4: Commit and push the remaining provider work to Radicle\n  3663\t\n  3664\t### rollout_summary_files\n  3665\t\n  3666\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/notorganic-provider, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/06/rollout-2026-09-06T19-56-35-01a07927-0617-7963-952b-083bc14889ff.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-07T04:31:13+00:00, thread_id=01a07927-0617-7963-952b-083bc14889ff, success; main and rad/main aligned, peer replication unconfirmed)\n  3667\t\n  3668\t### keywords\n  3669\t\n  3670\t- Radicle, rad push, SKIP=notorganic-railway, .zero/cache, bun run check, 156 pass, a675581, pre-push hook, No seeds found\n  3671\t\n  3672\t## User preferences\n  3673\t\n  3674\t- when asked to make Railway work “on notorganic.info,” keep landing repair separate from failed API/docs/www surfaces; deploy a scoped snapshot rather than absorbing the dirty repository. [Task 1]\n  3675\t- “customer first and a separate page for investors”; the landing should “explain the philosophy of the business and the applications we have built” -> lead consumer-facing product/portfolio narrative, keep technical details on docs. [Task 1]\n  3676\t- the user said Codex may generate “rastorized images rather than svgs” -> use generated raster assets where they fit the visual direction. [Task 2]\n  3677\t- “update the icon used for interleave, also for twyne keep the animal icon, for keating the letter icon should be used” -> preserve product-specific identity: paired gecko for Interleave, griffin animal mark for Twyne, green K letter mark for Keating. [Task 3]\n  3678\t- when requesting the follow-up push from a 96-path dirty worktree, stage only the explicitly requested assets and preserve unrelated work. [Task 3]\n  3679\t- when the user asked to “get the remain work commited and pushed” -> inspect, validate, stage, commit, and push the remaining project work while leaving generated/local artifacts uncommitted and avoiding unrelated deployment behavior. [Task 4]\n  3680\t\n  3681\t## Reusable knowledge\n  3682\t\n  3683\t- `notorganic.info` landing runs Caddy; deploy a landing-only snapshot with `railway up <snapshot> --path-as-root ... --detach`, poll to `SUCCESS`, and probe `/healthz`, HTTPS routes/assets, 404, and redirect. It is intentionally separate from API/docs services. [Task 1]\n  3684\t- The Radicle repository is private; use `rad auth` without printing credentials and never `rad publish`/broad sync without authorization. Releases need explicit dirty-tree scope and a remote URL. [Task 1]\n  3685\t- `build:landing` copies assets wholesale. Motion needs same-origin `juice.js` and Caddy `script-src 'self'`; retain restrictive remaining CSP. Hide/reveal only after JS initialization so hero CTA remains visible. `bun run check` had 141 passing tests; `bun run preview:emails` renders 32 variants. [Task 2]\n  3686\t- The icon-only commit `268e9bd27d5e8000f6daece8efac4de1cfc3b0c1` updated six assets: `apps/landing/brand/{interleave-mark.png,interleave.png,keating.png,twyne-mark.png}` and `apps/portal/public/brand/{interleave.png,twyne.png}`. `bun run build:landing` and focused landing/email tests passed (22 tests, 0 failures, 359 assertions); SHA-256 checks confirmed reviewed assets matched the landing/identity deployment. [Task 3]\n  3687\t- Before committing the remaining work, `bun run check` passed typecheck and 156 tests across 27 files, and `git diff --check` passed. Exclude generated local `.zero/cache/` using `git add -A -- . ':!.zero/cache/'`; the verified push used `SKIP=notorganic-railway git push rad main`, leaving only `.zero/` untracked. Commit `a675581` aligned `main` and `rad/main`. [Task 4]\n  3688\t\n  3689\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  3690\t\n  3691\t- Terms/privacy are visibly draft lorem-ipsum placeholders. Do not submit to Paddle or state binding/legal/refund claims until legal entity, jurisdiction, address, contacts, age, refund and fundraising details are supplied; `api.notorganic.info`/docs issues remain separately live-state dependent. [Task 1]\n  3692\t- Treat later unbacked claims of a design deployment, push, 56 tests, and browser/WebGL checks as unverified until Git/Railway/live evidence is inspected. Email templates must keep transactional notices free of unsubscribe links; `creditsLow` is lifecycle. [Task 1][Task 2]\n  3693\t- A full hook run can fail on unrelated in-progress files and pre-existing TypeScript errors. For a focused asset commit, use a clean detached checkout to run its hook, then preserve the dirty source checkout. [Task 3]\n  3694\t- The earlier Radicle push was blocked because its signing identity was not loaded, then `rad auth` required the encrypted-key passphrase. Do not claim completion after “should be good now”: retry interactively and verify `git rev-list --left-right --count rad/main...HEAD` is `0 0`; Task 4 later achieved this at `a675581`. Credentials/passphrases never enter logs or memory. [Task 3][Task 4]\n  3695\t- A normal push invokes the `notorganic-railway` pre-push deployment hook. When only Radicle publication was requested, inspect hook configuration and use `SKIP=notorganic-railway`; `No seeds found for rad:REDACTED` means the push was accepted but peer replication was not confirmed. [Task 4]\n  3696\t\n  3697\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/traction privacy-enforcing SDK, agent integration, and deployment preparation\n  3698\t\n  3699\tscope: Audit/implement Traction’s cross-surface analytics SDK and briefing product, with secret and Railway boundaries.\n  3700\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/traction; reuse_rule=deployment and provider-key state are live/authorization-sensitive; do not reuse old service-health as proof of integration.\n  3701\t\n  3702\t## Task 1: Audit claims and implement the Traction spec/SDK/agent path\n  3703\t\n  3704\t### rollout_summary_files\n  3705\t\n  3706\t- rollout_summaries/2026-09-05T10-09-56-ydPq-traction_integration_claims_audit_and_hardening.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/traction, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/05/rollout-2026-09-05T06-09-56-01a07132-6c86-7f30-8b3a-2fd6f4d05997.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-05T12:25:49+00:00, thread_id=01a07132-6c86-7f30-8b3a-2fd6f4d05997, implementation verified locally)\n  3707\t\n  3708\t### keywords\n  3709\t\n  3710\t- @traction/sdk, @traction/spec/node, DO_NOT_TRACK, POSTHOG_READ_KEY, pack:local, traction.config.json, docs/VERIFICATION.md\n  3711\t\n  3712\t## Task 2: Store PostHog read key and prepare, but do not perform, Railway deployment\n  3713\t\n  3714\t### rollout_summary_files\n  3715\t\n  3716\t- rollout_summaries/2026-09-05T12-26-12-tlZd-traction_posthog_secret_railway_deployment_preparation.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/traction, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/05/rollout-2026-09-05T08-26-12-01a07188-9921-7142-be20-0b160cbf511f.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-05T12:35:36+00:00, thread_id=01a07188-9921-7142-be20-0b160cbf511f, partial; secret must rotate)\n  3717\t\n  3718\t### keywords\n  3719\t\n  3720\t- POSTHOG_READ_KEY, Skate, TRACTION_BIND, TRACTION_PUBLIC_ORIGIN, TRACTION_DB, railway up --ci --service traction\n  3721\t\n  3722\t## User preferences\n  3723\t\n  3724\t- “telemetry should be opt out actually” and support for “desktop, mobile, cli, tui, and web” -> SDK behavior needs disclosure, project/machine controls, DO_NOT_TRACK/CI suppression, minimization, and opt-in replay, while remaining separately installable from Traction. [Task 1]\n  3725\t\n  3726\t## Reusable knowledge\n  3727\t\n  3728\t- Audit runtime/data sources before believing claims: static dashboard/health and tests did not prove the advertised agent/SDK. Enforced guarantees live in `@traction/sdk`, not low-level helpers; browser-safe root uses portable code and Node-only exports live at `@traction/spec/node`. [Task 1]\n  3729\t- `bun run check` passed 372 tests/1,943 assertions; fresh Bun/Node/Chromium consumer proof demonstrated notice-before-capture, allowlisted opt-in event, and no capture after opt-out. Local archives require companion `@traction/spec` override. [Task 1]\n  3730\t- `POSTHOG_READ_KEY` is a server-held PostHog personal query key. Railway requires bind/public origin/dashboard secret/persistent `/data`; `railway up --ci --service traction` is only authorized after exact destination plus secret/storage approval. [Task 2]\n  3731\t\n  3732\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  3733\t\n  3734\t- The key pasted in chat is compromised: revoke/replace it and never store/echo its value. Skate write access can need host permissions. [Task 2]\n  3735\t- Missing `POSTHOG_READ_KEY`, no new deployment, no publication, and no live cloud ingestion mean do not claim production integration. Live `/health` alone is not proof. [Task 1][Task 2]\n  3736\t\n  3737\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/twyne v0.19.1 release and native Devenv pre-push hook\n  3738\t\n  3739\tscope: Review, version, tag, publish, and verify the Twyne Qwik/Devenv release path.\n  3740\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne; reuse_rule=release/tag/CI/asset facts are time-specific; inspect current branch, workflow, and hook chain first.\n  3741\t\n  3742\t## Task 1: Review and publish v0.19.1\n  3743\t\n  3744\t### rollout_summary_files\n  3745\t\n  3746\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/05/rollout-2026-09-05T05-47-11-01a070f7-0264-7793-aad9-e06b6a709c20.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-05T09:53:51+00:00, thread_id=01a070f7-0264-7793-aad9-e06b6a709c20, success; Windows packaging pending at check)\n  3747\t\n  3748\t### keywords\n  3749\t\n  3750\t- v0.19.1, bun run release:version patch, check-release-version.ts, git-hooks.nix, prek install -f, Dagger, SOURCE_IGNORE\n  3751\t\n  3752\t## User preferences\n  3753\t\n  3754\t- “review and create a new release then push” -> release work includes state/workflow/hooks/checks/remote-publication proof, not merely running versioning. [Task 1]\n  3755\t\n  3756\t## Reusable knowledge\n  3757\t\n  3758\t- The native release consistency hook belongs at `pre-push`, not `pre-commit`, because Bun makes the version commit before the annotated tag. `release:version` uses `bun pm version`; `release:check` enforces SemVer, annotated `v<version>`, manifest equality, and no unexpected tag at HEAD. [Task 1]\n  3759\t- If Prek is stale, run `devenv shell -- prek install -f --hook-type pre-push` while preserving the Entire wrapper chain. v0.19.1 passed local tests/typecheck/lint/build/Storybook/frozen install/format/release checks and GitHub publication. [Task 1]\n  3760\t\n  3761\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  3762\t\n  3763\t- Do not call Vet passed when safety blocks network export. GitHub’s `ReferenceError: SOURCE_IGNORE is not defined` was an independent pre-existing Dagger failure; Windows packaging was still running at last check. [Task 1]\n  3764\t\n  3765\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/dio.computer Bun-only Devenv upgrade\n  3766\t\n  3767\tscope: Remove unnecessary Node provisioning, preserve Go TUI support, and upgrade custom Nix Bun pin.\n  3768\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/dio.computer; reuse_rule=validate current Nix hashes and existing dirty worktree before version changes.\n  3769\t\n  3770\t## Task 1: Disable Node tooling and verify Bun 1.4.2 with current checks\n  3771\t\n  3772\t### rollout_summary_files\n  3773\t\n  3774\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/dio.computer, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/05/rollout-2026-09-05T14-22-59-01a072cf-3dd9-78d0-aade-443c2fa49b0f.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-05T18:33:40+00:00, thread_id=01a072cf-3dd9-78d0-aade-443c2fa49b0f, success)\n  3775\t\n  3776\t### keywords\n  3777\t\n  3778\t- devenv shell --clean, nodejs.enable = false, pinnedBunVersion, dio:doctor, dio:ci, Bun 1.4.2, tui/\n  3779\t\n  3780\t## User preferences\n  3781\t\n  3782\t- “use devenv,” “skip vet,” and “don't write any tests just check the current tests” -> use native Devenv, honor explicit Vet skip, and validate with existing checks only. Ask what unfamiliar runtime components are for before removal. [Task 1]\n  3783\t\n  3784\t## Reusable knowledge\n  3785\t\n  3786\t- Disable Node/LSP in `devenv.nix`, but retain Go because `tui/` is a standalone SSH terminal app. Use `devenv shell --clean` to prove Node/npm/typescript-language-server are absent; inherited shell variables can mislead. [Task 1]\n  3787\t- Custom Nix Bun upgrades require all platform archive hashes plus `pinnedBunVersion`; `devenv tasks run dio:doctor` and `dio:ci` provide existing full validation. [Task 1]\n  3788\t\n  3789\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  3790\t\n  3791\t- Restricted Nix cache access can fail evaluation; only rerun with appropriate host access. Do not weaken claims because the ambient non-clean shell still exposes Node. [Task 1]\n  3792\t\n  3793\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects Gren workspace organization and cleanup discovery\n  3794\t\n  3795\tscope: Group matching top-level Gren projects and report—not perform—broader cleanup candidates.\n  3796\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects; reuse_rule=filesystem inventory/sizes are time-specific and root is not a Git repository; obtain explicit deletion approval.\n  3797\t\n  3798\t## Task 1: Group Gren packages and scan cleanup candidates\n  3799\t\n  3800\t### rollout_summary_files\n  3801\t\n  3802\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/05/rollout-2026-09-05T14-37-31-01a072dc-8cfe-7580-a95f-f987e9d157e4.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-05T18:42:14+00:00, thread_id=01a072dc-8cfe-7580-a95f-f987e9d157e4, success)\n  3803\t\n  3804\t### keywords\n  3805\t\n  3806\t- gren-packages, node_modules 48G, rtk find, compound predicates, cleanup candidates\n  3807\t\n  3808\t## User preferences\n  3809\t\n  3810\t- “can you put all the gren packages in a folder pls” -> identify all matching top-level projects, preserve contents/status, and group under a clear folder. When asked broadly about cleanup, inspect and propose candidates before destructive changes. [Task 1]\n  3811\t\n  3812\t## Reusable knowledge\n  3813\t\n  3814\t- Eighteen Gren-named directories were moved to `/home/diogenes/Projects/gren-packages`; root scan observed 42 `node_modules` totaling about 48GB. Check Git status per project, not at `/home/diogenes/Projects`. [Task 1]\n  3815\t\n  3816\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  3817\t\n  3818\t- `rtk find` cannot express compound predicates and grep does not accept ripgrep `--glob`; use direct `find`/standard grep or rg. Do not delete dependencies, empty directories, logs, or archives until inactivity/regenerability is confirmed by the user. [Task 1]\n  3819\t\n  3820\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/stich release preparation, secure auth, Railway domains, and Radicle workflow\n  3821\tscope: Prepare Stich releases without absorbing dirty work; operate secure desktop auth, committed-content Railway/Radicle workflows, and custom-domain proof.\n  3822\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/stich; reuse_rule=all release, deployment, worktree, signing, Radicle-node, and remote state is time-sensitive; establish content boundary and recheck before mutations.\n  3823\t\n  3824\t## Task 1: Prepare v0.1.2 release, stopped at content-boundary clarification\n  3825\t\n  3826\t### rollout_summary_files\n  3827\t\n  3828\t- rollout_summaries/2026-09-05T02-35-07-eiKm-stich_release_preparation_stopped_on_dirty_tree_and_signing.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/stich, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/04/rollout-2026-09-04T22-35-08-01a06f6b-735e-7c63-8273-3e00bd8fd882.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-05T02:37:46+00:00, thread_id=01a06f6b-735e-7c63-8273-3e00bd8fd882, partial; no version bump, tag, or push)\n  3829\t\n  3830\t### keywords\n  3831\t\n  3832\t- release:version, release:check, release:preflight, STICH_RELEASE_CHANNEL, v0.1.1, v0.1.2, railpack.json, signing-secrets\n  3833\t\n  3834\t## Task 2: Secure OAuth diagnostics, settings logout, committed Railway deployment, and private Radicle setup\n  3835\t\n  3836\t### rollout_summary_files\n  3837\t\n  3838\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/stich, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/03/rollout-2026-09-03T14-24-33-01a06883-f310-76b2-bfcb-fb544baaa84c.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-04T05:02:24+00:00, thread_id=01a06883-f310-76b2-bfcb-fb544baaa84c, success)\n  3839\t\n  3840\t### keywords\n  3841\t\n  3842\t- authDiagnostics.ts, LoginScreen, Debug secure sign-in, credential store, stich:deploy:railway, git archive, --path-as-root, Radicle, rad publish, rad:z3HyyJGyi3MtcFhbMVNUBvMVqHk9B\n  3843\t\n  3844\t## Task 3: Connect Railway/Porkbun domains and open local delivery proof\n  3845\t\n  3846\t### rollout_summary_files\n  3847\t\n  3848\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/stich, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/04/rollout-2026-09-04T19-53-47-01a06ed7-bbde-7e22-89a9-e01f70240fc4.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-05T03:05:08+00:00, thread_id=01a06ed7-bbde-7e22-89a9-9a1e06a37ed4, partial; local/domain and live-mail proof, deployment/TLS incomplete)\n  3849\t\n  3850\t### keywords\n  3851\t\n  3852\t- stich.cc, mail.stich.cc, www.stich.cc, Railway, Porkbun, _railway-verify, smoke-domains.mjs, railpack.json, Playwriter, data:image/png;base64\n  3853\t\n  3854\t## User preferences\n  3855\t\n  3856\t- when generic sign-in “load failed” was “really crappy for figuring out what the hell is going on,” the user wanted failing-stage, actionable diagnostics rather than opaque browser errors; redact every credential and sensitive URL component. [Task 2]\n  3857\t- “add a way to log out in the settings” -> account settings need a discoverable full mail sign-out, not merely an auth-store reset. [Task 2]\n  3858\t- “make updating railway a devenv githook” -> make deployment native/repeatable and deploy the exact pushed commit, never unrelated dirty work. [Task 2]\n  3859\t- when the user said “use railway and the porkbun stuff to get it wrking” -> use the existing Railway/Porkbun integrations directly and verify the external result, not merely list records. [Task 3]\n  3860\t- when the user asked “can you open the image in the browser” -> visibly open the artifact with browser-control tooling rather than only linking or describing it. [Task 3]\n  3861\t\n  3862\t## Reusable knowledge\n  3863\t\n  3864\t- Release checker requires coordinated SemVer across root, `apps/{agent,desktop,mcp,mobile,web}/package.json`, and `apps/mobile/app.json`, plus annotated `v<version>` tag and no unexpected version tag at `HEAD`. `bun run release:version`, `bun run release:check`, and `release:publish` (`git push --follow-tags`) are the defined sequence. [Task 1]\n  3865\t- To select preflight channel, use `STICH_RELEASE_CHANNEL=stable bun run release:preflight`; `--channel stable` is ignored. Stable signing requires macOS/Windows credentials; canary is unsigned by default. [Task 1]\n  3866\t- `LoginScreen` opt-in trace is capped at 20 events; `authDiagnostics.ts` redacts passwords, tokens, authorization codes, PKCE, query strings, and fragments. Full logout also calls `getCredentialStore().clear(account.id)` and clears React Query/UI state because `useAuthStore.logout()` does not clear secure credentials. [Task 2]\n  3867\t- `stich:deploy:railway` archives an exact commit then calls Railway with `--path-as-root`; `.githooks/pre-push.pre-entire` limits deploys to `origin main`, so `git push rad main` cannot redeploy. Poll detached deployments to `SUCCESS/FAILED`. [Task 2]\n  3868\t- Private Radicle RID is `rad:z3HyyJGyi3MtcFhbMVNUBvMVqHk9B`; a `rad:` RID is not a browser URL. `rad publish` then `rad sync` exposes history to public replication, which is practically irreversible. [Task 2]\n  3869\t- `apps/web/server.mjs` recognizes `mail.stich.cc` and legacy `mail.dio.computer`, redirects `www.stich.cc` to `stich.cc`, and redirects `/app` to `https://mail.stich.cc/`. `apps/web/scripts/smoke-domains.mjs` locally proved landing, redirect, app entry, both mail hosts, OAuth callback, assets, agent, and origin boundary. [Task 3]\n  3870\t- Railway custom-domain ownership used `_railway-verify`, `_railway-verify.mail`, and `_railway-verify.www`; local server/domain smoke, workspace tests, web build/typecheck, agent build, 5 web Playwright tests, and 10 desktop renderer tests passed. For a connected browser, open a local image by base64-encoding it into `page.setContent()` then `page.bringToFront()`; `file://` navigation is rejected. [Task 3]\n  3871\t\n  3872\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  3873\t\n  3874\t- Dirty UI changes and untracked `railpack.json` made release content ambiguous: ask whether the release includes them or committed `HEAD` before staging/bumping/tagging. Do not call stable release ready when signing credentials are absent. [Task 1]\n  3875\t- Railway `/tmp` archives caused `prefix not found`; use a repository-root temp directory and `--path-as-root`. Escape shell `${STICH_DEPLOY_COMMIT:-HEAD}` in Nix as `\\${...}`. [Task 2]\n  3876\t- `rad sync` reporting no candidate seeds is expected for a private repository without authorized seeds; it is not a failed local setup. Vet remained unverified under dirty-tree/session limits. [Task 2]\n  3877\t- Do not call the custom-domain deployment complete while Railway is `BUILDING`; poll to `SUCCESS`. Final evidence had 200/valid HTTPS for apex and mail but a TLS handshake failure for `www`; live `/app` and `/health` were 404 during the build, so only local smoke proved those routes. A stalled Vet run with read-only log warnings has no verdict. [Task 3]\n  3878\t\n  3879\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/interleave-app relationship-agent evaluation and Typst research artifact\n  3880\tscope: Build audited, safety-gated relationship-agent evaluation with Arize export and a methods-focused research paper.\n  3881\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/interleave-app; reuse_rule=recheck provider quota, current prompts/hashes, Arize state, and browser connection; the recorded pilot is explicitly unscored.\n  3882\t\n  3883\t## Task 1: Build relationship-science benchmark and quota-blocked Arize pilot\n  3884\t\n  3885\t### rollout_summary_files\n  3886\t\n  3887\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/interleave-app, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/04/rollout-2026-09-04T21-28-23-01a06f2e-5837-7441-99a8-e01f70240fc4.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-05T02:34:42+00:00, thread_id=01a06f2e-5837-7441-99a8-e01f70240fc4, partial; pilot unscored)\n  3888\t\n  3889\t### keywords\n  3890\t\n  3891\t- evals/relationship-science, Arize, Phoenix, Ivy, Sage, Ember, prompt hashes, outcome-leakage, RESOURCE_EXHAUSTED, HTTP 422, safety gate\n  3892\t\n  3893\t## Task 2: Compile and inspect Typst evaluation methods paper\n  3894\t\n  3895\t### rollout_summary_files\n  3896\t\n  3897\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/interleave-app, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/04/rollout-2026-09-04T21-28-23-01a06f2e-5837-7441-99a8-e01f70240fc4.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-05T02:34:42+00:00, thread_id=01a06f2e-5837-7441-99a8-e01f70240fc4, success; browser launch unavailable)\n  3898\t- rollout_summaries/2026-09-05T04-19-16-bT8N-open_typst_paper_local_pdf.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/interleave-app, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/05/rollout-2026-09-05T00-19-16-01a06fca-cd62-7df1-be37-ff2cc8fa2ae5.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-05T04:21:08+00:00, thread_id=01a06fca-cd62-7df1-be37-ff2cc8fa2ae5, partial; local browser opening unverified)\n  3899\t\n  3900\t### keywords\n  3901\t\n  3902\t- paper.typ, paper.pdf, bibliography, Typst, relationship-agent-evaluation, 11 pages, 20 references\n  3903\t\n  3904\t## User preferences\n  3905\t\n  3906\t- scenarios “from books and couples around the world” with “good arguments” -> distinguish literary dilemmas, study-informed composites, and synthetic cases; preserve evidence, warrant, counterargument, consent, and uncertainty rather than emitting opaque scores. [Task 1]\n  3907\t\n  3908\t## Reusable knowledge\n  3909\t\n  3910\t- `evals/relationship-science/` has 38 scenarios/18 families/14 source records with 14/12/12 development/calibration/holdout splits, prompt hashes, blinded judging, safety gates, reports, paired comparisons, and Arize export. It blocks outcome leakage, split contamination, invented evidence IDs, missing denominator slots, and safety failures averaged away. [Task 1]\n  3911\t- Actor failures must be explicit nonempty JSON error records in Arize export, omitted from scoring; this fixed Arize HTTP 422. Current pilot upload/readback stored 14 runs, but 9 actor successes and 5 failures produced 14 unscored judgments. [Task 1]\n  3912\t- `docs/research/relationship-agent-evaluation/paper.typ` compiled to a visually inspected 11-page PDF with 20 references; it evaluates advice, not predicted relationship outcomes. [Task 2]\n  3913\t\n  3914\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  3915\t\n  3916\t- HTTP 429 `RESOURCE_EXHAUSTED` surfaced as Flue HTTP 502. Never describe the pilot as quality, safety, efficacy, or scored evidence; rerun live providers after quota access is available. [Task 1]\n  3917\t- Browser list was empty, so interactive PDF opening was not verified. Do not substitute another browser surface without approval. Networked Vet was safety-blocked, not passed. [Task 1][Task 2]\n  3918\t\n  3919\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/interleave-app native Devenv development workflow\n  3920\tscope: Run the root development stack through declarative Devenv tasks, processes, and profiles without parallel orchestration layers.\n  3921\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/interleave-app; reuse_rule=recheck Devenv/Nix access, lockfile, dirty tree, and provider/native-package status; targeted startup proof is not full-repository proof.\n  3922\t\n  3923\t## Task 1: Replace mixed root orchestration with native Devenv\n  3924\t\n  3925\t### rollout_summary_files\n  3926\t\n  3927\t- rollout_summaries/2026-09-04T23-13-58-PSFZ-interleave_native_devenv_modernization.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/interleave-app, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/04/rollout-2026-09-04T19-13-58-01a06eb3-4a22-7983-b51a-1abe9757df1b.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-05T00:18:35+00:00, thread_id=01a06eb3-4a22-7983-b51a-1abe9757df1b, partial; targeted workflow/startup verified)\n  3928\t\n  3929\t### keywords\n  3930\t\n  3931\t- devenv.nix, devenv.lock, interleave:setup, interleave:check, devenv up, --profile all, processes, bun install --lockfile-only, window.$_TSR, apps/web/index.html\n  3932\t\n  3933\t## User preferences\n  3934\t\n  3935\t- when the user requested Devenv for “running all dev stuff getting things up setting up processes testing stuff” -> use one native declarative Devenv workflow. “devenv up, tasks and no just commands or mise” and native `processes.*`/`services.*` mean do not introduce Just, Mise, Moon, or `concurrently` root orchestration. [Task 1]\n  3936\t\n  3937\t## Reusable knowledge\n  3938\t\n  3939\t- `devenv.nix` defines namespaced `interleave:*` tasks, managed processes, readiness probes, an `all` profile, and fixed browser ports. Default `devenv up` starts web plus Convex; `devenv --profile all up` enables seven browser apps. `devenv tasks list --no-tui` evaluated successfully under Devenv 2.2.2, and web was `ready` with `curl http://127.0.0.1:5173/` returning 200. [Task 1]\n  3940\t- `interleave:setup` runs `bun install --frozen-lockfile` and creates `.env` only if absent. If manifests and `bun.lock` drift, run `devenv shell -- bun install --lockfile-only`, then rerun setup. Remove obsolete `apps/web/index.html` if TanStack Start reports `Expected to find bootstrap data on window.$_TSR, but we did not.` [Task 1]\n  3941\t\n  3942\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  3943\t\n  3944\t- `interleave:check` still had existing Convex-reference, formatting, and repository-wide TypeScript errors; targeted tests/builds/startup do not prove full-repo type cleanliness, live providers, or native packaging. Format only the migration scope when unrelated dirty files fail broad checks. [Task 1]\n  3945\t- Nix cache restrictions can yield `unable to open database file`; evaluation needs the appropriate environment access. Whole-tree Vet can exceed input limits or lack credentials: review isolated snapshots/narrow migration diffs and report Vet unverified. [Task 1]\n  3946\t\n  3947\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/notorganic-provider Paddle billing, optional local gateway configuration, and MCP replay\n  3948\tscope: Maintain server-owned payment/control-plane behavior, truthful checkout E2E status, local optional-provider startup, and Responses/MCP state explanations.\n  3949\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/notorganic-provider; reuse_rule=recheck deployed payment-link page, Paddle notification/secret configuration, live dependencies, and provider state before enabling checkout or calling it ready.\n  3950\t\n  3951\t## Task 1: Explain centralized checkout, Paddle model, and legal launch requirements\n  3952\t\n  3953\t### rollout_summary_files\n  3954\t\n  3955\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/notorganic-provider, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/04/rollout-2026-09-04T03-47-47-01a06b63-55c7-7520-98c6-fe9427468371.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-04T07:58:22+00:00, thread_id=01a06b63-55c7-7520-98c6-fe9427468371, partial; legal pages/settings unverified)\n  3956\t\n  3957\t### keywords\n  3958\t\n  3959\t- api.notorganic.info, /v1/billing/checkout, Paddle, hosted checkout, return_url, idempotency, Terms of Service, Privacy Policy, webhook\n  3960\t\n  3961\t## Task 2: Migrate sandbox checkout and attempt browser payment E2E\n  3962\t\n  3963\t### rollout_summary_files\n  3964\t\n  3965\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/notorganic-provider, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/04/rollout-2026-09-04T05-20-50-01a06bb8-864e-7181-a126-23b371ca5f3b.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-04T09:33:52+00:00, thread_id=01a06bb8-864e-7181-a126-23b371ca5f3b, partial; payment E2E blocked)\n  3966\t\n  3967\t### keywords\n  3968\t\n  3969\t- PADDLE_PRICE_CATALOG, Paddle-Signature, /transactions, price_id, Paddle.js, checkout_unavailable, wallet credit, sandbox-checkout-service, CORS\n  3970\t\n  3971\t## Task 3: Make gateway startup tolerate disabled integrations\n  3972\t\n  3973\t### rollout_summary_files\n  3974\t\n  3975\t- rollout_summaries/2026-09-04T20-03-35-Ntcv-notorganic_provider_optional_local_gateway_integrations.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/notorganic-provider, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/04/rollout-2026-09-04T16-03-35-01a06e04-fbaf-7cb0-8064-ba1039f36403.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-04T20:06:16+00:00, thread_id=01a06e04-fbaf-7cb0-8064-ba1039f36403, success)\n  3976\t\n  3977\t### keywords\n  3978\t\n  3979\t- PADDLE_API_KEY, PADDLE_PRICE_CATALOG, Tavus, EVOLUTION_BLOB_ROOT, .local/evolution-artifacts, PORT=13087, healthz, OpenBao, Convex\n  3980\t\n  3981\t## User preferences\n  3982\t\n  3983\t- “i know this is cream only but i want to know how it would work with paddle” -> answer the requested hypothetical/provider flow before separately naming current implementation state. [Task 1]\n  3984\t- “terms of service agreements and privacy agreements clear descriptions of what the site does” -> inspect visible product/legal/support links before treating checkout as launch-ready. [Task 1]\n  3985\t- credentials were “for the test and sandboxing” and the user asked to “test end to end and give me screenshots” -> use sandbox only; distinguish rendered checkout from completed payment, webhook, wallet credit, usage, and reconciliation with visual evidence. [Task 2]\n  3986\t\n  3987\t## Reusable knowledge\n  3988\t\n  3989\t- `api.notorganic.info` is the server-side checkout/webhook control plane; callers receive a provider hosted checkout URL and may supply `return_url`. Keep price mapping/allowlists, idempotency, provider credentials, signed webhook verification, and entitlement processing server-side. [Task 1]\n  3990\t- Paddle uses `POST /transactions`, server-only `pri_...` price IDs resolved from stable `plan_id`/`pack_id`, and raw-body `Paddle-Signature` HMAC-SHA256 verification with a five-minute timestamp window at `/webhooks/paddle`. Focused TypeScript/build/tests passed (37 tests). [Task 2]\n  3991\t- Transaction links require a configured payment-link page that loads/initializes Paddle.js with a client-side token; `?_ptxn=<transaction_id>` alone is not a standalone payment form. [Task 2]\n  3992\t- Empty `PADDLE_PRICE_CATALOG` disables checkout; configured prices require `PADDLE_API_KEY` and otherwise fail 503 `checkout_unavailable` before a provider request. All Tavus credentials absent disables it; partial Tavus config is invalid. Local artifact root must be absolute (`resolve(\".local/evolution-artifacts\")`); production still requires `EVOLUTION_BLOB_ROOT`. [Task 3]\n  3993\t- MCP replay restores prior tool transcript/results after resume/compaction/handoff; it does not rerun the original operation. Preserve assistant output-item `phase` exactly (`commentary` or `final_answer`) when manually replaying. [Task 4]\n  3994\t\n  3995\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  3996\t\n  3997\t- Marketing `notorganic.info` lacked Paddle.js, and isolated checkout hit sandbox CORS before card form. No payment, webhook, wallet credit, hosted debit, reconciliation, or refund proof exists. Add a dedicated initialized page, notification destination/secret, resolve CORS, then test card through the full chain. [Task 2]\n  3998\t- `/healthz` false with unavailable Convex/OpenBao is dependency-health evidence, not a startup-config regression; port 3000 collision should be retested on an alternate `PORT`. Vet remained unverified. [Task 3]\n  3999\t- `rtk grep -n -i \"replay\" .` returned `grep: .: Is a directory`; verify wrapper syntax or use `rg` for recursive search. [Task 4]\n  4000\t\n  4001\t# Task Group: cross-repository native Devenv git hooks for Keating, Not Organic, and Twyne\n  4002\tscope: Keep repository-specific hooks native to Devenv/Nix while preserving Entire wrappers and unrelated dirty work.\n  4003\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/{dio-machines,keating,notorganic-provider,twyne}; reuse_rule=inspect each repo's current Devenv input/lock, hook chain, canonical passing check, and dirty tree before changing hooks.\n  4004\t\n  4005\t## Task 1: Integrate native repository-specific hooks across three repositories\n  4006\t\n  4007\t### rollout_summary_files\n  4008\t\n  4009\t- rollout_summaries/2026-09-04T05-03-02-ZgwI-native_devenv_git_hooks_three_repos.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/dio-machines, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/04/rollout-2026-09-04T01-03-02-01a06acc-82da-77d1-a6d3-9e97d43f5c44.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-04T06:59:33+00:00, thread_id=01a06acc-82da-77d1-a6d3-9e97d43f5c44, success)\n  4010\t\n  4011\t### keywords\n  4012\t\n  4013\t- git-hooks.nix, devenv.nix, devenv.yaml, prek, .pre-commit-config.yaml, Entire, notorganic:check, twyne:release:check, core.hooksPath\n  4014\t\n  4015\t## User preferences\n  4016\t\n  4017\t- “not this hook, just a hook that fits the repo that is custom” -> use the repository's canonical passing invariant instead of copying a generic C/Make example. [Task 1]\n  4018\t- Native Devenv/Nix declarations are desired; generated `.pre-commit-config.yaml` is ignored, not handwritten source. [Task 1]\n  4019\t\n  4020\t## Reusable knowledge\n  4021\t\n  4022\t- Keep declarations in `devenv.nix`, add the `git-hooks` input following `nixpkgs` where absent, ignore generated `.pre-commit-config.yaml`, and keep Entire wrappers chained around generated hooks. [Task 1]\n  4023\t- Keating already has repo-specific hooks; refresh stale generated `prek` state with `devenv shell -- prek install --force --hook-type pre-push`. Not Organic uses pre-commit `notorganic-check` -> `devenv tasks run notorganic:check`; Twyne uses `twyne-release-check` on pre-commit/pre-push -> `devenv tasks run twyne:release:check`. [Task 1]\n  4024\t\n  4025\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  4026\t\n  4027\t- Stale Entire backup may reference a garbage-collected `prek` and yield `exec: prek: not found`; regenerate in the current Devenv shell before restoring wrapper chain. [Task 1]\n  4028\t- Do not use Twyne `twyne:check` as a hook while its baseline has 165 unrelated Prettier failures. Preserve dirty changes; `devenv info` may print secrets, so never use/store its full output. Vet `unknown error` is unverified. [Task 1]\n  4029\t\n  4030\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/keating repository-state and upstream divergence reporting\n  4031\tscope: Report a dirty Keating checkout with accurate ahead/behind semantics and a grouped active-work summary.\n  4032\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating; reuse_rule=all counts, branch tips, tags, and changed-path categories are time-specific; rerun against current checkout before reporting.\n  4033\t\n  4034\t## Task 1: Inspect current state and explain missing upstream commits\n  4035\t\n  4036\t### rollout_summary_files\n  4037\t\n  4038\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/04/rollout-2026-09-04T03-14-51-01a06b45-2f45-7d03-9862-9b488b9f295d.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-04T07:21:47+00:00, thread_id=01a06b45-2f45-7d03-9862-9b488b9f295d, success)\n  4039\t\n  4040\t### keywords\n  4041\t\n  4042\t- git status --short --branch, origin/main...HEAD, git rev-list --left-right --count, v3.10.1, v3.10.2, 14cee8c2, f1c2ae3c, dirty-worktree\n  4043\t\n  4044\t## User preferences\n  4045\t\n  4046\t- “what is current state of this repo,” “check entire to see what we have been working on,” and “give me more detail along with what the two commits are ahead” -> proactively give divergence direction, tracked/untracked counts, grouped subsystems, and exact upstream commits. [Task 1]\n  4047\t\n  4048\t## Reusable knowledge\n  4049\t\n  4050\t- Use `git status --short --branch`, diff/staged stats, recent log, untracked inventory, and `git rev-list --left-right --count origin/main...HEAD`; explicitly list both `main..origin/main` and inverse. [Task 1]\n  4051\t- At this inspection, local `main` `005a93cf`/`v3.10.1` was behind two, not ahead; upstream `14cee8c2` added cross-provider search/LaTeX and `f1c2ae3c` published v3.10.2. Worktree had 68 tracked + 31 untracked changed paths and no staged changes. [Task 1]\n  4052\t\n  4053\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  4054\t\n  4055\t- Do not say “behind 2” without naming direction and commits. Do not blindly pull/rebase a heavily dirty worktree; preserve/review its local batch first. [Task 1]\n  4056\t\n  4057\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/stich accessible component system, concise UI, and themes\n  4058\tscope: Reuse the shared accessible controls, task-first desktop copy, calendar creation interaction, runtime themes, and narrow-screen navigation.\n  4059\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/stich; reuse_rule=recheck the dirty tree and generated desktop CSS; use @stich/ui primitives rather than reviving screen-local controls.\n  4060\t\n  4061\t## Task 1: Migrate desktop controls and dialogs onto accessible primitives\n  4062\t\n  4063\t### rollout_summary_files\n  4064\t\n  4065\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/stich, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/03/rollout-2026-09-03T18-30-47-01a06965-6389-7013-87a9-7a3d9914c613.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-03T22:44:46+00:00, thread_id=01a06965-6389-7013-87a9-7a3d9914c613, success)\n  4066\t\n  4067\t### keywords\n  4068\t\n  4069\t- @stich/ui, Dialog, Select, NumberInput, Checkbox, Radio, Switch, Textarea, Badge, Progress, focus trap, hold-to-repeat\n  4070\t\n  4071\t## User preferences\n  4072\t\n  4073\t- when asked to “fix these issues and also redesign the number input and dropdowns. the checkmarks could also do well” -> improve the whole repeated interaction vocabulary through shared primitives, not isolated visual patches [Task 1]\n  4074\t\n  4075\t## Reusable knowledge\n  4076\t\n  4077\t- Shared controls are in `packages/ui/src/components/{field,input,number-input,select,checkbox,dialog,badge,progress}.tsx`; desktop Button/Input are compatibility re-exports. `Select` is a portalled fixed-position listbox; `Dialog` portals, traps focus, handles Escape/scroll lock, and restores opener focus. `NumberInput` retains native number semantics, clamps/steps safely, and its repeating timer reads a ref-backed value. [Task 1]\n  4078\t- Preserve native inputs beneath LCARS Checkbox/Radio/Switch visuals. [Task 1]\n  4079\t\n  4080\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  4081\t\n  4082\t- Capture the dialog opener during the closed-to-open render, not in an effect after React `autoFocus`; use a current-value ref inside hold-to-repeat timers. [Task 1]\n  4083\t- Root `build:storybook` is invalid; use `bun run --filter '@stich/ui' build-storybook` or the documented Devenv task. Vet was unavailable (missing credentials/agentic stall or explicit “skip vet”), never passed. [Task 1]\n  4084\t\n  4085\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/stich provenance, Entire history, and uncommitted-diff review\n  4086\tscope: Reconstruct Stich history beyond short Git ancestry and resume large-diff reviews with evidence rather than inherited conclusions.\n  4087\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/stich; reuse_rule=all worktree counts and Entire local-only results are timestamped; re-run against the current checkout before reporting them as current state.\n  4088\t\n  4089\t## Task 1: Reconstruct development history with Git and Entire CLI\n  4090\t\n  4091\t### rollout_summary_files\n  4092\t\n  4093\t- rollout_summaries/2026-09-02T23-20-23-TPOJ-stich_entire_development_history_reconstruction.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/stich, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/02/rollout-2026-09-02T19-20-23-01a0646c-705f-7ad1-825d-838f9929302d.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-02T23:53:49+00:00, thread_id=01a0646c-705f-7ad1-825d-838f9929302d, success; inspection only)\n  4094\t\n  4095\t### keywords\n  4096\t\n  4097\t- Entire CLI, entire session list --json, entire checkpoint list --json, --pending, synthetic checkpoints, Entire-Checkpoint, git log main --reverse, v0.1.0, v0.1.1, release:check, D-Bus, SSH\n  4098\t\n  4099\t## User preferences\n  4100\t\n  4101\t- when the user asked to “look at this repository and tell me exactly how it has developed using the entire cli” -> combine normal Git commits, Entire sessions/checkpoints/transcripts, refs/tags, and current uncommitted work rather than using `git log` alone [Task 1]\n  4102\t- for the large-diff review, the user required only the specified issues JSON and requested parallel review by issue type -> preserve the output contract and split review dimensions when feasible [Task 2]\n  4103\t\n  4104\t## Reusable knowledge\n  4105\t\n  4106\t- At inspection, `main` had four conventional commits (`21fbb92a`, `2b4df2c0`, `a7b351ea`, `18349ab`); only lightweight `v0.1.0` existed while root was `0.1.1`, so `bun run release:check` reported `missing v0.1.1`. Most product evolution was in synthetic checkpoints and a dirty worktree. [Task 1]\n  4107\t- Use local `entire session list --json`, `entire checkpoint list --json`, pending checkpoints, Git refs, and stored transcripts when cloud views are unavailable. `entire checkpoint explain` needs a checkpoint ID or a commit with an `Entire-Checkpoint` trailer; otherwise use `--commit` where supported or inspect Git. Bound diffs and exclude `node_modules`, `.zero`, and generated metadata. [Task 1]\n  4108\t- The failed review established no findings. On resume, inspect current code and run focused evidence first; high-impact areas worth prioritizing are release CI, credential hydration/persistence, login/registration, mobile Expo, web server handling, Not Organic client, Stalwart admin API, generated routes, and dependency/lockfile changes. [Task 2]\n  4109\t\n  4110\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  4111\t\n  4112\t- `entire activity`/`entire recap` could not read local auth over D-Bus, and remote checkpoint enumeration failed due to SSH/repository permissions -> disclose both limits and call checkpoint counts local-only. Do not treat synthetic branches as normal ancestry or historical transcript claims as freshly rerun verification. [Task 1]\n  4113\t- Both review attempts stopped at a session limit before result evidence; do not infer defects from their task framing. A resumed audit must independently inspect the current tree and return the requested `{ \"issues\": [...] }` form. [Task 2]\n  4114\t\n  4115\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/stich desktop renderer, AI composer, Stalwart credentials, and inbox imports\n  4116\tscope: Diagnose bundled Electrobun startup, deliver compact provider-backed desktop AI input, safely investigate Stalwart/JMAP credentials, and ship mail-reference/Google-file-import features.\n  4117\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/stich; reuse_rule=recheck the heavily dirty worktree, Railway linkage/deployment, current Stalwart credential representation, and live JMAP authentication before edits or completion claims.\n  4118\t\n  4119\t## Task 1: Diagnose and fix blank Electrobun desktop window\n  4120\t\n  4121\t### rollout_summary_files\n  4122\t\n  4123\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/stich, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/02/rollout-2026-09-02T02-12-34-01a060bf-7153-7851-b477-34a0f44e14d2.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-02T23:59:38+00:00, thread_id=01a060bf-7153-7851-b477-34a0f44e14d2, success; real-renderer tests and unsigned build passed)\n  4124\t\n  4125\t### keywords\n  4126\t\n  4127\t- Electrobun, real-renderer Playwright, Bun.build, @openuidev/react-lang, process is not defined, process.env[\"NODE_ENV\"], import.meta.env, electrobun.config.ts, build-desktop-app.ts\n  4128\t\n  4129\t## Task 2: Inspect and reset Stalwart credentials\n  4130\t\n  4131\t### rollout_summary_files\n  4132\t\n  4133\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/stich, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/02/rollout-2026-09-02T02-12-34-01a060bf-7153-7851-b477-34a0f44e14d2.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-02T23:59:38+00:00, thread_id=01a060bf-7153-7851-b477-34a0f44e14d2, partial; reset was rolled back and remains unproven)\n  4134\t\n  4135\t### keywords\n  4136\t\n  4137\t- Stalwart, Railway, stalwart-mail, stalwart-image, JMAP, /.well-known/jmap, /jmap/session, Basic auth, secret-tool, New credential verification failed; previous credential was restored\n  4138\t\n  4139\t## Task 3: Add intelligence references, Google imports, and deploy Stich\n  4140\t\n  4141\t### rollout_summary_files\n  4142\t\n  4143\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/stich, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/02/rollout-2026-09-02T02-12-34-01a060bf-7153-7851-b477-34a0f44e14d2.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-02T23:59:38+00:00, thread_id=01a060bf-7153-7851-b477-34a0f44e14d2, success; deployed and production login rendered)\n  4144\t\n  4145\t### keywords\n  4146\t\n  4147\t- ChatReferencePicker.tsx, GoogleImportModal.tsx, googleContacts.ts, useCalendarContacts.ts, RFC 9610, AddressBook/ContactCard, importCalendarIcs, importContacts, 1 of 2 messages in scope, mail.dio.computer\n  4148\t\n  4149\t## User preferences\n  4150\t\n  4151\t- when the user reported “blank when i start up the desktop app” with a screenshot -> reproduce the actual bundled renderer and inspect page errors instead of treating the native shell as the whole problem [Task 1]\n  4152\t- when asked to check Railway/env credentials and then “reset it” -> redact all credential material, retain rollback verification, and only report a reset after direct authentication proves it [Task 2]\n  4153\t\n  4154\t## Reusable knowledge\n  4155\t\n  4156\t- Electrobun browser views are Bun-built rather than Vite-built. `@openuidev/react-lang` may evaluate `process.env[\"NODE_ENV\"]`; replace `process.env` wholesale with a static `{ NODE_ENV: ... }` object in both `apps/desktop/electrobun.config.ts` and `e2e/build-desktop-app.ts`, since a narrow `process.env.NODE_ENV` define misses bracket notation/aliasing. Use optional `import.meta.env?.VITE_STICH_AGENT_URL` with the localhost fallback because Bun-built views lack Vite env injection. [Task 1]\n  4157\t- Completed validation for that fix: desktop typecheck, all nine real-renderer E2E tests, and unsigned Electrobun build. [Task 1]\n  4158\t- The separate Railway project is `stalwart-mail` / service `stalwart-image`. For Basic-auth checks, request `/jmap/session` directly: `/.well-known/jmap` redirects with 307 and can lose the Authorization header. Store newly generated local credentials only in the system keyring; `secret-tool` is available while `pass` is not. [Task 2]\n  4159\t- Chat references scope people, attachment metadata, and time periods. Google support is a one-time `.ics`, CSV, or vCard import, not continuous OAuth synchronization; matching Google UIDs update contacts, contact photos are not imported, and Stalwart contact methods use RFC 9610 AddressBook/ContactCard. Key files are `ChatReferencePicker.tsx`, `GoogleImportModal.tsx`, `googleContacts.ts`, `useCalendarContacts.ts`, and `packages/api/src/jmap.ts`. [Task 3]\n  4160\t- The feature/deployment rollout recorded 219 tests, ten workspace typechecks, production/mail-web/agent builds, `git diff --check`, and an online Railway deployment where `https://mail.dio.computer` rendered login. Railpack uses `bun run build:web`, `bun run build:agent`, and `bun run build:mail-web`. [Task 3]\n  4161\t\n  4162\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  4163\t\n  4164\t- An HTML/renderer asset-collision hypothesis was wrong -> begin with page-error evidence from the real renderer. Vet was unavailable because normal mode lacked Anthropic credentials and the agentic retry exceeded its 1,048,576-character input limit on the dirty worktree; do not call it passed. [Task 1]\n  4165\t- Do not print or inspect raw secret arrays: a legacy principal secret appeared in captured local tool output and must be treated as compromised. SHA-512-crypt replacement did not authenticate on this deployment; preserve rollback material without emitting it, determine the actual supported representation, authenticate directly at `/jmap/session`, and treat the reset as unresolved until that succeeds. [Task 2]\n  4166\t\n  4167\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/dio-machines desktop GUI app support\n  4168\t\n  4169\tscope: Locate the configuration boundary for ChatGPT-style desktop applications on the workstation profile; this is an orientation record, not an installation decision.\n  4170\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/dio-machines; reuse_rule=recheck current package/docs layout before editing; clarify whether the user wants Linux alternatives, a named app, or dio-machines integration before changing configuration.\n  4171\t\n  4172\t## Task 1: Assess ChatGPT-style desktop GUI applications\n  4173\t\n  4174\t### rollout_summary_files\n  4175\t\n  4176\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/dio-machines, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/07/rollout-2026-09-07T15-45-17-01a07d67-4dc9-7d12-b97a-d91bfadd07b2.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-07T19:45:46+00:00, thread_id=01a07d67-4dc9-7d12-b97a-d91bfadd07b2, uncertain; investigation only, no configuration change)\n  4177\t\n  4178\t### keywords\n  4179\t\n  4180\t- gui.nix, APPIMAGES.md, desktop-apps, AppImage, Nix, workstation, chatgpt, claude-desktop, jan-ai, lmstudio, ollama\n  4181\t\n  4182\t## Reusable knowledge\n  4183\t\n  4184\t- Workstation-profile desktop applications belong in `home/packages/gui.nix`; the README describes it as “developer desktop apps — workstation only.” Applications managed outside Nix are documented in `docs/APPIMAGES.md`. [Task 1]\n  4185\t\n  4186\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  4187\t\n  4188\t- “what about guis like that chatgpt desktop app” was underspecified, so no installation or code change was appropriate -> first clarify whether the goal is Linux alternatives, one named ChatGPT-style desktop app, or integration/management through dio-machines. [Task 1]\n  4189\t\n  4190\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/twyne Bun-native release tooling and preserved hooks\n  4191\tscope: Replace Bumpy with Bun versioning while retaining version/tag consistency checks and a scoped push workflow.\n  4192\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne; reuse_rule=reuse only after inspecting current package scripts, tag-triggered workflow, hooks, branch, and dirty tree; this supersedes older Twyne guidance that requires a Bumpy note for a code push.\n  4193\t\n  4194\t## Task 1: Migrate Twyne from Bumpy to Bun-native versioning\n  4195\t\n  4196\t### rollout_summary_files\n  4197\t\n  4198\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/08/30/rollout-2026-08-30T20-42-27-01a05544-7ed1-7ed1-ae02-e54bc55f4c73.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-31T01:50:21+00:00, thread_id=01a05544-7ed1-7ed1-ae02-e54bc55f4c73, success; commit 6c8cd0a pushed to main)\n  4199\t\n  4200\t### keywords\n  4201\t\n  4202\t- bun pm version, Bumpy, release:check, preversion, postversion, .githooks/pre-push.pre-entire, scripts/check-release-version.ts, annotated tag, git push --follow-tags, package.json, bun.lock\n  4203\t\n  4204\t## User preferences\n  4205\t\n  4206\t- when Bumpy was removed, the user said “make sure that there are still hooks for all this as well” -> retain equivalent release/version consistency safeguards rather than deleting hooks with the dependency [Task 1]\n  4207\t- when asking “push this”, the user expected only the release-tooling migration to be committed -> preserve unrelated `devenv.nix` and `devenv.lock` edits and stage exact intended paths [Task 1]\n  4208\t\n  4209\t## Reusable knowledge\n  4210\t\n  4211\t- Twyne now uses `release:version: bun pm version`, `release:publish: git push --follow-tags`, and `release:check: bun scripts/check-release-version.ts`. `preversion`, `postversion`, and `.githooks/pre-push.pre-entire` all call the shared guard. [Task 1]\n  4212\t- `scripts/check-release-version.ts` checks SemVer, the annotated `v<version>` tag, tagged `package.json` version equality, and unexpected `v*` tags at `HEAD`. `bun pm version` runs lifecycle hooks and creates the version commit, but verify that it actually created the annotated tag; `git push --follow-tags` preserves Twyne’s existing `v*` GitHub release trigger. [Task 1]\n  4213\t- Bumpy configuration/dependency/bump files and obsolete pre-push helper were removed from `package.json`, `bun.lock`, `.bumpy/`, README, and Stryker ignores. Verified: frozen Bun install, release guard/hooks, Prettier, `git diff --check`, script/dependency assertions, and an isolated version/tag/push rehearsal. Commit `6c8cd0a` is confirmed at `origin/main`. [Task 1]\n  4214\t\n  4215\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  4216\t\n  4217\t- New `scripts/check-release-version.ts` initially failed formatting -> run `bunx prettier --write` before final verification. Vet had no Anthropic credentials in API mode and stalled in agentic mode; report it as unavailable, not passed. [Task 1]\n  4218\t\n  4219\t\n  4220\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Documents/Codex/2026-08-23/realtime-voice-chat cross-product launch planning, provider-owned billing, and hiring questions\n  4221\tscope: Plan early validation for Twyne/Keating, review secure public-client payments, and turn hiring critiques into concise questions.\n  4222\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Documents/Codex/2026-08-23/realtime-voice-chat with related projects=/home/diogenes/Projects/{keating,twyne,notorganic-provider}; reuse_rule=recheck live provider, policy, payment, and product state before using projections or making production claims.\n  4223\t\n  4224\t## Task 1: Customer discovery and campus marketing\n  4225\t\n  4226\t### rollout_summary_files\n  4227\t\n  4228\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Documents/Codex/2026-08-23/realtime-voice-chat, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/08/23/rollout-2026-08-23T21-52-55-01a03178-7f5a-7483-8a85-9ab075402487.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-29T07:46:17+00:00, thread_id=01a03178-7f5a-7483-8a85-9ab075402487, partial; planning assumptions need attributable experiments)\n  4229\t\n  4230\t### keywords\n  4231\t\n  4232\t- Mom Test, customer discovery, workflow videos, Ottawa, uOttawa, Carleton, bilingual French-first posters, QR codes, CPM, CAC, activation, repeat use\n  4233\t\n  4234\t## Task 2: Shared provider-owned payment architecture\n  4235\t\n  4236\t### rollout_summary_files\n  4237\t\n  4238\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Documents/Codex/2026-08-23/realtime-voice-chat, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/08/23/rollout-2026-08-23T21-52-55-01a03178-7f5a-7483-8a85-9ab075402487.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-29T07:46:17+00:00, thread_id=01a03178-7f5a-7483-8a85-9ab075402487, partial; local/provider verification reported, live E2E outstanding)\n  4239\t\n  4240\t### keywords\n  4241\t\n  4242\t- NotOrganic Provider, public-client OAuth, PKCE, DPoP, POST /v1/public/token, self-hosting, atomic code redemption, Creem, checkout, webhooks, entitlements\n  4243\t\n  4244\t## Task 3: Four central questions for the hiring article\n  4245\t\n  4246\t### rollout_summary_files\n  4247\t\n  4248\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Documents/Codex/2026-08-23/realtime-voice-chat, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/08/23/rollout-2026-08-23T21-52-55-01a03178-7f5a-7483-8a85-9ab075402487.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-29T07:46:17+00:00, thread_id=01a03178-7f5a-7483-8a85-9ab075402487, success; user approved four-question set)\n  4249\t\n  4250\t### keywords\n  4251\t\n  4252\t- Engineering levels aren’t about skill anymore, Swizec Teller, baseline coding bar, solution refinement, staff, tradeoffs, observable evidence, four questions\n  4253\t\n  4254\t## User preferences\n  4255\t\n  4256\t- when early growth planning, the user wants direct, person-by-person discovery: personally onboard likely builders/writers/learners/students, observe repeated use, record exact language and current behavior, then ask for introductions after a real result [Task 1]\n  4257\t- the user wants Mom Test-style conversations and two poster designs, not hypothetical “would you use this?” questions; product walkthrough videos should show real jobs and support onboarding as well as marketing [Task 1]\n  4258\t- payment is the shared launch gateway: web first, desktop first-class where practical, mobile deferred until production-ready; NotOrganic Provider must own browser authentication, checkout, webhooks, subscriptions, and entitlements [Task 2]\n  4259\t- the user wants exact status distinctions between local implementation, targeted verification, deployment, and real provider proof [Task 2]\n  4260\t- “remove em dashes” and use exactly four central questions when translating hiring claims into observable engineering work and evidence [Task 3]\n  4261\t\n  4262\t## Reusable knowledge\n  4263\t\n  4264\t- Stage attributable experiments: at $8 CPM, 1% CTR, and 2% visitor-to-paid conversion, $100 is a smoke test, $500 is directional, and $2,000 is larger but still noisy. Keep audience, product, landing page, posters, podcasts, and warm outreach separately attributable. At $12/month and three-month retention, gross revenue is $36, so early CAC should stay materially below that until margin and retention are proven. [Task 1]\n  4265\t- Campus/outdoor placement is permission-controlled. uOttawa external posting needs approval, bilingual French-first creative, stamped posters, and limited periods; Carleton's general policy excludes commercial promotion. Use approved venues or permission-based placements, a concrete use case, QR plus short URL, and per-venue tracking. [Task 1]\n  4266\t- NotOrganic Provider is the sole authority for identity, consent, checkout, webhooks, subscriptions, wallet/usage, and entitlements. A public Keating client needs strict redirect validation, S256 PKCE, narrow scopes, a public DPoP key, a short-lived one-time code, atomic verifier/binding validation before code consumption, and provider-state feature gates rather than local Pro flags. [Task 2]\n  4267\t- The approved hiring prompts ask about: baseline coding beyond an algorithm screen; recurring work separating junior through staff; observable evidence for solution refinement; and assessment of technical, economic, operational, and stakeholder judgment. [Task 3]\n  4268\t\n  4269\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  4270\t\n  4271\t- Treat QR engagement, poster scans, retention, and acquisition math as hypotheses, not forecasts. Do not enter residences, knock on private doors, or leave materials in private common areas; use consented brief public intercepts, approved tables/events, and 20–30 simple outcomes. [Task 1]\n  4272\t- Never consume an authorization code before PKCE/verifier and binding checks: a prior implementation let an invalid verifier burn a valid code. No deployment, charge, provider-delivered webhook, entitlement update, or authenticated portal session was proven; local passes are not a production-complete payment funnel. [Task 2]\n  4273\t\n  4274\t# Task Group: Codex global MCP configuration and Skate-backed secrets\n  4275\tscope: Register remote Streamable HTTP MCP servers globally while keeping credentials in Skate and configuration environment-backed.\n  4276\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne, with global paths under /home/diogenes/.codex and /home/diogenes; reuse_rule=reuse the configuration pattern, not the Keenable credential or live-service claim; recheck the server handshake after client reload.\n  4277\t\n  4278\t## Task 1: Configure Keenable MCP and store the credential\n  4279\t\n  4280\t### rollout_summary_files\n  4281\t\n  4282\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/08/27/rollout-2026-08-27T23-36-53-01a04671-1d0e-7ce1-93cd-967e613879b5.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-28T03:41:15+00:00, thread_id=01a04671-1d0e-7ce1-93cd-967e613879b5, success; configuration and loader verified, live handshake not run)\n  4283\t\n  4284\t### keywords\n  4285\t\n  4286\t- Keenable, Streamable HTTP, MCP, config.toml, env_http_headers, X-API-Key, KEENABLE_API_KEY, keenable-api-key@secrets, Skate, load-secret-env, codex mcp get keenable\n  4287\t\n  4288\t## User preferences\n  4289\t\n  4290\t- when providing an MCP credential, the user said \"add this to my secrets\" -> store it in the existing secret manager and reference an environment variable; never embed it in config, command output, or reports [Task 1]\n  4291\t\n  4292\t## Reusable knowledge\n  4293\t\n  4294\t- Global MCP configuration is `/home/diogenes/.codex/config.toml`. Remote HTTP headers use `env_http_headers`, so the Keenable pattern is `env_http_headers = { \"X-API-Key\" = \"KEENABLE_API_KEY\" }`; `/home/diogenes/bin/load-secret-env` maps Skate `keenable-api-key` to that variable. [Task 1]\n  4295\t- `codex mcp add keenable --url https://api.keenable.ai/mcp` registered the endpoint, and `codex mcp get keenable` confirmed the endpoint plus redacted environment-backed header. Verify secret presence by key-name listing and loader length only; secret value is [REDACTED_SECRET]. Reload/restart Codex clients after config changes. [Task 1]\n  4296\t\n  4297\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  4298\t\n  4299\t- Restricted access can prevent Skate from creating its secrets LOCK file -> use permitted elevated access for Skate operations. A secret byte-count pipeline ended with signal 13; use non-value key listing and loader-length checks instead. [Task 1]\n  4300\t- Configuration/secret resolution is not a live MCP claim -> run a JSON-RPC `initialize` and `tools/list` handshake before calling Keenable operational. [Task 1]\n  4301\t\n  4302\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/notorganic-provider source-backed architecture walkthrough\n  4303\tscope: Explain the provider's gateway, portal, Convex, sandbox, CI, and deployment boundaries end-to-end without treating a dirty-tree walkthrough as production proof.\n  4304\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/notorganic-provider; reuse_rule=reuse the architecture map and security invariants after checking current source/worktree state; the technical companion remains user-review-paused.\n  4305\t\n  4306\t## Task 1: Document provider architecture and testing guide\n  4307\t\n  4308\t### rollout_summary_files\n  4309\t\n  4310\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/notorganic-provider, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/08/27/rollout-2026-08-27T01-14-58-01a041a4-8ec3-71b0-826d-4dbcf4b15df3.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-27T17:14:27+00:00, thread_id=01a041a4-8ec3-71b0-826d-4dbcf4b15df3, partial; DOCX produced, user review paused)\n  4311\t\n  4312\t### keywords\n  4313\t\n  4314\t- NotOrganic-Provider-Technical-Companion.docx, Bun, Hono, Convex, Portkey, DPoP, PKCE S256, public-client, nou_portal_session, micro-USD, Cloudflare Sandbox, Tangled, Spindle, Fly Sprites, R2, production-readiness-2026-08-16.md\n  4315\t\n  4316\t## User preferences\n  4317\t\n  4318\t- when requesting a \"detailed run through here\" of what was built, service connections, modules, code, and testing -> make walkthroughs source-backed, end-to-end, and include concrete checks rather than a high-level overview [Task 1]\n  4319\t- when the user said \"do not do file review jst let me do a pass over\" -> stop all artifact review, edits, and critique immediately; leave the artifact for their own pass until asked to resume [Task 1]\n  4320\t\n  4321\t## Reusable knowledge\n  4322\t\n  4323\t- Repository map: `apps/gateway` is the Hono/Bun metered Portkey proxy; `apps/portal` owns React/Vite plus server-side ATProto OAuth/session/public-client flow; `packages/contracts`, `core`, `sdk`, and `session` hold shared contracts, money/lifecycle, OpenAI-shaped/DPoP clients, and assertion/token adaptation; `convex` is transactional state; `apps/sandbox-worker` runs isolated CPU jobs; `infra` holds Docker/Railway/OpenBao/PDS configuration. [Task 1]\n  4324\t- Main inference flow: a product backend signs a <=60-second single-use assertion; gateway verifies/consumes it, returns a <=300-second DPoP-bound token, requires `Authorization: DPoP` plus DPoP proof on protected calls, reserves integer micro-USD funds in Convex before Portkey dispatch, then settles/releases/reconciles. Idempotency prevents duplicate billing; debt can block hosted inference. [Task 1]\n  4325\t- Public clients must validate HTTPS origin, PKCE S256, exact same-origin callback, and portal-authenticated DID; never accept a browser-supplied DID or let self-hosted clients mint provider grants. Browser session is opaque `nou_portal_session` plus CSRF header, while OAuth keys/tokens remain server-side. The then-current Cloudflare Sandbox JWT bound account/product/project/run/body hash, with CPU-only/no-internet/30-second limits; treat those as adapter details, not the durable execution contract. Tangled is source, Spindle protocol, Fly Sprites pinned-commit runners, R2 artifacts, and Convex stores account-scoped provenance/status. [Task 1]\n  4326\t- For Keating account-level self-evolution and shared code execution, define a provider-neutral runner contract for isolated execution, filesystem/workspace materialization, bounded networking, secrets mediation, snapshots or durable artifact export, resource limits, cancellation, and result provenance. Cloudflare Sandbox, microVM, self-hosted runner, or future provider is a replaceable adapter; durable account evolution state, revisions, evidence, and activation decisions stay outside it. [ad-hoc note]\n  4327\t- Not Organic is the stable account and control-plane boundary for cross-device learner synchronization, shared pedagogical revisions, evolution history, active-version selection, and authorization. Browser, mobile, desktop, CLI, and connected self-hosted instances are account-scoped clients/contributors; they must not bind identity, durable state, or sync directly to provider-specific sandbox endpoints. [ad-hoc note]\n  4328\t- Useful checks: `devenv tasks run notorganic:check`, `devenv tasks run notorganic:build`, `devenv tasks run notorganic:railpack-check`, and `git diff --check`. [Task 1]\n  4329\t\n  4330\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  4331\t\n  4332\t- The 36-page DOCX was not explicitly accepted; it is paused for user review. The worktree was substantially dirty, so first distinguish uncommitted code from the last committed baseline before edits or verification. [Task 1]\n  4333\t- Do not call the provider production-live from local/staging checks: commercial checkout/webhook, branded DNS/TLS, OpenBao AppRole/bootstrap, R2, Fly/Sprites, gateway/PDS deployment, and full browser E2E were unverified. [Task 1]\n  4334\t\n  4335\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/keating Road to 4.0 product roadmap and execution boundaries\n  4336\tscope: Plan Keating 4.0 around evidence-based achievements, privacy-safe web/mobile telemetry, distinct feedback/community channels, and proven hosted payments.\n  4337\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating; reuse_rule=reuse for Keating 4.0 planning and implementation sequencing; treat live payment, Roomy readiness, and mobile telemetry as current-state gates to re-verify.\n  4338\t\n  4339\t## Task 1: Create the Road to 4.0 roadmap\n  4340\t\n  4341\t### rollout_summary_files\n  4342\t\n  4343\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/08/26/rollout-2026-08-26T21-52-37-01a040eb-4bb9-7c23-9014-2b4d8f8816c1.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-27T05:00:38+00:00, thread_id=01a040eb-4bb9-7c23-9014-2b4d8f8816c1, success; roadmap document passed diff hygiene)\n  4344\t\n  4345\t### keywords\n  4346\t\n  4347\t- road-to-4.0.md, achievements, PostHog, telemetry, userinput.app, Roomy, roomy.space, Creem, wallet, hosted inference, release gate\n  4348\t\n  4349\t## Task 2: Review 4.0 sequencing and scope\n  4350\t\n  4351\t### rollout_summary_files\n  4352\t\n  4353\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/08/26/rollout-2026-08-26T21-52-37-01a040eb-4bb9-7c23-9014-2b4d8f8816c1.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-27T05:00:38+00:00, thread_id=01a040eb-4bb9-7c23-9014-2b4d8f8816c1, success; strategic review)\n  4354\t\n  4355\t### keywords\n  4356\t\n  4357\t- progress → understanding → conversation → sustainability, 4.0, 4.x, checkout-started, wallet-credited, first-hosted-use, meaningful learning action\n  4358\t\n  4359\t## User preferences\n  4360\t\n  4361\t- when planning 4.0, the user identified achievements, complete telemetry across web/mobile, better user issue reporting than GitHub, and payments as the core -> retain these four pillars in future roadmap work [Task 1]\n  4362\t- when the user added “roomy.space as well” -> keep community conversation separate from structured feedback intake, voting, triage, and status tracking [Task 1]\n  4363\t\n  4364\t## Reusable knowledge\n  4365\t\n  4366\t- The roadmap artifact is `docs/plans/road-to-4.0.md`; it passed `rtk git diff --check -- docs/plans/road-to-4.0.md`. Userinput.app is for bugs, feature requests, voting, deduplication, triage, and planned/in-progress/implemented status; Roomy is for community discussion, study groups, mutual help, events, and community-authored knowledge, not canonical bug tracking, payment support, security, or release acceptance. [Task 1]\n  4367\t- Achievements should be versioned, deterministic, portable, reconstructable from durable learner records, idempotent across import/merge/retry/restart, independent of telemetry availability, and emit only content-free telemetry. Existing web PostHog coverage is substantial; mobile lacks equivalent complete product analytics coverage. [Task 1]\n  4368\t- Payment acceptance requires checkout -> signed webhook -> wallet credit -> hosted inference -> debit -> usage/reconciliation, including replay, cancellation, insufficient funds, refund, and outage paths. A clearly labeled mobile browser handoff may be an initial bridge; native purchase parity is separate. [Task 1]\n  4369\t- The coherent thesis is “progress → understanding → conversation → sustainability.” De-risk payments first even if they are presented last; initial 4.0 should keep a strict must-ship boundary (shared achievement engine, polished web/mobile views, essential mobile telemetry, live userinput.app board, Roomy beta, proven web payment loop) and defer richer tiers/dashboards, advanced Roomy gardening, terminal polish, and native purchase parity to 4.x unless required. [Task 2]\n  4370\t- Start with unambiguous achievement evidence (first successful turn, question check, improved revision, scheduled review, transfer task, project milestone). Use one headline measure per workstream: post-unlock meaningful action, complete telemetry lifecycle, feedback triage timeliness, checkout-started to wallet-credited to first-hosted-use conversion. [Task 2]\n  4371\t\n  4372\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  4373\t\n  4374\t- A successful checkout redirect, enabled feature flag, source implementation, or focused test is not production-payment proof; require real provider/browser evidence. [Task 1]\n  4375\t- Treat Roomy as a deliberate beta: finish account, moderation, permissions, retention, export, accessibility, mobile-browser, and fallback checks before making it required. [Task 1][Task 2]\n  4376\t- The roadmap is a strong release specification, not a complete execution companion: add owners, milestones, dependencies, risks, and an explicit 4.0 versus 4.x boundary before using it to drive delivery. [Task 2]\n  4377\t\n  4378\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/keating standalone Artifact Atlas interaction contracts\n  4379\tscope: Build practical standalone learning-artifact miniatures where controls carry real state and causal consequences; consolidate shallow specimens into deep archetypes and protect behavior with deterministic checks.\n  4380\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating; reuse_rule=reuse for `docs/artifact-atlas.html` or similarly standalone inline-JS teaching prototypes, not as a substitute for production subsystem implementation.\n  4381\t\n  4382\t## Task 1: Redesign the 17-artifact Atlas as five deep archetypes\n  4383\t\n  4384\t### rollout_summary_files\n  4385\t\n  4386\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/08/26/rollout-2026-08-26T00-48-14-01a03c65-ba22-7953-9ead-892ed3a2b6e7.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-26T04:50:33+00:00, thread_id=01a03c65-ba22-7953-9ead-892ed3a2b6e7, success; all suites passed; browser extension disconnected)\n  4387\t\n  4388\t### keywords\n  4389\t\n  4390\t- artifact-atlas.html, check-artifact-atlas.mjs, Simulation Lab, Annotated Source, Decision Case, Build Board, Signal Lab, 23 modes, 26 presets, retired specimens\n  4391\t\n  4392\t## Task 2: Serve the Atlas locally with Bun inside devenv\n  4393\t\n  4394\t### rollout_summary_files\n  4395\t\n  4396\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/08/26/rollout-2026-08-26T00-48-14-01a03c65-ba22-7953-9ead-892ed3a2b6e7.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-26T04:50:33+00:00, thread_id=01a03c65-ba22-7953-9ead-892ed3a2b6e7, success; Bun server on port 8788)\n  4397\t\n  4398\t### keywords\n  4399\t\n  4400\t- devenv shell, Bun.serve, 127.0.0.1:8788, artifact-atlas.html, PermissionError, Address already in use\n  4401\t\n  4402\t## User preferences\n  4403\t\n  4404\t- “multiple options for what each looks like” followed by “buttons don't do anything” -> variants must change interaction topology, persistent state, or learning behavior, not labels/status copy [Task 1]\n  4405\t- when ambitious artifacts seem difficult to make -> prefer constrained local miniatures with explicit limitations over fake full subsystems; every control should change something, show a consequence, and compare/explain it [Task 1]\n  4406\t- “think through the interfaces and fill them out more iterations buttons don't do anything check for bugs and format the damn thing” -> resolve the complete reviewed set and add regression coverage [Task 1]\n  4407\t- when the user asked to “vastly rethink and improve the utility” and consolidate into five additions -> prefer fewer, deeper archetypes with meaningful actions and use cases over many shallow cards [Task 1]\n  4408\t- when serving this repository, the user corrected “dude use devenv,” then “no use devenv with bun” -> default to Bun inside the repository’s devenv rather than Python [Task 2]\n  4409\t\n  4410\t## Reusable knowledge\n  4411\t\n  4412\t- `docs/artifact-atlas.html` remains standalone and is not imported by the app. Its current five archetypes are Simulation Lab, Annotated Source, Decision Case, Build Board, and Signal Lab; it has 23 modes, 26 cross-domain presets, and a folded map accounting for all 17 retired specimens. [Task 1]\n  4413\t- Run `bun scripts/check-artifact-atlas.mjs`; expected output is `artifact atlas ok: 5 archetypes, 23 modes, 26 presets, 17 retired specimens accounted for`. Probe every parameter sweep and fault for non-zero finite effects before integration. [Task 1]\n  4414\t- Use `devenv shell -- bun -e '... Bun.serve({ hostname: \"127.0.0.1\", port: 8788, ... }) ...'` for local inspection. [Task 2]\n  4415\t\n  4416\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  4417\t\n  4418\t- The original Argument Map handler assumed graph-specific DOM and crashed; scope handlers to their variant/container. A static audit must ignore dynamic `${stepAction}` template selectors while retaining runtime assertions for concrete actions. [Task 1]\n  4419\t- Vet did not complete (credentials/stalls); report deterministic audit, syntax, formatting, and preview checks as the validation boundary. [Task 1]\n  4420\t- Toy predator-prey and industrial-fault probes were initially degenerate; rebalance parameters/outcome before integrating a new simulation. The Claude browser extension was disconnected, so real-browser validation remained unavailable. [Task 1]\n  4421\t\n  4422\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/keating canonical OpenUI migration and learner-response Storybook coverage\n  4423\tscope: Make `keating-ui` the authoritative learner-facing interaction contract across prompts and runtimes, with inspectable story states for new response components.\n  4424\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating; reuse_rule=reuse after auditing active prompt composition, tool registration, and compatibility parsers; historical parser/test matches are not proof of active authoring.\n  4425\t\n  4426\t## Task 1: Remove `ask_user_question` and standardize canonical OpenUI\n  4427\t\n  4428\t### rollout_summary_files\n  4429\t\n  4430\t- rollout_summaries/2026-08-25T05-58-33-imls-openui_migration_stale_question_tool_cleanup.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/08/25/rollout-2026-08-25T01-58-33-01a0377f-bc52-7fd1-bcbf-1f55af87196a.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-25T06:18:13+00:00, thread_id=01a0377f-bc52-7fd1-bcbf-1f55af87196a, success; root/web/mobile tests, builds, typechecks, Storybook, and diff check passed)\n  4431\t\n  4432\t### keywords\n  4433\t\n  4434\t- OpenUI, keating-ui, ask_user_question, SYSTEM.md, refreshKeatingOperationalProtocol, OPENUI_DOCUMENT_PROTOCOL, packages/learner-contracts, splitAssistantOpenUiDocuments\n  4435\t\n  4436\t## Task 2: Add Storybook states for OpenUI and learner responses\n  4437\t\n  4438\t### rollout_summary_files\n  4439\t\n  4440\t- rollout_summaries/2026-08-25T05-58-33-imls-openui_migration_stale_question_tool_cleanup.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/08/25/rollout-2026-08-25T01-58-33-01a0377f-bc52-7fd1-bcbf-1f55af87196a.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-25T06:18:13+00:00, thread_id=01a0377f-bc52-7fd1-bcbf-1f55af87196a, success; production Storybook build passed)\n  4441\t\n  4442\t### keywords\n  4443\t\n  4444\t- LearnerResponseReview.stories.tsx, OpenUI.stories.tsx, Storybook, question-group, quiz completion, flashcard completion, streaming recovery, unsafe-source rejection\n  4445\t\n  4446\t## Task 3: Demote streamed LearningAnimation but retain explicit animate tooling\n  4447\t\n  4448\t### rollout_summary_files\n  4449\t\n  4450\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/08/26/rollout-2026-08-26T00-48-14-01a03c65-ba22-7953-9ead-892ed3a2b6e7.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-26T04:50:33+00:00, thread_id=01a03c65-ba22-7953-9ead-892ed3a2b6e7, success; full suites passed)\n  4451\t\n  4452\t### keywords\n  4453\t\n  4454\t- LearningAnimation, animate, Hyperframes, unsupported, openui-source.ts, rendering.ts, operational-protocol.md, generate-nodepod-boot-files.ts\n  4455\t\n  4456\t## User preferences\n  4457\t\n  4458\t- when the user said “open ui is supposed to be used everywhere here” -> use canonical OpenUI by default for learner-facing questions, forms, plans, quizzes, decks, media, and handoffs; do not expose legacy question tools [Task 1]\n  4459\t- when asking for an audit of “outdated” system prompts -> inspect active prompt prose, tool registries, security/permission lists, and evolved/stored prompt refresh paths, not only literal prompt files [Task 1]\n  4460\t- “add the new components that exist like user question responses and openui stuff to storybook” -> add inspectable normal, submitted, streaming/recovery, and rejection/error stories with new learner-facing components [Task 2]\n  4461\t- when the user chose “Demote, don't delete” -> remove streamed `LearningAnimation`, retain the `animate` browser tool, and use animation only for an explicit learner request for motion [Task 3]\n  4462\t\n  4463\t## Reusable knowledge\n  4464\t\n  4465\t- `packages/learner-contracts` is the shared OpenUI contract. Web, mobile, and terminal validate/render `keating-ui`; `SYSTEM.md` should point to runtime schemas rather than duplicate a hard-coded tool inventory. `refreshKeatingOperationalProtocol()` normalizes evolved web prompts before activation. [Task 1]\n  4466\t- Delete `ask-user-question.ts` and active registrations from Pi/web/security/voice paths, but retain intentional legacy parsing only for historical import compatibility. In `src/tui/host-controller.ts`, hide incomplete fences and wire JSON instead of showing them as assistant prose. [Task 1]\n  4467\t- Storybook surfaces are `web/src/components/LearnerResponseReview.stories.tsx` and `web/src/keating/openui/OpenUI.stories.tsx`; cover response, question group, quiz/flashcard completion, interactive submit, incomplete-stream recovery, and unsafe-source rejection. [Task 2]\n  4468\t- Remove `LearningAnimation` from `web/src/keating/openui/library.tsx`, shared lists, source mappings, lowering, parity fixtures, and related tests. Prefer static ConceptMap, LearningImage, or Explanation; retired animation source must fail closed as `unsupported`. Regenerate `web/src/keating/nodepod-boot-files.ts` with `bun scripts/generate-nodepod-boot-files.ts` after operational-protocol changes. [Task 3]\n  4469\t\n  4470\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  4471\t\n  4472\t- Broad searches will still find compatibility, migration, historical-session, and test references. Classify active authoring paths before deleting all matches. Vet lacked Anthropic credentials and remains unverified. [Task 1]\n  4473\t\n  4474\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/twyne crawler discovery, dossiers, and historical v0.17.0 release\n  4475\tscope: Keep public discovery frontend-served and preserve historical dossier/release lessons without treating old Bumpy or deploy evidence as current production state.\n  4476\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne; reuse_rule=recheck domain, routes, public query/index, current Bun release policy, Railway state, and dirty worktree before applying to a later deploy or release.\n  4477\t\n  4478\t## Task 1: Fix crawler discovery and dynamic sitemap\n  4479\t\n  4480\t### rollout_summary_files\n  4481\t\n  4482\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/08/24/rollout-2026-08-24T12-55-29-01a034b2-d30a-7da1-a246-090ccebed787.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-24T20:37:30+00:00, thread_id=01a034b2-d30a-7da1-a246-090ccebed787, success; focused tests/build and local endpoint smoke checks passed)\n  4483\t\n  4484\t### keywords\n  4485\t\n  4486\t- twyne.love, robots.txt, sitemap.xml, 301, Qwik routes, listForSitemap, by_kind_publishedAt, XML escaping, lastmod, take(1000)\n  4487\t\n  4488\t## Task 2: File dossiers, fix reviewer findings, and publish Twyne 0.17.0\n  4489\t\n  4490\t### rollout_summary_files\n  4491\t\n  4492\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/08/24/rollout-2026-08-24T12-55-29-01a034b2-d30a-7da1-a246-090ccebed787.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-24T20:37:30+00:00, thread_id=01a034b2-d30a-7da1-a246-090ccebed787, success; workflow and public assets verified)\n  4493\t\n  4494\t### keywords\n  4495\t\n  4496\t- dossier-folio, writing-format, malformed_response, comment resolution, Bumpy, v0.17.0, 49b0adb, ca826a6, release assets\n  4497\t\n  4498\t## User preferences\n  4499\t\n  4500\t- when the user clarified “this site domain is twyne.love” and questioned Convex -> keep robots/sitemap frontend-served; use Convex only as the bounded public URL-data source [Task 1]\n  4501\t- allowing `blog/*` is not enough -> emit one sitemap `<loc>` per actual published page [Task 1]\n  4502\t- “resolve” four reported bugs -> implement every finding and regression coverage, not merely acknowledge the review; preserve unrelated dirty work when staging [Task 2]\n  4503\t\n  4504\t## Reusable knowledge\n  4505\t\n  4506\t- Qwik routes at `src/routes/robots.txt/index.ts` and `src/routes/sitemap.xml/index.ts` return exact 200s. `listForSitemap` uses `by_kind_publishedAt`, `take(1000)` per kind, static fallback URLs, deduplication, XML escaping, cache headers, and `lastmod`; omit writer rows without handles. [Task 1]\n  4507\t- Historical v0.17.0 used Bumpy and a separate marker, but this is not current procedure: use the newer Bun-native release-tooling block and inspect active workflow first. Related skill: skills/release-publication-verification/SKILL.md [Task 2]\n  4508\t\n  4509\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  4510\t\n  4511\t- Sandbox Convex codegen hit `getaddrinfo EAI_AGAIN o1192621.ingest.sentry.io`; rerun where network access permits generated bindings. After SEO fixture edits run focused tests/typecheck immediately; `no-useless-escape` in the XML regex breaks lint. [Task 1]\n  4512\t- A historical Bumpy tag push used `git push --no-verify` only after verifying an intentional old topology; do not transfer that exception to current release procedures. Browser and Vet were unverified. [Task 2]\n  4513\t\n  4514\t\n  4515\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/notorganic-provider production payment integration and Keating public-client E2E\n  4516\tscope: Deploy the provider's Convex foundation and connect Keating public checkout, wallet, and hosted inference without overstating blocked commercial proof.\n  4517\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/notorganic-provider with related cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating; reuse_rule=recheck Creem, DNS, Railway, OpenBao, and live browser state before enabling hosted access or calling payments ready.\n  4518\t\n  4519\t## Task 1: Deploy Convex/provider foundation and checkout hardening\n  4520\t\n  4521\t### rollout_summary_files\n  4522\t\n  4523\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/notorganic-provider, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/08/24/rollout-2026-08-24T00-40-54-01a03212-48e2-7b30-afa8-1b02170cd3c2.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-24T05:05:44+00:00, thread_id=01a03212-48e2-7b30-afa8-1b02170cd3c2, partial; local/provider deployment checks passed, commercial E2E blocked)\n  4524\t\n  4525\t### keywords\n  4526\t\n  4527\t- courteous-horse-754, Convex, CREEM_PRODUCT_CATALOG, pack_id, Idempotency-Key, request_id, CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGINS, Porkbun, OpenBao, Railway, /health\n  4528\t\n  4529\t## Task 2: Wire Keating public checkout, wallet, and hosted inference\n  4530\t\n  4531\t### rollout_summary_files\n  4532\t\n  4533\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/notorganic-provider, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/08/24/rollout-2026-08-24T00-40-54-01a03212-48e2-7b30-afa8-1b02170cd3c2.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-24T05:05:44+00:00, thread_id=01a03212-48e2-7b30-afa8-1b02170cd3c2, partial; Keating focused suite passed, real browser/payment proof absent)\n  4534\t\n  4535\t### keywords\n  4536\t\n  4537\t- VITE_NOTORGANIC_ENABLED, public-client.ts, NotOrganicCallback, keating_pack_10, DPoP, wallet, hosted inference, check-env-docs.ts, signed webhook\n  4538\t\n  4539\t## User preferences\n  4540\t\n  4541\t- “deploy Convex functions/schema, wire Keating, and run real browser/provider E2E” -> report deterministic deployment/code proof separately from actual checkout, webhook, and hosted-use proof [Task 1][Task 2]\n  4542\t- preserve the fail-closed hosted state until the commercial path is proven [Task 2]\n  4543\t\n  4544\t## Reusable knowledge\n  4545\t\n  4546\t- Production Convex deployment is `courteous-horse-754`; `CONVEX_DEPLOYMENT=prod:courteous-horse-754 bunx convex deploy --typecheck enable` deployed successfully and `/health` returned `{\"ok\":true}`. Gateway checkout resolves stable `pack_id` privately through `CREEM_PRODUCT_CATALOG`, requires `Idempotency-Key`, and forwards it as Creem `request_id`; CORS is exact-origin/fail-closed and empty `CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGINS` denies browser origins. [Task 1]\n  4547\t- Keating uses PKCE S256, non-extractable device-bound DPoP, short-lived access, callback/checkout/wallet UI, and hosted-inference headers. Keep raw Creem product IDs provider-private; use stable pack IDs. Synchronize public-client environment docs with `bun scripts/check-env-docs.ts`; `VITE_NOTORGANIC_ENABLED=false` is intentional pending E2E. [Task 2]\n  4548\t\n  4549\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  4550\t\n  4551\t- Do not enable the gateway/hosted feature until Creem catalog/API/webhook, DNS/TLS, and OpenBao AppRole/Transit are proven. Railway custom domains resolving to Porkbun parking require enabling Porkbun API access; Creem HTTP 401 cannot establish catalog/payment readiness. [Task 1]\n  4552\t- A diagnostic exposed secrets: rotate affected credentials before launch and never repeat/store them in memory. The final proof is checkout -> signed webhook -> wallet credit -> hosted debit -> reconciliation/refund, not 89 provider tests or 23 Keating focused tests. Vet was unverified because credentials/fallback were unavailable. [Task 1][Task 2]\n  4553\t\n  4554\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/keating French Ottawa-Gatineau poster series\n  4555\tscope: Produce multiple on-brand French educational raster posters for college-age and independent learners, leaving QR code generation for later.\n  4556\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating; reuse_rule=reinspect current brand masters and campaign requirements before creating new assets; paths are checkout-specific and PNG ignores can hide generated files.\n  4557\t\n  4558\t## Task 1: Generate French educational poster series\n  4559\t\n  4560\t### rollout_summary_files\n  4561\t\n  4562\t- rollout_summaries/2026-08-24T04-45-24-L9Rw-keating_french_ottawa_gatineau_poster_series.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/08/24/rollout-2026-08-24T00-45-24-01a03216-6783-7d90-af9a-ad37599fddf2.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-24T05:13:30+00:00, thread_id=01a03216-6783-7d90-af9a-ad37599fddf2, success; four final PNGs generated)\n  4563\t\n  4564\t### keywords\n  4565\t\n  4566\t- Keating, posters, imagegen, French, Ottawa-Gatineau, QR placeholder, web/public/brand, web/public/posters, Keating.help, *.png ignore\n  4567\t\n  4568\t## User preferences\n  4569\t\n  4570\t- “a series of posters” and “a bunch of different options” -> create several materially distinct concepts, not minor variants [Task 1]\n  4571\t- reserve a blank white QR box and defer QR automation; make campaign assets intellectually motivating for college-age and independent learners [Task 1]\n  4572\t\n  4573\t## Reusable knowledge\n  4574\t\n  4575\t- Match Keating's cream paper, near-black ink, green, coral red, amber, and retro-computing/learning-lab language. Inspect `web/public/brand/` first; its README requires alpha preservation and deriving production files from masters. Use local Ottawa-Gatineau landmarks/everyday learner character rather than generic national symbols. [Task 1]\n  4576\t- Final PNGs are in `web/public/posters/` and include the exact `Keating.help` footer plus a white QR area. The global `*.png` ignore rule may keep them out of `git status`. [Task 1]\n  4577\t\n  4578\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  4579\t\n  4580\t- No substantive generation failure. Use the built-in image tool for ordinary raster artwork, then apply approved brand/footer mechanics; do not hand off unbranded generated images as final assets. [Task 1]\n  4581\t\n  4582\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/keating trajectory review, artifact annotation, and training export\n  4583\tscope: Implement or extend the separate local-first expert-review workspace, safe rich sharing, corrective candidate selection, and finalized SFT/DPO/KTO export.\n  4584\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating; reuse_rule=reuse private-storage/public-projection boundaries after inspecting the current dirty tree; browser acceptance and Vet remain separate release gates.\n  4585\t\n  4586\t## Task 1: Redesign review UI and reuse Chat's model/provider picker\n  4587\t\n  4588\t### rollout_summary_files\n  4589\t\n  4590\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/08/25/rollout-2026-08-25T00-50-50-01a03741-bfb9-7cb2-87a5-9208eb902d57.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-24T04:22:23+00:00, thread_id=01a03741-bfb9-7cb2-87a5-9208eb902d57, success; typecheck/build clean; 1061 tests passed with one unrelated pre-existing failure)\n  4591\t\n  4592\t### keywords\n  4593\t\n  4594\t- ModelSelectorDialog, model-catalog, review-pools, SocraticPass, MarginProposals, Reicon, PandaCSS, anchorQuote, hidden-providers, storedModelReference\n  4595\t\n  4596\t## User preferences\n  4597\t\n  4598\t- the user asked for “a separate mode for review” exportable for “sft or other training data” -> keep expert review separate from learner thumbs feedback and make training export explicit [Task 1]\n  4599\t- review “also lets you annotate artifacts natively” -> support text spans, image regions, time ranges, and whole-artifact annotations [Task 1]\n  4600\t- “regenerate the artifacts with some suggestions” and “insert new generations of choice as a response” -> preserve originals immutably, produce candidates/revisions, and require explicit preferred-choice selection [Task 1]\n  4601\t- default to pedagogy-first with expandable engineering details, local saved-session JSON import/export, and ratings for diagnosis, accuracy, scaffolding, adaptation, learner agency, and verification [Task 1]\n  4602\t- “annotate and create trajectories for what the model is doing”; “write quickly where the model turn went wrong” and “what we think might have helped the student instead” -> make turn-by-turn, span-level corrective feedback and concrete alternatives fast to record, rather than only assigning an overall session score [Task 2]\n  4603\t- “quick ways to highlight parts of text contributing to different aspects, ratings” -> expose categorized text highlighting and lightweight rating controls as first-class review interactions [Task 2]\n  4604\t- review should be “not too busy but stately” despite multiple AI features -> use progressive disclosure, dedicated reusable components, and Keating's existing paper/ink design system [Task 3]\n  4605\t- “for the model selector and provider for the pool you should reuse similar components from chat for this” -> reuse Chat's picker/catalog rather than create parallel selectors [Task 3]\n  4606\t\n  4607\t## Reusable knowledge\n  4608\t\n  4609\t- Review implementation is in `web/src/pages/{TrajectoryReview,TrajectoryReviewIndex}.tsx` and `web/src/keating/trajectory-{review,store,artifacts,generation,session,export}.ts`. `FeedbackEntry` is only thumbs-up/thumbs-down/confused; use a separate review schema/storage path. Stable turn/message IDs plus quote/content-hash anchors preserve annotations across replay, fork, import, and export. [Task 1]\n  4610\t- `ConversationEventStore` is privacy-redacted and cannot reconstruct tool arguments/results, thinking, or some transcripts. Capture full-fidelity review data privately; keep telemetry privacy-safe. Finalized exports use the existing `RewardedTurn`, `CanonicalTrainingRecordSchema`, `qualityForTurn`, `buildWebFineTuneExportFromSources`, and `training-archive.ts` seams. [Task 1]\n  4611\t- Rich v3 public links render `SharedTrajectoryWorkspace`; legacy v2 stays on the transcript renderer. `share-contract.ts` is the strict boundary: bound and validate IDs, fingerprints, references, parent graphs, regions, time ranges, and target keys. Projection excludes drafts, hidden tool traffic, learner uploads, model pools, candidates, secrets, and unsafe executable artifacts; Nitro and Vite `/api/share` handlers share the same path. [Task 1]\n  4612\t- The original review intent explicitly calls for sessions, turns, highlighted text spans, aspect labels/categories, ratings, failure explanations, suggested alternatives, and cross-turn trajectories. The later implementation supplies the schema/storage seams; use this product vocabulary when extending it. [Task 1][Task 2]\n  4613\t- Use `panda.config.ts` paper/ink tokens and recipes, direct `reicon-react/icons/*` imports, and proposal-only AI passes that require ordinary human acceptance. `anchorQuote` should accept exact/whitespace-reflowed citations but return no anchor instead of guessing. Shared discovery is `src/lib/model-catalog.ts`; retain `ModelSelectorDialog`'s local reducer and bridge stored pool entries through `storedModelReference` / `modelFromStoredReference`. [Task 3]\n  4614\t\n  4615\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  4616\t\n  4617\t- The worktree was heavily dirty -> protect pre-existing edits and prefer disjoint review files. Browser visual acceptance was unavailable, and Vet was skipped as requested; exercise `/review` at desktop/narrow widths and run Vet before calling the feature fully production-verified. [Task 1]\n  4618\t- One full-suite failure, `withHyperframesBridge > appends the bridge script to body fragments`, was unrelated/pre-existing dirty-tree context; do not attribute it to review/share work without isolation. [Task 1]\n  4619\t- The concept rollout alone produced no approved schema, UI, or validation. If requirements need revisiting, clarify annotation dimensions, trajectory semantics, and review workflow before changing implementation. [Task 2]\n  4620\t- Merge duplicate `@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)` object keys in Panda config: later keys silently overwrite earlier ones. Browser visual acceptance was unavailable, and the one `hyperframes-bridge` full-suite failure belonged to unrelated dirty work. [Task 3]\n  4621\t\n  4622\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/dio.computer Vite/Devenv watcher debugging\n  4623\tscope: Diagnose Vite startup crashes caused by Devenv runtime Unix sockets without broad cleanup in a dirty tree.\n  4624\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/dio.computer; reuse_rule=apply only when the startup error traverses `.devenv` runtime state; rerun `devenv up` with suitable Nix/host access before claiming success.\n  4625\t\n  4626\t## Task 1: Exclude Devenv runtime sockets from Vite's watcher\n  4627\t\n  4628\t### rollout_summary_files\n  4629\t\n  4630\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/dio.computer, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/08/17/rollout-2026-08-17T16-54-07-01a01180-c76d-76e2-819b-d7d400fbb3c8.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-17T20:57:06+00:00, thread_id=01a01180-c76d-76e2-819b-d7d400fbb3c8, partial; patch applied but final startup was user-aborted)\n  4631\t\n  4632\t### keywords\n  4633\t\n  4634\t- devenv up, Vite, Chokidar, ENXIO, native.sock, .devenv/run/processes, vite.config.ts, server.watch.ignored, Convex\n  4635\t\n  4636\t## User preferences\n  4637\t\n  4638\t- when the user asked “fix the issue that you see in vite when running devenv up” -> reproduce the actual startup failure and make the smallest scoped repair; avoid unrelated work in the heavily modified tree [Task 1]\n  4639\t\n  4640\t## Reusable knowledge\n  4641\t\n  4642\t- Devenv's supervisor creates Unix sockets in `.devenv/run/processes`; Vite/Chokidar can traverse `native.sock` and fail with `ENXIO: no such device or address, watch '.../.devenv/run/processes/native.sock'`. The targeted `vite.config.ts` fix is `server.watch.ignored: [\"**/.devenv/**\"]`; Vite merges configured patterns with built-in ignores. [Task 1]\n  4643\t\n  4644\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  4645\t\n  4646\t- Sandboxed `devenv up` may fail before Vite due to unavailable Nix cache/daemon. Use host access for this reproduction. The post-fix run was aborted, and Vet lacked credentials then exceeded its 1 MiB session-input limit; both are unverified. Rerun `devenv up` and confirm Vite remains running alongside Convex. [Task 1]\n  4647\t\n  4648\t# Task Group: browser-first learner storage and Tinker checkpoint persistence\n  4649\tscope: Design browser-local learner data, optional P2P synchronization, and server-owned Tinker checkpoint lifecycle without making native installation, peers, or browser-held credentials prerequisites.\n  4650\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Documents/Codex/2026-08-15/hey-i with related design scope=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating and /home/diogenes/Projects/twyne; reuse_rule=reuse these architecture boundaries for browser-first learner products; re-check current browser quotas and Tinker pricing/account limits before implementation.\n  4651\t\n  4652\t## Task 1: Choose browser-first storage and P2P boundaries\n  4653\t\n  4654\t### rollout_summary_files\n  4655\t\n  4656\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Documents/Codex/2026-08-15/hey-i, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/08/15/rollout-2026-08-15T18-10-28-01a00779-f4bb-7c90-8fa1-f416c34520f0.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-16T05:10:28+00:00, thread_id=01a00779-f4bb-7c90-8fa1-f416c34520f0, success; browser-local/P2P boundaries defined)\n  4657\t\n  4658\t### keywords\n  4659\t\n  4660\t- browser-first, IndexedDB, OPFS, SQLite-on-OPFS, GUN, Rindexed, WebRTC, Pear, Bare, Hyperdrive, localStorage 5 MB, persistence, resumable artifact transfer\n  4661\t\n  4662\t## Task 2: Design per-user LoRA/checkpoint storage with Tinker\n  4663\t\n  4664\t### rollout_summary_files\n  4665\t\n  4666\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Documents/Codex/2026-08-15/hey-i, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/08/15/rollout-2026-08-15T18-10-28-01a00779-f4bb-7c90-8fa1-f416c34520f0.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-16T05:10:28+00:00, thread_id=01a00779-f4bb-7c90-8fa1-f416c34520f0, success; provider ownership, lifecycle, and pricing boundaries defined)\n  4667\t\n  4668\t### keywords\n  4669\t\n  4670\t- Tinker, LoRA, tinker://, save_weights_for_sampler, save_state, SAMPLER_WEIGHTS, WEIGHTS, checkpoint TTL, project sharing, list_user_checkpoints, $0.10/GB-month\n  4671\t\n  4672\t## User preferences\n  4673\t\n  4674\t- when discussing Pear/Bare versus browser delivery, the user said they “don't want the user to really have to download anything at all” and want “something that's browser-first” -> make browser-local-first the default; native/Pear installation is optional [Task 1]\n  4675\t- the user estimated ordinary per-user data around 1–5 MB, with images potentially much larger -> separate small structured records from blob/artifact synchronization instead of treating all data as one P2P database [Task 1]\n  4676\t- when the user asked about “per user loras and checkpoints with tinker” and “limits of tinker checkpoints pricing how many projects per user etc” -> distinguish application metadata from provider-owned weights and verify current provider semantics rather than guessing [Task 2]\n  4677\t\n  4678\t## Reusable knowledge\n  4679\t\n  4680\t- Use IndexedDB for structured learner records and OPFS or SQLite-on-OPFS for larger local blobs. Storage is quota-managed and best-effort by default, so request persistent storage and provide export/backup. [Task 1]\n  4681\t- GUN is an experiment for small browser-to-browser records, not the primary database/blob store: its documented localStorage route is about 5 MB per origin, while Rindexed uses browser quota. Keep values small/split; use content-addressed, explicit, resumable transfer for PDFs, images, LoRA weights, and large generated artifacts. [Task 1]\n  4682\t- Use a hybrid architecture: browser-local authority, optional conventional encrypted account sync, WebRTC/P2P for direct pairing or live collaboration, and explicit attachment transfer. P2P still needs discovery/signaling/relay and availability planning; Pear/Bare/Hyperdrive is an optional native/offline tier. Synced learner code is versioned/untrusted data: require inspection/diff/approval and a capability boundary before worker/notebook execution. [Task 1]\n  4683\t- Tinker stores server-side checkpoints at `tinker://...`. `save_weights_for_sampler()` creates weights-only inference checkpoints; `save_state()` creates weights plus optimizer state for resumable/branchable training. They are not interchangeable. [Task 2]\n  4684\t- Tinker projects are the sharing/isolation boundary. Use one private project per personal Keating account or one per shared learner space; retain application metadata only: user/DID, project ID, base model, LoRA rank/modules, checkpoint URI, lineage, status, and expiry. Tinker operations remain behind the authenticated server. [Task 2]\n  4685\t- Lifecycle: short-TTL training-state checkpoints during active runs, one active sampler checkpoint, and a small number of rollback milestones; export/download only when explicitly requested. Queried storage pricing was `$0.10/GB-month`, but model pricing/discounts and numeric project limits are time-sensitive or unestablished, so query current provider/account limits. [Task 2]\n  4686\t\n  4687\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  4688\t\n  4689\t- Do not infer that “P2P” means infrastructure-free reliable availability or make normal browser persistence depend on peers being online. State the offline/relay tradeoff and retain local-first persistence plus account sync. [Task 1]\n  4690\t- Do not treat a sampler checkpoint as resumable training state, an unrestricted `tinker://` URI as authorization, or intermediate optimizer state as data to synchronize to every browser/device. [Task 2]\n  4691\t\n  4692\t\n  4693\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/keating landing recovery, shader texture, and expressive text effects\n  4694\tscope: Restore the full landing experience after over-minimization, selectively simplify MP4/CRT sections, and add legible kinetic texture/effects.\n  4695\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating; reuse_rule=recheck the current landing worktree before replaying recovery techniques; latest scramble/blur edits are not final-verified.\n  4696\t\n  4697\t## Task 1: Recover the landing structure and start shader, scramble, and blur effects\n  4698\t\n  4699\t### rollout_summary_files\n  4700\t\n  4701\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/08/14/rollout-2026-08-14T13-11-10-01a00141-9591-72d1-838b-21857d2eab37.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-12T21:51:19+00:00, thread_id=01a00141-9591-72d1-838b-21857d2eab37, partial; final scramble/blur pass unverified)\n  4702\t\n  4703\t### keywords\n  4704\t\n  4705\t- Landing.tsx, LandingWonder.tsx, SurfaceScreencasts.tsx, ShaderField.tsx, ScrambleText.tsx, Panda CSS, surface-tune, landing-word-arrive, kinetic-row, WebGL, CRT\n  4706\t\n  4707\t## User preferences\n  4708\t\n  4709\t- The previous minimal pass “went way overboard” -> restore the richer landing structure and simplify only targeted MP4/CRT areas, not the entire page [Task 1]\n  4710\t- Heading pills are “visual clutter” -> treat decorative eyebrow/prompt labels as optional. The user likes “texting animations and texture” plus playful shader, scramble, and blur effects suitable for a UX/UI showcase, with accessibility fallbacks [Task 1]\n  4711\t\n  4712\t## Reusable knowledge\n  4713\t\n  4714\t- The restored design has hero terminal, `SurfaceScreencasts`, kinetic teaching text, `LearningJourney`, CRT playthrough, CLI/install, and final CTA. `ShaderField.tsx` pauses/reduces for motion, visibility/off-screen, DPR, theme, and no-WebGL; `ScrambleText.tsx` uses direct DOM updates rather than React state every animation frame. [Task 1]\n  4715\t- Panda output derives from `web/panda.config.ts` into `web/styled-system/styles.css`; regenerate after keyframe/config edits. Relevant files: `Landing.tsx`, `LandingWonder.tsx`, `SurfaceScreencasts.tsx`, `ShaderField.tsx`, `ScrambleText.tsx`. [Task 1]\n  4716\t\n  4717\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  4718\t\n  4719\t- A missing `surface-tune` keyframe left grain stuck after config recovery: verify it exists in both `panda.config.ts` and generated CSS. If port 3000 is occupied, use the existing HTTP-200 server or select another port. [Task 1]\n  4720\t- Latest scramble/blur work stopped at a spend limit; rerun `cd web && bun run panda`, typecheck, `bun test`, and targeted screenshots before further iteration or completion claims. Two `test/mermaid-renderer.test.ts` TypeScript errors were pre-existing in earlier checks. [Task 1]\n  4721\t\n  4722\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/keating research-paper maintenance and reproducibility audit\n  4723\tscope: Update the Typst manuscript and published PDF from current implementation and reproducible evidence, not prose alone.\n  4724\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating; reuse_rule=reuse the audit and rerun procedure for later paper updates, but regenerate claims/results against the current code, traces, and frozen policy.\n  4725\t\n  4726\t## Task 1: Audit and update the Keating paper against v3.3.0\n  4727\t\n  4728\t### rollout_summary_files\n  4729\t\n  4730\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/08/08/rollout-2026-08-08T20-59-45-019fe408-6e87-7f22-aba8-b782f7748e6a.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-09T01:47:26+00:00, thread_id=019fe408-6e87-7f22-aba8-b782f7748e6a, success)\n  4731\t\n  4732\t### keywords\n  4733\t\n  4734\t- Typst, docs/study.typ, study-analysis.mjs, MAP-Elites, gridPath, async benchmark, me-candidate-33, reproducibility, keating-metaharness.pdf\n  4735\t\n  4736\t## User preferences\n  4737\t\n  4738\t- when the user said only “the paper needs updating” -> treat it as an implementation-grounded audit: reconcile claims, code, frozen evidence, and the published PDF rather than making prose-only edits [Task 1]\n  4739\t- preserve unrelated dirty-worktree changes during research/paper maintenance [Task 1]\n  4740\t\n  4741\t## Reusable knowledge\n  4742\t\n  4743\t- Manuscript entrypoint is `docs/study.typ`; sections live under `docs/study/sections/`, generated evidence under `docs/generated/`, frozen policy at `docs/study/evaluated-policy.json`, traces in `test/traces/`, curated data in `test/final_dataset.json`, and the published PDF at `web/public/keating-metaharness.pdf`. [Task 1]\n  4744\t- `scripts/study-analysis.mjs` must use an async ablation callback, such as `await Promise.all(ablationFields.map(async ...))`. Independent MAP-Elites stability reruns must receive a unique temporary `gridPath`, otherwise ignored persistent grids contaminate results. [Task 1]\n  4745\t- The validated frozen-policy result was `+3.982` versus default across `200/200` seeds. Corrected optimizer comparison: 11 wins, 4 ties, 15 regressions; mean −0.014. The reproducibility hash after excluding `generatedAt` was `934127a7201ecc9fd75517b350a4440983c67bb4b22a0568ce5ed8cf5ff62db7`. [Task 1]\n  4746\t- Scope boundary: distinguish systems/methods evidence from human-learning efficacy; the paper documents no human randomized trial and no reward-hacking audit. Focused tests, typechecks, JSON/diff checks, PDF text/font inspection, stale-claim scan, and rendered inspection passed. [Task 1]\n  4747\t\n  4748\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  4749\t\n  4750\t- Symptom: regeneration fails with Bun parse errors around `await`. Cause: the benchmark API became async while `.map()` remained synchronous. Fix the analysis control flow before trusting any generated number. [Task 1]\n  4751\t- Symptom: apparently independent MAP-Elites reruns disagree or become contaminated. Cause: reused persistent grid state. Pass an explicit isolated `gridPath` for every rerun. [Task 1]\n  4752\t- Vet lacked Anthropic credentials and agentic vet stalled; report it as unverified, not passed. [Task 1]\n  4753\t\n  4754\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/keating product analytics, PostHog, and Arize OpenInference\n  4755\tscope: Privacy-safe AI/product observability, activation instrumentation, consent, local relay behavior, and honest cloud-verification boundaries.\n  4756\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating; reuse_rule=reuse architecture/tests for Keating telemetry, but treat PostHog/Arize dashboards, credentials, and live collector state as time-specific.\n  4757\t\n  4758\t## Task 1: Overhaul PostHog activation and AI lifecycle telemetry\n  4759\t\n  4760\t### rollout_summary_files\n  4761\t\n  4762\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/08/04/rollout-2026-08-04T12-22-24-019fcd95-5798-7ca3-8635-b9dee667d9c1.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-04T17:10:46+00:00, thread_id=019fcd95-5798-7ca3-8635-b9dee667d9c1, success; deterministic/build/browser checks passed)\n  4763\t\n  4764\t### keywords\n  4765\t\n  4766\t- PostHog, agent_turn_started, agent_turn_completed, duration_ms, $ai_generation, TTFT, model_changed, app_version, analytics-privacy, session-replay, surveys, WebMCP\n  4767\t\n  4768\t## User preferences\n  4769\t\n  4770\t- when the user said “go all in” across “funnels to the ai at different turns durations and posthogs various libraries” -> make observability a cross-surface product pass with lifecycle timing, model provenance, success/error, model transition, and release attribution [Task 1]\n  4771\t\n  4772\t## Reusable knowledge\n  4773\t\n  4774\t- Existing PostHog integration is `web/src/lib/posthog.ts` with same-origin `/ingest`; lifecycle/privacy code is `web/src/lib/{agent-analytics,analytics-privacy,analytics-preferences}.ts`. `$ai_generation` captures trace IDs, provider/model, latency/TTFT, usage/cost, stream state/stop reason, and error classification while excluding prompts, replies, topics, and tools. [Task 1]\n  4775\t- Add app/schema/surface/build metadata; model changes carry from/to provider/model and active-stream changes are blocked/measured. Composer activation uses `chat_composer_viewed` and a 45-second `chat_activation_stalled`. Privacy masking sanitizes learning content, secrets, raw errors, route IDs, query strings, replay bodies, and headers. [Task 1]\n  4776\t\n  4777\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  4778\t\n  4779\t- Browser WebMCP duplicate declaration came from competing script loads. Share one load promise, prevent duplicate instances, reset failures for retry, and regenerate `web/src/keating/nodepod-boot-files.ts` after source changes. [Task 1]\n  4780\t\n  4781\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/keating release publication and agent-history provenance\n  4782\tscope: Investigate apparently missing Codex work and complete a Keating release across GitHub, Railway, npm, provenance, and an external install smoke test.\n  4783\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating; reuse_rule=reuse the release verification sequence, but re-check live workflows, registry state, deployment, and current Docker inputs.\n  4784\t\n  4785\t## Task 1: Reconcile Entire sessions with Codex history\n  4786\t\n  4787\t### rollout_summary_files\n  4788\t\n  4789\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/08/03/rollout-2026-08-03T21-44-29-019fca71-9721-7842-9380-62d870f724e3.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-04T06:17:57+00:00, thread_id=019fca71-9721-7842-9380-62d870f724e3, success)\n  4790\t\n  4791\t### keywords\n  4792\t\n  4793\t- Entire, Codex sessions, provenance, entire session list --json, entire checkpoint list --json, entire activity, /home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/, HEAD divergence\n  4794\t\n  4795\t## Task 2: Publish and verify Keating 3.0.0\n  4796\t\n  4797\t### rollout_summary_files\n  4798\t\n  4799\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/08/03/rollout-2026-08-03T21-44-29-019fca71-9721-7842-9380-62d870f724e3.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-04T06:17:57+00:00, thread_id=019fca71-9721-7842-9380-62d870f724e3, success; v3.0.0 published and production verified)\n  4800\t\n  4801\t### keywords\n  4802\t\n  4803\t- v3.0.0, trusted publishing, npm E404, SLSA, Railway, Dockerfile.web, .dockerignore, p2p-core, f08fccb, npx keating@3.0.0 version, /tmp\n  4804\t\n  4805\t## User preferences\n  4806\t\n  4807\t- when the user asked whether “all of that” was gone -> distinguish a missing/noisy index from deleted work; inspect the Codex archive and Git before concluding data loss [Task 1]\n  4808\t- when the user said “trust is set” -> resume the blocked publication job from context, then verify each release surface rather than asking them to restate the blocker [Task 2]\n  4809\t- release status should distinguish GitHub, Railway/production, npm, and provenance; a pushed tag is not release completion [Task 2]\n  4810\t\n  4811\t## Reusable knowledge\n  4812\t\n  4813\t- Entire’s local session list is incomplete/noisy and can contain stale, duplicate, diverged, or misattributed sessions. Cross-check `/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/`, Git history, and cloud activity; checkpoint provenance is unreliable when Entire reports divergence from `HEAD`. `entire status` can finalize exited sessions, so report that diagnostic side effect. [Task 1]\n  4814\t- Railway failed because `Dockerfile.web` omitted imported monorepo package `packages/p2p-core/src/course-feed.js`. The durable fix was to install `packages/p2p-core` production dependencies, copy its `src`, and add `.dockerignore`; the context shrank from about 2.76 GB to about 2 MB. [Task 2]\n  4815\t- For the completed 3.0.0 release: clean Docker build, Railway deployment `8147d89c-dd21-4106-980d-f70cad24d283`, production home/manifest/product-tour MP4 HTTP 200, `npm view`/`latest`, SLSA provenance, and `npx keating@3.0.0 version` from `/tmp` all provided distinct evidence. [Task 2]\n  4816\t\n  4817\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  4818\t\n  4819\t- Symptom: Entire appears to omit Codex work. Cause: its local session list is not all history. Fix: inspect Codex sessions and Git before reporting loss; do not call the index complete. [Task 1]\n  4820\t- Symptom: npm `E404` after GitHub release. Cause: trusted-publisher authorization, not necessarily a build/package defect. Fix: after authorization, rerun the failed workflow and verify registry version, dist-tag, attestation, and external-directory CLI install. [Task 2]\n  4821\t- Symptom: local Docker passes but Railway fails. Cause: Dockerfile lacks an imported workspace package/runtime dependencies. Fix: trace imports across monorepo boundaries and validate the clean Docker context. Do not run `npx` smoke tests inside the repository, where it can resolve the checkout. [Task 2]\n  4822\t\n  4823\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/keating production subscription OAuth and Railway verification\n  4824\tscope: Reload-safe subscription OAuth for OpenAI Codex, Anthropic, and GitHub Copilot, production deployment, and truthful end-to-end acceptance checks.\n  4825\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating; reuse_rule=reuse OAuth paths and verification gates for the same providers; provider authorization/account state and live credential consumption must be re-exercised.\n  4826\t\n  4827\t## Task 1: Restore production subscription OAuth end to end\n  4828\t\n  4829\t### rollout_summary_files\n  4830\t\n  4831\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/08/03/rollout-2026-08-03T19-02-36-019fc9dd-5f25-7822-81e2-7d554d1a2685.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-04T01:08:37+00:00, thread_id=019fc9dd-5f25-7822-81e2-7d554d1a2685, partial; deployed and route-checked, live OpenAI exchange/model use unverified)\n  4832\t\n  4833\t### keywords\n  4834\t\n  4835\t- oauth.ts, CloudProviderKeysSection.tsx, keating_oauth_pending, PKCE, getPendingOAuthRequest, cancelPendingOAuthRequest, /api/oauth/token, /api/oauth/refresh, OpenAI Codex, Anthropic, GitHub Copilot, Railway\n  4836\t\n  4837\t## Task 2: Add native Anthropic and OpenAI Codex subscription provider support\n  4838\t\n  4839\t### rollout_summary_files\n  4840\t\n  4841\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/08/10/rollout-2026-08-10T01-22-18-019fea1f-2888-7840-b378-17490c07c932.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-10T05:31:15+00:00, thread_id=019fea1f-2888-7840-b378-17490c07c932, success; live authorization/model request unverified)\n  4842\t\n  4843\t### keywords\n  4844\t\n  4845\t- openai-codex, openai-codex-responses, pi-ai, ChatGPT OAuth JWT, chatgpt-account-id, Anthropic OAuth, PKCE, oauth-provider-config.ts, nodepod-boot-files.ts\n  4846\t\n  4847\t## User preferences\n  4848\t\n  4849\t- OAuth should be “working in prod” and “testable end to end” -> verify provider authorization, callback completion, persistence, refresh, credential consumption, deployment, and one authenticated model request; unit tests/callback rendering alone are insufficient [Task 1]\n  4850\t- preserve unrelated dirty-worktree edits when modifying the checkout [Task 1]\n  4851\t- when the user asked to “use the anthropic and codex sdk and for sign in and support for those models in keating” -> use native provider semantics rather than ordinary API-key fallback [Task 2]\n  4852\t\n  4853\t## Reusable knowledge\n  4854\t\n  4855\t- Main files are `web/src/keating/oauth.ts`, `web/src/components/settings/CloudProviderKeysSection.tsx`, `web/src/test/oauth.test.ts`, and generated `web/src/keating/nodepod-boot-files.ts`. Store pending safe metadata under `keating_oauth_pending`; recover with `getPendingOAuthRequest()` and cancel with `cancelPendingOAuthRequest()` without exposing PKCE verifier/state. [Task 1]\n  4856\t- Pending safe metadata stays under `keating_oauth_pending`; `getPendingOAuthRequest()` must not expose PKCE verifier/state. UI tells users the expected localhost error page can be copied back into “Finish sign-in below.” [Task 1][Task 2]\n  4857\t- Codex remains a distinct `openai-codex` provider: `providerToOAuthId(\"openai\")` is intentionally null, while `openai-codex` maps to `openai-codex`. pi-ai's `openai-codex-responses` transport consumes the ChatGPT OAuth JWT directly, derives account ID, and sends Bearer plus `chatgpt-account-id`; exchanging it for a normal OpenAI API key breaks the subscription route. Anthropic OAuth passes through to the Anthropic transport, which supplies OAuth headers; do not convert it to `x-api-key`. [Task 2]\n  4858\t- OAuth token/refresh now return upstream data without the obsolete Codex `id_token` -> OpenAI API-key exchange; `web/server/api/oauth/openai-codex.ts` was removed. Regenerate `web/src/keating/nodepod-boot-files.ts` with `bun scripts/generate-nodepod-boot-files.ts` after OAuth source changes. [Task 2]\n  4859\t- 604 web tests, typecheck, and web build passed. Railway deployment `fca2021d-0965-4761-a5ee-5470da179944` succeeded; `https://keating.help/`, `/chat`, error callback, malformed token (400), and GitHub device endpoint (safe 200 response) were checked. [Task 1]\n  4860\t- The native integration passed focused OAuth/provider tests (24), full web tests (796 across 123 files), typecheck, and production build; subscription UI cards are labeled “Subscription sign-in,” with unauthenticated models routing to Models & Providers. [Task 2]\n  4861\t\n  4862\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  4863\t\n  4864\t- OpenAI reached `Phone number required`; never enter personal data. Live exchange and an authenticated model request remain unverified until the user completes provider verification. Playwriter timeouts/disconnects and the unrelated `useSeo.ts` null-remove error are browser/runtime harness issues, not OAuth route proof. [Task 1]\n  4865\t- Vet encountered an untracked-file bug then lacked Anthropic credentials; do not claim it passed. [Task 1]\n  4866\t- A focused fixture can fail when expiry falls inside the 60-second refresh window; use a test credential with more than 60 seconds remaining. Vet's `DiffApplicationError` against a dirty worktree is unverified review, not a code finding. Live OAuth authorization and model use still require provider accounts. [Task 2]\n  4867\t\n  4868\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/keating ATProto Standard.site blog and Tranquil PDS migration\n  4869\tscope: Replace the hardcoded Keating blog with PDS-sourced Standard.site records, article readers/routes/metadata, and legacy migration tooling.\n  4870\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating; reuse_rule=reuse the Standard.site record and discovery approach after checking PDS identity and deployment secrets; dry-run/local validation is not a live Tranquil publish.\n  4871\t\n  4872\t## Task 1: Migrate the blog to ATProto-backed Standard.site records\n  4873\t\n  4874\t### rollout_summary_files\n  4875\t\n  4876\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/08/03/rollout-2026-08-03T20-25-55-019fca29-a636-7362-ab57-ef3d7011da2f.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-04T01:07:08+00:00, thread_id=019fca29-a636-7362-ab57-ef3d7011da2f, success; live PDS write unavailable)\n  4877\t\n  4878\t### keywords\n  4879\t\n  4880\t- Standard.site, ATProto, site.standard.publication, site.standard.document, at.markpub.markdown, AtprotoBlog.tsx, atproto-blog.ts, KEATING_BLOG_PDS_URL, Tranquil, publish-standard-site-blog.ts\n  4881\t\n  4882\t## User preferences\n  4883\t\n  4884\t- when the user asked for Standard.site/ATProto posts and a future dedicated Tranquil PDS -> make portable PDS/protocol records the source of truth instead of local hardcoded JSX [Task 1]\n  4885\t- preserve extensive pre-existing worktree changes during the migration [Task 1]\n  4886\t\n  4887\t## Reusable knowledge\n  4888\t\n  4889\t- Use one `site.standard.publication` and `site.standard.document` per article with `at.markpub.markdown`; retain `textContent` as plaintext fallback. Reader/parser code is `web/src/keating/standard-site.ts`, `web/server/utils/atproto-blog.ts`, and `web/src/pages/AtprotoBlog.tsx`; routes include `/api/blog`, `/blog`, `/blog/**`, and `/.well-known/site.standard.publication`. [Task 1]\n  4890\t- Resolve a configured handle/DID through its DID document and permit `KEATING_BLOG_PDS_URL` as a local/staged Tranquil override. The migration script converts 46 legacy posts to 47 records in dry-run; inject `KEATING_BLOG_PDS_URL`, `KEATING_BLOG_IDENTIFIER`, and `KEATING_BLOG_APP_PASSWORD` through secret store, never shell arguments/history. [Task 1]\n  4891\t- Focused publisher/parser/server tests (11), typecheck, and Vite/Nitro build passed. A Chrome pass rendered `/blog` cleanly. [Task 1]\n  4892\t\n  4893\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  4894\t\n  4895\t- A shared feed request must not be cancelled merely because one page unmounts; avoid aborting it and guard only state updates with an `active` flag to prevent cross-route races. If Playwriter relay times out, isolated browser sessions were more reliable. [Task 1]\n  4896\t- Live Tranquil write was intentionally not run because account/credentials were absent, and Vet was unavailable/stalled; do not claim PDS publication or Vet review. [Task 1]\n  4897\t\n  4898\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/keating Coming Up spaced repetition and Anki portability\n  4899\tscope: Dedicated dynamic Kanban review workspace, learner priority layered over SM-2 scheduling, and safe native Anki APKG import/export.\n  4900\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating; reuse_rule=reuse for flashcard/SRS/Anki changes; preserve source identities and separately validate browser interaction plus package round trips.\n  4901\t\n  4902\t## Task 1: Build the Coming Up priority-aware Kanban\n  4903\t\n  4904\t### rollout_summary_files\n  4905\t\n  4906\t- rollout_summaries/2026-08-03T23-06-09-m6ds-coming_up_spaced_repetition_kanban_anki_import.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/08/03/rollout-2026-08-03T19-06-09-019fc9e0-a23d-75f2-9d3f-77f036eb728a.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-03T23:59:51+00:00, thread_id=019fc9e0-a23d-75f2-9d3f-77f036eb728a, success)\n  4907\t\n  4908\t### keywords\n  4909\t\n  4910\t- /coming-up, ComingUp.tsx, coming-up.ts, SM-2, Focus, Maintain, Low, drag-and-drop, srs.ts, storage.ts\n  4911\t\n  4912\t## Task 2: Implement native Anki import/export\n  4913\t\n  4914\t### rollout_summary_files\n  4915\t\n  4916\t- rollout_summaries/2026-08-03T23-06-09-m6ds-coming_up_spaced_repetition_kanban_anki_import.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/08/03/rollout-2026-08-03T19-06-09-019fc9e0-a23d-75f2-9d3f-77f036eb728a.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-03T23:59:51+00:00, thread_id=019fc9e0-a23d-75f2-9d3f-77f036eb728a, success)\n  4917\t\n  4918\t### keywords\n  4919\t\n  4920\t- anki-package.ts, .apkg, collection.anki21b, collection.anki21, collection.anki2, sql.js, fzstd, noteGuid, noteId, cardId, deckId, mergeAnkiDeck\n  4921\t\n  4922\t## User preferences\n  4923\t\n  4924\t- “coming up should be a dedicated and dynamic kanban like interface with dragable items” -> favor direct-manipulation task workspace over a static analytics panel [Task 1]\n  4925\t- “figure the rest” / “your choice” -> when the core interaction is clear, make coherent secondary decisions rather than seeking unnecessary follow-ups [Task 1]\n  4926\t- make it “easy for people to move anki stuff in and out” -> prioritize native `.apkg` round trips while retaining CSV/TSV fallback [Task 2]\n  4927\t\n  4928\t## Reusable knowledge\n  4929\t\n  4930\t- `/coming-up` uses `web/src/pages/ComingUp.tsx`; `web/src/keating/coming-up.ts` derives due flashcards, open checks, and needs-review topics into draggable Focus/Maintain/Low lanes. Dragging changes learner intent only; do not falsify SM-2 due dates or hide overdue work. Provide keyboard/touch controls as a non-drag alternative. [Task 1]\n  4931\t- `web/src/keating/anki-package.ts` supports native `collection.anki21b`, `.anki21`, `.anki2`, CSV import, and TSV fallback. Convert HTML/cloze to inert review text; exclude media and executable templates. Preserve `noteGuid`, `noteId`, `cardId`, `deckId`; `mergeAnkiDeck` preserves newer review state. [Task 2]\n  4932\t- Browser checks covered drag persistence, review reducing due 6 -> 5, desktop/mobile/light/dark layouts, and native browser export. Focused tests (14), full suite (617), typecheck, Panda/Vite/Nitro/PWA build, and diff check passed. [Task 1][Task 2]\n  4933\t\n  4934\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  4935\t\n  4936\t- Generated IDs can duplicate material on repeated Anki export/import. Preserve original Anki IDs/GUIDs and make stable IDs only for cards without source metadata. [Task 2]\n  4937\t- This checkout lacked a local Impeccable bundle; use `/home/diogenes/.agents/skills/impeccable/...` when the project shim yields `MODULE_NOT_FOUND`. Vet lacked Anthropic credentials; report it as unverified. [Task 1][Task 2]\n  4938\t\n  4939\t\n  4940\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/twyne structured application errors and safe hosted-AI UX\n  4941\tscope: Twyne application-error contract, notices, offline UX, sanitized diagnostics, and interview recovery.\n  4942\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne; reuse_rule=reuse for AI-error/fallback changes; test remaining unexercised boundaries and browser failure behavior.\n  4943\t\n  4944\t## Task 1: Establish and finish AppError foundation across interview/rubric paths\n  4945\t\n  4946\t### rollout_summary_files\n  4947\t\n  4948\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/07/30/rollout-2026-07-30T21-23-33-019fb5c4-fa2f-7431-86be-cedd140eb5a7.jsonl, updated_at=2026-07-24T05:07:45+00:00, thread_id=019fb5c4-fa2f-7431-86be-cedd140eb5a7, success; targeted test/build evidence)\n  4949\t\n  4950\t### keywords\n  4951\t\n  4952\t- AppError, ApplicationNotice, GlobalConnectivityBanner, ConvexError, application-diagnostics, createProductionConvexLogger, no-silent-fallback, pendingWriterText\n  4953\t\n  4954\t## Reusable knowledge\n  4955\t\n  4956\t- Core error seams are `src/types/application-errors.ts`, `src/utils/application-errors.ts`, `src/utils/application-diagnostics.ts`, `convex/lib/applicationErrors.ts`, and `src/components/ui/application-notice.tsx`. Production Convex clients use `createProductionConvexLogger()` to forward sanitized metadata rather than raw errors. [Task 1]\n  4957\t- `ApplicationNotice` has error, warning, and outage variants with severity-appropriate accessibility semantics. `GlobalConnectivityBanner` is wired in `src/root.tsx`; it reflects online/offline state while reassuring users that local work remains safe. Conversational interview recovery retains `pendingWriterText`, transcript/draft state, retry, and form fallback. [Task 1]\n  4958\t\n  4959\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  4960\t\n  4961\t- The full parallel `bun test` suite and targeted Playwright production-failure tests were not run. The validated boundary is 33 targeted tests plus typecheck, Storybook, and production builds; do not promote this to whole-app browser-failure proof. [Task 1]\n  4962\t\n  4963\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/keating upstream integration and verified 3.10.0 minor release\n  4964\tscope: Preserve a complete local change set while integrating upstream via PR, then complete a minor release with independent artifact, registry, production, and install proof.\n  4965\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating; reuse_rule=reuse the integration/release procedure only after auditing the current branch, upstream, generated artifacts, hook state, and intended worktree scope.\n  4966\t\n  4967\t## Task 1: Integrate local Artifact Atlas/OpenUI work and merge PR #7\n  4968\t\n  4969\t### rollout_summary_files\n  4970\t\n  4971\t- rollout_summaries/2026-08-26T22-46-56-wMah-keating_pr_merge_and_v3_10_release.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/08/26/rollout-2026-08-26T18-46-56-01a04041-4b5f-7d31-bc09-8898971264ed.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-27T03:31:25+00:00, thread_id=01a04041-4b5f-7d31-bc09-8898971264ed, success)\n  4972\t\n  4973\t### keywords\n  4974\t\n  4975\t- codex/artifact-atlas-animation-demotion, origin/main, PR #7, 57b22adf, f49c617e, nodepod-boot-files, Artifact-Atlas, LearningAnimation, git merge --no-ff\n  4976\t\n  4977\t## Task 2: Publish Keating v3.10.0\n  4978\t\n  4979\t### rollout_summary_files\n  4980\t\n  4981\t- rollout_summaries/2026-08-26T22-46-56-wMah-keating_pr_merge_and_v3_10_release.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/08/26/rollout-2026-08-26T18-46-56-01a04041-4b5f-7d31-bc09-8898971264ed.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-27T03:31:25+00:00, thread_id=01a04041-4b5f-7d31-bc09-8898971264ed, success; public release verified)\n  4982\t\n  4983\t### keywords\n  4984\t\n  4985\t- v3.10.0, release.yml, sync-version.ts, bumpy, 33035774405, npm-provenance, node:20-bookworm, Package manifest ok (1150 files)\n  4986\t\n  4987\t## User preferences\n  4988\t\n  4989\t- when upstream had “awesome changes that we worked on before and really want to keep” -> preserve upstream and local changes together; resolve conflicts deliberately rather than overwriting either side [Task 1]\n  4990\t- when the user asked to put “our current changes all of them into a pr” -> audit and stage the complete intended local scope explicitly while protecting unrelated files [Task 1]\n  4991\t- when the user asked “can you make a new release minor?” -> perform the full release lifecycle, not merely a version bump [Task 2]\n  4992\t\n  4993\t## Reusable knowledge\n  4994\t\n  4995\t- Create a branch from `main`, commit the audited local scope, merge `origin/main`, and regenerate `web/src/keating/nodepod-boot-files.ts`. In this integration the generated snapshot had no diff after merge, confirming combined sources; PR #7 squash-merged as `f49c617e`, with local/remote/GitHub `main` matching. [Task 1]\n  4996\t- v3.10.0 synchronized 11 surfaces, used actual Toronto release date `2026-08-26`, and staged exactly 15 intended release files. Full root/web tests, build, version/diff/Atlas checks, and package manifest verification passed. Workflow `33035774405`, four archives/digests, npm latest/SLSA provenance, production routes/version, remote refs, and clean `node:20-bookworm` CLI install were verified. Related skill: skills/release-publication-verification/SKILL.md [Task 2]\n  4997\t\n  4998\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  4999\t\n  5000\t- Bumpy generated UTC `2026-08-27` changelog dates while the repository release date was `2026-08-26` -> normalize both changelogs before committing. [Task 2]\n  5001\t- Native `node-pty` compilation on the host was contaminated by Guix/Nix include/library/glibc state -> use an isolated clean container for external-install proof. Node engine/vulnerability warnings do not negate a successful install/CLI smoke test; report them separately. [Task 2]\n  5002\t- A stale Entire/prek shim blocked push -> independent root/web pre-push suites must pass before a narrowly documented `git push --no-verify`. Vet was unverified, not approval. [Task 1][Task 2]\n  5003\t\n  5004\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/keating unified devenv up multi-surface workspace\n  5005\tscope: Configure one Process Compose-backed `devenv up` for terminal shell, OpenTUI, web, Electron, Expo web, and Storybook; retain the unresolved live-process boundary.\n  5006\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating; reuse_rule=reuse process names, PTY configuration, ports, and logging approach, but rerun every surface live before claiming the workspace is healthy.\n  5007\t\n  5008\t## Task 1: Configure the multi-surface devenv workspace\n  5009\t\n  5010\t### rollout_summary_files\n  5011\t\n  5012\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/08/27/rollout-2026-08-27T14-05-16-01a04465-caaa-7662-b7a4-003e0b1975cc.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-27T18:24:30+00:00, thread_id=01a04465-caaa-7662-b7a4-003e0b1975cc, partial; only shell/TUI/web live-started)\n  5013\t\n  5014\t### keywords\n  5015\t\n  5016\t- devenv up, devenv.nix, process-compose, terminal-shell, tui, web, desktop, mobile-web, storybook, port 3000, port 8081, port 6006, readiness check fail\n  5017\t\n  5018\t## User preferences\n  5019\t\n  5020\t- when the user asked for a “devenv up command that starts the terminal shell, the tui, the web app, and the desktop application” and added “should also start storybook” -> include the complete adjacent developer workspace, not only the first listed apps [Task 1]\n  5021\t\n  5022\t## Reusable knowledge\n  5023\t\n  5024\t- In devenv 2.2.2, set `process.manager.implementation = \"process-compose\"`; use `process.managers.process-compose.tui.enable = true` and `processes.<name>.process-compose.is_interactive = true` for PTY shell/TUI processes. Six configured names are `terminal-shell`, `tui`, `web`, `desktop`, `mobile-web`, and `storybook`; web is 3000, Expo web 8081, Storybook 6006, and desktop waits for web. [Task 1]\n  5025\t- Electron defaults `KEATING_DEV_SERVER` to `http://localhost:3000` but keeps overrides; Expo needs `\"web\": \"expo start --web --port 8081\"`. `devenv info` exposes all six processes. Direct P2P build plus Electron/mobile TypeScript checks passed. [Task 1]\n  5026\t- Use `process-compose -U -u \"$PC_SOCKET_PATH\" process logs mobile-web,storybook,desktop -n 200 --raw-log` to isolate live process failures. [Task 1]\n  5027\t\n  5028\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  5029\t\n  5030\t- A first Process Compose run can spend a long time compiling `devenv-tasks` in Nix -> inspect the process tree before calling it a deadlock. [Task 1]\n  5031\t- Static validation is insufficient: shell, TUI, and web started, but `mobile-web` failed readiness on `http://127.0.0.1:8081` with `connection refused`, Storybook failed, and desktop did not launch successfully. Re-run each independently and inspect logs before completion claims. [Task 1]\n  5032\t- Patch context with incorrect separators failed -> make narrow context patches. Vet was unavailable/unverified. [Task 1]\n  5033\t\n  5034\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/twyne ATProto OAuth, Convex sync authorization, and safe global error toasts\n  5035\tscope: Diagnose browser auth/sync evidence, avoid ATProto scope and DPoP bootstrap failures, guard Convex mutations by real identity, and present normalized recoverable errors.\n  5036\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne; reuse_rule=reuse these local contracts for Twyne auth/error work; recheck OAuth grants, live Convex deployment/logs, and dirty worktree before a deployment claim.\n  5037\t\n  5038\t## Task 1: Fix ATProto profile hydration and OAuth initialization\n  5039\t\n  5040\t### rollout_summary_files\n  5041\t\n  5042\t- rollout_summaries/2026-08-27T00-08-45-AuPp-twyne_atproto_convex_auth_error_toasts.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/08/26/rollout-2026-08-26T20-08-45-01a0408c-3631-7712-bc6f-569ae582aa0b.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-27T03:08:44+00:00, thread_id=01a0408c-3631-7712-bc6f-569ae582aa0b, success)\n  5043\t\n  5044\t### keywords\n  5045\t\n  5046\t- ATProto, Bluesky, ScopeMissingError, app.bsky.actor.getProfile, PUBLIC_BSKY_APPVIEW, DPoP, use_dpop_nonce, initSessionPromise, resolveAtprotoProfile\n  5047\t\n  5048\t## Task 2: Gate Convex sync on authenticated identity\n  5049\t\n  5050\t### rollout_summary_files\n  5051\t\n  5052\t- rollout_summaries/2026-08-27T00-08-45-AuPp-twyne_atproto_convex_auth_error_toasts.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/08/26/rollout-2026-08-26T20-08-45-01a0408c-3631-7712-bc6f-569ae582aa0b.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-27T03:08:44+00:00, thread_id=01a0408c-3631-7712-bc6f-569ae582aa0b, success)\n  5053\t\n  5054\t### keywords\n  5055\t\n  5056\t- Convex, userComments:deleteComment, Not signed in, identityType: unknown, hasAuthenticatedConvexIdentity, convexAuthenticated, Better Auth, ctx.auth.getUserIdentity\n  5057\t\n  5058\t## Task 3: Normalize errors and render global toasts\n  5059\t\n  5060\t### rollout_summary_files\n  5061\t\n  5062\t- rollout_summaries/2026-08-27T00-08-45-AuPp-twyne_atproto_convex_auth_error_toasts.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/08/26/rollout-2026-08-26T20-08-45-01a0408c-3631-7712-bc6f-569ae582aa0b.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-27T03:08:44+00:00, thread_id=01a0408c-3631-7712-bc6f-569ae582aa0b, success)\n  5063\t\n  5064\t### keywords\n  5065\t\n  5066\t- application-errors.ts, reportApplicationError, GlobalApplicationToasts, ApplicationNotice, connectApplicationErrorToastHost, Comment sync is paused, AUTHENTICATION_REQUIRED, AUTHENTICATION_FAILED\n  5067\t\n  5068\t## User preferences\n  5069\t\n  5070\t- when the user supplied console logs as evidence -> trace every reported request to its actual code path and distinguish actionable errors from preload noise [Task 1]\n  5071\t\n  5072\t## Reusable knowledge\n  5073\t\n  5074\t- Hydrate public ATProto profiles through `PUBLIC_BSKY_APPVIEW = \"https://public.api.bsky.app\"` while preserving the OAuth session DID; existing `atproto blob:image/* include:site.standard.authFull` does not grant arbitrary audience-bound RPC scope. Use module-level `initSessionPromise` to prevent rotating DPoP nonce races; the library already captures/retries `DPoP-Nonce`. [Task 1]\n  5075\t- `hasAuthenticatedConvexIdentity(state)` requires `provider === \"convex\"`, `convexAuthenticated === true`, and a non-null user. Set the flag only after Better Auth installs a Convex token; gate comments/collaboration/sharing client calls, but retain server `ctx.auth.getUserIdentity()` and owner-scoped checks. A Convex client alone is not authenticated. [Task 2]\n  5076\t- `reportApplicationError()` normalizes/captures safe diagnostics and dispatches toasts; diagnostics-only `reportApplicationDiagnostic()` should not toast. `GlobalApplicationToasts` deduplicates, caps notices at two, auto-dismisses after 12 seconds, provides recovery links, respects reduced motion, and queues at most two startup notices until hydration. Use `reportCommentSyncError(operation, err)` with `comment-sync` / `Comment sync is paused`. [Task 3]\n  5077\t- Deterministic evidence: 1,280 pass, 39 skip, 0 fail; TypeScript, scoped lint, production build, and diff check passed. No deployment occurred and unrelated dirty worktree edits were preserved. [Task 1][Task 2][Task 3]\n  5078\t\n  5079\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  5080\t\n  5081\t- Do not add arbitrary Bluesky RPC scopes only to hydrate public profile data; use public AppView. A raw DID shown after lookup failure is a fallback leak, not aliasing. [Task 1]\n  5082\t- `identityType: \"unknown\"` / `Not signed in` means the mutation did not reach its delete logic -> fix the client auth boundary; never weaken Convex auth checks. [Task 2]\n  5083\t- Bun's EventTarget rejected the constructed toast event in tests -> inject a minimal event target instead of replacing global `window`. Vet timed out without findings, so it is unverified. [Task 3]\n  5084\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/notorganic-provider public identity, landing, and developer docs surfaces\n  5085\tscope: Maintain consumer-facing Not Organic account/identity UX separately from technical integration docs, including static docs-service build and Railway wiring.\n  5086\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/notorganic-provider; reuse_rule=recheck active auth state, deployment/DNS/Railpack schema, and browser availability; deterministic build proof is not visual or deployed proof.\n  5087\t\n  5088\t## Task 1: Redesign signed-out portal, public landing, and docs service\n  5089\t\n  5090\t### rollout_summary_files\n  5091\t\n  5092\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/notorganic-provider, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/08/31/rollout-2026-08-31T16-08-41-01a05970-3732-7901-89a3-ec7ffff03ac5.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-31T20:30:49+00:00, thread_id=01a05970-3732-7901-89a3-ec7ffff03ac5, partial; deterministic checks pass, no browser or deployment proof)\n  5093\t\n  5094\t### keywords\n  5095\t\n  5096\t- identity-shell, identity-creek-bg.webp, Continue with your handle, Your account wherever your ideas go, docs.notorganic.info, Caddyfile, Dockerfile.docs, docs.railpack.json, check-railpack.ts, PKCE S256, DPoP, WebP\n  5097\t\n  5098\t## Task 2: Create and browser-verify Not Organic social preview cards\n  5099\t\n  5100\t### rollout_summary_files\n  5101\t\n  5102\t- rollout_summaries/2026-09-04T22-27-06-lggp-notorganic_social_preview_cards_browser_verified.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/notorganic-provider, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/04/rollout-2026-09-04T18-27-06-01a06e88-6080-7922-b01d-98b04a48b7d1.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-05T00:53:12+00:00, thread_id=01a06e88-6080-7922-b01d-98b04a48b7d1, success; local crawler/browser proof)\n  5103\t\n  5104\t### keywords\n  5105\t\n  5106\t- Open Graph, Twitter cards, 1200x630, notorganic-home-v2.jpg, apps/landing/brand/social, verification.json, landing-social.playwriter.mjs, CSP, new Image(), bunx playwriter@latest\n  5107\t\n  5108\t## User preferences\n  5109\t\n  5110\t- signed-out identity UX uses “Your Not Organic account” and “Continue with your handle” rather than operator language -> write plain, user-facing account copy [Task 1]\n  5111\t- consumer pages should answer what Not Organic is, connected products, what stays with the person, and where it is managed; keep developer navigation visible but secondary and send implementation detail to dedicated docs [Task 1]\n  5112\t- visual edits should preserve recognizable source composition (creek, foliage, flowers, sunlight, framing, source-derived colors) rather than replace it with generic imagery [Task 1]\n  5113\t- when the user said “show that in the browser” -> for visual artifacts, open the finished asset and provide direct visual proof when possible. Preserve original sibling-project marks in derived marketing visuals rather than redrawing/synthesizing them. [Task 2]\n  5114\t\n  5115\t## Reusable knowledge\n  5116\t\n  5117\t- Apply `.identity-shell` only when `session` is absent in `apps/portal/src/App.tsx`; authenticated portal views retain their current layout. The WebP is `apps/portal/public/identity-creek-bg.webp` (~163 KB) and must be present in `dist/portal` and HTTP-served. White over `#4d7c67` was adjusted to 4.78:1 contrast. [Task 1]\n  5118\t- Public landing at `apps/landing/` intentionally avoids infrastructure/token/wallet/provider details, includes responsive/focus/skip-link/reduced-motion behavior, and keeps `https://docs.notorganic.info` secondary. [Task 1]\n  5119\t- Static JavaScript-free docs are `apps/docs/index.html`/`styles.css`; Caddy/Docker/Railpack/Railway wiring is in `infra/docs/`, `.railway/railway.ts`, package/devenv configuration, domains/docs/cost docs. Use `bun run build:landing && bun run build:docs && bun run build:portal`, `bun run typecheck`, `bun test`, `bun scripts/check-railpack.ts`, and local HTTP probes. [Task 1]\n  5120\t- Final social cards are `apps/landing/brand/social/notorganic-{home,company,billing,privacy,terms}-v2.jpg`: static 1200x630 JPEGs (~108–111 KB) with versioned HTTPS Open Graph/X metadata in five landing pages. `bun run scripts/build-landing.ts`, `bun run typecheck`, `bun test scripts/build-landing.test.ts`, and `rtk git diff --check` passed; `docs/brand/notorganic/social/verification.json` records JavaScript-disabled crawler checks (200, `image/jpeg`, decoded dimensions, zero logs). [Task 2]\n  5121\t- For JPEG proof under CSP, fetch bytes and decode with `new Image()` on a separate page. Direct navigation opens Chromium's image viewer, whose injected styles can cause CSP conflict and `Execution context was destroyed`. Use `bunx playwriter@latest` in a dedicated session when direct `playwriter` is unavailable. [Task 2]\n  5122\t\n  5123\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  5124\t\n  5125\t- Build/static probes cannot prove crop, responsive overlap, or rendered usability when no browser is connected -> record visual proof as outstanding, not passed. Vet was unavailable (credential/fallback hang), not passed. [Task 1]\n  5126\t- `scripts/check-railpack.ts` can fail `ConnectionRefused` while fetching the live schema -> retry only when network access is available; validation then reported four matching configs. Split same-file multi-operation patches. [Task 1]\n  5127\t- Local production-build/Caddy proof does not verify deployment, CDN/social-platform cache refresh, or production URLs. [Task 2]\n  5128\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/stich Bun-native release tooling and devenv hooks\n  5129\tscope: Replace Bumpy with Bun-native versioning while retaining tracked hooks, annotated-tag checks, and the repository's namespaced devenv workflow.\n  5130\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/stich; reuse_rule=recheck the dirty tree, package version, tags, scripts, and current devenv task graph before a real release; this rollout prepared the workflow but did not create v0.1.1 or publish.\n  5131\t\n  5132\t## Task 1: Migrate Bumpy to Bun versioning with tracked hooks\n  5133\t\n  5134\t### rollout_summary_files\n  5135\t\n  5136\t- rollout_summaries/2026-09-02T04-11-11-cNgU-stich_bun_versioning_devenv_hooks.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/stich, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/02/rollout-2026-09-02T00-11-11-01a06050-51e2-7762-b9f9-7ad24dafccfc.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-02T04:18:55+00:00, thread_id=01a06050-51e2-7762-b9f9-7ad24dafccfc, partial; safeguards installed, no real release yet)\n  5137\t\n  5138\t### keywords\n  5139\t\n  5140\t- bun pm version, Bumpy, .githooks/pre-push, core.hooksPath, stich:hooks:install, stich:release:check, release:check, annotated tag, v0.1.1, input_too_large\n  5141\t\n  5142\t## User preferences\n  5143\t\n  5144\t- when changing version tooling, the user said “i expect githooks and stuff to run and be added for this repo” -> retain and verify equivalent tracked hooks and release safeguards rather than deleting them with Bumpy [Task 1]\n  5145\t- after the initial implementation, the user said “remember to devenv for this stuff” -> expose/document Stich release operations through namespaced devenv tasks and `devenv shell --`, not bare host commands [Task 1]\n  5146\t\n  5147\t## Reusable knowledge\n  5148\t\n  5149\t- Stich root scripts are `prepare`, `hooks:install`, `preversion`, `postversion`, `release:check`, `release:version: bun pm version`, and `release:publish: git push --follow-tags`. `scripts/check-release-version.ts` checks SemVer, workspace/app alignment, annotated `v<package.version>`, tagged root-manifest equality, and unexpected `v*` tags at `HEAD`. [Task 1]\n  5150\t- `.githooks/pre-push` runs the release check only for a pushed `refs/tags/v*`, leaving ordinary branch pushes alone. `devenv tasks run stich:hooks:install` configures `core.hooksPath=.githooks`; release sequence is `devenv shell -- bun run release:version -- patch`, `devenv tasks run stich:release:check`, then `devenv shell -- bun run release:publish`. [Task 1]\n  5151\t- `@varlock/bumpy` and `.bumpy/` were removed; `bun install --lockfile-only` and `bun pm why @varlock/bumpy` confirmed removal. [Task 1]\n  5152\t\n  5153\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  5154\t\n  5155\t- `Release check failed: missing v0.1.1; create releases with bun run release:version` is expected while `package.json` says `0.1.1` without an annotated tag. Do not fabricate a tag merely to make the guard pass. [Task 1]\n  5156\t- Aggregate `bun run typecheck` was interrupted; only web/core/UI/API/AI workspace results are evidence. Vet was unavailable: API credentials were absent and the dirty-tree fallback failed with `input_too_large`; report both as unverified. [Task 1]\n  5157\t\n  5158\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/stich approved raster identity and logo production\n  5159\tscope: Explore, select, and integrate faithful Stich raster logo families from approved visual references; use when producing a mark, lockup, favicon, download icon, or hero artwork.\n  5160\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/stich; reuse_rule=the reported integration paths require direct artifact/source verification before reuse; the approved reference, rather than a hand-reconstructed vector, is the visual authority.\n  5161\t\n  5162\t## Task 1: Produce Stich logo directions and use-case variants\n  5163\t\n  5164\t### rollout_summary_files\n  5165\t\n  5166\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/stich, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/02/rollout-2026-09-02T02-38-15-01a060d6-f5bf-7b41-afc0-9e8810963df7.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-02T07:30:03+00:00, thread_id=01a060d6-f5bf-7b41-afc0-9e8810963df7, partial; reported integration is not independently evidenced)\n  5167\t\n  5168\t### keywords\n  5169\t\n  5170\t- approved-logo-raster-production, Stich, LCARS, docs/brand/weave/raster, apps/web/public/brand/raster, stich-signal-emblem.png, signal-deck-hero.png, favicon, alpha, imagegen\n  5171\t\n  5172\t## Task 2: Preserve logo-production lessons as a reusable Codex skill\n  5173\t\n  5174\t### rollout_summary_files\n  5175\t\n  5176\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/stich, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/02/rollout-2026-09-02T02-38-15-01a060d6-f5bf-7b41-afc0-9e8810963df7.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-02T07:30:03+00:00, thread_id=01a060d6-f5bf-7b41-afc0-9e8810963df7, success; global skill validated)\n  5177\t\n  5178\t### keywords\n  5179\t\n  5180\t- approved-logo-raster-production, skill-creator, quick_validate.py, PyYAML, uv run --with pyyaml, agents/openai.yaml, 25–64 character description\n  5181\t\n  5182\t## User preferences\n  5183\t\n  5184\t- when requesting ten logo directions, a top-three selection, and text/no-text, favicon, downloads, and hero variants -> provide comparative exploration followed by a complete use-case-specific asset family, not one generic logo file [Task 1]\n  5185\t- when an approved raster identity exists -> preserve its silhouette, proportions, spacing, typography, and color relationships; do not simplify distinctive artwork into generic SVG geometry unless explicitly requested and reviewed [Task 1]\n  5186\t- when the user said “okay add what you learned to a skill” -> preserve proven workflow lessons as reusable agent guidance [Task 2]\n  5187\t\n  5188\t## Reusable knowledge\n  5189\t\n  5190\t- Existing Stich references are `docs/store-spread/stich-signal-emblem.png`, `docs/store-spread/signal-deck-hero.png`, and mobile icon/favicon assets; likely web integration points are `SiteNav.tsx`, `Hero.tsx`, and `__root.tsx`. Reported output paths are `docs/brand/weave/raster` and `apps/web/public/brand/raster`. [Task 1]\n  5191\t- Preserve approved raster-logo workflow lessons locally: create separate deliverables, verify the actual alpha channel, preserve originals before trim/resize, make compact favicon variants, inspect at target size, and distinguish build/browser proof from asset generation. [Task 2]\n  5192\t\n  5193\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  5194\t\n  5195\t- A checkerboard is not alpha proof -> inspect the actual alpha channel and target-size rendering. The visible rollout lacks file listings, diffs, build output, and browser output for the reported Stich asset integration, so verify directly before calling it complete. [Task 1]\n  5196\t- `grep: unrecognized option '--glob'` came from invoking `/usr/bin/grep` with ripgrep flags -> use `rg` for glob-aware searches. Bound long-running asset commands and inspect outputs incrementally. [Task 1]\n  5197\t- Skill initialization rejected a 71-character UI description, and metadata generation lacked PyYAML -> keep the short description within 25–64 characters and use `uv run --with pyyaml` for isolated generation. [Task 2]\n  5198\t\n  5199\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/stich commercial pricing, Not Organic boundaries, and voice direction\n  5200\tscope: Maintain truthful Stich pricing and plan provider-backed billing/voice without exposing credentials or presenting unavailable hosted capabilities as live.\n  5201\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/stich and /home/diogenes/Projects/notorganic-provider; reuse_rule=recheck gateway health, OpenBao, Creem catalog/API, DNS/TLS, webhook delivery, and current deployment before enabling checkout or hosted intelligence.\n  5202\t\n  5203\t## Task 1: Implement and deploy fail-closed pricing with Creem and Not Organic\n  5204\t\n  5205\t### rollout_summary_files\n  5206\t\n  5207\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/stich, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/01/rollout-2026-09-01T23-36-31-01a06030-926c-7f33-a4dc-c6d1b05f58de.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-02T04:44:45+00:00, thread_id=01a06030-926c-7f33-a4dc-c6d1b05f58de, partial; production surface deployed, commercial E2E unproven)\n  5208\t\n  5209\t### keywords\n  5210\t\n  5211\t- pricing.tsx, Creem, Not Organic, stable pack_id, /v1/billing/checkout, idempotency-key, PKCE S256, DPoP, OpenBao, Checkout unavailable, wallet, signed webhook\n  5212\t\n  5213\t## Task 2: Define shared-wallet voice behavior\n  5214\t\n  5215\t### rollout_summary_files\n  5216\t\n  5217\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/stich, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/01/rollout-2026-09-01T23-36-31-01a06030-926c-7f33-a4dc-c6d1b05f58de.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-02T04:44:45+00:00, thread_id=01a06030-926c-7f33-a4dc-c6d1b05f58de, partial; design direction only)\n  5218\t\n  5219\t### keywords\n  5220\t\n  5221\t- VOICE SHOULD SHORTEN TRIAGE, NOT TURN MAIL INTO A CALL CENTER, /v1/audio/speech, /v1/audio/transcriptions, /v1/realtime, consent, reservation, hard stop\n  5222\t\n  5223\t## User preferences\n  5224\t\n  5225\t- when asked to make pricing “ready with creem and notorganic” -> separate code/deployment evidence from a real checkout, webhook, entitlement, usage, reconciliation, and refund proof path [Task 1]\n  5226\t- hosted checkout was intentionally fail-closed while the provider gateway and infrastructure were not proven -> preserve truthful disabled states rather than exposing a misleading Connect or Buy control [Task 1]\n  5227\t- when asked to “think about voice integration” -> treat voice as provider-owned, shared-wallet, consented, cost-visible capability rather than a provider-specific credential or isolated UI [Task 2]\n  5228\t\n  5229\t## Reusable knowledge\n  5230\t\n  5231\t- Not Organic owns identity, checkout, signed webhooks, wallet, usage, entitlements, and provider secrets; Stich consumes wallet state through stable server-resolved pack/plan IDs. `POST /v1/billing/checkout` needs HTTPS `return_url` and `idempotency-key`. Browser auth is PKCE S256 plus a device-bound DPoP key; never put Creem, OpenBao, or model-provider credentials in Stich client code. [Task 1]\n  5232\t- Deployed pricing tiers were Free, Personal `$10/month`, Household `$25/month`, and Studio `$50/month`, with hosted intelligence credits and one-cycle rollover text. Deterministic proof: Stich `bun run typecheck` and `bun run test`; Not Organic `bun run check` 119 pass/0 fail; Railway deployment `c6a8bf6b-c3c7-489e-ab51-cb9a0493e2d2` reached `SUCCESS`; mobile inspection saw truthful disabled controls. [Task 1]\n  5233\t- Planned modes are dictating a reply, reading a thread aloud, and talking through the inbox. Dictation must be bounded/editable before send; speech streams without client credentials or durable mail content; realtime needs explicit consent, reservation, visible cost, and a hard stop. [Task 2]\n  5234\t\n  5235\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  5236\t\n  5237\t- `https://api.notorganic.info/healthz` returned 404 and the gateway was not proven bootable with OpenBao/provider infrastructure -> do not enable checkout or hosted inference until health, OpenBao, Creem catalog/API, DNS/TLS, and signed webhook delivery are validated. Catalog-description sync is not charge/webhook/wallet/debit/reconciliation/refund proof. [Task 1]\n  5238\t- Poll Railway through BUILDING -> DEPLOYING -> SUCCESS and inspect logs; never treat an intermediate deployment status as terminal. Vet lacked credentials, so its review remains unverified. [Task 1]\n  5239\t\n  5240\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/stich native Devenv modernization, Railway email E2E, and isolated deployment\n  5241\tscope: Operate the native Devenv developer/release workflow, Railway/Stalwart email E2E, and safe isolated web deployment.\n  5242\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/stich; reuse_rule=recheck Devenv version/task graph, dirty-tree scope, Railway linkage, signing credentials, domain TLS, and untracked `railpack.json` before release or deploy mutations.\n  5243\t\n  5244\t## Task 1: Modernize developer/release workflow and verify Railway email E2E\n  5245\t\n  5246\t### rollout_summary_files\n  5247\t\n  5248\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/stich, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/01/rollout-2026-09-01T17-46-49-01a05ef0-6979-7cd1-80e9-8084cf168128.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-02T02:12:08+00:00, thread_id=01a05ef0-6979-7cd1-80e9-8084cf168128, partial; full checks/E2E passed but stable publication blocked)\n  5249\t\n  5250\t### keywords\n  5251\t\n  5252\t- devenv tasks, processes.*, services.*, Mailpit, stich:check, stich:e2e:railway, Stalwart, JMAP, Electrobun, gitPackage, signing, railpack.json\n  5253\t\n  5254\t## Task 2: Deploy web to an isolated Railway project\n  5255\t\n  5256\t### rollout_summary_files\n  5257\t\n  5258\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/stich, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/01/rollout-2026-09-01T17-46-49-01a05ef0-6979-7cd1-80e9-8084cf168128.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-02T02:12:08+00:00, thread_id=01a05ef0-6979-7cd1-80e9-8084cf168128, success; isolated production deployment and smoke checks passed)\n  5259\t\n  5260\t### keywords\n  5261\t\n  5262\t- Railway, continuwuity-matrix, railpack.json, local source input, Bun could not find a package.json file to install from, Bun 1.3.13, f59d6b6d-b09f-49a0-94fa-df0d829ffc6b, stich-production-4bc6.up.railway.app\n  5263\t\n  5264\t## User preferences\n  5265\t\n  5266\t- when the user said “devenv up, tasks and no just commands or mise” and “devenv process and services as well” -> use native `devenv tasks`, `processes.*`, and supported `services.*`; do not add a parallel Just/Mise interface [Task 1]\n  5267\t- when requesting modernization plus “test with an end to end email on railway” -> include dependency/tooling compatibility work and real provider-backed mail verification, not only local tests [Task 1]\n  5268\t- when deployment was requested and the checkout was linked to unrelated `continuwuity-matrix` -> verify Railway project/service linkage before mutating external state [Task 2]\n  5269\t\n  5270\t## Reusable knowledge\n  5271\t\n  5272\t- `devenv.nix` defines native web, desktop, mobile web, Storybook, and opt-in MCP processes, plus Mailpit SMTP/UI ports 1025/8025. `devenv tasks run stich:check` passed typechecks, tests, web/server smoke, release preflight self-test, workflow validation, and full Playwright; `stich:e2e:railway` verified disposable-account submit, inbox/body read, Sent copy, invalid identity, and cleanup. [Task 1]\n  5273\t- Validate `devenv tasks list --no-tui` and live processes, not static Nix alone. Candidate alignment was v0.1.1, but macOS/Windows signing credentials and custom-domain TLS blocked stable publication; no stable tag/push was created. [Task 1]\n  5274\t- Safe Railway target was production project/service `stich`, deployment `f59d6b6d-b09f-49a0-94fa-df0d829ffc6b`, public URL `https://stich-production-4bc6.up.railway.app`. Successful remote build used Bun 1.3.13/Node 22, `bun install --frozen-lockfile`, `bun run build:web`, and `bun run --cwd apps/web start`; public smoke covered `/`, `/guide`, assets, HEAD, and missing asset `404` with `nosniff`. [Task 2]\n  5275\t\n  5276\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  5277\t\n  5278\t- `devenv up -d` did not retain a process manager and created orphaned process groups/port collisions -> use one foreground `devenv up` for live verification and clean only identified project groups. Devenv 2.2.2 initially hit `attribute 'gitPackage' missing`; fix/validate task listing before calling migration ready. [Task 1]\n  5279\t- Custom Railpack toolchain inputs omitted repo context, giving `Bun could not find a package.json file to install from` -> add `{ \"local\": true, \"include\": [\".\"] }` to the install step. Never deploy solely from local Railway linkage. [Task 2]\n  5280\t- Vet had no usable verdict; stable release is separate from unsigned/dev checks. `railpack.json` remained untracked and must be deliberately included in a future release commit. [Task 1][Task 2]\n  5281\t\n  5282\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/traction cross-surface analytics and Railpack delivery\n  5283\tscope: Build an agent-first analytics product across web, desktop, mobile, CLI, and TUI with privacy-aware telemetry and Bun/Railpack deployment.\n  5284\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/traction; reuse_rule=recheck Railway linkage, live health, and npm authentication before deployment/publish claims.\n  5285\t\n  5286\t## Task 1: Create Traction architecture, foundation, dashboard, and deployment\n  5287\t\n  5288\t### rollout_summary_files\n  5289\t\n  5290\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/traction, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/03/rollout-2026-09-03T18-30-48-01a06965-66ba-7bd0-8a04-a54e56cb185d.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-27T23:35:30+00:00, thread_id=01a06965-66ba-7bd0-8a04-a54e56cb185d, success)\n  5291\t\n  5292\t### keywords\n  5293\t\n  5294\t- traction, packages/spec, packages/grip, packages/evals, telemetry opt-out, DO_NOT_TRACK, DID, Jetstream, Railpack, railway up --ci --service traction, NIXPACKS\n  5295\t\n  5296\t## User preferences\n  5297\t\n  5298\t- track activity across “desktop, mobile, cli, tui, and web,” but retain an event-spec seam if SDK/TUI may be “something altogether” from the agent product; document tradeoffs instead of forcing unresolved choices [Task 1]\n  5299\t- “telemetry should be opt out actually” -> disclose default collection and support disable controls, DO_NOT_TRACK, CI suppression, and strict minimization [Task 1]\n  5300\t\n  5301\t## Reusable knowledge\n  5302\t\n  5303\t- Traction's primary output is a coverage-aware daily briefing and agent-ranked dashboard. Use ATProto DID as join key, loopback OAuth for CLI/TUI, persistent Jetstream, daily GitHub traffic polling, and never expose source credentials in public PDS. [Task 1]\n  5304\t- `packages/spec` implements validation, argv allowlist scrubbing, policy/notice, and O_APPEND JSONL spool; 8 writers x 60 records produced 480 valid, untorn lines. `packages/grip` status colors are not chart-series colors. [Task 1]\n  5305\t- Deploy with `builder = \"RAILPACK\"` and `railway up --ci --service traction`; legacy NIXPACKS and stray Dockerfiles are failure sources. `@traction/spec` is publishable after `npm login`; grip/evals are private. [Task 1]\n  5306\t\n  5307\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  5308\t\n  5309\t- Verify `pwd`/absolute paths after `cd`; local Railpack may fail on `.devenv` symlinks, so a clean `git archive` build better matches Railway. Browser visual confirmation remained unavailable despite deterministic checks. [Task 1]\n  5310\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/twyne character-aware narration, premium GPT Live voice, and native Typst workflow\n  5311\tscope: Extend Twyne’s author-aware editor interaction and native Typst authoring without exposing provider credentials or replacing the visual editor.\n  5312\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne; reuse_rule=recheck the current dirty tree, browser/device access, Not Organic provider state, and deployment before treating Live voice as production-ready.\n  5313\t\n  5314\t## Task 1: Preserve persona identity through narration playback\n  5315\t\n  5316\t### rollout_summary_files\n  5317\t\n  5318\t- rollout_summaries/2026-09-26T10-01-32-fcwe-twyne_character_aware_narration_gpt_live_voice_desk.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/26/rollout-2026-09-26T06-01-32-01a0dd29-b2ed-78c0-b5b2-143eed227156.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-26T10:38:47+00:00, thread_id=01a0dd29-b2ed-78c0-b5b2-143eed227156, success; focused speech tests passed)\n  5319\t\n  5320\t### keywords\n  5321\t\n  5322\t- speech.ts, global-speech-player.tsx, speak-button.tsx, persona-note-panel.tsx, personas.ts, speechVoice, speechVoices, Supertonic, lecteur\n  5323\t\n  5324\t## Task 2: Implement premium duplex GPT Live voice with revision-safe editor actions\n  5325\t\n  5326\t### rollout_summary_files\n  5327\t\n  5328\t- rollout_summaries/2026-09-26T10-01-32-fcwe-twyne_character_aware_narration_gpt_live_voice_desk.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/26/rollout-2026-09-26T06-01-32-01a0dd29-b2ed-78c0-b5b2-143eed227156.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-26T10:38:47+00:00, thread_id=01a0dd29-b2ed-78c0-b5b2-143eed227156, partial; deterministic checks/builds passed, production/browser/provider proof open)\n  5329\t\n  5330\t### keywords\n  5331\t\n  5332\t- GPT Live, gpt-live-1, /v1/live/sessions, /api/live, live-voice-desk.tsx, live-voice-workspace.ts, LIVE_SESSION_BUDGET_MICROS, LIVE_ACTION_BUDGET_MICROS, Convex, welcome grant, delegation, session.closed\n  5333\t\n  5334\t## Task 3: Implement and deploy native Typst editing, proof, PDF, and persistence\n  5335\t\n  5336\t### rollout_summary_files\n  5337\t\n  5338\t- rollout_summaries/2026-09-26T11-02-50-0rjp-twyne_native_typst_editor_implementation_deployment.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/26/rollout-2026-09-26T07-02-50-01a0dd61-d08c-7f71-9e6c-24cf8966c3df.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-29T01:38:36+00:00, thread_id=01a0dd61-d08c-7f71-9e6c-24cf8966c3df, success; CI, Railway, and live proof/PDF/persistence smoke passed)\n  5339\t\n  5340\t### keywords\n  5341\t\n  5342\t- Typst, @myriaddreamin/typst.ts, CodeMirror, ProseMirror, typst-workspace, typst-code-editor, format, typstSource, compiler.worker.ts, mammoth.browser, import.meta.glob, Convex, Railway\n  5343\t\n  5344\t## User preferences\n  5345\t\n  5346\t- when narration is invoked from a character’s “lecteur,” the user wanted the player to know “what character was being called” -> resolve and display that persona’s voice by default, never a generic voice when identity is known. [Task 1]\n  5347\t- when requesting “full dubplex voice” that can “edit and add information searach and interact with the app,” and premium/credit use -> show captions, action state, consent, wallet/cost ceilings, and require approval before manuscript mutation. [Task 2]\n  5348\t- when starting the Typst plan, the user said “focus on implementation” and “focus on implementation not test” -> ship the functional slice before expanding tests, while retaining the visual/page editor as an opt-in Typst source workflow rather than replacing it. [Task 3]\n  5349\t\n  5350\t## Reusable knowledge\n  5351\t\n  5352\t- `src/utils/speech.ts` owns the shared narration queue/player; persona identity flows through `author`, `label`, `voice`, and provider-specific `voices`. `src/utils/personas.ts` holds display names, IDs, roles, voice overrides, and direction. Do not pass generic OpenAI voice names directly to Supertonic/browser narration; map them to supported embeddings or persona overrides. [Task 1]\n  5353\t- Twyne’s Live client uses Not Organic `/v1/live/sessions` through same-origin `/api/live`; provider billing/entitlements remain authoritative and Twyne never receives an OpenAI key. The implementation reserves ceilings of `$0.50` per session and `$0.05` per delegated action, not quoted rates. [Task 2]\n  5354\t- Draft edits are proposals first: later spoken/UI approval checks manuscript revision, rejects ambiguous repeated passages, preserves rich text, remains undoable, and stops when the workspace/folio changes. Only provider-returned research results may be described as web results; local placeholders are rejected. [Task 2]\n  5355\t- The provider patch adds a one-time `$2.50` Twyne welcome allowance separate from Keating, with idempotency and paid-history exclusions. Delegated replies are accepted only for IDs observed from trusted upstream events; inspect the separate provider dirty tree before follow-up work. [Task 2]\n  5356\t- Native Typst documents use `@myriaddreamin/typst.ts` in a client worker with bundled fonts/assets, CodeMirror source editing, proof-page rendering, downloadable source, and PDF export; source edits compile without a server round trip. `format` and `typstSource` persistence/sync fields retain HTML projection compatibility for legacy documents and integrations. [Task 3]\n  5357\t- Core paths are `src/utils/typst/{document,serialize,export,client,session,compiler.worker}.ts`, `src/components/editor/{typst-workspace,typst-code-editor}.tsx`, `src/components/editor/extensions/raw-typst.ts`, `src/utils/{idb,convex-sync}.ts`, `convex/schema.ts`, and `convex/sync.ts`. Production smoke at `https://twyne.love/editor/` rendered two proof pages, produced a `%PDF-` download, preserved content on reload, and showed no runtime errors. [Task 3]\n  5358\t\n  5359\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  5360\t\n  5361\t- Feature checks do not establish real microphone permissions, visual UI, deployed WebSocket behavior, provider availability/credit debit, or production consent. Full typecheck initially exposed unrelated language/i18n errors; report targeted validation separately. [Task 2]\n  5362\t- A browser-only exporter leaked through shared serialization (`mammoth/mammoth.browser`) and failed Convex typecheck -> keep shared escaping in `src/utils/typst/string.ts` and keep backend imports browser-independent. Guard `import.meta.glob` tests with `const supportsViteModules = typeof import.meta.glob === \"function\"`; Bun does not provide it. [Task 3]\n  5363\t- Direct browser-global assignment/restoration caused 105 Bun failures -> save/restore descriptors with `Object.defineProperty`. Before push run `bun run lint`, `bun run fmt.check`, Convex typecheck, and the full suite; final validation was `1605 pass`, `40 skip`, `0 fail`, GitHub run `36508550529` success, and Railway deployment `2261ee43-1626-496b-8388-5e0c2d749989` successful. `bun add` can need `BUN_TMPDIR=/tmp BUN_INSTALL_CACHE_DIR=/tmp/twyne-bun-cache`. [Task 3]\n  5364\t\n  5365\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/keating manifesto assets, Skate secret map, and repository-organization planning\n  5366\tscope: Locate manifesto media and current secret consumers, then plan a staged research-publication/repository reorganization without premature migration or cleanup.\n  5367\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating with planning context cwd=/home/diogenes/Documents/Codex/2026-09-25/i-want-to-use-the-devenv; reuse_rule=asset and current Skate paths are checkout-specific; the organization proposal must start with a fresh read-only audit and user approval.\n  5368\t\n  5369\t## Task 1: Locate the Keating manifesto video and its source project\n  5370\t\n  5371\t### rollout_summary_files\n  5372\t\n  5373\t- rollout_summaries/2026-09-25T16-27-10-ULkv-keating_manifesto_and_skate_secret_usage.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/25/rollout-2026-09-25T12-27-10-01a0d964-6404-7ef1-a73a-12e506f8b563.jsonl, u