anization, research publishing, output folders, video work, blog posts, scripts, hidden folders, taxonomy, migration plan\n  5399\t\n  5400\t## User preferences\n  5401\t\n  5402\t- when considering Keating organization, the user said: “We will think through an organization plan for this” -> begin with discussion, inventory, a proposed structure, migration risks, and an approval checkpoint; do not move or delete files first. [Task 3]\n  5403\t- the user wants “getting the research side published and organized and making it easy to work on” -> make the plan connect research work to publication, with clear homes for blog posts, scripts, video work, and outputs. [Task 3]\n  5404\t- when asking where Skate is “used or mentioned” and where it “load[s] as an env var” -> search direct CLI calls, fallback environment variables, generated shell commands, and documentation. [Task 2]\n  5405\t\n  5406\t## Reusable knowledge\n  5407\t\n  5408\t- Published manifesto media is `web/public/tapes/keating-manifesto.mp4`; its source is `video/spotlights/manifesto/`, with docs-site copies under `scripts/docs-site/assets/tapes/` and web captions/poster under `web/public/tapes/captions/` and `web/public/tapes/posters/`. [Task 1]\n  5409\t- `scripts/on-device-site/public/methods/index.html:42`, generated by `scripts/on-device-site/build.py:589`, injects `TYPESAFE_API_KEY` from Skate. `src/core/skate-secrets.ts` safely returns `undefined` when `skate get` is unavailable/nonzero/empty; known provider entry names include `openai-api@secrets`, `fal_api_key@secrets`, `minimax@secrets`, `typesafe_api_key@secrets`, and `runpod_api_key@secrets`. [Task 2]\n  5410\t- Current planning scope is broader than tool configuration: multiple output folders, scattered video work, blog posts in a hidden/secret folder, miscellaneous scripts, hidden possibly-obsolete directories, and secret/environment injection. No inspection established what is active or obsolete. [Task 3]\n  5411\t\n  5412\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  5413\t\n  5414\t- Never print or persist secret values: use `skate list --keys-only`, not plain `skate list`. Exclude generated reports, dependencies, lockfiles, and build output early so secret/asset searches do not truncate. [Task 2]\n  5415\t- No organization inventory, proposal, migration, or validation was completed. First classify paths by usage/configuration evidence, trace build/publishing scripts and secret consumers, then present a staged preservation/rollback plan for approval before any migration. [Task 3]\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"     1\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/baste Makepad versus GPUI studio-framework selection\n     2\tscope: Choose a Rust GUI foundation for Baste’s native studio based on whether productivity workflows or expressive cross-platform graphics are primary.\n     3\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/baste; reuse_rule=confirm the current GPUI/GPUI Kit release and target platforms before implementation because GPUI is pre-1.0.\n     4\t\n     5\t## Task 1: Compare Makepad and GPUI for a Baste studio\n     6\t\n     7\t### rollout_summary_files\n     8\t\n     9\t- rollout_summaries/2026-10-04T04-46-42-dK0S-makepad_vs_gpui_baste_studio.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/baste, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/10/04/rollout-2026-10-04T00-46-42-01a1053c-5484-7860-b895-c654c9e25fd6.jsonl, updated_at=2026-10-04T04:47:19+00:00, thread_id=01a1053c-5484-7860-b895-c654c9e25fd6, success; direct framework comparison)\n    10\t\n    11\t### keywords\n    12\t\n    13\t- Makepad, GPUI, GPUI Kit, Rust GUI, Zed, Studio, WASM, native desktop, candidate grids, inspectors, generation queues\n    14\t\n    15\t## User preferences\n    16\t\n    17\t- when asking “makepad v gpui” -> give a direct comparative assessment and decision fit rather than starting implementation work [Task 1]\n    18\t\n    19\t## Reusable knowledge\n    20\t\n    21\t- GPUI is the Baste default for a dense native productivity studio: entities/shared state, declarative views, imperative custom elements, keyboard actions, async services, and testing support fit projects, candidate grids, inspectors, and generation queues. [Task 1]\n    22\t- Prefer Makepad when animated visual design, custom GPU graphics, or one UI shared across native/web/mobile is central; it is Rust-first with a live-editable/scriptable UI DSL, Studio workflow, GPU 2D/3D rendering, and broad targets. [Task 1]\n    23\t- GPUI Kit is separate from core GPUI; verify its exact matching version and accessibility/component capabilities instead of attributing them to GPUI itself. [Task 1]\n    24\t\n    25\t## Failures and how to do differently\n    26\t\n    27\t- GPUI is pre-1.0 with frequent breaking changes -> inspect the exact release/fork and Zed source before committing Baste architecture to an API or platform assumption. [Task 1]\n    28\t\n    29\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/notorganic-provider shared account knowledge connections for Keating and Twyne\n    30\tscope: Implement account-owned knowledge sources with app-specific grants, explicit tool consent, and fail-closed revocation across Not Organic, Keating, and Twyne.\n    31\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/notorganic-provider with integrations in /home/diogenes/Projects/{keating,twyne}; reuse_rule=retest current provider contracts, dirty diffs, deployment/CORS, and a real account before claiming cross-app readiness.\n    32\t\n    33\t## Task 1: Establish provider-owned shared knowledge and app access\n    34\t\n    35\t### rollout_summary_files\n    36\t\n    37\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/notorganic-provider, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/10/03/rollout-2026-10-03T08-22-46-01a101b7-83a5-7863-897a-869bf3d11c1b.jsonl, updated_at=2026-10-03T23:33:08+00:00, thread_id=01a101b7-83a5-7863-897a-869bf3d11c1b, partial; implementation/focused validation passed, deployment and real-account proof open)\n    38\t\n    39\t### keywords\n    40\t\n    41\t- knowledge-bases, account-sources, Google Drive, OAuth, PKCE S256, DPoP, consent, revocation, apps/portal, apps/gateway, Convex, GitNexus\n    42\t\n    43\t## Task 2: Integrate reviewed knowledge tools in Keating\n    44\t\n    45\t### rollout_summary_files\n    46\t\n    47\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/notorganic-provider, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/10/03/rollout-2026-10-03T08-22-46-01a101b7-83a5-7863-897a-869bf3d11c1b.jsonl, updated_at=2026-10-03T23:33:08+00:00, thread_id=01a101b7-83a5-7863-897a-869bf3d11c1b, partial; 53 focused tests/260 assertions, full web build blocked)\n    48\t\n    49\t### keywords\n    50\t\n    51\t- web/src/notorganic-provider/knowledge.ts, KnowledgeSources.tsx, browser-tools/knowledge.ts, exact-argument review, Google Drive Coming soon, knowledge.test.ts\n    52\t\n    53\t## Task 3: Integrate account sources and MCP review in Twyne\n    54\t\n    55\t### rollout_summary_files\n    56\t\n    57\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/notorganic-provider, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/10/03/rollout-2026-10-03T08-22-46-01a101b7-83a5-7863-897a-869bf3d11c1b.jsonl, updated_at=2026-10-03T23:33:08+00:00, thread_id=01a101b7-83a5-7863-897a-869bf3d11c1b, partial; 98 targeted checks/typechecks/builds passed, live gateway proof open)\n    58\t\n    59\t### keywords\n    60\t\n    61\t- convex/knowledge.ts, account-knowledge.ts, account-tool-review.tsx, Settings, Apparatus, Your MCP servers, sessionVersion, DPoP, CORS\n    62\t\n    63\t## User preferences\n    64\t\n    65\t- when asking for knowledge bases to “carry over” into Keating and Twyne and be “easy to add or revoke an apps access to them” -> default to account-level ownership, per-app grants, explicit revocation, and guided setup [Task 1]\n    66\t- when mentioning Google sign-in and easy connection setup -> include understandable consent/onboarding, not only API plumbing [Task 1]\n    67\t\n    68\t## Reusable knowledge\n    69\t\n    70\t- Not Organic is the control plane: portal sessions and upstream credentials stay server-owned; public clients validate HTTPS origins, same-origin callbacks, PKCE S256, narrow allowlisted scopes, and DPoP-bound tokens; gateway checks capabilities immediately before dispatch. [Task 1]\n    71\t- Google Drive remains unimplemented. The narrow researched direction is Google Picker with `drive.file`, and product UI must label it “Coming soon,” never as an available connector. [Task 1][Task 2]\n    72\t- Keating selects account sources, browses/reads resources, separately opts into tools, and reviews exact arguments; cancellation, account change, revocation, tool-definition change, and failed/lost-network calls fail closed. [Task 2]\n    73\t- Twyne trusted Convex actions bind verified DID/sessionVersion to fresh DPoP tokens. Research requires enabling research, choosing a source search tool, and selecting “Your MCP servers”; sign-out, revocation, and schema changes clear/fail closed. [Task 3]\n    74\t\n    75\t## Failures and how to do differently\n    76\t\n    77\t- GitNexus `ENOENT: .../.gitnexus/registry-lock` -> run `node .gitnexus/run.cjs analyze --index-only`, but treat absent/truncated graph edges as unknown and confirm with `rg`/source. Preserve unrelated dirty provider work; aggregate impact reports are not feature-local evidence. [Task 1]\n    78\t- Focused Keating validation does not prove web production readiness: pre-existing assistant-ui/PDF/router incompatibilities blocked the full web build, and neither deployment nor live-account flow was tested. [Task 2]\n    79\t- `ERR_CONNECTION_REFUSED` after an owned Twyne preview stopped is an environment/process condition, while localhost-to-deployed Convex CORS preflight must be verified separately; neither establishes deployed feature behavior. [Task 3]\n    80\t\n    81\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/notorganic-provider explainer-film production and range-aware review gallery\n    82\tscope: Produce several distinct Not Organic explainers grounded in verified brand/product evidence, then serve a local multi-project review gallery whose MP4s can seek reliably.\n    83\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/notorganic-provider; reuse_rule=recheck current brand capture, project paths, available media providers, and local server state before re-serving or making current product/payment claims.\n    84\t\n    85\t## Task 1: Create and verify three distinct Not Organic explainer films\n    86\t\n    87\t### rollout_summary_files\n    88\t\n    89\t- rollout_summaries/2026-10-03T13-30-10-G3qy-notorganic_explainer_films_and_range_aware_review_serving.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/notorganic-provider, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/10/03/rollout-2026-10-03T09-30-10-01a101f5-38b5-7d00-b9ff-d150957132ba.jsonl, updated_at=2026-10-03T23:02:48+00:00, thread_id=01a101f5-38b5-7d00-b9ff-d150957132ba, success; three masters and completion audit verified)\n    90\t\n    91\t### keywords\n    92\t\n    93\t- HyperFrames, Cartesia, fal, Seedance, H3, Lyria, notorganic.info, storyboard, moodboard, VERIFICATION.json, built-to-grow, model-that-keeps-learning\n    94\t\n    95\t## Task 2: Restore the local multi-project review gallery with byte ranges\n    96\t\n    97\t### rollout_summary_files\n    98\t\n    99\t- rollout_summaries/2026-10-03T13-30-10-G3qy-notorganic_explainer_films_and_range_aware_review_serving.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/notorganic-provider, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/10/03/rollout-2026-10-03T09-30-10-01a101f5-38b5-7d00-b9ff-d150957132ba.jsonl, updated_at=2026-10-03T23:02:48+00:00, thread_id=01a101f5-38b5-7d00-b9ff-d150957132ba, success; all 26 references and beginning/end ranges verified)\n   100\t\n   101\t### keywords\n   102\t\n   103\t- serve@14.2.6, HTTP 206, Accept-Ranges, Content-Range, port 3090, review-server.pid, serving-verification.json, HyperFrames Studio, http.server\n   104\t\n   105\t## User preferences\n   106\t\n   107\t- when requesting “don’t just try once—do several different videos” -> make genuinely distinct cuts, not one generic draft; provide creative intros/outros, moodboards, jingles, and storyboard guidance [Task 1]\n   108\t- when the audience is investors and developers and registered apps/payments matter -> separate cinematic company, developer-mechanism, and payments-launch narratives [Task 1]\n   109\t- when asking to bring serving back up -> verify both gallery HTML and actual MP4 seekability, not only an HTTP 200 page response [Task 2]\n   110\t\n   111\t## Reusable knowledge\n   112\t\n   113\t- Three verified masters are `notorganic-built-to-grow.mp4` (1:48), `notorganic-a-model-that-keeps-learning.mp4` (1:15), and `notorganic-for-a-lifetime.mp4` (49.3s), under the respective `videos/notorganic-{explainer,developer,payments}/renders/` directories. Brand capture lives under `videos/notorganic-explainer/capture/`; `tokens.json` and `asset-descriptions.md` are the routing artifacts. [Task 1]\n   114\t- Ground the work in the knot mark, forest/cream/lime palette, and authentic Twyne, Keating, Interleave, Stich, Voxq, and Baste marks. Keep payment language bounded as “launching this October”/planned, not production-payment proof. [Task 1]\n   115\t- `videos/notorganic-explainer/VERIFICATION.json` recorded `COMPLETE`, three masters, nine satisfied requirements, and 26 served gallery references. [Task 1]\n   116\t- Start the gallery from the `videos` directory with `bunx serve@14.2.6 .. --listen tcp://127.0.0.1:3090 --no-clipboard --no-port-switching`; use `scripts/serving-verification.json` to prove beginning/end byte ranges for every master. [Task 2]\n   117\t\n   118\t## Failures and how to do differently\n   119\t\n   120\t- HeyGen auth was unavailable and local Kokoro/MusicGen dependencies were absent -> use available generation paths and never claim those providers ran. [Task 1]\n   121\t- Python `http.server` can return 200 for HTML/video yet fail reliable seeking; use `serve@14.2.6` to obtain HTTP 206 range responses. HyperFrames Studio on 3091 registered only the explainer project, so use the standalone range-aware server for sibling developer/payments routes. [Task 2]\n   122\t\n   123\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/twyne editor responsiveness and Typst export parity\n   124\tscope: Keep the active Tiptap/Typst authoring path responsive while making proof and downloaded PDF match editor typography; use for per-keystroke work, explicit freshness boundaries, and drop-cap/export regressions.\n   125\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne; reuse_rule=reprofile the current editor path and re-run real compiler/browser checks before quoting performance or live deployment results.\n   126\t\n   127\t## Task 1: Diagnose, remove, and benchmark typing stalls\n   128\t\n   129\t### rollout_summary_files\n   130\t\n   131\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/10/03/rollout-2026-10-03T03-57-25-01a100c4-9324-7193-800f-e17e11a4d1a2.jsonl, updated_at=2026-10-03T09:02:50+00:00, thread_id=01a100c4-9324-7193-800f-e17e11a4d1a2, success; benchmarked and production-smoked)\n   132\t\n   133\t### keywords\n   134\t\n   135\t- Tiptap, ProseMirror, Typst, typing-latency, flushVisual, mark-anchor-widgets, input-to-frame, p99, test:typing, typing-performance.yml\n   136\t\n   137\t## Task 2: Fix proof/PDF drop-cap wrapping\n   138\t\n   139\t### rollout_summary_files\n   140\t\n   141\t- rollout_summaries/2026-10-03T09-01-49-2W9P-twyne_typst_drop_cap_pdf_wrapping.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/10/03/rollout-2026-10-03T05-01-49-01a100ff-8abc-7091-a412-416182641879.jsonl, updated_at=2026-10-03T12:28:19+00:00, thread_id=01a100ff-8abc-7091-a412-416182641879, success; compiler, PDF, and live proof verified)\n   142\t\n   143\t### keywords\n   144\t\n   145\t- Typst, drop-cap, twyne-opening-tokens, twyne-wrap-opening, theme.ts, serialize.test.ts, to-absolute, LD_LIBRARY_PATH, twyne-drop-cap.pdf\n   146\t\n   147\t## User preferences\n   148\t\n   149\t- when typing lag was “unacceptable” -> prioritize measured keystroke responsiveness and production/browser evidence, not static code inspection; acceptance was “feels fairly fast now and smooth” [Task 1]\n   150\t- when the opening drop cap was “not word wrapping properly in the proof or the pdf generation” -> preserve visual parity between editor, proof, and downloaded PDF [Task 2]\n   151\t\n   152\t## Reusable knowledge\n   153\t\n   154\t- `src/utils/typst/session.ts` defers visual-to-Typst reconciliation and exposes `flushVisual()` for source requests/edits, remote changes, saves, proof compilation, and lifecycle boundaries. Write view must not continuously compile hidden proof; opening Source/Proof schedules it. [Task 1]\n   155\t- Avoid whole-document per-transaction work: `mark-anchor-widgets.ts` builds contiguous anchor runs in one pass; `twyne-editor.tsx` throttles/debounces structural and derived-content refreshes; `client.ts` shares SVG definitions while splitting proof pages. [Task 1]\n   156\t- Typst has no native float around an initial. `theme.ts` tokenizes rich opening inline content, measures side-column width, splits at a word boundary beside the initial, then resumes full-width prose; preserve inline styling and cover it through the real bundled compiler in `serialize.test.ts`. [Task 2]\n   157\t- In this environment Sharp needs `LD_LIBRARY_PATH=/nix/store/0iv8glcslgfcgn371lbjr5jjw5a6cqir-gcc-15.3.0-lib/lib` for `bun test src/utils/typst/serialize.test.ts`. [Task 2]\n   158\t\n   159\t## Failures and how to do differently\n   160\t\n   161\t- Cold Vite/lazy-module compilation can make `.ProseMirror` absent before latency sampling -> use a separately bounded readiness wait (up to 60 seconds), record startup independently, and do not retry/average it into typing measurements. Activate Proof before asserting proof page count because Write view intentionally leaves proof stale. [Task 1]\n   162\t- `cannot compare ... with 2em` -> resolve relative Typst units with `.to-absolute()` before comparison. Metadata queries were unreliable; verify real export via compiler, PDF text extraction, and rendered-page inspection. [Task 2]\n   163\t\n   164\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/interleave-app warm tactile design direction\n   165\tscope: Shape a confirmed redesign that is warmer and less generic-Tailwind while retaining Interleave’s calm product usability and component-system constraints.\n   166\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/interleave-app; reuse_rule=use as a discovery/design brief only until a user confirms a direction; do not claim implementation or visual QA from this exploration.\n   167\t\n   168\t## Task 1: Explore a warm, less-corporate component language\n   169\t\n   170\t### rollout_summary_files\n   171\t\n   172\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/interleave-app, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/10/03/rollout-2026-10-03T09-04-53-01a101de-12f1-7153-8062-4c77fcba2816.jsonl, updated_at=2026-10-03T15:51:57+00:00, thread_id=01a101de-12f1-7153-8062-4c77fcba2816, partial; exploration only, no confirmed brief or implementation)\n   173\t\n   174\t### keywords\n   175\t\n   176\t- less corporrate and cold, generic tailwindy, handmade tech, tactile, thread-weave, gecko adhesion, PRODUCT.md, vision/README.md, product-spreads, styles.css\n   177\t\n   178\t## User preferences\n   179\t\n   180\t- when requesting “ideas pictures and plans” for something “less corporrate and cold and more warm and sensible with component design and feel” -> deliver concrete visual directions, component examples, imagery/probes, and an actionable plan—not abstract brand adjectives [Task 1]\n   181\t- when the UI feels “too generic tailwindy” -> audit repeated cards, dashboard framing, generic spacing, and default component grammar rather than only changing colors [Task 1]\n   182\t\n   183\t## Reusable knowledge\n   184\t\n   185\t- The established register is tactile, dimensional, alive, calm, intimate “handmade tech”; thread/weaving means continuity/craft and gecko adhesion means contact/micro-forces. Keep familiar controls, fixed type scale, semantic states, 150–250 ms motion, skeletons, WCAG AA, and reduced-motion support. [Task 1]\n   186\t- Shared material/tokens live in `packages/ui/src/styles.css`, web-specific styling in `apps/web/src/index.css`; visual references are `apps/web/public/brand/product-spreads/`, `apps/web/public/brand/interfaces/`, `docs/PRODUCT_SPREADS.md`, and Storybook. [Task 1]\n   187\t\n   188\t## Failures and how to do differently\n   189\t\n   190\t- For this ambiguous redesign, ask 2–3 focused discovery questions, create 2–4 distinct probes, present a compact brief, and wait for confirmation before coding. The prior rollout generated imagery too early and ended without the requested plan. [Task 1]\n   191\t- `/home/diogenes/Projects/interleave-app/.agents/skills/impeccable/scripts/context.mjs` does not exist -> use `/home/diogenes/.agents/skills/impeccable/scripts/context.mjs`. Browser snapshots were not established, and the captured final response was unrelated; neither is completion evidence. [Task 1]\n   192\t\n   193\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/baste side-conversation recovery, saved Projects, and Not Organic integration\n   194\tscope: Recover the correct interrupted Baste plan, continue its dirty checkout safely, validate Studio runtime behavior, and keep proposed Not Organic integration clearly short of production proof.\n   195\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/baste and Codex /side forks; reuse_rule=inspect current thread ancestry, both Baste/provider diffs, Devenv state, and live provider boundaries before continuing or claiming completion.\n   196\t\n   197\t## Task 1: Recover the interrupted Baste `/side` plan and restore the Projects preview\n   198\t\n   199\t### rollout_summary_files\n   200\t\n   201\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Documents/Codex/2026-10-01/as-you-interact-with-the-persona, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/10/01/rollout-2026-10-01T20-15-52-01a0f9f7-a90e-7313-903d-8303742eea01.jsonl, updated_at=2026-10-02T01:58:55+00:00, thread_id=01a0f9f7-a90e-7313-903d-8303742eea01, success; Baste Projects persistence and browser repair verified)\n   202\t\n   203\t### keywords\n   204\t\n   205\t- /side, Codex fork, parent thread, Cannot find module, Vite SSR cache, ProjectsFlow, projects.tsx, devenv processes restart site, studio-main, repair-lock\n   206\t\n   207\t## Task 2: Document Baste Devenv workflow and scaffold server-side Not Organic access\n   208\t\n   209\t### rollout_summary_files\n   210\t\n   211\t- rollout_summaries/2026-10-01T23-35-05-TyGU-baste_devenv_notorganic_integration_audit.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/baste, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/10/01/rollout-2026-10-01T19-35-05-01a0f9d2-5142-74a3-8cfb-0809f2fe0564.jsonl, updated_at=2026-10-02T00:27:35+00:00, thread_id=01a0f9d2-5142-74a3-8cfb-0809f2fe0564, partial; Baste build and hosted tests passed; provider registration/live flows remain unverified)\n   212\t\n   213\t### keywords\n   214\t\n   215\t- Baste, devenv up, baste:install, PKCE, DPoP, baste_session, Not Organic, hosted-generation, EAI_AGAIN, FIRST_PARTY_PRODUCTS, notorganic-provider.patch\n   216\t\n   217\t## User preferences\n   218\t\n   219\t- when recovering work, the user corrected: “claude was a totally separate thing i started a /side convo in this chat” -> identify the requested Codex `/side` conversation through fork/parent metadata rather than conflating similarly timed work [Task 1]\n   220\t- when continuing an interrupted plan, the user wanted the existing plan continued rather than a fresh redesign -> preserve shared dirty edits and recover task context before proposing replacement work [Task 1]\n   221\t- when asking whether there was `devenv up` and then asking to “get them done” -> prefer native Devenv processes/tasks over ad-hoc workflow commands for Baste [Task 2]\n   222\t- when requesting profile creation, sign-in, models, and payments and authorizing reuse from other projects -> reuse server-side PKCE/DPoP, wallet, model-catalog, and checkout boundaries; never put provider credentials or durable upstream tokens in the browser [Task 2]\n   223\t\n   224\t## Reusable knowledge\n   225\t\n   226\t- For an interrupted `/side` task, inspect fork/parent relationships and local session metadata first. `list_threads` accepts at most 50; the parent Baste thread was `01a0f9d2-5142-74a3-8cfb-0809f2fe0564`, while the unrelated HyperFrames/Claude session was separate. [Task 1]\n   227\t- Saved Projects live in `site/src/components/studio/flows/projects.tsx`, client API `site/src/lib/projects.ts`, server wiring `src/gui/api.ts`, and persistence `src/projects/{commands,store,repair-lock}.ts`. The verified implementation supports account/DID isolation, CSRF-protected writes, receipts, stale-revision rejection, restore, and lock recovery. [Task 1]\n   228\t- A missing import that now exists can be stale Vite SSR state: run `devenv processes restart site`, then inspect rendered HTML for `studio-main` and browser console—not just HTTP 200. The repair command is `node dist/src/projects/repair-lock.js --project <id> [--account <did>] --server-stopped`, only after every writer is stopped. [Task 1]\n   229\t- Intended Baste workflow is `devenv shell`, `devenv tasks run baste:install`, then `devenv up`; API/site are intended at 3456/5173, with `/gui/` and `/docs/`. It was documented but not runtime-verified in the scaffold rollout. [Task 2]\n   230\t- `src/notorganic/server.ts` keeps PKCE/DPoP transport, HttpOnly `baste_session`, CSRF, verified account/models/wallet/checkout calls server-side. Hosted generation/judgement fails closed and does not silently fall back to local BYOK; checkout accepts only provider-advertised IDs and HTTPS return origins. [Task 2]\n   231\t\n   232\t## Failures and how to do differently\n   233\t\n   234\t- A development error page can return HTTP 200 -> inspect `<title>Error</title>`, `Cannot find module`, expected app markers, and console output before treating the preview as healthy. [Task 1]\n   235\t- Do not infer production readiness from Baste build/test success: live signup, callback, funded generation, checkout, webhook, provider registration, and deployment were not verified. In-memory sessions expire after eight hours and need shared storage or affinity for multi-replica production. [Task 2]\n   236\t- `npm outdated` failed with `EAI_AGAIN`; retry with working registry access before calling dependencies current. Inspect Baste and provider `git status`/diff before assuming the long-running provider patch applied; provider typecheck still needed a `baste` first-party product entry. [Task 2]\n   237\t\n   238\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/keating documentation visual audit and Textbook/OpenTUI workshop\n   239\tscope: Keep Keating documentation grounded in current product evidence and use the offline Textbook workshop to exercise production Sacred TUI components alongside Storybook.\n   240\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating; reuse_rule=reinspect current docs/assets, OpenTUI/Textbook version compatibility, fixture coverage, and actual browser evidence before calling captures or interactivity current.\n   241\t\n   242\t## Task 1: Audit current documentation visuals and reorganize guidance\n   243\t\n   244\t### rollout_summary_files\n   245\t\n   246\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/10/01/rollout-2026-10-01T01-51-01-01a0f604-2553-7eb2-8f