896\t- when the user said “we want a way to accept plans, also i want plan changes to autonomous by default” -> default plan mutations to autonomous while exposing an explicit approval mode; add the lifecycle/browser hook for applied revisions [Task 1]\n   897\t- when the user supplied `POST https://api.notorganic.info/v1/public/token 401 (Unauthorized)` -> trace the actual browser-to-provider token exchange and separate incidental preload/service-worker warnings from the failing authentication path [Task 2]\n   898\t- when the user asked for a natural/context-related placement rather than videos “all at the bottom with a picker,” then said “i think the right place is in docs or in onboarding” -> prefer one contextual docs/onboarding launch film over a landing-page gallery; do not modify onboarding without approval [Task 3]\n   899\t- when the user asked to “make more videos and different ones” -> use clear, large visual storytelling and varied formats, not another near-duplicate feature explainer; Seedance 2.5 and Lyria 3.5 were explicitly approved within the shared budget ledger [Task 3]\n   900\t\n   901\t## Reusable knowledge\n   902\t\n   903\t- `projectActiveWork`/`formatActiveWork` deterministically select focus items, join presentation/attempt evidence, bound outline/interactions, and keep independence unknown. `openui-presentations` (DB v8) persists source linkage `{documentId, revision, nodeId}`; thread `TeachingPolicyTurn.activeWork` through policy, draft gate, evidence, prompts, and receipts. [Task 1]\n   904\t- `PlanChangeMode` is `autonomous | approval`; `applyPlanRevision` supports `complete-item`, `insert-prerequisite`, and `expand-item`, validates the full document and rejects invalid/duplicate/over-limit changes without partial application. `planChanges` defaults to `autonomous`; `PlanRevisionCard`, `revise_study_plan`, `plan_revised`, and `keating:plan-revised` connect UI/tool/lifecycle paths. [Task 1]\n   905\t- For a restored OAuth turn, use `sendRestored()` when the message never reached Flue and reserve `resume()` for a previously delivered message that failed later. Browser device sessions request `device_session: true`, hold refresh credentials in `localStorage`, refresh 15 seconds early with DPoP bound to the refresh token, deduplicate refreshes, revoke at sign-out, and preserve a session on transient network/5xx failures. [Task 2]\n   906\t- Keating sends `device_session: true` from `web/src/notorganic-provider/public-client.ts`; the diagnosed provider failure is `convex/publicClientAuth.ts` allowing device sessions only for `environment === \"mobile\"` while browser codes are `\"browser\"`. Permit browser and mobile while retaining short-lived legacy environment-less codes; this provider change was identified but not made/deployed. Keating's deployed recovery offers fresh Not Organic `Sign in / Sign up`, retains API-key re-entry for other providers, and preserves/retries pending chat correctly. [Task 2]\n   907\t- `getting-started.json` already embeds `keating-4-launch.mp4`; `learning.json` embeds feature spotlights. The launch file is 69.5 seconds by `ffprobe`, so user-facing copy says 70 seconds. Shared films live at `video/spotlights/{id}`; `gen-video.mjs` has aspect/model/cache/ledger controls, and docs now accept `16:9`, `9:16`, and `1:1`. [Task 3]\n   908\t\n   909\t## Failures and how to do differently\n   910\t\n   911\t- Focused green plan-revision tests did not clear the full suite: tests that replace `window`/`EventTarget` made `window.dispatchEvent(new CustomEvent(...))` reject events. Guard non-DOM dispatch or use the active window constructor; keep unrelated dirty-tree/GitNexus and pre-existing type failures separate. [Task 1]\n   912\t- Do not call the auth work committed or full-suite clean: 43 focused tests/typecheck passed, but the full suite’s five failures reproduced with changes stashed and no commit was made. [Task 2]\n   913\t- The deployed recovery does not prove real Bluesky/provider authorization: no real approval/callback occurred. Keep provider-side root cause separate from the unrelated preload warning. Popmelt toolbar proof is independent of optional Codex plugin registration; two full-repo missing-module/fixture errors were pre-existing. [Task 2]\n   914\t- Reject generated clips that shift Keating green to yellow/orange or invent text rather than global hue-correcting; Seedance was more faithful than H3. Do not treat an instrumental Whisper transcript as proof of vocals; warm Vite before screenshot capture, and use an explicit `silent` flag so music-only films are not muted. [Task 3]\n   915\t\n   916\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/dio-machines COSMIC Machines manager and Devenv development workflow\n   917\tscope: Build, launch, and develop the native local/remote Machines utility without losing unsaved configuration drafts or mistaking a headless build for GUI proof.\n   918\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/dio-machines; reuse_rule=reinspect pinned COSMIC dependencies, Devenv process state, current GPU/runtime libraries, and local/remote target requirements before changing or claiming the app workflow.\n   919\t\n   920\t## Task 1: Build native local/remote COSMIC Machines manager\n   921\t\n   922\t### rollout_summary_files\n   923\t\n   924\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/dio-machines, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/27/rollout-2026-09-27T18-51-29-01a0e510-f62a-79d3-91d4-edfad7d98e79.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-28T08:28:37+00:00, thread_id=01a0e510-f62a-79d3-91d4-edfad7d98e79, success; app tests, benchmark, optimized GPU launch, and Devenv checks passed)\n   925\t\n   926\t### keywords\n   927\t\n   928\t- apps/machines, COSMIC, libcosmic, wgpu, Vulkan, Intel(R) Iris(R) Xe Graphics (ADL GT2), runner.rs, manifest.rs, SSH, AppImages, app:test, app:benchmark\n   929\t\n   930\t## Task 2: Make `devenv up` the native COSMIC development workflow\n   931\t\n   932\t### rollout_summary_files\n   933\t\n   934\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/dio-machines, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/27/rollout-2026-09-27T18-51-29-01a0e510-f62a-79d3-91d4-edfad7d98e79.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-28T08:28:37+00:00, thread_id=01a0e510-f62a-79d3-91d4-edfad7d98e79, success; GUI process and opt-in checker verified)\n   935\t\n   936\t### keywords\n   937\t\n   938\t- rtk devenv up, machines, machines-check, processes.machines-check.watch.paths, config.devenv.root, devenv processes list, devenv processes restart machines, cargo check, README.md\n   939\t\n   940\t## User preferences\n   941\t\n   942\t- when choosing the manager scope, the user selected “Include remote computers” and “All three equally” for inspection, editing, and maintenance -> make local and SSH targets plus all three workflows first-class, rather than treating remote administration as an afterthought [Task 1]\n   943\t- when delegating visual direction with “best judgement most helpful” -> default to a calm, practical native utility, not a decorative infrastructure dashboard [Task 1]\n   944\t- when the user asked for “devenv up for doing this sort of stuff and deving on the cosmic app and stuff” -> use documented native Devenv processes/tasks as the canonical workflow; do not auto-restart the GUI on source edits because drafts must survive [Task 2]\n   945\t\n   946\t## Reusable knowledge\n   947\t\n   948\t- `apps/machines/` is a libcosmic application pinned at revision `8768bce2e2a4921ced57d95cff74bc7c92ef08b8` with `wgpu`. `runner.rs` owns local/SSH execution, host validation, atomic saves, external-change detection, and confirmation; SSH uses `BatchMode=yes`, stores no passwords, and root operations require a terminal TTY. [Task 1]\n   949\t- Cache manifest parsing in `apps/machines/src/manifest.rs`: 200 redraws measured about 74.1 ms with repeated parsing versus about 21 µs cached. `devenv tasks run app:test` passed 17 Rust plus 3 Python safety tests; normal optimized launch selected Intel Iris Xe through Vulkan/Mesa 25.1.9. [Task 1]\n   950\t- `devenv.nix` supplies `machines` (optimized GUI) and opt-in `machines-check` (compile checks). The checker watches absolute `${config.devenv.root}/apps/machines/{src,scripts,Cargo.toml,Cargo.lock}` paths and intentionally never restarts the GUI. Use `rtk devenv up`, or `rtk devenv up machines machines-check`; then use `rtk devenv processes restart machines|logs machines|attach`, `rtk devenv down`, and `rtk devenv tasks run app:test`. Root `README.md` and `apps/machines/README.md` are the operational source. [Task 2]\n   951\t\n   952\t## Failures and how to do differently\n   953\t\n   954\t- Plain/offline Cargo builds can inherit the mixed Nix/Guix environment and fail on `libgcc_s.so.1` -> build in the pinned `devenv.nix` app environment. For GPU launches, Fedora Vulkan ICD dependencies can be hidden by Nix `LD_LIBRARY_PATH` -> scope Fedora driver paths to the final GUI process and keep matching Nix glibc first. [Task 1]\n   955\t- Makepad headless rendering had Linux modules gated out -> it is not evidence that the native COSMIC UI started. Verify an optimized real GUI launch and app log instead. [Task 1]\n   956\t- Relative `processes.machines-check.watch.paths` causes `...is not of type absolute path` -> use `${config.devenv.root}/...`. `devenv processes list` fails with no manager -> start `devenv up -d` first. [Task 2]\n   957\t\n   958\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/keating subscription value and offline-edition validation\n   959\tscope: Evaluate a compelling recurring Keating offer and validate a paid offline local-model edition before pricing, training, or hardware-support claims.\n   960\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating; reuse_rule=recheck current plan/catalog economics and current model documentation before changing pricing or publishing hardware requirements.\n   961\t\n   962\t## Task 1: Assess subscription value and $150 offline local-model edition\n   963\t\n   964\t### rollout_summary_files\n   965\t\n   966\t- rollout_summaries/2026-09-27T05-32-32-lTig-keating_subscription_offline_edition_monetization.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/27/rollout-2026-09-27T01-32-32-01a0e159-c770-7e33-8611-d18bf7cc6630.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-27T05:44:20+00:00, thread_id=01a0e159-c770-7e33-8611-d18bf7cc6630, uncertain; strategy analysis, no product/pricing change)\n   967\t\n   968\t### keywords\n   969\t\n   970\t- subscription, Personal, keating_personal_v2, hosted-credit, credit-packs, persistent study management, offline-model, Gemma-4-12B, 32GB unified memory, 16GB VRAM, waitlist, refundable reservation, post-training\n   971\t\n   972\t## User preferences\n   973\t\n   974\t- when the user said the subscription “currently doesn't seem appealing at all” and asked why people would buy it -> find one compelling recurring outcome rather than adding generic extras [Task 1]\n   975\t- when considering a $150 offline edition, the user wanted a waitlist and recognized post-training is expensive -> collect hardware, use case, willingness to pay, and testing commitment before funding training [Task 1]\n   976\t\n   977\t## Reusable knowledge\n   978\t\n   979\t- Current repo terms were Personal at $25/month, $5 monthly hosted credit, and one billing-cycle rollover; $10/$25/$50 top-up packs do not expire. The recurring promise proposed here is persistent study management across devices: materials, plan, next lesson/review, progress, and sufficient hosted use. Storage/workspace alone are weak subscription reasons. [Task 1]\n   980\t- Checkout is entitlement-gated: `subscriptionCheckoutEnabled` requires `VITE_NOTORGANIC_CHECKOUT_ENABLED === \"true\"` and `keating_v2`; `subscriptionAvailable` also needs wallet checkout availability and `keating_personal_v2`. [Task 1]\n   981\t- An offline edition sells installation, hardware detection, tested model configuration, Keating harness/tool behavior, local materials/progress, and a defined update period—not just weights. Candidate Gemma 4 12B tiers (32GB unified memory or 16GB VRAM) are hypotheses because context cache/runtime overhead matter. Measure tool calls, grading, lesson-state adherence, and teaching behavior in Keating before commissioning post-training. [Task 1]\n   982\t\n   983\t## Failures and how to do differently\n   984\t\n   985\t- Free users can buy non-expiring credit and retain the teaching tools, leaving an apparent $20/month without an obvious recurring benefit. Do not assume more credit fixes that; model full-allowance, storage, compute, support, and payment costs before promising $35 credit on a $25 plan. [Task 1]\n   986\t- Do not promise support for every 32GB unified-memory or 16GB-VRAM machine. Establish supported hardware, context limits, and measured speeds; a refundable reservation tied to concrete scope/funding threshold is stronger demand evidence than a free waitlist. [Task 1]\n   987\t\n   988\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/notorganic-provider judgement purpose telemetry\n   989\tscope: Trace and extend auditable Not Organic judgement usage without retaining submitted content by default.\n   990\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/notorganic-provider with investigation initiated from cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating; reuse_rule=reinspect current gateway/schema/portal code and obtain a product/privacy decision before implementing a purpose field.\n   991\t\n   992\t## Task 1: Trace judgement usage and purpose logging\n   993\t\n   994\t### rollout_summary_files\n   995\t\n   996\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/26/rollout-2026-09-26T20-02-33-01a0e02b-ac77-7f83-b60d-875d511511b1.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-27T00:04:06+00:00, thread_id=01a0e02b-ac77-7f83-b60d-875d511511b1, partial; analysis only, no implementation)\n   997\t\n   998\t### keywords\n   999\t\n  1000\t- JudgementGateway, judgement.settled, purpose, apps/gateway/src/judgement.ts, convex/schema.ts, Usage.tsx, feature: \"judgement\", TypeSafe, HMAC-SHA256, draft_review, venue_ranking, quiz_feedback\n  1001\t\n  1002\t## User preferences\n  1003\t\n  1004\t- when the user said Not Organic should “log the use of judgement api and what it was used for” -> expose concrete feature/use-case purpose, not merely generic model, token, and cost metrics [Task 1]\n  1005\t\n  1006\t## Reusable knowledge\n  1007\t\n  1008\t- `JudgementGateway.evaluate` reserves credit with `feature: \"judgement\"`, dispatches TypeSafe, settles actual usage, and emits `judgement.settled`. Current fields are `product`, `alias`, question count, `input_tokens`, `usage_complete`, and `billed_usd`; no purpose field exists in the inspected path. [Task 1]\n  1009\t- `#emitSettled` pseudonymizes `principal.accountId` using HMAC-SHA256 and swallows telemetry errors, so analytics cannot fail a paid/settled request. `convex/schema.ts` persists metered lifecycle/product/feature/model/token/cost data; portal `Usage.tsx` renders the feature but no purpose column. [Task 1]\n  1010\t\n  1011\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  1012\t\n  1013\t- This was not implemented or privacy-approved. First decide whether a caller supplies a bounded purpose (for example `draft_review`) and whether only aggregate usage is retained; do not store full questions/answers by default. Refresh GitNexus before treating its one-commit-stale graph as complete edit guidance. [Task 1]\n  1014\t\n  1015\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/keating GPT Live video corrections\n  1016\tscope: Keep the GPT Live spotlight’s captured product state and SVG budget-meter geometry accurate through deterministic HyperFrames verification.\n  1017\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating; reuse_rule=reinspect actual provider descriptors, capture manifests, browser configuration, and rendered frames for any new video edit.\n  1018\t\n  1019\t## Task 1: Correct the GPT Live picker capture\n  1020\t\n  1021\t### rollout_summary_files\n  1022\t\n  1023\t- rollout_summaries/2026-09-26T20-00-24-7c9T-fix_gpt_live_video_picker_budget_needle.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/26/rollout-2026-09-26T16-00-24-01a0df4d-f93b-75c2-baaa-3eb370d6335d.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-26T20:13:00+00:00, thread_id=01a0df4d-f93b-75c2-baaa-3eb370d6335d, success)\n  1024\t\n  1025\t### keywords\n  1026\t\n  1027\t- GPT Live, gpt-live-1, gptLiveProvider, ModelSelector.stories.tsx, models-modelselector--gpt-live-voice-models, shots.json, picker.png, Storybook\n  1028\t\n  1029\t## Task 2: Fix SVG spending-budget needle placement\n  1030\t\n  1031\t### rollout_summary_files\n  1032\t\n  1033\t- rollout_summaries/2026-09-26T20-00-24-7c9T-fix_gpt_live_video_picker_budget_needle.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/26/rollout-2026-09-26T16-00-24-01a0df4d-f93b-75c2-baaa-3eb370d6335d.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-26T20:13:00+00:00, thread_id=01a0df4d-f93b-75c2-baaa-3eb370d6335d, success; render, snapshots, and contact sheet reviewed)\n  1034\t\n  1035\t### keywords\n  1036\t\n  1037\t- HyperFrames 0.8.78, SVG needle, rotate(112 357 322), svgOrigin, video/spotlights/live/src/index.template.html, KEATING_CHROME_BINARY, check, snapshot, contact-sheet.jpg\n  1038\t\n  1039\t## User preferences\n  1040\t\n  1041\t- when the user pointed out that the picker “shows gpt realtime 2.1 and not gpt live 1” -> verify captured UI uses the exact requested provider/model, not a visually similar fixture [Task 1]\n  1042\t\n  1043\t## Reusable knowledge\n  1044\t\n  1045\t- `gptLiveProvider` in `web/src/keating/speech-providers/gpt-live.ts` supplies `gpt-live-1` / `GPT Live`. The capture manifest is `video/spotlight-live/shots.json`; the dedicated story is `models-modelselector--gpt-live-voice-models`, staged at `video/spotlights/live/assets/shots/picker.png`. [Task 1]\n  1046\t- For a sub-composition SVG dial, animate explicit transforms around its center (`rotate(0 357 322)` → `rotate(112 357 322)` → return) instead of GSAP `rotation` plus `svgOrigin`, which can shift when mounted. The validated render was copied to spotlight, `web/public/tapes`, and docs-site tape paths. [Task 2]\n  1047\t\n  1048\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  1049\t\n  1050\t- `spawnSync ffmpeg EPERM` blocked the first sandbox build; host execution completed it. A generated Chrome wrapper with unset `KEATING_CHROME_BINARY` blocked checks/snapshots; pass an explicit Chrome path. Ensure `history begin` actually succeeds before edits and close it with `history end`. [Task 2]\n  1051\t\n  1052\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/keating Gemini narration, voice casting, and campaign-video publication\n  1053\tscope: Replace narrated campaign-video voices, generate auditionable English and Québec French alternatives, regenerate captions/renders, and locate published versus full-quality deliverables.\n  1054\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating; reuse_rule=reinspect current voice scripts, HyperFrames pins, Chrome/runtime setup, and media outputs before rerendering or claiming audiovisual approval.\n  1055\t\n  1056\t## Task 1: Migrate campaign narration to Gemini 3.8 TTS and publish eight videos\n  1057\t\n  1058\t### rollout_summary_files\n  1059\t\n  1060\t- rollout_summaries/2026-09-26T17-39-31-7qyn-gemini_tts_video_voice_casting_and_regeneration.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/26/rollout-2026-09-26T13-39-31-01a0decc-ff7a-7d43-9968-7b95d1b8a263.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-26T19:54:33+00:00, thread_id=01a0decc-ff7a-7d43-9968-7b95d1b8a263, success; streams/captions/copy equality verified, no per-film audiovisual review)\n  1061\t\n  1062\t### keywords\n  1063\t\n  1064\t- Gemini 3.8 TTS, fal, voice design, Québec French, HyperFrames 0.8.78, voice.mjs, Whisper word timings, web/public/tapes, ffprobe, video/voice-casting\n  1065\t\n  1066\t## User preferences\n  1067\t\n  1068\t- when requesting narration, the user asked to “generate a ton of different voice options with voice design as well” and specifically requested Québec French -> deliver tangible auditionable alternatives instead of silently choosing one voice [Task 1]\n  1069\t- when the user asked “where arer all the videos” -> report exact filesystem locations and distinguish published encodes from source/full-quality renders [Task 1]\n  1070\t\n  1071\t## Reusable knowledge\n  1072\t\n  1073\t- `video/spotlights/shared/scripts/voice.mjs` and `video/keating-launch/scripts/voice.mjs` support Gemini/fal narration with content-hash caching keyed by engine/model/voice/instructions and retain Whisper word timings for captions. Voice galleries are `video/voice-casting/fal/` and `video/voice-casting/cartesia/`, with English and French Canadian/Québécois samples. [Task 1]\n  1074\t- Published deliverables are `web/public/tapes/{keating-4-launch,keating-intro,keating-spotlight-recall,keating-lesson,keating-manifesto,keating-spotlight-live,keating-spotlight-judgements,keating-spotlight-onboarding}.mp4`; docs mirrors are `scripts/docs-site/assets/tapes/`. Full renders are `video/keating-launch/renders/`, `.keating/outputs/video/keating-intro/`, and `video/spotlights/*/renders/`. [Task 1]\n  1075\t- HyperFrames pins were upgraded to 0.8.78. Standard checks passed for launch plus all six narrated spotlights; `ffprobe -v error -show_entries format=duration -show_entries stream=codec_type -of compact <file>` verified video/audio streams (38.4–69.5 seconds), and published web/docs copies matched. [Task 1]\n  1076\t\n  1077\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  1078\t\n  1079\t- Chrome shared-library preflight fails under the Nix loader -> render HyperFrames with `env -u LD_LIBRARY_PATH PATH=/usr/bin:$PATH`. `ffmpeg`/`ffprobe` child processes can return `EPERM` in the restricted sandbox even if output exists -> use the permitted proxy/escalated media command path for validation. [Task 1]\n  1080\t- Stream, duration, caption-count, and copy-equality checks do not establish creative quality -> explicitly listen and visually review every regenerated video before final audiovisual approval. [Task 1]\n  1081\t\n  1082\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/keating launch preview, staging health, and app-only packaging\n  1083\tscope: Diagnose the exact playback/deployment surface, verify staging beyond HTTP 200, and package chat/CLI/TUI independently from landing/docs without overclaiming publication or DNS completion.\n  1084\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating; reuse_rule=recheck browser, Railway, DNS/TLS, worktree, native-install environment, and release state before treating any partial evidence as shipped.\n  1085\t\n  1086\t## Task 1: Diagnose launch-video voiceover silence\n  1087\t\n  1088\t### rollout_summary_files\n  1089\t\n  1090\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/26/rollout-2026-09-26T16-35-25-01a0df6e-0774-78a2-b175-4a0a3a2be832.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-26T23:19:47+00:00, thread_id=01a0df6e-0774-78a2-b175-4a0a3a2be832, partial; browser/audio-output proof unavailable)\n  1091\t\n  1092\t### keywords\n  1093\t\n  1094\t- launch-video, Local video preview, video/keating-launch/index.html, mix.wav, HyperFrames 0.8.78, ffprobe, volumedetect, timeline --json, localhost:3017\n  1095\t\n  1096\t## Task 2: Investigate staging failure and Devenv\n  1097\t\n  1098\t### rollout_summary_files\n  1099\t\n  1100\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/26/rollout-2026-09-26T16-35-25-01a0df6e-0774-78a2-b175-4a0a3a2be832.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-26T23:19:47+00:00, thread_id=01a0df6e-0774-78a2-b175-4a0a3a2be832, partial; stale deployment identified)\n  1101\t\n  1102\t### keywords\n  1103\t\n  1104\t- scripts/staging.ts, devenv up, keating:staging-deploy, keating-staging.up.railway.app, staging-build.json, promotionEligible, Railway, /chat\n  1105\t\n  1106\t## Task 3: Create app-only chat/CLI/TUI package\n  1107\t\n  1108\t### rollout_summary_files\n  1109\t\n  1110\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/26/rollout-2026-09-26T16-35-25-01a0df6e-0774-78a2-b175-4a0a3a2be832.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-26T23:19:47+00:00, thread_id=01a0df6e-0774-78a2-b175-4a0a3a2be832, partial; package validated, unpublished and DNS/TLS unresolved)\n  1111\t\n  1112\t### keywords\n  1113\t\n  1114\t- chat.keating.help, KEATING_WEB_BUILD_TARGET=app, APP_ONLY, web-build-target.ts, nitro.config.ts, verify-package-manifest.mjs --app-only, node-pty, 46.7 MB, 837 files\n  1115\t\n  1116\t## Task 4: Correct chat DNS/TLS and deploy host-aware routing\n  1117\t\n  1118\t### rollout_summary_files\n  1119\t\n  1120\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/27/rollout-2026-09-27T23-25-54-01a0e60c-32ee-7f00-a6c2-e8a4640f63c4.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-28T22:12:46+00:00, thread_id=01a0e60c-32ee-7f00-a6c2-e8a4640f63c4, partial; DNS records and live host routing verified, Railway’s final explicit certificate status was not captured)\n  1121\t\n  1122\t### keywords\n  1123\t\n  1124\t- chat.keating.help, keating.help, Railway, Porkbun, Sesame, _railway-verify.chat, CERTIFICATE_STATUS_TYPE_VALIDATING_OWNERSHIP, hosted-navigation.ts, PWA cache IDs, v4.0.6\n  1125\t\n  1126\t## Task 5: Prepare 4.0.7 installer-size and release fixes\n  1127\t\n  1128\t### rollout_summary_files\n  1129\t\n  1130\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/27/rollout-2026-09-27T23-25-54-01a0e60c-32ee-7f00-a6c2-e8a4640f63c4.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-28T22:12:46+00:00, thread_id=01a0e60c-32ee-7f00-a6c2-e8a4640f63c4, partial; 4.0.7 remained uncommitted/unpublished)\n  1131\t\n  1132\t### keywords\n  1133\t\n  1134\t- 4.0.7, stage-onnx-runtime.mjs, onnx-packaging.test.ts, 2 GiB, full-payload-xz-proof.json, AppImage, promotional tapes, posters, release.yml\n  1135\t\n  1136\t## User preferences\n  1137\t\n  1138\t- when the user clarified “Local video preview” after saying “no sound” -> identify the exact playback surface before diagnosing or concluding [Task 1]\n  1139\t- when the user said “the page fails to load and devenv up doesnt seem to work” -> investigate both deployed-page behavior and the Devenv/service path [Task 2]\n  1140\t- when requesting `chat.keating.help`, the user clarified “the package only includes chat, cli, and tui instead of the landing page and docs” -> treat hostname routing and build/package separation as distinct deliverables; inspect requested Entire/OpenCode history before implementation [Task 3]\n  1141\t- when the user interrupted release work with “we’ll have to get the remain chat dns and tls please first” -> resolve DNS/TLS before commit/publish steps when it is an outstanding dependency [Task 4]\n  1142\t- when the user said “let’s get my changes commited and pushed all changs need to get released” -> after prerequisites are verified, carry the coherent intended worktree through commit, push, tag, and publication instead of stopping at local validation [Task 5]\n  1143\t\n  1144\t## Reusable knowledge\n  1145\t\n  1146\t- HyperFrames uses muted timed visual `<video>` clips and a separate identified audio element. `video/keating-launch/index.html` has `<audio id=\"mix\" ...>`; the MP4 has 69.5-second stereo AAC and the served `mix.wav`/timeline were valid, so the remaining boundary is browser/player mute or host audio output. [Task 1]\n  1147\t- Use `bun scripts/staging.ts deploy|status|snapshot` or `devenv tasks run keating:staging-deploy`. A staging homepage/main JS 200 can still be stale: observed `/tapes/keating-4-launch.mp4` and `/staging-build.json` were 404. Dirty snapshots are `promotionEligible: false`. [Task 2]\n  1148\t- `KEATING_WEB_BUILD_TARGET=app` keeps chat/auth/courses/shares/live/learner activity/review plus CLI/TUI runtime assets. `web/scripts/web-build-target.ts`, `web/nitro.config.ts`, and compile-time `APP_ONLY` remove landing/docs/videos/reports/downloads/source artwork. `scripts/verify-package-manifest.mjs --app-only` rejects excluded paths and archives over 70 MiB. The validated artifact was 46.7 MB/837 files; `/chat` was 200 while excluded video/reports were 404. [Task 3]\n  1149\t- Railway required CNAME `chat` → `j0huj6qp.up.railway.app` and TXT `_railway-verify.chat`; Sesame/Porkbun preserved all 23 existing records. App paths on `keating.help` map to `https://chat.keating.help/`, public paths map back to `https://keating.help`; app builds render chat at `/` while retaining `/chat`, query/course handoffs, and distinct site/app PWA cache IDs. Commit `6514b0fc3ecef30fd0e3f1e6a2b1e57a0069b833`/`v4.0.6` deployed successfully; 2,254 web tests (1 skip) and 936 root tests passed. [Task 4]\n  1150\t- `desktop/scripts/stage-onnx-runtime.mjs` stages only the target platform/architecture ONNX Runtime closure; `desktop/test/onnx-packaging.test.ts` passed 13 tests. Release workflow checks each Linux installer against GitHub’s 2 GiB per-file limit, but full-payload XZ remained over: x64 2,267,136,000 bytes and arm64 2,252,914,688 bytes. [Task 5]\n  1151\t\n  1152\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  1153\t\n  1154\t- Valid audio streams, timeline records, or served assets do not prove audible preview playback; use a real browser/player and inspect mute/volume/output. Railway SUCCESS or homepage 200 does not prove current assets, readiness, sign-in, hosted inference, judgement, DNS/TLS, or browser functionality. [Task 1][Task 2]\n  1155\t- Do not claim npm 4.0.2 publication or deploy app-only output over the shared production service: publication was pending, `node-pty` native install remained Nix-environment-dependent, `chat.keating.help` ownership/certificate validation was incomplete, and replacing the shared service could remove the apex landing. [Task 3]\n  1156\t- CNAME propagation is not sufficient: verify Railway ownership, certificate status, and `curl -I https://chat.keating.help` with certificate validation. `railway domain certificate retry` is unavailable until issuance fails; later HTTPS/browser success is not the same as captured explicit `ISSUED` status. [Task 4]\n  1157\t- SquashFS-only size is insufficient: include AppImage wrapper overhead and measure the actual target installer. Do not report 4.0.7 released until commit SHA, tag, GitHub workflow conclusion, npm version, release assets, and clean worktree are verified. [Task 5]\n  1158\t\n  1159\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/keating approachable Jev judgement-model setup\n  1160\tscope: Make independent judgement configuration discoverable in Providers & Models, recommend Jev, and route unavailable reviews into setup without exposing provider credentials.\n  1161\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating; reuse_rule=recheck desktop/browser capability, Not Organic authorization, and live provider behavior before asserting end-to-end availability.\n  1162\t\n  1163\t## Task 1: Add Jev judgement picker and setup guidance\n  1164\t\n  1165\t### rollout_summary_files\n  1166\t\n  1167\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/26/rollout-2026-09-26T19-06-37-01a0dff8-768f-7371-a6c0-67f2467f7b3b.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-26T23:12:08+00:00, thread_id=01a0dff8-768f-7371-a6c0-67f2467f7b3b, partial; focused tests/typecheck passed, browser/provider unverified)\n  1168\t\n  1169\t### keywords\n  1170\t\n  1171\t- Jev, JudgementSettings, ProvidersModelsTab, settings-section-judgement, backend-unavailable, backend-unauthorized, review-unavailable, docs/judgement-models.md, MiniCPM5, Not Organic, TypeSafe API key\n  1172\t\n  1173\t## User preferences\n  1174\t\n  1175\t- when the user asked for “an easy way to set one up just like other models” with “a picker with the various models and options” -> integrate judgement setup into normal Providers & Models instead of a hidden backend setting [Task 1]\n  1176\t- when requesting docs “linked to jev as well with that as our recommendation” -> visibly recommend Jev and link official documentation while making limits clear [Task 1]\n  1177\t\n  1178\t## Reusable knowledge\n  1179\t\n  1180\t- `web/src/components/settings/JudgementSettings.tsx` owns the picker/setup UI mounted from `ProvidersModelsTab.tsx` under `judgement`. It offers `Jev · Not Organic · Recommended`, desktop MiniCPM5 where supported, browser alternatives marked scoring-unavailable, and `Off · built-in checks only`; unavailable reviews link to `/chat?settings=judgement`. [Task 1]\n  1181\t- Hosted judgement remains separate from tutor model and uses Not Organic. Never ask users to paste a TypeSafe API key into the browser. `docs/judgement-models.md` covers authorization, local setup, browser limitations, token limits, and calibration boundaries. [Task 1]\n  1182\t\n  1183\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  1184\t\n  1185\t- UI-copy tests can false-match explanatory text (for example `judgement access is connected`); assert actual button markup or state-specific output. No browser interaction or live Jev/Not Organic authorization/review ran, and GitNexus was three commits stale, so do not promote this to end-to-end proof. [Task 1]\n  1186\t\n  1187\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/twyne persistence, Not Organic migration, rubric copy, and configurable judgement\n  1188\tscope: Preserve every Twyne writer’s work across guest/auth paths, make normal editing controls reliable, and migrate identity/judgement configuration without overstating live production proof.\n  1189\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne; reuse_rule=reinspect the broad dirty migration, production account scope/origins, PDS scopes, and real provider endpoints before deployment or irreversible account action.\n  1190\t\n  1191\t## Task 1: Repair dossier persistence, folio title carry-over, and editor Ctrl+A\n  1192\t\n  1193\t### rollout_summary_files\n  1194\t\n  1195\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/28/rollout-2026-09-28T22-53-14-01a0eb14-a6ed-79a2-bdfb-508802dcd4c2.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-23T15:23:10+00:00, thread_id=01a0eb14-a6ed-79a2-bdfb-508802dcd4c2, success; targeted browser tests passed)\n  1196\t\n  1197\t### keywords\n  1198\t\n  1199\t- DataCloneError, Qwik useStore, toStorable, IndexedDB, saveProjectBriefForFolio, withFolioTitle, dossier-persistence.e2e.ts, Ctrl+A, Mod-A, twyne-editor.tsx\n  1200\t\n  1201\t## Task 2: Replace legacy Twyne identity/billing with Not Organic-native sign-in\n  1202\t\n  1203\t### rollout_summary_files\n  1204\t\n  1205\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/28/rollout-2026-09-28T22-53-14-01a0eb14-a6ed-79a2-bdfb-508802dcd4c2.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-23T15:23:10+00:00, thread_id=01a0eb14-a6ed-79a2-bdfb-508802dcd4c2, partial; uncommitted migration, production/browser/PDS proof pending)\n  1206\t\n  1207\t### keywords\n  1208\t\n  1209\t- Not Organic, PKCE, providerIdentities, Better Auth, Creem, legacyAccounts.ts, sendDeprecationNotices, retireLegacyAccounts, Standard.site, include:site.standard.authFull\n  1210\t\n  1211\t## Task 3: Make rubric copy writer-readable and route judgement models/BYOK\n  1212\t\n  1213\t### rollout_summary_files\n  1214\t\n  1215\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/28/rollout-2026-09-28T22-53-14-01a0eb14-a65e-7873-ac1f-577a624acee3.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-26T04:27:48+00:00, thread_id=01a0eb14-a65e-7873-ac1f-577a624acee3, partial; UI/build checks passed, benchmark/live endpoint unverified)\n  1216\t\n  1217\t### keywords\n  1218\t\n  1219\t- rubric-copy.ts, SPINE_CRITERIA, rubric-grade.ts, 120-character truncation, JudgementSettings, judgement-client.ts, TypeSafe, POST /v1/systemone, Kev-4B, 127.0.0.1:8009\n  1220\t\n  1221\t## User preferences\n  1222\t\n  1223\t- when the user called dossier loss “critical” across signed-in/out and new-account paths -> fixes must cover guest and authenticated persistence, not just an account-specific path; a new folio title should seed its brief title unless the writer changes it [Task 1]\n  1224\t- when the user requested removal of old subscriptions/accounts and a deprecation email with zero real subscribers -> preserve the direction, but require recipient/count review, backup/export, and explicit confirmation before sending notices or deleting production data [Task 2]\n  1225\t- when the user said rubric copy should be “far more readable” -> use plain writer-facing explanations and actionable next moves, not model/scoring jargon; when asking for “a kev 4b” and other models, support local/private endpoints and benchmark-driven selection [Task 3]\n  1226\t\n  1227\t## Reusable knowledge\n  1228\t\n  1229\t- Qwik `useStore` values can be proxies despite plain TypeScript types; IndexedDB rejects them with `DataCloneError`. Detach values via `toStorable()` at every `.put()` boundary, never swallow write failures, and read after write. The dossier flow and named-folio title carry-over were exercised by two passing Playwright tests. [Task 1]\n  1230\t- A document capture-phase Mod-A handler restores editor selection from toolbar/page margins while preserving native selection in inputs, textareas, selects, dialogs, and editable controls; all 10 select-all scenarios passed. [Task 1]\n  1231\t- The migration removes Creem tables/webhooks/checkout and moves entitlement to the Not Organic wallet; verified DID maps to Better Auth plus `providerIdentities`. Keep ATProto only as a PDS publishing connection. `legacyAccounts.ts` supports dry-run notice/retirement commands; development only had e2e accounts. [Task 2]\n  1232\t- `rubric-copy.ts` centralizes visible score words/verdicts/next moves while frozen wording in `rubric-grade.ts` keeps historical judgement comparable. Keep summaries within the panel’s 120-character limit. `judgement-client.ts` routes Twyne-hosted, one-use TypeSafe BYOK through Convex, or a compatible direct endpoint and validates endpoint/response contracts. [Task 3]\n  1233\t\n  1234\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  1235\t\n  1236\t- Existing formatting E2E timeouts waiting for “Type options” reproduce against HEAD; do not attribute them to Ctrl+A. [Task 1]\n  1237\t- Migration is broad/uncommitted: review the diff, safely inspect production, register intended Not Organic origins, and test real sign-in/PDS publication. Do not send mail/delete accounts until dry-run recipient list, backup, and explicit approval; `include:site.standard.authFull` PDS scope remains unresolved. [Task 2]\n  1238\t- No benchmark, dataset, scores, report, real TypeSafe key flow, or ready Kev server was verified. CPU-only Kev was still starting/downloading; do not retry autonomous-agent spawning after denial—build the benchmark directly in the active session if authorized. [Task 3]\n  1239\t\n  1240\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/twyne persistent intentional grammar choices\n  1241\tscope: Preserve intentional wording as a compact, browser-local exception without silencing unrelated Harper grammar findings.\n  1242\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne; reuse_rule=reuse the precise local dictionary/matching design for Twyne grammar UI; manually exercise persistence and removal whenever a browser is available.\n  1243\t\n  1244\t## Task 1: Add persistent intentional grammar choices\n  1245\t\n  1246\t### rollout_summary_files\n  1247\t\n  1248\t- rollout_summaries/2026-09-26T09-40-38-4ytO-persistent_intentional_grammar_choices.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/26/rollout-2026-09-26T05-40-38-01a0dd16-8f41-7822-80c1-8224fb133b70.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-26T10:01:22+00:00, thread_id=01a0dd16-8f41-7822-80c1-8224fb133b70, success; focused tests passed, browser UI unverified)\n  1249\t\n  1250\t### keywords\n  1251\t\n  1252\t- Harper, grammar-panel, twyne:grammar-dictionary:v1, importWords, exportWords, clearWords, intentional choice, localStorage, ×, aria-label\n  1253\t\n  1254\t## User preferences\n  1255\t\n  1256\t- when the user asked for intentional wording to be remembered and then corrected that “this is intentional is too long just an cancel mark or something” -> use a compact ×/cancel control with tooltip and accessible label, plus a persistent exception rather than merely dismissing the current card [Task 1]\n  1257\t\n  1258\t## Reusable knowledge\n  1259\t\n  1260\t- `src/utils/grammar.ts` persists validated, deduplicated choices under `twyne:grammar-dictionary:v1`; match `problem`, `kind`, and `message` so one accepted wording does not disable an entire Harper rule. Spelling choices synchronize through `exportWords`, `clearWords`, and `importWords`; non-spelling choices filter only exact matches. [Task 1]\n  1261\t- `src/components/editor/grammar-panel.tsx` provides the × action, “Your dictionary” details list, removal/undo actions, and status notices. Focused grammar/runtime tests passed 10/0 and Prettier passed. [Task 1]\n  1262\t\n  1263\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  1264\t\n  1265\t- The visible sentence-length “This is intentional” control was rejected -> retain explanation in `title`/`aria-label`, not the button face. Browser clicking, reload persistence, and removal were not exercised, so do not call UI behavior verified without that pass. [Task 1]\n  1266\t\n  1267\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/twyne grade and workflow stamp effects\n  1268\tscope: Apply the editorial stamp system to grades and Filed/Revised workflow states, with dramatic but accessible tiered effects.\n  1269\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne; reuse_rule=recheck actual generated assets and visual behavior before reuse; the asset-count/model claim in this rollout is not independently established.\n  1270\t\n  1271\t## Task 1: Generate and integrate grade/workflow stamps\n  1272\t\n  1273\t### rollout_summary_files\n  1274\t\n  1275\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/26/rollout-2026-09-26T04-54-37-01a0dcec-6ed9-7913-b710-05f13e701fef.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-26T09:34:57+00:00, thread_id=01a0dcec-6ed9-7913-b710-05f13e701fef, partial; exact model, asset persistence, and claimed checks unverified)\n  1276\t\n  1277\t### keywords\n  1278\t\n  1279\t- GradeStamp, rubricGradeStampAsset, stamp-shader.tsx, WebGL, solar corona, sunburst, Filed, Revised, reduced-motion, context-loss, imagegen\n  1280\t\n  1281\t## User preferences\n  1282\t\n  1283\t- when the user asked for “a stamp with each grade,” “filed” and “revised,” and “really cool shaders” that become “more impressive with the highest” -> retain editorial ink-on-paper stamps while making B/A/A+ visibly escalating and honoring reduced motion [Task 1]\n  1284\t- when the user explicitly requested “gpt image 2.5 sunburst” -> report model-selector limitations rather than claiming exact model usage without tool evidence [Task 1]\n  1285\t\n  1286\t## Reusable knowledge\n  1287\t\n  1288\t- Extend existing `GradeStamp`, exact-grade `rubricGradeStampAsset`, sound profiles, `resultFresh`, and animation hooks instead of building a parallel grade-feedback system. A/B/C/D-F map to `a`/`b`/`c`/`revise`; `src/components/rubric/stamp-shader.tsx` is the WebGL solar-corona surface with reduced-motion/context-loss fallback. [Task 1]\n  1289\t- `src/components/ui/workflow-stamp.tsx` supplies Filed/Revised states; Revised is tied to accepted manuscript edits and dossier flows. Twyne’s expected visual baseline is editorial, ink-on-paper, restrained UI with reduced-motion handling. [Task 1]\n  1290\t\n  1291\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  1292\t\n  1293\t- `MODULE_NOT_FOUND` for a repo-local Impeccable script -> use `/home/diogenes/.agents/skills/impeccable/scripts/context.mjs` when the project path is absent. Only four generated files were visible at a checkpoint while 15 persisted assets were claimed -> enumerate `public/assets/...` and capture actual check output before declaring completion. [Task 1]\n  1294\t\n  1295\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/twyne dossier live title, brief editions, and Storybook\n  1296\tscope: Keep dossier editing visibly live and preserve folio-scoped, browsable saved brief history in established Twyne editorial cards.\n  1297\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne; reuse_rule=reuse the separate brief-edition model for saved replacements, not manuscript revisions or unsaved typing; browser interaction remains a required proof boundary.\n  1298\t\n  1299\t## Task 1: Fix live dossier title and add versioned briefs\n  1300\t\n  1301\t### rollout_summary_files\n  1302\t\n  1303\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/26/rollout-2026-09-26T04-13-58-01a0dcc7-3905-7aa3-9ad8-8db73307470f.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-26T08:55:04+00:00, thread_id=01a0dcc7-3905-7aa3-9ad8-8db73307470f, partial; typecheck passed, browser interaction unavailable)\n  1304\t\n  1305\t### keywords\n  1306\t\n  1307\t- AntiTabulaRasa, DossierPreview, ProjectBriefCard, brief-history.ts, brief-editions:<folioId>, IndexedDB, saveProjectBriefForFolio, onInput$, TS2322, EarlierEditions, Storybook\n  1308\t\n  1309\t## Task 2: Add a version-card Storybook state\n  1310\t\n  1311\t### rollout_summary_files\n  1312\t\n  1313\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/26/rollout-2026-09-26T04-13-58-01a0dcc7-3905-7aa3-9ad8-8db73307470f.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-26T08:55:04+00:00, thread_id=01a0dcc7-3905-7aa3-9ad8-8db73307470f, success; build.types and diff check passed)\n  1314\t\n  1315\t### keywords\n  1316\t\n  1317\t- project-brief-card.stories.tsx, EarlierEditions, BriefEdition, current filed copy, earlier editions\n  1318\t\n  1319\t## User preferences\n  1320\t\n  1321\t- when the user wanted the left-side title to show what was being entered and asked for “versioned briefs that i could look at and see” -> expose live state plus read-only historical saved versions [Task 1]\n  1322\t- when asking how “other posts” look -> reuse `ProjectBriefCard`/filed-dossier styling and vocabulary, not a novel visual pattern; when asking to “add this version card to storybook,” include representative interactive component states [Task 1][Task 2]\n  1323\t\n  1324\t## Reusable knowledge\n  1325\t\n  1326\t- `src/utils/brief-history.ts` keeps at most 20 superseded `ProjectBrief` records under IndexedDB metadata `brief-editions:<folioId>`. `saveProjectBriefForFolio` archives a changed previous brief then verifies the write; selection is wired through preview, card, form, conversational refinement, and editor load, and historical editions are read-only. [Task 1]\n  1327\t- Brief editions are distinct from `src/utils/revision-history.ts`: they are local-device saved replacements, never every unsaved keystroke. Qwik nested fields require explicit `onInput$` mutation of `store.answers[step.field!]`; the attempted `bind:value` path yielded TS2322. `EarlierEditions` provides two dated fixtures for Storybook. [Task 1][Task 2]\n  1328\t\n  1329\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  1330\t\n  1331\t- A first completion claimed the typing bug fixed without exercising it -> type checking/handler inspection is insufficient; verify real input interaction when a browser exists. CUA reported `Browser is not available: iab` and no browsers, so this remains unverified. [Task 1]\n  1332\t\n  1333\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/twyne rubric, writing-tools autosave, and drawer UI refinement\n  1334\tscope: Maintain concise paper/ink/vermilion editorial controls, workspace-owned automatic Jev review, autosaved notes, and meaningful drawer/access context.\n  1335\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne; reuse_rule=reuse existing Twyne UI primitives and live-review ownership; do not represent this rollout as browser visually verified.\n  1336\t\n  1337\t## Task 1: Refine rubric and writing-tools UI\n  1338\t\n  1339\t### rollout_summary_files\n  1340\t\n  1341\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/26/rollout-2026-09-26T03-30-40-01a0dc9f-9346-7ac0-9e6c-d4e92f4211cf.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-26T08:54:19+00:00, thread_id=01a0dc9f-9346-7ac0-9e6c-d4e92f4211cf, success; focused checks passed, browser visual verification unavailable)\n  1342\t\n  1343\t### keywords\n  1344\t\n  1345\t- rubric-panel, writing-tools, Reicon, icon-system.ts, SiteSelect, paper, ink, vermilion, help/review, revision-summary, cobalt\n  1346\t\n  1347\t## Task 2: Make writing-tool review automatic and notes autosaved\n  1348\t\n  1349\t### rollout_summary_files\n  1350\t\n  1351\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/26/rollout-2026-09-26T03-30-40-01a0dc9f-9346-7ac0-9e6c-d4e92f4211cf.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-26T08:54:19+00:00, thread_id=01a0dc9f-9346-7ac0-9e6c-d4e92f4211cf, success; focused storage/lens checks passed)\n  1352\t\n  1353\t### keywords\n  1354\t\n  1355\t- live-review.ts, twyne:live-review, writing-tools:${folioId}, writing-tools-storage.ts, cachedWritingLens, newest-write-wins, Run this check\n  1356\t\n  1357\t## Task 3: Make drawer identity and access meaningful\n  1358\t\n  1359\t### rollout_summary_files\n  1360\t\n  1361\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/26/rollout-2026-09-26T03-30-40-01a0dc9f-9346-7ac0-9e6c-d4e92f4211cf.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-26T08:54:19+00:00, thread_id=01a0dc9f-9346-7ac0-9e6c-d4e92f4211cf, success; TypeScript, ESLint, and diff check passed)\n  1362\t\n  1363\t### keywords\n  1364\t\n  1365\t- Drawer No. III, folioNumeral, owner, editor, commenter, Read and comment only, workspace-preview, Reicon\n  1366\t\n  1367\t## User preferences\n  1368\t\n  1369\t- when blue accents and dense explanatory copy were out of place, the user asked to remove redundant/onboarding text -> preserve paper/ink/vermilion styling, keep panels concise, and move limits/explanations to help links or tooltips [Task 1]\n  1370\t- when the user said icons “let people figure out what buttons and information do more easily” -> use accessible Reicon icons with short labels/tooltips; use `SiteSelect`, not native `<select>`, and preserve order: check buttons, selected description, inputs, results [Task 1]\n  1371\t- when material “should just be saved by default” and Jev should use checks automatically, with the tool reserved for explicit control -> autosave editable fields and make the board observe workspace-owned background results; adding passages/sources stays explicit [Task 2]\n  1372\t- when the target was “Drawer No. III / Pieces in Progress” and icons should communicate it quickly -> show dynamic drawer/folio/access context with compact icon-supported labels [Task 3]\n  1373\t\n  1374\t## Reusable knowledge\n  1375\t\n  1376\t- Use `src/components/ui/icon.tsx` and `src/utils/icon-system.ts`; `SiteSelect` is `src/components/ui/site-select.tsx`, and tokens are in `src/global.css`. `src/routes/help/review/index.tsx` holds long-form review explanation. Focused revision tests passed 7/0 and writing/lens tests 19/0. [Task 1]\n  1377\t- `src/utils/live-review.ts` owns background review and emits `twyne:live-review`; `cachedWritingLens` shares cache/in-flight work. Store folio notes as `writing-tools:${folioId}` in `src/utils/writing-tools-storage.ts`; serialized saves guarantee newest-write-wins. Automatic review remains read-only and retains findings, uncertainty, and evidence. [Task 2]\n  1378\t- Roles are `owner`, `editor`, `commenter`; commenters show “Read and comment only.” `folioNumeral()` in `src/utils/editorial-format.ts` provides Roman labels; live editor and landing preview should match. [Task 3]\n  1379\t\n  1380\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  1381\t\n  1382\t- CUA had no browser provider (`listBrowsers()` returned `[]`; `Browser is not available: iab`) -> report visual verification incomplete. The initial project-relative Impeccable context path failed; use `/home/diogenes/.agents/skills/impeccable/scripts/context.mjs`. [Task 1]\n  1383\t\n  1384\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/twyne HyperFrames launch-video audit and production\n  1385\tscope: Audit an interrupted agent video run against actual artifacts, then complete and verify all renderable Twyne launch films on this Linux workstation.\n  1386\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne; reuse_rule=reinspect the project/CLI/browser GPU configuration before rendering; the Intel ANGLE workaround is host-specific.\n  1387\t\n  1388\t## Task 1: Audit prior Entire/Claude launch-video work\n  1389\t\n  1390\t### rollout_summary_files\n  1391\t\n  1392\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/26/rollout-2026-09-26T02-10-19-01a0dc56-01ea-7e51-a7aa-600909e6091b.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-26T06:45:21+00:00, thread_id=01a0dc56-01ea-7e51-a7aa-600909e6091b, success)\n  1393\t\n  1394\t### keywords\n  1395\t\n  1396\t- Entire, Claude Code, be257798-5920-4b1f-a6d7-a542b054a90d, launch-videos, scaffold, MP4, render logs, contrast\n  1397\t\n  1398\t## Task 2: Finish, render, and verify six launch films\n  1399\t\n  1400\t### rollout_summary_files\n  1401\t\n  1402\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/26/rollout-2026-09-26T02-10-19-01a0dc56-01ea-7e51-a7aa-600909e6091b.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-26T06:45:21+00:00, thread_id=01a0dc56-01ea-7e51-a7aa-600909e6091b, success; six exports decoded and sampled)\n  1403\t\n  1404\t### keywords\n  1405\t\n  1406\t- HyperFrames 0.8.78, HYPERFRAMES_BROWSER_PATH, --use-angle=gl-egl, --use-angle=gl, BeginFrame, hardware gpu, render-newsreel.py, Sequential screenshot capture stalled, verification.json, ffprobe\n  1407\t\n  1408\t## Task 3: Generate the initial warm-editorial launch-media suite\n  1409\t\n  1410\t### rollout_summary_files\n  1411\t\n  1412\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/28/rollout-2026-09-28T22-53-14-01a0eb14-a661-78a0-90d3-a5ab174e7cc2.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-26T06:09:49+00:00, thread_id=01a0eb14-a661-78a0-90d3-a5ab174e7cc2, partial; source-media/compositions built, later completion is captured in Task 2)\n  1413\t\n  1414\t### keywords\n  1415\t\n  1416\t- Seedance 2.5, Gemini 3.8 Flash TTS, Lyria 3.5, GPT Image 2.5, launch-videos/_gen, 01-the-room, 02-roll-call, 03-edited, assets/js/words.js, paper-texture.jpg\n  1417\t\n  1418\t## User preferences\n  1419\t\n  1420\t- when the user asked to “check out the last entire session how far was claude from completing the task” -> inspect Entire metadata, transcript, composition source, actual MP4s, logs, and validation artifacts before estimating completion [Task 1]\n  1421\t- when the user said “finish the rest of the clean up” -> continue from saved project state through composition fixes, renders, and verification rather than merely reporting status [Task 2]\n  1422\t- when the user asked to “make a bunch of different commercials and videos” and “be creative” -> make autonomous creative decisions and retain the selected Seedance 2.5/Gemini 3.8 TTS/Lyria 3.5/GPT Image 2.5 toolset unless unavailable [Task 3]\n  1423\t\n  1424\t## Reusable knowledge\n  1425\t\n  1426\t- Session metadata/touched files do not distinguish authored, checked, rendered, and scaffolded output. In the audited run, only `01-the-room`/`02-roll-call` existed as MP4s; `03-edited` had contrast failures and `04-newsreel`/`05-the-strike`/`06-sting` were scaffolds. [Task 1]\n  1427\t- Pin was HyperFrames `0.8.78`. On this workstation, bundled Chrome’s Intel Mesa path worked with `--use-angle=gl`, whereas HyperFrames requested `gl-egl`; `rtk proxy python3 launch-videos/_gen/scripts/render-newsreel.py` translates the flag and sets `HYPERFRAMES_BROWSER_PATH`, enabling hardware BeginFrame rendering. [Task 2]\n  1428\t- Final evidence is `launch-videos/verification.json`: six MP4s at 60/46/46/34/15/6 seconds, expected dimensions, 30fps/audio, clean FFmpeg decode, and sampled frame review; outputs/gallery/readme/checks/posters are under `launch-videos/`. [Task 2]\n  1429\t- Twyne’s visual language is aged cream paper, near-black brown ink, vermilion, literary serif display type, DM Sans UI, and Special Elite/typewriter labels—avoid generic AI-chat/SaaS treatment. `_gen` scripts/manifests stage imagery, music, TTS, alignment, captions, fonts, SFX, and brand SVGs; word timing is bundled inline as `assets/js/words.js` to avoid render-time fetches. [Task 3]\n  1430\t\n  1431\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  1432\t\n  1433\t- Plain `--browser-gpu` fell back to software and stalled with `Sequential screenshot capture stalled: no frame progress for 60000ms (stuck at frame 114/1020)` -> use the saved host wrapper for shader/film compositions, not repeated retries. Fix contrast reported by `hyperframes check` before rendering; `03-edited` required darkening struck text and a vermilion label. [Task 2]\n  1434\t- Empty TTS `speakers: []`/`turns: []` triggers dialogue validation -> pass `speakers: null, turns: null`. A texture prompt needs explicit edge-to-edge/no-desk constraints; use `assets/img/paper-texture.jpg`, not `img/...`. `PATH=/usr/bin:$PATH npx hyperframes render -q delivery ...` works when bundled Chrome misses system libraries. [Task 3]\n  1435\t\n  1436\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/twyne Jev editor live-review, Not Organic linking, and v0.20.2 release\n  1437\tscope: Integrate typed Jev review into the real saved-draft editor loop, securely provision the Not Organic boundary, and verify clean CI/release evidence.\n  1438\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne; reuse_rule=recheck production provider funding, gateway configuration, and current release state; reuse editor wiring and clean-install lessons for this checkout.\n  1439\t\n  1440\t## Task 1: Move typed Jev review into the saved-draft/idle editor loop\n  1441\t\n  1442\t### rollout_summary_files\n  1443\t\n  1444\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/20/rollout-2026-09-20T01-56-11-01a0bd62-eabf-7a61-bb50-27a4047f7c4a.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-20T07:49:22+00:00, thread_id=01a0bd62-eabf-7a61-bb50-27a4047f7c4a, success; funded end-to-end review remains unverified)\n  1445\t\n  1446\t### keywords\n  1447\t\n  1448\t- live-review.ts, LiveReviewStatus, twyne:live-review, twyne:quick-review, twyne:content, twyne:draft-saved, saved-draft, idle delay, pause/resume, TypeSafe, Noul, Choice, Score\n  1449\t\n  1450\t## Task 2: Provision Not Organic and publish reproducible v0.20.2\n  1451\t\n  1452\t### rollout_summary_files\n  1453\t\n  1454\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/20/rollout-2026-09-20T01-56-11-01a0bd62-eabf-7a61-bb50-27a4047f7c4a.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-20T07:49:22+00:00, thread_id=01a0bd62-eabf-7a61-bb50-27a4047f7c4a, success; provider transport/release verified, no funded review probe)\n  1455\t\n  1456\t### keywords\n  1457\t\n  1458\t- judgement:evaluate, DPoP, PKCE, NOTORGANIC_AUDIENCE, invalid_product_assertion, hushed-aardvark-411, jsdom@26.1.0, Undici, .dagger/src/index.ts, twyne-tools, v0.20.2, 402 insufficient_funds\n  1459\t\n  1460\t## User preferences\n  1461\t\n  1462\t- when review should “no longer be on request” and happen “in editor ... as a person is saving” -> default editor AI to quiet saved-draft/idle processing, not isolated manual tools [Task 1]\n  1463\t- when asking whether features are “implemented in editor” -> verify real editor event wiring and visible in-editor output, not only a standalone route or panel [Task 1]\n  1464\t- when styling should be “consistent with our other styles” -> reuse Twyne tokens, shared controls, typography, and Editorial Board vocabulary rather than a local styling system [Task 1]\n  1465\t- when the user authorized “Configure the integration” -> provision and verify the live provider boundary rather than stopping at source code [Task 2]\n  1466\t\n  1467\t## Reusable knowledge\n  1468\t\n  1469\t- `src/utils/live-review.ts` owns saved-draft review, persistence by folio, retry/backoff, and `twyne:live-review` / `twyne:quick-review`; `src/components/writing-tools/live-review-status.tsx` provides status, findings, pause/resume, and unavailable-state routing. Preserve typed findings, uncertainty, evidence passages, and read-only behavior: review must not edit prose automatically. [Task 1]\n  1470\t- Background work needs spend guards: substantive word threshold, idle delay, minimum interval, and per-session cap. TypeSafe calls use typed `state` plus `noul`, `choice`, and `score`; Choice has a criteria map, Score ordered levels, and Noul has no confidence. [Task 1]\n  1471\t- Not Organic production uses `https://api.notorganic.info`, capability `judgement:evaluate`, and DPoP-bound tokens. Link with PKCE one-time state and server-side token/account verification; do not trust a browser-supplied DID, expose gateway credentials, or send upstream error bodies to browsers. [Task 2]\n  1472\t- Production gateway audience is `notorganic`, independent of issuer. The release added declared `jsdom@26.1.0` compatible with the pinned Undici and installs the separate `packages/twyne-tools/bun.lock` in `.dagger/src/index.ts` before CLI checks. Final evidence: 1,474 tests with 39 skips/0 failures, CLI 22 tests, type/build/lint/format/package checks, successful release assets, and Railway `SUCCESS` for `254ad09a8346972910fcab59e62d2b75033578b7`. [Task 2]\n  1473\t\n  1474\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  1475\t\n  1476\t- Isolated `/writing-tools/` and button-triggered rubric paths are not editor integration -> trace `twyne:content`, `twyne:draft-saved`, and folio lifecycle events, then inspect the visible editor state. [Task 1]\n  1477\t- `401 invalid_product_assertion` -> keep `NOTORGANIC_AUDIENCE` separate from `NOTORGANIC_ISSUER` and set the production audience to `notorganic`; direct `/v1/judgement` requests correctly fail without the signed assertion-to-DPoP path. A `402 insufficient_funds` probe proves the funded review itself was not verified. [Task 2]\n  1478\t- Local green tests can hide clean-CI dependency faults -> run an isolated install and the full CI dependency graph. `jsdom@29.1.1` expected an Undici handler absent from this checkout; missing `twyne-tools` install also failed Dagger. Preserve unrelated `devenv.lock` and `skills-lock.json` changes. [Task 2]\n  1479\t\n  1480\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/interleave-app Jev/TypeSafe integration, automatic Weave matching, and venue ranking\n  1481\tscope: Reuse the Not Organic judgement transport and conservative semantic decisions across Weave/Woven/Worn without replacing deterministic or safety-critical logic.\n  1482\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/interleave-app; reuse_rule=inspect the active branch/worktree and rerun Devenv codegen/typecheck/lint/test before claiming integration complete; this evidence has no live gateway/browser/deployment proof.\n  1483\t\n  1484\t## Task 1: Map a Jev foundation across Weave, Woven, and Worn\n  1485\t\n  1486\t### rollout_summary_files\n  1487\t\n  1488\t- rollout_summaries/2026-09-21T05-07-40-GKiq-jev_interleave_integration_investigation.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/interleave-app, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/21/rollout-2026-09-21T01-07-40-01a0c25c-da82-7483-8908-41db1075e4fe.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-20T05:23:06+00:00, thread_id=01a0c25c-da82-7483-8908-41db1075e4fe, partial; archaeology only, no plan/file implementation)\n  1489\t\n  1490\t### keywords\n  1491\t\n  1492\t- POST /v1/judgement, judgement:evaluate, notOrganicClient.ts, product assertion, DPoP, typed wire codec, calibrationSha256, abstention, confect/host/judgments, Woven, Worn\n  1493\t\n  1494\t## Task 2: Implement automatic Weave matchmaking and conservative venue ranking\n  1495\t\n  1496\t### rollout_summary_files\n  1497\t\n  1498\t- rollout_summaries/2026-09-20T05-28-30-RqmQ-jev_interleave_matchmaking_venue_ranking.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/interleave-app, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/20/rollout-2026-09-20T01-28-30-01a0bd49-92b6-7b73-8d4f-101d07ce09c8.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-20T06:38:38+00:00, thread_id=01a0bd49-92b6-7b73-8d4f-101d07ce09c8, partial; scoped tests passed, repository-wide verification incomplete)\n  1499\t\n  1500\t### keywords\n  1501\t\n  1502\t- weaveMatchmakingPolicy.ts, weaveMatchmaking.ts, probability >= 0.98, confidence >= 0.95, margin >= 0.9, uncalibrated judgement provenance, weaveVenueJudgement.ts, nearby order, CONVEX_TMPDIR\n  1503\t\n  1504\t## User preferences\n  1505\t\n  1506\t- when the user said “yeah continue from this session.” -> continue from existing session and Git context rather than restarting discovery or asking for a recap [Task 2]\n  1507\t- for deep integration across “weave, woven and worn,” start with cross-repository archaeology of Keating/Twyne/TypeSafe/Not Organic rather than editing one call site [Task 1]\n  1508\t- “matching won't require administrative review unless the profile spikes Jev's judgement. The bar should be high for getting admin review” -> submitted profiles match automatically; human review is only for unusually strong explicit serious-concern judgements [Task 2]\n  1509\t\n  1510\t## Reusable knowledge\n  1511\t\n  1512\t- Reuse `confect/handlers/lib/notOrganicClient.ts`: it signs a short-lived Ed25519 product assertion, exchanges a DPoP token, caches it, signs each request, and adds product/idempotency/cost headers. Route to `POST /v1/judgement` with `judgement:evaluate`; gateway keeps the TypeSafe key. Locally validate, return failures rather than throw, retry only retryable statuses, do not echo upstream bodies, and abstain/fallback when unavailable. [Task 1][Task 2]\n  1513\t- Keep arithmetic, counts, authorization, and closed deterministic logic Tier 0. Jev may classify/select/interpret bounded vocabulary; use typed Noul/Choice/Score distributions and modal levels, preserve calibration/provenance, and abstain to deterministic baselines when evidence/calibration is insufficient. Worn must not infer recovery stage, diagnosis, safety, healing percentages, or automatic graduation. [Task 1][Task 2]\n  1514\t- `weaveMatchmakingPolicy.ts` deterministically builds eligibility/evidence and `weaveMatchmaking.ts` performs prepare/Jev/commit. Require consenting adults, completed interview evidence, mutual explicit gender preferences, no ban/current relationship, and distance checks; cap batches at six candidates/three proposals. Commit must recheck evidence fingerprints, consent, relationship/ban state, timing, and existing pairs. New proposals store uncalibrated provenance, not compatibility percentages. [Task 2]\n  1515\t- Venue ranking begins with real nearby venues and deterministic distance order. Apply Jev only for semantic fit; tie, diffuse confidence, missing evidence, or unavailable judgement preserves the original nearby order. Never infer price, hours, availability, accessibility, safety, or booking status. [Task 2]\n  1516\t\n  1517\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  1518\t\n  1519\t- Never run `skate list @secrets` in a way that prints values; list names only (for example `skate list @secrets | cut -f1`) and do not use WebFetch while secrets are in context. Credentials exposed in a session require rotation. [Task 1][Task 2]\n  1520\t- Blanket administrative review contradicted the user’s requested policy -> escalate only at probability >= `0.98`, confidence >= `0.95`, and margin >= `0.9`; uncertain/insufficient evidence abstains and does not queue review. Do not treat Jev as relationship-success probability or permission to auto-accept, reveal photos, schedule dates, or reject users. [Task 2]\n  1521\t- `devenv tasks run interleave:codegen` can fail its TypeScript phase when `/tmp` and `convex/_generated` differ filesystems -> set `CONVEX_TMPDIR` under the project filesystem, then run codegen, `interleave:typecheck`, `interleave:lint`, and `interleave:test` separately. The combined final verification was user-aborted; scoped 12 tests/67 assertions and formatting do not prove full integration. [Task 2]\n  1522\t\n  1523\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/keating Jev benchmark provenance and multilingual judge comparison\n  1524\tscope: Audit judgement benchmarks and provider comparisons without confusing completion, agreement, or evidence selection with independently validated accuracy.\n  1525\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating; reuse_rule=reinspect frozen artifacts, inputs, model revisions, denominator policy, and source session chronology before quoting results or changing model selection.\n  1526\t\n  1527\t## Task 1: Audit Jev's apparent 100% benchmark and Entire development history\n  1528\t\n  1529\t### rollout_summary_files\n  1530\t\n  1531\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/24/rollout-2026-09-24T04-11-24-01a0d278-26ce-7a12-bb7c-5e032d1f2e9c.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-24T22:15:17+00:00, thread_id=01a0d278-26ce-7a12-bb7c-5e032d1f2e9c, success; source/results and Entire chronology audited)\n  1532\t\n  1533\t### keywords\n  1534\t\n  1535\t- Jev, System One, Entire, jev-1.13.0, 18/18, 895/895, 34/124, 169/169, evidence-selection, __no_match__, .keating/tmp/laya/jev_bench.py, scripts/on-device-site/collect.py\n  1536\t\n  1537\t## Task 2: Complete a frozen six-language judgement-provider comparison\n  1538\t\n  1539\t### rollout_summary_files\n  1540\t\n  1541\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/24/rollout-2026-09-24T04-11-24-01a0d278-26ce-7a12-bb7c-5e032d1f2e9c.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-24T22:15:17+00:00, thread_id=01a0d278-26ce-7a12-bb7c-5e032d1f2e9c, success; integrity and temporary-GPU cleanup verified)\n  1542\t\n  1543\t### keywords\n  1544\t\n  1545\t- multilingual-v1, Kev, CLM, Laya, Astra, final-integrity-check.json, gpu-cleanup.json, 3600 receipts, 3599 validResponses, Jev Spanish, native-speaker review, sjuxnw207vhqvd\n  1546\t\n  1547\t## User preferences\n  1548\t\n  1549\t- when Jev was “getting a hundred” and “it seems sus,” the user asked to “check with entire to see as well the session and how that developed” -> audit both saved artifacts/current source and the original agent-session chronology before judging credibility. [Task 1]\n  1550\t- for benchmark claims, report what each metric proves and does not prove; distinguish response coverage, agreement, evidence selection, and independently validated accuracy. [Task 1]\n  1551\t- for provider comparisons, preserve failed/aborted work, keep accuracy and abstention separate, and clean up temporary compute instead of obscuring spend/failure boundaries. [Task 2]\n  1552\t\n  1553\t## Reusable knowledge\n  1554\t\n  1555\t- `.keating/tmp/laya/jev_bench.py` defined 18 authored subject-routing cases and 11 categories before calling `jev-1.13.0`; recorded `18/18` shows exact matches on that small explicit-label probe, not general judgement accuracy. `895/895` is answered dispatched requests, `34/124` is KEV agreement with Jev over 11 requests, and `169/169` only means non-`__no_match__` selection; none independently validate correctness/support. [Task 1]\n  1556\t- The audited Entire session `01a0c25c-da83-74d3-9568-05dd6ed00110` showed labels existed before the Jev call and no later mutation made results match. Needle remains reliable for verbatim-span extraction/local retrieval, not semantic routing. [Task 1]\n  1557\t- Frozen artifacts live in `.keating/benchmarks/context-window/multilingual-v1/`; retain original questions, labels, rubrics, Choice IDs, request hashes, provider/native revisions, full-context proof, and invalid/missing responses in `execution/final-integrity-check.json`. [Task 2]\n  1558\t- Twelve retained models produced 3,600 receipts and 3,599 valid responses. Jev led fixed-0.5 authored-label accuracy at roughly 92.6–95.1%; Kev 9B led local models at roughly 81.5–86.4%. These are not production calibration or human-learning evidence; evidence selection is a separate metric. [Task 2]\n  1559\t\n  1560\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  1561\t\n  1562\t- Do not call 18/18 general judgement accuracy, compare models with unequal criteria/input information, or infer calibrated correctness from confidence/abstention without independently labelled data. [Task 1]\n  1563\t- Keep cancelled Astra and the Jev Spanish validation failure in planned denominators; do not silently rerun, replace, or rank partial work. Translation variants share 25 workflow families, and hosted/native latency includes unlike transport/preflight costs. [Task 2]\n  1564\t\n  1565\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/keating Jev cascade investigation and production chat/model-picker fixes\n  1566\tscope: Advance the Jev/model-cascade only from current evidence, then ship narrowly scoped Keating chat/model-picker behavior without overstating visual proof.\n  1567\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating; reuse_rule=reinspect the current cascade plan, imports, shared-picker callers, worktree, and Railway status before extending or claiming deployment success.\n  1568\t\n  1569\t## Task 1: Audit Jev/model-cascade implementation against the full plan\n  1570\t\n  1571\t### rollout_summary_files\n  1572\t\n  1573\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/19/rollout-2026-09-19T16-07-23-01a0bb47-dbc1-7973-907b-80bc6b52bec1.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-20T18:45:21+00:00, thread_id=01a0bb47-dbc1-7973-907b-80bc6b52bec1, partial; focused judgement checks passed, full plan remains open)\n  1574\t\n  1575\t### keywords\n  1576\t\n  1577\t- Jev, TypeSafe, System One, docs/plans/jev-model-cascade.md, Choice, Score, Noul, questionDigest, contracts.ts, router.ts, proxy, observed, calibration, 120 pass\n  1578\t\n  1579\t## Task 2: Hide empty Flue assistant placeholders while preserving saved failures\n  1580\t\n  1581\t### rollout_summary_files\n  1582\t\n  1583\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/19/rollout-2026-09-19T16-07-23-01a0bb47-dbc1-7973-907b-80bc6b52bec1.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-20T18:45:21+00:00, thread_id=01a0bb47-dbc1-7973-907b-80bc6b52bec1, success; focused tests/typecheck, commit, push, and Railway success verified)\n  1584\t\n  1585\t### keywords\n  1586\t\n  1587\t- Flue, empty assistant rows, shouldRenderFlueMessage, AssistantChatPanel.tsx, assistant-chat-messages.ts, flue-message-visibility.test.ts, 29d69253f436524c38f2b91100096871ac9fb62b\n  1588\t\n  1589\t## Task 3: Pin Keating Cloud's provider default in shared model search\n  1590\t\n  1591\t### rollout_summary_files\n  1592\t\n  1593\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/19/rollout-2026-09-19T16-07-23-01a0bb47-dbc1-7973-907b-80bc6b52bec1.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-20T18:45:21+00:00, thread_id=01a0bb47-dbc1-7973-907b-80bc6b52bec1, success; focused tests/typecheck, clean tree, push, and Railway success verified)\n  1594\t\n  1595\t### keywords\n  1596\t\n  1597\t- ModelPicker, ModelSelector, orderedPickerItems, NOTORGANIC_DEFAULT_MODEL, Provider default, Inkling Small, model-picker-pinning.test.tsx, 170652660840096c43829f6205f5fb4c115989ae\n  1598\t\n  1599\t## User preferences\n  1600\t\n  1601\t- when advancing the cascade, the user explicitly asked for “Entire history, TypeSafe/System One, decomposed Jev questions, exhaustive self-judgement, and subagents” -> inspect current state first; use narrow typed questions with abstention and prove every plan requirement from current files/tests/runtime evidence. [Task 1]\n  1602\t- when the user asked to push changes once done -> complete focused checks, commit, push, deployment-status, and clean-tree verification; do not call the UI visually verified without a browser/manual pass. [Task 2][Task 3]\n  1603\t- when the user clarified “it should have provider default and be pinned to the top” -> label the provider default explicitly and keep it first through model switching and search without resurrecting caller-excluded items. [Task 3]\n  1604\t\n  1605\t## Reusable knowledge\n  1606\t\n  1607\t- TypeSafe System One is `POST https://api.typesafe.ai/v1/systemone` with `{state, model, questions}`; batch independent questions over the same narrowly structured state. Use `Noul` for one absolute condition, `Choice` for relative alternatives, explicit abstention, and code-owned arithmetic/counts/dates. `Score` levels are not reliable magnitude interpolation. [Task 1]\n  1608\t- Judgement outputs are `proxy`, never `observed` or promotion eligibility; selected evidence must come from real learner spans. Calibration keys include backend/model/question digest and cannot cross backends. `questionDigest` lives in `packages/learner-contracts/src/judgement/contracts.ts`, not `router.ts`; importing it from `router.ts` caused module-load failures. [Task 1]\n  1609\t- Empty failed Flue attempts are a render-projection issue: `shouldRenderFlueMessage` hides only empty/whitespace assistant placeholders and non-visible diagnostics, while retaining user messages, partial text, reasoning, tools, attachments, settlement notices, lifecycle/error state, and retry controls. [Task 2]\n  1610\t- The shared picker serves chat/live/review/training/speech/image. Use opt-in item metadata: `NOTORGANIC_DEFAULT_MODEL` (`balanced`, `Inkling Small`) is pinned, then the selected non-default model, then ordinary query-filtered items; caller exclusions remain excluded. [Task 3]\n  1611\t\n  1612\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  1613\t\n  1614\t- Focused post-fix judgement validation (`120 pass, 0 fail`) does not establish the full cascade: benchmark agreement, remaining judge-site migrations, end-to-end learner integrations, and calibration/runtime gates remained unverified. Entire semantic search failed on authentication/keyring access; use local `entire session list`/`checkpoint explain` or restore auth. [Task 1]\n  1615\t- Production deployment status proves the scoped code shipped, not browser/manual behavior. The Flue and picker fixes had focused tests/typecheck plus Railway `SUCCESS`, but no browser/manual test. [Task 2][Task 3]\n  1616\t\n  1617\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/twyne production provider relay and auth/session recovery\n  1618\tscope: Operate Twyne's shared remote-BYOK transport and harden Convex, Not Organic, and ATProto browser-session recovery without overstating signed-in account proof.\n  1619\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne; reuse_rule=recheck current provider configuration, Railway proxy headers, OAuth grants, Convex deployment, live account state, and dirty worktree before reuse or production claims.\n  1620\t\n  1621\t## Task 1: Deploy a generalized remote-provider relay\n  1622\t\n  1623\t### rollout_summary_files\n  1624\t\n  1625\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/20/rollout-2026-09-20T13-41-47-01a0bfe8-ea41-7552-a283-0faea9208674.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-20T18:52:35+00:00, thread_id=01a0bfe8-ea41-7552-a283-0faea9208674, success; MiniMax/OpenAI dummy-key transport smoke verified)\n  1626\t\n  1627\t### keywords\n  1628\t\n  1629\t- /api/provider/, provider-fetch.ts, provider-relay.server.ts, SSRF, DNS pinning, X-Forwarded-Proto, PROTOCOL_HEADER, CSRF check failed, MiniMax, OpenAI, Railway d7378eae-ef0c-4369-ad4c-9e4dc0a70b65\n  1630\t\n  1631\t## Task 2: Refresh Convex tokens and reconnect existing Not Organic links\n  1632\t\n  1633\t### rollout_summary_files\n  1634\t\n  1635\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/20/rollout-2026-09-20T13-41-47-01a0bfe8-ea41-7552-a283-0faea9208674.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-20T18:52:35+00:00, thread_id=01a0bfe8-ea41-7552-a283-0faea9208674, partial; unit proof, signed-in account flow open)\n  1636\t\n  1637\t### keywords\n  1638\t\n  1639\t- createConvexTokenFetcher, forceRefreshToken, hasAuthenticatedConvexIdentity, convexAuthenticated, Reconnect Not Organic, Check again, providerIdentity.ts\n  1640\t\n  1641\t## Task 3: Recover ATProto/Bluesky stale sessions without consuming other callbacks\n  1642\t\n  1643\t### rollout_summary_files\n  1644\t\n  1645\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/20/rollout-2026-09-20T13-41-47-01a0bfe8-ea41-7552-a283-0faea9208674.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-20T18:52:35+00:00, thread_id=01a0bfe8-ea41-7552-a283-0faea9208674, partial; exact production 400 not reproduced)\n  1646\t\n  1647\t### keywords\n  1648\t\n  1649\t- atproto.ts, ATPROTO_SESSION_CHANGED, initSessionPromise, stale token set, invalid_grant, use_dpop_nonce, /auth/callback/, PUBLIC_BSKY_APPVIEW\n  1650\t\n  1651\t## User preferences\n  1652\t\n  1653\t- when the user said “make sure that this solution doesn't only work for minimax but is gen purpose” -> fix provider transport as a shared abstraction across configured remote providers, not a reported-provider special case. [Task 1]\n  1654\t- when an already-connected account could not connect in Settings, the user expected existing state to be queried/reactively exposed with a reconnect path rather than an initial-connect-only UI. [Task 2]\n  1655\t\n  1656\t## Reusable knowledge\n  1657\t\n  1658\t- Remote providers use same-origin `/api/provider/` via `src/utils/provider-fetch.ts`; loopback endpoints remain direct. `provider-relay.server.ts` restricts targets to public HTTPS, pins DNS, rejects private/reserved/mapped addresses and redirects, restricts headers/cookies, bounds bodies, and forwards streaming responses without response cookies/CORS headers. [Task 1]\n  1659\t- Railway TLS termination needs `PROTOCOL_HEADER=x-forwarded-proto` in `server.js`; otherwise Qwik inferred `http://twyne.love` and rejected production POSTs with `403 CSRF check failed`. Dummy MiniMax/OpenAI keys returned expected readable 401s, proving transport but not valid-key behavior for all providers. [Task 1]\n  1660\t- `createConvexTokenFetcher` single-flights refreshes and must honor `forceRefreshToken`; `hasAuthenticatedConvexIdentity` still requires a product user, `provider: \"convex\"`, and `convexAuthenticated === true`. Existing link UI supports reactive DID state, reconnect, and check-again. [Task 2]\n  1661\t- Reuse active ATProto session/profile with single-flight initialization; consume OAuth callback parameters only at `/auth/callback/`. Public profile hydration uses `https://public.api.bsky.app`; preserve the DID rather than adding arbitrary audience-bound scope. [Task 3]\n  1662\t\n  1663\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  1664\t\n  1665\t- Configure forwarded-protocol handling before live POST tests. Focused `76 pass`, typecheck/lint/build, diff check, `/settings/` 200, and smoke were verified, but a dirty worktree remained and no Convex production deployment occurred. [Task 1]\n  1666\t- Do not claim the account-specific Not Organic callback/link flow or the user's exact Bluesky 400 recovery is fixed until a signed-in browser verifies it. [Task 2][Task 3]\n  1667\t\n  1668\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/keating MiniCPM5 WebGPU diagnostics and error classification\n  1669\tscope: Diagnose actual browser-model runtime failures and expose bounded, privacy-safe diagnostic evidence without mistaking adapter support for model execution.\n  1670\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating; reuse_rule=reinspect target hardware, browser/runtime versions, model artifact, and deployment state; this verified instrumentation, not a Windows-GPU root-cause fix.\n  1671\t\n  1672\t## Task 1: Diagnose and instrument MiniCPM5 ONNX Runtime WebGPU failures\n  1673\t\n  1674\t### rollout_summary_files\n  1675\t\n  1676\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/20/rollout-2026-09-20T15-12-01-01a0c03b-8622-7e20-95bf-bb748d4fb7fc.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-20T19:41:27+00:00, thread_id=01a0c03b-8622-7e20-95bf-bb748d4fb7fc, partial; diagnostics/build verified, target device not retested)\n  1677\t\n  1678\t### keywords\n  1679\t\n  1680\t- MiniCPM5-2B-ONNX, RASMUS, q4f16, OrtRun, BufferManager::Download, mapAsync, Invalid Buffer, local-model-diagnostics.ts, keating:local-model-debug, shader-f16\n  1681\t\n  1682\t## User preferences\n  1683\t\n  1684\t- when the user supplied hardware and `edge://gpu` evidence, they wanted diagnosis based on the actual adapter/runtime rather than generic compatibility advice; when they asked to “see if we can expose this with some improved errors,” -> add observability before claiming a root-cause fix. [Task 1]\n  1685\t\n  1686\t## Reusable knowledge\n  1687\t\n  1688\t- `web/src/lib/local-model-diagnostics.ts` observes the actual ONNX Runtime device without creating a second adapter/device/model; reports capture model/dtype/phase, runtime versions, token limits, features/limits, adapter info, first device error/loss, capped operation errors, and original runtime error. Enable with `localStorage.setItem(\"keating:local-model-debug\", \"1\")`, reload, copy `[local-model] diagnostics`, then remove the key. [Task 1]\n  1689\t- `classifyLocalModelError` distinguishes device loss, allocation/buffer-limit failures, invalid-buffer readback, missing adapter/`shader-f16`, unsupported quantization, and generic WebGPU execution. Eight focused tests, web typecheck, production build, and `git diff --check` passed. [Task 1]\n  1690\t\n  1691\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  1692\t\n  1693\t- `shader-f16`, a working adapter, and 2 GiB limits do not prove MiniCPM5 can execute. `Invalid Buffer` alone does not prove OOM: capture the first validation/allocation error or device-loss reason. The Intel Iris Xe target root cause remains unverified. [Task 1]\n  1694\t\n  1695\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/keating Jev/Needle routing, teaching-policy benchmark, and draft gate\n  1696\tscope: Use typed Jev decisions and deterministic checks for teaching/OpenUI behavior; restrict Needle to measured extraction/shortlisting rather than semantic authority.\n  1697\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating; reuse_rule=recheck model/provider availability, corpus, benchmark configuration, and dirty-worktree state before activation or claims of learning efficacy.\n  1698\t\n  1699\t## Task 1: Evaluate Needle subject routing and local-model roles\n  1700\t\n  1701\t### rollout_summary_files\n  1702\t\n  1703\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/21/rollout-2026-09-21T01-07-40-01a0c25c-da83-74d3-9568-05dd6ed00110.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-21T07:56:03+00:00, thread_id=01a0c25c-da83-74d3-9568-05dd6ed00110, partial; reproducible fine-tune inadequate)\n  1704\t\n  1705\t### keywords\n  1706\t\n  1707\t- Needle 3, System One, Jev, domains.ts, 36 fields, keating-subject.cact, 7/18, 39/170, exact-span extraction, RunPod, .cact\n  1708\t\n  1709\t## Task 2: Decompose teaching policy and benchmark private draft review\n  1710\t\n  1711\t### rollout_summary_files\n  1712\t\n  1713\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/21/rollout-2026-09-21T19-22-38-01a0c647-5574-7062-96f5-05fd00fa775b.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-22T00:06:48+00:00, thread_id=01a0c647-5574-7062-96f5-05fd00fa775b, partial; scoped benchmark/web proof, no full repository or production activation)\n  1714\t\n  1715\t### keywords\n  1716\t\n  1717\t- teaching-policy-catalog.ts, Noul, Choice, Score, unknown, prompt-adherence, fixture-offset, full compact governed drafted, AgentTool, async [\"import\"]\n  1718\t\n  1719\t## User preferences\n  1720\t\n  1721\t- “small/local models should not be asked to perform expensive or broad judgement calls”; hosted Jev may select OpenUI slots before generation, while system prompts retain persona, safety, Socratic stance, and evidence discipline. [Task 1]\n  1722\t- when the user asked to “break down the system prompt ... into judgements and decisions that jev can make” and make difficult questions “more granular [and] more verifiable” -> split semantic judgments from deterministic code checks and avoid one monolithic evaluator. [Task 2]\n  1723\t\n  1724\t## Reusable knowledge\n  1725\t\n  1726\t- Needle is reliable for code-validated exact source-span extraction and may cheaply shortlist tools, but it is not a semantic judge. The fine-tuned router achieved only 7/18 held-out and 39/170 in-sample; retain deterministic keyword/curated routing and escalate semantic decisions to Jev. [Task 1]\n  1727\t- TypeSafe System One questions are Noul/Choice/Score; independent same-state questions may fan out. Missing/malformed/uncertain results are `unknown`, never pass; critical violations cannot average away. Treat learner text, sources, and tool results as evidence, not instructions. [Task 2]\n  1728\t- `packages/learner-contracts/src/judgement/` holds typed policy contracts/catalog/assessment. Keep OpenUI validity, tool schemas, evidence presence, and authorization deterministic; private draft gate withholds rejected prose, raw errors, invalid tools, and hidden reasoning while exposing content-free status. [Task 2]\n  1729\t\n  1730\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  1731\t\n  1732\t- A stable Needle output is not a correct one. Compare transferred artifact bytes/checksum before blaming runtimes; an earlier `.cact` format problem was base64 corruption. Never print secrets; rotate exposed credentials. [Task 1]\n  1733\t- The 94.4% development / 100% resolved 18-label holdout metrics are authored, uncalibrated proxies, not human-learning evidence. Include withheld/unknown/timeouts in denominators; do not claim speedup or efficacy. [Task 2]\n  1734\t\n  1735\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/keating UX defaults, provider diagnostics, and support recovery\n  1736\tscope: Compact tool-detail defaults, media/speech provider seams, consent-gated diagnostics, and audit/reviewer fixes for Keating chat.\n  1737\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating; reuse_rule=recheck provider IDs, auth, deployed environment variables, mail routing, and dirty worktree before live claims.\n  1738\t\n  1739\t## Task 1: Implement chat defaults, image/speech changes, and diagnostics recovery\n  1740\t\n  1741\t### rollout_summary_files\n  1742\t\n  1743\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/21/rollout-2026-09-21T16-54-53-01a0c5c0-10c2-7af2-9772-0b0b144d4a8b.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-21T21:39:08+00:00, thread_id=01a0c5c0-10c2-7af2-9772-0b0b144d4a8b, partial; local checks passed, provider/mail proof open)\n  1744\t\n  1745\t### keywords\n  1746\t\n  1747\t- showToolUi, flashcardSoundEnabled, image-generators.ts, gpt-image-2.5-flare, gemini-generate-content, GPT Live, microphoneEnabled, diagnosticsReporting, mailto:help@keating.help, Resend\n  1748\t\n  1749\t## Task 2: Audit Entire request coverage and repair reviewer findings\n  1750\t\n  1751\t### rollout_summary_files\n  1752\t\n  1753\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/21/rollout-2026-09-21T17-42-48-01a0c5eb-edbf-7a10-a2c8-1a938954381d.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-21T22:47:13+00:00, thread_id=01a0c5eb-edbf-7a10-a2c8-1a938954381d, success; local audit/focused fixes only)\n  1754\t\n  1755\t### keywords\n  1756\t\n  1757\t- entire checkpoint explain --raw-transcript, ModelPicker, KeatingApiKeyPromptDialog, Retry-After, 429, resolveImageQuality, nodepod-boot-files.ts, railway logs --service keating\n  1758\t\n  1759\t## User preferences\n  1760\t\n  1761\t- the user does not want “tool calling details to be shown in chat by default” and wants flashcard sounds on by default -> use compact transcripts and enabled feedback sounds unless settings explicitly say otherwise. [Task 1]\n  1762\t- for unknown failures, the user wants contextual diagnostics submission, an easy email fallback when declined, and a small consent step -> offer actionable recovery rather than generic error text. [Task 1]\n  1763\t- when auditing prior work, the user asked to check the Entire CLI session and “the things thata i requested” -> extract every substantive request and compare it item by item with implementation, distinguishing local completion, partial work, blocks, and live verification. [Task 2]\n  1764\t\n  1765\t## Reusable knowledge\n  1766\t\n  1767\t- Web settings are `showToolUi: false`, `flashcardSoundEnabled: true`; mobile's `showToolDetails: false` is distinct from interactive-card `showToolUi`. Diagnostics default off, redact/cap client data, use `/api/diagnostics/report`, then send via Resend or log fallback; specialized known errors keep specialized actions. [Task 1]\n  1768\t- GPT Live is gated by `NOTORGANIC_ENABLED`; duplex selection/enabling turns on `microphoneEnabled`, but TTS stays opt-in. `web/src/lib/image-generators.ts` is the catalog; provider model IDs have not had live smoke proof. [Task 1]\n  1769\t- Entire fallback for parser failure is `entire checkpoint explain <id> --raw-transcript`. Close `ModelPicker` before the API-key dialog. A per-process diagnostics limiter returns explicit `Response.json` 429 plus `Retry-After: 900`; regenerate NodePod boot files after source changes. [Task 2]\n  1770\t\n  1771\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  1772\t\n  1773\t- `help@keating.help` is not operational proof: forwarding MX/SPF without DKIM/DMARC, destination inbox, and external send/receive remains insufficient. Diagnostics throttling resets per replica/restart and is not a deployment-wide quota. [Task 1][Task 2]\n  1774\t- Do not treat Entire's index as complete, GitNexus stale/truncated output as conclusive, or local focused tests as browser/live-provider/deployment/email validation. [Task 2]\n  1775\t\n  1776\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/textbook package publication, Radicle, copyable docs, and production routing\n  1777\tscope: Publish Textbook safely, maintain the repo-local/public Radicle workflow, make dynamically rendered docs controls work, and keep production destinations distinct from local defaults.\n  1778\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/textbook; reuse_rule=reinspect package availability, configured Radicle remote/RID, Railway service state, and current URL variables before publishing/deploying.\n  1779\t\n  1780\t## Task 1: Publish textbook-sh and deploy all four product surfaces\n  1781\t\n  1782\t### rollout_summary_files\n  1783\t\n  1784\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/textbook, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/21/rollout-2026-09-21T02-00-34-01a0c28d-4957-75e2-8569-a6e6a687566f.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-21T09:28:16+00:00, thread_id=01a0c28d-4957-75e2-8569-a6e6a687566f, success; package/live surfaces verified)\n  1785\t\n  1786\t### keywords\n  1787\t\n  1788\t- textbook-sh, bunx textbook, delegated click handling, role=status, RAD_HOME, .radicle, railway pre-push, textbook.sh, docs.textbook.sh\n  1789\t\n  1790\t## Task 2: Repair public landing localhost redirects\n  1791\t\n  1792\t### rollout_summary_files\n  1793\t\n  1794\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/textbook, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/21/rollout-2026-09-21T18-11-14-01a0c605-f556-7002-8478-41263fd6c87e.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-21T23:06:56+00:00, thread_id=01a0c605-f556-7002-8478-41263fd6c87e, partial; diagnosis)\n  1795\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/textbook, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/21/rollout-2026-09-21T19-09-00-01a0c63a-d7fd-7161-81ad-7380b176e6e2.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-22T00:53:50+00:00, thread_id=01a0c63a-d7fd-7161-81ad-7380b176e6e2, success; public redirects verified)\n  1796\t\n  1797\t### keywords\n  1798\t\n  1799\t- railway.landing.json, LANDING_URL, DOCS_URL, TERMINAL_URL, CANVAS_URL, localhost:8008, /canvas, a53b9fd4-0bde-429f-a169-4667a13eac30, rad\n  1800\t\n  1801\t## User preferences\n  1802\t\n  1803\t- “if textbook-sh is free as a package name let's take that” -> prefer the simplest available unscoped package; “just push to main without republish right now” -> do not republish as an implied deploy step. [Task 1]\n  1804\t- “search for what is sending you to localhost in prod ... change it to the correct host unless we are launching local,” then “deplpy” -> preserve local defaults but make production navigation environment-driven and deploy the verified correction. [Task 2]\n  1805\t\n  1806\t## Reusable knowledge\n  1807\t\n  1808\t- `textbook-sh@0.2.0` provides `textbook`, `tb`, and `textbook-sh`. Docs injected after load need delegated document-level handling, with accessible copied/failure status. Repo-local Radicle uses `RAD_HOME=/home/diogenes/Projects/textbook/.radicle`; its pre-push hook deploys landing/docs/terminal/canvas independently. [Task 1]\n  1809\t- `src/site.ts` keeps local 8000/8001/8002/8008 defaults; `railway.landing.json` and live service variables must explicitly set all four public hosts. After config deployment, inspect actual Railway service state and live redirect locations. [Task 2]\n  1810\t\n  1811\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  1812\t\n  1813\t- Per-button listeners fail for dynamic docs; test DOM mocks require `addEventListener`/`removeEventListener`. Bare `git push rad main` can fail without repo-local `RAD_HOME`. [Task 1]\n  1814\t- Do not replace every `localhost` occurrence: local documentation may be intentional. Legacy Railway service-level settings can survive a repo-config deployment; verify `/canvas`, `/docs`, and `/terminal` publicly. [Task 2]\n  1815\t\n  1816\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/twyne Needle scope, v0.21.0 release, and adaptive editorial drafting\n  1817\tscope: Keep the Cactus Needle concept separate from an unrelated npm dependency, verify desktop/release boundaries, and apply Keating-style typed private review to editorial generation.\n  1818\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne; reuse_rule=recheck provider/model behavior, credentials, passkey deployment, and worktree state; local/static proof does not establish live judgement behavior.\n  1819\t\n  1820\t## Task 1: Investigate Needle and publish Twyne 0.21.0\n  1821\t\n  1822\t### rollout_summary_files\n  1823\t\n  1824\t- rollout_summaries/2026-09-21T06-48-19-f9lZ-twyne_needle_investigation_and_v0210_release.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/21/rollout-2026-09-21T02-48-19-01a0c2b9-00e5-79a2-be4b-13a578e0598f.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-21T09:41:56+00:00, thread_id=01a0c2b9-00e5-79a2-be4b-13a578e0598f, success; release/Railway/assets verified)\n  1825\t\n  1826\t### keywords\n  1827\t\n  1828\t- Cactus-Compute/needle, passage-triage.ts, nothing advice question evidence cut, MiniCPM5-2B, LFM2.5, --jinja, v0.21.0, passkey-origin.ts, twyne.love\n  1829\t\n  1830\t## Task 2: Implement adaptive editorial drafting with Jev\n  1831\t\n  1832\t### rollout_summary_files\n  1833\t\n  1834\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/21/rollout-2026-09-21T21-52-13-01a0c6d0-476b-7642-8dae-393ed1e4e8ad.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-22T02:34:25+00:00, thread_id=01a0c6d0-476b-7642-8dae-393ed1e4e8ad, success; static/full-suite verification, no live provider run)\n  1835\t\n  1836\t### keywords\n  1837\t\n  1838\t- buildSystemPrompt, editorial-protocol.md, adaptive-editorial-draft.ts, reviewEditorialNote, systemOne.ask, reasoning-effort.ts, unreviewed, withheld\n  1839\t\n  1840\t## User preferences\n  1841\t\n  1842\t- the user prefers a smaller local model over Gemma 4 E4B for packaging/performance, suggesting MiniCPM5-2B or LFM2.5 2B. [Task 1]\n  1843\t- for Twyne, use Keating’s approach: deconstruct persona/system behavior into typed inspectable Jev rules that control generation, rather than only locating or rewriting prompt prose. [Task 2]\n  1844\t\n  1845\t## Reusable knowledge\n  1846\t\n  1847\t- The npm `needle@3.5.0` is an unrelated transitive `less` dependency. Intended Cactus Needle has no loader in this checkout; `passage-triage.ts` describes a closed-label offline adapter while active live triage uses hosted Jev. [Task 1]\n  1848\t- Active prompt builder is `convex/agentPrompts.ts` `buildSystemPrompt()` with `buildUserPrompt()` context assembly. Separate persona identity from `prompts/editorial-protocol.md`; controller retries private candidates using code-owned repair instructions and exposes content-free statuses. Missing Jev output is `unreviewed`, never a synthetic pass; critical vetoes withhold output. [Task 2]\n  1849\t\n  1850\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  1851\t\n  1852\t- A discovered package name is not the product model integration. Passkey production must use RP ID `twyne.love` and allow both apex/www origins; validate the deployed endpoint. [Task 1]\n  1853\t- Static tests (1549 pass/39 skip) did not prove an actual Jev/provider/Not Organic run. Do not expose rejected candidate text or hidden reasoning in repair prompts/status UI. [Task 2]\n  1854\t\n  1855\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/notorganic-provider launch readiness, sandbox neutrality, and private Radicle release\n  1856\tscope: Keep legal/mail/payment launch gates explicit, expose replaceable code-execution through Not Organic, and release the provider only through its verified private Radicle boundary.\n  1857\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/notorganic-provider; reuse_rule=recheck legal review, DNS/mail, Paddle mode, paid-provider status, credentials, and current private RID before external claims/actions.\n  1858\t\n  1859\t## Task 1: Harden legal, Paddle, mail, and hosted-sandbox readiness\n  1860\t\n  1861\t### rollout_summary_files\n  1862\t\n  1863\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/notorganic-provider, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/21/rollout-2026-09-21T04-14-08-01a0c307-9223-7c91-82d5-ed9d8bfb43f9.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-21T09:38:45+00:00, thread_id=01a0c307-9223-7c91-82d5-ed9d8bfb43f9, partial; checks/catalog/worker upload succeeded, launch gates r