1961\t### keywords\n  1962\t\n  1963\t- Railway, staging, devenv up, scripts/staging.ts, keating:staging-deploy, Entire, Claude, dirty-worktree, promotionEligible, keating-staging.up.railway.app/chat, RAILWAY_TOKEN, RAILWAY_STAGING_TOKEN\n  1964\t\n  1965\t## User preferences\n  1966\t\n  1967\t- when deploying the current work, the user asked for “the work that is done in the claude session” to be “up in the staging environment for me to try” -> reconcile Entire, Git, Codex sessions, and the worktree together; include intended dirty work in a staging snapshot and provide a directly usable URL, but never promote it as a clean production candidate. [Task 1]\n  1968\t- when the user explicitly asked to “use `sh entire`” -> do not infer missing work from Git or Entire alone; cross-check both with Codex session archives/checkpoints. [Task 1]\n  1969\t\n  1970\t## Reusable knowledge\n  1971\t\n  1972\t- `scripts/staging.ts` snapshots tracked and untracked application files while excluding `.env*`, credentials, generated state, databases, and build output. `devenv up` includes the staging process; use `bun scripts/staging.ts deploy`, `bun scripts/staging.ts status`, or `devenv tasks run keating:staging-deploy`. Dirty snapshots are marked `promotionEligible: false` and deliberately cannot promote. [Task 1]\n  1973\t- Captured staging proof: Railway project `keating` has a `staging` environment; deployment `7fe59e0f-300f-43f5-95a5-56bf04c0302f` reached `SUCCESS`, and `https://keating-staging.up.railway.app/chat` rendered the chat UI. Production branch auto-deploy was disconnected; staging uploads do not use GitHub. [Task 1]\n  1974\t- Promotion service `keating-promotion` uses hourly cron `17 * * * *` and persistent `/data`. A fresh diagnostic container, not sealed-variable metadata, established that `RAILWAY_STAGING_TOKEN` was nonempty and could access staging while `RAILWAY_TOKEN` was present but empty; edit only the production token value, then freshly verify both environment accesses. [Task 1]\n  1975\t- Local judgement direct mode is `KEATING_JUDGEMENT_DEV_DIRECT=1|true` with server-only `TYPESAFE_API_KEY`; browser same-origin is exact `VITE_KEATING_JUDGEMENT_SAME_ORIGIN=true`. Captured checks: root `bun run test` 837 pass/0 fail, web 2,215 pass/1 skipped/0 failures, `git diff --check`, and `bun scripts/check-env-docs.ts` passed. [Task 1]\n  1976\t\n  1977\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  1978\t\n  1979\t- A staging `SUCCESS` and rendered shell do not prove signed-in login, hosted inference, hosted judgement, or `chat.keating.help` DNS/TLS. Keep those as open runtime checks. [Task 1]\n  1980\t- Sealed Railway variable metadata does not prove a usable secret: symptom `RAILWAY_TOKEN present=true nonEmpty=false` -> re-enter only that production value and run a fresh worker/container probe before calling promotion operational. [Task 1]\n  1981\t- `bun test test` selects unrelated mobile/native suites. Use canonical root `bun run test`; report the known wider judgement-runtime local-first versus hosted-first test conflict separately. [Task 1]\n  1982\t\n  1983\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/keating OpenUI component selection and sticky learning state\n  1984\tscope: Trace and improve OpenUI generation/judgement so component use is capability-based, longitudinal, and bounded rather than a narrow question-answer gate.\n  1985\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating; reuse_rule=reinspect the dirty worktree and actual runtime turns; this rollout provides source-backed architecture and partial code evidence, not a verified live root cause or completed redesign.\n  1986\t\n  1987\t## Task 1: Trace OpenUI generation, judgment, budgets, and reasoning ratings\n  1988\t\n  1989\t### rollout_summary_files\n  1990\t\n  1991\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/23/rollout-2026-09-23T17-57-52-01a0d046-715d-7b92-b395-bacd83824b1c.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-24T00:58:17+00:00, thread_id=01a0d046-715d-7b92-b395-bacd83824b1c, partial; trace complete, reasoning-rating change lacks package-green proof)\n  1992\t\n  1993\t### keywords\n  1994\t\n  1995\t- OpenUI, keatingOpenUIPrompt, AssistantChatPanel, withTeachingDraftGate, teaching-drafts.ts, 90 seconds, max_length 1024, openui_valid, TS2345, local fallback, hosted-primary\n  1996\t\n  1997\t## Task 2: Design capability-based component selection and sticky active work\n  1998\t\n  1999\t### rollout_summary_files\n  2000\t\n  2001\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/23/rollout-2026-09-23T17-57-52-01a0d046-715d-7b92-b395-bacd83824b1c.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-24T00:58:17+00:00, thread_id=01a0d046-715d-7b92-b395-bacd83824b1c, uncertain; design direction only)\n  2002\t\n  2003\t### keywords\n  2004\t\n  2005\t- component-selection, interactive-underuse, sticky-context, teachingDraftEvidence, ComingUpReadiness, StudyPlan, ConceptMap, assisted correctness, independent correctness, retention, transfer, nested judgments\n  2006\t\n  2007\t## User preferences\n  2008\t\n  2009\t- when diagnosing absent interfaces, the user asked for “where the budget code is,” “which model is the judge,” and “what happens when creating one” -> explain prompt, private generation, validation, rendering, persistence, and runtime configuration as separate stages. [Task 1]\n  2010\t- “local should be the fallback not the default” -> use hosted-primary/local-fallback as the target direction, while clearly marking that this rollout did not implement it. [Task 1]\n  2011\t- “depend on question would also underuse openui” -> do not gate interaction only on immediate learner answers; assess useful component capabilities across all component families and preserve active lesson-plan/result context beyond the sliding transcript window. [Task 2]\n  2012\t\n  2013\t## Reusable knowledge\n  2014\t\n  2015\t- Tutor output contains fenced OpenUI source: `useKeatingAgent.tsx` appends `keatingOpenUIPrompt`, then `AssistantChatPanel` parses/renders it. `withTeachingDraftGate` privately generates, runs Jev/deterministic review, retries/revises, and releases only approved text. Default budget is 90 seconds (cap 180), normally 3 attempts; local browser generation defaults to `max_length: 1024`. [Task 1]\n  2016\t- OpenUI compilation is inert and bounded: source 131072, 64 statements, collection 512, depth 24. Current checks validate OpenUI when emitted (`openui_valid`, activity/checkpoint constraints), so no OpenUI generally passes and underuse is not detected. [Task 1][Task 2]\n  2017\t- Use deterministic state for presented/submitted/tested/graded/completed facts; use Jev for open-response adequacy, support need, move-on readiness, plan-item detail, and revision. `teachingDraftEvidence()` already exposes learner state/goals/results/gaps/pending submissions; `ComingUpReadiness` binds saved plans to document revisions, prerequisites, and receipts. [Task 2]\n  2018\t- Sticky active-work records should retain component/document/revision, objective or plan-item linkage, presented content, submission, assistance/grading, unresolved work, and next action; send only a bounded outline/current branch/relevant prerequisites/evidence projection to the judge. Keep exposure, completion, assisted correctness, independent correctness, retention, and transfer distinct. [Task 2]\n  2019\t\n  2020\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  2021\t\n  2022\t- Do not claim a runtime root cause without a real observed turn; source review identified plausible suppressors only. GitNexus was stale/incomplete, so pivot to `rg` and direct source reads. [Task 1]\n  2023\t- Source-only TypeScript passed after replacing one broad reasoning Choice with three Score questions, but package typecheck had `TS2345` in `packages/learner-contracts/test/teaching-drafts.test.ts:23,42` and tests were not run. Do not call it green until package checks are repaired/rerun. [Task 1]\n  2024\t- Avoid maximizing interface count or reevaluating a full curriculum every turn. Use benefit/burden, existing active artifacts, and relevant nested state; a binary “interactive needed?” selector suppresses simulations, maps, and plans. [Task 2]\n  2025\t\n  2026\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/keating Needle on-device retrieval audit and measurement plan\n  2027\tscope: Evaluate Needle and phone-suitable retrieval/judgement alternatives with local corpus/device measurements, preserving exact-span extraction while not overstating unmeasured replacements.\n  2028\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating; reuse_rule=recheck pinned runtime, corpus, device profile, artifact licenses, and current benchmark harnesses before choosing or shipping a replacement.\n  2029\t\n  2030\t## Task 1: Audit Needle and identify a measured replacement path\n  2031\t\n  2032\t### rollout_summary_files\n  2033\t\n  2034\t- rollout_summaries/2026-09-22T19-25-32-LkDZ-needle_on_device_alternatives_and_measurement_plan.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/22/rollout-2026-09-22T15-25-32-01a0ca94-9f32-7140-b035-542d903b93b7.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-24T07:23:12+00:00, thread_id=01a0ca94-9f32-7140-b035-542d903b93b7, partial; existing Needle evidence found, alternatives unmeasured)\n  2035\t\n  2036\t### keywords\n  2037\t\n  2038\t- Needle 3.0.1, b274efcb211a9eef48c9a88da4b43bd569696a39, 3072-dimensional, docs/blog/needle-subject-routing.md, Model2Vec, Potion, reranker, LiteRT, ONNX, needle-recall-bench.ts, KEV, mobile\n  2039\t\n  2040\t## User preferences\n  2041\t\n  2042\t- when considering a replacement, the user said it must be “reasonable to package with application and not be absurd to run on phones” -> treat package bytes, RAM, battery/thermal behavior, cancellation, portability, and offline support as first-class acceptance criteria. [Task 1]\n  2043\t- the user asked to “try measuring them” and inspect “entire cli sessions for experiments” -> use reproducible local corpus/device measurements and inspect the actual historical session artifacts before recommendations. [Task 1]\n  2044\t\n  2045\t## Reusable knowledge\n  2046\t\n  2047\t- Needle 3.0.1 is pinned at `b274efcb211a9eef48c9a88da4b43bd569696a39`; weights are 35,335,380 bytes, embeddings are 3,072-dimensional, and execution spans CLI Python subprocess, browser WASM, and native C-ABI mobile bindings. Native mobile execution is process-global without cancellation/unload. [Task 1]\n  2048\t- Existing `docs/blog/needle-subject-routing.md` evidence: subject classification 2/8 with tool calls, 1/8 enum extraction, 0/8 embedding-prototype top-1; paraphrase recall R@1 10%, below lexical baselines. Needle remains reliable for exact quote/span extraction but not semantic routing/classification. [Task 1]\n  2049\t- Candidate architecture remains a proposal: static embeddings for shortlist/ranking, tiny cross-encoder reranking/exact-span/category selection, and existing LiteRT/ONNX or hosted Jev for consequential judgement. Start from `.keating/tmp/needle-recall-bench.ts`, `needle-recall-bench2.ts`, and Laya/Von/GLiNER harnesses. [Task 1]\n  2050\t\n  2051\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  2052\t\n  2053\t- No candidate benchmark, phone profile, license check, or artifact integration was completed. Measure latency, resident memory, artifact size, recall/classification accuracy, cancellation, battery, and thermal impact on Keating corpus/target phone before treating published claims as comparable. [Task 1]\n  2054\t- Historical CLI/KEV search was partial; enumerate `/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions` and inspect relevant rollout/session artifacts directly rather than relying only on repo grep. [Task 1]\n  2055\t\n  2056\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/dio-machines environment configuration and Fugu tool sync\n  2057\tscope: Route machine, service, project, and secret environment variables correctly and mirror the canonical Codex Fugu catalog/default into OpenCode and Crush.\n  2058\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/dio-machines with user config paths under /home/diogenes; reuse_rule=reinspect current Home Manager configuration, live secret-store access, provider availability, and persisted tool state before edits or claims.\n  2059\t\n  2060\t## Task 1: Map environment-variable scope and secret handling\n  2061\t\n  2062\t### rollout_summary_files\n  2063\t\n  2064\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/dio-machines, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/22/rollout-2026-09-22T14-04-16-01a0ca4a-36df-77e2-aedd-cc561a1f7447.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-22T18:06:21+00:00, thread_id=01a0ca4a-36df-77e2-aedd-cc561a1f7447, uncertain; repository map verified, live secret contents unavailable)\n  2065\t\n  2066\t### keywords\n  2067\t\n  2068\t- home.sessionVariables, home.sessionPath, load-secret-env, Skate, @secrets, secrets.env.sops, EnvironmentFile, services/.env, Home Manager, machine:switch\n  2069\t\n  2070\t## Task 2: Mirror Codex Fugu catalog and pin fugu-max/high defaults\n  2071\t\n  2072\t### rollout_summary_files\n  2073\t\n  2074\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/dio-machines, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/22/rollout-2026-09-22T14-57-28-01a0ca7a-eac3-7a41-8e91-6e2fb318a526.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-22T19:34:41+00:00, thread_id=01a0ca7a-eac3-7a41-8e91-6e2fb318a526, success; live defaults and outgoing effort verified)\n  2075\t\n  2076\t### keywords\n  2077\t\n  2078\t- fugu, sakana, fugu-max, fugu-ultra-v2.0, opencode.jsonc, crush.json, reasoningEffort, reasoning_effort, models.large, ProviderModelNotFoundError, recent_models.large\n  2079\t\n  2080\t## User preferences\n  2081\t\n  2082\t- when the user asked to “figure out how i add environment variables to this computer in this repo” -> first map actual scope and secret conventions instead of assuming one env mechanism. [Task 1]\n  2083\t- “just look at the codex profile and copy that to the others”; “adding max and the latest ultra models is important” -> use `/home/diogenes/.codex/sakana-models.json` and `fugu.config.toml` as catalog source of truth, then verify questionable IDs live. [Task 2]\n  2084\t- “set fugu max as the default model for both at high” -> change declarative config and persisted active state, then validate outgoing requests rather than merely listing models. [Task 2]\n  2085\t\n  2086\t## Reusable knowledge\n  2087\t\n  2088\t- Put shared non-secret variables in `home/default.nix` `home.sessionVariables`; narrower non-secrets in host/profile Nix files; PATH additions in `home.sessionPath`; apply Home Manager changes with `devenv tasks run machine:switch`. Project-only variables normally belong in that project’s `devenv.nix`. [Task 1]\n  2089\t- Credentials are outside tracked Nix: `~/bin/load-secret-env` reads Skate `@secrets` and optional `~/.config/mise/secrets.env.sops`; `load-secrets` evaluates its shell-safe exports. Service Compose secrets are git-ignored `services/<name>/.env` copied from `.env.example`; systemd non-secrets can use `Environment`, but file-backed secrets require `EnvironmentFile` because `Environment` lands in the Nix store. [Task 1]\n  2090\t- OpenCode deep-merges `~/.config/opencode/opencode.json` and `opencode.jsonc`; set default `\"model\": \"sakana/fugu-max\"` and its `options.reasoningEffort: \"high\"`. Crush requires both `~/.config/crush/crush.json` and persisted `~/.local/share/crush/crush.json`: `models.large = { model: \"fugu-max\", provider: \"sakana\", reasoning_effort: \"high\" }`, with `fugu-max/sakana` first in `recent_models.large`. [Task 2]\n  2091\t- Captured catalog supported `fugu`, `fugu-ultra`, `fugu-ultra-v2.0`, `fugu-ultra-20260615`, `fugu-ultra-v1.0`, `fugu-ultra-v1.1`, `fugu-max`, `fugu-max-v1.0`, and `fugu-cyber`; `fugu-cyber-v1.0`/`sakana-namazu*` returned 404, while `fugu-cyber` was form-gated 403. [Task 2]\n  2092\t\n  2093\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  2094\t\n  2095\t- Sandbox `skate list -k @secrets` hit a read-only lock-file failure, and the SOPS file was absent. Do not infer current secret contents; re-run on the writable machine and use `~/bin/secrets-edit`, never tracked Nix credentials. [Task 1]\n  2096\t- `sakana/fugu-max/high` is invalid as OpenCode’s global model (`ProviderModelNotFoundError`); keep plain model ID and pin effort in `options`. A JSONC insertion script first failed parsing: test a throwaway copy and run sync twice for idempotency before live writes. [Task 2]\n  2097\t- Updating only Crush config leaves a prior `models.large` active because persisted data overrides it. Crush supports only `low|medium|high`; use OpenCode variants/session overrides for xhigh/max. [Task 2]\n  2098\t\n  2099\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/notorganic-provider Jev semantic-rules API\n  2100\tscope: Implement and extend account/product-scoped, developer-reviewed Jev rulesets through the metered Not Organic judgement boundary; keep Phase 1 limits explicit.\n  2101\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/notorganic-provider; reuse_rule=reinspect the dirty worktree, current rules schema, and gateway deployment; do not infer calibration, spans, training, continuous encoding, or revision-aware serving from Phase 1.\n  2102\t\n  2103\t## Task 1: Implement first-class Jev rules API\n  2104\t\n  2105\t### rollout_summary_files\n  2106\t\n  2107\t- rollout_summaries/2026-09-22T04-39-43-JM9T-implement_jev_rules_api_phase_one.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/notorganic-provider, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/22/rollout-2026-09-22T00-39-43-01a0c769-9eae-7de1-8e79-8e3d4d46462d.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-28T23:24:42+00:00, thread_id=01a0c769-9eae-7de1-8e79-8e3d4d46462d, success; focused tests/typecheck/build passed; full suite had one sandbox socket-permission failure)\n  2108\t\n  2109\t### keywords\n  2110\t\n  2111\t- Jev, TypeSafe, RulesService, JudgementGateway, /v1/rules/decompose, /v1/rulesets, rules:write, rules:read, rules:evaluate, expected_revision, RULESET_STALE_REVISION, state_binding, state_digest, calibration.status\n  2112\t\n  2113\t## User preferences\n  2114\t\n  2115\t- when the user proposed using “another model to deconstruct some things into jev rules” and adding spans/general-purpose rules -> preserve a reviewable draft workflow; do not auto-activate model-generated rules. [Task 1]\n  2116\t- when the user clarified “jev refers to typesafe's model” and approved reading the ledger before planning -> keep TypeSafe behind Not Organic’s authenticated, metered provider boundary rather than exposing direct credentials. [Task 1]\n  2117\t\n  2118\t## Reusable knowledge\n  2119\t\n  2120\t- `RulesService` in `apps/gateway/src/rules.ts` performs decomposition, developer-reviewed publication, immutable revision retrieval, state binding, digest calculation, author/scorer separation, and Jev evaluation. `POST /v1/rules/decompose` uses the metered Portkey `reasoning` model, validates 1–64 unique claims, and leaves output draft-only. [Task 1]\n  2121\t- Accepted claims compile to Jev `choice` questions with `satisfied`, `violated`, `insufficient_context`, and `not_applicable`. Rulesets persist account/product-scoped in `convex/rules.ts`; `expected_revision` is CAS and stale writes map to `409 ruleset_stale_revision`. [Task 1]\n  2122\t- Evaluation loads the exact immutable revision, filters dotted `state_binding` paths such as `metadata.source`, canonicalizes state, computes `state_digest`, and invokes `JudgementGateway.evaluate` with deterministic inner idempotency/request hashes. The gateway retains DPoP/authentication, wallet reservation, dispatch, usage settlement, and conservative reconciliation; TypeSafe credentials remain server-held. [Task 1]\n  2123\t- SDK surface: `client.rules.decompose` and `client.rulesets.create/list/retrieve/evaluate`; capabilities are `rules:write`, `rules:read`, `rules:evaluate`. Responses expose `backend_model`, `questions_digest`, `state_digest`, usage, and `calibration.status = \"advisory\"`; schema-only `rulesetCalibrations` is not fitted calibration. Author/scorer matching is rejected as `rules_author_scorer_conflict`; limits are 64 questions and about 96k state/question characters. Inference endpoints do not yet consume a ruleset or active evolution revision. [Task 1]\n  2124\t\n  2125\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  2126\t\n  2127\t- GitNexus `UNKNOWN`/partial coverage means unresolved, not safe: the index was one commit stale, so refresh it, resolve exact symbols, then confirm callers with text search. Dotted bindings initially behaved as literal keys; use explicit path traversal and nested-binding tests. [Task 1]\n  2128\t- `apps/gateway/src/bun-live.test.ts` failed under sandbox socket permissions with `EPERM` but passed with socket access. Report it as an environment limitation separate from implementation failure. [Task 1]\n  2129\t\n  2130\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/keating Railway static report deployment and naming\n  2131\tscope: Resume, verify, retitle, rebuild, and deploy the `on-device-ledger` static report on Railway with live positive and negative HTTP proof.\n  2132\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating; reuse_rule=recheck current Railway project/service/deployment status and report sources before changing content or claiming live behavior.\n  2133\t\n  2134\t## Task 1: Resume and verify Railway deployment\n  2135\t\n  2136\t### rollout_summary_files\n  2137\t\n  2138\t- rollout_summaries/2026-09-23T12-38-01-qzCo-railway_report_title_redeploy.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/23/rollout-2026-09-23T08-38-01-01a0ce45-e3b1-7e81-9dd6-5d6c57921238.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-23T12:54:14+00:00, thread_id=01a0ce45-e3b1-7e81-9dd6-5d6c57921238, success; live routes, title, health, and 404 verified)\n  2139\t\n  2140\t### keywords\n  2141\t\n  2142\t- Railway, on-device-ledger, on-device-ledger-production.up.railway.app, railway.toml, Dockerfile, /healthz, railway up --service, deployment SUCCESS\n  2143\t\n  2144\t## Task 2: Rename and redeploy report\n  2145\t\n  2146\t### rollout_summary_files\n  2147\t\n  2148\t- rollout_summaries/2026-09-23T12-38-01-qzCo-railway_report_title_redeploy.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/23/rollout-2026-09-23T08-38-01-01a0ce45-e3b1-7e81-9dd6-5d6c57921238.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-23T12:54:14+00:00, thread_id=01a0ce45-e3b1-7e81-9dd6-5d6c57921238, success; final deployment `ed7a8e47-aa26-4c4f-a5f5-f70cffd79d2d`)\n  2149\t\n  2150\t### keywords\n  2151\t\n  2152\t- A Measure of Machine Judgement, scripts/on-device-site/build.py, shell(...), homepage hero, wordmark, Railway logs --deployment, --build\n  2153\t\n  2154\t## User preferences\n  2155\t\n  2156\t- when continuing a deployment, the user said \"hey continue the railway deployment\" and supplied a prior Entire session ID -> inspect the concrete prior session/checkpoint state rather than restarting diagnosis. [Task 1]\n  2157\t- the user rejected \"actually,\" said \"think outside on device,\" and selected \"A Measure of Machine Judgement\" -> prefer concept-led, distinctive report titles over implementation-focused wording. [Task 2]\n  2158\t\n  2159\t## Reusable knowledge\n  2160\t\n  2161\t- Railway project `keating` service `on-device-ledger` is served at `https://on-device-ledger-production.up.railway.app`; source deploy context is `scripts/on-device-site`, with `railway.toml`, Dockerfile, and `/healthz`. Use `railway up --service on-device-ledger --path-as-root scripts/on-device-site --detach`. [Task 1]\n  2162\t- Rebuild titles consistently in `scripts/on-device-site/build.py`: its `shell(...)` title calls plus homepage hero/wordmark. Run `python3 scripts/on-device-site/build.py`, deploy, then check final title/heading, `/healthz` 200, expected site routes, and an unknown route 404. [Task 1][Task 2]\n  2163\t\n  2164\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  2165\t\n  2166\t- Interrupted polling, approval limits, and transient DNS do not prove deploy failure; inspect current Railway status/domain. GitNexus did not index `scripts/on-device-site/build.py`, so direct `rg`/file inspection was the correct pivot. [Task 1][Task 2]\n  2167\t- `railway logs --deployment` and `--build` are mutually exclusive; run them separately. [Task 2]\n  2168\t\n  2169\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/keating structured learner profile and guided onboarding\n  2170\tscope: Maintain optional local learner details, migration-compatible prompt composition, guided web onboarding, and consentful pursuit switching without overstating unfinished UI or end-to-end verification.\n  2171\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating; reuse_rule=reinspect high-impact learner-context callers and generated NodePod artifacts; preserve local-only/privacy boundaries and legacy free-text compatibility.\n  2172\t\n  2173\t## Task 1: Add structured learner profile and local migration, partial\n  2174\t\n  2175\t### rollout_summary_files\n  2176\t\n  2177\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/19/rollout-2026-09-19T18-16-34-01a0bbbe-1e34-7900-abf6-56c41c92e53a.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-19T23:22:34+00:00, thread_id=01a0bbbe-1e34-7900-abf6-56c41c92e53a, partial; targeted checks passed, full end-to-end completion not shown)\n  2178\t\n  2179\t### keywords\n  2180\t\n  2181\t- learner-profile-declared, AGE_BANDS, parseDeclaredProfile, keating:learner-profile:v2, createLocalSetting, loadLearnerContext, GitNexus, learner-context\n  2182\t\n  2183\t## Task 2: Add settings profile UI, guided onboarding, and pursuits, partial\n  2184\t\n  2185\t### rollout_summary_files\n  2186\t\n  2187\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/19/rollout-2026-09-19T18-16-34-01a0bbbe-1e34-7900-abf6-56c41c92e53a.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-19T23:22:34+00:00, thread_id=01a0bbbe-1e34-7900-abf6-56c41c92e53a, partial; coachmarks, locale override, and complete telemetry remain unfinished)\n  2188\t\n  2189\t### keywords\n  2190\t\n  2191\t- ChatOnboarding, ProfileFieldGroups, LearnerProfileTab, Panda CSS, seedCurrentPursuitFromGoal, pursuitCandidatesFromNeedle, applyPursuitSwitchProposal, EPERM, nodepod-boot-files\n  2192\t\n  2193\t## User preferences\n  2194\t\n  2195\t- when requesting learner details, the user said \"personal details about the learner age etc language etc\" and \"think of more things here\" -> offer broad optional fields, never mandatory or overly sensitive intake. [Task 1]\n  2196\t- when the user said \"wait just continue on the plan now\" -> after an approved plan, make reasonable implementation decisions instead of repeatedly reopening clarification. [Task 1]\n  2197\t- the user wanted onboarding to \"guide people using the interface\" -> explain composer, side panel, sessions, and Settings, not merely provider setup. [Task 2]\n  2198\t\n  2199\t## Reusable knowledge\n  2200\t\n  2201\t- Shared dependency-free contract is `packages/learner-contracts/src/learner-profile-declared.ts`. Use age bands (including `prefer-not-to-say`), not date of birth. `parseDeclaredProfile()` never throws; it validates enums, bounds text/lists/durations, and distinguishes unanswered from declined values. Persist v2 at `keating:learner-profile:v2`; migrate legacy `keating:learner-profile` text into `notes` and retain the legacy mirror. [Task 1]\n  2202\t- `loadLearnerContext()` had 99 upstream impacts/CRITICAL GitNexus risk: preserve its signature and add structured context only through optional prompt parameters plus the parallel store. The prompt must not infer ability, intelligence, personality, or learning style from age, language, pronouns, or education stage. Telemetry-safe helpers expose field IDs/counts, not values. [Task 1]\n  2203\t- Use Panda CSS and existing `Select`, `Toggle`, `fieldInput`, and `textarea` recipes. Share `ProfileFieldGroups.tsx` between settings and onboarding. `ChatOnboarding.tsx` has resumable v2 eight-step metadata while recognizing completed v1 records; it stays non-modal so provider/account dialogs do not compete for focus. [Task 2]\n  2204\t- `seedCurrentPursuitFromGoal()` makes a non-empty onboarding goal a current declared pursuit. Prompt it as `Standing pursuit (not assumed for this session)`. Observed pursuits require exact evidence, SHA-256 quote hash, and provenance offsets; only exact `study-context` candidates with valid provenance are accepted, and `applyPursuitSwitchProposal()` requires explicit approval. [Task 2]\n  2205\t\n  2206\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  2207\t\n  2208\t- GitNexus `--target-uid` is invalid; use `-u/--uid`. `UNKNOWN` on new symbols is unresolved: bound callers with direct grep/import searches, never treat it as safe. [Task 1]\n  2209\t- Coachmark tour, getting-started checklist, locale override, complete telemetry, full Storybook/build validation, and final `detect_changes --scope all` were not demonstrated. Do not claim them complete. [Task 2]\n  2210\t- An offline learner-context harness failed `EPERM .../.keating/tmp/.../rpc.sock`; rerun where Unix socket creation is allowed. After source changes regenerate `web/src/keating/nodepod-boot-files.ts` with `bun scripts/generate-nodepod-boot-files.ts` or generated copies become stale. [Task 2]\n  2211\t\n  2212\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/keating Jev/model-cascade shared judgement foundation\n  2213\tscope: Continue the shared cross-surface judgement foundation while completing the still-unreplaced judge sites, telemetry, evolution wiring, and full validation.\n  2214\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating; reuse_rule=reinspect the heavily dirty branch and targeted diffs; treat the shared contracts as partial implementation, not completion of docs/plans/jev-model-cascade.md.\n  2215\t\n  2216\t## Task 1: Add typed Jev/model-cascade contracts and pure decision helpers, partial\n  2217\t\n  2218\t### rollout_summary_files\n  2219\t\n  2220\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/19/rollout-2026-09-19T08-03-45-01a0b98d-1310-7722-85ad-98bdd317bee4.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-19T12:41:05+00:00, thread_id=01a0b98d-1310-7722-85ad-98bdd317bee4, partial; foundation implemented, post-boosting full suite not rerun)\n  2221\t\n  2222\t### keywords\n  2223\t\n  2224\t- Jev, TypeSafe, System One, JudgementCaller, learner-contracts, cascade-router, MiniCPM5, Needle, evidence-by-selection, assessment, retrieval, boosting\n  2225\t\n  2226\t## Task 2: Replace all LLM-as-judge paths and finish cascade phases, partial\n  2227\t\n  2228\t### rollout_summary_files\n  2229\t\n  2230\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/19/rollout-2026-09-19T08-03-45-01a0b98d-1310-7722-85ad-98bdd317bee4.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-19T12:41:05+00:00, thread_id=01a0b98d-1310-7722-85ad-98bdd317bee4, partial; all three delegated workers hit usage limits)\n  2231\t\n  2232\t### keywords\n  2233\t\n  2234\t- benchmark_judge.py, export-judge.ts, trajectory-passes.ts, model-adapters.ts, policy-judgement.ts, mastery.ts, learner-state.ts, runtime_or_model_changed, telemetry, injection tests\n  2235\t\n  2236\t## User preferences\n  2237\t\n  2238\t- when the user required “do it all end to end” and “Full replacement everywhere” -> continue through all planned judge sites; do not present the contract layer as sufficient completion [Task 1][Task 2]\n  2239\t- when the user required a local judgement model “separate model configurable in settings” -> keep tutor-model and judgement-model settings independent [Task 1]\n  2240\t\n  2241\t## Reusable knowledge\n  2242\t\n  2243\t- The shared cross-platform location is `packages/learner-contracts/src/judgement/`: `contracts.ts`, `projections.ts`, `router.ts`, `wire.ts`, `system-one.ts`, `local-backend.ts`, `assessment.ts`, `retrieval.ts`, and `boosting.ts`, exported through the package root. CLI, web, and mobile already consume `@keating/learner-contracts`. [Task 1]\n  2244\t- Cascade routing starts at the cheapest tier, escalates only residue, skips uncalibrated tiers, never falls back from a pinned backend, and returns deterministic baseline plus abstention when exhausted. Thresholds key on backend/model/calibration/question digest. [Task 1]\n  2245\t- Hosted System One is `POST https://api.typesafe.ai/v1/systemone`; Choice is a criteria map, Score an ordered criteria array, and Noul has no confidence. Do not surface upstream bodies; same-origin gateway calls omit credentials. [Task 1]\n  2246\t- `web/src/keating/judgement-model.ts` stores the independent `off|local|hosted` setting, defaults local to `RASMUS/MiniCPM5-2B-ONNX`, and accepts only same-origin gateway paths. Local Needle answers are typed/closed-vocabulary and omit unanswerable questions. [Task 1]\n  2247\t- Assessment helpers keep readiness Nouls one-directional, use per-item performance Nouls, bucket duration/due dates, and mark uncertain open answers `grading: \"pending\"`. Retrieval uses calibrated z-scores, exact learner-message evidence, observed confidence <=0.65, and a 128-fact cap. Start boosting with a depth-limited tree and deterministic held-out rows. [Task 1]\n  2248\t- The remaining plan targets include `scripts/training/benchmark_judge.py`, `web/src/keating/export-judge.ts`, `web/src/keating/trajectory-passes.ts`, `shared/evolution/model-adapters.ts`, `src/core/policy-judgement.ts`, `src/core/mastery.ts`, and `src/core/learner-state.ts`. Preserve server-side-only TypeSafe credentials, `NEEDLE_TELEMETRY=0`, `DO_NOT_TRACK=1`, evidence taxonomy, and no automatic irreversible action from judgement alone. [Task 2]\n  2249\t\n  2250\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  2251\t\n  2252\t- Bun tests can pass while a type-only import is wrong because imports are stripped. After tests, always run `bun run typecheck`; assessment types belong in `contracts.ts`, not `projections.ts`. [Task 1]\n  2253\t- Symptom: `ReferenceError: localStorage is not defined` in web setting tests -> use the existing inline storage/window/custom-event shim pattern in `web/src/test/learner-context.test.ts`. [Task 1]\n  2254\t- The recorded `187 pass / 0 fail` package result and typecheck predate later boosting changes. Rerun the entire package suite before calling it green. For web: `cd web && bun run panda`, `bunx tsc --noEmit`, then `bun test`; also run root/Bun, benchmark, evidence-integrity, cache-key, offline/no-network, and injection checks. [Task 1][Task 2]\n  2255\t- All three workers terminated with usage-limit errors and delivered no implementation result. Continue directly or use smaller bounded tasks; do not assume their files changed. [Task 2]\n  2256\t\n  2257\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/textbook native terminal UI Canvas parity and Jev review\n  2258\tscope: Continue native OpenTUI/Canvas parity and targeted UX refinement with modular TUI seams, verified local behavior, and an honest boundary around the blocked second Jev review.\n  2259\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/textbook; reuse_rule=reuse the module/layout and OpenTUI behavior findings after checking the current TUI API and worktree; do not infer a second external review or new tests from this rollout.\n  2260\t\n  2261\t## Task 1: Implement Canvas parity in the native TUI, partial\n  2262\t\n  2263\t### rollout_summary_files\n  2264\t\n  2265\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/textbook, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/19/rollout-2026-09-19T08-03-45-01a0b98d-1314-74b3-b9ff-f31175a6e455.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-19T05:08:40+00:00, thread_id=01a0b98d-1314-74b3-b9ff-f31175a6e455, partial; implementation and local verification succeeded, new tests intentionally deferred)\n  2266\t\n  2267\t### keywords\n  2268\t\n  2269\t- textbook, native-tui, canvas, OpenTUI, src/tui, src/themes.ts, renderer.keyInput, destroyRecursively, VHS, similarity-ts\n  2270\t\n  2271\t## Task 2: Apply Jev terminal UX review refinements, partial\n  2272\t\n  2273\t### rollout_summary_files\n  2274\t\n  2275\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/textbook, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/19/rollout-2026-09-19T08-03-45-01a0b98d-1314-74b3-b9ff-f31175a6e455.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-19T05:08:40+00:00, thread_id=01a0b98d-1314-74b3-b9ff-f31175a6e455, partial; first external review plus local follow-up, second review blocked)\n  2276\t\n  2277\t### keywords\n  2278\t\n  2279\t- Jev, TypeSafe, systemone, search_typing_safe, borderless inspector, footer scanability, auto-mode classifier, skate typesafe_api_key@secrets\n  2280\t\n  2281\t## User preferences\n  2282\t\n  2283\t- when scoping implementation, the user said \"use your best judgement tbh\" after rejecting repeated questions -> decide a reasonable product scope and proceed rather than asking more product questions. [Task 1]\n  2284\t- when asked for Canvas parity, the user said \"Don't write tests right now, just focus on implementation\" -> do not add new tests until that boundary is re-enabled; retain existing tests as evidence only. [Task 1]\n  2285\t\n  2286\t## Reusable knowledge\n  2287\t\n  2288\t- The native TUI is modular under `src/tui/{index,state,keymap,focus,preview,sidebar,panel}.ts`; `src/app.ts` is a compatibility re-export, and `src/themes.ts` is the shared Canvas/TUI palette and chrome source consumed by `src/web/html.ts`. Generation guards plus `destroyRecursively()` prevent stale asynchronous story renderables and leaks. [Task 1]\n  2289\t- In this OpenTUI version, use `renderer.keyInput.on(\"keypress\", ...)`; `renderer.on(\"keypress\")` is a no-op. `InputRenderableOptions` excludes `height`, so collapse its wrapping `BoxRenderable`; omit `borderColor` entirely when `border: false`, because supplying it forces a border. [Task 1]\n  2290\t- Verified locally: `npx tsc --noEmit` clean, `bun test` 36 pass/0 fail, VHS showed search/navigation/sidebar/inspector/theme/viewport/footer behavior, and `similarity-ts src/tui src/themes.ts` found no duplicate functions or similar types. [Task 1]\n  2291\t- Search-mode safety was checked mechanically by enumerating printable characters through `resolveAction(..., \"search\")`; none are intercepted. Apply the evidence rather than trusting Jev's lower `search_typing_safe` score. [Task 2]\n  2292\t\n  2293\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  2294\t\n  2295\t- VHS reports `Module not found \"dist/index.js\"` from a scratchpad -> put an explicit `cd /home/diogenes/Projects/textbook` inside the tape and use relative output filenames; an apparent `>` artifact can be the VHS shell prompt, not a TUI scrollbar defect. [Task 1]\n  2296\t- The second Jev submission was blocked by the auto-mode classifier -> do not bypass it; retain the first HTTP-200 review and local checks as the available external-review evidence. Never print or persist the Skate-provided TypeSafe credential. [Task 2]\n  2297\t\n  2298\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/twyne Jev provider, rubric, and writing tools\n  2299\tscope: Route typed Jev judgements through Not Organic, maintain Jev-first rubric and optional writing lenses, and distinguish local implementation from verified provider production.\n  2300\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne plus /home/diogenes/Projects/notorganic-provider; reuse_rule=reinspect both dirty worktrees and deploy state; direct TypeSafe use is local-only when Not Organic is enabled.\n  2301\t\n  2302\t## Task 1: Stage then complete the Not Organic Jev provider boundary, partial\n  2303\t\n  2304\t### rollout_summary_files\n  2305\t\n  2306\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/18/rollout-2026-09-18T19-43-22-01a0b6e7-3c95-7543-9f88-4698f314c385.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-18T23:58:45+00:00, thread_id=01a0b6e7-3c95-7543-9f88-4698f314c385, partial; source changes uncommitted and undeployed)\n  2307\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/18/rollout-2026-09-18T19-09-28-01a0b6c8-324a-7d60-a2fa-a16f00cc5a18.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-18T23:37:12+00:00, thread_id=01a0b6c8-324a-7d60-a2fa-a16f00cc5a18, partial; staged gateway work preceded guarded completion)\n  2308\t\n  2309\t### keywords\n  2310\t\n  2311\t- Jev, TypeSafe, Not Organic, POST /v1/judgement, judgement:evaluate, DPoP, GatewayConfig.typesafe, TYPESAFE_API_KEY, ProviderStore, reserve dispatch accept settle\n  2312\t\n  2313\t## Task 2: Use Jev-first rubric scoring with safe fallback, partial\n  2314\t\n  2315\t### rollout_summary_files\n  2316\t\n  2317\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/18/rollout-2026-09-18T19-43-22-01a0b6e7-3c95-7543-9f88-4698f314c385.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-18T23:58:45+00:00, thread_id=01a0b6e7-3c95-7543-9f88-4698f314c385, partial; final checks intentionally omitted)\n  2318\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/18/rollout-2026-09-18T19-09-28-01a0b6c8-324a-7d60-a2fa-a16f00cc5a18.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-18T23:37:12+00:00, thread_id=01a0b6c8-324a-7d60-a2fa-a16f00cc5a18, partial; earlier 1104-test evidence)\n  2319\t\n  2320\t### keywords\n  2321\t\n  2322\t- runRubricPass, judgementRubricResult, rubric-grade, rubric-judgement-result, draftFingerprint, scoringMethod: judgement, Choice map, Score criteria\n  2323\t\n  2324\t## Task 3: Add optional read-only writing lenses, partial\n  2325\t\n  2326\t### rollout_summary_files\n  2327\t\n  2328\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/18/rollout-2026-09-18T19-43-22-01a0b6e7-3c95-7543-9f88-4698f314c385.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-18T23:58:45+00:00, thread_id=01a0b6e7-3c95-7543-9f88-4698f314c385, partial; UI checks deferred to user)\n  2329\t\n  2330\t### keywords\n  2331\t\n  2332\t- writing-lenses, WRITING_LENSES, reader, revision, voice, promises, scraps, room, circling, research, writing-tools-storage, stale-result\n  2333\t\n  2334\t## User preferences\n  2335\t\n  2336\t- when hosted TypeSafe/Jev integration was discussed, the user said it \"should work through notorganic in actuality rather than tied through this deployment directly\" and wanted an API \"that just works with jev\" -> place provider credentials, authorization, customer inspection, and ledger accounting behind Not Organic. [Task 1]\n  2337\t- when dirty provider files were deliberately left alone, the user asked to \"finish the application\" -> complete the requested product side with guarded/narrow patches while preserving unrelated in-flight provider work. [Task 1]\n  2338\t- when implementation was requested, the user said \"don't manual test things here ... don't bother with tests either pure implementation\" -> stop tests and browser/manual UI checks at that explicit boundary and report the resulting verification gap plainly. [Task 2][Task 3]\n  2339\t\n  2340\t## Reusable knowledge\n  2341\t\n  2342\t- Production Twyne calls Not Organic using DPoP and `judgement:evaluate` at `POST /v1/judgement`; direct `TYPESAFE_API_KEY` is only loopback/local fallback. The provider owns the key, typed state/questions transport, model alias resolution, and per-account reserve -> dispatch -> accept -> settle/reconcile accounting. [Task 1]\n  2343\t- Jev question types are `noul`, `choice`, and `score`; normalize Twyne arrays into TypeSafe Choice maps, retain Score ordered arrays, bound requests, avoid upstream response bodies that may echo documents, and surface uncertain/missing usage rather than silently billing zero. The observed rate was `0.042` microUSD per input token. [Task 1]\n  2344\t- `runRubricPass()` batches enabled criteria and degrades safely; `judgementRubricResult()` rejects incomplete criteria and protects saves with folio/brief/criteria/draft fingerprint freshness guards. Confidence is distribution concentration, not truth or permission to act. [Task 2]\n  2345\t- The eight read-only lenses (`reader`, `revision`, `voice`, `promises`, `scraps`, `room`, `circling`, `research`) live in `src/utils/writing-lenses.ts`, with UI/storage at `src/components/writing-tools/writing-tools.tsx` and `src/utils/writing-tools-storage.ts`. Quote supplied passages, bound inputs, expose missing evidence/uncertainty, reject stale results, and never edit prose automatically. [Task 3]\n  2346\t\n  2347\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  2348\t\n  2349\t- Source edits, a configured gateway variable, and a later successful Railway status call are not deployment/live-route/ledger proof. Final state was uncommitted and undeployed, with no final typecheck, tests, browser checks, or live request after the last edits. [Task 1][Task 2][Task 3]\n  2350\t- Broken Python `PYTHONHOME`/`PYTHONPATH` -> use `env -u PYTHONHOME -u PYTHONPATH python3 ...` for required scripts. GitNexus `UNKNOWN` from wrong symbols -> resolve the exact symbol (`createGateway`) before treating impact output as evidence. [Task 1]\n  2351\t\n  2352\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/twyne editor drag/drop and offline interaction plan\n  2353\tscope: Restore native ProseMirror dragging without false file overlays; route remaining editor-UX, offline-banner, and local-model work through verified seams.\n  2354\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne; reuse_rule=retest exact browser/editor behavior before claiming completion; planning notes are not implementation authority.\n  2355\t\n  2356\t## Task 1: Restore native selected-text dragging and file-drop handling, partial\n  2357\t\n  2358\t### rollout_summary_files\n  2359\t\n  2360\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/18/rollout-2026-09-18T19-09-28-01a0b6c8-3247-7842-bca9-9750c78aad2e.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-18T21:18:15+00:00, thread_id=01a0b6c8-3247-7842-bca9-9750c78aad2e, partial; focused tests passed but E2E has two unresolved cases)\n  2361\t\n  2362\t### keywords\n  2363\t\n  2364\t- Qwik, TipTap, ProseMirror, preventdefault:dragover, preventdefault:dragleave, preventdefault:drop, Dropcursor, twyne-dropcursor, file-drag.ts, drag-selection.e2e.ts\n  2365\t\n  2366\t## Task 2: Plan slash menu, viewport, offline toast, and browser/desktop local models, partial\n  2367\t\n  2368\t### rollout_summary_files\n  2369\t\n  2370\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/18/rollout-2026-09-18T19-09-28-01a0b6c8-3247-7842-bca9-9750c78aad2e.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-18T21:18:15+00:00, thread_id=01a0b6c8-3247-7842-bca9-9750c78aad2e, partial; combined plan selected, local-model design incomplete)\n  2371\t\n  2372\t### keywords\n  2373\t\n  2374\t- slash-command-menu, computePopoverGeometry, DEFAULT_LAYOUT.marginBottom, scrollMargin, global-connectivity-banner, sticky top-0 z-50, IndexedDB, service-worker, Transformers.js, WebGPU, LiteRT\n  2375\t\n  2376\t## User preferences\n  2377\t\n  2378\t- for editor dragging, the user expects selected prose to move on drop, show where it will land, and work for paragraphs and larger blocks. [Task 1]\n  2379\t- the user chose \"Everything in one plan,\" including browser and desktop local models, and chose a bottom-left toast-pattern offline notice; markdown shortcuts were \"not a required part of the editor.\" [Task 2]\n  2380\t- uncertain H1 behavior should be reproduced/verified before being treated as a bug. [Task 2]\n  2381\t\n  2382\t## Reusable knowledge\n  2383\t\n  2384\t- Ancestor `preventdefault:dragover`, `preventdefault:dragleave`, and `preventdefault:drop` in `src/components/editor/manuscript-panel.tsx` are handled by Qwik's capture listener before ProseMirror, making events `defaultPrevented` and disabling native text/image drops. Remove them; `SectionReorder` is not the general blocker. Filter the overlay by `event.dataTransfer` so it appears only for file drags. [Task 1]\n  2385\t- Focused evidence: `bun test --conditions=production --preload ./tests/qwik-test-preload.ts src/utils/file-drag.test.ts` passed 6/0 and `bun run build.types` passed. [Task 1]\n  2386\t- Generalize tested `computePopoverGeometry` for slash-menu flip/clamp/height behavior; current `coords.bottom + 6` has no flip, clamp, or scroll/resize refresh. The fixed toast region in `src/global.css` is the right pattern for replacing `global-connectivity-banner.tsx`'s normal-flow `sticky top-0 z-50` banner. [Task 2]\n  2387\t- `DEFAULT_LAYOUT.marginBottom: 1` overrides the normal 4rem fallback, and nested scrollers lack `scrollMargin`/`scrollThreshold`. Twyne's IndexedDB/service-worker shell is genuinely local-first, but sync, AI, auth, collaboration, and publishing remain remote; browser local models likely use Transformers.js/WebGPU/cached ONNX and desktop has a LiteRT seam. [Task 2]\n  2388\t\n  2389\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  2390\t\n  2391\t- After Chromium installation, E2E had 1 pass/2 fail: multi-paragraph move works, but single-paragraph movement and drop-caret visibility fail and `.twyne-dropcursor` was absent. Inspect the exact test plus generated Dropcursor DOM/configuration before claiming drag/drop complete. [Task 1]\n  2392\t- The rollout ended after an interrupted/rejected follow-up tool call; do not continue edits without renewed direction when that interruption is material. A plan-agent timeout left the local-model design incomplete. [Task 1][Task 2]\n  2393\t\n  2394\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/twyne local Codex Fugu/Sakana catalog configuration\n  2395\tscope: Update and strictly validate the user-level Fugu/Sakana Codex profile and catalog.\n  2396\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne with user config at /home/diogenes/.codex; reuse_rule=recheck provider documentation/live model endpoint and installed config before changing aliases, versions, or defaults.\n  2397\t\n  2398\t## Task 1: Expand Fugu/Sakana model IDs, aliases, and default profile\n  2399\t\n  2400\t### rollout_summary_files\n  2401\t\n  2402\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/18/rollout-2026-09-18T18-47-44-01a0b6b4-4bfc-7fe2-8b6a-2c1695320c03.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-18T23:09:36+00:00, thread_id=01a0b6b4-4bfc-7fe2-8b6a-2c1695320c03, success; installed and strict-config validated)\n  2403\t\n  2404\t### keywords\n  2405\t\n  2406\t- fugu, fugu-ultra, fugu-max, fugu-cyber, sakana-namazu, sakana-models.json, fugu.config.toml, model_catalog_json, strict-config, react-grab-mcp\n  2407\t\n  2408\t## User preferences\n  2409\t\n  2410\t- when the user said \"update fugu config to support the new models\" and supplied all IDs -> update the actual user-level catalog/profile, not merely a proposed configuration. [Task 1]\n  2411\t\n  2412\t## Reusable knowledge\n  2413\t\n  2414\t- Installed paths are `/home/diogenes/.codex/sakana-models.json` and `/home/diogenes/.codex/fugu.config.toml`; the profile defaults to `model = \"fugu-ultra\"` and uses `model_catalog_json` for the 11-model catalog. Custom metadata supports `context_window`, `default_reasoning_level`, and `supported_reasoning_levels`. [Task 1]\n  2415\t- Fugu variants are represented at 1,000,000 context tokens; Namazu at 256,000. `fugu-ultra-v1.1` supports `high,xhigh,max`; other Fugu entries support `high,xhigh`; Namazu uses `none` because thinking is provider-specific. [Task 1]\n  2416\t- Validate with `codex -c 'model_catalog_json=\"/home/diogenes/.codex/sakana-models.json\"' debug models` and `codex exec -p fugu --strict-config --ephemeral`; the latter reaching expected `No prompt provided via stdin` proves strict config loaded. The parent `[mcp_servers.react-grab-mcp]` transport with `npx -y @react-grab/mcp --stdio` is required for strict parsing. [Task 1]\n  2417\t\n  2418\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  2419\t\n  2420\t- `ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'encodings'` in the system Python -> generate JSON with Bun/Node. Sandboxed `api.sakana.ai` DNS failed while an escalated read-only call returned HTTP 200; live `/v1/models` validated current Fugu IDs only, so clearly label Namazu/Cyber version entries as documentation-validated. [Task 1]\n  2421\t\n  2422\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/keating training corpus audit and Learning to Teach artifact\n  2423\tscope: Audit training/benchmark evidence into a narrative report, reuse the canonical Learning to Teach theme, and maintain strict measurement/evidence boundaries.\n  2424\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating; reuse_rule=reinspect benchmark inputs, generated outputs, stylesheet authority, artifact publication state, and mobile rendering before revising or quoting counts.\n  2425\t\n  2426\t## Task 1: Audit the entire training/benchmark corpus and publish The Null Ledger\n  2427\t\n  2428\t### rollout_summary_files\n  2429\t\n  2430\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/18/rollout-2026-09-18T19-09-28-01a0b6c8-3246-7761-bb3d-00f3fdfd84bf.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-15T21:04:50+00:00, thread_id=01a0b6c8-3246-7761-bb3d-00f3fdfd84bf, success; artifact republished at same URL)\n  2431\t\n  2432\t### keywords\n  2433\t\n  2434\t- training corpus, benchmark, The Null Ledger, Learning to Teach, teaching-v4, Delivery Contracts Teaching, benchmark gaps, scripts/training/BENCHMARK.md\n  2435\t\n  2436\t## Task 2: Restyle report with the canonical Learning to Teach visual system\n  2437\t\n  2438\t### rollout_summary_files\n  2439\t\n  2440\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/18/rollout-2026-09-18T19-09-28-01a0b6c8-3246-7761-bb3d-00f3fdfd84bf.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-15T21:04:50+00:00, thread_id=01a0b6c8-3246-7761-bb3d-00f3fdfd84bf, success; rendering follow-up still advisable)\n  2441\t\n  2442\t### keywords\n  2443\t\n  2444\t- report.css, research-story.css, paper-ink-phosphor, VT323, Roboto, JetBrains Mono, claude.ai/artifact, null-ledger.html\n  2445\t\n  2446\t## User preferences\n  2447\t\n  2448\t- when auditing, the user asked to \"check entire,\" create \"a page and story,\" and review improvements and gaps -> combine inventory, editorial judgment, narrative chronology, and ranked actionable gaps rather than only listing files. [Task 1]\n  2449\t- when restyling, the user said \"use the theme from learning to teach\" -> use existing canonical tokens and typography instead of a bespoke visual system. [Task 2]\n  2450\t\n  2451\t## Reusable knowledge\n  2452\t\n  2453\t- The audit counted 155 authored benchmark cases across seven suites, 320 pinned multidomain sources, 460 accepted contextual examples, 42 native-learning artifact directories, and roughly 51 GB under `.keating`. Delivery, Contracts, and Teaching are separate result classes; unreviewed Teaching dimensions remain null. [Task 1]\n  2454\t- Preserve material gaps: broken Python 3.12 environment, no full-corpus human teaching ratings, incomplete/void comparison arms, v3 cohort interruption, small v4 paid pilot, 12 drifted frozen contract sources, 38 untested modules, and 139 untracked training files. The strongest found protocol was blinded two-grader review with pre-unblinding adjudication. [Task 1]\n  2455\t- `web/public/reports/learning-to-teach/report.css` is authoritative; `scripts/report-site/research-story.css` is companion-only. Use paper `#f1ece0`, deep paper `#e9e2d2`, card `#f6f2e8`, ink `#1c211b`, green `#14743c`, terminal `#0c1510`, phosphor `#4be388`, VT323/Roboto/JetBrains Mono, and semantic measured/null/void colors. Artifact-hosted fonts need Google Fonts links, not local paths. [Task 2]\n  2456\t- Republish the existing scratchpad path or use its artifact URL to retain the link: `https://claude.ai/artifact/1meBvkGXLs6Mm9aTST5o3P`. [Task 2]\n  2457\t\n  2458\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  2459\t\n  2460\t- Do not confuse `research-story.css` with the canonical stylesheet; verify authority first. A report can be republished successfully without final rendering proof, so inspect mobile bar rows and inverted legend/state-color contrast before the next revision. [Task 2]\n  2461\t\n  2462\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/keating multidomain teaching corpus expansion and queue generation\n  2463\tscope: Maintain the source-grounded 16-domain corpus catalog and safely run/verify small asynchronous generation jobs.\n  2464\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating; reuse_rule=reinspect catalog, licenses, queue status, worker receipts, and validated exports; do not treat live workers or receipts as completed corpus output.\n  2465\t\n  2466\t## Task 1: Expand and validate the 16-domain source catalog\n  2467\t\n  2468\t### rollout_summary_files\n  2469\t\n  2470\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/13/rollout-2026-09-13T05-30-49-01a09a1a-e577-7681-a64c-a576ae11485e.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-15T04:14:07+00:00, thread_id=01a09a1a-e577-7681-a64c-a576ae11485e, partial; catalog verified, generation remains incomplete)\n  2471\t\n  2472\t### keywords\n  2473\t\n  2474\t- multidomain_corpus, agy_multidomain, music, OpenStax, Open-Music-Theory, multidomain_sources.py, ORIGINAL_URLS, families_per_batch, catalog.json\n  2475\t\n  2476\t## Task 2: Relaunch 32,000-contrast generation in small worker jobs, partial\n  2477\t\n  2478\t### rollout_summary_files\n  2479\t\n  2480\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/13/rollout-2026-09-13T05-30-49-01a09a1a-e577-7681-a64c-a576ae11485e.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-15T04:14:07+00:00, thread_id=01a09a1a-e577-7681-a64c-a576ae11485e, partial; workers running with no completed/reviewed batches at final check)\n  2481\t\n  2482\t### keywords\n  2483\t\n  2484\t- MiniMax-M3, DeepSeek, 32768, music-00-f01, music-01-f01, status.json, worker-process.json, completed_batches, validated artifacts\n  2485\t\n  2486\t## User preferences\n  2487\t\n  2488\t- during domain expansion, the user added \"music too\" -> include music as a complete first-class domain with source and task constraints. [Task 1]\n  2489\t\n  2490\t## Reusable knowledge\n  2491\t\n  2492\t- The validated catalog has 320 source groups: 20 each for history, biology, ml, geology, philosophy, chemistry, physics, computer-science, statistics, economics, psychology, literature, writing, civics, environmental-science, and music. `test_multidomain_expansion.py` passed 16 tests; all 320 raw/text hashes and extraction results matched the catalog/config. [Task 1]\n  2493\t- Preserve literal music chord notation such as `<c e g>4` in `multidomain_sources.py`; HTML-style parsing corrupts it. `multidomain_corpus.py` supports `families_per_batch=1|5`, priority scheduling, `batch_order`, pilot/checkpoint metadata; `agy_multidomain.py` holds `run_locked_queue`, validates membership, and checkpoints reviewed exports. [Task 1]\n  2494\t- The durable v2 design is one family/job, two learner profiles, 20 contrasts. Each MiniMax/DeepSeek worker targets 16,000 contrasts (800 families, 1,600 profiles, 160 source groups) and uses worker-local 32,768 output cap; DeepSeek uses low reasoning effort. [Task 2]\n  2495\t\n  2496\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  2497\t\n  2498\t- Source selection overlapped original URLs -> exclude `ORIGINAL_URLS` before asserting disjointness. When a patch's expected text differs, inspect exact anchors with `rg`/`sed`. [Task 1]\n  2499\t- The original 100-contrast jobs timed out/exhausted output and produced no usable final JSON; retain receipts/logs as superseded, not corpus output. At final check v2 had zero completed batches/reviews, so require `status.json`, `worker-process.json`, drafts/reviews, validation, and exported artifacts before claiming quality or completion. [Task 2]\n  2500\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/voxq platform, canonical research exports, and private Radicle workflow\n  2501\tscope: Extend Voxq without overstating unfinished live integrations; maintain canonical exports and native Devenv-managed private Radicle lifecycle.\n  2502\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/voxq and /home/diogenes/Projects/notorganic-provider; reuse_rule=recheck the heavily dirty worktrees, live assertion configuration, and authorized remote-peer state before committing, deploying, or claiming replication.\n  2503\t\n  2504\t## Task 1: Register Voxq and delegate the broader survey platform, partial\n  2505\t\n  2506\t### rollout_summary_files\n  2507\t\n  2508\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/12/rollout-2026-09-12T17-02-31-01a0976d-cff1-7600-a08d-7d054ba9c9ca.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-10T03:09:16+00:00, thread_id=01a0976d-cff1-7600-a08d-7d054ba9c9ca, partial; registration passed, Codex build exit -1)\n  2509\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/12/rollout-2026-09-12T17-02-31-01a0976d-d008-7870-adcf-810fb461d97e.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-10T02:43:32+00:00, thread_id=01a0976d-d008-7870-adcf-810fb461d97e, partial; platform work unverified)\n  2510\t\n  2511\t### keywords\n  2512\t\n  2513\t- voxq, PRODUCT_IDS, FIRST_PARTY_PRODUCTS, ProductTheme, VOXQ_ASSERTION_PUBLIC_JWK, DPoP, micro-USD, --approve-for-me, --sandbox, adaptive-interviews, SSE\n  2514\t\n  2515\t## Task 2: Complete canonical CSV/JSON exports, docs, and marketing site\n  2516\t\n  2517\t### rollout_summary_files\n  2518\t\n  2519\t- rollout_summaries/2026-09-12T21-02-31-bjn0-voxq_site_export_readme_completion.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/voxq, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/12/rollout-2026-09-12T17-02-31-01a0976d-cff6-7bc2-bec8-12607e1b3476.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-13T00:26:03+00:00, thread_id=01a0976d-cff6-7bc2-bec8-12607e1b3476, success)\n  2520\t\n  2521\t### keywords\n  2522\t\n  2523\t- csv and json should be identical, exportRecords, resultsCsv, resultsJson, ExportResults.tsx, Cache-Control: no-store, smoke-exports.ts, landing/server.ts, embed/embed.js, SurveySim\n  2524\t\n  2525\t## Task 3: Add native Devenv Radicle hooks and verify local node/peers, partial\n  2526\t\n  2527\t### rollout_summary_files\n  2528\t\n  2529\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/voxq, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/12/rollout-2026-09-12T20-58-53-01a09846-3743-7a80-ab37-2f04b80438f4.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-13T01:07:50+00:00, thread_id=01a09846-3743-7a80-ab37-2f04b80438f4, partial; local node healthy, remote replication unconfirmed)\n  2530\t\n  2531\t### keywords\n  2532\t\n  2533\t- git-hooks.nix, voxq:radicle:init, voxq:radicle:status, scripts/radicle.sh, rad:z3X34hv7fz8WAgzTHnMmhJ8rvZz87, core.hooksPath=/dev/null, rad://<rid>/<did>, Railway\n  2534\t\n  2535\t## Task 4: Resume triage in a broadly dirty Voxq worktree\n  2536\t\n  2537\t### rollout_summary_files\n  2538\t\n  2539\t- rollout_summaries/2026-09-12T22-15-23-K2z1-voxq_resume_triage.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/voxq, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/12/rollout-2026-