tion slice without reopening scope; report unrun tests/evaluations plainly [Task 5]\n  2562\t\n  2563\t## Reusable knowledge\n  2564\t\n  2565\t- Voxq registration requires `PRODUCT_IDS`, `FIRST_PARTY_PRODUCTS`, and exhaustive email `ProductTheme`; an unset optional `VOXQ_ASSERTION_PUBLIC_JWK` keeps the gateway booting but rejects Voxq assertions. `bun run typecheck` and 231 tests passed. GitNexus `risk: UNKNOWN` is not clearance: search literal arrays and `.includes()` gates. [Task 1]\n  2566\t- `--sandbox` and `--approve-for-me` cannot be combined. The corrected background Codex task exited `-1`; inspect its output/diff rather than treating intended platform files as delivered. [Task 1]\n  2567\t- Export route/UI uses one `exportRecords` list for `resultsCsv` and `resultsJson`; include study, responses, discoveries/comparisons, population, costs, and caveats, but omit credentials, session capabilities, private interview IDs, and raw provider payloads. Browser downloads matched 106 records/22 columns; Rust 43 and web 184 tests passed. [Task 2]\n  2568\t- Private Radicle initialization succeeded as `rad:z3X34hv7fz8WAgzTHnMmhJ8rvZz87`; `rad/main...main` was `0 0`, and the local node was active on `0.0.0.0:8776` with 11 peers. `scripts/radicle.sh` skips direct `rad`/non-main pushes, bypasses internal mirror hooks, and prevents direct Radicle pushes from deploying Railway. [Task 3]\n  2569\t- Resume requests in this checkout are ambiguous: preserve the broad dirty tree and use the recent cwd/task context; ask a concise clarification when several unfinished workstreams remain. Local survey simulation passed previously, but live Persimmon/Portkey remains credential- and route-gated. [Task 4]\n  2570\t- Twin-2K-500 is pinned to release `f883165a3026fde855dfd448e0cd16443ab257b6`, CC BY 4.0, and seven fixed Parquet parts. The adapter uses fixed publisher URLs/SHA-256, 32 MB/120-second bounded downloads, atomic caching under `webapp/.data/datasets/twin-2k-500/<release>` (or `VOXQ_DATASET_CACHE`), and workspace-scoped transactional/idempotent imports. [Task 5]\n  2571\t- Keep projection narrow: selected demographics QID11/QID13/QID14/QID21/QID23/QID24, QID25 personality items, and QID224–QID229 economic preferences. `dataset_evidence` binds provenance/observations to the importing workspace; observations enter prompts as labeled data, with `survey-persona-v3-dataset-evidence`, never as instructions. Do not infer OCEAN scores; explicit researcher-authored Big Five remains separate. [Task 5]\n  2572\t- Dataset UI permits up to 30 selected profiles and response groups; imports/audience creation call no models. Cost uses a documented four-characters-per-token heuristic and remains an estimate, not a spending ceiling. `bun run check`, `bun run build`, `cargo build --quiet`, and `git diff --check` passed; Cargo retained an existing unused-`qid` warning. [Task 5]\n  2573\t\n  2574\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  2575\t\n  2576\t- Do not claim the delegated platform implementation or landing deployment succeeded from a background launch; registration/typecheck proof is narrower. [Task 1]\n  2577\t- Do not serialize CSV and JSON from separate fresh API responses; do not infer competitor details from an empty SPA shell. [Task 2]\n  2578\t- `rad init` needs the signing key in `ssh-agent`/`rad auth` and must bootstrap with `core.hooksPath=/dev/null`; accept bare and DID-qualified Radicle URLs. Connected peers/local refs do not prove remote private-repository replication. [Task 3]\n  2579\t- GitNexus missing edges/zero callers are unknown, not safety proof: supplement with repository text search. Browser tool inventory was empty and no automated tests, model evaluations, or full acceptance checks ran; do not call the dataset UI visually or end-to-end verified. [Task 5]\n  2580\t\n  2581\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects filesystem organization and Markdown catalog maintenance\n  2582\tscope: Classify/move repositories without losing local work, delete only explicitly approved targets, and repair Projects/Programs catalogs.\n  2583\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects and /home/diogenes/Programs; reuse_rule=inspect current origin/author history and filesystem boundaries before moving or deleting; treat catalog paths as checkout-specific.\n  2584\t\n  2585\t## Task 1: Move third-party repositories, remove approved redundant data, and repair catalogs\n  2586\t\n  2587\t### rollout_summary_files\n  2588\t\n  2589\t- rollout_summaries/2026-09-12T21-02-31-9H9T-projects_programs_cleanup_and_catalog_repair.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/12/rollout-2026-09-12T17-02-31-01a0976d-cff4-7022-a2dd-4f8596be7579.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-12T20:37:49+00:00, thread_id=01a0976d-cff4-7022-a2dd-4f8596be7579, success; 22 moves and 239 catalog-link checks passed)\n  2590\t\n  2591\t### keywords\n  2592\t\n  2593\t- Projects, Programs, mv -n, git origin, authorship, SUMMARY.md, INDEX.md, ../../Programs, ../.archive, keating.bc, bad object HEAD\n  2594\t\n  2595\t## User preferences\n  2596\t\n  2597\t- when organizing files, the user said “don’t delete anything” and clarified “for repos that don't have any git repo assume they are me and local to this computer” -> default to non-destructive moves and leave non-git directories in place [Task 1]\n  2598\t- deletion became allowed only after explicit requests to “remove empty dirs” and “remove keating.bc” -> resolve exact targets and preserve data unless deletion is expressly approved [Task 1]\n  2599\t\n  2600\t## Reusable knowledge\n  2601\t\n  2602\t- Projects and Programs share one filesystem, so `mv -n` is an atomic rename that preserves dirty/untracked work; use source/destination existence checks. Inspect both git origin and author history before moving mixed-ownership repositories. The completed move reported `moved:22 failed:0`; `semdiff` stayed by user choice. [Task 1]\n  2603\t- A stray empty `Projects/.git` can cause false repository detection. Before recursive deletion, move the shell cwd out of the target; `keating.bc` had corrupt history (`fatal: bad object HEAD`) but deletion followed explicit approval and active `keating` was checked intact. [Task 1]\n  2604\t- In Projects category `SUMMARY.md`, use `../X` for Projects targets, `../../Programs/X` for moved targets, and `../.archive/X` for archived targets. Keep genuinely absent rows as `_no longer on disk_` when organizing rather than deleting catalog information; 239 catalog links were checked with no catalog failures. [Task 1]\n  2605\t\n  2606\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  2607\t\n  2608\t- Do not classify a directory as a real repository only because a parent/empty `.git` exists; confirm the repository and history first. Do not run `rm -rf` while the shell remains inside the target. [Task 1]\n  2609\t\n  2610\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/autopsy benchmark playground and provider-boundary review\n  2611\tscope: Review runtime correctness beyond passing typecheck/tests; this records findings only, not fixes.\n  2612\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/autopsy; reuse_rule=reinspect the current implementation and add focused regression tests before applying any repair.\n  2613\t\n  2614\t## Task 1: Review benchmark playground and custom-provider changes\n  2615\t\n  2616\t### rollout_summary_files\n  2617\t\n  2618\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/autopsy, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/10/rollout-2026-09-10T05-48-28-01a08ab7-fafb-7db3-8fec-6b0670cc88d7.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-10T09:50:16+00:00, thread_id=01a08ab7-fafb-7db3-8fec-6b0670cc88d7, success; findings only)\n  2619\t\n  2620\t### keywords\n  2621\t\n  2622\t- benchmark/server.ts, JSON.stringify cannot serialize cyclic structures, cycle-free DTO, diagnostic-service.ts, diagnosis cache, Error serialization, minimaxApiKey, MINIMAX_API_KEY\n  2623\t\n  2624\t## Reusable knowledge\n  2625\t\n  2626\t- Keep the intentional circular todo graph internal and return a cycle-free DTO; use a fresh diagnosis cache per benchmark invocation; serialize `Error` name/message/stack explicitly at HTTP boundaries; honor configured `minimaxApiKey` before falling back to `MINIMAX_API_KEY`. [Task 1]\n  2627\t\n  2628\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  2629\t\n  2630\t- Passing typecheck and 75 tests did not exercise these runtime boundaries. No fixes or post-change verification happened; write focused regression coverage before declaring any repair complete. [Task 1]\n  2631\t\n  2632\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/keating chat sign-in continuation and Not Organic inference failure handling\n  2633\tscope: Keep learner chat immediate through account authorization and diagnose the actual Keating-to-Not Organic inference path without treating health checks as end-to-end proof.\n  2634\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating and /home/diogenes/Projects/notorganic-provider; reuse_rule=recheck dirty worktrees, installed desktop version, fresh token/DPoP flow, Portkey configuration, and Convex behavior.\n  2635\t\n  2636\t## Task 1: Preserve a pending chat send across Not Organic sign-in and push focused changes\n  2637\t\n  2638\t### rollout_summary_files\n  2639\t\n  2640\t- rollout_summaries/2026-09-09T09-07-30-nEVR-keating_landing_and_signin_message_continuation_push.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/09/rollout-2026-09-09T05-07-30-01a0856c-1ddf-73c3-a1a7-04c0f52e6c4b.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-09T21:03:57+00:00, thread_id=01a0856c-1ddf-73c3-a1a7-04c0f52e6c4b, success; mocked browser proof only)\n  2641\t\n  2642\t### keywords\n  2643\t\n  2644\t- pending-chat-turn.ts, sessionStorage, stream_not_found, AppStorage, IndexedDB oncomplete, FlueConversation.resume, b45e0d8b, core.hooksPath=/dev/null\n  2645\t\n  2646\t## Task 2: Diagnose immediate-send/retry and production funding failures, partial\n  2647\t\n  2648\t### rollout_summary_files\n  2649\t\n  2650\t- rollout_summaries/2026-09-09T21-09-56-9d3N-keating_notorganic_chat_e2e_inference_retry_partial.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Documents/Codex/2026-09-09/recently-in-keeting-we-worked-on, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/09/rollout-2026-09-09T17-09-56-01a08801-84fe-7a31-be23-ea11379e0ac7.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-10T00:43:27+00:00, thread_id=01a08801-84fe-7a31-be23-ea11379e0ac7, partial)\n  2651\t\n  2652\t### keywords\n  2653\t\n  2654\t- optimistic UI, retry, DPoP, Portkey, pc-keatin-bb473e, product: keating, INSUFFICIENT_FUNDS, HTTP 402, Passthrough target requires a provider\n  2655\t\n  2656\t## User preferences\n  2657\t\n  2658\t- when the user said a send “should immediately see it in the chat” and requested retry -> independently accept optimistic insertion, sending status, failed-turn retention, and retry without manual resend [Task 2]\n  2659\t- when the user said “most computer use, don't do computer use on your own” -> use code/logs/HTTP/tests and leave desktop/browser interaction to the user [Task 2]\n  2660\t- when the user said “you will need to push changes then we shall see” -> push explicitly requested focused work after validation while leaving unrelated dirty work unstaged [Task 1]\n  2661\t\n  2662\t## Reusable knowledge\n  2663\t\n  2664\t- Persist `{sessionId, timestamp, ready}` before sign-in; only mark ready after callback exchange and claim once by exact session/message timestamp. Clear before resume to avoid StrictMode duplicates. New Flue streams legitimately yield 404 `stream_not_found` before their first prompt, and IndexedDB must await transaction `oncomplete`. Focused tests: 35 pass; mocked flow rendered one learner turn/one answer and cleared the marker. [Task 1]\n  2665\t- Portkey `balanced` only worked with metadata `product: \"keating\"`; `fast` returned `Passthrough target requires a provider`. Convex `INSUFFICIENT_FUNDS` was hidden behind a generic 500 because production wraps ordinary errors; propagate a structured code and map it to non-retryable 402. [Task 2]\n  2666\t\n  2667\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  2668\t\n  2669\t- `git -c core.hooksPath=/dev/null push` was an exceptional, separately validated bypass after unrelated failures/locked key/checkpoint rejection, not normal release procedure. Mocked OAuth/provider tests and remote ref proof do not establish real-account or production inference. [Task 1]\n  2670\t- Health/Railway success/direct Portkey stream do not prove desktop chat. Verify fresh public token exchange, DPoP request, exact stream, reservation, and rendered UI. Retryable failures get fresh DPoP proofs; insufficient credits do not retry. [Task 2]\n  2671\t\n  2672\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/keating MiniCPM5 offline tutoring, v3.15.0 release, and publication/privacy boundary\n  2673\tscope: Evaluate MiniCPM5 for browser/native tutoring, retain safe text-only media behavior, and distinguish release artifacts from verified public publication and credential remediation.\n  2674\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating; reuse_rule=recheck model/runtime support, JDK/NDK environment, release assets, GitHub cache state, and secrets rotation before reuse.\n  2675\t\n  2676\t## Task 1: Keep MiniCPM5 out of unsupported browser runtime; add native offline path, partial\n  2677\t\n  2678\t### rollout_summary_files\n  2679\t\n  2680\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/10/rollout-2026-09-10T05-12-38-01a08a97-2eee-70c3-87c4-20f4245238ef.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-10T11:05:38+00:00, thread_id=01a08a97-2eee-70c3-87c4-20f4245238ef, partial)\n  2681\t\n  2682\t### keywords\n  2683\t\n  2684\t- MiniCPM5-2B-LiteRT, .litertlm, BROWSER_MODELS, WeakMap<Blob,string>, recording-transcripts, JDK 21, CPATH, keating-litert, SHA-256\n  2685\t\n  2686\t## Task 2: Publish v3.15.0, remediate public checkpoint credential exposure, and assess Windows/APK assets, partial\n  2687\t\n  2688\t### rollout_summary_files\n  2689\t\n  2690\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/10/rollout-2026-09-10T07-05-46-01a08afe-c05c-7ba3-868b-da12a887728f.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-10T20:56:02+00:00, thread_id=01a08afe-c05c-7ba3-868b-da12a887728f, partial; public cache/rotation unresolved)\n  2691\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/10/rollout-2026-09-10T16-55-01-01a08d1a-3be9-7611-9f53-4aafb458285a.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-10T23:13:11+00:00, thread_id=01a08d1a-3be9-7611-9f53-4aafb458285a, partial; assets absent/Windows check failed)\n  2692\t\n  2693\t### keywords\n  2694\t\n  2695\t- v3.15.0, Entire checkpoints, Paddle, GitHub cached objects, credential rotation, release.yml, desktop-release.yml, Windows .exe, Android .apk\n  2696\t\n  2697\t## User preferences\n  2698\t\n  2699\t- when the user asked for MiniCPM5 as primary browser model plus image/audio errors -> verify model/runtime compatibility before changing defaults and visibly reject unsupported media [Task 1]\n  2700\t- when the user said “new release”/“do that” -> take commit/tag/push/publication through independent proof and distinguish preparation from public release [Task 2]\n  2701\t\n  2702\t## Reusable knowledge\n  2703\t\n  2704\t- MiniCPM5 LiteRT is text-only `.litertlm`; Keating browser loader is Transformers.js ONNX, and LiteRT-LM JS did not support arbitrary bundles. Keep it out of `BROWSER_MODELS`. For recordings, suppress only a successful transcript tied to that exact Blob via `WeakMap<Blob,string>`; focused web tests 16 passed. [Task 1]\n  2705\t- Native Android build requires a full JDK 21 with `javac`; clear `CPATH`, `C_INCLUDE_PATH`, `CPLUS_INCLUDE_PATH`, and `LIBRARY_PATH` before NDK builds. APK compilation/package inclusion and 57 focused tests do not prove device inference/iOS. [Task 1]\n  2706\t- The checkpoint incident requires private copy/removal from public branch plus credential rotation and GitHub cached-object purge; never retain or reproduce the exposed credential. Treat release/tag/workflow claims and Windows/APK publication as separate checks. [Task 2]\n  2707\t\n  2708\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  2709\t\n  2710\t- Do not change high-impact shared `modelInputModalities` for a narrow attachment fix, and do not claim arbitrary LiteRT browser support without actual loading/generation. [Task 1]\n  2711\t- Release assets were absent, Windows verification failed, and Android retry remained in progress. A release workflow trigger or source publication is not proof that `.exe`/`.apk` assets exist and install. [Task 2]\n  2712\t\n  2713\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/textbook web review, OpenTUI branding, docs separation, and deployment\n  2714\tscope: Apply bounded review fixes and product presentation changes while keeping broad implementation claims separate from final verification.\n  2715\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/textbook; reuse_rule=recheck current dirty tree, generated assets, Railway deployment, and browser behavior before claiming completion.\n  2716\t\n  2717\t## Task 1: Address review findings, branding/docs work, and deployment, partial\n  2718\t\n  2719\t### rollout_summary_files\n  2720\t\n  2721\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/textbook, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/11/rollout-2026-09-11T01-13-09-01a08ee2-48f5-7292-876b-cd7fca859165.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-11T06:31:38+00:00, thread_id=01a08ee2-48f5-7292-876b-cd7fca859165, partial; final verification generally skipped)\n  2722\t\n  2723\t### keywords\n  2724\t\n  2725\t- textbook, OpenTUI, review P1 P2, social cards, Railway, hosted-vs-local docs, verification skipped\n  2726\t\n  2727\t## Reusable knowledge\n  2728\t\n  2729\t- This rollout is a routing record for broad review/branding/docs/deployment implementation; open its summary before making completion claims because final verification was generally skipped. [Task 1]\n  2730\t\n  2731\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  2732\t\n  2733\t- Do not convert wide code changes or deployment setup into security/reliability/browser proof without the missing targeted checks. [Task 1]\n  2734\t\n  2735\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/dio.computer research-grounded high-impact design direction and content QA\n  2736\tscope: Explore actual browser-shaped personal-site directions from repository/blog/photo evidence; avoid restrained generic moodboards and preserve source data integrity boundaries.\n  2737\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/dio.computer with Keating indexing context; reuse_rule=recheck Paper quota, source content, photo mapping, and user feedback before making design or source edits.\n  2738\t\n  2739\t## Task 1: Index repos, recover Keating files, and explore a louder dio.computer direction, partial\n  2740\t\n  2741\t### rollout_summary_files\n  2742\t\n  2743\t- rollout_summaries/2026-09-12T21-02-31-lJJC-dio_computer_design_direction_and_multi_repo_indexing.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/12/rollout-2026-09-12T17-02-31-01a0976d-d04b-77f2-91de-e06f4b2bea68.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-09T20:02:02+00:00, thread_id=01a0976d-d04b-77f2-91de-e06f4b2bea68, partial; second UI artifact awaiting feedback)\n  2744\t\n  2745\t### keywords\n  2746\t\n  2747\t- yell HERE I AM, bland and muted, agentFacts.ts, sitePhotos.ts, Paper Desktop, Weekly MCP limit reached, GitNexus, graft build, PYTHONHOME\n  2748\t\n  2749\t## User preferences\n  2750\t\n  2751\t- when the user said “it isn't a celebration of myself and my interests,” “bland and muted,” and “yell HERE I AM” -> favor strong personality, saturation, contrast, density, real interests/photos, humor, and memorable hierarchy [Task 1]\n  2752\t- when the user said eight directions “just feel off” -> change the format/assumption rather than generating more themed poster variants [Task 1]\n  2753\t- when the user said inspect code/blog/site information and “use your best judgement” -> research before asking more design questions [Task 1]\n  2754\t\n  2755\t## Reusable knowledge\n  2756\t\n  2757\t- Start with `src/data/agentFacts.ts`, `src/data/sitePhotos.ts`, `PRODUCT.md`, `soul.md`, and `posts/*.md`. Show actual browser/UI composition, navigation, hierarchy, and interaction rather than illustrative moodboards. [Task 1]\n  2758\t- `graft build` creates ignored cache; `gitnexus analyze <path>` indexes a repo, while `gitnexus status` takes no path. Keating `release.yml` is separate from `devenv.nix`; `OPERATIONS.md` is checked against config by `bun scripts/check-env-docs.ts`. [Task 1]\n  2759\t- A contact sheet found photos 01–11 likely shuffled in `sitePhotos.ts`; Paper usage was corrected but application source remains an open bug pending explicit scope. Use `env -u PYTHONHOME -u PYTHONPATH python3` for poisoned Python env. [Task 1]\n  2760\t\n  2761\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  2762\t\n  2763\t- The initial genre-pastiche poster directions were rejected; desaturation, sparse accents, and hairline borders reinforced the muted result. Paper MCP had a weekly hard limit; do not attempt a workaround without user direction. [Task 1]\n  2764\t- Verify architecture/references before restoring suspected zero-byte files; an auto-mode denial should be handled through a safe alternate command or reported, not bypassed. [Task 1]\n  2765\t\n  2766\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/voxq survey webapp and contract-only Persimmon persona tier\n  2767\tscope: Run and verify the local survey studio, keep its Rust/Bun boundary safe, and expose a Not Organic model alias without falsely advertising an unwired upstream.\n  2768\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/voxq and /home/diogenes/Projects/notorganic-provider; reuse_rule=reuse local webapp and alias-contract guidance after checking both dirty worktrees; Persimmon/Portkey production availability requires fresh credentials and a real route.\n  2769\t\n  2770\t## Task 1: Fix and verify the voxq survey webapp\n  2771\t\n  2772\t### rollout_summary_files\n  2773\t\n  2774\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/voxq, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/12/rollout-2026-09-12T17-02-31-01a0976d-cff7-7932-863d-f23bba79fa99.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-11T07:26:51+00:00, thread_id=01a0976d-cff7-7932-863d-f23bba79fa99, success; local end-to-end simulation verified)\n  2775\t\n  2776\t### keywords\n  2777\t\n  2778\t- voxq, webapp/server.ts, 127.0.0.1:3100, 127.0.0.1:3101, api_version === 2, reqwest, rustls-tls, openssl-sys, embed-config, PIPESTATUS\n  2779\t\n  2780\t## Task 2: Add the `persona` alias contract-only\n  2781\t\n  2782\t### rollout_summary_files\n  2783\t\n  2784\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/voxq, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/12/rollout-2026-09-12T17-02-31-01a0976d-cff7-7932-863d-f23bba79fa99.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-11T07:26:51+00:00, thread_id=01a0976d-cff7-7932-863d-f23bba79fa99, success; live Persimmon/Portkey intentionally gated)\n  2785\t\n  2786\t### keywords\n  2787\t\n  2788\t- persona, infer:persona, catalog.ts, ADMIN_CAPS_MICROUSD, ENABLED_MODEL_ALIASES, /v1/models, Portkey, missing bearer API key, Unsupported model alias\n  2789\t\n  2790\t## Task 3: Produce an honest Persimmon access appeal and walkthrough\n  2791\t\n  2792\t### rollout_summary_files\n  2793\t\n  2794\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/voxq, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/12/rollout-2026-09-12T17-02-31-01a0976d-cff7-7932-863d-f23bba79fa99.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-11T07:26:51+00:00, thread_id=01a0976d-cff7-7932-863d-f23bba79fa99, success)\n  2795\t\n  2796\t### keywords\n  2797\t\n  2798\t- TutorMoments, simulated respondents, authored learner replies, research-access appeal, detect-changes, no commits or deployments\n  2799\t\n  2800\t## User preferences\n  2801\t\n  2802\t- when the user asked to “get the web app working” and requested a walkthrough -> verify the running application end-to-end and distinguish verified behavior from unwired behavior [Task 1]\n  2803\t- when the user selected alias `persona` and said “Contract-only, not enabled” -> define it for local tooling but do not advertise or deploy it until a verified Persimmon key and Portkey route exist [Task 2]\n  2804\t\n  2805\t## Reusable knowledge\n  2806\t\n  2807\t- `webapp/server.ts` starts Rust privately at `127.0.0.1:3101`; the Bun BFF at `127.0.0.1:3100` requires Rust `/healthz` with `api_version === 2`. `reqwest` was the only `openssl-sys` consumer; disabling default features and selecting `rustls-tls` produced a clean build without it. [Task 1]\n  2808\t- Verify create -> estimate -> run -> analysis -> cost -> publish -> embed-config. Demo cost is explicitly zero; unknown provider rates must remain nonzero/unknown. Public embed config must expose only accepting state, name, product, and question count. [Task 1]\n  2809\t- Not Organic aliases are capability tiers (`infer:<alias>`), not upstream IDs. Add `persona` to contracts and the exhaustive admin-cap map, but omit it from Railway `ENABLED_MODEL_ALIASES` and gateway `/v1/models` fallbacks until configuration is real. Local deterministic fixtures do not prove human-like realism. [Task 2]\n  2810\t- The provisional 2,000,000 µUSD cap is a ceiling, not published Persimmon pricing. Current evidence is HTTP 401 `missing bearer API key` and WorkOS-gated docs; no live request or Portkey mapping was verified. [Task 2]\n  2811\t- The appeal may connect voxq's simulated-respondent benchmarking to Keating's authored-learner limitation and Persimmon TutorMoments, but must not claim a human interview or live Persimmon flow. Run repository `detect-changes` before later commits because unrelated Not Organic changes exist. [Task 3]\n  2812\t\n  2813\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  2814\t\n  2815\t- `cargo build 2>&1 | tail` masks Cargo status: inspect `PIPESTATUS[0]` or avoid the pipe. Shell cwd does not persist between background calls, so use absolute paths or explicit `cd`; direct Rust health without its internal bearer token should return 401. [Task 1]\n  2816\t- Treat GitNexus `risk: UNKNOWN` as unresolved and confirm by text search. Do not enable `persona` or invent upstream pricing from the admin ceiling. [Task 2]\n  2817\t\n  2818\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/keating MiniCPM5 browser WebGPU diagnosis and model-loading UX\n  2819\tscope: Diagnose local MiniCPM5 WebGPU execution failures, preserve loading visibility, align ONNX Runtime Web packages, and source-review model generation guidance.\n  2820\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating; reuse_rule=recheck target GPU/browser, npm publication state, model artifacts, and branch before reuse; no target-device MiniCPM5 fix was proven.\n  2821\t\n  2822\t## Task 1: Diagnose MiniCPM5 `Invalid Buffer` during WebGPU execution\n  2823\t\n  2824\t### rollout_summary_files\n  2825\t\n  2826\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/11/rollout-2026-09-11T19-20-26-01a092c5-ba40-79b1-8a49-6c9c2b750e63.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-12T01:41:26+00:00, thread_id=01a092c5-ba40-79b1-8a49-6c9c2b750e63, partial; target-device failure unresolved)\n  2827\t\n  2828\t### keywords\n  2829\t\n  2830\t- MiniCPM5, RASMUS/MiniCPM5-2B-ONNX, WebGPU, shader-f16, OrtRun, mapAsync, Invalid Buffer, q4f16, GPU device-lost, GitNexus\n  2831\t\n  2832\t## Task 2: Keep browser-model download/loading visible across navigation\n  2833\t\n  2834\t### rollout_summary_files\n  2835\t\n  2836\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/11/rollout-2026-09-11T19-20-26-01a092c5-ba40-79b1-8a49-6c9c2b750e63.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-12T01:41:26+00:00, thread_id=01a092c5-ba40-79b1-8a49-6c9c2b750e63, success; page/tab close still cancels)\n  2837\t\n  2838\t### keywords\n  2839\t\n  2840\t- BrowserModelDownloadStatus, ModelDownloadBar.tsx, model-download-progress.ts, describeDownload, Cancel download, GPU preparation, 1 of 2 files\n  2841\t\n  2842\t## Task 3: Pin published ONNX Runtime Web packages and review MiniCPM5 guidance\n  2843\t\n  2844\t### rollout_summary_files\n  2845\t\n  2846\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/11/rollout-2026-09-11T19-20-26-01a092c5-ba40-79b1-8a49-6c9c2b750e63.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-12T01:41:26+00:00, thread_id=01a092c5-ba40-79b1-8a49-6c9c2b750e63, success)\n  2847\t\n  2848\t### keywords\n  2849\t\n  2850\t- onnxruntime-web@1.29.0, onnxruntime-common, onnxruntime-node, Transformers.js, max_new_tokens, top_p=0.95, enable_thinking, XML tool calls\n  2851\t\n  2852\t## User preferences\n  2853\t\n  2854\t- when the user said browser acceleration was enabled and Edge was version 153 -> do not repeat generic compatibility advice; separate adapter preflight from actual runtime/backend errors [Task 1]\n  2855\t- when the user asked to read the Hugging Face README, generation notes, and model report before behavior changes -> source-review model integration guidance first [Task 3]\n  2856\t\n  2857\t## Reusable knowledge\n  2858\t\n  2859\t- `checkWebGpuAvailable()` only proves `navigator.gpu`, adapter, and `shader-f16`; MiniCPM5 is a ~1.83 GB `q4f16` export with a ~535 MB unquantized embedding table, and passing preflight does not prove `OrtRun`. Refresh GitNexus (`analyze`, then `status`) before trusting its call graph. [Task 1]\n  2860\t- `BrowserModelDownloadStatus` in `web/src/components/ModelDownloadBar.tsx`, mounted by `web/src/App.tsx`, keeps store-owned loads visible after picker close/route change; show percentage, bytes, file count, rate, ETA, preparation/GPU loading, and accessible cancellation. 1,713 web tests, production build, and `git diff --check` passed. [Task 2]\n  2861\t- Browser JS packages published at 1.29.0 while native ONNX Runtime was 1.30.0. Pin `onnxruntime-common`, `onnxruntime-node`, and `onnxruntime-web` together at published 1.29.0; do not pin a native-only version. [Task 3]\n  2862\t- MiniCPM5's documented browser path uses `device: 'webgpu'`, `dtype: 'q4f16'`, message arrays, and `max_new_tokens`; OpenBMB guidance is `temperature=1.0, top_p=0.95`. Current browser chat disables thinking and does not convert XML-style tool calls, so treat it as direct-answer chat. [Task 3]\n  2863\t\n  2864\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  2865\t\n  2866\t- `failed to call OrtRun(). ... Invalid Buffer (unlabeled)` remains unresolved model/backend/GPU compatibility or device loss, not evidence that Edge/acceleration is unsupported. Capture device-lost diagnostics, test smaller/q4 models, and compare runtimes on target hardware. [Task 1]\n  2867\t- Raw Hugging Face file URLs were blocked by the web tool; use model-card/README pages or repository tools. [Task 3]\n  2868\t\n  2869\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/keating immediate chat, production account auth, and signed desktop distribution\n  2870\t\n  2871\tscope: Make chat publication immediate, keep account authorization distinct from hosted inference, and package Keating for Windows plus signed Linux/AppImage/DEB/RPM/Flatpak distribution.\n  2872\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating; reuse_rule=recheck the heavily dirty worktree, live Railway configuration, CI/desktop runners, signing/publication state, and real desktop/browser flows; focused/local checks do not prove public release or authenticated production use.\n  2873\t\n  2874\t## Task 1: Immediate learner-message visibility and Not Organic account sign-in, partial\n  2875\t\n  2876\t### rollout_summary_files\n  2877\t\n  2878\t- rollout_summaries/2026-09-09T04-11-52-opTc-keating_auth_chat_windows_flatpak_packaging.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/09/rollout-2026-09-09T00-11-52-01a0845d-7684-7db2-a6bb-71e3adda3052.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-09T08:36:03+00:00, thread_id=01a0845d-7684-7db2-a6bb-71e3adda3052, partial; focused tests and endpoint checks passed, browser callback/inference not proved)\n  2879\t\n  2880\t### keywords\n  2881\t\n  2882\t- AssistantChatPanel, FlueConversation, sendPrepared, optimistic-message, flue-immediate-send.test.ts, NotOrganic, PKCE, DPoP, publicClientConfig, VITE_NOTORGANIC_ENABLED, keating.help, spawnSync bun EPERM\n  2883\t\n  2884\t## Task 2: Windows Electron packaging and native runtime hardening, partial\n  2885\t\n  2886\t### rollout_summary_files\n  2887\t\n  2888\t- rollout_summaries/2026-09-09T04-11-52-opTc-keating_auth_chat_windows_flatpak_packaging.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/09/rollout-2026-09-09T00-11-52-01a0845d-7684-7db2-a6bb-71e3adda3052.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-09T08:36:03+00:00, thread_id=01a0845d-7684-7db2-a6bb-71e3adda3052, partial; local Nitro/Lean tests passed, no Windows runner)\n  2889\t\n  2890\t### keywords\n  2891\t\n  2892\t- dist:windows, NSIS, Electron, windows-latest, native-runtime.ts, nitro-runtime.ts, lean-verifier.ts, verify-windows-runtime.cjs, taskkill, Job Object, .elan/bin/lean.exe\n  2893\t\n  2894\t## Task 3: Signed AppImage/DEB/RPM releases and self-hosted Flatpak, partial\n  2895\t\n  2896\t### rollout_summary_files\n  2897\t\n  2898\t- rollout_summaries/2026-09-09T04-11-52-opTc-keating_auth_chat_windows_flatpak_packaging.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/09/rollout-2026-09-09T00-11-52-01a0845d-7684-7db2-a6bb-71e3adda3052.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-09T08:36:03+00:00, thread_id=01a0845d-7684-7db2-a6bb-71e3adda3052, partial; local signed exports/install passed, public repository/release unproved)\n  2899\t\n  2900\t### keywords\n  2901\t\n  2902\t- AppImage, DEB, RPM, SHA256SUMS, sign-release.mjs, keating-release-key.asc, fingerprint.txt, Flatpak, Electron2.BaseApp//25.08, Zypak, appstreamcli compose, --no-net, OSTree, .flatpakrepo, .flatpakref, GitHub Pages\n  2903\t\n  2904\t## User preferences\n  2905\t\n  2906\t- when the user said a sent message “should appear in chat immediately” and be visible “the moment i press enter” -> publish the learner turn before credentials, workspace preparation, or model admission; reconcile later rather than delaying visible feedback. [Task 1]\n  2907\t- when the user wanted Anthropic token handling “done automatically” -> distinguish provider/browser OAuth limits from desktop-native callbacks, and do not claim automatic web authentication without real provider/browser verification. [Task 1]\n  2908\t- when the user said “we should also get the desktop app working for windows” -> cross-platform delivery includes an installer plus native dependencies, process handling, filesystem/OAuth/credential paths, and GUI/runtime smoke proof, not merely a build target. [Task 2]\n  2909\t- when the user requested DEB/RPM “along with a signed key,” retained AppImage, and chose self-hosted Flatpak -> preserve all three Linux formats, publish an out-of-band public signing key, and use a signed self-hosted Flatpak repository rather than Flathub unless redirected. [Task 3]\n  2910\t\n  2911\t## Reusable knowledge\n  2912\t\n  2913\t- `web/src/keating/flue/conversation.ts` supports synchronous local publication through `sendPrepared`, cancellable preparation, retained failed/repeated submissions, and native acknowledgement reconciliation. `web/src/test/flue-immediate-send.test.ts` covered delayed preparation, repeated failed text, and cancellation; focused immediate-send/chat/audio tests reported 13 passing tests. [Task 1]\n  2914\t- Not Organic browser auth uses PKCE plus a device-bound DPoP key, pending state in browser storage, exact issuer/client/redirect matching, and callback receipt/code-hash guards. `VITE_NOTORGANIC_ENABLED` should gate hosted inference, not account sign-in; authorization instead requires explicit issuer and authorization URL configuration. The inspected Railway production value was `VITE_NOTORGANIC_ENABLED=false`; focused Not Organic suites reported 25 passing tests, authorization redirected, token preflight returned 204 for `https://keating.help`, and the OpenAI device route returned 200. [Task 1]\n  2915\t- Windows packaging adds `dist:windows`/NSIS and a `windows-latest` release job that packages, silently installs, and runs a packaged native-runtime smoke test. Windows runtime needs command quoting, case-insensitive environment overrides, early spawn/exit listeners, hidden background processes, and distinct immutable `resources/nitro` versus mutable user-data paths. Lean verification resolves `~/.elan/bin/lean.exe`, restricts syntax/tactics, bounds execution/output, and audits axioms; focused Nitro/Lean tests reported 16 tests/68 assertions, with Lean 4.30 accepting valid and rejecting invalid examples. [Task 2]\n  2916\t- The dedicated release key's public fingerprint/key live at `desktop/signing/fingerprint.txt` and `desktop/signing/keating-release-key.asc`; private material belongs only in isolated CI secrets/keyrings. `sign-release.mjs` makes deterministic `SHA256SUMS`, detached signatures, public-key export, and optional embedded RPM signatures. [Task 3]\n  2917\t- Flatpak can be self-hosted: retain OSTree objects, refs, summary, signatures, AppStream catalogs, `.flatpakrepo`, `.flatpakref`, and the public key. Build from an already-published architecture-matching AppImage or unpacked Electron app after ELF-architecture validation. Local x86_64/aarch64 signed exports and installation succeeded, and packaged `hyperswarm`/`corestore` loaded in sandbox; Flatpak runtime dependencies are not bundled and may still come from Flathub. [Task 3]\n  2918\t\n  2919\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  2920\t\n  2921\t- Browser automation lacked a connected Playwriter extension, headless navigation timed out, and CUA had no browser. Endpoint/CORS/focused-test evidence is not real callback completion, persistence, refresh, or authenticated model-use proof. Treat local `spawnSync bun EPERM` from the `keating-flue-runtime` Vite plugin as an environment limitation unless CI reproduces it. [Task 1]\n  2922\t- No Windows runner executed. Do not claim installer launch, GUI startup, OAuth return, encrypted credential persistence, native dependency loading, or descendant cleanup; `taskkill` fallback is not a Job Object guarantee, and symlink tests may need junctions or Developer Mode. [Task 2]\n  2923\t- AppStream compose initially failed from a missing compose addon and partial URLs: require host `appstreamcli compose`, run `--no-net`, and fail before export if catalog generation is unavailable. `rpmsign` was initially missing and end-to-end RPM embedded signing remains unproved. Headless Flatpak DBus errors are not desktop-session/OAuth/audio/permissions/storage proof; local exports/GitHub Pages enablement do not prove the repository or release artifacts were committed, pushed, public, or install-tested. [Task 3]\n  2924\t\n  2925\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/keating settings controls, Codex search UX, and Railway production deployment\n  2926\t\n  2927\tscope: Maintain responsive settings/provider controls and deploy the Keating web surface, including native Codex web search and copyable diagnostics, while preserving unrelated dirty work.\n  2928\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating; reuse_rule=recheck the current dependency graph, Railway target, and dirty-tree scope; local tests/typechecks do not establish live search behavior.\n  2929\t\n  2930\t## Task 1: Responsive settings navigation and complete provider visibility controls\n  2931\t\n  2932\t### rollout_summary_files\n  2933\t\n  2934\t- rollout_summaries/2026-09-08T03-25-44-ctrB-keating_settings_cleanup_and_context_report_site.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/07/rollout-2026-09-07T23-25-44-01a07f0c-dd35-75f0-b5c3-9ce89342b033.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-08T05:01:02+00:00, thread_id=01a07f0c-dd35-75f0-b5c3-9ce89342b033, success; web typecheck passed)\n  2935\t\n  2936\t### keywords\n  2937\t\n  2938\t- SettingsDialog, Panda CSS, md breakpoint, aria-label, title, double-box, setProvidersVisibility, hiddenProviders, customProviders, ProviderVisibilitySection\n  2939\t\n  2940\t## Task 2: Codex native web search and copyable diagnostics\n  2941\t\n  2942\t### rollout_summary_files\n  2943\t\n  2944\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/08/rollout-2026-09-08T07-47-21-01a080d8-1ab0-79f0-a1af-6170040588bf.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-08T21:43:08+00:00, thread_id=01a080d8-1ab0-79f0-a1af-6170040588bf, success locally; live behavior unverified)\n  2945\t\n  2946\t### keywords\n  2947\t\n  2948\t- web_search, external_web_access, codex-search-fetch.ts, response.output_item.done, zstd, pdfjs-dist, WebSearchPart, CopyDiagnosticButton, DiagnosticsTab\n  2949\t\n  2950\t## Task 3: Deploy the scoped Keating snapshot to Railway\n  2951\t\n  2952\t### rollout_summary_files\n  2953\t\n  2954\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/08/rollout-2026-09-08T07-47-21-01a080d8-1ab0-79f0-a1af-6170040588bf.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-08T21:43:08+00:00, thread_id=01a080d8-1ab0-79f0-a1af-6170040588bf, success; deployment 2459726e-340e-477b-8b79-db0c5601eea4)\n  2955\t\n  2956\t### keywords\n  2957\t\n  2958\t- Railway, keating.help, --path-as-root, filtered snapshot, Dockerfile.web, railway.toml, pdfjs-dist@5.4.394, Healthcheck succeeded\n  2959\t\n  2960\t## User preferences\n  2961\t\n  2962\t- when mobile tab text was occluded, the user asked for icons only, then clarified “they should expand as the size increses” -> use icon-only controls at narrow widths and reveal labels at a larger breakpoint. [Task 1]\n  2963\t- the user called nested bordered settings elements an anti-pattern -> avoid double-boxed sections; retain one clear boundary around actionable rows. [Task 1]\n  2964\t- when the user requested “toggle all of them at once,” then only desired providers, including custom providers -> provide bulk hide/show plus individual controls over the complete loaded provider set. [Task 1]\n  2965\t- when the user asked for “better search visuals” and “copy diagnostic failures in settings” -> expose scannable sources with progressive disclosure and individual/failures-only copy with a selectable fallback. [Task 2]\n  2966\t- when the user said “push to prod” -> deploy the scoped current changes while preserving unrelated dirty work; do not commit or delete the whole dirty checkout. [Task 3]\n  2967\t\n  2968\t## Reusable knowledge\n  2969\t\n  2970\t- In `SettingsDialog.tsx`, Panda CSS hides tab labels below `md` and shows them at `md`; preserve accessible names with `aria-label` and `title`. Remove a surrounding Storybook border when bordered rows already provide the actionable surface. Run `bun run typecheck` from `web/`, not the repository root. [Task 1]\n  2971\t- `setProvidersVisibility(providers, hidden)` in `web/src/keating/model-prefs.ts` supports bulk persistence while retaining unrelated entries; derive the deduplicated list from built-ins plus asynchronously loaded `customProviders` in `ProvidersModelsTab.tsx`. [Task 1]\n  2972\t- Codex native search sends `{ type: \"web_search\", external_web_access: true }`. Preserve URL citations from `response.output_item.done` in `web/src/keating/search/codex-search-fetch.ts`, because the SDK drops URL annotations; zstd-decompress SDK request bodies before JSON assertions. [Task 2]\n  2973\t- Explicitly declare every imported dependency: the local `node_modules` masked undeclared `pdfjs-dist`, while Railway failed until `pdfjs-dist@5.4.394` was added and locked. The corrected filtered-snapshot deployment reached `SUCCESS` and `/` healthcheck succeeded. [Task 2][Task 3]\n  2974\t\n  2975\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  2976\t\n  2977\t- Root `bun run typecheck` fails because there is no root script; use `/home/diogenes/Projects/keating/web`. Vet was unavailable without Anthropic credentials, so leave it unverified. [Task 1]\n  2978\t- Do not infer a clean production dependency graph from local builds with preexisting modules. Simulate a clean install/build before upload, then poll Railway to terminal `SUCCESS` and inspect healthcheck output. [Task 2][Task 3]\n  2979\t\n  2980\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/notorganic-provider authorization UI and Railway gateway custom-domain routing\n  2981\t\n  2982\tscope: Repair and prove the Not Organic OAuth/authorization path across Keating client, portal styling, and the public gateway; distinguish client or container health from a working public token exchange.\n  2983\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/notorganic-provider and /home/diogenes/Projects/keating; reuse_rule=recheck Railway authentication, domain attachment, DNS/TLS, exact CORS allowlist, and a fresh browser/token exchange before enabling sign-in or billing.\n  2984\t\n  2985\t## Task 1: Make Keating OAuth callback handling idempotent and Firefox-safe\n  2986\t\n  2987\t### rollout_summary_files\n  2988\t\n  2989\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/08/rollout-2026-09-08T01-03-11-01a07f66-1500-77f2-99d3-21882a4658b9.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-08T11:46:55+00:00, thread_id=01a07f66-1500-77f2-99d3-21882a4658b9, partial; client checks passed, live sign-in blocked)\n  2990\t\n  2991\t### keywords\n  2992\t\n  2993\t- OAuth, PKCE, public-client.ts, sessionStorage, NotOrganicCallback, globalThis.fetch.bind(globalThis), Firefox, receipt, exchange map, CORS\n  2994\t\n  2995\t## Task 2: Apply and prove the portal authorization styling\n  2996\t\n  2997\t### rollout_summary_files\n  2998\t\n  2999\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/08/rollout-2026-09-08T07-47-21-01a080d8-1ab0-79f0-a1af-6170040588bf.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-08T21:43:08+00:00, thread_id=01a080d8-1ab0-79f0-a1af-6170040588bf, partial; stylesheet deployed and HTTP-verified)\n  3000\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/08/rollout-2026-09-08T01-03-11-01a07f66-1500-77f2-99d3-21882a4658b9.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-08T11:46:55+00:00, thread_id=01a07f66-1500-77f2-99d3-21882a4658b9, partial; original patch was prepared only)\n  3001\t\n  3002\t### keywords\n  3003\t\n  3004\t- authorization-page.ts, authorization.css, CSP, escaped dynamic values, exact POST transaction, id.notorganic.info, authorizationStyles\n  3005\t\n  3006\t## Task 3: Diagnose the `api.notorganic.info` public-routing failure\n  3007\t\n  3008\t### rollout_summary_files\n  3009\t\n  3010\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/08/rollout-2026-09-08T07-47-21-01a080d8-1ab0-79f0-a1af-6170040588bf.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-08T21:43:08+00:00, thread_id=01a080d8-1ab0-79f0-a1af-6170040588bf, partial; generated hostname healthy, custom domain still 404)\n  3011\t\n  3012\t### keywords\n  3013\t\n  3014\t- api.notorganic.info, gateway-production-8930.up.railway.app, Application not found, /healthz, /v1/public/token, CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGINS, Railway custom domain, gateway service\n  3015\t\n  3016\t## User preferences\n  3017\t\n  3018\t- when the user supplied successive browser errors, they expected the integration to be traced and fixed end-to-end, not merely explained. [Task 1]\n  3019\t- when the authorization page was “once again unstyled” -> deploy and verify the live stylesheet, not just a local patch. [Task 2]\n  3020\t- after a claimed success still produced CORS/404, the user established that signup is working only after a real browser/token exchange succeeds. [Task 3]\n  3021\t\n  3022\t## Reusable knowledge\n  3023\t\n  3024\t- Preserve pending callback state until validation/token exchange succeeds. Validate issuer, client ID, redirect URI, state, verifier, expiry, and cancellation; make exchange idempotent per transaction and share concurrent exchanges. Store a default fetcher as `globalThis.fetch.bind(globalThis)` to avoid Firefox’s `'fetch' called on an object that does not implement interface Window.'` [Task 1]\n  3025\t- Provider consent UI must escape dynamic values, preserve the exact approve/deny POST transaction, use external `/authorization.css` under `style-src 'self'`, and have tests. Public `https://id.notorganic.info/authorization.css` returned 200 and matched local `authorizationStyles`; that proves styling, not signup. [Task 2]\n  3026\t- The gateway itself was healthy internally and through generated Railway hostname `gateway-production-8930.up.railway.app`, but `api.notorganic.info` returned Railway fallback `404 Application not found`; isolate this as custom-domain edge attachment/routing rather than browser CORS or container failure. [Task 3]\n  3027\t\n  3028\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  3029\t\n  3030\t- Passing client tests, local portal checks, internal health, valid DNS/TLS, and stylesheet deployment do not prove public signup. Re-authenticate Railway, inspect gateway custom-domain attachment/service deployment, restore routing, then verify `/healthz`, `/v1/public/token`, and CORS from `https://keating.help` in a fresh browser. [Task 1][Task 2][Task 3]\n  3031\t- A patch in `/tmp` is not an applied provider change; open the provider repository as an authorized workspace, apply it, run its tests/build, deploy, and prove the public asset. [Task 2]\n  3032\t\n  3033\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Documents/Codex/2026-09-07/realtime-voice-chat Keating learner-activity brief and static benchmark clarification\n  3034\t\n  3035\tscope: Route conceptual learner-activity/product discussion separately from implementation and from the static benchmark; use the linked worktree handbook for the actual shared-contract implementation.\n  3036\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Documents/Codex/2026-09-07/realtime-voice-chat; reuse_rule=the preferences/design distinction generalize to Keating, but implementation facts belong to the cited worktree and benchmark files were not inspected here.\n  3037\t\n  3038\t## Task 1: Specify the complete learner-activity set and game-shell boundary\n  3039\t\n  3040\t### rollout_summary_files\n  3041\t\n  3042\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Documents/Codex/2026-09-07/realtime-voice-chat, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/07/rollout-2026-09-07T15-33-18-01a07d5c-56f8-7333-a1bf-8ae4c7d898ff.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-24T07:04:04+00:00, thread_id=01a07d5c-56f8-7333-a1bf-8ae4c7d898ff, partial; implementation was resumed in another worktree)\n  3043\t\n  3044\t### keywords\n  3045\t\n  3046\t- transition learning, Representation Transfer, Spot & Repair, Build Assemble, Predict Next State, game shell, streamed OpenUI payload, learner-contracts, shared-renderer.tsx\n  3047\t\n  3048\t## Task 2: Keep static benchmark integration separate from games and components\n  3049\t\n  3050\t### rollout_summary_files\n  3051\t\n  3052\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Documents/Codex/2026-09-07/realtime-voice-chat, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/07/rollout-2026-09-07T15-33-18-01a07d5c-56f8-7333-a1bf-8ae4c7d898ff.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-24T07:04:04+00:00, thread_id=01a07d5c-56f8-7333-a1bf-8ae4c7d898ff, uncertain; no benchmark files changed)\n  3053\t\n  3054\t### keywords\n  3055\t\n  3056\t- static benchmark, benchmark page, benchmark-real.ts, shared/pedagogy, docs/study.typ, test/traces, final_dataset.json, keating.help\n  3057\t\n  3058\t## User preferences\n  3059\t\n  3060\t- “transition learning” includes equation→code, French→English, and program→mathematics -> treat representation transformation as its own activity family. [Task 1]\n  3061\t- “find the mistake,” “find the difference,” and finding N issues, optionally timed -> support diagnosis, multi-error selection, repair/explanation, and timers that are not speed-only. [Task 1]\n  3062\t- after additional activity ideas, “Let’s make all those” -> implement the complete agreed set rather than only the top few. [Task 1]\n  3063\t- “No, I'm talking about ... the static benchmark” -> acknowledge topic shifts and keep benchmark work distinct from game mechanics/component monitoring. [Task 2]\n  3064\t\n  3065\t## Reusable knowledge\n  3066\t\n  3067\t- Architect reusable game shells for movement, pacing, feedback, and score separately from bounded streamed OpenUI round payloads. The implementation guide is `/home/diogenes/.codex/worktrees/36ab/keating/docs/learner-activities.md`; consult the shared-worktree learner-activities task group for tested contract details. [Task 1]\n  3068\t- The static benchmark is a running view of system evolution/improvement, conceptually distinct from visual game shells; inspect the existing benchmark page and define presentation/integration before altering it. No benchmark-page files were verified in this rollout. [Task 2]\n  3069\t\n  3070\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  3071\t\n  3072\t- Initial delegation stalled without readable coordinator state. The successful fallback was `mcp__codex_app__send_message_to_thread` / `wait_threads` with thread `01a07d66-6098-7180-97a0-f2382279d2da`; dynamic app tools were unavailable. [Task 1]\n  3073\t- Do not claim full implementation verification: focused 318-test/build/typecheck/Storybook evidence was reported, but browser/native interaction remained unverified and broad unrelated failures were reported. [Task 1]\n  3074\t\n  3075\t# Task Group: cross-repository agent-context cleanup audit and private Sites report\n  3076\t\n  3077\tscope: Audit instruction/context cleanup with measured evidence, identify repeatable automation candidates, and publish a verified private visual report.\n  3078\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating with evidence across multiple repositories; reuse_rule=recompute aggregate counts and deployment state for a new audit; reported file-word reduction is not direct token-savings measurement.\n  3079\t\n  3080\t## Task 1: Measure cleanup and publish “Headroom — context cleanup”\n  3081\t\n  3082\t### rollout_summary_files\n  3083\t\n  3084\t- rollout_summaries/2026-09-08T03-25-44-ctrB-keating_settings_cleanup_and_context_report_site.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/07/rollout-2026-09-07T23-25-44-01a07f0c-dd35-75f0-b5c3-9ce89342b033.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-08T05:01:02+00:00, thread_id=01a07f0c-dd35-75f0-b5c3-9ce89342b033, success; private deployment succeeded)\n  3085\t\n  3086\t### keywords\n  3087\t\n  3088\t- Headroom, context cleanup, Graft, GitNexus, analyze --index-only, package-site.sh, context-cleanup-ledger, verify-site.ts, 73,638, 16,053\n  3089\t\n  3090\t## User preferences\n  3091\t\n  3092\t- when the user asked to “create a site visualizing the clean up” -> make the primary report immediately usable and interactive, distinguish verified measurements from possible future savings, and avoid a marketing-landing substitute. [Task 1]\n  3093\t\n  3094\t## Reusable knowledge\n  3095\t\n  3096\t- The applied manifest measured 50 files in 30 repositories, 73,638 words before and 16,053 after (78.2% aggregate file-word reduction). Browser verification/capture was the strongest measured repeat-work candidate: 19 reviewed snippets across 4 sessions/3 repositories, about 19,653 command-input characters. [Task 1]\n  3097\t- Use GitNexus `analyze --index-only` to avoid AGENTS/CLAUDE/skill injection and Graft structural builds without deep summaries for low-risk trials. The existing browser-verification harness is `/home/diogenes/Projects/dio.computer/scripts/verify-site.ts`. [Task 1]\n  3098\t- For Sites: validate local HTTP 200 plus production build/typecheck, initialize site-local Git, package through `package-site.sh`, save a version, deploy privately, and poll until `status: succeeded`. The report deployed to `https://context-cleanup-ledger.diothedebugger.chatgpt.site`. [Task 1]\n  3099\t\n  3100\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  3101\t\n  3102\t- Mixed Guix/Nix compiler/linker/glibc paths caused native Graft/GitNexus parser failures; isolate system compiler/linker paths or use a clean container. [Task 1]\n  3103\t- Do not submit multiple `apply_patch` operations against the same file in one patch; replace content separately, then apply CSS/layout updates. [Task 1]\n  3104\t\n  3105\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/.codex/worktrees/36ab/keating shared OpenUI learner activities\n  3106\t\n  3107\tscope: Implement or audit the canonical 12-kind learner-activity contract across OpenUI source compilation, web, mobile, TUI, durable review evidence, Storybook, and generated NodePod artifacts.\n  3108\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/.codex/worktrees/36ab/keating; reuse_rule=reuse the cross-surface contract and failure shields in another Keating checkout only after reconciling its current branch/worktree and generated files; focused verification does not prove browser, native-device, live-provider, or clean-install behavior.\n  3109\t\n  3110\t## Task 1: Shared activity contracts and OpenUI source mappings\n  3111\t\n  3112\t### rollout_summary_files\n  3113\t\n  3114\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/.codex/worktrees/36ab/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/07/rollout-2026-09-07T15-44-16-01a07d66-6098-7180-97a0-f2382279d2da.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-24T07:04:40+00:00, thread_id=01a07d66-6098-7180-97a0-f2382279d2da, success; 12 canonical activity kinds and fixture pack 6)\n  3115\t\n  3116\t### keywords\n  3117\t\n  3118\t- UiActivityNode, UiActivityResponse, submit-activity, activityResponseIsComplete, formatActivityResponse, learner-contracts, openui-source.ts, compare-defend, fixture pack 6\n  3119\t\n  3120\t## Task 2: Tactile accessible web, mobile, and TUI activity controls\n  3121\t\n  3122\t### rollout_summary_files\n  3123\t\n  3124\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/.codex/worktrees/36ab/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/07/rollout-2026-09-07T15-44-16-01a07d66-6098-7180-97a0-f2382279d2da.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-24T07:04:40+00:00, thread_id=01a07d66-6098-7180-97a0-f2382279d2da, success; focused suites and Storybook passed)\n  3125\t\n  3126\t### keywords\n  3127\t\n  3128\t- ActivityRenderer.tsx, activity.css, ActivityLearner.stories.tsx, mobile/src/components/Activity.tsx, activity-input.ts, 21 activity stories, paused timer, not scored\n  3129\t\n  3130\t## Task 3: Durable ungraded evidence, review presentation, and generated artifacts\n  3131\t\n  3132\t### rollout_summary_files\n  3133\t\n  3134\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/.codex/worktrees/36ab/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/07/rollout-2026-09-07T15-44-16-01a07d66-6098-7180-97a0-f2382279d2da.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-24T07:04:40+00:00, thread_id=01a07d66-6098-7180-97a0-f2382279d2da, success; deterministic NodePod generation and focused checks passed)\n  3135\t\n  3136\t### keywords\n  3137\t\n  3138\t- shared-actions.ts, IndexedDB, learner-response.ts, durable receipts, pending/ungraded, OpenUIPreview, nodepod-boot-files.ts, generate-nodepod-boot-files.ts, learner-activities.md\n  3139\t\n  3140\t## User preferences\n  3141\t\n  3142\t- when implementing learner activities, the brief required “canonical shared OpenUI path and shared learner-contracts, not web-only or legacy rendering” -> extend the shared contract and every consuming surface rather than create parallel UI concepts. [Task 1]\n  3143\t- the brief required timers to be optional and “never speed-only scoring” -> preserve elapsed time as descriptive evidence only; never use it for scoring, deadlines, or auto-submit. [Task 1][Task 2]\n  3144\t- the brief explicitly requested activities to be “tactile and accessible” and sensible Storybook states -> include keyboard/native controls, focus states, readable labels, narrow layouts, submitted/retry states, and inspectable stories rather than static rendering alone. [Task 2]\n  3145\t- preserve pre-existing dirty work; inspect status first and do not revert unrelated changes. Do not commit, tag, release, or deploy when the delegated implementation brief excludes them. [Task 2][Task 3]\n  3146\t- completion is not correctness or mastery -> reviews should say “judgement required,” accept defensible alternatives, and never expose transport JSON as learner-facing prose. [Task 3]\n  3147\t\n  3148\t## Reusable knowledge\n  3149\t\n  3150\t- `packages/learner-contracts/src/activity.ts` defines all 12 canonical kinds, structured responses, labels, positional fields, bounded validation, `activityResponseIsComplete`, and `formatActivityResponse`. `openui-source.ts` registers positional field order `id,title,prompt,context,items,options,targets,issueCount,requireReason,timeLimit,responseLabel`. [Task 1]\n  3151\t- Reject fresh `submit-activity` when its target node already has a response, while separately allowing durable receipt replay. `compare-defend` needs exactly two options, a selected alternative, and a reason; best explanation needs a reason; apply-in-context needs one method plus written application; build/order need a full permutation; classification is many-to-one and matching one-to-one. [Task 1]\n  3152\t- Surface implementation anchors are `web/src/keating/openui/ActivityRenderer.tsx`, `activity.css`, `library.tsx`, `ActivityLearner.stories.tsx`; `mobile/src/components/Activity.tsx`, `activity-state.ts`, `UiDocumentRenderer.tsx`, `ui-action-mutations.ts`; and `src/tui/ui/activity-input.ts`, `host-controller.ts`, `render.ts`, `rpc-action-transport.ts`. Timers can pause or disable, remain usable after expiration, and display elapsed time as not scored. [Task 2]\n  3153\t- Persist readable, ungraded activity evidence atomically in IndexedDB with action receipts through `shared-actions.ts`, `storage.ts`, and `learner-response.ts`; render activity nodes as inert preview chips in comparison/review. Individual activity text is bounded to 16,384 characters, while formatted portable question-check evidence allows `MAX_QUESTION_ANSWER_LENGTH = 524_288`. Regenerate `web/src/keating/nodepod-boot-files.ts` with `bun scripts/generate-nodepod-boot-files.ts`. [Task 3]\n  3154\t- Recorded focused evidence: shared contracts 91 pass, web 127 pass, mobile 47 pass, TUI 53 pass (318 total); Storybook static build, root build/typecheck, mobile/shared typechecks, deterministic NodePod generation, and `git diff --check` passed. [Task 1][Task 2][Task 3]\n  3155\t\n  3156\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  3157\t\n  3158\t- Answered documents initially accepted a second fresh submission -> reject a new submission against an existing response but retain idempotent receipt replay. New components initially missed web parity -> register each in the live web library and update parity fixtures together. [Task 1]\n  3159\t- TUI drafts keyed by document revision orphaned sibling activity drafts after a submission -> key by document ID plus node definition excluding the response. Mobile evidence exceeded the old question-check limit -> bound input fields separately from the persisted formatted-evidence capacity. [Task 2]\n  3160\t- Playwriter was disconnected, so browser click-through and native-device interaction are unverified. Vet was unavailable through DNS/credentials; production web build hit existing Flue `Error: spawnSync bun EPERM`; Devenv could not create `/run/user/1000/devenv-*` on the read-only filesystem. Record these as environment boundaries, not activity regressions, and keep focused results distinct from unrelated broad-suite failures. [Task 2][Task 3]\n  3161\t\n  3162\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/keating Learning to Teach report, benchmark audit, and account-owned continual-learning boundary\n  3163\t\n  3164\tscope: Improve and publish the Learning to Teach report with explainable trajectory evidence, audited public data, and an honest boundary between a proposed account-owned Tinker pilot and executed training/serving.\n  3165\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating; reuse_rule=report files and packaging workflow are reusable after rechecking current benchmark inputs and Railway state; Tinker/Not Organic integration remains an unverified feasibility direction until an authorized account, spend cap, and end-to-end run exist.\n  3166\t\n  3167\t## Task 1: Explain learner profiles and trajectories; produce a substantive report conclusion\n  3168\t\n  3169\t### rollout_summary_files\n  3170\t\n  3171\t- rollout_summaries/2026-09-07T00-00-16-dkxb-keating_learning_to_teach_report_tinker_and_railway_deployme.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/06/rollout-2026-09-06T20-00-16-01a0792a-645e-7ac0-9052-ab9fa401b691.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-07T13:39:27+00:00, thread_id=01a0792a-645e-7ac0-9052-ab9fa401b691, success; user will conduct visual review on Railway)\n  3172\t\n  3173\t### keywords\n  3174\t\n  3175\t- Learning to Teach, learner-memory.json, benchmark-trajectories.js, loadV3Data, memoryFacts, memoryChanges, trajectory walkthrough, conclusion, reduced-motion\n  3176\t\n  3177\t## Task 2: Package audited benchmark data, deploy report to Railway, and verify public assets\n  3178\t\n  3179\t### rollout_summary_files\n  3180\t\n  3181\t- rollout_summaries/2026-09-07T00-00-16-dkxb-keating_learning_to_teach_report_tinker_and_railway_deployme.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/06/rollout-2026-09-06T20-00-16-01a0792a-645e-7ac0-9052-ab9fa401b691.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-07T13:39:27+00:00, thread_id=01a0792a-645e-7ac0-9052-ab9fa401b691, success; deployment b868eb5b-8c40-434a-b7bd-2f583a928eb8)\n  3182\t\n  3183\t### keywords\n  3184\t\n  3185\t- benchmark-v3, package.py, railway-report-v17, snapshot.json, /healthz, deployment-verification.json, 184 attempts, 14 public assets, BUILDING, SUCCESS\n  3186\t\n  3187\t## Task 3: Assess account-owned Tinker continual learning and serving feasibility\n  3188\t\n  3189\t### rollout_summary_files\n  3190\t\n  3191\t- rollout_summaries/2026-09-07T00-00-16-dkxb-keating_learning_to_teach_report_tinker_and_railway_deployme.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/06/rollout-2026-09-06T20-00-16-01a0792a-645e-7ac0-9052-ab9fa401b691.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-07T13:39:27+00:00, thread_id=01a0792a-645e-7ac0-9052-ab9fa401b691, partial; architecture assessed, no end-to-end run)\n  3192\t\n  3193\t### keywords\n  3194\t\n  3195\t- Tinker, SDFT, SDPO, sampler checkpoint, training-state checkpoint, account evolution, active revision, Unsloth LoRA SFT, adapter serving, spend cap\n  3196\t\n  3197\t## User preferences\n  3198\t\n  3199\t- when a report “assumes you know what the learner's profile is,” the user requested “a visual of a long trajectory,” then a “better visual of the json” and “better transitions” -> explain unfamiliar structured data through concrete facts, evidence, source, confidence, provenance, and changes over time, not raw JSON or disconnected charts. [Task 1]\n  3200\t- when the conclusion was too short, the user said “conclusion could be way more detailed disappointed” -> substantial reports need evidence-backed synthesis, limitations, next experiment, and what success means before being called complete. [Task 1]\n  3201\t- when reviewing deployment, the user said “don’t check browser i will just update railway” and “push the latest to railway and i will check that my self” -> do not reopen a browser; leave visual review to the user and verify the deployment technically over HTTP. [Task 1][Task 2]\n  3202\t- for continual learning, the user asked for a Keating-created user and case-study data -> favor a real account-owned pilot over abstract architecture, while explicitly requesting/confirming account identity and spend authority before running it. [Task 3]\n  3203\t\n  3204\t## Reusable knowledge\n  3205\t\n  3206\t- `benchmark-trajectories.js` provides `loadV3Data`, `memoryFacts`, `memoryChanges`, `messageText`, interactive step navigation, profile-memory change labels, full-source disclosures, keyboard navigation, and reduced-motion handling. The v3.2 example separates benchmark starting context from facts learned during the run, preserving evidence, `explicit`/`observed` source, confidence semantics, and provenance. [Task 1]\n  3207\t- The report conclusion should cover training effects, benchmark revisions, harness failures, result limitations, a proposed next experiment, and human learning/retention requirements. [Task 1]\n  3208\t- Final benchmark audit: 184 attempts, 183 completed, 1 call-limit failure, 154 scored, 29 output-limited; all 184 hashes verified and runtime attestations unchanged. The 1,021 receipt-bound native calls have an uncached estimate of `$4.89493897`; unknown cache usage means that view is not an invoice. Do not aggregate semantic scores for output-limited episodes. [Task 2]\n  3209\t- Package only through `uv run --project scripts/training --locked --no-sync python scripts/report-site/package.py --output-dir .keating/outputs/railway-report-v17`; deploy the package with Railway `--path-as-root --no-gitignore --detach --json`. Verify every public asset hash against `snapshot.json`, `/healthz` is `200 ok`, and a missing JSON path returns 404. [Task 2]\n  3210\t- Keating has canonical/provenance-rich training exports and an Unsloth LoRA SFT starter, but no integrated Tinker trainer, SDPO loop, or per-user adapter-serving path. Not Organic supplies account-scoped evolution metadata, authorization, artifact/result attestation, and atomic active revisions, not a verified authorized-Tinker-checkpoint connection. Tinker's continual-learning recipe is SDFT, not SDPO; it distinguishes sampler checkpoints from resumable training state. [Task 3]\n  3211\t\n  3212\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  3213\t\n  3214\t- The initial conclusion was rejected as too brief; expand the synthesis before claiming completion. Once the user says they will inspect Railway, browser inspection is unnecessary and should not be substituted for HTTP/hash deployment verification. [Task 1][Task 2]\n  3215\t- `python -m unittest scripts/report-site/test_export_benchmark_v3.py` failed from the wrong import path. Use `python -m unittest discover -s scripts/report-site -p test_export_benchmark_v3.py`. Wait through Railway `BUILDING`/`DEPLOYING` until `SUCCESS` before reporting deployment complete. [Task 2]\n  3216\t- No end-to-end Tinker run occurred because no account/DID or spend cap was supplied and local Tinker modules were absent. Do not describe SFT/DPO/KTO/GRPO exports as executed training, or checkpoint metadata as serving integration; keep provider credentials and model bytes server-side. [Task 3]\n  3217\t\n  3218\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/notorganic-provider first-party PDS signup, ATProto identity, and Resend DNS\n  3219\t\n  3220\tscope: Operate Not Organic's own ATProto PDS signup path, retain the current did:plc decision, and provision Resend DNS without overstating live account/email readiness.\n  3221\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/notorganic-provider; reuse_rule=recheck Railway domain/TLS, Resend domain verification/SMTP, PDS configuration, and live signup in a fresh browser before calling this production-complete.\n  3222\t\n  3223\t## Task 1: Direct Not Organic PDS account signup and deployment\n  3224\t\n  3225\t### rollout_summary_files\n  3226\t\n  3227\t- rollout_summaries/2026-09-06T20-20-28-hyl9-notorganic_pds_signup_webvh_resend_dns.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/notorganic-provider, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/06/rollout-2026-09-06T16-20-28-01a07861-27f5-7df1-ab23-4e06ec4986df.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-06T22:23:21+00:00, thread_id=01a07861-27f5-7df1-ab23-4e06ec4986df, partial; deployment/internal PDS checks passed, public signup remains unproven)\n  3228\t\n  3229\t### keywords\n  3230\t\n  3231\t- ATProto, PDS, OAuth, prompt=create, /api/auth/signup, pds.notorganic.info, PDS_INVITE_REQUIRED, Railway, Litestream, notorganic-pds, SMTP, TLS\n  3232\t\n  3233\t## Task 2: WebVH architecture assessment, retain did:plc\n  3234\t\n  3235\t### rollout_summary_files\n  3236\t\n  3237\t- rollout_summaries/2026-09-06T20-20-28-hyl9-notorganic_pds_signup_webvh_resend_dns.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/notorganic-provider, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/06/rollout-2026-09-06T16-20-28-01a07861-27f5-7df1-ab23-4e06ec4986df.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-06T22:23:21+00:00, thread_id=01a07861-27f5-7df1-ab23-4e06ec4986df, success; documented assessment, no migration)\n  3238\t\n  3239\t### keywords\n  3240\t\n  3241\t- WebVH, did:plc, PLC directory, docs/webvh-assessment.md, verifiable history, witnesses, portability, ATProto compatibility\n  3242\t\n  3243\t## Task 3: Provision Resend DNS records at Porkbun\n  3244\t\n  3245\t### rollout_summary_files\n  3246\t\n  3247\t- rollout_summaries/2026-09-06T20-20-28-hyl9-notorganic_pds_signup_webvh_resend_dns.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/notorganic-provider, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/06/rollout-2026-09-06T16-20-28-01a07861-27f5-7df1-ab23-4e06ec4986df.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-06T22:23:21+00:00, thread_id=01a07861-27f5-7df1-ab23-4e06ec4986df, success; records re-read and unrelated records preserved)\n  3248\t\n  3249\t### keywords\n  3250\t\n  3251\t- Resend, Porkbun, Sesame, resend._domainkey, rsend.forge.rmta.net, send.forge.rmta.net, _dmarc, smtp.resend.com, port 465\n  3252\t\n  3253\t## Task 4: Patch and deploy same-site PDS OAuth authorization\n  3254\t\n  3255\t### rollout_summary_files\n  3256\t\n  3257\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/notorganic-provider, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/20/rollout-2026-09-20T13-54-17-01a0bff4-5931-7fe2-8285-537770cb3f69.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-20T18:56:35+00:00, thread_id=01a0bff4-5931-7fe2-8285-537770cb3f69, success; exact header regression fixed/deployed, full browser lifecycle open)\n  3258\t\n  3259\t### keywords\n  3260\t\n  3261\t- Sec-Fetch-Site, same-site, atproto-5147, patch-oauth-same-site.mjs, check-oauth-same-site.mjs, Dockerfile.pds, Forbidden sec-fetch-site header, 907d0552-a6df-4043-9df3-4227546431e3\n  3262\t\n  3263\t## User preferences\n  3264\t\n  3265\t- when discussing identity/signup, the user said Not Organic “should have its own pds” and people “should be able to create an account that way without going through bsky” -> implement and verify first-party PDS signup rather than redirecting account creation through Bluesky. [Task 1]\n  3266\t- when WebVH was raised, the user corrected that “removing reliance on plc directory is not a central requirement at all” and asked to “note webvh down sides and advantages somewhere” -> retain `did:plc` unless a concrete need changes; document tradeoffs rather than proposing a migration. [Task 2]\n  3267\t- when the user said “please just add these you have the ability” and specified “resend should be used for smtp” -> with authorization and working integrations, apply the DNS records directly, verify them, and preserve the provider decision. [Task 3]\n  3268\t- after confirming scope, the user said “deploy”; when they later asked whether it was “a mock tested,” -> confirm production scope first and clearly distinguish local/container checks from real production HTTP and unverified browser proof. [Task 4]\n  3269\t\n  3270\t## Reusable knowledge\n  3271\t\n  3272\t- `/api/auth/signup` uses an operator-configured HTTPS PDS origin and `oauth.authorize(pdsUrl.origin, { scope: \"atproto\", prompt: \"create\" })`; do not accept browser-supplied PDS or DID values. Defaults were `PDS_HOSTNAME=pds.notorganic.info`, `PDS_SERVICE_HANDLE_DOMAINS=.pds.notorganic.info`, and `PDS_INVITE_REQUIRED=false`. [Task 1]\n  3273\t- PDS/portal/landing deployments succeeded; internal PDS checks returned health 200, version `0.4.219`, `inviteCodeRequired:false`, hosted handle domain, and OAuth metadata. The private Railway bucket `notorganic-pds` passed empty-object PUT/GET/DELETE `200/200/204`; Litestream uploaded an initial SQLite snapshot. [Task 1]\n  3274\t- `docs/webvh-assessment.md` records verifiable history, key rotation, optional witnesses, portability, hosting model, ATProto incompatibility, DID-string changes on portability, operational overhead, and lack of account/recovery semantics. Current decision: retain `did:plc`; reconsider only for a concrete organizational/service identity need or future ecosystem support. [Task 2]\n  3275\t- For Porkbun via Sesame, list records at exact target names, detect conflicts, apply only intended changes, then re-list and compare while preserving existing IDs. The verified TTL-600 records were TXT `resend._domainkey`, CNAME `rsend` -> `rsend.forge.rmta.net`, CNAME `send` -> `send.forge.rmta.net`, and TXT `_dmarc` -> `v=DMARC1; p=none;`. Resend SMTP is `smtp.resend.com`, port 465 implicit TLS, username `resend`, API key as password, after sending-domain verification. [Task 3]\n  3276\t- Live PDS `0.4.219` rejected `Sec-Fetch-Site: same-site` at `/oauth/authorize`. `infra/pds/patch-oauth-same-site.mjs`, wired by `infra/docker/Dockerfile.pds`, asserts OAuth provider version/source shape and narrowly backports atproto PR #5147. The local original image fails the same-site test; patched container passed nine checks, and Railway deployment retained `/pds` volume. Remove the patch when upgrading to a PDS release containing the upstream fix. [Task 4]\n  3277\t\n  3278\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  3279\t\n  3280\t- Passing focused tests/builds and internal PDS checks do not prove live signup: require public DNS/TLS, Resend domain verification, SMTP delivery, and a fresh-browser registration before declaring account creation complete. Railway certificates were still `ISSUING`/`VALIDATING_OWNERSHIP` and public HTTPS had certificate-name errors during this rollout. [Task 1]\n  3281\t- No Resend key was found in Skate. Do not retrieve or reuse another project's production credential without explicit cross-project authorization. [Task 1]\n  3282\t- DNS record success does not prove Resend domain verification or SMTP delivery. CNAMEs cannot coexist with other records at the same name, so abort on conflicts rather than overwriting them. [Task 3]\n  3283\t- Browser `fetch` overwrites `Sec-Fetch-Mode` as `cors`; use raw Node HTTP to reproduce navigation Fetch Metadata headers. Health/header/invalid-case checks and fresh signup authorization-page load prove the narrow same-site fix, not consent, email verification, cookies, callback/PKCE, token exchange, or an authenticated app session. [Task 4]\n  3284\t\n  3285\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/keating product-promise and educational-efficacy assessment\n  3286\tscope: Conduct candid, outcome-oriented assessment of Keating against its hyperteacher promise without mistaking implementation breadth, dirty work, or deterministic benchmarks for validated learner outcomes.\n  3287\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating; reuse_rule=re-read current PRODUCT.md, SYSTEM.md, study limitations, worktree state, and complete browser/test evidence before issuing any rating; this assessment was not completed.\n  3288\t\n  3289\t## Task 1: Rate Keating against its product promise, incomplete\n  3290\t\n  3291\t### rollout_summary_files\n  3292\t\n  3293\t- rollout_summaries/2026-09-06T10-49-02-OJTS-keating_application_goal_assessment_incomplete.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/06/rollout-2026-09-06T06-49-02-01a07655-ffbe-75a0-80e8-b2f9f2ec7edc.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-07T00:30:16+00:00, thread_id=01a07655-ffbe-75a0-80e8-b2f9f2ec7edc, partial; no final rating or synthesized conclusion)\n  3294\t\n  3295\t### keywords\n  3296\t\n  3297\t- Keating, PRODUCT.md, SYSTEM.md, hyperteacher, cognitive empowerment, educational efficacy, human participants, benchmark, Playwriter, unable to open database file\n  3298\t\n  3299\t## User preferences\n  3300\t\n  3301\t- when asking to “rate how good this current application is at accomplishing its goals and promise,” the user seeks a candid, outcome-oriented assessment rather than a feature inventory or purely aesthetic review. [Task 1]\n  3302\t\n  3303\t## Reusable knowledge\n  3304\t\n  3305\t- `PRODUCT.md` defines Keating’s purpose as a hyperteacher that helps learners configure a model, start useful tutoring, understand changes, and trust local-first privacy and self-improvement boundaries. `SYSTEM.md` requires learner authorship through diagnosis, questioning, reconstruction, retrieval, verification, and learner-created artifacts; AI must not become a surrogate for thought. [Task 1]\n  3306\t- Separate broad implemented capability from educational efficacy. `docs/study/sections/limitations.typ` says no human participants were studied; archived learners are language models in student roles, and deterministic benchmark behavior is not evidence of human mastery, retention, engagement, transfer, or confusion. [Task 1]\n  3307\t- The assessed checkout was heavily dirty with active OpenUI, learner-response, courses, submissions, simulation, and renderer work. Distinguish committed baseline behavior from work in progress. [Task 1]\n  3308\t\n  3309\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  3310\t\n  3311\t- This rollout never reached a final rating, strengths/gaps synthesis, or complete test conclusion. Treat it as incomplete evidence; restart from the stated product criteria and finish the evidence table before giving a score. [Task 1]\n  3312\t- Browser learner-flow evidence was unavailable: Playwriter reported `The Playwriter Chrome extension is not connected` after CLI/temporary-directory failures. Do not imply visual validation. [Task 1]\n  3313\t- `devenv tasks run keating:test keating:test-web` was blocked by `unable to open database file` and Nix daemon `Operation not permitted`; report infrastructure blockage separately from application failure, then rerun with suitable access or narrower direct commands. [Task 1]\n  3314\t\n  3315\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/keating Bun-native v3.11.0 release publication\n  3316\t\n  3317\tscope: Release Keating with Bun-native versioning, preserve a confirmed content boundary, and distinguish publication from registry propagation.\n  3318\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating; reuse_rule=release/registry/provider/browser facts are time-specific; inspect current branch, workflow, tag, and artifacts before action.\n  3319\t\n  3320\t## Task 1: Review, publish, and verify Keating 3.11.0\n  3321\t\n  3322\t### rollout_summary_files\n  3323\t\n  3324\t- rollout_summaries/2026-09-05T09-46-39-tkNY-keating_3_11_0_release_bun_versioning.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/05/rollout-2026-09-05T05-46-39-01a070f6-84ec-78e0-af81-0b5adf3e5652.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-05T10:25:31+00:00, thread_id=01a070f6-84ec-78e0-af81-0b5adf3e5652, partial; GitHub release verified, npm processing)\n  3325\t\n  3326\t### keywords\n  3327\t\n  3328\t- bun pm version, sync-version.ts, v3.11.0, Prek, Entire wrapper, nodepod-boot-files.ts, npm provenance, 33959745612\n  3329\t\n  3330\t## User preferences\n  3331\t\n  3332\t- “yes include the uncommited changes” -> include a complete dirty worktree only after explicit scope confirmation; never silently reduce it to committed content. [Task 1]\n  3333\t- “hey instead of bumpy you should use bun pm version” -> Keating releases use Bun-native versioning, not Bumpy, unless explicitly overridden. [Task 1]\n  3334\t\n  3335\t## Reusable knowledge\n  3336\t\n  3337\t- Use `bun pm version <increment> --no-git-tag-version`, `scripts/sync-version.ts`, changelog edits/checks, explicit annotated tag and push. The Devenv task is `keating:bump-version`; regenerate generated NodePod artifacts after source-integration conflicts instead of hand-merging output. [Task 1]\n  3338\t- v3.11.0 GitHub workflow `33959745612` and four Darwin/Linux assets were verified; its downloaded Linux x64 bundle ran independently and matched published digest. [Task 1]\n  3339\t\n  3340\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  3341\t\n  3342\t- An accepted npm publish is not registry availability: v3.11.0 was still processing and registry metadata remained v3.10.2 at final check. Browser/provider/physical-device/full Vet evidence remained unavailable. [Task 1]\n  3343\t\n  3344\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/keating Flue worktree, NodePod boundary, and platform-aware downloads\n  3345\t\n  3346\tscope: Locate the isolated Flue prototype, state the exact NodePod proof boundary, or update Keating’s downloads showcase and direct release links.\n  3347\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating and sibling /home/diogenes/Projects/keating-flue-runtime; reuse_rule=worktree/branch facts require a live git-worktree check; v3.11.0 artifact availability is time-specific.\n  3348\t\n  3349\t## Task 1: Locate and assess the Flue worktree and real-NodePod proof\n  3350\t\n  3351\t### rollout_summary_files\n  3352\t\n  3353\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/06/rollout-2026-09-06T09-18-04-01a076de-6f27-7e91-994f-59f477efae8a.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-06T13:34:53+00:00, thread_id=01a076de-6f27-7e91-994f-59f477efae8a, partial proof boundary)\n  3354\t\n  3355\t### keywords\n  3356\t\n  3357\t- keating-flue-runtime, spike/flue-runtime, git worktree list, @flue/runtime, NodePod, sandbox-adapter.ts, flue-host, proof.txt\n  3358\t\n  3359\t## Task 2: Redesign Downloads with real app captures and platform-specific artifacts\n  3360\t\n  3361\t### rollout_summary_files\n  3362\t\n  3363\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/06/rollout-2026-09-06T08-03-56-01a0769a-914d-7531-b321-a4f223dd58f3.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-06T12:50:34+00:00, thread_id=01a0769a-914d-7531-b321-a4f223dd58f3, partial; test typing unresolved)\n  3364\t\n  3365\t### keywords\n  3366\t\n  3367\t- Download.tsx, detect-platform.ts, TutorialShot.tsx, react-icons, v3.11.0, darwin-arm64, linux-x64, gh api, Cache miss\n  3368\t\n  3369\t## User preferences\n  3370\t\n  3371\t- when repository evidence conflicted with their expectation, the user said “but there should be a worktree that does can you look in the dir above” -> inspect sibling worktrees/repositories before concluding a feature is absent. [Task 1]\n  3372\t- when discussing product downloads, the user asked for “actual shots of a phone with the app in a spread that makes sense” and that images be replaceable later -> use real product captures in a coherent sequence, isolate screenshot paths, and keep frame sizing stable. [Task 2]\n  3373\t- “detect the platform and give the user the file to download use icons for each platform” -> make the primary CTA platform-aware/direct when an artifact exists, retain all choices, and use real icon-library logos. [Task 2]\n  3374\t\n  3375\t## Reusable knowledge\n  3376\t\n  3377\t- Main Keating v3.11.0 has no `flue`/`@flue/*` dependency; `/home/diogenes/Projects/keating-flue-runtime` is sibling worktree `spike/flue-runtime`, an older-base prototype. `spikes/flue-host` is a real Node Flue host; `spikes/flue-browser` consumes hosted conversations but cannot run `@flue/runtime`; portable `packages/agent-runtime` intentionally does not execute turns. [Task 1]\n  3378\t- NodePod is the sandbox layer, Flue the orchestration layer. The decisive proof starts a real NodePod, runs built host with the production adapter, creates/reads `/workspace/proof.txt`, checks both reply and pod filesystem, then disposes it; add isolation, cancellation, capability, credential, restart, and provider tests. [Task 1]\n  3379\t- `web/src/lib/detect-platform.ts` is SSR-safe, uses `userAgentData` with iPadOS touch-point handling; `TutorialShot.tsx` is the replacement-friendly image-frame pattern. Verify current releases with `gh api` plus direct artifact `HEAD` rather than relying on a cached public release page. [Task 2]\n  3380\t\n  3381\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  3382\t\n  3383\t- Do not claim “Keating runs its Flue agent in NodePod”: existing normal-Node host proof plus adapter contract only support “NodePod-to-Flue adapter and working Flue host spike.” [Task 1]\n  3384\t- v3.11.0 had macOS/Linux archives only; no Windows installer, Android APK, or iOS download was verified. Fix `download-release.test.ts` fixtures (`unknown` before `Navigator`, `DetectedPlatform` expected values) and rerun tests/typecheck before claiming page completion. [Task 2]\n  3385\t\n  3386\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/keating game-like learner activities and shared OpenUI rendering\n  3387\t\n  3388\tscope: Redesign quizzes, flashcards, language/activity rounds, and their shared learner-facing renderer without breaking durable learning behavior.\n  3389\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating; reuse_rule=use for learner-activity UI work; preserve the heavily dirty worktree and separately verify live browser behavior.\n  3390\t\n  3391\t## Task 1: Flashcard and quiz minigame styling with a prominent urgency timer\n  3392\t\n  3393\t### rollout_summary_files\n  3394\t\n  3395\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/06/rollout-2026-09-06T04-37-01-01a075dd-21ab-7b10-a78d-5dfeadb38633.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-06T10:09:03+00:00, thread_id=01a075dd-21ab-7b10-a78d-5dfeadb38633, partial; deterministic/Storybook build evidence only)\n  3396\t\n  3397\t### keywords\n  3398\t\n  3399\t- FlashcardRenderer, QuizRenderer, QuizSessionPanel, FlashcardShaderField, quizTimerState, keating:quiz-shader-preset, quiz-game.test.ts, PandaCSS, reduced-motion\n  3400\t\n  3401\t## Task 2: Shared activity renderer, learner interactions, and simulation evidence boundary\n  3402\t\n  3403\t### rollout_summary_files\n  3404\t\n  3405\t- rollout_summaries/2026-09-06T09-59-01-YxOq-keating_learning_ui_session_library_redesign.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/06/rollout-2026-09-06T05-59-01-01a07628-3290-74d1-947d-9cb9c6253bda.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-06T12:33:56+00:00, thread_id=01a07628-3290-74d1-947d-9cb9c6253bda, partial; full web/root suites pass, production browser incomplete)\n  3406\t\n  3407\t### keywords\n  3408\t\n  3409\t- shared-renderer.tsx, retryableAggregateAttempt, RenderingSmoke, QuestionRenderer, LanguagePractice, ActivityRounds.stories.tsx, rendering-smoke, SimulationRenderer, simulation-chart.test.tsx\n  3410\t\n  3411\t## User preferences\n  3412\t\n  3413\t- when redesigning learner interaction, the user asked for “really good styling,” “a variety of animations,” and “preset shaders that would make it pop and be fun to play” -> use polished state feedback, purposeful motion, and selectable visual atmospheres, not merely functional styling. [Task 1]\n  3414\t- “i think the timer should be more prominent to give a sense of urgency” -> make time a primary instrument: large digits, progress rail, warning/critical states, and accessible status messaging. [Task 1]\n  3415\t- quizzes and flashcards should “feel like games,” with “less overall text,” “jolts movement,” “dynamism,” and excitement -> prefer compact, tactile, action-driven flows over form-heavy layouts. [Task 2]\n  3416\t\n  3417\t## Reusable knowledge\n  3418\t\n  3419\t- `FlashcardRenderer.tsx` already owns SRS review, flip/swipe/keyboard interaction, bookmarks, sounds, completion effects, and persistence; extend it rather than building a parallel reviewer. `useCardGestures.ts` maps left/down/right/up to Again/Hard/Good/Easy. [Task 1]\n  3420\t- `QuizSessionPanel` delegates active behavior to canonical `QuizRenderer`; do not restore separate timing/scoring logic. `quizTimerState` clamps values, warns in the final quarter (maximum 20 seconds), becomes critical at 5 seconds or less, and the shader preference key is `keating:quiz-shader-preset`. [Task 1]\n  3421\t- `web/src/keating/openui/shared-renderer.tsx` is the cross-surface activity path for question, question-group, quiz, deck, simulation, and task nodes; legacy-renderer-only changes do not reach all learner activities. Aggregate host actions should use `retryableAggregateAttempt` so failed delivery retains byte-identical retry intent. [Task 2]\n  3422\t- Open-ended answers remain pending teacher grading and must not enter settled score. `/rendering-smoke` uses isolated local journals, so it is safe for rendering smoke checks without learner-session writes. [Task 2]\n  3423\t- Final recorded deterministic evidence: targeted quiz/flashcard/open-ended tests 35/0 and Storybook build passed in Task 1; later full web suite 1284/0 and root suite 425/0 passed in Task 2. [Task 1][Task 2]\n  3424\t\n  3425\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  3426\t\n  3427\t- Passing typecheck, focused tests, or Storybook build does not establish live visual quality, timer smoothness, mobile layout, or click-through. The rollout was interrupted before final browser inspection; keep that boundary explicit. [Task 1]\n  3428\t- Large replacements can leave duplicate component code/display names; inspect boundaries with `rg` immediately after bulk edits. Use `rg` rather than malformed directory-as-file `grep`. [Task 1]\n  3429\t- Long-running Playwriter/CDP interactions timed out, and Storybook had parse/index errors in existing stories. Treat earlier focused browser checks as scoped; run a clean Storybook index/build and actual production scenario before a broad health claim. Simulation graph completion remains unverified until the delegated patch, chart tests, and rendered scenario are inspected. [Task 2]\n  3430\t\n  3431\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/keating OpenUI task contracts, review presentation, and local-first course submissions\n  3432\t\n  3433\tscope: Extend OpenUI safely across review, quiz recovery, declarative task/simulation contracts, course integration, and offline learner submission delivery.\n  3434\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating; reuse_rule=use for OpenUI/course submission changes; contract changes require cross-surface compilation, and final local-first edits require fresh verification.\n  3435\t\n  3436\t## Task 1: Inert OpenUI previews and partial/recoverable quiz presentation\n  3437\t\n  3438\t### rollout_summary_files\n  3439\t\n  3440\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/06/rollout-2026-09-06T05-41-36-01a07618-40fd-7e92-bdb6-7dfb2dd7a5aa.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-06T10:06:03+00:00, thread_id=01a07618-40fd-7e92-bdb6-7dfb2dd7a5aa, mixed success/partial; final local-first state unverified)\n  3441\t\n  3442\t### keywords\n  3443\t\n  3444\t- OpenUIPreview, parseOpenUIMessageSegments, ResponseComparisonPanel, TrajectoryCanvas, quiz-progress.ts, complete-quiz, shared-renderer.tsx, unsafe, regeneration\n  3445\t\n  3446\t## Task 2: Four task kinds, declarative simulation, and two-way course assignment integration\n  3447\t\n  3448\t### rollout_summary_files\n  3449\t\n  3450\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/06/rollout-2026-09-06T05-41-36-01a07618-40fd-7e92-bdb6-7dfb2dd7a5aa.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-06T10:06:03+00:00, thread_id=01a07618-40fd-7e92-bdb6-7dfb2dd7a5aa, partial)\n  3451\t\n  3452\t### keywords\n  3453\t\n  3454\t- task node, Assignment, Practice, Draft, Fieldwork, complete-task-item, submit-task, learner-contracts, task-assignments.ts, SaveTaskToCourse, src/tui/ui/render.ts\n  3455\t\n  3456\t## Task 3: Local-first attachments and asynchronous course submission delivery\n  3457\t\n  3458\t### rollout_summary_files\n  3459\t\n  3460\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/06/rollout-2026-09-06T05-41-36-01a07618-40fd-7e92-bdb6-7dfb2dd7a5aa.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-06T10:06:03+00:00, thread_id=01a07618-40fd-7e92-bdb6-7dfb2dd7a5aa, uncertain; no final checks)\n  3461\t\n  3462\t### keywords\n  3463\t\n  3464\t- local-store.ts, course-outbox.ts, IndexedDB, SubmissionAttachments, SubmissionDeliveryStatus, Saved on this device, Delivered to course, submission-attachments, immutable revisions\n  3465\t\n  3466\t## User preferences\n  3467\t\n  3468\t- the user selected “Inert preview + chip” -> comparison/review should preserve prose but collapse OpenUI artifacts and never wire interactive state/actions. [Task 1]\n  3469\t- for malformed components, the user wanted “partial results for quizzes and stuff to have a nicer render then just text,” auto-retry up to three attempts, and “Score + status, answers hidden” -> show structured status, cap safe regeneration, and avoid answer-key disclosure. [Task 1]\n  3470\t- the user chose Assignment, Practice set, Draft with revisions, Fieldwork/investigation, and “Both directions” -> task-to-course saving and existing-course-to-task rendering are both required. [Task 2]\n  3471\t- when the server-first design was challenged with “do you know why this can't just be local first?” -> save answer, metadata, and file blobs immediately; show “Saved on this device” separately from “Delivered to course.” [Task 3]\n  3472\t- “just get straight to implemetnation and i will verify don't even write tests for now” and “skip vet” -> for this requested OpenUI implementation mode, do not add tests or run Vet unless asked; hand off concisely and preserve the verification boundary. [Task 1][Task 3]\n  3473\t\n  3474\t## Reusable knowledge\n  3475\t\n  3476\t- Live OpenUI is unsuitable for response comparison: it can mount controls, persist state, or dispatch actions. `preview.ts`/`OpenUIPreview.tsx` parse source/JSON fences in document order; use distinct side scopes and preserve/rebase review offsets. [Task 1]\n  3477\t- `complete-quiz` can be canonical without `params.interaction`; response summaries must branch on action type. Auto-retry malformed/unsupported component failures, but never retry `unsafe` failures. [Task 1]\n  3478\t- OpenUI simulation evaluators must be declarative, bounded, deterministic, and fail closed: no arbitrary JS, calls, property access, or generated HTML execution. [Task 2]\n  3479\t- Contract additions touch learner-contracts UI/source/rendering, parity fixtures, web/mobile/TUI renderers, action mutation/storage, and generated NodePod boot files. Extend existing course authoring/submission/review infrastructure rather than parallel course concepts. [Task 2]\n  3480\t- IndexedDB in `local-store.ts` is immediate submission truth. `course-outbox.ts` queues immutable revisions with predecessor ordering, account checks, attachment upload during sync, retries, and conflict preservation; server attachment storage is sync destination only. Limits are 10 files and 25 MB each. [Task 3]\n  3481\t\n  3482\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  3483\t\n  3484\t- Parser fixtures initially had closing-fence/cursor offset and positional-argument errors: use parser output and exact mapper signatures. Contract expansion broke parity fixtures and TUI exhaustive rendering: update expected node lists and compile every consumer. [Task 1][Task 2]\n  3485\t- Final recovery and local-first changes were not typechecked/tested. Preserve the pre-existing dirty worktree, inspect `git status`, and run focused checks before calling them complete. [Task 1][Task 3]\n  3486\t\n  3487\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/keating mobile session library and session-switch performance\n  3488\t\n  3489\tscope: Design a responsive session browser with hierarchy/filtering and harden session switching without claiming speed gains that were not measured.\n  3490\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating; reuse_rule=use for session-library/mobile selector work; remeasure performance after current changes.\n  3491\t\n  3492\t## Task 1: Rebuild mobile and desktop session library with fork/category navigation\n  3493\t\n  3494\t### rollout_summary_files\n  3495\t\n  3496\t- rollout_summaries/2026-09-06T09-59-01-YxOq-keating_learning_ui_session_library_redesign.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/06/rollout-2026-09-06T05-59-01-01a07628-3290-74d1-947d-9cb9c6253bda.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-06T12:33:56+00:00, thread_id=01a07628-3290-74d1-947d-9cb9c6253bda, partial; web/root suites pass, final build blocked elsewhere)\n  3497\t\n  3498\t### keywords\n  3499\t\n  3500\t- SessionBrowser, SessionBrowserDesktop, SessionBrowserSheet, SESSION_BROWSER_BREAKPOINT, SessionCard, Select.tsx, session-switch.ts, session-library-refresh.ts, 320px, 109.4ms, 147.6ms\n  3501\t\n  3502\t## User preferences\n  3503\t\n  3504\t- the mobile session list needed redesign “from scratch,” elegantly representing sessions, forks, categories, descriptions, and future tag/category navigation -> hierarchy, metadata, filtering, and mobile ergonomics are core requirements. [Task 1]\n  3505\t\n  3506\t## Reusable knowledge\n  3507\t\n  3508\t- `SESSION_BROWSER_BREAKPOINT = 1024`: desktop uses `SessionBrowserDesktop`, mobile uses `SessionBrowserSheet`. Filters live inside the mobile dialog; shared `Select` replaces native selects and needs dialog-safe positioning, keyboard support, long-menu scrolling, and label truncation. [Task 1]\n  3509\t- `session-switch.ts` provides latest-request protection, save-before-commit sequencing, and ordered per-session writes; `session-library-refresh.ts` coalesces storage-notification bursts and only publishes the freshest read. [Task 1]\n  3510\t- Browser checks at 320px found no dropdown overflow, correct category filtering/fork tree, and focus return to trigger on Escape. [Task 1]\n  3511\t\n  3512\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  3513\t\n  3514\t- Do not say switching is faster: baseline median was 109.4ms, first post-change measure was 147.6ms, and no post-memoization comparison was captured. [Task 1]\n  3515\t- Repository-wide build remained blocked by unrelated root TypeScript nullability errors in benchmark-evolution code; distinguish that from the passing web/root test suites. [Task 1]\n  3516\t\n  3517\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/keating landing-page code review and accessibility maintenance\n  3518\t\n  3519\tscope: Diagnose and prioritize Keating landing defects in install copy, hero motion, semantic accessibility, navigation, and orphaned code/styles.\n  3520\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating; reuse_rule=review findings are checkout-specific; inspect current code and perform a browser pass before closing fixes.\n  3521\t\n  3522\t## Task 1: Review landing implementation and reproduce user-facing install failure\n  3523\t\n  3524\t### rollout_summary_files\n  3525\t\n  3526\t- rollout_summaries/2026-09-06T09-41-36-Wvsi-landing_page_code_review_findings.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/06/rollout-2026-09-06T05-41-36-01a07618-40ca-73a1-b131-11cb0c47dd56.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-06T07:51:30+00:00, thread_id=01a07618-40ca-73a1-b131-11cb0c47dd56, success; review only)\n  3527\t\n  3528\t### keywords\n  3529\t\n  3530\t- Landing.tsx, LandingWonder.tsx, TAB_COPY_TEXT, navigator.clipboard, bash: line 1: $: command not found, requestAnimationFrame, resetDepth, CrtPlaythrough, scroll-margin-top, crt-program, Panda CSS\n  3531\t\n  3532\t## Reusable knowledge\n  3533\t\n  3534\t- Landing entry is `web/src/pages/Landing.tsx`; hero interaction is `web/src/components/LandingWonder.tsx`; sticky nav is `src/components/Nav.tsx`; landing CSS is generated from `panda.config.ts`. `bun run typecheck` passed after Panda generation. [Task 1]\n  3535\t- Keep executable clipboard payload separate from formatted terminal display text. Guard missing/rejected `navigator.clipboard` and do not make analytics depend solely on a successful copy. [Task 1]\n  3536\t- `resetDepth` must cancel pending `requestAnimationFrame` before clearing CSS variables. Use a real visually-hidden alternative for hero text, headings for use-card titles, visible/touch pause-status controls for `CrtPlaythrough`, and `scroll-margin-top` for sticky-nav anchors. [Task 1]\n  3537\t- `TerminalDemo`, `TERM_LINES`, `lineSpeed`, `INSTALL_TABS[].isAgent`, and associated terminal styles were unused; `crt-program-*`, `manifesto-grid`, and `manifesto-quote` styles were orphaned. Audit before deleting because missing CRT controls may indicate an incomplete replacement. [Task 1]\n  3538\t\n  3539\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  3540\t\n  3541\t- The reproduced copied display command failed with `bash: line 1: $: command not found`; never copy decorative prompts/comments as executable shell input. [Task 1]\n  3542\t- Static review/typecheck is not interaction proof: test the CRT carousel, sticky anchors, lazy hero, clipboard fallback, and reduced-motion behavior in a browser. [Task 1]\n  3543\t\n  3544\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/interleave-app product surfaces, effects, Storybook, and Railway snapshot deployment\n  3545\t\n  3546\tscope: Marketing/product-spread work, shared UI effects, Storybook routing, and the dedicated Railway web snapshot.\n  3547\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/interleave-app; reuse_rule=inspect the dirty `feat/storybook-coverage` worktree and live Railway/trusted-origin state before reuse.\n  3548\t\n  3549\t## Task 1: Product spreads, generated About asset, and Events runtime restoration\n  3550\t\n  3551\t### rollout_summary_files\n  3552\t\n  3553\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/interleave-app, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/04/rollout-2026-09-04T20-26-19-01a06ef5-8656-7032-8e06-1f6bf398b1cf.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-05T05:07:56+00:00, thread_id=01a06ef5-8656-7032-8e06-1f6bf398b1cf, mixed partial/success)\n  3554\t\n  3555\t### keywords\n  3556\t\n  3557\t- Landing.tsx, landing.stories.tsx, WovenDashboard, storybook:build, loom-photoreal-v2.webp, eventsAtproto.ts, Convex functions ready\n  3558\t\n  3559\t## Task 2: Recover Claude interaction effects and deploy the Railway snapshot\n  3560\t\n  3561\t### rollout_summary_files\n  3562\t\n  3563\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/interleave-app, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/05/rollout-2026-09-05T05-04-26-01a070cf-df3e-7133-924c-837b7a82c9b8.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-05T10:48:04+00:00, thread_id=01a070cf-df3e-7133-924c-837b7a82c9b8, partial; deployment health verified)\n  3564\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/interleave-app, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/06/rollout-2026-09-06T05-41-36-01a07618-40cf-71b0-9419-13ddb45523c1.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-05T08:05:01+00:00, thread_id=01a07618-40cf-71b0-9419-13ddb45523c1, rate-limited)\n  3565\t\n  3566\t### keywords\n  3567\t\n  3568\t- Claude Code, session limit, HTTP 429, surface-shader, Ripple, ChangeFlash, NavIndicator, RAILPACK_START_CMD, healthz, Access-Control-Allow-Origin\n  3569\t\n  3570\t## User preferences\n  3571\t\n  3572\t- for landing work, “take screenshots of various parts of the application” and “create product spreads” -> use authentic application workflows rather than generic marketing cards; “components are in storybook to test as well” means realistic inspectable stories. [Task 1]\n  3573\t- “add texture and juice with generated assets” -> tactile generated material is welcome when product readability survives. [Task 1]\n  3574\t- the user said “check the entire session,” continue “the one done by claude last session,” then “just get straight to it” and “use the claude subagents yourself don't use crush” -> inspect history/worktree once, then implement directly with Claude workers; Codex may generate assets. [Task 2]\n  3575\t\n  3576\t## Reusable knowledge\n  3577\t\n  3578\t- Storybook discovers `apps/web/src/**/*.stories.@(ts|tsx)` through `packages/ui/.storybook/main.ts`; use `bun run storybook`/`storybook:build` or `devenv up web storybook`. New UI components need package export-map entries and `packages/ui/src/index.ts` exports. [Task 1][Task 2]\n  3579\t- Landing implementation/captures are not evidenced, but the About asset is `apps/web/public/brand/about/loom-photoreal-v2.webp`; Events restoration returned `0 groups, 0 events, 7 lexicons`, fixed five `eventsAtproto` queries, and passed 5 tests/22 assertions. [Task 1]\n  3580\t- Deployment `a9f7b958-16af-4a42-aee8-62820c287200` used `bun run prepare:railway`, `RAILPACK_BUILD_CMD=bun run build:railway`, `RAILPACK_START_CMD=bun run start:railway`, and `/healthz`; SSR/assets/routes/locales/mobile checks passed. [Task 2]\n  3581\t\n  3582\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  3583\t\n  3584\t- CDP failures (`Failed to start CDP relay server within 5031ms`, `No connected browsers detected`) mean no visual-QA claim. Agent 429 status is not proof of missing files: inspect the worktree, but do not call exports/stories/repo checks complete. [Task 1][Task 2]\n  3585\t- Railway-hostname authentication remains blocked because `api.interleave.love` omitted `Access-Control-Allow-Origin`; update trusted origins or move canonical domain before claiming sign-in works. Separate pre-existing Storybook/typecheck diagnostics from new effects. [Task 2]\n  3586\t\n  3587\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/interleave-app release/Radicle lifecycle and settings-led Weave memory\n  3588\t\n  3589\tscope: Native Devenv release mirror/hook design and privacy-controlled long-term memory injection.\n  3590\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/interleave-app; reuse_rule=checkout is dirty and release remains unverified; validate generated API and current consent behavior first.\n  3591\t\n  3592\t## Task 1: Native Devenv main-push private Radicle mirror and blocked release\n  3593\t\n  3594\t### rollout_summary_files\n  3595\t\n  3596\t- rollout_summaries/2026-09-05T22-38-05-esl2-interleave_release_native_devenv_radicle_hook.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/interleave-app, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/05/rollout-2026-09-05T18-38-05-01a073b8-c9d7-7782-b923-1ac78450ec78.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-05T23:54:18+00:00, thread_id=01a073b8-c9d7-7782-b923-1ac78450ec78, partial)\n  3597\t\n  3598\t### keywords\n  3599\t\n  3600\t- git-hooks.nix, interleave-private-radicle, mirror-radicle-main.ts, rad inspect --visibility, interleave:check, convex codegen, .githooks\n  3601\t\n  3602\t## Task 2: Settings-led shared Weave memory and saved-reply injection\n  3603\t\n  3604\t### rollout_summary_files\n  3605\t\n  3606\t- rollout_summaries/2026-09-06T00-08-32-j0vp-interleave_settings_led_weave_memory_sharing.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/interleave-app, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/05/rollout-2026-09-05T20-08-32-01a0740b-9853-7f02-b21d-1b6e5cbf5e93.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-06T00:43:42+00:00, thread_id=01a0740b-9853-7f02-b21d-1b6e5cbf5e93, partial; focused checks pass)\n  3607\t\n  3608\t### keywords\n  3609\t\n  3610\t- weave-memory:v1, AppSettings.tsx, memorySystem.ts, conversationReplies.ts, getMemoryContextForConversation, userConsents, 8000 characters\n  3611\t\n  3612\t## User preferences\n  3613\t\n  3614\t- “use the devenv githooks feature pls not .githooks” -> use `git-hooks.nix` declarations in `devenv.nix`, never a tracked custom `.githooks` solution. [Task 1]\n  3615\t- “but that would be in settings rather than up front” -> consent/privacy controls belong in Settings without interrupting shared-chat start; preserve global default, partner overrides, and individual approval model. [Task 2]\n  3616\t\n  3617\t## Reusable knowledge\n  3618\t\n  3619\t- `mirror-radicle-main.ts` skips non-main, requires `rad` remote/private visibility, and performs the internal mirror without recursive hooks. Private Radicle repos must not use `rad publish`; a different repository RID is never reusable. [Task 1]\n  3620\t- Memory refresh runs every six hours, flush every three minutes, and stale reset hourly. `getMemoryContextForConversation` injects bounded reference data, never instructions/verbatim memory; shared context only applies to eligible Weave matches and non-Weave shared chat stays isolated. [Task 2]\n  3621\t\n  3622\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  3623\t\n  3624\t- Release is blocked: use native hook declarations, but do not tag/publish while `interleave:check` has unresolved stale API/type errors. Codegen alone cannot repair UI references to absent namespaces. [Task 1]\n  3625\t- Security/format/lint/diff checks passed, but project `tsc` still had 68 unrelated errors and there was no authenticated live-Weave/browser proof; report that boundary. [Task 2]\n  3626\t\n  3627\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/notorganic-provider public landing, portal/emails, release scope, and private Radicle\n  3628\t\n  3629\tscope: Not Organic public/company surfaces, branded portal and email package, Railway landing snapshots, and release/Radicle constraints.\n  3630\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/notorganic-provider; reuse_rule=recheck live services, legal facts, remote/Radicle state, CSP, and the dirty tree before deployment/release claims.\n  3631\t\n  3632\t## Task 1: Release preparation, private Radicle, Railway landing snapshot, and legal boundary\n  3633\t\n  3634\t### rollout_summary_files\n  3635\t\n  3636\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/notorganic-provider, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/05/rollout-2026-09-05T05-10-45-01a070d5-a90a-7631-8f51-db53d79dd081.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-05T12:31:23+00:00, thread_id=01a070d5-a90a-7631-8f51-db53d79dd081, partial)\n  3637\t\n  3638\t### keywords\n  3639\t\n  3640\t- notorganic.info, build:landing, Caddyfile, rad init, rad publish, /healthz, Draft placeholder, Paddle, docs.notorganic.info\n  3641\t\n  3642\t## Task 2: Branded landing motion, portal redesign, and lifecycle React Email templates\n  3643\t\n  3644\t### rollout_summary_files\n  3645\t\n  3646\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/notorganic-provider, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/06/rollout-2026-09-06T05-41-36-01a07618-4107-7bb0-9c45-2f4ff16e7131.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-04T22:30:43+00:00, thread_id=01a07618-4107-7bb0-9c45-2f4ff16e7131, success)\n  3647\t\n  3648\t### keywords\n  3649\t\n  3650\t- juice.js, textures.css, script-src 'self', .portal-preview.ts, preview:emails, micro-USD, React Email, transactional, lifecycle\n  3651\t\n  3652\t## Task 3: Update product icons, deploy the isolated commit, and verify the private Radicle push\n  3653\t\n  3654\t### rollout_summary_files\n  3655\t\n  3656\t- 