icon should be used” -> preserve product-specific identity: paired gecko for Interleave, griffin animal mark for Twyne, green K letter mark for Keating. [Task 3]\n  3678\t- when requesting the follow-up push from a 96-path dirty worktree, stage only the explicitly requested assets and preserve unrelated work. [Task 3]\n  3679\t- when the user asked to “get the remain work commited and pushed” -> inspect, validate, stage, commit, and push the remaining project work while leaving generated/local artifacts uncommitted and avoiding unrelated deployment behavior. [Task 4]\n  3680\t\n  3681\t## Reusable knowledge\n  3682\t\n  3683\t- `notorganic.info` landing runs Caddy; deploy a landing-only snapshot with `railway up <snapshot> --path-as-root ... --detach`, poll to `SUCCESS`, and probe `/healthz`, HTTPS routes/assets, 404, and redirect. It is intentionally separate from API/docs services. [Task 1]\n  3684\t- The Radicle repository is private; use `rad auth` without printing credentials and never `rad publish`/broad sync without authorization. Releases need explicit dirty-tree scope and a remote URL. [Task 1]\n  3685\t- `build:landing` copies assets wholesale. Motion needs same-origin `juice.js` and Caddy `script-src 'self'`; retain restrictive remaining CSP. Hide/reveal only after JS initialization so hero CTA remains visible. `bun run check` had 141 passing tests; `bun run preview:emails` renders 32 variants. [Task 2]\n  3686\t- The icon-only commit `268e9bd27d5e8000f6daece8efac4de1cfc3b0c1` updated six assets: `apps/landing/brand/{interleave-mark.png,interleave.png,keating.png,twyne-mark.png}` and `apps/portal/public/brand/{interleave.png,twyne.png}`. `bun run build:landing` and focused landing/email tests passed (22 tests, 0 failures, 359 assertions); SHA-256 checks confirmed reviewed assets matched the landing/identity deployment. [Task 3]\n  3687\t- Before committing the remaining work, `bun run check` passed typecheck and 156 tests across 27 files, and `git diff --check` passed. Exclude generated local `.zero/cache/` using `git add -A -- . ':!.zero/cache/'`; the verified push used `SKIP=notorganic-railway git push rad main`, leaving only `.zero/` untracked. Commit `a675581` aligned `main` and `rad/main`. [Task 4]\n  3688\t\n  3689\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  3690\t\n  3691\t- Terms/privacy are visibly draft lorem-ipsum placeholders. Do not submit to Paddle or state binding/legal/refund claims until legal entity, jurisdiction, address, contacts, age, refund and fundraising details are supplied; `api.notorganic.info`/docs issues remain separately live-state dependent. [Task 1]\n  3692\t- Treat later unbacked claims of a design deployment, push, 56 tests, and browser/WebGL checks as unverified until Git/Railway/live evidence is inspected. Email templates must keep transactional notices free of unsubscribe links; `creditsLow` is lifecycle. [Task 1][Task 2]\n  3693\t- A full hook run can fail on unrelated in-progress files and pre-existing TypeScript errors. For a focused asset commit, use a clean detached checkout to run its hook, then preserve the dirty source checkout. [Task 3]\n  3694\t- The earlier Radicle push was blocked because its signing identity was not loaded, then `rad auth` required the encrypted-key passphrase. Do not claim completion after “should be good now”: retry interactively and verify `git rev-list --left-right --count rad/main...HEAD` is `0 0`; Task 4 later achieved this at `a675581`. Credentials/passphrases never enter logs or memory. [Task 3][Task 4]\n  3695\t- A normal push invokes the `notorganic-railway` pre-push deployment hook. When only Radicle publication was requested, inspect hook configuration and use `SKIP=notorganic-railway`; `No seeds found for rad:REDACTED` means the push was accepted but peer replication was not confirmed. [Task 4]\n  3696\t\n  3697\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/traction privacy-enforcing SDK, agent integration, and deployment preparation\n  3698\t\n  3699\tscope: Audit/implement Traction’s cross-surface analytics SDK and briefing product, with secret and Railway boundaries.\n  3700\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/traction; reuse_rule=deployment and provider-key state are live/authorization-sensitive; do not reuse old service-health as proof of integration.\n  3701\t\n  3702\t## Task 1: Audit claims and implement the Traction spec/SDK/agent path\n  3703\t\n  3704\t### rollout_summary_files\n  3705\t\n  3706\t- rollout_summaries/2026-09-05T10-09-56-ydPq-traction_integration_claims_audit_and_hardening.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/traction, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/05/rollout-2026-09-05T06-09-56-01a07132-6c86-7f30-8b3a-2fd6f4d05997.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-05T12:25:49+00:00, thread_id=01a07132-6c86-7f30-8b3a-2fd6f4d05997, implementation verified locally)\n  3707\t\n  3708\t### keywords\n  3709\t\n  3710\t- @traction/sdk, @traction/spec/node, DO_NOT_TRACK, POSTHOG_READ_KEY, pack:local, traction.config.json, docs/VERIFICATION.md\n  3711\t\n  3712\t## Task 2: Store PostHog read key and prepare, but do not perform, Railway deployment\n  3713\t\n  3714\t### rollout_summary_files\n  3715\t\n  3716\t- rollout_summaries/2026-09-05T12-26-12-tlZd-traction_posthog_secret_railway_deployment_preparation.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/traction, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/05/rollout-2026-09-05T08-26-12-01a07188-9921-7142-be20-0b160cbf511f.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-05T12:35:36+00:00, thread_id=01a07188-9921-7142-be20-0b160cbf511f, partial; secret must rotate)\n  3717\t\n  3718\t### keywords\n  3719\t\n  3720\t- POSTHOG_READ_KEY, Skate, TRACTION_BIND, TRACTION_PUBLIC_ORIGIN, TRACTION_DB, railway up --ci --service traction\n  3721\t\n  3722\t## User preferences\n  3723\t\n  3724\t- “telemetry should be opt out actually” and support for “desktop, mobile, cli, tui, and web” -> SDK behavior needs disclosure, project/machine controls, DO_NOT_TRACK/CI suppression, minimization, and opt-in replay, while remaining separately installable from Traction. [Task 1]\n  3725\t\n  3726\t## Reusable knowledge\n  3727\t\n  3728\t- Audit runtime/data sources before believing claims: static dashboard/health and tests did not prove the advertised agent/SDK. Enforced guarantees live in `@traction/sdk`, not low-level helpers; browser-safe root uses portable code and Node-only exports live at `@traction/spec/node`. [Task 1]\n  3729\t- `bun run check` passed 372 tests/1,943 assertions; fresh Bun/Node/Chromium consumer proof demonstrated notice-before-capture, allowlisted opt-in event, and no capture after opt-out. Local archives require companion `@traction/spec` override. [Task 1]\n  3730\t- `POSTHOG_READ_KEY` is a server-held PostHog personal query key. Railway requires bind/public origin/dashboard secret/persistent `/data`; `railway up --ci --service traction` is only authorized after exact destination plus secret/storage approval. [Task 2]\n  3731\t\n  3732\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  3733\t\n  3734\t- The key pasted in chat is compromised: revoke/replace it and never store/echo its value. Skate write access can need host permissions. [Task 2]\n  3735\t- Missing `POSTHOG_READ_KEY`, no new deployment, no publication, and no live cloud ingestion mean do not claim production integration. Live `/health` alone is not proof. [Task 1][Task 2]\n  3736\t\n  3737\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/twyne v0.19.1 release and native Devenv pre-push hook\n  3738\t\n  3739\tscope: Review, version, tag, publish, and verify the Twyne Qwik/Devenv release path.\n  3740\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne; reuse_rule=release/tag/CI/asset facts are time-specific; inspect current branch, workflow, and hook chain first.\n  3741\t\n  3742\t## Task 1: Review and publish v0.19.1\n  3743\t\n  3744\t### rollout_summary_files\n  3745\t\n  3746\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/05/rollout-2026-09-05T05-47-11-01a070f7-0264-7793-aad9-e06b6a709c20.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-05T09:53:51+00:00, thread_id=01a070f7-0264-7793-aad9-e06b6a709c20, success; Windows packaging pending at check)\n  3747\t\n  3748\t### keywords\n  3749\t\n  3750\t- v0.19.1, bun run release:version patch, check-release-version.ts, git-hooks.nix, prek install -f, Dagger, SOURCE_IGNORE\n  3751\t\n  3752\t## User preferences\n  3753\t\n  3754\t- “review and create a new release then push” -> release work includes state/workflow/hooks/checks/remote-publication proof, not merely running versioning. [Task 1]\n  3755\t\n  3756\t## Reusable knowledge\n  3757\t\n  3758\t- The native release consistency hook belongs at `pre-push`, not `pre-commit`, because Bun makes the version commit before the annotated tag. `release:version` uses `bun pm version`; `release:check` enforces SemVer, annotated `v<version>`, manifest equality, and no unexpected tag at HEAD. [Task 1]\n  3759\t- If Prek is stale, run `devenv shell -- prek install -f --hook-type pre-push` while preserving the Entire wrapper chain. v0.19.1 passed local tests/typecheck/lint/build/Storybook/frozen install/format/release checks and GitHub publication. [Task 1]\n  3760\t\n  3761\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  3762\t\n  3763\t- Do not call Vet passed when safety blocks network export. GitHub’s `ReferenceError: SOURCE_IGNORE is not defined` was an independent pre-existing Dagger failure; Windows packaging was still running at last check. [Task 1]\n  3764\t\n  3765\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/dio.computer Bun-only Devenv upgrade\n  3766\t\n  3767\tscope: Remove unnecessary Node provisioning, preserve Go TUI support, and upgrade custom Nix Bun pin.\n  3768\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/dio.computer; reuse_rule=validate current Nix hashes and existing dirty worktree before version changes.\n  3769\t\n  3770\t## Task 1: Disable Node tooling and verify Bun 1.4.2 with current checks\n  3771\t\n  3772\t### rollout_summary_files\n  3773\t\n  3774\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/dio.computer, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/05/rollout-2026-09-05T14-22-59-01a072cf-3dd9-78d0-aade-443c2fa49b0f.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-05T18:33:40+00:00, thread_id=01a072cf-3dd9-78d0-aade-443c2fa49b0f, success)\n  3775\t\n  3776\t### keywords\n  3777\t\n  3778\t- devenv shell --clean, nodejs.enable = false, pinnedBunVersion, dio:doctor, dio:ci, Bun 1.4.2, tui/\n  3779\t\n  3780\t## User preferences\n  3781\t\n  3782\t- “use devenv,” “skip vet,” and “don't write any tests just check the current tests” -> use native Devenv, honor explicit Vet skip, and validate with existing checks only. Ask what unfamiliar runtime components are for before removal. [Task 1]\n  3783\t\n  3784\t## Reusable knowledge\n  3785\t\n  3786\t- Disable Node/LSP in `devenv.nix`, but retain Go because `tui/` is a standalone SSH terminal app. Use `devenv shell --clean` to prove Node/npm/typescript-language-server are absent; inherited shell variables can mislead. [Task 1]\n  3787\t- Custom Nix Bun upgrades require all platform archive hashes plus `pinnedBunVersion`; `devenv tasks run dio:doctor` and `dio:ci` provide existing full validation. [Task 1]\n  3788\t\n  3789\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  3790\t\n  3791\t- Restricted Nix cache access can fail evaluation; only rerun with appropriate host access. Do not weaken claims because the ambient non-clean shell still exposes Node. [Task 1]\n  3792\t\n  3793\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects Gren workspace organization and cleanup discovery\n  3794\t\n  3795\tscope: Group matching top-level Gren projects and report—not perform—broader cleanup candidates.\n  3796\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects; reuse_rule=filesystem inventory/sizes are time-specific and root is not a Git repository; obtain explicit deletion approval.\n  3797\t\n  3798\t## Task 1: Group Gren packages and scan cleanup candidates\n  3799\t\n  3800\t### rollout_summary_files\n  3801\t\n  3802\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/05/rollout-2026-09-05T14-37-31-01a072dc-8cfe-7580-a95f-f987e9d157e4.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-05T18:42:14+00:00, thread_id=01a072dc-8cfe-7580-a95f-f987e9d157e4, success)\n  3803\t\n  3804\t### keywords\n  3805\t\n  3806\t- gren-packages, node_modules 48G, rtk find, compound predicates, cleanup candidates\n  3807\t\n  3808\t## User preferences\n  3809\t\n  3810\t- “can you put all the gren packages in a folder pls” -> identify all matching top-level projects, preserve contents/status, and group under a clear folder. When asked broadly about cleanup, inspect and propose candidates before destructive changes. [Task 1]\n  3811\t\n  3812\t## Reusable knowledge\n  3813\t\n  3814\t- Eighteen Gren-named directories were moved to `/home/diogenes/Projects/gren-packages`; root scan observed 42 `node_modules` totaling about 48GB. Check Git status per project, not at `/home/diogenes/Projects`. [Task 1]\n  3815\t\n  3816\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  3817\t\n  3818\t- `rtk find` cannot express compound predicates and grep does not accept ripgrep `--glob`; use direct `find`/standard grep or rg. Do not delete dependencies, empty directories, logs, or archives until inactivity/regenerability is confirmed by the user. [Task 1]\n  3819\t\n  3820\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/stich release preparation, secure auth, Railway domains, and Radicle workflow\n  3821\tscope: Prepare Stich releases without absorbing dirty work; operate secure desktop auth, committed-content Railway/Radicle workflows, and custom-domain proof.\n  3822\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/stich; reuse_rule=all release, deployment, worktree, signing, Radicle-node, and remote state is time-sensitive; establish content boundary and recheck before mutations.\n  3823\t\n  3824\t## Task 1: Prepare v0.1.2 release, stopped at content-boundary clarification\n  3825\t\n  3826\t### rollout_summary_files\n  3827\t\n  3828\t- rollout_summaries/2026-09-05T02-35-07-eiKm-stich_release_preparation_stopped_on_dirty_tree_and_signing.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/stich, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/04/rollout-2026-09-04T22-35-08-01a06f6b-735e-7c63-8273-3e00bd8fd882.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-05T02:37:46+00:00, thread_id=01a06f6b-735e-7c63-8273-3e00bd8fd882, partial; no version bump, tag, or push)\n  3829\t\n  3830\t### keywords\n  3831\t\n  3832\t- release:version, release:check, release:preflight, STICH_RELEASE_CHANNEL, v0.1.1, v0.1.2, railpack.json, signing-secrets\n  3833\t\n  3834\t## Task 2: Secure OAuth diagnostics, settings logout, committed Railway deployment, and private Radicle setup\n  3835\t\n  3836\t### rollout_summary_files\n  3837\t\n  3838\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/stich, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/03/rollout-2026-09-03T14-24-33-01a06883-f310-76b2-bfcb-fb544baaa84c.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-04T05:02:24+00:00, thread_id=01a06883-f310-76b2-bfcb-fb544baaa84c, success)\n  3839\t\n  3840\t### keywords\n  3841\t\n  3842\t- authDiagnostics.ts, LoginScreen, Debug secure sign-in, credential store, stich:deploy:railway, git archive, --path-as-root, Radicle, rad publish, rad:z3HyyJGyi3MtcFhbMVNUBvMVqHk9B\n  3843\t\n  3844\t## Task 3: Connect Railway/Porkbun domains and open local delivery proof\n  3845\t\n  3846\t### rollout_summary_files\n  3847\t\n  3848\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/stich, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/04/rollout-2026-09-04T19-53-47-01a06ed7-bbde-7e22-89a9-e01f70240fc4.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-05T03:05:08+00:00, thread_id=01a06ed7-bbde-7e22-89a9-9a1e06a37ed4, partial; local/domain and live-mail proof, deployment/TLS incomplete)\n  3849\t\n  3850\t### keywords\n  3851\t\n  3852\t- stich.cc, mail.stich.cc, www.stich.cc, Railway, Porkbun, _railway-verify, smoke-domains.mjs, railpack.json, Playwriter, data:image/png;base64\n  3853\t\n  3854\t## User preferences\n  3855\t\n  3856\t- when generic sign-in “load failed” was “really crappy for figuring out what the hell is going on,” the user wanted failing-stage, actionable diagnostics rather than opaque browser errors; redact every credential and sensitive URL component. [Task 2]\n  3857\t- “add a way to log out in the settings” -> account settings need a discoverable full mail sign-out, not merely an auth-store reset. [Task 2]\n  3858\t- “make updating railway a devenv githook” -> make deployment native/repeatable and deploy the exact pushed commit, never unrelated dirty work. [Task 2]\n  3859\t- when the user said “use railway and the porkbun stuff to get it wrking” -> use the existing Railway/Porkbun integrations directly and verify the external result, not merely list records. [Task 3]\n  3860\t- when the user asked “can you open the image in the browser” -> visibly open the artifact with browser-control tooling rather than only linking or describing it. [Task 3]\n  3861\t\n  3862\t## Reusable knowledge\n  3863\t\n  3864\t- Release checker requires coordinated SemVer across root, `apps/{agent,desktop,mcp,mobile,web}/package.json`, and `apps/mobile/app.json`, plus annotated `v<version>` tag and no unexpected version tag at `HEAD`. `bun run release:version`, `bun run release:check`, and `release:publish` (`git push --follow-tags`) are the defined sequence. [Task 1]\n  3865\t- To select preflight channel, use `STICH_RELEASE_CHANNEL=stable bun run release:preflight`; `--channel stable` is ignored. Stable signing requires macOS/Windows credentials; canary is unsigned by default. [Task 1]\n  3866\t- `LoginScreen` opt-in trace is capped at 20 events; `authDiagnostics.ts` redacts passwords, tokens, authorization codes, PKCE, query strings, and fragments. Full logout also calls `getCredentialStore().clear(account.id)` and clears React Query/UI state because `useAuthStore.logout()` does not clear secure credentials. [Task 2]\n  3867\t- `stich:deploy:railway` archives an exact commit then calls Railway with `--path-as-root`; `.githooks/pre-push.pre-entire` limits deploys to `origin main`, so `git push rad main` cannot redeploy. Poll detached deployments to `SUCCESS/FAILED`. [Task 2]\n  3868\t- Private Radicle RID is `rad:z3HyyJGyi3MtcFhbMVNUBvMVqHk9B`; a `rad:` RID is not a browser URL. `rad publish` then `rad sync` exposes history to public replication, which is practically irreversible. [Task 2]\n  3869\t- `apps/web/server.mjs` recognizes `mail.stich.cc` and legacy `mail.dio.computer`, redirects `www.stich.cc` to `stich.cc`, and redirects `/app` to `https://mail.stich.cc/`. `apps/web/scripts/smoke-domains.mjs` locally proved landing, redirect, app entry, both mail hosts, OAuth callback, assets, agent, and origin boundary. [Task 3]\n  3870\t- Railway custom-domain ownership used `_railway-verify`, `_railway-verify.mail`, and `_railway-verify.www`; local server/domain smoke, workspace tests, web build/typecheck, agent build, 5 web Playwright tests, and 10 desktop renderer tests passed. For a connected browser, open a local image by base64-encoding it into `page.setContent()` then `page.bringToFront()`; `file://` navigation is rejected. [Task 3]\n  3871\t\n  3872\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  3873\t\n  3874\t- Dirty UI changes and untracked `railpack.json` made release content ambiguous: ask whether the release includes them or committed `HEAD` before staging/bumping/tagging. Do not call stable release ready when signing credentials are absent. [Task 1]\n  3875\t- Railway `/tmp` archives caused `prefix not found`; use a repository-root temp directory and `--path-as-root`. Escape shell `${STICH_DEPLOY_COMMIT:-HEAD}` in Nix as `\\${...}`. [Task 2]\n  3876\t- `rad sync` reporting no candidate seeds is expected for a private repository without authorized seeds; it is not a failed local setup. Vet remained unverified under dirty-tree/session limits. [Task 2]\n  3877\t- Do not call the custom-domain deployment complete while Railway is `BUILDING`; poll to `SUCCESS`. Final evidence had 200/valid HTTPS for apex and mail but a TLS handshake failure for `www`; live `/app` and `/health` were 404 during the build, so only local smoke proved those routes. A stalled Vet run with read-only log warnings has no verdict. [Task 3]\n  3878\t\n  3879\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/interleave-app relationship-agent evaluation and Typst research artifact\n  3880\tscope: Build audited, safety-gated relationship-agent evaluation with Arize export and a methods-focused research paper.\n  3881\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/interleave-app; reuse_rule=recheck provider quota, current prompts/hashes, Arize state, and browser connection; the recorded pilot is explicitly unscored.\n  3882\t\n  3883\t## Task 1: Build relationship-science benchmark and quota-blocked Arize pilot\n  3884\t\n  3885\t### rollout_summary_files\n  3886\t\n  3887\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/interleave-app, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/04/rollout-2026-09-04T21-28-23-01a06f2e-5837-7441-99a8-e01f70240fc4.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-05T02:34:42+00:00, thread_id=01a06f2e-5837-7441-99a8-e01f70240fc4, partial; pilot unscored)\n  3888\t\n  3889\t### keywords\n  3890\t\n  3891\t- evals/relationship-science, Arize, Phoenix, Ivy, Sage, Ember, prompt hashes, outcome-leakage, RESOURCE_EXHAUSTED, HTTP 422, safety gate\n  3892\t\n  3893\t## Task 2: Compile and inspect Typst evaluation methods paper\n  3894\t\n  3895\t### rollout_summary_files\n  3896\t\n  3897\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/interleave-app, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/04/rollout-2026-09-04T21-28-23-01a06f2e-5837-7441-99a8-e01f70240fc4.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-05T02:34:42+00:00, thread_id=01a06f2e-5837-7441-99a8-e01f70240fc4, success; browser launch unavailable)\n  3898\t- rollout_summaries/2026-09-05T04-19-16-bT8N-open_typst_paper_local_pdf.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/interleave-app, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/05/rollout-2026-09-05T00-19-16-01a06fca-cd62-7df1-be37-ff2cc8fa2ae5.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-05T04:21:08+00:00, thread_id=01a06fca-cd62-7df1-be37-ff2cc8fa2ae5, partial; local browser opening unverified)\n  3899\t\n  3900\t### keywords\n  3901\t\n  3902\t- paper.typ, paper.pdf, bibliography, Typst, relationship-agent-evaluation, 11 pages, 20 references\n  3903\t\n  3904\t## User preferences\n  3905\t\n  3906\t- scenarios “from books and couples around the world” with “good arguments” -> distinguish literary dilemmas, study-informed composites, and synthetic cases; preserve evidence, warrant, counterargument, consent, and uncertainty rather than emitting opaque scores. [Task 1]\n  3907\t\n  3908\t## Reusable knowledge\n  3909\t\n  3910\t- `evals/relationship-science/` has 38 scenarios/18 families/14 source records with 14/12/12 development/calibration/holdout splits, prompt hashes, blinded judging, safety gates, reports, paired comparisons, and Arize export. It blocks outcome leakage, split contamination, invented evidence IDs, missing denominator slots, and safety failures averaged away. [Task 1]\n  3911\t- Actor failures must be explicit nonempty JSON error records in Arize export, omitted from scoring; this fixed Arize HTTP 422. Current pilot upload/readback stored 14 runs, but 9 actor successes and 5 failures produced 14 unscored judgments. [Task 1]\n  3912\t- `docs/research/relationship-agent-evaluation/paper.typ` compiled to a visually inspected 11-page PDF with 20 references; it evaluates advice, not predicted relationship outcomes. [Task 2]\n  3913\t\n  3914\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  3915\t\n  3916\t- HTTP 429 `RESOURCE_EXHAUSTED` surfaced as Flue HTTP 502. Never describe the pilot as quality, safety, efficacy, or scored evidence; rerun live providers after quota access is available. [Task 1]\n  3917\t- Browser list was empty, so interactive PDF opening was not verified. Do not substitute another browser surface without approval. Networked Vet was safety-blocked, not passed. [Task 1][Task 2]\n  3918\t\n  3919\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/interleave-app native Devenv development workflow\n  3920\tscope: Run the root development stack through declarative Devenv tasks, processes, and profiles without parallel orchestration layers.\n  3921\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/interleave-app; reuse_rule=recheck Devenv/Nix access, lockfile, dirty tree, and provider/native-package status; targeted startup proof is not full-repository proof.\n  3922\t\n  3923\t## Task 1: Replace mixed root orchestration with native Devenv\n  3924\t\n  3925\t### rollout_summary_files\n  3926\t\n  3927\t- rollout_summaries/2026-09-04T23-13-58-PSFZ-interleave_native_devenv_modernization.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/interleave-app, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/04/rollout-2026-09-04T19-13-58-01a06eb3-4a22-7983-b51a-1abe9757df1b.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-05T00:18:35+00:00, thread_id=01a06eb3-4a22-7983-b51a-1abe9757df1b, partial; targeted workflow/startup verified)\n  3928\t\n  3929\t### keywords\n  3930\t\n  3931\t- devenv.nix, devenv.lock, interleave:setup, interleave:check, devenv up, --profile all, processes, bun install --lockfile-only, window.$_TSR, apps/web/index.html\n  3932\t\n  3933\t## User preferences\n  3934\t\n  3935\t- when the user requested Devenv for “running all dev stuff getting things up setting up processes testing stuff” -> use one native declarative Devenv workflow. “devenv up, tasks and no just commands or mise” and native `processes.*`/`services.*` mean do not introduce Just, Mise, Moon, or `concurrently` root orchestration. [Task 1]\n  3936\t\n  3937\t## Reusable knowledge\n  3938\t\n  3939\t- `devenv.nix` defines namespaced `interleave:*` tasks, managed processes, readiness probes, an `all` profile, and fixed browser ports. Default `devenv up` starts web plus Convex; `devenv --profile all up` enables seven browser apps. `devenv tasks list --no-tui` evaluated successfully under Devenv 2.2.2, and web was `ready` with `curl http://127.0.0.1:5173/` returning 200. [Task 1]\n  3940\t- `interleave:setup` runs `bun install --frozen-lockfile` and creates `.env` only if absent. If manifests and `bun.lock` drift, run `devenv shell -- bun install --lockfile-only`, then rerun setup. Remove obsolete `apps/web/index.html` if TanStack Start reports `Expected to find bootstrap data on window.$_TSR, but we did not.` [Task 1]\n  3941\t\n  3942\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  3943\t\n  3944\t- `interleave:check` still had existing Convex-reference, formatting, and repository-wide TypeScript errors; targeted tests/builds/startup do not prove full-repo type cleanliness, live providers, or native packaging. Format only the migration scope when unrelated dirty files fail broad checks. [Task 1]\n  3945\t- Nix cache restrictions can yield `unable to open database file`; evaluation needs the appropriate environment access. Whole-tree Vet can exceed input limits or lack credentials: review isolated snapshots/narrow migration diffs and report Vet unverified. [Task 1]\n  3946\t\n  3947\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/notorganic-provider Paddle billing, optional local gateway configuration, and MCP replay\n  3948\tscope: Maintain server-owned payment/control-plane behavior, truthful checkout E2E status, local optional-provider startup, and Responses/MCP state explanations.\n  3949\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/notorganic-provider; reuse_rule=recheck deployed payment-link page, Paddle notification/secret configuration, live dependencies, and provider state before enabling checkout or calling it ready.\n  3950\t\n  3951\t## Task 1: Explain centralized checkout, Paddle model, and legal launch requirements\n  3952\t\n  3953\t### rollout_summary_files\n  3954\t\n  3955\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/notorganic-provider, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/04/rollout-2026-09-04T03-47-47-01a06b63-55c7-7520-98c6-fe9427468371.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-04T07:58:22+00:00, thread_id=01a06b63-55c7-7520-98c6-fe9427468371, partial; legal pages/settings unverified)\n  3956\t\n  3957\t### keywords\n  3958\t\n  3959\t- api.notorganic.info, /v1/billing/checkout, Paddle, hosted checkout, return_url, idempotency, Terms of Service, Privacy Policy, webhook\n  3960\t\n  3961\t## Task 2: Migrate sandbox checkout and attempt browser payment E2E\n  3962\t\n  3963\t### rollout_summary_files\n  3964\t\n  3965\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/notorganic-provider, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/04/rollout-2026-09-04T05-20-50-01a06bb8-864e-7181-a126-23b371ca5f3b.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-04T09:33:52+00:00, thread_id=01a06bb8-864e-7181-a126-23b371ca5f3b, partial; payment E2E blocked)\n  3966\t\n  3967\t### keywords\n  3968\t\n  3969\t- PADDLE_PRICE_CATALOG, Paddle-Signature, /transactions, price_id, Paddle.js, checkout_unavailable, wallet credit, sandbox-checkout-service, CORS\n  3970\t\n  3971\t## Task 3: Make gateway startup tolerate disabled integrations\n  3972\t\n  3973\t### rollout_summary_files\n  3974\t\n  3975\t- rollout_summaries/2026-09-04T20-03-35-Ntcv-notorganic_provider_optional_local_gateway_integrations.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/notorganic-provider, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/04/rollout-2026-09-04T16-03-35-01a06e04-fbaf-7cb0-8064-ba1039f36403.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-04T20:06:16+00:00, thread_id=01a06e04-fbaf-7cb0-8064-ba1039f36403, success)\n  3976\t\n  3977\t### keywords\n  3978\t\n  3979\t- PADDLE_API_KEY, PADDLE_PRICE_CATALOG, Tavus, EVOLUTION_BLOB_ROOT, .local/evolution-artifacts, PORT=13087, healthz, OpenBao, Convex\n  3980\t\n  3981\t## User preferences\n  3982\t\n  3983\t- “i know this is cream only but i want to know how it would work with paddle” -> answer the requested hypothetical/provider flow before separately naming current implementation state. [Task 1]\n  3984\t- “terms of service agreements and privacy agreements clear descriptions of what the site does” -> inspect visible product/legal/support links before treating checkout as launch-ready. [Task 1]\n  3985\t- credentials were “for the test and sandboxing” and the user asked to “test end to end and give me screenshots” -> use sandbox only; distinguish rendered checkout from completed payment, webhook, wallet credit, usage, and reconciliation with visual evidence. [Task 2]\n  3986\t\n  3987\t## Reusable knowledge\n  3988\t\n  3989\t- `api.notorganic.info` is the server-side checkout/webhook control plane; callers receive a provider hosted checkout URL and may supply `return_url`. Keep price mapping/allowlists, idempotency, provider credentials, signed webhook verification, and entitlement processing server-side. [Task 1]\n  3990\t- Paddle uses `POST /transactions`, server-only `pri_...` price IDs resolved from stable `plan_id`/`pack_id`, and raw-body `Paddle-Signature` HMAC-SHA256 verification with a five-minute timestamp window at `/webhooks/paddle`. Focused TypeScript/build/tests passed (37 tests). [Task 2]\n  3991\t- Transaction links require a configured payment-link page that loads/initializes Paddle.js with a client-side token; `?_ptxn=<transaction_id>` alone is not a standalone payment form. [Task 2]\n  3992\t- Empty `PADDLE_PRICE_CATALOG` disables checkout; configured prices require `PADDLE_API_KEY` and otherwise fail 503 `checkout_unavailable` before a provider request. All Tavus credentials absent disables it; partial Tavus config is invalid. Local artifact root must be absolute (`resolve(\".local/evolution-artifacts\")`); production still requires `EVOLUTION_BLOB_ROOT`. [Task 3]\n  3993\t- MCP replay restores prior tool transcript/results after resume/compaction/handoff; it does not rerun the original operation. Preserve assistant output-item `phase` exactly (`commentary` or `final_answer`) when manually replaying. [Task 4]\n  3994\t\n  3995\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  3996\t\n  3997\t- Marketing `notorganic.info` lacked Paddle.js, and isolated checkout hit sandbox CORS before card form. No payment, webhook, wallet credit, hosted debit, reconciliation, or refund proof exists. Add a dedicated initialized page, notification destination/secret, resolve CORS, then test card through the full chain. [Task 2]\n  3998\t- `/healthz` false with unavailable Convex/OpenBao is dependency-health evidence, not a startup-config regression; port 3000 collision should be retested on an alternate `PORT`. Vet remained unverified. [Task 3]\n  3999\t- `rtk grep -n -i \"replay\" .` returned `grep: .: Is a directory`; verify wrapper syntax or use `rg` for recursive search. [Task 4]\n  4000\t\n  4001\t# Task Group: cross-repository native Devenv git hooks for Keating, Not Organic, and Twyne\n  4002\tscope: Keep repository-specific hooks native to Devenv/Nix while preserving Entire wrappers and unrelated dirty work.\n  4003\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/{dio-machines,keating,notorganic-provider,twyne}; reuse_rule=inspect each repo's current Devenv input/lock, hook chain, canonical passing check, and dirty tree before changing hooks.\n  4004\t\n  4005\t## Task 1: Integrate native repository-specific hooks across three repositories\n  4006\t\n  4007\t### rollout_summary_files\n  4008\t\n  4009\t- rollout_summaries/2026-09-04T05-03-02-ZgwI-native_devenv_git_hooks_three_repos.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/dio-machines, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/04/rollout-2026-09-04T01-03-02-01a06acc-82da-77d1-a6d3-9e97d43f5c44.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-04T06:59:33+00:00, thread_id=01a06acc-82da-77d1-a6d3-9e97d43f5c44, success)\n  4010\t\n  4011\t### keywords\n  4012\t\n  4013\t- git-hooks.nix, devenv.nix, devenv.yaml, prek, .pre-commit-config.yaml, Entire, notorganic:check, twyne:release:check, core.hooksPath\n  4014\t\n  4015\t## User preferences\n  4016\t\n  4017\t- “not this hook, just a hook that fits the repo that is custom” -> use the repository's canonical passing invariant instead of copying a generic C/Make example. [Task 1]\n  4018\t- Native Devenv/Nix declarations are desired; generated `.pre-commit-config.yaml` is ignored, not handwritten source. [Task 1]\n  4019\t\n  4020\t## Reusable knowledge\n  4021\t\n  4022\t- Keep declarations in `devenv.nix`, add the `git-hooks` input following `nixpkgs` where absent, ignore generated `.pre-commit-config.yaml`, and keep Entire wrappers chained around generated hooks. [Task 1]\n  4023\t- Keating already has repo-specific hooks; refresh stale generated `prek` state with `devenv shell -- prek install --force --hook-type pre-push`. Not Organic uses pre-commit `notorganic-check` -> `devenv tasks run notorganic:check`; Twyne uses `twyne-release-check` on pre-commit/pre-push -> `devenv tasks run twyne:release:check`. [Task 1]\n  4024\t\n  4025\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  4026\t\n  4027\t- Stale Entire backup may reference a garbage-collected `prek` and yield `exec: prek: not found`; regenerate in the current Devenv shell before restoring wrapper chain. [Task 1]\n  4028\t- Do not use Twyne `twyne:check` as a hook while its baseline has 165 unrelated Prettier failures. Preserve dirty changes; `devenv info` may print secrets, so never use/store its full output. Vet `unknown error` is unverified. [Task 1]\n  4029\t\n  4030\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/keating repository-state and upstream divergence reporting\n  4031\tscope: Report a dirty Keating checkout with accurate ahead/behind semantics and a grouped active-work summary.\n  4032\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating; reuse_rule=all counts, branch tips, tags, and changed-path categories are time-specific; rerun against current checkout before reporting.\n  4033\t\n  4034\t## Task 1: Inspect current state and explain missing upstream commits\n  4035\t\n  4036\t### rollout_summary_files\n  4037\t\n  4038\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/04/rollout-2026-09-04T03-14-51-01a06b45-2f45-7d03-9862-9b488b9f295d.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-04T07:21:47+00:00, thread_id=01a06b45-2f45-7d03-9862-9b488b9f295d, success)\n  4039\t\n  4040\t### keywords\n  4041\t\n  4042\t- git status --short --branch, origin/main...HEAD, git rev-list --left-right --count, v3.10.1, v3.10.2, 14cee8c2, f1c2ae3c, dirty-worktree\n  4043\t\n  4044\t## User preferences\n  4045\t\n  4046\t- “what is current state of this repo,” “check entire to see what we have been working on,” and “give me more detail along with what the two commits are ahead” -> proactively give divergence direction, tracked/untracked counts, grouped subsystems, and exact upstream commits. [Task 1]\n  4047\t\n  4048\t## Reusable knowledge\n  4049\t\n  4050\t- Use `git status --short --branch`, diff/staged stats, recent log, untracked inventory, and `git rev-list --left-right --count origin/main...HEAD`; explicitly list both `main..origin/main` and inverse. [Task 1]\n  4051\t- At this inspection, local `main` `005a93cf`/`v3.10.1` was behind two, not ahead; upstream `14cee8c2` added cross-provider search/LaTeX and `f1c2ae3c` published v3.10.2. Worktree had 68 tracked + 31 untracked changed paths and no staged changes. [Task 1]\n  4052\t\n  4053\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  4054\t\n  4055\t- Do not say “behind 2” without naming direction and commits. Do not blindly pull/rebase a heavily dirty worktree; preserve/review its local batch first. [Task 1]\n  4056\t\n  4057\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/stich accessible component system, concise UI, and themes\n  4058\tscope: Reuse the shared accessible controls, task-first desktop copy, calendar creation interaction, runtime themes, and narrow-screen navigation.\n  4059\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/stich; reuse_rule=recheck the dirty tree and generated desktop CSS; use @stich/ui primitives rather than reviving screen-local controls.\n  4060\t\n  4061\t## Task 1: Migrate desktop controls and dialogs onto accessible primitives\n  4062\t\n  4063\t### rollout_summary_files\n  4064\t\n  4065\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/stich, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/03/rollout-2026-09-03T18-30-47-01a06965-6389-7013-87a9-7a3d9914c613.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-03T22:44:46+00:00, thread_id=01a06965-6389-7013-87a9-7a3d9914c613, success)\n  4066\t\n  4067\t### keywords\n  4068\t\n  4069\t- @stich/ui, Dialog, Select, NumberInput, Checkbox, Radio, Switch, Textarea, Badge, Progress, focus trap, hold-to-repeat\n  4070\t\n  4071\t## User preferences\n  4072\t\n  4073\t- when asked to “fix these issues and also redesign the number input and dropdowns. the checkmarks could also do well” -> improve the whole repeated interaction vocabulary through shared primitives, not isolated visual patches [Task 1]\n  4074\t\n  4075\t## Reusable knowledge\n  4076\t\n  4077\t- Shared controls are in `packages/ui/src/components/{field,input,number-input,select,checkbox,dialog,badge,progress}.tsx`; desktop Button/Input are compatibility re-exports. `Select` is a portalled fixed-position listbox; `Dialog` portals, traps focus, handles Escape/scroll lock, and restores opener focus. `NumberInput` retains native number semantics, clamps/steps safely, and its repeating timer reads a ref-backed value. [Task 1]\n  4078\t- Preserve native inputs beneath LCARS Checkbox/Radio/Switch visuals. [Task 1]\n  4079\t\n  4080\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  4081\t\n  4082\t- Capture the dialog opener during the closed-to-open render, not in an effect after React `autoFocus`; use a current-value ref inside hold-to-repeat timers. [Task 1]\n  4083\t- Root `build:storybook` is invalid; use `bun run --filter '@stich/ui' build-storybook` or the documented Devenv task. Vet was unavailable (missing credentials/agentic stall or explicit “skip vet”), never passed. [Task 1]\n  4084\t\n  4085\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/stich provenance, Entire history, and uncommitted-diff review\n  4086\tscope: Reconstruct Stich history beyond short Git ancestry and resume large-diff reviews with evidence rather than inherited conclusions.\n  4087\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/stich; reuse_rule=all worktree counts and Entire local-only results are timestamped; re-run against the current checkout before reporting them as current state.\n  4088\t\n  4089\t## Task 1: Reconstruct development history with Git and Entire CLI\n  4090\t\n  4091\t### rollout_summary_files\n  4092\t\n  4093\t- rollout_summaries/2026-09-02T23-20-23-TPOJ-stich_entire_development_history_reconstruction.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/stich, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/02/rollout-2026-09-02T19-20-23-01a0646c-705f-7ad1-825d-838f9929302d.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-02T23:53:49+00:00, thread_id=01a0646c-705f-7ad1-825d-838f9929302d, success; inspection only)\n  4094\t\n  4095\t### keywords\n  4096\t\n  4097\t- Entire CLI, entire session list --json, entire checkpoint list --json, --pending, synthetic checkpoints, Entire-Checkpoint, git log main --reverse, v0.1.0, v0.1.1, release:check, D-Bus, SSH\n  4098\t\n  4099\t## User preferences\n  4100\t\n  4101\t- when the user asked to “look at this repository and tell me exactly how it has developed using the entire cli” -> combine normal Git commits, Entire sessions/checkpoints/transcripts, refs/tags, and current uncommitted work rather than using `git log` alone [Task 1]\n  4102\t- for the large-diff review, the user required only the specified issues JSON and requested parallel review by issue type -> preserve the output contract and split review dimensions when feasible [Task 2]\n  4103\t\n  4104\t## Reusable knowledge\n  4105\t\n  4106\t- At inspection, `main` had four conventional commits (`21fbb92a`, `2b4df2c0`, `a7b351ea`, `18349ab`); only lightweight `v0.1.0` existed while root was `0.1.1`, so `bun run release:check` reported `missing v0.1.1`. Most product evolution was in synthetic checkpoints and a dirty worktree. [Task 1]\n  4107\t- Use local `entire session list --json`, `entire checkpoint list --json`, pending checkpoints, Git refs, and stored transcripts when cloud views are unavailable. `entire checkpoint explain` needs a checkpoint ID or a commit with an `Entire-Checkpoint` trailer; otherwise use `--commit` where supported or inspect Git. Bound diffs and exclude `node_modules`, `.zero`, and generated metadata. [Task 1]\n  4108\t- The failed review established no findings. On resume, inspect current code and run focused evidence first; high-impact areas worth prioritizing are release CI, credential hydration/persistence, login/registration, mobile Expo, web server handling, Not Organic client, Stalwart admin API, generated routes, and dependency/lockfile changes. [Task 2]\n  4109\t\n  4110\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  4111\t\n  4112\t- `entire activity`/`entire recap` could not read local auth over D-Bus, and remote checkpoint enumeration failed due to SSH/repository permissions -> disclose both limits and call checkpoint counts local-only. Do not treat synthetic branches as normal ancestry or historical transcript claims as freshly rerun verification. [Task 1]\n  4113\t- Both review attempts stopped at a session limit before result evidence; do not infer defects from their task framing. A resumed audit must independently inspect the current tree and return the requested `{ \"issues\": [...] }` form. [Task 2]\n  4114\t\n  4115\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/stich desktop renderer, AI composer, Stalwart credentials, and inbox imports\n  4116\tscope: Diagnose bundled Electrobun startup, deliver compact provider-backed desktop AI input, safely investigate Stalwart/JMAP credentials, and ship mail-reference/Google-file-import features.\n  4117\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/stich; reuse_rule=recheck the heavily dirty worktree, Railway linkage/deployment, current Stalwart credential representation, and live JMAP authentication before edits or completion claims.\n  4118\t\n  4119\t## Task 1: Diagnose and fix blank Electrobun desktop window\n  4120\t\n  4121\t### rollout_summary_files\n  4122\t\n  4123\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/stich, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/02/rollout-2026-09-02T02-12-34-01a060bf-7153-7851-b477-34a0f44e14d2.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-02T23:59:38+00:00, thread_id=01a060bf-7153-7851-b477-34a0f44e14d2, success; real-renderer tests and unsigned build passed)\n  4124\t\n  4125\t### keywords\n  4126\t\n  4127\t- Electrobun, real-renderer Playwright, Bun.build, @openuidev/react-lang, process is not defined, process.env[\"NODE_ENV\"], import.meta.env, electrobun.config.ts, build-desktop-app.ts\n  4128\t\n  4129\t## Task 2: Inspect and reset Stalwart credentials\n  4130\t\n  4131\t### rollout_summary_files\n  4132\t\n  4133\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/stich, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/02/rollout-2026-09-02T02-12-34-01a060bf-7153-7851-b477-34a0f44e14d2.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-02T23:59:38+00:00, thread_id=01a060bf-7153-7851-b477-34a0f44e14d2, partial; reset was rolled back and remains unproven)\n  4134\t\n  4135\t### keywords\n  4136\t\n  4137\t- Stalwart, Railway, stalwart-mail, stalwart-image, JMAP, /.well-known/jmap, /jmap/session, Basic auth, secret-tool, New credential verification failed; previous credential was restored\n  4138\t\n  4139\t## Task 3: Add intelligence references, Google imports, and deploy Stich\n  4140\t\n  4141\t### rollout_summary_files\n  4142\t\n  4143\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/stich, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/02/rollout-2026-09-02T02-12-34-01a060bf-7153-7851-b477-34a0f44e14d2.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-02T23:59:38+00:00, thread_id=01a060bf-7153-7851-b477-34a0f44e14d2, success; deployed and production login rendered)\n  4144\t\n  4145\t### keywords\n  4146\t\n  4147\t- ChatReferencePicker.tsx, GoogleImportModal.tsx, googleContacts.ts, useCalendarContacts.ts, RFC 9610, AddressBook/ContactCard, importCalendarIcs, importContacts, 1 of 2 messages in scope, mail.dio.computer\n  4148\t\n  4149\t## User preferences\n  4150\t\n  4151\t- when the user reported “blank when i start up the desktop app” with a screenshot -> reproduce the actual bundled renderer and inspect page errors instead of treating the native shell as the whole problem [Task 1]\n  4152\t- when asked to check Railway/env credentials and then “reset it” -> redact all credential material, retain rollback verification, and only report a reset after direct authentication proves it [Task 2]\n  4153\t\n  4154\t## Reusable knowledge\n  4155\t\n  4156\t- Electrobun browser views are Bun-built rather than Vite-built. `@openuidev/react-lang` may evaluate `process.env[\"NODE_ENV\"]`; replace `process.env` wholesale with a static `{ NODE_ENV: ... }` object in both `apps/desktop/electrobun.config.ts` and `e2e/build-desktop-app.ts`, since a narrow `process.env.NODE_ENV` define misses bracket notation/aliasing. Use optional `import.meta.env?.VITE_STICH_AGENT_URL` with the localhost fallback because Bun-built views lack Vite env injection. [Task 1]\n  4157\t- Completed validation for that fix: desktop typecheck, all nine real-renderer E2E tests, and unsigned Electrobun build. [Task 1]\n  4158\t- The separate Railway project is `stalwart-mail` / service `stalwart-image`. For Basic-auth checks, request `/jmap/session` directly: `/.well-known/jmap` redirects with 307 and can lose the Authorization header. Store newly generated local credentials only in the system keyring; `secret-tool` is available while `pass` is not. [Task 2]\n  4159\t- Chat references scope people, attachment metadata, and time periods. Google support is a one-time `.ics`, CSV, or vCard import, not continuous OAuth synchronization; matching Google UIDs update contacts, contact photos are not imported, and Stalwart contact methods use RFC 9610 AddressBook/ContactCard. Key files are `ChatReferencePicker.tsx`, `GoogleImportModal.tsx`, `googleContacts.ts`, `useCalendarContacts.ts`, and `packages/api/src/jmap.ts`. [Task 3]\n  4160\t- The feature/deployment rollout recorded 219 tests, ten workspace typechecks, production/mail-web/agent builds, `git diff --check`, and an online Railway deployment where `https://mail.dio.computer` rendered login. Railpack uses `bun run build:web`, `bun run build:agent`, and `bun run build:mail-web`. [Task 3]\n  4161\t\n  4162\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  4163\t\n  4164\t- An HTML/renderer asset-collision hypothesis was wrong -> begin with page-error evidence from the real renderer. Vet was unavailable because normal mode lacked Anthropic credentials and the agentic retry exceeded its 1,048,576-character input limit on the dirty worktree; do not call it passed. [Task 1]\n  4165\t- Do not print or inspect raw secret arrays: a legacy principal secret appeared in captured local tool output and must be treated as compromised. SHA-512-crypt replacement did not authenticate on this deployment; preserve rollback material without emitting it, determine the actual supported representation, authenticate directly at `/jmap/session`, and treat the reset as unresolved until that succeeds. [Task 2]\n  4166\t\n  4167\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/dio-machines desktop GUI app support\n  4168\t\n  4169\tscope: Locate the configuration boundary for ChatGPT-style desktop applications on the workstation profile; this is an orientation record, not an installation decision.\n  4170\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/dio-machines; reuse_rule=recheck current package/docs layout before editing; clarify whether the user wants Linux alternatives, a named app, or dio-machines integration before changing configuration.\n  4171\t\n  4172\t## Task 1: Assess ChatGPT-style desktop GUI applications\n  4173\t\n  4174\t### rollout_summary_files\n  4175\t\n  4176\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/dio-machines, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/07/rollout-2026-09-07T15-45-17-01a07d67-4dc9-7d12-b97a-d91bfadd07b2.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-07T19:45:46+00:00, thread_id=01a07d67-4dc9-7d12-b97a-d91bfadd07b2, uncertain; investigation only, no configuration change)\n  4177\t\n  4178\t### keywords\n  4179\t\n  4180\t- gui.nix, APPIMAGES.md, desktop-apps, AppImage, Nix, workstation, chatgpt, claude-desktop, jan-ai, lmstudio, ollama\n  4181\t\n  4182\t## Reusable knowledge\n  4183\t\n  4184\t- Workstation-profile desktop applications belong in `home/packages/gui.nix`; the README describes it as “developer desktop apps — workstation only.” Applications managed outside Nix are documented in `docs/APPIMAGES.md`. [Task 1]\n  4185\t\n  4186\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  4187\t\n  4188\t- “what about guis like that chatgpt desktop app” was underspecified, so no installation or code change was appropriate -> first clarify whether the goal is Linux alternatives, one named ChatGPT-style desktop app, or integration/management through dio-machines. [Task 1]\n  4189\t\n  4190\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/twyne Bun-native release tooling and preserved hooks\n  4191\tscope: Replace Bumpy with Bun versioning while retaining version/tag consistency checks and a scoped push workflow.\n  4192\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne; reuse_rule=reuse only after inspecting current package scripts, tag-triggered workflow, hooks, branch, and dirty tree; this supersedes older Twyne guidance that requires a Bumpy note for a code push.\n  4193\t\n  4194\t## Task 1: Migrate Twyne from Bumpy to Bun-native versioning\n  4195\t\n  4196\t### rollout_summary_files\n  4197\t\n  4198\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/08/30/rollout-2026-08-30T20-42-27-01a05544-7ed1-7ed1-ae02-e54bc55f4c73.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-31T01:50:21+00:00, thread_id=01a05544-7ed1-7ed1-ae02-e54bc55f4c73, success; commit 6c8cd0a pushed to main)\n  4199\t\n  4200\t### keywords\n  4201\t\n  4202\t- bun pm version, Bumpy, release:check, preversion, postversion, .githooks/pre-push.pre-entire, scripts/check-release-version.ts, annotated tag, git push --follow-tags, package.json, bun.lock\n  4203\t\n  4204\t## User preferences\n  4205\t\n  4206\t- when Bumpy was removed, the user said “make sure that there are still hooks for all this as well” -> retain equivalent release/version consistency safeguards rather than deleting hooks with the dependency [Task 1]\n  4207\t- when asking “push this”, the user expected only the release-tooling migration to be committed -> preserve unrelated `devenv.nix` and `devenv.lock` edits and stage exact intended paths [Task 1]\n  4208\t\n  4209\t## Reusable knowledge\n  4210\t\n  4211\t- Twyne now uses `release:version: bun pm version`, `release:publish: git push --follow-tags`, and `release:check: bun scripts/check-release-version.ts`. `preversion`, `postversion`, and `.githooks/pre-push.pre-entire` all call the shared guard. [Task 1]\n  4212\t- `scripts/check-release-version.ts` checks SemVer, the annotated `v<version>` tag, tagged `package.json` version equality, and unexpected `v*` tags at `HEAD`. `bun pm version` runs lifecycle hooks and creates the version commit, but verify that it actually created the annotated tag; `git push --follow-tags` preserves Twyne’s existing `v*` GitHub release trigger. [Task 1]\n  4213\t- Bumpy configuration/dependency/bump files and obsolete pre-push helper were removed from `package.json`, `bun.lock`, `.bumpy/`, README, and Stryker ignores. Verified: frozen Bun install, release guard/hooks, Prettier, `git diff --check`, script/dependency assertions, and an isolated version/tag/push rehearsal. Commit `6c8cd0a` is confirmed at `origin/main`. [Task 1]\n  4214\t\n  4215\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  4216\t\n  4217\t- New `scripts/check-release-version.ts` initially failed formatting -> run `bunx prettier --write` before final verification. Vet had no Anthropic credentials in API mode and stalled in agentic mode; report it as unavailable, not passed. [Task 1]\n  4218\t\n  4219\t\n  4220\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Documents/Codex/2026-08-23/realtime-voice-chat cross-product launch planning, provider-owned billing, and hiring questions\n  4221\tscope: Plan early validation for Twyne/Keating, review secure public-client payments, and turn hiring critiques into concise questions.\n  4222\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Documents/Codex/2026-08-23/realtime-voice-chat with related projects=/home/diogenes/Projects/{keating,twyne,notorganic-provider}; reuse_rule=recheck live provider, policy, payment, and product state before using projections or making production claims.\n  4223\t\n  4224\t## Task 1: Customer discovery and campus marketing\n  4225\t\n  4226\t### rollout_summary_files\n  4227\t\n  4228\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Documents/Codex/2026-08-23/realtime-voice-chat, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/08/23/rollout-2026-08-23T21-52-55-01a03178-7f5a-7483-8a85-9ab075402487.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-29T07:46:17+00:00, thread_id=01a03178-7f5a-7483-8a85-9ab075402487, partial; planning assumptions need attributable experiments)\n  4229\t\n  4230\t### keywords\n  4231\t\n  4232\t- Mom Test, customer discovery, workflow videos, Ottawa, uOttawa, Carleton, bilingual French-first posters, QR codes, CPM, CAC, activation, repeat use\n  4233\t\n  4234\t## Task 2: Shared provider-owned payment architecture\n  4235\t\n  4236\t### rollout_summary_files\n  4237\t\n  4238\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Documents/Codex/2026-08-23/realtime-voice-chat, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/08/23/rollout-2026-08-23T21-52-55-01a03178-7f5a-7483-8a85-9ab075402487.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-29T07:46:17+00:00, thread_id=01a03178-7f5a-7483-8a85-9ab075402487, partial; local/provider verification reported, live E2E outstanding)\n  4239\t\n  4240\t### keywords\n  4241\t\n  4242\t- NotOrganic Provider, public-client OAuth, PKCE, DPoP, POST /v1/public/token, self-hosting, atomic code redemption, Creem, checkout, webhooks, entitlements\n  4243\t\n  4244\t## Task 3: Four central questions for the hiring article\n  4245\t\n  4246\t### rollout_summary_files\n  4247\t\n  4248\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Documents/Codex/2026-08-23/realtime-voice-chat, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/08/23/rollout-2026-08-23T21-52-55-01a03178-7f5a-7483-8a85-9ab075402487.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-29T07:46:17+00:00, thread_id=01a03178-7f5a-7483-8a85-9ab075402487, success; user approved four-question set)\n  4249\t\n  4250\t### keywords\n  4251\t\n  4252\t- Engineering levels aren’t about skill anymore, Swizec Teller, baseline coding bar, solution refinement, staff, tradeoffs, observable evidence, four questions\n  4253\t\n  4254\t## User preferences\n  4255\t\n  4256\t- when early growth planning, the user wants direct, person-by-person discovery: personally onboard likely builders/writers/learners/students, observe repeated use, record exact language and current behavior, then ask for introductions after a real result [Task 1]\n  4257\t- the user wants Mom Test-style conversations and two poster designs, not hypothetical “would you use this?” questions; product walkthrough videos should show real jobs and support onboarding as well as marketing [Task 1]\n  4258\t- payment is the shared launch gateway: web first, desktop first-class where practical, mobile deferred until production-ready; NotOrganic Provider must own browser authentication, checkout, webhooks, subscriptions, and entitlements [Task 2]\n  4259\t- the user wants exact status distinctions between local implementation, targeted verification, deployment, and real provider proof [Task 2]\n  4260\t- “remove em dashes” and use exactly four central questions when translating hiring claims into observable engineering work and evidence [Task 3]\n  4261\t\n  4262\t## Reusable knowledge\n  4263\t\n  4264\t- Stage attributable experiments: at $8 CPM, 1% CTR, and 2% visitor-to-paid conversion, $100 is a smoke test, $500 is directional, and $2,000 is larger but still noisy. Keep audience, product, landing page, posters, podcasts, and warm outreach separately attributable. At $12/month and three-month retention, gross revenue is $36, so early CAC should stay materially below that until margin and retention are proven. [Task 1]\n  4265\t- Campus/outdoor placement is permission-controlled. uOttawa external posting needs approval, bilingual French-first creative, stamped posters, and limited periods; Carleton's general policy excludes commercial promotion. Use approved venues or permission-based placements, a concrete use case, QR plus short URL, and per-venue tracking. [Task 1]\n  4266\t- NotOrganic Provider is the sole authority for identity, consent, checkout, webhooks, subscriptions, wallet/usage, and entitlements. A public Keating client needs strict redirect validation, S256 PKCE, narrow scopes, a public DPoP key, a short-lived one-time code, atomic verifier/binding validation before code consumption, and provider-state feature gates rather than local Pro flags. [Task 2]\n  4267\t- The approved hiring prompts ask about: baseline coding beyond an algorithm screen; recurring work separating junior through staff; observable evidence for solution refinement; and assessment of technical, economic, operational, and stakeholder judgment. [Task 3]\n  4268\t\n  4269\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  4270\t\n  4271\t- Treat QR engagement, poster scans, retention, and acquisition math as hypotheses, not forecasts. Do not enter residences, knock on private doors, or leave materials in private common areas; use consented brief public intercepts, approved tables/events, and 20–30 simple outcomes. [Task 1]\n  4272\t- Never consume an authorization code before PKCE/verifier and binding checks: a prior implementation let an invalid verifier burn a valid code. No deployment, charge, provider-delivered webhook, entitlement update, or authenticated portal session was proven; local passes are not a production-complete payment funnel. [Task 2]\n  4273\t\n  4274\t# Task Group: Codex global MCP configuration and Skate-backed secrets\n  4275\tscope: Register remote Streamable HTTP MCP servers globally while keeping credentials in Skate and configuration environment-backed.\n  4276\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne, with global paths under /home/diogenes/.codex and /home/diogenes; reuse_rule=reuse the configuration pattern, not the Keenable credential or live-service claim; recheck the server handshake after client reload.\n  4277\t\n  4278\t## Task 1: Configure Keenable MCP and store the credential\n  4279\t\n  4280\t### rollout_summary_files\n  4281\t\n  4282\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/08/27/rollout-2026-08-27T23-36-53-01a04671-1d0e-7ce1-93cd-967e613879b5.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-28T03:41:15+00:00, thread_id=01a04671-1d0e-7ce1-93cd-967e613879b5, success; configuration and loader verified, live handshake not run)\n  4283\t\n  4284\t### keywords\n  4285\t\n  4286\t- Keenable, Streamable HTTP, MCP, config.toml, env_http_headers, X-API-Key, KEENABLE_API_KEY, keenable-api-key@secrets, Skate, load-secret-env, codex mcp get keenable\n  4287\t\n  4288\t## User preferences\n  4289\t\n  4290\t- when providing an MCP credential, the user said \"add this to my secrets\" -> store it in the existing secret manager and reference an environment variable; never embed it in config, command output, or reports [Task 1]\n  4291\t\n  4292\t## Reusable knowledge\n  4293\t\n  4294\t- Global MCP configuration is `/home/diogenes/.codex/config.toml`. Remote HTTP headers use `env_http_headers`, so the Keenable pattern is `env_http_headers = { \"X-API-Key\" = \"KEENABLE_API_KEY\" }`; `/home/diogenes/bin/load-secret-env` maps Skate `keenable-api-key` to that variable. [Task 1]\n  4295\t- `codex mcp add keenable --url https://api.keenable.ai/mcp` registered the endpoint, and `codex mcp get keenable` confirmed the endpoint plus redacted environment-backed header. Verify secret presence by key-name listing and loader length only; secret value is [REDACTED_SECRET]. Reload/restart Codex clients after config changes. [Task 1]\n  4296\t\n  4297\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  4298\t\n  4299\t- Restricted access can prevent Skate from creating its secrets LOCK file -> use permitted elevated access for Skate operations. A secret byte-count pipeline ended with signal 13; use non-value key listing and loader-length checks instead. [Task 1]\n  4300\t- Configuration/secret resolution is not a live MCP claim -> run a JSON-RPC `initialize` and `tools/list` handshake before calling Keenable operational. [Task 1]\n  4301\t\n  4302\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/notorganic-provider source-backed architecture walkthrough\n  4303\tscope: Explain the provider's gateway, portal, Convex, sandbox, CI, and deployment boundaries end-to-end without treating a dirty-tree walkthrough as production proof.\n  4304\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/notorganic-provider; reuse_rule=reuse the architecture map and security invariants after checking current source/worktree state; the technical companion remains user-review-paused.\n  4305\t\n  4306\t## Task 1: Document provider architecture and testing guide\n  4307\t\n  4308\t### rollout_summary_files\n  4309\t\n  4310\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/notorganic-provider, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/08/27/rollout-2026-08-27T01-14-58-01a041a4-8ec3-71b0-826d-4dbcf4b15df3.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-27T17:14:27+00:00, thread_id=01a041a4-8ec3-71b0-826d-4dbcf4b15df3, partial; DOCX produced, user review paused)\n  4311\t\n  4312\t### keywords\n  4313\t\n  4314\t- NotOrganic-Provider-Technical-Companion.docx, Bun, Hono, Convex, Portkey, DPoP, PKCE S256, public-client, nou_portal_session, micro-USD, Cloudflare Sandbox, Tangled, Spindle, Fly Sprites, R2, production-readiness-2026-08-16.md\n  4315\t\n  4316\t## User preferences\n  4317\t\n  4318\t- when requesting a \"detailed run through here\" of what was built, service connections, modules, code, and testing -> make walkthroughs source-backed, end-to-end, and include concrete checks rather than a high-level overview [Task 1]\n  4319\t- when the user said \"do not do file review jst let me do a pass over\" -> stop all artifact review, edits, and critique immediately; leave the artifact for their own pass until asked to resume [Task 1]\n  4320\t\n  4321\t## Reusable knowledge\n  4322\t\n  4323\t- Repository map: `apps/gateway` is the Hono/Bun metered Portkey proxy; `apps/portal` owns React/Vite plus server-side ATProto OAuth/session/public-client flow; `packages/contracts`, `core`, `sdk`, and `session` hold shared contracts, money/lifecycle, OpenAI-shaped/DPoP clients, and assertion/token adaptation; `convex` is transactional state; `apps/sandbox-worker` runs isolated CPU jobs; `infra` holds Docker/Railway/OpenBao/PDS configuration. [Task 1]\n  4324\t- Main inference flow: a product backend signs a <=60-second single-use assertion; gateway verifies/consumes it, returns a <=300-second DPoP-bound token, requires `Authorization: DPoP` plus DPoP proof on protected calls, reserves integer micro-USD funds in Convex before Portkey dispatch, then settles/releases/reconciles. Idempotency prevents duplicate billing; debt can block hosted inference. [Task 1]\n  4325\t- Public clients must validate HTTPS origin, PKCE S256, exact same-origin callback, and portal-authenticated DID; never accept a browser-supplied DID or let self-hosted clients mint provider grants. Browser session is opaque `nou_portal_session` plus CSRF header, while OAuth keys/tokens remain server-side. The then-current Cloudflare Sandbox JWT bound account/product/project/run/body hash, with CPU-only/no-internet/30-second limits; treat those as adapter details, not the durable execution contract. Tangled is source, Spindle protocol, Fly Sprites pinned-commit runners, R2 artifacts, and Convex stores account-scoped provenance/status. [Task 1]\n  4326\t- For Keating account-level self-evolution and shared code execution, define a provider-neutral runner contract for isolated execution, filesystem/workspace materialization, bounded networking, secrets mediation, snapshots or durable artifact export, resource limits, cancellation, and result provenance. Cloudflare Sandbox, microVM, self-hosted runner, or future provider is a replaceable adapter; durable account evolution state, revisions, evidence, and activation decisions stay outside it. [ad-hoc note]\n  4327\t- Not Organic is the stable account and control-plane boundary for cross-device learner synchronization, shared pedagogical revisions, evolution history, active-version selection, and authorization. Browser, mobile, desktop, CLI, and connected self-hosted instances are account-scoped clients/contributors; they must not bind identity, durable state, or sync directly to provider-specific sandbox endpoints. [ad-hoc note]\n  4328\t- Useful checks: `devenv tasks run notorganic:check`, `devenv tasks run notorganic:build`, `devenv tasks run notorganic:railpack-check`, and `git diff --check`. [Task 1]\n  4329\t\n  4330\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  4331\t\n  4332\t- The 36-page DOCX was not explicitly accepted; it is paused for user review. The worktree was substantially dirty, so first distinguish uncommitted code from the last committed baseline before edits or verification. [Task 1]\n  4333\t- Do not call the provider production-live from local/staging checks: commercial checkout/webhook, branded DNS/TLS, OpenBao AppRole/bootstrap, R2, Fly/Sprites, gateway/PDS deployment, and full browser E2E were unverified. [Task 1]\n  4334\t\n  4335\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/keating Road to 4.0 product roadmap and execution boundaries\n  4336\tscope: Plan Keating 4.0 around evidence-based achievements, privacy-safe web/mobile telemetry, distinct feedback/community channels, and proven hosted payments.\n  4337\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating; reuse_rule=reuse for Keating 4.0 planning and implementation sequencing; treat live payment, Roomy readiness, and mobile telemetry as current-state gates to re-verify.\n  4338\t\n  4339\t## Task 1: Create the Road to 4.0 roadmap\n  4340\t\n  4341\t### rollout_summary_files\n  4342\t\n  4343\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/08/26/rollout-2026-08-26T21-52-37-01a040eb-4bb9-7c23-9014-2b4d8f8816c1.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-27T05:00:38+00:00, thread_id=01a040eb-4bb9-7c23-9014-2b4d8f8816c1, success; roadmap document passed diff hygiene)\n  4344\t\n  4345\t### keywords\n  4346\t\n  4347\t- road-to-4.0.md, achievements, PostHog, telemetry, userinput.app, Roomy, roomy.space, Creem, wallet, hosted inference, release gate\n  4348\t\n  4349\t## Task 2: Review 4.0 sequencing and scope\n  4350\t\n  4351\t### rollout_summary_files\n  4352\t\n  4353\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/08/26/rollout-2026-08-26T21-52-37-01a040eb-4bb9-7c23-9014-2b4d8f8816c1.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-27T05:00:38+00:00, thread_id=01a040eb-4bb9-7c23-9014-2b4d8f8816c1, success; strategic review)\n  4354\t\n  4355\t### keywords\n  4356\t\n  4357\t- progress → understanding → conversation → sustainability, 4.0, 4.x, checkout-started, wallet-credited, first-hosted-use, meaningful learning action\n  4358\t\n  4359\t## User preferences\n  4360\t\n  4361\t- when planning 4.0, the user identified achievements, complete telemetry across web/mobile, better user issue reporting than GitHub, and payments as the core -> retain these four pillars in future roadmap work [Task 1]\n  4362\t- when the user added “roomy.space as well” -> keep community conversation separate from structured feedback intake, voting, triage, and status tracking [Task 1]\n  4363\t\n  4364\t## Reusable knowledge\n  4365\t\n  4366\t- The roadmap artifact is `docs/plans/road-to-4.0.md`; it passed `rtk git diff --check -- docs/plans/road-to-4.0.md`. Userinput.app is for bugs, feature requests, voting, deduplication, triage, and planned/in-progress/implemented status; Roomy is for community discussion, study groups, mutual help, events, and community-authored knowledge, not canonical bug tracking, payment support, security, or release acceptance. [Task 1]\n  4367\t- Achievements should be versioned, deterministic, portable, reconstructable from durable learner records, idempotent across import/merge/retry/restart, independent of telemetry availability, and emit only content-free telemetry. Existing web PostHog coverage is substantial; mobile lacks equivalent complete product analytics coverage. [Task 1]\n  4368\t- Payment acceptance requires checkout -> signed webhook -> wallet credit -> hosted inference -> debit -> usage/reconciliation, including replay, cancellation, insufficient funds, refund, and outage paths. A clearly labeled mobile browser handoff may be an initial bridge; native purchase parity is separate. [Task 1]\n  4369\t- The coherent thesis is “progress → understanding → conversation → sustainability.” De-risk payments first even if they are presented last; initial 4.0 should keep a strict must-ship boundary (shared achievement engine, polished web/mobile views, essential mobile telemetry, live userinput.app board, Roomy beta, proven web payment loop) and defer richer tiers/dashboards, advanced Roomy gardening, terminal polish, and native purchase parity to 4.x unless required. [Task 2]\n  4370\t- Start with unambiguous achievement evidence (first successful turn, question check, improved revision, scheduled review, transfer task, project milestone). Use one headline measure per workstream: post-unlock meaningful action, complete telemetry lifecycle, feedback triage timeliness, checkout-started to wallet-credited to first-hosted-use conversion. [Task 2]\n  4371\t\n  4372\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  4373\t\n  4374\t- A successful checkout redirect, enabled feature flag, source implementation, or focused test is not production-payment proof; require real provider/browser evidence. [Task 1]\n  4375\t- Treat Roomy as a deliberate beta: finish account, moderation, permissions, retention, export, accessibility, mobile-browser, and fallback checks before making it required. [Task 1][Task 2]\n  4376\t- The roadmap is a strong release specification, not a complete execution companion: add owners, milestones, dependencies, risks, and an explicit 4.0 versus 4.x boundary before using it to drive delivery. [Task 2]\n  4377\t\n  4378\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/keating standalone Artifact Atlas interaction contracts\n  4379\tscope: Build practical standalone learning-artifact miniatures where controls carry real state and causal consequences; consolidate shallow specimens into deep archetypes and protect behavior with deterministic checks.\n  4380\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating; reuse_rule=reuse for `docs/artifact-atlas.html` or similarly standalone inline-JS teaching prototypes, not as a substitute for production subsystem implementation.\n  4381\t\n  4382\t## Task 1: Redesign the 17-artifact Atlas as five deep archetypes\n  4383\t\n  4384\t### rollout_summary_files\n  4385\t\n  4386\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/08/26/rollout-2026-08-26T00-48-14-01a03c65-ba22-7953-9ead-892ed3a2b6e7.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-26T04:50:33+00:00, thread_id=01a03c65-ba22-7953-9ead-892ed3a2b6e7, success; all suites passed; browser extension disconnected)\n  4387\t\n  4388\t### keywords\n  4389\t\n  4390\t- artifact-atlas.html, check-artifact-atlas.mjs, Simulation Lab, Annotated Source, Decision Case, Build Board, Signal Lab, 23 modes, 26 presets, retired specimens\n  4391\t\n  4392\t## Task 2: Serve the Atlas locally with Bun inside devenv\n  4393\t\n  4394\t### rollout_summary_files\n  4395\t\n  4396\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/08/26/rollout-2026-08-26T00-48-14-01a03c65-ba22-7953-9ead-892ed3a2b6e7.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-26T04:50:33+00:00, thread_id=01a03c65-ba22-7953-9ead-892ed3a2b6e7, success; Bun server on port 8788)\n  4397\t\n  4398\t### keywords\n  4399\t\n  4400\t- devenv shell, Bun.serve, 127.0.0.1:8788, artifact-atlas.html, PermissionError, Address already in use\n  4401\t\n  4402\t## User preferences\n  4403\t\n  4404\t- “multiple options for what each looks like” followed by “buttons don't do anything” -> variants must change interaction topology, persistent state, or learning behavior, not labels/status copy [Task 1]\n  4405\t- when ambitious artifacts seem difficult to make -> prefer constrained local miniatures with explicit limitations over fake full subsystems; every control should change something, show a consequence, and compare/explain it [Task 1]\n  4406\t- “think through the interfaces and fill them out more iterations buttons don't do anything check for bugs and format the damn thing” -> resolve the complete reviewed set and add regression coverage [Task 1]\n  4407\t- when the user asked to “vastly rethink and improve the utility” and consolidate into five additions -> prefer fewer, deeper archetypes with meaningful actions and use cases over many shallow cards [Task 1]\n  4408\t- when serving this repository, the user corrected “dude use devenv,” then “no use devenv with bun” -> default to Bun inside the repository’s devenv rather than Python [Task 2]\n  4409\t\n  4410\t## Reusable knowledge\n  4411\t\n  4412\t- `docs/artifact-atlas.html` remains standalone and is not imported by the app. Its current five archetypes are Simulation Lab, Annotated Source, Decision Case, Build Board, and Signal Lab; it has 23 modes, 26 cross-domain presets, and a folded map accounting for all 17 retired specimens. [Task 1]\n  4413\t- Run `bun scripts/check-artifact-atlas.mjs`; expected output is `artifact atlas ok: 5 archetypes, 23 modes, 26 presets, 17 retired specimens accounted for`. Probe every parameter sweep and fault for non-zero finite effects before integration. [Task 1]\n  4414\t- Use `devenv shell -- bun -e '... Bun.serve({ hostname: \"127.0.0.1\", port: 8788, ... }) ...'` for local inspection. [Task 2]\n  4415\t\n  4416\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  4417\t\n  4418\t- The original Argument Map handler assumed graph-specific DOM and crashed; scope handlers to their variant/container. A static audit must ignore dynamic `${stepAction}` template selectors while retaining runtime assertions for concrete actions. [Task 1]\n  4419\t- Vet did not complete (credentials/stalls); report deterministic audit, syntax, formatting, and preview checks as the validation boundary. [Task 1]\n  4420\t- Toy predator-prey and industrial-fault probes were initially degenerate; rebalance parameters/outcome before integrating a new simulation. The Claude browser extension was disconnected, so real-browser validation remained unavailable. [Task 1]\n  4421\t\n  4422\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/keating canonical OpenUI migration and learner-response Storybook coverage\n  4423\tscope: Make `keating-ui` the authoritati