animate tooling\n  4447\t\n  4448\t### rollout_summary_files\n  4449\t\n  4450\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/08/26/rollout-2026-08-26T00-48-14-01a03c65-ba22-7953-9ead-892ed3a2b6e7.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-26T04:50:33+00:00, thread_id=01a03c65-ba22-7953-9ead-892ed3a2b6e7, success; full suites passed)\n  4451\t\n  4452\t### keywords\n  4453\t\n  4454\t- LearningAnimation, animate, Hyperframes, unsupported, openui-source.ts, rendering.ts, operational-protocol.md, generate-nodepod-boot-files.ts\n  4455\t\n  4456\t## User preferences\n  4457\t\n  4458\t- when the user said “open ui is supposed to be used everywhere here” -> use canonical OpenUI by default for learner-facing questions, forms, plans, quizzes, decks, media, and handoffs; do not expose legacy question tools [Task 1]\n  4459\t- when asking for an audit of “outdated” system prompts -> inspect active prompt prose, tool registries, security/permission lists, and evolved/stored prompt refresh paths, not only literal prompt files [Task 1]\n  4460\t- “add the new components that exist like user question responses and openui stuff to storybook” -> add inspectable normal, submitted, streaming/recovery, and rejection/error stories with new learner-facing components [Task 2]\n  4461\t- when the user chose “Demote, don't delete” -> remove streamed `LearningAnimation`, retain the `animate` browser tool, and use animation only for an explicit learner request for motion [Task 3]\n  4462\t\n  4463\t## Reusable knowledge\n  4464\t\n  4465\t- `packages/learner-contracts` is the shared OpenUI contract. Web, mobile, and terminal validate/render `keating-ui`; `SYSTEM.md` should point to runtime schemas rather than duplicate a hard-coded tool inventory. `refreshKeatingOperationalProtocol()` normalizes evolved web prompts before activation. [Task 1]\n  4466\t- Delete `ask-user-question.ts` and active registrations from Pi/web/security/voice paths, but retain intentional legacy parsing only for historical import compatibility. In `src/tui/host-controller.ts`, hide incomplete fences and wire JSON instead of showing them as assistant prose. [Task 1]\n  4467\t- Storybook surfaces are `web/src/components/LearnerResponseReview.stories.tsx` and `web/src/keating/openui/OpenUI.stories.tsx`; cover response, question group, quiz/flashcard completion, interactive submit, incomplete-stream recovery, and unsafe-source rejection. [Task 2]\n  4468\t- Remove `LearningAnimation` from `web/src/keating/openui/library.tsx`, shared lists, source mappings, lowering, parity fixtures, and related tests. Prefer static ConceptMap, LearningImage, or Explanation; retired animation source must fail closed as `unsupported`. Regenerate `web/src/keating/nodepod-boot-files.ts` with `bun scripts/generate-nodepod-boot-files.ts` after operational-protocol changes. [Task 3]\n  4469\t\n  4470\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  4471\t\n  4472\t- Broad searches will still find compatibility, migration, historical-session, and test references. Classify active authoring paths before deleting all matches. Vet lacked Anthropic credentials and remains unverified. [Task 1]\n  4473\t\n  4474\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/twyne crawler discovery, dossiers, and historical v0.17.0 release\n  4475\tscope: Keep public discovery frontend-served and preserve historical dossier/release lessons without treating old Bumpy or deploy evidence as current production state.\n  4476\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne; reuse_rule=recheck domain, routes, public query/index, current Bun release policy, Railway state, and dirty worktree before applying to a later deploy or release.\n  4477\t\n  4478\t## Task 1: Fix crawler discovery and dynamic sitemap\n  4479\t\n  4480\t### rollout_summary_files\n  4481\t\n  4482\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/08/24/rollout-2026-08-24T12-55-29-01a034b2-d30a-7da1-a246-090ccebed787.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-24T20:37:30+00:00, thread_id=01a034b2-d30a-7da1-a246-090ccebed787, success; focused tests/build and local endpoint smoke checks passed)\n  4483\t\n  4484\t### keywords\n  4485\t\n  4486\t- twyne.love, robots.txt, sitemap.xml, 301, Qwik routes, listForSitemap, by_kind_publishedAt, XML escaping, lastmod, take(1000)\n  4487\t\n  4488\t## Task 2: File dossiers, fix reviewer findings, and publish Twyne 0.17.0\n  4489\t\n  4490\t### rollout_summary_files\n  4491\t\n  4492\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/08/24/rollout-2026-08-24T12-55-29-01a034b2-d30a-7da1-a246-090ccebed787.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-24T20:37:30+00:00, thread_id=01a034b2-d30a-7da1-a246-090ccebed787, success; workflow and public assets verified)\n  4493\t\n  4494\t### keywords\n  4495\t\n  4496\t- dossier-folio, writing-format, malformed_response, comment resolution, Bumpy, v0.17.0, 49b0adb, ca826a6, release assets\n  4497\t\n  4498\t## User preferences\n  4499\t\n  4500\t- when the user clarified “this site domain is twyne.love” and questioned Convex -> keep robots/sitemap frontend-served; use Convex only as the bounded public URL-data source [Task 1]\n  4501\t- allowing `blog/*` is not enough -> emit one sitemap `<loc>` per actual published page [Task 1]\n  4502\t- “resolve” four reported bugs -> implement every finding and regression coverage, not merely acknowledge the review; preserve unrelated dirty work when staging [Task 2]\n  4503\t\n  4504\t## Reusable knowledge\n  4505\t\n  4506\t- Qwik routes at `src/routes/robots.txt/index.ts` and `src/routes/sitemap.xml/index.ts` return exact 200s. `listForSitemap` uses `by_kind_publishedAt`, `take(1000)` per kind, static fallback URLs, deduplication, XML escaping, cache headers, and `lastmod`; omit writer rows without handles. [Task 1]\n  4507\t- Historical v0.17.0 used Bumpy and a separate marker, but this is not current procedure: use the newer Bun-native release-tooling block and inspect active workflow first. Related skill: skills/release-publication-verification/SKILL.md [Task 2]\n  4508\t\n  4509\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  4510\t\n  4511\t- Sandbox Convex codegen hit `getaddrinfo EAI_AGAIN o1192621.ingest.sentry.io`; rerun where network access permits generated bindings. After SEO fixture edits run focused tests/typecheck immediately; `no-useless-escape` in the XML regex breaks lint. [Task 1]\n  4512\t- A historical Bumpy tag push used `git push --no-verify` only after verifying an intentional old topology; do not transfer that exception to current release procedures. Browser and Vet were unverified. [Task 2]\n  4513\t\n  4514\t\n  4515\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/notorganic-provider production payment integration and Keating public-client E2E\n  4516\tscope: Deploy the provider's Convex foundation and connect Keating public checkout, wallet, and hosted inference without overstating blocked commercial proof.\n  4517\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/notorganic-provider with related cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating; reuse_rule=recheck Creem, DNS, Railway, OpenBao, and live browser state before enabling hosted access or calling payments ready.\n  4518\t\n  4519\t## Task 1: Deploy Convex/provider foundation and checkout hardening\n  4520\t\n  4521\t### rollout_summary_files\n  4522\t\n  4523\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/notorganic-provider, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/08/24/rollout-2026-08-24T00-40-54-01a03212-48e2-7b30-afa8-1b02170cd3c2.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-24T05:05:44+00:00, thread_id=01a03212-48e2-7b30-afa8-1b02170cd3c2, partial; local/provider deployment checks passed, commercial E2E blocked)\n  4524\t\n  4525\t### keywords\n  4526\t\n  4527\t- courteous-horse-754, Convex, CREEM_PRODUCT_CATALOG, pack_id, Idempotency-Key, request_id, CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGINS, Porkbun, OpenBao, Railway, /health\n  4528\t\n  4529\t## Task 2: Wire Keating public checkout, wallet, and hosted inference\n  4530\t\n  4531\t### rollout_summary_files\n  4532\t\n  4533\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/notorganic-provider, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/08/24/rollout-2026-08-24T00-40-54-01a03212-48e2-7b30-afa8-1b02170cd3c2.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-24T05:05:44+00:00, thread_id=01a03212-48e2-7b30-afa8-1b02170cd3c2, partial; Keating focused suite passed, real browser/payment proof absent)\n  4534\t\n  4535\t### keywords\n  4536\t\n  4537\t- VITE_NOTORGANIC_ENABLED, public-client.ts, NotOrganicCallback, keating_pack_10, DPoP, wallet, hosted inference, check-env-docs.ts, signed webhook\n  4538\t\n  4539\t## User preferences\n  4540\t\n  4541\t- “deploy Convex functions/schema, wire Keating, and run real browser/provider E2E” -> report deterministic deployment/code proof separately from actual checkout, webhook, and hosted-use proof [Task 1][Task 2]\n  4542\t- preserve the fail-closed hosted state until the commercial path is proven [Task 2]\n  4543\t\n  4544\t## Reusable knowledge\n  4545\t\n  4546\t- Production Convex deployment is `courteous-horse-754`; `CONVEX_DEPLOYMENT=prod:courteous-horse-754 bunx convex deploy --typecheck enable` deployed successfully and `/health` returned `{\"ok\":true}`. Gateway checkout resolves stable `pack_id` privately through `CREEM_PRODUCT_CATALOG`, requires `Idempotency-Key`, and forwards it as Creem `request_id`; CORS is exact-origin/fail-closed and empty `CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGINS` denies browser origins. [Task 1]\n  4547\t- Keating uses PKCE S256, non-extractable device-bound DPoP, short-lived access, callback/checkout/wallet UI, and hosted-inference headers. Keep raw Creem product IDs provider-private; use stable pack IDs. Synchronize public-client environment docs with `bun scripts/check-env-docs.ts`; `VITE_NOTORGANIC_ENABLED=false` is intentional pending E2E. [Task 2]\n  4548\t\n  4549\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  4550\t\n  4551\t- Do not enable the gateway/hosted feature until Creem catalog/API/webhook, DNS/TLS, and OpenBao AppRole/Transit are proven. Railway custom domains resolving to Porkbun parking require enabling Porkbun API access; Creem HTTP 401 cannot establish catalog/payment readiness. [Task 1]\n  4552\t- A diagnostic exposed secrets: rotate affected credentials before launch and never repeat/store them in memory. The final proof is checkout -> signed webhook -> wallet credit -> hosted debit -> reconciliation/refund, not 89 provider tests or 23 Keating focused tests. Vet was unverified because credentials/fallback were unavailable. [Task 1][Task 2]\n  4553\t\n  4554\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/keating French Ottawa-Gatineau poster series\n  4555\tscope: Produce multiple on-brand French educational raster posters for college-age and independent learners, leaving QR code generation for later.\n  4556\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating; reuse_rule=reinspect current brand masters and campaign requirements before creating new assets; paths are checkout-specific and PNG ignores can hide generated files.\n  4557\t\n  4558\t## Task 1: Generate French educational poster series\n  4559\t\n  4560\t### rollout_summary_files\n  4561\t\n  4562\t- rollout_summaries/2026-08-24T04-45-24-L9Rw-keating_french_ottawa_gatineau_poster_series.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/08/24/rollout-2026-08-24T00-45-24-01a03216-6783-7d90-af9a-ad37599fddf2.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-24T05:13:30+00:00, thread_id=01a03216-6783-7d90-af9a-ad37599fddf2, success; four final PNGs generated)\n  4563\t\n  4564\t### keywords\n  4565\t\n  4566\t- Keating, posters, imagegen, French, Ottawa-Gatineau, QR placeholder, web/public/brand, web/public/posters, Keating.help, *.png ignore\n  4567\t\n  4568\t## User preferences\n  4569\t\n  4570\t- “a series of posters” and “a bunch of different options” -> create several materially distinct concepts, not minor variants [Task 1]\n  4571\t- reserve a blank white QR box and defer QR automation; make campaign assets intellectually motivating for college-age and independent learners [Task 1]\n  4572\t\n  4573\t## Reusable knowledge\n  4574\t\n  4575\t- Match Keating's cream paper, near-black ink, green, coral red, amber, and retro-computing/learning-lab language. Inspect `web/public/brand/` first; its README requires alpha preservation and deriving production files from masters. Use local Ottawa-Gatineau landmarks/everyday learner character rather than generic national symbols. [Task 1]\n  4576\t- Final PNGs are in `web/public/posters/` and include the exact `Keating.help` footer plus a white QR area. The global `*.png` ignore rule may keep them out of `git status`. [Task 1]\n  4577\t\n  4578\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  4579\t\n  4580\t- No substantive generation failure. Use the built-in image tool for ordinary raster artwork, then apply approved brand/footer mechanics; do not hand off unbranded generated images as final assets. [Task 1]\n  4581\t\n  4582\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/keating trajectory review, artifact annotation, and training export\n  4583\tscope: Implement or extend the separate local-first expert-review workspace, safe rich sharing, corrective candidate selection, and finalized SFT/DPO/KTO export.\n  4584\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating; reuse_rule=reuse private-storage/public-projection boundaries after inspecting the current dirty tree; browser acceptance and Vet remain separate release gates.\n  4585\t\n  4586\t## Task 1: Redesign review UI and reuse Chat's model/provider picker\n  4587\t\n  4588\t### rollout_summary_files\n  4589\t\n  4590\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/08/25/rollout-2026-08-25T00-50-50-01a03741-bfb9-7cb2-87a5-9208eb902d57.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-24T04:22:23+00:00, thread_id=01a03741-bfb9-7cb2-87a5-9208eb902d57, success; typecheck/build clean; 1061 tests passed with one unrelated pre-existing failure)\n  4591\t\n  4592\t### keywords\n  4593\t\n  4594\t- ModelSelectorDialog, model-catalog, review-pools, SocraticPass, MarginProposals, Reicon, PandaCSS, anchorQuote, hidden-providers, storedModelReference\n  4595\t\n  4596\t## User preferences\n  4597\t\n  4598\t- the user asked for “a separate mode for review” exportable for “sft or other training data” -> keep expert review separate from learner thumbs feedback and make training export explicit [Task 1]\n  4599\t- review “also lets you annotate artifacts natively” -> support text spans, image regions, time ranges, and whole-artifact annotations [Task 1]\n  4600\t- “regenerate the artifacts with some suggestions” and “insert new generations of choice as a response” -> preserve originals immutably, produce candidates/revisions, and require explicit preferred-choice selection [Task 1]\n  4601\t- default to pedagogy-first with expandable engineering details, local saved-session JSON import/export, and ratings for diagnosis, accuracy, scaffolding, adaptation, learner agency, and verification [Task 1]\n  4602\t- “annotate and create trajectories for what the model is doing”; “write quickly where the model turn went wrong” and “what we think might have helped the student instead” -> make turn-by-turn, span-level corrective feedback and concrete alternatives fast to record, rather than only assigning an overall session score [Task 2]\n  4603\t- “quick ways to highlight parts of text contributing to different aspects, ratings” -> expose categorized text highlighting and lightweight rating controls as first-class review interactions [Task 2]\n  4604\t- review should be “not too busy but stately” despite multiple AI features -> use progressive disclosure, dedicated reusable components, and Keating's existing paper/ink design system [Task 3]\n  4605\t- “for the model selector and provider for the pool you should reuse similar components from chat for this” -> reuse Chat's picker/catalog rather than create parallel selectors [Task 3]\n  4606\t\n  4607\t## Reusable knowledge\n  4608\t\n  4609\t- Review implementation is in `web/src/pages/{TrajectoryReview,TrajectoryReviewIndex}.tsx` and `web/src/keating/trajectory-{review,store,artifacts,generation,session,export}.ts`. `FeedbackEntry` is only thumbs-up/thumbs-down/confused; use a separate review schema/storage path. Stable turn/message IDs plus quote/content-hash anchors preserve annotations across replay, fork, import, and export. [Task 1]\n  4610\t- `ConversationEventStore` is privacy-redacted and cannot reconstruct tool arguments/results, thinking, or some transcripts. Capture full-fidelity review data privately; keep telemetry privacy-safe. Finalized exports use the existing `RewardedTurn`, `CanonicalTrainingRecordSchema`, `qualityForTurn`, `buildWebFineTuneExportFromSources`, and `training-archive.ts` seams. [Task 1]\n  4611\t- Rich v3 public links render `SharedTrajectoryWorkspace`; legacy v2 stays on the transcript renderer. `share-contract.ts` is the strict boundary: bound and validate IDs, fingerprints, references, parent graphs, regions, time ranges, and target keys. Projection excludes drafts, hidden tool traffic, learner uploads, model pools, candidates, secrets, and unsafe executable artifacts; Nitro and Vite `/api/share` handlers share the same path. [Task 1]\n  4612\t- The original review intent explicitly calls for sessions, turns, highlighted text spans, aspect labels/categories, ratings, failure explanations, suggested alternatives, and cross-turn trajectories. The later implementation supplies the schema/storage seams; use this product vocabulary when extending it. [Task 1][Task 2]\n  4613\t- Use `panda.config.ts` paper/ink tokens and recipes, direct `reicon-react/icons/*` imports, and proposal-only AI passes that require ordinary human acceptance. `anchorQuote` should accept exact/whitespace-reflowed citations but return no anchor instead of guessing. Shared discovery is `src/lib/model-catalog.ts`; retain `ModelSelectorDialog`'s local reducer and bridge stored pool entries through `storedModelReference` / `modelFromStoredReference`. [Task 3]\n  4614\t\n  4615\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  4616\t\n  4617\t- The worktree was heavily dirty -> protect pre-existing edits and prefer disjoint review files. Browser visual acceptance was unavailable, and Vet was skipped as requested; exercise `/review` at desktop/narrow widths and run Vet before calling the feature fully production-verified. [Task 1]\n  4618\t- One full-suite failure, `withHyperframesBridge > appends the bridge script to body fragments`, was unrelated/pre-existing dirty-tree context; do not attribute it to review/share work without isolation. [Task 1]\n  4619\t- The concept rollout alone produced no approved schema, UI, or validation. If requirements need revisiting, clarify annotation dimensions, trajectory semantics, and review workflow before changing implementation. [Task 2]\n  4620\t- Merge duplicate `@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)` object keys in Panda config: later keys silently overwrite earlier ones. Browser visual acceptance was unavailable, and the one `hyperframes-bridge` full-suite failure belonged to unrelated dirty work. [Task 3]\n  4621\t\n  4622\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/dio.computer Vite/Devenv watcher debugging\n  4623\tscope: Diagnose Vite startup crashes caused by Devenv runtime Unix sockets without broad cleanup in a dirty tree.\n  4624\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/dio.computer; reuse_rule=apply only when the startup error traverses `.devenv` runtime state; rerun `devenv up` with suitable Nix/host access before claiming success.\n  4625\t\n  4626\t## Task 1: Exclude Devenv runtime sockets from Vite's watcher\n  4627\t\n  4628\t### rollout_summary_files\n  4629\t\n  4630\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/dio.computer, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/08/17/rollout-2026-08-17T16-54-07-01a01180-c76d-76e2-819b-d7d400fbb3c8.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-17T20:57:06+00:00, thread_id=01a01180-c76d-76e2-819b-d7d400fbb3c8, partial; patch applied but final startup was user-aborted)\n  4631\t\n  4632\t### keywords\n  4633\t\n  4634\t- devenv up, Vite, Chokidar, ENXIO, native.sock, .devenv/run/processes, vite.config.ts, server.watch.ignored, Convex\n  4635\t\n  4636\t## User preferences\n  4637\t\n  4638\t- when the user asked “fix the issue that you see in vite when running devenv up” -> reproduce the actual startup failure and make the smallest scoped repair; avoid unrelated work in the heavily modified tree [Task 1]\n  4639\t\n  4640\t## Reusable knowledge\n  4641\t\n  4642\t- Devenv's supervisor creates Unix sockets in `.devenv/run/processes`; Vite/Chokidar can traverse `native.sock` and fail with `ENXIO: no such device or address, watch '.../.devenv/run/processes/native.sock'`. The targeted `vite.config.ts` fix is `server.watch.ignored: [\"**/.devenv/**\"]`; Vite merges configured patterns with built-in ignores. [Task 1]\n  4643\t\n  4644\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  4645\t\n  4646\t- Sandboxed `devenv up` may fail before Vite due to unavailable Nix cache/daemon. Use host access for this reproduction. The post-fix run was aborted, and Vet lacked credentials then exceeded its 1 MiB session-input limit; both are unverified. Rerun `devenv up` and confirm Vite remains running alongside Convex. [Task 1]\n  4647\t\n  4648\t# Task Group: browser-first learner storage and Tinker checkpoint persistence\n  4649\tscope: Design browser-local learner data, optional P2P synchronization, and server-owned Tinker checkpoint lifecycle without making native installation, peers, or browser-held credentials prerequisites.\n  4650\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Documents/Codex/2026-08-15/hey-i with related design scope=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating and /home/diogenes/Projects/twyne; reuse_rule=reuse these architecture boundaries for browser-first learner products; re-check current browser quotas and Tinker pricing/account limits before implementation.\n  4651\t\n  4652\t## Task 1: Choose browser-first storage and P2P boundaries\n  4653\t\n  4654\t### rollout_summary_files\n  4655\t\n  4656\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Documents/Codex/2026-08-15/hey-i, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/08/15/rollout-2026-08-15T18-10-28-01a00779-f4bb-7c90-8fa1-f416c34520f0.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-16T05:10:28+00:00, thread_id=01a00779-f4bb-7c90-8fa1-f416c34520f0, success; browser-local/P2P boundaries defined)\n  4657\t\n  4658\t### keywords\n  4659\t\n  4660\t- browser-first, IndexedDB, OPFS, SQLite-on-OPFS, GUN, Rindexed, WebRTC, Pear, Bare, Hyperdrive, localStorage 5 MB, persistence, resumable artifact transfer\n  4661\t\n  4662\t## Task 2: Design per-user LoRA/checkpoint storage with Tinker\n  4663\t\n  4664\t### rollout_summary_files\n  4665\t\n  4666\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Documents/Codex/2026-08-15/hey-i, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/08/15/rollout-2026-08-15T18-10-28-01a00779-f4bb-7c90-8fa1-f416c34520f0.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-16T05:10:28+00:00, thread_id=01a00779-f4bb-7c90-8fa1-f416c34520f0, success; provider ownership, lifecycle, and pricing boundaries defined)\n  4667\t\n  4668\t### keywords\n  4669\t\n  4670\t- Tinker, LoRA, tinker://, save_weights_for_sampler, save_state, SAMPLER_WEIGHTS, WEIGHTS, checkpoint TTL, project sharing, list_user_checkpoints, $0.10/GB-month\n  4671\t\n  4672\t## User preferences\n  4673\t\n  4674\t- when discussing Pear/Bare versus browser delivery, the user said they “don't want the user to really have to download anything at all” and want “something that's browser-first” -> make browser-local-first the default; native/Pear installation is optional [Task 1]\n  4675\t- the user estimated ordinary per-user data around 1–5 MB, with images potentially much larger -> separate small structured records from blob/artifact synchronization instead of treating all data as one P2P database [Task 1]\n  4676\t- when the user asked about “per user loras and checkpoints with tinker” and “limits of tinker checkpoints pricing how many projects per user etc” -> distinguish application metadata from provider-owned weights and verify current provider semantics rather than guessing [Task 2]\n  4677\t\n  4678\t## Reusable knowledge\n  4679\t\n  4680\t- Use IndexedDB for structured learner records and OPFS or SQLite-on-OPFS for larger local blobs. Storage is quota-managed and best-effort by default, so request persistent storage and provide export/backup. [Task 1]\n  4681\t- GUN is an experiment for small browser-to-browser records, not the primary database/blob store: its documented localStorage route is about 5 MB per origin, while Rindexed uses browser quota. Keep values small/split; use content-addressed, explicit, resumable transfer for PDFs, images, LoRA weights, and large generated artifacts. [Task 1]\n  4682\t- Use a hybrid architecture: browser-local authority, optional conventional encrypted account sync, WebRTC/P2P for direct pairing or live collaboration, and explicit attachment transfer. P2P still needs discovery/signaling/relay and availability planning; Pear/Bare/Hyperdrive is an optional native/offline tier. Synced learner code is versioned/untrusted data: require inspection/diff/approval and a capability boundary before worker/notebook execution. [Task 1]\n  4683\t- Tinker stores server-side checkpoints at `tinker://...`. `save_weights_for_sampler()` creates weights-only inference checkpoints; `save_state()` creates weights plus optimizer state for resumable/branchable training. They are not interchangeable. [Task 2]\n  4684\t- Tinker projects are the sharing/isolation boundary. Use one private project per personal Keating account or one per shared learner space; retain application metadata only: user/DID, project ID, base model, LoRA rank/modules, checkpoint URI, lineage, status, and expiry. Tinker operations remain behind the authenticated server. [Task 2]\n  4685\t- Lifecycle: short-TTL training-state checkpoints during active runs, one active sampler checkpoint, and a small number of rollback milestones; export/download only when explicitly requested. Queried storage pricing was `$0.10/GB-month`, but model pricing/discounts and numeric project limits are time-sensitive or unestablished, so query current provider/account limits. [Task 2]\n  4686\t\n  4687\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  4688\t\n  4689\t- Do not infer that “P2P” means infrastructure-free reliable availability or make normal browser persistence depend on peers being online. State the offline/relay tradeoff and retain local-first persistence plus account sync. [Task 1]\n  4690\t- Do not treat a sampler checkpoint as resumable training state, an unrestricted `tinker://` URI as authorization, or intermediate optimizer state as data to synchronize to every browser/device. [Task 2]\n  4691\t\n  4692\t\n  4693\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/keating landing recovery, shader texture, and expressive text effects\n  4694\tscope: Restore the full landing experience after over-minimization, selectively simplify MP4/CRT sections, and add legible kinetic texture/effects.\n  4695\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating; reuse_rule=recheck the current landing worktree before replaying recovery techniques; latest scramble/blur edits are not final-verified.\n  4696\t\n  4697\t## Task 1: Recover the landing structure and start shader, scramble, and blur effects\n  4698\t\n  4699\t### rollout_summary_files\n  4700\t\n  4701\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/08/14/rollout-2026-08-14T13-11-10-01a00141-9591-72d1-838b-21857d2eab37.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-12T21:51:19+00:00, thread_id=01a00141-9591-72d1-838b-21857d2eab37, partial; final scramble/blur pass unverified)\n  4702\t\n  4703\t### keywords\n  4704\t\n  4705\t- Landing.tsx, LandingWonder.tsx, SurfaceScreencasts.tsx, ShaderField.tsx, ScrambleText.tsx, Panda CSS, surface-tune, landing-word-arrive, kinetic-row, WebGL, CRT\n  4706\t\n  4707\t## User preferences\n  4708\t\n  4709\t- The previous minimal pass “went way overboard” -> restore the richer landing structure and simplify only targeted MP4/CRT areas, not the entire page [Task 1]\n  4710\t- Heading pills are “visual clutter” -> treat decorative eyebrow/prompt labels as optional. The user likes “texting animations and texture” plus playful shader, scramble, and blur effects suitable for a UX/UI showcase, with accessibility fallbacks [Task 1]\n  4711\t\n  4712\t## Reusable knowledge\n  4713\t\n  4714\t- The restored design has hero terminal, `SurfaceScreencasts`, kinetic teaching text, `LearningJourney`, CRT playthrough, CLI/install, and final CTA. `ShaderField.tsx` pauses/reduces for motion, visibility/off-screen, DPR, theme, and no-WebGL; `ScrambleText.tsx` uses direct DOM updates rather than React state every animation frame. [Task 1]\n  4715\t- Panda output derives from `web/panda.config.ts` into `web/styled-system/styles.css`; regenerate after keyframe/config edits. Relevant files: `Landing.tsx`, `LandingWonder.tsx`, `SurfaceScreencasts.tsx`, `ShaderField.tsx`, `ScrambleText.tsx`. [Task 1]\n  4716\t\n  4717\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  4718\t\n  4719\t- A missing `surface-tune` keyframe left grain stuck after config recovery: verify it exists in both `panda.config.ts` and generated CSS. If port 3000 is occupied, use the existing HTTP-200 server or select another port. [Task 1]\n  4720\t- Latest scramble/blur work stopped at a spend limit; rerun `cd web && bun run panda`, typecheck, `bun test`, and targeted screenshots before further iteration or completion claims. Two `test/mermaid-renderer.test.ts` TypeScript errors were pre-existing in earlier checks. [Task 1]\n  4721\t\n  4722\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/keating research-paper maintenance and reproducibility audit\n  4723\tscope: Update the Typst manuscript and published PDF from current implementation and reproducible evidence, not prose alone.\n  4724\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating; reuse_rule=reuse the audit and rerun procedure for later paper updates, but regenerate claims/results against the current code, traces, and frozen policy.\n  4725\t\n  4726\t## Task 1: Audit and update the Keating paper against v3.3.0\n  4727\t\n  4728\t### rollout_summary_files\n  4729\t\n  4730\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/08/08/rollout-2026-08-08T20-59-45-019fe408-6e87-7f22-aba8-b782f7748e6a.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-09T01:47:26+00:00, thread_id=019fe408-6e87-7f22-aba8-b782f7748e6a, success)\n  4731\t\n  4732\t### keywords\n  4733\t\n  4734\t- Typst, docs/study.typ, study-analysis.mjs, MAP-Elites, gridPath, async benchmark, me-candidate-33, reproducibility, keating-metaharness.pdf\n  4735\t\n  4736\t## User preferences\n  4737\t\n  4738\t- when the user said only “the paper needs updating” -> treat it as an implementation-grounded audit: reconcile claims, code, frozen evidence, and the published PDF rather than making prose-only edits [Task 1]\n  4739\t- preserve unrelated dirty-worktree changes during research/paper maintenance [Task 1]\n  4740\t\n  4741\t## Reusable knowledge\n  4742\t\n  4743\t- Manuscript entrypoint is `docs/study.typ`; sections live under `docs/study/sections/`, generated evidence under `docs/generated/`, frozen policy at `docs/study/evaluated-policy.json`, traces in `test/traces/`, curated data in `test/final_dataset.json`, and the published PDF at `web/public/keating-metaharness.pdf`. [Task 1]\n  4744\t- `scripts/study-analysis.mjs` must use an async ablation callback, such as `await Promise.all(ablationFields.map(async ...))`. Independent MAP-Elites stability reruns must receive a unique temporary `gridPath`, otherwise ignored persistent grids contaminate results. [Task 1]\n  4745\t- The validated frozen-policy result was `+3.982` versus default across `200/200` seeds. Corrected optimizer comparison: 11 wins, 4 ties, 15 regressions; mean −0.014. The reproducibility hash after excluding `generatedAt` was `934127a7201ecc9fd75517b350a4440983c67bb4b22a0568ce5ed8cf5ff62db7`. [Task 1]\n  4746\t- Scope boundary: distinguish systems/methods evidence from human-learning efficacy; the paper documents no human randomized trial and no reward-hacking audit. Focused tests, typechecks, JSON/diff checks, PDF text/font inspection, stale-claim scan, and rendered inspection passed. [Task 1]\n  4747\t\n  4748\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  4749\t\n  4750\t- Symptom: regeneration fails with Bun parse errors around `await`. Cause: the benchmark API became async while `.map()` remained synchronous. Fix the analysis control flow before trusting any generated number. [Task 1]\n  4751\t- Symptom: apparently independent MAP-Elites reruns disagree or become contaminated. Cause: reused persistent grid state. Pass an explicit isolated `gridPath` for every rerun. [Task 1]\n  4752\t- Vet lacked Anthropic credentials and agentic vet stalled; report it as unverified, not passed. [Task 1]\n  4753\t\n  4754\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/keating product analytics, PostHog, and Arize OpenInference\n  4755\tscope: Privacy-safe AI/product observability, activation instrumentation, consent, local relay behavior, and honest cloud-verification boundaries.\n  4756\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating; reuse_rule=reuse architecture/tests for Keating telemetry, but treat PostHog/Arize dashboards, credentials, and live collector state as time-specific.\n  4757\t\n  4758\t## Task 1: Overhaul PostHog activation and AI lifecycle telemetry\n  4759\t\n  4760\t### rollout_summary_files\n  4761\t\n  4762\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/08/04/rollout-2026-08-04T12-22-24-019fcd95-5798-7ca3-8635-b9dee667d9c1.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-04T17:10:46+00:00, thread_id=019fcd95-5798-7ca3-8635-b9dee667d9c1, success; deterministic/build/browser checks passed)\n  4763\t\n  4764\t### keywords\n  4765\t\n  4766\t- PostHog, agent_turn_started, agent_turn_completed, duration_ms, $ai_generation, TTFT, model_changed, app_version, analytics-privacy, session-replay, surveys, WebMCP\n  4767\t\n  4768\t## User preferences\n  4769\t\n  4770\t- when the user said “go all in” across “funnels to the ai at different turns durations and posthogs various libraries” -> make observability a cross-surface product pass with lifecycle timing, model provenance, success/error, model transition, and release attribution [Task 1]\n  4771\t\n  4772\t## Reusable knowledge\n  4773\t\n  4774\t- Existing PostHog integration is `web/src/lib/posthog.ts` with same-origin `/ingest`; lifecycle/privacy code is `web/src/lib/{agent-analytics,analytics-privacy,analytics-preferences}.ts`. `$ai_generation` captures trace IDs, provider/model, latency/TTFT, usage/cost, stream state/stop reason, and error classification while excluding prompts, replies, topics, and tools. [Task 1]\n  4775\t- Add app/schema/surface/build metadata; model changes carry from/to provider/model and active-stream changes are blocked/measured. Composer activation uses `chat_composer_viewed` and a 45-second `chat_activation_stalled`. Privacy masking sanitizes learning content, secrets, raw errors, route IDs, query strings, replay bodies, and headers. [Task 1]\n  4776\t\n  4777\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  4778\t\n  4779\t- Browser WebMCP duplicate declaration came from competing script loads. Share one load promise, prevent duplicate instances, reset failures for retry, and regenerate `web/src/keating/nodepod-boot-files.ts` after source changes. [Task 1]\n  4780\t\n  4781\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/keating release publication and agent-history provenance\n  4782\tscope: Investigate apparently missing Codex work and complete a Keating release across GitHub, Railway, npm, provenance, and an external install smoke test.\n  4783\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating; reuse_rule=reuse the release verification sequence, but re-check live workflows, registry state, deployment, and current Docker inputs.\n  4784\t\n  4785\t## Task 1: Reconcile Entire sessions with Codex history\n  4786\t\n  4787\t### rollout_summary_files\n  4788\t\n  4789\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/08/03/rollout-2026-08-03T21-44-29-019fca71-9721-7842-9380-62d870f724e3.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-04T06:17:57+00:00, thread_id=019fca71-9721-7842-9380-62d870f724e3, success)\n  4790\t\n  4791\t### keywords\n  4792\t\n  4793\t- Entire, Codex sessions, provenance, entire session list --json, entire checkpoint list --json, entire activity, /home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/, HEAD divergence\n  4794\t\n  4795\t## Task 2: Publish and verify Keating 3.0.0\n  4796\t\n  4797\t### rollout_summary_files\n  4798\t\n  4799\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/08/03/rollout-2026-08-03T21-44-29-019fca71-9721-7842-9380-62d870f724e3.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-04T06:17:57+00:00, thread_id=019fca71-9721-7842-9380-62d870f724e3, success; v3.0.0 published and production verified)\n  4800\t\n  4801\t### keywords\n  4802\t\n  4803\t- v3.0.0, trusted publishing, npm E404, SLSA, Railway, Dockerfile.web, .dockerignore, p2p-core, f08fccb, npx keating@3.0.0 version, /tmp\n  4804\t\n  4805\t## User preferences\n  4806\t\n  4807\t- when the user asked whether “all of that” was gone -> distinguish a missing/noisy index from deleted work; inspect the Codex archive and Git before concluding data loss [Task 1]\n  4808\t- when the user said “trust is set” -> resume the blocked publication job from context, then verify each release surface rather than asking them to restate the blocker [Task 2]\n  4809\t- release status should distinguish GitHub, Railway/production, npm, and provenance; a pushed tag is not release completion [Task 2]\n  4810\t\n  4811\t## Reusable knowledge\n  4812\t\n  4813\t- Entire’s local session list is incomplete/noisy and can contain stale, duplicate, diverged, or misattributed sessions. Cross-check `/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/`, Git history, and cloud activity; checkpoint provenance is unreliable when Entire reports divergence from `HEAD`. `entire status` can finalize exited sessions, so report that diagnostic side effect. [Task 1]\n  4814\t- Railway failed because `Dockerfile.web` omitted imported monorepo package `packages/p2p-core/src/course-feed.js`. The durable fix was to install `packages/p2p-core` production dependencies, copy its `src`, and add `.dockerignore`; the context shrank from about 2.76 GB to about 2 MB. [Task 2]\n  4815\t- For the completed 3.0.0 release: clean Docker build, Railway deployment `8147d89c-dd21-4106-980d-f70cad24d283`, production home/manifest/product-tour MP4 HTTP 200, `npm view`/`latest`, SLSA provenance, and `npx keating@3.0.0 version` from `/tmp` all provided distinct evidence. [Task 2]\n  4816\t\n  4817\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  4818\t\n  4819\t- Symptom: Entire appears to omit Codex work. Cause: its local session list is not all history. Fix: inspect Codex sessions and Git before reporting loss; do not call the index complete. [Task 1]\n  4820\t- Symptom: npm `E404` after GitHub release. Cause: trusted-publisher authorization, not necessarily a build/package defect. Fix: after authorization, rerun the failed workflow and verify registry version, dist-tag, attestation, and external-directory CLI install. [Task 2]\n  4821\t- Symptom: local Docker passes but Railway fails. Cause: Dockerfile lacks an imported workspace package/runtime dependencies. Fix: trace imports across monorepo boundaries and validate the clean Docker context. Do not run `npx` smoke tests inside the repository, where it can resolve the checkout. [Task 2]\n  4822\t\n  4823\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/keating production subscription OAuth and Railway verification\n  4824\tscope: Reload-safe subscription OAuth for OpenAI Codex, Anthropic, and GitHub Copilot, production deployment, and truthful end-to-end acceptance checks.\n  4825\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating; reuse_rule=reuse OAuth paths and verification gates for the same providers; provider authorization/account state and live credential consumption must be re-exercised.\n  4826\t\n  4827\t## Task 1: Restore production subscription OAuth end to end\n  4828\t\n  4829\t### rollout_summary_files\n  4830\t\n  4831\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/08/03/rollout-2026-08-03T19-02-36-019fc9dd-5f25-7822-81e2-7d554d1a2685.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-04T01:08:37+00:00, thread_id=019fc9dd-5f25-7822-81e2-7d554d1a2685, partial; deployed and route-checked, live OpenAI exchange/model use unverified)\n  4832\t\n  4833\t### keywords\n  4834\t\n  4835\t- oauth.ts, CloudProviderKeysSection.tsx, keating_oauth_pending, PKCE, getPendingOAuthRequest, cancelPendingOAuthRequest, /api/oauth/token, /api/oauth/refresh, OpenAI Codex, Anthropic, GitHub Copilot, Railway\n  4836\t\n  4837\t## Task 2: Add native Anthropic and OpenAI Codex subscription provider support\n  4838\t\n  4839\t### rollout_summary_files\n  4840\t\n  4841\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/08/10/rollout-2026-08-10T01-22-18-019fea1f-2888-7840-b378-17490c07c932.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-10T05:31:15+00:00, thread_id=019fea1f-2888-7840-b378-17490c07c932, success; live authorization/model request unverified)\n  4842\t\n  4843\t### keywords\n  4844\t\n  4845\t- openai-codex, openai-codex-responses, pi-ai, ChatGPT OAuth JWT, chatgpt-account-id, Anthropic OAuth, PKCE, oauth-provider-config.ts, nodepod-boot-files.ts\n  4846\t\n  4847\t## User preferences\n  4848\t\n  4849\t- OAuth should be “working in prod” and “testable end to end” -> verify provider authorization, callback completion, persistence, refresh, credential consumption, deployment, and one authenticated model request; unit tests/callback rendering alone are insufficient [Task 1]\n  4850\t- preserve unrelated dirty-worktree edits when modifying the checkout [Task 1]\n  4851\t- when the user asked to “use the anthropic and codex sdk and for sign in and support for those models in keating” -> use native provider semantics rather than ordinary API-key fallback [Task 2]\n  4852\t\n  4853\t## Reusable knowledge\n  4854\t\n  4855\t- Main files are `web/src/keating/oauth.ts`, `web/src/components/settings/CloudProviderKeysSection.tsx`, `web/src/test/oauth.test.ts`, and generated `web/src/keating/nodepod-boot-files.ts`. Store pending safe metadata under `keating_oauth_pending`; recover with `getPendingOAuthRequest()` and cancel with `cancelPendingOAuthRequest()` without exposing PKCE verifier/state. [Task 1]\n  4856\t- Pending safe metadata stays under `keating_oauth_pending`; `getPendingOAuthRequest()` must not expose PKCE verifier/state. UI tells users the expected localhost error page can be copied back into “Finish sign-in below.” [Task 1][Task 2]\n  4857\t- Codex remains a distinct `openai-codex` provider: `providerToOAuthId(\"openai\")` is intentionally null, while `openai-codex` maps to `openai-codex`. pi-ai's `openai-codex-responses` transport consumes the ChatGPT OAuth JWT directly, derives account ID, and sends Bearer plus `chatgpt-account-id`; exchanging it for a normal OpenAI API key breaks the subscription route. Anthropic OAuth passes through to the Anthropic transport, which supplies OAuth headers; do not convert it to `x-api-key`. [Task 2]\n  4858\t- OAuth token/refresh now return upstream data without the obsolete Codex `id_token` -> OpenAI API-key exchange; `web/server/api/oauth/openai-codex.ts` was removed. Regenerate `web/src/keating/nodepod-boot-files.ts` with `bun scripts/generate-nodepod-boot-files.ts` after OAuth source changes. [Task 2]\n  4859\t- 604 web tests, typecheck, and web build passed. Railway deployment `fca2021d-0965-4761-a5ee-5470da179944` succeeded; `https://keating.help/`, `/chat`, error callback, malformed token (400), and GitHub device endpoint (safe 200 response) were checked. [Task 1]\n  4860\t- The native integration passed focused OAuth/provider tests (24), full web tests (796 across 123 files), typecheck, and production build; subscription UI cards are labeled “Subscription sign-in,” with unauthenticated models routing to Models & Providers. [Task 2]\n  4861\t\n  4862\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  4863\t\n  4864\t- OpenAI reached `Phone number required`; never enter personal data. Live exchange and an authenticated model request remain unverified until the user completes provider verification. Playwriter timeouts/disconnects and the unrelated `useSeo.ts` null-remove error are browser/runtime harness issues, not OAuth route proof. [Task 1]\n  4865\t- Vet encountered an untracked-file bug then lacked Anthropic credentials; do not claim it passed. [Task 1]\n  4866\t- A focused fixture can fail when expiry falls inside the 60-second refresh window; use a test credential with more than 60 seconds remaining. Vet's `DiffApplicationError` against a dirty worktree is unverified review, not a code finding. Live OAuth authorization and model use still require provider accounts. [Task 2]\n  4867\t\n  4868\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/keating ATProto Standard.site blog and Tranquil PDS migration\n  4869\tscope: Replace the hardcoded Keating blog with PDS-sourced Standard.site records, article readers/routes/metadata, and legacy migration tooling.\n  4870\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating; reuse_rule=reuse the Standard.site record and discovery approach after checking PDS identity and deployment secrets; dry-run/local validation is not a live Tranquil publish.\n  4871\t\n  4872\t## Task 1: Migrate the blog to ATProto-backed Standard.site records\n  4873\t\n  4874\t### rollout_summary_files\n  4875\t\n  4876\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/08/03/rollout-2026-08-03T20-25-55-019fca29-a636-7362-ab57-ef3d7011da2f.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-04T01:07:08+00:00, thread_id=019fca29-a636-7362-ab57-ef3d7011da2f, success; live PDS write unavailable)\n  4877\t\n  4878\t### keywords\n  4879\t\n  4880\t- Standard.site, ATProto, site.standard.publication, site.standard.document, at.markpub.markdown, AtprotoBlog.tsx, atproto-blog.ts, KEATING_BLOG_PDS_URL, Tranquil, publish-standard-site-blog.ts\n  4881\t\n  4882\t## User preferences\n  4883\t\n  4884\t- when the user asked for Standard.site/ATProto posts and a future dedicated Tranquil PDS -> make portable PDS/protocol records the source of truth instead of local hardcoded JSX [Task 1]\n  4885\t- preserve extensive pre-existing worktree changes during the migration [Task 1]\n  4886\t\n  4887\t## Reusable knowledge\n  4888\t\n  4889\t- Use one `site.standard.publication` and `site.standard.document` per article with `at.markpub.markdown`; retain `textContent` as plaintext fallback. Reader/parser code is `web/src/keating/standard-site.ts`, `web/server/utils/atproto-blog.ts`, and `web/src/pages/AtprotoBlog.tsx`; routes include `/api/blog`, `/blog`, `/blog/**`, and `/.well-known/site.standard.publication`. [Task 1]\n  4890\t- Resolve a configured handle/DID through its DID document and permit `KEATING_BLOG_PDS_URL` as a local/staged Tranquil override. The migration script converts 46 legacy posts to 47 records in dry-run; inject `KEATING_BLOG_PDS_URL`, `KEATING_BLOG_IDENTIFIER`, and `KEATING_BLOG_APP_PASSWORD` through secret store, never shell arguments/history. [Task 1]\n  4891\t- Focused publisher/parser/server tests (11), typecheck, and Vite/Nitro build passed. A Chrome pass rendered `/blog` cleanly. [Task 1]\n  4892\t\n  4893\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  4894\t\n  4895\t- A shared feed request must not be cancelled merely because one page unmounts; avoid aborting it and guard only state updates with an `active` flag to prevent cross-route races. If Playwriter relay times out, isolated browser sessions were more reliable. [Task 1]\n  4896\t- Live Tranquil write was intentionally not run because account/credentials were absent, and Vet was unavailable/stalled; do not claim PDS publication or Vet review. [Task 1]\n  4897\t\n  4898\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/keating Coming Up spaced repetition and Anki portability\n  4899\tscope: Dedicated dynamic Kanban review workspace, learner priority layered over SM-2 scheduling, and safe native Anki APKG import/export.\n  4900\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating; reuse_rule=reuse for flashcard/SRS/Anki changes; preserve source identities and separately validate browser interaction plus package round trips.\n  4901\t\n  4902\t## Task 1: Build the Coming Up priority-aware Kanban\n  4903\t\n  4904\t### rollout_summary_files\n  4905\t\n  4906\t- rollout_summaries/2026-08-03T23-06-09-m6ds-coming_up_spaced_repetition_kanban_anki_import.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/08/03/rollout-2026-08-03T19-06-09-019fc9e0-a23d-75f2-9d3f-77f036eb728a.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-03T23:59:51+00:00, thread_id=019fc9e0-a23d-75f2-9d3f-77f036eb728a, success)\n  4907\t\n  4908\t### keywords\n  4909\t\n  4910\t- /coming-up, ComingUp.tsx, coming-up.ts, SM-2, Focus, Maintain, Low, drag-and-drop, srs.ts, storage.ts\n  4911\t\n  4912\t## Task 2: Implement native Anki import/export\n  4913\t\n  4914\t### rollout_summary_files\n  4915\t\n  4916\t- rollout_summaries/2026-08-03T23-06-09-m6ds-coming_up_spaced_repetition_kanban_anki_import.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/08/03/rollout-2026-08-03T19-06-09-019fc9e0-a23d-75f2-9d3f-77f036eb728a.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-03T23:59:51+00:00, thread_id=019fc9e0-a23d-75f2-9d3f-77f036eb728a, success)\n  4917\t\n  4918\t### keywords\n  4919\t\n  4920\t- anki-package.ts, .apkg, collection.anki21b, collection.anki21, collection.anki2, sql.js, fzstd, noteGuid, noteId, cardId, deckId, mergeAnkiDeck\n  4921\t\n  4922\t## User preferences\n  4923\t\n  4924\t- “coming up should be a dedicated and dynamic kanban like interface with dragable items” -> favor direct-manipulation task workspace over a static analytics panel [Task 1]\n  4925\t- “figure the rest” / “your choice” -> when the core interaction is clear, make coherent secondary decisions rather than seeking unnecessary follow-ups [Task 1]\n  4926\t- make it “easy for people to move anki stuff in and out” -> prioritize native `.apkg` round trips while retaining CSV/TSV fallback [Task 2]\n  4927\t\n  4928\t## Reusable knowledge\n  4929\t\n  4930\t- `/coming-up` uses `web/src/pages/ComingUp.tsx`; `web/src/keating/coming-up.ts` derives due flashcards, open checks, and needs-review topics into draggable Focus/Maintain/Low lanes. Dragging changes learner intent only; do not falsify SM-2 due dates or hide overdue work. Provide keyboard/touch controls as a non-drag alternative. [Task 1]\n  4931\t- `web/src/keating/anki-package.ts` supports native `collection.anki21b`, `.anki21`, `.anki2`, CSV import, and TSV fallback. Convert HTML/cloze to inert review text; exclude media and executable templates. Preserve `noteGuid`, `noteId`, `cardId`, `deckId`; `mergeAnkiDeck` preserves newer review state. [Task 2]\n  4932\t- Browser checks covered drag persistence, review reducing due 6 -> 5, desktop/mobile/light/dark layouts, and native browser export. Focused tests (14), full suite (617), typecheck, Panda/Vite/Nitro/PWA build, and diff check passed. [Task 1][Task 2]\n  4933\t\n  4934\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  4935\t\n  4936\t- Generated IDs can duplicate material on repeated Anki export/import. Preserve original Anki IDs/GUIDs and make stable IDs only for cards without source metadata. [Task 2]\n  4937\t- This checkout lacked a local Impeccable bundle; use `/home/diogenes/.agents/skills/impeccable/...` when the project shim yields `MODULE_NOT_FOUND`. Vet lacked Anthropic credentials; report it as unverified. [Task 1][Task 2]\n  4938\t\n  4939\t\n  4940\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/twyne structured application errors and safe hosted-AI UX\n  4941\tscope: Twyne application-error contract, notices, offline UX, sanitized diagnostics, and interview recovery.\n  4942\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne; reuse_rule=reuse for AI-error/fallback changes; test remaining unexercised boundaries and browser failure behavior.\n  4943\t\n  4944\t## Task 1: Establish and finish AppError foundation across interview/rubric paths\n  4945\t\n  4946\t### rollout_summary_files\n  4947\t\n  4948\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/07/30/rollout-2026-07-30T21-23-33-019fb5c4-fa2f-7431-86be-cedd140eb5a7.jsonl, updated_at=2026-07-24T05:07:45+00:00, thread_id=019fb5c4-fa2f-7431-86be-cedd140eb5a7, success; targeted test/build evidence)\n  4949\t\n  4950\t### keywords\n  4951\t\n  4952\t- AppError, ApplicationNotice, GlobalConnectivityBanner, ConvexError, application-diagnostics, createProductionConvexLogger, no-silent-fallback, pendingWriterText\n  4953\t\n  4954\t## Reusable knowledge\n  4955\t\n  4956\t- Core error seams are `src/types/application-errors.ts`, `src/utils/application-errors.ts`, `src/utils/application-diagnostics.ts`, `convex/lib/applicationErrors.ts`, and `src/components/ui/application-notice.tsx`. Production Convex clients use `createProductionConvexLogger()` to forward sanitized metadata rather than raw errors. [Task 1]\n  4957\t- `ApplicationNotice` has error, warning, and outage variants with severity-appropriate accessibility semantics. `GlobalConnectivityBanner` is wired in `src/root.tsx`; it reflects online/offline state while reassuring users that local work remains safe. Conversational interview recovery retains `pendingWriterText`, transcript/draft state, retry, and form fallback. [Task 1]\n  4958\t\n  4959\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  4960\t\n  4961\t- The full parallel `bun test` suite and targeted Playwright production-failure tests were not run. The validated boundary is 33 targeted tests plus typecheck, Storybook, and production builds; do not promote this to whole-app browser-failure proof. [Task 1]\n  4962\t\n  4963\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/keating upstream integration and verified 3.10.0 minor release\n  4964\tscope: Preserve a complete local change set while integrating upstream via PR, then complete a minor release with independent artifact, registry, production, and install proof.\n  4965\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating; reuse_rule=reuse the integration/release procedure only after auditing the current branch, upstream, generated artifacts, hook state, and intended worktree scope.\n  4966\t\n  4967\t## Task 1: Integrate local Artifact Atlas/OpenUI work and merge PR #7\n  4968\t\n  4969\t### rollout_summary_files\n  4970\t\n  4971\t- rollout_summaries/2026-08-26T22-46-56-wMah-keating_pr_merge_and_v3_10_release.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/08/26/rollout-2026-08-26T18-46-56-01a04041-4b5f-7d31-bc09-8898971264ed.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-27T03:31:25+00:00, thread_id=01a04041-4b5f-7d31-bc09-8898971264ed, success)\n  4972\t\n  4973\t### keywords\n  4974\t\n  4975\t- codex/artifact-atlas-animation-demotion, origin/main, PR #7, 57b22adf, f49c617e, nodepod-boot-files, Artifact-Atlas, LearningAnimation, git merge --no-ff\n  4976\t\n  4977\t## Task 2: Publish Keating v3.10.0\n  4978\t\n  4979\t### rollout_summary_files\n  4980\t\n  4981\t- rollout_summaries/2026-08-26T22-46-56-wMah-keating_pr_merge_and_v3_10_release.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/08/26/rollout-2026-08-26T18-46-56-01a04041-4b5f-7d31-bc09-8898971264ed.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-27T03:31:25+00:00, thread_id=01a04041-4b5f-7d31-bc09-8898971264ed, success; public release verified)\n  4982\t\n  4983\t### keywords\n  4984\t\n  4985\t- v3.10.0, release.yml, sync-version.ts, bumpy, 33035774405, npm-provenance, node:20-bookworm, Package manifest ok (1150 files)\n  4986\t\n  4987\t## User preferences\n  4988\t\n  4989\t- when upstream had “awesome changes that we worked on before and really want to keep” -> preserve upstream and local changes together; resolve conflicts deliberately rather than overwriting either side [Task 1]\n  4990\t- when the user asked to put “our current changes all of them into a pr” -> audit and stage the complete intended local scope explicitly while protecting unrelated files [Task 1]\n  4991\t- when the user asked “can you make a new release minor?” -> perform the full release lifecycle, not merely a version bump [Task 2]\n  4992\t\n  4993\t## Reusable knowledge\n  4994\t\n  4995\t- Create a branch from `main`, commit the audited local scope, merge `origin/main`, and regenerate `web/src/keating/nodepod-boot-files.ts`. In this integration the generated snapshot had no diff after merge, confirming combined sources; PR #7 squash-merged as `f49c617e`, with local/remote/GitHub `main` matching. [Task 1]\n  4996\t- v3.10.0 synchronized 11 surfaces, used actual Toronto release date `2026-08-26`, and staged exactly 15 intended release files. Full root/web tests, build, version/diff/Atlas checks, and package manifest verification passed. Workflow `33035774405`, four archives/digests, npm latest/SLSA provenance, production routes/version, remote refs, and clean `node:20-bookworm` CLI install were verified. Related skill: skills/release-publication-verification/SKILL.md [Task 2]\n  4997\t\n  4998\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  4999\t\n  5000\t- Bumpy generated UTC `2026-08-27` changelog dates while the repository release date was `2026-08-26` -> normalize both changelogs before committing. [Task 2]\n  5001\t- Native `node-pty` compilation on the host was contaminated by Guix/Nix include/library/glibc state -> use an isolated clean container for external-install proof. Node engine/vulnerability warnings do not negate a successful install/CLI smoke test; report them separately. [Task 2]\n  5002\t- A stale Entire/prek shim blocked push -> independent root/web pre-push suites must pass before a narrowly documented `git push --no-verify`. Vet was unverified, not approval. [Task 1][Task 2]\n  5003\t\n  5004\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/keating unified devenv up multi-surface workspace\n  5005\tscope: Configure one Process Compose-backed `devenv up` for terminal shell, OpenTUI, web, Electron, Expo web, and Storybook; retain the unresolved live-process boundary.\n  5006\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating; reuse_rule=reuse process names, PTY configuration, ports, and logging approach, but rerun every surface live before claiming the workspace is healthy.\n  5007\t\n  5008\t## Task 1: Configure the multi-surface devenv workspace\n  5009\t\n  5010\t### rollout_summary_files\n  5011\t\n  5012\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/08/27/rollout-2026-08-27T14-05-16-01a04465-caaa-7662-b7a4-003e0b1975cc.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-27T18:24:30+00:00, thread_id=01a04465-caaa-7662-b7a4-003e0b1975cc, partial; only shell/TUI/web live-started)\n  5013\t\n  5014\t### keywords\n  5015\t\n  5016\t- devenv up, devenv.nix, process-compose, terminal-shell, tui, web, desktop, mobile-web, storybook, port 3000, port 8081, port 6006, readiness check fail\n  5017\t\n  5018\t## User preferences\n  5019\t\n  5020\t- when the user asked for a “devenv up command that starts the terminal shell, the tui, the web app, and the desktop application” and added “should also start storybook” -> include the complete adjacent developer workspace, not only the first listed apps [Task 1]\n  5021\t\n  5022\t## Reusable knowledge\n  5023\t\n  5024\t- In devenv 2.2.2, set `process.manager.implementation = \"process-compose\"`; use `process.managers.process-compose.tui.enable = true` and `processes.<name>.process-compose.is_interactive = true` for PTY shell/TUI processes. Six configured names are `terminal-shell`, `tui`, `web`, `desktop`, `mobile-web`, and `storybook`; web is 3000, Expo web 8081, Storybook 6006, and desktop waits for web. [Task 1]\n  5025\t- Electron defaults `KEATING_DEV_SERVER` to `http://localhost:3000` but keeps overrides; Expo needs `\"web\": \"expo start --web --port 8081\"`. `devenv info` exposes all six processes. Direct P2P build plus Electron/mobile TypeScript checks passed. [Task 1]\n  5026\t- Use `process-compose -U -u \"$PC_SOCKET_PATH\" process logs mobile-web,storybook,desktop -n 200 --raw-log` to isolate live process failures. [Task 1]\n  5027\t\n  5028\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  5029\t\n  5030\t- A first Process Compose run can spend a long time compiling `devenv-tasks` in Nix -> inspect the process tree before calling it a deadlock. [Task 1]\n  5031\t- Static validation is insufficient: shell, TUI, and web started, but `mobile-web` failed readiness on `http://127.0.0.1:8081` with `connection refused`, Storybook failed, and desktop did not launch successfully. Re-run each independently and inspect logs before completion claims. [Task 1]\n  5032\t- Patch context with incorrect separators failed -> make narrow context patches. Vet was unavailable/unverified. [Task 1]\n  5033\t\n  5034\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/twyne ATProto OAuth, Convex sync authorization, and safe global error toasts\n  5035\tscope: Diagnose browser auth/sync evidence, avoid ATProto scope and DPoP bootstrap failures, guard Convex mutations by real identity, and present normalized recoverable errors.\n  5036\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne; reuse_rule=reuse these local contracts for Twyne auth/error work; recheck OAuth grants, live Convex deployment/logs, and dirty worktree before a deployment claim.\n  5037\t\n  5038\t## Task 1: Fix ATProto profile hydration and OAuth initialization\n  5039\t\n  5040\t### rollout_summary_files\n  5041\t\n  5042\t- rollout_summaries/2026-08-27T00-08-45-AuPp-twyne_atproto_convex_auth_error_toasts.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/08/26/rollout-2026-08-26T20-08-45-01a0408c-3631-7712-bc6f-569ae582aa0b.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-27T03:08:44+00:00, thread_id=01a0408c-3631-7712-bc6f-569ae582aa0b, success)\n  5043\t\n  5044\t### keywords\n  5045\t\n  5046\t- ATProto, Bluesky, ScopeMissingError, app.bsky.actor.getProfile, PUBLIC_BSKY_APPVIEW, DPoP, use_dpop_nonce, initSessionPromise, resolveAtprotoProfile\n  5047\t\n  5048\t## Task 2: Gate Convex sync on authenticated identity\n  5049\t\n  5050\t### rollout_summary_files\n  5051\t\n  5052\t- rollout_summaries/2026-08-27T00-08-45-AuPp-twyne_atproto_convex_auth_error_toasts.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/08/26/rollout-2026-08-26T20-08-45-01a0408c-3631-7712-bc6f-569ae582aa0b.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-27T03:08:44+00:00, thread_id=01a0408c-3631-7712-bc6f-569ae582aa0b, success)\n  5053\t\n  5054\t### keywords\n  5055\t\n  5056\t- Convex, userComments:deleteComment, Not signed in, identityType: unknown, hasAuthenticatedConvexIdentity, convexAuthenticated, Better Auth, ctx.auth.getUserIdentity\n  5057\t\n  5058\t## Task 3: Normalize errors and render global toasts\n  5059\t\n  5060\t### rollout_summary_files\n  5061\t\n  5062\t- rollout_summaries/2026-08-27T00-08-45-AuPp-twyne_atproto_convex_auth_error_toasts.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/08/26/rollout-2026-08-26T20-08-45-01a0408c-3631-7712-bc6f-569ae582aa0b.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-27T03:08:44+00:00, thread_id=01a0408c-3631-7712-bc6f-569ae582aa0b, success)\n  5063\t\n  5064\t### keywords\n  5065\t\n  5066\t- application-errors.ts, reportApplicationError, GlobalApplicationToasts, ApplicationNotice, connectApplicationErrorToastHost, Comment sync is paused, AUTHENTICATION_REQUIRED, AUTHENTICATION_FAILED\n  5067\t\n  5068\t## User preferences\n  5069\t\n  5070\t- when the user supplied console logs as evidence -> trace every reported request to its actual code path and distinguish actionable errors from preload noise [Task 1]\n  5071\t\n  5072\t## Reusable knowledge\n  5073\t\n  5074\t- Hydrate public ATProto profiles through `PUBLIC_BSKY_APPVIEW = \"https://public.api.bsky.app\"` while preserving the OAuth session DID; existing `atproto blob:image/* include:site.standard.authFull` does not grant arbitrary audience-bound RPC scope. Use module-level `initSessionPromise` to prevent rotating DPoP nonce races; the library already captures/retries `DPoP-Nonce`. [Task 1]\n  5075\t- `hasAuthenticatedConvexIdentity(state)` requires `provider === \"convex\"`, `convexAuthenticated === true`, and a non-null user. Set the flag only after Better Auth installs a Convex token; gate comments/collaboration/sharing client calls, but retain server `ctx.auth.getUserIdentity()` and owner-scoped checks. A Convex client alone is not authenticated. [Task 2]\n  5076\t- `reportApplicationError()` normalizes/captures safe diagnostics and dispatches toasts; diagnostics-only `reportApplicationDiagnostic()` should not toast. `GlobalApplicationToasts` deduplicates, caps notices at two, auto-dismisses after 12 seconds, provides recovery links, respects reduced motion, and queues at most two startup notices until hydration. Use `reportCommentSyncError(operation, err)` with `comment-sync` / `Comment sync is paused`. [Task 3]\n  5077\t- Deterministic evidence: 1,280 pass, 39 skip, 0 fail; TypeScript, scoped lint, production build, and diff check passed. No deployment occurred and unrelated dirty worktree edits were preserved. [Task 1][Task 2][Task 3]\n  5078\t\n  5079\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  5080\t\n  5081\t- Do not add arbitrary Bluesky RPC scopes only to hydrate public profile data; use public AppView. A raw DID shown after lookup failure is a fallback leak, not aliasing. [Task 1]\n  5082\t- `identityType: \"unknown\"` / `Not signed in` means the mutation did not reach its delete logic -> fix the client auth boundary; never weaken Convex auth checks. [Task 2]\n  5083\t- Bun's EventTarget rejected the constructed toast event in tests -> inject a minimal event target instead of replacing global `window`. Vet timed out without findings, so it is unverified. [Task 3]\n  5084\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/notorganic-provider public identity, landing, and developer docs surfaces\n  5085\tscope: Maintain consumer-facing Not Organic account/identity UX separately from technical integration docs, including static docs-service build and Railway wiring.\n  5086\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/notorganic-provider; reuse_rule=recheck active auth state, deployment/DNS/Railpack schema, and browser availability; deterministic build proof is not visual or deployed proof.\n  5087\t\n  5088\t## Task 1: Redesign signed-out portal, public landing, and docs service\n  5089\t\n  5090\t### rollout_summary_files\n  5091\t\n  5092\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/notorganic-provider, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/08/31/rollout-2026-08-31T16-08-41-01a05970-3732-7901-89a3-ec7ffff03ac5.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-31T20:30:49+00:00, thread_id=01a05970-3732-7901-89a3-ec7ffff03ac5, partial; deterministic checks pass, no browser or deployment proof)\n  5093\t\n  5094\t### keywords\n  5095\t\n  5096\t- identity-shell, identity-creek-bg.webp, Continue with your handle, Your account wherever your ideas go, docs.notorganic.info, Caddyfile, Dockerfile.docs, docs.railpack.json, check-railpack.ts, PKCE S256, DPoP, WebP\n  5097\t\n  5098\t## Task 2: Create and browser-verify Not Organic social preview cards\n  5099\t\n  5100\t### rollout_summary_files\n  5101\t\n  5102\t- rollout_summaries/2026-09-04T22-27-06-lggp-notorganic_social_preview_cards_browser_verified.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/notorganic-provider, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/04/rollout-2026-09-04T18-27-06-01a06e88-6080-7922-b01d-98b04a48b7d1.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-05T00:53:12+00:00, thread_id=01a06e88-6080-7922-b01d-98b04a48b7d1, success; local crawler/browser proof)\n  5103\t\n  5104\t### keywords\n  5105\t\n  5106\t- Open Graph, Twitter cards, 1200x630, notorganic-home-v2.jpg, apps/landing/brand/social, verification.json, landing-social.playwriter.mjs, CSP, new Image(), bunx playwriter@latest\n  5107\t\n  5108\t## User preferences\n  5109\t\n  5110\t- signed-out identity UX uses “Your Not Organic account” and “Continue with your handle” rather than operator language -> write plain, user-facing account copy [Task 1]\n  5111\t- consumer pages should answer what Not Organic is, connected products, what stays with the person, and where it is managed; keep developer navigation visible but secondary and send implementation detail to dedicated docs [Task 1]\n  5112\t- visual edits should preserve recognizable source composition (creek, foliage, flowers, sunlight, framing, source-derived colors) rather than replace it with generic imagery [Task 1]\n  5113\t- when the user said “show that in the browser” -> for visual artifacts, open the finished asset and provide direct visual proof when possible. Preserve original sibling-project marks in derived marketing visuals rather than redrawing/synthesizing them. [Task 2]\n  5114\t\n  5115\t## Reusable knowledge\n  5116\t\n  5117\t- Apply `.identity-shell` only when `session` is absent in `apps/portal/src/App.tsx`; authenticated portal views retain their current layout. The WebP is `apps/portal/public/identity-creek-bg.webp` (~163 KB) and must be present in `dist/portal` and HTTP-served. White over `#4d7c67` was adjusted to 4.78:1 contrast. [Task 1]\n  5118\t- Public landing at `apps/landing/` intentionally avoids infrastructure/token/wallet/provider details, includes responsive/focus/skip-link/reduced-motion behavior, and keeps `https://docs.notorganic.info` secondary. [Task 1]\n  5119\t- Static JavaScript-free docs are `apps/docs/index.html`/`styles.css`; Caddy/Docker/Railpack/Railway wiring is in `infra/docs/`, `.railway/railway.ts`, package/devenv configuration, domains/docs/cost docs. Use `bun run build:landing && bun run build:docs && bun run build:portal`, `bun run typecheck`, `bun test`, `bun scripts/check-railpack.ts`, and local HTTP probes. [Task 1]\n  5120\t- Final social cards are `apps/landing/brand/social/notorganic-{home,company,billing,privacy,terms}-v2.jpg`: static 1200x630 JPEGs (~108–111 KB) with versioned HTTPS Open Graph/X metadata in five landing pages. `bun run scripts/build-landing.ts`, `bun run typecheck`, `bun test scripts/build-landing.test.ts`, and `rtk git diff --check` passed; `docs/brand/notorganic/social/verification.json` records JavaScript-disabled crawler checks (200, `image/jpeg`, decoded dimensions, zero logs). [Task 2]\n  5121\t- For JPEG proof under CSP, fetch bytes and decode with `new Image()` on a separate page. Direct navigation opens Chromium's image viewer, whose injected styles can cause CSP conflict and `Execution context was destroyed`. Use `bunx playwriter@latest` in a dedicated session when direct `playwriter` is unavailable. [Task 2]\n  5122\t\n  5123\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  5124\t\n  5125\t- Build/static probes cannot prove crop, responsive overlap, or rendered usability when no browser is connected -> record visual proof as outstanding, not passed. Vet was unavailable (credential/fallback hang), not passed. [Task 1]\n  5126\t- `scripts/check-railpack.ts` can fail `ConnectionRefused` while fetching the live schema -> retry only when network access is available; validation then reported four matching configs. Split same-file multi-operation patches. [Task 1]\n  5127\t- Local production-build/Caddy proof does not verify deployment, CDN/social-platform cache refresh, or production URLs. [Task 2]\n  5128\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/stich Bun-native release tooling and devenv hooks\n  5129\tscope: Replace Bumpy with Bun-native versioning while retaining tracked hooks, annotated-tag checks, and the repository's namespaced devenv workflow.\n  5130\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/stich; reuse_rule=recheck the dirty tree, package version, tags, scripts, and current devenv task graph before a real release; this rollout prepared the workflow but did not create v0.1.1 or publish.\n  5131\t\n  5132\t## Task 1: Migrate Bumpy to Bun versioning with tracked hooks\n  5133\t\n  5134\t### rollout_summary_files\n  5135\t\n  5136\t- rollout_summaries/2026-09-02T04-11-11-cNgU-stich_bun_versioning_devenv_hooks.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/stich, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/02/rollout-2026-09-02T00-11-11-01a06050-51e2-7762-b9f9-7ad24dafccfc.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-02T04:18:55+00:00, thread_id=01a06050-51e2-7762-b9f9-7ad24dafccfc, partial; safeguards installed, no real release yet)\n  5137\t\n  5138\t### keywords\n  5139\t\n  5140\t- bun pm version, Bumpy, .githooks/pre-push, core.hooksPath, stich:hooks:install, stich:release:check, release:check, annotated tag, v0.1.1, input_too_large\n  5141\t\n  5142\t## User preferences\n  5143\t\n  5144\t- when changing version tooling, the user said “i expect githooks and stuff to run and be added for this repo” -> retain and verify equivalent tracked hooks and release safeguards rather than deleting them with Bumpy [Task 1]\n  5145\t- after the initial implementation, the user said “remember to devenv for this stuff” -> expose/document Stich release operations through namespaced devenv tasks and `devenv shell --`, not bare host commands [Task 1]\n  5146\t\n  5147\t## Reusable knowledge\n  5148\t\n  5149\t- Stich root scripts are `prepare`, `hooks:install`, `preversion`, `postversion`, `release:check`, `release:version: bun pm version`, and `release:publish: git push --follow-tags`. `scripts/check-release-version.ts` checks SemVer, workspace/app alignment, annotated `v<package.version>`, tagged root-manifest equality, and unexpected `v*` tags at `HEAD`. [Task 1]\n  5150\t- `.githooks/pre-push` runs the release check only for a pushed `refs/tags/v*`, leaving ordinary branch pushes alone. `devenv tasks run stich:hooks:install` configures `core.hooksPath=.githooks`; release sequence is `devenv shell -- bun run release:version -- patch`, `devenv tasks run stich:release:check`, then `devenv shell -- bun run release:publish`. [Task 1]\n  5151\t- `@varlock/bumpy` and `.bumpy/` were removed; `bun install --lockfile-only` and `bun pm why @varlock/bumpy` confirmed removal. [Task 1]\n  5152\t\n  5153\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  5154\t\n  5155\t- `Release check failed: missing v0.1.1; create releases with bun run release:version` is expected while `package.json` says `0.1.1` without an annotated tag. Do not fabricate a tag merely to make the guard pass. [Task 1]\n  5156\t- Aggregate `bun run typecheck` was interrupted; only web/core/UI/API/AI workspace results are evidence. Vet was unavailable: API credentials were absent and the dirty-tree fallback failed with `input_too_large`; report both as unverified. [Task 1]\n  5157\t\n  5158\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/stich approved raster identity and logo production\n  5159\tscope: Explore, select, and integrate faithful Stich raster logo families from approved visual references; use when producing a mark, lockup, favicon, download icon, or hero artwork.\n  5160\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/stich; reuse_rule=the reported integration paths require direct artifact/source verification before reuse; the approved reference, rather than a hand-reconstructed vector, is the visual authority.\n  5161\t\n  5162\t## Task 1: Produce Stich logo directions and use-case variants\n  5163\t\n  5164\t### rollout_summary_files\n  5165\t\n  5166\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/stich, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/02/rollout-2026-09-02T02-38-15-01a060d6-f5bf-7b41-afc0-9e8810963df7.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-02T07:30:03+00:00, thread_id=01a060d6-f5bf-7b41-afc0-9e8810963df7, partial; reported integration is not independently evidenced)\n  5167\t\n  5168\t### keywords\n  5169\t\n  5170\t- approved-logo-raster-production, Stich, LCARS, docs/brand/weave/raster, apps/web/public/brand/raster, stich-signal-emblem.png, signal-deck-hero.png, favicon, alpha, imagegen\n  5171\t\n  5172\t## Task 2: Preserve logo-production lessons as a reusable Codex skill\n  5173\t\n  5174\t### rollout_summary_files\n  5175\t\n  5176\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/stich, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/02/rollout-2026-09-02T02-38-15-01a060d6-f5bf-7b41-afc0-9e8810963df7.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-02T07:30:03+00:00, thread_id=01a060d6-f5bf-7b41-afc0-9e8810963df7, success; global skill validated)\n  5177\t\n  5178\t### keywords\n  5179\t\n  5180\t- approved-logo-raster-production, skill-creator, quick_validate.py, PyYAML, uv run --with pyyaml, agents/openai.yaml, 25–64 character description\n  5181\t\n  5182\t## User preferences\n  5183\t\n  5184\t- when requesting ten logo directions, a top-three selection, and text/no-text, favicon, downloads, and hero variants -> provide comparative exploration followed by a complete use-case-specific asset family, not one generic logo file [Task 1]\n  5185\t- when an approved raster identity exists -> preserve its silhouette, proportions, spacing, typography, and color relationships; do not simplify distinctive artwork into generic SVG geometry unless explicitly requested and reviewed [Task 1]\n  5186\t- when the user said “okay add what you learned to a skill” -> preserve proven workflow lessons as reusable agent guidance [Task 2]\n  5187\t\n  5188\t## Reusable knowledge\n  5189\t\n  5190\t- Existing Stich references are `docs/store-spread/stich-signal-emblem.png`, `docs/store-spread/signal-deck-hero.png`, and mobile icon/favicon assets; likely web integration points are `SiteNav.tsx`, `Hero.tsx`, and `__root.tsx`. Reported output paths are `docs/brand/weave/raster` and `apps/web/public/brand/raster`. [Task 1]\n  5191\t- Preserve approved raster-logo workflow lessons locally: create separate deliverables, verify the actual alpha channel, preserve originals before trim/resize, make compact favicon variants, inspect at target size, and distinguish build/browser proof from asset generation. [Task 2]\n  5192\t\n  5193\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  5194\t\n  5195\t- A checkerboard is not alpha proof -> inspect the actual alpha channel and target-size rendering. The visible rollout lacks file listings, diffs, build output, and browser output for the reported Stich asset integration, so verify directly before calling it complete. [Task 1]\n  5196\t- `grep: unrecognized option '--glob'` came from invoking `/usr/bin/grep` with ripgrep flags -> use `rg` for glob-aware searches. Bound long-running asset commands and inspect outputs incrementally. [Task 1]\n  5197\t- Skill initialization rejected a 71-character UI description, and metadata generation lacked PyYAML -> keep the short description within 25–64 characters and use `uv run --with pyyaml` for isolated generation. [Task 2]\n  5198\t\n  5199\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/stich commercial pricing, Not Organic boundaries, and voice direction\n  5200\tscope: Maintain truthful Stich pricing and plan provider-backed billing/voice without exposing credentials or presenting unavailable hosted capabilities as live.\n  5201\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/stich and /home/diogenes/Projects/notorganic-provider; reuse_rule=recheck gateway health, OpenBao, Creem catalog/API, DNS/TLS, webhook delivery, and current deployment before enabling checkout or hosted intelligence.\n  5202\t\n  5203\t## Task 1: Implement and deploy fail-closed pricing with Creem and Not Organic\n  5204\t\n  5205\t### rollout_summary_files\n  5206\t\n  5207\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/stich, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/01/rollout-2026-09-01T23-36-31-01a06030-926c-7f33-a4dc-c6d1b05f58de.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-02T04:44:45+00:00, thread_id=01a06030-926c-7f33-a4dc-c6d1b05f58de, partial; production surface deployed, commercial E2E unproven)\n  5208\t\n  5209\t### keywords\n  5210\t\n  5211\t- pricing.tsx, Creem, Not Organic, stable pack_id, /v1/billing/checkout, idempotency-key, PKCE S256, DPoP, OpenBao, Checkout unavailable, wallet, signed webhook\n  5212\t\n  5213\t## Task 2: Define shared-wallet voice behavior\n  5214\t\n  5215\t### rollout_summary_files\n  5216\t\n  5217\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/stich, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/01/rollout-2026-09-01T23-36-31-01a06030-926c-7f33-a4dc-c6d1b05f58de.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-02T04:44:45+00:00, thread_id=01a06030-926c-7f33-a4dc-c6d1b05f58de, partial; design direction only)\n  5218\t\n  5219\t### keywords\n  5220\t\n  5221\t- VOICE SHOULD SHORTEN TRIAGE, NOT TURN MAIL INTO A CALL CENTER, /v1/audio/speech, /v1/audio/transcriptions, /v1/realtime, consent, reservation, hard stop\n  5222\t\n  5223\t## User preferences\n  5224\t\n  5225\t- when asked to make pricing “ready with creem and notorganic” -> separate code/deployment evidence from a real checkout, webhook, entitlement, usage, reconciliation, and refund proof path [Task 1]\n  5226\t- hosted checkout was intentionally fail-closed while the provider gateway and infrastructure were not proven -> preserve truthful disabled states rather than exposing a misleading Connect or Buy control [Task 1]\n  5227\t- when asked to “think about voice integration” -> treat voice as provider-owned, shared-wallet, consented, cost-visible capability rather than a provider-specific credential or isolated UI [Task 2]\n  5228\t\n  5229\t## Reusable knowledge\n  5230\t\n  5231\t- Not Organic owns identity, checkout, signed webhooks, wallet, usage, entitlements, and provider secrets; Stich consumes wallet state through stable server-resolved pack/plan IDs. `POST /v1/billing/checkout` needs HTTPS `return_url` and `idempotency-key`. Browser auth is PKCE S256 plus a device-bound DPoP key; never put Creem, OpenBao, or model-provider credentials in Stich client code. [Task 1]\n  5232\t- Deployed pricing tiers were Free, Personal `$10/month`, Household `$25/month`, and Studio `$50/month`, with hosted intelligence credits and one-cycle rollover text. Deterministic proof: Stich `bun run typecheck` and `bun run test`; Not Organic `bun run check` 119 pass/0 fail; Railway deployment `c6a8bf6b-c3c7-489e-ab51-cb9a0493e2d2` reached `SUCCESS`; mobile inspection saw truthful disabled controls. [Task 1]\n  5233\t- Planned modes are dictating a reply, reading a thread aloud, and talking through the inbox. Dictation must be bounded/editable before send; speech streams without client credentials or durable mail content; realtime needs explicit consent, reservation, visible cost, and a hard stop. [Task 2]\n  5234\t\n  5235\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  5236\t\n  5237\t- `https://api.notorganic.info/healthz` returned 404 and the gateway was not proven bootable with OpenBao/provider infrastructure -> do not enable checkout or hosted inference until health, OpenBao, Creem catalog/API, DNS/TLS, and signed webhook delivery are validated. Catalog-description sync is not charge/webhook/wallet/debit/reconciliation/refund proof. [Task 1]\n  5238\t- Poll Railway through BUILDING -> DEPLOYING -> SUCCESS and inspect logs; never treat an intermediate deployment status as terminal. Vet lacked credentials, so its review remains unverified. [Task 1]\n  5239\t\n  5240\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/stich native Devenv modernization, Railway email E2E, and isolated deployment\n  5241\tscope: Operate the native Devenv developer/release workflow, Railway/Stalwart email E2E, and safe isolated web deployment.\n  5242\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/stich; reuse_rule=recheck Devenv version/task graph, dirty-tree scope, Railway linkage, signing credentials, domain TLS, and untracked `railpack.json` before release or deploy mutations.\n  5243\t\n  5244\t## Task 1: Modernize developer/release workflow and verify Railway email E2E\n  5245\t\n  5246\t### rollout_summary_files\n  5247\t\n  5248\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/stich, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/01/rollout-2026-09-01T17-46-49-01a05ef0-6979-7cd1-80e9-8084cf168128.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-02T02:12:08+00:00, thread_id=01a05ef0-6979-7cd1-80e9-8084cf168128, partial; full checks/E2E passed but stable publication blocked)\n  5249\t\n  5250\t### keywords\n  5251\t\n  5252\t- devenv tasks, processes.*, services.*, Mailpit, stich:check, stich:e2e:railway, Stalwart, JMAP, Electrobun, gitPackage, signing, railpack.json\n  5253\t\n  5254\t## Task 2: Deploy web to an isolated Railway project\n  5255\t\n  5256\t### rollout_summary_files\n  5257\t\n  5258\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/stich, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/01/rollout-2026-09-01T17-46-49-01a05ef0-6979-7cd1-80e9-8084cf168128.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-02T02:12:08+00:00, thread_id=01a05ef0-6979-7cd1-80e9-8084cf168128, success; isolated production deployment and smoke checks passed)\n  5259\t\n  5260\t### keywords\n  5261\t\n  5262\t- Railway, continuwuity-matrix, railpack.json, local source input, Bun could not find a package.json file to install from, Bun 1.3.13, f59d6b6d-b09f-49a0-94fa-df0d829ffc6b, stich-production-4bc6.up.railway.app\n  5263\t\n  5264\t## User preferences\n  5265\t\n  5266\t- when the user said “devenv up, tasks and no just commands or mise” and “devenv process and services as well” -> use native `devenv tasks`, `processes.*`, and supported `services.*`; do not add a parallel Just/Mise interface [Task 1]\n  5267\t- when requesting modernization plus “test with an end to end email on railway” -> include dependency/tooling compatibility work and real provider-backed mail verification, not only local tests [Task 1]\n  5268\t- when deployment was requested and the checkout was linked to unrelated `continuwuity-matrix` -> verify Railway project/service linkage before mutating external state [Task 2]\n  5269\t\n  5270\t## Reusable knowledge\n  5271\t\n  5272\t- `devenv.nix` defines native web, desktop, mobile web, Storybook, and opt-in MCP processes, plus Mailpit SMTP/UI ports 1025/8025. `devenv tasks run stich:check` passed typechecks, tests, web/server smoke, release preflight self-test, workflow validation, and full Playwright; `stich:e2e:railway` verified disposable-account submit, inbox/body read, Sent copy, invalid identity, and cleanup. [Task 1]\n  5273\t- Validate `devenv tasks list --no-tui` and live processes, not static Nix alone. Candidate alignment was v0.1.1, but macOS/Windows signing credentials and custom-domain TLS blocked stable publication; no stable tag/push was created. [Task 1]\n  5274\t- Safe Railway target was production project/service `stich`, deployment `f59d6b6d-b09f-49a0-94fa-df0d829ffc6b`, public URL `https://stich-production-4bc6.up.railway.app`. Successful remote build used Bun 1.3.13/Node 22, `bun install --frozen-lockfile`, `bun run build:web`, and `bun run --cwd apps/web start`; public smoke covered `/`, `/guide`, assets, HEAD, and missing asset `404` with `nosniff`. [Task 2]\n  5275\t\n  5276\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  5277\t\n  5278\t- `devenv up -d` did not retain a process manager and created orphaned process groups/port collisions -> use one foreground `devenv up` for live verification and clean only identified project groups. Devenv 2.2.2 initially hit `attribute 'gitPackage' missing`; fix/validate task listing before calling migration ready. [Task 1]\n  5279\t- Custom Railpack toolchain inputs omitted repo context, giving `Bun could not find a package.json file to install from` -> add `{ \"local\": true, \"include\": [\".\"] }` to the install step. Never deploy solely from local Railway linkage. [Task 2]\n  5280\t- Vet had no usable verdict; stable release is separate from unsigned/dev checks. `railpack.json` remained untracked and must be deliberately included in a future release commit. [Task 1][Task 2]\n  5281\t\n  5282\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/traction cross-surface analytics and Railpack delivery\n  5283\tscope: Build an agent-first analytics product across web, desktop, mobile, CLI, and TUI with privacy-aware telemetry and Bun/Railpack deployment.\n  5284\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/traction; reuse_rule=recheck Railway linkage, live health, and npm authentication before deployment/publish claims.\n  5285\t\n  5286\t## Task 1: Create Traction architecture, foundation, dashboard, and deployment\n  5287\t\n  5288\t### rollout_summary_files\n  5289\t\n  5290\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/traction, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/03/rollout-2026-09-03T18-30-48-01a06965-66ba-7bd0-8a04-a54e56cb185d.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-27T23:35:30+00:00, thread_id=01a06965-66ba-7bd0-8a04-a54e56cb185d, success)\n  5291\t\n  5292\t### keywords\n  5293\t\n  5294\t- traction, packages/spec, packages/grip, packages/evals, telemetry opt-out, DO_NOT_TRACK, DID, Jetstream, Railpack, railway up --ci --service traction, NIXPACKS\n  5295\t\n  5296\t## User preferences\n  5297\t\n  5298\t- track activity across “desktop, mobile, cli, tui, and web,” but retain an event-spec seam if SDK/TUI may be “something altogether” from the agent product; document tradeoffs instead of forcing unresolved choices [Task 1]\n  5299\t- “telemetry should be opt out actually” -> disclose default collection and support disable controls, DO_NOT_TRACK, CI suppression, and strict minimization [Task 1]\n  5300\t\n  5301\t## Reusable knowledge\n  5302\t\n  5303\t- Traction's primary output is a coverage-aware daily briefing and agent-ranked dashboard. Use ATProto DID as join key, loopback OAuth for CLI/TUI, persistent Jetstream, daily GitHub traffic polling, and never expose source credentials in public PDS. [Task 1]\n  5304\t- `packages/spec` implements validation, argv allowlist scrubbing, policy/notice, and O_APPEND JSONL spool; 8 writers x 60 records produced 480 valid, untorn lines. `packages/grip` status colors are not chart-series colors. [Task 1]\n  5305\t- Deploy with `builder = \"RAILPACK\"` and `railway up --ci --service traction`; legacy NIXPACKS and stray Dockerfiles are failure sources. `@traction/spec` is publishable after `npm login`; grip/evals are private. [Task 1]\n  5306\t\n  5307\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  5308\t\n  5309\t- Verify `pwd`/absolute paths after `cd`; local Railpack may fail on `.devenv` symlinks, so a clean `git archive` build better matches Railway. Browser visual confirmation remained unavailable despite deterministic checks. [Task 1]\n  5310\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/twyne character-aware narration, premium GPT Live voice, and native Typst workflow\n  5311\tscope: Extend Twyne’s author-aware editor interaction and native Typst authoring without exposing provider credentials or replacing the visual editor.\n  5312\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne; reuse_rule=recheck the current dirty tree, browser/device access, Not Organic provider state, and deployment before treating Live voice as production-ready.\n  5313\t\n  5314\t## Task 1: Preserve persona identity through narration playback\n  5315\t\n  5316\t### rollout_summary_files\n  5317\t\n  5318\t- rollout_summaries/2026-09-26T10-01-32-fcwe-twyne_character_aware_narration_gpt_live_voice_desk.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/26/rollout-2026-09-26T06-01-32-01a0dd29-b2ed-78c0-b5b2-143eed227156.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-26T10:38:47+00:00, thread_id=01a0dd29-b2ed-78c0-b5b2-143eed227156, success; focused speech tests passed)\n  5319\t\n  5320\t### keywords\n  5321\t\n  5322\t- speech.ts, global-speech-player.tsx, speak-button.tsx, persona-note-panel.tsx, personas.ts, speechVoice, speechVoices, Supertonic, lecteur\n  5323\t\n  5324\t## Task 2: Implement premium duplex GPT Live voice with revision-safe editor actions\n  5325\t\n  5326\t### rollout_summary_files\n  5327\t\n  5328\t- rollout_summaries/2026-09-26T10-01-32-fcwe-twyne_character_aware_narration_gpt_live_voice_desk.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/26/rollout-2026-09-26T06-01-32-01a0dd29-b2ed-78c0-b5b2-143eed227156.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-26T10:38:47+00:00, thread_id=01a0dd29-b2ed-78c0-b5b2-143eed227156, partial; deterministic checks/builds passed, production/browser/provider proof open)\n  5329\t\n  5330\t### keywords\n  5331\t\n  5332\t- GPT Live, gpt-live-1, /v1/live/sessions, /api/live, live-voice-desk.tsx, live-voice-workspace.ts, LIVE_SESSION_BUDGET_MICROS, LIVE_ACTION_BUDGET_MICROS, Convex, welcome grant, delegation, session.closed\n  5333\t\n  5334\t## Task 3: Implement and deploy native Typst editing, proof, PDF, and persistence\n  5335\t\n  5336\t### rollout_summary_files\n  5337\t\n  5338\t- rollout_summaries/2026-09-26T11-02-50-0rjp-twyne_native_typst_editor_implementation_deployment.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/26/rollout-2026-09-26T07-02-50-01a0dd61-d08c-7f71-9e6c-24cf8966c3df.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-29T01:38:36+00:00, thread_id=01a0dd61-d08c-7f71-9e6c-24cf8966c3df, success; CI, Railway, and live proof/PDF/persistence smoke passed)\n  5339\t\n  5340\t### keywords\n  5341\t\n  5342\t- Typst, @myriaddreamin/typst.ts, CodeMirror, ProseMirror, typst-workspace, typst-code-editor, format, typstSource, compiler.worker.ts, mammoth.browser, import.meta.glob, Convex, Railway\n  5343\t\n  5344\t## User preferences\n  5345\t\n  5346\t- when narration is invoked from a character’s “lecteur,” the user wanted the player to know “what character was being called” -> resolve and display that persona’s voice by default, never a generic voice when identity is known. [Task 1]\n  5347\t- when requesting “full dubplex voice” that can “edit and add information searach and interact with the app,” and premium/credit use -> show captions, action state, consent, wallet/cost ceilings, and require approval before manuscript mutation. [Task 2]\n  5348\t- when starting the Typst plan, the user said “focus on implementation” and “focus on implementation not test” -> ship the functional slice before expanding tests, while retaining the visual/page editor as an opt-in Typst source workflow rather than replacing it. [Task 3]\n  5349\t\n  5350\t## Reusable knowledge\n  5351\t\n  5352\t- `src/utils/speech.ts` owns the shared narration queue/player; persona identity flows through `author`, `label`, `voice`, and provider-specific `voices`. `src/utils/personas.ts` holds display names, IDs, roles, voice overrides, and direction. Do not pass generic OpenAI voice names directly to Supertonic/browser narration; map them to supported embeddings or persona overrides. [Task 1]\n  5353\t- Twyne’s Live client uses Not Organic `/v1/live/sessions` through same-origin `/api/live`; provider billing/entitlements remain authoritative and Twyne never receives an OpenAI key. The implementation reserves ceilings of `$0.50` per session and `$0.05` per delegated action, not quoted rates. [Task 2]\n  5354\t- Draft edits are proposals first: later spoken/UI approval checks manuscript revision, rejects ambiguous repeated passages, preserves rich text, remains undoable, and stops when the workspace/folio changes. Only provider-returned research results may be described as web results; local placeholders are rejected. [Task 2]\n  5355\t- The provider patch adds a one-time `$2.50` Twyne welcome allowance separate from Keating, with idempotency and paid-history exclusions. Delegated replies are accepted only for IDs observed from trusted upstream events; inspect the separate provider dirty tree before follow-up work. [Task 2]\n  5356\t- Native Typst documents use `@myriaddreamin/typst.ts` in a client worker with bundled fonts/assets, CodeMirror source editing, proof-page rendering, downloadable source, and PDF export; source edits compile without a server round trip. `format` and `typstSource` persistence/sync fields retain HTML projection compatibility for legacy documents and integrations. [Task 3]\n  5357\t- Core paths are `src/utils/typst/{document,serialize,export,client,session,compiler.worker}.ts`, `src/components/editor/{typst-workspace,typst-code-editor}.tsx`, `src/components/editor/extensions/raw-typst.ts`, `src/utils/{idb,convex-sync}.ts`, `convex/schema.ts`, and `convex/sync.ts`. Production smoke at `https://twyne.love/editor/` rendered two proof pages, produced a `%PDF-` download, preserved content on reload, and showed no runtime errors. [Task 3]\n  5358\t\n  5359\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  5360\t\n  5361\t- Feature checks do not establish real microphone permissions, visual UI, deployed WebSocket behavior, provider availability/credit debit, or production consent. Full typecheck initially exposed unrelated language/i18n errors; report targeted validation separately. [Task 2]\n  5362\t- A browser-only exporter leaked through shared serialization (`mammoth/mammoth.browser`) and failed Convex typecheck -> keep shared escaping in `src/utils/typst/string.ts` and keep backend imports browser-independent. Guard `import.meta.glob` tests with `const supportsViteModules = typeof import.meta.glob === \"function\"`; Bun does not provide it. [Task 3]\n  5363\t- Direct browser-global assignment/restoration caused 105 Bun failures -> save/restore descriptors with `Object.defineProperty`. Before push run `bun run lint`, `bun run fmt.check`, Convex typecheck, and the full suite; final validation was `1605 pass`, `40 skip`, `0 fail`, GitHub run `36508550529` success, and Railway deployment `2261ee43-1626-496b-8388-5e0c2d749989` successful. `bun add` can need `BUN_TMPDIR=/tmp BUN_INSTALL_CACHE_DIR=/tmp/twyne-bun-cache`. [Task 3]\n  5364\t\n  5365\t# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/keating manifesto assets, Skate secret map, and repository-organization planning\n  5366\tscope: Locate manifesto media and current secret consumers, then plan a staged research-publication/repository reorganization without premature migration or cleanup.\n  5367\tapplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating with planning context cwd=/home/diogenes/Documents/Codex/2026-09-25/i-want-to-use-the-devenv; reuse_rule=asset and current Skate paths are checkout-specific; the organization proposal must start with a fresh read-only audit and user approval.\n  5368\t\n  5369\t## Task 1: Locate the Keating manifesto video and its source project\n  5370\t\n  5371\t### rollout_summary_files\n  5372\t\n  5373\t- rollout_summaries/2026-09-25T16-27-10-ULkv-keating_manifesto_and_skate_secret_usage.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/25/rollout-2026-09-25T12-27-10-01a0d964-6404-7ef1-a73a-12e506f8b563.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-25T22:56: