]\n    66\t- when mentioning Google sign-in and easy connection setup -> include understandable consent/onboarding, not only API plumbing [Task 1]\n    67\t\n    68\t## Reusable knowledge\n    69\t\n    70\t- Not Organic is the control plane: portal sessions and upstream credentials stay server-owned; public clients validate HTTPS origins, same-origin callbacks, PKCE S256, narrow allowlisted scopes, and DPoP-bound tokens; gateway checks capabilities immediately before dispatch. [Task 1]\n    71\t- Google Drive remains unimplemented. The narrow researched direction is Google Picker with `drive.file`, and product UI must label it “Coming soon,” never as an available connector. [Task 1][Task 2]\n    72\t- Keating selects account sources, browses/reads resources, separately opts into tools, and reviews exact arguments; cancellation, account change, revocation, tool-definition change, and failed/lost-network calls fail closed. [Task 2]\n    73\t- Twyne trusted Convex actions bind verified DID/sessionVersion to fresh DPoP tokens. Research requires enabling research, choosing a source search tool, and selecting “Your MCP servers”; sign-out, revocation, and schema changes clear/fail closed. [Task 3]\n    74\t\n    75\t## Failures and how to do differently\n    76\t\n    77\t- GitNexus `ENOENT: .../.gitnexus/registry-lock` -> run `node .gitnexus/run.cjs analyze --index-only`, but treat absent/truncated graph edges as unknown and confirm with `rg`/source. Preserve unrelated dirty provider work; aggregate impact reports are not feature-local evidence. [Task 1]\n    78\t- Focused Keating validation does not prove web production readiness: pre-existing assistant-ui/PDF/router incompatibilities blocked the full web build, and neither deployment nor live-account flow was tested. [Task 2]\n    79\t- `ERR_CONNECTION_REFUSED` after an owned Twyne preview stopped is an environment/process condition, while localhost-to-deployed Convex CORS preflight must be verified separately; neither