{"timestamp":"2026-10-05T16:15:30.386Z","ordinal":42501,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a10537-909f-77a3-96d8-dd07161f91ae","turn_id":"01a10ca3-f662-7822-9d58-47f08a989563","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-d6109e6b-34a0-4551-b409-04c96fb3cc0b","process_id":"84360","command":["/bin/bash","-lc","rtk proxy sed -n '20,64p' convex/knowledge.ts"],"cwd":"file:///home/diogenes/Projects/twyne","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"rtk proxy sed -n '20,64p' convex/knowledge.ts"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"    throw new ConvexError(\"Invalid knowledge source.\");\n  return encodeURIComponent(value);\n}\nasync function request(\n  ctx: ActionCtx,\n  path: string,\n  call = false,\n  body?: unknown,\n): Promise<unknown> {\n  const identity = await ctx.auth.getUserIdentity();\n  if (!identity)\n    throw new ConvexError(\"Sign in with Not Organic to use account sources.\");\n  const link = await ctx.runQuery(linkRef, {\n    productSubject: identity.subject || identity.tokenIdentifier,\n  });\n  if (!link)\n    throw new ConvexError(\n      \"Reconnect your Not Organic account to use account sources.\",\n    );\n  try {\n    const token = await issueNotOrganicAccessToken({\n      did: link.did,\n      sessionVersion: link.sessionVersion,\n      feature: \"knowledge\",\n      capabilities: [call ? \"knowledge:tools\" : \"knowledge:read\"],\n    });\n    return await providerJsonRequest<unknown>(\n      path,\n      token,\n      body === undefined\n        ? { signal: AbortSignal.timeout(30_000) }\n        : {\n            method: \"POST\",\n            body: JSON.stringify(body),\n            signal: AbortSignal.timeout(30_000),\n          },\n      { issuer: notOrganicIssuer(), feature: \"knowledge\" },\n    );\n  } catch (error) {\n    const message = error instanceof Error ? error.message : \"\";\n    if (/\\(403\\)|knowledge_access_denied/.test(message))\n      throw new ConvexError(\n        \"Access to this source was revoked. Share it with Twyne in Not Organic, then refresh sources.\",\n      );\n    if (/\\(409\\)|knowledge_tool_changed/.test(message))\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"    throw new ConvexError(\"Invalid knowledge source.\");\n  return encodeURIComponent(value);\n}\nasync function request(\n  ctx: ActionCtx,\n  path: string,\n  call = false,\n  body?: unknown,\n): Promise<unknown> {\n  const identity = await ctx.auth.getUserIdentity();\n  if (!identity)\n    throw new ConvexError(\"Sign in with Not Organic to use account sources.\");\n  const link = await ctx.runQuery(linkRef, {\n    productSubject: identity.subject || identity.tokenIdentifier,\n  });\n  if (!link)\n    throw new ConvexError(\n      \"Reconnect your Not Organic account to use account sources.\",\n    );\n  try {\n    const token = await issueNotOrganicAccessToken({\n      did: link.did,\n      sessionVersion: link.sessionVersion,\n      feature: \"knowledge\",\n      capabilities: [call ? \"knowledge:tools\" : \"knowledge:read\"],\n    });\n    return await providerJsonRequest<unknown>(\n      path,\n      token,\n      body === undefined\n        ? { signal: AbortSignal.timeout(30_000) }\n        : {\n            method: \"POST\",\n            body: JSON.stringify(body),\n            signal: AbortSignal.timeout(30_000),\n          },\n      { issuer: notOrganicIssuer(), feature: \"knowledge\" },\n    );\n  } catch (error) {\n    const message = error instanceof Error ? error.message : \"\";\n    if (/\\(403\\)|knowledge_access_denied/.test(message))\n      throw new ConvexError(\n        \"Access to this source was revoked. Share it with Twyne in Not Organic, then refresh sources.\",\n      );\n    if (/\\(409\\)|knowledge_tool_changed/.test(message))\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":17942},"formatted_output":"    throw new ConvexError(\"Invalid knowledge source.\");\n  return encodeURIComponent(value);\n}\nasync function request(\n  ctx: ActionCtx,\n  path: string,\n  call = false,\n  body?: unknown,\n): Promise<unknown> {\n  const identity = await ctx.auth.getUserIdentity();\n  if (!identity)\n    throw new ConvexError(\"Sign in with Not Organic to use account sources.\");\n  const link = await ctx.runQuery(linkRef, {\n    productSubject: identity.subject || identity.tokenIdentifier,\n  });\n  if (!link)\n    throw new ConvexError(\n      \"Reconnect your Not Organic account to use account sources.\",\n    );\n  try {\n    const token = await issueNotOrganicAccessToken({\n      did: link.did,\n      sessionVersion: link.sessionVersion,\n      feature: \"knowledge\",\n      capabilities: [call ? \"knowledge:tools\" : \"knowledge:read\"],\n    });\n    return await providerJsonRequest<unknown>(\n      path,\n      token,\n      body === undefined\n        ? { signal: AbortSignal.timeout(30_000) }\n        : {\n            method: \"POST\",\n            body: JSON.stringify(body),\n            signal: AbortSignal.timeout(30_000),\n          },\n      { issuer: notOrganicIssuer(), feature: \"knowledge\" },\n    );\n  } catch (error) {\n    const message = error instanceof Error ? error.message : \"\";\n    if (/\\(403\\)|knowledge_access_denied/.test(message))\n      throw new ConvexError(\n        \"Access to this source was revoked. Share it with Twyne in Not Organic, then refresh sources.\",\n      );\n    if (/\\(409\\)|knowledge_tool_changed/.test(message))\n"},"started_at_ms":1791216930386,"completed_at_ms":1791216930386}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-05T16:15:30.418Z","ordinal":42502,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a10537-909f-77a3-96d8-dd07161f91ae","turn_id":"01a10ca3-f662-7822-9d58-47f08a989563","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-1182deb5-5600-4186-ab4d-163dddf2ba68","process_id":"57506","command":["/bin/bash","-lc","rtk proxy sed -n '1,140p' desktop/gpui/fixtures/connected-work/execution.md"],"cwd":"file:///home/diogenes/Projects/twyne","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"rtk proxy sed -n '1,140p' desktop/gpui/fixtures/connected-work/execution.md"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"# Connected and generated UI work\n\nThe full hosted desktop remains the reference. The running preview is the\nimmutable offline build; this wave must preserve its library and leave its\nwindow open. Existing web, Convex and configuration edits are protected.\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart TD\n  S[Current Source contracts] --> P[Four component prop schemas]\n  S --> T[Append-only tool streams]\n  S --> A[Native auth and sync transport contract]\n  S --> E[Deterministic writer seeding and offline fill]\n  P --> T\n  P --> V[GPUI tool bodies and retained controls]\n  T --> I[Editor and provider integration]\n  V --> I\n  E --> I\n  A --> C[Trusted sign-in and connected library adapter]\n  C --> K[Account knowledge transport and controls]\n  I --> Q[Source comparisons and actual native interaction]\n  K --> Q\n  Q --> F[Full port audit]\n```\n\n| Node | Ownership | Deliverable and gate |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| P | Sakana fugu-max; proposed `src/gen_ui/props.rs` only | Source Zod-compatible validation, Unicode and numeric edge cases; Root compares with the unchanged Source oracle |\n| T | Sakana fugu-max; proposed `src/gen_ui/stream.rs` only | Original cumulative JSONL append contract; uses the fixed P API; no writer-field rewrites or invented recovery behavior |\n| A | Sakana fugu-max; bounded contract JSON only | Actual auth/sync names, wire fields, missing trust and concrete adapter boundary; no account or registration action |\n| V | Root; new native tool view | Original four components, labels, local working state and Source-derived styling |\n| E | Sakana fugu-max proposal; Root adoption | Original sentence spans, seeds and no-provider branches compared with the unchanged Source oracle |\n| I | Root; shared exports, editor and provider coordinators | Actual accepted requests and retained UI; stale folio/range/revision checks; meaningful undo and failure behavior |\n| C/K | Root, after A | Trusted native sign-in, account-scoped sync/conflicts and knowledge sources/tool review; foundations alone do not enable capability |\n| Q | Root; Cargo and runtime ownership | Focused checks, Source/native interaction and render comparisons; real providers/account proof remain separate |\n\nWorkers return proposals without executing tools or changing files. Root reviews\nand adopts each proposal in a separate directory before production edits.\nDisjoint input bundles and their SHA256 pins are retained under\n`target/verification/sakana-genui-inputs`. Root owns manifests, barrels,\n`app.rs`, `main.rs`, every runtime and the user preview. No worker may revert\nor overwrite another participant's work.\n\nWave one runs P/T/A in parallel after the P function signature is fixed.\nRoot works on V while they run. Integration follows review and Source checks;\nrendered/runtime checks follow a successful build. This graph does not claim\nthat AI, account sync, knowledge sources or generated UI are complete.\n\nP/T/E now have integrated native/Source contract comparisons. V has compiled\ntool bodies, retained controls and typed requests; its actual editor mounting,\nSource/native geometry and interaction gates remain open. I/C/K remain\nimplementation work. The user's preview uses its existing immutable binary.\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"# Connected and generated UI work\n\nThe full hosted desktop remains the reference. The running preview is the\nimmutable offline build; this wave must preserve its library and leave its\nwindow open. Existing web, Convex and configuration edits are protected.\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart TD\n  S[Current Source contracts] --> P[Four component prop schemas]\n  S --> T[Append-only tool streams]\n  S --> A[Native auth and sync transport contract]\n  S --> E[Deterministic writer seeding and offline fill]\n  P --> T\n  P --> V[GPUI tool bodies and retained controls]\n  T --> I[Editor and provider integration]\n  V --> I\n  E --> I\n  A --> C[Trusted sign-in and connected library adapter]\n  C --> K[Account knowledge transport and controls]\n  I --> Q[Source comparisons and actual native interaction]\n  K --> Q\n  Q --> F[Full port audit]\n```\n\n| Node | Ownership | Deliverable and gate |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| P | Sakana fugu-max; proposed `src/gen_ui/props.rs` only | Source Zod-compatible validation, Unicode and numeric edge cases; Root compares with the unchanged Source oracle |\n| T | Sakana fugu-max; proposed `src/gen_ui/stream.rs` only | Original cumulative JSONL append contract; uses the fixed P API; no writer-field rewrites or invented recovery behavior |\n| A | Sakana fugu-max; bounded contract JSON only | Actual auth/sync names, wire fields, missing trust and concrete adapter boundary; no account or registration action |\n| V | Root; new native tool view | Original four components, labels, local working state and Source-derived styling |\n| E | Sakana fugu-max proposal; Root adoption | Original sentence spans, seeds and no-provider branches compared with the unchanged Source oracle |\n| I | Root; shared exports, editor and provider coordinators | Actual accepted requests and retained UI; stale folio/range/revision checks; meaningful undo and failure behavior |\n| C/K | Root, after A | Trusted native sign-in, account-scoped sync/conflicts and knowledge sources/tool review; foundations alone do not enable capability |\n| Q | Root; Cargo and runtime ownership | Focused checks, Source/native interaction and render comparisons; real providers/account proof remain separate |\n\nWorkers return proposals without executing tools or changing files. Root reviews\nand adopts each proposal in a separate directory before production edits.\nDisjoint input bundles and their SHA256 pins are retained under\n`target/verification/sakana-genui-inputs`. Root owns manifests, barrels,\n`app.rs`, `main.rs`, every runtime and the user preview. No worker may revert\nor overwrite another participant's work.\n\nWave one runs P/T/A in parallel after the P function signature is fixed.\nRoot works on V while they run. Integration follows review and Source checks;\nrendered/runtime checks follow a successful build. This graph does not claim\nthat AI, account sync, knowledge sources or generated UI are complete.\n\nP/T/E now have integrated native/Source contract comparisons. V has compiled\ntool bodies, retained controls and typed requests; its actual editor mounting,\nSource/native geometry and interaction gates remain open. I/C/K remain\nimplementation work. The user's preview uses its existing immutable binary.\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":16722},"formatted_output":"# Connected and generated UI work\n\nThe full hosted desktop remains the reference. The running preview is the\nimmutable offline build; this wave must preserve its library and leave its\nwindow open. Existing web, Convex and configuration edits are protected.\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart TD\n  S[Current Source contracts] --> P[Four component prop schemas]\n  S --> T[Append-only tool streams]\n  S --> A[Native auth and sync transport contract]\n  S --> E[Deterministic writer seeding and offline fill]\n  P --> T\n  P --> V[GPUI tool bodies and retained controls]\n  T --> I[Editor and provider integration]\n  V --> I\n  E --> I\n  A --> C[Trusted sign-in and connected library adapter]\n  C --> K[Account knowledge transport and controls]\n  I --> Q[Source comparisons and actual native interaction]\n  K --> Q\n  Q --> F[Full port audit]\n```\n\n| Node | Ownership | Deliverable and gate |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| P | Sakana fugu-max; proposed `src/gen_ui/props.rs` only | Source Zod-compatible validation, Unicode and numeric edge cases; Root compares with the unchanged Source oracle |\n| T | Sakana fugu-max; proposed `src/gen_ui/stream.rs` only | Original cumulative JSONL append contract; uses the fixed P API; no writer-field rewrites or invented recovery behavior |\n| A | Sakana fugu-max; bounded contract JSON only | Actual auth/sync names, wire fields, missing trust and concrete adapter boundary; no account or registration action |\n| V | Root; new native tool view | Original four components, labels, local working state and Source-derived styling |\n| E | Sakana fugu-max proposal; Root adoption | Original sentence spans, seeds and no-provider branches compared with the unchanged Source oracle |\n| I | Root; shared exports, editor and provider coordinators | Actual accepted requests and retained UI; stale folio/range/revision checks; meaningful undo and failure behavior |\n| C/K | Root, after A | Trusted native sign-in, account-scoped sync/conflicts and knowledge sources/tool review; foundations alone do not enable capability |\n| Q | Root; Cargo and runtime ownership | Focused checks, Source/native interaction and render comparisons; real providers/account proof remain separate |\n\nWorkers return proposals without executing tools or changing files. Root reviews\nand adopts each proposal in a separate directory before production edits.\nDisjoint input bundles and their SHA256 pins are retained under\n`target/verification/sakana-genui-inputs`. Root owns manifests, barrels,\n`app.rs`, `main.rs`, every runtime and the user preview. No worker may revert\nor overwrite another participant's work.\n\nWave one runs P/T/A in parallel after the P function signature is fixed.\nRoot works on V while they run. Integration follows review and Source checks;\nrendered/runtime checks follow a successful build. This graph does not claim\nthat AI, account sync, knowledge sources or generated UI are complete.\n\nP/T/E now have integrated native/Source contract comparisons. V has compiled\ntool bodies, retained controls and typed requests; its actual editor mounting,\nSource/native geometry and interaction gates remain open. I/C/K remain\nimplementation work. The user's preview uses its existing immutable binary.\n"},"started_at_ms":1791216930418,"completed_at_ms":1791216930418}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-05T16:15:30.500Z","ordinal":42503,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a10cd9-4ec4-7063-ad29-bc0a3f7818c2","call_id":"call_vvHpxxicf3CQzLgt0ZrNhEpG","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.2 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"check\":0,\"chunk_id\":\"085625\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000017942,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":379,\"output\":\"    throw new ConvexError(\\\"Invalid knowledge source.\\\");\\n  return encodeURIComponent(value);\\n}\\nasync function request(\\n  ctx: ActionCtx,\\n  path: string,\\n  call = false,\\n  body?: unknown,\\n): Promise<unknown> {\\n  const identity = await ctx.auth.getUserIdentity();\\n  if (!identity)\\n    throw new ConvexError(\\\"Sign in with Not Organic to use account sources.\\\");\\n  const link = await ctx.runQuery(linkRef, {\\n    productSubject: identity.subject || identity.tokenIdentifier,\\n  });\\n  if (!link)\\n    throw new ConvexError(\\n      \\\"Reconnect your Not Organic account to use account sources.\\\",\\n    );\\n  try {\\n    const token = await issueNotOrganicAccessToken({\\n      did: link.did,\\n      sessionVersion: link.sessionVersion,\\n      feature: \\\"knowledge\\\",\\n      capabilities: [call ? \\\"knowledge:tools\\\" : \\\"knowledge:read\\\"],\\n    });\\n    return await providerJsonRequest<unknown>(\\n      path,\\n      token,\\n      body === undefined\\n        ? { signal: AbortSignal.timeout(30_000) }\\n        : {\\n            method: \\\"POST\\\",\\n            body: JSON.stringify(body),\\n            signal: AbortSignal.timeout(30_000),\\n          },\\n      { issuer: notOrganicIssuer(), feature: \\\"knowledge\\\" },\\n    );\\n  } catch (error) {\\n    const message = error instanceof Error ? error.message : \\\"\\\";\\n    if (/\\\\(403\\\\)|knowledge_access_denied/.test(message))\\n      throw new ConvexError(\\n        \\\"Access to this source was revoked. Share it with Twyne in Not Organic, then refresh sources.\\\",\\n      );\\n    if (/\\\\(409\\\\)|knowledge_tool_changed/.test(message))\\n\"}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"check\":1,\"chunk_id\":\"d161f7\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.00001055,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":395,\"output\":\"export async function refreshAccountKnowledge(): Promise<AccountSource[]> {\\n  const active = client,\\n    epoch = generation,\\n    request = ++catalogRequest;\\n  if (!active || !snapshot.account) return [];\\n  snapshot.loading = true;\\n  snapshot.error = \\\"\\\";\\n  publish();\\n  try {\\n    const raw = (await active.action(refs.sources, {})) as { data?: unknown };\\n    if (epoch !== generation || active !== client || request !== catalogRequest)\\n      return [];\\n    if (!Array.isArray(raw?.data)) throw new Error(\\\"Invalid sources response\\\");\\n    if (JSON.stringify(raw.data).length > 1_048_576)\\n      throw new Error(\\\"Source catalog is too large\\\");\\n    if (raw.data.length > 100) throw new Error(\\\"Source catalog is too large\\\");\\n    const seen = new Set<string>();\\n    const sources: AccountSource[] = raw.data.map((value) => {\\n      if (!value || typeof value !== \\\"object\\\")\\n        throw new Error(\\\"Invalid source catalog\\\");\\n      const source = value as AccountSource;\\n      if (\\n        typeof source.id !== \\\"string\\\" ||\\n        !source.id ||\\n        source.id.length > 256 ||\\n        seen.has(source.id) ||\\n        typeof source.label !== \\\"string\\\" ||\\n        source.label.length > 200 ||\\n        !Array.isArray(source.tools) ||\\n        source.tools.length > 128 ||\\n        typeof source.resources_allowed !== \\\"boolean\\\"\\n      )\\n        throw new Error(\\\"Invalid source catalog\\\");\\n      seen.add(source.id);\\n      const toolNames = new Set<string>();\\n      for (const tool of source.tools) {\\n        if (\\n          !tool ||\\n          typeof tool.name !== \\\"string\\\" ||\\n          !tool.name ||\\n\"}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"check\":2,\"chunk_id\":\"e326ac\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000016722,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":799,\"output\":\"# Connected and generated UI work\\n\\nThe full hosted desktop remains the reference. The running preview is the\\nimmutable offline build; this wave must preserve its library and leave its\\nwindow open. Existing web, Convex and configuration edits are protected.\\n\\n```mermaid\\nflowchart TD\\n  S[Current Source contracts] --> P[Four component prop schemas]\\n  S --> T[Append-only tool streams]\\n  S --> A[Native auth and sync transport contract]\\n  S --> E[Deterministic writer seeding and offline fill]\\n  P --> T\\n  P --> V[GPUI tool bodies and retained controls]\\n  T --> I[Editor and provider integration]\\n  V --> I\\n  E --> I\\n  A --> C[Trusted sign-in and connected library adapter]\\n  C --> K[Account knowledge transport and controls]\\n  I --> Q[Source comparisons and actual native interaction]\\n  K --> Q\\n  Q --> F[Full port audit]\\n```\\n\\n| Node | Ownership | Deliverable and gate |\\n| --- | --- | --- |\\n| P | Sakana fugu-max; proposed `src/gen_ui/props.rs` only | Source Zod-compatible validation, Unicode and numeric edge cases; Root compares with the unchanged Source oracle |\\n| T | Sakana fugu-max; proposed `src/gen_ui/stream.rs` only | Original cumulative JSONL append contract; uses the fixed P API; no writer-field rewrites or invented recovery behavior |\\n| A | Sakana fugu-max; bounded contract JSON only | Actual auth/sync names, wire fields, missing trust and concrete adapter boundary; no account or registration action |\\n| V | Root; new native tool view | Original four components, labels, local working state and Source-derived styling |\\n| E | Sakana fugu-max proposal; Root adoption | Original sentence spans, seeds and no-provider branches compared with the unchanged Source oracle |\\n| I | Root; shared exports, editor and provider coordinators | Actual accepted requests and retained UI; stale folio/range/revision checks; meaningful undo and failure behavior |\\n| C/K | Root, after A | Trusted native sign-in, account-scoped sync/conflicts and knowledge sources/tool review; foundations alone do not enable capability |\\n| Q | Root; Cargo and runtime ownership | Focused checks, Source/native interaction and render comparisons; real providers/account proof remain separate |\\n\\nWorkers return proposals without executing tools or changing files. Root reviews\\nand adopts each proposal in a separate directory before production edits.\\nDisjoint input bundles and their SHA256 pins are retained under\\n`target/verification/sakana-genui-inputs`. Root owns manifests, barrels,\\n`app.rs`, `main.rs`, every runtime and the user preview. No worker may revert\\nor overwrite another participant's work.\\n\\nWave one runs P/T/A in parallel after the P function signature is fixed.\\nRoot works on V while they run. Integration follows review and Source checks;\\nrendered/runtime checks follow a successful build. This graph does not claim\\nthat AI, account sync, knowledge sources or generated UI are complete.\\n\\nP/T/E now have integrated native/Source contract comparisons. V has compiled\\ntool bodies, retained controls and typed requests; its actual editor mounting,\\nSource/native geometry and interaction gates remain open. I/C/K remain\\nimplementation work. The user's preview uses its existing immutable binary.\\n\"}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"check\":3,\"chunk_id\":\"9863f6\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000013311,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":1956,\"output\":\"# Account/sync foundation — HANDOFF\\n\\nFrozen scoped files: `src/native_accounts/**` and this fixture directory. This is an offline protocol/state/persistence foundation, not connected sign-in or a connected library. `auth::CONNECTED_AUTH_AVAILABLE` is deliberately false. Root owns all runtime exports, manifests, app/Store/UI/transport integration; `integration.patch` is **unapplied**.\\n\\nRead [contracts.md](contracts.md) before integration. Its separate source policies, identities, callback approvals, capacity constraints, sharing/publishing boundaries, and native gaps are authoritative for this slice.\\n\\n## Exact interfaces\\n\\n| Interface | Purpose / required Root boundary |\\n| --- | --- |\\n| `auth::CallbackRegistration::require_supported()` | Syntax + explicit exact-origin Twyne trust and Not Organic Twyne-product registration. Operator configuration is required; URL syntax or `product=twyne` is not approval. |\\n| `auth::SignInAttempt::prepare(registration, verifier_entropy:[u8;32], state_entropy:[u8;32], now_ms, return_to)` | Same Source PKCE S256 request. Root supplies fresh OS CSPRNG entropy; this does not open a browser or listener. |\\n| `SignInAttempt::{authorization_url,consume_callback}` | Parsed components preserve duplicate query values; consumption is once even on failure. A returned request is only data for the unimplemented trusted redemption transport. Debug output redacts code/verifier/state. |\\n| `auth::SignInReceipt::consistent_account(trusted_issuer)` | Issued/refreshed/session user consistency only. A constructed or parsed receipt is **not** authenticated identity/JWT/session proof. |\\n| `AccountIdentity`, `SessionLease` | Exact issuer/subject/token-identifier consistency and unique operation-lifetime guard. Root creates a lease only after real accepted Convex auth; invalidate it at sign-out/account change. |\\n| `protocol::{SyncPayload,PullSnapshot,ContentSnapshot}` | Original section names, canonical source, HTML, nullable-persona distinction and pull metadata; retain unknown fields. No caller owner is added to requests. |\\n| `SyncPayload::{normalized,push_arguments}` | Source-compatible row/whole-section diff, omitted/empty semantics, removals, expected head. Known pull timestamps are omitted without rewriting source. Conservative changed-content JSON budget 950,000 bytes; Source UTF-16 bound 5,000,000. Server encoding/whole-account capacity remains independently enforced. |\\n| `AccountJournal::enqueue(payload)` | Explicitly associate a candidate with **this** account. Durable latest-unsent intent coalesces; an in-flight desired snapshot remains immutable. Run only at an explicit save/flush boundary, never a whole-doc per-key path. |\\n| `AccountJournal::prepare_dispatch(lease,active)` | Requires observed baseline/head and no pending pull/stage/conflict. Persist candidate journal before transport submission. Request data does not prove transport/auth availability. |\\n| `AccountJournal::{acknowledge_push,mark_rejected,mark_outcome_unknown}` | Exact dispatch/current-lease guards. ACK advances only sent baseline; newer intent survives. Only proven noncommit can use `mark_rejected`; timeout/socket-loss/ambiguous result requires pull. No server idempotency key exists. |\\n| `AccountJournal::{stage_pull,commit_pull}` | Retain remote snapshot and base/local/remote conflicts. Root must perform actual guarded local application/persistence, then give exact stage/payload/edit-generation and unchanged pending-Source-set receipt. These consistency fields alone are not local I/O proof. |\\n| `AccountJournal::resolve_conflicts(lease,active,expected_conflicts,expected_edit_generation,candidate)` | Explicit resolution after actual guarded Root local persistence. Rejects an old account/lease/dialogue generation. Native three-way preservation is deliberately **not** the Source timestamp merge or a Lix CRDT. |\\n| `AccountJournal::{suspend_session,native_id_for}` | Startup/sign-out leaves uncertain in-flight data and requires a pull; remote string ID ↔ local UUID mapping must be persisted before hydrate. |\\n| `AccountSyncStore::{open,load,save_request,expected_value,acknowledge_expected}` | `open(app_root)` uses only `app_root/account-sync`. Per-account SHA-256 names, OS lock across handles/processes, exact primary+backup byte/value CAS, fsynced atomic save/previous backup, warnings on recovery, untouched future/invalid versions. Exact expected-save acknowledgement re-syncs primary/dir under lock. 64 MiB journal cap; Unix modes 0700/0600. No credentials stored. |\\n\\nPull receipts and queue records preserve the original canonical source; they do not compile it, regenerate HTML, establish a verified projection, change Source selection/history, or write the current native manuscript. Root must preserve its Source pending/conflict/revision guards and use a staged/recoverable two-store application protocol. Do not emit 'saved' from a journal-only receipt.\\n\\n## Dependencies/export\\n\\nNo new dependencies: existing `anyhow`, `serde`, `serde_json`, `fs2`, `tempfile`, `uuid`, plus desktop-enabled `base64` and `sha2`. The proposed export is `#[cfg(feature=\\\"desktop\\\")] pub mod native_accounts;`, so no-default core keeps optional auth dependencies unreferenced. No app, manifest, credential vault, auth transport, browser storage, or existing Store was edited.\\n\\n## Reproduction and evidence\\n\\nExecuted here:\\n\\n```sh\\nrtk proxy bun desktop/gpui/fixtures/account-sync/capture-contracts.ts\\nrtk proxy bun desktop/gpui/fixtures/account-sync/capture-contracts.ts --check\\nrtk proxy rustfmt --edition 2024 --check desktop/gpui/src/native_accounts/mod.rs desktop/gpui/src/native_accounts/auth.rs desktop/gpui/src/native_accounts/protocol.rs desktop/gpui/src/native_accounts/journal.rs desktop/gpui/src/native_accounts/store.rs desktop/gpui/src/native_accounts/tests.rs\\n```\\n\\nThe generator AST-selects four original sync helpers and four auth helpers plus the callback constant, with drift guards and a forbidden-network/global-context guard. It records exact source SHA-256. Only selected pure bodies execute; no app module is imported. Eight original wire diff cases, nine callback cases, six return paths and a deterministic PKCE request are captured. Fixture entropy/codes/session IDs are synthetic and confer no access.\\n\\nPrepared, **not run here**, because Root owns Cargo scheduling:\\n\\n```sh\\n# After Root reviews and applies integration.patch:\\nrtk proxy devenv shell -- rtk proxy cargo test --manifest-path desktop/gpui/Cargo.toml --locked --offline --features ui-tests --lib native_accounts::tests\\nrtk proxy devenv shell -- rtk proxy cargo check --manifest-path desktop/gpui/Cargo.toml --locked --offline --no-default-features --lib\\n```\\n\\nThe 26 prepared tests include real temporary-filesystem restart/backup/corruption/blocked-path retry and simultaneous separate-handle CAS tests, alongside synthetic protocol/lease/conflict tests. They have not established passing Rust type-checks, filesystem behavior, native account UI, OS secure storage, registered callbacks, live identity, live sync, multi-device convergence, service limits, or platform portability. Root must run/review these gates before runtime use.\\n\\n## First connected slice remains separate\\n\\nBoth native callback origin approvals must exist before auth transport. Implement external-browser/listener routing, protected Better Auth cookie jar, refreshed-session authenticity, Convex JWT acquisition/accepted-auth state and current-lease cancellation. Then use **read-only staged pull into a separate account partition**, with explicit device-library association before any upload. Do not silently carry the browser's unpartitioned automatic seeding into native. Sharing/Lix, roles/presence, invitations, publication, global provider sessions and deletion are outside this foundation and owned by other lanes.\\n\"}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"check\":4,\"chunk_id\":\"24b5e8\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000021764,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":16,\"output\":\"    Finished `dev` profile [unoptimized] target(s) in 12.58s\\n\"}"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a10ca3-f662-7822-9d58-47f08a989563","create_time":1791216930.500788}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
