` passed typechecks, tests, web/server smoke, release preflight self-test, workflow validation, and full Playwright; `stich:e2e:railway` verified disposable-account submit, inbox/body read, Sent copy, invalid identity, and cleanup. [Task 1]\n5283:scope: Build an agent-first analytics product across web, desktop, mobile, CLI, and TUI with privacy-aware telemetry and Bun/Railpack deployment.\n5298:- track activity across “desktop, mobile, cli, tui, and web,” but retain an event-spec seam if SDK/TUI may be “something altogether” from the agent product; document tradeoffs instead of forcing unresolved choices [Task 1]\n5310:# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/twyne character-aware narration, premium GPT Live voice, and native Typst workflow\n5311:scope: Extend Twyne’s author-aware editor interaction and native Typst authoring without exposing provider credentials or replacing the visual editor.\n5312:applies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne; reuse_rule=recheck the current dirty tree, browser/device access, Not Organic provider state, and deployment before treating Live voice as production-ready.\n5318:- rollout_summaries/2026-09-26T10-01-32-fcwe-twyne_character_aware_narration_gpt_live_voice_desk.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/26/rollout-2026-09-26T06-01-32-01a0dd29-b2ed-78c0-b5b2-143eed227156.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-26T10:38:47+00:00, thread_id=01a0dd29-b2ed-78c0-b5b2-143eed227156, success; focused speech tests passed)\n5328:- rollout_summaries/2026-09-26T10-01-32-fcwe-twyne_character_aware_narration_gpt_live_voice_desk.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/26/rollout-2026-09-26T06-01-32-01a0dd29-b2ed-78c0-b5b2-143eed227156.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-26T10:38:47+00:00, thread_id=01a0dd29-b2ed-78c0-b5b2-143eed227156, partial; deterministic checks/builds passed, production/browser/provider proof open)\n5338:- rollout_summaries/2026-09-26T11-02-50-0rjp-twyne_native_typst_editor_implementation_deployment.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/26/rollout-2026-09-26T07-02-50-01a0dd61-d08c-7f71-9e6c-24cf8966c3df.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-29T01:38:36+00:00, thread_id=01a0dd61-d08c-7f71-9e6c-24cf8966c3df, success; CI, Railway, and live proof/PDF/persistence smoke passed)\n5353:- Twyne’s Live client uses Not Organic `/v1/live/sessions` through same-origin `/api/live`; provider billing/entitlements remain authoritative and Twyne never receives an OpenAI key. The implementation reserves ceilings of `$0.50` per session and `$0.05` per delegated action, not quoted rates. [Task 2]\n5355:- The provider patch adds a one-time `$2.50` Twyne welcome allowance separate from Keating, with idempotency and paid-history exclusions. Delegated replies are accepted only for IDs observed from trusted upstream events; inspect the separate provider dirty tree before follow-up work. [Task 2]\n5357:- Core paths are `src/utils/typst/{document,serialize,export,client,session,compiler.worker}.ts`, `src/components/editor/{typst-workspace,typst-code-editor}.tsx`, `src/components/editor/extensions/raw-typst.ts`, `src/utils/{idb,convex-sync}.ts`, `convex/schema.ts`, and `convex/sync.ts`. Production smoke at `https://twyne.love/editor/` rendered two proof pages, produced a `%PDF-` download, preserved content on reload, and showed no runtime errors. [Task 3]\n5363:- Direct browser-global assignment/restoration caused 105 Bun failures -> save/restore descriptors with `Object.defineProperty`. Before push run `bun run lint`, `bun run fmt.check`, Convex typecheck, and the full suite; final validation was `1605 pass`, `40 skip`, `0 fail`, GitHub run `36508550529` success, and Railway deployment `2261ee43-1626-496b-8388-5e0c2d749989` successful. `bun add` can need `BUN_TMPDIR=/tmp BUN_INSTALL_CACHE_DIR=/tmp/twyne-bun-cache`. [Task 3]\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"1:# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/baste Makepad versus GPUI studio-framework selection\n3:applies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/baste; reuse_rule=confirm the current GPUI/GPUI Kit release and target platforms before implementation because GPUI is pre-1.0.\n5:## Task 1: Compare Makepad and GPUI for a Baste studio\n9:- rollout_summaries/2026-10-04T04-46-42-dK0S-makepad_vs_gpui_baste_studio.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/baste, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/10/04/rollout-2026-10-04T00-46-42-01a1053c-5484-7860-b895-c654c9e25fd6.jsonl, updated_at=2026-10-04T04:47:19+00:00, thread_id=01a1053c-5484-7860-b895-c654c9e25fd6, success; direct framework comparison)\n13:- Makepad, GPUI, GPUI Kit, Rust GUI, Zed, Studio, WASM, native desktop, candidate grids, inspectors, generation queues\n17:- when asking “makepad v gpui” -> give a direct comparative assessment and decision fit rather than starting implementation work [Task 1]\n21:- GPUI is the Baste default for a dense native productivity studio: entities/shared state, declarative views, imperative custom elements, keyboard actions, async services, and testing support fit projects, candidate grids, inspectors, and generation queues. [Task 1]\n23:- GPUI Kit is separate from core GPUI; verify its exact matching version and accessibility/component capabilities instead of attributing them to GPUI itself. [Task 1]\n27:- GPUI is pre-1.0 with frequent breaking changes -> inspect the exact release/fork and Zed source before committing Baste architecture to an API or platform assumption. [Task 1]\n29:# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/notorganic-provider shared account knowledge connections for Keating and Twyne\n30:scope: Implement account-owned knowledge sources with app-specific grants, explicit tool consent, and fail-closed revocation across Not Organic, Keating, and Twyne.\n31:applies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/notorganic-provider with integrations in /home/diogenes/Projects/{keating,twyne}; reuse_rule=retest current provider contracts, dirty diffs, deployment/CORS, and a real account before claiming cross-app readiness.\n37:- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/notorganic-provider, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/10/03/rollout-2026-10-03T08-22-46-01a101b7-83a5-7863-897a-869bf3d11c1b.jsonl, updated_at=2026-10-03T23:33:08+00:00, thread_id=01a101b7-83a5-7863-897a-869bf3d11c1b, partial; implementation/focused validation passed, deployment and real-account proof open)\n47:- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/notorganic-provider, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/10/03/rollout-2026-10-03T08-22-46-01a101b7-83a5-7863-897a-869bf3d11c1b.jsonl, updated_at=2026-10-03T23:33:08+00:00, thread_id=01a101b7-83a5-7863-897a-869bf3d11c1b, partial; 53 focused tests/260 assertions, full web build blocked)\n53:## Task 3: Integrate account sources and MCP review in Twyne\n57:- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/notorganic-provider, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/10/03/rollout-2026-10-03T08-22-46-01a101b7-83a5-7863-897a-869bf3d11c1b.jsonl, updated_at=2026-10-03T23:33:08+00:00, thread_id=01a101b7-83a5-7863-897a-869bf3d11c1b, partial; 98 targeted checks/typechecks/builds passed, live gateway proof open)\n65:- when asking for knowledge bases to “carry over” into Keating and Twyne and be “easy to add or revoke an apps access to them” -> default to account-level ownership, per-app grants, explicit revocation, and guided setup [Task 1]\n73:- Twyne trusted Convex actions bind verified DID/sessionVersion to fresh DPoP tokens. Research requires enabling research, choosing a source search tool, and selecting “Your MCP servers”; sign-out, revocation, and schema changes clear/fail closed. [Task 3]\n79:- `ERR_CONNECTION_REFUSED` after an owned Twyne preview stopped is an environment/process condition, while localhost-to-deployed Convex CORS preflight must be verified separately; neither establishes deployed feature