er/offline-download, credit recovery, completed feedback, assignment delivery, populated TUI, and desktop/mobile learner surfaces. [Task 1]\n382:- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/10/01/rollout-2026-10-01T17-48-48-01a0f971-0209-7402-b50e-0e91fadc49a8.jsonl, updated_at=2026-10-02T00:15:26+00:00, thread_id=01a0f971-0209-7402-b50e-0e91fadc49a8, partial; desktop passed but root/web compatibility update incomplete)\n396:- GPT Image, ReviewDesk, TrajectoryReviewWorkspace, CommitReviewArticle, one task panel at a time, margin annotation, prompts-and-behavior.json, desktop-panel-flow.png\n400:- when asking to “update all our dependencies” -> include root, web, mobile, desktop, packages, training/tooling, CI, and lockfiles, while separating risky major upgrades and preserving unrelated dirty work [Task 1]\n406:- Static storyboards are at `output/imagegen/2026-10-01-review-redesign/v2/`. The useful interaction principle is “one task panel at a time”: preserve passage/reading position/draft; desktop annotations occupy margins without reflowing text; mobile replaces stages, pins selected quote above keyboard, preserves drafts on close, and makes discard/preferred choice explicit. [Task 2]\n410:- `Export named 'AuthStorage' not found`, `config_hooks_removed`, removed assistant-ui hooks, and missing TypeScript compiler APIs show incompatibility, not an update success. Desktop’s 148 passing tests did not establish root/web/mobile success; root reached 634 pass, 44 fail, 43 errors. Run each package’s intended check in its supported environment. [Task 1]\n494:# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/twyne fluid manuscript editor, House attention policy, and Claude-work continuation\n495:scope: Continue and critique Twyne’s in-flow writing surfaces while preserving deliberate side-panel browsing, authorship, scoped validation boundaries, and return-to-writing continuity.\n496:applies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne; reuse_rule=reinspect the dirty worktree, running Vite server, current House/flow contracts, and authenticated/model/sync behavior before treating local fixture results as complete product proof.\n502:- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/30/rollout-2026-09-30T02-30-15-01a0f101-b3b4-7e41-9e3c-8d3ec580aba0.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-30T08:46:14+00:00, thread_id=01a0f101-b3b4-7e41-9e3c-8d3ec580aba0, partial; scoped E2E/format/diff/TypeScript checks passed, full typecheck remained blocked)\n506:- all in flow, flow-surface.tsx, flow-ribbon.tsx, manuscript-panel.tsx, twyne-editor.tsx, margin-surface.ts, MARGIN_SLOT_EVENT, OPEN_MARGIN_THREAD_EVENT, pneumatic post, galley slip, way in, 5180\n512:- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/30/rollout-2026-09-30T02-30-15-01a0f101-b3b4-7e41-9e3c-8d3ec580aba0.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-30T08:46:14+00:00, thread_id=01a0f101-b3b4-7e41-9e3c-8d3ec580aba0, success; source, plan, tests, browser evidence, and gaps compared)\n521:- on large Twyne features, the user explicitly prefers UI/design work first and allows backend/plumbing to be delegated to Codex -> preserve that sequencing [Task 1]\n561:- when the user asked to “add the cdn caching for this project and also twyne” -> favor invisible server-side limits and CDN controls that preserve ordinary browsing; do not add CAPTCHAs or sign-in friction unless explicitly needed [Task 2]\n568:- Relevant limits are documented in `docs/public-endpoint-security.md`; the rollout verified 62 focused tests, 9 Redis cross-client tests, TypeScript, Nitro build, and built-server page/OAuth/oversized-body/missing-Redis behavior. Railway Redis, Keating’s Redis reference, CDN for Keating/Twyne, a $75 workspace alert, and service ceilings were configured. [Task 2]\n616:# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/twyne Open Graph editorial preview and Seedance desk-scene video\n617:scope: Replace generic Twyne social previews with project-bound editorial assets and produce a real physical-motion desk video only when the requested fal Seedance output is available and validated.\n618:applies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne; reuse_rule=reinspect current metadata, generated assets, provider balance, and final video evidence before claiming crawler or Seedance completion.\n624:- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/29/rollout-2026-09-29T17-06-37-01a0eefd-acc3-7f01-a57d-1f767284796b.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-29T23:43:49+00:00, thread_id=01a0eefd-acc3-7f01-a57d-1f767284796b, partial; metadata and an earlier local HyperFrames MP4 were validated, crawler proof remains open)\n628:- opengraph, og:image, TWYNE_SOCIAL_IMAGE, RouterHead, router-head.tsx, seo.ts, twyne-editorial-v2.jpg, magick, twyne-writers-desk-loop-v1.mp4, ffprobe\n634:- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/29/rollout-2026-09-29T17-06-37-01a0eefd-acc3-7f01-a57d-1f767284796b.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-29T23:43:49+00:00, thread_id=01a0eefd-acc3-7f01-a57d-1f767284796b, failed/pending; fal rejected before queueing for exhausted balance)\n638:- bytedance/seedance-2.5/image-to-video, Seedance 2.5, fal, SUBMISSION_REJECTED, exhausted balance, seedance-job-v1.json, generate-social-desk-video.ts, twyne-writers-desk-overlay.svg\n648:- Site defaults come from `src/components/router-head/router-head.tsx`, route declarations override them, and social constants belong in `src/utils/seo.ts` with `TWYNE_SITE_ORIGIN=https://twyne.love`. The new source asset is `public/assets/social/twyne-editorial-v2.jpg`; Prettier and ESLint passed, but final crawler/browser proof was not recorded. [Task 1]\n649:- The old `twyne-writers-desk-loop-v1.mp4` is a verified 1200×630, 30 fps, 6-second silent H.264 local artifact. Intel Mesa HyperFrames capture required translating Chrome `--use-angle=gl-egl` to `--use-angle=gl`; it is historical camera-shift output, not a Seedance result. [Task 1]\n650:- Seedance preparation is resumable: `scripts/generate-social-desk-video.ts` persists `social-preview-video/seedance-job-v1.json` before submission to avoid duplicate charges. Request 720p, 6 seconds, silent, high-bitrate H.264 with the clean background as start/end; composite `twyne-writers-desk-overlay.svg` in HyperFrames, never in generated footage. [Task 2]\n686:# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/twyne illuminated initials, Typst proof, and editorial-native tooling\n687:scope: Make Typst authoring/proof and generated initial artwork feel native to Twyne’s paper/ink/vermilion writing desk while preserving editable manuscript text, export fidelity, and explicit publication gates.\n688:applies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne; reuse_rule=reinspect current editor/export contracts, actual generated-asset inventory, and landing-image approval before changing styling, claiming asset coverage, or publishing.\n694:- rollout_summaries/2026-09-29T02-53-14-wfgW-twyne_typst_native_tooling_proof_styling.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/28/rollout-2026-09-28T22-53-14-01a0eb14-a63e-75c1-840d-6c9f28175f26.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-29T03:56:43+00:00, thread_id=01a0eb14-a63e-75c1-840d-6c9f28175f26, partial; final browser/typecheck claim was reported, earlier focused E2E setup failed)\n704:- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/29/rollout-2026-09-29T00-33-25-01a0eb70-5e56-7400-88f6-69c619eb553f.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-29T19:26:16+00:00, thread_id=01a0eb70-5e56-7400-88f6-69c619eb553f, success; editor/export and rendered pages validated, publication awaits user landing-image selection)\n708:- illuminated-initials, drop-cap, imagegen, transparent-assets, AVIF, Typst, browser-print, twyne-release-023, landing-options, manuscript garden\n712:- when the user said the Typst UI looked “tagged on as an afterthought” and requested “much better tooling that also appears visually native to the rest of the editor” -> reuse Twyne’s established paper/ink/vermilion toolbar language rather than creating a separate Typst visual system [Task 1]\n721:- The current drop cap is CSS-driven at `.twyne-editor .ProseMirror > p:first-of-type::first-letter`; artwork must layer around the editable opening character, not replace manuscript text. Relevant helpers include `src/utils/illuminated-initials.ts`, `print-ornaments.ts`, `page-ornaments.ts`, and `src/utils/typst/decorative-assets.ts`. [Task 2]\n722:- For transparent initials, explicitly prohibit parchment, frames, shadows, glow, captions, watermarks, and extra lettering. Normalize generated output before committing; generated workspace assets must not remain only in an image-generation cache. AVIF conversion was reported as 62.49 MB to 12.14 MB. The isolated commit in `/tmp/twyne-release-023` passed the full 1,628-test suite, production build, and `git diff --check`, but was not published. [Task 2]\n726:- A focused Playwright run was blocked first by sandbox frontend startup and then by missing `.ProseMirror` during seed/setup. Treat the later claim of four passing browser checks as reported evidence needing an independent rerun after final changes; four existing lint warnings also remained. `bun add` can need `BUN_TMPDIR=/tmp BUN_INSTALL_CACHE_DIR=/tmp/twyne-bun-cache`. [Task 1]\n730:# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/twyne landing artwork, avatars, editor actions, and fluid House work\n731:scope: Apply Twyne's editorial UI direction across landing imagery, writer identity, compact editor actions, and the in-flow/House experience without overstating incomplete browser or sync proof.\n732:applies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne; reuse_rule=reinspect the live worktree, SSR route, current editor/store contracts, and authenticated profile flow before claiming UI or persistence completion.\n738:- rollout_summaries/2026-09-29T16-46-26-rtLH-twyne_landing_artwork_and_profile_avatars.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/29/rollout-2026-09-29T12-46-26-01a0ee0f-7a28-7c02-91fa-0e4cc2271ce9.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-29T19:27:49+00:00, thread_id=01a0ee0f-7a28-7c02-91fa-0e4cc2271ce9, partial; landing composition planned, avatar code/assets added but final browser and checks remain open)\n748:- rollout_summaries/2026-09-29T19-19-02-GE0c-twyne_editor_icon_and_dossier_label_polish.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/29/rollout-2026-09-29T15-19-02-01a0ee9b-2e36-7f43-904b-e4af84b76ebc.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-29T19:23:21+00:00, thread_id=01a0ee9b-2e36-7f43-904b-e4af84b76ebc, partial; icon/state implementation checked, final copy and browser spacing unverified)\n758:- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/29/rollout-2026-09-29T21-21-53-01a0efe7-60c8-7c41-aeae-38137ec6cbde.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-29T18:54:27+00:00, thread_id=01a0efe7-60c8-7c41-aeae-38137ec6cbde, partial; route/flow/backend work exists but SSR, browser, codegen, and deployment proof are open)\n759:- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/29/rollout-2026-09-29T21-21-53-01a0efe7-60e5-7fa1-b18e-e9b4851fd5d4.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-30T10:14:40+00:00, thread_id=01a0efe7-60e5-7fa1-b18e-e9b4851fd5d4, partial; UI/architecture exists, but flow/House browser-sync proof remains bounded)\n763:- House, Collection, Folio, Editions, Charter, Amendments, Revisions, flow-conductor.ts, FlowSurface, twyne:zen-mode, house-sync.ts, convex/house.ts, cover lookups\n769:- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/29/rollout-2026-09-29T21-21-53-01a0efe7-60e5-7fa1-b18e-e9b4851fd5d4.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-30T10:14:40+00:00, thread_id=01a0efe7-60e5-7fa1-b18e-e9b4851fd5d4, success; release/production navigation replay passed, authenticated flows remain unexercised)\n786:- Landing page already has `.landing-hero`, `WorkspaceTour`, preview plates, and `.landing-closing-photo`; integrate chosen imagery there. AVIF avatars are `public/assets/avatars/engraved-2026-09/{owl,fox,hare,raven}.avif`; settings fetches/wraps them through the existing upload path, while `account-menu.tsx` follows `api.profiles.getMyHandle` updates. A claimed Twyne handle is required and this is separate from a Not Organic account profile. [Task 1]\n788:- Existing flow primitives are `struggle-tracker.ts`, `struggle-signals.ts`, `margin-rail.tsx`, `background-research.ts`, `user-comments.ts`, and `twyne:zen-mode`. New work is `flow-conductor.ts`, `flow-surface.tsx`, House model/store/sync, and `src/routes/house/index.tsx`; use Twyne palette tokens plus `.dept-label`, `.btn-paper`, `.btn-press`. Cover lookup sends only a Jev-selected title, never draft text. Reconcile legacy comment/persona popovers and anchor widgets with `FlowSurface`: route to the flow card when available and reserve popovers for narrow/docked/offline fallback. [Task 3]\n798:# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/twyne Devenv port separation\n799:scope: Prevent `devenv up` from colliding with standalone Twyne Vite and Storybook processes while keeping configuration and proof boundaries explicit.\n800:applies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne; reuse_rule=recheck live listeners, `devenv.nix`, package scripts, and the full app path before treating process startup as full application proof.\n806:- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/29/rollout-2026-09-29T16-52-56-01a0eef1-251c-7410-a715-47ba2909ea0c.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-29T21:03:08+00:00, thread_id=01a0eef1-251c-7410-a715-47ba2909ea0c, partial; individual processes and task evaluation passed, full `devenv up`/app behavior unverified)\n810:- devenv.nix, package.json, TWYNE_DEV_PORT, TWYNE_STORYBOOK_PORT, 5173, 6006, 5180, 6010, readiness probes, devenv tasks list\n818:- Standalone `dev.frontend`/Storybook defaults are 5173/6006; `devenv.nix` gives `devenv up` 5180/6010 through `TWYNE_DEV_PORT` and `TWYNE_STORYBOOK_PORT`. Keep readiness probes on those same variables and document both URL pairs. Storybook uses `--host 127.0.0.1`, configured port, and `--ci`. [Task 1]\n825:# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/twyne v0.22.1 bilingual launch-film release and deployment\n826:scope: Release Twyne with one locale-resolved landing/docs film while preserving unrelated work and requiring CI, public assets, deployment, and browser proof before completion.\n827:applies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne; reuse_rule=reinspect the dirty tree, native release scripts, current Convex/Railway credentials, remote CI, and live locale behavior before publishing another release.\n833:- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/28/rollout-2026-09-28T17-54-33-01a0ea03-320c-7363-8153-d4a4fe122ae8.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-29T01:19:04+00:00, thread_id=01a0ea03-320c-7363-8153-d4a4fe122ae8, success; CI, GitHub release/assets, Railway, and live locale smoke passed)\n847:- Twyne’s release sequence is `bun run release:version`, `bun run release:check`, then `bun run release:publish`; release check requires an annotated matching `v<package.version>` tag. v0.22.1 is `692fe6b6d3c48a2a09299e616a58548e3569b5da` / `v0.22.1`, with source plus Linux/macOS/Windows desktop assets. [Task 1]\n849:- Railway production used service `twyne`, deployment `e802c911-53ff-4d0b-b500-fb8c9b8e6f0a`, and Convex target `prod:hushed-aardvark-411`. For deploy-only keys, pin `npx --yes convex@1.46.0 deploy --cmd 'bun run build.client && bun run build.server'` in `scripts/railway-build.sh`. [Task 1]\n1150:- `desktop/scripts/stage-onnx-runtime.mjs` stages only the target platform/architecture ONNX Runtime closure; `desktop/test/onnx-packaging.test.ts` passed 13 tests. Release workflow checks each Linux installer against GitHub’s 2 GiB per-file limit, but full-payload XZ remained over: x64 2,267,136,000 bytes and arm64 2,252,914,688 bytes. [Task 5]\n1161:applies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating; reuse_rule=recheck desktop/browser capability, Not Organic authorization, and live provider behavior before asserting end-to-end availability.\n1180:- `web/src/components/settings/JudgementSettings.tsx` owns the picker/setup UI mounted from `ProvidersModelsTab.tsx` under `judgement`. It offers `Jev · Not Organic · Recommended`, desktop MiniCPM5 where supported, browser alternatives marked scoring-unavailable, and `Off · built-in checks only`; unavailable reviews link to `/chat?settings=judgement`. [Task 1]\n1187:# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/twyne persistence, Not Organic migration, rubric copy, and configurable judgement\n1188:scope: Preserve every Twyne writer’s work across guest/auth paths, make normal editing controls reliable, and migrate identity/judgement configuration without overstating live production proof.\n1189:applies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne; reuse_rule=reinspect the broad dirty migration, production account scope/origins, PDS scopes, and real provider endpoints before deployment or irreversible account action.\n1195:- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/28/rollout-2026-09-28T22-53-14-01a0eb14-a6ed-79a2-bdfb-508802dcd4c2.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-23T15:23:10+00:00, thread_id=01a0eb14-a6ed-79a2-bdfb-508802dcd4c2, success; targeted browser tests passed)\n1199:- DataCloneError, Qwik useStore, toStorable, IndexedDB, saveProjectBriefForFolio, withFolioTitle, dossier-persistence.e2e.ts, Ctrl+A, Mod-A, twyne-editor.tsx\n1201:## Task 2: Replace legacy Twyne identity/billing with Not Organic-native sign-in\n1205:- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/28/rollout-2026-09-28T22-53-14-01a0eb14-a6ed-79a2-bdfb-508802dcd4c2.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-23T15:23:10+00:00, thread_id=01a0eb14-a6ed-79a2-bdfb-508802dcd4c2, partial; uncommitted migration, production/browser/PDS proof pending)\n1215:- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/28/rollout-2026-09-28T22-53-14-01a0eb14-a65e-7873-ac1f-577a624acee3.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-26T04:27:48+00:00, thread_id=01a0eb14-a65e-7873-ac1f-577a624acee3, partial; UI/build checks passed, benchmark/live endpoint unverified)\n1232:- `rubric-copy.ts` centralizes visible score words/verdicts/next moves while frozen wording in `rubric-grade.ts` keeps historical judgement comparable. Keep summaries within the panel’s 120-character limit. `judgement-client.ts` routes Twyne-hosted, one-use TypeSafe BYOK through Convex, or a compatible direct endpoint and validates endpoint/response contracts. [Task 3]\n1240:# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/twyne persistent intentional grammar choices\n1242:applies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne; reuse_rule=reuse the precise local dictionary/matching design for Twyne grammar UI; manually exercise persistence and removal whenever a browser is available.\n1248:- rollout_summaries/2026-09-26T09-40-38-4ytO-persistent_intentional_grammar_choices.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/26/rollout-2026-09-26T05-40-38-01a0dd16-8f41-7822-80c1-8224fb133b70.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-26T10:01:22+00:00, thread_id=01a0dd16-8f41-7822-80c1-8224fb133b70, success; focused tests passed, browser UI unverified)\n1252:- Harper, grammar-panel, twyne:grammar-dictionary:v1, importWords, exportWords, clearWords, intentional choice, localStorage, ×, aria-label\n1260:- `src/utils/grammar.ts` persists validated, deduplicated choices under `twyne:grammar-dictionary:v1`; match `problem`, `kind`, and `message` so one accepted wording does not disable an entire Harper rule. Spelling choices synchronize through `exportWords`, `clearWords`, and `importWords`; non-spelling choices filter only exact matches. [Task 1]\n1267:# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/twyne grade and workflow stamp effects\n1269:applies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne; reuse_rule=recheck actual generated assets and visual behavior before reuse; the asset-count/model claim in this rollout is not independently established.\n1275:- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/26/rollout-2026-09-26T04-54-37-01a0dcec-6ed9-7913-b710-05f13e701fef.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-26T09:34:57+00:00, thread_id=01a0dcec-6ed9-7913-b710-05f13e701fef, partial; exact model, asset persistence, and claimed checks unverified)\n1289:- `src/components/ui/workflow-stamp.tsx` supplies Filed/Revised states; Revised is tied to accepted manuscript edits and dossier flows. Twyne’s expected visual baseline is editorial, ink-on-paper, restrained UI with reduced-motion handling. [Task 1]\n1295:# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/twyne dossier live title, brief editions, and Storybook\n1296:scope: Keep dossier editing visibly live and preserve folio-scoped, browsable saved brief history in established Twyne editorial cards.\n1297:applies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne; reuse_rule=reuse the separate brief-edition model for saved replacements, not manuscript revisions or unsaved typing; browser interaction remains a required proof boundary.\n1303:- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/26/rollout-2026-09-26T04-13-58-01a0dcc7-3905-7aa3-9ad8-8db73307470f.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-26T08:55:04+00:00, thread_id=01a0dcc7-3905-7aa3-9ad8-8db73307470f, partial; typecheck passed, browser interaction unavailable)\n1313:- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/26/rollout-2026-09-26T04-13-58-01a0dcc7-3905-7aa3-9ad8-8db73307470f.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-26T08:55:04+00:00, thread_id=01a0dcc7-3905-7aa3-9ad8-8db73307470f, success; build.types and diff check passed)\n1333:# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/twyne rubric, writing-tools autosave, and drawer UI refinement\n1335:applies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne; reuse_rule=reuse existing Twyne UI primitives and live-review ownership; do not represent this rollout as browser visually verified.\n1341:- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/26/rollout-2026-09-26T03-30-40-01a0dc9f-9346-7ac0-9e6c-d4e92f4211cf.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-26T08:54:19+00:00, thread_id=01a0dc9f-9346-7ac0-9e6c-d4e92f4211cf, success; focused checks passed, browser visual verification unavailable)\n1351:- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/26/rollout-2026-09-26T03-30-40-01a0dc9f-9346-7ac0-9e6c-d4e92f4211cf.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-26T08:54:19+00:00, thread_id=01a0dc9f-9346-7ac0-9e6c-d4e92f4211cf, success; focused storage/lens checks passed)\n1355:- live-review.ts, twyne:live-review, writing-tools:${folioId}, writing-tools-storage.ts, cachedWritingLens, newest-write-wins, Run this check\n1361:- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/26/rollout-2026-09-26T03-30-40-01a0dc9f-9346-7ac0-9e6c-d4e92f4211cf.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-26T08:54:19+00:00, thread_id=01a0dc9f-9346-7ac0-9e6c-d4e92f4211cf, success; TypeScript, ESLint, and diff check passed)\n1377:- `src/utils/live-review.ts` owns background review and emits `twyne:live-review`; `cachedWritingLens` shares cache/in-flight work. Store folio notes as `writing-tools:${folioId}` in `src/utils/writing-tools-storage.ts`; serialized saves guarantee newest-write-wins. Automatic review remains read-only and retains findings, uncertainty, and evidence. [Task 2]\n1384:# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/twyne HyperFrames launch-video audit and production\n1385:scope: Audit an interrupted agent video run against actual artifacts, then complete and verify all renderable Twyne launch films on this Linux workstation.\n1386:applies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne; reuse_rule=reinspect the project/CLI/browser GPU configuration before rendering; the Intel ANGLE workaround is host-specific.\n1392:- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/26/rollout-2026-09-26T02-10-19-01a0dc56-01ea-7e51-a7aa-600909e6091b.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-26T06:45:21+00:00, thread_id=01a0dc56-01ea-7e51-a7aa-600909e6091b, success)\n1402:- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/26/rollout-2026-09-26T02-10-19-01a0dc56-01ea-7e51-a7aa-600909e6091b.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-26T06:45:21+00:00, thread_id=01a0dc56-01ea-7e51-a7aa-600909e6091b, success; six exports decoded and sampled)\n1412:- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/28/rollout-2026-09-28T22-53-14-01a0eb14-a661-78a0-90d3-a5ab174e7cc2.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-26T06:09:49+00:00, thread_id=01a0eb14-a661-78a0-90d3-a5ab174e7cc2, partial; source-media/compositions built, later completion is captured in Task 2)\n1429:- Twyne’s visual language is aged cream paper, near-black brown ink, vermilion, literary serif display type, DM Sans UI, and Special Elite/typewriter labels—avoid generic AI-chat/SaaS treatment. `_gen` scripts/manifests stage imagery, music, TTS, alignment, captions, fonts, SFX, and brand SVGs; word timing is bundled inline as `assets/js/words.js` to avoid render-time fetches. [Task 3]\n1436:# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/twyne Jev editor live-review, Not Organic linking, and v0.20.2 release\n1438:applies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne; reuse_rule=recheck production provider funding, gateway configuration, and current release state; reuse editor wiring and clean-install lessons for this checkout.\n1444:- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/20/rollout-2026-09-20T01-56-11-01a0bd62-eabf-7a61-bb50-27a4047f7c4a.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-20T07:49:22+00:00, thread_id=01a0bd62-eabf-7a61-bb50-27a4047f7c4a, success; funded end-to-end review remains unverified)\n1448:- live-review.ts, LiveReviewStatus, twyne:live-review, twyne:quick-review, twyne:content, twyne:draft-saved, saved-draft, idle delay, pause/resume, TypeSafe, Noul, Choice, Score\n1454:- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/20/rollout-2026-09-20T01-56-11-01a0bd62-eabf-7a61-bb50-27a4047f7c4a.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-20T07:49:22+00:00, thread_id=01a0bd62-eabf-7a61-bb50-27a4047f7c4a, success; provider transport/release verified, no funded review probe)\n1458:- judgement:evaluate, DPoP, PKCE, NOTORGANIC_AUDIENCE, invalid_product_assertion, hushed-aardvark-411, jsdom@26.1.0, Undici, .dagger/src/index.ts, twyne-tools, v0.20.2, 402 insufficient_funds\n1464:- when styling should be “consistent with our other styles” -> reuse Twyne tokens, shared controls, typography, and Editorial Board vocabulary rather than a local styling system [Task 1]\n1469:- `src/utils/live-review.ts` owns saved-draft review, persistence by folio, retry/backoff, and `twyne:live-review` / `twyne:quick-review`; `src/components/writing-tools/live-review-status.tsx` provides status, findings, pause/resume, and unavailable-state routing. Preserve typed findings, uncertainty, evidence passages, and read-only behavior: review must not edit prose automatically. [Task 1]\n1472:- Production gateway audience is `notorganic`, independent of issuer. The release added declared `jsdom@26.1.0` compatible with the pinned Undici and installs the separate `packages/twyne-tools/bun.lock` in `.dagger/src/index.ts` before CLI checks. Final evidence: 1,474 tests with 39 skips/0 failures, CLI 22 tests, type/build/lint/format/package checks, successful release assets, and Railway `SUCCESS` for `254ad09a8346972910fcab59e62d2b75033578b7`. [Task 2]\n1476:- Isolated `/writing-tools/` and button-triggered rubric paths are not editor integration -> trace `twyne:content`, `twyne:draft-saved`, and folio lifecycle events, then inspect the visible editor state. [Task 1]\n1478:- Local green tests can hide clean-CI dependency faults -> run an isolated install and the full CI dependency graph. `jsdom@29.1.1` expected an Undici handler absent from this checkout; missing `twyne-tools` install also failed Dagger. Preserve unrelated `devenv.lock` and `skills-lock.json` changes. [Task 2]\n1507:- for deep integration across “weave, woven and worn,” start with cross-repository archaeology of Keating/Twyne/TypeSafe/Not Organic rather than editing one call site [Task 1]\n1617:# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/twyne production provider relay and auth/session recovery\n1618:scope: Operate Twyne's shared remote-BYOK transport and harden Convex, Not Organic, and ATProto browser-session recovery without overstating signed-in account proof.\n1619:applies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne; reuse_rule=recheck current provider configuration, Railway proxy headers, OAuth grants, Convex deployment, live account state, and dirty worktree before reuse or production claims.\n1625:- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/20/rollout-2026-09-20T13-41-47-01a0bfe8-ea41-7552-a283-0faea9208674.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-20T18:52:35+00:00, thread_id=01a0bfe8-ea41-7552-a283-0faea9208674, success; MiniMax/OpenAI dummy-key transport smoke verified)\n1635:- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/20/rollout-2026-09-20T13-41-47-01a0bfe8-ea41-7552-a283-0faea9208674.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-20T18:52:35+00:00, thread_id=01a0bfe8-ea41-7552-a283-0faea9208674, partial; unit proof, signed-in account flow open)\n1645:- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/20/rollout-2026-09-20T13-41-47-01a0bfe8-ea41-7552-a283-0faea9208674.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-20T18:52:35+00:00, thread_id=01a0bfe8-ea41-7552-a283-0faea9208674, partial; exact production 400 not reproduced)\n1659:- Railway TLS termination needs `PROTOCOL_HEADER=x-forwarded-proto` in `server.js`; otherwise Qwik inferred `http://twyne.love` and rejected production POSTs with `403 CSRF check failed`. Dummy MiniMax/OpenAI keys returned expected readable 401s, proving transport but not valid-key behavior for all providers. [Task 1]\n1816:# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/twyne Needle scope, v0.21.0 release, and adaptive editorial drafting\n1817:scope: Keep the Cactus Needle concept separate from an unrelated npm dependency, verify desktop/release boundaries, and apply Keating-style typed private review to editorial generation.\n1818:applies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne; reuse_rule=recheck provider/model behavior, credentials, passkey deployment, and worktree state; local/static proof does not establish live judgement behavior.\n1820:## Task 1: Investigate Needle and publish Twyne 0.21.0\n1824:- rollout_summaries/2026-09-21T06-48-19-f9lZ-twyne_needle_investigation_and_v0210_release.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/21/rollout-2026-09-21T02-48-19-01a0c2b9-00e5-79a2-be4b-13a578e0598f.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-21T09:41:56+00:00, thread_id=01a0c2b9-00e5-79a2-be4b-13a578e0598f, success; release/Railway/assets verified)\n1828:- Cactus-Compute/needle, passage-triage.ts, nothing advice question evidence cut, MiniCPM5-2B, LFM2.5, --jinja, v0.21.0, passkey-origin.ts, twyne.love\n1834:- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/21/rollout-2026-09-21T21-52-13-01a0c6d0-476b-7642-8dae-393ed1e4e8ad.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-22T02:34:25+00:00, thread_id=01a0c6d0-476b-7642-8dae-393ed1e4e8ad, success; static/full-suite verification, no live provider run)\n1843:- for Twyne, use Keating’s approach: deconstruct persona/system behavior into typed inspectable Jev rules that control generation, rather than only locating or rewriting prompt prose. [Task 2]\n1852:- A discovered package name is not the product model integration. Passkey production must use RP ID `twyne.love` and allow both apex/www origins; validate the deployed endpoint. [Task 1]\n2298:# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/twyne Jev provider, rubric, and writing tools\n2300:applies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne plus /home/diogenes/Projects/notorganic-provider; reuse_rule=reinspect both dirty worktrees and deploy state; direct TypeSafe use is local-only when Not Organic is enabled.\n2306:- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/18/rollout-2026-09-18T19-43-22-01a0b6e7-3c95-7543-9f88-4698f314c385.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-18T23:58:45+00:00, thread_id=01a0b6e7-3c95-7543-9f88-4698f314c385, partial; source changes uncommitted and undeployed)\n2307:- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/18/rollout-2026-09-18T19-09-28-01a0b6c8-324a-7d60-a2fa-a16f00cc5a18.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-18T23:37:12+00:00, thread_id=01a0b6c8-324a-7d60-a2fa-a16f00cc5a18, partial; staged gateway work preceded guarded completion)\n2317:- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/18/rollout-2026-09-18T19-43-22-01a0b6e7-3c95-7543-9f88-4698f314c385.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-18T23:58:45+00:00, thread_id=01a0b6e7-3c95-7543-9f88-4698f314c385, partial; final checks intentionally omitted)\n2318:- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/18/rollout-2026-09-18T19-09-28-01a0b6c8-324a-7d60-a2fa-a16f00cc5a18.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-18T23:37:12+00:00, thread_id=01a0b6c8-324a-7d60-a2fa-a16f00cc5a18, partial; earlier 1104-test evidence)\n2328:- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/18/rollout-2026-09-18T19-43-22-01a0b6e7-3c95-7543-9f88-4698f314c385.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-18T23:58:45+00:00, thread_id=01a0b6e7-3c95-7543-9f88-4698f314c385, partial; UI checks deferred to user)\n2342:- Production Twyne calls Not Organic using DPoP and `judgement:evaluate` at `POST /v1/judgement`; direct `TYPESAFE_API_KEY` is only loopback/local fallback. The provider owns the key, typed state/questions transport, model alias resolution, and per-account reserve -> dispatch -> accept -> settle/reconcile accounting. [Task 1]\n2343:- Jev question types are `noul`, `choice`, and `score`; normalize Twyne arrays into TypeSafe Choice maps, retain Score ordered arrays, bound requests, avoid upstream response bodies that may echo documents, and surface uncertain/missing usage rather than silently billing zero. The observed rate was `0.042` microUSD per input token. [Task 1]\n2352:# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/twyne editor drag/drop and offline interaction plan\n2354:applies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne; reuse_rule=retest exact browser/editor behavior before claiming completion; planning notes are not implementation authority.\n2360:- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/18/rollout-2026-09-18T19-09-28-01a0b6c8-3247-7842-bca9-9750c78aad2e.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-18T21:18:15+00:00, thread_id=01a0b6c8-3247-7842-bca9-9750c78aad2e, partial; focused tests passed but E2E has two unresolved cases)\n2364:- Qwik, TipTap, ProseMirror, preventdefault:dragover, preventdefault:dragleave, preventdefault:drop, Dropcursor, twyne-dropcursor, file-drag.ts, drag-selection.e2e.ts\n2366:## Task 2: Plan slash menu, viewport, offline toast, and browser/desktop local models, partial\n2370:- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/18/rollout-2026-09-18T19-09-28-01a0b6c8-3247-7842-bca9-9750c78aad2e.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-18T21:18:15+00:00, thread_id=01a0b6c8-3247-7842-bca9-9750c78aad2e, partial; combined plan selected, local-model design incomplete)\n2379:- the user chose \"Everything in one plan,\" including browser and desktop local models, and chose a bottom-left toast-pattern offline notice; markdown shortcuts were \"not a required part of the editor.\" [Task 2]\n2387:- `DEFAULT_LAYOUT.marginBottom: 1` overrides the normal 4rem fallback, and nested scrollers lack `scrollMargin`/`scrollThreshold`. Twyne's IndexedDB/service-worker shell is genuinely local-first, but sync, AI, auth, collaboration, and publishing remain remote; browser local models likely use Transformers.js/WebGPU/cached ONNX and desktop has a LiteRT seam. [Task 2]\n2391:- After Chromium installation, E2E had 1 pass/2 fail: multi-paragraph move works, but single-paragraph movement and drop-caret visibility fail and `.twyne-dropcursor` was absent. Inspect the exact test plus generated Dropcursor DOM/configuration before claiming drag/drop complete. [Task 1]\n2394:# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/twyne local Codex Fugu/Sakana catalog configuration\n2396:applies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne with user config at /home/diogenes/.codex; reuse_rule=recheck provider documentation/live model endpoint and installed config before changing aliases, versions, or defaults.\n2402:- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/18/rollout-2026-09-18T18-47-44-01a0b6b4-4bfc-7fe2-8b6a-2c1695320c03.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-18T23:09:36+00:00, thread_id=01a0b6b4-4bfc-7fe2-8b6a-2c1695320c03, success; installed and strict-config validated)\n2634:applies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating and /home/diogenes/Projects/notorganic-provider; reuse_rule=recheck dirty worktrees, installed desktop version, fresh token/DPoP flow, Portkey configuration, and Convex behavior.\n2659:- when the user said “most computer use, don't do computer use on your own” -> use code/logs/HTTP/tests and leave desktop/browser interaction to the user [Task 2]\n2670:- Health/Railway success/direct Portkey stream do not prove desktop chat. Verify fresh public token exchange, DPoP request, exact stream, reservation, and rendered UI. Retryable failures get fresh DPoP proofs; insufficient credits do not retry. [Task 2]\n2695:- v3.15.0, Entire checkpoints, Paddle, GitHub cached objects, credential rotation, release.yml, desktop-release.yml, Windows .exe, Android .apk\n2747:- yell HERE I AM, bland and muted, agentFacts.ts, sitePhotos.ts, Paper Desktop, Weekly MCP limit reached, GitNexus, graft build, PYTHONHOME\n2869:# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/keating immediate chat, production account auth, and signed desktop distribution\n2872:applies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating; reuse_rule=recheck the heavily dirty worktree, live Railway configuration, CI/desktop runners, signing/publication state, and real desktop/browser flows; focused/local checks do not prove public release or authenticated production use.\n2907:- when the user wanted Anthropic token handling “done automatically” -> distinguish provider/browser OAuth limits from desktop-native callbacks, and do not claim automatic web authentication without real provider/browser verification. [Task 1]\n2908:- when the user said “we should also get the desktop app working for windows” -> cross-platform delivery includes an installer plus native dependencies, process handling, filesystem/OAuth/credential paths, and GUI/runtime smoke proof, not merely a build target. [Task 2]\n2916:- The dedicated release key's public fingerprint/key live at `desktop/signing/fingerprint.txt` and `desktop/signing/keating-release-key.asc`; private material belongs only in isolated CI secrets/keyrings. `sign-release.mjs` makes deterministic `SHA256SUMS`, detached signatures, public-key export, and optional embedded RPM signatures. [Task 3]\n2923:- AppStream compose initially failed from a missing compose addon and partial URLs: require host `appstreamcli compose`, run `--no-net`, and fail before export if catalog generation is unavailable. `rpmsign` was initially missing and end-to-end RPM embedded signing remains unproved. Headless Flatpak DBus errors are not desktop-session/OAuth/audio/permissions/storage proof; local exports/GitHub Pages enablement do not prove the repository or release artifacts were committed, pushed, public, or install-tested. [Task 3]\n3492:## Task 1: Rebuild mobile and desktop session library with fork/category navigation\n3500:- SessionBrowser, SessionBrowserDesktop, SessionBrowserSheet, SESSION_BROWSER_BREAKPOINT, SessionCard, Select.tsx, session-switch.ts, session-library-refresh.ts, 320px, 109.4ms, 147.6ms\n3508:- `SESSION_BROWSER_BREAKPOINT = 1024`: desktop uses `SessionBrowserDesktop`, mobile uses `SessionBrowserSheet`. Filters live inside the mobile dialog; shared `Select` replaces native selects and needs dialog-safe positioning, keyboard support, long-menu scrolling, and label truncation. [Task 1]\n3660:- Interleave, Twyne, Keating, product-icons, interleave-mark.png, twyne-mark.png, 268e9bd, git push rad main, rad auth, dirty-worktree, prek\n3677:- “update the icon used for interleave, also for twyne keep the animal icon, for keating the letter icon should be used” -> preserve product-specific identity: paired gecko for Interleave, griffin animal mark for Twyne, green K letter mark for Keating. [Task 3]\n3686:- The icon-only commit `268e9bd27d5e8000f6daece8efac4de1cfc3b0c1` updated six assets: `apps/landing/brand/{interleave-mark.png,interleave.png,keating.png,twyne-mark.png}` and `apps/portal/public/brand/{interleave.png,twyne.png}`. `bun run build:landing` and focused landing/email tests passed (22 tests, 0 failures, 359 assertions); SHA-256 checks confirmed reviewed assets matched the landing/identity deployment. [Task 3]\n3724:- “telemetry should be opt out actually” and support for “desktop, mobile, cli, tui, and web” -> SDK behavior needs disclosure, project/machine controls, DO_NOT_TRACK/CI suppression, minimization, and opt-in replay, while remaining separately installable from Traction. [Task 1]\n3737:# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/twyne v0.19.1 release and native Devenv pre-push hook\n3739:scope: Review, version, tag, publish, and verify the Twyne Qwik/Devenv release path.\n3740:applies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne; reuse_rule=release/tag/CI/asset facts are time-specific; inspect current branch, workflow, and hook chain first.\n3746:- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/05/rollout-2026-09-05T05-47-11-01a070f7-0264-7793-aad9-e06b6a709c20.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-05T09:53:51+00:00, thread_id=01a070f7-0264-7793-aad9-e06b6a709c20, success; Windows packaging pending at check)\n3821:scope: Prepare Stich releases without absorbing dirty work; operate secure desktop auth, committed-content Railway/Radicle workflows, and custom-domain proof.\n3864:- Release checker requires coordinated SemVer across root, `apps/{agent,desktop,mcp,mobile,web}/package.json`, and `apps/mobile/app.json`, plus annotated `v<version>` tag and no unexpected version tag at `HEAD`. `bun run release:version`, `bun run release:check`, and `release:publish` (`git push --follow-tags`) are the defined sequence. [Task 1]\n3870:- Railway custom-domain ownership used `_railway-verify`, `_railway-verify.mail`, and `_railway-verify.www`; local server/domain smoke, workspace tests, web build/typecheck, agent build, 5 web Playwright tests, and 10 desktop renderer tests passed. For a connected browser, open a local image by base64-encoding it into `page.setContent()` then `page.bringToFront()`; `file://` navigation is rejected. [Task 3]\n4001:# Task Group: cross-repository native Devenv git hooks for Keating, Not Organic, and Twyne\n4003:applies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/{dio-machines,keating,notorganic-provider,twyne}; reuse_rule=inspect each repo's current Devenv input/lock, hook chain, canonical passing check, and dirty tree before changing hooks.\n4013:- git-hooks.nix, devenv.nix, devenv.yaml, prek, .pre-commit-config.yaml, Entire, notorganic:check, twyne:release:check, core.hooksPath\n4023:- Keating already has repo-specific hooks; refresh stale generated `prek` state with `devenv shell -- prek install --force --hook-type pre-push`. Not Organic uses pre-commit `notorganic-check` -> `devenv tasks run notorganic:check`; Twyne uses `twyne-release-check` on pre-commit/pre-push -> `devenv tasks run twyne:release:check`. [Task 1]\n4028:- Do not use Twyne `twyne:check` as a hook while its baseline has 165 unrelated Prettier failures. Preserve dirty changes; `devenv info` may print secrets, so never use/store its full output. Vet `unknown error` is unverified. [Task 1]\n4058:scope: Reuse the shared accessible controls, task-first desktop copy, calendar creation interaction, runtime themes, and narrow-screen navigation.\n4059:applies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/stich; reuse_rule=recheck the dirty tree and generated desktop CSS; use @stich/ui primitives rather than reviving screen-local controls.\n4061:## Task 1: Migrate desktop controls and dialogs onto accessible primitives\n4077:- Shared controls are in `packages/ui/src/components/{field,input,number-input,select,checkbox,dialog,badge,progress}.tsx`; desktop Button/Input are compatibility re-exports. `Select` is a portalled fixed-position listbox; `Dialog` portals, traps focus, handles Escape/scroll lock, and restores opener focus. `NumberInput` retains native number semantics, clamps/steps safely, and its repeating timer reads a ref-backed value. [Task 1]\n4115:# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/stich desktop renderer, AI composer, Stalwart credentials, and inbox imports\n4116:scope: Diagnose bundled Electrobun startup, deliver compact provider-backed desktop AI input, safely investigate Stalwart/JMAP credentials, and ship mail-reference/Google-file-import features.\n4119:## Task 1: Diagnose and fix blank Electrobun desktop window\n4123:- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/stich, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/02/rollout-2026-09-02T02-12-34-01a060bf-7153-7851-b477-34a0f44e14d2.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-02T23:59:38+00:00, thread_id=01a060bf-7153-7851-b477-34a0f44e14d2, success; real-renderer tests and unsigned build passed)\n4127:- Electrobun, real-renderer Playwright, Bun.build, @openuidev/react-lang, process is not defined, process.env[\"NODE_ENV\"], import.meta.env, electrobun.config.ts, build-desktop-app.ts\n4133:- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/stich, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/02/rollout-2026-09-02T02-12-34-01a060bf-7153-7851-b477-34a0f44e14d2.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-02T23:59:38+00:00, thread_id=01a060bf-7153-7851-b477-34a0f44e14d2, partial; reset was rolled back and remains unproven)\n4143:- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/stich, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/02/rollout-2026-09-02T02-12-34-01a060bf-7153-7851-b477-34a0f44e14d2.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-02T23:59:38+00:00, thread_id=01a060bf-7153-7851-b477-34a0f44e14d2, success; deployed and production login rendered)\n4151:- when the user reported “blank when i start up the desktop app” with a screenshot -> reproduce the actual bundled renderer and inspect page errors instead of treating the native shell as the whole problem [Task 1]\n4156:- Electrobun browser views are Bun-built rather than Vite-built. `@openuidev/react-lang` may evaluate `process.env[\"NODE_ENV\"]`; replace `process.env` wholesale with a static `{ NODE_ENV: ... }` object in both `apps/desktop/electrobun.config.ts` and `e2e/build-desktop-app.ts`, since a narrow `process.env.NODE_ENV` define misses bracket notation/aliasing. Use optional `import.meta.env?.VITE_STICH_AGENT_URL` with the localhost fallback because Bun-built views lack Vite env injection. [Task 1]\n4157:- Completed validation for that fix: desktop typecheck, all nine real-renderer E2E tests, and unsigned Electrobun build. [Task 1]\n4167:# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/dio-machines desktop GUI app support\n4169:scope: Locate the configuration boundary for ChatGPT-style desktop applications on the workstation profile; this is an orientation record, not an installation decision.\n4172:## Task 1: Assess ChatGPT-style desktop GUI applications\n4176:- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/dio-machines, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/07/rollout-2026-09-07T15-45-17-01a07d67-4dc9-7d12-b97a-d91bfadd07b2.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-07T19:45:46+00:00, thread_id=01a07d67-4dc9-7d12-b97a-d91bfadd07b2, uncertain; investigation only, no configuration change)\n4180:- gui.nix, APPIMAGES.md, desktop-apps, AppImage, Nix, workstation, chatgpt, claude-desktop, jan-ai, lmstudio, ollama\n4184:- Workstation-profile desktop applications belong in `home/packages/gui.nix`; the README describes it as “developer desktop apps — workstation only.” Applications managed outside Nix are documented in `docs/APPIMAGES.md`. [Task 1]\n4188:- “what about guis like that chatgpt desktop app” was underspecified, so no installation or code change was appropriate -> first clarify whether the goal is Linux alternatives, one named ChatGPT-style desktop app, or integration/management through dio-machines. [Task 1]\n4190:# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/twyne Bun-native release tooling and preserved hooks\n4192:applies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne; reuse_rule=reuse only after inspecting current package scripts, tag-triggered workflow, hooks, branch, and dirty tree; this supersedes older Twyne guidance that requires a Bumpy note for a code push.\n4194:## Task 1: Migrate Twyne from Bumpy to Bun-native versioning\n4198:- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/08/30/rollout-2026-08-30T20-42-27-01a05544-7ed1-7ed1-ae02-e54bc55f4c73.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-31T01:50:21+00:00, thread_id=01a05544-7ed1-7ed1-ae02-e54bc55f4c73, success; commit 6c8cd0a pushed to main)\n4211:- Twyne now uses `release:version: bun pm version`, `release:publish: git push --follow-tags`, and `release:check: bun scripts/check-release-version.ts`. `preversion`, `postversion`, and `.githooks/pre-push.pre-entire` all call the shared guard. [Task 1]\n4212:- `scripts/check-release-version.ts` checks SemVer, the annotated `v<version>` tag, tagged `package.json` version equality, and unexpected `v*` tags at `HEAD`. `bun pm version` runs lifecycle hooks and creates the version commit, but verify that it actually created the annotated tag; `git push --follow-tags` preserves Twyne’s existing `v*` GitHub release trigger. [Task 1]\n4221:scope: Plan early validation for Twyne/Keating, review secure public-client payments, and turn hiring critiques into concise questions.\n4222:applies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Documents/Codex/2026-08-23/realtime-voice-chat with related projects=/home/diogenes/Projects/{keating,twyne,notorganic-provider}; reuse_rule=recheck live provider, policy, payment, and product state before using projections or making production claims.\n4258:- payment is the shared launch gateway: web first, desktop first-class where practical, mobile deferred until production-ready; NotOrganic Provider must own browser authentication, checkout, webhooks, subscriptions, and entitlements [Task 2]\n4276:applies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne, with global paths under /home/diogenes/.codex and /home/diogenes; reuse_rule=reuse the configuration pattern, not the Keenable credential or live-service claim; recheck the server handshake after client reload.\n4282:- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/08/27/rollout-2026-08-27T23-36-53-01a04671-1d0e-7ce1-93cd-967e613879b5.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-28T03:41:15+00:00, thread_id=01a04671-1d0e-7ce1-93cd-967e613879b5, success; configuration and loader verified, live handshake not run)\n4327:- Not Organic is the stable account and control-plane boundary for cross-device learner synchronization, shared pedagogical revisions, evolution history, active-version selection, and authorization. Browser, mobile, desktop, CLI, and connected self-hosted instances are account-scoped clients/contributors; they must not bind identity, durable state, or sync directly to provider-specific sandbox endpoints. [ad-hoc note]\n4474:# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/twyne crawler discovery, dossiers, and historical v0.17.0 release\n4476:applies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne; reuse_rule=recheck domain, routes, public query/index, current Bun release policy, Railway state, and dirty worktree before applying to a later deploy or release.\n4482:- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/08/24/rollout-2026-08-24T12-55-29-01a034b2-d30a-7da1-a246-090ccebed787.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-24T20:37:30+00:00, thread_id=01a034b2-d30a-7da1-a246-090ccebed787, success; focused tests/build and local endpoint smoke checks passed)\n4486:- twyne.love, robots.txt, sitemap.xml, 301, Qwik routes, listForSitemap, by_kind_publishedAt, XML escaping, lastmod, take(1000)\n4488:## Task 2: File dossiers, fix reviewer findings, and publish Twyne 0.17.0\n4492:- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/08/24/rollout-2026-08-24T12-55-29-01a034b2-d30a-7da1-a246-090ccebed787.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-24T20:37:30+00:00, thread_id=01a034b2-d30a-7da1-a246-090ccebed787, success; workflow and public assets verified)\n4500:- when the user clarified “this site domain is twyne.love” and questioned Convex -> keep robots/sitemap frontend-served; use Convex only as the bounded public URL-data source [Task 1]\n4617:- The worktree was heavily dirty -> protect pre-existing edits and prefer disjoint review files. Browser visual acceptance was unavailable, and Vet was skipped as requested; exercise `/review` at desktop/narrow widths and run Vet before calling the feature fully production-verified. [Task 1]\n4650:applies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Documents/Codex/2026-08-15/hey-i with related design scope=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating and /home/diogenes/Projects/twyne; reuse_rule=reuse these architecture boundaries for browser-first learner products; re-check current browser quotas and Tinker pricing/account limits before implementation.\n4932:- Browser checks covered drag persistence, review reducing due 6 -> 5, desktop/mobile/light/dark layouts, and native browser export. Focused tests (14), full suite (617), typecheck, Panda/Vite/Nitro/PWA build, and diff check passed. [Task 1][Task 2]\n4940:# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/twyne structured application errors and safe hosted-AI UX\n4941:scope: Twyne application-error contract, notices, offline UX, sanitized diagnostics, and interview recovery.\n4942:applies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne; reuse_rule=reuse for AI-error/fallback changes; test remaining unexercised boundaries and browser failure behavior.\n4948:- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/07/30/rollout-2026-07-30T21-23-33-019fb5c4-fa2f-7431-86be-cedd140eb5a7.jsonl, updated_at=2026-07-24T05:07:45+00:00, thread_id=019fb5c4-fa2f-7431-86be-cedd140eb5a7, success; targeted test/build evidence)\n5016:- devenv up, devenv.nix, process-compose, terminal-shell, tui, web, desktop, mobile-web, storybook, port 3000, port 8081, port 6006, readiness check fail\n5020:- when the user asked for a “devenv up command that starts the terminal shell, the tui, the web app, and the desktop application” and added “should also start storybook” -> include the complete adjacent developer workspace, not only the first listed apps [Task 1]\n5024:- In devenv 2.2.2, set `process.manager.implementation = \"process-compose\"`; use `process.managers.process-compose.tui.enable = true` and `processes.<name>.process-compose.is_interactive = true` for PTY shell/TUI processes. Six configured names are `terminal-shell`, `tui`, `web`, `desktop`, `mobile-web`, and `storybook`; web is 3000, Expo web 8081, Storybook 6006, and desktop waits for web. [Task 1]\n5026:- Use `process-compose -U -u \"$PC_SOCKET_PATH\" process logs mobile-web,storybook,desktop -n 200 --raw-log` to isolate live process failures. [Task 1]\n5031:- Static validation is insufficient: shell, TUI, and web started, but `mobile-web` failed readiness on `http://127.0.0.1:8081` with `connection refused`, Storybook failed, and desktop did not launch successfully. Re-run each independently and inspect logs before completion claims. [Task 1]\n5034:# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/twyne ATProto OAuth, Convex sync authorization, and safe global error toasts\n5036:applies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne; reuse_rule=reuse these local contracts for Twyne auth/error work; recheck OAuth grants, live Convex deployment/logs, and dirty worktree before a deployment claim.\n5042:- rollout_summaries/2026-08-27T00-08-45-AuPp-twyne_atproto_convex_auth_error_toasts.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/08/26/rollout-2026-08-26T20-08-45-01a0408c-3631-7712-bc6f-569ae582aa0b.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-27T03:08:44+00:00, thread_id=01a0408c-3631-7712-bc6f-569ae582aa0b, success)\n5052:- rollout_summaries/2026-08-27T00-08-45-AuPp-twyne_atproto_convex_auth_error_toasts.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/08/26/rollout-2026-08-26T20-08-45-01a0408c-3631-7712-bc6f-569ae582aa0b.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-27T03:08:44+00:00, thread_id=01a0408c-3631-7712-bc6f-569ae582aa0b, success)\n5062:- rollout_summaries/2026-08-27T00-08-45-AuPp-twyne_atproto_convex_auth_error_toasts.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/08/26/rollout-2026-08-26T20-08-45-01a0408c-3631-7712-bc6f-569ae582aa0b.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-27T03:08:44+00:00, thread_id=01a0408c-3631-7712-bc6f-569ae582aa0b, success)\n5272:- `devenv.nix` defines native web, desktop, mobile web, Storybook, and opt-in MCP processes, plus Mailpit SMTP/UI ports 1025/8025. `devenv tasks run stich:check` passed typechecks, tests, web/server smoke, release preflight self-test, workflow validation, and full Playwright; `stich:e2e:railway` verified disposable-account submit, inbox/body read, Sent copy, invalid identity, and cleanup. [Task 1]\n5283:scope: Build an agent-first analytics product across web, desktop, mobile, CLI, and TUI with privacy-aware telemetry and Bun/Railpack deployment.\n5298:- track activity across “desktop, mobile, cli, tui, and web,” but retain an event-spec seam if SDK/TUI may be “something altogether” from the agent product; document tradeoffs instead of forcing unresolved choices [Task 1]\n5310:# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/twyne character-aware narration, premium GPT Live voice, and native Typst workflow\n5311:scope: Extend Twyne’s author-aware editor interaction and native Typst authoring without exposing provider credentials or replacing the visual editor.\n5312:applies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne; reuse_rule=recheck the current dirty tree, browser/device access, Not Organic provider state, and deployment before treating Live voice as production-ready.\n5318:- rollout_summaries/2026-09-26T10-01-32-fcwe-twyne_character_aware_narration_gpt_live_voice_desk.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/26/rollout-2026-09-26T06-01-32-01a0dd29-b2ed-78c0-b5b2-143eed227156.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-26T10:38:47+00:00, thread_id=01a0dd29-b2ed-78c0-b5b2-143eed227156, success; focused speech tests passed)\n5328:- rollout_summaries/2026-09-26T10-01-32-fcwe-twyne_character_aware_narration_gpt_live_voice_desk.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/26/rollout-2026-09-26T06-01-32-01a0dd29-b2ed-78c0-b5b2-143eed227156.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-26T10:38:47+00:00, thread_id=01a0dd29-b2ed-78c0-b5b2-143eed227156, partial; deterministic checks/builds passed, production/browser/provider proof open)\n5338:- rollout_summaries/2026-09-26T11-02-50-0rjp-twyne_native_typst_editor_implementation_deployment.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/26/rollout-2026-09-26T07-02-50-01a0dd61-d08c-7f71-9e6c-24cf8966c3df.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-29T01:38:36+00:00, thread_id=01a0dd61-d08c-7f71-9e6c-24cf8966c3df, success; CI, Railway, and live proof/PDF/persistence smoke passed)\n5353:- Twyne’s Live client uses Not Organic `/v1/live/sessions` through same-origin `/api/live`; provider billing/entitlements remain authoritative and Twyne never receives an OpenAI key. The implementation reserves ceilings of `$0.50` per session and `$0.05` per delegated action, not quoted rates. [Task 2]\n5355:- The provider patch adds a one-time `$2.50` Twyne welcome allowance separate from Keating, with idempotency and paid-history exclusions. Delegated replies are accepted only for IDs observed from trusted upstream events; inspect the separate provider dirty tree before follow-up work. [Task 2]\n5357:- Core paths are `src/utils/typst/{document,serialize,export,client,session,compiler.worker}.ts`, `src/components/editor/{typst-workspace,typst-code-editor}.tsx`, `src/components/editor/extensions/raw-typst.ts`, `src/utils/{idb,convex-sync}.ts`, `convex/schema.ts`, and `convex/sync.ts`. Production smoke at `https://twyne.love/editor/` rendered two proof pages, produced a `%PDF-` download, preserved content on reload, and showed no runtime errors. [Task 3]\n5363:- Direct browser-global assignment/restoration caused 105 Bun failures -> save/restore descriptors with `Object.defineProperty`. Before push run `bun run lint`, `bun run fmt.check`, Convex typecheck, and the full suite; final validation was `1605 pass`, `40 skip`, `0 fail`, GitHub run `36508550529` success, and Railway deployment `2261ee43-1626-496b-8388-5e0c2d749989` successful. `bun add` can need `BUN_TMPDIR=/tmp BUN_INSTALL_CACHE_DIR=/tmp/twyne-bun-cache`. [Task 3]\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":21078},"formatted_output":"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 18066)\nTotal output lines: 273\n\n1:# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/baste Makepad versus GPUI studio-framework selection\n3:applies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/baste; reuse_rule=confirm the current GPUI/GPUI Kit release and target platforms before implementation because GPUI is pre-1.0.\n5:## Task 1: Compare Makepad and GPUI for a Baste studio\n9:- rollout_summaries/2026-10-04T04-46-42-dK0S-makepad_vs_gpui_baste_studio.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/baste, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/10/04/rollout-2026-10-04T00-46-42-01a1053c-5484-7860-b895-c654c9e25fd6.jsonl, updated_at=2026-10-04T04:47:19+00:00, thread_id=01a1053c-5484-7860-b895-c654c9e25fd6, success; direct framework comparison)\n13:- Makepad, GPUI, GPUI Kit, Rust GUI, Zed, Studio, WASM, native desktop, candidate grids, inspectors, generation queues\n17:- when asking “makepad v gpui” -> give a direct comparative assessment and decision fit rather than starting implementation work [Task 1]\n21:- GPUI is the Baste default for a dense native productivity studio: entities/shared state, declarative views, imperative custom elements, keyboard actions, async services, and testing support fit projects, candidate grids, inspectors, and generation queues. [Task 1]\n23:- GPUI Kit is separate from core GPUI; verify its exact matching version and accessibility/component capabilities instead of attributing them to GPUI itself. [Task 1]\n27:- GPUI is pre-1.0 with frequent breaking changes -> inspect the exact release/fork and Zed source before committing Baste architecture to an API or platform assumption. [Task 1]\n29:# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/notorganic-provider shared account knowledge connections for Keating and Twyne\n30:scope: Implement account-owned knowledge sources with app-specific grants, explicit tool consent, and fail-closed revocation across Not Organic, Keating, and Twyne.\n31:applies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/notorganic-provider with integrations in /home/diogenes/Projects/{keating,twyne}; reuse_rule=retest current provider contracts, dirty diffs, deployment/CORS, and a real account before claiming cross-app readiness.\n37:- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/notorganic-provider, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/10/03/rollout-2026-10-03T08-22-46-01a101b7-83a5-7863-897a-869bf3d11c1b.jsonl, updated_at=2026-10-03T23:33:08+00:00, thread_id=01a101b7-83a5-7863-897a-869bf3d11c1b, partial; implementation/focused validation passed, deployment and real-account proof open)\n47:- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/notorganic-provider, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/10/03/rollout-2026-10-03T08-22-46-01a101b7-83a5-7863-897a-869bf3d11c1b.jsonl, updated_at=2026-10-03T23:33:08+00:00, thread_id=01a101b7-83a5-7863-897a-869bf3d11c1b, partial; 53 focused tests/260 assertions, full web build blocked)\n53:## Task 3: Integrate account sources and MCP review in Twyne\n57:- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/notorganic-provider, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/10/03/rollout-2026-10-03T08-22-46-01a101b7-83a5-7863-897a-869bf3d11c1b.jsonl, updated_at=2026-10-03T23:33:08+00:00, thread_id=01a101b7-83a5-7863-897a-869bf3d11c1b, partial; 98 targeted checks/typechecks/builds passed, live gateway proof open)\n65:- when asking for knowledge bases to “carry over” into Keating and Twyne and be “easy to add or revoke an apps access to them” -> default to account-level ownership, per-app grants, explicit revocation, and guided setup [Task 1]\n73:- Twyne trusted Convex actions bind verified DID/sessionVersion to fresh DPoP tokens. Research requires enabling research, choosing a source search tool, and selecting “Your MCP servers”; sign-out, revocation, and schema changes clear/fail closed. [Task 3]\n79:- `ERR_CONNECTION_REFUSED` after an owned Twyne preview stopped is an environment/process condition, while localhost-to-deployed Convex CORS preflight must be verified separately; neither establishes deployed feature behavior. [Task 3]\n114:- Ground the work in the knot mark, forest/cream/lime palette, and authentic Twyne, Keating, Interleave, Stich, Voxq, and Baste marks. Keep payment language bounded as “launching this October”/planned, not production-payment proof. [Task 1]\n123:# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/twyne editor responsiveness and Typst export parity\n125:applies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne; reuse_rule=reprofile the current editor path and re-run real compiler/browser checks before quoting performance or live deployment results.\n131:- rollout_summari