llout-2026-09-29T17-06-37-01a0eefd-acc3-7f01-a57d-1f767284796b.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-29T23:43:49+00:00, thread_id=01a0eefd-acc3-7f01-a57d-1f767284796b, partial; metadata and an earlier local HyperFrames MP4 were validated, crawler proof remains open)\n628:- opengraph, og:image, TWYNE_SOCIAL_IMAGE, RouterHead, router-head.tsx, seo.ts, twyne-editorial-v2.jpg, magick, twyne-writers-desk-loop-v1.mp4, ffprobe\n634:- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/29/rollout-2026-09-29T17-06-37-01a0eefd-acc3-7f01-a57d-1f767284796b.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-29T23:43:49+00:00, thread_id=01a0eefd-acc3-7f01-a57d-1f767284796b, failed/pending; fal rejected before queueing for exhausted balance)\n638:- bytedance/seedance-2.5/image-to-video, Seedance 2.5, fal, SUBMISSION_REJECTED, exhausted balance, seedance-job-v1.json, generate-social-desk-video.ts, twyne-writers-desk-overlay.svg\n648:- Site defaults come from `src/components/router-head/router-head.tsx`, route declarations override them, and social constants belong in `src/utils/seo.ts` with `TWYNE_SITE_ORIGIN=https://twyne.love`. The new source asset is `public/assets/social/twyne-editorial-v2.jpg`; Prettier and ESLint passed, but final crawler/browser proof was not recorded. [Task 1]\n649:- The old `twyne-writers-desk-loop-v1.mp4` is a verified 1200×630, 30 fps, 6-second silent H.264 local artifact. Intel Mesa HyperFrames capture required translating Chrome `--use-angle=gl-egl` to `--use-angle=gl`; it is historical camera-shift output, not a Seedance result. [Task 1]\n650:- Seedance preparation is resumable: `scripts/generate-social-desk-video.ts` persists `social-preview-video/seedance-job-v1.json` before submission to avoid duplicate charges. Request 720p, 6 seconds, silent, high-bitrate H.264 with the clean background as start/end; composite `twyne-writers-desk-overlay.svg` in HyperFrames, never in generated footage. [Task 2]\n686:# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/twyne illuminated initials, Typst proof, and editorial-native tooling\n687:scope: Make Typst authoring/proof and generated initial artwork feel native to Twyne’s paper/ink/vermilion writing desk while preserving editable manuscript text, export fidelity, and explicit publication gates.\n688:applies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne; reuse_rule=reinspect current editor/export contracts, actual generated-asset inventory, and landing-image approval before changing styling, claiming asset coverage, or publishing.\n694:- rollout_summaries/2026-09-29T02-53-14-wfgW-twyne_typst_native_tooling_proof_styling.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/28/rollout-2026-09-28T22-53-14-01a0eb14-a63e-75c1-840d-6c9f28175f26.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-29T03:56:43+00:00, thread_id=01a0eb14-a63e-75c1-840d-6c9f28175f26, partial; final browser/typecheck claim was reported, earlier focused E2E setup failed)\n704:- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/29/rollout-2026-09-29T00-33-25-01a0eb70-5e56-7400-88f6-69c619eb553f.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-29T19:26:16+00:00, thread_id=01a0eb70-5e56-7400-88f6-69c619eb553f, success; editor/export and rendered pages validated, publication awaits user landing-image selection)\n708:- illuminated-initials, drop-cap, imagegen, transparent-assets, AVIF, Typst, browser-print, twyne-release-023, landing-options, manuscript garden\n712:- when the user said the Typst UI looked “tagged on as an afterthought” and requested “much better tooling that also appears visually native to the rest of the editor” -> reuse Twyne’s established paper/ink/vermilion toolbar language rather than creating a separate Typst visual system [Task 1]\n721:- The current drop cap is CSS-driven at `.twyne-editor .ProseMirror > p:first-of-type::first-letter`; artwork must layer around the editable opening character, not replace manuscript text. Relevant helpers include `src/utils/illuminated-initials.ts`, `print-ornaments.ts`, `page-ornaments.ts`, and `src/utils/typst/decorative-assets.ts`. [Task 2]\n722:- For transparent initials, explicitly prohibit parchment, frames, shadows, glow, captions, watermarks, and extra lettering. Normalize generated output before committing; generated workspace assets must not remain only in an image-generation cache. AVIF conversion was reported as 62.49 MB to 12.14 MB. The isolated commit in `/tmp/twyne-release-023` passed the full 1,628-test suite, production build, and `git diff --check`, but was not published. [Task 2]\n726:- A focused Playwright run was blocked first by sandbox frontend startup and then by missing `.ProseMirror` during seed/setup. Treat the later claim of four passing browser checks as reported evidence needing an independent rerun after final changes; four existing lint warnings also remained. `bun add` can need `BUN_TMPDIR=/tmp BUN_INSTALL_CACHE_DIR=/tmp/twyne-bun-cache`. [Task 1]\n730:# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/twyne landing artwork, avatars, editor actions, and fluid House work\n731:scope: Apply Twyne's editorial UI direction across landing imagery, writer identity, compact editor actions, and the in-flow/House experience without overstating incomplete browser or sync proof.\n732:applies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne; reuse_rule=reinspect the live worktree, SSR route, current editor/store contracts, and authenticated profile flow before claiming UI or persistence completion.\n738:- rollout_summaries/2026-09-29T16-46-26-rtLH-twyne_landing_artwork_and_profile_avatars.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/29/rollout-2026-09-29T12-46-26-01a0ee0f-7a28-7c02-91fa-0e4cc2271ce9.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-29T19:27:49+00:00, thread_id=01a0ee0f-7a28-7c02-91fa-0e4cc2271ce9, partial; landing composition planned, avatar code/assets added but final browser and checks remain open)\n748:- rollout_summaries/2026-09-29T19-19-02-GE0c-twyne_editor_icon_and_dossier_label_polish.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/29/rollout-2026-09-29T15-19-02-01a0ee9b-2e36-7f43-904b-e4af84b76ebc.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-29T19:23:21+00:00, thread_id=01a0ee9b-2e36-7f43-904b-e4af84b76ebc, partial; icon/state implementation checked, final copy and browser spacing unverified)\n758:- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/29/rollout-2026-09-29T21-21-53-01a0efe7-60c8-7c41-aeae-38137ec6cbde.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-29T18:54:27+00:00, thread_id=01a0efe7-60c8-7c41-aeae-38137ec6cbde, partial; route/flow/backend work exists but SSR, browser, codegen, and deployment proof are open)\n759:- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/29/rollout-2026-09-29T21-21-53-01a0efe7-60e5-7fa1-b18e-e9b4851fd5d4.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-30T10:14:40+00:00, thread_id=01a0efe7-60e5-7fa1-b18e-e9b4851fd5d4, partial; UI/architecture exists, but flow/House browser-sync proof remains bounded)\n763:- House, Collection, Folio, Editions, Charter, Amendments, Revisions, flow-conductor.ts, FlowSurface, twyne:zen-mode, house-sync.ts, convex/house.ts, cover lookups\n769:- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/29/rollout-2026-09-29T21-21-53-01a0efe7-60e5-7fa1-b18e-e9b4851fd5d4.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-30T10:14:40+00:00, thread_id=01a0efe7-60e5-7fa1-b18e-e9b4851fd5d4, success; release/production navigation replay passed, authenticated flows remain unexercised)\n786:- Landing page already has `.landing-hero`, `WorkspaceTour`, preview plates, and `.landing-closing-photo`; integrate chosen imagery there. AVIF avatars are `public/assets/avatars/engraved-2026-09/{owl,fox,hare,raven}.avif`; settings fetches/wraps them through the existing upload path, while `account-menu.tsx` follows `api.profiles.getMyHandle` updates. A claimed Twyne handle is required and this is separate from a Not Organic account profile. [Task 1]\n788:- Existing flow primitives are `struggle-tracker.ts`, `struggle-signals.ts`, `margin-rail.tsx`, `background-research.ts`, `user-comments.ts`, and `twyne:zen-mode`. New work is `flow-conductor.ts`, `flow-surface.tsx`, House model/store/sync, and `src/routes/house/index.tsx`; use Twyne palette tokens plus `.dept-label`, `.btn-paper`, `.btn-press`. Cover lookup sends only a Jev-selected title…8066 tokens truncated… Stich releases without absorbing dirty work; operate secure desktop auth, committed-content Railway/Radicle workflows, and custom-domain proof.\n3864:- Release checker requires coordinated SemVer across root, `apps/{agent,desktop,mcp,mobile,web}/package.json`, and `apps/mobile/app.json`, plus annotated `v<version>` tag and no unexpected version tag at `HEAD`. `bun run release:version`, `bun run release:check`, and `release:publish` (`git push --follow-tags`) are the defined sequence. [Task 1]\n3870:- Railway custom-domain ownership used `_railway-verify`, `_railway-verify.mail`, and `_railway-verify.www`; local server/domain smoke, workspace tests, web build/typecheck, agent build, 5 web Playwright tests, and 10 desktop renderer tests passed. For a connected browser, open a local image by base64-encoding it into `page.setContent()` then `page.bringToFront()`; `file://` navigation is rejected. [Task 3]\n4001:# Task Group: cross-repository native Devenv git hooks for Keating, Not Organic, and Twyne\n4003:applies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/{dio-machines,keating,notorganic-provider,twyne}; reuse_rule=inspect each repo's current Devenv input/lock, hook chain, canonical passing check, and dirty tree before changing hooks.\n4013:- git-hooks.nix, devenv.nix, devenv.yaml, prek, .pre-commit-config.yaml, Entire, notorganic:check, twyne:release:check, core.hooksPath\n4023:- Keating already has repo-specific hooks; refresh stale generated `prek` state with `devenv shell -- prek install --force --hook-type pre-push`. Not Organic uses pre-commit `notorganic-check` -> `devenv tasks run notorganic:check`; Twyne uses `twyne-release-check` on pre-commit/pre-push -> `devenv tasks run twyne:release:check`. [Task 1]\n4028:- Do not use Twyne `twyne:check` as a hook while its baseline has 165 unrelated Prettier failures. Preserve dirty changes; `devenv info` may print secrets, so never use/store its full output. Vet `unknown error` is unverified. [Task 1]\n4058:scope: Reuse the shared accessible controls, task-first desktop copy, calendar creation interaction, runtime themes, and narrow-screen navigation.\n4059:applies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/stich; reuse_rule=recheck the dirty tree and generated desktop CSS; use @stich/ui primitives rather than reviving screen-local controls.\n4061:## Task 1: Migrate desktop controls and dialogs onto accessible primitives\n4077:- Shared controls are in `packages/ui/src/components/{field,input,number-input,select,checkbox,dialog,badge,progress}.tsx`; desktop Button/Input are compatibility re-exports. `Select` is a portalled fixed-position listbox; `Dialog` portals, traps focus, handles Escape/scroll lock, and restores opener focus. `NumberInput` retains native number semantics, clamps/steps safely, and its repeating timer reads a ref-backed value. [Task 1]\n4115:# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/stich desktop renderer, AI composer, Stalwart credentials, and inbox imports\n4116:scope: Diagnose bundled Electrobun startup, deliver compact provider-backed desktop AI input, safely investigate Stalwart/JMAP credentials, and ship mail-reference/Google-file-import features.\n4119:## Task 1: Diagnose and fix blank Electrobun desktop window\n4123:- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/stich, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/02/rollout-2026-09-02T02-12-34-01a060bf-7153-7851-b477-34a0f44e14d2.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-02T23:59:38+00:00, thread_id=01a060bf-7153-7851-b477-34a0f44e14d2, success; real-renderer tests and unsigned build passed)\n4127:- Electrobun, real-renderer Playwright, Bun.build, @openuidev/react-lang, process is not defined, process.env[\"NODE_ENV\"], import.meta.env, electrobun.config.ts, build-desktop-app.ts\n4133:- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/stich, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/02/rollout-2026-09-02T02-12-34-01a060bf-7153-7851-b477-34a0f44e14d2.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-02T23:59:38+00:00, thread_id=01a060bf-7153-7851-b477-34a0f44e14d2, partial; reset was rolled back and remains unproven)\n4143:- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/stich, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/02/rollout-2026-09-02T02-12-34-01a060bf-7153-7851-b477-34a0f44e14d2.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-02T23:59:38+00:00, thread_id=01a060bf-7153-7851-b477-34a0f44e14d2, success; deployed and production login rendered)\n4151:- when the user reported “blank when i start up the desktop app” with a screenshot -> reproduce the actual bundled renderer and inspect page errors instead of treating the native shell as the whole problem [Task 1]\n4156:- Electrobun browser views are Bun-built rather than Vite-built. `@openuidev/react-lang` may evaluate `process.env[\"NODE_ENV\"]`; replace `process.env` wholesale with a static `{ NODE_ENV: ... }` object in both `apps/desktop/electrobun.config.ts` and `e2e/build-desktop-app.ts`, since a narrow `process.env.NODE_ENV` define misses bracket notation/aliasing. Use optional `import.meta.env?.VITE_STICH_AGENT_URL` with the localhost fallback because Bun-built views lack Vite env injection. [Task 1]\n4157:- Completed validation for that fix: desktop typecheck, all nine real-renderer E2E tests, and unsigned Electrobun build. [Task 1]\n4167:# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/dio-machines desktop GUI app support\n4169:scope: Locate the configuration boundary for ChatGPT-style desktop applications on the workstation profile; this is an orientation record, not an installation decision.\n4172:## Task 1: Assess ChatGPT-style desktop GUI applications\n4176:- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/dio-machines, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/07/rollout-2026-09-07T15-45-17-01a07d67-4dc9-7d12-b97a-d91bfadd07b2.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-07T19:45:46+00:00, thread_id=01a07d67-4dc9-7d12-b97a-d91bfadd07b2, uncertain; investigation only, no configuration change)\n4180:- gui.nix, APPIMAGES.md, desktop-apps, AppImage, Nix, workstation, chatgpt, claude-desktop, jan-ai, lmstudio, ollama\n4184:- Workstation-profile desktop applications belong in `home/packages/gui.nix`; the README describes it as “developer desktop apps — workstation only.” Applications managed outside Nix are documented in `docs/APPIMAGES.md`. [Task 1]\n4188:- “what about guis like that chatgpt desktop app” was underspecified, so no installation or code change was appropriate -> first clarify whether the goal is Linux alternatives, one named ChatGPT-style desktop app, or integration/management through dio-machines. [Task 1]\n4190:# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/twyne Bun-native release tooling and preserved hooks\n4192:applies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne; reuse_rule=reuse only after inspecting current package scripts, tag-triggered workflow, hooks, branch, and dirty tree; this supersedes older Twyne guidance that requires a Bumpy note for a code push.\n4194:## Task 1: Migrate Twyne from Bumpy to Bun-native versioning\n4198:- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/08/30/rollout-2026-08-30T20-42-27-01a05544-7ed1-7ed1-ae02-e54bc55f4c73.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-31T01:50:21+00:00, thread_id=01a05544-7ed1-7ed1-ae02-e54bc55f4c73, success; commit 6c8cd0a pushed to main)\n4211:- Twyne now uses `release:version: bun pm version`, `release:publish: git push --follow-tags`, and `release:check: bun scripts/check-release-version.ts`. `preversion`, `postversion`, and `.githooks/pre-push.pre-entire` all call the shared guard. [Task 1]\n4212:- `scripts/check-release-version.ts` checks SemVer, the annotated `v<version>` tag, tagged `package.json` version equality, and unexpected `v*` tags at `HEAD`. `bun pm version` runs lifecycle hooks and creates the version commit, but verify that it actually created the annotated tag; `git push --follow-tags` preserves Twyne’s existing `v*` GitHub release trigger. [Task 1]\n4221:scope: Plan early validation for Twyne/Keating, review secure public-client payments, and turn hiring critiques into concise questions.\n4222:applies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Documents/Codex/2026-08-23/realtime-voice-chat with related projects=/home/diogenes/Projects/{keating,twyne,notorganic-provider}; reuse_rule=recheck live provider, policy, payment, and product state before using projections or making production claims.\n4258:- payment is the shared launch gateway: web first, desktop first-class where practical, mobile deferred until production-ready; NotOrganic Provider must own browser authentication, checkout, webhooks, subscriptions, and entitlements [Task 2]\n4276:applies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne, with global paths under /home/diogenes/.codex and /home/diogenes; reuse_rule=reuse the configuration pattern, not the Keenable credential or live-service claim; recheck the server handshake after client reload.\n4282:- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/08/27/rollout-2026-08-27T23-36-53-01a04671-1d0e-7ce1-93cd-967e613879b5.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-28T03:41:15+00:00, thread_id=01a04671-1d0e-7ce1-93cd-967e613879b5, success; configuration and loader verified, live handshake not run)\n4327:- Not Organic is the stable account and control-plane boundary for cross-device learner synchronization, shared pedagogical revisions, evolution history, active-version selection, and authorization. Browser, mobile, desktop, CLI, and connected self-hosted instances are account-scoped clients/contributors; they must not bind identity, durable state, or sync directly to provider-specific sandbox endpoints. [ad-hoc note]\n4474:# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/twyne crawler discovery, dossiers, and historical v0.17.0 release\n4476:applies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne; reuse_rule=recheck domain, routes, public query/index, current Bun release policy, Railway state, and dirty worktree before applying to a later deploy or release.\n4482:- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/08/24/rollout-2026-08-24T12-55-29-01a034b2-d30a-7da1-a246-090ccebed787.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-24T20:37:30+00:00, thread_id=01a034b2-d30a-7da1-a246-090ccebed787, success; focused tests/build and local endpoint smoke checks passed)\n4486:- twyne.love, robots.txt, sitemap.xml, 301, Qwik routes, listForSitemap, by_kind_publishedAt, XML escaping, lastmod, take(1000)\n4488:## Task 2: File dossiers, fix reviewer findings, and publish Twyne 0.17.0\n4492:- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/08/24/rollout-2026-08-24T12-55-29-01a034b2-d30a-7da1-a246-090ccebed787.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-24T20:37:30+00:00, thread_id=01a034b2-d30a-7da1-a246-090ccebed787, success; workflow and public assets verified)\n4500:- when the user clarified “this site domain is twyne.love” and questioned Convex -> keep robots/sitemap frontend-served; use Convex only as the bounded public URL-data source [Task 1]\n4617:- The worktree was heavily dirty -> protect pre-existing edits and prefer disjoint review files. Browser visual acceptance was unavailable, and Vet was skipped as requested; exercise `/review` at desktop/narrow widths and run Vet before calling the feature fully production-verified. [Task 1]\n4650:applies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Documents/Codex/2026-08-15/hey-i with related design scope=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating and /home/diogenes/Projects/twyne; reuse_rule=reuse these architecture boundaries for browser-first learner products; re-check current browser quotas and Tinker pricing/account limits before implementation.\n4932:- Browser checks covered drag persistence, review reducing due 6 -> 5, desktop/mobile/light/dark layouts, and native browser export. Focused tests (14), full suite (617), typecheck, Panda/Vite/Nitro/PWA build, and diff check passed. [Task 1][Task 2]\n4940:# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/twyne structured application errors and safe hosted-AI UX\n4941:scope: Twyne application-error contract, notices, offline UX, sanitized diagnostics, and interview recovery.\n4942:applies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne; reuse_rule=reuse for AI-error/fallback changes; test remaining unexercised boundaries and browser failure behavior.\n4948:- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/07/30/rollout-2026-07-30T21-23-33-019fb5c4-fa2f-7431-86be-cedd140eb5a7.jsonl, updated_at=2026-07-24T05:07:45+00:00, thread_id=019fb5c4-fa2f-7431-86be-cedd140eb5a7, success; targeted test/build evidence)\n5016:- devenv up, devenv.nix, process-compose, terminal-shell, tui, web, desktop, mobile-web, storybook, port 3000, port 8081, port 6006, readiness check fail\n5020:- when the user asked for a “devenv up command that starts the terminal shell, the tui, the web app, and the desktop application” and added “should also start storybook” -> include the complete adjacent developer workspace, not only the first listed apps [Task 1]\n5024:- In devenv 2.2.2, set `process.manager.implementation = \"process-compose\"`; use `process.managers.process-compose.tui.enable = true` and `processes.<name>.process-compose.is_interactive = true` for PTY shell/TUI processes. Six configured names are `terminal-shell`, `tui`, `web`, `desktop`, `mobile-web`, and `storybook`; web is 3000, Expo web 8081, Storybook 6006, and desktop waits for web. [Task 1]\n5026:- Use `process-compose -U -u \"$PC_SOCKET_PATH\" process logs mobile-web,storybook,desktop -n 200 --raw-log` to isolate live process failures. [Task 1]\n5031:- Static validation is insufficient: shell, TUI, and web started, but `mobile-web` failed readiness on `http://127.0.0.1:8081` with `connection refused`, Storybook failed, and desktop did not launch successfully. Re-run each independently and inspect logs before completion claims. [Task 1]\n5034:# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/twyne ATProto OAuth, Convex sync authorization, and safe global error toasts\n5036:applies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne; reuse_rule=reuse these local contracts for Twyne auth/error work; recheck OAuth grants, live Convex deployment/logs, and dirty worktree before a deployment claim.\n5042:- rollout_summaries/2026-08-27T00-08-45-AuPp-twyne_atproto_convex_auth_error_toasts.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/08/26/rollout-2026-08-26T20-08-45-01a0408c-3631-7712-bc6f-569ae582aa0b.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-27T03:08:44+00:00, thread_id=01a0408c-3631-7712-bc6f-569ae582aa0b, success)\n5052:- rollout_summaries/2026-08-27T00-08-45-AuPp-twyne_atproto_convex_auth_error_toasts.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/08/26/rollout-2026-08-26T20-08-45-01a0408c-3631-7712-bc6f-569ae582aa0b.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-27T03:08:44+00:00, thread_id=01a0408c-3631-7712-bc6f-569ae582aa0b, success)\n5062:- rollout_summaries/2026-08-27T00-08-45-AuPp-twyne_atproto_convex_auth_error_toasts.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/08/26/rollout-2026-08-26T20-08-45-01a0408c-3631-7712-bc6f-569ae582aa0b.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-27T03:08:44+00:00, thread_id=01a0408c-3631-7712-bc6f-569ae582aa0b, success)\n5272:- `devenv.nix` defines native web, desktop, mobile web, Storybook, and opt-in MCP processes, plus Mailpit SMTP/UI ports 1025/8025. `devenv tasks run stich:check` passed typechecks, tests, web/server smoke, release preflight self-test, workflow validation, and full Playwright; `stich:e2e:railway` verified disposable-account submit, inbox/body read, Sent copy, invalid identity, and cleanup. [Task 1]\n5283:scope: Build an agent-first analytics product across web, desktop, mobile, CLI, and TUI with privacy-aware telemetry and Bun/Railpack deployment.\n5298:- track activity across “desktop, mobile, cli, tui, and web,” but retain an event-spec seam if SDK/TUI may be “something altogether” from the agent product; document tradeoffs instead of forcing unresolved choices [Task 1]\n5310:# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/twyne character-aware narration, premium GPT Live voice, and native Typst workflow\n5311:scope: Extend Twyne’s author-aware editor interaction and native Typst authoring without exposing provider credentials or replacing the visual editor.\n5312:applies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne; reuse_rule=recheck the current dirty tree, browser/device access, Not Organic provider state, and deployment before treating Live voice as production-ready.\n5318:- rollout_summaries/2026-09-26T10-01-32-fcwe-twyne_character_aware_narration_gpt_live_voice_desk.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/26/rollout-2026-09-26T06-01-32-01a0dd29-b2ed-78c0-b5b2-143eed227156.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-26T10:38:47+00:00, thread_id=01a0dd29-b2ed-78c0-b5b2-143eed227156, success; focused speech tests passed)\n5328:- rollout_summaries/2026-09-26T10-01-32-fcwe-twyne_character_aware_narration_gpt_live_voice_desk.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/26/rollout-2026-09-26T06-01-32-01a0dd29-b2ed-78c0-b5b2-143eed227156.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-26T10:38:47+00:00, thread_id=01a0dd29-b2ed-78c0-b5b2-143eed227156, partial; deterministic checks/builds passed, production/browser/provider proof open)\n5338:- rollout_summaries/2026-09-26T11-02-50-0rjp-twyne_native_typst_editor_implementation_deployment.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/26/rollout-2026-09-26T07-02-50-01a0dd61-d08c-7f71-9e6c-24cf8966c3df.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-29T01:38:36+00:00, thread_id=01a0dd61-d08c-7f71-9e6c-24cf8966c3df, success; CI, Railway, and live proof/PDF/persistence smoke passed)\n5353:- Twyne’s Live client uses Not Organic `/v1/live/sessions` through same-origin `/api/live`; provider billing/entitlements remain authoritative and Twyne never receives an OpenAI key. The implementation reserves ceilings of `$0.50` per session and `$0.05` per delegated action, not quoted rates. [Task 2]\n5355:- The provider patch adds a one-time `$2.50` Twyne welcome allowance separate from Keating, with idempotency and paid-history exclusions. Delegated replies are accepted only for IDs observed from trusted upstream events; inspect the separate provider dirty tree before follow-up work. [Task 2]\n5357:- Core paths are `src/utils/typst/{document,serialize,export,client,session,compiler.worker}.ts`, `src/components/editor/{typst-workspace,typst-code-editor}.tsx`, `src/components/editor/extensions/raw-typst.ts`, `src/utils/{idb,convex-sync}.ts`, `convex/schema.ts`, and `convex/sync.ts`. Production smoke at `https://twyne.love/editor/` rendered two proof pages, produced a `%PDF-` download, preserved content on reload, and showed no runtime errors. [Task 3]\n5363:- Direct browser-global assignment/restoration caused 105 Bun failures -> save/restore descriptors with `Object.defineProperty`. Before push run `bun run lint`, `bun run fmt.check`, Convex typecheck, and the full suite; final validation was `1605 pass`, `40 skip`, `0 fail`, GitHub run `36508550529` success, and Railway deployment `2261ee43-1626-496b-8388-5e0c2d749989` successful. `bun add` can need `BUN_TMPDIR=/tmp BUN_INSTALL_CACHE_DIR=/tmp/twyne-bun-cache`. [Task 3]\n"},"started_at_ms":1791218340112,"completed_at_ms":1791218340113}}
