{"timestamp":"2026-10-05T16:44:24.363Z","ordinal":42730,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a10537-909f-77a3-96d8-dd07161f91ae","turn_id":"01a10cf3-25ca-7a90-895c-0aef2c6d86fb","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-5347d4ea-e3aa-417d-b878-2f55baa4986b","process_id":"85636","command":["/bin/bash","-lc","rtk proxy sed -n '70,80p' /home/diogenes/.codex/memories/MEMORY.md"],"cwd":"file:///home/diogenes/Projects/twyne","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"rtk proxy sed -n '70,80p' /home/diogenes/.codex/memories/MEMORY.md"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"- Not Organic is the control plane: portal sessions and upstream credentials stay server-owned; public clients validate HTTPS origins, same-origin callbacks, PKCE S256, narrow allowlisted scopes, and DPoP-bound tokens; gateway checks capabilities immediately before dispatch. [Task 1]\n- Google Drive remains unimplemented. The narrow researched direction is Google Picker with `drive.file`, and product UI must label it “Coming soon,” never as an available connector. [Task 1][Task 2]\n- Keating selects account sources, browses/reads resources, separately opts into tools, and reviews exact arguments; cancellation, account change, revocation, tool-definition change, and failed/lost-network calls fail closed. [Task 2]\n- Twyne trusted Convex actions bind verified DID/sessionVersion to fresh DPoP tokens. Research requires enabling research, choosing a source search tool, and selecting “Your MCP servers”; sign-out, revocation, and schema changes clear/fail closed. [Task 3]\n\n## Failures and how to do differently\n\n- GitNexus `ENOENT: .../.gitnexus/registry-lock` -> run `node .gitnexus/run.cjs analyze --index-only`, but treat absent/truncated graph edges as unknown and confirm with `rg`/source. Preserve unrelated dirty provider work; aggregate impact reports are not feature-local evidence. [Task 1]\n- Focused Keating validation does not prove web production readiness: pre-existing assistant-ui/PDF/router incompatibilities blocked the full web build, and neither deployment nor live-account flow was tested. [Task 2]\n- `ERR_CONNECTION_REFUSED` after an owned Twyne preview stopped is an environment/process condition, while localhost-to-deployed Convex CORS preflight must be verified separately; neither establishes deployed feature behavior. [Task 3]\n\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"- Not Organic is the control plane: portal sessions and upstream credentials stay server-owned; public clients validate HTTPS origins, same-origin callbacks, PKCE S256, narrow allowlisted scopes, and DPoP-bound tokens; gateway checks capabilities immediately before dispatch. [Task 1]\n- Google Drive remains unimplemented. The narrow researched direction is Google Picker with `drive.file`, and product UI must label it “Coming soon,” never as an available connector. [Task 1][Task 2]\n- Keating selects account sources, browses/reads resources, separately opts into tools, and reviews exact arguments; cancellation, account change, revocation, tool-definition change, and failed/lost-network calls fail closed. [Task 2]\n- Twyne trusted Convex actions bind verified DID/sessionVersion to fresh DPoP tokens. Research requires enabling research, choosing a source search tool, and selecting “Your MCP servers”; sign-out, revocation, and schema changes clear/fail closed. [Task 3]\n\n## Failures and how to do differently\n\n- GitNexus `ENOENT: .../.gitnexus/registry-lock` -> run `node .gitnexus/run.cjs analyze --index-only`, but treat absent/truncated graph edges as unknown and confirm with `rg`/source. Preserve unrelated dirty provider work; aggregate impact reports are not feature-local evidence. [Task 1]\n- Focused Keating validation does not prove web production readiness: pre-existing assistant-ui/PDF/router incompatibilities blocked the full web build, and neither deployment nor live-account flow was tested. [Task 2]\n- `ERR_CONNECTION_REFUSED` after an owned Twyne preview stopped is an environment/process condition, while localhost-to-deployed Convex CORS preflight must be verified separately; neither establishes deployed feature behavior. [Task 3]\n\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":30763},"formatted_output":"- Not Organic is the control plane: portal sessions and upstream credentials stay server-owned; public clients validate HTTPS origins, same-origin callbacks, PKCE S256, narrow allowlisted scopes, and DPoP-bound tokens; gateway checks capabilities immediately before dispatch. [Task 1]\n- Google Drive remains unimplemented. The narrow researched direction is Google Picker with `drive.file`, and product UI must label it “Coming soon,” never as an available connector. [Task 1][Task 2]\n- Keating selects account sources, browses/reads resources, separately opts into tools, and reviews exact arguments; cancellation, account change, revocation, tool-definition change, and failed/lost-network calls fail closed. [Task 2]\n- Twyne trusted Convex actions bind verified DID/sessionVersion to fresh DPoP tokens. Research requires enabling research, choosing a source search tool, and selecting “Your MCP servers”; sign-out, revocation, and schema changes clear/fail closed. [Task 3]\n\n## Failures and how to do differently\n\n- GitNexus `ENOENT: .../.gitnexus/registry-lock` -> run `node .gitnexus/run.cjs analyze --index-only`, but treat absent/truncated graph edges as unknown and confirm with `rg`/source. Preserve unrelated dirty provider work; aggregate impact reports are not feature-local evidence. [Task 1]\n- Focused Keating validation does not prove web production readiness: pre-existing assistant-ui/PDF/router incompatibilities blocked the full web build, and neither deployment nor live-account flow was tested. [Task 2]\n- `ERR_CONNECTION_REFUSED` after an owned Twyne preview stopped is an environment/process condition, while localhost-to-deployed Convex CORS preflight must be verified separately; neither establishes deployed feature behavior. [Task 3]\n\n"},"started_at_ms":1791218664363,"completed_at_ms":1791218664363}}
