changing files. Root reviews\ndesktop/gpui/fixtures/connected-work/execution.md:39:`target/verification/sakana-genui-inputs`. Root owns manifests, barrels,\ndesktop/gpui/fixtures/connected-work/execution.md:44:Root works on V while they run. Integration follows review and Source checks;\ndesktop/gpui/fixtures/connected-work/execution.md:46:that AI, account sync, knowledge sources or generated UI are complete.\ndesktop/gpui/fixtures/connected-work/execution.md:48:P/T/E now have integrated native/Source contract comparisons. V has compiled\ndesktop/gpui/fixtures/connected-work/execution.md:50:Source/native geometry and interaction gates remain open. I/C/K remain\ndesktop/gpui/fixtures/account-sync/README.md:3:Frozen scoped files: `src/native_accounts/**` and this fixture directory. This is an offline protocol/state/persistence foundation, not connected sign-in or a connected library. `auth::CONNECTED_AUTH_AVAILABLE` is deliberately false. Root owns all runtime exports, manifests, app/Store/UI/transport integration; `integration.patch` is **unapplied**.\ndesktop/gpui/fixtures/account-sync/README.md:5:Read [contracts.md](contracts.md) before integration. Its separate source policies, identities, callback approvals, capacity constraints, sharing/publishing boundaries, and native gaps are authoritative for this slice.\ndesktop/gpui/fixtures/account-sync/README.md:9:| Interface | Purpose / required Root boundary |\ndesktop/gpui/fixtures/account-sync/README.md:12:| `auth::SignInAttempt::prepare(registration, verifier_entropy:[u8;32], state_entropy:[u8;32], now_ms, return_to)` | Same Source PKCE S256 request. Root supplies fresh OS CSPRNG entropy; this does not open a browser or listener. |\ndesktop/gpui/fixtures/account-sync/README.md:13:| `SignInAttempt::{authorization_url,consume_callback}` | Parsed components preserve duplicate query values; consumption is once even on failure. A returned request is only data for the unimplemented trusted redemption transport. Debug output redacts code/verifier/state. |\ndesktop/gpui/fixtures/account-sync/README.md:14:| `auth::SignInReceipt::consistent_account(trusted_issuer)` | Issued/refreshed/session user consistency only. A constructed or parsed receipt is **not** authenticated identity/JWT/session proof. |\ndesktop/gpui/fixtures/account-sync/README.md:15:| `AccountIdentity`, `SessionLease` | Exact issuer/subject/token-identifier consistency and unique operation-lifetime guard. Root creates a lease only after real accepted Convex auth; invalidate it at sign-out/account change. |\ndesktop/gpui/fixtures/account-sync/README.md:16:| `protocol::{SyncPayload,PullSnapshot,ContentSnapshot}` | Original section names, canonical source, HTML, nullable-persona distinction and pull metadata; retain unknown fields. No caller owner is added to requests. |\ndesktop/gpui/fixtures/account-sync/README.md:17:| `SyncPayload::{normalized,push_arguments}` | Source-compatible row/whole-section diff, omitted/empty semantics, removals, expected head. Known pull timestamps are omitted without rewriting source. Conservative changed-content JSON budget 950,000 bytes; Source UTF-16 bound 5,000,000. Server encoding/whole-account capacity remains independently enforced. |\ndesktop/gpui/fixtures/account-sync/README.md:18:| `AccountJournal::enqueue(payload)` | Explicitly associate a candidate with **this** account. Durable latest-unsent intent coalesces; an in-flight desired snapshot remains immutable. Run only at an explicit save/flush boundary, never a whole-doc per-key path. |\ndesktop/gpui/fixtures/account-sync/README.md:21:| `AccountJournal::{stage_pull,commit_pull}` | Retain remote snapshot and base/local/remote conflicts. Root must perform actual guarded local application/persistence, then give exact stage/payload/edit-generation and unchanged pending-Source-set receipt. These consistency fields alone are not local I/O proof. |\ndesktop/gpui/fixtures/account-sync/README.md:22:| `AccountJournal::resolve_conflicts(lease,active,expected_conflicts,expected_edit_generation,candidate)` | Explicit resolution after actual guarded Root local persistence. Rejects an old account/lease/dialogue generation. Native three-way preservation is deliberately **not** the Source timestamp merge or a Lix CRDT. |\ndesktop/gpui/fixtures/account-sync/README.md:24:| `AccountSyncStore::{open,load,save_request,expected_value,acknowledge_expected}` | `open(app_root)` uses only `app_root/account-sync`. Per-account SHA-256 names, OS lock across handles/processes, exact primary+backup byte/value CAS, fsynced atomic save/previous backup, warnings on recovery, untouched future/invalid versions. Exact expected-save acknowledgement re-syncs primary/dir under lock. 64 MiB journal cap; Unix modes 0700/0600. No credentials stored. |\ndesktop/gpui/fixtures/account-sync/README.md:26:Pull receipts and queue records preserve the original canonical source; they do not compile it, regenerate HTML, establish a verified projection, change Source selection/history, or write the current native manuscript. Root must preserve its Source pending/conflict/revision guards and use a staged/recoverable two-store application protocol. Do not emit 'saved' from a journal-only receipt.\ndesktop/gpui/fixtures/account-sync/README.md:30:No new dependencies: existing `anyhow`, `serde`, `serde_json`, `fs2`, `tempfile`, `uuid`, plus desktop-enabled `base64` and `sha2`. The proposed export is `#[cfg(feature=\"desktop\")] pub mod native_accounts;`, so no-default core keeps optional auth dependencies unreferenced. No app, manifest, credential vault, auth transport, browser storage, or existing Store was edited.\ndesktop/gpui/fixtures/account-sync/README.md:37:rtk proxy bun desktop/gpui/fixtures/account-sync/capture-contracts.ts\ndesktop/gpui/fixtures/account-sync/README.md:38:rtk proxy bun desktop/gpui/fixtures/account-sync/capture-contracts.ts --check\ndesktop/gpui/fixtures/account-sync/README.md:39:rtk proxy rustfmt --edition 2024 --check desktop/