ruggle detection, classification and shared budget semantics have\nexecuted Source oracles. ProseMirror StepMap primitives match 9,476 executed\nresults across 112 forward/inverse cases, including floating-point recovery.\nOrdered native transaction mapping, mirror pipelines, automatic classification\nand live model transport remain unfinished. These checks do not prove account\nsync, AI/knowledge integration, Electrobun-host equivalence or full-app parity.\n\nRetained receipts for this checked state:\n\n- `target/verification/genui-ui-65f5c0d33c83/receipt.json`\n- `target/verification/genui-lint-1ec48e587e24/receipt.json`\n- `target/verification/genui-build-ffad677d6c9d/build.json`\n- `target/verification/genui-source-cards-20261005-e/receipt.json`\n- `target/verification/genui-native-cards-f0c3870058b1/comparison.json`\n\nThe running user preview remains open on its immutable earlier build. Its\nlibrary and writing were preserved while verification used isolated displays\nand temporary libraries. The full port goal remains active.\n"},"started_at_ms":1791219936856,"completed_at_ms":1791219936856}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-05T17:05:37.000Z","ordinal":43017,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a10d07-2ee8-7f02-8fe1-6af0595df613","call_id":"call_rRAan7aehH89zADC0Xh1YYlX","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.3 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"i\":0,\"result\":{\"status\":\"fulfilled\",\"value\":{\"chunk_id\":\"937af8\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000028925,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":16,\"output\":\"    Finished `dev` profile [unoptimized] target(s) in 11.27s\\n\"}}}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"i\":1,\"result\":{\"status\":\"fulfilled\",\"value\":{\"chunk_id\":\"953a92\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000020003,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":27,\"output\":\"{\\\"output\\\":\\\"desktop/gpui/target/verification/account-source-20261005-c\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"passed\\\",\\\"pageErrors\\\":0}\\n\"}}}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"i\":2,\"result\":{\"status\":\"fulfilled\",\"value\":{\"chunk_id\":\"bfdfe2\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000032564,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":799,\"output\":\"# Connected and generated UI work\\n\\nThe full hosted desktop remains the reference. The running preview is the\\nimmutable offline build; this wave must preserve its library and leave its\\nwindow open. Existing web, Convex and configuration edits are protected.\\n\\n```mermaid\\nflowchart TD\\n  S[Current Source contracts] --> P[Four component prop schemas]\\n  S --> T[Append-only tool streams]\\n  S --> A[Native auth and sync transport contract]\\n  S --> E[Deterministic writer seeding and offline fill]\\n  P --> T\\n  P --> V[GPUI tool bodies and retained controls]\\n  T --> I[Editor and provider integration]\\n  V --> I\\n  E --> I\\n  A --> C[Trusted sign-in and connected library adapter]\\n  C --> K[Account knowledge transport and controls]\\n  I --> Q[Source comparisons and actual native interaction]\\n  K --> Q\\n  Q --> F[Full port audit]\\n```\\n\\n| Node | Ownership | Deliverable and gate |\\n| --- | --- | --- |\\n| P | Sakana fugu-max; proposed `src/gen_ui/props.rs` only | Source Zod-compatible validation, Unicode and numeric edge cases; Root compares with the unchanged Source oracle |\\n| T | Sakana fugu-max; proposed `src/gen_ui/stream.rs` only | Original cumulative JSONL append contract; uses the fixed P API; no writer-field rewrites or invented recovery behavior |\\n| A | Sakana fugu-max; bounded contract JSON only | Actual auth/sync names, wire fields, missing trust and concrete adapter boundary; no account or registration action |\\n| V | Root; new native tool view | Original four components, labels, local working state and Source-derived styling |\\n| E | Sakana fugu-max proposal; Root adoption | Original sentence spans, seeds and no-provider branches compared with the unchanged Source oracle |\\n| I | Root; shared exports, editor and provider coordinators | Actual accepted requests and retained UI; stale folio/range/revision checks; meaningful undo and failure behavior |\\n| C/K | Root, after A | Trusted native sign-in, account-scoped sync/conflicts and knowledge sources/tool review; foundations alone do not enable capability |\\n| Q | Root; Cargo and runtime ownership | Focused checks, Source/native interaction and render comparisons; real providers/account proof remain separate |\\n\\nWorkers return proposals without executing tools or changing files. Root reviews\\nand adopts each proposal in a separate directory before production edits.\\nDisjoint input bundles and their SHA256 pins are retained under\\n`target/verification/sakana-genui-inputs`. Root owns manifests, barrels,\\n`app.rs`, `main.rs`, every runtime and the user preview. No worker may revert\\nor overwrite another participant's work.\\n\\nWave one runs P/T/A in parallel after the P function signature is fixed.\\nRoot works on V while they run. Integration follows review and Source checks;\\nrendered/runtime checks follow a successful build. This graph does not claim\\nthat AI, account sync, knowledge sources or generated UI are complete.\\n\\nP/T/E now have integrated native/Source contract comparisons. V has compiled\\ntool bodies, retained controls and typed requests; its actual editor mounting,\\nSource/native geometry and interaction gates remain open. I/C/K remain\\nimplementation work. The user's preview uses its existing immutable binary.\\n\"}}}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"i\":3,\"result\":{\"status\":\"fulfilled\",\"value\":{\"chunk_id\":\"d6c6e5\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000024587,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":1956,\"output\":\"# Account/sync foundation — HANDOFF\\n\\nFrozen scoped files: `src/native_accounts/**` and this fixture directory. This is an offline protocol/state/persistence foundation, not connected sign-in or a connected library. `auth::CONNECTED_AUTH_AVAILABLE` is deliberately false. Root owns all runtime exports, manifests, app/Store/UI/transport integration; `integration.patch` is **unapplied**.\\n\\nRead [contracts.md](contracts.md) before integration. Its separate source policies, identities, callback approvals, capacity constraints, sharing/publishing boundaries, and native gaps are authoritative for this slice.\\n\\n## Exact interfaces\\n\\n| Interface | Purpose / required Root boundary |\\n| --- | --- |\\n| `auth::CallbackRegistration::require_supported()` | Syntax + explicit exact-origin Twyne trust and Not Organic Twyne-product registration. Operator configuration is required; URL syntax or `product=twyne` is not approval. |\\n| `auth::SignInAttempt::prepare(registration, verifier_entropy:[u8;32], state_entropy:[u8;32], now_ms, return_to)` | Same Source PKCE S256 request. Root supplies fresh OS CSPRNG entropy; this does not open a browser or listener. |\\n| `SignInAttempt::{authorization_url,consume_callback}` | Parsed components preserve duplicate query values; consumption is once even on failure. A returned request is only data for the unimplemented trusted redemption transport. Debug output redacts code/verifier/state. |\\n| `auth::SignInReceipt::consistent_account(trusted_issuer)` | Issued/refreshed/session user consistency only. A constructed or parsed receipt is **not** authenticated identity/JWT/session proof. |\\n| `AccountIdentity`, `SessionLease` | Exact issuer/subject/token-identifier consistency and unique operation-lifetime guard. Root creates a lease only after real accepted Convex auth; invalidate it at sign-out/account change. |\\n| `protocol::{SyncPayload,PullSnapshot,ContentSnapshot}` | Original section names, canonical source, HTML, nullable-persona distinction and pull metadata; retain unknown fields. No caller owner is added to requests. |\\n| `SyncPayload::{normalized,push_arguments}` | Source-compatible row/whole-section diff, omitted/empty semantics, removals, expected head. Known pull timestamps are omitted without rewriting source. Conservative changed-content JSON budget 950,000 bytes; Source UTF-16 bound 5,000,000. Server encoding/whole-account capacity remains independently enforced. |\\n| `AccountJournal::enqueue(payload)` | Explicitly associate a candidate with **this** account. Durable latest-unsent intent coalesces; an in-flight desired snapshot remains immutable. Run only at an explicit save/flush boundary, never a whole-doc per-key path. |\\n| `AccountJournal::prepare_dispatch(lease,active)` | Requires observed baseline/head and no pending pull/stage/conflict. Persist candidate journal before transport submission. Request data does not prove transport/auth availability. |\\n| `AccountJournal::{acknowledge_push,mark_rejected,mark_outcome_unknown}` | Exact dispatch/current-lease guards. ACK advances only sent baseline; newer intent survives. Only proven noncommit can use `mark_rejected`; timeout/socket-loss/ambiguous result requires pull. No server idempotency key exists. |\\n| `AccountJournal::{stage_pull,commit_pull}` | Retain remote snapshot and base/local/remote conflicts. Root must perform actual guarded local application/persistence, then give exact stage/payload/edit-generation and unchanged pending-Source-set receipt. These consistency fields alone are not local I/O proof. |\\n| `AccountJournal::resolve_conflicts(lease,active,expected_conflicts,expected_edit_generation,candidate)` | Explicit resolution after actual guarded Root local persistence. Rejects an old account/lease/dialogue generation. Native three-way preservation is deliberately **not** the Source timestamp merge or a Lix CRDT. |\\n| `AccountJournal::{suspend_session,native_id_for}` | Startup/sign-out leaves uncertain in-flight data and requires a pull; remote string ID ↔ local UUID mapping must be persisted before hydrate. |\\n| `AccountSyncStore::{open,load,save_request,expected_value,acknowledge_expected}` | `open(app_root)` uses only `app_root/account-sync`. Per-account SHA-256 names, OS lock across handles/processes, exact primary+backup byte/value CAS, fsynced atomic save/previous backup, warnings on recovery, untouched future/invalid versions. Exact expected-save acknowledgement re-syncs primary/dir under lock. 64 MiB journal cap; Unix modes 0700/0600. No credentials stored. |\\n\\nPull receipts and queue records preserve the original canonical source; they do not compile it, regenerate HTML, establish a verified projection, change Source selection/history, or write the current native manuscript. Root must preserve its Source pending/conflict/revision guards and use a staged/recoverable two-store application protocol. Do not emit 'saved' from a journal-only receipt.\\n\\n## Dependencies/export\\n\\nNo new dependencies: existing `anyhow`, `serde`, `serde_json`, `fs2`, `tempfile`, `uuid`, plus desktop-enabled `base64` and `sha2`. The proposed export is `#[cfg(feature=\\\"desktop\\\")] pub mod native_accounts;`, so no-default core keeps optional auth dependencies unreferenced. No app, manifest, credential vault, auth transport, browser storage, or existing Store was edited.\\n\\n## Reproduction and evidence\\n\\nExecuted here:\\n\\n```sh\\nrtk proxy bun desktop/gpui/fixtures/account-sync/capture-contracts.ts\\nrtk proxy bun desktop/gpui/fixtures/account-sync/capture-contracts.ts --check\\nrtk proxy rustfmt --edition 2024 --check desktop/gpui/src/native_accounts/mod.rs desktop/gpui/src/native_accounts/auth.rs desktop/gpui/src/native_accounts/protocol.rs desktop/gpui/src/native_accounts/journal.rs desktop/gpui/src/native_accounts/store.rs desktop/gpui/src/native_accounts/tests.rs\\n```\\n\\nThe generator AST-selects four original sync helpers and four auth helpers plus the callback constant, with drift guards and a forbidden-network/global-context guard. It records exact source SHA-256. Only selected pure bodies execute; no app module is imported. Eight original wire diff cases, nine callback cases, six return paths and a deterministic PKCE request are captured. Fixture entropy/codes/session IDs are synthetic and confer no access.\\n\\nPrepared, **not run here**, because Root owns Cargo scheduling:\\n\\n```sh\\n# After Root reviews and applies integration.patch:\\nrtk proxy devenv shell -- rtk proxy cargo test --manifest-path desktop/gpui/Cargo.toml --locked --offline --features ui-tests --lib native_accounts::tests\\nrtk proxy devenv shell -- rtk proxy cargo check --manifest-path desktop/gpui/Cargo.toml --locked --offline --no-default-features --lib\\n```\\n\\nThe 26 prepared tests include real temporary-filesystem restart/backup/corruption/blocked-path retry and simultaneous separate-handle CAS tests, alongside synthetic protocol/lease/conflict tests. They have not established passing Rust type-checks, filesystem behavior, native account UI, OS secure storage, registered callbacks, live identity, live sync, multi-device convergence, service limits, or platform portability. Root must run/review these gates before runtime use.\\n\\n## First connected slice remains separate\\n\\nBoth native callback origin approvals must exist before auth transport. Implement external-browser/listener routing, protected Better Auth cookie jar, refreshed-session authenticity, Convex JWT acquisition/accepted-auth state and current-lease cancellation. Then use **read-only staged pull into a separate account partition**, with explicit device-library association before any upload. Do not silently carry the browser's unpartitioned automatic seeding into native. Sharing/Lix, roles/presence, invitations, publication, global provider sessions and deletion are outside this foundation and owned by other lanes.\\n\"}}}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"i\":4,\"result\":{\"status\":\"fulfilled\",\"value\":{\"chunk_id\":\"71ac3f\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000033812,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":1674,\"output\":\"  collected endnotes and footnotes, and guarded navigation back to the actual\\n  manuscript atom. Save, route changes and citation preparation flush unblurred\\n  input. Nine note checks, three mounted citation checks and four mounted host\\n  save/navigation checks pass after the bounded paint/field corrections. A\\n  reproduced queued-event regression now keeps an accepted note revision clean\\n  while later edits still become dirty. Actual X11 verifies the focused note\\n  Save state separately. Original parser whitespace and\\n  research-text projections have separate source-backed corpora. Insertion and\\n  hover animation, vertical textarea resizing, original/native popup raster\\n  comparison and screen-reader announcement remain separate gaps.\\n- Source uses GPUI Kit's native code editor with the original Typst syntax\\n  rules and snippets. Ordinary syntax edits reparse only the affected line\\n  unless a block comment changes later lexical state. Unicode snippet,\\n  undo/redo, search, navigation and separate recovery checks pass; final\\n  Source screenshots and all-current integration gates remain in progress.\\n  Source comment/snippet undo and redo restore the actual native caret and\\n  selected Unicode text, including mixed-indent comments and CRLF mapping.\\n  The original Noto Sans Mono regular and semibold faces, with Chromium's\\n  synthetic comment oblique, are embedded for Source alone. Mounted checks\\n  select the actual faces and retain source bytes, read-only selection, and\\n  measured caret positions in the CJK/heading/comment fixtures. This does not\\n  establish matching antialiasing or platform emoji/Hangul fallback.\\n  Four actual resize widths (1280/640/320/160) preserve real marker ranges,\\n  helper rows, caret/IME bounds, read-only unfolding and source history. The\\n  exact generated marker receives its verified hyphen break; ordinary and\\n  unfolded printable-ASCII rows now use an optional cached actual-font CSS\\n  wrapping policy. All126 executed browser rows match across six widths;\\n  16 scoped native/GPU gates preserve bytes, selection, IME, history and\\n  resize behavior. None/Unicode/tab/control/inline-metric fallback stays\\n  upstream. The21 remaining unsupported-row differences and raster limits\\n  remain explicit. Linux Source also\\n  retains the original Ctrl+Shift+Z alias alongside Ctrl+Y.\\n- Source opening and edits schedule the actual Typst compiler after the\\n  original 450 ms pause. A real mounted compiler check proves that leaving\\n  Source cancels the scheduled work, invalid drafts retain the last valid\\n  proof, corrected proof text remains a draft until Apply, and Discard restores\\n  a proof of canonical source. Generated helpers fold the closing body marker;\\n  native line navigation reveals it without changing source or undo history.\\n  These scoped checks do not establish full UI, operating-system or connected-flow\\n  parity, or a current aggregate suite.\\n\\nBuild and runtime receipts apply to their recorded local inputs. Cross-platform\\nworkflow configuration and metadata scaffolds do not prove CI, a runnable macOS\\nbundle, Windows runtime, clean installation, signing, audio devices, providers or\\nauthenticated connected workflows. Dossier lifecycle/filing, real math NodeViews,\\nfull visual parity and mounted account/AI/audio/collaboration remain unfinished.\\n\\n## Reviewed equation host, inline child and Dossier stamp checkpoint\\n\\nThe actual writing room now installs a folio/visit-qualified equation source form for inline and block atoms. Submit runs the existing canonical converter against a copied current manuscript; accepted commands use the real editor history and Save pipeline. The measured inline child reserves one source scalar in its paragraph, sharing caret, selection/IME and neighboring baseline geometry. Route changes retire the current form. The original Special Elite reviewed-count stamp now uses prepared original outlines, rotation and Source box dimensions.\\n\\nRoot's current local checkpoint passes 678 checks (563 library, 97 application, 18 audio contracts), with eight hardware checks ignored. All-target Clippy denies warnings and passes. See `fixtures/math-write/parent-inline-stamp-gates.json` for the exact tested inputs/logs. Broader gates caught and repaired unsupported equation hit-target interception and block-drag propagation; the old draft-switch fixture now follows the real Dossier Cancel route.\\n\\nNative X11 equation input/save/history and refreshed Dossier interactions are separate active gates. Browser inline first-baseline/intrinsic sizing, current KaTeX geometry/preview, vertical textarea resizing, paper descendant multiply, renderer epoch retirement and full visual parity remain unfinished. Unmounted connected foundations and release/platform proof also remain open.\\n\\n\\n## Writing-tool integration evidence (2026-10-05)\\n\\nThe four original writing tools are now mounted in the native editor. The\\n[writing-tool notes](fixtures/gen-ui/README.md) record retained inputs, editor\\nreplacement/Undo, durable Keep/Jot acknowledgments, stale scope guards and the\\nremaining provider and notebook-surface work.\\n\\nThe current focused check passes 63 contracts and six mounted editor tests;\\nstrict all-target lint passes. Seven number-field interactions were executed in\\nthe original browser and replayed in the native editor. Four default cards were\\ncaptured from both real renderers at 1280 x 860, scale 1. The final native capture\\nverifies the outer three-pixel accent and visible minimum/maximum inputs. Two\\ncards still have approximately 2–3 pixels of height difference, and other\\nfractional/raster, focus, tooltip and responsive states remain unverified.\\n\\nPure struggle detection, classification and shared budget semantics have\\nexecuted Source oracles. ProseMirror StepMap primitives match 9,476 executed\\nresults across 112 forward/inverse cases, including floating-point recovery.\\nOrdered native transaction mapping, mirror pipelines, automatic classification\\nand live model transport remain unfinished. These checks do not prove account\\nsync, AI/knowledge integration, Electrobun-host equivalence or full-app parity.\\n\\nRetained receipts for this checked state:\\n\\n- `target/verification/genui-ui-65f5c0d33c83/receipt.json`\\n- `target/verification/genui-lint-1ec48e587e24/receipt.json`\\n- `target/verification/genui-build-ffad677d6c9d/build.json`\\n- `target/verification/genui-source-cards-20261005-e/receipt.json`\\n- `target/verification/genui-native-cards-f0c3870058b1/comparison.json`\\n\\nThe running user preview remains open on its immutable earlier build. Its\\nlibrary and writing were preserved while verification used isolated displays\\nand temporary libraries. The full port goal remains active.\\n\"}}}"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a10cf3-25ca-7a90-895c-0aef2c6d86fb","create_time":1791219937.000065}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
