"user_input_order":2270},{"client_authored":false,"mcp_attribution":{"sources":[{"first_turn_id":"01a10555-dfb0-7570-9355-0ebfebd2abb9","plugin_id":"unified-computer-use@openai-bundled","server_name":"cua_repl","tool_name":"js"}],"status":"complete"},"retained_source":{"complete":true,"id":{"message_id":"msg_01a10b54-68e0-7e10-a51e-719395495580","role":"user","turn_id":"01a10a1b-b650-7660-b5ef-56e1a3784ac1"},"revision":"retained_01a10b54-68e0-7e10-a51e-71be7882db09"},"user_input_order":2271},{"client_authored":false,"mcp_attribution":{"sources":[{"first_turn_id":"01a10555-dfb0-7570-9355-0ebfebd2abb9","plugin_id":"unified-computer-use@openai-bundled","server_name":"cua_repl","tool_name":"js"}],"status":"complete"},"retained_source":{"complete":true,"id":{"message_id":"msg_01a10b57-fa01-7481-83c6-cd438ad53be0","role":"user","turn_id":"01a10a1b-b650-7660-b5ef-56e1a3784ac1"},"revision":"retained_01a10b57-fa01-7481-83c6-cd6d219dd390"},"user_input_order":2274},{"client_authored":false},{"client_authored":false},{"client_authored":false},{"client_authored":false},{"client_authored":false,"mcp_attribution":{"sources":[{"first_turn_id":"01a10555-dfb0-7570-9355-0ebfebd2abb9","plugin_id":"unified-computer-use@openai-bundled","server_name":"cua_repl","tool_name":"js"}],"status":"complete"},"retained_source":{"complete":true,"id":{"message_id":"msg_01a10d17-d63e-7422-b308-733ebf06665a","role":"user","turn_id":"01a10d17-989f-7150-9fa5-0c502f3fed47"},"revision":"retained_01a10d17-d63e-7422-b308-735bca3ecf6f"},"user_input_order":2365},{"client_authored":false,"compaction_model_hash":"3000","mcp_attribution":{"sources":[{"first_turn_id":"01a10555-dfb0-7570-9355-0ebfebd2abb9","plugin_id":"unified-computer-use@openai-bundled","server_name":"cua_repl","tool_name":"js"}],"status":"complete"}}],"resume_metadata":{"last_started_turn_id":"01a10d17-989f-7150-9fa5-0c502f3fed47","multi_agent_version":"v2","previous_turn_settings":{"comp_hash":"3000","model":"gpt-6.1-sol","realtime_active":false}},"retained_context":{"assistant_messages":[{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_0acb6e766bb0227d016ac3d3c1cda487d1bb6525468cca3d74","order":2357,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a10cf3-3222-7761-be96-cd66c198167c","text":"The preview is running. I’m continuing the account and sync work in separate fixtures so you can keep trying the writing app uninterrupted.","turn_id":"01a10cf3-25ca-7a90-895c-0aef2c6d86fb"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_0acb6e766bb0227d016ac3d47f946887d1b0168d81b62a226d","order":2358,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a10cf6-1bdd-7e63-8053-8a911aee005b","text":"The session checks now keep remembered credentials during temporary outages and clear them after an explicit revocation. All 18 SDK tests pass. Next I’m testing the browser callback through the native process and bringing the Editor’s Office menu into the GPUI interface.","turn_id":"01a10cf3-25ca-7a90-895c-0aef2c6d86fb"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_0acb6e766bb0227d016ac3d494616887d1848dd1d18fd4af7f","order":2359,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a10cf6-6bb8-78e0-99e3-782834bb9ffc","text":"I’m using the Impeccable skill to preserve Twyne’s existing visual system. I’m also giving Sakana two small, isolated tasks: check the account menu’s Source behavior and extract the knowledge catalog rules for review.","turn_id":"01a10cf3-25ca-7a90-895c-0aef2c6d86fb"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_0acb6e766bb0227d016ac3d5b5a09c87d1afe0739cc6dc03e3","order":2360,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a10cfa-d75d-7c60-8af5-c18553119e66","text":"The browser callback test passed: Chrome reached the native listener, the callback code was removed from browser history, and the Rust bridge retrieved a snapshot through the SDK helper. The fixture also confirmed sync-conflict handling and cancellation on sign-out. Live account registration and sync remain unverified.","turn_id":"01a10cf3-25ca-7a90-895c-0aef2c6d86fb"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_0acb6e766bb0227d016ac3d79ad27887d19c006a36cfa7f8b6","order":2361,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a10d02-3990-7a01-88e6-40fb93f646d3","text":"The account menu now uses Source’s labels, icons, typography and spacing, with native Preferences and My Desk navigation. Sign-in still reports that this build cannot connect yet. Sakana’s catalog extraction is ready for comparison against the actual Source functions; its menu response was malformed, so I used the Source components directly.","turn_id":"01a10cf3-25ca-7a90-895c-0aef2c6d86fb"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_0acb6e766bb0227d016ac3d9e2db7087d19f2fa039e296fb97","order":2362,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a10d0b-23e5-7f62-ab95-d6c520cd8e6c","text":"The render comparison caught a difference the interaction tests missed: Source wraps “Continue with Not Organic” onto two centered lines, while the native button kept one line. I’m fixing the wrapping. The native Escape, outside-click and Preferences navigation checks already pass.","turn_id":"01a10cf3-25ca-7a90-895c-0aef2c6d86fb"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_0acb6e766bb0227d016ac3dc756a3087d18129dafea45bea6a","order":2363,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a10d15-3040-7050-8aae-a594366e1ac5","text":"The catalog comparisons pass, including JavaScript length limits and tool-definition ordering. I also corrected public account labels to follow Source’s email/DID filtering, and widened the native tool metadata reader so it accepts the values Source admits. The final native render and transport checks are next.","turn_id":"01a10cf3-25ca-7a90-895c-0aef2c6d86fb"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_0acb6e766bb0227d016ac3dd287b9087d1a7fecc15c4166929","order":2366,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a10d17-ebf5-7522-bd05-ab7ec5b265b9","text":"I’ll check the title’s clipping and focus behavior, then adjust it to feel like part of the manuscript. I’ll preserve your current writing while testing the fix separately.","turn_id":"01a10d17-989f-7150-9fa5-0c502f3fed47"}],"assistant_messages_incomplete":true,"incomplete":false,"next_order":2367,"user_messages":[{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_01a10931-8cb5-7ee3-8b64-1eee53ca7038","order":1753,"revision":"retained_01a10931-8cb6-7f33-aabe-bd041f1cbc4a","text":"sakana key in skate","turn_id":"01a10931-6b4d-7c72-953d-7b1209c0cbbd"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_01a1094e-fdd9-74b1-ba79-fdf8b8804d27","order":1755,"revision":"retained_01a1094e-fdd9-74b1-ba79-fe1d8d16d077","text":".","turn_id":"01a1094e-b771-7df1-ad6f-c626cab96d12"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_01a10a1c-0a9a-76d0-862e-5312c97a9f56","order":1992,"revision":"retained_01a10a1c-0a9a-76d0-862e-53338800e0ce","text":".","turn_id":"01a10a1b-b650-7660-b5ef-56e1a3784ac1"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_01a10b52-46ed-7f41-959e-f106ea1871fb","order":2268,"revision":"retained_01a10b52-46ed-7f41-959e-f12f4e3b1fa4","text":"status report","turn_id":"01a10a1b-b650-7660-b5ef-56e1a3784ac1"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_01a10b53-da43-7270-80cd-7083547d38fa","order":2270,"revision":"retained_01a10b53-da43-7270-80cd-70adcb767628","text":"okay and what about online writing and sync?","turn_id":"01a10a1b-b650-7660-b5ef-56e1a3784ac1"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_01a10b54-68e0-7e10-a51e-719395495580","order":2271,"revision":"retained_01a10b54-68e0-7e10-a51e-71be7882db09","text":"what about the ai integration? knowledge base integration, gen ui components?","turn_id":"01a10a1b-b650-7660-b5ef-56e1a3784ac1"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_01a10b57-fa01-7481-83c6-cd438ad53be0","order":2274,"revision":"retained_01a10b57-fa01-7481-83c6-cd6d219dd390","text":"start the application i want to see what its like","turn_id":"01a10a1b-b650-7660-b5ef-56e1a3784ac1"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_01a10d17-d63e-7422-b308-733ebf06665a","order":2365,"revision":"retained_01a10d17-d63e-7422-b308-735bca3ecf6f","text":"some interface bugs i noticed the title doesn't fully appear, getting cutoff on the bottom and top text, seems like some other field instead of just part of the same document.","turn_id":"01a10d17-989f-7150-9fa5-0c502f3fed47"}],"user_messages_incomplete":true,"verified_answers":[]},"window_id":"01a10d1c-0393-7eb0-8bf9-bbdb9927cb18","window_number":61}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-05T17:28:22.168Z","ordinal":43207,"type":"world_state","payload":{"full":true,"state":{"agents_md":{"directory":"/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne","text":"<!-- headroom:rtk-instructions -->\n# Shell commands\n\nPrefix shell commands with `rtk`, including each segment of a command chain.\nUse `rtk proxy <command>` for unfiltered output or when debugging filter behavior.\n<!-- /headroom:rtk-instructions -->\n\n--- project-doc ---\n\n<!-- convex-ai-start -->\n\nThis project uses [Convex](https://convex.dev) as its backend.\n\nWhen working on Convex code, **always read `convex/_generated/ai/guidelines.md` first** for important guidelines on how to correctly use Convex APIs and patterns. The file contains rules that override what you may have learned about Convex from training data.\n\nConvex agent skills for common tasks can be installed by running `npx convex ai-files install`.\n\n<!-- convex-ai-end -->\n"},"apps_instructions":false,"collaboration_mode":{"mode":"default","model":"gpt-6.1-sol","instructions":"0a11049b0421e1e86f1e129af8d547a89548a0c3"},"context_window_guidance":"","environments":{"environments":{"local":{"cwd":"/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne","status":"available","shell":"bash"}},"current_date":"2026-10-05","timezone":"America/Toronto","filesystem":"<filesystem><workspace_roots><root>/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne</root></workspace_roots><permission_profile type=\"disabled\"><file_system type=\"unrestricted\" /></permission_profile></filesystem>","subagents":"<agent name=\"/root/native_assets\" />\n<agent name=\"/root/rich_document\" />\n<agent name=\"/root/workspace_exchange\" />\n<agent name=\"/root/cli_repair\" />\n<agent name=\"/root/port_contract\" />"},"environments_instructions":false,"git_attribution":false,"host_skills":{"body":"\n## Skills\nA skill is a set of local instructions to follow that is stored in a `SKILL.md` file. Below is the list of skills that can be used. Each entry includes a name, description, and a short path that can be expanded into an absolute path using the skill roots table.\n### Skill roots\n- `r0` = `/home/diogenes/.codex/skills`\n- `r1` = `/home/diogenes/.agents/skills`\n- `r2` = `/home/diogenes/.codex/skills/.system`\n- `r3` = `/home/diogenes/.codex/plugins/cache/openai-bundled`\n- `r4` = `/home/diogenes/.codex/plugins/cache/openai-curated-remote/google-drive/0.1.16/skills`\n- `r5` = `/home/diogenes/.codex/plugins/cache/openai-curated-remote/pages/0.1.19/skills`\n- `r6` = `/home/diogenes/.codex/plugins/cache/openai-curated-remote`\n- `r7` = `/home/diogenes/.codex/plugins/cache/openai-curated-remote/work-pets/0.1.6/skills`\n- `r8` = `/home/diogenes/.codex/plugins/cache/openai-primary-runtime`\n- `r9` = `/home/diogenes/.codex/plugins/cache/openai-primary-runtime/spreadsheets/26.905.11957/skills`\n- `r10` = `/home/diogenes/.codex/plugins/cache/typesafe-ai`\n- `r11` = `/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne/.agents/skills`\n### Available skills\n- imagegen: Generate or edit raster images when the task benefits from AI-created bitmap visuals such as photos, illustrations, textures,  (file: r2/imagegen/SKILL.md)\n- openai-docs: Use for Codex models/pricing, scheduled tasks, skills, settings, setup, troubleshooting, customization, automations, and sel (file: r2/openai-docs/SKILL.md)\n- skill-creator: Create or update a Codex skill with appropriately scoped instructions and any needed supporting resources. (file: r2/skill-creator/SKILL.md)\n- skill-installer: Install Codex skills into $CODEX_HOME/skills from a curated list or a GitHub repo path. Use when a user asks to list install (file: r2/skill-installer/SKILL.md)\n- arize-admin: Manages Arize users, organizations, spaces, projects, roles, role bindings, resource restrictions, and API keys via the ax CLI. (file: r11/arize-admin/SKILL.md)\n- arize-ai-provider-integration: Creates, reads, updates, and deletes Arize AI integrations that store LLM provider credentials used by evaluators and other Ari (file: r11/arize-ai-provider-integration/SKILL.md)\n- arize-annotation: Creates and manages annotation configs (categorical, continuous, freeform label schemas) and annotation queues (human review  (file: r11/arize-annotation/SKILL.md)\n- arize-compliance-audit: INVOKE THIS SKILL when auditing an AI agent or LLM app for regulatory compliance. Covers EU AI Act, GPAI Code of Practice, GD (file: r11/arize-compliance-audit/SKILL.md)\n- arize-dataset: Creates, manages, and queries Arize datasets and examples. Covers dataset CRUD, appending examples, exporting data, and file-ba (file: r11/arize-dataset/SKILL.md)\n- arize-evaluator: Handles LLM-as-judge and code evaluator workflows on Arize including creating/updating evaluators, running evaluations on spans (file: r11/arize-evaluator/SKILL.md)\n- arize-experiment: Creates, runs, and analyzes Arize experiments for evaluating and comparing model performance. Covers experiment CRUD, exporti (file: r11/arize-experiment/SKILL.md)\n- arize-instrumentation: Adds Arize AX tracing to an LLM application for the first time. Follows a two-phase agent-assisted flow to analyze the codebase (file: r11/arize-instrumentation/SKILL.md)\n- arize-link: Generates deep links to the Arize UI for traces, spans, sessions, datasets, labeling queues, evaluators, and annotation confi (file: r11/arize-link/SKILL.md)\n- arize-prompt-optimization: Optimizes, improves, and debugs LLM prompts using production trace data, evaluations, and annotations. Extracts prompts from sp (file: r11/arize-prompt-optimization/SKILL.md)\n- arize-prompts: INVOKE THIS SKILL for Arize Prompt Hub and `ax prompts` workflows: author or import templates and save (Workflows A–B), label (file: r11/arize-prompts/SKILL.md)\n- arize-trace: Downloads, exports, and inspects existing Arize traces and spans to understand what an LLM app is doing or debug runtime issues (file: r11/arize-trace/SKILL.md)\n- convex: Convex is the backend agents get right on the first try: an all-TypeScript reactive platform where the 