{"timestamp":"2026-10-05T17:28:51.844Z","ordinal":43228,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a10537-909f-77a3-96d8-dd07161f91ae","turn_id":"01a10d17-989f-7150-9fa5-0c502f3fed47","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-3478fe92-f37b-4be4-b3c0-3b5b085aa8bf","process_id":"43353","command":["/bin/bash","-lc","rtk proxy rg -n 'all in flow|fluid manuscript|manuscript-panel|Twyne' /home/diogenes/.codex/memories/MEMORY.md --max-count 12"],"cwd":"file:///home/diogenes/Projects/twyne","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"rtk proxy rg -n 'all in flow|fluid manuscript|manuscript-panel|Twyne' /home/diogenes/.codex/memories/MEMORY.md --max-count 12"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"88:# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/notorganic-provider shared account knowledge connections for Keating and Twyne\n89:scope: Implement account-owned knowledge sources with app-specific grants, explicit tool consent, and fail-closed revocation across Not Organic, Keating, and Twyne.\n112:## Task 3: Integrate account sources and MCP review in Twyne\n124:- when asking for knowledge bases to “carry over” into Keating and Twyne and be “easy to add or revoke an apps access to them” -> default to account-level ownership, per-app grants, explicit revocation, and guided setup [Task 1]\n132:- Twyne trusted Convex actions bind verified DID/sessionVersion to fresh DPoP tokens. Research requires enabling research, choosing a source search tool, and selecting “Your MCP servers”; sign-out, revocation, and schema changes clear/fail closed. [Task 3]\n138:- `ERR_CONNECTION_REFUSED` after an owned Twyne preview stopped is an environment/process condition, while localhost-to-deployed Convex CORS preflight must be verified separately; neither establishes deployed feature behavior. [Task 3]\n173:- Ground the work in the knot mark, forest/cream/lime palette, and authentic Twyne, Keating, Interleave, Stich, Voxq, and Baste marks. Keep payment language bounded as “launching this October”/planned, not production-payment proof. [Task 1]\n553:# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/twyne fluid manuscript editor, House attention policy, and Claude-work continuation\n554:scope: Continue and critique Twyne’s in-flow writing surfaces while preserving deliberate side-panel browsing, authorship, scoped validation boundaries, and return-to-writing continuity.\n565:- all in flow, flow-surface.tsx, flow-ribbon.tsx, manuscript-panel.tsx, twyne-editor.tsx, margin-surface.ts, MARGIN_SLOT_EVENT, OPEN_MARGIN_THREAD_EVENT, pneumatic post, galley slip, way in, 5180\n579:- when shaping the manuscript experience, the user wants it “all in flow,” with the side panel retained for deliberate browsing -> prioritize inline margin surfaces, quiet queues, and progressive disclosure over new panel-first workflows [Task 1]\n580:- on large Twyne features, the user explicitly prefers UI/design work first and allows backend/plumbing to be delegated to Codex -> preserve that sequencing [Task 1]\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"88:# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/notorganic-provider shared account knowledge connections for Keating and Twyne\n89:scope: Implement account-owned knowledge sources with app-specific grants, explicit tool consent, and fail-closed revocation across Not Organic, Keating, and Twyne.\n112:## Task 3: Integrate account sources and MCP review in Twyne\n124:- when asking for knowledge bases to “carry over” into Keating and Twyne and be “easy to add or revoke an apps access to them” -> default to account-level ownership, per-app grants, explicit revocation, and guided setup [Task 1]\n132:- Twyne trusted Convex actions bind verified DID/sessionVersion to fresh DPoP tokens. Research requires enabling research, choosing a source search tool, and selecting “Your MCP servers”; sign-out, revocation, and schema changes clear/fail closed. [Task 3]\n138:- `ERR_CONNECTION_REFUSED` after an owned Twyne preview stopped is an environment/process condition, while localhost-to-deployed Convex CORS preflight must be verified separately; neither establishes deployed feature behavior. [Task 3]\n173:- Ground the work in the knot mark, forest/cream/lime palette, and authentic Twyne, Keating, Interleave, Stich, Voxq, and Baste marks. Keep payment language bounded as “launching this October”/planned, not production-payment proof. [Task 1]\n553:# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/twyne fluid manuscript editor, House attention policy, and Claude-work continuation\n554:scope: Continue and critique Twyne’s in-flow writing surfaces while preserving deliberate side-panel browsing, authorship, scoped validation boundaries, and return-to-writing continuity.\n565:- all in flow, flow-surface.tsx, flow-ribbon.tsx, manuscript-panel.tsx, twyne-editor.tsx, margin-surface.ts, MARGIN_SLOT_EVENT, OPEN_MARGIN_THREAD_EVENT, pneumatic post, galley slip, way in, 5180\n579:- when shaping the manuscript experience, the user wants it “all in flow,” with the side panel retained for deliberate browsing -> prioritize inline margin surfaces, quiet queues, and progressive disclosure over new panel-first workflows [Task 1]\n580:- on large Twyne features, the user explicitly prefers UI/design work first and allows backend/plumbing to be delegated to Codex -> preserve that sequencing [Task 1]\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":35820},"formatted_output":"88:# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/notorganic-provider shared account knowledge connections for Keating and Twyne\n89:scope: Implement account-owned knowledge sources with app-specific grants, explicit tool consent, and fail-closed revocation across Not Organic, Keating, and Twyne.\n112:## Task 3: Integrate account sources and MCP review in Twyne\n124:- when asking for knowledge bases to “carry over” into Keating and Twyne and be “easy to add or revoke an apps access to them” -> default to account-level ownership, per-app grants, explicit revocation, and guided setup [