{"timestamp":"2026-10-05T17:39:56.083Z","ordinal":43479,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a10537-909f-77a3-96d8-dd07161f91ae","turn_id":"01a10d17-989f-7150-9fa5-0c502f3fed47","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-04facbc4-ac1a-4165-a4cd-03babca7a981","process_id":"18830","command":["/bin/bash","-lc","rtk proxy sed -n '1,155p' desktop/gpui/target/verification/sakana-title-review-5e786077ad8a/response.txt"],"cwd":"file:///home/diogenes/Projects/twyne","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"rtk proxy sed -n '1,155p' desktop/gpui/target/verification/sakana-title-review-5e786077ad8a/response.txt"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"```json\n{\n  \"risks\": [\n    {\n      \"risk\": \"Title glyph clipping may persist despite the 40px/44px typography. In 'page render' the title textarea gets `.xsmall()` before `.text_size(px(40.))` and `.line_height(px(44.))`, and the wrapper only constrains `min_h(px(44.))`. The line-box ratio is 44/40 = 1.1, and any residual xsmall metrics or internal textarea vertical padding is subtracted from that 44px, so bold display ascenders/accents and descenders (e.g. \\\"É\\\", \\\"Å\\\", \\\"g\\\", \\\"y\\\") can still be cropped at top and bottom, which is exactly the reported symptom. Verify by measuring rendered glyph bounds, not the box.\",\n      \"evidence\": \"page render: `Textarea::new(&self.title).xsmall()...text_size(px(40.)).line_height(px(44.))`; wrapper `.min_h(px(44.))`\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"risk\": \"The Enter-as-submit path can alter stored text, breaking the exact-text requirement. Per 'input submit behavior', `submit_on_enter(true)` only suppresses newline insertion for a plain Enter in multi-line mode; `Shift+Enter` still inserts a newline, and the title subscription in 'initialization' only reacts to `PressEnter { shift: false, .. }`. If the emitted event's `shift` field does not track the action's shift, Shift+Enter would both insert a newline and jump focus to the body; conversely, if any submit-side handling trims or normalizes the value, a plain Enter would rewrite the title. The empty-title placeholder \\\"Untitled manuscript\\\" must also never be persisted.\",\n      \"evidence\": \"initialization: `submit_on_enter(true)` + `InputEvent::PressEnter { shift: false, .. }`; input submit behavior: `insert_newline = is_multi_line() && (!self.submit_on_enter || action.shift)`\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"risk\": \"Single shared page scroll plus the caret-reveal heuristics can leave the title cropped or off-screen. The same `writing_scroll` handle is tracked by the rich `body-field` branch and by `manuscript-page`, and `reveal_caret_next_frame` reads `this.writing_scroll.bounds()` on the next frame (potentially stale immediately after the title auto-grows), clamps `offset.y = offset.y.min(px(0.))`, and applies fixed `px(8.)`/`px(16.)` margins to a 40px glyph. When the page is scrolled down or modes are toggled (reading/source/rich), the offset may not reset, so clicking or focusing the title can still show it clipped at the top, re-creating the 'title feels separate' effect. The Enter transition also targets `focus_writing`, not the body entity directly.\",\n      \"evidence\": \"caret reveal: `let viewport = this.writing_scroll.bounds();` ... `offset.y = offset.y.min(px(0.));`; page render: both `body-field` and `manuscript-page` call `.track_scroll(&self.writing_scroll)`\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"tests\": [\n    {\n      \"case\": \"Fresh manuscript, title focused with placeholder visible and stored title empty: press Enter.\",\n      \"expect\": \"Focus lands in the body field; exactly one transition occurs; no newline is inserted into the title; stored title remains exactly \\\"\\\" (placeholder not persisted); body text unchanged.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"case\": \"Exact-text round trip: paste a title containing leading/trailing spaces, an embedded newline, and ascender/descender/accent glyphs (e.g. \\\"Ĝg y É Å\\\"), then blur and reload the manuscript.\",\n      \"expect\": \"Stored title is byte-identical to the pasted value, rendered centered, with no top or bottom glyph clipping inside the 40px text on the 44px line, and the title block grows without overlapping the body.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"case\": \"Shift+Enter versus Enter while the title is focused.\",\n      \"expect\": \"Shift+Enter inserts a newline into the title, keeps focus in the title, and stores that newline; a subsequent plain Enter moves focus to the body and preserves every previously entered title character exactly.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"case\": \"Long body scrolled to the bottom, then click/focus the title; then toggle reading, source, and back to the writing page.\",\n      \"expect\": \"The single page scroll brings the full title glyphs (including descenders and accents) into view with the top not cropped; after returning to the writing page the title sits at the top of the same scroll container, is not left scrolled, and does not appear visually separated from the body.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"```json\n{\n  \"risks\": [\n    {\n      \"risk\": \"Title glyph clipping may persist despite the 40px/44px typography. In 'page render' the title textarea gets `.xsmall()` before `.text_size(px(40.))` and `.line_height(px(44.))`, and the wrapper only constrains `min_h(px(44.))`. The line-box ratio is 44/40 = 1.1, and any residual xsmall metrics or internal textarea vertical padding is subtracted from that 44px, so bold display ascenders/accents and descenders (e.g. \\\"É\\\", \\\"Å\\\", \\\"g\\\", \\\"y\\\") can still be cropped at top and bottom, which is exactly the reported symptom. Verify by measuring rendered glyph bounds, not the box.\",\n      \"evidence\": \"page render: `Textarea::new(&self.title).xsmall()...text_size(px(40.)).line_height(px(44.))`; wrapper `.min_h(px(44.))`\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"risk\": \"The Enter-as-submit path can alter stored text