cktick run in the body, or use a safe alternate fence.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"file\": \"desktop/gpui/src/insert_menu/markdown.rs\",\n      \"claim\": \"`insert.mermaid` always wraps source in triple backticks. A triple-backtick line in the source closes the generated fence early, so the Markdown no longer contains the full Mermaid block.\",\n      \"reproductionInput\": {\n        \"text\": \"/mermaid\",\n        \"query\": { \"query\": \"mermaid\", \"range\": [0, 8] },\n        \"id\": \"insert.mermaid\",\n        \"values\": { \"Text\": \"graph TD\\n```\\nA --> B\" }\n      },\n      \"expected\": \"The generated Markdown parses as one Mermaid block containing the complete source.\",\n      \"fix\": \"Choose a fence longer than the longest backtick run in the source.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"file\": \"desktop/gpui/src/insert_menu/markdown.rs\",\n      \"claim\": \"`insert.math-inline` interpolates source without protecting its `$` delimiter. Source `x$y` produces `$x$y$`, which splits the intended inline math at the source dollar.\",\n      \"reproductionInput\": {\n        \"text\": \"/math\",\n        \"query\": { \"query\": \"math\", \"range\": [0, 5] },\n        \"id\": \"insert.math-inline\",\n        \"values\": { \"Text\": \"x$y\" }\n      },\n      \"expected\": \"Markdown that round-trips as one inline math node with source `x$y`.\",\n      \"fix\": \"Use parser-compatible escaping or a delimiter strategy that cannot be terminated by the source.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"tests\": [\n    {\n      \"name\": \"unicode_offsets_use_bytes_for_markdown_and_scalars_for_rich\",\n      \"input\": \"Detect `/x` in `é /x` with both adapters.\",\n      \"expected\": \"Markdown range is 3..5 bytes; rich range is 2..4 Unicode scalars.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"stale_query_cannot_match_prefix_of_extended_token\",\n      \"input\": \"Plan against `/hello` using stale query `he` at range 0..3.\",\n      \"expected\": \"Return the changed-position error without producing an edit.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"prefix_replacement_preserves_suffix_marker\",\n      \"input\": \"Apply `paragraph.heading-1` to `/heading - item` with query range 0..8.\",\n      \"expected\": \"Preserve `- item` in the replacement; do not strip it as an existing prefix.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"code_block_fence_exceeds_body_backtick_run\",\n      \"input\": \"Apply `paragraph.code-block` to `/code ````` with query range 0..5.\",\n      \"expected\": \"The generated Markdown parses as a fenced block whose body retains the four-backtick run.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"mermaid_fence_exceeds_source_backtick_run\",\n      \"input\": \"Insert Mermaid source `graph TD\\\\n```\\\\nA --> B`.\",\n      \"expected\": \"The generated Markdown parses as one Mermaid block containing the complete source.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"inline_math_dollar_round_trip\",\n      \"input\": \"Insert inline math source `x$y`.\",\n      \"expected\": \"Parsing the generated Markdown yields one inline math node with source `x$y`.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"rich_insert_is_one_undo_transaction\",\n      \"input\": \"Apply a valid rich link insertion over a slash query, then undo once.\",\n      \"expected\": \"One undo restores the original document containing the slash query.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n"},"started_at_ms":1791225642941,"completed_at_ms":1791225642941}}
