{"timestamp":"2026-10-05T18:44:29.077Z","ordinal":44190,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a10d61-b315-7960-876e-73ad1578dd5c","call_id":"call_Ky5ipaQyR2rW9FaW4ofsFkoT","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.4 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"ff5ecf\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000019571,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":123,\"output\":\"    Finished `test` profile [unoptimized] target(s) in 40.46s\\n     Running unittests src/main.rs (desktop/gpui/target/debug/deps/twyne_desktop-714b0cd2f900cfba)\\n\\nrunning 2 tests\\ntest app::slash_coordinator::tests::slash_escape_and_form_cancel_preserve_text_and_editor_selection ... ok\\ntest app::slash_coordinator::tests::slash_menu_filters_inserts_and_undoes_through_markdown_controls ... ok\\n\\ntest result: ok. 2 passed; 0 failed; 0 ignored; 0 measured; 108 filtered out; finished in 3.50s\\n\\n\"}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"i\":0,\"chunk_id\":\"67c4b6\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000015431,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":991,\"output\":\"# Twyne GPUI\\n\\nTwyne's native desktop port uses Rust and [GPUI Kit 0.7](https://gpui-kit.com/).\\nThe goal is the full hosted desktop experience with identical styling, original\\nassets and behavior. The working offline slice includes the rich editor, Dossier,\\nlocal editorial panels and native Typst proof/PDF.\\n\\nThe full Electrobun application remains the reference. The port is unfinished;\\n[PORT_PLAN.md](PORT_PLAN.md) separates implemented behavior, retained checks,\\nunmounted foundations and remaining work.\\n\\n## Run\\n\\nUse Bun, the repository's Rust toolchain, and the native libraries in\\n[GPUI Kit's installation guide](https://gpui-kit.com/docs/installation/).\\nThe repository's Devenv shell provides the Rust toolchain and Linux libraries.\\n\\nFrom the repository root:\\n\\n```bash\\nrtk proxy bun install --frozen-lockfile\\nrtk proxy devenv shell -- rtk proxy bun run desktop.gpui\\n```\\n\\nUse an isolated library or import files on startup:\\n\\n```bash\\nrtk proxy devenv shell -- rtk proxy bun run desktop.gpui --data-dir /tmp/twyne-native-library /path/to/draft.typ\\n```\\n\\nImports create library copies. Original files remain independent.\\n\\nThe developer build creates `twyne-document` from Twyne's existing TypeScript\\ndocument converters. Its compiled executable includes the Bun runtime. Offline\\nwriting needs no web server or account; GPUI renders the interface and the native\\nRust Typst engine renders proof/PDF. The helper handles source/HTML reconciliation,\\nstarter generation and the original MathJax export conversion.\\n\\nThe helper build also creates `twyne-math-write`. It is a diagnostic executable,\\nnot the main editor's math renderer or evidence of Write-view parity.\\n\\nFor direct Cargo development, build the helper first:\\n\\n```bash\\nrtk proxy bun run desktop.gpui.build-helper\\nrtk proxy devenv shell -- rtk proxy cargo run --locked --manifest-path desktop/gpui/Cargo.toml\\n```\\n\\nLinux requires X11 or Wayland and a graphics driver supported by WGPU. Native\\nfile pickers use the desktop's XDG portal. macOS requires Xcode command line\\ntools; Windows requires the MSVC C++ toolchain. Bundles, installers, signing, and\\nautomatic updates remain pending.\\n\\n## Writing and proof\\n\\n- **Write:** native rich text with Unicode input, selection, clipboard, IME,\\n  formatting, and undo/redo. Typing bursts form one undo group. Imported cached\\n  HTML is projected from canonical source before editing. Footnote and endnote\\n  markers open an editable note; collected notes navigate back to their\\n  manuscript references. Save and navigation capture unblurred note input.\\n- **Equation source:** activate an inline or block equation to edit its retained native textarea. Render equation submits through the actual canonical converter and preserves independent manuscript undo; Cancel keeps the saved source. Inline editing uses a measured child inside the original atom. Preview currently reports unavailable. Actual OS input and original-browser baseline/pixel parity remain separate gates.\\n- **Dossier:** the original ten sections, imported material, references, local\\n  probes, create/refine filing, and scoped recovery. Filing opens Write after\\n  the document is actually saved.\\n- **Source:** canonical Typst with a separate recoverable draft. Apply requires\\n  a successful current compile and verified projection. Discard preserves the\\n  manuscript. Source edits update the real proof after 450 ms of quiet. The\\n  native code editor provides Typst highlighting, line numbers,\\n  folded generated helpers, search/replace, source snippets, comments, wrapping,\\n  and line navigation. Pending Source edits lock the rich view.\\n- **Proof/Split:** the same pinned Typst fork and ordered fonts as the web\\n  renderer, original artwork, real SVG pages, zoom, page navigation, and PDF\\n  export. Failed compilation retains the last valid proof.\\n  The footer retains the selected page across Write/Proof transitions. Its\\n  count option leaves the current mode active; page choices reveal the page's\\n\"}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"i\":1,\"chunk_id\":\"80503f\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000023483,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":654,\"output\":\"import type { EditorCommandContext } from \\\"./editor-commands\\\";\\nimport {\\n  getSlashCommands,\\n  type EditorCommandDefinition,\\n} from \\\"./editor-commands\\\";\\nimport { shortcutHints, type ShortcutPlatform } from \\\"./keybindings\\\";\\n\\nexport interface SlashCommandCandidate {\\n  command: EditorCommandDefinition;\\n  score: number;\\n  shortcut: string | null;\\n}\\n\\nfunction normalise(value: string): string {\\n  return value\\n    .toLocaleLowerCase()\\n    .replace(/[^a-z0-9]+/g, \\\" \\\")\\n    .trim();\\n}\\n\\n/**\\n * Small fuzzy scorer tuned for command menus.\\n *\\n * Exact prefixes win, then word prefixes, then ordered subsequences. A query\\n * that cannot be found in order is excluded rather than returning every\\n * command with an arbitrary low score.\\n */\\nexport function fuzzyCommandScore(\\n  command: EditorCommandDefinition,\\n  query: string,\\n): number | null {\\n  const needle = normalise(query);\\n  if (!needle) return 0;\\n\\n  const label = normalise(command.label);\\n  const haystack = normalise(\\n    [\\n      command.label,\\n      command.description,\\n      command.id,\\n      ...command.searchTerms,\\n      ...(command.slash?.keywords ?? []),\\n    ].join(\\\" \\\"),\\n  );\\n\\n  if (label === needle) return 1000;\\n  if (label.startsWith(needle)) return 800 - (label.length - needle.length);\\n  const wordPrefix = label\\n    .split(\\\" \\\")\\n    .findIndex((word) => word.startsWith(needle));\\n  if (wordPrefix >= 0) return 650 - wordPrefix * 10;\\n  const contained = haystack.indexOf(needle);\\n  if (contained >= 0) return 500 - Math.min(contained, 200);\\n\\n  let cursor = 0;\\n  let gapPenalty = 0;\\n  for (const character of needle.replace(/\\\\s/g, \\\"\\\")) {\\n    const found = haystack.indexOf(character, cursor);\\n    if (found < 0) return null;\\n    gapPenalty += found - cursor;\\n    cursor = found + 1;\\n  }\\n  return 250 - Math.min(gapPenalty, 200);\\n}\\n\\nexport function fuzzySlashCommands(\\n  query: string,\\n  context: EditorCommandContext = {},\\n  platform: ShortcutPlatform = \\\"mac\\\",\\n): SlashCommandCandidate[] {\\n  return getSlashCommands(\\\"\\\", context)\\n    .flatMap((command): SlashCommandCandidate[] => {\\n      const score = fuzzyCommandScore(command, query);\\n      if (score == null) return [];\\n      return [\\n        {\\n          command,\\n          score,\\n          shortcut: shortcutHints(command.id as never, platform)[0] ?? null,\\n        },\\n      ];\\n    })\\n    .sort((a, b) => {\\n      if (a.score !== b.score) return b.score - a.score;\\n      const group = (a.command.slash?.group ?? \\\"\\\").localeCompare(\\n        b.command.slash?.group ?? \\\"\\\",\\n      );\\n      if (group !== 0) return group;\\n      return (a.command.slash?.order ?? 0) - (b.command.slash?.order ?? 0);\\n    });\\n}\\n\"}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"i\":2,\"chunk_id\":\"8f5d71\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000016464,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":377,\"output\":\"desktop/gpui/src/compositor.rs:202:    fn heading(&self) -> Option<u8> {\\ndesktop/gpui/src/compositor.rs:220:        self.heading().is_some() || self.attribute(\\\"data-keep-with-next\\\") == Some(\\\"true\\\")\\ndesktop/gpui/src/compositor.rs:751:                (\\\"Subheading\\\", \\\"h3\\\"),\\ndesktop/gpui/src/compositor.rs:874:        let style = match self.active.heading() {\\ndesktop/gpui/src/compositor.rs:1174:                    self.active.heading() == Some(level),\\ndesktop/gpui/src/compositor.rs:1773:                        .disabled(!self.editable() || self.active.heading().is_some())\\ndesktop/gpui/src/compositor.rs:1787:                    if self.active.heading().is_some() {\\ndesktop/gpui/src/compositor.rs:1788:                        \\\"Always on for headings.\\\"\\ndesktop/gpui/src/compositor.rs:1910:                \\\"Alternate\\\",\\ndesktop/gpui/src/compositor.rs:1911:                OpeningInitialCollection::Alternate,\\ndesktop/gpui/src/compositor.rs:2021:                    .when(opening.collection == OpeningInitialCollection::Alternate, |this| this.child(help(\\\"A complete alternate A–Z collection, with a different botanical illustration for every letter.\\\", cx)))))\\ndesktop/gpui/src/compositor.rs:2175:            (\\\"⌘/Ctrl Shift Z\\\", \\\"Redo\\\"),\\ndesktop/gpui/src/compositor.rs:2176:            (\\\"Tab / Shift Tab\\\", \\\"Indent / outdent\\\"),\\ndesktop/gpui/src/compositor.rs:2177:            (\\\"Shift Enter\\\", \\\"Line break\\\"),\\ndesktop/gpui/src/editor/view.rs:2598:            container = container.child(dragging::heading_handle(\\n\"}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"i\":3,\"chunk_id\":\"c0dbf2\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000020229,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":138,\"output\":\"  7260 desktop/gpui/src/app.rs\\n   235 desktop/gpui/src/app/slash_coordinator.rs\\n    55 desktop/gpui/src/insert_menu/catalog.rs\\n    56 desktop/gpui/src/insert_menu/context.rs\\n    74 desktop/gpui/src/insert_menu/filter.rs\\n    76 desktop/gpui/src/insert_menu/form.rs\\n   122 desktop/gpui/src/insert_menu/markdown.rs\\n    18 desktop/gpui/src/insert_menu/mod.rs\\n    66 desktop/gpui/src/insert_menu/parameters.rs\\n    55 desktop/gpui/src/insert_menu/rich.rs\\n   123 desktop/gpui/src/insert_menu/tests.rs\\n   102 desktop/gpui/src/insert_menu/view.rs\\n  8242 total\\n\"}"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a10d4c-a644-7d71-9054-bf5cd3583d03","create_time":1791225869.0779357}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
