{"timestamp":"2026-10-05T19:10:44.188Z","ordinal":44485,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_0acb6e766bb0227d016ac3f618df7c87d194c2f486be06f1a1","status":"completed","call_id":"call_9MxuXv5IUfM7vAI2Nhv4EmIL","name":"exec","input":"text(await tools.apply_patch(\"*** Begin Patch\\n*** Add File: /home/diogenes/Projects/twyne/desktop/gpui/tools/sync-insert-menu.ts\\n+// Regenerate or verify native fixtures by executing the actual Source registry.\\n+import { getSlashCommands } from \\\"../../../src/utils/editor-commands\\\";\\n+import { fuzzySlashCommands } from \\\"../../../src/utils/slash-command-filter\\\";\\n+import { readFile, writeFile } from \\\"node:fs/promises\\\";\\n+import { resolve } from \\\"node:path\\\";\\n+import { isDeepStrictEqual } from \\\"node:util\\\";\\n+\\n+const check = process.argv.includes(\\\"--check\\\");\\n+const directory = resolve(import.meta.dir, \\\"../fixtures/insert-menu\\\");\\n+const context = { readOnly: false, hasSelection: false };\\n+const catalog = getSlashCommands(\\\"\\\", context).map(command => ({\\n+  id: command.id, label: command.label, description: command.description,\\n+  group: command.slash!.group, order: command.slash!.order,\\n+  searchTerms: command.searchTerms, keywords: command.slash!.keywords ?? [],\\n+  availability: command.availability,\\n+}));\\n+const oldCases = JSON.parse(await readFile(resolve(directory, \\\"source-filter-cases.json\\\"), \\\"utf8\\\")) as { query: string }[];\\n+const cases = oldCases.map(({ query }) => ({\\n+  query, results: fuzzySlashCommands(query, context).map(({ command, score }) => ({ id: command.id, score })),\\n+}));\\n+for (const [name, value] of [[\\\"source-catalog.json\\\", catalog], [\\\"source-filter-cases.json\\\", cases]] as const) {\\n+  const path = resolve(directory, name);\\n+  if (check) {\\n+    const stored = JSON.parse(await readFile(path, \\\"utf8\\\"));\\n+    if (!isDeepStrictEqual(stored, value)) throw new Error(`${name} differs from the current Source registry. Review and regenerate the fixture.`);\\n+  } else { await writeFile(path, JSON.stringify(value, null, 2) + \\\"\\\\n\\\"); }\\n+}\\n+console.log(JSON.stringify({ status: check ? \\\"matched\\\" : \\\"generated\\\", commands: catalog.length, queries: cases.length, nativeLinkIncluded: false, networkUsed: false }));\\n*** Add File: /home/diogenes/Projects/twyne/desktop/gpui/fixtures/insert-menu/README.md\\n+# In-document insertion\\n+\\n+`src/insert_menu/` is independent of the writing-room host. Source's 17 editable,\\n+collapsed-selection commands supply the catalog, descriptions, grouping, search\\n+terms and keywords. Native adds `insert.link` at the user's request. The differential\\n+filter check compares the Source subset separately from that addition.\\n+\\n+Regenerate or check these fixtures by running the actual original registry:\\n+\\n+```bash\\n+rtk proxy bun desktop/gpui/tools/sync-insert-menu.ts --check\\n+rtk proxy bun desktop/gpui/tools/sync-insert-menu.ts\\n+```\\n+\\n+`source-receipt.json` records the initial snapshot's input hashes. Regeneration\\n+does not rewrite that historical receipt. Later capture/build receipts record\\n+their own inputs.\\n+\\n+`capture-source.ts` drives the real web editor in an isolated browser and IDB\\n+library. It records the menu's actual fonts, bounds and styles and exercises\\n+filtering, arrows, Escape and heading insertion. It waits for Source's asynchronous\\n+command completion before typing the heading's content.\\n+\\n+```bash\\n+rtk proxy bun desktop/gpui/fixtures/insert-menu/capture-source.ts /tmp/new-source-insert-capture\\n+```\\n+\\n+The local Vite reference must already be running on `127.0.0.1:5207` (override\\n+`TWYNE_INSERT_SOURCE_URL` with another loopback origin). This is browser evidence,\\n+not Electrobun-host or real-account evidence.\\n+\\n+Native `tools/capture-native.py` accepts `slash`, `slash-filtered`, and `slash-form`.\\n+Use a synthetic `.twyne`/HTML fixture whose final paragraph ends with `/` or\\n+`/table`. Capture mode only places the caret and opens the menu; it does not\\n+insert a diagnostic slash into the user's writing. Run with an immutable build\\n+and isolated library.\\n+\\n+Markdown and rich adapters apply the query removal and insertion as one undoable\\n+edit. Native parameter forms leave the query untouched until commit, including\\n+when cancelled; Source removes its query before opening a parameter dialog.\\n+Native also clamps the popup to the visible window. Exact parameter-dialog styling\\n+and Source shortcut hints remain comparison work.\\n+\\n+Sakana's bounded catalog/filter/Markdown/review outputs are retained under\\n+`advisory-*`. Each has a root adoption review. Only the fuzzy scorer was adopted\\n+as model-produced code; its results are checked against 21 actual Source queries.\\n*** End Patch\"));\nconst r=await Promise.allSettled([\n tools.exec_command({cmd:\"rtk proxy bun desktop/gpui/tools/sync-insert-menu.ts --check\",max_output_tokens:1800}),\n tools.exec_command({cmd:\"rtk proxy bun desktop/gpui/tools/build-helper.ts\",yield_time_ms:1000,max_output_tokens:1700}),\n tools.write_stdin({session_id:70378,chars:\"\",yield_time_ms:1000,max_output_tokens:3000}),\n]);r.forEach((x,i)=>text({i,...(x.status===\"fulfilled\"?x.value:{error:String(x.reason)})}));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a10d4c-a644-7d71-9054-bf5cd3583d03","create_time":1791227359.881843}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-05T19:10:44.222Z","ordinal":44486,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a10537-909f-77a3-96d8-dd07161f91ae","turn_id":"01a10d4c-a644-7d71-9054-bf5cd3583d03","item":{"type":"FileChange","id":"exec-6f141bc5-a7f5-4d19-b660-13350b0c81c3","changes":{"/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne/desktop/gpui/tools/sync-insert-menu.ts":{"type":"add","content":"// Regenerate or verify native fixtures by executing the actual Source registry.\nimport { getSlashCommands } from \"../../../src/utils/editor-commands\";\nimport { fuzzySlashCommands } from \"../../../src/utils/slash-command-filter\";\nimport { readFile, writeFile } from \"node:fs/promises\";\nimport { resolve } from \"node:path\";\nimport { isDeepStrictEqual } from \"node:util\";\n\nconst check = process.argv.includes(\"--check\");\nconst directory = resolve(import.meta.dir, \"../fixtures/insert-menu\");\nconst context = { readOnly: false, hasSelection: false };\nconst catalog = getSlashCommands(\"\", context).map(command => ({\n  id: command.id, label: command.label, description: command.description,\n  group: command.slash!.group, order: command.slash!.order,\n  searchTerms: command.searchTerms, keywords: command.slash!.keywords ?? [],\n  availability: command.availability,\n}));\nconst oldCases = JSON.parse(await readFile(resolve(directory, \"source-filter-cases.json\"), \"utf8\")) as { query: string }[];\nconst cases = oldCases.map(({ query }) => ({\n  query, results: fuzzySlashCommands(query, context).map(({ command, score }) => ({ id: command.id, score })),\n}));\nfor (const [name, value] of [[\"source-catalog.json\", catalog], [\"source-filter-cases.json\", cases]] as const) {\n  const path = resolve(directory, name);\n  if (check) {\n    const stored = JSON.parse(await readFile(path, \"utf8\"));\n    if (!isDeepStrictEqual(stored, value)) throw new Error(`${name} differs from the current Source registry. Review and regenerate the fixture.`);\n  } else { await writeFile(path, JSON.stringify(value, null, 2) + \"\\n\"); }\n}\nconsole.log(JSON.stringify({ status: check ? \"matched\" : \"generated\", commands: catalog.length, queries: cases.length, nativeLinkIncluded: false, networkUsed: false }));\n"},"/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne/desktop/gpui/fixtures/insert-menu/README.md":{"type":"add","content":"# In-document insertion\n\n`src/insert_menu/` is independent of the writing-room host. Source's 17 editable,\ncollapsed-selection commands supply the catalog, descriptions, grouping, search\nterms and keywords. Native adds `insert.link` at the user's request. The differential\nfilter check compares the Source subset separately from that addition.\n\nRegenerate or check these fixtures by running the actual original registry:\n\n```bash\nrtk proxy bun desktop/gpui/tools/sync-insert-menu.ts --check\nrtk proxy bun desktop/gpui/tools/sync-insert-menu.ts\n```\n\n`source-receipt.json` records the initial snapshot's input hashes. Regeneration\ndoes not rewrite that historical receipt. Later capture/build receipts record\ntheir own inputs.\n\n`capture-source.ts` drives the real web editor in an isolated browser and IDB\nlibrary. It records the menu's actual fonts, bounds and styles and exercises\nfiltering, arrows, Escape and heading insertion. It waits for Source's asynchronous\ncommand completion before typing the heading's content.\n\n```bash\nrtk proxy bun desktop/gpui/fixtures/insert-menu/capture-source.ts /tmp/new-source-insert-capture\n```\n\nThe local Vite reference must already be running on `127.0.0.1:5207` (override\n`TWYNE_INSERT_SOURCE_URL` with another loopback origin). This is browser evidence,\nnot Electrobun-host or real-account evidence.\n\nNative `tools/capture-native.py` accepts `slash`, `slash-filtered`, and `slash-form`.\nUse a synthetic `.twyne`/HTML fixture whose final paragraph ends with `/` or\n`/table`. Capture mode only places the caret and opens the menu; it does not\ninsert a diagnostic slash into the user's writing. Run with an immutable build\nand isolated library.\n\nMarkdown and rich adapters apply the query removal and insertion as one undoable\nedit. Native parameter forms leave the query untouched until commit, including\nwhen cancelled; Source removes its query before opening a parameter dialog.\nNative also clamps the popup to the visible window. Exact parameter-dialog styling\nand Source shortcut hints remain comparison work.\n\nSakana's bounded catalog/filter/Markdown/review outputs are retained under\n`advisory-*`. Each has a root adoption review. Only the fuzzy scorer was adopted\nas model-produced code; its results are checked against 21 actual Source queries.\n"}},"status":"completed","stdout":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA /home/diogenes/Projects/twyne/desktop/gpui/tools/sync-insert-menu.ts\nA /home/diogenes/Projects/twyne/desktop/gpui/fixtures/insert-menu/README.md\n","stderr":""},"started_at_ms":1791227444221,"completed_at_ms":1791227444222}}
