thored":false},{"client_authored":false,"mcp_attribution":{"sources":[{"first_turn_id":"01a10555-dfb0-7570-9355-0ebfebd2abb9","plugin_id":"unified-computer-use@openai-bundled","server_name":"cua_repl","tool_name":"js"}],"status":"complete"},"retained_source":{"complete":true,"id":{"message_id":"msg_01a10d5f-b8d1-7bb0-bf15-011f62014650","role":"user","turn_id":"01a10d4c-a644-7d71-9054-bf5cd3583d03"},"revision":"retained_01a10d5f-b8d1-7bb0-bf15-013c3e7533d6"},"user_input_order":2381},{"client_authored":false,"compaction_model_hash":"3000","mcp_attribution":{"sources":[{"first_turn_id":"01a10555-dfb0-7570-9355-0ebfebd2abb9","plugin_id":"unified-computer-use@openai-bundled","server_name":"cua_repl","tool_name":"js"}],"status":"complete"}}],"resume_metadata":{"last_started_turn_id":"01a10d4c-a644-7d71-9054-bf5cd3583d03","multi_agent_version":"v2","previous_turn_settings":{"comp_hash":"3000","model":"gpt-6.1-sol","realtime_active":false}},"retained_context":{"assistant_messages":[{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_0acb6e766bb0227d016ac3ebf8df6087d1adbf0a281d4780d7","order":2378,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a10d51-cbdf-7903-9a72-8da2c8697931","text":"The title now passes the wrapping, centering, caret, and save/reopen checks. The slash menu will use the web editor’s command catalog and search ranking. I’m adding Link as well, since you requested it and it isn’t currently in the web slash catalog.","turn_id":"01a10d4c-a644-7d71-9054-bf5cd3583d03"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_0acb6e766bb0227d016ac3ecb014ac87d19db57741572212b2","order":2379,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a10d54-9329-75f1-9a85-dbfbfbbbdf80","text":"Each command will go through a document adapter that removes the slash query and inserts the element as one undoable edit. Tables, links, images, notes, diagrams, and equations will open input forms; cancelling a form will leave what you typed intact.","turn_id":"01a10d4c-a644-7d71-9054-bf5cd3583d03"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_0acb6e766bb0227d016ac3ede6698087d1b7e886fed62d2130","order":2380,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a10d59-524f-7cd3-a41c-2da3526e06e7","text":"The catalog, filtering, Markdown edits, rich-document edits, menu, and forms now live in separate files. I’ve also given Sakana a bounded review of the insertion adapters while I wire up the UI; I’ll check its findings against tests before using them.","turn_id":"01a10d4c-a644-7d71-9054-bf5cd3583d03"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_0acb6e766bb0227d016ac3efb0ff0c87d192d699fd59784831","order":2382,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a10d60-7cb8-7313-83d0-73ba29b5d590","text":"I’m structuring it around features and document boundaries, with `app.rs` responsible for assembling the writing room. It still carries too much rendering and lifecycle code; the existing coordinators help, and I’m moving new work out of it consistently.\n\n| Area | Responsibility |\n|---|---|\n| `src/app/` | Connect features to the active manuscript, focus, routing, and saving |\n| `src/editor/` | Rich document model, transactions, history, selection, and native editor views |\n| `src/insert_menu/` | Slash catalog, detection, filtering, Markdown/rich insertion adapters, menu, and forms |\n| `workspace`, `source_session`, `semantic_bridge` | Authored Typst and its visual projection |\n| `storage`, `revisions` | Local persistence and document history |\n| `native_accounts`, `tools/connected` | Rust account contracts and the Bun SDK boundary |\n\nMy grasp is strongest around the editor, document preservation, local saving, and how the GPUI screen connects those pieces. I also know where the connected-work scaffolding stops: online sync and live AI/knowledge-base integration still need host wiring and real-account verification. I’m not treating prepared APIs or passing unit tests as completed features.\n\nThe biggest improvements for working faster here are:\n\n- **A searchable module map:** Rust module → corresponding web component → relevant tests. I’m adding that so investigations start at the right boundary.\n- **Reproducible UI fixtures:** a known document, window size, scale, and editor mode, exercised in an isolated library. That makes clipping and keyboard bugs much easier to reproduce.\n- **Smaller delegation units:** pure filtering, placement, conversion, or contract tasks with frozen inputs. Sakana’s review found useful Markdown edge cases, but also made a stale-query claim that conflicts with the web editor’s caret behavior—so delegated output needs direct checks.\n- **Separate implementation from evidence:** record which build was actually inspected, rather than assuming an older screenshot proves current code.\n\nThe next structural step is to separate the writing-room layout from its lifecycle orchestration. I’m finishing the slash interaction first so that extraction follows working boundaries.","turn_id":"01a10d4c-a644-7d71-9054-bf5cd3583d03"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_0acb6e766bb0227d016ac3f071406c87d191679cedd8214db0","order":2383,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a10d63-4227-7c50-b69e-d3ff25a146b7","text":"The mounted menu checks now pass for filtering, arrow navigation, insertion, Escape, form cancellation, and Markdown undo. I’m checking real form values and rich-document table insertion next. I’m also separating the room layout and existing UI tests from `app.rs`, which will make future work easier to divide between agents.","turn_id":"01a10d4c-a644-7d71-9054-bf5cd3583d03"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_0acb6e766bb0227d016ac3f18f245487d1aeee26a6d183559f","order":2384,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a10d67-9eeb-7dc2-a63b-5854d77927e7","text":"The layout and existing UI tests are now outside `app.rs`, and the module map is in place. The rich-table check caught a form issue that the pure transaction tests couldn’t reveal. I’m tracing it through the mounted controls so the fix covers the interaction you’ll use.","turn_id":"01a10d4c-a644-7d71-9054-bf5cd3583d03"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_0acb6e766bb0227d016ac3f351ae9487d1842f75a03aa75f73","order":2385,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a10d6e-7f93-7a40-aa5f-58c8b29044aa","text":"The rich-table form now works. Its clicks were reaching the editor underneath; the popup now intercepts them correctly. The broader suite passed 113 checks. One new test used “New draft,” which correctly opens Dossier, when it needed to switch directly to another writing document—I’m correcting that fixture setup.","turn_id":"01a10d4c-a644-7d71-9054-bf5cd3583d03"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_0acb6e766bb0227d016ac3f520778087d1b8769836a6ca0134","order":2386,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a10d75-89bd-7ab2-9cae-e14812f7fa36","text":"All six slash interaction checks now pass, including rich tables, link entry by keyboard, undo, and stale menu actions after a document switch. The web reference also passes the matching browser checks. I’m now comparing the native rendering with the real fonts.","turn_id":"01a10d4c-a644-7d71-9054-bf5cd3583d03"}],"assistant_messages_incomplete":true,"incomplete":false,"next_order":2387,"user_messages":[{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_01a10b52-46ed-7f41-959e-f106ea1871fb","order":2268,"revision":"retained_01a10b52-46ed-7f41-959e-f12f4e3b1fa4","text":"status report","turn_id":"01a10a1b-b650-7660-b5ef-56e1a3784ac1"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_01a10b53-da43-7270-80cd-7083547d38fa","order":2270,"revision":"retained_01a10b53-da43-7270-80cd-70adcb767628","text":"okay and what about online writing and sync?","turn_id":"01a10a1b-b650-7660-b5ef-56e1a3784ac1"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_01a10b54-68e0-7e10-a51e-719395495580","order":2271,"revision":"retained_01a10b54-68e0-7e10-a51e-71be7882db09","text":"what about the ai integration? knowledge base integration, gen ui components?","turn_id":"01a10a1b-b650-7660-b5ef-56e1a3784ac1"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_01a10b57-fa01-7481-83c6-cd438ad53be0","order":2274,"revision":"retained_01a10b57-fa01-7481-83c6-cd6d219dd390","text":"start the application i want to see what its like","turn_id":"01a10a1b-b650-7660-b5ef-56e1a3784ac1"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_01a10d17-d63e-7422-b308-733ebf06665a","order":2365,"revision":"retained_01a10d17-d63e-7422-b308-735bca3ecf6f","text":"some interface bugs i noticed the title doesn't fully appear, getting cutoff on the bottom and top text, seems like some other field instead of just part of the same document.","turn_id":"01a10d17-989f-7150-9fa5-0c502f3fed47"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_01a10d2c-8564-7413-b861-aca58880da0a","order":2371,"revision":"retained_01a10d2c-8564-7413-b861-accc583a263c","text":"slash commands also don't seem to work yet, when typing / a menu should appear like on web with different options for me to input corresponding to different elements in a typist/markdown document like headers, tables, links, etc. just like the editor on web","turn_id":"01a10d17-989f-7150-9fa5-0c502f3fed47"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_01a10d2c-f33d-7770-858b-3dbbffeac92d","order":2372,"revision":"retained_01a10d2c-f33d-7770-858b-3dd16a2cc42d","text":"you should also cocnsider not dumpuing everything in app.rs and instead splitting things up more to make easy to parallelize work. think of your package structure. make things easily searchable.","turn_id":"01a10d17-989f-7150-9fa5-0c502f3fed47"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_01a10d5f-b8d1-7bb0-bf15-011f62014650","order":2381,"revision":"retained_01a10d5f-b8d1-7bb0-bf15-013c3e7533d6","text":"how have you decided to structure the project so far? how are you doing with grasping the current state? are thehre  ways that wouldl help you investigate issues a nd solve problems here faster?","turn_id":"01a10d4c-a644-7d71-9054-bf5cd3583d03"}],"user_messages_incomplete":true,"verified_answers":[]},"window_id":"01a10d80-09cc-7b72-84e5-0310ef2b5fec","window_number":63}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-05T19:17:37.360Z","ordinal":44520,"type":"world_state","payload":{"full":true,"state":{"agents_md":{"directory":"/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne","text":"<!-- headroom:rtk-instructions -->\n# Shell commands\n\nPrefix shell commands with `rtk`, including each segment of a command chain.\nUse `rtk proxy <command>` for unfiltered output or when debugging filter behavior.\n<!-- /headroom:rtk-instructions -->\n\n--- project-doc ---\n\n<!-- convex-ai-start -->\n\nThis project uses [Convex](https://convex.dev) as its backend.\n\nWhen working on Convex code, **always read `convex/_generated/ai/guidelines.md` first** for important guidelines on how to correctly use Convex APIs and patterns. The file contains rules that override what you may have learned about Convex from training data.\n\nConvex agent skills for common tasks can be installed by running `npx convex ai-files install`.\n\n<!-- convex-ai-end -->\n"},"apps_instructions":false,"collaboration_mode":{"mode":"default","model":"gpt-6.1-sol","instructions":"0a11049b0421e1e86f1e129af8d547a89548a0c3"},"context_window_guidance":"","environments":{"environments":{"local":{"cwd":"/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne","status":"available","shell":"bash"}},"current_date":"2026-10-05","timezone":"America/Toronto","filesystem":"<filesystem><workspace_roots><root>/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne</root></workspace_roots><permission_profile type=\"disabled\"><file_system type=\"unrestricted\" /></permission_profile></filesystem>","subagents":"<agent name=\"/root/cli_repair\" />\n<agent name=\"/root/native_assets\" />\n<agent name=\"/root/port_contract\" />\n<agent name=\"/root/rich_document\" />\n<agent name=\"/root/workspace_exchange\" />"},"environments_instructions":false,"git_attribution":false,"host_skills":{"body":"\n## Skills\nA skill is a set of local instructions to follow that is stored in a `SKILL.md` file. Below is the list of skills that can be used. Each entry includes a name, description, and a short path that can be expanded into an absolute path using the skill roots table.\n### Skill roots\n- `r0` = `/home/diogenes/.codex/skills`\n- `r1` = `/home/diogenes/.agents/skills`\n- `r2` = `/home/diogenes/.codex/skills/.system`\n- `r3` = `/home/diogenes/.codex/plugins/cache/openai-bundled`\n- `r4` = `/home/diogenes/.codex/plugins/cache/openai-curated-remote/google-drive/0.1.16/skills`\n- `r5` = `/home/diogenes/.codex/plugins/cache/openai-curated-remote/pages/0.1.19/skills`\n- `r6` = `/home/diogenes/.codex/plugins/cache/openai-curated-remote`\n- `r7` = `/home/diogenes/.codex/plugins/cache/openai-curated-remote/sites/0.1.75/skills`\n- `r8` = `/home/diogenes/.codex/plugins/cache/openai-curated-remote/work-pets/0.1.6/skills`\n- `r9` = `/home/diogenes/.codex/plugins/cache/openai-primary-runtime`\n- `r10` = `/home/diogenes/.codex/plugins/cache/openai-primary-runtime/spreadsheets/26.905.11957/skills`\n- `r11` = `/home/diogenes/.codex/plugins/cache/typesafe-ai`\n- `r12` = `/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne/.agents/skills`\n### Available skills\n- imagegen: Generate or edit raster images when the task benefits from AI-created bitmap visuals such as photos, illustrations, te (file: r2/imagegen/SKILL.md)\n- openai-docs: Use for Codex models/pricing, scheduled tasks, skills, settings, setup, troubleshooting, customization, automations, and (file: r2/openai-docs/SKILL.md)\n- skill-creator: Create or update a Codex skill with appropriately scoped instructions and any needed supporting resources. (file: r2/skill-creator/SKILL.md)\n- skill-installer: Install Codex skills into $CODEX_HOME/skills from a curated list or a GitHub repo path. Use when a user asks to list ins (file: r2/skill-installer/SKILL.md)\n- arize-admin: Manages Arize users, organizations, spaces, projects, roles, role bindings, resource restrictions, and API keys via the (file: r12/arize-admin/SKILL.md)\n- arize-ai-provider-integration: Creates, reads, updates, and deletes Arize AI integrations that store LLM provider credentials used by evaluators and o (file: r12/arize-ai-provider-integration/SKILL.md)\n- arize-annotation: Creates and manages annotation configs (categorical, continuous, freeform label schemas) and annotation queues (human (file: r12/arize-annotation/SKILL.md)\n- arize-compliance-audit: INVOKE THIS SKILL when auditing an AI agent or LLM app for regulatory compliance. Covers EU AI Act, GPAI Code of Prac (file: r12/arize-compliance-audit/SKILL.md)\n- arize-dataset: Creates, manages, and queries Arize datasets and examples. Covers dataset CRUD, appending examples, exporting data, and (file: r12/arize-dataset/SKILL.md)\n- arize-evaluator: Handles LLM-as-judge and code evaluator workflows on Arize including creating/updating evaluators, running evaluations  (file: r12/arize-evaluator/SKILL.md)\n- arize-experiment: Creates, runs, and analyzes Arize experiments for evaluating and comparing model performance. Covers experiment CRUD, (file: r12/arize-experiment/SKILL.md)\n- arize-instrumentation: Adds Arize AX tracing to an LLM application for the first time. Follows a two-phase agent-assisted flow to analyze the  (file: r12/arize-instrumentation/SKILL.md)\n- arize-link: Generates deep links to the Arize UI for traces, spans, sessions, datasets, labeling queues, evaluators, and annotati (file: r12/arize-link/SKILL.md)\n- arize-prompt-optimization: Optimizes, improves, and debugs LLM prompts using production trace data, evaluations, and annotations. Extracts prompts (file: r12/arize-prompt-optimization/SKILL.md)\n- arize-prompts: INVOKE THIS SKILL for Arize Prompt Hub and `ax prompts` workflows: author or import templates and save (Workflows A–B (file: r12/arize-prompts/SKILL.md)\n- arize-trace: Downloads, exports, and inspects existing Arize traces and spans to understand what an LLM app is doing or debug runtim (file: r12/arize-trace/SKILL.md)\n- convex: Convex is the backend agents get right on the first try: an all-TypeScript reactive platform where the database, serv (file: r12/convex/SKILL.md)\n- convex-acquire-domain: Find and buy a domain for the current Convex app through Convex, then bind it (labs; spend action). (file: r12/convex-acquire-domain/SKILL.md)\n- convex-add: Add a capability to the CURRENT Convex app — consults the served Convex capability catalog for always-current procedure (file: r12/convex-add/SKILL.md)\n- convex-advisor: Read the Convex deployment's 72h insights (read limits, OCC contention), root-cause each event in code, report eviden (file: r12/convex-advisor/SKILL.md)\n- convex-agent: Add an AI agent / RAG backend (@convex-dev/agent) to the Convex app. (file: r12/convex-agent/SKILL.md)\n- convex-auth: Add authentication (passkeys/OAuth) to the current Convex app, including the auth.config.ts wiring. (file: r12/convex-auth/SKILL.md)\n- convex-authz: Audit and harden Convex authorization: identity-from-arg impersonation, missing per-document ownership checks, PII-le (file: r12/convex-authz/SKILL.md)\n- convex-backup: Set up Convex backups and run a restore DRILL that proves recovery — snapshot, restore into a throwaway preview, asse (file: r12/convex-backup/SKILL.md)\n- convex-billing: Add Stripe billing/payments to the Convex app via @convex-dev/stripe (checkout + webhook + gating). (file: r12/convex-billing/SKILL.md)\n- convex-check-updates: Check the current app's pinned Convex components against recommended versions and upgrade them behind a build gate. (file: r12/convex-check-updates/SKILL.md)\n- convex-cost: Preview Convex spend — rank functions by bytes/documents-read × call-volume from insights, project each cost driver's gr (file: r12/convex-cost/SKILL.md)\n- convex-create-component: Builds reusable Convex components with isolated tables and app-facing APIs. Use for new components, reusable backend mo (file: r12/convex-create-component/SKILL.md)\n- convex-crons: Add recurring scheduled jobs (crons) to the Convex app. (file: r12/convex-crons/SKILL.md)\n- convex-deploy-guard: Classify + announce the targ