{"timestamp":"2026-10-05T19:18:43.930Z","ordinal":44565,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a10d81-0dda-70e2-b3db-7b0b62ad41b5","call_id":"call_YKUPVHATgo5gByMwZQJUr2ZV","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.2 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"part\":0,\"result\":{\"status\":\"fulfilled\",\"value\":{\"chunk_id\":\"b48885\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.00001684,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":1354,\"output\":\"desktop/gpui/README.md:55:automatic updates remain pending.\\ndesktop/gpui/README.md:73:  and line navigation. Pending Source edits lock the rich view.\\ndesktop/gpui/README.md:173:KaTeX helper's `CurrentSource` mode refuses the observed engine/CSS mismatch;\\ndesktop/gpui/README.md:175:geometry proof remain pending. Navigation and panel parity, connected\\ndesktop/gpui/README.md:295:  pending. Constructed receipts are not verified authentication.\\ndesktop/gpui/README.md:305:  are active work. Aggregate, rendered and live filing evidence remain pending.\\ndesktop/gpui/PORT_PLAN.md:14:| Requirement                                                                                           | Authoritative source                                                                                            | Completion evidence                                                                                        | Current state                                                                                                                                                                                   |\\ndesktop/gpui/PORT_PLAN.md:22:| Cast, Rubric, Marginalia, Apparatus, Tools and Versions with matching state retention                 | `board-tabs.ts`, `editorial-board-overlay.tsx`, panel components and background services                        | Working panel actions, original assets, background/unread behavior and comparison screenshots              | Local Cast, retained Rubric, Apparatus/citation placement, Versions, writer Marginalia and Tools implemented with scoped checks; full panel styling and connected behavior pending              |\\ndesktop/gpui/PORT_PLAN.md:23:| Dossier form/conversation/refinement, contextual amendments and in-flow writing behavior              | `src/components/onboarding`, `src/routes/dossier`, `src/components/in-flow`, `src/utils/flow-*`                 | Same creation/refinement and return-to-writing workflows with retained authorship/context                  | Offline form/create/refine and local Flow implemented; conversation repair/host proposal active, mounted lifecycle/filing and connected amendments/gathering pending                            |\\ndesktop/gpui/PORT_PLAN.md:24:| Account identity, settings, sync, sharing/collaboration, writer-owned publishing                      | Current auth/Convex/ATProto client contracts                                                                    | Actual authorized account, sync/conflict, shared-role and publishing flows; mocks alone are insufficient   | Account outbox/CAS/conflict and collaboration preparation exported with 26/9 library checks; mounted UI, native client registration, trusted auth transport and connected backend flows pending |\\ndesktop/gpui/PORT_PLAN.md:25:| AI providers, local LiteRT process lifecycle, editor/rubric/research requests and errors              | `desktop/litert-server.ts`, `src/utils/ai-client.ts`, background services, settings                             | Actual configured providers and local process shutdown/readiness checks                                    | Exported routing/stream/freshness foundation passes 16 corrected library checks; mounted requests, actual providers and local-model readiness/process proof pending                             |\\ndesktop/gpui/PORT_PLAN.md:26:| Narration, speech transport, Live voice desk and spoken notes/interview                               | `src/utils/speech.ts`, `src/components/ui/live-voice-desk.*`, speech transport                                  | Native audio/device and provider checks, including pause/seek/cancel/error recovery                        | Optional `native-audio` foundation passes 18 synthetic Rust checks and 6 Source-backed Bun checks / 109 assertions; mounted voice, real devices and provider transport pending                  |\\ndesktop/gpui/PORT_PLAN.md:27:| Desktop build, packaging, updates and OS integrations                                                 | Existing desktop build configuration and GPUI platform APIs                                                     | Clean builds and native runtime/file-picker/keyboard checks on target operating systems                    | Linux runtime receipts and reviewed 47-file/3-executable staging integrity retained; current-source release, relocation, installers, signing, updates and other-OS runtime pending              |\\ndesktop/gpui/PORT_PLAN.md:67:| 2    | Document foundation and independent feature modules after contracts are fixed; central `app.rs`, `main.rs`, manifests and existing web files stay coordinator-owned | Relevant feature behavior is implemented with focused checks                           |\\ndesktop/gpui/PORT_PLAN.md:100:## Current evidence\\ndesktop/gpui/PORT_PLAN.md:162:  original row text. Display-only shaping boundaries retain slash kerning\\ndesktop/gpui/PORT_PLAN.md:206:  module/type checks do not establish aggregate, rendered or live filing behavior.\\ndesktop/gpui/PORT_PLAN.md:210:  only: `CurrentSource` refuses the observed KaTeX engine/CSS mismatch, rather\\ndesktop/gpui/PORT_PLAN.md:213:  rendering, paragraph integration and actual GPU geometry remain pending in the\\ndesktop/gpui/PORT_PLAN.md:326:  metadata timestamp. An immediately submitted citation captures pending note\\ndesktop/gpui/PORT_PLAN.md:343:  original failure guards; account/provider research and previews remain pending.\\n\"}}}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"part\":1,\"result\":{\"status\":\"fulfilled\",\"value\":{\"chunk_id\":\"c3fb69\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000017148,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":15,\"output\":\"desktop/gpui/target/verification/user-preview-pointer.json\\n\"}}}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"part\":2,\"result\":{\"status\":\"fulfilled\",\"value\":{\"chunk_id\":\"fd3fff\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000014811,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":2255,\"output\":\"#!/usr/bin/env python3\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"Render Twyne in an isolated Xvfb display; never use the user's desktop.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\nimport argparse\\nimport json\\nimport os\\nfrom pathlib import Path\\nimport shutil\\nimport subprocess\\nimport tempfile\\nimport time\\n\\nparser = argparse.ArgumentParser()\\nparser.add_argument(\\\"--binary\\\", required=True)\\nparser.add_argument(\\\"--output\\\", required=True)\\nparser.add_argument(\\\"--geometry\\\", help=\\\"Write observed interface bounds from the UI-test build\\\")\\nparser.add_argument(\\\"--width\\\", type=int, default=1280)\\nparser.add_argument(\\\"--height\\\", type=int, default=860)\\nparser.add_argument(\\\"--state\\\", choices=[\\\"quiet\\\", \\\"writing\\\", \\\"slash\\\", \\\"slash-filtered\\\", \\\"slash-form\\\", \\\"desk\\\", \\\"drawer\\\", \\\"board\\\", \\\"source\\\", \\\"proof\\\", \\\"split\\\", \\\"dossier\\\", \\\"settings\\\", \\\"account\\\", \\\"account-error\\\", \\\"versions\\\", \\\"house\\\", \\\"library\\\", \\\"flow\\\", \\\"tools\\\", \\\"marginalia\\\", \\\"margin-thread\\\", \\\"margin-composer\\\", \\\"cast\\\", \\\"editors\\\", \\\"analysis\\\", \\\"rubric\\\", \\\"galley\\\", \\\"apparatus\\\", \\\"apparatus-page\\\", \\\"sentence-lab\\\", \\\"rhythm-strip\\\", \\\"claim-check\\\", \\\"reader-questions\\\"], default=\\\"quiet\\\")\\nparser.add_argument(\\\"--fixture\\\")\\nparser.add_argument(\\\"--comments\\\")\\nparser.add_argument(\\\"--comments-folio\\\")\\nparser.add_argument(\\\"--cast\\\")\\nparser.add_argument(\\\"--cast-folio\\\")\\nparser.add_argument(\\\"--rubric\\\")\\nparser.add_argument(\\\"--rubric-folio\\\")\\nparser.add_argument(\\\"--apparatus\\\")\\nparser.add_argument(\\\"--apparatus-folio\\\")\\nargs = parser.parse_args()\\nif not 320 <= args.width <= 3840 or not 360 <= args.height <= 2160:\\n    parser.error(\\\"Capture size must be 320–3840 by 360–2160 pixels.\\\")\\nif bool(args.comments) != bool(args.comments_folio):\\n    parser.error(\\\"--comments and --comments-folio must be provided together\\\")\\nif bool(args.cast) != bool(args.cast_folio):\\n    parser.error(\\\"--cast and --cast-folio must be provided together\\\")\\nif bool(args.rubric) != bool(args.rubric_folio):\\n    parser.error(\\\"--rubric and --rubric-folio must be provided together\\\")\\nif bool(args.apparatus) != bool(args.apparatus_folio):\\n    parser.error(\\\"--apparatus and --apparatus-folio must be provided together\\\")\\nfor executable in (\\\"Xvfb\\\", \\\"xwd\\\", \\\"magick\\\"):\\n    if not shutil.which(executable):\\n        parser.error(f\\\"{executable} is required; run inside the project's Devenv shell.\\\")\\n\\nwith tempfile.TemporaryDirectory(prefix=\\\"twyne-native-render-\\\") as temporary:\\n    root = Path(temporary)\\n    # Let Xvfb allocate an unused display, with no TCP listener.\\n    read_fd, write_fd = os.pipe()\\n    # GPUI's X11 backend offsets a new window by two pixels. Leave room for\\n    # the full client and capture that window, so root-screen position never\\n    # shifts the comparison or clips the application's right edge.\\n    screen = f\\\"{args.width + 4}x{args.height + 4}x24\\\"\\n    server = subprocess.Popen([\\\"Xvfb\\\", \\\"-displayfd\\\", str(write_fd), \\\"-screen\\\", \\\"0\\\", screen, \\\"-nolisten\\\", \\\"tcp\\\"], pass_fds=(write_fd,), stdout=subprocess.DEVNULL, stderr=subprocess.PIPE)\\n    os.close(write_fd)\\n    app = None\\n    try:\\n        with os.fdopen(read_fd) as display_file:\\n            number = display_file.readline().strip()\\n        if not number:\\n            raise RuntimeError(\\\"The isolated display did not start.\\\")\\n        environment = os.environ.copy()\\n        environment.pop(\\\"WAYLAND_DISPLAY\\\", None)\\n        environment[\\\"DISPLAY\\\"] = f\\\":{number}\\\"\\n        environment[\\\"GPUI_X11_SCALE_FACTOR\\\"] = \\\"1\\\"\\n        environment[\\\"XDG_RUNTIME_DIR\\\"] = str(root)\\n        if environment.get(\\\"TWYNE_GPUI_RENDER_ICD\\\"):\\n            environment[\\\"VK_DRIVER_FILES\\\"] = environment[\\\"TWYNE_GPUI_RENDER_ICD\\\"]\\n        command = [str(Path(args.binary).resolve()), \\\"--data-dir\\\", str(root / \\\"library\\\"), \\\"--capture-state\\\", args.state, \\\"--capture-size\\\", f\\\"{args.width}x{args.height}\\\"]\\n        if args.fixture:\\n            command.append(str(Path(args.fixture).resolve()))\\n        if args.comments:\\n            command.extend([\\\"--capture-comments\\\", str(Path(args.comments).resolve()), \\\"--capture-comments-folio\\\", args.comments_folio])\\n        if args.cast:\\n            command.extend([\\\"--capture-cast\\\", str(Path(args.cast).resolve()), \\\"--capture-cast-folio\\\", args.cast_folio])\\n        if args.rubric:\\n            command.extend([\\\"--capture-rubric\\\", str(Path(args.rubric).resolve()), \\\"--capture-rubric-folio\\\", args.rubric_folio])\\n        if args.apparatus:\\n            command.extend([\\\"--capture-apparatus\\\", str(Path(args.apparatus).resolve()), \\\"--capture-apparatus-folio\\\", args.apparatus_folio])\\n        if args.geometry:\\n            command.extend([\\\"--capture-geometry\\\", str(Path(args.geometry).resolve()), \\\"--capture-geometry-watch\\\"])\\n        with (root / \\\"app.log\\\").open(\\\"w\\\") as log:\\n            app = subprocess.Popen(command, env=environment, stdout=log, stderr=log)\\n            # Wait for the application to render, bounded and isolated. The\\n            # saved image is native pixels, independent of GPUI's test fonts.\\n            deadline = time.monotonic() + 20\\n            while time.monotonic() < deadline:\\n                if app.poll() is not None:\\n                    raise RuntimeError((root / \\\"app.log\\\").read_text())\\n                if args.geometry:\\n                    status = (root / \\\"app.log\\\").read_text()\\n                    if \\\"TWYNE_CAPTURE_GEOMETRY_ERROR\\\" in status:\\n                        raise RuntimeError(status)\\n                    if \\\"TWYNE_CAPTURE_GEOMETRY_READY\\\" not in status:\\n                        time.sleep(0.1)\\n                        continue\\n                    try:\\n                        if not json.loads(Path(args.geometry).read_text()).get(\\\"captureReady\\\", False):\\n                            time.sleep(0.1)\\n                            continue\\n                    except (FileNotFoundError, json.JSONDecodeError):\\n                        time.sleep(0.1)\\n                        continue\\n                if args.state in (\\\"source\\\", \\\"proof\\\", \\\"split\\\"):\\n                    status = (root / \\\"app.log\\\").read_text()\\n                    if \\\"TWYNE_CAPTURE_PROOF_ERROR\\\" in status:\\n                        raise RuntimeError(status)\\n                    if \\\"TWYNE_CAPTURE_PROOF_READY\\\" not in status:\\n                        time.sleep(0.25)\\n                        continue\\n                if args.state == \\\"library\\\" and \\\"TWYNE_CAPTURE_LIBRARY_READY\\\" not in (root / \\\"app.log\\\").read_text():\\n                    time.sleep(0.25)\\n                    continue\\n                if args.state == \\\"flow\\\":\\n                    status = (root / \\\"app.log\\\").read_text()\\n                    if \\\"TWYNE_CAPTURE_FLOW_ERROR\\\" in status:\\n                        raise RuntimeError(status)\\n                    if \\\"TWYNE_CAPTURE_FLOW_READY\\\" not in status:\\n                        time.sleep(0.25)\\n                        continue\\n                    # Original chrome fade lasts 1.2 seconds after the mode\\n                    # transition. Record its settled native pixels.\\n                    time.sleep(1.25)\\n                time.sleep(0.25)\\n                capture = subprocess.run([\\\"xwd\\\", \\\"-name\\\", \\\"Twyne\\\", \\\"-silent\\\", \\\"-out\\\", str(root / \\\"frame.xwd\\\")], env=environment, stdout=subprocess.DEVNULL, stderr=subprocess.PIPE)\\n                # Asset preparation can finish after the first poll. An absent\\n                # window is not a frame, so wait within the same deadline.\\n                if capture.returncode:\\n                    time.sleep(0.1)\\n                    continue\\n                subprocess.run([\\\"magick\\\", str(root / \\\"frame.xwd\\\"), str(root / \\\"frame.png\\\")], check=True, stdout=subprocess.DEVNULL, stderr=subprocess.DEVNULL)\\n                # GPUI clears the client surface to the paper palette. Until\\n                # its first rendered frame, that surface remains black.\\n                sample_position = f\\\"%[pixel:p{{{args.width // 2},{args.height // 2}}}]\\\"\\n                sample = subprocess.check_output([\\\"magick\\\", str(root / \\\"frame.png\\\"), \\\"-format\\\", sample_position, \\\"info:\\\"]).decode()\\n                if sample not in (\\\"srgb(0,0,0)\\\", \\\"gray(0)\\\"):\\n                    time.sleep(0.4)\\n                    subprocess.run([\\\"xwd\\\", \\\"-name\\\", \\\"Twyne\\\", \\\"-silent\\\", \\\"-out\\\", str(root / \\\"frame.xwd\\\")], env=environment, check=True, stdout=subprocess.DEVNULL, stderr=subprocess.DEVNULL)\\n                    dimensions = subprocess.check_output([\\\"magick\\\", str(root / \\\"frame.xwd\\\"), \\\"-format\\\", \\\"%wx%h\\\", \\\"info:\\\"]).decode()\\n                    if dimensions != f\\\"{args.width}x{args.height}\\\":\\n                        raise RuntimeError(f\\\"Unexpected native client size: {dimensions}\\\")\\n                    subprocess.run([\\\"magick\\\", str(root / \\\"frame.xwd\\\"), str(Path(args.output).resolve())], check=True)\\n                    print(f\\\"Native {args.state} render: {Path(args.output).resolve()}\\\")\\n                    break\\n            else:\\n                raise RuntimeError(\\\"No native frame was rendered.\\\\n\\\" + (root / \\\"app.log\\\").read_text())\\n    finally:\\n        if app is not None and app.poll() is None:\\n            app.terminate()\\n            try:\\n                app.wait(timeout=5)\\n            except subprocess.TimeoutExpired:\\n                app.kill()\\n                app.wait()\\n        server.terminate()\\n        server.wait(timeout=5)\\n\"}}}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"part\":3,\"result\":{\"status\":\"fulfilled\",\"value\":{\"chunk_id\":\"ec50ad\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000021455,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":250,\"output\":\"devenv.nix:52:  env.TWYNE_GPUI_RENDER_ICD = lib.mkIf pkgs.stdenv.isLinux\\ndesktop/gpui/src/main.rs:8:use gpui_kit::{AppContext, Bounds, TitlebarOptions, WindowBounds, WindowOptions, px, size};\\ndesktop/gpui/src/main.rs:51:                \\\"Twyne GPUI desktop.\\\\n\\\\nUsage: twyne-desktop [--data-dir PATH] [FILE.twyne.json | FILE.typ | FILE.html | FILE.md | FILE.txt | FILE.twyne ...]\\\\n\\\\nFiles are imported as copies into your library.\\\\nTWYNE_GPUI_DATA_DIR also overrides the library location.\\\"\\ndesktop/gpui/src/main.rs:512:            let bounds = Bounds::new(gpui_kit::point(px(80.), px(60.)), window_size);\\ndesktop/gpui/src/main.rs:515:                Bounds::centered(None, window_size, cx)\\ndesktop/gpui/src/main.rs:524:                window_bounds: Some(WindowBounds::Windowed(bounds)),\\ndesktop/gpui/src/storage.rs:52:        if let Some(path) = std::env::var_os(\\\"TWYNE_GPUI_DATA_DIR\\\") {\\ndesktop/gpui/src/storage.rs:53:            ensure!(!path.is_empty(), \\\"TWYNE_GPUI_DATA_DIR cannot be empty.\\\");\\n\"}}}"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a10d4c-a644-7d71-9054-bf5cd3583d03","create_time":1791227923.9308093}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
