{"timestamp":"2026-10-05T19:26:54.715Z","ordinal":44671,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a10537-909f-77a3-96d8-dd07161f91ae","turn_id":"01a10d4c-a644-7d71-9054-bf5cd3583d03","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_0acb6e766bb0227d016ac3f9f3410487d196089ce2c98e56c0","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"I’m structuring it around **feature ownership and one active-document host**. The map is in [ARCHITECTURE.md](/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne/desktop/gpui/ARCHITECTURE.md).\n\n| Area | Responsibility |\n|---|---|\n| `app/` | Room layout, navigation, focus, feature coordination |\n| `editor/` | Document model, transactions, selection, undo, native editing |\n| `insert_menu/` | Slash catalog, filtering, forms, Markdown/rich insertion |\n| Workspace/source modules | Canonical Typst, recovery, visual projection, proof |\n| Storage/revisions | Local persistence and history |\n| Account/AI packages | SDK transport, sync contracts, provider and tool integration |\n\n`app.rs` is down from roughly 7,300 to **4,380 lines** after extracting layout, coordinators, and tests. It still needs further extraction by responsibility.\n\nMy grasp is strongest around **offline editing, undo, saving, document switching, and Typst/proof**. I can trace those paths through the host and their tests. Account sync and live AI/knowledge-base integration need more runtime investigation: prepared contracts do not yet establish working connected flows.\n\nThe biggest ways to investigate faster are:\n\n- **Feature maps:** native entry point → original implementation → focused checks. This is now documented.\n- **Reproducible fixtures:** exact document, keystrokes, window size, and scale, captured in both implementations.\n- **Small delegated tasks:** bounded modules and source comparisons, with integration reviewed centrally.\n- **Event tracing:** a compact trace of focus, document switches, transactions, and saves would help diagnose interactions between features.\n\nThe current desktop UI suite passes **115 tests**, and the updated preview is open with your existing writing. Full port parity remains unfinished.\n\n"}],"phase":"final_answer","memory_citation":{"entries":[{"path":"MEMORY.md","lineStart":579,"lineEnd":580,"note":"Manuscript continuity and deliberate side panels"}],"rolloutIds":["01a0f101-b3b4-7e41-9e3c-8d3ec580aba0"]}},"started_at_ms":1791228403290,"completed_at_ms":1791228414715}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-05T19:26:54.728Z","ordinal":44672,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"message","id":"msg_0acb6e766bb0227d016ac3f9f3410487d196089ce2c98e56c0","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"output_text","text":"I’m structuring it around **feature ownership and one active-document host**. The map is in [ARCHITECTURE.md](/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne/desktop/gpui/ARCHITECTURE.md).\n\n| Area | Responsibility |\n|---|---|\n| `app/` | Room layout, navigation, focus, feature coordination |\n| `editor/` | Document model, transactions, selection, undo, native editing |\n| `insert_menu/` | Slash catalog, filtering, forms, Markdown/rich insertion |\n| Workspace/source modules | Canonical Typst, recovery, visual projection, proof |\n| Storage/revisions | Local persistence and history |\n| Account/AI packages | SDK transport, sync contracts, provider and tool integration |\n\n`app.rs` is down from roughly 7,300 to **4,380 lines** after extracting layout, coordinators, and tests. It still needs further extraction by responsibility.\n\nMy grasp is strongest around **offline editing, undo, saving, document switching, and Typst/proof**. I can trace those paths through the host and their tests. Account sync and live AI/knowledge-base integration need more runtime investigation: prepared contracts do not yet establish working connected flows.\n\nThe biggest ways to investigate faster are:\n\n- **Feature maps:** native entry point → original implementation → focused checks. This is now documented.\n- **Reproducible fixtures:** exact document, keystrokes, window size, and scale, captured in both implementations.\n- **Small delegated tasks:** bounded modules and source comparisons, with integration reviewed centrally.\n- **Event tracing:** a compact trace of focus, document switches, transactions, and saves would help diagnose interactions between features.\n\nThe current desktop UI suite passes **115 tests**, and the updated preview is open with your existing writing. Full port parity remains unfinished.\n\n<oai-mem-citation>\n<citation_entries>\nMEMORY.md:579-580|note=[Manuscript continuity and deliberate side panels]\n</citation_entries>\n<rollout_ids>\n01a0f101-b3b4-7e41-9e3c-8d3ec580aba0\n</rollout_ids>\n</oai-mem-citation>"}],"phase":"final_answer","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a10d4c-a644-7d71-9054-bf5cd3583d03","create_time":1791228371.381457,"content_item_kinds":["unknown"]}},"metadata":{"retained_source":{"id":{"message_id":"msg_0acb6e766bb0227d016ac3f9f3410487d196089ce2c98e56c0","turn_id":"01a10d4c-a644-7d71-9054-bf5cd3583d03","role":"assistant"},"revision":"retained_01a10d88-8b08-79f0-9562-b01b47e11e89","complete":true},"client_authored":false,"user_input_order":2392}}
