{"timestamp":"2026-10-05T19:27:48.827Z","ordinal":44689,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a10537-909f-77a3-96d8-dd07161f91ae","turn_id":"01a10d89-1468-7f62-b4ea-9863445ef047","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-45c3b24e-ff09-4c77-8afd-2e5b0c88f277","process_id":"63330","command":["/bin/bash","-lc","rtk proxy rg -n -C 2 'GPUI|gpui|typing-stall|flushVisual|manuscript experience' /home/diogenes/.codex/memories/MEMORY.md"],"cwd":"file:///home/diogenes/Projects/twyne","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"rtk proxy rg -n -C 2 'GPUI|gpui|typing-stall|flushVisual|manuscript experience' /home/diogenes/.codex/memories/MEMORY.md"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"58-- Restricted environments can make `devenv shell` fail on Nix cache/daemon access; when authorized, rerun with the necessary environment access rather than blaming the sizzle code. [Task 1]\n59-\n60:# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/baste Makepad versus GPUI studio-framework selection\n61-scope: Choose a Rust GUI foundation for Baste’s native studio based on whether productivity workflows or expressive cross-platform graphics are primary.\n62:applies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/baste; reuse_rule=confirm the current GPUI/GPUI Kit release and target platforms before implementation because GPUI is pre-1.0.\n63-\n64:## Task 1: Compare Makepad and GPUI for a Baste studio\n65-\n66-### rollout_summary_files\n67-\n68:- rollout_summaries/2026-10-04T04-46-42-dK0S-makepad_vs_gpui_baste_studio.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/baste, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/10/04/rollout-2026-10-04T00-46-42-01a1053c-5484-7860-b895-c654c9e25fd6.jsonl, updated_at=2026-10-04T04:47:19+00:00, thread_id=01a1053c-5484-7860-b895-c654c9e25fd6, success; direct framework comparison)\n69-\n70-### keywords\n71-\n72:- Makepad, GPUI, GPUI Kit, Rust GUI, Zed, Studio, WASM, native desktop, candidate grids, inspectors, generation queues\n73-\n74-## User preferences\n75-\n76:- when asking “makepad v gpui” -> give a direct comparative assessment and decision fit rather than starting implementation work [Task 1]\n77-\n78-## Reusable knowledge\n79-\n80:- GPUI is the Baste default for a dense native productivity studio: entities/shared state, declarative views, imperative custom elements, keyboard actions, async services, and testing support fit projects, candidate grids, inspectors, and generation queues. [Task 1]\n81-- Prefer Makepad when animated visual design, custom GPU graphics, or one UI shared across native/web/mobile is central; it is Rust-first with a live-editable/scriptable UI DSL, Studio workflow, GPU 2D/3D rendering, and broad targets. [Task 1]\n82:- GPUI Kit is separate from core GPUI; verify its exact matching version and accessibility/component capabilities instead of attributing them to GPUI itself. [Task 1]\n83-\n84-## Failures and how to do differently\n85-\n86:- GPUI is pre-1.0 with frequent breaking changes -> inspect the exact release/fork and Zed source before committing Baste architecture to an API or platform assumption. [Task 1]\n87-\n88-# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/notorganic-provider shared account knowledge connections for Keating and Twyne\n--\n192-### keywords\n193-\n194:- Tiptap, ProseMirror, Typst, typing-latency, flushVisual, mark-anchor-widgets, input-to-frame, p99, test:typing, typing-performance.yml\n195-\n196-## Task 2: Fix proof/PDF drop-cap wrapping\n--\n211-## Reusable knowledge\n212-\n213:- `src/utils/typst/session.ts` defers visual-to-Typst reconciliation and exposes `flushVisual()` for source requests/edits, remote changes, saves, proof compilation, and lifecycle boundaries. Write view must not continuously compile hidden proof; opening Source/Proof schedules it. [Task 1]\n214-- Avoid whole-document per-transaction work: `mark-anchor-widgets.ts` builds contiguous anchor runs in one pass; `twyne-editor.tsx` throttles/debounces structural and derived-content refreshes; `client.ts` shares SVG definitions while splitting proof pages. [Task 1]\n215-- Typst has no native float around an initial. `theme.ts` tokenizes rich opening inline content, measures side-column width, splits at a word boundary beside the initial, then resumes full-width prose; preserve inline styling and cover it through the real bundled compiler in `serialize.test.ts`. [Task 2]\n--\n577-## User preferences\n578-\n579:- when shaping the manuscript experience, the user wants it “all in flow,” with the side panel retained for deliberate browsing -> prioritize inline margin surfaces, quiet queues, and progressive disclosure over new panel-first workflows [Task 1]\n580-- on large Twyne features, the user explicitly prefers UI/design work first and allows backend/plumbing to be delegated to Codex -> preserve that sequencing [Task 1]\n581-\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"58-- Restricted environments can make `devenv shell` fail on Nix cache/daemon access; when authorized, rerun with the necessary environment access rather than blaming the sizzle code. [Task 1]\n59-\n60:# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/baste Makepad versus GPUI studio-framework selection\n61-scope: Choose a Rust GUI foundation for Baste’s native studio based on whether productivity workflows or expressive cross-platform graphics are primary.\n62:applies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/baste; reuse_rule=confirm the current GPUI/GPUI Kit release and target platforms before implementation because GPUI is pre-1.0.\n63-\n64:## Task 1: Compare Makepad and GPUI for a Baste studio\n65-\n66-### rollout_summary_files\n67-\n68:- rollout_summaries/2026-10-04T04-46-42-dK0S-makepad_vs_gpui_baste_studio.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/baste, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/10/04/rollout-2026-10-04T00-46-42-01a1053c-5484-7860-b895-c654c9e25fd6.jsonl, updated_at=2026-10-04T04:47:19+00:00, thread_id=01a1053c-5484-7860-b895-c654c9e25fd6, success; direct framework comparison)\n69-\n70-### keywords\