ed `ProjectBrief` records under IndexedDB metadata `brief-editions:<folioId>`. `saveProjectBriefForFolio` archives a changed previous brief then verifies the write; selection is wired through preview, card, form, conversational refinement, and editor load, and historical editions are read-only. [Task 1]\n1386:- Brief editions are distinct from `src/utils/revision-history.ts`: they are local-device saved replacements, never every unsaved keystroke. Qwik nested fields require explicit `onInput$` mutation of `store.answers[step.field!]`; the attempted `bind:value` path yielded TS2322. `EarlierEditions` provides two dated fixtures for Storybook. [Task 1][Task 2]\n1387-\n1388-## Failures and how to do differently\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":28320},"formatted_output":"181-\n182-# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/twyne editor responsiveness and Typst export parity\n183:scope: Keep the active Tiptap/Typst authoring path responsive while making proof and downloaded PDF match editor typography; use for per-keystroke work, explicit freshness boundaries, and drop-cap/export regressions.\n184-applies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne; reuse_rule=reprofile the current editor path and re-run real compiler/browser checks before quoting performance or live deployment results.\n185-\n--\n206-## User preferences\n207-\n208:- when typing lag was “unacceptable” -> prioritize measured keystroke responsiveness and production/browser evidence, not static code inspection; acceptance was “feels fairly fast now and smooth” [Task 1]\n209-- when the opening drop cap was “not word wrapping properly in the proof or the pdf generation” -> preserve visual parity between editor, proof, and downloaded PDF [Task 2]\n210-\n--\n563-### keywords\n564-\n565:- all in flow, flow-surface.tsx, flow-ribbon.tsx, manuscript-panel.tsx, twyne-editor.tsx, margin-surface.ts, MARGIN_SLOT_EVENT, OPEN_MARGIN_THREAD_EVENT, pneumatic post, galley slip, way in, 5180\n566-\n567-## Task 2: Assess at