{"timestamp":"2026-10-05T19:53:43.403Z","ordinal":45148,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a10da1-16eb-7332-8b47-4a6fa457b0a2","call_id":"call_exQTGW8TgMjhvuufRGwtuDNG","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.8 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"index\":0,\"result\":{\"status\":\"fulfilled\",\"value\":{\"goal\":{\"threadId\":\"01a10537-909f-77a3-96d8-dd07161f91ae\",\"objective\":\"port the desktop electron app to gpui. styling and assets should be used. the application should look and feel identical in both.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"tokensUsed\":56712769,\"timeUsedSeconds\":132253,\"createdAt\":1791090201,\"updatedAt\":1791230022},\"remainingTokens\":null,\"completionBudgetReport\":null}}}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"index\":1,\"result\":{\"status\":\"fulfilled\",\"value\":{\"chunk_id\":\"bef63a\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.00002832,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":1247,\"output\":\"181-\\n182-# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/twyne editor responsiveness and Typst export parity\\n183:scope: Keep the active Tiptap/Typst authoring path responsive while making proof and downloaded PDF match editor typography; use for per-keystroke work, explicit freshness boundaries, and drop-cap/export regressions.\\n184-applies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne; reuse_rule=reprofile the current editor path and re-run real compiler/browser checks before quoting performance or live deployment results.\\n185-\\n--\\n206-## User preferences\\n207-\\n208:- when typing lag was “unacceptable” -> prioritize measured keystroke responsiveness and production/browser evidence, not static code inspection; acceptance was “feels fairly fast now and smooth” [Task 1]\\n209-- when the opening drop cap was “not word wrapping properly in the proof or the pdf generation” -> preserve visual parity between editor, proof, and downloaded PDF [Task 2]\\n210-\\n--\\n563-### keywords\\n564-\\n565:- all in flow, flow-surface.tsx, flow-ribbon.tsx, manuscript-panel.tsx, twyne-editor.tsx, margin-surface.ts, MARGIN_SLOT_EVENT, OPEN_MARGIN_THREAD_EVENT, pneumatic post, galley slip, way in, 5180\\n566-\\n567-## Task 2: Assess attention-policy and House-model direction\\n--\\n577-## User preferences\\n578-\\n579:- when shaping the manuscript experience, the user wants it “all in flow,” with the side panel retained for deliberate browsing -> prioritize inline margin surfaces, quiet queues, and progressive disclosure over new panel-first workflows [Task 1]\\n580-- on large Twyne features, the user explicitly prefers UI/design work first and allows backend/plumbing to be delegated to Codex -> preserve that sequencing [Task 1]\\n581-\\n--\\n837-- when the user followed avatar work with “avif” -> use AVIF assets and correct `image/avif` references when feasible [Task 1]\\n838-- when the user said File and dossier text was “too similar” and requested a pulse -> use semantically mapped Reicon controls, concise differentiated copy, and subtle reduced-motion-safe missing-state emphasis; the later “the text is a bit redundant” means the final wording remains unresolved [Task 2]\\n839:- when the user said “the side panel is fine but i want to get everything all in flow” -> prioritize inline/margin surfaces and quiet queues, not panel-first navigation [Task 3]\\n840-- when the user said “go User interface first here, the backend you can send off to codex” -> prioritize the writer-facing UI and use bounded backend delegation rather than delaying the visible slice [Task 3]\\n841-- when the user interrupted test work with “just do the house page first” -> complete the visible writer-facing House route before expanding into planned tests [Task 3]\\n--\\n846-- Extend `src/utils/icon-system.ts` and render through `src/components/ui/icon.tsx`, not raw symbols/SVGs. Pending dossier state is `store.hydrated && store.activeFolioId && !store.brief`; `dossier-action-pending` pulses only under `prefers-reduced-motion: no-preference`, otherwise uses a steady vermilion border. [Task 2]\\n847-- Existing flow primitives are `struggle-tracker.ts`, `struggle-signals.ts`, `margin-rail.tsx`, `background-research.ts`, `user-comments.ts`, and `twyne:zen-mode`. New work is `flow-conductor.ts`, `flow-surface.tsx`, House model/store/sync, and `src/routes/house/index.tsx`; use Twyne palette tokens plus `.dept-label`, `.btn-paper`, `.btn-press`. Cover lookup sends only a Jev-selected title, never draft text. Reconcile legacy comment/persona popovers and anchor widgets with `FlowSurface`: route to the flow card when available and reserve popovers for narrow/docked/offline fallback. [Task 3]\\n848:- The v0.23.3 draft-loss fix uses explicit departure state, lifecycle flushing, a folio-scoped crash mirror, matching acknowledgements, enqueue-time timestamps, transactional recovery, and remote-restoration/native-Typst protections without per-keystroke synchronous serialization. It passed 3/3 browser regressions, 56 focused tests, 1,751 application tests, and production replay on both domains (4/4 immediate-navigation preserves, 2/2 settled-autosave controls). [Task 4]\\n849-\\n850-## Failures and how to do differently\\n--\\n1384-\\n1385-- `src/utils/brief-history.ts` keeps at most 20 superseded `ProjectBrief` records under IndexedDB metadata `brief-editions:<folioId>`. `saveProjectBriefForFolio` archives a changed previous brief then verifies the write; selection is wired through preview, card, form, conversational refinement, and editor load, and historical editions are read-only. [Task 1]\\n1386:- Brief editions are distinct from `src/utils/revision-history.ts`: they are local-device saved replacements, never every unsaved keystroke. Qwik nested fields require explicit `onInput$` mutation of `store.answers[step.field!]`; the attempted `bind:value` path yielded TS2322. `EarlierEditions` provides two dated fixtures for Storybook. [Task 1][Task 2]\\n1387-\\n1388-## Failures and how to do differently\\n\"}}}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"index\":2,\"result\":{\"status\":\"fulfilled\",\"value\":{\"chunk_id\":\"bd8e7b\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000037395,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":5,\"output\":\"?? desktop/gpui/\\n\"}}}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"index\":3,\"result\":{\"status\":\"fulfilled\",\"value\":{\"chunk_id\":\"622e43\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000037685,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":1511,\"output\":\"# Native module map\\n\\nThe original Electrobun-hosted Twyne is the behavioral and visual reference.\\nRust owns the native UI, local manuscripts, rich transactions, and Typst rendering.\\nThe Bun document helper reuses the existing source converters. The connected SDK\\nis a separate prepared boundary; its presence does not mean account sync is mounted.\\n\\n## Package boundaries and ownership\\n\\n| Package or module | Owns | Keep outside it |\\n| --- | --- | --- |\\n| `src/app.rs` | Writing-room state, startup, active document, save/navigation orchestration | New feature rendering, command catalogs, document algorithms |\\n| `src/app/room_layout.rs` | Room composition and mounting existing surfaces | Insertion algorithms, provider calls, persistence |\\n| `src/app/*_coordinator.rs` | One feature's host state, subscriptions, focus and document identity | Another feature's implementation |\\n| `src/editor/{model,transaction,command}.rs` | Structured document tree, scalar selections, transactions, history | GPUI, account state, file/network access |\\n| `src/editor/view*.rs` | Native input, layout, pagination and editor interaction | Authored Typst reconciliation, room routing |\\n| `src/insert_menu/` | Source catalog/search, query detection, insertion adapters, retained list and forms | Active manuscript ownership and saving |\\n| `workspace`, `source_session`, `semantic_bridge`, `source_editor`, `source_view` | Authored Typst, recoverable source drafts and verified visual projection | Treating cached HTML as canonical authored source |\\n| `storage`, `manuscript`, `revisions` | Local files, manuscript metadata and revision persistence | UI focus and popup state |\\n| `native_accounts/`, `tools/connected/` | Native account contracts and Bun SDK transport/session boundary | Implicit attachment of guest writing to an account |\\n| `theme`, `assets`, `chrome` | Shared original colors, fonts, artwork and controls | Feature-specific document behavior |\\n\\n`app.rs` is still larger than intended. Move coherent responsibilities into sibling\\nmodules as they are worked on, keeping the host entry points small. Do not split a\\nfile solely to meet a line count or add a second owner of document state.\\n\\n## Investigate a feature\\n\\n| Native entry point | Original reference | Focused verification |\\n| --- | --- | --- |\\n| `app/manuscript_coordinator.rs` | `components/editor/manuscript-panel.tsx`, `global.css` | `app/manuscript_tests.rs` |\\n| `app/slash_coordinator.rs`, `insert_menu/` | `components/editor/extensions/slash-command.ts`, `slash-command-menu.tsx`, `utils/editor-commands.ts`, `utils/slash-command-filter.ts` | `insert_menu/tests.rs`, `app/slash_tests.rs`, `fixtures/insert-menu/` |\\n| `editor/view_insert.rs` | `components/editor/twyne-editor.tsx` registry dispatch | Pure rich transaction tests and mounted slash tests |\\n| `compositor.rs` | `components/editor/compositor-panel.tsx`, `utils/compositor-toolbar.ts` | `fixtures/chrome/`, `fixtures/editor/` |\\n| `app/account_coordinator.rs` | `components/auth/{account-menu,auth-panel}.tsx` | `app/tests.rs`, `fixtures/connected-work/` |\\n| `source_view.rs`, `source_editor.rs` | `components/editor/typst-code-editor.ts` | `fixtures/source_view/` |\\n| `gen_ui/`, `app/gen_ui_coordinator.rs` | Writing-tool cards and tool contracts | `fixtures/gen-ui/` |\\n\\nOriginal paths in this table are relative to the repository's `src/` directory.\\nStart with the feature's coordinator, then its package and original counterpart:\\n\\n```bash\\nrtk proxy rg -n 'insert_from_slash|refresh_insert_menu' desktop/gpui/src\\nrtk proxy rg -n 'insert.table|runRegistryCommand' src/components/editor/twyne-editor.tsx\\n```\\n\\n## Editor contracts\\n\\n- Plain-text input offsets are **UTF-8 bytes**. Rich document offsets are\\n  **Unicode scalars**. Source ProseMirror offsets are **UTF-16 positions**.\\n  Convert at the adapter boundary, never guess from string length.\\n- Detect a slash from the current line/text block before the collapsed caret.\\n  Opening or dismissing the menu does not modify the document.\\n- Activation binds the manuscript, selection/query and revision. A form must\\n  validate that binding again before committing.\\n- Remove the query and insert its element as one history transaction. Failed\\n  or cancelled insertion preserves the authored query. IME confirmation belongs\\n  to the composing input.\\n- Feature surfaces emit intent; the active-document host accepts it. Each surface\\n  has an explicit owner and clears its pending work on document departure.\\n- Keep keystroke work local. Whole-document conversion and serialization happen\\n  at explicit freshness boundaries, not as a side effect of showing a menu.\\n\\n## Fast checks and evidence\\n\\nOne owner runs Cargo commands to avoid competing for the build lock. Other agents\\ncan work on independent pure modules, fixtures, or original behavior in parallel.\\nGive weaker external agents bounded inputs and inspect their output before adoption.\\n\\n```bash\\nrtk proxy devenv shell -- rtk proxy cargo test --locked --offline --no-default-features --lib --manifest-path desktop/gpui/Cargo.toml insert_menu\\nrtk proxy devenv shell -- rtk proxy cargo test --locked --offline --features ui-tests --bin twyne-desktop --manifest-path desktop/gpui/Cargo.toml slash_\\nrtk proxy devenv shell -- rtk proxy cargo test --locked --offline --features ui-tests --bin twyne-desktop --manifest-path desktop/gpui/Cargo.toml manuscript_title_\\n```\\n\\nMounted tests exercise controls and history using GPUI's test text system. Check\\nfonts, clipping and actual pixels separately with `tools/capture-native.py`, an\\nimmutable binary, a known fixture, window size and scale, and an isolated library.\\nRecord the binary and source hashes with that observation. Do not use the user's\\nopen writing session as a test fixture.\\n\\nBuilds, pure tests, mounted controls, native GPU captures, browser comparisons,\\nreal account/provider use, and distribution/device checks are separate evidence.\\nCurrent feature status belongs in `PORT_PLAN.md`; do not infer readiness from\\nthe existence of a module or a prepared contract.\\n\"}}}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"index\":4,\"result\":{\"status\":\"fulfilled\",\"value\":{\"chunk_id\":\"1d0b17\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.00002826,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":567,\"output\":\"pub enum TableCommand {\\n    AddRowBefore,\\n    AddRowAfter,\\n    DeleteRow,\\n    AddColumnBefore,\\n    AddColumnAfter,\\n    DeleteColumn,\\n    DeleteTable,\\n    MergeCells { from: NodePath, to: NodePath },\\n    SplitCell,\\n    ToggleHeaderRow,\\n}\\n\\n#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq)]\\npub enum Command {\\n    InsertText(String),\\n    ReplaceSelection(String),\\n    PasteFragment(super::RichFragment),\\n    DeleteBackward,\\n    DeleteForward,\\n    SplitBlock,\\n    ToggleMark(Mark),\\n    SetMark(Mark),\\n    UnsetMark(MarkKind),\\n    AddComment(super::CommentAttributes),\\n    RemoveComment {\\n        id: String,\\n    },\\n    ClearFormatting,\\n    Recase(TextCase),\\n    SetParagraph,\\n    SetHeading(u8),\\n    SetAlignment(Alignment),\\n    SetParagraphFormat(ParagraphFormat),\\n    Indent,\\n    Outdent,\\n    ToggleList(ListKind),\\n    ToggleBlockQuote,\\n    ToggleCodeBlock,\\n    InsertInline(InlineObject),\\n    InsertBlock(BlockObject),\\n    SetAttributes {\\n        path: NodePath,\\n        attributes: Vec<(String, Option<String>)>,\\n    },\\n    DeleteNode {\\n        path: NodePath,\\n    },\\n    /// Commit raw LaTeX to the same current math atom. Rendering/preview never\\n    /// changes this payload, and an old descriptor cannot edit a replacement.\\n    UpdateMathSource {\\n        path: NodePath,\\n        expected: Node,\\n        source: String,\\n    },\\n    /// Patch the actual note atom, refusing an old descriptor rather than\\n    /// editing whichever node later occupies the same path.\\n    UpdateNote {\\n        path: NodePath,\\n        expected: Node,\\n        text: Option<String>,\\n        kind: Option<NoteKind>,\\n    },\\n    DeleteNote {\\n        path: NodePath,\\n        expected: Node,\\n    },\\n    MoveSection {\\n        source: NodePath,\\n        target: NodePath,\\n        placement: super::DropPlacement,\\n    },\\n    MoveBlocks {\\n        parent: NodePath,\\n        source: std::ops::Range<usize>,\\n        insert_at: usize,\\n    },\\n    Table {\\n        cell: NodePath,\\n        command: TableCommand,\\n    },\\n    Undo,\\n    Redo,\\n}\\n\\n#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, PartialEq, Eq)]\\npub enum TextCase {\\n    Upper,\\n    Lower,\\n    Title,\\n    Sentence,\\n}\\n\\nimpl Command {\\n    /// Parameterless intents share the web command catalogue's stable IDs.\\n    /// Commands requiring a dialog/value use the explicit typed variants.\\n\"}}}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"index\":5,\"result\":{\"status\":\"fulfilled\",\"value\":{\"chunk_id\":\"e5b628\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000025776,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":677,\"output\":\"//! Registry keyboard bindings for the structural commands shown in slash hints.\\nuse super::*;\\nuse crate::editor::{BlockObject, ListKind};\\nuse gpui_kit::InteractiveElement;\\n\\ngpui_kit::actions!(twyne_editor_commands, [HeadingOne, HeadingTwo, HeadingThree, BulletList, NumberedList, PullQuote, CodeBlock, PageBreak]);\\n\\npub(super) fn init(cx: &mut App) {\\n    #[cfg(target_os = \\\"macos\\\")]\\n    let primary = \\\"cmd\\\";\\n    #[cfg(not(target_os = \\\"macos\\\"))]\\n    let primary = \\\"ctrl\\\";\\n    macro_rules! bind {\\n        ($id:literal, $action:ident) => {\\n            if let Some(chord) = crate::insert_menu::commands().iter().find(|command| command.id == $id).and_then(|command| command.keybinding.as_ref()) {\\n                let chord = chord.replace(\\\"Mod\\\", primary).to_ascii_lowercase();\\n                cx.bind_keys([KeyBinding::new(&chord, $action, Some(EDITOR_KEY_CONTEXT))]);\\n            }\\n        };\\n    }\\n    bind!(\\\"paragraph.heading-1\\\", HeadingOne);\\n    bind!(\\\"paragraph.heading-2\\\", HeadingTwo);\\n    bind!(\\\"paragraph.heading-3\\\", HeadingThree);\\n    bind!(\\\"paragraph.bullet-list\\\", BulletList);\\n    bind!(\\\"paragraph.numbered-list\\\", NumberedList);\\n    bind!(\\\"paragraph.blockquote\\\", PullQuote);\\n    bind!(\\\"paragraph.code-block\\\", CodeBlock);\\n    bind!(\\\"insert.page-break\\\", PageBreak);\\n}\\n\\nimpl RichEditorView {\\n    pub(super) fn shortcut_handlers<E: InteractiveElement>(&self, element: E, cx: &mut Context<Self>) -> E {\\n        element\\n            .on_action(cx.listener(|this, _: &HeadingOne, window, cx| this.run_shortcut(Command::SetHeading(1), window, cx)))\\n            .on_action(cx.listener(|this, _: &HeadingTwo, window, cx| this.run_shortcut(Command::SetHeading(2), window, cx)))\\n            .on_action(cx.listener(|this, _: &HeadingThree, window, cx| this.run_shortcut(Command::SetHeading(3), window, cx)))\\n            .on_action(cx.listener(|this, _: &BulletList, window, cx| this.run_shortcut(Command::ToggleList(ListKind::Bullet), window, cx)))\\n            .on_action(cx.listener(|this, _: &NumberedList, window, cx| this.run_shortcut(Command::ToggleList(ListKind::Ordered), window, cx)))\\n            .on_action(cx.listener(|this, _: &PullQuote, window, cx| this.run_shortcut(Command::ToggleBlockQuote, window, cx)))\\n            .on_action(cx.listener(|this, _: &CodeBlock, window, cx| this.run_shortcut(Command::ToggleCodeBlock, window, cx)))\\n            .on_action(cx.listener(|this, _: &PageBreak, window, cx| this.run_shortcut(Command::InsertBlock(BlockObject::PageBreak), window, cx)))\\n    }\\n    fn run_shortcut(&mut self, command: Command, window: &mut Window, cx: &mut Context<Self>) {\\n        if self.is_composing() { cx.propagate(); return; }\\n        let _ = self.execute(command, window, cx);\\n    }\\n}\\n\"}}}"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a10d89-1468-7f62-b4ea-9863445ef047","create_time":1791230023.4036853}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
