{"timestamp":"2026-10-05T19:54:04.939Z","ordinal":45176,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a10537-909f-77a3-96d8-dd07161f91ae","turn_id":"01a10d89-1468-7f62-b4ea-9863445ef047","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_0e6e2e948f59cffe016ac4005b73bc87d182bf7167ba652daa","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"My strongest grasp is of offline editing: document ownership, title/body layout, slash commands, Unicode positions, undo, and saving. Connected sync and AI are less complete—the contracts exist, but native end-to-end use still needs proof.\n\nThe biggest investigation speedup has been pairing each native feature with its original implementation, a focused test, and a reproducible screenshot fixture. That has already exposed differences a successful build would miss, including table insertion and cancellation behavior.\n"}],"phase":"commentary"},"started_at_ms":1791230043484,"completed_at_ms":1791230044938}}
