{"timestamp":"2026-10-05T19:56:05.428Z","ordinal":45309,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a10537-909f-77a3-96d8-dd07161f91ae","turn_id":"01a10d89-1468-7f62-b4ea-9863445ef047","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-8a876979-26c4-4a33-8523-cbcda6326ed5","process_id":"97720","command":["/bin/bash","-lc","rtk proxy rg -n 'slash-table|slash-insert-form|slash-command-menu|captureReady|slash-form' desktop/gpui/src/capture_geometry.rs"],"cwd":"file:///home/diogenes/Projects/twyne","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"rtk proxy rg -n 'slash-table|slash-insert-form|slash-command-menu|captureReady|slash-form' desktop/gpui/src/capture_geometry.rs"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"86:        \"captureReady\": room.upgrade().is_some_and(|room| room.read(cx).capture_apparatus_ready(cx)),\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"86:        \"captureReady\": room.upgrade().is_some_and(|room| room.read(cx).capture_apparatus_ready(cx)),\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":20095},"formatted_output":"86:        \"captureReady\": room.upgrade().is_some_and(|room| room.read(cx).capture_apparatus_ready(cx)),\n"},"started_at_ms":1791230165428,"completed_at_ms":1791230165428}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-05T19:56:05.467Z","ordinal":45310,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a10537-909f-77a3-96d8-dd07161f91ae","turn_id":"01a10d89-1468-7f62-b4ea-9863445ef047","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-2a9a1e4a-5cd4-465b-9938-f9c19351f5fd","process_id":"50523","command":["/bin/bash","-lc","rtk proxy sed -n '1,160p' desktop/gpui/README.md"],"cwd":"file:///home/diogenes/Projects/twyne","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"rtk proxy sed -n '1,160p' desktop/gpui/README.md"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"# Twyne GPUI\n\nTwyne's native desktop port uses Rust and [GPUI Kit 0.7](https://gpui-kit.com/).\nThe goal is the full hosted desktop experience with identical styling, original\nassets and behavior. The working offline slice includes the rich editor, Dossier,\nlocal editorial panels and native Typst proof/PDF.\n\nThe full Electrobun application remains the reference. The port is unfinished;\n[PORT_PLAN.md](PORT_PLAN.md) separates implemented behavior, retained checks,\nunmounted foundations and remaining work.\n\n[ARCHITECTURE.md](ARCHITECTURE.md) maps native packages to their original web\ncounterparts, records ownership boundaries, and gives focused investigation checks.\n\n## Run\n\nUse Bun, the repository's Rust toolchain, and the native libraries in\n[GPUI Kit's installation guide](https://gpui-kit.com/docs/installation/).\nThe repository's Devenv shell provides the Rust toolchain and Linux libraries.\n\nFrom the repository root:\n\n```bash\nrtk proxy bun install --frozen-lockfile\nrtk proxy devenv shell -- rtk proxy bun run desktop.gpui\n```\n\nUse an isolated library or import files on startup:\n\n```bash\nrtk proxy devenv shell -- rtk proxy bun run desktop.gpui --data-dir /tmp/twyne-native-library /path/to/draft.typ\n```\n\nImports create library copies. Original files remain independent.\n\nThe developer build creates `twyne-document` from Twyne's existing TypeScript\ndocument converters. Its compiled executable includes the Bun runtime. Offline\nwriting needs no web server or account; GPUI renders the interface and the native\nRust Typst engine renders proof/PDF. The helper handles source/HTML reconciliation,\nstarter generation and the original MathJax export conversion.\n\nThe helper build also creates `twyne-math-write`. It is a diagnostic executable,\nnot the main editor's math renderer or evidence of Write-view parity.\n\nFor direct Cargo development, build the helper first:\n\n```bash\nrtk proxy bun run desktop.gpui.build-helper\nrtk proxy devenv shell -- rtk proxy cargo run --locked --manifest-path desktop/gpui/Cargo.toml\n```\n\nLinux requires X11 or Wayland and a graphics driver supported by WGPU. Native\nfile pickers use the desktop's XDG portal. macOS requires Xcode command line\ntools; Windows requires the MSVC C++ toolchain. Bundles, installers, signing, and\nautomatic updates remain pending.\n\n## Writing and proof\n\n- **Write:** native rich text with Unicode input, selection, clipboard, IME,\n  formatting, and undo/redo. Typing bursts form one undo group. Imported cached\n  HTML is projected from canonical source before editing. Footnote and endnote\n  markers open an editable note; collected notes navigate back to their\n  manuscript references. Save and navigation capture unblurred note input.\n- **Equation source:** activate an inline or block equation to edit its retained native textarea. Render equation submits through the actual canonical converter and preserves independent manuscript undo; Cancel keeps the saved source. Inline editing uses a measured child inside the original atom. Preview currently reports unavailable. Actual OS input and original-browser baseline/pixel parity remain separate gates.\n- **Dossier:** the original ten sections, imported material, references, local\n  probes, create/refine filing, and scoped recovery. Filing opens Write after\n  the document is actually saved.\n- **Source:** canonical Typst with a separate recoverable draft. Apply requires\n  a successful current compile and verified projection. Discard preserves the\n  manuscript. Source edits update the real proof after 450 ms of quiet. The\n  native code editor provides Typst highlighting, line numbers,\n  folded generated helpers, search/replace, source snippets, comments, wrapping,\n  and line navigation. Pending Source edits lock the rich view.\n- **Proof/Split:** the same pinned Typst fork and ordered fonts as the web\n  renderer, original artwork, real SVG pages, zoom, page navigation, and PDF\n  export. Failed compilation retains the last valid proof.\n  The footer retains the selected page across Write/Proof transitions. Its\n  count option leaves the current mode active; page choices reveal the page's\n  top, and a shorter valid proof falls back to the count option.\n  Closed Arrow/Home/End and PageUp/PageDown keys retain native focus. The\n  combobox exposes its selected label and actual popup open state.\n  Typed page labels retain focus; repeated letters cycle matching labels and\n  search expires after the original one-second pause. Space continues an\n  active prefix or opens the popup when search is idle.\n- **Compositor:** Home, Insert, Review, and View controls act on the native\n  document. Arrow keys change tabs and retain native focus through wrapping;\n  Undo/Redo use the actual manuscript history and respect read-only mode.\n  Page settings and header/footer text are saved with the folio.\n  The page ruler changes the actual margins through drag or keyboard input.\n  Optional native pagination has physical-page and input checks; the current\n  web editor route does not register its existing pagination engine, so this\n  does not establish matching active-route behavior.\n  Local PNG/JPEG/GIF/WebP files become portable offline images; choosing a file\n  retains the original bytes and one undo restores the preceding manuscript.\n  File insertion checks the original converter in the background first: a\n  valid image that exceeds the 5 MB Typst editing limit leaves the draft intact.\n  Connected actions stay disabled until their native adapters exist.\n- **Appearance:** original presets and colour overrides preview immediately\n  and persist separately from manuscript formatting. Save failures retain the\n  preview and expose a retry; the stored System choice follows OS appearance.\n- **Versions:** local checkpoints and passage comparisons in the Editorial\n  Board. Restore saves the current manuscript first and refuses to replace\n  typing or Source edits made while a restore is being prepared. Saved status\n  follows the actual durable write.\n- **Cast:** the Room of Editors, local roster and assistance settings, retained\n  editorial notes/replies, and saved Full Analysis use the original profiles\n  and assets. The Board, roster page and analysis page share one retained room.\n  Local writer replies can be filed without contacting a provider. Unfinished\n  replies and roster forms survive navigation and closing; failed writes hold\n  the exact request and block departure until retry. Existing analyses can be\n  copied or downloaded. Provider notes, proposed edits, new analyses, spoken\n  notes and persona-mark navigation remain unavailable.\n- **Rubric:** local weights, custom criteria and retained grades share the\n  Board and Galley. Changes follow the actual durable write, and a failed save\n  keeps its candidate for retry. New provider grading remains unavailable.\n- **Apparatus:** saved sources share the Board and full page. Local scans use\n  the original citation rules; Copy publishes only the active folio's sources.\n  Cite inserts an undoable footnote and saves the manuscript before confirming\n  its source timestamp. Failed metadata writes retain a retry without repeating\n  that insertion. Offline steering retains its draft and original provider\n  error; connected research and source previews remain unavailable.\n- **Marginalia:** anchored writer notes, replies, resolve/reopen, passage\n  navigation, and erase use the actual manuscript marks and local note store.\n  The inline thread and Board share one reply draft. Unblurred replies survive\n  folio visits and closing; failed writes keep the exact request for retry and\n  block departure. Placing a note saves its manuscript mark before filing its\n  metadata. Deleting a marked passage reconciles only that folio after the\n  manuscript save. Writer previews use the original Flow policy and measured\n  passage geometry. Setting one aside is transient; reopening recalls its\n  shared thread. An admitted rail thread follows width changes while retaining\n  its reply and reserving the full measured card height.\n  Connected editor replies, speech, and recorded audio remain\n  unavailable until their native adapters exist.\n- **House and Library:** offline House, collection, and folio context with\n  original fields, inherited context, filing, and a shared context ledger.\n  Library cards use the original preview/count rules; source-only imports stay\n  visible while their writing projection is unavailable. Context changes are\n  published only after their actual durable write.\n- **Flow:** focused writing drives the original local rhythm classifier and\n  spool ribbon. Automatic focus fades desk chrome while keeping the page in\n  place; hovering, keyboard focus, or Escape restores the controls. Writing\n  tools opens from the Drawer or Board and saves the automatic-focus setting\n  and a separate local rhythm profile.\n  Review, live margin tools, cover lookup, and contextual amendments need their\n  connected adapters.\n- **Save:** autosave follows 700 ms of quiet. Explicit Save, switches, mode\n  transitions, and closing capture controls immediately. Serialization and\n  conversion stay off the per-keystroke path.\n\nZen and compositor choices persist locally. Drawer, Board and its selected\npanel remain part of the current desk visit.\nArchive/restore preserves documents; archived text is read-only. Find selects\nliteral matches in the active editor.\n\nRich copy/paste preserves formatting and Twyne object metadata. Linux X11\nexchanges HTML and UTF-8 text with other applications, and preserves the full\nmetadata between native instances. Actual native Paste/Copy/Undo/Redo checks\nalso cover clipboard ownership, focus, selection and editor changes during a\nbackground import, verified multi-megabyte incremental transfers, and the\noriginal 5 MB canonical-source limit before insertion. RTF-only input and\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"# Twyne GPUI\n\nTwyne's native desktop port uses Rust and [GPUI Kit 0.7](https://gpui-kit.com/).\nThe goal is the full hosted desktop experience with identical styling, original\nassets and behavior. The working offline slice includes the rich editor, Dossier,\nlocal editorial panels and native Typst proof/PDF.\n\nThe full Electrobun application remains the reference. The port is unfinished;\n[PORT_PLAN.md](PORT_PLAN.md) separates implemented behavior, retained checks,\nunmounted foundations and remaining work.\n\n[ARCHITECTURE.md](ARCHITECTURE.md) maps native packages to their original web\ncounterparts, records ownership boundaries, and gives focused investigation checks.\n\n## Run\n\nUse Bun, the repository's Rust toolchain, and the native libraries in\n[GPUI Kit's installation guide](https://gpui-kit.com/docs/installation/).\nThe repository's Devenv shell provides the Rust toolchain and Linux libraries.\n\nFrom the repository root:\n\n```bash\nrtk proxy bun install --frozen-lockfile\nrtk proxy devenv shell -- rtk proxy bun run desktop.gpui\n```\n\nUse an isolated library or import files on startup:\n\n```bash\nrtk proxy devenv shell -- rtk proxy bun run desktop.gpui --data-dir /tmp/twyne-native-library /path/to/draft.typ\n```\n\nImports create library copies. Original files remain independent.\n\nThe developer build creates `twyne-document` from Twyne's existing TypeScript\ndocument converters. Its compiled executable includes the Bun runtime. Offline\nwriting needs no web server or account; GPUI renders the interface and the native\nRust Typst engine renders proof/PDF. The helper handles source/HTML reconciliation,\nstarter generation and the original MathJax export conversion.\n\nThe helper build also creates `twyne-math-write`. It is a diagnostic executable,\nnot the main editor's math renderer or evidence of Write-view parity.\n\nFor direct Cargo development, build the helper first:\n\n```bash\nrtk proxy bun run desktop.gpui.build-helper\nrtk proxy devenv shell -- rtk proxy cargo run --locked --manifest-path desktop/gpui/Cargo.toml\n```\n\nLinux requires X11 or Wayland and a graphics driver supported by WGPU. Native\nfile pickers use the desktop's XDG portal. macOS requires Xcode command line\ntools; Windows requires the MSVC C++ toolchain. Bundles, installers, signing, and\nautomatic updates remain pending.\n\n## Writing and proof\n\n- **Write:** native rich text with Unicode input, selection, clipboard, IME,\n  formatting, and undo/redo. Typing bursts form one undo group. Imported cached\n  HTML is projected from canonical source before editing. Footnote and endnote\n  markers open an editable note; collected notes navigate back to their\n  manuscript references. Save and navigation capture unblurred note input.\n- **Equation source:** activate an inline or block equation to edit its retained native textarea. Render equation submits through the actual canonical converter and preserves independent manuscript undo; Cancel keeps the saved source. Inline editing uses a measured child inside the original atom. Preview currently reports unavailable. Actual OS input and original-browser baseline/pixel parity remain separate gates.\n- **Dossier:** the original ten sections, imported material, references, local\n  probes, create/refine filing, and scoped recovery. Filing opens Write after\n  the document is actually saved.\n- **Source:** canonical Typst with a separate recoverable draft. Apply requires\n  a successful current compile and verified projection. Discard preserves the\n  manuscript. Source edits update the real proof after 450 ms of quiet. The\n  native code editor provides Typst highlighting, line numbers,\n  folded generated helpers, search/replace, source snippets, comments, wrapping,\n  and line navigation. Pending Source edits lock the rich view.\n- **Proof/Split:** the same pinned Typst fork and ordered fonts as the web\n  renderer, original artwork, real SVG pages, zoom, page navigation, and PDF\n  export. Failed compilation retains the last valid proof.\n  The footer retains the selected page across Write/Proof transitions. Its\n  count option leaves the current mode active; page choices reveal the page's\n  top, and a shorter valid proof falls back to the count option.\n  Closed Arrow/Home/End and PageUp/PageDown keys retain native focus. The\n  combobox exposes its selected label and actual popup open state.\n  Typed page labels retain focus; repeated letters cycle matching labels and\n  search expires after the original one-second pause. Space continues an\n  active prefix or opens the popup when search is idle.\n- **Compositor:** Home, Insert, Review, and View controls act on the native\n  document. Arrow keys change tabs and retain native focus through wrapping;\n  Undo/Redo use the actual manuscript history and respect read-only mode.\n  Page settings and header/footer text are saved with the folio.\n  The page ruler changes the actual margins through drag or keyboard input.\n  Optional native pagination has physical-page and input checks; the current\n  web editor route does not register its existing pagination engine, so this\n  does not establish matching active-route behavior.\n  Local PNG/JPEG/GIF/WebP files become portable offline images; choosing a file\n  retains the original bytes and one undo restores the preceding manuscript.\n  File insertion checks the original converter in the background first: a\n  valid image that exceeds the 5 MB Typst editing limit leaves the draft intact.\n  Connected actions stay disabled until their native adapters exist.\n- **Appearance:** original presets and colour overrides preview immediately\n  and persist separately from manuscript formatting. Save failures retain the\n  preview and expose a retry; the stored System choice follows OS appearance.\n- **Versions:** local checkpoints and passage comparisons in the Editorial\n  Board. Restore saves the current manuscript first and refuses to replace\n  typing or Source edits made while a restore is being prepared. Saved status\n  follows the actual durable write.\n- **Cast:** the Room of Editors, local roster and assistance settings, retained\n  editorial notes/replies, and saved Full Analysis use the original profiles\n  and assets. The Board, roster page and analysis page share one retained room.\n  Local writer replies can be filed without contacting a provider. Unfinished\n  replies and roster forms survive navigation and closing; failed writes hold\n  the exact request and block departure until retry. Existing analyses can be\n  copied or downloaded. Provider notes, proposed edits, new analyses, spoken\n  notes and persona-mark navigation remain unavailable.\n- **Rubric:** local weights, custom criteria and retained grades share the\n  Board and Galley. Changes follow the actual durable write, and a failed save\n  keeps its candidate for retry. New provider grading remains unavailable.\n- **Apparatus:** saved sources share the Board and full page. Local scans use\n  the original citation rules; Copy publishes only the active folio's sources.\n  Cite inserts an undoable footnote and saves the manuscript before confirming\n  its source timestamp. Failed metadata writes retain a retry without repeating\n  that insertion. Offline steering retains its draft and original provider\n  error; connected research and source previews remain unavailable.\n- **Marginalia:** anchored writer notes, replies, resolve/reopen, passage\n  navigation, and erase use the actual manuscript marks and local note store.\n  The inline thread and Board share one reply draft. Unblurred replies survive\n  folio visits and closing; failed writes keep the exact request for retry and\n  block departure. Placing a note saves its manuscript mark before filing its\n  metadata. Deleting a marked passage reconciles only that folio after the\n  manuscript save. Writer previews use the original Flow policy and measured\n  passage geometry. Setting one aside is transient; reopening recalls its\n  shared thread. An admitted rail thread follows width changes while retaining\n  its reply and reserving the full measured card height.\n  Connected editor replies, speech, and recorded audio remain\n  unavailable until their native adapters exist.\n- **House and Library:** offline House, collection, and folio context with\n  original fields, inherited context, filing, and a shared context ledger.\n  Library cards use the original preview/count rules; source-only imports stay\n  visible while their writing projection is unavailable. Context changes are\n  published only after their actual durable write.\n- **Flow:** focused writing drives the original local rhythm classifier and\n  spool ribbon. Automatic focus fades desk chrome while keeping the page in\n  place; hovering, keyboard focus, or Escape restores the controls. Writing\n  tools opens from the Drawer or Board and saves the automatic-focus setting\n  and a separate local rhythm profile.\n  Review, live margin tools, cover lookup, and contextual amendments need their\n  connected adapters.\n- **Save:** autosave follows 700 ms of quiet. Explicit Save, switches, mode\n  transitions, and closing capture controls immediately. Serialization and\n  conversion stay off the per-keystroke path.\n\nZen and compositor choices persist locally. Drawer, Board and its selected\npanel remain part of the current desk visit.\nArchive/restore preserves documents; archived text is read-only. Find selects\nliteral matches in the active editor.\n\nRich copy/paste preserves formatting and Twyne object metadata. Linux X11\nexchanges HTML and UTF-8 text with other applications, and preserves the full\nmetadata between native instances. Actual native Paste/Copy/Undo/Redo checks\nalso cover clipboard ownership, focus, selection and editor changes during a\nbackground import, verified multi-megabyte incremental transfers, and the\noriginal 5 MB canonical-source limit before insertion. RTF-only input and\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":22566},"formatted_output":"# Twyne GPUI\n\nTwyne's native desktop port uses Rust and [GPUI Kit 0.7](https://gpui-kit.com/).\nThe goal is the full hosted desktop experience with identical styling, original\nassets and behavior. The working offline slice includes the rich editor, Dossier,\nlocal editorial panels and native Typst proof/PDF.\n\nThe full Electrobun application remains the reference. The port is unfinished;\n[PORT_PLAN.md](PORT_PLAN.md) separates implemented behavior, retained checks,\nunmounted foundations and remaining work.\n\n[ARCHITECTURE.md](ARCHITECTURE.md) maps native packages to their original web\ncounterparts, records ownership boundaries, and gives focused investigation checks.\n\n## Run\n\nUse Bun, the repository's Rust toolchain, and the native libraries in\n[GPUI Kit's installation guide](https://gpui-kit.com/docs/installation/).\nThe repository's Devenv shell provides the Rust toolchain and Linux libraries.\n\nFrom the repository root:\n\n```bash\nrtk proxy bun install --frozen-lockfile\nrtk proxy devenv shell -- rtk proxy bun run desktop.gpui\n```\n\nUse an isolated library or import files on startup:\n\n```bash\nrtk proxy devenv shell -- rtk proxy bun run desktop.gpui --data-dir /tmp/twyne-native-library /path/to/draft.typ\n```\n\nImports create library copies. Original files remain independent.\n\nThe developer build creates `twyne-document` from Twyne's existing TypeScript\ndocument converters. Its compiled executable includes the Bun runtime. Offline\nwriting needs no web server or account; GPUI renders the interface and the native\nRust Typst engine renders proof/PDF. The helper handles source/HTML reconciliation,\nstarter generation and the original MathJax export conversion.\n\nThe helper build also creates `twyne-math-write`. It is a diagnostic executable,\nnot the main editor's math renderer or evidence of Write-view parity.\n\nFor direct Cargo development, build the helper first:\n\n```bash\nrtk proxy bun run desktop.gpui.build-helper\nrtk proxy devenv shell -- rtk proxy cargo run --locked --manifest-path desktop/gpui/Cargo.toml\n```\n\nLinux requires X11 or Wayland and a graphics driver supported by WGPU. Native\nfile pickers use the desktop's XDG portal. macOS requires Xcode command line\ntools; Windows requires the MSVC C++ toolchain. Bundles, installers, signing, and\nautomatic updates remain pending.\n\n## Writing and proof\n\n- **Write:** native rich text with Unicode input, selection, clipboard, IME,\n  formatting, and undo/redo. Typing bursts form one undo group. Imported cached\n  HTML is projected from canonical source before editing. Footnote and endnote\n  markers open an editable note; collected notes navigate back to their\n  manuscript references. Save and navigation capture unblurred note input.\n- **Equation source:** activate an inline or block equation to edit its retained native textarea. Render equation submits through the actual canonical converter and preserves independent manuscript undo; Cancel keeps the saved source. Inline editing uses a measured child inside the original atom. Preview currently reports unavailable. Actual OS input and original-browser baseline/pixel parity remain separate gates.\n- **Dossier:** the original ten sections, imported material, references, local\n  probes, create/refine filing, and scoped recovery. Filing opens Write after\n  the document is actually saved.\n- **Source:** canonical Typst with a separate recoverable draft. Apply requires\n  a successful current compile and verified projection. Discard preserves the\n  manuscript. Source edits update the real proof after 450 ms of quiet. The\n  native code editor provides Typst highlighting, line numbers,\n  folded generated helpers, search/replace, source snippets, comments, wrapping,\n  and line navigation. Pending Source edits lock the rich view.\n- **Proof/Split:** the same pinned Typst fork and ordered fonts as the web\n  renderer, original artwork, real SVG pages, zoom, page navigation, and PDF\n  export. Failed compilation retains the last valid proof.\n  The footer retains the selected page across Write/Proof transitions. Its\n  count option leaves the current mode active; page choices reveal the page's\n  top, and a shorter valid proof falls back to the count option.\n  Closed Arrow/Home/End and PageUp/PageDown keys retain native focus. The\n  combobox exposes its selected label and actual popup open state.\n  Typed page labels retain focus; repeated letters cycle matching labels and\n  search expires after the original one-second pause. Space continues an\n  active prefix or opens the popup when search is idle.\n- **Compositor:** Home, Insert, Review, and View controls act on the native\n  document. Arrow keys change tabs and retain native focus through wrapping;\n  Undo/Redo use the actual manuscript history and respect read-only mode.\n  Page settings and header/footer text are saved with the folio.\n  The page ruler changes the actual margins through drag or keyboard input.\n  Optional native pagination has physical-page and input checks; the current\n  web editor route does not register its existing pagination engine, so this\n  does not establish matching active-route behavior.\n  Local PNG/JPEG/GIF/WebP files become portable offline images; choosing a file\n  retains the original bytes and one undo restores the preceding manuscript.\n  File insertion checks the original converter in the background first: a\n  valid image that exceeds the 5 MB Typst editing limit leaves the draft intact.\n  Connected actions stay disabled until their native adapters exist.\n- **Appearance:** original presets and colour overrides preview immediately\n  and persist separately from manuscript formatting. Save failures retain the\n  preview and expose a retry; the stored System choice follows OS appearance.\n- **Versions:** local checkpoints and passage comparisons in the Editorial\n  Board. Restore saves the current manuscript first and refuses to replace\n  typing or Source edits made while a restore is being prepared. Saved status\n  follows the actual durable write.\n- **Cast:** the Room of Editors, local roster and assistance settings, retained\n  editorial notes/replies, and saved Full Analysis use the original profiles\n  and assets. The Board, roster page and analysis page share one retained room.\n  Local writer replies can be filed without contacting a provider. Unfinished\n  replies and roster forms survive navigation and closing; failed writes hold\n  the exact request and block departure until retry. Existing analyses can be\n  copied or downloaded. Provider notes, proposed edits, new analyses, spoken\n  notes and persona-mark navigation remain unavailable.\n- **Rubric:** local weights, custom criteria and retained grades share the\n  Board and Galley. Changes follow the actual durable write, and a failed save\n  keeps its candidate for retry. New provider grading remains unavailable.\n- **Apparatus:** saved sources share the Board and full page. Local scans use\n  the original citation rules; Copy publishes only the active folio's sources.\n  Cite inserts an undoable footnote and saves the manuscript before confirming\n  its source timestamp. Failed metadata writes retain a retry without repeating\n  that insertion. Offline steering retains its draft and original provider\n  error; connected research and source previews remain unavailable.\n- **Marginalia:** anchored writer notes, replies, resolve/reopen, passage\n  navigation, and erase use the actual manuscript marks and local note store.\n  The inline thread and Board share one reply draft. Unblurred replies survive\n  folio visits and closing; failed writes keep the exact request for retry and\n  block departure. Placing a note saves its manuscript mark before filing its\n  metadata. Deleting a marked passage reconciles only that folio after the\n  manuscript save. Writer previews use the original Flow policy and measured\n  passage geometry. Setting one aside is transient; reopening recalls its\n  shared thread. An admitted rail thread follows width changes while retaining\n  its reply and reserving the full measured card height.\n  Connected editor replies, speech, and recorded audio remain\n  unavailable until their native adapters exist.\n- **House and Library:** offline House, collection, and folio context with\n  original fields, inherited context, filing, and a shared context ledger.\n  Library cards use the original preview/count rules; source-only imports stay\n  visible while their writing projection is unavailable. Context changes are\n  published only after their actual durable write.\n- **Flow:** focused writing drives the original local rhythm classifier and\n  spool ribbon. Automatic focus fades desk chrome while keeping the page in\n  place; hovering, keyboard focus, or Escape restores the controls. Writing\n  tools opens from the Drawer or Board and saves the automatic-focus setting\n  and a separate local rhythm profile.\n  Review, live margin tools, cover lookup, and contextual amendments need their\n  connected adapters.\n- **Save:** autosave follows 700 ms of quiet. Explicit Save, switches, mode\n  transitions, and closing capture controls immediately. Serialization and\n  conversion stay off the per-keystroke path.\n\nZen and compositor choices persist locally. Drawer, Board and its selected\npanel remain part of the current desk visit.\nArchive/restore preserves documents; archived text is read-only. Find selects\nliteral matches in the active editor.\n\nRich copy/paste preserves formatting and Twyne object metadata. Linux X11\nexchanges HTML and UTF-8 text with other applications, and preserves the full\nmetadata between native instances. Actual native Paste/Copy/Undo/Redo checks\nalso cover clipboard ownership, focus, selection and editor changes during a\nbackground import, verified multi-megabyte incremental transfers, and the\noriginal 5 MB canonical-source limit before insertion. RTF-only input and\n"},"started_at_ms":1791230165467,"completed_at_ms":1791230165467}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-05T19:56:05.615Z","ordinal":45311,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a10da3-426f-7f22-9655-4a0263f4aafa","call_id":"call_4vKpWCYGZq31RSMZSfY0aPBt","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.3 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"index\":0,\"result\":{\"status\":\"fulfilled\",\"value\":{\"chunk_id\":\"916f8f\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000024796,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":566,\"output\":\"desktop/gpui/target/verification/insert-parameters-source-20261005-a/receipt.json\\ndesktop/gpui/target/verification/insert-parameters-source-20261005-a/image-full.png\\ndesktop/gpui/target/verification/insert-parameters-source-20261005-a/image.png\\ndesktop/gpui/target/verification/insert-parameters-source-20261005-a/mermaid-full.png\\ndesktop/gpui/target/verification/insert-parameters-source-20261005-a/mermaid.png\\ndesktop/gpui/target/verification/insert-parameters-source-20261005-a/footnote-full.png\\ndesktop/gpui/target/verification/insert-parameters-source-20261005-a/footnote.png\\ndesktop/gpui/target/verification/insert-parameters-source-20261005-a/endnote-full.png\\ndesktop/gpui/target/verification/insert-parameters-source-20261005-a/endnote.png\\ndesktop/gpui/target/verification/insert-parameters-source-20261005-a/table-full.png\\ndesktop/gpui/target/verification/insert-parameters-source-20261005-a/table.png\\ndesktop/gpui/target/verification/sakana-insert-modal-contract-4e1a54591296/stderr.txt\\ndesktop/gpui/target/verification/sakana-insert-modal-contract-4e1a54591296/response.txt\\ndesktop/gpui/target/verification/sakana-insert-modal-contract-4e1a54591296/process.json\\ndesktop/gpui/target/verification/sakana-insert-modal-contract-4e1a54591296/prompt.txt\\ndesktop/gpui/target/verification/sakana-insert-modal-contract-4e1a54591296/input-bundle.json\\ndesktop/gpui/target/verification/sakana-insert-modal-contract-4e1a54591296/data/crush.db-shm\\ndesktop/gpui/target/verification/sakana-insert-modal-contract-4e1a54591296/data/crush.db-wal\\ndesktop/gpui/target/verification/sakana-insert-modal-contract-4e1a54591296/data/logs/crush.log\\ndesktop/gpui/target/verification/sakana-insert-modal-contract-4e1a54591296/data/crush.db\\ndesktop/gpui/target/verification/sakana-insert-modal-contract-4e1a54591296/data/projects.json\\ndesktop/gpui/target/verification/sakana-insert-modal-contract-4e1a54591296/data/.gitignore\\ndesktop/gpui/target/verification/sakana-insert-modal-contract-4e1a54591296/config/crush.json\\ndesktop/gpui/target/verification/sakana-insert-modal-prompt.txt\\ndesktop/gpui/target/verification/sakana-insert-modal-input.json\\ndesktop/gpui/target/verification/insert-title-build-20261005-b/build.json\\ndesktop/gpui/target/verification/user-preview-pointer.json\\n\"}}}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"index\":1,\"result\":{\"status\":\"fulfilled\",\"value\":{\"chunk_id\":\"591fae\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000015726,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":1738,\"output\":\"// Parameter flows in the actual original editor, with synthetic local writing.\\nimport { chromium, expect, type Locator } from \\\"@playwright/test\\\";\\nimport { mkdir, readFile, writeFile } from \\\"node:fs/promises\\\";\\nimport { createHash } from \\\"node:crypto\\\";\\nimport { resolve } from \\\"node:path\\\";\\n\\nconst output = process.argv[2];\\nif (!output) throw new Error(\\\"A new owned output directory is required\\\");\\nconst origin = process.env.TWYNE_INSERT_SOURCE_URL ?? \\\"http://127.0.0.1:5207\\\";\\nif (!/^http:\\\\/\\\\/127\\\\.0\\\\.0\\\\.1:\\\\d+$/.test(origin)) throw new Error(\\\"A loopback Source origin is required\\\");\\nawait mkdir(output, { recursive: false, mode: 0o700 });\\nconst paths = [\\\"src/components/editor/table-insertion-grid.tsx\\\", \\\"src/components/editor/insert-panels.tsx\\\", \\\"src/components/ui/text-modal.tsx\\\", \\\"src/components/editor/twyne-editor.tsx\\\", \\\"src/components/editor/slash-command-menu.tsx\\\", \\\"src/utils/keybindings.ts\\\", \\\"src/global.css\\\", \\\"desktop/gpui/fixtures/insert-menu/capture-parameters.ts\\\"];\\nconst hashes = Object.fromEntries(await Promise.all(paths.map(async path => [path, createHash(\\\"sha256\\\").update(await readFile(path)).digest(\\\"hex\\\")])));\\nconst receipt: any = { status: \\\"running\\\", origin, hashes, viewport: { width: 948, height: 640 }, deviceScaleFactor: 1, accountAuthenticated: false, userLibraryAccessed: false, scope: \\\"Original browser editor; no Electrobun host proof\\\", cases: [], pageErrors: [] };\\nconst browser = await chromium.launch({ executablePath: process.env.TWYNE_FIXTURE_CHROME ?? \\\"/usr/bin/google-chrome\\\", headless: true });\\ntry {\\n  for (const kind of [\\\"table\\\", \\\"endnote\\\", \\\"footnote\\\", \\\"mermaid\\\", \\\"image\\\"]) {\\n    const context = await browser.newContext({ viewport: receipt.viewport, deviceScaleFactor: 1 });\\n    await context.route(\\\"**/*\\\", route => {\\n      const url = new URL(route.request().url());\\n      return url.origin === origin || [\\\"fonts.googleapis.com\\\", \\\"fonts.gstatic.com\\\"].includes(url.hostname) ? route.continue() : route.abort();\\n    });\\n    const page = await context.newPage();\\n    page.on(\\\"pageerror\\\", error => receipt.pageErrors.push(error.message));\\n    await page.route(/\\\\/api\\\\/auth\\\\//, route => route.fulfill({ contentType: \\\"application/json\\\", body: \\\"null\\\" }));\\n    await page.route(\\\"**/__insert-seed\\\", route => route.fulfill({ contentType: \\\"text/html\\\", body: \\\"<!doctype html><title>Parameter fixture</title>\\\" }));\\n    await page.goto(origin + \\\"/__insert-seed\\\");\\n    await page.evaluate(async () => {\\n      const path = \\\"/src/utils/idb.ts\\\";\\n      const idb = await import(/* @vite-ignore */ path);\\n      const now = Date.now();\\n      await idb.saveFoliosToIdb([{ id: \\\"insert-parameter-fixture\\\", name: \\\"The writing page\\\", type: \\\"draft\\\", createdAt: now, updatedAt: now }]);\\n      await idb.saveFolioContentToIdb(\\\"insert-parameter-fixture\\\", \\\"<p>The manuscript stays on this page.</p><p></p>\\\");\\n      await idb.saveActiveFolioIdToIdb(\\\"insert-parameter-fixture\\\");\\n      await idb.saveMetaToIdb(\\\"signin-toast-dismissed\\\", true);\\n    });\\n    await page.goto(origin + \\\"/editor/?platform=desktop\\\");\\n    const editor = page.locator(\\\".ProseMirror\\\");\\n    await expect(editor).toContainText(\\\"The manuscript stays on this page.\\\", { timeout: 90_000 });\\n    const zen = page.getByRole(\\\"button\\\", { name: \\\"Toggle Zen mode\\\", exact: true });\\n    if (await zen.getAttribute(\\\"aria-pressed\\\") === \\\"true\\\") await zen.click();\\n    await editor.locator(\\\"p\\\").last().click();\\n    await page.keyboard.type(\\\"/\\\" + kind);\\n    const menu = page.getByRole(\\\"listbox\\\", { name: \\\"Insert command\\\", exact: true });\\n    await expect(menu).toBeVisible();\\n    await menu.locator(`#slash-command-insert-${kind}`).click();\\n    await expect(menu).toHaveCount(0);\\n    await expect(editor).not.toContainText(\\\"/\\\" + kind);\\n    await page.evaluate(() => document.fonts.ready);\\n    let surface: Locator;\\n    if (kind === \\\"table\\\") {\\n      surface = page.locator(\\\"[data-table-insertion-grid]\\\");\\n      const grid = page.getByRole(\\\"grid\\\", { name: \\\"Choose table size\\\", exact: true });\\n      await expect(grid).toHaveAttribute(\\\"aria-rowcount\\\", \\\"8\\\");\\n      await expect(grid).toHaveAttribute(\\\"aria-colcount\\\", \\\"10\\\");\\n      await grid.focus();\\n      await page.keyboard.press(\\\"ArrowDown\\\");\\n      await expect(surface.locator(\\\"p\\\").first()).toHaveText(\\\"2 × 1 table\\\");\\n      for (let i = 0; i < 3; i++) {\\n        await page.keyboard.press(\\\"ArrowRight\\\");\\n        await expect(surface.locator(\\\"p\\\").first()).toHaveText(`2 × ${i + 2} table`);\\n      }\\n      await expect(grid.locator('[aria-selected=\\\"true\\\"]')).toHaveCount(8);\\n    } else if (kind === \\\"image\\\") {\\n      surface = page.getByText(\\\"Plate URL:\\\", { exact: true }).locator(\\\"..\\\");\\n    } else {\\n      surface = page.getByRole(\\\"dialog\\\");\\n    }\\n    await expect(surface).toBeVisible();\\n    await page.mouse.move(0, 0);\\n    await surface.screenshot({ path: resolve(output, kind + \\\".png\\\"), animations: \\\"disabled\\\" });\\n    await page.screenshot({ path: resolve(output, kind + \\\"-full.png\\\"), animations: \\\"disabled\\\" });\\n    const observed = await surface.evaluate(element => {\\n      const rect = (node: Element) => { const b = node.getBoundingClientRect(); return { x: b.x, y: b.y, width: b.width, height: b.height }; };\\n      return { rect: rect(element), nodes: [element, ...element.querySelectorAll(\\\"p, h2, label, button, textarea, input, [role='grid']\\\")].map(node => {\\n        const s = getComputedStyle(node);\\n        return { tag: node.tagName, text: node.textContent, role: node.getAttribute(\\\"role\\\"), label: node.getAttribute(\\\"aria-label\\\"), placeholder: node.getAttribute(\\\"placeholder\\\"), rect: rect(node), fontFamily: s.fontFamily, fontSize: s.fontSize, fontWeight: s.fontWeight, lineHeight: s.lineHeight, padding: s.padding, color: s.color, background: s.backgroundColor, border: s.border, borderRadius: s.borderRadius, boxShadow: s.boxShadow };\\n      }) };\\n    });\\n    const result: any = { kind, queryRemovedAtActivation: true, observed };\\n    if (kind === \\\"table\\\") {\\n      await page.keyboard.press(\\\"Enter\\\");\\n      await expect(surface).toHaveCount(0);\\n      await expect(editor.locator(\\\"table tr\\\")).toHaveCount(2);\\n      await expect(editor.locator(\\\"table th\\\")).toHaveCount(4);\\n      await expect(editor.locator(\\\"table td\\\")).toHaveCount(4);\\n      result.keyboardInserts2By4WithHeader = true;\\n    } else {\\n      await surface.getByRole(\\\"button\\\", { name: \\\"Cancel\\\", exact: true }).click();\\n      await expect(surface).toHaveCount(0);\\n      await expect(editor).not.toContainText(\\\"/\\\" + kind);\\n      result.cancelKeepsQueryRemoved = true;\\n    }\\n    receipt.cases.push(result);\\n    await context.close();\\n  }\\n  receipt.status = \\\"passed\\\";\\n} catch (error) {\\n  receipt.status = \\\"failed\\\";\\n  receipt.failure = error instanceof Error ? error.message : String(error);\\n  throw error;\\n} finally {\\n  await writeFile(resolve(output, \\\"receipt.json\\\"), JSON.stringify(receipt, null, 2) + \\\"\\\\n\\\");\\n  await browser.close();\\n}\\nconsole.log(JSON.stringify({ output, status: receipt.status, cases: receipt.cases.length, pageErrors: receipt.pageErrors.length }));\\n\"}}}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"index\":2,\"result\":{\"status\":\"fulfilled\",\"value\":{\"chunk_id\":\"16a1ee\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000020095,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":27,\"output\":\"86:        \\\"captureReady\\\": room.upgrade().is_some_and(|room| room.read(cx).capture_apparatus_ready(cx)),\\n\"}}}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"index\":3,\"result\":{\"status\":\"fulfilled\",\"value\":{\"chunk_id\":\"111fb4\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000022566,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":2459,\"output\":\"# Twyne GPUI\\n\\nTwyne's native desktop port uses Rust and [GPUI Kit 0.7](https://gpui-kit.com/).\\nThe goal is the full hosted desktop experience with identical styling, original\\nassets and behavior. The working offline slice includes the rich editor, Dossier,\\nlocal editorial panels and native Typst proof/PDF.\\n\\nThe full Electrobun application remains the reference. The port is unfinished;\\n[PORT_PLAN.md](PORT_PLAN.md) separates implemented behavior, retained checks,\\nunmounted foundations and remaining work.\\n\\n[ARCHITECTURE.md](ARCHITECTURE.md) maps native packages to their original web\\ncounterparts, records ownership boundaries, and gives focused investigation checks.\\n\\n## Run\\n\\nUse Bun, the repository's Rust toolchain, and the native libraries in\\n[GPUI Kit's installation guide](https://gpui-kit.com/docs/installation/).\\nThe repository's Devenv shell provides the Rust toolchain and Linux libraries.\\n\\nFrom the repository root:\\n\\n```bash\\nrtk proxy bun install --frozen-lockfile\\nrtk proxy devenv shell -- rtk proxy bun run desktop.gpui\\n```\\n\\nUse an isolated library or import files on startup:\\n\\n```bash\\nrtk proxy devenv shell -- rtk proxy bun run desktop.gpui --data-dir /tmp/twyne-native-library /path/to/draft.typ\\n```\\n\\nImports create library copies. Original files remain independent.\\n\\nThe developer build creates `twyne-document` from Twyne's existing TypeScript\\ndocument converters. Its compiled executable includes the Bun runtime. Offline\\nwriting needs no web server or account; GPUI renders the interface and the native\\nRust Typst engine renders proof/PDF. The helper handles source/HTML reconciliation,\\nstarter generation and the original MathJax export conversion.\\n\\nThe helper build also creates `twyne-math-write`. It is a diagnostic executable,\\nnot the main editor's math renderer or evidence of Write-view parity.\\n\\nFor direct Cargo development, build the helper first:\\n\\n```bash\\nrtk proxy bun run desktop.gpui.build-helper\\nrtk proxy devenv shell -- rtk proxy cargo run --locked --manifest-path desktop/gpui/Cargo.toml\\n```\\n\\nLinux requires X11 or Wayland and a graphics driver supported by WGPU. Native\\nfile pickers use the desktop's XDG portal. macOS requires Xcode command line\\ntools; Windows requires the MSVC C++ toolchain. Bundles, installers, signing, and\\nautomatic updates remain pending.\\n\\n## Writing and proof\\n\\n- **Write:** native rich text with Unicode input, selection, clipboard, IME,\\n  formatting, and undo/redo. Typing bursts form one undo group. Imported cached\\n  HTML is projected from canonical source before editing. Footnote and endnote\\n  markers open an editable note; collected notes navigate back to their\\n  manuscript references. Save and navigation capture unblurred note input.\\n- **Equation source:** activate an inline or block equation to edit its retained native textarea. Render equation submits through the actual canonical converter and preserves independent manuscript undo; Cancel keeps the saved source. Inline editing uses a measured child inside the original atom. Preview currently reports unavailable. Actual OS input and original-browser baseline/pixel parity remain separate gates.\\n- **Dossier:** the original ten sections, imported material, references, local\\n  probes, create/refine filing, and scoped recovery. Filing opens Write after\\n  the document is actually saved.\\n- **Source:** canonical Typst with a separate recoverable draft. Apply requires\\n  a successful current compile and verified projection. Discard preserves the\\n  manuscript. Source edits update the real proof after 450 ms of quiet. The\\n  native code editor provides Typst highlighting, line numbers,\\n  folded generated helpers, search/replace, source snippets, comments, wrapping,\\n  and line navigation. Pending Source edits lock the rich view.\\n- **Proof/Split:** the same pinned Typst fork and ordered fonts as the web\\n  renderer, original artwork, real SVG pages, zoom, page navigation, and PDF\\n  export. Failed compilation retains the last valid proof.\\n  The footer retains the selected page across Write/Proof transitions. Its\\n  count option leaves the current mode active; page choices reveal the page's\\n  top, and a shorter valid proof falls back to the count option.\\n  Closed Arrow/Home/End and PageUp/PageDown keys retain native focus. The\\n  combobox exposes its selected label and actual popup open state.\\n  Typed page labels retain focus; repeated letters cycle matching labels and\\n  search expires after the original one-second pause. Space continues an\\n  active prefix or opens the popup when search is idle.\\n- **Compositor:** Home, Insert, Review, and View controls act on the native\\n  document. Arrow keys change tabs and retain native focus through wrapping;\\n  Undo/Redo use the actual manuscript history and respect read-only mode.\\n  Page settings and header/footer text are saved with the folio.\\n  The page ruler changes the actual margins through drag or keyboard input.\\n  Optional native pagination has physical-page and input checks; the current\\n  web editor route does not register its existing pagination engine, so this\\n  does not establish matching active-route behavior.\\n  Local PNG/JPEG/GIF/WebP files become portable offline images; choosing a file\\n  retains the original bytes and one undo restores the preceding manuscript.\\n  File insertion checks the original converter in the background first: a\\n  valid image that exceeds the 5 MB Typst editing limit leaves the draft intact.\\n  Connected actions stay disabled until their native adapters exist.\\n- **Appearance:** original presets and colour overrides preview immediately\\n  and persist separately from manuscript formatting. Save failures retain the\\n  preview and expose a retry; the stored System choice follows OS appearance.\\n- **Versions:** local checkpoints and passage comparisons in the Editorial\\n  Board. Restore saves the current manuscript first and refuses to replace\\n  typing or Source edits made while a restore is being prepared. Saved status\\n  follows the actual durable write.\\n- **Cast:** the Room of Editors, local roster and assistance settings, retained\\n  editorial notes/replies, and saved Full Analysis use the original profiles\\n  and assets. The Board, roster page and analysis page share one retained room.\\n  Local writer replies can be filed without contacting a provider. Unfinished\\n  replies and roster forms survive navigation and closing; failed writes hold\\n  the exact request and block departure until retry. Existing analyses can be\\n  copied or downloaded. Provider notes, proposed edits, new analyses, spoken\\n  notes and persona-mark navigation remain unavailable.\\n- **Rubric:** local weights, custom criteria and retained grades share the\\n  Board and Galley. Changes follow the actual durable write, and a failed save\\n  keeps its candidate for retry. New provider grading remains unavailable.\\n- **Apparatus:** saved sources share the Board and full page. Local scans use\\n  the original citation rules; Copy publishes only the active folio's sources.\\n  Cite inserts an undoable footnote and saves the manuscript before confirming\\n  its source timestamp. Failed metadata writes retain a retry without repeating\\n  that insertion. Offline steering retains its draft and original provider\\n  error; connected research and source previews remain unavailable.\\n- **Marginalia:** anchored writer notes, replies, resolve/reopen, passage\\n  navigation, and erase use the actual manuscript marks and local note store.\\n  The inline thread and Board share one reply draft. Unblurred replies survive\\n  folio visits and closing; failed writes keep the exact request for retry and\\n  block departure. Placing a note saves its manuscript mark before filing its\\n  metadata. Deleting a marked passage reconciles only that folio after the\\n  manuscript save. Writer previews use the original Flow policy and measured\\n  passage geometry. Setting one aside is transient; reopening recalls its\\n  shared thread. An admitted rail thread follows width changes while retaining\\n  its reply and reserving the full measured card height.\\n  Connected editor replies, speech, and recorded audio remain\\n  unavailable until their native adapters exist.\\n- **House and Library:** offline House, collection, and folio context with\\n  original fields, inherited context, filing, and a shared context ledger.\\n  Library cards use the original preview/count rules; source-only imports stay\\n  visible while their writing projection is unavailable. Context changes are\\n  published only after their actual durable write.\\n- **Flow:** focused writing drives the original local rhythm classifier and\\n  spool ribbon. Automatic focus fades desk chrome while keeping the page in\\n  place; hovering, keyboard focus, or Escape restores the controls. Writing\\n  tools opens from the Drawer or Board and saves the automatic-focus setting\\n  and a separate local rhythm profile.\\n  Review, live margin tools, cover lookup, and contextual amendments need their\\n  connected adapters.\\n- **Save:** autosave follows 700 ms of quiet. Explicit Save, switches, mode\\n  transitions, and closing capture controls immediately. Serialization and\\n  conversion stay off the per-keystroke path.\\n\\nZen and compositor choices persist locally. Drawer, Board and its selected\\npanel remain part of the current desk visit.\\nArchive/restore preserves documents; archived text is read-only. Find selects\\nliteral matches in the active editor.\\n\\nRich copy/paste preserves formatting and Twyne object metadata. Linux X11\\nexchanges HTML and UTF-8 text with other applications, and preserves the full\\nmetadata between native instances. Actual native Paste/Copy/Undo/Redo checks\\nalso cover clipboard ownership, focus, selection and editor changes during a\\nbackground import, verified multi-megabyte incremental transfers, and the\\noriginal 5 MB canonical-source limit before insertion. RTF-only input and\\n\"}}}"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a10d89-1468-7f62-b4ea-9863445ef047","create_time":1791230165.6156554}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
