{"timestamp":"2026-10-05T19:56:30.654Z","ordinal":45315,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_0e6e2e948f59cffe016ac400e0dca487d180f1b6b56a66a957","status":"completed","call_id":"call_zNRoldNoIl8AdcfK8KTMdwH8","name":"exec","input":"text(await tools.apply_patch(\"*** Begin Patch\\n*** Update File: /home/diogenes/Projects/twyne/desktop/gpui/fixtures/insert-menu/capture-parameters.ts\\n@@\\n-    let surface: Locator;\\n+    let surface: Locator;\\n+    let tableInitial: unknown;\\n@@\\n       await expect(grid).toHaveAttribute(\\\"aria-rowcount\\\", \\\"8\\\");\\n       await expect(grid).toHaveAttribute(\\\"aria-colcount\\\", \\\"10\\\");\\n+      await expect(surface.locator(\\\"p\\\").first()).toHaveText(\\\"1 × 1 table\\\");\\n+      await expect(grid.locator('[aria-selected=\\\"true\\\"]')).toHaveCount(1);\\n+      await page.mouse.move(0, 0);\\n+      await surface.screenshot({ path: resolve(output, \\\"table-initial.png\\\"), animations: \\\"disabled\\\" });\\n+      tableInitial = await surface.evaluate(element => {\\n+        const b = element.getBoundingClientRect();\\n+        return { rect: { x: b.x, y: b.y, width: b.width, height: b.height }, caption: element.querySelector(\\\"p\\\")?.textContent,\\n+          gridFocused: Boolean(document.activeElement?.closest(\\\"[role='grid']\\\")), selectedCells: element.querySelectorAll('[aria-selected=\\\"true\\\"]').length };\\n+      });\\n@@\\n-    const result: any = { kind, queryRemovedAtActivation: true, observed };\\n+    const result: any = { kind, queryRemovedAtActivation: true, observed, ...(tableInitial ? { initial: tableInitial } : {}) };\\n*** Update File: /home/diogenes/Projects/twyne/desktop/gpui/ARCHITECTURE.md\\n@@\\n | `editor/view_insert.rs` | `components/editor/twyne-editor.tsx` registry dispatch | Pure rich transaction tests and mounted slash tests |\\n+| `insert_menu/table_grid.rs`, `insert_menu/table_picker.rs` | `components/editor/table-insertion-grid.tsx` | Executed Source vectors, mounted pointer/key tests, actual-font captures |\\n+| `editor/view_shortcuts.rs` | `utils/keybindings.ts` and command priority | Mounted rich shortcuts; code-block exit/undo in `editor/tests.rs` |\\n@@\\n-- Activation binds the manuscript, selection/query and revision. A form must\\n-  validate that binding again before committing.\\n-- Remove the query and insert its element as one history transaction. Failed\\n-  or cancelled insertion preserves the authored query. IME confirmation belongs\\n-  to the composing input.\\n+- Activation binds the manuscript, selection/query and revision. Immediate\\n+  commands remove the query and insert the element in one native history group.\\n+- Parameter commands remove the query when activated, as the original editor\\n+  does. Cancel leaves that removal intact. The retained picker/form must validate\\n+  its manuscript, editor, post-removal caret and revision before committing;\\n+  plain input also compares the retained post-removal body at that boundary.\\n+  Failed or stale commits leave the document at its current state.\\n+- Native parameter removal and commit are separate undo steps. Original\\n+  ProseMirror time grouping is a separate comparison gate. IME confirmation\\n+  belongs to the composing input.\\n@@\\n Give weaker external agents bounded inputs and inspect their output before adoption.\\n+\\n+The crate gates GPUI behind `desktop`; document rules can be checked without\\n+loading a UI. `tools/sync-insert-menu.ts --check` executes the original catalog,\\n+search and extracted pure table helpers, so reference drift is detected before\\n+native adapter work. A displayed shortcut must also have a mounted behavior\\n+check; a matching label alone is insufficient.\\n@@\\n Current feature status belongs in `PORT_PLAN.md`; do not infer readiness from\\n the existence of a module or a prepared contract.\\n+\\n+## Reproduce an issue quickly\\n+\\n+1. Identify the owning coordinator and original counterpart in the table above.\\n+2. Reduce the issue to an isolated manuscript and explicit route, view, selection,\\n+   window size and scale. Reuse an existing fixture when possible.\\n+3. Check document rules with a pure test, focus/events with a mounted test, and\\n+   clipping or spacing with original-browser and actual-native captures.\\n+4. Record the exact binary, helper and source hashes. Keep historical receipts\\n+   intact so an old successful build is never mistaken for the current one.\\n+\\n+For parallel work, assign one package or fixture with an explicit input/output\\n+contract. The host retains document ownership; workers emit intent. Small\\n+external-model tasks work best for reference extraction and bounded review,\\n+with root validation of every proposed behavioral change. Cargo stays serial.\\n*** End Patch\"));\nconst results = await Promise.allSettled([\n  tools.exec_command({cmd:\"rtk proxy python - <<'PY'\\nimport json\\nfrom pathlib import Path\\np=Path('desktop/gpui/target/verification/sakana-insert-modal-contract-4e1a54591296/response.txt')\\ns=p.read_text()\\nprint(s[:14500])\\nPY\",max_output_tokens:4700}),\n  tools.write_stdin({session_id:5945,chars:\"\",max_output_tokens:2300,yield_time_ms:1000})\n]);for(let i=0;i<results.length;i++)text({index:i,result:results[i]});\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a10d89-1468-7f62-b4ea-9863445ef047","create_time":1791230166.094593}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-05T19:56:30.689Z","ordinal":45316,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a10537-909f-77a3-96d8-dd07161f91ae","turn_id":"01a10d89-1468-7f62-b4ea-9863445ef047","item":{"type":"FileChange","id":"exec-f2ebc8ff-e30f-4a1e-8cea-dada78f58fb7","changes":{"/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne/desktop/gpui/fixtures/insert-menu/capture-parameters.ts":{"type":"update","unified_diff":"@@ -50,2 +50,3 @@\n     let surface: Locator;\n+    let tableInitial: unknown;\n     if (kind === \"table\") {\n@@ -55,2 +56,11 @@\n       await expect(grid).toHaveAttribute(\"aria-colcount\", \"10\");\n+      await expect(surface.locator(\"p\").first()).toHaveText(\"1 × 1 table\");\n+      await expect(grid.locator('[aria-selected=\"true\"]')).toHaveCount(1);\n+      await page.mouse.move(0, 0);\n+      await surface.screenshot({ path: resolve(output, \"table-initial.png\"), animations: \"disabled\" });\n+      tableInitial = await surface.evaluate(element => {\n+        const b = element.getBoundingClientRect();\n+        return { rect: { x: b.x, y: b.y, width: b.width, height: b.height }, caption: element.querySelector(\"p\")?.textContent,\n+          gridFocused: Boolean(document.activeElement?.closest(\"[role='grid']\")), selectedCells: element.querySelectorAll('[aria-selected=\"true\"]').length };\n+      });\n       await grid.focus();\n@@ -79,3 +89,3 @@\n     });\n-    const result: any = { kind, queryRemovedAtActivation: true, observed };\n+    const result: any = { kind, queryRemovedAtActivation: true, observed, ...(tableInitial ? { initial: tableInitial } : {}) };\n     if (kind === \"table\") {\n","move_path":null},"/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne/desktop/gpui/ARCHITECTURE.md":{"type":"update","unified_diff":"@@ -33,2 +33,4 @@\n | `editor/view_insert.rs` | `components/editor/twyne-editor.tsx` registry dispatch | Pure rich transaction tests and mounted slash tests |\n+| `insert_menu/table_grid.rs`, `insert_menu/table_picker.rs` | `components/editor/table-insertion-grid.tsx` | Executed Source vectors, mounted pointer/key tests, actual-font captures |\n+| `editor/view_shortcuts.rs` | `utils/keybindings.ts` and command priority | Mounted rich shortcuts; code-block exit/undo in `editor/tests.rs` |\n | `compositor.rs` | `components/editor/compositor-panel.tsx`, `utils/compositor-toolbar.ts` | `fixtures/chrome/`, `fixtures/editor/` |\n@@ -53,7 +55,12 @@\n   Opening or dismissing the menu does not modify the document.\n-- Activation binds the manuscript, selection/query and revision. A form must\n-  validate that binding again before committing.\n-- Remove the query and insert its element as one history transaction. Failed\n-  or cancelled insertion preserves the authored query. IME confirmation belongs\n-  to the composing input.\n+- Activation binds the manuscript, selection/query and revision. Immediate\n+  commands remove the query and insert the element in one native history group.\n+- Parameter commands remove the query when activated, as the original editor\n+  does. Cancel leaves that removal intact. The retained picker/form must validate\n+  its manuscript, editor, post-removal caret and revision before committing;\n+  plain input also compares the retained post-removal body at that boundary.\n+  Failed or stale commits leave the document at its current state.\n+- Native parameter removal and commit are separate undo steps. Original\n+  ProseMirror time grouping is a separate comparison gate. IME confirmation\n+  belongs to the composing input.\n - Feature surfaces emit intent; the active-document host accepts it. Each surface\n@@ -69,2 +76,8 @@\n \n+The crate gates GPUI behind `desktop`; document rules can be checked without\n+loading a UI. `tools/sync-insert-menu.ts --check` executes the original catalog,\n+search and extracted pure table helpers, so reference drift is detected before\n+native adapter work. A displayed shortcut must also have a mounted behavior\n+check; a matching label alone is insufficient.\n+\n ```bash\n@@ -85 +98,16 @@\n the existence of a module or a prepared contract.\n+\n+## Reproduce an issue quickly\n+\n+1. Identify the owning coordinator and original counterpart in the table above.\n+2. Reduce the issue to an isolated manuscript and explicit route, view, selection,\n+   window size and scale. Reuse an existing fixture when possible.\n+3. Check document rules with a pure test, focus/events with a mounted test, and\n+   clipping or spacing with original-browser and actual-native captures.\n+4. Record the exact binary, helper and source hashes. Keep historical receipts\n+   intact so an old successful build is never mistaken for the current one.\n+\n+For parallel work, assign one package or fixture with an explicit input/output\n+contract. The host retains document ownership; workers emit intent. Small\n+external-model tasks work best for reference extraction and bounded review,\n+with root validation of every proposed behavioral change. Cargo stays serial.\n","move_path":null}},"status":"completed","stdout":"Success. Updated the following files:\nM /home/diogenes/Projects/twyne/desktop/gpui/fixtures/insert-menu/capture-parameters.ts\nM /home/diogenes/Projects/twyne/desktop/gpui/ARCHITECTURE.md\n","stderr":""},"started_at_ms":1791230190687,"completed_at_ms":1791230190689}}
