{"timestamp":"2026-10-05T20:02:19.171Z","ordinal":45488,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a10537-909f-77a3-96d8-dd07161f91ae","turn_id":"01a10d89-1468-7f62-b4ea-9863445ef047","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_0e6e2e948f59cffe016ac40249a48487d19ac8c1bb2610961a","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"The broader check passed: 118 mounted desktop tests and strict Clippy. Fresh native captures show the table grid and shortcut hints with the original font.\n\nThose captures also make the remaining differences concrete: table cells still round differently, the caption weight differs, and note, diagram, and image insertion surfaces need more work. The module map and isolated fixtures now make those issues much quicker to locate.\n"}],"phase":"commentary"},"started_at_ms":1791230537679,"completed_at_ms":1791230539171}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-05T20:02:19.175Z","ordinal":45489,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"message","id":"msg_0e6e2e948f59cffe016ac40249a48487d19ac8c1bb2610961a","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"output_text","text":"The broader check passed: 118 mounted desktop tests and strict Clippy. Fresh native captures show the table grid and shortcut hints with the original font.\n\nThose captures also make the remaining differences concrete: table cells still round differently, the caption weight differs, and note, diagram, and image insertion surfaces need more work. The module map and isolated fixtures now make those issues much quicker to locate.\n"}],"phase":"commentary","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a10d89-1468-7f62-b4ea-9863445ef047","create_time":1791230523.924075,"content_item_kinds":["unknown"]}},"metadata":{"retained_source":{"id":{"message_id":"msg_0e6e2e948f59cffe016ac40249a48487d19ac8c1bb2610961a","turn_id":"01a10d89-1468-7f62-b4ea-9863445ef047","role":"assistant"},"revision":"retained_01a10da8-f5a7-7313-ab9f-f6cfdae4ff8e","complete":true},"client_authored":false,"user_input_order":2402}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-05T20:02:43.427Z","ordinal":45490,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_0e6e2e948f59cffe016ac4024b257887d19605ba753cfe0588","status":"completed","call_id":"call_2j6uvLOIHNE5oIZUzjUJdAm9","name":"exec","input":"text(await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"rtk proxy python - <<'PY'\\nimport json, hashlib, time\\nfrom pathlib import Path\\nroot=Path('.').resolve()\\nbase=root/'desktop/gpui/target/verification/insert-parameters-build-20261005-a'\\nsource=root/'desktop/gpui/target/verification/insert-parameters-source-20261005-b/receipt.json'\\nsha=lambda path:hashlib.sha256(path.read_bytes()).hexdigest()\\nartifact=lambda path:{'path':str(path),'sha256':sha(path)}\\nbuild=json.loads((base/'build.json').read_text())\\ndrift=[path for path,expected in build['sources'].items() if sha(root/path)!=expected]\\nassert not drift,drift\\nui=json.loads((base/'checks/full-ui.json').read_text())\\nclippy=json.loads((base/'checks/clippy.json').read_text())\\nassert ui['status']=='passed' and ui['passed']==118 and ui['failed']==0 and ui['filtered']==0\\nassert clippy['status']=='passed'\\nchecks=[dict(ui,evidence=artifact(base/'checks/full-ui.log')),dict(clippy,evidence=artifact(base/'checks/clippy.log')),\\n {'command':'rtk proxy devenv shell -- rtk proxy cargo test --locked --offline --no-default-features --lib --manifest-path desktop/gpui/Cargo.toml insert_menu','status':'passed','passed':10,'failed':0,'evidence':'Observed terminal completion in root session 88730','warning':'Existing section_ranges dead-code warning in the pure build; strict desktop Clippy passed'},\\n {'command':'rtk proxy devenv shell -- rtk proxy cargo test --locked --offline --no-default-features --lib --manifest-path desktop/gpui/Cargo.toml exit_code_','status':'passed','passed':1,'failed':0,'evidence':'Observed terminal completion, root chunk 4c777b'},\\n {'command':'rtk proxy bun desktop/gpui/tools/sync-insert-menu.ts --check','status':'passed','commands':17,'queries':21,'tableCases':27,'networkUsed':False,'evidence':'Observed terminal completion, root chunk dbfdd1'}]\\ncaptures=[]\\nfor name,state in [('table','slash-form'),('hint','slash-filtered'),('menu','slash')]:\\n d=json.loads((base/(name+'-geometry.json')).read_text())\\n assert d['captureReady'] and d['scaleFactor']==1 and d['viewport']=={'width':948.0,'height':640.0}\\n names={'Name(\\\"slash-table-picker\\\")','Name(\\\"slash-table-grid\\\")','Name(\\\"slash-table-size\\\")','Name(\\\"slash-table-cell-1-1\\\")','Name(\\\"slash-table-cell-8-10\\\")','Name(\\\"slash-command-menu\\\")','Name(\\\"slash-hint-paragraph-heading-2\\\")'}\\n captures.append({'state':state,'image':artifact(base/(name+'.png')),'geometry':artifact(base/(name+'-geometry.json')),'fixture':build['fixtures'][state],'viewport':d['viewport'],'scaleFactor':1,'observedElements':[{'element':e['path'][-1],'rect':e['rect'],'visible':e['visible'],'focused':e['focused']} for e in d['elements'] if e['path'][-1] in names]})\\ns=json.loads(source.read_text())\\nassert s['status']=='passed' and len(s['cases'])==5 and not s['pageErrors']\\ntable=next(x for x in s['cases'] if x['kind']=='table')\\nrecord={\\n 'schemaVersion':1,'recordedUnix':time.time(),'status':'passed_scoped_checks',\\n 'scope':'Source table-size grid, parameter activation/cancel, retained cursor guards, shortcut hints and rich structural keys',\\n 'build':artifact(base/'build.json'),'artifacts':build['artifacts'],'sourceHashes':build['sources'],\\n 'checks':checks,'captures':captures,'sourceBrowser':artifact(source),'sourceBrowserCases':5,\\n 'sourceTableInitial':table['initial'],\\n 'advisoryReview':artifact(root/'desktop/gpui/fixtures/insert-menu/advisory-modal/adoption-review.json'),\\n 'observations':[\\n  'The 8 by 10 native picker accepts pointer/keyboard dimensions; mounted tests insert 2 by 4 with header cells, cover bounds/cancel and reject a queued choice after a document switch.',\\n  'Original browser table/note/diagram/image activation removes the slash query; cancel does not restore it. Native parameter activation follows that boundary.',\\n  'Native rich registry keys implement heading/list/quote/code/page-break commands. Mod-Enter first exits a code block without deleting selected code; one undo restores the node and selection.',\\n  'Actual-font native captures show the picker at x351 y64 width246 height246, the filtered heading shortcut, and an unfiltered width288 menu.',\\n  'Sakana fugu-max reviewed four frozen files. Root corrected incomplete/false claims; no proposed product code was adopted from this modal review.'\\n ],\\n 'knownDifferences':[\\n  'The original table box is 245.90625 by 249.265625. Native flex layout rounds 18.4-pixel cells to 18 pixels and the box to 246 by 246; caption synthetic weight and rasterization still differ.',\\n  'Native opens with grid focus; the original caller returns focus to the editor. Original keyboard fixture explicitly focuses the grid.',\\n  'Native parameter removal/commit use separate undo steps. Original ProseMirror time grouping still needs a matching interaction test.',\\n  'Original note/Mermaid modal styling, Mermaid preview, immediate blank equation atoms and the inline image URL bar are still implementation work.',\\n  'Native adds Link as requested and clamps the menu to the visible viewport.',\\n  'Hints reproduce the original default Mac labels; native rich keybindings resolve Mod for the host OS. Prototype plain-text manuscripts do not yet implement these structural keyboard bindings.',\\n  'The rich import and original browser fixtures exercise different room/document presentation defaults; these captures compare insertion surfaces, not full-room or title parity.'\\n ],\\n 'boundaries':[\\n  'Synthetic local manuscripts and isolated native libraries; no user preview library access.',\\n  'The new immutable UI build reuses the documented frozen document helper; no new helper release is claimed.',\\n  'Mounted GPUI tests and actual native font/GPU captures are separate evidence.',\\n  'Original browser evidence does not establish the Electrobun host.',\\n  'No authenticated account sync, live AI/knowledge-base request, real audio/device, release, installation or other-OS claim.'\\n ]\\n}\\noutput=root/'desktop/gpui/fixtures/insert-menu/parameter-acceptance.json'\\noutput.write_text(json.dumps(record,indent=2)+'\\\\n')\\nprint({'status':record['status'],'receipt':str(output),'currentInputHashesMatch':True,'uiTests':ui['passed'],'nativeCaptures':len(captures),'sourceBrowserCases':len(s['cases'])})\\nPY\",max_output_tokens:1600}));\ntext(await tools.apply_patch(\"*** Begin Patch\\n*** Update File: /home/diogenes/Projects/twyne/desktop/gpui/PORT_PLAN.md\\n@@\\n-The October 5 title/insertion checkpoint has [recorded acceptance](fixtures/insert-menu/native-acceptance.json):\\n+The earlier October 5 title/insertion checkpoint has [recorded acceptance](fixtures/insert-menu/native-acceptance.json):\\n@@\\n-and its table form. These are local feature checks. Shortcut hints and exact\\n-parameter-dialog styling remain comparison work; the native Link command,\\n-cancel-preserves-query behavior, and viewport clamping are documented differences.\\n+and its then-current table form. This is historical feature evidence. The\\n+parameter checkpoint below supersedes its query-cancellation and hint behavior;\\n+the native Link command and viewport clamping remain documented differences.\\n@@\\n fixtures. This checkpoint does not establish connected workflows or full parity.\\n+\\n+The current [parameter checkpoint](fixtures/insert-menu/parameter-acceptance.json)\\n+records 118 mounted desktop tests, 10 pure insertion tests, a pure code-block\\n+exit/undo check, strict UI Clippy, and 27 executed original table helper vectors.\\n+Five original-browser parameter cases pass with no page errors. The native\\n+8 × 10 table picker inserts keyboard/pointer dimensions with a header row;\\n+parameter activation removes the query before opening, and Cancel leaves that\\n+removal intact. Retained targets reject changed manuscripts, editors, revisions\\n+and carets. Registry hint labels and rich structural keybindings are mounted;\\n+Mod-Enter exits a code block before falling through to page-break insertion.\\n+\\n+Three actual-native captures use an immutable current build, original font\\n+faces, rich import fixtures and isolated libraries at 948 × 640 / scale 1.\\n+The original table box is 245.90625 × 249.265625; native flex rounding currently\\n+produces 246 × 246 with 18-pixel cells. Caption weight, initial grid focus and\\n+original time-based undo grouping remain comparison work. Note/Mermaid modal\\n+styling, diagram preview, immediate blank equation insertion and the inline image\\n+URL bar remain implementation work. Prototype text manuscripts do not yet bind\\n+the rich structural shortcuts. This checkpoint compares insertion surfaces;\\n+the capture defaults do not establish full-room or title parity.\\n+\\n+A bounded [Sakana modal review](fixtures/insert-menu/advisory-modal/adoption-review.json)\\n+retains its frozen inputs and root corrections. Missing host context produced\\n+several false findings; no product code was adopted from that review. The normal\\n+user preview remains on its prior title/insertion build with its library intact.\\n*** End Patch\"));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a10d89-1468-7f62-b4ea-9863445ef047","create_time":1791230523.924075}}}
