{"timestamp":"2026-10-05T20:03:36.344Z","ordinal":45510,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a10537-909f-77a3-96d8-dd07161f91ae","turn_id":"01a10d89-1468-7f62-b4ea-9863445ef047","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_0e6e2e948f59cffe016ac402921f0887d19543611c45c4e1a8","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"So far, it’s **one Rust crate using GPUI Kit**, organized into feature modules, plus a Bun helper that reuses Twyne’s document converters.\n\n| Area | Responsibility |\n|---|---|\n| `app/` | Active manuscript, navigation, saving, and feature coordination |\n| `editor/` | Document model, commands, history, input, and rendering |\n| `insert_menu/`, `gen_ui/`, other features | Their own rules and UI; they emit actions to the manuscript owner |\n| Workspace/Source/Proof modules | Canonical Typst, recoverable drafts, conversion, and compilation |\n| Native account/AI/audio modules | Separate integration contracts and transport |\n| Theme/assets/chrome | Original fonts, colors, artwork, and shared controls |\n\nI’ve documented the boundaries and original-source counterparts in [ARCHITECTURE.md](/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne/desktop/gpui/ARCHITECTURE.md).\n\n**The structure still needs work.** `app.rs` remains 4,380 lines, and the main editor view is 3,747. The next useful extractions are Source/Proof coordination, library/file actions, and chrome rendering.\n\nMy grasp is strongest around offline editing: document ownership, saving, Unicode positions, undo, title layout, and slash commands. Connected sync and AI have prepared foundations, but native end-to-end behavior remains unfinished. Visual parity also needs continued comparison.\n\nThe most useful ways to investigate faster are:\n\n- Map each feature to its original implementation and focused checks.\n- Reproduce bugs with a small manuscript, explicit selection, view, window size, and scale.\n- Test document rules separately from focus/events and actual rendered pixels.\n- Give smaller agents bounded reference or fixture tasks, then validate their conclusions.\n- Keep exact build receipts so older previews cannot masquerade as current evidence.\n\nThat workflow is producing concrete results: **118 mounted desktop tests and strict Clippy pass**, while fresh captures expose remaining table sizing and font-weight differences. Your open preview remains on the prior build; these checks used isolated copies.\n\n"}],"phase":"final_answer","memory_citation":{"entries":[{"path":"MEMORY.md","lineStart":579,"lineEnd":580,"note":"Manuscript continuity and deliberate side panels"}],"rolloutIds":["01a0f101-b3b4-7e41-9e3c-8d3ec580aba0"]}},"started_at_ms":1791230610166,"completed_at_ms":1791230616344}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-05T20:03:36.359Z","ordinal":45511,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"message","id":"msg_0e6e2e948f59cffe016ac402921f0887d19543611c45c4e1a8","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"output_text","text":"So far, it’s **one Rust crate using GPUI Kit**, organized into feature modules, plus a Bun helper that reuses Twyne’s document converters.\n\n| Area | Responsibility |\n|---|---|\n| `app/` | Active manuscript, navigation, saving, and feature coordination |\n| `editor/` | Document model, commands, history, input, and rendering |\n| `insert_menu/`, `gen_ui/`, other features | Their own rules and UI; they emit actions to the manuscript owner |\n| Workspace/Source/Proof modules | Canonical Typst, recoverable drafts, conversion, and compilation |\n| Native account/AI/audio modules | Separate integration contracts and transport |\n| Theme/assets/chrome | Original fonts, colors, artwork, and shared controls |\n\nI’ve documented the boundaries and original-source counterparts in [ARCHITECTURE.md](/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne/desktop/gpui/ARCHITECTURE.md).\n\n**The structure still needs work.** `app.rs` remains 4,380 lines, and the main editor view is 3,747. The next useful extractions are Source/Proof coordination, library/file actions, and chrome rendering.\n\nMy grasp is strongest around offline editing: document ownership, saving, Unicode positions, undo, title layout, and slash commands. Connected sync and AI have prepared foundations, but native end-to-end behavior remains unfinished. Visual parity also needs continued comparison.\n\nThe most useful ways to investigate faster are:\n\n- Map each feature to its original implementation and focused checks.\n- Reproduce bugs with a small manuscript, explicit selection, view, window size, and scale.\n- Test document rules separately from focus/events and actual rendered pixels.\n- Give smaller agents bounded reference or fixture tasks, then validate their conclusions.\n- Keep exact build receipts so older previews cannot masquerade as current evidence.\n\nThat workflow is producing concrete results: **118 mounted desktop tests and strict Clippy pass**, while fresh captures expose remaining table sizing and font-weight differences. Your open preview remains on the prior build; these checks used isolated copies.\n\n<oai-mem-citation>\n<citation_entries>\nMEMORY.md:579-580|note=[Manuscript continuity and deliberate side panels]\n</citation_entries>\n<rollout_ids>\n01a0f101-b3b4-7e41-9e3c-8d3ec580aba0\n</rollout_ids>\n</oai-mem-citation>"}],"phase":"final_answer","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a10d89-1468-7f62-b4ea-9863445ef047","create_time":1791230588.482166,"content_item_kinds":["unknown"]}},"metadata":{"retained_source":{"id":{"message_id":"msg_0e6e2e948f59cffe016ac402921f0887d19543611c45c4e1a8","turn_id":"01a10d89-1468-7f62-b4ea-9863445ef047","role":"assistant"},"revision":"retained_01a10daa-2327-7632-941b-8311e8a4f5de","complete":true},"client_authored":false,"user_input_order":2403}}
