hored":false},{"client_authored":false,"mcp_attribution":{"sources":[{"first_turn_id":"01a10555-dfb0-7570-9355-0ebfebd2abb9","plugin_id":"unified-computer-use@openai-bundled","server_name":"cua_repl","tool_name":"js"}],"status":"complete"},"retained_source":{"complete":true,"id":{"message_id":"msg_01a10d5f-b8d1-7bb0-bf15-011f62014650","role":"user","turn_id":"01a10d4c-a644-7d71-9054-bf5cd3583d03"},"revision":"retained_01a10d5f-b8d1-7bb0-bf15-013c3e7533d6"},"user_input_order":2381},{"client_authored":false,"compaction_model_hash":"3000","mcp_attribution":{"sources":[{"first_turn_id":"01a10555-dfb0-7570-9355-0ebfebd2abb9","plugin_id":"unified-computer-use@openai-bundled","server_name":"cua_repl","tool_name":"js"}],"status":"complete"}}],"resume_metadata":{"last_started_turn_id":"01a10daa-98ac-7341-8bf7-59561f3acc7f","multi_agent_version":"v2","previous_turn_settings":{"comp_hash":"3000","model":"gpt-6.1-sol","realtime_active":false}},"retained_context":{"assistant_messages":[{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_0e6e2e948f59cffe016ac400adf1d487d19bf90a30a13d9279","order":2399,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a10da2-b041-75b3-8d53-bca3d800a423","text":"Two files remain larger than I want: `app.rs` is 4,380 lines and the main editor view is 3,747. Feature coordinators and pure document modules make work easier to assign, but those two files still slow navigation.\n\nI’m documenting the current boundaries and using smaller reproductions for fixes. One just caught a shortcut mismatch: Ctrl/Cmd+Enter inside a code block should leave the code block, while elsewhere it inserts a page break.\n","turn_id":"01a10d89-1468-7f62-b4ea-9863445ef047"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_0e6e2e948f59cffe016ac40126223487d18b0cdb99bf585c1e","order":2400,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a10da4-8134-7c53-8bfc-341496959539","text":"The focused insertion tests are green, including table selection, document-switch guards, cancellation, undo, and rich-editor shortcuts. The original browser fixture also passed five parameter flows.\n\nThe Sakana review helped identify modal differences, but I rejected several findings after checking the host and input bindings. Bounded delegation helps with reference extraction; I still need to validate changes against the running UI.\n","turn_id":"01a10d89-1468-7f62-b4ea-9863445ef047"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_0e6e2e948f59cffe016ac401c1875c87d187ef88ab35a701ea","order":2401,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a10da6-dfbb-7853-a209-60051e8a7bc6","text":"The ownership map is now in `desktop/gpui/ARCHITECTURE.md`, with original-source counterparts and focused checks. I’m also saving the current test and capture results against an exact build, so later debugging can distinguish current behavior from an older preview.\n\nThe font check caught another concrete mismatch: the table picker and shortcut hints were using the code font. They now use the original Special Elite face.\n","turn_id":"01a10d89-1468-7f62-b4ea-9863445ef047"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_0e6e2e948f59cffe016ac40249a48487d19ac8c1bb2610961a","order":2402,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a10da8-f5a7-7313-ab9f-f6cfdae4ff8e","text":"The broader check passed: 118 mounted desktop tests and strict Clippy. Fresh native captures show the table grid and shortcut hints with the original font.\n\nThose captures also make the remaining differences concrete: table cells still round differently, the caption weight differs, and note, diagram, and image insertion surfaces need more work. The module map and isolated fixtures now make those issues much quicker to locate.\n","turn_id":"01a10d89-1468-7f62-b4ea-9863445ef047"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_0e6e2e948f59cffe016ac402921f0887d19543611c45c4e1a8","order":2403,"phase":"final_answer","revision":"retained_01a10daa-2327-7632-941b-8311e8a4f5de","text":"So far, it’s **one Rust crate using GPUI Kit**, organized into feature modules, plus a Bun helper that reuses Twyne’s document converters.\n\n| Area | Responsibility |\n|---|---|\n| `app/` | Active manuscript, navigation, saving, and feature coordination |\n| `editor/` | Document model, commands, history, input, and rendering |\n| `insert_menu/`, `gen_ui/`, other features | Their own rules and UI; they emit actions to the manuscript owner |\n| Workspace/Source/Proof modules | Canonical Typst, recoverable drafts, conversion, and compilation |\n| Native account/AI/audio modules | Separate integration contracts and transport |\n| Theme/assets/chrome | Original fonts, colors, artwork, and shared controls |\n\nI’ve documented the boundaries and original-source counterparts in [ARCHITECTURE.md](/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne/desktop/gpui/ARCHITECTURE.md).\n\n**The structure still needs work.** `app.rs` remains 4,380 lines, and the main editor view is 3,747. The next useful extractions are Source/Proof coordination, library/file actions, and chrome rendering.\n\nMy grasp is strongest around offline editing: document ownership, saving, Unicode positions, undo, title layout, and slash commands. Connected sync and AI have prepared foundations, but native end-to-end behavior remains unfinished. Visual parity also needs continued comparison.\n\nThe most useful ways to investigate faster are:\n\n- Map each feature to its original implementation and focused checks.\n- Reproduce bugs with a small manuscript, explicit selection, view, window size, and scale.\n- Test document rules separately from focus/events and actual rendered pixels.\n- Give smaller agents bounded reference or fixture tasks, then validate their conclusions.\n- Keep exact build receipts so older previews cannot masquerade as current evidence.\n\nThat workflow is producing concrete results: **118 mounted desktop tests and strict Clippy pass**, while fresh captures expose remaining table sizing and font-weight differences. Your open preview remains on the prior build; these checks used isolated copies.\n\n\u003coai-mem-citation\u003e\n\u003ccitation_entries\u003e\nMEMORY.md:579-580|note=[Manuscript continuity and deliberate side panels]\n\u003c/citation_entries\u003e\n\u003crollout_ids\u003e\n01a0f101-b3b4-7e41-9e3c-8d3ec580aba0\n\u003c/rollout_ids\u003e\n\u003c/oai-mem-citation\u003e","turn_id":"01a10d89-1468-7f62-b4ea-9863445ef047"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_0e6e2e948f59cffe016ac402d05db887d18585b7ae1b553fe2","order":2404,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a10dab-042b-74f3-b8fc-c7bc81ae7253","text":"I’m continuing with the insertion surfaces. Notes should open the original centered writing dialog, diagrams should use the source-and-preview layout, and equations should insert directly into the document. I’ll use the current browser captures and source contracts to guide those changes.\n","turn_id":"01a10daa-98ac-7341-8bf7-59561f3acc7f"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_0e6e2e948f59cffe016ac403fab54c87d1b7dd0ae47cc77a67","order":2405,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a10daf-9158-7681-81e6-fa25170a923c","text":"The Source dialogs are clear: notes use a 512-pixel dialog with specific labels and descriptions, multiline input, and an empty-submit guard. The diagram dialog adds a live preview. I’ve also started a bounded Sakana review of the Mermaid backend, since its browser-rendered SVG needs a real native rendering path.\n","turn_id":"01a10daa-98ac-7341-8bf7-59561f3acc7f"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_0e6e2e948f59cffe016ac40797778087d196672b05c5e1691b","order":2406,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a10dbd-af4d-7543-b858-f46be594aa0f","text":"The note dialog now has the original copy and centered layout, with multiline input and an empty-submit guard. Equations now insert a blank editable atom directly.\n\nI also found an input issue: the textarea emits an Enter event after inserting a newline. The form was treating that event as submission. I’ve corrected the handler and added a test that lets the event settle before typing the next line.\n","turn_id":"01a10daa-98ac-7341-8bf7-59561f3acc7f"}],"assistant_messages_incomplete":true,"incomplete":false,"next_order":2407,"user_messages":[{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_01a10b52-46ed-7f41-959e-f106ea1871fb","order":2268,"revision":"retained_01a10b52-46ed-7f41-959e-f12f4e3b1fa4","text":"status report","turn_id":"01a10a1b-b650-7660-b5ef-56e1a3784ac1"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_01a10b53-da43-7270-80cd-7083547d38fa","order":2270,"revision":"retained_01a10b53-da43-7270-80cd-70adcb767628","text":"okay and what about online writing and sync?","turn_id":"01a10a1b-b650-7660-b5ef-56e1a3784ac1"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_01a10b54-68e0-7e10-a51e-719395495580","order":2271,"revision":"retained_01a10b54-68e0-7e10-a51e-71be7882db09","text":"what about the ai integration? knowledge base integration, gen ui components?","turn_id":"01a10a1b-b650-7660-b5ef-56e1a3784ac1"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_01a10b57-fa01-7481-83c6-cd438ad53be0","order":2274,"revision":"retained_01a10b57-fa01-7481-83c6-cd6d219dd390","text":"start the application i want to see what its like","turn_id":"01a10a1b-b650-7660-b5ef-56e1a3784ac1"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_01a10d17-d63e-7422-b308-733ebf06665a","order":2365,"revision":"retained_01a10d17-d63e-7422-b308-735bca3ecf6f","text":"some interface bugs i noticed the title doesn't fully appear, getting cutoff on the bottom and top text, seems like some other field instead of just part of the same document.","turn_id":"01a10d17-989f-7150-9fa5-0c502f3fed47"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_01a10d2c-8564-7413-b861-aca58880da0a","order":2371,"revision":"retained_01a10d2c-8564-7413-b861-accc583a263c","text":"slash commands also don't seem to work yet, when typing / a menu should appear like on web with different options for me to input corresponding to different elements in a typist/markdown document like headers, tables, links, etc. just like the editor on web","turn_id":"01a10d17-989f-7150-9fa5-0c502f3fed47"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_01a10d2c-f33d-7770-858b-3dbbffeac92d","order":2372,"revision":"retained_01a10d2c-f33d-7770-858b-3dd16a2cc42d","text":"you should also cocnsider not dumpuing everything in app.rs and instead splitting things up more to make easy to parallelize work. think of your package structure. make things easily searchable.","turn_id":"01a10d17-989f-7150-9fa5-0c502f3fed47"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_01a10d5f-b8d1-7bb0-bf15-011f62014650","order":2381,"revision":"retained_01a10d5f-b8d1-7bb0-bf15-013c3e7533d6","text":"how have you decided to structure the project so far? how are you doing with grasping the current state? are thehre  ways that wouldl help you investigate issues a nd solve problems here faster?","turn_id":"01a10d4c-a644-7d71-9054-bf5cd3583d03"}],"user_messages_incomplete":true,"verified_answers":[]},"window_id":"01a10dcd-3be4-7563-a430-6a2bafc39153","window_number":65}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-05T20:41:56.467Z","ordinal":45905,"type":"world_state","payload":{"full":true,"state":{"agents_md":{"directory":"/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne","text":"<!-- headroom:rtk-instructions -->\n# Shell commands\n\nPrefix shell commands with `rtk`, including each segment of a command chain.\nUse `rtk proxy <command>` for unfiltered output or when debugging filter behavior.\n<!-- /headroom:rtk-instructions -->\n\n--- project-doc ---\n\n<!-- convex-ai-start -->\n\nThis project uses [Convex](https://convex.dev) as its backend.\n\nWhen working on Convex code, **always read `convex/_generated/ai/guidelines.md` first** for important guidelines on how to correctly use Convex APIs and patterns. The file contains rules that override what you may have learned about Convex from training data.\n\nConvex agent skills for common tasks can be installed by running `npx convex ai-files install`.\n\n<!-- convex-ai-end -->\n"},"apps_instructions":false,"collaboration_mode":{"mode":"default","model":"gpt-6.1-sol","instructions":"0a11049b0421e1e86f1e129af8d547a89548a0c3"},"context_window_guidance":"","environments":{"environments":{"local":{"cwd":"/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne","status":"available","shell":"bash"}},"current_date":"2026-10-05","timezone":"America/Toronto","filesystem":"<filesystem><workspace_roots><root>/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne</root></workspace_roots><permission_profile type=\"disabled\"><file_system type=\"unrestricted\" /></permission_profile></filesystem>","subagents":"<agent name=\"/root/cli_repair\" />\n<agent name=\"/root/native_assets\" />\n<agent name=\"/root/port_contract\" />\n<agent name=\"/root/rich_document\" />\n<agent name=\"/root/workspace_exchange\" />"},"environments_instructions":false,"git_attribution":false,"host_skills":{"body":"\n## Skills\nA skill is a set of local instructions to follow that is stored in a `SKILL.md` file. Below is the list of skills that can be used. Each entry includes a name, description, and a short path that can be expanded into an absolute path using the skill roots table.\n### Skill roots\n- `r0` = `/home/diogenes/.codex/skills`\n- `r1` = `/home/diogenes/.agents/skills`\n- `r2` = `/home/diogenes/.codex/skills/.system`\n- `r3` = `/home/diogenes/.codex/plugins/cache/openai-bundled`\n- `r4` = `/home/diogenes/.codex/plugins/cache/openai-curated-remote/google-drive/0.1.16/skills`\n- `r5` = `/home/diogenes/.codex/plugins/cache/openai-curated-remote/pages/0.1.20/skills`\n- `r6` = `/home/diogenes/.codex/plugins/cache/openai-curated-remote`\n- `r7` = `/home/diogenes/.codex/plugins/cache/openai-curated-remote/sites/0.1.75/skills`\n- `r8` = `/home/diogenes/.codex/plugins/cache/openai-curated-remote/work-pets/0.1.6/skills`\n- `r9` = `/home/diogenes/.codex/plugins/cache/openai-primary-runtime`\n- `r10` = `/home/diogenes/.codex/plugins/cache/openai-primary-runtime/spreadsheets/26.905.11957/skills`\n- `r11` = `/home/diogenes/.codex/plugins/cache/typesafe-ai`\n- `r12` = `/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne/.agents/skills`\n### Available skills\n- imagegen: Generate or edit raster images when the task benefits from AI-created bitmap visuals such as photos, illustrations, te (file: r2/imagegen/SKILL.md)\n- openai-docs: Use for Codex models/pricing, scheduled tasks, skills, settings, setup, troubleshooting, customization, automations, and (file: r2/openai-docs/SKILL.md)\n- skill-creator: Create or update a Codex skill with appropriately scoped instructions and any needed supporting resources. (file: r2/skill-creator/SKILL.md)\n- skill-installer: Install Codex skills into $CODEX_HOME/skills from a curated list or a GitHub repo path. Use when a user asks to list ins (file: r2/skill-installer/SKILL.md)\n- arize-admin: Manages Arize users, organizations, spaces, projects, roles, role bindings, resource restrictions, and API keys via the (file: r12/arize-admin/SKILL.md)\n- arize-ai-provider-integration: Creates, reads, updates, and deletes Arize AI integrations that store LLM provider credentials used by evaluators and o (file: r12/arize-ai-provider-integration/SKILL.md)\n- arize-annotation: Creates and manages annotation configs (categorical, continuous, freeform label schemas) and annotation queues (human (file: r12/arize-annotation/SKILL.md)\n- arize-compliance-audit: INVOKE THIS SKILL when auditing an AI agent or LLM app for regulatory compliance. Covers EU AI Act, GPAI Code of Prac (file: r12/arize-compliance-audit/SKILL.md)\n- arize-dataset: Creates, manages, and queries Arize datasets and examples. Covers dataset CRUD, appending examples, exporting data, and (file: r12/arize-dataset/SKILL.md)\n- arize-evaluator: Handles LLM-as-judge and code evaluator workflows on Arize including creating/updating evaluators, running evaluations  (file: r12/arize-evaluator/SKILL.md)\n- arize-experiment: Creates, runs, and analyzes Arize experiments for evaluating and comparing model performance. Covers experiment CRUD, (file: r12/arize-experiment/SKILL.md)\n- arize-instrumentation: Adds Arize AX tracing to an LLM application for the first time. Follows a two-phase agent-assisted flow to analyze the  (file: r12/arize-instrumentation/SKILL.md)\n- arize-link: Generates deep links to the Arize UI for traces, spans, sessions, datasets, labeling queues, evaluators, and annotati (file: r12/arize-link/SKILL.md)\n- arize-prompt-optimization: Optimizes, improves, and debugs LLM prompts using production trace data, evaluations, and annotations. Extracts prompts (file: r12/arize-prompt-optimization/SKILL.md)\n- arize-prompts: INVOKE THIS SKILL for Arize Prompt Hub and `ax prompts` workflows: author or import templates and save (Workflows A–B (file: r12/arize-prompts/SKILL.md)\n- arize-trace: Downloads, exports, and inspects existing Arize traces and spans to understand what an LLM app is doing or debug runtim (file: r12/arize-trace/SKILL.md)\n- convex: Convex is the backend agents get right on the first try: an all-TypeScript reactive platform where the database, serv (file: r12/convex/SKILL.md)\n- convex-acquire-domain: Find and buy a domain for the current Convex app through Convex, then bind it (labs; spend action). (file: r12/convex-acquire-domain/SKILL.md)\n- convex-add: Add a capability to the CURRENT Convex app — consults the served Convex capability catalog for always-current procedure (file: r12/convex-add/SKILL.md)\n- convex-advisor: Read the Convex deployment's 72h insights (read limits, OCC contention), root-cause each event in code, report eviden (file: r12/convex-advisor/SKILL.md)\n- convex-agent: Add an AI agent / RAG backend (@convex-dev/agent) to the Convex app. (file: r12/convex-agent/SKILL.md)\n- convex-auth: Add authentication (passkeys/OAuth) to the current Convex app, including the auth.config.ts wiring. (file: r12/convex-auth/SKILL.md)\n- convex-authz: Audit and harden Convex authorization: identity-from-arg impersonation, missing per-document ownership checks, PII-le (file: r12/convex-authz/SKILL.md)\n- convex-backup: Set up Convex backups and run a restore DRILL that proves recovery — snapshot, restore into a throwaway preview, asse (file: r12/convex-backup/SKILL.md)\n- convex-billing: Add Stripe billing/payments to the Convex app via @convex-dev/stripe (checkout + webhook + gating). (file: r12/convex-billing/SKILL.md)\n- convex-check-updates: Check the current app's pinned Convex components against recommended versions and upgrade them behind a build gate. (file: r12/convex-check-updates/SKILL.md)\n- convex-cost: Preview Convex spend — rank functions by bytes/documents-read × call-volume from insights, project each cost driver's gr (file: r12/convex-cost/SKILL.md)\n- convex-create-component: Builds reusable Convex components with isolated tables and app-facing APIs. Use for new components, reusable backend mo (file: r12/convex-create-component/SKILL.md)\n- convex-crons: Add recurring scheduled jobs (crons) to the Convex app. (file: r12/convex-crons/SKILL.md)\n- convex-deploy-guard: Classify + announce the targ