{"timestamp":"2026-10-05T20:42:16.227Z","ordinal":45919,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a10dcd-8923-7c93-8f7a-ff510bb69e10","call_id":"call_8tquLhUAoBrKIZtGIobGYvGI","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.4 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"i\":0,\"status\":\"fulfilled\",\"value\":{\"chunk_id\":\"2f2138\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000023358,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":2528,\"output\":\"60:# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/baste Makepad versus GPUI studio-framework selection\\n62:applies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/baste; reuse_rule=confirm the current GPUI/GPUI Kit release and target platforms before implementation because GPUI is pre-1.0.\\n64:## Task 1: Compare Makepad and GPUI for a Baste studio\\n68:- rollout_summaries/2026-10-04T04-46-42-dK0S-makepad_vs_gpui_baste_studio.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/baste, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/10/04/rollout-2026-10-04T00-46-42-01a1053c-5484-7860-b895-c654c9e25fd6.jsonl, updated_at=2026-10-04T04:47:19+00:00, thread_id=01a1053c-5484-7860-b895-c654c9e25fd6, success; direct framework comparison)\\n72:- Makepad, GPUI, GPUI Kit, Rust GUI, Zed, Studio, WASM, native desktop, candidate grids, inspectors, generation queues\\n76:- when asking “makepad v gpui” -> give a direct comparative assessment and decision fit rather than starting implementation work [Task 1]\\n80:- GPUI is the Baste default for a dense native productivity studio: entities/shared state, declarative views, imperative custom elements, keyboard actions, async services, and testing support fit projects, candidate grids, inspectors, and generation queues. [Task 1]\\n82:- GPUI Kit is separate from core GPUI; verify its exact matching version and accessibility/component capabilities instead of attributing them to GPUI itself. [Task 1]\\n86:- GPUI is pre-1.0 with frequent breaking changes -> inspect the exact release/fork and Zed source before committing Baste architecture to an API or platform assumption. [Task 1]\\n186:## Task 1: Diagnose, remove, and benchmark typing stalls\\n190:- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/10/03/rollout-2026-10-03T03-57-25-01a100c4-9324-7193-800f-e17e11a4d1a2.jsonl, updated_at=2026-10-03T09:02:50+00:00, thread_id=01a100c4-9324-7193-800f-e17e11a4d1a2, success; benchmarked and production-smoked)\\n194:- Tiptap, ProseMirror, Typst, typing-latency, flushVisual, mark-anchor-widgets, input-to-frame, p99, test:typing, typing-performance.yml\\n208:- when typing lag was “unacceptable” -> prioritize measured keystroke responsiveness and production/browser evidence, not static code inspection; acceptance was “feels fairly fast now and smooth” [Task 1]\\n220:- Cold Vite/lazy-module compilation can make `.ProseMirror` absent before latency sampling -> use a separately bounded readiness wait (up to 60 seconds), record startup independently, and do not retry/average it into typing measurements. Activate Proof before asserting proof page count because Write view intentionally leaves proof stale. [Task 1]\\n472:# Task Group: intent-first prompting and autonomous comparative prototyping\\n480:- rollout_summaries/2026-10-02T00-14-41-Rkbe-intent_first_prototyping_prompting_workflow.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/10/01/rollout-2026-10-01T20-14-41-01a0f9f6-93bb-7e81-89ce-93463a016870.jsonl, updated_at=2026-10-02T00:15:59+00:00, thread_id=01a0f9f6-93bb-7e81-89ce-93463a016870, success; workflow preference assessed, not quantitatively measured)\\n484:- intent behind the solution, use its best judgement, three separate solutions, prototyping, fluid organization, joyful interaction, fewer intuitive flags, human in the loop\\n491:- when the user is “prototyping the whole way through ... less human in the loop” -> build inspectable prototypes autonomously, then reserve their attention for comparison and experiential acceptance [Task 1]\\n553:# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/twyne fluid manuscript editor, House attention policy, and Claude-work continuation\\n565:- all in flow, flow-surface.tsx, flow-ribbon.tsx, manuscript-panel.tsx, twyne-editor.tsx, margin-surface.ts, MARGIN_SLOT_EVENT, OPEN_MARGIN_THREAD_EVENT, pneumatic post, galley slip, way in, 5180\\n579:- when shaping the manuscript experience, the user wants it “all in flow,” with the side panel retained for deliberate browsing -> prioritize inline margin surfaces, quiet queues, and progressive disclosure over new panel-first workflows [Task 1]\\n590:- Scoped success is not full-project success: unrelated docs typing issues (`bun:test`/Bun types and `marked`) blocked full TypeScript. Report the focused E2E, formatting, diff check, and temporary scoped TypeScript result precisely. [Task 1]\\n746:scope: Make Typst authoring/proof and generated initial artwork feel native to Twyne’s paper/ink/vermilion writing desk while preserving editable manuscript text, export fidelity, and explicit publication gates.\\n767:- illuminated-initials, drop-cap, imagegen, transparent-assets, AVIF, Typst, browser-print, twyne-release-023, landing-options, manuscript garden\\n778:- Preserve Typst E2E accessible names `Write`, `Source`, `Proof`, `Apply source`, `Manuscript workspace`, `Typst source`, and `Typeset page N`. The workspace sources are `src/components/editor/typst-workspace.tsx`, `typst-workspace.css`, and `typst-code-editor.ts`; established toolbar/icon conventions are `compositor-panel.tsx`, `global.css`, `src/components/ui/icon.tsx`, and `src/utils/icon-system.ts`. [Task 1]\\n780:- The current drop cap is CSS-driven at `.twyne-editor .ProseMirror > p:first-of-type::first-letter`; artwork must layer around the editable opening character, not replace manuscript text. Relevant helpers include `src/utils/illuminated-initials.ts`, `print-ornaments.ts`, `page-ornaments.ts`, and `src/utils/typst/decorative-assets.ts`. [Task 2]\\n787:- A successful isolated commit is not publication. The gallery at `public/assets/landing/options-2026-09/index.html` contains five options; option 3 “the manuscript garden” was only an assistant recommendation and publication remains on hold. [Task 2]\\n801:- option-01, option-03, option-05, The editorial table, The manuscript garden, The impression, landing-page.tsx, WorkspaceTour, engraved-2026-09, image/avif, handleDefaultAvatar\\n836:- when the user said “i really like one three and five, I would like those to be used” and approved the sequence -> use option 3 “The manuscript garden” as hero, option 1 “The editorial table” at the editorial-room introduction, and option 5 “The impression” at the closing invitation; use existing landing surfaces rather than a carousel [Task 1]\\n906:- Twyne’s release sequence is `bun run release:version`, `bun run release:check`, then `bun run release:publish`; release check requires an annotated matching `v<package.version>` tag. v0.22.1 is `692fe6b6d3c48a2a09299e616a58548e3569b5da` / `v0.22.1`, with source plus Linux/macOS/Windows desktop assets. [Task 1]\\n1348:- `src/components/ui/workflow-stamp.tsx` supplies Filed/Revised states; Revised is tied to accepted manuscript edits and dossier flows. Twyne’s expected visual baseline is editorial, ink-on-paper, restrained UI with reduced-motion handling. [Task 1]\\n1356:applies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne; reuse_rule=reuse the separate brief-edition model for saved replacements, not manuscript revisions or unsaved typing; browser interaction remains a required proof boundary.\\n1390:- A first completion claimed the typing bug fixed without exercising it -> type checking/handler inspection is insufficient; verify real input interaction when a browser exists. CUA reported `Browser is not available: iab` and no browsers, so this remains unverified. [Task 1]\\n2338:- Jev, TypeSafe, systemone, search_typing_safe, borderless inspector, footer scanability, auto-mode classifier, skate typesafe_api_key@secrets\\n2350:- Search-mode safety was checked mechanically by enumerating printable characters through `resolveAction(..., \\\"search\\\")`; none are intercepted. Apply the evidence rather than trusting Jev's lower `search_typing_safe` score. [Task 2]\\n2443:- Ancestor `preventdefault:dragover`, `preventdefault:dragleave`, and `preventdefault:drop` in `src/components/editor/manuscript-panel.tsx` are handled by Qwik's capture listener before ProseMirror, making events `defaultPrevented` and disabling native text/image drops. Remove them; `SectionReorder` is not the general blocker. Filter the overlay by `event.dataTransfer` so it appears only for file drags. [Task 1]\\n2446:- `DEFAULT_LAYOUT.marginBottom: 1` overrides the normal 4rem fallback, and nested scrollers lack `scrollMargin`/`scrollThreshold`. Twyne's IndexedDB/service-worker shell is genuinely local-first, but sync, AI, auth, collaboration, and publishing remain remote; browser local models likely use Transformers.js/WebGPU/cached ONNX and desktop has a LiteRT seam. [Task 2]\\n3422:- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/06/rollout-2026-09-06T08-03-56-01a0769a-914d-7531-b321-a4f223dd58f3.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-06T12:50:34+00:00, thread_id=01a0769a-914d-7531-b321-a4f223dd58f3, partial; test typing unresolved)\\n4548:scope: Update the Typst manuscript and published PDF from current implementation and reproducible evidence, not prose alone.\\n4568:- Manuscript entrypoint is `docs/study.typ`; sections live under `docs/study/sections/`, generated evidence under `docs/generated/`, frozen policy at `docs/study/evaluated-policy.json`, traces in `test/traces/`, curated data in `test/final_dataset.json`, and the published PDF at `web/public/keating-metaharness.pdf`. [Task 1]\\n5075:- when requesting “full dubplex voice” that can “edit and add information searach and interact with the app,” and premium/credit use -> show captions, action state, consent, wallet/cost ceilings, and require approval before manuscript mutation. [Task 2]\\n5082:- Draft edits are proposals first: later spoken/UI approval checks manuscript revision, rejects ambiguous repeated passages, preserves rich text, remains undoable, and stops when the workspace/folio changes. Only provider-returned research results may be described as web results; local placeholders are rejected. [Task 2]\\n\"}}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"i\":1,\"status\":\"fulfilled\",\"value\":{\"chunk_id\":\"eac2e4\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000030415,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":2499,\"output\":\" M .env.example\\n M .storybook/preview.ts\\n M README.md\\n M bun.lock\\n M convex/_generated/api.d.ts\\n M convex/account.ts\\n M convex/auth.ts\\n M convex/integrations.ts\\n M convex/lib/notorganicSignIn.ts\\n M convex/schema.ts\\n M convex/sync.ts\\n M devenv.lock\\n M devenv.nix\\n M docs/DEPLOYMENT.md\\n M docs/launch-film.md\\n M docs/typst-native-editor-plan.md\\n M e2e/typst-export.e2e.ts\\n M package.json\\n M playwright.config.ts\\n M public/licenses/typst-fonts.txt\\n M scripts/live-voice-relay.mjs\\n M server.js\\n M skills-lock.json\\n M src/assets/typst/README.md\\n M src/components/auth/account-menu.tsx\\n M src/components/auth/auth-panel.tsx\\n M src/components/collaboration/share-dialog.tsx\\n M src/components/editor/compositor-panel.tsx\\n M src/components/editor/editor-state.ts\\n M src/components/editor/extensions/mark-anchor-widgets.ts\\n M src/components/editor/extensions/quick-review.test.ts\\n M src/components/editor/extensions/quick-review.ts\\n M src/components/editor/extensions/remote-cursors.ts\\n M src/components/editor/extensions/section-reorder.ts\\n M src/components/editor/extensions/struggle-tracker.ts\\n M src/components/editor/floating-table-toolbar.tsx\\n M src/components/editor/manuscript-panel.tsx\\n M src/components/edit