_center()\n                    .gap(px(8.))\n                    .child(cancel)\n                    .child(confirm),\n            )\n            .into_any_element()\n    }\n}\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":31248},"formatted_output":"//! Original centered note/diagram dialog presentation; document ownership stays\n//! in the host. Copy is generated from insert-panels.tsx.\nuse super::*;\nuse crate::{\n    chrome::{press_button, tracked_typewriter},\n    theme::{BUTTON_FONT, DISPLAY_FONT, TYPEWRITER_FONT},\n};\nuse gpui_kit::component::button::{Button, ButtonVariants};\nuse gpui_kit::{AnyElement, BoxShadow, FontWeight, MouseButton, point};\n\nimpl InsertFormView {\n    pub(super) fn render_text_modal(&self, window: &Window, cx: &mut Context<Self>) -> AnyElement {\n        let p = *palette(cx);\n        let spec = crate::insert_menu::modal_spec::spec(self.kind).unwrap();\n        let focused = self.primary.read(cx).focus_handle(cx).is_focused(window);\n        let disabled = self.retired || self.primary.read(cx).value().trim().is_empty();\n        let wide =\n            self.kind == FormKind::Mermaid && f32::from(window.viewport_size().width) >= 768.;\n        let input = div()\n            .flex_1()\n            .min_w_0()\n            .child(\n                div()\n                    .id(\"slash-insert-label\")\n                    .test_support()\n                    .mb(px(4.))\n                    .child(tracked_typewriter(\n                        &spec.input_label.to_uppercase(),\n                        10.4,\n                        1.872,\n                        p.ink_muted,\n                    )),\n            )\n            .child(\n                div()\n                    .id(\"slash-insert-primary\")\n                    .test_support()\n                    .relative()\n                    .child(\n                        Textarea::new(&self.primary)\n                            .accessibility_id(\"slash-text-modal-input\")\n                            .aria_label(spec.input_label.clone())\n                            .appearance(false)\n                            .w_full()\n                            .h(px(spec.min_height_rem * 16.))\n                            .min_h(px(spec.min_height_rem * 16.))\n                            .px(px(12.))\n                            .py(px(8.))\n                            .border_1()\n                            .border_color(rgb(if focused { p.vermilion } else { p.rule }))\n                            .rounded(px(2.))\n                            .bg(rgb(p.paper_soft))\n                            .text_color(rgb(p.ink))\n                            .font_family(TYPEWRITER_FONT)\n                            .font_weight(FontWeight::NORMAL)\n                            .text_size(px(14.))\n                            .line_height(px(21.)),\n                    ),\n            )\n            .child(\n                div()\n                    .id(\"slash-insert-help\")\n                    .test_support()\n                    .mt(px(8.))\n                    .font_family(TYPEWRITER_FONT)\n                    .text_size(px(10.88))\n                    .line_height(px(16.32))\n                    .text_color(rgb(p.ink_muted))\n                    .child(spec.help_text.clone()),\n            );\n        let body = div()\n            .mt(px(16.))\n            .flex()\n            .when(wide, |s| s.flex_row().gap(px(16.)))\n            .when(!wide, |s| s.flex_col().gap(px(16.)))\n            .child(input)\n            .when(self.kind == FormKind::Mermaid, |s| {\n                s.child(\n                    div()\n                        .flex_1()\n                        .min_w_0()\n                        .child(\n                            div().mb(px(4.)).child(tracked_typewriter(\n                                &spec\n                                    .preview_label\n                                    .as_deref()\n                                    .unwrap_or(\"Preview\")\n                                    .to_uppercase(),\n                                10.4,\n                                1.872,\n                                p.ink_muted,\n                            )),\n                        )\n                        .child(self.preview_element(cx)),\n                )\n            });\n        let cancel = Button::new(\"slash-insert-cancel\")\n            .ghost()\n            .h_auto()\n            .track_focus(&self.cancel_focus)\n            .accessibility_label(\"Cancel\")\n            .px(px(14.4))\n            .py(px(7.2))\n            .border_1()\n            .border_color(rgb(p.rule))\n            .rounded(px(2.))\n            .bg(rgb(p.paper_soft))\n            .text_color(rgb(p.ink))\n            .font_family(BUTTON_FONT)\n            .font_weight(FontWeight::SEMIBOLD)\n            .text_size(px(12.))\n            .line_height(px(16.))\n            .child(\"Cancel\")\n            .on_click(cx.listener(|this, _, _, cx| this.cancel(cx)));\n        // Existing press chrome uses the original font/tracking and button padding.\n        // Literal copied labels have a stable lifetime in the generated catalog.\n        let label: &'static str = crate::insert_menu::modal_spec::spec(self.kind)\n            .unwrap()\n            .submit_label\n            .as_str();\n        let confirm = press_button(\"slash-insert-confirm\", label, 11.2, cx)\n            .h_auto()\n            .track_focus(&self.submit_focus)\n            .bg(rgb(p.vermilion))\n            .border_color(rgb(p.vermilion))\n            .line_height(px(14.933333))\n            .disabled(disabled)\n            .on_click(cx.listener(|this, _, _, cx| this.submit(cx)));\n        div()\n            .id(\"slash-insert-form\")\n            .test_support()\n            .role(Role::Dialog)\n            .aria_label(spec.title.clone())\n            .occlude()\n            .w_full()\n            .max_w(px(if self.kind == FormKind::Mermaid {\n                896.\n            } else {\n                512.\n            }))\n            .flex()\n            .flex_col()\n            .p(px(20.))\n            .bg(rgb(p.paper_soft))\n            .text_color(rgb(p.ink))\n            .border_1()\n            .border_color(rgb(p.rule))\n            .shadow(vec![\n                BoxShadow {\n                    color: rgb(p.emboss).opacity(0.6).into(),\n                    offset: point(px(0.), px(1.)),\n                    blur_radius: px(0.),\n                    spread_radius: px(0.),\n                    inset: true,\n                },\n                BoxShadow {\n                    color: rgb(p.shade).opacity(0.4).into(),\n                    offset: point(px(0.), px(14.)),\n                    blur_radius: px(32.),\n                    spread_radius: px(-22.),\n                    inset: false,\n                },\n                BoxShadow {\n                    color: rgb(p.shade).opacity(0.05).into(),\n                    offset: point(px(0.), px(2.)),\n                    blur_radius: px(0.),\n                    spread_radius: px(0.),\n                    inset: false,\n                },\n            ])\n            .on_mouse_down(MouseButton::Left, |_, _, cx| cx.stop_propagation())\n            .on_click(|_, _, cx| cx.stop_propagation())\n            .capture_action(\n                cx.listener(|this, _: &gpui_kit::base::input::Escape, _, cx| {\n                    if this.primary.read(cx).is_composing() {\n                        cx.propagate();\n                        return;\n                    }\n                    this.cancel(cx);\n                    cx.stop_propagation();\n                }),\n            )\n            .capture_action(\n                cx.listener(|this, action: &gpui_kit::base::input::Enter, _, cx| {\n                    if action.secondary && !this.primary.read(cx).is_composing() {\n                        this.submit(cx);\n                        cx.stop_propagation();\n                    } else {\n                        cx.propagate();\n                    }\n                }),\n            )\n            .capture_action(cx.listener(\n                |_, _: &gpui_kit::base::input::IndentInline, window, cx| {\n                    window.focus_next(cx);\n                    cx.stop_propagation();\n                },\n            ))\n            .capture_action(cx.listener(\n                |_, _: &gpui_kit::base::input::OutdentInline, window, cx| {\n                    window.focus_prev(cx);\n                    cx.stop_propagation();\n                },\n            ))\n            .child(div().mb(px(8.)).child(tracked_typewriter(\n                &spec.kicker.to_uppercase(),\n                10.,\n                3.2,\n                p.ink_muted,\n            )))\n            .child(\n                div()\n                    .id(\"slash-insert-title\")\n                    .test_support()\n                    .font_family(DISPLAY_FONT)\n                    .font_weight(FontWeight::SEMIBOLD)\n                    .text_size(px(16.))\n                    .line_height(px(24.))\n                    .child(spec.title.clone()),\n            )\n            .child(\n                div()\n                    .id(\"slash-insert-description\")\n                    .test_support()\n                    .mt(px(8.))\n                    .font_family(SANS_FONT)\n                    .text_size(px(14.))\n                    .line_height(px(22.75))\n                    .text_color(rgb(p.ink_light))\n                    .child(spec.description.clone()),\n            )\n            .child(body)\n            .child(\n                div()\n                    .mt(px(20.))\n                    .flex()\n                    .justify_end()\n                    .items_center()\n                    .gap(px(8.))\n                    .child(cancel)\n                    .child(confirm),\n            )\n            .into_any_element()\n    }\n}\n"},"started_at_ms":1791232949206,"completed_at_ms":1791232949207}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-05T20:42:29.254Z","ordinal":45929,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a10537-909f-77a3-96d8-dd07161f91ae","turn_id":"01a10daa-98ac-7341-8bf7-59561f3acc7f","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-3ef2cd89-be38-4325-8c69-59aa9277ffbf","process_id":"83324","command":["/bin/bash","-lc","rtk proxy python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('desktop/gpui/src')\nfor d in sorted(p.iterdir()):\n if d.is_dir():\n  files=list(d.rglob('*.rs')); print(f'{d.name}/: {len(files)} files, {sum(len(f.read_text().splitlines()) for f in files)} lines')\nfor file in ['app.rs','rich_editor/view.rs','main.rs','lib.rs']:\n p=Path('desktop/gpui/src')/file\n if p.exists(): print(f'{file}: {len(p.read_text().splitlines())} lines')\nPY"],"cwd":"file:///home/diogenes/Projects/twyne","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"rtk proxy python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('desktop/gpui/src')\nfor d in sorted(p.iterdir()):\n if d.is_dir():\n  files=list(d.rglob('*.rs')); print(f'{d.name}/: {len(files)} files, {sum(len(f.read_text().splitlines()) for f in files)} lines')\nfor file in ['app.rs','rich_editor/view.rs','main.rs','lib.rs']:\n p=Path('desktop/gpui/src')/file\n if p.exists(): print(f'{file}: {len(p.read_text().splitlines())} lines')\nPY"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"app/: 29 files, 19797 lines\nchrome/: 2 files, 162 lines\ndossier_conversation/: 7 files, 3650 lines\neditor/: 34 files, 25924 lines\ngen_ui/: 27 files, 6647 lines\ninsert_menu/: 15 files, 2482 lines\nnative_accounts/: 9 files, 3651 lines\nnative_ai/: 9 files, 3027 lines\nnative_audio/: 10 files, 2998 lines\nnative_collaboration/: 8 files, 1528 lines\napp.rs: 4399 lines\nmain.rs: 577 lines\nlib.rs: 83 lines\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"app/: 29 files, 19797 lines\nchrome/: 2 files, 162 lines\ndossier_conversation/: 7 files, 3650 lines\neditor/: 34 files, 25924 lines\ngen_ui/: 27 files, 6647 lines\ninsert_menu/: 15 files, 2482 lines\nnative_accounts/: 9 files, 3651 lines\nnative_ai/: 9 files, 3027 lines\nnative_audio/: 10 files, 2998 lines\nnative_collaboration/: 8 files, 1528 lines\napp.rs: 4399 lines\nmain.rs: 577 lines\nlib.rs: 83 lines\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":34342},"formatted_output":"app/: 29 files, 19797 lines\nchrome/: 2 files, 162 lines\ndossier_conversation/: 7 files, 3650 lines\neditor/: 34 files, 25924 lines\ngen_ui/: 27 files, 6647 lines\ninsert_menu/: 15 files, 2482 lines\nnative_accounts/: 9 files, 3651 lines\nnative_ai/: 9 files, 3027 lines\nnative_audio/: 10 files, 2998 lines\nnative_collaboration/: 8 files, 1528 lines\napp.rs: 4399 lines\nmain.rs: 577 lines\nlib.rs: 83 lines\n"},"started_at_ms":1791232949254,"completed_at_ms":1791232949254}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-05T20:42:29.418Z","ordinal":45930,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a10dcd-bca9-7a32-a691-0346cfa5ebb7","call_id":"call_4nsX0JCrKk5GI6cFwBvEn3Gi","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.4 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"i\":0,\"status\":\"fulfilled\",\"value\":{\"chunk_id\":\"8cd577\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000027153,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":2173,\"output\":\"# Native module map\\n\\nThe original Electrobun-hosted Twyne is the behavioral and visual reference.\\nRust owns the native UI, local manuscripts, rich transactions, and Typst rendering.\\nThe Bun document helper reuses the existing source converters. The connected SDK\\nis a separate prepared boundary; its presence does not mean account sync is mounted.\\n\\n## Package boundaries and ownership\\n\\n| Package or module | Owns | Keep outside it |\\n| --- | --- | --- |\\n| `src/app.rs` | Writing-room state, startup, active document, save/navigation orchestration | New feature rendering, command catalogs, document algorithms |\\n| `src/app/room_layout.rs` | Room composition and mounting existing surfaces | Insertion algorithms, provider calls, persistence |\\n| `src/app/*_coordinator.rs` | One feature's host state, subscriptions, focus and document identity | Another feature's implementation |\\n| `src/editor/{model,transaction,command}.rs` | Structured document tree, scalar selections, transactions, history | GPUI, account state, file/network access |\\n| `src/editor/view*.rs` | Native input, layout, pagination and editor interaction | Authored Typst reconciliation, room routing |\\n| `src/insert_menu/` | Source catalog/search, query detection, insertion adapters, retained list and forms | Active manuscript ownership and saving |\\n| `workspace`, `source_session`, `semantic_bridge`, `source_editor`, `source_view` | Authored Typst, recoverable source drafts and verified visual projection | Treating cached HTML as canonical authored source |\\n| `storage`, `manuscript`, `revisions` | Local files, manuscript metadata and revision persistence | UI focus and popup state |\\n| `native_accounts/`, `tools/connected/` | Native account contracts and Bun SDK transport/session boundary | Implicit attachment of guest writing to an account |\\n| `native_collaboration/` | Sharing roles, presence and publishing contracts | Claiming prepared requests are live collaborative editing |\\n| `native_ai/`, `gen_ui/` | AI request/stream/freshness rules and retained writing-tool cards | Network calls or document mutation from a card renderer |\\n| `native_audio/` | Optional audio state, PCM, segment and transport rules | Claiming synthetic checks establish device/provider behavior |\\n| `theme`, `assets`, `chrome` | Shared original colors, fonts, artwork and controls | Feature-specific document behavior |\\n\\n`app.rs` is still larger than intended. Move coherent responsibilities into sibling\\nmodules as they are worked on, keeping the host entry points small. Do not split a\\nfile solely to meet a line count or add a second owner of document state.\\n\\nThe next coherent host extractions are Source/Proof coordination, library/file\\nactions, and room chrome rendering. Their existing host methods and feature\\ntests provide the boundary; extraction must preserve flush and departure order.\\n\\n## Investigate a feature\\n\\n| Native entry point | Original reference | Focused verification |\\n| --- | --- | --- |\\n| `app/manuscript_coordinator.rs` | `components/editor/manuscript-panel.tsx`, `global.css` | `app/manuscript_tests.rs` |\\n| `app/slash_coordinator.rs`, `insert_menu/` | `components/editor/extensions/slash-command.ts`, `slash-command-menu.tsx`, `utils/editor-commands.ts`, `utils/slash-command-filter.ts` | `insert_menu/tests.rs`, `app/slash_tests.rs`, `fixtures/insert-menu/` |\\n| `editor/view_insert.rs` | `components/editor/twyne-editor.tsx` registry dispatch | Pure rich transaction tests and mounted slash tests |\\n| `insert_menu/table_grid.rs`, `insert_menu/table_picker.rs` | `components/editor/table-insertion-grid.tsx` | Executed Source vectors, mounted pointer/key tests, actual-font captures |\\n| `editor/view_shortcuts.rs` | `utils/keybindings.ts` and command priority | Mounted rich shortcuts; code-block exit/undo in `editor/tests.rs` |\\n| `compositor.rs` | `components/editor/compositor-panel.tsx`, `utils/compositor-toolbar.ts` | `fixtures/chrome/`, `fixtures/editor/` |\\n| `app/account_coordinator.rs` | `components/auth/{account-menu,auth-panel}.tsx` | `app/tests.rs`, `fixtures/connected-work/` |\\n| `source_view.rs`, `source_editor.rs` | `components/editor/typst-code-editor.ts` | `fixtures/source_view/` |\\n| `gen_ui/`, `app/gen_ui_coordinator.rs` | Writing-tool cards and tool contracts | `fixtures/gen-ui/` |\\n\\nOriginal paths in this table are relative to the repository's `src/` directory.\\nStart with the feature's coordinator, then its package and original counterpart:\\n\\n```bash\\nrtk proxy rg -n 'insert_from_slash|refresh_insert_menu' desktop/gpui/src\\nrtk proxy rg -n 'insert.table|runRegistryCommand' src/components/editor/twyne-editor.tsx\\n```\\n\\n## Editor contracts\\n\\n- Plain-text input offsets are **UTF-8 bytes**. Rich document offsets are\\n  **Unicode scalars**. Source ProseMirror offsets are **UTF-16 positions**.\\n  Convert at the adapter boundary, never guess from string length.\\n- Detect a slash from the current line/text block before the collapsed caret.\\n  Opening or dismissing the menu does not modify the document.\\n- Activation binds the manuscript, selection/query and revision. Immediate\\n  commands remove the query and insert the element in one native history group.\\n- Parameter commands remove the query when activated, as the original editor\\n  does. Cancel leaves that removal intact. The retained picker/form must validate\\n  its manuscript, editor, post-removal caret and revision before committing;\\n  plain input also compares the retained post-removal body at that boundary.\\n  Failed or stale commits leave the document at its current state.\\n- Native parameter removal and commit are separate undo steps. Original\\n  ProseMirror time grouping is a separate comparison gate. IME confirmation\\n  belongs to the composing input.\\n- Feature surfaces emit intent; the active-document host accepts it. Each surface\\n  has an explicit owner and clears its pending work on document departure.\\n- Keep keystroke work local. Whole-document conversion and serialization happen\\n  at explicit freshness boundaries, not as a side effect of showing a menu.\\n\\n## Fast checks and evidence\\n\\nOne owner runs Cargo commands to avoid competing for the build lock. Other agents\\ncan work on independent pure modules, fixtures, or original behavior in parallel.\\nGive weaker external agents bounded inputs and inspect their output before adoption.\\n\\nThe crate gates GPUI behind `desktop`; document rules can be checked without\\nloading a UI. `tools/sync-insert-menu.ts --check` executes the original catalog,\\nsearch and extracted pure table helpers, so reference drift is detected before\\nnative adapter work. A displayed shortcut must also have a mounted behavior\\ncheck; a matching label alone is insufficient.\\n\\n```bash\\nrtk proxy devenv shell -- rtk proxy cargo test --locked --offline --no-default-features --lib --manifest-path desktop/gpui/Cargo.toml insert_menu\\nrtk proxy devenv shell -- rtk proxy cargo test --locked --offline --features ui-tests --bin twyne-desktop --manifest-path desktop/gpui/Cargo.toml slash_\\nrtk proxy devenv shell -- rtk proxy cargo test --locked --offline --features ui-tests --bin twyne-desktop --manifest-path desktop/gpui/Cargo.toml manuscript_title_\\n```\\n\\nMounted tests exercise controls and history using GPUI's test text system. Check\\nfonts, clipping and actual pixels separately with `tools/capture-native.py`, an\\nimmutable binary, a known fixture, window size and scale, and an isolated library.\\nRecord the binary and source hashes with that observation. Do not use the user's\\nopen writing session as a test fixture.\\n\\nBuilds, pure tests, mounted controls, native GPU captures, browser comparisons,\\nreal account/provider use, and distribution/device checks are separate evidence.\\nCurrent feature status belongs in `PORT_PLAN.md`; do not infer readiness from\\nthe existence of a module or a prepared contract.\\n\\n## Reproduce an issue quickly\\n\\n1. Identify the owning coordinator and original counterpart in the table above.\\n2. Reduce the issue to an isolated manuscript and explicit route, view, selection,\\n   window size and scale. Reuse an existing fixture when possible.\\n3. Check document rules with a pure test, focus/events with a mounted test, and\\n   clipping or spacing with original-browser and actual-native captures.\\n4. Record the exact binary, helper and source hashes. Keep historical receipts\\n   intact so an old successful build is never mistaken for the current one.\\n\\nFor parallel work, assign one package or fixture with an explicit input/output\\ncontract. The host retains document ownership; workers emit intent. Small\\nexternal-model tasks work best for reference extraction and bounded review,\\nwith root validation of every proposed behavioral change. Cargo stays serial.\\n\"}}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"i\":1,\"status\":\"fulfilled\",\"value\":{\"chunk_id\":\"ed6910\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000028714,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":773,\"output\":\"[package]\\nname = \\\"twyne-desktop\\\"\\nversion = \\\"0.1.0\\\"\\nedition = \\\"2024\\\"\\nrust-version = \\\"1.92\\\"\\ndescription = \\\"Twyne's native, offline writing room, built with GPUI\\\"\\npublish = false\\n\\n[features]\\ndefault = [\\\"desktop\\\"]\\ndesktop = [\\\"dep:gpui-kit\\\", \\\"dep:image\\\", \\\"dep:roxmltree\\\", \\\"dep:base64\\\", \\\"dep:hypher\\\", \\\"dep:unicode-linebreak\\\", \\\"dep:x11rb\\\", \\\"dep:gpui-linux\\\", \\\"native-typst\\\"]\\nnative-typst = [\\\"dep:typst\\\", \\\"dep:typst-pdf\\\", \\\"dep:typst-svg\\\", \\\"dep:sha2\\\", \\\"dep:image\\\"]\\nnative-audio = [\\\"dep:sha2\\\"]\\nui-tests = [\\\"desktop\\\", \\\"gpui-kit/test-support\\\", \\\"gpui-linux?/test-support\\\"]\\n\\n[dependencies]\\nanyhow = \\\"1.0\\\"\\ndirectories = \\\"6.0\\\"\\nfs2 = \\\"0.4\\\"\\ngpui-kit = { version = \\\"=0.7.0\\\", optional = true }\\nchrono = \\\"=0.4.45\\\"\\nhtml5ever = \\\"=0.27.0\\\"\\nunicode-segmentation = \\\"=1.13.3\\\"\\nmarkup5ever_rcdom = \\\"=0.3.0\\\"\\nimage = { version = \\\"=0.25.10\\\", default-features = false, features = [\\\"png\\\", \\\"webp\\\", \\\"jpeg\\\", \\\"gif\\\"], optional = true }\\nroxmltree = { version = \\\"=0.20.0\\\", optional = true }\\nbase64 = { version = \\\"=0.22.1\\\", optional = true }\\nhypher = { version = \\\"=0.1.8\\\", default-features = false, features = [\\\"alloc\\\", \\\"english\\\"], optional = true }\\nunicode-linebreak = { version = \\\"=0.1.5\\\", optional = true }\\nserde = { version = \\\"1.0\\\", features = [\\\"derive\\\", \\\"rc\\\"] }\\nserde_json = \\\"1.0\\\"\\nregex = \\\"=1.13.1\\\"\\nunicode-normalization = \\\"=0.1.25\\\"\\nurl = \\\"=2.5.8\\\"\\ntempfile = \\\"3.23\\\"\\nuuid = { version = \\\"1.18\\\", features = [\\\"v4\\\", \\\"serde\\\"] }\\nsha2 = { version = \\\"=0.10.9\\\", optional = true }\\ntypst = { git = \\\"https://github.com/Myriad-Dreamin/typst.git\\\", rev = \\\"951788cc614cd805d5d786e17bbf93796df73d10\\\", optional = true }\\ntypst-pdf = { git = \\\"https://github.com/Myriad-Dreamin/typst.git\\\", rev = \\\"951788cc614cd805d5d786e17bbf93796df73d10\\\", optional = true }\\ntypst-svg = { git = \\\"https://github.com/Myriad-Dreamin/typst.git\\\", rev = \\\"951788cc614cd805d5d786e17bbf93796df73d10\\\", optional = true }\\n\\n[target.'cfg(target_os = \\\"linux\\\")'.dependencies]\\nx11rb = { version = \\\"=0.13.2\\\", optional = true }\\ngpui-linux = { package = \\\"gpui-pre-linux\\\", version = \\\"=0.3.7\\\", default-features = false, features = [\\\"wayland\\\"], optional = true }\\n\\n[[bin]]\\nname = \\\"twyne-desktop\\\"\\npath = \\\"src/main.rs\\\"\\nrequired-features = [\\\"desktop\\\"]\\n\\n[[example]]\\nname = \\\"twyne-clipboard-probe\\\"\\npath = \\\"fixtures/editor/clipboard-probe.rs\\\"\\nrequired-features = [\\\"desktop\\\"]\\n\\n[[example]]\\nname = \\\"twyne-wayland-clipboard-probe\\\"\\npath = \\\"fixtures/wayland-clipboard/native-probe.rs\\\"\\nrequired-features = [\\\"desktop\\\"]\\n\\n[[example]]\\nname = \\\"twyne-dossier-multiply-probe\\\"\\npath = \\\"fixtures/dossier-multiply/native-probe/main.rs\\\"\\nrequired-features = [\\\"ui-tests\\\"]\\n\\n[[test]]\\nname = \\\"native-audio-contract\\\"\\npath = \\\"fixtures/native-audio/synthetic_loopback.rs\\\"\\nrequired-features = [\\\"native-audio\\\"]\\n\\n[[example]]\\nname = \\\"twyne-connected-probe\\\"\\npath = \\\"fixtures/connected-work/native-probe.rs\\\"\\nrequired-features = [\\\"desktop\\\"]\\n\\n[profile.dev]\\ndebug = 0\\n\\n[patch.crates-io]\\ngpui-base = { path = \\\"vendor/gpui-base\\\" }\\ngpui-pre = { path = \\\"vendor/gpui-pre\\\" }\\ngpui-pre-wgpu = { path = \\\"vendor/gpui-pre-wgpu\\\" }\\ngpui-pre-linux = { path = \\\"vendor/gpui-pre-linux\\\" }\\n\\n[profile.release]\\nlto = \\\"thin\\\"\\ncodegen-units = 1\\nstrip = true\\n\"}}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"i\":2,\"status\":\"fulfilled\",\"value\":{\"chunk_id\":\"3e7e85\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000031248,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":2370,\"output\":\"//! Original centered note/diagram dialog presentation; document ownership stays\\n//! in the host. Copy is generated from insert-panels.tsx.\\nuse super::*;\\nuse crate::{\\n    chrome::{press_button, tracked_typewriter},\\n    theme::{BUTTON_FONT, DISPLAY_FONT, TYPEWRITER_FONT},\\n};\\nuse gpui_kit::component::button::{Button, ButtonVariants};\\nuse gpui_kit::{AnyElement, BoxShadow, FontWeight, MouseButton, point};\\n\\nimpl InsertFormView {\\n    pub(super) fn render_text_modal(&self, window: &Window, cx: &mut Context<Self>) -> AnyElement {\\n        let p = *palette(cx);\\n        let spec = crate::insert_menu::modal_spec::spec(self.kind).unwrap();\\n        let focused = self.primary.read(cx).focus_handle(cx).is_focused(window);\\n        let disabled = self.retired || self.primary.read(cx).value().trim().is_empty();\\n        let wide =\\n            self.kind == FormKind::Mermaid && f32::from(window.viewport_size().width) >= 768.;\\n        let input = div()\\n            .flex_1()\\n            .min_w_0()\\n            .child(\\n                div()\\n                    .id(\\\"slash-insert-label\\\")\\n                    .test_support()\\n                    .mb(px(4.))\\n                    .child(tracked_typewriter(\\n                        &spec.input_label.to_uppercase(),\\n                        10.4,\\n                        1.872,\\n                        p.ink_muted,\\n                    )),\\n            )\\n            .child(\\n                div()\\n                    .id(\\\"slash-insert-primary\\\")\\n                    .test_support()\\n                    .relative()\\n                    .child(\\n                        Textarea::new(&self.primary)\\n                            .accessibility_id(\\\"slash-text-modal-input\\\")\\n                            .aria_label(spec.input_label.clone())\\n                            .appearance(false)\\n                            .w_full()\\n                            .h(px(spec.min_height_rem * 16.))\\n                            .min_h(px(spec.min_height_rem * 16.))\\n                            .px(px(12.))\\n                            .py(px(8.))\\n                            .border_1()\\n                            .border_color(rgb(if focused { p.vermilion } else { p.rule }))\\n                            .rounded(px(2.))\\n                            .bg(rgb(p.paper_soft))\\n                            .text_color(rgb(p.ink))\\n                            .font_family(TYPEWRITER_FONT)\\n                            .font_weight(FontWeight::NORMAL)\\n                            .text_size(px(14.))\\n                            .line_height(px(21.)),\\n                    ),\\n            )\\n            .child(\\n                div()\\n                    .id(\\\"slash-insert-help\\\")\\n                    .test_support()\\n                    .mt(px(8.))\\n                    .font_family(TYPEWRITER_FONT)\\n                    .text_size(px(10.88))\\n                    .line_height(px(16.32))\\n                    .text_color(rgb(p.ink_muted))\\n                    .child(spec.help_text.clone()),\\n            );\\n        let body = div()\\n            .mt(px(16.))\\n            .flex()\\n            .when(wide, |s| s.flex_row().gap(px(16.)))\\n            .when(!wide, |s| s.flex_col().gap(px(16.)))\\n            .child(input)\\n            .when(self.kind == FormKind::Mermaid, |s| {\\n                s.child(\\n                    div()\\n                        .flex_1()\\n                        .min_w_0()\\n                        .child(\\n                            div().mb(px(4.)).child(tracked_typewriter(\\n                                &spec\\n                                    .preview_label\\n                                    .as_deref()\\n                                    .unwrap_or(\\\"Preview\\\")\\n                                    .to_uppercase(),\\n                                10.4,\\n                                1.872,\\n                                p.ink_muted,\\n                            )),\\n                        )\\n                        .child(self.preview_element(cx)),\\n                )\\n            });\\n        let cancel = Button::new(\\\"slash-insert-cancel\\\")\\n            .ghost()\\n            .h_auto()\\n            .track_focus(&self.cancel_focus)\\n            .accessibility_label(\\\"Cancel\\\")\\n            .px(px(14.4))\\n            .py(px(7.2))\\n            .border_1()\\n            .border_color(rgb(p.rule))\\n            .rounded(px(2.))\\n            .bg(rgb(p.paper_soft))\\n            .text_color(rgb(p.ink))\\n            .font_family(BUTTON_FONT)\\n            .font_weight(FontWeight::SEMIBOLD)\\n            .text_size(px(12.))\\n            .line_height(px(16.))\\n            .child(\\\"Cancel\\\")\\n            .on_click(cx.listener(|this, _, _, cx| this.cancel(cx)));\\n        // Existing press chrome uses the original font/tracking and button padding.\\n        // Literal copied labels have a stable lifetime in the generated catalog.\\n        let label: &'static str = crate::insert_menu::modal_spec::spec(self.kind)\\n            .unwrap()\\n            .submit_label\\n            .as_str();\\n        let confirm = press_button(\\\"slash-insert-confirm\\\", label, 11.2, cx)\\n            .h_auto()\\n            .track_focus(&self.submit_focus)\\n            .bg(rgb(p.vermilion))\\n            .border_color(rgb(p.vermilion))\\n            .line_height(px(14.933333))\\n            .disabled(disabled)\\n            .on_click(cx.listener(|this, _, _, cx| this.submit(cx)));\\n        div()\\n            .id(\\\"slash-insert-form\\\")\\n            .test_support()\\n            .role(Role::Dialog)\\n            .aria_label(spec.title.clone())\\n            .occlude()\\n            .w_full()\\n            .max_w(px(if self.kind == FormKind::Mermaid {\\n                896.\\n            } else {\\n                512.\\n            }))\\n            .flex()\\n            .flex_col()\\n            .p(px(20.))\\n            .bg(rgb(p.paper_soft))\\n            .text_color(rgb(p.ink))\\n            .border_1()\\n            .border_color(rgb(p.rule))\\n            .shadow(vec![\\n                BoxShadow {\\n                    color: rgb(p.emboss).opacity(0.6).into(),\\n                    offset: point(px(0.), px(1.)),\\n                    blur_radius: px(0.),\\n                    spread_radius: px(0.),\\n                    inset: true,\\n                },\\n                BoxShadow {\\n                    color: rgb(p.shade).opacity(0.4).into(),\\n                    offset: point(px(0.), px(14.)),\\n                    blur_radius: px(32.),\\n                    spread_radius: px(-22.),\\n                    inset: false,\\n                },\\n                BoxShadow {\\n                    color: rgb(p.shade).opacity(0.05).into(),\\n                    offset: point(px(0.), px(2.)),\\n                    blur_radius: px(0.),\\n                    spread_radius: px(0.),\\n                    inset: false,\\n                },\\n            ])\\n            .on_mouse_down(MouseButton::Left, |_, _, cx| cx.stop_propagation())\\n            .on_click(|_, _, cx| cx.stop_propagation())\\n            .capture_action(\\n                cx.listener(|this, _: &gpui_kit::base::input::Escape, _, cx| {\\n                    if this.primary.read(cx).is_composing() {\\n                        cx.propagate();\\n                        return;\\n                    }\\n                    this.cancel(cx);\\n                    cx.stop_propagation();\\n                }),\\n            )\\n            .capture_action(\\n                cx.listener(|this, action: &gpui_kit::base::input::Enter, _, cx| {\\n                    if action.secondary && !this.primary.read(cx).is_composing() {\\n                        this.submit(cx);\\n                        cx.stop_propagation();\\n                    } else {\\n                        cx.propagate();\\n                    }\\n                }),\\n            )\\n            .capture_action(cx.listener(\\n                |_, _: &gpui_kit::base::input::IndentInline, window, cx| {\\n                    window.focus_next(cx);\\n                    cx.stop_propagation();\\n                },\\n            ))\\n            .capture_action(cx.listener(\\n                |_, _: &gpui_kit::base::input::OutdentInline, window, cx| {\\n                    window.focus_prev(cx);\\n                    cx.stop_propagation();\\n                },\\n            ))\\n            .child(div().mb(px(8.)).child(tracked_typewriter(\\n                &spec.kicker.to_uppercase(),\\n                10.,\\n                3.2,\\n                p.ink_muted,\\n            )))\\n            .child(\\n                div()\\n                    .id(\\\"slash-insert-title\\\")\\n                    .test_support()\\n                    .font_family(DISPLAY_FONT)\\n                    .font_weight(FontWeight::SEMIBOLD)\\n                    .text_size(px(16.))\\n                    .line_height(px(24.))\\n                    .child(spec.title.clone()),\\n            )\\n            .child(\\n                div()\\n                    .id(\\\"slash-insert-description\\\")\\n                    .test_support()\\n                    .mt(px(8.))\\n                    .font_family(SANS_FONT)\\n                    .text_size(px(14.))\\n                    .line_height(px(22.75))\\n                    .text_color(rgb(p.ink_light))\\n                    .child(spec.description.clone()),\\n            )\\n            .child(body)\\n            .child(\\n                div()\\n                    .mt(px(20.))\\n                    .flex()\\n                    .justify_end()\\n                    .items_center()\\n                    .gap(px(8.))\\n                    .child(cancel)\\n                    .child(confirm),\\n            )\\n            .into_any_element()\\n    }\\n}\\n\"}}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"i\":3,\"status\":\"fulfilled\",\"value\":{\"chunk_id\":\"48d0e7\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000034342,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":100,\"output\":\"app/: 29 files, 19797 lines\\nchrome/: 2 files, 162 lines\\ndossier_conversation/: 7 files, 3650 lines\\neditor/: 34 files, 25924 lines\\ngen_ui/: 27 files, 6647 lines\\ninsert_menu/: 15 files, 2482 lines\\nnative_accounts/: 9 files, 3651 lines\\nnative_ai/: 9 files, 3027 lines\\nnative_audio/: 10 files, 2998 lines\\nnative_collaboration/: 8 files, 1528 lines\\napp.rs: 4399 lines\\nmain.rs: 577 lines\\nlib.rs: 83 lines\\n\"}}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"i\":4,\"status\":\"fulfilled\",\"value\":{\"chunk_id\":\"87259b\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.00003228,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":616,\"output\":\"# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/twyne fluid manuscript editor, House attention policy, and Claude-work continuation\\nscope: Continue and critique Twyne’s in-flow writing surfaces while preserving deliberate side-panel browsing, authorship, scoped validation boundaries, and return-to-writing continuity.\\napplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne; reuse_rule=reinspect the dirty worktree, running Vite server, current House/flow contracts, and authenticated/model/sync behavior before treating local fixture results as complete product proof.\\n\\n## Task 1: Continue and verify Claude’s unfinished fluid-editor UI\\n\\n### rollout_summary_files\\n\\n- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/30/rollout-2026-09-30T02-30-15-01a0f101-b3b4-7e41-9e3c-8d3ec580aba0.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-30T08:46:14+00:00, thread_id=01a0f101-b3b4-7e41-9e3c-8d3ec580aba0, partial; scoped E2E/format/diff/TypeScript checks passed, full typecheck remained blocked)\\n\\n### keywords\\n\\n- all in flow, flow-surface.tsx, flow-ribbon.tsx, manuscript-panel.tsx, twyne-editor.tsx, margin-surface.ts, MARGIN_SLOT_EVENT, OPEN_MARGIN_THREAD_EVENT, pneumatic post, galley slip, way in, 5180\\n\\n## Task 2: Assess attention-policy and House-model direction\\n\\n### rollout_summary_files\\n\\n- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/30/rollout-2026-09-30T02-30-15-01a0f101-b3b4-7e41-9e3c-8d3ec580aba0.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-30T08:46:14+00:00, thread_id=01a0f101-b3b4-7e41-9e3c-8d3ec580aba0, success; source, plan, tests, browser evidence, and gaps compared)\\n\\n### keywords\\n\\n- shared attention policy, flow-conductor.ts, House, Collection, Folio, dossier, amendments, flow-state.ts, flow-profile.ts, flow-connections.ts, TF-IDF, Jev, stuckPauseMs\\n\\n## User preferences\\n\\n- when shaping the manuscript experience, the user wants it “all in flow,” with the side panel retained for deliberate browsing -> prioritize inline margin surfaces, quiet queues, and progressive disclosure over new panel-first workflows [Task 1]\\n- on large Twyne features, the user explicitly prefers UI/design work first and allows backend/plumbing to be delegated to Codex -> preserve that sequencing [Task 1]\\n\\n## Reusable knowledge\\n\\n\"}}"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a10daa-98ac-7341-8bf7-59561f3acc7f","create_time":1791232949.4179368}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
