{"timestamp":"2026-10-05T20:45:29.699Z","ordinal":46012,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a10537-909f-77a3-96d8-dd07161f91ae","turn_id":"01a10daa-98ac-7341-8bf7-59561f3acc7f","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-b3673049-d3a0-45f2-a162-87f7b0be4acb","process_id":"32742","command":["/bin/bash","-lc","rtk proxy sed -n '1,100p' desktop/gpui/target/verification/sakana-mermaid-backend-cb6894944912/response.txt"],"cwd":"file:///home/diogenes/Projects/twyne","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"rtk proxy sed -n '1,100p' desktop/gpui/target/verification/sakana-mermaid-backend-cb6894944912/response.txt"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"{\n  \"review\": {\n    \"kind\": \"read-only design review\",\n    \"target\": \"Twyne GPUI native port: live Mermaid preview and manuscript diagrams at parity with the web renderer\",\n    \"status\": \"proposal only; no files edited; no rendering executed; no completion claimed\",\n    \"constraint_acknowledged\": \"No system Chrome, provider, package, or implementation is assumed installed. A configured diagnostic browser may supply evidence but does not establish a bundled default. Static fixtures are treated as test oracles only, never as a production renderer.\"\n  },\n\n  \"frozen_inputs\": {\n    \"src/components/editor/mermaid-theme.ts\": {\n      \"sha256\": \"db26bb43aa9fee42faa825cdf6c2d4220c59e854cfba61dec70121cb5526cb12\",\n      \"role\": \"Shared web Mermaid config and render entry point\"\n    },\n    \"desktop/gpui/tools/semantic-worker.ts\": {\n      \"sha256\": \"7a0846d1f8dc2013b9e6b819b376790bf90195676a446cc63d37014fbbbc8aa3\",\n      \"role\": \"Bun local document helper; JSON over stdin/stdout; contains no Mermaid command\"\n    },\n    \"desktop/gpui/src/inline_proof.rs\": {\n      \"sha256\": \"5d3650ae4f3bc4c3a084792e0be697f243afbb5f7d7f527129240bd9252821f7\",\n      \"role\": \"Native bounded atom renderer plus SVG admission contract\"\n    },\n    \"desktop/gpui/tools/build-helper.ts\": {\n      \"sha256\": \"bf836dcaccae6474b5f47aaa16beefef4197d378ab83574816280f6fb63f85f4\",\n      \"role\": \"Build orchestration for helper binaries and cargo\"\n    }\n  },\n\n  \"current_state\": {\n    \"web_reference\": {\n      \"symbols\": [\"initializeTwyneMermaid\", \"renderTwyneMermaid\"],\n      \"behavior\": \"Dynamic import('mermaid'); initialize({startOnLoad:false, theme:'base', themeVariables:{...16 concrete editorial tokens...}}); renderTwyneMermaid(id, source) returns mermaid.render(id, source).svg.\",\n      \"theme_tokens\": {\n        \"fontFamily\": \"Lora, 'Crimson Pro', Georgia, 'Times New Roman', serif\",\n        \"primaryColor\": \"#f4ecd8\",\n        \"primaryBorderColor\": \"#1f1b16\",\n        \"primaryTextColor\": \"#1f1b16\",\n        \"secondaryColor\": \"#efe6cf\",\n        \"secondaryBorderColor\": \"#1f1b16\",\n        \"secondaryTextColor\": \"#1f1b16\",\n        \"tertiaryColor\": \"#f4ecd8\",\n        \"tertiaryBorderColor\": \"#c1272d\",\n        \"tertiaryTextColor\": \"#1f1b16\",\n        \"lineColor\": \"#1f1b16\",\n        \"textColor\": \"#1f1b16\",\n        \"mainBkg\": \"#f4ecd8\",\n        \"nodeBorder\": \"#1f1b16\",\n        \"clusterBkg\": \"#efe6cf\",\n        \"clusterBorder\": \"#1f1b16\",\n        \"edgeLabelBackground\": \"#f4ecd8\"\n      },\n      \"note\": \"The frozen config sets neither securityLevel nor flowchart.htmlLabels.\"\n    },\n    \"native_helper\": {\n      \"symbols\": [\"Request\", \"execute\", \"MAX_REQUEST_BYTES\", \"isBibliographyEntry\", \"import.meta.main\"],\n      \"behavior\": \"The Request union has no Mermaid member. The only rendering case is command 'renderInline', which throws 'This inline renderer is unavailable.' unless kind === 'latex'. LaTeX is rendered by embedding #twyne-math(...) into Typst via prepareTypstAssets and extracting the SVG from image(bytes(...), format:\\\"svg\\\"). The only DOM available is JSDOM used for DOMParser and textContent; it provides no SVG layout or text measurement.\"\n    },\n    \"native_renderer\": {\n      \"symbols\": [\n        \"AtomKind\",\n        \"AtomRenderRequest::key\",\n        \"AtomRenderKey\",\n        \"AtomFidelity\",\n        \"AtomRenderImage\",\n        \"AtomErrorKind\",\n        \"AtomRenderError::retryable\",\n        \"InlineSvgBackend\",\n        \"DocumentHelperBackend::render\",\n        \"InlineProofRenderer::render\",\n        \"InlineProofRenderer::render_uncached\",\n        \"image_from_svg\",\n        \"svg_length\"\n      ],\n      \"behavior\": \"AtomKind::Mermaid exists. DocumentHelperBackend::render forwards to bridge.render_inline(\\\"mermaid\\\", source, true) and maps every error to AtomErrorKind::RendererUnavailable because kind == AtomKind::Mermaid. Success would carry AtomFidelity::MermaidBackend. image_from_svg is the admission gate.\"\n    },\n    \"build\": {\n      \"symbols\": [\"build-helper.ts top-level steps\"],\n      \"behavior\": \"Bun build --compile for semantic-worker.ts -> target/document/twyne-document (minified), then copy to target/release; build-connected.ts is a separate resident SDK helper; math-write.ts -> twyne-math-write is explicitly NOT minified because KaTeX tree classes are inspected. Optional cargo build/run --locked follows. No Mermaid asset, browser, or font is staged anywhere.\"\n    }\n  },\n\n  \"what_existing_helper_can_render\": [\n    \"LaTeX math to SVG via command 'renderInline' with kind 'latex' (Typst-embedded #twyne-math), surfaced in Rust as AtomFidelity::WebMathJaxProof. The source comment states KaTeX Write font/layout parity is unverified.\",\n    \"Standalone native Typst atoms to SVG via TypstEngine::compile, surfaced as AtomFidelity::NativeTypst (not through the helper).\",\n    \"SVG shapes that pass admission: standalone SVG namespace, positive finite viewBox, width/height in ex/em/pt/px/unitless, only '#'-or-'data:' hrefs/src, <text> and <path> content.\",\n    \"Non-rendering document semantics: fromMarkdown, starter, project, fromHtml, reconcile, libraryCardText, orderFolioNames, localTimestamp, rubricDraftContext, apparatusDetect, apparatusScanHtml, citationFindRange, apparatusFormat, apparatusBuildDetected, rubricRoomParts, prepareProof.\"\n  ],\n\n  \"what_existing_helper_cannot_render\": [\n    \"Mermaid, at all. There is no Mermaid command in the Request union and no Mermaid case in execute. DocumentHelperBackend::render reaches renderInline, which rejects kind !== 'latex'. The test mermaid_unavailability_never_substitutes_a_fake_diagram asserts RendererUnavailable with the real bridge.\",\n    \"Any SVG containing <foreignObject> or <script>. image_from_svg rejects these by tag name.\",\n    \"Any SVG whose href or src is not '#'- or 'data:'-prefixed. Remote image resources are rejected.\",\n    \"Anything requiring browser text measurement. JSDOM supplies DOMParser only; it has no getBBox, no computed layout, no font metrics.\",\n    \"RawTypst nodes, which are intentionally source-visible per the module doc comment.\",\n    \"Mermaid fences inside manuscript markdown: fromMarkdown runs marked then htmlToTypst; no Mermaid-to-diagram step exists in that path.\"\n  ],\n\n  \"browser_only_constraints\": {\n    \"why_foreignObject_matters\": \"Mermaid's default flowchart renderer emits HTML labels inside <foreignObject>. No native SVG rasterizer in this stack renders foreignObject, so the guard in image_from_svg is not incidental; it is the exact boundary that makes a default browser Mermaid SVG unusable natively.\",\n    \"dom_bound_layout\": \"mermaid.render requires a document plus real layout and text measurement (node sizing, label wrapping, cluster spacing). A parser-only DOM cannot produce geometry.\",\n    \"config_implication\": \"Reusing the frozen mermaid-theme.ts as written is likely to produce foreignObject output for flowcharts, because neither securityLevel nor flowchart.htmlLabels is set. Producing admission-safe SVG requires htmlLabels:false, or evidence that the pinned Mermaid version already disables HTML labels under its default security level.\",\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"{\n  \"review\": {\n    \"kind\": \"read-only design review\",\n    \"target\": \"Twyne GPUI native port: live Mermaid preview and manuscript diagrams at parity with the web renderer\",\n    \"status\": \"proposal only; no files edited; no rendering executed; no completion claimed\",\n    \"constraint_acknowledged\": \"No system Chrome, provider, package, or implementation is assumed installed. A configured diagnostic browser may supply evidence but does not establish a bundled default. Static fixtures are treated as test oracles only, never as a production renderer.\"\n  },\n\n  \"frozen_inputs\": {\n    \"src/components/editor/mermaid-theme.ts\": {\n      \"sha256\": \"db26bb43aa9fee42faa825cdf6c2d4220c59e854cfba61dec70121cb5526cb12\",\n      \"role\": \"Shared web Mermaid config and render entry point\"\n    },\n    \"desktop/gpui/tools/semantic-worker.ts\": {\n      \"sha256\": \"7a0846d1f8dc2013b9e6b819b376790bf90195676a446cc63d37014fbbbc8aa3\",\n      \"role\": \"Bun local document helper; JSON over stdin/stdout; contains no Mermaid command\"\n    },\n    \"desktop/gpui/src/inline_proof.rs\": {\n      \"sha256\": \"5d3650ae4f3bc4c3a084792e0be697f243afbb5f7d7f527129240bd9252821f7\",\n      \"role\": \"Native bounded atom renderer plus SVG admission contract\"\n    },\n    \"desktop/gpui/tools/build-helper.ts\": {\n      \"sha256\": \"bf836dcaccae6474b5f47aaa16beefef4197d378ab83574816280f6fb63f85f4\",\n      \"role\": \"Build orchestration for helper binaries and cargo\"\n    }\n  },\n\n  \"current_state\": {\n    \"web_reference\": {\n      \"symbols\": [\"initializeTwyneMermaid\", \"renderTwyneMermaid\"],\n      \"behavior\": \"Dynamic import('mermaid'); initialize({startOnLoad:false, theme:'base', themeVariables:{...16 concrete editorial tokens...}}); renderTwyneMermaid(id, source) returns mermaid.render(id, source).svg.\",\n      \"theme_tokens\": {\n        \"fontFamily\": \"Lora, 'Crimson Pro', Georgia, 'Times New Roman', serif\",\n        \"primaryColor\": \"#f4ecd8\",\n        \"primaryBorderColor\": \"#1f1b16\",\n        \"primaryTextColor\": \"#1f1b16\",\n        \"secondaryColor\": \"#efe6cf\",\n        \"secondaryBorderColor\": \"#1f1b16\",\n        \"secondaryTextColor\": \"#1f1b16\",\n        \"tertiaryColor\": \"#f4ecd8\",\n        \"tertiaryBorderColor\": \"#c1272d\",\n        \"tertiaryTextColor\": \"#1f1b16\",\n        \"lineColor\": \"#1f1b16\",\n        \"textColor\": \"#1f1b16\",\n        \"mainBkg\": \"#f4ecd8\",\n        \"nodeBorder\": \"#1f1b16\",\n        \"clusterBkg\": \"#efe6cf\",\n        \"clusterBorder\": \"#1f1b16\",\n        \"edgeLabelBackground\": \"#f4ecd8\"\n      },\n      \"note\": \"The frozen config sets neither securityLevel nor flowchart.htmlLabels.\"\n    },\n    \"native_helper\": {\n      \"symbols\": [\"Request\", \"execute\", \"MAX_REQUEST_BYTES\", \"isBibliographyEntry\", \"import.meta.main\"],\n      \"behavior\": \"The Request union has no Mermaid member. The only rendering case is command 'renderInline', which throws 'This inline renderer is unavailable.' unless kind === 'latex'. LaTeX is rendered by embedding #twyne-math(...) into Typst via prepareTypstAssets and extracting the SVG from image(bytes(...), format:\\\"svg\\\"). The only DOM available is JSDOM used for DOMParser and textContent; it provides no SVG layout or text measurement.\"\n    },\n    \"native_renderer\": {\n      \"symbols\": [\n        \"AtomKind\",\n        \"AtomRenderRequest::key\",\n        \"AtomRenderKey\",\n        \"AtomFidelity\",\n        \"AtomRenderImage\",\n        \"AtomErrorKind\",\n        \"AtomRenderError::retryable\",\n        \"InlineSvgBackend\",\n        \"DocumentHelperBackend::render\",\n        \"InlineProofRenderer::render\",\n        \"InlineProofRenderer::render_uncached\",\n        \"image_from_svg\",\n        \"svg_length\"\n      ],\n      \"behavior\": \"AtomKind::Mermaid exists. DocumentHelperBackend::render forwards to bridge.render_inline(\\\"mermaid\\\", source, true) and maps every error to AtomErrorKind::RendererUnavailable because kind == AtomKind::Mermaid. Success would carry AtomFidelity::MermaidBackend. image_from_svg is the admission gate.\"\n    },\n    \"build\": {\n      \"symbols\": [\"build-helper.ts top-level steps\"],\n      \"behavior\": \"Bun build --compile for semantic-worker.ts -> target/document/twyne-document (minified), then copy to target/release; build-connected.ts is a separate resident SDK helper; math-write.ts -> twyne-math-write is explicitly NOT minified because KaTeX tree classes are inspected. Optional cargo build/run --locked follows. No Mermaid asset, browser, or font is staged anywhere.\"\n    }\n  },\n\n  \"what_existing_helper_can_render\": [\n    \"LaTeX math to SVG via command 'renderInline' with kind 'latex' (Typst-embedded #twyne-math), surfaced in Rust as AtomFidelity::WebMathJaxProof. The source comment states KaTeX Write font/layout parity is unverified.\",\n    \"Standalone native Typst atoms to SVG via TypstEngine::compile, surfaced as AtomFidelity::NativeTypst (not through the helper).\",\n    \"SVG shapes that pass admission: standalone SVG namespace, positive finite viewBox, width/height in ex/em/pt/px/unitless, only '#'-or-'data:' hrefs/src, <text> and <path> content.\",\n    \"Non-rendering document semantics: fromMarkdown, starter, project, fromHtml, reconcile, libraryCardText, orderFolioNames, localTimestamp, rubricDraftContext, apparatusDetect, apparatusScanHtml, citationFindRange, apparatusFormat, apparatusBuildDetected, rubricRoomParts, prepareProof.\"\n  ],\n\n  \"what_existing_helper_cannot_render\": [\n    \"Mermaid, at all. There is no Mermaid command in the Request union and no Mermaid case in execute. DocumentHelperBackend::render reaches renderInline, which rejects kind !== 'latex'. The test mermaid_unavailability_never_substitutes_a_fake_diagram asserts RendererUnavailable with the real bridge.\",\n    \"Any SVG containing <foreignObject> or <script>. image_from_svg rejects these by tag name.\",\n    \"Any SVG whose href or src is not '#'- or 'data:'-prefixed. Remote image resources are rejected.\",\n    \"Anything requiring browser text measurement. JSDOM supplies DOMParser only; it has no getBBox, no computed layout, no font metrics.\",\n    \"RawTypst nodes, which are intentionally source-visible per the module doc comment.\",\n    \"Mermaid fences inside manuscript markdown: fromMarkdown runs marked then htmlToTypst; no Mermaid-to-diagram step exists in that path.\"\n  ],\n\n  \"browser_only_constraints\": {\n    \"why_foreignObject_matters\": \"Mermaid's default flowchart renderer emits HTML labels inside <foreignObject>. No native SVG rasterizer in this stack renders foreignObject, so the guard in image_from_svg is not incidental; it is the exact boundary that makes a default browser Mermaid SVG unusable natively.\",\n    \"dom_bound_layout\": \"mermaid.render requires a document plus real layout and text measurement (node sizing, label wrapping, cluster spacing). A parser-only DOM cannot produce geometry.\",\n    \"config_implication\": \"Reusing the frozen mermaid-theme.ts as written is likely to produce foreignObject output for flowcharts, because neither securityLevel nor flowchart.htmlLabels is set. Producing admission-safe SVG requires htmlLabels:false, or evidence that the pinned Mermaid version already disables HTML labels under its default security level.\",\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":12929},"formatted_output":"{\n  \"review\": {\n    \"kind\": \"read-only design review\",\n    \"target\": \"Twyne GPUI native port: live Mermaid preview and manuscript diagrams at parity with the web renderer\",\n    \"status\": \"proposal only; no files edited; no rendering executed; no completion claimed\",\n    \"constraint_